\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Outcry over stalemate on Gaetz report; Bernie Sanders\u8217\'20\'19 Senate vote on blocking some arms to Israel fails \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); with Maanvi Singh, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, Anna Betts and Amy Sedghi (earlier) \par \uc2 14,254 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 November 2024\par 02:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live coverage has ended. Read the latest at the links below: House ethics committee deadlocked on releasing \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  reportUS Senate rejects Bernie Sanders effort to block sales of tank rounds to Israel\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 This live coverage is ending now, thanks for following along.\par \par \uc2 Here is the latest on the \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  report:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/20/matt-gaetz-house-ethics-committee-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House ethics committee deadlocked on whether to release Matt Gaetz report }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 China has renewed efforts to curry favour in Pacific island nations, a new report has found, after charting a \u8220\'20\'1Cresurgence\u8221\'20\'1D in Beijing-backed aid and infrastructure funding.\par \par \uc2 Over the past decade, China has lavished billions of dollars on Pacific island nations, part of ongoing efforts to build influence in competition with the US and its allies.\par \par \uc2 Having cut back on Pacific aid at the height of the Covid pandemic, China\u8217\'20\'19s commitments have climbed in recent years, Australia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Lowy Institute\uc2  said in a new study.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBeijing has emerged from a pandemic-induced lull with a more competitive, politically targeted model of aid engagement,\u8221\'20\'1D the thinktank said in its annual Pacific aid report on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe uptick in Chinese spending has been accompanied by a resurgence in new Chinese project commitments, signalling a revival in its ambition to engage in major infrastructure works in the Pacific.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Australia \u8211\'20\'13 traditionally the Pacific\u8217\'20\'19s partner of choice \u8211\'20\'13 remained the largest donor.\par \par \uc2 But US funding now narrowly trails that of China, the second-largest bilateral donor in the region, authors Alexandre Dayant and Riley Duke said.\par \par \uc2 In 2022, the most recent year with complete data, China spent $256m \u8211\'20\'13 up nearly 14% from three years earlier.\par \par \uc2 Australia spent $1.5bn, and the US $249m \u8211\'20\'13 both figures falling after a sharp increase the previous year.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/21/china-pacific-islands-aid-us-relationship-influence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Resurgence\u8217\'20\'19 in China aid to Pacific amid tussle with US for influence }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 US Secretary of Defense \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  expressed regret Wednesday that his Chinese counterpart chose not to hold talks with him during meetings of Southeast Asian defense chiefs in Laos, calling it a setback for the entire region.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Association of Southeast Asian Nations\uc2  is holding security talks in Vientiane at a time of increasing maritime disputes with China and as the transition to a new U.S. president approaches.\par \par \uc2 The decision by Chinese Defense Minister Dong Jun \u8220\'20\'1Cis a setback for the whole region,\u8221\'20\'1D Austin said after the first day of meetings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s unfortunate. It affects the region because the region really wants to see us, two significant players in the region, two significant powers, talk to each other, and that reassures the entire region,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 There was no immediate comment from China on its decision not to meet with Austin.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump nominates Pete Hoekstra as ambassador to Canada\par \par \uc2 Trump has nominated his former ambassador to the Netherlands, Pete Hoekstra, as his ambassador to Canada. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/jan/11/netherlands-holland-peter-hoekstra-ambassador"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here is how his first day as ambassador to the Netherlands went }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a statement released a moment ago, the president-elect said:\par \par \uc2 I am very pleased to announce that former Ambassador, and former Congressman, Pete Hoekstra, has been nominated as my United States Ambassador to Canada. Pete is well-respected in the Great State of Michigan - A State we won sizably. He represented Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s 2nd District in Congress for nearly 20 years, where he was also Chairman of the House Intelligence Committee, and was a great help to our Campaign as Chairman of the Michigan Republican Party.\par \par \uc2 I overhauled the disastrous NAFTA Agreement, the worst Trade Deal in the History of the United States, which was switched to the USMCA (Mexico/Canada), which no one thought could be done. We brought Trade with Mexico and Canada to a level playing field for our wonderful Farmers and Working Families. In my Second Term, Pete will help me once again put AMERICA FIRST. He did an outstanding job as United States Ambassador to the Netherlands during our first four years, and I am confident that he will continue to represent our Country well in this new role. Thank you, Pete!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 The US senate has blocked a measure to stop the sale of mortar rounds to Israel, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 Seventy-nine of the 100 senators have now opposed a resolution that would have blocked sales of tank rounds to Israel, while 18 approved it and one voted present.\par \par \uc2 The Senate is due to vote later today on two other resolutions that would stop shipments of two other types of offensive military equipment.\par \par \uc2 All of the votes in favour of the measure came from Democrats, while \u8220\'20\'1Cno\u8221\'20\'1D votes came from both Democrats and Republicans. Approval would have been a marked departure from decades of US congressional support for Israel, which for years was the biggest recipient of US military assistance.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1Cresolutions of disapproval\u8221\'20\'1D were filed by Senator Bernie Sanders, an independent who caucuses with Democrats, and co-sponsored by a handful of Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Backers hope that forcing a vote would encourage Israel\u8217\'20\'19s government and President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration to do more to prevent Israel from killing more civilians, and particularly children. Israeli forces have killed 17,400 children in Gaza in just over a year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 More detail now on the measure on tank rounds.\par \par \uc2 US Senate\uc2  has blocked legislation that would have halted the sale of some weapons to Israel, which had been introduced out of concern about the human rights catastrophe, and extremely high number of civilians and children Israeli forces have killed in the Palestinian territories.\par \par \uc2 As voting continued, 59 of the 100 senators opposed a resolution that would have blocked sales of tank rounds to Israel, while 15 supported it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate blocks measure to halt sales of tank rounds to Israel\par \par \uc2 The senate has blocked a measure that would have halted the sales of tank rounds to Israel, Reuters reports. Voting continues on the other measures.\par \par \uc2 The resolutions being voted on are to block the sale of 120mm mortar rounds, joint direct attack munitions (JDAMS), and tank rounds. They must pass both the Senate and the House of Representatives with a simple majority. If they pass, they go to the president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump likely to choose Johns Hopkins surgeon Martin Makary to lead \uc2 FDA\uc2  - report\par \par \uc2 Trump will probably choose Johns Hopkins surgeon and writer Martin Makary to lead the Food and Drug Administration, two sources familiar with the matter told Reuters on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Makary raised concerns about a number of public health issues during the Covid-19 pandemic, touting the protection from natural immunity and opposing Covid vaccine mandates.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  is the world\u8217\'20\'19s most influential drug regulator with a more than $7 billion budget. It is responsible for approving new treatments and assuring they are safe and effective before entering the biggest and most lucrative market. It has regulatory authority over human and veterinary drugs, biological medicines, medical devices and vaccines.\par \par \uc2 The agency is also responsible for maintaining safety standards for the food supply, tobacco, cosmetics, and products that emit radiation.\par \par \uc2 Brian Hughes, a spokesperson for the Trump transition team, said he would not speculate on or get ahead of any announcement.\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 FDA\uc2  commissioner, Makary would report to the head of the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 To lead \uc2 HHS\uc2 , Trump has nominated Robert F Kennedy Junior, an environmental activist who has spread misinformation about the safety of vaccines and one of several unconventional Trump picks for top administration jobs.\par \par \uc2 As a doctor, Makary was a co-developer of the Surgery Checklist, a routine for surgeons that improved patient outcomes and has been spread around the globe by the \uc2 World Health Organization\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 North Carolina Republican legislators gave final approval Wednesday to a series of political power moves that would weaken the incoming governor and other Democratic elected officials in the ninth-largest state, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re contained in a massive bill sprinkled with a new round of Hurricane Helene relief provisions and rushed through a lame-duck General Assembly session.\par \par \uc2 The Senate voted along party lines for the 131-page measure, which would alter yet again how the State Board of Elections is appointed, likely leading to a GOP majority on a panel now controlled by Democrats. It also would move up in 2025 several post-election deadlines after Republican complaints that counties took too long this month to count provisional and absentee ballots, especially in light of an extremely close Supreme Court race.\par \par \uc2 The House approved the same measure Tuesday night, so the bill goes next to the desk of outgoing Democratic Governor \uc2 Roy Cooper\uc2 , who has blasted the effort as \u8220\'20\'1Cmassive power grabs.\u8221\'20\'1D Other Democrats called provisions unconstitutional. Any veto override attempt would happen early next month.\par \par \uc2 The measure was approved less than 24 hours after it was made broadly public in the final weeks before Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 veto-proof majority ends, after electoral defeats in the House this month.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Federal investigators 'established trail of payments from Gaetz to women who testified he paid them for sex' \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/11/20/us/politics/matt-gaetz-venmo-payments-sex.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports }}}\uc2  that, "Federal investigators established a trail of payments from \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , President-elect \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s choice to be attorney general, to women including some who testified that Mr. Gaetz hired them for sex\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The story cites a document obtained by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and a lawyer who represents some of the women.\par \par \uc2 The story continues:\par \par \uc2 Federal investigators established a trail of payments from \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , President-elect \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s choice to be attorney general, to women including some who testified that Mr. Gaetz hired them for sex, according to a document obtained by \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  and a lawyer representing some of the women.\par \par \uc2 The document, assembled by investigators during a three-year sex-trafficking investigation into Mr. Gaetz, is a chart that shows a web of thousands of dollars in Venmo payments between Mr. Gaetz and a group of his friends, associates and women who had drug-fueled sex parties between 2017 and 2020, according to testimony that participants are said to have given to federal and congressional investigators.\par \par \uc2 At the parties, women, and a girl who was 17 at the time, were paid for sex, according to accounts of the participants\u8217\'20\'19 testimony from people briefed on what they said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Sanders addresses Senate ahead of vote to prevent further arms sales to Israel\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders is addressing the Senate now.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will tell you that our role [in the world] is significantly diminished if we continue to support Netanyahu,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. It will diminish the US\u8217\'20\'19s ability to critique other countries for their human rights records.\par \par \uc2 The war on Gaza is supported by American taxpayer dollars, as is the mass starvation of children, Sanders days.\par \par \uc2 He is speaking ahead of a vote on the joint resolutions of disapproval (JRDs), introduced by Senator Bernie Sanders in September, would prevent the Pentagon from sending another $20bn to Israel as it continues its assault on Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 which has killed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/gaza-war-deaths-surpass-43000-palestinian-health-ministry-reports-1975910"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 43,000 people }}}\uc2 , most of them women and children.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump could change his mind on the selection of Vought, Reuters reports, and there were other candidates for the role as recently as earlier this week, according to one of the sources.\par \par \uc2 The Trump transition team and Vought did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Trump repeatedly denied when campaigning for president that he had any links to Project 2025, although many of its authors were former officials from his first administration, including Vought.\par \par \uc2 At OMB, Vought will work with X CEO \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and former Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  to carry out Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign pledge to slash government spending and regulations.\par \par \uc2 Musk and Ramaswamy have been tapped by Trump to co-lead a newly created Department of Government Efficiency, an entity Trump has indicated will operate outside the confines of government.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is planning to tap conservative loyalist \uc2 Russell Vought\uc2  to be the director of the \uc2 US Office of Management and Budget\uc2 , according to two sources close to his transition effort who spoke to Reuters, putting him at the helm of a powerful agency that helps decide a president\u8217\'20\'19s policy priorities and how to pay for them.\par \par \uc2 Vought was OMB chief in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term and would play a key role in rolling back government regulations and setting budget priorities. In this position, he would be in a position to implement a policy known as Schedule F, which would in practice strip thousands of federal employees of some key civil service protections.\par \par \uc2 Vought helped produce a blueprint called Project 2025 by a coalition of conservative groups for a second Trump White House term. One of its proposals is to dramatically restructure the government so that appointed conservatives have power over key decisions typically relegated to civil servants.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Members of the House ethics committee were appeared to be deadlocked whether to release a report on their investigation into allegations of sexual misconduct involving \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorney general pick, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 . The former Florida congressman, shepherded by vice president-elect JD Vance, held meetings with key Senate allies involved in the Cabinet confirmation process at the Capitol on Wednesday, as Senate Democrats officially requested the files from the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s probe into whether Gaetz engaged in child sex trafficking.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Republican House speaker Mike Johnson announced that transgender women are not permitted to use women\u8217\'20\'19s bathrooms in the Capitol building, weeks after the election of the first transgender member of Congress, Sarah McBride. She responded: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not here to fight about bathrooms. I\u8217\'20\'19m here to fight for Delawareans and to bring down costs facing families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Also:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump announced he has chosen the former acting attorney general, \uc2 Matthew Whitaker\uc2 , as his nominee to serve as US ambassador to Nato. Trump is also expected to name his pick for treasury secretary as soon as today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers asked the judge overseeing his Manhattan hush-money criminal case for permission to make yet another play for dismissal.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  confirmed the Biden administration will allow Ukraine to use US-supplied antipersonnel landmines to help fight off Russian forces.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Austin said women in the US military \u8220\'20\'1Cmake us stronger\u8221\'20\'1D as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick for his successor, Pete Hegseth, faces scrutiny for previous remarks suggesting banning women from combat roles.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tech entrepreneurs \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  laid out their plans for the new Department of Government Efficiency, or Doge, in a Wall Street Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/opinion/musk-and-ramaswamy-the-doge-plan-to-reform-government-supreme-court-guidance-end-executive-power-grab-fa51c020?mod=hp_opin_pos_0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  op-ed }}}\uc2 . They pointed to recent Supreme Court rulings that they say can be used to take power away from federal agencies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A vote to block arms sales to Israel will be held on Wednesday in the Senate. The joint resolutions of disapproval (JRDs), introduced by the senator Bernie Sanders would prevent the Pentagon from sending another $20bn to Israel as it continues its assault on Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The state of Texas offered thousands of acres of land to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump }}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cto construct deportation facilities\u8221\'20\'1D and aid in his plans to begin a mass deportation of migrants as soon as he takes office.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 60 members of Congress have written to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden }}}\uc2  calling on him to use his presidential clemency powers to reunite families, address unfair sentencing policies, and begin to tackle the scourge of mass incarceration, which they said was eroding \u8220\'20\'1Cthe soul of America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  should be held in civil contempt for continuing to lie about two election workers to whom he already owes $148m for defaming, lawyers for the two women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.dcd.263084/gov.uscourts.dcd.263084.19.0_1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in a court filing Wednesday }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The request comes months after Giuliani {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/05/21/politics/giuliani-freeman-moss-agreement/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed in court }}}\uc2  to never again accuse Ruby Freeman and her daughter Shaye Moss of election fraud. Despite that agreement earlier this year, Giuliani continued to spread lies about them on his live-streamed show.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou would think that they wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be allowed to take all my property until the thing was affirmed on appeal and I got a chance to show them that they never let me show the tapes that show them quadruple counting the \u8230\'20\'26 ballots,\u8221\'20\'1D he said during one episode on 12 November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThen \u8230\'20\'26 another one is, uh, they\u8217\'20\'19re passing these little, little hard drives that we maintain were used to fix the machines, right, and they say it was candy. Well, you look at it \u8230\'20\'26 looks like a hard drive to me, and they told me it was a hard drive and there\u8217\'20\'19s no proof that it was candy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/20/rudy-giuliani-georgia-contempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia election workers ask judge to hold Rudy Giuliani in contempt }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  award s Medal of Freedom to Cecile Richards, former president of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , in a private ceremony.\par \par \uc2 The White House shared the commendation with the press:\par \par \uc2 With absolute courage and conviction, Cecile Richards fearlessly leads us forward to be the America we say we are \u8211\'20\'13 a Nation of freedom. Carrying her parents\u8217\'20\'19 torch for justice, she\u8217\'20\'19s led some of our Nation\u8217\'20\'19s most important civil rights causes \u8211\'20\'13 to lift up the dignity of workers, defend and advance women\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  and equality, and mobilize Americans to exercise their power to vote. A leader of utmost character, she has carved an inspiring legacy that endures in her incredible family, the countless lives she has made better, and a Nation seeking the light of equality, justice, and freedom.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden urged to use clemency powers to tackle \u8216\'20\'18crisis\u8217\'20\'19 of US mass incarceration\par \par \uc2 More than 60 members of Congress have written to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden }}}\uc2  calling on him to use his presidential clemency powers to reunite families, address unfair sentencing policies, and begin to tackle the scourge of mass incarceration, which they said was eroding \u8220\'20\'1Cthe soul of America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden has 61 days before he leaves the White House in which he could pardon or commute the sentences of incarcerated Americans. The letter, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25354946-2024-11-20-letter-to-president-biden-on-clemency?responsive=1&title=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed by }}}\uc2  a number of prominent Democratic politicians and spearheaded by the progressive politician \uc2 Ayanna Pressley\uc2  of Massachusetts and \uc2 Jim Clyburn\uc2  of South Carolina, urges Biden to act while he still can.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow is the time to use your clemency authority to rectify unjust and unnecessary criminal laws passed by Congress and draconian sentences given by judges,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter demands.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s clemency power is one of the most concrete tools at his disposal during the lame-duck period of his presidency. During his term in the White House, he has already granted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/pardon/clemency-statistics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 25 pardons and 132 commutations }}}\uc2 , including for people imprisoned for simple possession of marijuana and several court-martialed from the military because of their sexual orientation.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/20/biden-clemency-prison-incarceration-pardons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden urged to use clemency powers to tackle \u8216\'20\'18crisis\u8217\'20\'19 of US mass incarceration }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat accuses ethics committee chair of 'betraying process'\par \par \uc2 Susan Wild, the ranking Democrat on the House ethics committee, accused the committee\u8217\'20\'19s chair, Michael Guest, of \u8220\'20\'1Cbetraying the process\u8221\'20\'1D and mischaracterizing the meeting.\par \par \uc2 She said that the committee voted on whether to release the report but were in deadlock along party lines.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn order to affirmatively move something forward, somebody has to cross party lines and vote with the other side,\u8221\'20\'1D Wild told reporters, noting that there were five Democrats and five Republicans on the committee.\par \par \uc2 She said that the committee will reconvene on 5 December to discuss.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Texas offers thousands of acres to Trump for \u8216\'20\'18deportation facilities\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The state of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas }}}\uc2  has offered thousands of acres of land to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cto construct deportation facilities\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Texas land commissioner Dawn Buckingham wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.glo.texas.gov/the-glo/news/press-releases/2024/files/11-19-24_trump-donald-starr-county-offer.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter }}}\uc2  to Trump that her \u8220\'20\'1Coffice is fully prepared to enter into an agreement with the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2 , or the US border patrol to allow a facility to be built for the processing, detention, and coordination of the largest deportation of violent criminals in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In October, Buckingham\u8217\'20\'19s office, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas }}}\uc2  general land office (GLO), purchased 355,000 acres (144,000 hectares) of land \u8211\'20\'13 equivalent to half the size of Rhode Island. Of this, 1,402 acres have been offered to the federal government.\par \par \uc2 The land sits on a ranch in Starr county in the Rio Grande valley on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-mexico-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US-Mexico border }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Terms of the purchase were not disclosed, but Buckingham writes in his letter that the land was purchased from a woman who previously had refused to let state officials build a border wall on her property. Now, the state plans to build 1.5 miles (2.4km) of the border wall where they were once denied.\par \par \uc2 The rest of the 353,598 acres, collectively known as \u8220\'20\'1CBrewster Ranch\u8221\'20\'1D, located near Big Bend national park, were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://trerc.tamu.edu/news-talk/glo-buys-two-ranches-totaling-355k-acres-near-border/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 purchased }}}\uc2  in October for roughly $245m from billionaire and tobacco tycoon Brad Kelley, the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest private landowner. It was one of the most significant public purchases of land in the history of Texas.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/20/trump-texas-mass-deportation-facilities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas offers thousands of acres to Trump for \u8216\'20\'18deportation facilities\u8217\'20\'19 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More than two weeks after election day, there are more than half a million ballots left to count in California, and one of the most closely watched US House races remains too close to call with a razor-thin margin between Michelle Steel and Derek Tran.\par \par \uc2 Democratic challenger Tran has a 314-vote lead over the Republican incumbent in the congressional contest in the southern California district. Republicans already control the US House, as well as the Senate, but picking up the seat would be a big win for Democrats, who lost it to Steel in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Although Steel initially had a commanding lead, the race became neck and neck as election workers tallied more ballots. There are nearly 40,000 ballots left to process in Orange county and more than 30,000 in Los Angeles county, where the district is based.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/20/election-california-house-race-tran-steel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Razor-thin House race in California too close to call weeks after election day }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House ethics committee chair says no agreement on releasing Gaetz report\par \par \uc2 Michael Guest, the chair of the House ethics committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/bresreports/status/1859333925568475326"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told }}}\uc2  reporters that \u8220\'20\'1Cthere was not an agreement by the committee to release the report\u8221\'20\'1D on \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pick for attorney general.\par \par \uc2 Guest did not say if the committee took an official vote, but did not say when it would meet again.\par \par \uc2 The committee is evenly split between the two parties.\par \par \uc2 The panel has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ethics.house.gov/press-releases/statement-regarding-matter-representative-matt-gaetz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously said }}}\uc2  it was investigating claims that Gaetz \u8220\'20\'1Cmay have engaged in sexual misconduct and/or illicit drug use, shared inappropriate images or videos on the House floor, misused state identification records, converted campaign funds to personal use, and/or accepted a bribe, improper gratuity, or impermissible gift\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The justice department launched its own inquiry into accusations that Gaetz engaged in a sexual relationship with a 17-year-old girl, but the department closed its investigation last year without filing charges. Gaetz has consistently denied the allegations.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Sean Casten, a Democratic congressman from Illinois, has threatened to move to force a vote on the House floor to release the House ethics committee\u8217\'20\'19s report on \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pick for attorney general.\par \par \uc2 If the House ethics committee does not vote to release the Gaetz report on Wednesday, Casten said he will introduce a privileged resolution forcing a vote to require the committee to release its report.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe allegations against \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  are serious. They are credible. The House ethics committee has spent years conducting a thorough investigation to get to the bottom of it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://casten.house.gov/media/press-releases/casten-to-introduce-privileged-resolution-requiring-house-vote-to-release-gaetz-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement. }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the Ethics Committee chooses to withhold this information, later today I will introduce a privileged resolution to require a vote by the full House of Representatives on the release of the Gaetz report.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tech entrepreneurs \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  have laid out their plans for the new Department of Government Efficiency, or Doge, in a Wall Street Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/opinion/musk-and-ramaswamy-the-doge-plan-to-reform-government-supreme-court-guidance-end-executive-power-grab-fa51c020?mod=hp_opin_pos_0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  op-ed  }}}\uc2  published today.\par \par \uc2 The pair said they will follow recent Supreme Court rulings that they say can be used to take power away from federal agencies to reduce rules that are unnecessary, costly and inefficient, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 With an electoral mandate and the 6-3 conservative majority in the court, Musk and Ramaswamy said, the panel has an opportunity to enact substantial structural downsizing within the federal government.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe two of us will advise DOGE at every step to pursue three major kinds of reform: regulatory rescissions, administrative reductions and cost savings,\u8221\'20\'1D they wrote.\par \par \uc2 The panel will give its list of regulations to president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cwho can, by executive action, immediately pause the enforcement of those regulations and initiate the process for review and rescission,\u8221\'20\'1D they wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate to vote on Bernie Sanders resolution to block arms sales to Israel\par \par \uc2 A vote to block arms sales to Israel will be held on Wednesday in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 The joint resolutions of disapproval (JRDs), introduced by the senator Bernie Sanders in September, would prevent the Pentagon from sending another $20bn to Israel as it continues its assault on Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 which has killed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/gaza-war-deaths-surpass-43000-palestinian-health-ministry-reports-1975910"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 43,000 people }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The resolutions to be voted on the floor, and would block the sale of 120mm mortar rounds, joint direct attack munitions (JDAMS), and tank rounds, must pass both the Senate and the House with a simple majority. If they pass, they go to the president.\par \par \uc2 The Sanders-led effort to stop the flow of arms to Israel comes after the country failed to meet the US-imposed deadline of 12 November to increase humanitarian aid and allow at least 350 trucks into Gaza a day. Despite Israel\u8217\'20\'19s failure, the US took no action.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/20/bernie-sanders-israel-gaza-resolution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate to vote on Bernie Sanders resolution to block arms sales to Israel  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  marked his 82nd birthday on Wednesday as Democrats began searching for a younger generation of party leaders following \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s morale-sapping defeat in this month\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are engaged in seeking replacements for the octogenarian leadership represented by the president and 84-year-old \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , the former House speaker who was recently re-elected to a 20th term as a member of Congress and continues to wield much influence.\par \par \uc2 New leadership may also be on the horizon in the Senate, where the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 leader, Senator \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , is 73 and recently oversaw the loss of the party\u8217\'20\'19s single-seat majority to the Republicans, who have just replaced their 82-year-old leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 54, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , Pelosi\u8217\'20\'19s successor as the party\u8217\'20\'19s leader in the House, is less vulnerable to challenge on age-related grounds, but youth \u8211\'20\'13 at least in relative terms \u8211\'20\'13 is on Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 minds as they contemplate the road to recovery from a catastrophic reversal at the polls.\par \par \uc2 The party is looking at a younger generation of state governors to emerge as presidential candidates in four years\u8217\'20\'19 time, many of whom would have been in the mix had Biden passed the torch earlier and had there been an open primary or had he not immediately endorsed Harris when he finally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stepped aside }}}\uc2 . They include Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Josh Shapiro, 51, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  of Michigan, who is 53, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , 57, of California, 49-year-old \uc2 Jared Polis\uc2 , the governor of Colorado, and \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2 , 46, the governor of Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 Future leadership may also be available in the person of \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , 42, the transportation secretary, who has been notably effective in arguing the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 case in conservative forums like Fox News.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/20/biden-82-birthday-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden turns 82 as Democrats begin search for younger party leaders }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Sarah McBride responds to Capitol bathroom ban\par \par \uc2 Sarah McBride, the first out transgender person elected to Congress, has issued a longer statement after Republican House speaker Mike Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/20/donald-trump-linda-mcmahon-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673e19988f08bad5f60530fa#block-673e19988f08bad5f60530fa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  announced }}}\uc2  that transgender women are not permitted to use women\u8217\'20\'19s bathrooms in the Capitol building.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not here to fight about bathrooms. I\u8217\'20\'19m here to fight for Delawareans and to bring down costs facing families,\u8221\'20\'1D McBride said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SarahEMcBride/status/1859316328793862610"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2  posted to X.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis effort to distract from the real issues facing this country hasn\u8217\'20\'19t distracted me over the last several days, as I\u8217\'20\'19ve remained hard at work preparing to represent the greatest state in the union come January.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Delaware congresswoman-elect goes on to say that she is looking forward to getting to know her future colleagues on both sides of the aisle, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CEach of us were sent here because voters saw something in us that they value.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have loved getting to see those qualities in the future colleagues that I\u8217\'20\'19ve met and I look forward to seeing those qualities in every member come January. I hope all of my colleagues will seek to do the same with me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic Representative \uc2 Mark Pocan\uc2 , who is the chair of the congressional Equality Caucus, has released a statement condemning Speaker Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s announcement that transgender women are not permitted to use women\u8217\'20\'19s bathrooms in the Capitol building.\par \par \uc2 The statement reads:\par \par \uc2 Speaker Johnson\u8217\'20\'19s holier-than-thou decree to ban transgender people from using bathrooms that align with their identity is a cruel and unnecessary rule that puts countless staff, interns, and visitors to the United States Capitol at risk.\par \par \uc2 How will this even be enforced? Will the serjeant at arms post officers in bathrooms? Will everyone who works at the Capitol have to carry around their birth certificate or undergo a genetic test? This policy isn\u8217\'20\'19t going to protect anyone-but it is going to open the door to rampant abuse, harassment, and discrimination in the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Republicans can\u8217\'20\'19t even pass a Farm Bill or pass major appropriations bills, so they turn to using these cruel attacks to distract from their inability to govern and failure to deliver for the American people.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s team is reportedly discussing with the digital asset industry whether to create a new White House post dedicated to crypto policy and is vetting candidates, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-11-20/trump-team-mulls-creating-first-ever-white-house-crypto-role?sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg }}}\uc2  reported this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 If created, it would be the first-ever crypto-specific White House job, per Bloomberg.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House Ethics committee begins meeting to discuss Gaetz - report\par \par \uc2 The House Ethics Committee meeting has begun, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2024/11/20/congress/ethics-committee-hearing-begins-00190671"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/11/20/trump-administration-transition/#link-7HXXZIPZBNCB5OO66TX3FD7PAM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At the meeting, members are expected to discuss whether to release a report on their investigation into allegations of sexual misconduct involving \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s attorney general pick, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  has released a statement on his influence over president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s transition process.\par \par \uc2 In a post on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1859296375113961850"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 X  }}}\uc2  this afternoon, Musk said that \u8220\'20\'1Cto be clear, while I have offered my opinion on some cabinet candidates, many selections occur without my knowledge and decisions are 100% that of the President.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to say that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe large number of loyal, good people at Mar-a-Lago who have worked for him for many years is also very telling. People can sometimes be very good at hiding their own bad moral character, but they cannot hide the moral character of their friends & colleagues.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the same post, Musk also describes Trump is that he is a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat guy with an excellent sense of humor.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican Senator \uc2 Rand Paul\uc2  of Kentucky has criticized \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/18/trump-military-mass-deportation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plan to deploy the military  }}}\uc2  to carry out mass deportions, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cterrible image\u8221\'20\'1D for the country.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsmax.com/newsmax-tv/rand-paul-deportation-donald-trump/2024/11/19/id/1188730/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  NewsMax }}}\uc2  on Tuesday, Paul, who is a member of the Senate Committee on homeland Security and Governmental Affairs, said that he was not \u8220\'20\'1Cin favor of sending the Army in uniforms into our cities to collect people\u8221\'20\'1D adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cthat\u8217\'20\'19s not what we use our military for; we never have, and it\u8217\'20\'19s actually been illegal for over 100 years to bring the Army into our cities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur Army and our military are trained to shoot the enemy. They\u8217\'20\'19re not trained to get a warrant to do what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing,\u8221\'20\'1D Paul said, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe police have a difficult job, but the people removing people from our country need to be a police enforcement domestic agency, not the military.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He continued, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not in favor of sending the Army in uniforms into our cities to collect people. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s a terrible image.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican Representative Michael Guest, who chairs the House Ethics Committee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/trump-transition-news-11-20-24#cm3q63zp900053b6osng1agtt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has told CNN }}}\uc2  that he has \u8220\'20\'1Creservations\u8221\'20\'1D about releasing the committee\u8217\'20\'19s report on former representative \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have some reservations about releasing any unfinished work product\u8221\'20\'1D Guest reportedly said.\par \par \uc2 Guest also told the broadcaster that the committee will consider is whether to publicly release the report or send it directly to the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2 . He also did not confirm whether the committee would vote today on the report or sat how he would vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More than 60 members of Congress have written to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden }}}\uc2  calling on him to use his presidential clemency powers to reunite families, address unfair sentencing policies, and begin to tackle the scourge of mass incarceration, which they said was eroding \u8220\'20\'1Cthe soul of America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden has 61 days left before he leaves the White House in which he could pardon or commute the sentences of incarcerated Americans. The letter, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25354946-2024-11-20-letter-to-president-biden-on-clemency?responsive=1&title=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed by }}}\uc2  a number of prominent Democratic politicians and spearheaded by the progressive politician \uc2 Ayanna Pressley\uc2  of Massachusetts and \uc2 Jim Clyburn\uc2  of South Carolina, urges Biden to act while he still can.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/20/biden-clemency-prison-incarceration-pardons"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden urged to use clemency powers to tackle \u8216\'20\'18crisis\u8217\'20\'19 of US mass incarceration }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Members of the House ethics committee are gathering this afternoon for a closed-door meeting to discuss whether to release a report on their investigation into allegations of sexual misconduct involving \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorney general pick, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 . The former Florida congressman, shepherded by vice president-elect JD Vance, held meetings with key Senate allies involved in the Cabinet confirmation process at the Capitol on Wednesday, as Senate Democrats officially requested the files from the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s probe into whether Gaetz engaged in child sex trafficking.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Republican House speaker Mike Johnson announced that transgender women are not permitted to use women\u8217\'20\'19s bathrooms in the Capitol building, weeks after the election of the first transgender member of Congress, Sarah McBride. Also:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump announced he has chosen the former acting attorney general, \uc2 Matthew Whitaker\uc2 , as his nominee to serve as US ambassador to Nato. Trump is also expected to name his pick for treasury secretary as soon as today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers asked the judge overseeing his Manhattan hush-money criminal case for permission to make yet another play for dismissal.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  confirmed the Biden administration will allow Ukraine to use US-supplied antipersonnel landmines to help fight off Russian forces.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Austin said women in the US military \u8220\'20\'1Cmake us stronger\u8221\'20\'1D as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick for his successor, Pete Hegseth, faces scrutiny for previous remarks suggesting banning women from combat roles.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Linda McMahon\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pick for education secretary, incorrectly claimed in 2009 that she had a bachelor\u8217\'20\'19s degree in education on a questionnaire for a position on the Connecticut state board of education, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/11/20/mcmahon-trump-education-degree/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports }}}\uc2  that McMahon said at the time that she mistakenly thought her degree was in education because she did a semester of student teaching.\par \par \uc2 McMahon resigned from the state education board after the Hartford Courant told her it intended to write about the error, the paper reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate Republicans must soon consider several of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s cabinet picks whose nominations were met with intense criticism: \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  as director of national intelligence, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  as attorney general, Pete Hegseth as secretary of defense and \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  as secretary of health and human services.\par \par \uc2 Each of those cabinet announcements landed with somewhat of a thud on Capitol Hill, raising questions about whether the nominees will be able to muster the majority-level support needed in the Senate to get confirmed.\par \par \uc2 But the president-elect has proposed an archaic and in recent years little-used mechanism to get his nominees installed without Senate confirmation: recess appointments.\par \par \uc2 If Trump pursues a strategy of recess appointments, it could severely curtail the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s power to serve as a check on the new president\u8217\'20\'19s nominations and allow controversial picks to move forward.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/trump-senate-recess-appointments-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s everything to know about recess appointments. }}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/trump-senate-recess-appointments-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What are recess appointments and can Trump confirm nominees that way? }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate judiciary committee Democrats officially request \uc2 FBI\uc2  file on Gaetz\par \par \uc2 Senate judiciary committee Democrats have officially requested the \uc2 FBI\uc2  file on \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pick for attorney general.\par \par \uc2 In a letter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/f/?id=00000193-4a95-da7a-a3d3-5ebd7a3b0000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  obtained }}}\uc2  by Politico sent to \uc2 FBI\uc2  director \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 , Democratic members of the committee requested the evidentiary file from law enforcement\u8217\'20\'19s probe into whether Gaetz engaged in child sex trafficking.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn order for the Senate to perform its constitutional duty in this instance, we must be able to thoroughly review all relevant materials that speak to the credibility of these serious allegations against Mr. Gaetz,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter reads.\par \par \uc2 All panel Democrats except Georgia senator \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2  signed the letter, according to Politico.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaker Mike Johnson \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/20/donald-trump-linda-mcmahon-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673e19988f08bad5f60530fa#block-673e19988f08bad5f60530fa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcement }}}\uc2  barring transgender women from using women\u8217\'20\'19s bathrooms in the Capitol enacts into policy a push led by the Republican representative Nancy Mace.\par \par \uc2 Mace has led the charge against banning Sarah McBride, who is due to be sworn in as the first openly transgender member of Congress, from using the bathroom that corresponds with her gender identity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSarah McBride doesn\u8217\'20\'19t get a say. I mean, this is a biological man,\u8221\'20\'1D Mace told reporters on Monday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/11/18/politics/nancy-mace-anti-transgender-bathroom-ban-capitol-sarah-mcbride/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to CNN }}}\uc2 . She added that McBride \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not belong in women\u8217\'20\'19s spaces, women\u8217\'20\'19s bathrooms, locker rooms, changing rooms, period, full stop\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 McBride responded on X by saying the issue was a distraction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery day Americans go to work with people who have life journeys different than their own and engage with them respectfully, I hope members of Congress can muster that same kindness,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SarahEMcBride/status/1858672770084647214"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 she wrote }}}\uc2  on X.\par \par \uc2 Mace\u8217\'20\'19s bill came as Republicans have attacked transgender people as part of a broader political culture war strategy, limiting what bathrooms they can use and the youth sports teams they can play on.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrc.org/resources/state-maps/anti-transgender-bathroom-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fourteen states currently }}}\uc2  have laws that prohibit transgender people from using the bathroom that corresponds with their gender identity, according to the \uc2 Human Rights Campaign\uc2 , an LGBTQ+ rights group.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaker Johnson announces policy banning trans women from some bathrooms in Capitol building\par \par \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson has announced that transgender women are not permitted to use women\u8217\'20\'19s bathrooms in the Capitol building.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll single-sex facilities in the Capitol and House Office Buildings \u8212\'20\'14 such as restrooms, changing rooms, and locker rooms \u8212\'20\'14 are reserved for individuals of that biological sex,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said in a statement on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is important to note that each Member office has its own private restroom, and unisex restrooms are available throughout the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen deserve women\u8217\'20\'19s only spaces,\u8221\'20\'1D his statement concluded.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/20/donald-trump-linda-mcmahon-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673e02428f08b8d1c90a69d5#block-673e02428f08b8d1c90a69d5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported earlier, }}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has announced he has chosen the former acting attorney general, \uc2 Matthew Whitaker\uc2 , as his nominee to serve as US ambassador to Nato.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s choice is an unusual one, Associated Press writes, given that Whitaker\u8217\'20\'19s background is in law enforcement and not in foreign policy.\par \par \uc2 The Nato post is a particularly sensitive one given Trump\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with the alliance. During his first term, Trump criticized Nato and accused European members of not meeting their commitments to spend at least 2% of their GDP on defense.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/11/donald-trump-says-he-would-encourage-russia-to-attack-nato-countries-who-dont-pay-bills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned Nato allies  }}}\uc2  that if re-elected, he would \u8220\'20\'1Cencourage\u8221\'20\'1D Russia \u8220\'20\'1Cto do whatever the hell they want\u8221\'20\'1D to countries that are \u8220\'20\'1Cdelinquent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18You didn\u8217\'20\'19t pay? You\u8217\'20\'19re delinquent?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18No I would not protect you. In fact, I would encourage them to do whatever the hell they want. You gotta pay. You gotta pay your bills.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whitaker has been actively involved with the \uc2 America First Policy Institute\uc2 , a right-leaning think tank that has been working closely with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign to shape policy for his second term, Reuters writes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The letter by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers asking Judge Juan Merchan for permission to make yet another play for dismissal came after prosecutors told the court that they planned on fighting back against Trump\u8217\'20\'19s expected push for its dismissal following his win.\par \par \uc2 The Manhattan district attorney \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office contended that Merchan should schedule a timeline for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s expected motion to dismiss, which prosecutors said they \u8220\'20\'1Cintend to oppose\u8221\'20\'1D. They also said other proceedings in this case should be postponed until the dismissal issue is determined.\par \par \uc2 These latest developments suggest that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s scheduled 26 November sentencing in his Manhattan criminal hush-money case is all but certainly postponed, given the litany of issues to be litigated.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump lawyers seek dismissal of hush-money case on immunity grounds\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lawyers asked the judge overseeing his Manhattan hush-money criminal case for permission to make yet another play for dismissal, arguing that throwing out the case was necessary \u8220\'20\'1Cin order to facilitate the orderly transition of Executive power\u8221\'20\'1D following his election victory.\par \par \uc2 Todd Blanche, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lead attorney and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/trump-doj-todd-blanche-emil-bove"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pick for deputy US attorney general }}}\uc2 , and Emil Bove, his choice for principal associate deputy attorney general, railed against the Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , in their missive to Judge Juan Merchan, which was made public Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Bragg\u8217\'20\'19s office, they complained, \u8220\'20\'1Cappears not to yet be ready to dismiss this politically-motivated and fatally flawed case, which is what is mandated by the law and will happen as justice takes its course\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 They noted that the justice department (DoJ) is poised to toss federal cases against Trump, given DoJ policy that bars prosecuting sitting presidents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs in those cases, dismissal is necessary here,\u8221\'20\'1D their filing contended. \u8220\'20\'1CJust as a sitting President is completely immune from any criminal process, so too is President Trump as President-elect.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The attorneys requested a 20 December deadline for filing their pitch on why Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election merits dismissal of this case.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/20/trump-hush-money-immunity-dismissal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump lawyers seek dismissal of hush-money case on immunity grounds }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House Republicans have renewed a push to pass a bill that would allow the treasury department to strip non-profit groups it deems to be supporting \u8220\'20\'1Cterrorism\u8221\'20\'1D of their tax-exempt status.\par \par \uc2 The so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-profit killer\u8221\'20\'1D bill would give the government broad powers to sanction civil society organizations. Progressive groups have rallied in opposition to the bill in recent days, arguing that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s administration could invoke it to punish his political opponents.\par \par \uc2 The bill, titled Stop Terror-Financing and Tax Penalties on American Hostages Act, or HR 9495, failed to clear the House of Representatives last week after members attempted to fast-track it by suspending House rules, which would have required a supermajority to pass.\par \par \uc2 When it failed, Republicans brought it back through the House rules committee \u8211\'20\'13 paving the way for a floor vote, this time requiring only a simple majority.\par \par \uc2 When it was first introduced, progressive activists warned that the bill would be used to crack down on Palestinian advocacy groups, which politicians frequently accuse of supporting \uc2 Hamas\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a US-designated terrorist organization.\par \par \uc2 The measure \u8220\'20\'1Cwould be profoundly damaging to all sorts of non-profits\u8221\'20\'1D, said \uc2 American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  federal policy counsel Kia Hamadanchy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s the stigma of being called a terrorist-supporting organization, there are banks who may not want to transact with you once you have that status, there are donors who may not want to give you money because they\u8217\'20\'19re afraid, themselves, of being called supporters of terrorism.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/20/non-profit-terrorism-bill-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans renew push to expand government powers to punish non-profits }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump 'deserves a cabinet that is loyal', says Vance\par \par \uc2 Vice president-elect JD Vance has said that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cdeserves a cabinet that is loyal to the agenda he was elected to implement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JDVance/status/1859253884415332418?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1859253884415332418%7Ctwgr%5E704c15ab341fbbe27e41ddc01f7cc08977640bf5%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.washingtonpost.com%2Fpolitics%2F2024%2F11%2F20%2Ftrump-administration-transition%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post }}}\uc2  to X, Vance credited Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor\u8221\'20\'1D electoral victory for the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s Republican majority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHis coattails turned a 49-51 senate to a 53-47 senate,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance wrote.\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/20/donald-trump-linda-mcmahon-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673df32e8f082515be94eee2#block-673df32e8f082515be94eee2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier, }}}\uc2  Vance is on Capitol Hill with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick for attorney general, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , as well as \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s choice for secretary of state, for meetings with key Republican Senators involved in the Cabinet confirmation process.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , the Republican senator from Missouri, held a meeting with vice president-elect JD Vance and \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  at the Capitol this morning , a meeting he described as \u8220\'20\'1Cgood\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Scripps News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/slisker/status/1859262078881521691"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports  }}}\uc2  that Hawley said Gaetz outlined his vision for the Justice Department\u8217\'20\'19s house ethics investigation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe real question is, is Gaetz going to have the opportunity to answer this in a forum that is reasonable?\u8221\'20\'1D Hawley reportedly said.\par \par \uc2 CNN reports that Hawley said a confirmation hearing would allow Gaetz to answer questions about misconduct allegations against him. \u8220\'20\'1CMy view is that we ought to move forward with this, do the hearing, let him respond to everything under oath,\u8221\'20\'1D Hawley said. \u8220\'20\'1CGive him a shot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s denied everything, but the hearing is an opportunity for him to under oath in front of everybody, to walk through it,\u8221\'20\'1D he reportedly added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump picks \uc2 Matthew Whitaker\uc2  for US ambassador to Nato\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has named his former acting attorney general, \uc2 Matthew G Whitaker\uc2 , to be the US ambassador to the \uc2 North Atlantic Treaty Organization (Nato)\uc2  in his upcoming administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMatt is a strong warrior and loyal Patriot, who will ensure the United States\u8217\'20\'19 interests are advanced and defended,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMatt will strengthen relationships with our NATO Allies, and stand firm in the face of threats to Peace and Stability - He will put AMERICA FIRST.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whitaker served as acting attorney general in the first Trump administration after Jeff Sessions was ousted in 2018. He was seen as a partisan loyalist who was critical of special counsel \uc2 Robert Mueller\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s investigation of Russian interference in the 2016 election, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 He was previously seen as a contender for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, according to reports, and said the president-elect is \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to want someone that he knows, likes and trusts\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vice president-elect JD Vance, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/20/donald-trump-linda-mcmahon-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673df32e8f082515be94eee2#block-673df32e8f082515be94eee2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who is at Capitol Hill  }}}\uc2  today to shore up support for \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , has been tasked as the main liaison between the Trump-Vance transition team and Republican senators who could make or break Gaetz\u8217\'20\'19s nomination as attorney general.\par \par \uc2 Vance is doing a lot of\u8221\'20\'1D the outreach \u8220\'20\'1Con the Senate side,\u8221\'20\'1D the Hill {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4999745-gaetz-vance-senate-nomination/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quoted }}}\uc2  one GOP senator as saying.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think he\u8217\'20\'19s worked through the whole Judiciary Committee. He\u8217\'20\'19s calling folks, trying to get a sense of where things are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Gaetz 'deserves a chance to make his argument why he should be attorney general,' says \uc2 Lindsey Graham\par \par \uc2 South Carolina senator \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , the outgoing top Republican on the House judiciary committee, was the first to meet with vice president-elect JD Vance and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick for attorney general, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , at the Capitol this morning.\par \par \uc2 Graham said he had a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood meeting\u8221\'20\'1D with Vance and Gaetz and described the confirmation process for Gaetz as becoming a \u8220\'20\'1Clynch mob\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former Florida congressman \u8220\'20\'1Cwill be held to account in the confirmation process. He deserves his chance to make his argument why (he) should be attorney general,\u8221\'20\'1D Graham told reporters after the meeting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to be part of a process that leaks information that shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be leaked. I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to legitimize the process to destroy the man, because people don\u8217\'20\'19t like his politics,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 American Oversight, a nonpartisan watchdog group, filed a motion on Tuesday night in federal court to compel the Justice Department to release all records related to its investigation off the former congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , who \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has nominated to serve as his attorney general.\par \par \uc2 The group has been trying to get the documents since last year, when the Justice Department ended its inquiry into accusations that Gaetz engaged in a sexual relationship with a 17-year-old girl.\par \par \uc2 The department closed its investigation without filing charges, and Gaetz has consistently denied the allegations.\par \par \uc2 In its motion, American Oversight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://americanoversight.org/american-oversight-demands-prompt-release-of-fbi-records-of-matt-gaetz-investigation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  that releasing the documents is \u8220\'20\'1Cessential for transparency, accountability, and public trust\u8221\'20\'1D, arguing that the \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican people deserve to know the facts before the Senate votes on his nomination.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSex trafficking, obstruction of justice, and abuse of power are not the kind of questions that should hang over the head of someone being considered for US attorney general,\u8221\'20\'1D the watchdog\u8217\'20\'19s executive director, Chioma Chukwu, said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vance arrives on Capitol Hill to shore up support for Trump's cabinet picks\par \par \uc2 Vice president-elect JD Vance has arrived at the Capitol this morning where he will spend the week arranging meetings between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s cabinet picks, \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  and Pete Hegseth, and key Republican senators involved in their confirmation process.\par \par \uc2 Vance will be on Capitol Hill today to usher Gaetz, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick for attorney general, around Senate offices as the House ethics committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/20/matt-gaetz-house-ethics-committee-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meets to vote }}}\uc2  on releasing a report examining allegations of sexual misconduct against the former congressman, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 Vance is expected to sit in on some of the meetings, with CNN reporting that Louisiana senator \uc2 John Kennedy\uc2 , a member of the Senate judiciary committee, plans to meet with Gaetz and Vance today.\par \par \uc2 New York representative \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick to serve as the ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2 , and \uc2 Doug Collins\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick for secretary of veterans affairs, will also meet with senators this week, according to CNN.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/20/donald-trump-linda-mcmahon-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673deae48f087edee0b63bbd#block-673deae48f087edee0b63bbd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s move  }}}\uc2  to allow Ukraine to use American supplied anti-personnel landmines comes despite the weapons being banned by scores of countries, including the UK.\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , the US defense secretary, told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CThe landmines that we would look to provide them would be landmines that are not persistent, you know, we can control when they would self-activate, self-detonate and that makes it far more safer eventually than the things that they are creating on their own.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A US official said it was a step that could help slow Russian advances in the east of the country, especially when used with other munitions from the US.\par \par \uc2 The US expects Ukraine to use the mines in its own territory, though it has committed not to use them in areas populated with its own civilians, the official said.\par \par \uc2 The US has provided Ukraine with anti-tank mines throughout its war with Russia, but the addition of anti-personnel mines aims to blunt the advance of Russian ground troops, the official added, speaking on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US approves antipersonnel land mines for Ukraine against Russian forces\par \par \uc2 The US defense secretary, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , has confirmed the Biden administration will allow Ukraine to use US-supplied antipersonnel landmines to help fight off Russian forces, a further step after Washington granted Kyiv permission to use long-range missiles inside Russia.\par \par \uc2 Austin, speaking to reporters in Laos on Wednesday, said the shift in Washington\u8217\'20\'19s policy on antipersonnel landmines for Ukraine follows changing tactics by the Russians, according to the AP.\par \par \uc2 Russian ground troops are leading the movement on the battlefield, Austin said, so Ukraine has \u8220\'20\'1Ca need for things that can help slow down that effort on the part of the Russians\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/20/donald-trump-linda-mcmahon-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673dca748f087edee0b63a63#block-673dca748f087edee0b63a63"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier }}}\uc2 , the Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19s spokesperson Dmitry Peskov accused the US of prolonging the war in Ukraine and of \u8220\'20\'1Cdoing everything they can to do so\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/20/ukraine-landmines-biden-approves"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 temporarily closed }}}\uc2  its embassy in Kyiv after receiving warning of a \u8220\'20\'1Cpotential significant air attack\u8221\'20\'1D, advising American citizens to be prepared to move immediately to a shelter in the event of an air raid warning.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Women in military 'make us stronger', says Austin\par \par \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , the defense secretary, said women in the US military \u8220\'20\'1Cmake us stronger\u8221\'20\'1D as he prepares to shortly exit the top military post after four years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have spent 41 years in uniform, three long tours in Iraq, one in Afghanistan, and everywhere I went on a battlefield, there were women in our formation,\u8221\'20\'1D Austin said in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/military/defense-secretary-austin-says-women-military-make-us-stronger-rcna180937"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  interview }}}\uc2  with NBC News published this morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would tell you that, you know, our women are the finest troops in the world. Quite frankly, some of the finest in the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His comments came after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s announcement that he had picked Pete Hegseth, a national guard veteran and Fox News presenter, to succeed Austin as secretary of defense.\par \par \uc2 Hegseth has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/military-women-defense-hegseth-combat-916d50a7b465ccfea1aeb13bb91064b3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made it clear }}}\uc2 , in his own book and in interviews, that he believes men and women should not serve together in combat units. During a podcast released this month, he said the military \u8220\'20\'1Cshould not have women in combat roles\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Cmen in those positions are more capable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Austin, during his interview, argued that women \u8220\'20\'1Cdo impact readiness. They make us better. They make us stronger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However he did not weigh in on what he thinks about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s choice of Hegseth, only saying that the president-elect \u8220\'20\'1Chas the opportunity to nominate anyone that he chooses for any position, and certainly, you know, we respect that\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was attending the launch of \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Starship rocket launch in Texas yesterday when he was asked whether he was reconsidering his controversial nomination of \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  as attorney general.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo,\u8221\'20\'1D the president-elect told reporters. He did not respond when asked how far he was willing to go to get Gaetz confirmed.\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/20/donald-trump-linda-mcmahon-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673dc8758f08839232017c38#block-673dc8758f08839232017c38"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier }}}\uc2 , the House ethics committee is expected to meet today to vote on releasing a report examining allegations of sexual misconduct against the former Republican congressman.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former \uc2 WWE\uc2  executive \uc2 Linda McMahon\uc2 , who has been named as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s pick for education secretary, donated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nhregister.com/politics/article/ct-biggest-donors-presidential-donors-biden-trump-19548857.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $814,600 to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 campaign }}}\uc2  as of July.\par \par \uc2 She served in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet in his first term as the administrator of the \uc2 Small Business Administration\uc2  from 2017 to 2019.\par \par \uc2 McMahon chaired America First Action, a Super PAC that backed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s re-election campaign, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ctmirror.org/2020/10/09/linda-mcmahon-is-raising-millions-with-her-pro-trump-super-pac-but-not-from-ct/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raising $83m }}}\uc2  in 2020. She provided $6m to help Trump\u8217\'20\'19s candidacy after he secured the Republican presidential nomination in 2016, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 In October, McMahon and her husband, Vince, were named in a new lawsuit involving \uc2 WWE\uc2 . The suit alleges that she and other leaders of the company allowed the sexual abuse of young boys at the hands of a ringside announcer, former \uc2 WWE\uc2  ring crew chief Melvin Phillips Jr.\par \par \uc2 The complaint specifically alleges that the McMahons knew about the abuse and failed to stop it.\par \par \uc2 An attorney for the McMahons told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/2024/10/23/ww-ring-boys-sexual-abuse-negligence-lawsuit-vince-mcmahon-linda-tko/75814539007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USA Today Sports }}}\uc2  that the allegations are \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse claims\u8221\'20\'1D stemming from reporting that the couple deems \u8220\'20\'1Cabsurd, defamatory and utterly meritless\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US envoy travels to Israel in effort to secure Lebanon ceasefire\par \par \uc2 US envoy \uc2 Amos Hochstein\uc2  said he will travel to Israel on Wednesday to try to secure a ceasefire ending the war with \uc2 Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s Hezbollah\uc2  group after declaring additional progress in talks in Beirut.\par \par \uc2 Hochstein, who arrived a day earlier in Beirut, said he saw a \u8220\'20\'1C real opportunity \u8221\'20\'1D to end the conflict after the Lebanese government and \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  agreed to a US ceasefire proposal, although with some comments.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that the diplomacy aims to end a conflict that has inflicted massive devastation in Lebanon since Israel went on the offensive against \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  in September.\par \par \uc2 Although diplomacy to end the Gaza war has largely stalled, the Biden administration aims to seal a ceasefire in the parallel conflict in Lebanon before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  takes office in January.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to work with the incoming administration. We\u8217\'20\'19re already going to be discussing this with them. They will be fully aware of what we\u8217\'20\'19re doing,\u8221\'20\'1D Hochstein said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump expected to invoke 'global gag rule' on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services\par \par \uc2 As he did in his first term, US president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is likely in January to invoke the \u8220\'20\'1Cglobal gag rule\u8221\'20\'1D, officially called the Mexico City policy, which bans US federal funding for NGOs in foreign countries that provide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services or \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocacy.\par \par \uc2 The gag rule has a 40-year history of being applied by Republican presidents and rescinded by Democratic presidents. Every GOP president since the mid-1980s has invoked the rule, reports the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 As one of his first acts as president in 2017, Trump expanded the rule to the extent that foreign NGOs were cut off from about $600m in US family planning funds and more than $11bn in US global health aid between 2017 and 2018 alone, according to the \uc2 US Government Accountability Office\uc2 , the investigative arm of Congress, reports the AP.\par \par \uc2 The money \u8211\'20\'13 much of it intended for Africa \u8211\'20\'13 covered efforts such as preventing malaria and tuberculosis, providing water and sanitation, and distributing health information and contraception, which might also have repercussions for HIV prevention.\par \par \uc2 The policy stipulates that foreign NGOs that receive \uc2 US government\uc2  funding must agree to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related activities, including discussing it as a family planning option \u8212\'20\'14 even when they are using non-\uc2 US government\uc2  funds for such activities.\par \par \uc2 The gag-rule policy \u8220\'20\'1Cleads to more unintended, unwanted, unsupportable pregnancies and therefore an increase in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Catriona Macleod, a professor of psychology at South Africa\u8217\'20\'19s Rhodes University.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis legislation does not protect life \u8230\'20\'26 it\u8217\'20\'19s been called America\u8217\'20\'19s deadly export,\u8221\'20\'1D said Macleod, who heads the university\u8217\'20\'19s studies in sexuality and reproduction.\par \par \uc2 Trump \u8217\'20\'19s transition team did not respond to a request for comment from The Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election as US president has prompted fears that he will cut off American support for Ukraine, forcing it into peace talks with Russia that would culminate in a settlement on terms favourable to \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, as my colleague Andrew Sparrow reports, the UK foreign secretary, \uc2 David Lammy\uc2 , has argued that Trump would not go that far.\par \par \uc2 Lammy and the UK prime minister, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/keir-starmer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Keir Starmer }}}\uc2 , had dinner with Trump in the autumn. Lammy discusses that too in an interview in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newstatesman.com/politics/politics-interview/2024/11/david-lammy-interview-donald-trump-doesnt-want-vladimir-putin-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UK\u8217\'20\'19s New Statesmen with George Eaton }}}\uc2 . Here are the key lines.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lammy argued that Trump would not accept a deal over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine }}}\uc2  that would look like a victory for Putin. Asked about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stance on Ukraine, Lammy said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been a politician for 25 years and I understand the different philosophies at play. There\u8217\'20\'19s a deep philosophical underpinning to friends in the Republican party that I\u8217\'20\'19ve known for many years, thinking back to people like [former US secretary of state] Condoleezza Rice. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has some continuity with this position, which is \u8216\'20\'18peace through strength\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 What I do know about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is that he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like losers and he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want to lose; he wants to get the right deal for the American people. And he knows that the right deal for the American people is peace in Europe and that means a sustainable peace \u8211\'20\'13 not Russia achieving its aims and coming back for more in the years ahead.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lammy said he found Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cvery funny, very engaging and very charismatic\u8221\'20\'1D when he and Starmer met Trump for dinner at his home in New York. He also said Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Ca consummate politician\u8221\'20\'1D and very interested in learning how {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/labour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Labour }}}\uc2  won the election in the UK.\par \par \uc2 Following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory earlier this month, Lammy described his previous remarks about the US president-elect as being \u8220\'20\'1Cdeluded, dishonest, xenophobic, narcissistic\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cneo-Nazi-sympathising sociopath\u8221\'20\'1D as old news.\par \par \uc2 You can read Andrew\u8217\'20\'19s full post on Lammy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2024/nov/20/farming-inheritance-tax-keir-starmer-angela-rayner-uk-politics-live?page=with:block-673dc9578f08839232017c41#block-673dc9578f08839232017c41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump loyalist Kash Patel in contention to be named \uc2 FBI\uc2  director\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  is keeping his controversial adviser Kash Patel in the running to be the next \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, according to two people familiar with the matter, as the transition team conducted interviews for the role on Monday night at the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago club.\par \par \uc2 The existence of the interviews, made public in a since-deleted post by the vice president-elect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance }}}\uc2  , underscored the intent to fire the current \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 , years before his current term is up.\par \par \uc2 Vance revealed that he and Trump had been interviewing finalists for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI }}}\uc2  director in a post responding to criticism he received for missing a Senate vote last night that confirmed one of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s nominees for the US court of appeals for the 11th circuit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen this 11th circuit vote happened, I was meeting President Trump to interview multiple positions for our government, including for \uc2 FBI\uc2  director,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance wrote.\par \par \uc2 Trump has a special interest in the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , having fired \uc2 James Comey\uc2  as director in 2017 over his refusal to close the investigation into possible collusion between the Trump campaign and Russia, and then complaining about perceived disloyalty from Wray.\par \par \uc2 Patel\u8217\'20\'19s continued position as a top candidate for the role makes clear Trump\u8217\'20\'19s determination to install loyalists in key national security and law enforcement positions, as well as the support Patel has built up among key Trump allies.\par \par \uc2 The push for Patel \u8211\'20\'13 who has frequently railed against the \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep state\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 has come from some of the longest-serving Trump advisers, notably those close to former Trump strategist \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , a faction that got Trump\u8217\'20\'19s personal lawyers picked for top justice department roles.\par \par \uc2 That faction has also suggested to Trump in recent days that if Patel gets passed over for the director role, he should be given the deputy \uc2 FBI\uc2  director position, one of the people said \u8211\'20\'13 a powerful job that helps run the bureau day to day and is crucially not subject to Senate confirmation.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/19/trump-kash-patel-fbi-director"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump loyalist Kash Patel in contention to be named FBI director }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  must not remove \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s $1.95tn asset cap until the bank has fixed its risk management and compliance issues, top Democratic Senator Elizabeth Warren told the US central bank on Wednesday, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 In a letter to Fed chair, \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , and the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s regulatory chief, \uc2 Michael Barr\uc2 , Warren said the Fed must reject \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  reported appeal to have the punishment imposed in 2018 lifted until it \u8220\'20\'1Ccan show that it can properly manage the risks associated with running a large bank\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Spokespeople for \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  and the Fed declined to comment on the letter, which was seen by Reuters, according to the news agency.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  reported in September that \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  had sent a third-party review of its risk and control overhauls to the Fed in an attempt to end the unprecedented cap imposed after the bank\u8217\'20\'19s long-running fake accounts scandal and other issues.\par \par \uc2 Republican president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is to overhaul bank regulation and slash burdensome rules, boosting analysts\u8217\'20\'19 expectations that the cap could be removed as early as next year and alarming many Democrats in favor of tough rules.\par \par \uc2 A prominent Wall Street critic and one-time presidential candidate, Warren will next year become the top Democrat on the Senate Banking Committee. Long a thorn in \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s side, Warren cannot force the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s hand but her letter can pressure it to take a tough line and highlight the bank\u8217\'20\'19s missteps, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Warren pointed to a number of regulatory actions against \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  since 2018, including in September when the Comptroller of the Currency dinged the bank for shortcomings in policing money laundering. The country\u8217\'20\'19s fourth-largest lender is still grappling with a class action lawsuit over its diversity hiring practices, she also noted.\par \par \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  CEO, \uc2 Charlie Scharf\uc2 , has repeatedly said upgrading the bank\u8217\'20\'19s risk and control framework has been a top priority, and the bank has convinced regulators to terminate six regulatory consent orders since 2019.\par \par \uc2 In response to Warren\u8217\'20\'19s request at a 2018 hearing, Powell committed that the Fed would put any decision to lift the asset cap to a vote of its board of governors. On Wednesday, Warren reminded him of that promise and called on the Fed to make public any third-party review Wells submitted as part of its bid to lift the cap.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will name who he has picked to be Treasury secretary as soon as Wednesday, Reuters reports, citing two sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 No one has been has been chosen yet for the role, CNN also reported.\par \par \uc2 You can take a look at the people who have been and still could be offered key positions when Trump takes office via this explainer:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/19/trump-cabinet-picks-administration-appointees"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet and White House picks \u8211\'20\'13 so far }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the US, \uc2 Kevin Rudd\uc2 , says Australia is \u8220\'20\'1Cready\u8221\'20\'1D for a second Trump presidency.\par \par \uc2 In a speech to the Sydney International Strategy Forum via video link, Rudd said \u8220\'20\'1Cthe team here at the embassy and the government of Australia are ready to work closely with the new Trump administration to continue to realise the benefits of what is a very strong economic and security partnership\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 You can listen to his comments here:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 Russia on Wednesday accused the US of prolonging the \u8220\'20\'1Cwar in Ukraine\u8221\'20\'1D by stepping up weapons deliveries to Kyiv ahead of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House, reports Agence France-Presse (AFP).\par \par \uc2 Both Moscow and Kyiv are jockeying to secure an upper hand on the battlefield before Trump assumes office in January 2025.\par \par \uc2 The Republican has repeatedly criticised US support for Ukraine and claimed he could secure a ceasefire within hours \u8211\'20\'13 comments that have triggered fears in Kyiv and Europe about Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s ability to withstand the Russian attacks without US support.\par \par \uc2 Moscow has significantly escalated its aerial campaign this week, launching multiple deadly missile strikes and targeting Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s energy grid. Ukraine meanwhile has fired long-range US-supplied Atacms missiles at Russian territory for the first time since the White House authorised such strikes, drawing scorn and promises of retribution in Moscow, reports AFP.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you look at the trends of the outgoing US administration, they are fully committed to continuing the war in Ukraine and are doing everything they can to do so,\u8221\'20\'1D Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov told reporters.\par \par \uc2 According to AFP, Peskov was responding to the US saying it would soon provide Ukraine with antipersonnel landmines.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 House ethics committee to vote on publication of \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  report\par \par \uc2 The House ethics committee is expected to meet on Wednesday to vote on releasing a report examining allegations of sexual misconduct against former Republican representative \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s nominee to lead the US justice department.\par \par \uc2 The panel has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ethics.house.gov/press-releases/statement-regarding-matter-representative-matt-gaetz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously said }}}\uc2  it was investigating claims that Gaetz \u8220\'20\'1Cmay have engaged in sexual misconduct and/or illicit drug use, shared inappropriate images or videos on the House floor, misused state identification records, converted campaign funds to personal use, and/or accepted a bribe, improper gratuity, or impermissible gift\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The justice department launched its own inquiry into accusations that Gaetz engaged in a sexual relationship with a 17-year-old girl, but the department closed its investigation last year without filing charges. Gaetz has consistently denied the allegations.\par \par \uc2 Two women testified to congressional investigators that Gaetz paid them for sex and that he was seen having sex with the 17-year-old, a lawyer for the women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-attorney-general-matt-gaetz-justice-department-dca401813d9b84638d250f273a2d3942"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As the ethics committee is evenly split between the two parties, it would take only one Republican siding with every Democrat on the panel to have the report released. But prominent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans }}}\uc2 , including House speaker Mike Johnson, have cautioned against releasing the report on Gaetz, who resigned his seat immediately after Trump announced his nomination as attorney general.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that would be a Pandora\u8217\'20\'19s box,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson told CNN on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think we want the House ethics committee using all of its vast resources and powers to go after private citizens, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/matt-gaetz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Matt Gaetz }}}\uc2  is now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But other Republicans, including Senator \uc2 Markwayne Mullin\uc2 , have suggested the report should be at least made available to the senators who will vote on confirming Gaetz\u8217\'20\'19s nomination.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe the Senate should have access to that,\u8221\'20\'1D Mullin told NBC News on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CNow, should it be released to the public or not? I guess that will be part of the negotiations. But that should be definitely part of our decision-making.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/20/matt-gaetz-house-ethics-committee-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House ethics committee to vote on publication of Matt Gaetz report }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has chosen Mehmet Oz, best known for starring in his eponymous daytime talkshow for more than a decade and leaning heavily into Trumpism during his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/john-fetterman-wins-pennsylvania-senate-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed 2022 run }}}\uc2  for a Pennsylvania Senate seat, to lead the \uc2 Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services\uc2  (CMS). The cardiothoracic surgeon, who faced immense backlash from the medical and scientific communities for pushing misinformation at the height of the Covid-19 pandemic, will oversee the agency that operates on a $2.6tn annual budget and provides healthcare to more than 100 million people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am honored to be nominated by [\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ] to lead CMS,\u8221\'20\'1D Oz posted on X on Tuesday. \u8220\'20\'1CI look forward to serving my country to Make America Healthy Again under the leadership of \uc2 HHS\uc2  Secretary [\uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 ].\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the announcement of Oz\u8217\'20\'19s selection, Trump said that Oz will \u8220\'20\'1Cmake America healthy again\u8221\'20\'1D and described him as \u8220\'20\'1Can eminent Physician, Heart Surgeon, Inventor, and World-Class Communicator, who has been at the forefront of healthy living for decades\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Oz has been on US television screens for nearly 20 years, first appearing on the \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2  show in 2004. In that time, he\u8217\'20\'19s talked to his audience about losing weight with fad diets and what it takes to have healthy poops and, toward the end of his run, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/think/opinion/dr-oz-s-hydroxychloroquine-advocacy-seduces-trump-coronavirus-wellness-woo-ncna1185596"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 touting hydroxychloroquine }}}\uc2  as a potential remedy for Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 You can see the full explainer on what to know about the \uc2 New York University\uc2  professor and surgeon turned television show host, and now Trump appointee, at this link:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/19/mehmet-oz-trump-administration-medicare-medicaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who is Mehmet Oz, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pick to lead Medicare and Medicaid? }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 In case you missed it, here is our news article on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  picking the former \uc2 WWE\uc2  executive, \uc2 Linda McMahon\uc2 , for education secretary:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/19/trump-nominates-linda-mcmahon-education-secretary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump picks former WWE executive Linda McMahon for education secretary }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s some more from the Associated Press\u8217\'20\'19s education writer, Annie Ma, on some of the Department of Education \u8217\'20\'19s key functions, and how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said he might approach them:\par \par \uc2 Student loans and financial aid\par \par \uc2 The education department manages approximately $1.5tn in student loan debt for more than 40 million borrowers. It also oversees the Pell grant, which provides aid to students below a certain income threshold, and administers the Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA), which universities use to allocate financial aid.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has made cancellation of student loans a signature effort of the department\u8217\'20\'19s work. Since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s initial attempt to cancel student loans was overturned by the supreme court, the administration has forgiven over $175bn for more than 4.8 million borrowers through a range of changes to programs it administers, such as Public Service Loan Forgiveness.\par \par \uc2 The loan forgiveness efforts have faced Republican pushback, including litigation from several GOP-led states.\par \par \uc2 Trump has criticized Biden\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to cancel debt as illegal and unfair, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Ctotal catastrophe\u8221\'20\'1D that \u8220\'20\'1Ctaunted young people.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plan for student debt is uncertain: He has not put out detailed plans.\par \par \uc2 Civil rights enforcement\par \par \uc2 Through its Office for Civil Rights, the education department conducts investigations and issues guidance on how civil rights laws should be applied, such as for LGBTQ+ students and students of color. The office also oversees a large data collection project that tracks disparities in resources, course access and discipline for students of different racial and socioeconomic groups.\par \par \uc2 Trump has suggested a different interpretation of the office\u8217\'20\'19s civil rights role. In his campaign platform, he said he would pursue civil rights cases to \u8220\'20\'1Cstop schools from discriminating on the basis of race.\u8221\'20\'1D He has described diversity and equity policies in education as \u8220\'20\'1Cexplicit unlawful discrimination\u8221\'20\'1D and said colleges that use them will pay fines and have their endowments taxed.\par \par \uc2 Trump also has pledged to exclude transgender students from Title IX protections, which affect school policies on students\u8217\'20\'19 use of pronouns, bathrooms and locker rooms. Originally passed in 1972, Title IX was first used as a women\u8217\'20\'19s rights law. This year, Biden\u8217\'20\'19s administration said the law forbids discrimination based on gender identity and sexual orientation, but Trump can undo that.\par \par \uc2 College accreditation\par \par \uc2 While the education department does not directly accredit colleges and universities, it oversees the system by reviewing all federally recognized accrediting agencies. Institutions of higher education must be accredited to gain access to federal money for student financial aid.\par \par \uc2 Accreditation came under scrutiny from conservatives in 2022, when the \uc2 Southern Association of Colleges and Schools\uc2  questioned political interference at Florida public colleges and universities. Trump has said he would fire \u8220\'20\'1Cradical left accreditors\u8221\'20\'1D and take applications for new accreditors that would uphold standards including \u8220\'20\'1Cdefending the American tradition\u8221\'20\'1D and removing \u8220\'20\'1CMarxist\u8221\'20\'1D diversity administrators.\par \par \uc2 Although the education secretary has the authority to terminate its relationship with individual accrediting agencies, it is an arduous process that has rarely been pursued. Under president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , the department took steps to cancel accreditors for a now defunct for-profit college chain, but the Trump administration blocked the move. The group, the Accrediting Council for Independent Colleges and Schools, was terminated by the Biden administration in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Money for schools\par \par \uc2 Much of the education department\u8217\'20\'19s money for K-12 schools goes through large federal programs, such as Title I for low-income schools and the Individuals with Disabilities Education Act. Those programs support services for students with disabilities, lower class sizes with additional teaching positions, and pay for social workers and other non-teaching roles in schools.\par \par \uc2 During his campaign, Trump called for shifting those functions to the states. He has not offered details on how the agency\u8217\'20\'19s core functions of sending federal money to local districts and schools would be handled.\par \par \uc2 The Heritage Foundation\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Project 2025, a sweeping proposal outlining a far-right vision for the country that overlaps in areas with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, offers a blueprint. It suggests sending oversight of programs for kids with disabilities and low-income children first to the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , before eventually phasing out the funding and converting it to no-strings-attached grants to states.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump has called for dismantling the education department: Here's what that would mean\par \par \uc2 Throughout his campaign, president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  heaped scorn on the federal Department of Education, describing it as being infiltrated by \u8220\'20\'1Cradicals, zealots and Marxists.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He has picked \uc2 Linda McMahon\uc2 , a former wrestling executive, to lead the department. But like many conservative politicians before him, Trump has called for dismantling the department altogether \u8211\'20\'13 a cumbersome task that likely would require action from Congress.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has this short explainer on what that would mean:\par \par \uc2 The agency\u8217\'20\'19s main role is financial. Annually, it distributes billions in federal money to colleges and schools and manages the federal student loan portfolio. Closing the department would mean redistributing each of those duties to another agency. The education department also plays an important regulatory role in services for students, ranging from those with disabilities to low-income and homeless kids.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, federal education money is central to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans for colleges and schools. Trump has vowed to cut off federal money for schools and colleges that push \u8220\'20\'1Ccritical race theory, transgender insanity, and other inappropriate racial, sexual or political content\u8221\'20\'1D and to reward states and schools that end teacher tenure and enact universal school choice programs.\par \par \uc2 Federal funding makes up a relatively small portion of public school budgets \u8211\'20\'13 roughly 14%. Colleges and universities are more reliant on it, through research grants along with federal financial aid that helps students pay their tuition.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 National Education Association\uc2  says nominating McMahon as education secretary shows Trump 'could not care less about our students' futures'\par \par \uc2 The president of the \uc2 National Education Association (NEA )\uc2  said that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/19/trump-nominates-linda-mcmahon-education-secretary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s decision to name  }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/19/trump-nominates-linda-mcmahon-education-secretary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Linda McMahon }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/19/trump-nominates-linda-mcmahon-education-secretary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  as his pick for education secretary }}}\uc2  in his upcoming administration, shows \u8220\'20\'1Cthat he could not care less about our students\u8217\'20\'19 futures\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released on Tuesday after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s announcement, \uc2 Becky Pringle\uc2  criticised the naming of McMahon, the billionaire co-founder of \uc2 World Wrestling Entertainment\uc2  (\uc2 WWE\uc2 ), and called on the Senate to reject \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s unqualified nominee\u8221\'20\'1D. She warned that \u8220\'20\'1CMcMahon\u8217\'20\'19s only mission is to eliminate the Department of Education and take away taxpayer dollars from public schools\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Pringle wrote:\par \par \uc2 Every student \u8211\'20\'13 no matter where they live, how much their family earns, or the color of their skin \u8211\'20\'13 deserves the opportunity, resources, and support they need to grow into their full brilliance. In every community across this country parents and educators are partners in this effort.\par \par \uc2 By selecting \uc2 Linda McMahon\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is showing that he could not care less about our students\u8217\'20\'19 futures. Rather than working to strengthen public schools, expand learning opportunities for students, and support educators, McMahon\u8217\'20\'19s only mission is to eliminate the Department of Education and take away taxpayer dollars from public schools, where 90% of students \u8211\'20\'13 and 95% of students with disabilities \u8211\'20\'13 learn, and give them to unaccountable and discriminatory private schools.\par \par \uc2 During his first term, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appointed \uc2 Betsy DeVos\uc2  to undermine and ultimately privatize public schools through vouchers. Now, he and \uc2 Linda McMahon\uc2  are back at it with their extreme Project 2025 proposal to eliminate the Department of Education, steal resources for our most vulnerable students, increase class sizes, cut job training programs, make higher education more expensive and out of reach for middle class families, take away special education services for disabled students, and put student civil rights protections at risk.\par \par \uc2 She added:\par \par \uc2 Parents and educators will stand together to support students and reject the harmful, outlandish, and insulting policies being pushed by the Trump administration. They will make their voices heard, just as they did by resoundingly defeating vouchers in states like Colorado, Kentucky, and Nebraska.\par \par \uc2 The Department of education plays such a critical role in the success of each and every student in this country.\par \par \uc2 The Senate must stand up for our students and reject \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s unqualified nominee, \uc2 Linda McMahon\uc2 . Our students and our nation deserve so much better than \uc2 Betsy DeVos\uc2  2.0.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Tuesday, Trump extolled the \u8220\'20\'1Cincredible\u8221\'20\'1D job McMahon has been doing as transition team co-chair and said:\par \par \uc2 As Secretary of Education, Linda will fight tirelessly to expand \u8216\'20\'18Choice\u8217\'20\'19 to every State in America, and empower parents to make the best Education decisions for their families. \u8230\'20\'26 We will send Education BACK TO THE STATES, and Linda will spearhead that effort.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More on this story in a moment, but first, here are some other key developments\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/19/mehmet-oz-trump-administration-medicare-medicaid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump has chosen Mehmet Oz }}}\uc2 , best known for starring in his eponymous daytime talkshow for more than a decade and leaning heavily into Trumpism during his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/nov/09/john-fetterman-wins-pennsylvania-senate-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed 2022 run }}}\uc2  for a Pennsylvania Senate seat, to lead the \uc2 Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services\uc2  (CMS). The cardiothoracic surgeon, who faced immense backlash from the medical and scientific communities for pushing misinformation at the height of the Covid-19 pandemic, will oversee the agency that operates on a $2.6tn annual budget and provides healthcare to more than 100 million people.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump is keeping his controversial adviser Kash Patel in the running to be the next \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, according to two people familiar with the matter, as the transition team conducted interviews for the role on Monday night at the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago club. The existence of the interviews, made public in a since-deleted post by the vice president-elect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance }}}\uc2 , underscored the intent to fire the current \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 , years before his current term is up.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russia on Wednesday accused the US of prolonging the \u8220\'20\'1Cwar in Ukraine\u8221\'20\'1D by stepping up weapons deliveries to Kyiv ahead of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House. Both Moscow and Kyiv are jockeying to secure an upper hand on the battlefield ahead of Trump assuming office in January 2025.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s health advocates in Africa are worried that Trump will again invoke the so-called global gag rule, a policy that cuts off \uc2 US government\uc2  funding for groups that offer \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related services. The gag rule has been imposed by all Republican presidents since 1984. In 2017, Trump expanded it, cutting foreign NGOs off not only from family planning money, but from broader US global health assistance covering malaria and tuberculosis prevention, water and sanitation, and the distribution of health information.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the US, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/video/2024/nov/20/kevin-rudd-says-he-is-ready-to-work-with-incoming-trump-administration-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kevin Rudd, says Australia is \u8216\'20\'18ready\u8217\'20\'19 for a second Trump presidency }}}\uc2 . In a speech to the Sydney International Strategy Forum via video link, Rudd said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe team here at the embassy and the government of Australia are ready to work closely with the new Trump administration to continue to realise the benefits of what is a very strong economic and security partnership.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241120ekbk001pg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
