\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Emboldened anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  groups create wishlist for second Trump term\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,412 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 November 2024\par 12:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Make America pro-life again\u8217\'20\'19 legislation includes banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills entirely and outlawing telehealth abortions\par \par \uc2 The anti- {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  movement is ready for its comeback in 2025.\par \par \uc2 With the return of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  to the White House, complete with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican }}}\uc2  -dominated Congress, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups are unfurling ambitious lists of policies they hope to see enacted under a sympathetic administration.\par \par \uc2 In the two years since the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade }}}\uc2 , the movement has largely been relegated to playing defense. Popular support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights surged, while red-state voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/florida-abortion-ballot-ban-measure-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended }}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights through ballot measures and many Republicans downplayed their opposition to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Now, they are ready to go back on the offense.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the powerful Students for Life of America released its wishlist of federal legislation, entitled \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Pro-Life Again\u8221\'20\'1D, which takes direct aim at access to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills }}}\uc2 . The group is backing federal bills that would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/5806?q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22H.R.+5806%22%7D&s=1&r=2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills entirely }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.congress.gov/bill/118th-congress/house-bill/421?q=%7B%22search%22%3A%22chemical+abortion%22%7D&s=3&r=3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outlaw telehealth abortions }}}\uc2  and require medical-grade cleanup of the pregnancy remains left behind by medication abortions. (Students for Life argues that the pills pose a threat to the US water supply because people may pass the remains of their pregnancy into the toilet.) Currently, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills account for roughly two-thirds of US abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a willingness to listen, there\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a willingness to have conversation,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Kristan Hawkins\uc2 , president of Students for Life, said of the incoming Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail, Trump was far from a loyal ally to the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement. Although he bragged that he was the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost pro-life president\u8221\'20\'1D ever and took credit for Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise \u8211\'20\'13 having appointed three of the justices that overturned it \u8211\'20\'13 he also repeatedly insisted that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was now a matter for states to decide. Trump also flip-flopped on whether he would veto a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/09/republican-abortion-ban-policy-platform-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban }}}\uc2  passed by Congress.\par \par \uc2 But he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily have to. In an interview with the Guardian, Hawkins said she believed the Trump administration should enforce the Comstock Act \u8211\'20\'13 which may be the easiest way for a Trump administration to effectively implement a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 A 19th-century anti-vice law that bans the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related materials, the Comstock Act was dormant while Roe v Wade was the law of the land, but has never been fully repealed. It could be used to ban the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed }}}\uc2  by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/14/project-2025-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025 }}}\uc2 , the controversial playbook of conservative policies assembled by the thinktank \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 . In the second quarter of 2024, providers performed more than 57,000 abortions through mail-order prescriptions, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://societyfp.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/WeCount-Report-8-June-2024-data.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data from #WeCount }}}\uc2 , a project to track post-Roe abortions by the Society of Family Planning.\par \par \uc2 But other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents think the law can be used to stop \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics from obtaining all of the materials they need to do their jobs.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Department of Justice has issued guidance that offers a more lax interpretation of the Comstock Act. But a Trump justice department, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/13/republicans-matt-gaetz-trump-attorney-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 led }}}\uc2  by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/13/who-is-matt-gaetz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Matt Gaetz }}}\uc2 , could easily rescind that guidance without involving Congress. Gaetz\u8217\'20\'19s record on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has earned him an A+ from the powerful anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe letter of the law should be followed,\u8221\'20\'1D Hawkins said. Pointing to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/31/election-trump-immigration-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposals on immigration }}}\uc2 , she said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe incoming Trump administration has been very clear that laws in our country are there for a reason, and laws should be upheld.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to be a country of law and order.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America\u8217\'20\'19s president, Marjorie Dannenfelser, seemed to echo the point. \u8220\'20\'1CThe commonsense policies of Pres Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term become the baseline for the second, along with reversing the Biden-Harris administration\u8217\'20\'19s unprecedented violation of longstanding federal laws,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Dannenfelser\u8217\'20\'19s statement also included a laundry list of policies that she would like to see implemented, many of which would involve redirecting federal funds. For example, she called for Trump to reinstate a rule that would reshape the nation\u8217\'20\'19s oldest family planning program, Title X, which helps people obtain services such as contraception and STI screenings at little to no cost. Most people who rely on Title X are women and have incomes that are below or around the poverty level.\par \par \uc2 Although a longstanding rule known as the Hyde amendment already blocks federal dollars from funding abortions, the Trump administration also implemented a rule that blocked Title X-funded family planning providers from mentioning the word \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and required them to physically separate any services that involve \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from those that don\u8217\'20\'19t, such as by creating entirely separate waiting rooms, examination rooms and office entrances solely for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provision.\par \par \uc2 Rather than comply, about 1,200 family planning clinics \u8211\'20\'13 including every clinic run by \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement\u8217\'20\'19s greatest antagonist \u8211\'20\'13 left Title X. More than 1.5 million people are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/05/legal-right-contraception-senate-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 thought to have lost access }}}\uc2  to Title X services as a direct result of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s changes.\par \par \uc2 In a strategy memo issued earlier this week and shared with the Guardian, Dannenfelser indicated that her group would work to lay the groundwork for \u8220\'20\'1Cfetal personhood\u8221\'20\'1D, a legal doctrine that would grant embyros and fetuses full legal rights and protections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn order to go on offense and truly defeat the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  industry in the long term, we must strengthen the pro-life, pro-woman, pro-family resolve of the Republican Party, centered on the unalienable right to life for the unborn child that exists under the 14th Amendment,\u8221\'20\'1D Dannenfelser said in the memo.\par \par \uc2 Some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  foes cite the 14th amendment as the legal foundation for fetal personhood. If fully enacted, it would not only ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/mar/20/states-fetal-personhood-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rewrite vast swaths of US law }}}\uc2 , such as by outlawing in vitro fertilization as it is currently practiced. Alabama offered a sneak peek at what this may look like when the state supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/21/alabama-ivf-embryo-extrauterine-children-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled }}}\uc2  earlier this year that embryos created through IVF are \u8220\'20\'1Cextrauterine children\u8221\'20\'1D. The ruling temporarily threw fertility services in the state into chaos.\par \par \uc2 A fresh mandate\par \par \uc2 There are other ways that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists may strike at \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in the coming months. Earlier this year, the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected a lawsuit }}}\uc2 , argued by the Christian legal powerhouse \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2 , that aimed to roll back the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of mifepristone, the common \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill. That rejection, however, was based on technical grounds. Three states \u8211\'20\'13 Idaho, Kansas and Missouri \u8211\'20\'13 are now attempting to resurrect the case. The Republican attorneys general of those states have filed a new complaint that repeatedly cites the Comstock Act and pushes for new restrictions, such as limits on minors\u8217\'20\'19 access to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill.\par \par \uc2 But Project 2025 suggested another workaround: what if, under a conservative administration, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  reversed its own approval of mifepristone? Such a move could make it much harder to obtain the pill in the United States. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  could also roll back later measures that have made the medication more accessible without reversing course on its approval entirely.\par \par \uc2 Hawkins enthusiastically endorsed that course of action. The key, she said, may lie in the 2024 supreme court case Loper Bright Enterprises v Raimondo. In that case, the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative supermajority {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/28/us-supreme-court-chevron-doctrine-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down the 40-year-old Chevron doctrine }}}\uc2 , which required courts to defer to federal agencies\u8217\'20\'19 expertise.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe supreme court confirms what we knew all along: federal agencies are not God,\u8221\'20\'1D Hawkins said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey do not get the power to create their own regulations and enforce their own laws.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In their own post-election statements, \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  affirmed their commitment to \u8220\'20\'1Cdismantling the administrative state\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election }}}\uc2  ultimately proved to be a mixed bag for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights: despite Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voters in seven states }}}\uc2  passed ballot measures to amend their state constitutions to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. In Arizona and Nevada \u8211\'20\'13 both of which Trump won \u8211\'20\'13 those measures passed with a whopping 60-plus per cent of the vote.\par \par \uc2 Still, Hawkins feels like the 2024 election issued a clear mandate to her movement and the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmericans want less \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They don\u8217\'20\'19t want more,\u8221\'20\'1D Hawkins said. \u8220\'20\'1CNo matter what type of color lipstick you want to put on this pig, you\u8217\'20\'19re still talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241117ekbh0015q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
