\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump names Karoline Leavitt as White House press secretary \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos (now); Chris Stein, Maya Yang and Tom Ambrose (earlier) \par \uc2 10,845 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 November 2024\par 01:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Leavitt was Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s national press secretary and assistant press secretary in first administration. This blog is now closed.Trump\u8217\'20\'19s staffing picks and likely contenders \u8211\'20\'13 so far\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now but you can continue to read our latest US political coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 . Thank you for reading.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here are the key developments from the last few hours:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  named Karoline Leavitt as his pick for White House press secretary. Leavitt, who would be the youngest White House press secretary in history, was the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s national press secretary and served as assistant press secretary during his last administration. \u8220\'20\'1CKaroline is smart, tough, and has proven to be a highly effective communicator,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said in a statement that he will appoint \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  as both interior secretary and the head of a new National Energy Council. Trump announced that the North Dakota governor would head up the department that handles oil and gas drilling on federal lands, rattling environmentalists who fear Burgum will pursue policies that will exacerbate the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican speaker of the House, Mike Johnson, said he is against the ethics committee releasing its report into drug use and sexual misconduct by \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , the former representative nominated by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to serve as attorney general.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has appointed his campaign spokesperson \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  as the next White House communications director.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pete Hegseth, the defense secretary nominee, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/15/donald-trump-rfk-jr-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673769ec8f087357b48296c6#block-673769ec8f087357b48296c6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly }}}\uc2  involved in a sexual assault investigation in 2017 \u8211\'20\'13 a surprise to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s transition team \u8211\'20\'13 but no charges were filed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2 , the outgoing Senate judiciary committee chair, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/15/donald-trump-rfk-jr-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673781e88f087357b48298b6#block-673781e88f087357b48298b6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned }}}\uc2  that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s justice department will use its powers to \u8220\'20\'1Cseek vengeance\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/15/donald-trump-rfk-jr-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673765748f087357b482966c#block-673765748f087357b482966c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 came out against }}}\uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  to lead the health department, citing the nominee\u8217\'20\'19s support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Scott Bessent, a hedge fund founder, and \uc2 Howard Lutnick\uc2 , the co-chair of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s transition team, are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/15/donald-trump-rfk-jr-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-67375bc48f087357b482958a#block-67375bc48f087357b482958a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly in the running }}}\uc2  to head up the treasury.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  surrendered a \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2 , watches and a ring on Friday to two Georgia election workers who successfully sued him for defamation, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/11/15/rudy-giuliani-down-payment-00189990"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 PoliticoO }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former New York City mayor is still refusing to turn over other property to comply with a $148m judgment against him.\par \par \uc2 The car and other valuables are the first pieces of property, aside from access to his New York City apartment, Giuliani has been forced to hand over to Ruby Freeman and Shaye Moss, who won the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/rudy-giuliani-defamation-georgia-election-assets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $148m defamation verdict }}}\uc2  against him in 2023.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2  of Minnesota said \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  was an \u8220\'20\'1Cabsurd\u8221\'20\'1D choice for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, during an interview with CNN\u8217\'20\'19s Jake Tapper:\par \par \uc2 This is an absurd choice given that he has been outwardly under investigation by the House Ethics Committee, and then he resigned right before the report is to be released on charges of everything and allegations of sex trafficking and illicit drug use, and it appears as though a number of House members on both sides of the aisle has information about this.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  recalled that the last time \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  took office, he pledged to rip up the \uc2 North American Free Trade Agreement\uc2 , according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Trudeau made these comments among leaders of Pacific rim countries including the US and China on Friday, as they gathered in Peru for an \uc2 Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation\uc2  summit.\par \par \uc2 Instead, Canada\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister said, the nations worked hard to find ways to forge new terms, known as the US-Mexico-Canada Agreement, that served as proof trade can be beneficial to all parties.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt wasn\u8217\'20\'19t easy. And nothing is going to be easy this time,\u8221\'20\'1D Trudeau said. \u8220\'20\'1CLittle secret: there is no American administration that is automatically easy for a \uc2 Canadian government\uc2 . They take a very robust look at their own interests, and Canada adjusts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Karoline Leavitt, who would be the youngest White House press secretary in history, ran for election to the US House to represent New Hampshire\u8217\'20\'19s 1st congressional district in 2022, losing in the general election, according to Iowa State University\u8217\'20\'19s Archives of Women\u8217\'20\'19s Political Communication.\par \par \uc2 Leavitt graduated from Saint Anselm College in the state in 2019, earning a degree in politics and communication. As a student during the 2016 election, she began working for Fox News. After graduating, she worked for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and served as a presidential writer and assistant press secretary in the press office.\par \par \uc2 In June, CNN abruptly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/24/cnn-interview-karoline-leavitt-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended a live interview with Leavitt }}}\uc2  after she criticized the network\u8217\'20\'19s debate moderators, Dana Bash and Jake Tapper, both of whom had hosted the debate between Trump and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 Leavitt described the debate as a \u8220\'20\'1Chostile environment on this very network\u8221\'20\'1D and accused the moderators of having a biased history with Trump. This led to a heated exchange with CNN presenter Kasie Hunt.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  names Karoline Leavitt as pick for White House press secretary\par \par \uc2 Karoline Leavitt was the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s national press secretary and served as assistant press secretary during his last administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKaroline is smart, tough, and has proven to be a highly effective communicator,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CI have the utmost confidence she will excel at the podium, and help deliver our message to the American People as we, Make America Great Again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nomination of North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , as the interior secretary has prompted swift backlash from environmental advocacy groups alarmed at the incoming administration\u8217\'20\'19s plans to use federal lands for oil and gas drilling.\par \par \uc2 Trump also announced in a statement on Friday his intention to make Burgum chair of a National {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/energy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Energy }}}\uc2  Council he intends to form to \u8220\'20\'1Coversee the path to U.S. ENERGY DOMINANCE\u8221\'20\'1D and to focus on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe battle for AI superiority\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Burgum, a former businessman, has been governor since 2016 of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/north-dakota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Dakota }}}\uc2 , which is the third largest oil and natural gas producer in the country. Burgum, if confirmed by the Senate, would manage US federal lands including national parks and wildlife refuges, as well as oversee relations with 574 federally recognized Native American tribes.\par \par \uc2 Major {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/sep/28/trump-oil-national-parks-wildlife-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 concerns }}}\uc2  have loomed over the country\u8217\'20\'19s wildlife refuges and public lands as Trump prepares to enter the White House for a second term. Throughout his campaign trail, Trump has repeatedly said \u8220\'20\'1Cdrill, baby, drill\u8221\'20\'1D and has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-06-13/trump-says-he-ll-restart-oil-drilling-in-alaska-wildlife-refuge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed }}}\uc2  to carve up the Arctic national wildlife refuge in Alaska\u8217\'20\'19s northern tundra for oil and gas drilling.\par \par \uc2 The Sierra Club\uc2 , the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest non-profit environmental organization, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt was climate skeptic \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  who helped arrange the Mar-a-Lago meeting with wealthy oil and gas executives where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  offered to overturn dozens of environmental rules and regulations in exchange for $1bn in campaign contributions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Maya Yang and Maanvi Singh wrote all about it:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/doug-burgum-interior-department-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Environmental groups alarmed as Doug Burgum picked for US interior secretary }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Congresswoman \uc2 Debbie Wasserman Schultz\uc2  of Florida said that former representative \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s pick for national intelligence director, is \u8220\'20\'1Clikely a Russian asset.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no question I consider her someone who is likely a Russian asset,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Wasserman Schultz\uc2  told MSNBC on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  is someone who has met with war criminals, violated the Department of State\u8217\'20\'19s guidance and secretly, clandestinely went to Syria and met with [Syrian President Bashar al-]Assad, who gassed and attacked his own people with chemical weapons,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s considered to be, essentially, by most assessments, a Russian asset.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Members of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  are already bracing for a fight to reorder the primary contests in the next presidential election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe 2024 calendar will absolutely not be the calendar for 2028,\u8221\'20\'1D Nebraska state party chair \uc2 Jane Kleeb\uc2  told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/democrats-revamp-2028-early-state-primary-calendar-rcna180397"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At least half a dozen DNC members, state chairs and DNC officials said there will be a full reexamination of the order of the states before the 2028 Democratic primary.\par \par \uc2 Whatever calendar is settled on is a major factor to those presidential primary contenders, who spend most of their time and resources in states like South Carolina and Nevada, which serve to winnow down the pack before moving on to Super Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45pm GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s transition team has bypassed standard background checks by the \uc2 Federal Bureau of Investigation\uc2  ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FBI }}}\uc2  ) on some of the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet nominees, it has been reported, minimising the chances of them being rejected for Senate confirmation based on any past transgressions or conflicts of interest.\par \par \uc2 Such background checks \u8211\'20\'13 a longstanding tradition for incoming presidential nominations dating back decades to the early cold war \u8211\'20\'13 have instead been outsourced to private investigators.\par \par \uc2 The revelation, first reported by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/11/15/politics/security-clearances-fbi-gabbard-gaetz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN }}}\uc2 , comes as shock waves reverberate in Washington from at least three of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s proposed appointees: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/13/who-is-matt-gaetz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Matt Gaetz, }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/14/trump-tulsi-gabbard-national-intelligence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/14/who-is-rfk-jr-and-what-might-his-top-priorities-be"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr }}}\uc2  for attorney general, director of national intelligence and health secretary, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Moves to cut out the \uc2 FBI\uc2  appear to be in line with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/28/trump-fbi-security-clearance-check"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pre-election memo }}}\uc2  drafted by his legal advisers and fit with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s enduring suspicion that the agency is part of what, without evidence, he believes to be a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/15/fbi-durham-report-trump-russia-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deep state }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D machine within the federal government bent on undermining him.\par \par \uc2 The bureau\u8217\'20\'19s checks, based on convention rather than legislation, are intended to review nominees\u8217\'20\'19 track records for criminal histories, conflicts of interest or personal liabilities that might disqualify a candidate from being given security clearance.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more context:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/trump-cabinet-fbi-background-checks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump skips FBI background checks for controversial cabinet picks \u8211\'20\'13 report }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Wall Street ended a turbulent week with its biggest weekly losses in more than two months, as post-election optimism faded.\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 fell 1.3% on Friday and 2.1% for the week, while the Nasdaq declined 3.15% for the week. Early gains fueled by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pro-business election win and a Federal Reserve rate cut gave way to concerns over slower future rate cuts and inflation risks.\par \par \uc2 Stocks in tech, healthcare and consumer-staples sectors slid, while vaccine makers dipped upon Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nomination of \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  to lead the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  said that the racist text messages being sent to Black people across the country are now targeting high school students and Latino and LGBTQ+ communities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome recipients reported being told they were selected for deportation or to report to a re-education camp,\u8221\'20\'1D reads a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fbi.gov/news/press-releases/fbi-statement-regarding-offensive-text-messages"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2  from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  released Friday. \u8220\'20\'1CThe messages have also been reported as being received via email communication.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the wake of the presidential election, college students and working professionals have received mass texts from unrecognized phone numbers.\par \par \uc2 The hate-filled rhetoric has been reported in at least 30 states. People of color in states including Alabama, South Carolina, Georgia, New York, New Jersey, Nevada, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcwashington.com/news/local/slave-texts-telling-people-to-pick-cotton-sent-to-dc-virginia-residents/3763360/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the DC area }}}\uc2  and elsewhere reported receiving the messages.\par \par \uc2 The messages were sent to Black adults and students, including to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/boston/news/racist-text-messages-stoughton-high-school-massachusetts/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high schoolers in Massachusetts }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lohud.com/story/news/local/rockland/2024/11/07/slave-texts-with-trump-vance-named-sent-to-new-york-middle-school-high-school-students/76112531007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York }}}\uc2 , and students at historically Black colleges and universities (HBCUs), such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RegalBasil/status/1854297048410980404"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama State University }}}\uc2  and other schools, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tallahassee.com/story/news/state/2024/11/07/racist-text-messages-are-being-reported-in-multiple-states/76110486007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ones across Ohio }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tallahassee.com/story/news/local/2024/11/07/racist-text-spams-black-students-at-clemson-and-across-the-u-s/76111264007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clemson University }}}\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/educationlab/2024/11/black-students-at-alabama-colleges-get-racist-texts-about-cotton-plantations-after-trump-win.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 University of Alabama }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.news-leader.com/story/news/education/2024/11/07/springfield-naacp-condemns-racist-text-messages-targeting-missouri-state-university-students/76113081007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri State }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  praised the cooperation among South Korea, Japan and the US in countering what he described as North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous and destabilizing cooperation with Russia \u8221\'20\'1D, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Biden spoke at the start of a meeting in Peru on Friday with \uc2 Yoon Suk Yeol\uc2 , the South Korean president, and \uc2 Shigeru Ishiba\uc2 , the Japanese prime minister, on the sidelines of the \uc2 Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation\uc2  summit.\par \par \uc2 The talks came amid heightened concerns about North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s growing military partnership with Russia and Pyongyang\u8217\'20\'19s stepped-up cadence of ballistic missile tests.\par \par \uc2 Biden celebrated the partnership between Japan and South Korea, two countries that have historical enmity but that under Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidency are now tightening security and economic ties as their corner of the world becomes more complicated.\par \par \uc2 Biden noted that it would be his last meeting with them but that the trilateral partnership should be preserved for years to come.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m proud of how far we\u8217\'20\'19ve come,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhatever the issue, we\u8217\'20\'19ve taken it on together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The meeting comes as North Korea has deployed thousands of troops to Russia to help Moscow try to claw back land in the Kursk border region that Ukraine seized earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Iran sent a message to the Biden administration in October stating it was not attempting to kill \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , aiming to reduce tensions with the US, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/iran-told-u-s-it-wasnt-trying-to-kill-trump-c2d8267d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Wall Street Journal }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The message, delivered through an intermediary, followed a September warning from the Biden administration that any Iranian attempt to kill Trump, then a Republican presidential candidate, would be considered \u8220\'20\'1Can act of war\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Since Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election victory last week, some Iranian former officials, analysts and media figures have encouraged Tehran to engage with the president-elect and adopt a more cooperative stance, despite Trump allies\u8217\'20\'19 promises to reintroduce a hardline approach against Iran.\par \par \uc2 The news comes the same week \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , whom Trump named as one of the heads of the newly created Department of Government Efficiency, reportedly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/14/elon-musk-iran-ambassador-un"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 met with Iran\u8217\'20\'19s UN ambassador }}}\uc2  to discuss how to defuse tensions between Iran and the United States.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A former Virginia lawmaker has pleaded guilty to felony gun and drug charges and been sentenced to time already served in jail, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Matt Fariss, who had served in the House of Delegates as a Republican since 2012 before running unsuccessfully last year as an independent, pleaded guilty Wednesday to meth possession and having a firearm while possessing an illegal drug, the Lynchburg News and Advance reported.\par \par \uc2 Judge Dennis Lee Hupp sentenced Fariss in Campbell circuit court to three years in prison and suspended all but 20 days, according to the News and Advance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The appointment of a US health secretary with anti-vaccine views could cause deaths and have profound consequences around the world, global health experts fear.\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/14/trump-administration-rfk-criticisms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pick for the position }}}\uc2 , has a history of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jmir.org/2023/1/e42227"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spreading misinformation }}}\uc2  on vaccines and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://web.archive.org/web/20230502001519/http://www.skyhorsepublishing.com/9781510766808/the-real-anthony-fauci/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questioning }}}\uc2  the science of HIV and Aids.\par \par \uc2 His nomination has been greeted with bemusement and alarm. One global health activist, speaking on background, said the move was akin to making the disgraced doctor Andrew Wakefield, who falsely claimed that the MMR vaccine caused autism, the UK\u8217\'20\'19s health secretary.\par \par \uc2 Prof Sir Simon Wessely, a regius professor of psychiatry at King\u8217\'20\'19s College London, said of the move: \u8220\'20\'1CThat sound that you just heard was my jaw dropping, hitting the floor and rolling out of the door.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Prof Sir \uc2 Andrew Pollard\uc2 , the director of the Oxford Vaccine Group, said there was real concern that Kennedy might use the platform \u8220\'20\'1Cto pursue the same anti-science positions on life-saving public health interventions that he has advanced previously\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CIf this makes families hesitate to immunise against the deadly diseases that threaten children, the consequence will be fatal for some.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Kat Lay and Kate Connolly explain what the latest appointment could mean:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2024/nov/15/rfk-jr-disastrous-global-impact-public-health-us-secretary-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RFK Jr could have disastrous global impact on public health, experts fear }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  nominated him to lead the interior department and the new National Energy Council, \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  , North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s governor, wrote on X:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m deeply grateful to President @RealDonaldTrump for this amazing opportunity to serve the American people and achieve ENERGY DOMINANCE!\par \par \uc2 Expect that energy dominance to involve a lot of fossil fuels. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on what environmentalists fear Burgum as interior secretary could portend for fighting the climate crisis:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/doug-burgum-interior-department-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Environmental groups alarmed as Doug Burgum picked for US interior secretary }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/alice-herman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alice Herman }}}\uc2  has more on defense secretary nominee Pete Hegseth, who concerns experts for his adherence to a number of rightwing ideologies:\par \par \uc2 Extremism experts are sounding the alarm about Pete Hegseth, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s pick for secretary of defense, whose writings and online presence reveal someone immersed in a culture of rightwing Christianity, political extremism and violent ideation.\par \par \uc2 The Fox & Friends host, who has served in the US army but has no experience in government, drew {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/11/13/pentagon-hegseth-lack-of-experience-00189424"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shock from Pentagon officials }}}\uc2  when Trump nominated him. Hegseth\u8217\'20\'19s books on American culture and the military, his commentary on Fox and his frequent posts on social media showcase his far-right ideology. On these platforms, Hegseth telegraphs paranoia and anger toward \u8220\'20\'1Cleftists\u8221\'20\'1D, an ultra-masculine Maga persona and apparent revulsion toward service members who do not fit his vision \u8211\'20\'13 including women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe thing that really worries me, is both the ideology of Christian nationalism and what that\u8217\'20\'19s going to mean for the kind of policies he tries to put in place for the defense department,\u8221\'20\'1D said Thomas Lecaque, a historian focusing on religion and political violence.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/trump-cabinet-pete-hegseth-defense"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pete Hegseth, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Pentagon pick, sparks alarm over far-right extremism }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says North Dakota governor Burgum will head up new energy council\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said in a statement that he will appoint \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  as both interior secretary and the head of a new National Energy Council.\par \par \uc2 Trump announced the North Dakota governor would head up the department that handles oil and gas drilling on federal lands, rattling environmentalists who fear Burgum will pursue policies that will exacerbate the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am thrilled to announce that \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , the Governor of North Dakota, will be joining my Administration as both Secretary of the Interior and, as Chairman of the newly formed, and very important, National Energy Council, which will consist of all Departments and Agencies involved in the permitting, production, generation, distribution, regulation, transportation, of ALL forms of American Energy,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis Council will oversee the path to U.S. ENERGY DOMINANCE by cutting red tape, enhancing private sector investments across all sectors of the Economy, and by focusing on INNOVATION over longstanding, but totally unnecessary, regulation. With U.S. Energy Dominance, we will drive down Inflation, win the A.I. arms race with China (and others), and expand American Diplomatic Power to end Wars all across the World.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Much can change between now and whenever the Senate begins considering \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nomination for attorney general, likely after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is sworn in on 20 January.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/gaetz-nomination-seen-as-doomed-by-some-senate-republicans-bc594ae8?mod=politics_lead_pos1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Wall Street Journal reports }}}\uc2  that perhaps as many as 30 Republican senators will not support the former representative\u8217\'20\'19s nomination:\par \par \uc2 Trump can afford to lose the support of no more than three GOP senators on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/trump-sends-shockwaves-through-washington-with-gaetz-pick-c1a7f468?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his most contentious picks }}}\uc2 , assuming all Democrats are opposed, in a chamber that will be split 53-47 in the new Congress. People familiar with discussions among Senate Republicans said that far more than three of them are prepared to vote no if the matter comes to a vote, and some said there was already talk of trying to convince Trump to pull Gaetz, or get Gaetz to voluntarily withdraw his name.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s simply that \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  has a very long, steep hill to get across the finish line,\u8217\'20\'19 said Sen \uc2 Kevin Cramer\uc2  (R, ND). \u8216\'20\'18And it will require the spending of a lot of capital, and you just have to ask: if you could get him across the finish line, was it worth the cost?\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Cramer said he didn\u8217\'20\'19t think Gaetz would have the votes to be approved by the Judiciary Committee, much less to be confirmed by the full Senate.\par \par \uc2 One person familiar with the conversations among Republican senators said \u8216\'20\'18significantly more than four\u8217\'20\'19 of them are opposed, which would be enough to tank Gaetz\u8217\'20\'19s chances. \u8216\'20\'18People are pissed,\u8217\'20\'19 the person said.\par \par \uc2 Other estimates ranged from more than a dozen Republican \u8216\'20\'18no\u8217\'20\'19 votes to more than 30. \u8216\'20\'18It won\u8217\'20\'19t even be close,\u8217\'20\'19 another person said.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be very difficult,\u8217\'20\'19 said Sen \uc2 Markwayne Mullin\uc2  (R, Okla), when asked if Gaetz could win the votes necessary for confirmation. Mullin, a close Trump ally, said he would keep an open mind because he trusts Trump to pick his cabinet. But he said Gaetz will have to go through the vigorous vetting process required of any nominee, and said the former Florida congressman might decide to opt out and withdraw.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve seen a lot of nominees, when they go through the process, they\u8217\'20\'19re like, \u8216\'20\'18You know, it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to happen,\u8217\'20\'19 and they pull out,\u8221\'20\'1D Mullin said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/mkraju/status/1857490861069598791"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with CNN }}}\uc2 , \uc2 Mike Rounds\uc2 , a Republican senator from South Dakota, said that the chamber should be able to see the House ethics committee\u8217\'20\'19s report into \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do have a process in place which includes the ability to get that type of information, in many cases. And what we want to do is make good decisions based upon all the relevant facts and information that we can get,\u8221\'20\'1D Rounds said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe should be able to get a hold of it, and we should have access to it one way or another, based on the way that we do all of these nominations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican House Speaker Mike Johnson opposes releasing ethics report on Gaetz - report\par \par \uc2 Politico reports that the Republican speaker of the House, Mike Johnson, said he is against the ethics committee releasing its report into drug use and sexual misconduct by \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , the former representative nominated by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to serve as attorney general.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to strongly request that the ethics committee not issue the report, because that is not the way we do things in the House,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said, hours after returning from a visit to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago resort in Florida. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I think that would be a terrible precedent to set.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The committee had reportedly been near to releasing its inquiry, but Gaetz\u8217\'20\'19s resignation has thrown into question whether such a report can be made public once a lawmaker exits the House. Some senators from both parties have said it should be shared with them, so they can assess Gaetz\u8217\'20\'19s candidacy to serve as the nation\u8217\'20\'19s top law enforcement officer.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has also appointed his top ally Sergio Gor as assistant to the president and director of the presidential personnel office.\par \par \uc2 Gor was the CEO of Winning Team Publishing while also serving for the pro-Trump Super Pac Right for America, the Trump-Vance campaign said.\par \par \uc2 Commenting on the nominations of \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  (as White House communications director) and Gor, Trump said:\par \par \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  and Sergio Gor have been trusted advisors since my first presidential campaign in 2016, and have continued to champion American First principles throughout my first term, all the way to our historic victory in 2024 \u8230\'20\'26 I am thrilled to have them join my White House as we, Make America Great Again.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump confirms campaign spokesperson \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  as White House communications director\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has appointed his campaign spokesperson \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  as the next White House communications director.\par \par \uc2 Replacing Ben LaBolt, Cheung will be tasked with steering Trump\u8217\'20\'19s strategy of selling his presidency to the American people.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Friday, the Trump-Vance campaign said:\par \par \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  will return to the White House as assistant to the president and director of communications. Cheung was director of communications on the Trump-Vance 2024 presidential campaign and previously served in the Trump White House as director of strategic response.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/pompeo-kennedy-and-musk-who-could-be-in-trumps-new-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration and White House staffing picks and likely contenders \u8211\'20\'13 so far }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will appoint his main campaign spokesperson, \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2 , as the White House communications director, Politico reports, citing someone familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Throughout the 2024 presidential campaign, Cheung was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s primary vessel to mainstream media outlets, frequently defending the president-elect and remaining close to his side at campaign events and rallies.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Environmental groups are sounding the alarm over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nomination of North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , as interior secretary.\par \par \uc2 Since 2016, the former businessman has been governor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/north-dakota"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Dakota }}}\uc2 , which is the third-largest oil and natural gas producer in the country. Burgum, if confirmed by the Senate, would manage US federal lands including national parks and wildlife refuges, as well as oversee relations with 574 federally recognized Native American tribes.\par \par \uc2 The Sierra Club\uc2 , the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest non-profit environmental organization, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt was climate skeptic \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  who helped arrange the Mar-a-Lago meeting with wealthy oil and gas executives where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  offered to overturn dozens of environmental rules and regulations in exchange for $1bn in campaign contributions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Similarly, the Center for Western Priorities, a conservation policy organization focused on land and energy issues across the western states, said: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  comes from an oil state, but North Dakota is not a public lands state. His cozy relationship with oil billionaires may endear him to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but he has no experience that qualifies him to oversee the management of 20% of America\u8217\'20\'19s lands.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/doug-burgum-interior-department-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Environmental groups alarmed as Doug Burgum picked for US interior secretary }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has not nominated anyone new for his cabinet yet today, but many names are flying around for top posts. \uc2 Larry Kudlow{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/15/donald-trump-rfk-jr-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673777ae8f08916386e22ade#block-673777ae8f08916386e22ade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could reportedly }}}\uc2  return to his old job heading the National Economic Council, or even the treasury, while \uc2 Mike Rogers\uc2 , who just lost election to the Senate from Michigan, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/15/donald-trump-rfk-jr-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673773aa8f087357b482976e#block-673773aa8f087357b482976e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may be tapped }}}\uc2  to lead the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . Meanwhile, we have learned more about Pete Hegseth, the defense secretary nominee. He was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/15/donald-trump-rfk-jr-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673769ec8f087357b48296c6#block-673769ec8f087357b48296c6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly }}}\uc2  involved in a sexual assault investigation in 2017 \u8211\'20\'13 a surprise to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s transition team \u8211\'20\'13 but no charges were ever filed. The president-elect has taken to announcing his nominations in the later half of the day, so perhaps we will hear from him this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2 , the outgoing Senate judiciary committee chair, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/15/donald-trump-rfk-jr-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673781e88f087357b48298b6#block-673781e88f087357b48298b6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned }}}\uc2  that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s justice department will use its powers to \u8220\'20\'1Cseek vengeance\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/15/donald-trump-rfk-jr-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673765748f087357b482966c#block-673765748f087357b482966c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 came out against }}}\uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  to lead the health department, citing the nominee\u8217\'20\'19s support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Scott Bessent, a hedge fund founder, and \uc2 Howard Lutnick\uc2 , the co-chair of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s transition team, are also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/15/donald-trump-rfk-jr-matt-gaetz-us-politics-live?page=with:block-67375bc48f087357b482958a#block-67375bc48f087357b482958a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly in the running }}}\uc2  to head up the treasury.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Democrat says nominees show Trump will 'weaponize the justice department to seek vengeance'\par \par \uc2 The outgoing Democratic chair of the Senate judiciary committee \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2  warned that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s appointees to top justice department posts are a sign that he will direct prosecutors and law enforcement to retaliate against his political opponents.\par \par \uc2 Durbin singled out the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s nomination of Todd Blanche, who defended Trump in his hush-money trial in New York, as deputy attorney general, and John Sauer, who argued before the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/01/supreme-court-decision-trump-immunity-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in his immunity case }}}\uc2 , as solicitor general:\par \par \uc2 Coupled with the announcement that he intends to nominate former Congressman \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  to be attorney general, these selections show \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  intends to weaponize the justice department to seek vengeance. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  viewed the justice department as his personal law firm during his first term, and these selections \u8211\'20\'13 his personal attorneys \u8211\'20\'13 are poised to do his bidding.\par \par \uc2 The American people deserve a justice department that fights for equal justice under the law. This isn\u8217\'20\'19t it.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are losing control of the Senate at the beginning of next year, and it will be up to the incoming Republican majority to confirm Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appointees.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It is ultimately up to the Senate, and in particular its incoming Republican majority, to decide the fate of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nominees for cabinet posts.\par \par \uc2 For a taste of the sentiment among congressional Republicans towards Trump\u8217\'20\'19s picks, here is the comment Steve Scalise, the Republican majority leader in the House of Representatives, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JakeSherman/status/1857442989884477449"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gave to Punchbowl News }}}\uc2  when asked about \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s anti-vaccine views:\par \par \uc2 Look, ultimately, he\u8217\'20\'19s going to be carrying out President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda. You know, everybody comes in, with their own ideas, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be RFK, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  and foreign policy, but ultimately, when you take on a position like that, you\u8217\'20\'19re there to carry out President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda for all the Cabinet Secretaries, and I have no doubt that they\u8217\'20\'19re all going to be focused on that mission and carrying out the mandate the voters gave us.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump considering \uc2 Larry Kudlow\uc2  for top economic jobs, including treasury secretary - report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  may be bringing \uc2 Larry Kudlow\uc2 , a top economic adviser during his first term, back to his administration, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/larry-kudlow-economic-role-trump-cabinet-3af2a446"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Wall Street Journal reports }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kudlow is under consideration to perhaps lead the treasury department or the National Economic Council, which he led during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term. In that job, he was often on television downplaying the severity of the economic collapse caused by Covid-19 and predicting a rapid recovery. Kudlow has since become a host on \uc2 Fox Business Network\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from the Journal:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is considering tapping \uc2 Fox Business Network\uc2  host \uc2 Larry Kudlow\uc2  for a senior economic policy role in his administration, according to people familiar with the matter, amid the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s mounting frustration with jockeying for top jobs.\par \par \uc2 Kudlow met with Trump at Mar-a-Lago, the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s private Florida club, late this week, the people said. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s advisers see Kudlow as a contender to lead the National Economic Council and possibly the Treasury Department.\par \par \uc2 Kudlow and a spokeswoman for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s transition team didn\u8217\'20\'19t respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Kudlow, 77, served as NEC director for nearly three years, remaining in the role until the end of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s time in office. He has kept in regular touch with Trump.\par \par \uc2 Kudlow has made regular appearances on Fox Business since leaving the White House. On his weekday show, Kudlow regularly touts Trump\u8217\'20\'19s economic policy proposals. His allies have made appeals directly to Trump to bring him back into the administration, the people said.\par \par \uc2 Kudlow\u8217\'20\'19s stock has risen in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s orbit amid what one adviser to the president called a \u8220\'20\'1Ccold war\u8221\'20\'1D between two other leading candidates for senior economic roles in the second term: billionaire \uc2 Cantor Fitzgerald\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Howard Lutnick\uc2  and investor Scott Bessent.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump considering former representative \uc2 Mike Rogers\uc2  to lead \uc2 FBI\uc2  - report\par \par \uc2 Mike Rogers\uc2 , a Republican former representative who just narrowly lost election to the Senate representing Michigan, is in the running to be \uc2 FBI\uc2  director under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/politics/mike-rogers-consideration-fbi-chief-after-meeting-mar-a-lago-trump-transition-team-sources-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News reports }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Citing sources familiar with the situation, the broadcaster reports Rogers met with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s transition team yesterday at Mar-a-Lago in Florida. Rogers is a former \uc2 FBI\uc2  special agent, who was under consideration to lead the bureau during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, a job that ultimately went to \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from Fox:\par \par \uc2 Will the second time be the charm for one-time {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/category/tech/topics/fbi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Bureau of Investigation }}}\uc2  special agent and former Rep \uc2 Mike Rogers\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Rogers, the 2024 Republican Senate nominee in Michigan who lost his election last week by a razor-thin margin, met Thursday with President-elect Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/category/politics/elections/presidential/trump-transition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 transition team }}}\uc2  regarding potentially serving as \uc2 FBI\uc2  director in the former and future president\u8217\'20\'19s second administration, sources familiar tell Fox News.\par \par \uc2 The meeting took place at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago club in Palm Beach, Florida.\par \par \uc2 Rogers worked as a special agent with the \uc2 FBI\uc2  in its Chicago office and who served as chair of the House Intelligence Committee during the final four years of his decade-long tenure in Congress, was interviewed in 2017 during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first administration to serve as \uc2 FBI\uc2  director after \uc2 James Comey\uc2  was dismissed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foxnews.com/category/person/donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 But Trump }}}\uc2  at the time decided to appoint \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  to the traditional ten-year term steering the federal law enforcement agency.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House represents a setback for women who say he sexually assaulted them, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/victoria-bekiempis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victoria Bekiempis }}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 When {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/donald-trump-wins-us-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elected }}}\uc2  to a second term last week, women who say he sexually assaulted them, and other victims of sexual abuse, voiced disappointment that a man repeatedly accused of sexual misconduct could once again become president, with one of them describing this win as a \u8220\'20\'1Cgut punch\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/10/28/trump-sexual-misconduct-allegations-women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than two dozen }}}\uc2  women have made such claims against Trump, including E Jean Carroll, who was awarded nearly $90m total in two civil trials after jurors found that Trump sexually abused and defamed her. She {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ejeancarroll/status/1854225543773749729?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Etweet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  on X: \u8220\'20\'1CI tried to tell you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several survivors of sexual assault interviewed by the Guardian, as well as advocates for persons who have suffered abuse, said they were not surprised by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s win. They felt it was another example of how sexual abuse is not taken seriously, or pointed to the fact that powerful people who perpetrate abuse seem to be able to avoid repercussions.\par \par \uc2 Stacey Williams, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/donald-trump-accuser-stacey-williams-jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  she met Trump through \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  about three decades ago, and told the Guardian that the now president-elect groped her at Trump Tower in 1993 in what seemed to be a \u8220\'20\'1Ctwisted game\u8221\'20\'1D with the late sex predator, is among the many processing election results.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think what we were all hoping was that [the] truth would come through and the stories would affect people\u8217\'20\'19s vote once they had [them] in front of them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But, she said: \u8220\'20\'1CDisinformation won this election at the end of the day, and if we don\u8217\'20\'19t figure out an answer for that, I don\u8217\'20\'19t have a lot of hope for this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/trump-win-sexual-assault-victims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A \u8216\'20\'18gut punch\u8217\'20\'19: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s alleged sexual assault victims and their advocates on his win }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump defense secretary nominee involved in 2017 sexual assault investigation, no charges filed - report\par \par \uc2 Fox News host Pete Hegseth, who \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  nominated to be defense secretary, was involved in a sexual assault investigation in California seven years ago, but no charges were filed against him, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/us-world/article/pete-hegseth-monterey-19918048.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the San Francisco Chronicle reports }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The incident happened in 2017 at a hotel and golf course in the city of Monterey, but there were few details of how Hegseth was involved, or what happened. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from the Chronicle:\par \par \uc2 In a brief statement late Thursday, the city manager\u8217\'20\'19s office in Monterey confirmed the sexual assault investigation, but provided few details.\par \par \uc2 The city said the incident was reported to have happened between almost midnight on Oct. 7, 2017, and 7 a.m. the next morning at the Hyatt Regency Monterey Hotel and Spa on Del Monte Golf Course, less than a mile from Monterey Bay and across Highway 1 from the \uc2 Naval Postgraduate School\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Monterey Police Department investigated an alleged sexual assault at 1 Old Golf Course Road,\u8221\'20\'1D the city said. It said the victim\u8217\'20\'19s name was confidential and that the alleged assault was reported on Oct. 12, 2017. The city said no weapons were involved, but that there was a report of \u8220\'20\'1Ccontusions to right thigh.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The city declined to release the police report, saying it was exempt from public disclosure, and said it would not make any further remarks on the probe.\par \par \uc2 The Monterey County District Attorney\u8217\'20\'19s Office did not reply to a request for comment late Thursday, but an online database indicated no criminal charges had been filed against Hegseth in that county.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/story/pete-hegseth-misconduct-allegation-meeting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vanity Fair reports }}}\uc2  that news of the allegation sent Trump\u8217\'20\'19s transition team scrambling over the past few days:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s transition team scrambled Thursday after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s incoming chief of staff Susie Wiles was presented with an allegation that former Fox & Friends cohost Pete Hegseth, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nominee to be Defense Secretary, had engaged in sexual misconduct. According to two sources, Wiles was briefed Wednesday night about an allegation that Hegseth had acted inappropriately with a woman. One of the sources said the alleged incident took place in Monterey, California in 2017.\par \par \uc2 According to the transition source, the allegation is serious enough that Wiles and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers spoke to Hegseth about it on Thursday. A source with knowledge of the meeting said that Hegseth said the allegation stemmed from a consensual encounter and characterized the episode as he-said, she-said.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday evening, Hegseth\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Timothy Parlatore said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis allegation was already investigated by the Monterey police department and they found no evidence for it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s communications director \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump is nominating high-caliber and extremely qualified candidates to serve in his Administration. Mr. Hegseth has vigorously denied any and all accusations, and no charges were filed. We look forward to his confirmation as United States Secretary of Defense so he can get started on Day One to Make America Safe and Great Again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former vice-president Pence opposes Kennedy as health secretary, citing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views\par \par \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , who served as vice-president during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s first term, announced his opposition to appointing \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  as secretary of health and human services, citing his views on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Trump-Pence administration was unapologetically pro-life for our four years in office. There are hundreds of decisions made at \uc2 HHS\uc2  every day that either lead our nation toward a respect for life or away from it, and \uc2 HHS\uc2  under our administration always stood for life,\u8221\'20\'1D Pence said in a statement released by his conservative nonprofit, Advancing American Freedom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe the nomination of RFK Jr. to serve as Secretary of \uc2 HHS\uc2  is an abrupt departure from the pro-life record of our administration and should be deeply concerning to millions of Pro-Life Americans who have supported the Republican Party and our nominees for decades.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During his presidential campaign, which he ended in August and announced his support for Trump, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/rfkjr/videos/2747714242055909/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kennedy said }}}\uc2  he is in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  being legal up to a certain point.\par \par \uc2 Pence fell out with Trump after refusing to go along with his attempts to stop \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from taking office after the 2020 election. Nonetheless, his words may hold some sway with conservative senators opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s the rest of his statement:\par \par \uc2 For the majority of his career, RFK Jr. has defended \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand during all nine months of pregnancy, supports overturning the Dobbs decision and has called for legislation to codify Roe v Wade. If confirmed, RFK, Jr. would be the most pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republican appointed secretary of \uc2 HHS\uc2  in modern history.\par \par \uc2 The pro-life movement has always looked to the Republican party to stand for life, to affirm an unborn child has a fundamental right to life which cannot be infringed.\par \par \uc2 On behalf of tens of millions of pro-life Americans, I respectfully urge Senate Republicans to reject this nomination and give the American people a leader who will respect the sanctity of life as secretary of \uc2 Health and Human Services\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 John Thune\uc2 , the South Dakota lawmaker who earlier this week was elected leader of the Senate Republicans, will be at the center of the confirmation hearings for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s cabinet picks.\par \par \uc2 He has said little about the nominees themselves, but emphasized that he is squarely on the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s side. The Senate will \u8220\'20\'1Cdo the normal thing in vetting and confirmations hearings, etc. And it\u8217\'20\'19s a process. And we\u8217\'20\'19ll adhere to it, but try and expedite it,\u8221\'20\'1D Thune {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/11/14/2024/why-john-thune-has-the-hardest-job-in-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Semafor }}}\uc2  in a piece looking at the dynamics around Thune and the confirmation process.\par \par \uc2 The upshot of the story: there\u8217\'20\'19s no reason to think that Senate Republicans are gearing up to block Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nominees, or at least not many of them. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJohn is talented at bringing people together and trying to find a path forward,\u8221\'20\'1D Sen. \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2 , R-Maine, told Semafor. \u8220\'20\'1CBut to have the \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  nomination on the very day that he became chosen as leader was certainly unfortunate timing. And it illustrates the challenges he\u8217\'20\'19s going to face in defending the Senate as an institution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Trump 2.0 era on Capitol Hill is already here, with the president-elect pushing his party\u8217\'20\'19s lawmakers to fall in line regardless of their individual concerns. And the coming Senate confirmation fights over his advisers will be the first act in that drama.\par \par \uc2 Collins is one of several more centrist Republicans whose votes Trump cannot necessarily count on for more contentious nominees; she made no secret this week of her shock over the Gaetz pick and said she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t sure Kennedy would even get a Senate-confirmed role.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Thune\u8217\'20\'19s personal confirmation battle next year will require him to bridge the gaps between more establishment-aligned Republicans like Collins, who are already skeptical about one or more of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s choices, and more MAGA-friendly GOP senators.\par \par \uc2 The South Dakotan won the leadership battle in part by emphasizing his rebuilt relationship with the incoming president. And there\u8217\'20\'19s a substantial bloc of Senate Republicans who are eager to see Thune do whatever it takes to confirm Trump\u8217\'20\'19s advisers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was struck [Wednesday] by how far he went and saying that \u8216\'20\'18there\u8217\'20\'19s no daylight between me and President Trump, we\u8217\'20\'19ll advance his agenda,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said one Republican senator, noting Thune\u8217\'20\'19s openness to using recess appointments on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s picks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf he tries to walk that back,\u8221\'20\'1D this senator added, \u8220\'20\'1CI think there will be hellfire and brimstone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36pm GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2024/11/15/trump-treasury-secretary-lutnick-bessent/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Washington Post reports }}}\uc2  that among the candidates for Treasury secretary are the co-chair of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s transition team, \uc2 Howard Lutnick\uc2 , as well as hedge fund founder Scott Bessent.\par \par \uc2 Other names being tossed around are \uc2 Larry Kudlow\uc2 , a prominent White House economist during his first administration, or \uc2 Robert Lighthizer\uc2 , who served as a trade advisor. Whoever Trump picks will likely be tasked with implementing the tariffs he has threatened to impose on US trade partners, in order to bend them to his will on issues such as immigration and reshoring jobs.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from the Post:\par \par \uc2 When Scott Bessent left President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago compound in Palm Beach, Florida, last Friday, his allies were optimistic that the hedge fund executive was virtually certain to be named the next treasury secretary.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, however, Bessent again flew to Florida with his bid for the Cabinet post still hanging in the balance. Bessent is expected to be interviewed by Trump on Friday \u8212\'20\'14 as a rival contender for the post, the Trump transition co-chair and Wall Street banker \uc2 Howard Lutnick\uc2 , makes his own bid to become the most senior economic official in the \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 , according to two people familiar with the matter, who spoke on the condition of anonymity to describe private meetings.\par \par \uc2 The internal jockeying could have major repercussions not just for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration, but the trajectory of the U.S. economy over the next four years. The treasury secretary is responsible for a huge range of policy decisions, from taxes to tariffs to bank regulation, and will be tasked with executing some of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2024/10/16/trump-tariffs-impact-economy/?itid=lk_inline_manual_5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promises central }}}\uc2  to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 campaign.\par \par \uc2 Trump, however, has not yet announced his choice for the pick even as he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/11/14/trump-lawyers-justice-department-blanche-bove-sauer/?itid=hp-top-table-main_p001_f001&itid=lk_inline_manual_8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fills out much of his Cabinet }}}\uc2 . The impasse has prompted speculation among transition officials that Trump could still pick a third candidate for treasury secretary, such as former White House economist \uc2 Larry Kudlow\uc2  or top trade adviser \uc2 Robert E. Lighthizer\uc2 , although Bessent or Lutnick are still viewed as the favorites, according to two other people, who also spoke on the condition of anonymity to reflect private deliberations. (Kudlow {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/trumps-transition-effort-kicks-into-high-gear-f4f1a752"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said }}}\uc2  Bessent is his own top pick for the position.)\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Might \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s allies in the Senate wind up rejecting some of his most controversial picks to lead federal departments, such as \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  for health secretary?\par \par \uc2 Perhaps, but we will probably only find that out for sure in the weeks to come, and particularly once confirmation hearings for the nominees begin early next year.\par \par \uc2 Despite Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s peddling of conspiracy theories and misinformation about vaccines, Republican senators appeared open to considering him for the job leading the country\u8217\'20\'19s health policy and research. Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Bill Cassidy\uc2  who, it should be noted, is himself a doctor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SenBillCassidy/status/1857178897848103023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said Kennedy }}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Chas championed issues like healthy foods and the need for greater transparency in our public health infrastructure. I look forward to learning more about his other policy positions and how they will support a conservative, pro-American agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 News that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had nominated conspiracy theorist and vaccine critic \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  as his health secretary sent shares of major pharmaceutical companies lower in European trading today, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/marksweney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Sweney }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/graemewearden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Graeme Wearden }}}\uc2  report. US markets have not opened yet, but we\u8217\'20\'19ll see if the bloodletting continues:\par \par \uc2 Investors in pharmaceutical companies are selling off stock after \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/14/trump-administration-rfk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nominated the anti-vaccine activist Robert F Kennedy Jr }}}\uc2  to lead the US Department of Health and Human Services.\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/14/who-is-rfk-jr-and-what-might-his-top-priorities-be"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 embraced numerous health-related conspiracy theories, }}}\uc2  and is one of the most persistent and influential vaccine deniers in the US.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s announcement sent shares in some of the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest pharmaceutical companies \u8211\'20\'13 including \uc2 Moderna\uc2 , \uc2 AstraZeneca\uc2  and \uc2 GSK\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 falling on Friday morning.\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr has said vaccines are linked to autism in children, that HIV is not the cause of Aids and that some antidepressants are linked to a rise in school shootings.\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr \u8211\'20\'13 and Trump \u8211\'20\'13 are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/fluoride-explainer-what-is-us-election-donald-trump-robert-f-kennedy-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mulling banning fluoride in drinking water }}}\uc2 , while he has also called for bans on hundreds of food additives and chemicals and wants to cut ultra-processed foods from school lunches as part of a plan to reduce diet-related chronic diseases.\par \par \uc2 Announcing his choice, Trump said the health department would play a \u8220\'20\'1Cbig role in helping ensure that everybody will be protected from harmful chemicals, pollutants, pesticides, pharmaceutical products, and food additives that have contributed to the overwhelming health crisis in this country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/15/pharma-shares-trump-rfk-jr-health-vaccine-drugmakers-moderna-astrazeneca-gsk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pharma shares hit as Trump picks RFK Jr to lead health department }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans are set to take control of the Senate next year, where one of their first jobs will be to confirm \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nominees for cabinet posts. Should they object to the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s picks, he has threatened to make use of recess appointments, an archaic tactic that would allow him to circumvent the chamber and its objectors. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on how that would work, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joan-greve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joan E Greve }}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Several Republican senators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/13/republicans-matt-gaetz-trump-attorney-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expressed }}}\uc2  shock on Wednesday when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced he would nominate \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , the hard-right congressman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/13/who-is-matt-gaetz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 known for }}}\uc2  instigating fights with members of his own party, as attorney general.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe president obviously has the right to nominate whomever he wants, but I think this is an example of why it\u8217\'20\'19s so important that we have the advice and consent provisions in the constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican senator \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/11/13/g-s1-34082/senate-reaction-gaetz-gabbard-trump-cabinet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters }}}\uc2  on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sure that there will be many, many questions raised at Mr Gaetz\u8217\'20\'19s hearing, if in fact the nomination goes forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the president-elect has proposed an archaic and in recent years little-used mechanism to get his nominees installed without Senate confirmation: recess appointments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny Republican Senator seeking the coveted LEADERSHIP position in the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  must agree to Recess Appointments (in the Senate!), without which we will not be able to get people confirmed in a timely manner,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/realDonaldTrump/status/1855692242981155259"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need positions filled IMMEDIATELY!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If Trump pursues a strategy of recess appointments, it could severely curtail the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s power to serve as a check on the new president\u8217\'20\'19s nominations and allow controversial picks such as Gaetz to move forward.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s everything to know about recess appointments:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/trump-senate-recess-appointments-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What are recess appointments and can Trump confirm nominees that way? }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has made several nominations to his cabinet, including \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  for health secretary and \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  for attorney general, both picks that have drawn objections from Democrats.\par \par \uc2 But many roles remain unfilled. Among these is Treasury secretary, a key role when it comes to managing the economy and government expenditures, and energy secretary, which could have huge influence on fighting the climate crisis (to the extent that Trump is interested in that) and regulating oil and gas production.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at who he has picked so far, and which nominees we are still waiting for:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/pompeo-kennedy-and-musk-who-could-be-in-trumps-new-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration and White House staffing picks and likely contenders \u8211\'20\'13 so far }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Betting markets had a great election. With billions of dollars wagered on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who would take the White House }}}\uc2 , their projections proved closer to the actual result than many opinion polls. Now the operators behind them want the US to wager on almost everything else.\par \par \uc2 Forget {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump }}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris }}}\uc2 . Is Billie Eilish going to win album of the year at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/grammys"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Grammys }}}\uc2  ? How many federal government employees are about to lose their jobs? Will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/monkeypox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mpox }}}\uc2  be declared a pandemic this year?\par \par \uc2 All these markets, and hundreds more, were available this week on \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the platform which, just five weeks before polling day, won approval in a federal appeals court to legally host election betting in the US for the first time.\par \par \uc2 The result was \u8220\'20\'1Castronomical\u8221\'20\'1D, according to its CEO, \uc2 Tarek Mansour\uc2 , with more than $1bn worth of trades in a single month. But by the next presidential election, in November 2028, he wants hundreds of billions of dollars worth of trades in a single month.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/online-betting-markets-expansion-after-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Online prediction betting markets look ahead after US presidential election triumph: \u8216\'20\'18We\u8217\'20\'19re just getting started\u8217\'20\'19 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Members of Congress and other US public officials targeted for \u8220\'20\'1Cretribution\u8221\'20\'1D by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  say they are taking extraordinary security precautions for themselves and their families and are now bracing for scenarios as extreme as the possibility of being rounded up and arrested, after Trump returns to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Two Democratic House members who have been vocal in their criticisms of Trump and his policy agenda told the Guardian they and their colleagues are preparing for \u8220\'20\'1Csome pretty surreal and dystopic scenarios\u8221\'20\'1D. They range from bogus investigations or tax audits of present and former members of the federal government to out-and-out violence inspired by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric of revenge.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope none of my Democratic colleagues become American corollaries to Alexander Navalny,\u8221\'20\'1D said congressman \uc2 Jared Huffman\uc2  of California, referring to the Russian opposition leader and outspoken critic of \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  who survived being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/aug/20/alexei-navalny-russian-opposition-figure-unconscious-in-hospital-says-aide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  poisoned }}}\uc2  before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/feb/16/russian-activist-and-putin-critic-alexei-navalny-dies-in-prison"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  dying }}}\uc2  in an Arctic prison.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[My colleagues in the House] are thinking about legal defenses against a weaponized Department of Justice,\u8221\'20\'1D Huffman added. \u8220\'20\'1CThey may have to be ready to be arrested and rounded up. They have to have family plans protecting themselves in ways I don\u8217\'20\'19t even like to talk about publicly \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have so many colleagues living under constant violent threats toward them and their families and their staff \u8230\'20\'26 These are dark times. We all have our eyes wide open.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/trump-critics-retribution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We all have our eyes wide open\u8217\'20\'19: Trump critics brace for dark time of retribution }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 When {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/donald-trump-wins-us-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 elected }}}\uc2  to a second term last week, women who say he sexually assaulted them, and other victims of sexual abuse, voiced disappointment that a man repeatedly accused of sexual misconduct could once again become president, with one of them describing this win as a \u8220\'20\'1Cgut punch\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/10/28/trump-sexual-misconduct-allegations-women"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More than two dozen }}}\uc2  women have made such claims against Trump, including E Jean Carroll, who was awarded nearly $90m total in two civil trials after jurors found that Trump sexually abused and defamed her. She {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ejeancarroll/status/1854225543773749729?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Etweet"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  on X: \u8220\'20\'1CI tried to tell you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several survivors of sexual assault interviewed by the Guardian, as well as advocates for persons who have suffered abuse, said they were not surprised by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s win. They felt it was another example of how sexual abuse is not taken seriously, or pointed to the fact that powerful people who perpetrate abuse seem to be able to avoid repercussions.\par \par \uc2 Stacey Williams, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/donald-trump-accuser-stacey-williams-jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  she met Trump through \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  about three decades ago, and told the Guardian that the now president-elect groped her at Trump Tower in 1993 in what seemed to be a \u8220\'20\'1Ctwisted game\u8221\'20\'1D with the late sex predator, is among the many processing election results.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think what we were all hoping was that [the] truth would come through and the stories would affect people\u8217\'20\'19s vote once they had [them] in front of them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But, \u8220\'20\'1Cdisinformation won this election at the end of the day, and if we don\u8217\'20\'19t figure out an answer for that, I don\u8217\'20\'19t have a lot of hope for this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Emails to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s camp did not receive an immediate response. Trump has previously denied all allegations of misconduct.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/15/trump-win-sexual-assault-victims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A \u8216\'20\'18gut punch\u8217\'20\'19: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s alleged sexual assault victims and their advocates on his win }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said on Thursday that a government efficiency panel headed up by billionaire \uc2 Tesla\uc2  CEO \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  will issue reports in its work to streamline the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey will be coming out with individual reports and a big one at the end,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a speech at his Mar-a-Lago resort in Florida, providing the first new detail on the panel\u8217\'20\'19s output since it was announced earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Trump on Tuesday said the panel would \u8220\'20\'1Cprovide advice and guidance from outside government,\u8221\'20\'1D on slimming down the government, cutting regulations, reducing spending and restructuring federal agencies, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump picks North Dakota governor Burgum for interior secretary\par \par \uc2 President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said on Thursday that North Dakota Governor \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , a wealthy former software company executive, will be his pick for interior secretary.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s going to head the Department of Interior, and it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be fantastic,\u8221\'20\'1D a tuxedo-wearing Trump said at a gala at his Mar-a-Lago Florida retreat, adding that he would make an official announcement on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Burgum, 68, has portrayed himself as a traditional, business-minded conservative. He ran against Trump for the Republican presidential nomination before quitting and becoming a loyal Trump supporter, appearing at fundraisers and advocating for Trump on television, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 At the gala, which featured tech billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , actor Sylvester Stallone and members of his incoming administration, Trump praised his latest cabinet picks and made some of his longest remarks since his presidential election victory speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNobody knew we were going to win it the way we won it,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 He teased Musk about his ongoing post-election stay at Mar-a-Lago. Musk is involved in some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s meetings at the oceanfront property.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t get him out of here. He just loves this place. And I like having him here,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump.\par \par \uc2 At the end of the event, Musk mounted the stage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe public has given us a mandate that could not be more clear. The people have spoken, the people want change,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 Fears that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s second presidency will be more extreme than his first have intensified amid a flurry of senior nominations that opponents have criticised as going from bad to worse.\par \par \uc2 Dismay over some of the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s early picks escalated to outrage after the far-right Florida congressman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/13/republicans-matt-gaetz-trump-attorney-general"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Matt Gaetz }}}\uc2  was unveiled as his selection to be attorney general \u8211\'20\'13 a position Trump has previously said he views as the most important in his administration.\par \par \uc2 The choice provoked disbelief, even among {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans }}}\uc2 , and has fueled concerns that Trump is intent on carrying out mass firings at the Department of Justice in retribution for criminal investigations it instigated against him.\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thebulwark.com/p/donald-trump-is-dead-serious-about"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly }}}\uc2  chose Gaetz, 42, after the congressman \u8211\'20\'13 who himself was subject to a two-year justice department investigation into suspected sex-trafficking that ended without charges \u8211\'20\'13 told Trump: \u8220\'20\'1CYeah, I\u8217\'20\'19ll go over there and start cuttin\u8217\'20\'19 fuckin\u8217\'20\'19 heads.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Others considered for the post were dismissed as too concerned with legal concepts or constitutional niceties.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/14/trump-cabinet-administration-maga-extremism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fears mount over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second term amid flurry of shock selections }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Musk asks \u8216\'20\'18high-IQ revolutionaries\u8217\'20\'19 to work for no pay on new Trump project\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  are asking Americans who are \u8220\'20\'1Chigh-IQ small-government revolutionaries\u8221\'20\'1D and willing to work over 80 hours a week to join their new Department of Government Efficiency \u8211\'20\'13 at zero pay.\par \par \uc2 In a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 X }}}\uc2  post on Thursday that doubled as a job announcement and another one of Musk\u8217\'20\'19s trolling attempts, the account for the newly formed Doge wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t need more part-time idea generators. We need super high-IQ small-government revolutionaries willing to work 80+ hours per week on unglamorous cost-cutting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The name of the department, which is not part of the federal government, harkens back to a meme of an expressive shiba inu dog.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf that\u8217\'20\'19s you, DM this account with your CV. Elon & Vivek will review the top 1% of applicants,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement added.\par \par \uc2 In a separate post, Musk chimed in on the callout, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CIndeed, this will be tedious work, make lots of enemies & compensation is zero.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat a great deal!\u8221\'20\'1D Musk, the richest man in the world, wrote with a laughing emoji. He has promised to reduce federal bureaucracy by a third and cut $2tn from \uc2 US government\uc2  spending, an endeavor he said \u8220\'20\'1Cnecessarily involves some temporary hardship\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  announced the appointment of Musk and Ramaswamy to Doge, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CTogether, these two wonderful Americans will pave the way for my administration to dismantle government bureaucracy, slash excess regulations, cut wasteful expenditures, and restructure federal agencies \u8211\'20\'13 essential to the \u8216\'20\'18Save America\u8217\'20\'19 movement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump went on to describe the newly formed department as the \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18Manhattan Project\u8217\'20\'19 of our time,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to the US-led research program during the second world war that sought to create the nuclear bomb, which killed an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.icanw.org/hiroshima_and_nagasaki_bombings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated }}}\uc2  214,000 people in Japan in 1945.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/nov/14/elon-musk-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Musk asks \u8216\'20\'18high-IQ revolutionaries\u8217\'20\'19 to work for no pay on new Trump project }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr role condemned as a 'public health catastrophe'\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to the US politics live blog. I\u8217\'20\'19m Tom Ambrose and I\u8217\'20\'19ll be bringing you all the latest news from Washington over the next few hours.\par \par \uc2 We start with the news that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s nomination of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/robert-f-kennedy-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr }}}\uc2  as US secretary of health and human services has prompted widespread criticisms towards Kennedy, an anti-vaccine activist who has embraced a slew of other debunked health-related conspiracy theories.\par \par \uc2 In a Truth Social post on Thursday, Trump claimed that Americans have been \u8220\'20\'1Ccrushed by the industrial food complex and drug companies\u8221\'20\'1D and that Kennedy \u8220\'20\'1Cwill restore these Agencies to the traditions of Gold Standard Scientific Research, and beacons of Transparency, to end the Chronic Disease epidemic, and to Make America Great and Healthy Again!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response to Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s nomination, \uc2 Public Citizen\uc2 , a progressive nonprofit organization focusing on consumer advocacy, said: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  is a clear and present danger to the nation\u8217\'20\'19s health. He shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be allowed in the building at the department of health and human services (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ), let alone be placed in charge of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s public health agency.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bungling of public health policy during the Covid pandemic cost hundreds of thousands of lives. By appointing Kennedy as his secretary of \uc2 HHS\uc2 , Trump is courting another, policy-driven public health catastrophe,\u8221\'20\'1D the organization added.\par \par \uc2 For more on that, see our full report here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/14/trump-administration-rfk-criticisms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 RFK Jr condemned as \u8216\'20\'18clear and present danger\u8217\'20\'19 after Trump nomination }}}\par \par \uc2 In other news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  should investigate both Gaetz and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/14/trump-tulsi-gabbard-national-intelligence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard }}}\uc2  before they are confirmed for their cabinet posts, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former national security adviser \uc2 John Bolton\uc2  has said. Gabbard, who Trump nominated as director of national intelligence, is known for her tolerant view of Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  and Syrian president \uc2 Bashar al-Assad\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  reportedly met Iran\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the United Nations on Monday, and discussed how to defuse tensions between Iran and the US, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/14/elon-musk-iran-ambassador-un"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two Iranian officials told the New York Times }}}\uc2 . As Trump prepares to address conflicts in Ukraine and the Middle East, Musk, the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man, has been assisting in discussions with foreign officials, establishing himself as the country\u8217\'20\'19s most influential civilian come January.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Musk and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  are seeking Americans who are \u8220\'20\'1Chigh-IQ small-government revolutionaries\u8221\'20\'1D and willing to work over 80 hours a week to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/nov/14/elon-musk-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 join their new department }}}\uc2 , at zero pay. Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/trump-appoints-elon-musk-government-efficiency-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 named }}}\uc2  Musk to co-lead the newly created government efficiency department that sits outside the federal government.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Advocates have urged state governments to find new ways to defend immigrants and block Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mass deportation plan. California shielded many non-citizen residents from removal in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term but immigrants rights groups warn an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/14/trump-mass-deportation-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aggressive, multi-pronged response will be needed }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Democratic lawmaker will file a motion specifically mentioning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/14/trump-two-terms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump can only serve two terms }}}\uc2 , after the president-elect joked he would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=74vcsDCfFlg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 willing to serve an unconstitutional third term }}}\uc2  as president while meeting with House Republicans on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump announced his former Georgia congressman \uc2 Doug Collins\uc2  as secretary of veterans affairs. Collins ran for Senate in 2020, finishing third in the primary. He also \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/trump-campaign-press-release-trump-campaign-announces-rep-doug-collins-lead-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provided counsel }}}\uc2  to Trump in the aftermath of the 2020 presidential election as Trump sought to challenge Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s election results\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241115ekbf001uq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
