\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll need to fight to protect US  \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights \highlight\uc2 . Here\u8217\'20\'19s what to expect\b0\par\par\uc2 Sophie Brickman \par \uc2 1,253 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 November 2024\par 17:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Will there be a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban? A ban on mailed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication? I talked to some experts\par \par \uc2 At around 10pm ET on election night, with prediction needles listing rightwards, and various friends\u8217\'20\'19 group chats starting to become inundated by the river-of-tears-down-my-face emoji \u8211\'20\'13 even that early, we were collectively way beyond a single tear \u8211\'20\'13 I left Steve Kornacki frantically bobbing and weaving around a map of Georgia, and went to bed. Somehow, I slept through until the morning, when I awoke in \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s America\u8221\'20\'1D, as news organizations were calling it, and to a torrent of emails and notes from friends bemoaning, among other things, the very real possibility of a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAre we still gonna have birth control?\u8221\'20\'1D one friend texted, in disbelief.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSorry for the US you\u8217\'20\'19re waking up to,\u8221\'20\'1D another wrote from Oxford. \u8220\'20\'1CConfounding,\u8221\'20\'1D his wife echoed, from across the pond.\par \par \uc2 And so, to get a clear-eyed, postmortem picture of what might be facing women and their loved ones in America, two days after the election I called up \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , the president and CEO of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Center for \b  \highlight22Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , an advocacy group with a stated mission of \u8220\'20\'1Cusing the power of law to advance \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  as fundamental human rights around the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In practice, that means unleashing an army of seasoned litigators to fight for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, among other things, in courtrooms across the country and around the world \u8211\'20\'13 they currently work in five continents. She began as CEO in 2003, 30 years after Roe v Wade constitutionally protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Twenty years later, after fighting the good fight for decades, she and her litigators are revving up for what might be the fight of their careers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe were always accused before Roe v Wade was overturned [of] crying wolf,\u8221\'20\'1D Northup told me on the phone from her office in Manhattan. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople don\u8217\'20\'19t need to worry about whether or not we\u8217\'20\'19re crying wolf now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There are the women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/josseli-barnica-death-miscarriage-texas-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who have died }}}\uc2  when denied abortions by healthcare providers who are unsure of the legal ramifications of performing abortions unless the mother\u8217\'20\'19s life is at risk. There are those {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/nov/04/amanda-zurawski-abortion-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who have spent days in the ICU }}}\uc2  after being denied care, and emerge with their future fertility forever compromised. There are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://idahocapitalsun.com/2024/04/05/idaho-is-losing-ob-gyns-after-strict-abortion-ban-but-health-exceptions-unlikely-this-year/#:~:text=Idaho%20%E2%80%98digging%20workforce%20hole%E2%80%99%20that%20could%20take%20decades%20to%20fill%2C%20medical%20leader%20says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the obstetricians }}}\uc2  fleeing states with strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans (over 20% of practitioners in Idaho, and over half of high-risk obstetricians), feeling that they are unable to safely, and properly, do the job they trained years to do. There are the downstream consequences of bans in restrictive states affecting states with robust \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, simply because those who can travel to receive care end up taking appointments away from local residents.\par \par \uc2 The question that kept circulating among my friends in the hours after the election results became clear was: How come seven out of 10 measures to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  passed at the state level, and Trump still won?\par \par \uc2 Northup chalks the dissonance up to two things.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a difference between what policy do I want, and what candidate do I like,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1COf course they should be linked, but we can see that they aren\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On top of that, Northup fears there are too many mental leaps to make.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost people think, You know what, if the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is protected in my state, I\u8217\'20\'19m good. They don\u8217\'20\'19t realize a federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could override their state\u8217\'20\'19s rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While she wrote in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reproductiverights.org/trump-declared-winner-of-2024-presidential-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2  after the results came in that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term \u8220\'20\'1Clead to the deaths of numerous women who are likely the tip of the iceberg\u8221\'20\'1D, she said it was too early to paint a picture of just how large that iceberg might loom in his second. Still, she underscored that even if a bill isn\u8217\'20\'19t signed into law \u8211\'20\'13 something she pointed out Trump has said he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t do, though \u8220\'20\'1Cconsistency isn\u8217\'20\'19t the hallmark of the president-elect\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 there are ways to threaten \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access at a national level.\par \par \uc2 Northup and other colleagues at the Center held an open video meeting a few hours before we spoke, the tone of which was sober, with lots of \u8220\'20\'1Cno way to sugarcoat what we\u8217\'20\'19re facing right nows\u8221\'20\'1Ds, and \u8220\'20\'1Cserious situation\u8221\'20\'1Ds and \u8220\'20\'1Ctough road ahead\u8221\'20\'1Ds.\par \par \uc2 Among her top concerns are, first, the fear that new laws will threaten patients\u8217\'20\'19 access to medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 something she calls \u8220\'20\'1Ca lifeline\u8221\'20\'1D, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/2024/03/medication-abortion-accounted-63-all-us-abortions-2023-increase-53-2020#:~:text=Medication%20Abortion%20Accounted%20for%2063,53%25%20in%202020%20%7C%20Guttmacher%20Institute"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two-thirds }}}\uc2  of patients in the US use it \u8211\'20\'13 either by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  restricting mifepristone, or states using a 1873 chastity law known as the Comstock Act, which bans \u8220\'20\'1Cany drug, medicine, article, or thing designed, adapted, or intended for producing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D from being transported by a mail carrier; and, second, the targeting of populations in states with bans. She recently found herself on the phone with a woman whose family was leaving Texas to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York, and wasn\u8217\'20\'19t sure if her husband should come with her or not.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a culture, or a climate, of fear of prosecution, and intimidation, and silencing,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt has a chilling effect.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And it\u8217\'20\'19s a chilling effect that the minority of American voters want to cast over the country. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-elections/exit-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 One exit poll }}}\uc2  noted that while voters in 10 \u8220\'20\'1Ckey states\u8221\'20\'1D believe by a wide margin that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal, only 14% considered it their most important voting issue.\par \par \uc2 I reached out to a friend who works in the \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  space for help parsing through this disconnect.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe lack of urgency that voters placed on this issue may reflect an erroneous belief that state protections can save them; misplaced faith in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s softened messaging on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; or simply a reality that many are struggling to make ends meet and feel \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an issue they can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to think about today,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CWho knows.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Whatever the reason, it means the litigators at CRR have their work cut out for them, as they fight for what the majority of Americans want.\par \par \uc2 Right now, Northup is revving up for a case that will start on Tuesday in Idaho, arguing that the state, by refusing to give stabilizing care to pregnant women in emergencies, is violating the Emergency Medical Treatment and Active Labor Act (Emtala), a federal law that ensures access to emergency care. And she is gaining strength from success stories, like Missouri, which overturned its near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban on Tuesday, despite electing Trump, something she called \u8220\'20\'1Cstunning\u8221\'20\'1D. (She remembers having a conversation with a senator in Missouri years ago, and bringing up the question of just how to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state. The senator\u8217\'20\'19s advice: \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t.\u8221\'20\'1D)\par \par \uc2 How does she feel?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CArmored up and ready to go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For those of us who might not feel that way, there are other ways to help. On the video call, one colleague offered three action items: First, take care of yourselves and your communities. Second: sign up for alerts from the Center. Finally, find and donate to a local \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access fund.\par \par \uc2 Godspeed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sophie Brickman is a contributor to the New Yorker, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and other publications, and the author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.amazon.com/Baby-Unplugged-Mothers-Balance-Digital/dp/0062966480/ref=tmm_hrd_swatch_0?_encoding=UTF8&qid=&sr="}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Baby, Unplugged: One Mother\u8217\'20\'19s Search for Balance, Reason, and Sanity in the Digital Age }}}\uc2  and the novel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.harpercollins.com/products/plays-well-with-others-sophie-brickman?variant=41223635697698"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Plays Well With Others }}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241114ekbe001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
