\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump nominates Musk and Ramaswamy to lead new efficiency department \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Philip Wen (now); Helen Sullivan, Maanvi Singh, Chris Stein, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong and Yohannes Lowe (earlier) \par \uc2 14,272 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 November 2024\par 04:09 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  handpicked by Trump to carry out slash-and-burn cuts planTrump picks Huckabee as Israel envoy and taps Fox News host for PentagonTrump\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet picks and likely contenders so far\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 This blog has now closed. Thanks for reading.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here is a summary of the latest developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and former Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  will lead the newly created Department of Government Efficiency, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said on Tuesday. Despite the name, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/trump-appoints-elon-musk-government-efficiency-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the department will not be a government agency }}}\uc2 . Trump said the pair will work from outside the government to offer the White House \u8220\'20\'1Cadvice and guidance\u8221\'20\'1D and will partner with the Office of Management and Budget to \u8220\'20\'1Cdrive large scale structural reform, and create an entrepreneurial approach to government never seen before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has tapped Fox News host {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/trump-appoints-mike-huckabee-ambassador-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pete Hegseth to be secretary of defense }}}\uc2 . Hegseth, 44, is a co-host of \u8220\'20\'1CFox & Friends Weekend\u8221\'20\'1D and has been a contributor with the network since 2014, where he developed a friendship with Trump, who made regular appearances on the show.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has confirmed that he has chosen South Dakota governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kristi-noem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kristi Noem }}}\uc2 , to serve as the next secretary of the homeland security department. The choice was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/kristi-noem-homeland-security-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 widely reported yesterday }}}\uc2 , but not yet announced by Trump.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration said Tuesday it won\u8217\'20\'19t limit weapons transfers to Israel because the US says its key ally has made good but limited progress in increasing the flow of humanitarian aid to Gaza. That is despite eight international aid groups saying Israel has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/12/aid-groups-accuse-israel-of-ignoring-us-ultimatum-on-apocalyptic-gaza-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to meet US demands for greater humanitarian access }}}\uc2  to the war-ravaged Gaza Strip, where hunger experts say the north may already be experiencing famine.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  named the former Arkansas governor \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2  as the next US ambassador to Israel. Huckabee has a track record of hardline, occasionally provocative, pro-Israel rhetoric and previously said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel }}}\uc2  has a rightful claim to the West Bank, which he refers to by its Hebrew and biblical name of Judea and Samaria.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump chose a real-estate mogul as Middle East envoy. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has picked Steven Witkoff, a New York City-based real estate executive and longtime friend, to serve as Middle East envoy in his upcoming administration.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-67337b9b8f081746a2e89efd#block-67337b9b8f081746a2e89efd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will reportedly oppose }}}\uc2  a US law that could lead to popular social media app TikTok being banned, despite bipartisan support for the measure.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin Republican \uc2 Eric Hovde\uc2  refused to concede defeat on Tuesday to Democratic incumbent \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  in their \uc2 US Senate\uc2  race, saying he was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply concerned\u8221\'20\'1D about the election results but that seeking a recount was a \u8220\'20\'1Cserious\u8221\'20\'1D decision and he was still reviewing his options, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The judge who presided over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hush money case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-67336df48f08a71aa0e1f978#block-67336df48f08a71aa0e1f978"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has paused }}}\uc2  legal proceedings at the request of prosecutors and the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys, both of whom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673370ba8f081746a2e89e5a#block-673370ba8f081746a2e89e5a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointed to }}}\uc2  his victory in last week\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , a long-serving conservative justice on the supreme court, has no plans to step down, the Wall Street Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-67336a938f081746a2e89dc2#block-67336a938f081746a2e89dc2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2 . If he changes his mind, Trump and the Republican-controlled Senate could confirm a replacement and likely prolong the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative supermajority.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  has been posting busily on X, even by his own standards, in the hours after president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced he will head up the newly created government efficiency department.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/1856520760656797801"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Posting on X }}}\uc2 , which the billionaire owns, Musk pledged to document all actions of the department online for \u8220\'20\'1Cmaximum transparency\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnytime the public thinks we are cutting something important or not cutting something wasteful, just let us know!\u8221\'20\'1D he said, while also promise to keep \u8220\'20\'1Ca leaderboard for most insanely dumb spending of your tax dollars\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has also called the race in Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s 8th congressional district for Republican Gabe Evans. Evans flipped the seat north of Denver for the Republicans, defeating Democratic incumbent Yadira Caraveo in one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most-watched races.\par \par \uc2 The toss-up race for Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s 8th congressional district, which was created after redistricting in 2020, was a crucial part to Republican\u8217\'20\'19s goal of retaining control of the House. It also tested Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 and Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 appeal to Latinos, who make up nearly 40% of the district\u8217\'20\'19s population.\par \par \uc2 The AP\u8217\'20\'19s tally now has the Republicans on 216 seats, just two shy of the 218 needed to secure control of the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have already secured a majority in the 100-member US senate, though it is shy of the 60-vote threshold needed to advance most legislation in that chamber. That means Democrats will retain some leverage in Washington next year even if Republicans win the House majority.\par \par \uc2 But keeping hold of the House would give Republicans sweeping powers to potentially push through a broad agenda of tax and spending cuts, energy deregulation and border security controls.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/11/progressive-caucus-democrats-populist-economic-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US progressives urge Democrats to back populist policies as party reels from loss }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican David Valadao has won reelection in California\u8217\'20\'19s 22nd congressional district, Associated Press reports, defeating Democrat Rudy Salas for the second time. Valadao is an anomaly \u8211\'20\'13 an elected Republican in a heavily Democratic district in a heavily Democratic state.\par \par \uc2 Democrats hold a 14-point registration edge in the Central Valley district, but Valadao has kept a grip on the seat nonetheless. Valadao held the seat from 2013 until 2019, lost it for a term, then won it back in a 2020 rematch with Democrat TJ Cox. Valadao stressed his efforts to secure more water for farmers and his willingness to work across the aisle, while painting Salas as a tax-and-spend Democrat.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 Who is \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , Trump's nomination for the department of homeland security?\par \par \uc2 As we reported earlier, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has selected South Dakota Gover \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  to head the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , one of the biggest government agencies that will be integral to his vow to secure the border and carry out a massive deportation operation.\par \par \uc2 The 52-year-old was born in Watertown, South Dakota, and raised on a ranch and farm outside the city. Her father died in a grain-bin collapse at the age of 49.\par \par \uc2 She was involved in a number of family businesses before successfully running for the South Dakota House of Representatives in 2006. In 2010, she won the state\u8217\'20\'19s at-large House seat, and in 2018, she was elected the state\u8217\'20\'19s first female governor. She was reelected in 2022.\par \par \uc2 After becoming governor, Noem started working closely with \uc2 Corey Lewandowski\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 campaign manager. Then, during the pandemic, she rose to prominence in conservative circles for resisting most government regulations to slow the spread of infections. She has since become a regular presence in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s political world and at one point was considered to be his running mate.\par \par \uc2 She was criticised this year for a story she told in her book about killing her 14-month-old wirehaired pointer named Cricket.\par \par \uc2 Noem has been a key Trump supporter, including backing his tough immigration talk.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump will deport the most dangerous illegal aliens first \u8211\'20\'13 the murderers, rapists, and other criminals that Harris and Biden let into the country. They do not belong here, and we will not let them back in,\u8221\'20\'1D Noem said in a post on X after Trump was elected.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is our full story on Trump selecting \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  to lead his efficiency department:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/trump-appoints-elon-musk-government-efficiency-department"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump selects Elon Musk to lead government efficiency department }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , president-elect of the US, announced on Tuesday that he has selected \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man, and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  to lead the Department of Government Efficiency, with plans to reduce bureaucracy in the federal government by roughly a third.\par \par \uc2 Musk had pushed for a government efficiency department and has since relentlessly promoted it, emphasizing the acronym for the agency: Doge, a reference {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/doge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to a meme }}}\uc2  of an expressive Shiba Inu. Trump said the agency will be conducting a \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplete financial and performance audit of the entire federal government, and making recommendations for drastic reforms\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CollinRugg/status/1854716187512651808"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video posted on X }}}\uc2  two days after the election, Trump said he would \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediately re-issue my 2020 executive order, restoring the president\u8217\'20\'19s authority to remove rogue bureaucrats\u8221\'20\'1D. He wants to \u8220\'20\'1Cclean out the deep state\u8221\'20\'1D. His promises echo his slogan on The Apprentice: \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re fired!\u8221\'20\'1D And {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/25/project-2025-trump-plan-fire-civil-service-employees"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025 }}}\uc2 , an influential and controversial blueprint for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second term, lays out ways to make bureaucrats fireable.\par \par \uc2 Musk has extensive experience slashing corporate spending, and he has promised to cull federal payrolls in much the same way. He cut staff at X, formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , by 80% after buying it in 2022, a move he said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-12-21/musk-says-cost-cutting-averted-3-billion-twitter-shortfall?sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prevented a $3bn shortfall }}}\uc2 , but which has not otherwise paid off. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/27/technology/linda-yaccarino-x-ceo-elon-musk.html#:~:text=Internal%20documents%20obtained%20by%20The,decline%20from%20the%20previous%20year."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Revenue is in steep decline }}}\uc2  and advertisers have absconded, making a comeback seem unlikely. As the CEO of \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , however, he has garnered a reputation for launching rockets more cheaply than competitors by negotiating with suppliers and keeping operations lean.\par \par \uc2 The billionaire does not seem to be under any illusions of what will happen after his proposed cuts, admitting that reducing spending \u8220\'20\'1Cnecessarily involves some temporary hardship\u8221\'20\'1D. Americans do want to spend less \u8211\'20\'13 of their own money. Do they want austerity and less financial assistance from the federal government? Do they want the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest person admonishing them to cut their expenses?\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/trump-elon-musk-vivek-ramaswamy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump handpicks key ally Elon to carry out slash-and-burn cuts plan }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 A senior adviser to US president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has fuelled speculation about the future of Australia\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to Washington, former prime minister {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/kevin-rudd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kevin Rudd }}}\uc2 , by reposting Rudd\u8217\'20\'19s congratulatory statement to Trump on social media with a gif of an hourglass.\par \par \uc2 The provocative time-is-running-out post by former Trump deputy chief of staff for communications Dan Scavino reignited suggestions that the incoming president may prefer another Australian representative in Washington when he takes office in January.\par \par \uc2 Scavino spoke at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s now-infamous Madison Square Garden rally in New York ahead of the election and was billed as a \u8220\'20\'1Csenior adviser\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A new video emerged earlier this week of Rudd in an interview in 2021 describing Trump as \u8220\'20\'1Ca village idiot\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a leading intellectual force\u8221\'20\'1D. Rudd last week \u8211\'20\'13 following the US election \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/as-rudd-scrubs-social-media-posts-albanese-to-advocate-free-trade-and-climate-action-with-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deleted old social media posts criticising Trump }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/13/kevin-rudd-australia-us-ambassador-trump-adviser-hourglass-post-dan-scavino-abbott-dutton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senior Trump adviser suggests Rudd\u8217\'20\'19s time as US ambassador could be up with hourglass gif }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 How will the efficiency department operate \u8211\'20\'13 and is Trump required to disclose conflicts of interest?\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear how the new efficiency department will operate. The Associated Press reports that it could come under the Federal Advisory Committee Act, which dictates how external groups that advise the government must operate and be accountable to the public.\par \par \uc2 Federal employees are generally required to disclose their assets and entanglements to ward off any potential conflicts of interest, and to divest significant holdings relating to their work. Because Musk and Ramaswamy would not be formal federal workers, they would not face those requirements or ethical limitations.\par \par \uc2 The president-elect has often said he would give Musk a formal role overseeing a group akin to a blue-ribbon commission that would recommend ways to slash spending and make the federal government more efficient. Musk at one point suggested he could find more than $2tn in savings \u8211\'20\'13 nearly a third of total annual government spending.\par \par \uc2 Trump had made clear that Musk would likely not hold any kind of full-time position, given his other commitments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think I can get him full-time because he\u8217\'20\'19s a little bit busy sending rockets up and all the things he does,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said at a rally in Michigan in September.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe said the waste in this country is crazy. And we\u8217\'20\'19re going to get \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  to be our cost cutter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy suspended his campaign in January and threw his support behind Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  have responded to the announcement on X, the social media platform owned by Musk.\par \par \uc2 Ramaswamy said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe will not go gently, @elonmusk\u8221\'20\'1D and added an American flag emoji.\par \par \uc2 Musk said, \u8220\'20\'1CThreat to democracy? Nope, threat to BUREAUCRACY!!!\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 Musk and Ramaswamy to lead Department of Government Efficiency: what we know\par \par \uc2 Here is what we know about the new Department of Government Efficiency, and the two men Trump has chosen to lead it:\par \par \uc2 Trump said on Tuesday \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and former Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  will lead the newly created Department of Government Efficiency.\par \par \uc2 Musk and Ramaswamy \u8220\'20\'1Cwill pave the way for my Administration to dismantle Government Bureaucracy, slash excess regulations, cut wasteful expenditures, and restructure Federal Agencies,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said their work would conclude by 4 July 2026, adding that a smaller and more efficient government would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cgift\u8221\'20\'1D to the country on the 250th anniversary of the signing of the Declaration of Independence.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The appointments reward two Trump supporters from the private sector. Musk leads electric car company \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , social media platform X and rocket company \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , while Ramaswamy is the founder of a pharmaceutical company who ran for the Republican presidential nomination against Trump and then threw his support behind the former president after dropping out.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Musk gave millions of dollars to support Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign and made public appearances with him. Trump had said he would offer Musk, the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest person, a role in his administration promoting government efficiency.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The acronym of the new department \u8211\'20\'13 DOGE \u8211\'20\'13 coincides with the name of the cryptocurrency Dogecoin that Musk promotes, and the internet meme after which the cryptocurrency is named.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will send shock waves through the system, and anyone involved in government waste, which is a lot of people!\u8221\'20\'1D Musk said, according to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s statement, which called the new government initiative \u8220\'20\'1Cpotentially \u8216\'20\'18The Manhattan Project\u8217\'20\'19 of our time,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to the US plan to build the atomic bomb that helped end the second world war.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Who is John Ratcliffe, Trump's pick for CIA director?\par \par \uc2 John Ratcliffe served as director of national intelligence (DNI) for the final months of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, leading the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s spy agencies during the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 His position as DNI also made him responsible for detecting and countering foreign efforts to interfere in American politics. That experience makes him a more traditional pick for the job, which requires Senate confirmation, than some rumored loyalists pushed by some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters.\par \par \uc2 As DNI, Ratcliffe participated in an unusual night-time news conference just weeks before the 2020 presidential election in which he and other officials accused Iran of being responsible for a barrage of emails meant to intimidate voters in the US.\par \par \uc2 Also while in that role, Ratcliffe faced criticism for declassifying Russian intelligence that purported to reveal information about Democrats during the 2016 election even as he acknowledged it might not be true. Democrats decried the move as a partisan stunt that politicized intelligence.\par \par \uc2 Ratcliffe was elected to Congress in 2014, but his visibility rose in 2019 as an ardent defender of Trump during the House\u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment proceedings against him.\par \par \uc2 He was a member of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s impeachment advisory team and strenuously questioned witnesses during the impeachment hearings.\par \par \uc2 When former special counsel \uc2 Robert Mueller\uc2  appeared before the House judiciary ommittee to testify about his investigation into Russian interference in the 2016 election, Ratcliffe was one of the more ardent Republican interrogators, forcefully questioning the prosecutor and blasting the report he produced.\par \par \uc2 Ratcliffe has repeatedly sounded the alarm about China, calling the country the top threat to US interests and the rest of the free world.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has called the race for Democrat \uc2 George Whitesides\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former Nasa chief of staff, who had the support of national Democrats, has won a tough race to unseat Republican incumbent represenative Mike Garcia in California\u8217\'20\'19s 27 congressional district.\par \par \uc2 As we reported earlier, Garcia conceded on Monday, saying he had congratulated Whitesides and would ensure a smooth handoff.\par \par \uc2 Whitesides said on Monday in a statement that he had spoken with Garcia and thanked him for his service to the district and the nation. He said he would fight in Congress for good jobs and lower household costs.\par \par \uc2 Whitesides, who is also a former CEO of Virgin Galactic, said during the campaign that he would use his business experience to solve problems. He spotlighted Garcia\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, calling him an extremist.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Some background: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk }}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s super political action committee (Pac) spent about $200m to help elect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  to a second presidency, according to a person familiar with the group\u8217\'20\'19s spending, funding an effort that set a new standard for how billionaires can influence elections.\par \par \uc2 The billionaire chief executive officer of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/tesla"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tesla }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/spacex"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SpaceX }}}\uc2  provided the vast majority of the money to America Pac, which focused on low-propensity and first-time voters, according to the Associated Press source, who was not authorized to disclose the figure publicly and spoke on condition of anonymity. In turn, as CNBC reported, Musk\u8217\'20\'19s net worth jumped $70bn since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump }}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/elon-musk-america-pac-donald-trump-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s Super Pac spent $200m to help elect Donald Trump }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man, whose companies have billions of dollars of federal contracts, has been a constant presence at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago estate this week. Some see Musk as the second-most influential figure in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s immediate orbit after his campaign chief-turned-incoming chief of staff, Susie Wiles.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1CDepartment of Government Efficiency\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 essentially an independent advisory panel \u8211\'20\'13 that Musk will help lead, is intended to \u8220\'20\'1Cdrive out the massive waste and fraud\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will send shockwaves through the system,\u8221\'20\'1D said a statement from Musk.\par \par \uc2 As we reported, \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , a biotech entrepreneur who ran for president himself, is helping Musk lead the department.\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to return to public view on Wednesday, when he goes to the White House to meet with President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and visits Capitol Hill to consult with House speaker Mike Johnson and Republican legislators. Overall, Trump is laying the groundwork for his second presidency at a much faster clip than his first.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 Who is Pete Hegseth, Trump's nominee for secretary of defense?\par \par \uc2 More now on Pete Hegseth, the Fox News host Trump has just announced as his nominee for secretary of defense, via the Associated Press:\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s selection of Hegseth, who lacks senior military or national security experience, was sure to draw questions about his qualifications to lead the department.\par \par \uc2 Hegseth, 44, is a co-host of Fox News Channel\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CFox & Friends Weekend\u8221\'20\'1D and has been a contributor with the network since 2014, where he developed a friendship with Trump, who made regular appearances on the show.\par \par \uc2 If confirmed by the Senate, he would inherit the top job during a series of global crises \u8212\'20\'14 ranging from Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine and the ongoing attacks in the Middle East by Iranian proxies to the push for a cease-fire between Israel, \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  and escalating worries about the growing alliance between Russia and North Korea.\par \par \uc2 Hegseth is also the author of \u8220\'20\'1CThe War on Warriors: Behind the Betrayal of the Men Who Keep Us Free,\u8221\'20\'1D published earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 The book, according to its promo, combines \u8220\'20\'1Chis own war experiences, tales of outrage, and an incisive look at how the chain of command got so kinked,\u8221\'20\'1D and bills itself as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe key to saving our warriors \u8212\'20\'14 and winning future wars.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 While the Pentagon is considered a key coveted post in any administration, the defense secretary was a tumultuous post during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term. Five men held the job during his four years only to resign, be fired or serve briefly as a stopgap. Just two of them were actually confirmed by the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with his civilian and military leaders during those years was fraught with tension, confusion and frustration, as they struggled to temper or even simply interpret presidential tweets and pronouncements that blindsided them with abrupt policy decisions they weren\u8217\'20\'19t prepared to explain or defend. Many of the generals who worked in his first administration \u8212\'20\'14 both on active duty and retired \u8212\'20\'14 have slammed him as unfit to serve in the Oval Office and he has condemned them in return.\par \par \uc2 Hegseth was an infantry captain in the Army National Guard and served overseas in Afghanistan, Iraq and Guantanamo Bay, Cuba. He was formerly head of the Concerned Veterans for America, a group backed by conservative billionaires Charles and \uc2 David Koch\uc2 , and he unsuccessfully ran for the Senate in Minnesota in 2012.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith Pete at the helm, America\u8217\'20\'19s enemies are on notice \u8212\'20\'14 Our Military will be Great Again, and America will Never Back Down,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CNobody fights harder for the Troops, and Pete will be a courageous and patriotic champion of our \u8216\'20\'18Peace through Strength\u8217\'20\'19 policy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Hegseth has \u8220\'20\'1Can excellent background as a junior officer but does not have the senior national security experience that secretaries need,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mark Cancian, a senior advisor at the Center for Strategic and International Studies. \u8220\'20\'1CI think Trump was tired of fighting with his secretaries of defense and picked one who would be loyal to him.\u8221\'20\'1D Cancian said the lack of experience might make it more difficult for Hegseth to get through Senate confirmation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump confirms \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  as pick for \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\par \par \uc2 Trump has confirmed that he has chosen South Dakota governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kristi-noem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kristi Noem }}}\uc2 , to serve as the next secretary of the homeland security department. The choice was widely reported yesterday, but not yet announced by Trump.\par \par \uc2 In his statement, Trump says:\par \par \uc2 I am pleased to announce that the Governor and former congresswoman from South Dakota, \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , will be appointed to serve as the Secretary of the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  (DHS).\par \par \uc2 Kristi has been very strong on Border Security. She was the first Governor to send National Guard Soldiers to help Texas fight the Biden Border Crisis, and they were sent a total of eight times.\par \par \uc2 She will work closely with \u8220\'20\'1CBorder Czar\u8221\'20\'1D Tom Homan to secure the Border, and will guarantee that our American Homeland is secure from our adversaries. I have known Kristi for years, and have worked with her on a wide variety of projects - She will be a great part of our mission to Make America Safe Again.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump, in his statement, lays out a vision of the department as \u8220\'20\'1Cpotentially \u8216\'20\'18The Manhattan Project\u8217\'20\'19 of our time\u8221\'20\'1D. The Manhattan Project was the second world war research program that developed nuclear weapons. Only this one is named after an internet meme and type of cryptocurrency.\par \par \uc2 Here is more from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s statement:\par \par \uc2 It will become, potentially, \u8216\'20\'18The Manhattan Project\u8217\'20\'19of our time. Republican politicians have dreamed about the objectives of \u8220\'20\'1CDOGE\u8221\'20\'1D for a very long time. To drive this kind of drastic change, the Department of Government Efficiency will provide advice and guidance from outside of Government, and will partner with the White House and Office of Management & Budget to drive large scale structural reform, and create an entrepreneurial approach to Government never seen before.\par \par \uc2 I look forward to Elon and Vivek making changes to the Federal Bureaucracy with an eye on efficiency and, at the same time, making life better for all Americans. Importantly, we will drive out the massive waste and fraud which exists throughout our annual $6.5 Trillion Dollars of Government Spending. They will work together to liberate our Economy, and make the \uc2 U.S. Government\uc2  accountable to \u8220\'20\'1CWE THE PEOPLE.\u8221\'20\'1D Their work will conclude no later than July 4, 2026 - A smaller Government, with more efficiency and less bureaucracy, will be the perfect gift to America on the 250th Anniversary of The Declaration of Independence. I am confident they will succeed!\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump announces \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  as heads of Department of Government Efficiency\par \par \uc2 Trump has announced that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  will lead the Department of Government Efficiency.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Trump said:\par \par \uc2 I am pleased to announce that the Great \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , working in conjunction with American Patriot \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2 , will lead the Department of Government Efficiency (\u8220\'20\'1CDOGE\u8221\'20\'1D). Together, these two wonderful Americans will pave the way for my Administration to dismantle Government Bureaucracy, slash excess regulations, cut wasteful expenditures, and restructure Federal Agencies \u8211\'20\'13 Essential to the \u8220\'20\'1CSave America\u8221\'20\'1D Movement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis will send shockwaves through the system, and anyone involved in Government waste, which is a lot of people!\u8221\'20\'1D Musk said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is a bit more on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Pentagon pick:\par \par \uc2 Pete Hegseth, 44, is a co-host of Fox News Channel\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CFox & Friends Weekend\u8221\'20\'1D and has been a contributor with the network since 2014, where he developed a friendship with Trump, who made regular appearances on the show. He is also the author of The War on Warriors: Behind the Betrayal of the Men Who Keep Us Free.\par \par \uc2 Hegseth was an infantry captain in the Army National Guard and served overseas in Afghanistan, Iraq and Guant\u225\'00\'E1namo Bay, Cuba.\par \par \uc2 He was formerly head of the Concerned Veterans for America, a group backed by conservative billionaires Charles and \uc2 David Koch\uc2 , and he unsuccessfully ran for the Senate in Minnesota in 2012.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Hegseth deployed to Iraq and Afghanistan and unsuccessfully ran for Senate in Minnesota in 2012 before joining Fox News.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump chooses Fox News host Pete Hegseth as secretary of defense\par \par \uc2 Trump has just announced another cabinet pick: Pete Hegseth as secretary of defense.\par \par \uc2 Hegseth is a Fox news host. We\u8217\'20\'19ll have information shortly.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, he says:\par \par \uc2 I am honored to announce that I have nominated Pete Hegseth to serve in my Cabinet as The Secretary of Defense. Pete has spent his entire life as a Warrior for the Troops, and for the Country. Pete is tough, smart and a true believer in America First. With Pete at the helm, America\u8217\'20\'19s enemies are on notice - Our Military will be Great Again, and America will Never Back Down.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 A pregnant woman in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kentucky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky }}}\uc2  seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  filed a lawsuit on Tuesday asking a court to strike down the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 The woman, who is known in court records as Mary Poe and is about seven or eight weeks pregnant, is challenging Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and the six-week ban simultaneously in effect. These bans, Poe argues, violate the Kentucky constitution\u8217\'20\'19s rights to privacy and self-determination and should not be enforced.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor many individuals, the bans altogether foreclose the ability to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , thus forcing them to carry their pregnancies to term and give birth, which carries a risk of death up to 14 times higher than that associated with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawsuit alleges. \u8220\'20\'1COthers, pushed by the bans to travel out of state for legal care, bear the burdens both of increased health risks from being pushed later into pregnancy and of the cost and logistical difficulties of long-distance travel.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit also requests class-action status for all people who may be pregnant or can become so but are unable to get a \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel overwhelmed and frustrated that I cannot access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care here in my own state, and I have started the difficult process of arranging to get care in another state where it\u8217\'20\'19s legal,\u8221\'20\'1D Poe said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThis involves trying to take time off work and securing child care, all of which place an enormous burden on me. This is my personal decision, a decision I believe should be mine alone, not one made by anyone else.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 , the ACLU of Kentucky, and the law firm Kaplan, Johnson, Abate & Bird are representing Poe.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/12/kentucky-abortion-ban-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kentucky woman seeking \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  files lawsuit challenging state\u8217\'20\'19s bans }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 After spending four months in federal prison for snubbing a congressional subpoena, conservative strategist \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  has spoken to media outside a New York court where he\u8217\'20\'19s facing a state conspiracy trial as soon as next month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou wait. The hunted are about to become the hunters,\u8221\'20\'1D Bannon said, according to the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 He stepped into a waiting car without elaborating on what \u8220\'20\'1Cthe hunters\u8221\'20\'1D intend to do.\par \par \uc2 The longtime Trump ally\u8217\'20\'19s latest trial is scheduled to start 9 December \u8211\'20\'13 but could be postponed after a hearing Monday \u8211\'20\'13 at the same Manhattan courthouse where the past-and-next president was convicted in his hush-money case. Separately, a judge Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/trump-hush-money-conviction-presidential-immunity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delayed a key ruling }}}\uc2  in the hush-money case for at least a week as prosecutors ponder how to proceed in light of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s impending presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump has spent most of his first week as president-elect behind closed doors at Mar-a-Lago, his private club in Florida, where he\u8217\'20\'19s working the phones, reconnecting with foreign leaders and building his new administration, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Trump is hardly in seclusion. He\u8217\'20\'19s surrounded by advisers, friends and paying members of his club, who weigh in with advice as he selects people for top government jobs. \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man, whose companies have billions of dollars of federal contracts, has been a constant presence. Some see Musk as the second-most influential figure in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s immediate orbit after his campaign chief-turned-incoming chief of staff, Susie Wiles.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVery productive day of work by the transition team,\u8221\'20\'1D Musk posted on X, his social media company, on Monday evening.\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to return to public view on Wednesday, when he goes to the White House to meet with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and visits Capitol Hill to consult with House speaker Mike Johnson and Republican legislators. Overall, Trump is laying the groundwork for his second presidency at a much faster clip than his first.\par \par \uc2 Trump is also expected to meet with Republicans on Capitol Hill as they prepare for his day one priorities in a potentially unified government with a sweep of GOP power in Washington.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden won't limit US weapons transfers to Israel\par \par \uc2 Eight international aid groups said on Tuesday that Israel has failed to meet US demands for greater humanitarian access to the war-ravaged Gaza Strip, where hunger experts say the north may already be experiencing famine, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 However, the Biden administration said Tuesday it won\u8217\'20\'19t limit weapons transfers to Israel because the US says its key ally has made good but limited progress in increasing the flow of humanitarian aid to Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Washington told Israel to boost aid to Gaza within 30 days, or else it could trigger US laws requiring it to scale back American military support as Israel wages war against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in Gaza and \uc2 Hezbollah in Lebanon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Israeli strikes killed at least 46 people in Gaza in the past 24 hours, and killed at least 33 people in Lebanon, local health officials said Tuesday. Two people in northern Israel also died from rockets fired from Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s relentless bombardment of Gaza has killed more than 43,000 people, Palestinian health officials say. More than half of those killed were women and children.\par \par \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  began firing into Israel on 8 October 2023, in solidarity with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in Gaza. Since then, more than 3,200 people have been killed in Lebanon and more than 14,200 wounded, the country\u8217\'20\'19s health ministry reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hovde pointed to what he claimed were irregularities with the vote results. There is no evidence of any wrongdoing in the election, the results of which are still being reviewed by counties before they submit the canvassed totals to the state by 19 November for certification by 1 December.\par \par \uc2 Democrats, and even some Republicans, immediately called out Hovde for what they said was a perpetuation of lies about the integrity of the election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStop trying to erode trust in our elections (and I say that as someone who supported Hovde),\u8221\'20\'1D said Jim Villa, a longtime Republican who previously worked in the legislature and Milwaukee county executive\u8217\'20\'19s office under Scott Walker before Walker became governor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat grift needs to stop!\u8221\'20\'1D Villa posted on X.\par \par \uc2 Baldwin campaign spokesperson Andrew Mamo accused Hovde of \u8220\'20\'1Csowing doubt about our very democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLeaders on both sides of the aisle should condemn the lies he\u8217\'20\'19s spreading and the pathetic campaign he continues to run,\u8221\'20\'1D Mamo said. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  has won this race and there is only one thing for \uc2 Eric Hovde\uc2  to do: concede.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin Republican \uc2 Eric Hovde\uc2  refuses to concede to Democrat \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  in Senate race\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin Republican \uc2 Eric Hovde\uc2  refused to concede defeat on Tuesday to Democratic incumbent \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  in their \uc2 US Senate\uc2  race, saying he was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply concerned\u8221\'20\'1D about the election results but that seeking a recount was a \u8220\'20\'1Cserious\u8221\'20\'1D decision and he was still reviewing his options, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Hovde can request a recount because his margin of defeat was less than 1 percentage point, at about 29,000 votes. But he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t said yet whether he will request one, explaining in a video directed at his supporters that he wants to review all of the information and options that are available.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a difficult decision because I want to honor your support and, at the same time, bring closure to this election for our state,\u8221\'20\'1D Hovde said in the video posted on X.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Here is a summary of the key recent developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The judge who presided over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hush money case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-67336df48f08a71aa0e1f978#block-67336df48f08a71aa0e1f978"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has paused }}}\uc2  legal proceedings at the request of prosecutors and the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys, both of whom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673370ba8f081746a2e89e5a#block-673370ba8f081746a2e89e5a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointed to }}}\uc2  his victory in last week\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans are getting ready for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s visit to the White House, with House speaker Mike Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673377218f081746a2e89eba#block-673377218f081746a2e89eba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying }}}\uc2  he planned to have Trump address his lawmakers. Speaking of Congress, we still do not know for sure which party will control the House for the next two years. Counting of ballots in key races {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673362028f08a71aa0e1f8d5#block-673362028f08a71aa0e1f8d5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remains ongoing }}}\uc2 , though Republicans seem on track to keep their majority.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , a long-serving conservative justice on the supreme court, has no plans to step down, the Wall Street Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-67336a938f081746a2e89dc2#block-67336a938f081746a2e89dc2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2 . If he changes his mind, Trump and the Republican-controlled Senate could confirm a replacement and likely prolong the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative supermajority.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-67337b9b8f081746a2e89efd#block-67337b9b8f081746a2e89efd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will reportedly oppose }}}\uc2  a US law that could lead to popular social media app TikTok being banned, despite bipartisan support for the measure.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Despite taking office with Republicans in control of Congress in 2017, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first years in office were marked by legislative chaos. Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673380558f081746a2e89f6b#block-673380558f081746a2e89f6b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed that won\u8217\'20\'19t happen again }}}\uc2  when Trump returns to the White House in January.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump chose an ex-national intelligence chief as CIA director. Trump has named John Ratcliffe, who served as the director of national intelligence during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, as his pick for CIA director, and William Joseph McGinley, who served as cabinet secretary in the first term, to serve as White House counsel.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump chose a real-estate mogul as Middle East envoy. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has picked Steven Witkoff, a New York City-based real estate executive and longtime friend, to serve as Middle East envoy in his upcoming administration.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump announced that he will nominate \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 , the former governor of Arkansas, to be the US ambassador to Israel. Huckabee \u8220\'20\'1Cloves Israel, and the people of Israel, and likewise, the people of Israel love him,\u8221\'20\'1D the president-elect said in a statement on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump advisers mulling a \u8216\'20\'18warrior board\u8217\'20\'19 to organize purge of top military officers \u8211\'20\'13 report. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s transition team is working on an executive order that would create a new body tasked with naming military leaders who should be demoted, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/national-security/trump-draft-executive-order-would-create-board-to-purge-generals-7ebaa606?st=Phr48B&reflink=article_copyURL_share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Wall Street Journal reports }}}\uc2 . The reported proposal for a \u8220\'20\'1Cwarrior board\u8221\'20\'1D staffed by former military officers loyal to the president-elect is the latest sign that Trump may make due on his threat to retaliate against leaders at all levels of government who have broken with him, or who are perceived as disloyal.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump issued a statement announcing his appointment of Mike Waltz to serve in his cabinet as the national security adviser. Waltz \u8220\'20\'1Chas been a strong champion of my America First Foreign Policy agenda, and will be a tremendous champion of our pursuit of Peace through Strength!\u8221\'20\'1D the president-elect said in a statement on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump chooses ex-national intelligence chief as CIA director\par \par \uc2 Trump has also named John Ratcliffe, who served as the director of national intelligence during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, as his pick for CIA director, and William Joseph McGinley, who served as cabinet secretary in the first term, to serve as White House counsel.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump picks real-estate mogul as Middle East envoy\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has picked Steven Witkoff, a New York City-based real estate executive and longtime friend, to serve as Middle East envoy in his upcoming administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSteve is a Highly Respected Leader in Business and Philanthropy, who has made every project and community he has been involved with stronger and more prosperous,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement announcing the appointment. \u8220\'20\'1CSteve will be an unrelenting Voice for PEACE, and make us all proud.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Witkoff has longtime ties to Trump and the Trump organization, serving as a major donor and as an adviser. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courthousenews.com/trumps-longtime-buddy-testifies-as-defense-expert-in-manhattan-fraud-case/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 testified }}}\uc2  as an expert witness in the New York attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s case against the Trump family and its namesake business.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet picks and likely contenders \u8211\'20\'13 so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has tasked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/10/howard-lutnick-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Howard Lutnick }}}\uc2 , a longtime friend, with recruiting officials who will deliver, rather than dilute, his agenda. During his first term, several of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s key appointees tried to convince Trump out of his more extreme plans.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at those who have been and could be offered key positions when Trump takes office:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/pompeo-kennedy-and-musk-who-could-be-in-trumps-new-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cabinet picks and likely contenders \u8211\'20\'13 so far }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The House is scheduled to vote today on a bill targeting non-profit organizations deemed to be supporting \u8220\'20\'1Cterrorism\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Civil rights advocates have raised alarm that bill, which was first introduced in response to nationwide protests on college campuses against Israel\u8217\'20\'19s bombardment of Gaza, could be used against pro-Palestinian groups as well as those that environmental groups, \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups and other human rights organizations during the upcoming Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 The language in the bill would give the Treasury Department broad authority to determine which organizations are \u8220\'20\'1Cterrorist-supporting\u8221\'20\'1D without requiring evidence, and allow the agency to revoke tax-exempt status from those non-profits.\par \par \uc2 Republicans drafted the policy as part of a popular measure to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2024/09/14/congress-irs-penalties-us-hostages/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prevent the IRS from issuing fines and tax penalties }}}\uc2  to Americans held hostage by terrorist groups. The measure, which is being fast-tracked in the House, would need a two-thirds majority in the Senate to pass.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis bill requires no oversight. No due-process. No justification. In Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hands, it would be a weapon of mass destruction against dissent,\u8221\'20\'1D said Andrew O\u8217\'20\'19Neill, legislative director of the group Indivisible. \u8220\'20\'1CThe vote today requires a two-thirds threshold to pass, so Democrats really do have agency here. The question is whether they\u8217\'20\'19ll use it to stand up against authoritarian overreach, or if they\u8217\'20\'19ll sit back and hand Trump more power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPassing this bill would hand the incoming Trump administration a dangerous new tool it could use to stifle free speech, target political opponents, and punish disfavored groups,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kia Hamadanchy, senior policy counsel at \uc2 ACLU\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThe freedom to dissent without fear of government retribution is a vital part of any well-functioning democracy, which is why Congress must block HR 9495 before it\u8217\'20\'19s too late.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump advisers mulling 'warrior board' to organize purge of top military officers \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s transition team is working on an executive order that would create a new body tasked with naming military leaders who should be demoted, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/national-security/trump-draft-executive-order-would-create-board-to-purge-generals-7ebaa606?st=Phr48B&reflink=article_copyURL_share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Wall Street Journal reports }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The reported proposal for a \u8220\'20\'1Cwarrior board\u8221\'20\'1D staffed by former military officers loyal to the president-elect is the latest sign that Trump may make due on his threat to retaliate against leaders at all levels of government who have broken with him, or who are perceived as disloyal.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the proposal, from the Journal:\par \par \uc2 If {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  approves the order, it could fast-track the removal of generals and admirals found to be \u8220\'20\'1Clacking in requisite leadership qualities,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a draft of the order reviewed by The Wall Street Journal. But it could also create a chilling effect on top military officers, given the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s past vow to fire \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke generals,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to officers seen as promoting diversity in the ranks at the expense of military readiness.\par \par \uc2 As commander in chief, Trump can fire any officer at will, but an outside board whose members he appoints would bypass the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s regular promotion system, signaling across the military that he intends to purge a number of generals and admirals.\par \par \uc2 The draft order says it aims to establish a review that focuses \u8220\'20\'1Con leadership capability, strategic readiness, and commitment to military excellence.\u8221\'20\'1D The draft doesn\u8217\'20\'19t specify what officers need to do or present to show if they meet those standards. The draft order originated with one of several outside policy groups collaborating with the transition team, and is one of numerous executive orders under review by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team, a transition official said.\par \par \uc2 The warrior board would be made up of retired generals and noncommissioned officers, who would send their recommendations to the president. Those identified for removal would be retired at their current rank within 30 days.\par \par \uc2 Karoline Leavitt, the Trump-Vance Transition spokeswoman, declined to comment on this draft executive order but said \u8220\'20\'1Cthe American people re-elected President Trump by a resounding margin giving him a mandate to implement the promises he made on the campaign trail. He will deliver.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At the White House, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  is taking questions from reporters who are asking for an idea of what to expect when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  meets \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 But the US press secretary does not have much to say. Responding to a reporter who wanted to know if they would discuss foreign policy issues such as US assistance to Ukraine and Israel, she said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to get into the details of what\u8217\'20\'19s going to be discussed tomorrow. That\u8217\'20\'19s not something I\u8217\'20\'19m going to get into here.\par \par \uc2 What about concerns about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s contacts with foreign leaders, many of whom have spoken to him by phone since he won the election? Jean-Pierre didn\u8217\'20\'19t have much of a comment on that question, either:\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s the president-elect. Every president-elect receives calls from world leaders, takes calls from world leaders, has calls from world leaders. It is not unusual. [I] don\u8217\'20\'19t have a comment beyond that, any specifics or details. That\u8217\'20\'19s something for the \u8230\'20\'26 Trump transition.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  plans to begin his second presidential term with a bang, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait }}}\uc2  reports:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  will mark the first day of his return to the White House by signing a spate of executive orders to reinstate signature policies from his first presidency that were revoked by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden }}}\uc2 , according to his incoming chief of staff.\par \par \uc2 Susie Wiles\u8217\'20\'19s disclosure came in a closed-door meeting in Las Vegas of the Rockbridge Network, a group of conservative donors co-founded by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, JD Vance, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/11/11/us/politics/trump-executive-orders-susie-wiles.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reported }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She did not specify which policies were likely to be reintroduced in the flurry of signing that is expected on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first day back in the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 But several of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s higher-profile executive orders that Biden revoked include leaving the Paris climate agreement, withdrawing from the \uc2 World Health Organization (WHO)\uc2  and banning entry to citizens from a list of predominantly Muslim countries.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/trump-executive-orders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump planning flurry of executive orders for first day, top aide says }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Did a majority of Latino men support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , as some national exit polls suggest?\par \par \uc2 No, according to the researchers behind the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://2024electionpoll.us/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 American Electorate Voter Poll }}}\uc2 , a survey of more than 9,400 voters that emphasizes accurately representing Black, Latino and AAPI voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe national exit polls are wrong about Latinos in general and Latino men in particular. They did shift more Republican, however a majority of Latino men continued to vote Democrat in 2024,\u8221\'20\'1D said Matt Baretto, a co-founder of BSP Research, told reporters on a call in which he presented the survey\u8217\'20\'19s findings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re extremely confident that our sample is accurate \u8211\'20\'13 that it is an accurate portrait of Latino men and Latino women and that it is balanced to measure the demographics and that it was available in Spanish at every stopping point in the survey.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to the survey, Hispanic men supported \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  over Trump by a 13-point margin, compared with the 34-point margin among Hispanic women. Among Hispanic men under 40, Harris held an only four-point margin.\par \par \uc2 Baretto said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cincorrect, categorically\u8221\'20\'1D to suggest that any cohort of Latino men supported Trump over Harris.\par \par \uc2 Even as he acknowledged Trump had made clear gains with Hispanic voters, he noted that Democrats performed worse this election cycle with \u8220\'20\'1Cevery single racial and ethnic group\u8221\'20\'1D than they did four years ago.\par \par \uc2 The poll also found an uptick in support for Harris among Puerto Ricans, particularly in Pennsylvania, which Hispanic organizers attributed to a surge in fundraising after a shock-jock comic made disparaging comments about the island during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden rally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe participation rate of Puerto Ricans and Latinos in Pennsylvania increased noticeably after the \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally \u8211\'20\'13 a nine-point shift in Latino voter sentiment in Pennsylvania towards Harris,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Frankie Miranda\uc2 , president and CEO at \uc2 Hispanic Federation\uc2 , on the call.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe effect is undeniable, but it took a fluke very late in the game to get the attention of the campaigns and funders to provide investment desperately needed to ensure mobilization.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Newly elected senators are in Washington DC for orientation, and true to form, West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Jim Justice\uc2  brought along his bulldog, Babydog.\par \par \uc2 The dog has been by Justice\u8217\'20\'19s side throughout his term as West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s governor, and the senator-elect was hoping to bring Babydog into the Senate chambers. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/11/12/babydog-jim-justice-senate-floor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reports }}}\uc2  that is against the rules:\par \par \uc2 Justice was told by Senate floor staff that only service dogs are allowed onto the floor of the Senate, and that even in that case there would need to be an analysis on potential allergies.\par \par \uc2 Justice had no such problems at the Republican national convention in Milwaukee this past summer, where Babydog was by his side throughout.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson has congratulated congressman Mike Waltz on being selected as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s national security advisor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongressman Mike Waltz is a brilliant and faithful patriot, who has served our country as a Green Beret and a member of Congress. It has been his life\u8217\'20\'19s mission to help protect the United States, and he will continue to do so as the President\u8217\'20\'19s National Security Advisor,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican House speaker said.\par \par \uc2 He added that the Florida congressman is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe perfect person to advise President Trump and defend our interests on the world stage. I look forward to continuing to engage with him as Congress works to implement America First national security policies under the new Trump administration\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Waltz just won re-election to his district just north of Orlando, and his departure from Congress will trigger a special election to replace him. But Democrats are unlikely to win in Waltz\u8217\'20\'19s district, which is sharply Republican.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A new Louisiana law that requires the Ten Commandments to be displayed in every public classroom by the beginning of 2025 has been temporarily blocked after a federal judge granted a preliminary injunction on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The judge said the law was \u8220\'20\'1Cunconstitutional on its face\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and plaintiffs were likely to win their case with claims that the law violates the US constitution\u8217\'20\'19s first amendment, which bars the government from establishing a religion and guarantees the right to religious freedom.\par \par \uc2 The ruling marks a win for opponents of the law, who argue that it is a violation of the constitutionally mandated separation of church and state.\par \par \uc2 They also argue that the poster-sized display of the Ten Commandments would isolate students, especially those who are not Christian.\par \par \uc2 Proponents say that the measure is not solely religious, but that it has historical significance to the foundation of US law.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/judge-blocks-louisiana-ten-commandments-school"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge blocks Louisiana law requiring schools to display Ten Commandments }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he will nominate \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2  to be ambassador to Israel\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has announced that he will nominate \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 , the former governor of Arkansas, to be the US ambassador to Israel.\par \par \uc2 Huckabee \u8220\'20\'1Cloves Israel, and the people of Israel, and likewise, the people of Israel love him,\u8221\'20\'1D the president-elect said in a statement on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMike will work tirelessly to bring about Peace in the Middle East!\u8221\'20\'1D Trump added.\par \par \uc2 Huckabee, who served as Arkansas governor from 1996 to 2007, is two-time Republican presidential hopeful and father to \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 , the current governor of the state and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former White House press secretary.\par \par \uc2 He is an outspoken settlement backer; in 2018, he said he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/aug/01/mike-huckabee-israeli-occupied-west-bank-efrat-holiday-home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dreamed of building a \u8220\'20\'1Choliday home\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  in the Israeli-occupied West Bank.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Several hundred White House staffers loudly cheered for the vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who was arriving for her lunch with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Staffers shouted \u8220\'20\'1CMVP\u8221\'20\'1D, for Madame vice-president, as she got out of her SUV and clapped and waved, per pool report.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe still have a lot of work to do,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris addressed staffers. \u8220\'20\'1CSo thank you all very much.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CListen, we do the best work anybody could do, which is to dedicate ourselves to the people, to public service, to lifting folks up, knowing we have the power, and when we do that work, we make a difference, and you all are a part of doing that work every single day, and I am so grateful to each of you.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo let\u8217\'20\'19s get back to work, because we still have work to get done. And I am sending all my love and thanks. Thank you, everyone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joni Ernst\uc2 , the Republican senator for Iowa, has privately expressed interest in becoming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s defense secretary, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 If nominated and confirmed, Ernst, a retired Army lieutenant colonel, Iraq War veteran and member of the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s armed services committee, would be the first woman to serve in the role.\par \par \uc2 National security leaders have told Ernst that she would be a good fit for the job, but those conversations have not yet escalated to anything official, Notus reported.\par \par \uc2 A source told the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  on Tuesday that the idea started \u8220\'20\'1Cgaining a life of its own yesterday\u8221\'20\'1D, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear whether Trump will consider her for the role.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump confirms appointment of Mike Waltz as his national security adviser\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has issued a statement announcing his appointment of Mike Waltz to serve in his cabinet as the national security adviser.\par \par \uc2 Waltz \u8220\'20\'1Chas been a strong champion of my America First Foreign Policy agenda, and will be a tremendous champion of our pursuit of Peace through Strength!\u8221\'20\'1D the president-elect said in a statement on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Waltz, a Republican congressman representing east-central Florida and Trump loyalist who served in the national guard as a colonel, has criticized Chinese activity in the Asia-Pacific and voiced the need for the US to be ready for a potential conflict in the region.\par \par \uc2 Waltz is a combat-decorated Green Beret and a former White House and Pentagon policy adviser. He was first elected in 2018, replacing \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , who ran for governor, in Florida\u8217\'20\'19s sixth congressional district.\par \par \uc2 Waltz served multiple combat tours in Afghanistan, and he was awarded four bronze stars. He was one of the lawmakers appointed in July to serve on a bipartisan congressional taskforce to investigate the attempted assassination of Trump in Butler, Pennsylvania, in July.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The judge who presided over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s hush money case {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-67336df48f08a71aa0e1f978#block-67336df48f08a71aa0e1f978"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has paused }}}\uc2  legal proceedings at the request of prosecutors and the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys, both of whom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673370ba8f081746a2e89e5a#block-673370ba8f081746a2e89e5a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointed to }}}\uc2  his victory in last week\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election. Republicans are getting ready for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s visit to the White House, with House speaker Mike Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673377218f081746a2e89eba#block-673377218f081746a2e89eba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying }}}\uc2  he planned to have Trump address his lawmakers. Speaking of Congress, we still do not know for sure which party will control the House for the next two years. Counting of ballots in key races {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673362028f08a71aa0e1f8d5#block-673362028f08a71aa0e1f8d5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remains ongoing }}}\uc2 , though Republicans seem on track to keep their majority.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , a long-serving conservative justice on the supreme court, has no plans to step down, the Wall Street Journal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-67336a938f081746a2e89dc2#block-67336a938f081746a2e89dc2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2 . If he changes his mind, Trump and the Republican-controlled Senate could confirm a replacement and likely prolong the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative supermajority.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-67337b9b8f081746a2e89efd#block-67337b9b8f081746a2e89efd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will reportedly oppose }}}\uc2  a US law that could lead to popular social media app TikTok being banned, despite bipartisan support for the measure.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Despite taking office with Republicans in control of Congress in 2017, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first years in office were marked by legislative chaos. Johnson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/12/donald-trump-marco-rubio-juan-merchan-stormy-daniels-us-politics-live?page=with:block-673380558f081746a2e89f6b#block-673380558f081746a2e89f6b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed that won\u8217\'20\'19t happen again }}}\uc2  when Trump returns to the White House in January.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appoints his cabinet, and searches for a treasury secretary, the billionaire hedge fund manager John Paulson \u8211\'20\'13 a key backer of the president-elect \u8211\'20\'13 has withdrawn his name. He had been widely tipped as a likely candidate for the role.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlthough various media outlets have mentioned me as a candidate for secretary of the treasury, my complex financial obligations would prevent me from holding an official position in President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration at this time,\u8221\'20\'1D Paulson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/john-paulson-treasury-secretary-trump-cabinet-f18b24e0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told The Wall Street Journal }}}\uc2  in a statement.\par \par \uc2 He pledged to remain \u8220\'20\'1Cactively involved\u8221\'20\'1D with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s economic team, however, and in helping to implement the incoming administration\u8217\'20\'19s policy agenda.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in Pennsylvania, Bob Casey still is not conceding, despite grim signs for the Democratic senator\u8217\'20\'19s prospects of re-election.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has already called the race for Republican challenger David McCormick, but ballot counting is ongoing. In a new statement, Casey signaled he is waiting for that process to finish:\par \par \uc2 My priority has always been standing up for the people of Pennsylvania. Across our Commonwealth, close to seven million people cast their votes in a free and fair election. Our county election officials will finish counting those votes, just like they do in every election. The American democratic process was born in Pennsylvania and that process will play out.\par \par \uc2 I want to thank the election workers across our Commonwealth who have been working diligently over the weekend. Their work will ensure Pennsylvanians\u8217\'20\'19 voices are heard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  follows through on his promise to carry out mass deportations of undocumented immigrations, his \u8220\'20\'1Cborder tsar\u8221\'20\'1D Tom Homan will play a leading role. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about his rise to power, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-leingang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Leingang }}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 In 2018, then acting director of \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) Thomas Homan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.huffpost.com/entry/thomas-homan-trump-ice-director_n_5acbae94e4b09d0a11964dc4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told HuffPost }}}\uc2  that Congress needed to fix immigration laws because: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m the first one to say, I can\u8217\'20\'19t arrest 11 million people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Now, newly tapped as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cborder tsar\u8221\'20\'1D, he will be tasked with just that. The president-elect said on Monday that Homan, a former law enforcement official who has served in immigration enforcement under multiple presidencies, would be \u8220\'20\'1Cin charge of all Deportation of Illegal Aliens back to their Country of Origin\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Homan has been describing mass deportation in stark terms for the past year, angling for a role in helping Trump with his signature campaign promise. Asked about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/trump-deportation-plan-economic-disaster"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high price tag }}}\uc2  of a mass deportation, he turned the question back on 60 Minutes: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat price do you put on our national security? Is it worth it?\u8221\'20\'1D When the outlet followed up to ask if there was a way for mass deportations not to separate families with mixed immigration statuses, Homan responded: \u8220\'20\'1CFamilies can be deported together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It is a likely next step for a man who served as acting director of Ice for 16 months under Trump in what was seen as a period of intense controversy for the agency. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2022/09/trump-administration-family-separation-policy-immigration/670604/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Atlantic documented }}}\uc2  how Homan was the \u8220\'20\'1Cfather\u8221\'20\'1D of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s family separation policy, tracing its roots to a 2014 meeting during which Homan pushed the idea. He defended the policy to the outlet by saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThe goal wasn\u8217\'20\'19t to traumatize. The goal was to stop the madness, stop the death, stop the rape, stop the children dying, stop the cartels doing what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/who-is-tom-homan-trump-border-czar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tom Homan: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new \u8216\'20\'18border czar\u8217\'20\'19 who vowed to \u8216\'20\'18run the biggest deportation\u8217\'20\'19 the US has ever seen }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Sunday announced that Tom Homan, a proponent of hardline immigration policies including separating migrant parents from their children, will become his \u8220\'20\'1Cborder tsar\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Homan has made clear he\u8217\'20\'19ll continue pushing for policies that would crack down on people who have entered the United States illegally. Yesterday, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2024/11/11/us-news/trump-border-czar-tom-homan-vows-sanctuary-city-crackdown/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the New York Post }}}\uc2  that he would surge immigration officers onto the streets of cities that refuse to allow them into their jails:\par \par \uc2 Homan \u8212\'20\'14 whom Trump tasked with both securing the border and carrying out the deportation of millions of migrants who are in the US illegally \u8212\'20\'14 told The Post that he wants his boss to put maximum pressure on the leaders of New York and other sanctuary cities that refuse to cooperate with efforts to lock up and deport migrants who commit crimes in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m hoping the president files a lawsuit against them and withholds federal funding,\u8221\'20\'1D Homan said.\par \par \uc2 He said that he would rather work with local cops to identify migrants who have been arrested and take them into ICE custody.\par \par \uc2 But, if police are barred from helping the feds identify suspects, \u8220\'20\'1Cthen we\u8217\'20\'19ll wait til they get out of jail, then we\u8217\'20\'19ll go out into the neighborhoods and get them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CIf they\u8217\'20\'19re not willing to do it then get out of the way \u8212\'20\'14 we\u8217\'20\'19re coming.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Homan said enforcing immigration laws like that will require a lot of manpower, \u8220\'20\'1Cso if I have to flood agents to the sanctuary cities to get the job done then that\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Earlier, at the Capitol, Republican House speaker Mike Johnson pledged that his lawmakers will do all they can to help \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  enact his policies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis leadership will hit the ground running to deliver President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda in the 119th Congress, and we will work closely with him and his administration to turn this country around and unleash, as he says, a new golden age in America,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 Trump began his first term in 2017 with both houses of Congress in Republican control, a situation that appears to be on track to happen again next year, since the GOP has recaptured the Senate and appears on course to preserve their house majority.\par \par \uc2 But Trump and the Republicans were criticized for a chaotic and disorganized approach during his first two years in office (before the GOP lost control of the House in 2018 and, with it, the ability to pass major Trump-backed legislation) that led to many legislative priorities stalling. Johnson said that once Trump takes office next year, he will not let that happen again:\par \par \uc2 When President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the presidency in 2016, we all look back and recognize that the Republican Party was not fully prepared for that moment, and precious time was wasted in the beginning of that Congress. I know it well, because that was my freshman year in Congress \u8211\'20\'13 we began in 2017. We are not going to make those mistakes again. We will be ready on day one. We are prepared this time. And as we wind down, the 118th Congress will be ready to take the ball and run full speed in the 119th Congress that begins in January.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wants to halt US TikTok ban \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will attempt to block a recently passed US law that could lead to popular social media app TikTok being banned, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2024/11/12/trump-tiktok-ban-sale/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The measure enacted with bipartisan support earlier this year imposes a 19 January deadline for Chinese firm ByteDance to sell its stake in TikTok or face a ban in the United States on national security grounds.\par \par \uc2 The Post heard from Kellyanne Conway, a former advisor to Trump who now advocates for TikTok. She said:\par \par \uc2 He appreciates the breadth and reach of TikTok, which he used masterfully along with podcasts and new media entrants to win \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 There are many ways to hold China to account outside alienating 180 million U.S. users each month. Trump recognized early on that Democrats are the party of bans \u8212\'20\'14 gas-powered cars, menthol cigarettes, vapes, plastic straws and TikTok \u8212\'20\'14 and to let them own that draconian, anti-personal choice space.\par \par \uc2 TikTok is currently in court over the law, though no decision has yet been made:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/sep/16/threatened-us-ban-against-tiktok-unconstitutional-platform-to-argue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Threatened US ban against TikTok \u8216\'20\'18unconstitutional\u8217\'20\'19, platform argues }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson says House Republicans planning meeting with Trump\par \par \uc2 The Republican House speaker Mike Johnson said that their lawmakers are planning to meet with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Wednesday, before he heads to the White House to discuss the presidential transition with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump is going to meet with President Biden at the White House. And so it was suggested \u8211\'20\'13 in fact \u8230\'20\'26 I think he said it first before I did \u8211\'20\'13 but that he wanted to come and visit with House Republicans. So, we\u8217\'20\'19re working out the details of him gathering with us potentially tomorrow morning before he goes to the White House, and that would be a great meeting and a moment for all of us,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 The speaker and other top Republicans just held a press conference at the Capitol to tout their victories in last Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election. While all the ballots have not been counted yet, the GOP appears on course to continue their majority in the House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York prosecutors requested pause in hush money case after Trump re-elected\par \par \uc2 New York Judge Juan Merchan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/trump-hush-money-conviction-presidential-immunity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 halted proceedings }}}\uc2  in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s hush money case after a request from the office of the Manhattan district attorney, \uc2 Alvin Bragg\uc2 , who cited the former president\u8217\'20\'19s victory in the presidential election, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The president-elect had asked Bragg to agree to the delay, and Merchan paused all proceedings through 19 November. Trump had been scheduled to be sentenced on 26 November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Judge halts proceeding in Trump hush money case\par \par \uc2 New York judge Juan Merchan has paused the proceedings in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s hush money case, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Merchan was today expected to decide whether Trump\u8217\'20\'19s conviction on 34 felony charges related to falsifying business documents would be thrown out under the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling earlier this year granting presidents immunity for official acts.\par \par \uc2 The judge\u8217\'20\'19s decision comes after Trump won the presidential election a week ago.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Alito not planning to leave supreme court \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  intends to continue serving on the supreme court, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/us-news/law/justice-samuel-alito-plans-to-remain-on-supreme-court-f14aac9e?mod=hp_lead_pos4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Wall Street Journal reports }}}\uc2 , despite fears from liberals that the 74-year-old conservative justice will soon step down and allow \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the newly Republican-controlled Senate to confirm a younger replacement.\par \par \uc2 Such a decision by Alito could prolong the conservative dominance of the supreme court, where they have a six-justice supermajority and the liberals a three-justice minority. But the Journal says that Alito plans to stick around:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite what some people may think, this is a man who has never thought about this job from a political perspective,\u8221\'20\'1D said one person close to Alito. \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that he\u8217\'20\'19s going to retire for political considerations is not consistent with who he is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election last week set off renewed discussions over the future of the Supreme Court, where the three eldest justices are in their 70s.\par \par \uc2 With Republicans set to take both the White House and Senate come January, there will be at least a two-year span when the GOP can fill vacancies without need of compromise with Democrats. Some Republicans have suggested that would be a good time for Alito, appointed in 2006 by President \uc2 George W. Bush\uc2 , and Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , 76, a 1991 appointee of President George H.W. Bush, to step aside for younger nominees who could perpetuate the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative direction for decades to come.\par \par \uc2 A majority of Americans view the Supreme Court as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.marquette.edu/news-center/2024/new-marquette-law-poll-national-survey-finds-approval-of-supreme-court-falls-to-39.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 politically motivated }}}\uc2 , public opinion surveys have shown. But across the ideological spectrum, the justices prefer to see themselves as standing apart from partisan politics, and Washington\u8217\'20\'19s postelection chatter is proving irksome within the court, people familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme court declines to hear Trump ally's bid to move Georgia election case to federal court\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has turned down an effort by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2  to move the Georgia election meddling case to federal court.\par \par \uc2 Meadows first made the petition earlier this year, after the supreme court ruled that presidents are immune from prosecution for official acts. The case brought by Atlanta-area district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  against Meadows, Trump and more than a dozen others for allegedly plotting to overturn the results of the election in Georgia has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/12/trump-election-interference-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since stalled }}}\uc2 , and it is unclear if it will continue now that Trump is headed back to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about Meadows\u8217\'20\'19s petition:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/29/mark-meadows-georgia-election-case-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump ally asks supreme court to move Georgia election case to federal court }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans near House majority despite losing seat in California\par \par \uc2 The GOP is on track to maintain its majority in the House of Representatives, even as Democrats managed to claim a hotly contested seat in the Los Angeles suburbs.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, Republican congressman Mike Garcia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ElectMikeGarcia/status/1856170146118893597"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conceded }}}\uc2  to his challenger \uc2 George Whitesides\uc2  in California\u8217\'20\'19s 27th congressional district, flipping a district that Democrats have wanted to conquer for the past two elections. But it may not be enough to return the party to the majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber, and give them the ability to block \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s legislative agenda.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports that the GOP had won 214 seats in the House, four shy of the majority, while the Democrats have 205. Counting in 16 races is ongoing, many of which are swing seats where every vote will matter, but Republicans are generally seen as having the edge in several crucial races.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know if the AP calls any outstanding House races over the course of today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is meeting with two foreign leaders at the White House today.\par \par \uc2 At 11.15am, he will speak with Israel\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Isaac Herzog\uc2 , then with Indonesia\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Prabowo Subianto\uc2 , at 2pm.\par \par \uc2 Biden is also scheduled to have a private lunch with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  around noon. The vice-president has no other meetings publicly scheduled.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Debbie Mucarsel-Powell\uc2 , the Democratic former Florida congresswoman who mounted an unsuccessful bid to unseat Republican Senator \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2  in last week\u8217\'20\'19s election, had a few words for \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  as he heads to the state department.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongrats @marcorubio on your appointment as US Secretary of State. I\u8217\'20\'19m sure in a few weeks, after January 20, you\u8217\'20\'19ll finally take down Maduro\u8217\'20\'19s narco-regime and free the Cuban people from D\u237\'00\'EDaz-Canel\u8217\'20\'19s communist dictatorship. It\u8217\'20\'19s been all talk so far\u8212\'20\'14let\u8217\'20\'19s see if you\u8217\'20\'19re actually ready to do something about it,\u8221\'20\'1D she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/DebbieforFL/status/1856157442045829382"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on X }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Those are references to Venezuela\u8217\'20\'19s president, Nicolas Maduro, and Cuba\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Miguel D\u237\'00\'EDaz-Canel\uc2 , both of whom leads governments Rubio is opposed to.\par \par \uc2 Mucarsel-Powell lost badly to Scott last week, picking up just under 43% of the vote to the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s 55%, further confirming the strength of the Republican party in Florida.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Should Florida senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  become \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s next secretary of state, Arkansas\u8217\'20\'19s Tom Cotton is set to become the chair of the Senate intelligence committee, Punchbowl News reports.\par \par \uc2 Cotton, who is known for his hardline views on the US relationship with China, was seen as a potential contender for a cabinet post in a second Trump administration, but reportedly withdrew his name following the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s election victory.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump considering \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2  for 'energy tsar' \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is reportedly considering making North Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Doug Burgum\uc2 , his new \u8220\'20\'1Cenergy tsar\u8221\'20\'1D. The Financial Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ft.com/content/6c390cc1-f5b8-4096-a361-c53d8145b85a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were the first to report this on Friday }}}\uc2 . The outlet said that Burgum, who last year ran a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/04/who-is-doug-burgum-republican-presidential-candidate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 short-lived campaign }}}\uc2  for the Republican nomination for president, is the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s preferred candidate for the role, though former energy secretary \uc2 Dan Brouillette\uc2  is also said to be a strong contender. The role and its powers have yet to be finalised but the FT reports that role would likely replace the \u8220\'20\'1Cclimate tsar\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 or National Climate Advisor \u8211\'20\'13 established by the Biden administration. You can read more on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s (potential) cabinet picks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/pompeo-kennedy-and-musk-who-could-be-in-trumps-new-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As my colleagues {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/dharna-noor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dharna Noor }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/oliver-milman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Milman }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/nov/11/john-podesta-cop29-climate-crisis-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 note in this story }}}\uc2 , Trump has pledged to deregulate the energy sector, allow the oil and gas industry to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/10/trump-rallies-extreme-heat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drill, baby, drill }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, and pull the US from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/paris-climate-agreement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Paris climate agreement }}}\uc2 , which committed countries to taking steps to avoid the worst impacts of the crisis.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vietnam\u8217\'20\'19s Communist Party head To Lam has congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on his US presidential election victory in a phone call and the two discussed ways their countries could boost economic ties, according to the communist party.\par \par \uc2 The US is Vietnam\u8217\'20\'19s largest export market, and the two countries upgraded their relationship to a comprehensive strategic partnership last September, the highest level in Vietnam\u8217\'20\'19s ranking.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVietnam is ready to promote stable and long-term development of bilateral relations for the benefit of the people of the two countries,\u8221\'20\'1D Lam said during the call, which took place on Monday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.dangcongsan.vn/international-cooperation/party-leader-of-vietnam-holds-phone-talks-with-president-elect-of-us-20004937.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to a statement posted on the communist party\u8217\'20\'19s website }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lam stated that Vietnam is ready to promote the stable and long-term development of the bilateral ties for the sake of the two peoples, as well as for regional and global peace, cooperation, and sustainable development\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Trump expressed his satisfaction with the positive development in the bilateral relations, and affirmed the importance he attaches to the relationship with Vietnam, particularly economic cooperation. He highlighted specific areas of economic and trade collaboration that the US seeks to advance.\par \par \uc2 Last week, officials and supply chain experts told Reuters Vietnam could face trade volatility with a new Trump presidency, as it could become \u8220\'20\'1Ccollateral damage\u8221\'20\'1D of protectionist measures.\par \par \uc2 Both leaders invited the other to visit their country, according to the party statement.\par \par \uc2 Trump travelled to Vietnam twice in his first term as president, first to attend an \uc2 Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC)\uc2  summit and then for a meeting with North Korean leader \uc2 Kim Jong Un\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 My colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-leingang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Leingang }}}\uc2  has done a profile on Tom Homan, the former law enforcement official who has been selected to be in charge of the country\u8217\'20\'19s borders following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration in January. Here is an extract {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/12/who-is-tom-homan-trump-border-czar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from her piece }}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Homan has been describing mass deportation in stark terms for the past year, angling for a role in helping Trump with his signature campaign promise. Asked about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/trump-deportation-plan-economic-disaster"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high price tag }}}\uc2  of a mass deportation, he turned the question back on 60 Minutes: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat price do you put on our national security? Is it worth it?\u8221\'20\'1D When the outlet followed up to ask if there was a way for mass deportations not to separate families with mixed immigration statuses, Homan responded: \u8220\'20\'1CFamilies can be deported together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It is a likely next step for a man who served as acting director of Ice for 16 months under Trump in what was seen as a period of intense controversy for the agency. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2022/09/trump-administration-family-separation-policy-immigration/670604/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Atlantic documented }}}\uc2  how Homan was the \u8220\'20\'1Cfather\u8221\'20\'1D of the Trump administration\u8217\'20\'19s family separation policy, tracing its roots to a 2014 meeting where Homan pushed the idea. He defended the policy to the outlet by saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThe goal wasn\u8217\'20\'19t to traumatize. The goal was to stop the madness, stop the death, stop the rape, stop the children dying, stop the cartels doing what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr"I hear a lot of people say, 'The talk of a mass deportation is racist. It's threatening to the immigrant community,'" says Tom Homan, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former acting director of immigration enforcement. He argues it should only \u8220\'20\'1Cbe threatening to the illegal immigrant community.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IsU7yrcxIb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IsU7yrcxIb }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 60 Minutes (@60Minutes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/60Minutes/status/1850687101332865526?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 27, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 This year, his speech to the Republican national convention started with a folksy \u8220\'20\'1Chow you doin\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D and a shoutout to New York, his home state. He then launched into an impassioned speech defending Trump and lambasting the Biden administration on immigration, saying \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policies were essentially \u8220\'20\'1Cnational suicide\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a guy who spent 34 years deporting illegal aliens, I got a message to the millions of illegal aliens that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s released in our country in violation of federal law: you better start packing now \u8211\'20\'13 you\u8217\'20\'19re damn right \u8211\'20\'13 because you\u8217\'20\'19re going home,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, to raucous applause.\par \par \uc2 To the cartels in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/mexico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mexico }}}\uc2  trafficking fentanyl, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen President Trump gets back in office, he\u8217\'20\'19s going to designate you a terrorist organization. He\u8217\'20\'19s going to wipe you off the face of the earth. You\u8217\'20\'19re done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Republicans already have a majority in the Senate and need to win just a few seats to take control of the 435-member House (a party needs 218 seats to win a House majority). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/08/us-house-senate-and-governor-elections-2024-results-from-all-50-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to our latest tally }}}\uc2 , Republicans have 214 seats, while the Democrats have 205.\par \par \uc2 Keeping hold of the House would give {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans }}}\uc2  sweeping powers to potentially enact a broad agenda of tax and spending cuts, energy deregulation and border security controls. As well as giving the party the power to initiate spending legislation, control of the House would allow Republicans to launch impeachment proceedings against officials.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  due in court over border-wall fraud trial\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  is due in court today ahead of his trial on criminal fraud charges over a push to fund Trump\u8217\'20\'19s border wall, weeks after he was released from prison on a separate conviction. Bannon, the 70-year-old former Trump adviser, is scheduled to stand trial starting on 9 December in New York state court in Manhattan.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors allege that he deceived donors who contributed more than $15 million in 2019 to a private fundraising drive to build a barrier along the US-Mexico border. Bannon has pleaded not guilty. He is set to appear for a final pretrial conference before acting justice April Newbauer at 2:15 pm EST (1915 GMT).\par \par \uc2 Last month, Bannon was released from prison, following a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/21/steve-bannon-sentenced-prison-contempt-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four-month sentence }}}\uc2  for defying a congressional subpoena in an investigation of the 6 January 2021 US Capitol attack.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump demands Senate allow him to circumvent hearings to appoint cabinet\par \par \uc2 Robert Tait is a journalist based in Washington DC\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/11/us-election-briefing-donald-trump-latest-news-updates-putin-house-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demanded }}}\uc2  that the three frontrunners to lead the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate }}}\uc2  allow him to appoint officials to his new administration without confirmation hearings on Capitol Hill, as a future {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican }}}\uc2  government began to take shape the week after his election victory.\par \par \uc2 In a demonstration of his political muscle, the US president-elect urged support for \u8220\'20\'1Crecess appointments\u8221\'20\'1D, which allow the president to make appointments while the Senate is temporarily paused, and can be used to circumvent the confirmation process, which can result in appointments being delayed or blocked.\par \par \uc2 The demand amounted to a full-frontal intervention in this week\u8217\'20\'19s GOP\u8217\'20\'19s election for a new Senate leader to replace \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the party\u8217\'20\'19s longtime leader who is retiring. The three men tipped to lead the Senate \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , \uc2 John Thune\uc2  and \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 all quickly agreed to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request.\par \par \uc2 It also signalled Trump\u8217\'20\'19s determination to press ahead with his agenda without being encumbered by congressional oversight, which is mandated by the US constitution.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/11/trump-senate-administration-hearings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump demands Senate allow him to circumvent hearings to appoint cabinet }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump poised to appoint Rubio; judge decides whether to overturn criminal conviction\par \par \uc2 Good morning, and welcome to our US politics blog.\par \par \uc2 US President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  announced several new members of his incoming administration on Monday, and is reportedly expected to name \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a one time challenger in the 2016 Republican presidential primaries \u8211\'20\'13 as secretary of state.\par \par \uc2 It comes as justice Juan Merchan, a New York judge, is set to decide later today whether Trump\u8217\'20\'19s criminal conviction on charges involving hush money paid to a porn star should be overturned in light of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/01/supreme-court-decision-trump-immunity-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the US Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s July ruling on presidential immunity }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, officials at the US justice department are assessing how to wind down the two federal criminal cases brought against Trump by special counsel Jack Smith due to its longstanding policy against prosecuting a sitting president.\par \par \uc2 A separate case in Georgia involving state criminal charges concerning Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn his 2020 presidential election loss remains in limbo.\par \par \uc2 We will give you more on the developments in the legal cases Trump faces when news breaks throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 Here are the main political appointments Trump has already made or is expected to announce shortly:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nytimes.com/2024/11/11/us/politics/trump-rubio-secretary-of-state.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports }}}\uc2  that Trump is expected to name Florida senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  his secretary of state. The paper cites three unnamed sources \u8220\'20\'1Cfamiliar with [Trump\u8217\'20\'19s] thinking\u8221\'20\'1D. Rubio has said that Ukraine needs to seek a negotiated settlement with Moscow rather than focus on regaining all territory that Russia has taken in the last decade. He was also one of 15 Republican senators to vote against a $95 billion military aid package for Ukraine, passed in April. Rubio serves as the vice-chairman of the Senate intelligence committee and sits on the foreign relations committee.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US president-elect has reportedly asked US Representative Michael Waltz, a retired Army National Guard officer and war veteran, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/11/trump-mike-waltz-national-security-adviser"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to be his national security adviser }}}\uc2 . Waltz, regarded by many in Washington as hawkish on China and Iran, has also been a member of the intelligence and foreign affairs committees.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump picked South Dakota governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  to serve as the next secretary of the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , CNN reported on Tuesday, citing two sources. The \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  is responsible for a range of issues, including border protection, immigration, disaster response and the US secret service. Noem, once seen as a possible running mate for Trump, made headlines after refusing to impose a statewide mask mandate during the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump announced that the former New York congressman \uc2 Lee Zeldin\uc2  will be selected to lead the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2 . Trump, who oversaw the rollback of more than 100 environmental rules when he last was US president, said Zeldin was a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrue fighter for America First policies\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Che will ensure fair and swift deregulatory decisions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , the author of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s so-called \u8220\'20\'1CMuslim ban\u8221\'20\'1D immigration policy during his first term, is set to be his deputy chief of staff with a broad portfolio.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said on Sunday that Tom Homan, the former acting director of \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice), will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/31/election-trump-immigration-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in charge of the country\u8217\'20\'19s borders }}}\uc2  in his new administration. Homan told Fox News: \u8220\'20\'1CIf sanctuary cities don\u8217\'20\'19t want to help us, then get the hell out of the way, because we\u8217\'20\'19re coming.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New York Congresswoman \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2 , 40, has been made ambassador to the United Nations. Stefanik, a Trump-skeptic turned Trump-ally, is the House Republican Conference chair, making her the fourth-ranking House Republican.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Trump made his first appointment, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/trump-susie-wiles-chief-of-staff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 naming }}}\uc2 Susie Wiles, who has worked on Republican campaigns since the days of \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 , White House chief of staff. She was previously the campaign manager for his victorious bid for re-election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241112ekbc001mn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
