\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Idaho  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  trial to hear from women denied medically necessary abortions\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 702 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 November 2024\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Lawsuit filed by pro-choice protesters seeks to clarify medical exceptions in states\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Women denied medically necessary abortions in Idaho are expected to testify this week in a trial over the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 The trial, which starts on Tuesday and is expected to last through at least Thursday, is part of a lawsuit filed by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters who want to clarify the medical exceptions in Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Currently, abortions are only permitted in Idaho to preserve a patient\u8217\'20\'19s health. The vagueness of the exception means women have been forced to go out of state for the procedure, or wait until they get sick enough that doctors can legally intervene.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis has got to be better. This just cannot continue to happen to people,\u8221\'20\'1D Jen Adkins, the lead plaintiff in the case, recently told the Guardian. Adkins was denied an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Idaho after learning that she was likely to miscarry and that continuing her pregnancy could endanger her health.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want people to know how these bans affect real people in real life, because I guarantee you that everybody has somebody in their life that this similar type of thing has happened to. And if they don\u8217\'20\'19t know somebody, it\u8217\'20\'19s just because that person does not feel safe enough to share.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the two years since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, paving the way for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 18 states to ban almost all abortions }}}\uc2 , dozens of women have come forward to say that they were denied medically necessary abortions. At least four women \u8212\'20\'14 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amber Nicole Thurman }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/candi-miller-abortion-ban-death-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Candi Miller }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/josseli-barnica-death-miscarriage-texas-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jossica Barnica }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/nevaeh-crain-death-texas-abortion-ban-emtala"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nevaeh Crain }}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 have reportedly died because they were unable to access legal abortions or because bans delayed their care.\par \par \uc2 Similar lawsuits, filed in Texas and Tennessee, have also asked the states to clarify the scope of the medical exceptions in their near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. In Texas, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/31/texas-abortion-ban-medical-exceptions-supreme-court-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the state supreme court in May 2024 }}}\uc2  rejected the lawsuit and let the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban stand as is.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe overarching theme of all of these cases is that exceptions do not work, and we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing this time and time again,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gail Deady, a senior attorney at the \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is representing the women in the Texas, Tennessee and Idaho cases.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise, Idaho has become a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/21/idaho-abortion-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kind of cautionary tale }}}\uc2  about the consequences of banning abortions. Many doctors have fled the state, which already had rising rates of maternal and infant mortality, or stopped practicing rather than risk facing criminal consequences due to the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Originally, the ban only allowed abortions to save patients\u8217\'20\'19 lives. However, the Biden administration sued Idaho over that narrow exception, arguing that it violated a federal law known as Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act, or Emtala, which requires hospitals to stabilize patients in medical emergencies. The case went all the way to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/27/supreme-court-allows-emergency-abortions-idaho"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ultimately punted on the case }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the justices restored a court order that temporarily permits providers to perform abortions to protect patients\u8217\'20\'19 health \u8211\'20\'13 a slightly lower threshold for medical intervention \u8211\'20\'13 while the case winds through the lower courts.\par \par \uc2 The other plaintiffs in the Idaho case include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/sep/13/idaho-extreme-abortion-ban-medical-emergency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jillaine St.Michel }}}\uc2 , who fled Idaho for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after her fetus was diagnosed with severe genetic and developmental conditions that would have required palliative care immediately after birth. Adkins and St.Michel are both expected to testify, as are plaintiffs Kayla Smith and Rebecca Vincen-Brown, two other women who were denied abortions.\par \par \uc2 Two doctors and the Idaho Academy of Family Physicians have also joined the case.\par \par \uc2 The last few weeks have been rocky for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters. Although seven states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed ballot measures to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2  on election day, measures failed in three other states.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s impending return to the White House may also lead to additional restrictions. Of particular concern to advocates is the possibility that his administration could invoke {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/07/abortion-donald-trump-return-to-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  a 19th-century anti-vice law }}}\uc2  to effectively ban all abortions nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241112ekbc001mi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
