\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Make no mistake: this Trump presidency will continue to attack  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights\b0\par\par\uc2 Moira Donegan \par \uc2 1,319 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 November 2024\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Just because Trump is publicly distancing himself from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not mean Republicans won\u8217\'20\'19t enact a national ban\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights initiatives were on the ballot in 10 states on Tuesday, and won in seven of them. One of the losers was prop 4, Florida\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights measure, which received a whopping 57% of the vote but failed to meet the state\u8217\'20\'19s unusually high 60% threshold, meaning that the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban will remain in place. Asked about the Florida \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights proposition ahead of the election, Trump said that when he went to cast his ballot near Palm Beach, he would vote against it.\par \par \uc2 It has always been a little hard to believe that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  personally hates \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even if it is abundantly clear how little he thinks of women. Trump, after all, has claimed to have numerous conflicting positions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights throughout his life. And his brand of masculinity is boorish, vulgar, and above all, sexually entitled \u8211\'20\'13 far from the priggish, repressed moralism of more classical anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures like \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Maybe this is why, though Trump appointed three of the six justices who overturned Roe v Wade and has boasted about his role in ending the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , many voters seem to not quite believe that he will continue to suppress the procedure further in his coming second term. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights measures won in several states that Trump carried on Tuesday \u8211\'20\'13 including Arizona, Nevada, Montana and Missouri, all states that Trump won. A lot of people, it seems, voted for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in their own states, and then also voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who, make no mistake, will move to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access nationwide when he returns to the White House next year.\par \par \uc2 Trump, of course, has insisted that this will not happen \u8211\'20\'13 which on its own might be a decent indication that it will. But there is evidence that the new Trump administration will pursue a broad agenda restricting women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, including nationwide attacks on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, even beyond that offered by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s habitual pattern of self-serving dishonesty.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have won control of the Senate and are likely to capture the House of Representatives; if they do, they may well advance legislation to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide. (And to pass it: there is no reason to believe that a Republican governing trifecta will preserve the filibuster.) A bill like this would probably not be termed a \u8220\'20\'1Cban\u8221\'20\'1D by its sponsors: Republicans, wary of the public disapproval of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, have started calling their new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions by chillingly imprecise euphemisms, such as \u8220\'20\'1Cstandard\u8221\'20\'1D or even \u8220\'20\'1Cprotection\u8221\'20\'1D. But the effect of the laws are the same: to outlaw abortions. This could take the form of a gestational limit, or of the federal recognition of fetal personhood. Trump may well sign such legislation into law, eliminating \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights even in Democratic-controlled states and those that have recently passed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights referendums with the stroke of a pen.\par \par \uc2 But Republicans do not even need to manage to pass a bill through Congress to make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  much more difficult to get. Trump can simply restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through federal agencies. He will soon be in control of the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , for example, which regulates the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drug mifepristone, part of a two-drug regimen that now accounts for most abortions in the United States. Mifepristone is a safe, effective drug that allows abortions to be performed in the privacy of patients\u8217\'20\'19 homes, with little of the expensive clinical involvement and overhead that makes surgical abortions more time-intensive and costly for providers and patients alike.\par \par \uc2 Naturally, the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement hates it. Since Dobbs, a coalition of anti-choice groups and Republican attorneys general have been suing the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , seeking to overturn the agency\u8217\'20\'19s 2000 approval of the drug. Trump will be able to rescind access to it almost immediately, taking the drug off the legal US market. If he gives the anti-choice movement what they want, he may also direct the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to revoke approval of the most reliable forms of female-controlled contraception, like Plan B, IUDs, and certain birth control pills, which the anti-choice movement falsely claims cause abortions.\par \par \uc2 Trump is likely to also revive enforcement of the Comstock Act, a long-dormant 1873 law that bans the shipment of anything that could be used to induce an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the US mail. The Comstock Act has not been enforced in decades \u8211\'20\'13 parts of it were repealed in the 20th century, and other sections were long rendered moot by supreme court precedents like Roe and Casey \u8211\'20\'13 and would have the effect of criminalizing much \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care. Since Dobbs, several Democratic-controlled states have passed what are called shield laws, which protect doctors who mail \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drugs from states where the procedure is legal into states that have bans. This mail-order \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  operation is, for now, technically legal: it has preserved women\u8217\'20\'19s independence and dignity and no doubt saved thousands of lives.\par \par \uc2 But when the Comstock Act is enforced, much of this sector of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provision will disappear. Combined with the revocation of \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval for mifepristone, this will inevitably mean that many women seeking abortions will turn to black market surgical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, and suffer the risks attendant to such procedures. A return to pre-Roe levels of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban-related mortality could probably follow.\par \par \uc2 Trump is also likely to reverse the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s guidance on Emtala, the Emergency Medical Treatment and Active Labor Act, a federal law that requires emergency rooms to provide stabilizing care to all patients facing health crises. Emtala has been the subject of much post-Dobbs litigation, as states like Idaho and Texas have sought to argue that their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans supersede the federal law, thus requiring hospitals in their states to withhold emergency abortions from women in medical emergencies who will suffer or die without them. The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  declined to decide the issue last summer; a Trump administration may help to resolve it for them.\par \par \uc2 This is all just what Trump could do on his own in his first years back in office. But the impact of a Trump term on American women\u8217\'20\'19s access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be felt long after Trump himself is no longer with us. Trump will probably appoint at least two supreme court justices to lifetime seats in his coming term; he will also fill an unknown number of vacancies on the lower federal courts, whose judges also serve for life. These judges are all likely to be anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  zealots, as are the federal bureaucrats Trump will bring in to staff agencies such as the \uc2 FDA\uc2 , CDC and Department of Health and Human Services.\par \par \uc2 We are already living in an era when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is restricted more than it has been in decades. Now, it will be restricted more. We may well never have as much reproductive freedom as we do now ever again.\par \par \uc2 American women are well advised to prepare for this, to not wait for the Trump administration to restrict the tools they use to control their own bodies. Sterilization and long-acting birth control remain accessible, for now; women who want these should move quickly to get them. Plan B and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills can both be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aidaccess.org/en/page/2880027/advance-provision"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 purchased ahead of time }}}\uc2  and kept on hand in the privacy of a medicine cabinet; such purchases may provide security and peace of mind to those staring down the barrel of another Trump term. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as we know, will never be eliminated; it can only be less safe, and less dignified. But there are few things as strong as women\u8217\'20\'19s determination to control their own lives. That determination is certainly stronger than the law.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan is a Guardian US columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241112ekbc001mg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
