\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Kentucky woman seeking  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  files lawsuit challenging state\u8217\'20\'19s bans\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 433 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 November 2024\par 23:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Woman argues both near-total ban and six-week ban violate state constitution\u8217\'20\'19s rights to privacy and self-determination\par \par \uc2 A pregnant woman in Kentucky seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  filed a lawsuit on Tuesday asking a court to strike down the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 The woman, who is known in court records as Mary Poe and is about seven or eight weeks pregnant, is challenging Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and the six-week ban simultaneously in effect. These bans, Poe argues, violate the Kentucky constitution\u8217\'20\'19s rights to privacy and self-determination and should not be enforced.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor many individuals, the bans altogether foreclose the ability to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , thus forcing them to carry their pregnancies to term and give birth, which carries a risk of death up to 14 times higher than that associated with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawsuit alleges. \u8220\'20\'1COthers, pushed by the bans to travel out of state for legal care, bear the burdens both of increased health risks from being pushed later into pregnancy and of the cost and logistical difficulties of long-distance travel.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit also requests class-action status for all people who may be pregnant or can become so but are unable to get a \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel overwhelmed and frustrated that I cannot access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care here in my own state, and I have started the difficult process of arranging to get care in another state where it\u8217\'20\'19s legal,\u8221\'20\'1D Poe said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThis involves trying to take time off work and securing child care, all of which place an enormous burden on me. This is my personal decision, a decision I believe should be mine alone, not one made by anyone else.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 , the ACLU of Kentucky, and the law firm Kaplan, Johnson, Abate & Bird are representing Poe.\par \par \uc2 Kentucky is one of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than a dozen states }}}\uc2  that have banned almost all abortions in the two years since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade. It is also one of several states that have overlapping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans on the books \u8211\'20\'13 a result of Roe-era efforts by state legislators to pile up \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions to both score political points with the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement and generate opportunities for the supreme court to take up a challenge to Roe.\par \par \uc2 Last year, another pregnant Kentucky woman also sued the state over its anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, but she later learned that her embryo was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/13/kentucky-abortion-ban-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no longer viable }}}\uc2 . That case was ultimately dismissed.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241112ekbc003ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
