\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 With Trump returning to the presidency, everything from  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  to immigration is under threat\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff \par \uc2 1,905 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 November 2024\par 21:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 With Trump back in the White House. The impact will be felt in many aspects of American life and across the worldUS election results 2024: live map and tracker\par \par \uc2 With {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  returning to the White House for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/trump-election-watch-party-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 second term as president}}}\uc2 , the impact will be felt in many aspects of American life and also across the world.\par \par \uc2 From {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/trump-deportation-plan-economic-disaster"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 immigration}}}\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 environment}}}\uc2 , gun laws and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/lgbt-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LGBTQ+}}}\uc2  rights: all are at stake with Trump and his allies back in power.\par \par \uc2 Here is a list of the main threats Trump represents:\par \par \uc2 Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could go nationwide\par \par \uc2 When the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in 2022, it paved the way for more than a dozen states to ban almost all abortions. While these bans allow for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in emergencies, the language and fear of criminal consequences mean doctors are forced to wait and watch as patients grow sicker.\par \par \uc2 Now, it\u8217\'20\'19s possible federal restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are next. Although Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stance on a national ban isn\u8217\'20\'19t entirely clear \u8211\'20\'13 he has repeatedly flip-flopped on the issue \u8211\'20\'13 his administration wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t need Congress to attack \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access nationwide.\par \par \uc2 Project 2025, the rightwing playbook for a second Trump term, proposes using the 1873 Comstock Act, which outlaws the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related materials, to ban people from shipping \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills. These pills account for about two-thirds of US abortions.\par \par \uc2 If enacted to its fullest extent, the Comstock Act could not only ban pills but the very equipment that clinics need to do their jobs, and Trump could use the legislation to implement a nationwide de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Trump could also weaken the Emergency Medical Treatment and Labor Act (Emtala), a federal law that protects emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban has been at the center of a legal debate over the law, which recently reached the supreme court. The court restored the right of Idaho doctors to perform a broader range of emergency abortions, but left the door open to reconsider Emtala in the future.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/21/idaho-abortion-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Read the full article }}}\par \par \uc2 Mass deportations could wreak havoc on immigrants\par \par \uc2 Raids and mass deportations lie at the heart of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vision for a second term.\par \par \uc2 He has promised to restore and expand his most controversial immigration policies, including the travel ban aimed at mostly Muslim countries. He has consistently promised to stage the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest deportation operation in American history\u8221\'20\'1D. It\u8217\'20\'19s a refrain he repeated so often that \u8220\'20\'1CMass deportations now!\u8221\'20\'1D became a rallying cry at this summer\u8217\'20\'19s Republican national convention.\par \par \uc2 Trump has offered few details of his plan to expel \u8220\'20\'1Cmaybe as many as 20 million\u8221\'20\'1D people. But in public remarks and interviews, he and his allies have detailed a vision that matches plans laid out in Project 2025. The strategy, as Trump has described it, may involve the extraordinary use of US troops for immigration enforcement and border security and the application of 18th-century wartime powers.\par \par \uc2 Immigrant advocates and leaders say they are better prepared and more organized than they were in his first term. Groups are already considering legal action against key pieces of his immigration agenda and activists say they have learned how to harness public outcry.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/31/election-trump-immigration-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Read the full article }}}\par \par \uc2 Trump could launch a \u8216\'20\'18catastrophic\u8217\'20\'19 rollback of LGBTQ+ rights\par \par \uc2 In his first term, Trump banned trans people from the military. If re-elected, he has promised even more aggressive attacks on LGBTQ+ rights.\par \par \uc2 Trump pledges to order all federal agencies to end programs that \u8220\'20\'1Cpromote \u8230\'20\'26 gender transition at any age\u8221\'20\'1D, cut funding from hospitals providing gender-affirming care, push for a federal law stating the government doesn\u8217\'20\'19t legally recognize trans people and rescind federal LGBTQ+ non-discrimination policies.\par \par \uc2 Project 2025, meanwhile, calls for replacing Biden-Harris policies with those that support \u8220\'20\'1Cheterosexual, intact marriage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Legal scholars warn that marriage equality could further be threatened under Trump, especially if he has the chance to appoint additional justices.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/sep/24/donald-trump-presidency-republican-lawmakers-targeting-lgbtq-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Read the full article }}}\par \par \uc2 He will doom efforts to slow the climate disaster\par \par \uc2 In his first term, Trump pulled the US out of the Paris climate accords, undermining the progress the talks had produced. In his second term, Trump would be a disaster for efforts to slow the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 Project 2025 outlined the myriad ways his administration could harm environmental policy, from bolstering oil, gas and coal to closing down the \uc2 National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\uc2 , the agency that measures how much the temperature is rising.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has called the climate crisis a \u8220\'20\'1Choax\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the great scams of all time\u8221\'20\'1D, has promised to \u8220\'20\'1Cdrill, baby, drill\u8221\'20\'1D and end Biden\u8217\'20\'19s pause on liquefied natural gas export terminals, among other things. And his four-year term arrives at precisely the moment the Earth most needs to accelerate efforts to curb climate change.\par \par \uc2 Climate scientists say emissions must be cut by 2030 for a chance at a Paris pathway. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s term would extend until 2029.\par \par \uc2 The climate effects may not be immediate but will be felt for years to come.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/sep/06/presidential-election-climate-crisis-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Read the full article }}}\par \par \uc2 Freedom of the press will be under threat\par \par \uc2 In his first term and as a candidate, Trump has consistently attacked the mainstream press and used conservative media for his political purposes. He threatened to weaken libel laws and called the press \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D and the \u8220\'20\'1Cenemy of the people\u8221\'20\'1D. There\u8217\'20\'19s nothing to suggest a re-elected Trump would tone down his aggression.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, Trump demanded that CBS News be stripped of its broadcast license as punishment for airing an edited answer of an interview with his Democratic rival, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , and he threatened that other broadcasters ought to suffer the same fate.\par \par \uc2 This rhetoric, along with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s past actions, prompted one science journalist to consider whether press freedom and democracy should be added to the \u8220\'20\'1Cendangered list\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/commentisfree/ng-interactive/2024/oct/27/trump-press-freedom-stakes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Read the full article }}}\par \par \uc2 Sensible gun-safety policies could be revoked\par \par \uc2 As president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  oversaw the passage of the first major federal gun-safety law in almost three decades. Now, advocates fear that those policies could be easily reversed if Trump and congressional Republicans win this election.\par \par \uc2 In a second term, advocates expect him to immediately close the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/22/biden-harris-federal-gun-prevention-office"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House Office of Gun Violence Prevention}}}\uc2 , created in 2023 and overseen by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and nominate a gun industry-friendly leader as director of the \uc2 Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives\uc2 . He could also disrupt implementation of the law Biden signed and wind back some of his administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to broaden background checks.\par \par \uc2 The gun-safety advocate Angela Ferrell-Zabala says a second Trump term would mean having to \u8220\'20\'1Cfight like hell\u8221\'20\'1D to secure progress made on \u8220\'20\'1Ccommon basic gun-safety measures\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/24/trump-gun-safety-stakes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Read the full article }}}\par \par \uc2 US cities are at risk of military takeovers\par \par \uc2 Trump has threatened to use presidential powers to seize control of cities largely run by Democrats, to use federal immigration agents to carry out mass deportations, and to obliterate the progressive criminal justice policies of left-leaning prosecutors. He threatened to deploy the national guard to combat urban protests and crime \u8211\'20\'13 and wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t wait to be called in by mayors or governors but would act unilaterally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn cities where there has been a complete breakdown of law and order \u8230\'20\'26 I will not hesitate to send in federal assets including the national guard until safety is restored,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says in his campaign platform.\par \par \uc2 Mayors and prosecutors in several US cities are collaborating over strategies to minimize the fallout. But as \uc2 Levar Stoney\uc2 , the Democratic mayor of Richmond, Virginia, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very difficult to autocrat-proof your city.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/17/trump-wins-elections-outcomes-stakes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Read the full article }}}\par \par \uc2 Biden-era accomplishments like the Inflation Reduction Act would be repealed\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, JD Vance, called the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s Inflation Reduction Act \u8211\'20\'13 the $370bn bill aimed at accelerating the move to clean energy \u8211\'20\'13 a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreen energy scam\u8221\'20\'1D. That\u8217\'20\'19s despite the millions in climate investments made in Vance\u8217\'20\'19s home town in Middletown, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Congress have attempted to gut the legislation and Project 2025 has called for it to be repealed under Trump.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/sep/16/trump-vance-election-climate-ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Read the full article }}}\par \par \uc2 Public lands would be opened up to oil and gas production\par \par \uc2 Early plans suggest a re-elected Trump would gut the Department of the Interior, the agency responsible for national parks, wildlife refuges and the protection of endangered species. The department is the focus of one chapter of Project 2025, the policy document that also calls for reinstating Trump\u8217\'20\'19s energy-dominant agenda, reducing national monument designations and weakening protections for endangered species.\par \par \uc2 In office, it\u8217\'20\'19s likely Trump would reverse the efforts made by the Biden administration on the green transition and protecting public lands. A second Trump term could cut regulations, weaken environmental protections and, in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s words, \u8220\'20\'1Cdrill, baby, drill\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/sep/28/trump-oil-national-parks-wildlife-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Read the full article }}}\par \par \uc2 US protest movements could face serious crackdowns\par \par \uc2 Since \uc2 George Floyd\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s death in 2020 and the resulting racial justice protests, Republican-led states have expanded anti-protest laws \u8211\'20\'13 a push that comes from Trump, the party\u8217\'20\'19s standard-bearer.\par \par \uc2 Trump campaigned on a platform that includes suppressing protests and has vowed to bring in the national guard where \u8220\'20\'1Claw and order\u8221\'20\'1D has broken down. Meanwhile, the House speaker, Mike Johnson, a key Trump ally, called for the national guard to be used against students protesting against Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 In his second term, Trump could direct a militarized response to protests and pressure congressional Republicans to pass legislation that would impose nationwide penalties like those already in effect in Tennessee; the Republican-led state passed a bill that, among other things, created a new felony for protest encampments on state property.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/05/trump-presidency-protest-rights-black-lives-matter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Read the full article }}}\par \par \uc2 He would bring instability to foreign policy\par \par \uc2 During his first term, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s brand of \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica first\u8221\'20\'1D politics created instability among both partners and adversaries. \uc2 Nato\uc2  members said that never before had the US been seen as the \u8220\'20\'1Cunpredictable ally\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His second term could bring more instability to a time when conflicts \u8211\'20\'13 including the widening war in the Middle East and the continuing Russia-Ukraine war \u8211\'20\'13 are raging around the world.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, Trump hinted at leaving \uc2 Nato\uc2  in an effort to force member countries to increase their defense spending. This year, he implied he would let Russia do \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/11/donald-trump-says-he-would-encourage-russia-to-attack-nato-countries-who-dont-pay-bills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 whatever the hell they want}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D to countries he says are not contributing enough to \uc2 Nato\uc2 . A Trump win would be likely to threaten Nato cohesion.\par \par \uc2 Trump is also likely to be surrounded by \u8220\'20\'1Cadvisers who are hawkish on China and very likely pro-Taiwan\u8221\'20\'1D, says Jude Blanchette, a China expert at the Center for Strategic and International Studies. However, Blanchette says, it\u8217\'20\'19s likely US-China relations would have been strained even if Harris were elected to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , would not have to deal with US opposition to greater Israeli control of the West Bank. Annexation of the West Bank would become a \u8220\'20\'1Cmuch more active possibility\u8221\'20\'1D under Trump, said Khaled Elgindy, a senior fellow at the Middle East Institute. It\u8217\'20\'19s less clear whether a Trump win would see the Israeli prime minister recruit the US for a decisive attack on Iran\u8217\'20\'19s nuclear programme, a longstanding goal of the Israeli leader.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/if-trump-wins-the-election-nato-can-expect-more-turbulence-ahead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Read the full article }}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241103ekb3000um\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
