\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Tracking  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ballot measures: Missouri and Arizona expand rights as Florida vote falls short\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman, Noa Yachot and Andrew Witherspoon \par \uc2 1,028 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 November 2024\par 18:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Seven states, including Montana and Nevada, pass measures in favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 follow our tracker as voters decide on access to abortionUS election results 2024: live map and trackerSenate and House results 2024: live maps and tracker\par \par \uc2 Americans in 10 US states voted on Tuesday on whether to enshrine the right to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  into their state constitutions.\par \par \uc2 In a major victory, Missouri voted to amend its state constitution to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights \u8211\'20\'13 a move that sets the state up to become the first since the fall of Roe v Wade to overturn its near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 So too did voters in the swing state of Arizona, which approved a ballot measure that would establish a fundamental right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and prohibit the state from restricting or banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before 24 weeks \u8211\'20\'13 a victory for activists who sought to expand access beyond 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Similar decisions in Montana \u8211\'20\'13 which enshrined a 1999 state supreme court ruling that said the constitutional right to privacy protects the right to a pre-viability \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by a provider of the patient\u8217\'20\'19s choice \u8211\'20\'13 and in Nevada, a presidential battleground state, added to the list of major wins for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters.\par \par \uc2 Colorado, New York and Maryland also all passed measures to amend their state constitutions to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and cement the blue states\u8217\'20\'19 status as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  havens.\par \par \uc2 However, in Florida, an effort to roll back a six-week ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/florida-abortion-ballot-ban-measure-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell short}}}\uc2 , as did to expands protections in Nebraska and North Dakota.\par \par \uc2 Before Tuesday, seven states had held \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot referendums, and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters won all of them before Florida broke their streak. The results of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s measures will not be the final word; states that vote to overturn bans will see litigation or legislation before those bans are repealed. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/donald-trump-wins-us-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 return to the White House}}}\uc2  will also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/21/idaho-abortion-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significantly shape the future of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  access}}}\uc2  in the United States.\par \par \uc2 The final vote counts are still processing, updated as of 6pm ET on 7 November.\par \par \uc2 Arizona\par \par \uc2 In a major victory for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters in Arizona, a key battleground state in the presidential election, voters approved their ballot measure to establish a fundamental right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and prohibit the state from restricting or banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability, or about 24 weeks, in the state constitution. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently banned in the state after 15 weeks.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/colorado"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Colorado}}}\par \par \uc2 Colorado voters passed a measure to amend the state constitution to block the state government from denying, impeding or discriminating against individuals\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/17/colorado-abortion-rights-ballot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. The amendment also repeals a provision in the state constitution that bans public funding for abortions. There is currently no gestational limit on the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/florida-abortion-ballot-ban-measure-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida shattered a string of success.}}}\uc2  A measure to roll back the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/02/florida-abortion-ban-six-weeks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week ban}}}\uc2  by adding the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until viability to the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution had amassed a clear majority, 57% of the vote, at the time it was called by the Associated Press. However, it needed 60% to pass, the highest threshold of any of the ballots.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/maryland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maryland}}}\par \par \uc2 Voters in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/28/abortion-rights-parental-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maryland approved a measure}}}\uc2  to amend the state constitution to confirm individuals\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Cright to reproductive freedom, including but not limited to the ability to make and effectuate decisions to prevent, continue, or end the individual\u8217\'20\'19s pregnancy\u8221\'20\'1D. There is currently no gestational limit on the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 Missouri\par \par \uc2 Voters decided to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s current, near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and establish a constitutional guarantee to the \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamental {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/07/missouri-abortion-rights-ballot-measure-ruled-invalid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 right to reproductive freedom}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care until fetal viability.\par \par \uc2 Montana\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Montana is currently legal, following a 1999 state supreme court ruling \u8211\'20\'13 and voters chose to amend the state constitution to explicitly include \u8220\'20\'1Ca right to make and carry out decisions about one\u8217\'20\'19s own pregnancy\u8221\'20\'1D. That includes the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/21/montana-becomes-eighth-state-to-put-measure-protecting-abortion-on-ballot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  up until fetal viability, or after viability to protect a patient\u8217\'20\'19s life or health. Though there\u8217\'20\'19s no defined time frame, doctors say viability is sometime around 24 weeks.\par \par \uc2 Nebraska\par \par \uc2 Nebraska was the lone state with two {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/13/nebraska-supreme-court-abortion-ballot-measures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 competing ballot measures}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The first, which did not pass, would have enshrined the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until viability into the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 The second one, which passed, will enshrine the current 12-week ban.\par \par \uc2 Nevada\par \par \uc2 Nevada voted to amend its state constitution to protect the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until viability, or after viability in cases where a patient\u8217\'20\'19s health or life may be threatened.\par \par \uc2 Voters must also approve the ballot question in 2026 in order to amend the state constitution. The political action committee Nevadans for Reproductive Freedom organized the ballot initiative and gathered enough signatures to put the question before voters. Although a 1990 state law makes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  available up to 24 weeks of pregnancy, supporters in Nevada and elsewhere have been pressing to strengthen \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access after Roe v Wade was overturned.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\par \par \uc2 New York voters approved a measure to broaden the state\u8217\'20\'19s anti-discrimination laws by adding, among other things, protections against discrimination on the basis of \u8220\'20\'1Csex, including sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy outcomes, and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. It does not explicitly reference \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but advocates say its pregnancy-related language encompasses \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is protected in New York until fetal viability.\par \par \uc2 South Dakota\par \par \uc2 South Dakota voters rejected a proposal to add protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the state constitution. The outcome preserves a state law that makes it a felony to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  except to save the life of the mother. The ban took effect when the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in 2022 and allowed states to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 South Dakota\u8217\'20\'19s measure was less sweeping than other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights measures, because it would only have protected the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/17/south-dakota-abortion-vote-rights-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 right to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in the first trimester of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 The Florida graph in this article was amended on 7 November 2024; an earlier version had the Yes and No percentages the wrong way round.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241105ekb50028w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
