\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Putin commends Trump victory \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now and earlier); Sam Levin, Chris Stein and Amy Sedghi \par \uc2 21,982 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2024\par 13:44 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. You can find all of the latest US elections stories here.Ten key takeaways from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s winThe key swing states and counties that handed Trump the White House\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. You can find all of the latest US elections stories {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NAACP\uc2  on Thursday condemned racist text messages referencing slavery that were sent anonymously to Black Americans this week as a contentious election was coming to an end in the United States.\par \par \uc2 The messages urged recipients in multiple states, including Alabama, North Carolina, Virginia, and Pennsylvania, to report to a plantation to pick cotton, the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  said on Thursday it was in touch with the US justice department and other federal authorities about the \u8220\'20\'1Coffensive and racist messages\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese actions are not normal. And we refuse to let them be normalized,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 NAACP\uc2  president \uc2 Derrick Johnson\uc2  said in a statement from the organization, which advocates for racial justice and rights for Black Americans.\par \par \uc2 High school and college students were among the recipients, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 Johnson said the messages were a reflection of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential election victory on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Arizona supreme court has declined to hear Republican Kari Lake\u8217\'20\'19s latest appeal over her defeat in the 2022 governor\u8217\'20\'19s race, marking yet another loss in her attempt to overturn the race\u8217\'20\'19s outcome, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The court made its refusal to take up the former TV anchor\u8217\'20\'19s appeal public on Thursday without explaining its decision.\par \par \uc2 Lake, now locked in a \uc2 US Senate\uc2  race against Democrat \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2 , had lost the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race to Democrat \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  by over 17,000 votes.\par \par \uc2 The courts had previously rejected Lake\u8217\'20\'19s claims that problems with ballot printers at some Maricopa county polling places on election day in 2022 were the result of intentional misconduct and that Maricopa county didn\u8217\'20\'19t verify signatures on mail ballots as required by law.\par \par \uc2 A judge also turned down Lake\u8217\'20\'19s request to examine the ballot envelopes of 1.3 million early voters. In all, Lake had three trials related to the 2022 election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 San Francisco\u8217\'20\'19s first Black female mayor, London Breed, conceded the race for mayor to \uc2 Levi Strauss\uc2  heir Daniel Lurie on Thursday, pledging a smooth transition as he takes over the job.\par \par \uc2 Breed, who was raised by her grandmother in public housing, could not overcome deep voter discontent and was trailing Lurie, a philanthropist and anti-poverty nonprofit founder.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the end of the day, this job is bigger than any one person and what matters is that we keep moving this city forward,\u8221\'20\'1D Breed said, adding that she had called Lurie to congratulate him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know we are both committed to improving this city we love.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has not yet declared a winner because tens of thousand of ballots have not yet been counted and added to the ranked choice voting calculations.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 In a profile, Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/magazine/2024/04/26/susie-wiles-trump-desantis-profile-00149654"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 describes }}}\uc2  Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new chief of staff, Susie Wiles, as a \u8220\'20\'1Cforce more sensed than seen\u8221\'20\'1D, crediting her as the reason the former president\u8217\'20\'19s latest campaign has been \u8220\'20\'1Cmore professional than its fractious, seat-of-the-pants antecedents\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Maanvi Singh writes:\par \par \uc2 Wiles is a veteran of Florida politics who led Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 campaign in the state. She also worked with \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  and \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 , Florida\u8217\'20\'19s current and former governors. The Trump campaign had fired her after a falling out with DeSantis, but brought her back for the 2020 campaign in the state.\par \par \uc2 A self-described moderate, Wiles has also been credited \u8211\'20\'13 by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s allies and opponents \u8211\'20\'13 as the person who has given him the discipline and focus to succeed politically. She has been known to keep good relationships with reporters, and holds a wealth of knowledge about all aspects of running a campaign.\par \par \uc2 Some have also described her as an enabler of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s dictatorial ambitions. \u8220\'20\'1CSusie Wiles is way too smart of a human being and way too sophisticated a political operator to not understand,\u8221\'20\'1D Fernand Amandi, a Miami-based Democratic pollster and MSNBC analyst, told Politico.\par \par \uc2 Wiles has little experience in Washington, however, aside from working in the Ronald Regan administration as a scheduler at the labor department and on Capitol Hill for the late congressman Jack Kemp.\par \par \uc2 During Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, the president had a series of chiefs of staff: \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  chair \uc2 Reince Priebus\uc2 , General \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 , former South Carolina representative \uc2 Mick Mulvaney\uc2  and former North Carolina representative \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former president often disagreed with or tired of his appointees. In the weeks before the election, Kelly, the retired marine general, notably said that Trump fits \u8220\'20\'1Cinto the general definition of fascist\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat Julia Brownley re-elected to House\par \par \uc2 Democratic Julia Brownley has won re-election to a US House seat representing California, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Brownley, who previously served in the state assembly for six years, was first elected to the House in 2012. Before her political career, she worked in marketing and sales. Brownley\u8217\'20\'19s district comprises a small part of Los Angeles County and most of Ventura County, including the cities of Oxnard, Santa Paula, Thousand Oaks and Moorpark.\par \par \uc2 She defeated Republican Michael Koslow. The Associated Press declared Brownley the winner at 8.31pm ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 Who is Susie Wiles?\par \par \uc2 Here is our full profile of Susie Wiles, who was named \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new White House chief of staff, by Maanvi Singh :\par \par \uc2 Wiles will be the first woman in history to serve in the role as gatekeeper to the president, a position that typically wields great influence.\par \par \uc2 The chief of staff position is usually the first appointee that a president-elect names, and may oversee the transition from one administration. Once Trump is sworn in as president, Wiles will also be in charge of all White House policy, serving as a confidante and adviser and managing day-to-day affairs.\par \par \uc2 Wiles, 67, is a veteran of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida }}}\uc2  politics who ran Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 and 2020 campaigns in the state and served as his \u8220\'20\'1Cde facto chief of staff\u8221\'20\'1D over the last three years to lead his successful re-election bid and helped him work with lawyers on his various criminal and civil cases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSusie Wiles just helped me achieve one of the greatest political victories in American history, and was an integral part of both my 2016 and 2020 successful campaigns,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CSusie is tough, smart, innovative, and is universally admired and respected.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also mentioned her in his victory speech in Palm Beach, Florida. \u8220\'20\'1CSusie likes to stay sort of in the back, let me tell you. The Ice Maiden. We call her the Ice Maiden,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/susie-wiles-trump-profile"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Susie Wiles: \u8216\'20\'18tough, smart\u8217\'20\'19 operator who led Trump back to the White House }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has confirmed that the US will continue the surge of aid to Ukraine before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  becomes president in January. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s not going to change. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to surge and get that out there to Ukraine. We understand how important it is to make sure they have what they need,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , White House spokesperson.\par \par \uc2 A Guardian editorial on US aid to Ukraine says: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Biden administration is reportedly attempting to expedite as much as $9bn worth of military aid, agreed but not yet transferred. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/nov/07/the-guardian-view-on-ukraine-after-trumps-victory-bracing-for-what-lies-ahead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This is far from straightforward }}}\uc2 , not least because weaponry and ammunition are still being produced and because the next president could stop agreed shipments. But it is essential.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/08/ukraine-war-briefing-biden-administration-confirms-surge-of-military-aid-to-kyiv-will-continue"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine war briefing: Biden administration confirms surge of military aid to Kyiv will continue  }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 After years of negative headlines and post-pandemic economic struggle, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/san-francisco"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 San Francisco }}}\uc2  has picked a wealthy Democratic outsider with no government experience to serve as the city\u8217\'20\'19s new mayor.\par \par \uc2 Daniel Lurie, 47, is one of the heirs to the \uc2 Levi Strauss\uc2  jeans company fortune, and previously spent 15 years as the executive of a San Francisco non-profit he founded. He defeated several Democratic challengers, including the current mayor, London Breed, in an election that was expected to break {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/san-francisco-mayor-elections-tech-elite-money-influence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 local campaign spending records }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lurie poured more than $8m of his own money into his campaign, while his billionaire mother, Mimi Haas, backed him with another $1m. He will be the first San Francisco mayor since 1911 to win office without previously serving in government, making him the city\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cleast experienced mayor in a long time\u8221\'20\'1D, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/sf/article/daniel-lurie-mayor-experience-19841692.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 San Francisco Chronicle reported }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/san-francisco-mayor-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Levi Strauss heir Daniel Lurie elected mayor of San Francisco }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 In 2021, Democrats sacrificed part of Titus\u8217\'20\'19s district \u8211\'20\'13 the party\u8217\'20\'19s traditional stronghold \u8211\'20\'13 in exchange for some gains in neighboring swing districts.\par \par \uc2 Titus, the longest-serving member of the Nevada delegation in Washington DC, has been re-elected every two years since winning her seat in 2013. Robertson, her opponent this year, has never held political office and echoed policies favored by Trump on border security, inflation and the economy.\par \par \uc2 Horsford, meanwhile, became the first Black person to represent Nevada in Congress when he was elected to the House in 2012. He lost in 2014 but has since won in four straight elections.\par \par \uc2 Susie Lee first won her seat in 2018, succeeding now Democratic senator \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 AP hasn\u8217\'20\'19t yet declared a winner in the race for Rosen\u8217\'20\'19s seat in the upper chamber of Congress. It pits her against Republican Sam Brown, a retired army captain whose face is still scarred from injuries he suffered in Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 Johnson said in a statement he was proud of the race he ran, and that he was encouraged by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s decisive victory, the AP reports.\par \par \uc2 John Lee, in a brief phone call with AP, also said he ran a good race and was now \u8220\'20\'1Clooking forward to Trump bringing this nation back around.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Robertson, meanwhile, told AP he had called Titus to congratulate her, saying he respected the will of Nevada voters and that he and Titus spoke about possibly working together \u8220\'20\'1Con a future issue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats retain three US House seats in Nevada\par \par \uc2 Three US House seats in Nevada will remain under Democratic control after a sweeping win Thursday for the incumbents, while the state\u8217\'20\'19s tight Senate race was still too early to call.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has declared Democratic Representatives \uc2 Dina Titus\uc2 , Susie Lee and Steven Horsford winners in their respective races. The state\u8217\'20\'19s lone Republican Congressman, Mark Amodei, cruised to victory Tuesday night in his reliably red district in northern Nevada.\par \par \uc2 Lee won over conservative policy analyst Drew Johnson in what is widely considered the state\u8217\'20\'19s most competitive district, which covers a large swath of the culturally diverse Spring Valley neighborhood in Las Vegas and more rural areas of southern Nevada.\par \par \uc2 Horsford, a four-term congressman who chairs the Congressional Black Caucus, defeated former North Las Vegas mayor John Lee in a district that stretches north from Las Vegas, toward rural Nye county in the west and along the Utah border in the eastern portion of the district.\par \par \uc2 For Titus, it was the second election in a row that she defeated Republican Mark Robertson, a retired army colonel, to keep her seat in the Las Vegas district she has represented for more than a decade.\par \par \uc2 All three incumbents, in separate statements, vowed to continue their work to lower costs in the state and to create more jobs. Their challengers conceded Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 David McCormick wins Pennsylvania Senate seat\par \par \uc2 David McCormick is thanking voters in a brief statement after the Associated Press called the race for him in his bid to oust three-term Democrat Bob Casey.\par \par \uc2 On social media, the former CEO of the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest hedge fund, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThank you, Pennsylvania! Looking forward to representing every citizen of our great commonwealth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThank you, Pennsylvania! Looking forward to representing every citizen of our great Commonwealth ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/o8IkQUYSjY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/o8IkQUYSjY }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2  (@DaveMcCormickPA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DaveMcCormickPA/status/1854662536462774491?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 7, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 The victory pads Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 majority in the Senate, which they wrested from Democratic control this week, and clocked in as the nation\u8217\'20\'19s second-most expensive race.\par \par \uc2 Casey isn\u8217\'20\'19t conceding. His campaign\u8217\'20\'19s pointing to a statement from the state\u8217\'20\'19s top election official saying that at least 100,000 ballots still remained to be counted, including provisional ballots and military and overseas ballots.\par \par \uc2 Casey\u8217\'20\'19s campaign says it\u8217\'20\'19ll \u8220\'20\'1Cmake sure every Pennsylvanian\u8217\'20\'19s voice is heard\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is more on Susie Wiles, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff:\par \par \uc2 Trump has named Susie Wiles, the manager of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/donald-trump-wins-us-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 victorious campaign }}}\uc2 , as his White House chief of staff, the first woman to hold the influential role.\par \par \uc2 Wiles is widely credited within and outside Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inner circle for running what was, by far, his most disciplined and well-executed campaign, and was seen as the leading contender for the position. She largely avoided the spotlight, even refusing to take the mic to speak as Trump celebrated his victory early on Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 Wiles\u8217\'20\'19s hire is Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first major decision as president-elect and one that could be a defining test of his incoming administration, as he must quickly build the team that will help run the federal government. Wiles does not bring government experience to the role, but has a close relationship with the president-elect.\par \par \uc2 She was able to do what few others have been able to: help control Trump\u8217\'20\'19s impulses \u8211\'20\'13 not by chiding him or lecturing, but by earning his respect and showing him that he was better off when he followed her advice than flouting it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSusie is tough, smart, innovative, and is universally admired and respected. Susie will continue to work tirelessly to Make America Great Again,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a well deserved honor to have Susie as the first-ever female Chief of Staff in United States history. I have no doubt that she will make our country proud.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump went through four chiefs of staff \u8211\'20\'13 including one who served in an acting capacity for a year \u8211\'20\'13 during his first administration, part of record-setting personnel churn in his administration.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/trump-susie-wiles-chief-of-staff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump names campaign manager Susie Wiles as his White House chief of staff }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 JD Vance has posted his thoughts on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff pick, Susie Wiles, calling her a \u8220\'20\'1Chuge asset\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ca really good person\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrThis is great news. Susie was a huge asset to President Trump on the campaign and will be a huge asset in the White House. She's also just a really good person. Onward! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Yj1aLYK4So"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Yj1aLYK4So }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 JD Vance (@JDVance) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JDVance/status/1854656937813852476?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 7, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 California \u8216\'20\'18Trump-proofing\u8217\'20\'19 itself against federal reprisal\par \par \uc2 California prided itself on its resistance to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  during his first term as president and will hardly have to scramble to assume the same role a second time around.\par \par \uc2 Indeed, as a bastion of Democratic party strength in a country moving sharply to the right, it has been preparing for this moment for a long time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia will continue to be at the forefront of progress, the fulcrum of democracy, the champion of innovation, and the protector of our rights and freedoms,\u8221\'20\'1D Adam Schiff, the state\u8217\'20\'19s newly elected senator and a frequent target of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s wrath, promised supporters on election night.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  announced a special session of the California legislature to ensure the attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office and other state agencies have the funding they need. \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t sit idle,\u8221\'20\'1D the governor said. \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia has faced this challenge before, and we know how to respond.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Even with Trump out of power since 2021, California has been setting up guardrails to protect its resident\u8217\'20\'19s rights under an adversarial federal government. The state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2022/11/08/us/elections/results-california-proposition-1-constitutional-right-to-reproductive-freedom.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has enshrined \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2  in its constitution, passed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://calmatters.org/politics/elections/2024/11/california-election-result-same-sex-marriage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ballot initiative }}}\uc2  explicitly defending the right of same-sex couples to marry and pushed for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.ca.gov/2024/09/24/governor-newsom-signs-bipartisan-legislation-to-strengthen-californias-gun-laws/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tougher gun laws }}}\uc2  that still adhere to the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s narrow interpretation of the right to bear arms.\par \par \uc2 More here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/california-resistance-state-trump-federal-government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How California has been \u8216\'20\'18Trump-proofing\u8217\'20\'19 itself against federal reprisal }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of defense, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , has urged the military to carry out a smooth transition to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , reminding the force of its responsibility to follow the lawful orders of the next commander in chief, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/live/trump-harris-election-updates-11-7-2024#00000193-08bd-dd3b-abfb-9aff38dd0000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AP reports }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Memos of this kind are not common, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not the first time the Pentagon chief has reminded the military of its constitutional obligations, the AP says, noting, \u8220\'20\'1CIn the context of the incoming president\u8217\'20\'19s suggestion that he may use federal forces at the southern border, and Project 2025 plans to force out career civilians and fill positions with Trump loyalists, the Biden administration has taken unusual steps both to try to insulate those civil servants and to remind the military of its own sworn oaths.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Who is Susie Wiles, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's new chief of staff?\par \par \uc2 Wiles, announced today as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new chief of staff, is a veteran political operative who has been in the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s orbit for years.\par \par \uc2 The 67-year-old, who will be the first woman to be chief of staff for a US president, is the daughter of the late \uc2 NFL\uc2  broadcaster Pat Summerall and one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s longest-serving advisers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/11/07/politics/susie-wiles-trump-chief-of-staff/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN noted }}}\uc2 . She ran his Florida campaigns in 2020 and 2016 and served as a \u8220\'20\'1Cde facto chief of staff\u8221\'20\'1D over the last four years as she helped lead his successful re-election bid.\par \par \uc2 She has been repeatedly credited for his win this week and Trump directly praised her in his victory speech, but she declined to take the mic and comment.\par \par \uc2 Before supporting Trump, she ran \uc2 Rick Scott\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2010 gubernatorial campaign in Florida and briefly served as campaign manager of former Utah governor \uc2 Jon Huntsman\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidential bid in 2012, the AP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/live/trump-harris-election-updates-11-7-2024#00000193-08cc-dd3b-abfb-9aeec51f0000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/15/trump-campaign-leadership"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended Wiles in September }}}\uc2  when there were concerns that the campaign was flailing and he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/26/trump-campaign-palace-intrigue-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeatedly expressed faith in her }}}\uc2  amid reports of an internal power struggle.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/04/08/trump-biden-cabinet-turnover/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 marked by significant turnover }}}\uc2 , including four chiefs of staff. \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s longest serving chief of staff during his first administration, spent the final weeks of this year\u8217\'20\'19s election warning that his former boss was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfascist\u8221\'20\'1D who had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/trump-fascist-reaction-john-kelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 privately and repeatedly praised Hitler }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump announces Susie Wiles as chief of staff\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has announced that Susie Wiles, co-manager of his re-election campaign, will be his chief of staff:\par \par \uc2 Susie Wiles just helped me achieve one of the greatest political victories in American history, and was an integral part of both my 2016 and 2020 successful campaigns \u8230\'20\'26 Susie is tough, smart, innovative, and is universally admired and respected. Susie will continue to work tirelessly to Make America great again. It is a well deserved honor to have Susie as the first-ever female chief of staff in United States history. I have no doubt that she will make our country proud.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wiles is a veteran operative who is seen as playing an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/11/07/us/politics/trump-win-election-harris.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 integral part }}}\uc2  in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s successful bid to reclaim the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re just catching up on the latest developments two days after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decisive victory, here are some key updates from the day so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/election-biden-address-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden promised a smooth transfer of power }}}\uc2  to Trump in an address to the nation, as he implored Americans to \u8220\'20\'1Cbring down the temperature\u8221\'20\'1D of partisan divisions and keep their faith in democratic systems.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/07/election-putin-congratulates-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vladimir Putin congratulated Trump }}}\uc2  on winning the US election, and expressed admiration for the way Trump reacted to an assassination attempt during the campaign.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/trump-blank-check-netanyahu-war-iran-panetta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 give Benjamin Netanyahu a \u8220\'20\'1Cblank check\u8221\'20\'1D in the Middle East }}}\uc2 , possibly opening the way for all-out war between Israel and Iran, the former CIA director and US defense secretary \uc2 Leon Panetta\uc2  predicted.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Americans are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/abortion-pills-hormones-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stockpiling \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills and hormones }}}\uc2  in response to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/us-senate-house-and-governor-elections-2024-results-from-all-50-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Control of the House of Representatives still remains uncertain }}}\uc2  as neither party have secured enough wins yet to security the majority, but Republicans remain ahead.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/election-pennsylvania-senate-race-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican Dave McCormick }}}\uc2  was declared by AP the winner of the Senate race in Pennsylvania in a razor-thin contest, but incumbent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672d33d18f089a6420f07427#block-672d33d18f089a6420f07427"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrat Bob Casey has not yet conceded }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said there was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672d1e868f089a6420f0739d#block-672d1e868f089a6420f0739d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cno price tag\u8221\'20\'1D for his mass deportation plan }}}\uc2 , which he indicated would be a priority.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Federal Reserve chair, \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672d1c5e8f083dc4c0059c73#block-672d1c5e8f083dc4c0059c73"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he will not resign if Donald Trump requests it }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672cf8948f08cfbf3817c1b3#block-672cf8948f08cfbf3817c1b3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called the legislature into a special session }}}\uc2  to the prepare the most populous state for the fight against Trump.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nevada and Arizona still remained {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/06/us-election-results-map-2024-live-donald-trump-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 too close to call in the presidential race }}}\uc2 , though Trump was leading in both key swing states.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic incumbent Bob Casey not conceding in Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Even though the Associated Press has called the Pennsylvania Senate race for Republican \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2 , the campaign of Bob Casey is not yet conceding.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Casey insisted that thousands of ballots remained uncounted as of Thursday, when McCormick led the race by 0.5 points.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the Pennsylvania secretary of state said this afternoon, there are tens of thousands of ballots across the Commonwealth still to count, which includes provisional ballots, military and overseas ballots and mail ballots,\u8221\'20\'1D Maddy McDaniel, Casey spokesperson, said in a new statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis race is within half a point and cannot be called while the votes of thousands of Pennsylvanians are still being counted. We will make sure every Pennsylvanian\u8217\'20\'19s voice is heard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A breakdown of popular vote margins in 2020 and 2024\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at how the popular vote margins shifted from 2020 to 2024 in Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 favor, helping Trump flip key states and secure victory.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2024/11/archive-6-zip/giv-4559Ncw1TzwcJG2V/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2  ousts Democrat in Pennsylvania Senate\par \par \uc2 The Republican \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2  won the Senate race in the battleground state of Pennsylvania on Thursday, denying the Democratic incumbent, Bob Casey, a fourth term and expanding his party\u8217\'20\'19s majority in the upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 When the Associated Press called the race at 4.09pm ET on Thursday, two days after polls closed in Pennsylvania, McCormick led by 0.4 points. The narrow margin raised the possibility of a recount, although his victory is expected to stand given his lead of roughly 30,000 votes.\par \par \uc2 With McCormick\u8217\'20\'19s victory, Republicans have now secured at least 53 seats in the Senate, erasing Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 previous majority in the chamber. Two Senate races in Nevada and Arizona remained too close to call as of Thursday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/election-pennsylvania-senate-race-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania Senate election: Republican Dave McCormick wins seat }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Protesters gathered at Trump Tower in Chicago\par \par \uc2 At least 200 people gathered outside the Trump International Hotel and Tower in Chicago on Wednesday night to protest \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election and call for an end to the war in Gaza. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a video and some photos:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made inroads in two Michigan cities that are home to some of the largest Arab American and Muslim communities in the United States, after those voters grew disenchanted with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over his support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 In addition to winning Michigan overall, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/11/06/trump-wins-dearborn-and-makes-gains-in-hamtramck/76085841007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Detroit Free Press reports }}}\uc2  that Trump was the pick of most voters in Dearborn, and performed well in Hamtramck \u8211\'20\'13 both cities where many people of Middle Eastern descent live.\par \par \uc2 In previous elections, Democrats had performed well in those communities, but Biden\u8217\'20\'19s decision to supply Israel with weapons it has used in Gaza and, more recently, Lebanon, sparked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/03/muslim-arab-american-reject-biden-outreach-michigan-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a sustained backlash }}}\uc2  that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/arab-muslim-americans-vote-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extended to his vice-president,  }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/arab-muslim-americans-vote-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris }}}\uc2  . Trump has said little about how he would handle Israel\u8217\'20\'19s conflicts as president, but was supportive of \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s government during his first term, and also implemented a ban on travelers from several majority Muslim countries.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about the backlash Harris faced in Michigan, from the \uc2 Free Press\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 In Dearborn, where 55% of the residents are of Middle Eastern descent, Trump won with 42.48% of the vote over Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who received 36.26%, according to results, with 100% of precincts counted, provided to the Free Press from City Clerk George Darany. Jill Stein received 18.37% of the vote. Voter turnout in Dearborn was smaller compared to 2020.\par \par \uc2 Trump also won in Dearborn Heights, where 39% of the residents are of Middle Eastern descent, defeating Harris 44% to 38.3%, with Stein at 15.1%.\par \par \uc2 In the November 2020 election, Biden received 68.8% in Dearborn while Trump received 29.9%. Muslim voters interviewed Tuesday at polling sites said they were disappointed with the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s attacks and also preferred Trump\u8217\'20\'19s views on economics.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 In Hamtramck, Trump also had a substantial increase in support, but Harris won the working-class city that has the highest percentage of immigrants among cities in Michigan. In November 2020, Biden won Hamtramck, winning with 85.4% of the vote over Trump, who only got 13.4%.\par \par \uc2 With 100% of the vote counted, Harris got 46.2% in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election in Hamtramck, a significant decrease from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 85% four years ago, while Trump got 42.7% and Jill Stein was at 8.96%, according to results provided to the Free Press by City Clerk Rana Faraj.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Now that he\u8217\'20\'19s heading back to the White House, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will need a chief of staff \u8211\'20\'13 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/susie-wiles-frontrunner-trump-white-house-chief-staff-rcna179124"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports }}}\uc2  that Susie Wiles, a co-manager of his successful re-election campaign, is among the top contenders for the job.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19d be the first female White House chief of staff ever, if Trump picks her. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18She has commanded a ton of respect amongst the staff, as well as loyalty. She doesn\u8217\'20\'19t play games. And she means what she says: On the campaign, she said we are checking egos at the door and held everyone to it,\u8217\'20\'19 said one campaign official, who, like others in this piece, was granted anonymity to speak candidly or because they were not authorized to speak on the record. \u8216\'20\'18The team of rivals concept did not apply here.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Susie is as good as they get,\u8217\'20\'19 a second Trump campaign official said. \u8216\'20\'18She ran a great campaign and has the respect of all \u8211\'20\'13 including Democrats who recognize her talent. She\u8217\'20\'19d make for a great chief of staff and would serve at the president\u8217\'20\'19s pleasure. After all, it is his White House.\u8217\'20\'19 A third Trump campaign official said Wiles is already playing the de-facto chief of staff role and that staffers widely want her to get the job. A large staff meeting is taking place at the campaign headquarters on Thursday, and Wiles will lead it.\par \par \uc2 The sense among advisers is that if Trump makes a strong appeal to Wiles, she would take the job \u8211\'20\'13 and it is widely hoped she will.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18If she wants it, it\u8217\'20\'19s hers,\u8217\'20\'19 said an adviser familiar with the discussions. \u8216\'20\'18Her standing with Trump and what she just helped pull off [winning by huge margins], makes it an easy choice if she wants it.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to focus on government funding, hurricane relief in final weeks as president\par \par \uc2 With the clock ticking toward the end of his presidency, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will focus on keeping the government funded and open, pass the National Defense Authorization Act (NDAA), rush assistance to communities battered by hurricanes Helene and Milton, as well as confirm judicial nominees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s going to be certainly our focus in the next 74 days,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , told reporters.\par \par \uc2 She repeatedly declined to engage in questions about whether Biden felt partly responsible for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s loss, whether he had any regrets about his decision to seek re-election or whether he believed he might have beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had he remained in the race.\par \par \uc2 Stating what she said was \u8220\'20\'1Cjust a fact\u8221\'20\'1D, Jean-Pierre pushed back on the accusation that it was arrogant for the 81-year-old president to run for a second term: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the president who has been the only person [who] has been able to beat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She repeated that Biden believes his decision to \u8220\'20\'1Cpass the torch\u8221\'20\'1D to his vice-president was the right one. \u8220\'20\'1CShe was the right person for the job,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said.\par \par \uc2 She also cited the global post-pandemic headwinds that have doomed incumbent parties around the world.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt had a political toll on many incumbents. That\u8217\'20\'19s part of what you saw,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'No price tag' for mass deportation plan, Trump says in interview\par \par \uc2 Speaking to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/trump-says-no-price-tag-mass-deportation-plan-rcna179178"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News }}}\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made clear that the mass deportations of undocumented immigrants that he campaigned on will be a top priority of his administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe obviously have to make the border strong and powerful and, and we have to \u8211\'20\'13 at the same time, we want people to come into our country,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, adding that, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not somebody that says, \u8216\'20\'18No, you can\u8217\'20\'19t come in.\u8217\'20\'19 We want people to come in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 NBC asked about how he would pay for the plan, which immigration experts believe would be beyond the current capacities of the federal government agencies who deal with immigration. Trump replied:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not a question of a price tag. It\u8217\'20\'19s not \u8211\'20\'13 really, we have no choice. When people have killed and murdered, when drug lords have destroyed countries and now they\u8217\'20\'19re going to go back to those countries because they\u8217\'20\'19re not staying here. There is no price tag.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  is loathe to comment on political issues, and kept that up today, when asked for his reaction to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s criticism of his tenure leading the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , and the impact it may have on its independence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not going to get into any of the political things here today, but thank you,\u8221\'20\'1D the central bank chief said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  chair says he will not resign if asked by Trump\par \par \uc2 The Federal Reserve chair, \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , says he will not resign if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  requests it.\par \par \uc2 Trump appointed Powell, a Republican, to his first term leading the central bank, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  renominated him in 2021. But during his first administration, Trump called the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s rate-setting committee \u8220\'20\'1Cboneheads\u8221\'20\'1D for not cutting rates aggressively enough, and has said he should have a role in controlling rates \u8211\'20\'13 threatening the independence of the central bank.\par \par \uc2 In his press conference held after the committee announced a quarter-point cut in interest rates, Powell was asked if he would resign at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s request. Some advisors to the president-elect have proposed replacing Powell before his term is up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo,\u8221\'20\'1D the central bank chief replied.\par \par \uc2 He again said \u8220\'20\'1Cno,\u8221\'20\'1D when asked if he believed he had no legal requirement to leave the post when asked.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At a press conference, the Federal Reserve chair, \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , was asked how the central bank would react to potentially inflationary policies from the second Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 Trump has said he will impose tariffs on imported goods, which many economists argue will increase prices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the near term the election will have no effects on our policy decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D said Powell. \u8220\'20\'1CMany, many things affect the economy \u8230\'20\'26 We don\u8217\'20\'19t guess, we don\u8217\'20\'19t speculate and we don\u8217\'20\'19t assume.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  cuts interest rates again, shifting from fighting inflation to defending labor market\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  has cut interest rates further, saying progress has been made against the wave of inflation that struck the United States during \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, which was likely a major factor in voters choosing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the next president.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, the central bank\u8217\'20\'19s rate-setting Federal Open Market Committee pointed to the need to support the labor market in cutting its benchmark interest rate by a quarter percentage point to the 4.5% to 4.75% range. Government data released in recent months has shown a slowdown in hiring and uptick in unemployment, even as economic growth has remained strong.\par \par \uc2 The Fed raised interest rates to their highest levels in decades as consumer prices climbed at rates not seen since the 1980s over the past three years. But inflation has eased recently, and the Fed began lowering rates with a half-point cut in September.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s approval ratings dropped as inflation rose, with voters citing the unaffordability of groceries, gas and housing as one of their top issues. Those concerns paved the way for the re-election of Trump, who has campaigned on cutting taxes and expanding oil and gas production.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Putin calls Trump 'courageous man' for surviving assassination attempt\par \par \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  also praised \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for surviving an assassination attempt during his rally in Pennsylvania in July, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHis behavior at the time of the attempt on his life made an impression on me,\u8221\'20\'1D Putin said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe turned out to be a courageous man. And it\u8217\'20\'19s not just about the raised hand and the call to fight for his and their common ideals... He behaved, in my opinion, in a very correct way, courageously, like a man.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After being pulled to the ground by Secret Service agents when a gunman opened fire as he was speaking at an outdoor rally, Trump stood up and, pumping his fist in the air, yelled, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/19/donald-trump-rnc-speech-american-messiah-with-swagger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFight! Fight! Fight!\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  It became a rallying cry at his rallies in his successful campaign to return to the presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports that \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  did not reveal his expectations for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s second term, but said he was interested in his proposal to end the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Trump has made a vague promise to end the conflict that began when Russia invaded its neighbor within \u8220\'20\'1C24 hours\u8221\'20\'1D of becoming president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know what will happen now, I have no idea,\u8221\'20\'1D Putin responded, when asked about his expectations of Trump. He added that the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s statements \u8220\'20\'1Cabout the desire to restore relations with Russia, to help end the Ukrainian crisis, in my opinion, deserves attention at least\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Putin congratulates Trump on election win, says he's ready to talk\par \par \uc2 The Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on winning the US presidential election, and said he was willing to talk to him, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would like to congratulate him on his election as president,\u8221\'20\'1D Putin said in Sochi, a resort on the Black Sea.\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/27/trump-zelenskyy-meet-high-stakes-ukraine-talks-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promised to quickly end }}}\uc2  the war in Ukraine, which began when Russia invaded in February 2022, but has not said how. During his first term, Trump was known for a relationship with Putin that many viewed as uncomfortably close for a leader of one of the US\u8217\'20\'19s top global rivals, and last month, investigative journalist Bob Woodward revealed that Trump sent Russia Covid-19 testing machines during a period in 2020 when they were scarce:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/08/trump-putin-covid-test-machines-bob-woodward"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump secretly gave Putin Covid test machines, Bob Woodward book says }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican Rob Bresnahan won election to a US House seat representing Pennsylvania today, defeating the Democratic representative \uc2 Matt Cartwright\uc2 , the Associated Press reports after calling the race.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have long sought to unseat Cartwright in this Scranton-based seat.\par \par \uc2 Bresnahan is a first-time candidate and the CEO of an electrical contracting company founded by his grandfather.\par \par \uc2 Cartwright has represented the district for six terms. The AP declared Bresnahan the winner at 1.46pm Eastern Standard Time.\par \par \uc2 Scranton is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s birthplace and the county scraped out a win for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in this election, while she lost Pennsylvania and the presidential race to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans }}}\uc2  this week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/senate-elections-republicans-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won }}}\uc2  a majority in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/house-representatives-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  whether they have control }}}\uc2  of the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives }}}\uc2  remains unclear, with many of the most competitive races still uncalled.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former New York mayor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jan/19/rudy-giuliani-president-white-house-2008"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential candidate }}}\uc2  and lawyer for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , has been engaging in \u8220\'20\'1Cdelay and then evasion\u8221\'20\'1D over surrendering assets to help cover the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/15/rudy-giuliani-pay-damages-election-workers-defamation-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $148m judgment }}}\uc2  against him in favor of two Georgia election workers he defamed, a Manhattan court heard earlier today.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani told the judge in the case that he\u8217\'20\'19d been \u8220\'20\'1Ctreated rudely\u8221\'20\'1D by those trying to seize his property and belongings.\par \par \uc2 As the legal wrangling goes on, a recap that Ruby Freeman and Shaye Moss faced an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/12/rudy-giuliani-election-workers-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 avalanche of abuse }}}\uc2  from the right, including death threats, after Giuliani accused them of sneaking ballots in suitcases during the fraught 2020 presidential election count in Georgia, and also of counting ballots multiple times and interfering with voting machines. They {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/13/rudy-giuliani-defamation-trial-georgia-third-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued him }}}\uc2  for defamation and won.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The possessions that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/rudygiuliani"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rudy Giuliani }}}\uc2  is obliged to surrender {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/30/georgia-election-workers-giuliani-assets-defamation-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 against his }}}\uc2  court-ordered $148m payment to the Georgia election workers he defamed include his $5m Upper East Side apartment, a 1980 Mercedes once owned by the movie star Lauren Bacall, a shirt signed by the \uc2 New York Yankees\uc2  legend Joe DiMaggio, dozens of luxury watches and other valuables.\par \par \uc2 Judge Lewis Liman ordered Giuliani to hand over the Mercedes by Monday, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Liman originally scheduled a phone conference about the situation, but he changed it to a hearing in Manhattan federal court that Giuliani must attend after learning about the visit to the former mayor\u8217\'20\'19s apartment.\par \par \uc2 Aaron Nathan, an attorney for the election workers, wrote in a letter to Liman that the residence was already \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantially empty\u8221\'20\'1D when representatives for his clients visited with a moving company official to assess the transportation and storage needs for the property Giuliani was ordered to surrender.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/rudy-giuliani-defamation-georgia-election-workers-mercedes-benz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Giuliani shows up to vote in Mercedes he was supposed to give to poll workers }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A combative \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  said a civil case to take his most prized assets was like \u8220\'20\'1Ca political persecution\u8221\'20\'1D before he entered a New York courthouse earlier today to explain to a federal judge why he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t surrendered his valuables by the 29 October deadline as part of a $148m defamation judgment.\par \par \uc2 The judge, Lewis Liman, ordered the former New York City mayor to report to court after lawyers for the two former Georgia election workers, Ruby Freeman and her daughter, Wandrea \u8220\'20\'1CShaye\u8221\'20\'1D Moss, who were awarded the massive judgment, visited Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s Manhattan apartment last week to discover it had been cleared out weeks earlier, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Every bit of property that they want is available, if they are entitled to it. Now, the law says they\u8217\'20\'19re not entitled to a lot of them. For example, they want my grandfather\u8217\'20\'19s watch, which is 150 years old. That\u8217\'20\'19s a bit of an heirloom. Usually you don\u8217\'20\'19t get those unless you\u8217\'20\'19re involved in a political persecution. In fact, having me here today is like a political persecution,\u8217\'20\'19 Giuliani told reporters as he arrived at court in Manhattan.\par \par \uc2 During the court proceeding, which lasted over an hour, a lawyer for Freeman and Moss and a lawyer for Giuliani disputed whether the longtime politican had done all he could to turn over assets. More details to follow.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  reflected on the defeat of his vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, saying in a speech from the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672ce9f78f089a6420f070b6#block-672ce9f78f089a6420f070b6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he will }}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Censure a peaceful and orderly transition\u8221\'20\'1D to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672cea788f08cfbf3817c0c3#block-672cea788f08cfbf3817c0c3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling on the country }}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cbring down the temperature\u8221\'20\'1D. Several {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672cc0e28f08622c7b94f0c6#block-672cc0e28f08622c7b94f0c6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 key races }}}\uc2  remain to be called, including the presidential outcomes in swing states Arizona and Nevada (where Trump is tipped to win), Senate races in those two states plus Pennsylvania and, perhaps most importantly, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672cbc298f088ef67e7e1bad#block-672cbc298f088ef67e7e1bad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 control of the House }}}\uc2 . Based on analyses of election results so far, it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672cced98f08622c7b94f195#block-672cced98f08622c7b94f195"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appears that Trump won }}}\uc2  by driving out the Republican base and making gains among certain groups that typically back Democrats. But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672cfb398f083dc4c0059ab2#block-672cfb398f083dc4c0059ab2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 split-ticket voters stepped up }}}\uc2  for Democratic senators and a governor in swing states, reducing their losses in what was otherwise a rough election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sentencing in his business fraud trial scheduled for later this month? Probably not happening, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672cd8278f088ef67e7e1d58#block-672cd8278f088ef67e7e1d58"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , the California governor and potential presidential candidate some day, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672cf8948f08cfbf3817c1b3#block-672cf8948f08cfbf3817c1b3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called }}}\uc2  the legislature into a special session to prepare to fight Trump.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672cdbed8f088ef67e7e1d99#block-672cdbed8f088ef67e7e1d99"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aired grievances }}}\uc2  over Harris\u8217\'20\'19s election loss, with many pointing the finger at Biden and his aborted attempt at a second term.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672cb3a08f0808f2b62a551c#block-672cb3a08f0808f2b62a551c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are stockpiling }}}\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory seems set to put foes of the procedure into positions of power.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris was unable to settle on an effective message against Trump, and was hobbled from the start by Biden\u8217\'20\'19s low approval ratings, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris?page=with:block-672cd4278f088ef67e7e1d16#block-672cd4278f088ef67e7e1d16"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times postmortem }}}\uc2  of her campaign finds.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump might be back, but split-ticket voters limited Democratic losses in historic election\par \par \uc2 Democrats have been described as heading for the political wilderness after voters nationwide rejected \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Tuesday and voted out enough of the party\u8217\'20\'19s senators to return the GOP to the majority in the chamber. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s allies believe they are course to again control the House, though ballot counting in key races is ongoing.\par \par \uc2 But Democrats were saved from an even-worse wipeout by split-ticket voters across swing states who supported the party\u8217\'20\'19s down-ballot candidates even while rejecting Harris. Consider the following races that the Associated Press has called:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 North Carolina voters gave Trump 51.1% of the vote, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-results-north-carolina-governor-mark-robinson-josh-stein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed Democratic attorney  }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-results-north-carolina-governor-mark-robinson-josh-stein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Josh Stein }}}\uc2  for governor over Mark Robinson, the lieutenant-governor who once called himself a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michigan voters broke for Trump with 49.8% of the vote, but also narrowly elected Democrat \uc2 Elissa Slotkin\uc2  to the Senate with 48.6% of the vote over her challenger Mike Rogers \u8217\'20\'19s 48.3%.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 It was a bit more comfortable for Democratic senator \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  in Wisconsin, a state Trump won with 49.7% of the vote. Baldwin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/election-wisconsin-senate-baldwin-hovde"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won re-election }}}\uc2  with 49.4% support, over Republican \uc2 Eric Hovde\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 48.5%.\par \par \uc2 The AP has not yet called the outcomes of the presidential or Senate races in Arizona and Nevada. Trump appears likely to win both states, though Democratic Senate candidates \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  in Arizona and \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2  in Nevada both seem poised for victory. Jon Ralston, the authoritative Nevada political analyst, has a look at how split-ticket voters are making the difference for Rosen in that state:\par \par \uc2 enltrNV numbers tell an amazing story:\par \par \uc2 Trump: +51K over Harris, or just over 3.5% -- 17K voted for none of the above\par \par \uc2 Brown: -13K losing to Rosen, -1%--39K (!) voted for NOTA\par \par \uc2 Trump has 67K (!) more votes than Brown.\par \par \uc2 You can hug MAGA all you want, but only Trump is Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jon Ralston (@RalstonReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RalstonReports/status/1854564973437178206?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 7, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 The one swing state where the GOP appears to be about to gain a Senate seat is Pennsylvania. The state went to Trump, but the AP has not called its Senate race, where Democratic incumbent Bob Casey is narrowly behind his Republican challenger, David McCormick, in ballots that have been counted so far.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Newsom calls California legislature into special session to ready for Trump's return\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , has called the legislature into a special session to the prepare the most populous state for the fight against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s second administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe freedoms we hold dear in California are under attack \u8211\'20\'13 and we won\u8217\'20\'19t sit idle. California has faced this challenge before, and we know how to respond. We are prepared, and we will do everything necessary to ensure Californians have the support and resources they need to thrive,\u8221\'20\'1D said Newsom, a rising star in the Democratic party who is viewed as having presidential ambitions.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are the strongest party in California, and control both chambers of its legislature in Sacramento. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.gov.ca.gov/2024/11/07/special-session-ca-values/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Newsom\u8217\'20\'19s office said }}}\uc2  lawmakers would be asked to pass legislation that will allow the state to pursue lawsuits against the policies that Trump is expected to enact:\par \par \uc2 The special session responds to the public statements and proposals put forward by President-elect Trump and his advisors, and actions taken during his first term in office \u8211\'20\'13 an agenda that could erode essential freedoms and individual rights, including women\u8217\'20\'19s rights and LGBTQ+ rights. A special session allows for expedited action that will best protect California and its values from attacks. The special session will begin December 2, when the Legislature convenes.\par \par \uc2 The Governor has outlined several urgent priorities to be defended in this special session by bolstering legal defenses against federal actions. The Governor\u8217\'20\'19s proclamation calls for legislation to provide additional resources to the \uc2 California Department of Justice\uc2  and other state entities to pursue robust affirmative litigation against any unlawful actions by the incoming Trump Administration, as well as defend against federal lawsuits aimed at undermining California\u8217\'20\'19s laws and policies. The funding will support the ability to immediately file litigation and seek injunctive relief against unlawful federal actions.\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  won the state\u8217\'20\'19s 54 electoral votes and voters sent Democrat Adam Schiff to the Senate, California may also be where Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes of winning the House die. The state is home to several closely fought House districts, where Republicans have hung on to their seats thanks to split-ticket voters. Counting is ongoing in many of these districts, and it remains to be seen if enough Democrats can win to give the party the majority in the US House, and thus the ability to block Trump from passing legislation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The former New York City mayor and Democratic presidential candidate \uc2 Michael Bloomberg\uc2  shared a few thoughts about why \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  failed in keeping \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from returning to the White House.\par \par \uc2 They come at the end of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2024-11-06/michael-bloomberg-donald-trump-once-again"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a column }}}\uc2  published by his eponymous news agency where \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  lays out his policy recommendations to Trump for his second term:\par \par \uc2 Democrats, for their part, might ask themselves how exactly they lost to Trump, an ailing 78-year-old who much of the country despises. It probably wasn\u8217\'20\'19t great to cover up President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s infirmities until they became undeniable on live TV. It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t ideal that party elders replaced him with Harris, a nominee who had received no electoral votes and had failed decisively in a previous presidential run.\par \par \uc2 But for now, the country will simply need to deal with Trump, and begin to restrain his worst excesses, one more time.\par \par \uc2 Dealing with a reckless president is an exhausting job, but it can and must be done \u8211\'20\'13 and it\u8217\'20\'19s a job for members of both parties.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 If there\u8217\'20\'19s any silver lining for Democrats in this election, it might be found in the House, and even then, it may not add up to much.\par \par \uc2 Control of the House has not been decided, but based on how key races are trending, the GOP is generally viewed as having a better chance at keeping its small majority than Democrats are of gaining one.\par \par \uc2 The chamber\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic minority leader, \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , just released a brief statement acknowledging that reality, noting that races in a few western states where counting is still ongoing are likely to determine the majority:\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  are remarkable public servants who ran an inspired and positive campaign focused on lifting people up. We look forward to our continued partnership on behalf of the American people in the next chapter of their public service journey.\par \par \uc2 It has yet to be decided who will control the House of Representatives in the 119th Congress. We must count every vote and wait until the results in Oregon, Arizona and California are clear.\par \par \uc2 I am proud that the Democratic Party does not believe in election denial. Our Democracy is precious and it involves elevating public trust in our system of free and fair elections, not undermining it.\par \par \uc2 We cannot love America only when we win.\par \par \uc2 The American people have spoken. I congratulate President-elect \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s final words were a promise to keep fighting in the final weeks of his presidency, and an exhortation to his supporters to do the same.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTogether, we\u8217\'20\'19ve changed America for the better. Now, we have 74 days to finish the term, our term. Let\u8217\'20\'19s make every day count. That\u8217\'20\'19s the responsibility we have to the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSetbacks are unavoidable, but giving up is unforgivable. We all get knocked down, but the measure of our character, as my dad would say, is how quickly we get back up. Remember, a defeat does not mean we are defeated. We lost this battle. The America of your dreams is calling for you to get back up. That\u8217\'20\'19s the story of America for over 240 years and counting. It\u8217\'20\'19s a story for all of us, not just some of us. The American experiment endures. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to be okay, but we need to stay engaged.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 With Democrats in retreat, Biden defends 'historic presidency', acknowledges party is 'hurting'\par \par \uc2 As he wrapped up his speech, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  directed a few words at his fellow Democrats, who on Tuesday saw their candidate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  defeated and their lawmakers lose control of the Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know it\u8217\'20\'19s a difficult time. You\u8217\'20\'19re hurting. I hear you and I see you, but don\u8217\'20\'19t forget, don\u8217\'20\'19t forget all that we accomplished. It\u8217\'20\'19s been a historic presidency, not because I\u8217\'20\'19m president, because what we\u8217\'20\'19ve done, what you\u8217\'20\'19ve done,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 He then appeared to defend his own policies, saying:\par \par \uc2 Much of the work we\u8217\'20\'19ve done is already being felt by the American people, but the vast majority of it will not be felt \u8230\'20\'26 over the next 10 years \u8230\'20\'26 We have legislation we passed that\u8217\'20\'19s just only now, just really kicking in. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to see over a trillion dollars worth of infrastructure work done, changing people\u8217\'20\'19s lives in rural communities and communities that are in real difficulty.\par \par \uc2 However, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his Republican allies in Congress could vote to undo Biden\u8217\'20\'19s legislative accomplishments \u8211\'20\'13 something the Democratic president nodded to.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe road ahead is clear, assuming we sustain it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden says American election system 'can be trusted' and urges people to 'bring down temperature'\par \par \uc2 Nodding to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s baseless insistence that he fraudulently lost the 2020 election, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he hopes Trump\u8217\'20\'19s re-election on Tuesday puts to rest doubts about the fairness of US elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomething to hope we can do, no matter who you voted for, is see each other not as adversaries, but as fellow Americans. Bring down the temperature,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI also hope we can lay to rest the question about the integrity of the American electoral system. It is honest, it is fair, and it is transparent, and it can be trusted, win or lose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden added that, \u8220\'20\'1CI also hope we can restore the respect for all our election workers who busted their necks and took risks,\u8221\'20\'1D and likened their work to his duties in his final weeks in office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the outset, we should thank them. Thank them for staffing voting sites, counting the votes, protecting the very integrity of the election. Many of them are volunteers who do it simply out of love for their country. And, as they did, as they did their duty as citizens, I will do my duty as president. I will fulfill my oath, and I will honor the constitution. On January 20, we\u8217\'20\'19ll have a peaceful transfer of power here in America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden says he will 'ensure a peaceful and orderly transition' to Trump\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  says he has instructed his officials to ensure there are no hiccups in the transition to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s second administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYesterday, I spoke with president-elect Trump to congratulate him on his victory, and I assured him that I direct my entire administration to work with his team to ensure a peaceful and orderly transition. That\u8217\'20\'19s what the American people deserve,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden speaks from White House on transition to Trump\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has just begun speaking from the White House, where he is set to address the transition to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s second administration.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know what the outgoing president has to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporters have just been let into the Rose Garden, where \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will soon address the nation on the results of the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 There is a healthy crowd of journalists here to see Biden, who campaigned for his vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  after withdrawing from the race in July.\par \par \uc2 enltrJoe Biden will soon speak in the White House Rose Garden to address the results of the presidential race and the transfer of power to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/54qLDVPcsN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/54qLDVPcsN }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1854558595968377302?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 7, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech from the White House about the transition to a second Trump administration was supposed to start at 11am, but the president is late.\par \par \uc2 We will let you know when he begins talking.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bob Casey, Democratic senator, continues to trail his Republican opponent, \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2 , in Pennsylvania, but the incumbent\u8217\'20\'19s campaign remains confident in his re-election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe count in Pennsylvania is still continuing. Yesterday, the vote margin shrunk by 50,000 votes and this race is now within half a point, the threshold for automatic recounts in Pennsylvania,\u8221\'20\'1D Maddy McDaniel, a spokesperson for Casey, said in a newly released statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith tens of thousands more votes to be counted, we are committed to ensuring every Pennsylvanian\u8217\'20\'19s vote is heard and confident that at the end of that process, senator Casey will be re-elected.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As of this morning, Casey still trailed McCormick by about 30,000 votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Independent senator Angus King has won re-election in Maine, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The victory by King, who caucuses with the Democrats, was not unexpected in a state that leans blue. The party is nonetheless in the minority in the next Congress, having lost Senate seats representing West Virginia, Ohio and Montana. Democrats may also lose another seat in Pennsylvania, though that race has not yet been called.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Politico\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2024/11/07/trump-returns-and-so-does-the-drama-00188123?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 morning Playbook newsletter }}}\uc2  was rife with Democrats pointing the finger at each other over \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election loss.\par \par \uc2 But there was one name repeated more than many others: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Politico heard from several plugged-in Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 though note that all of them are former advisors to top politicians, not current ones \u8211\'20\'13 who say the president set the stage for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s return by pursuing re-election amid broad unpopularity, then calling his campaign off at the last moment. From Playbook:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C He shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have run,\u8221\'20\'1D said JIM MANLEY , a top aide to former Senate Majority Leader HARRY REID. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is no time to pull punches or be concerned about anyone\u8217\'20\'19s feelings. He and his staff have done an enormous amount of damage to this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere was a Biden weariness,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 JAMES ZOGBY\uc2 , a three-decade veteran of the DNC. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd he hung on too long.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[Harris] ran an extraordinary campaign with a very tough hand that was handed to her,\u8221\'20\'1D said MARK LONGABAUGH, a former Sanders adviser. \u8220\'20\'1CThe truth of the matter is, Biden should have stepped aside earlier and let the party put together a longer game plan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump's re-election means judge unlikely to sentence him over business fraud conviction - report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s sentencing scheduled for later this month on the business fraud charges he was convicted of in New York is unlikely to happen, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/11/06/trump-sentencing-probably-wont-happen-00187999?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump was convicted in May on 34 felony counts related to falsifying business documents, but his lawyers have managed to get his sentencing date delayed twice. Now, he\u8217\'20\'19s the president-elect, and legal experts that Politico spoke to say that it\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely judge Juan Merchan will go through with sentencing him on 26 November:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think any reasonable judge wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t sentence the president-elect,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jill Konviser, a retired New York trial judge.\par \par \uc2 Imposing a sentence now \u8212\'20\'14 even a non-prison sentence like home confinement, probation or community service \u8212\'20\'14 would interfere with the soon-to-be president\u8217\'20\'19s duties, legal experts say.\par \par \uc2 In theory, the judge who presided over the hush money trial, Justice Juan Merchan, could try to proceed with the sentencing as scheduled and order that any sentence be deferred until 2029, when Trump will complete his term. But even that would pose problems, as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers are sure to argue that hauling the president-elect into a state courtroom in the middle of the presidential transition would impede the orderly transfer of power.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHis lawyers will say he\u8217\'20\'19s busy with the transition and therefore he won\u8217\'20\'19t show up, and they will ask that any sentencing be adjourned until after the presidency,\u8221\'20\'1D predicted former prosecutor Catherine Christian.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/11/07/us/politics/trump-win-election-harris.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The New York Times }}}\uc2  has its own look at how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  lost, focusing on decisions made by their respective campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign was his most disciplined yet, even if he continued his streak of making surprising and unguarded statements in public. Harris, meanwhile, couldn\u8217\'20\'19t quite settle on a winning message, and began her campaign at a disadvantage owing to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s unpopularity. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump successfully harnessed the anger and frustration millions of Americans felt about some of the very institutions and systems he will soon control as the country\u8217\'20\'19s 47th president. Voters unhappy with the nation\u8217\'20\'19s direction turned him into a vessel for their rage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe elites cannot come to grips with how alienated they are from the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Newt Gingrich, the former House speaker, an informal adviser to the former and now future president.\par \par \uc2 But more than just broad societal forces were at play. His victory owed, in part, to strategic decisions by a campaign operation that was his most stable yet and was held together for nearly four years by a veteran operative, Susie Wiles \u8212\'20\'14 even if the candidate himself was, for much of 2024, as erratic as ever.\par \par \uc2 The Trump team {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/15/us/politics/trump-campaign-costs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 schemed ways to save its cash }}}\uc2  for a final ad blitz, abandoning a traditional ground game to turn out its voters and relying instead on a relatively small paid staff buttressed by volunteers and outsiders, including the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . Mr. Trump relentlessly pushed to define Ms. Harris not just as radically liberal but as foolishly out of the mainstream. The inspiration, his advisers said, was a memorable Nixon-era saying by the Republican strategist Arthur Finkelstein: \u8220\'20\'1CA crook\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 or, in Mr. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s case, a convict \u8212\'20\'14 \u8220\'20\'1Calways beats a fool.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s aides gambled on mobilizing men, though men vote less than women, and it paid off. And they gambled on trying to cut into Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 typically big margins among Black and Latino voters, and that paid off, too.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 How Mr. Trump won is also the story of how Ms. Harris lost.\par \par \uc2 She was hobbled by President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s low approval ratings and struggled to break from him in the eyes of voters yearning for a change in direction. She had only three-plus months to reintroduce herself to the country and she vacillated until the end with how \u8212\'20\'14 and how much \u8212\'20\'14 to talk about Mr. Trump.\par \par \uc2 First, she and her running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , tried minimizing him by mocking him as \u8220\'20\'1Cweird\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cunserious,\u8221\'20\'1D setting aside Mr. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s grave warnings that Mr. Trump was an existential threat to American democracy. Then she focused on a populist message: Mr. Trump cared only about his rich friends, while she would bring down the prices of groceries and housing for ordinary people. Finally, late in the campaign, Ms. Harris pivoted again: Mr. Trump was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfascist,\u8221\'20\'1D she warned \u8212\'20\'14 just the existential threat Mr. Biden had invoked.\par \par \uc2 Some finger-pointing emerged from the wreckage, including over whether Ms. Harris had focused too much on appealing to wayward Republicans or whether Mr. Biden had dealt her an unwinnable hand. \u8220\'20\'1CWe dug out of a deep hole but not enough,\u8221\'20\'1D David Plouffe, a senior Harris adviser, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/davidplouffe/status/1854244538036195432"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote on X }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump won by getting out Republican base, making gains with left-leaning groups\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has just published a look at how different demographic groups across the US voted in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election, which offers some clues into the question of how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  triumphed over \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump won by getting lots of voters who traditionally support Republicans out to the polls, while also shaving off slivers of support from groups that typically vote for Democrats. Harris, meanwhile, did not make comparable gains among groups that lean towards the GOP, despite spending the run-up to the election campaigning alongside Republicans who had broken with Trump.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/election-harris-trump-women-latinos-black-voters-0f3fbda3362f3dcfe41aa6b858f22d12"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the AP }}}\uc2  :\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  won the presidency after holding tight to his core base of voters and slightly expanding his coalition to include several groups that have traditionally been a part of the Democratic base. That finding comes from AP VoteCast, a sweeping survey of more than 120,000 voters nationwide that shows what issues mattered to voters in this election.\par \par \uc2 Trump picked up a small but significant share of Black and Hispanic voters, and made narrow gains with men and women. As Trump chipped away at parts of Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 coalition, Vice President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris }}}\uc2  wasn\u8217\'20\'19t able to make enough of her own gains. Trump succeeded in locking down his traditionally older, white base of voters, and he slightly expanded his margins with other groups into a winning coalition.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s how five key demographic groups voted, according to AP VoteCast.\par \par \uc2 Most Trump voters were white, a trend that continued from 2020\par \par \uc2 Slightly more than 8 in 10 Trump voters in this election were white, roughly in line with 2020. About two-thirds of Harris\u8217\'20\'19 voters were white, and that largely matched President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s coalition in the last election. White voters make up a bulk of the voting electorate in the United States, and they did not shift their support significantly at the national level compared to 2020.\par \par \uc2 A majority of white voters cast their ballot for Trump, unchanged from the 2020 election that he narrowly lost. About 4 in 10 white voters backed Harris, which is about the same as Biden received in 2020. White voters were also more likely to support Trump over Harris and Biden in Pennsylvania, Michigan and Wisconsin, even though Trump lost those states in 2020.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 How did \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  win the presidential election?\par \par \uc2 This topic will be discussed for years, and with ballot counting still ongoing in parts of the country (though not expected to change the election result), we don\u8217\'20\'19t yet have full data on how everyone who cast ballots voted.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, local news outlets in swing states have started digging in to the dynamics that led to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory. Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/politics/election/donald-trump-philadelphia-voter-totals-20241107.html?cid=Philly.com+Twitter&utm_campaign=Philly.com+Twitter+Account&utm_medium=social&utm_source=t.co"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Philadelphia Inquirer\u8217\'20\'19s reporting }}}\uc2  on how Trump won Pennsylvania, which they find was due to to a poor showing by Democrats in the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest city:\par \par \uc2 President-elect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/topic/donald-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  won one out of five Philadelphia voters in one of the strongest performances by a Republican presidential candidate in the deep-blue city in years, doing so by increasing his support in working-class communities across racial groups.\par \par \uc2 Despite winning Philadelphia handily, Vice President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/topic/kamala-harris/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris }}}\uc2  failed to capture enough votes in the city \u8212\'20\'14 where registered Democrats outnumber Republicans 7-1 \u8212\'20\'14 to offset Republican gains elsewhere in the state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/politics/election/trump-campaign-philadelphia-20241021.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a key factor in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s decisive statewide win }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With some ballots still left to count, Harris was carrying the city with about 78% of the vote compared to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 20%. As of Wednesday afternoon, she had a 407,000-vote advantage over Trump \u8212\'20\'14 if that holds, it would be the lowest margin for a Democratic presidential candidate in more than two decades. The rightward trend was reflected throughout the country, including in other big cities, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/11/05/us/elections/results-president-forecast-needle.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  and Trump improved on his 2020 performance }}}\uc2  in every state that had counted most of its votes.\par \par \uc2 All told, Philadelphia was on pace to shift about 2 percentage points to the right. But turnout was roughly flat compared to 2020 \u8212\'20\'14 lower than Democrats had hoped. Harris was on track to receive at least 50,000 fewer votes in the city than President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.inquirer.com/topic/joe-biden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden }}}\uc2  won in 2020.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to address nation after Trump re-elected president\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is scheduled to address the nation from the White House after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The 11am speech will likely be a tough one for the Democratic president, who cut short his own re-election bid in July and endorsed his vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , only to see her lose to Trump. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s predecessor attempted to block him from taking office after losing to him in 2020, and has vowed to undo many of his policies once he returns to power.\par \par \uc2 Biden and Trump spoke by phone yesterday, and agreed to soon meet to discuss the transition between administrations. The date of that meeting has not yet been set.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Key states, Senate races still have not been called\par \par \uc2 This is more of a formality than anything, but we still do not know the official winner of two swing states, as well as three close Senate races.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press, who the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  relies on to call races, has not determined the election result in Nevada and Arizona, but \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  already has the electoral votes he needs to become the next president, and appears poised to win both states. When the AP speaks, we\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know.\par \par \uc2 The AP has not yet called the winner of the Senate race in Nevada, where Democrat \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2  is neck-in-neck with Republican Sam Brown. The GOP has already regained control of the chamber, after picking up seats in West Virginia, Ohio and Montana, but a victory by Brown would make their majority even larger.\par \par \uc2 Also uncalled is the Senate race in Arizona. The independent incumbent \uc2 Kyrsten Sinema\uc2  is not running again, and Democrat \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  is ahead in the votes counted so far. Republican candidate Kari Lake, who still has not acknowledged {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/31/trump-kari-lake-arizona-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her defeat }}}\uc2  in the governor\u8217\'20\'19s race two years ago, is trailing.\par \par \uc2 Finally, the AP has not yet called the winner of the Senate race in Pennsylvania. Democratic incumbent Bob Casey has been trailing his Republican challenger David McCormick, but it\u8217\'20\'19s close. A loss for Democrats here would give them 47 Senate seats in the next Congress, and Republicans 53.\par \par \uc2 This post has been updated to note that the Arizona Senate race has not yet been called\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Two days after election, control of House remains undecided\par \par \uc2 Americans sent \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  back to the White House and handed Republicans control of the Senate in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election, but we still don\u8217\'20\'19t know who controls the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s largely due to ballot counting in western states, particularly California, which is ongoing and may take days to resolve. Republicans currently have a tiny majority of about three seats in the chamber, and Democrats were hoping to gain back that ground.\par \par \uc2 Should Democrats win the chamber, it will likely be by only a small amount, but will put them in a position to block many of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s legislative proposals.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The US has elected \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for a second time after a convincing victory over \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . In the final instalment of Anywhere but Washington, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/laughland-oliver"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Laughland }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/tom-silverstone"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tom Silverstone }}}\uc2  travel to Michigan to watch the final days of the race; as fervent Trump supporters hit the streets, young women mobilise behind Harris, and chaos and despair drive rival election night parties:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At a Republican watch party early Tuesday evening in the Milwaukee suburbs, Dimitra Anderson, a 64-year-old bellydancer, clutched her boa constrictor \u8211\'20\'13 a pet that travels with her everywhere \u8211\'20\'13 and issued a confident proclamation: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m ecstatic because I believe he\u8217\'20\'19s going to win in a tidal wave.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The night was young, no swing states had been called yet, but Anderson, who describes herself as a born-again believer, had been following the preachings of the self-styled prophets of the Christian right. They were saying \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would win.\par \par \uc2 And they were right.\par \par \uc2 After a narrow electoral defeat in 2020 and two assassination attempts in 2024, Trump has emerged victorious \u8211\'20\'13 an event that Christian nationalists are celebrating as a critical win for their movement.\par \par \uc2 Now that Trump has secured his victory, figures on the Christian far right whose prominence grew during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 presidency will enjoy larger followings and most importantly, close proximity to the highest office in the US. Among these figures are leaders in the New Apostolic Reformation, a movement which rejects secularism and embraces \u8220\'20\'1CChristian dominionism\u8221\'20\'1D, the idea that Christians are tasked by God to rule over society and government.\par \par \uc2 During his election night broadcast on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 , Lance Wallnau, a Trump ally and televangelist whose \u8220\'20\'1Cseven mountains\u8221\'20\'1D mandate for Christian leadership of key pillars of society has taken hold on the Christian far right, celebrated the results.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a reformation on America,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wallnau, describing a strategy for activists who share his ideology to capture key positions in local and state government. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not done, it\u8217\'20\'19s not over, it\u8217\'20\'19s just starting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/christian-right-trump-victory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Christian right celebrates after prophecy of Trump win comes to pass }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Americans stockpile \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills and hormones ahead of \u8216\'20\'18reproductive apocalypse\u8217\'20\'19 under Trump\par \par \uc2 When the presidential election results were handed down on Wednesday, Rebecca Gomperts, the founder of Aid Access, the No 1 supplier of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills by mail in the United States, was huddled in a Paris apartment with her team of eight American physicians and 15 support staff. The group \u8211\'20\'13 which usually operates remotely, shipping out more than 9,000 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills a month \u8211\'20\'13 had convened in person before the election, knowing they might have to spring into action.\par \par \uc2 They were right: as news of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory spread, the website received more than 5,000 requests for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills in less than 12 hours \u8211\'20\'13 a surge even larger than the day after Roe v Wade fell. \u8220\'20\'1CI can see all the new requests ticking in as we\u8217\'20\'19re talking,\u8221\'20\'1D Gomperts said in a phone call on Wednesday afternoon. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen this before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The scenario repeated itself across the country as news of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory broke, with women\u8217\'20\'19s health and trans health providers getting inundated with requests for services that their patients feared might be banned in a Trump administration. The telehealth service Wisp saw a 300% increase in requests for emergency contraception; the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill finder site Plan C saw a 625% increase in traffic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClearly, people are trying to plan for the reproductive apocalypse that we anticipate will be happening under a Trump presidency,\u8221\'20\'1D said Elisa Wells, the co-founder of Plan C.\par \par \uc2 For Gomperts and her team at Aid Access, the moment did not come as a shock: they\u8217\'20\'19d been preparing for it since the last Trump administration, when Gomperts, a Dutch physician, expanded her international \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill service into the United States. Since then, Aid Access has devised a system in which physicians in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal prescribe and ship \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills to patients in states where it is not. The nonprofit eventually expanded to the team of eight physicians in four states they have now, along with a help desk that is available 24/7.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/abortion-pills-hormones-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Americans stockpile \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pills and hormones ahead of \u8216\'20\'18reproductive apocalypse\u8217\'20\'19 under Trump }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nevada on verge of voting Republican for first time in two decades\par \par \uc2 Nevada appears to be on the precipice of electing a Republican to the White House for the first time in two decades.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel so happy right now, I feel fantastic,\u8221\'20\'1D said Yolanda Wright, 47, beaming as state after state lit up red on the big screen at the Republican watch party in Las Vegas. Like many voters in this swing state, Wright voted with the GOP for the first time this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been a Democrat my whole life,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I haven\u8217\'20\'19t seen any benefit from it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has yet to project {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  as the winner of the presidential race in the Silver state, and it could take days before all the state\u8217\'20\'19s mail-in ballots are counted and a true tally of votes is revealed. Regardless of the final results, the former president\u8217\'20\'19s political gains in this deeply diverse state are emblematic of a national political realignment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere it\u8217\'20\'19s clear that what we knew as true in politics, a lot of the normal rules we had, those are dead and gone,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mike Noble, an independent pollster who has been studying the electorate in Nevada, Arizona and Utah. \u8220\'20\'1CNow we have new rules, a new game to play.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a state with one of the largest proportions of working-class voters and blue-collar workers, where the economy is dominated by the service and entertainment, as well as mining and construction, a populist message seems to have overcome prior political allegiances. Voters who felt trapped in a dark economic rut chose the person they thought would bring the most change.\par \par \uc2 Exit polls indicate that more than half of white and Asian voters, and about half of Hispanic/Latino voters cast ballots for Trump. Both the NBC and \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  exit polls found that majorities of white women and white men without a college degree backed Trump, and polls suggest he had also gained support among non-white voters without college degrees. Overwhelming majorities of those who voted for Trump said the economy was doing poorly.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/election-nevada-republican-votes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nevada on verge of voting Republican for first time in two decades }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  lawmaker Ibrahim al-Moussawi said on Thursday, when asked about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election victory, that the group welcomes any effort to stop the war in Lebanon but does not pin its hopes for a ceasefire on any particular US administration.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 European leaders struggle for show of unity in wake of Trump victory\par \par \uc2 European leaders are gathering in Budapest for two days of top-level talks that should give an indication of how united the continent can remain in response to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s second term as US president, but could also reveal its divisions.\par \par \uc2 Hosted by Hungary\u8217\'20\'19s authoritarian prime minister, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/viktor-orban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n }}}\uc2  , a Trump ally who has enthusiastically hailed the Republican candidate\u8217\'20\'19s re-election, the EU27\u8217\'20\'19s leaders are being joined on Thursday by the Turkish president, \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 , the UK\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 , the Nato secretary general \uc2 Mark Rutte\uc2  and Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On the agenda for the long-scheduled meeting of the European Political Community were support for Ukraine, migration, global trade and economic security, with an informal EU leaders\u8217\'20\'19 summit on Friday due to focus on the bloc\u8217\'20\'19s declining competitiveness, laid bare in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/09/eu-mario-draghi-report-spending-boost"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report by the former Italian leader  }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/09/eu-mario-draghi-report-spending-boost"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mario Draghi }}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Leaders were upbeat as they arrived, stressing the need for a strong Europe and effective transatlantic cooperation with Trump, whose return to the White House could herald an abrupt halt to US support for Ukraine and a potentially damaging trade war with Europe.\par \par \uc2 Europe aims to be a \u8220\'20\'1Crespected partner\u8221\'20\'1D and deepen its ties with the US, the president of the European council, \uc2 Charles Michel\uc2 , said, while recognising \u8220\'20\'1Csome differences\u8221\'20\'1D. The commission\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , said the bloc must maintain unity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have shown Europe can take responsibility by standing together \u8211\'20\'13 we showed it during the pandemic and the energy crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we are facing challenges, no country can handle them alone but by standing together we can overcome them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  said she was looking forward to working with Trump again \u8220\'20\'1Cin a good manner \u8230\'20\'26 to strengthen the transatlantic bond\u8221\'20\'1D based on a clear-headed analysis of shared interests. \u8220\'20\'1CThe future of Europe is in our hands,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/07/european-leaders-struggle-for-show-of-unity-in-wake-of-trump-victory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 European leaders struggle for show of unity in wake of Trump victory }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory adds record $64bn to wealth of richest top 10\par \par \uc2 The wealth of the 10 richest people in the world \u8211\'20\'13 a list dominated by US tech billionaires \u8211\'20\'13 increased by a record amount after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the presidential election, according to a widely cited index.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/billionaires/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg Billionaires Index }}}\uc2  estimated that the world\u8217\'20\'19s 10 wealthiest people gained nearly $64bn (about \u163\'00\'A349.5bn) on Wednesday \u8211\'20\'13 the largest daily increase since the index began in 2012.\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest person, registered the largest increase with a $26.5bn addition to his fortune, which now stands at $290bn. Musk, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/nov/06/how-elon-musk-stands-to-benefit-from-trump-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prominent backer of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign }}}\uc2 , benefited from a surge in the share price of \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , the electric carmaker where he is chief executive and in which he owns a 13% stake.\par \par \uc2 The gains came as tech business leaders, including \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/oct/28/jeff-bezos-washington-post-endorsements"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeff Bezos }}}\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/mark-zuckerberg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Zuckerberg }}}\uc2  , chief executive of \uc2 Facebook\uc2  parent Meta, and \uc2 Apple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/tim-cook"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Cook }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/trump-election-win-billionaires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 publicly congratulated }}}\uc2  Trump on his election win.\par \par \uc2 Much of the gains for the top 10 were because of a surge in US stocks on Wednesday as investors anticipated a low-tax and regulation-light policy platform.\par \par \uc2 Other beneficiaries were Bezos, the founder of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and the world\u8217\'20\'19s second richest person, who added $7bn to his near-$230bn fortune, and \uc2 Larry Ellison\uc2 , the chair of the software company \uc2 Oracle\uc2 , historically a Republican supporter, who increased his wealth by $9bn to $193bn.\par \par \uc2 Other members of the top 10 whose wealth grew included \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s co-founder \uc2 Bill Gates\uc2 , the former \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  chief executive \uc2 Steve Ballmer\uc2 , and \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s co-founders \uc2 Larry Page\uc2  and \uc2 Sergey Brin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/07/trump-victory-adds-record-wealth-richest-top-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory adds record $64bn to wealth of richest top 10 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 What has been the reaction to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's election loss?\par \par \uc2 After Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election, and subsequent sweeping victory for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , vice-president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris }}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s gave her concession speech on Wednesday afternoon. But, what has been the reaction to Harris\u8217\'20\'19s loss and what does it mean for the Democratic party and its supporters?\par \par \uc2 After Harris\u8217\'20\'19s concession speech, her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/harris-election-concession-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supporters expressed shock, grief and disillusionment }}}\uc2  as they reflected upon the harrowing hours since the election was called for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump }}}\uc2 . Instead of feeling galvanized to build resistance movements, voters said that they needed time to rest and reset before thinking of next steps after the election.\par \par \uc2 Nadia Brown, a political science professor at \uc2 Georgetown University\uc2  and a fellow \uc2 Howard University\uc2  alumna, had watched the election results pour in from the campus on election night. For Brown, she said that the election results posed \u8220\'20\'1Clarger questions to ask around what the Democratic party needs to do to maintain the core voting bloc\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic pollster Paul Maslin argued that Harris did as well as she could have, given the environment and circumstance. Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cdid a really good job\u8221\'20\'1D, Maslin told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/11/06/democrats-despair-trump-swing-states-00187722"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico }}}\uc2 , but ultimately \u8220\'20\'1Cthis race was unwinnable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump, rightly or wrongly, his persona and his fundamental attack line against the condition of the country, the Biden-Harris administration and frankly the Democratic party, was in the end unbeatable,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s national political correspondent Alex Thompson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AxiosComms/status/1854096532498264553"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted that a former adviser }}}\uc2  to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  criticised the Harris campaign, asking: \u8220\'20\'1CHow do you spend $1bn and not win?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Others, Thompson said, have suggested that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  should have exited the race sooner.\par \par \uc2 He said one longtime Democratic operative told him the party \u8220\'20\'1Csleepwalked into disaster\u8221\'20\'1D on Tuesday night, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cswapping the pitcher in at the sixth inning wasn\u8217\'20\'19t enough, and that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris }}}\uc2  did as good of a job as she could have done\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Mark Longabaugh, a veteran Democratic strategist who previously advised Senator \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2 , also said Harris was handed the reins \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo late\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that it was a \u8220\'20\'1Ctough environment\u8221\'20\'1D according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/11/06/democrats-despair-trump-swing-states-00187722"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Others, such as Lindy Li, a senior Democratic official in Pennsylvania, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JacquiHeinrich/status/1854052736641212687"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are questioning }}}\uc2  whether the outcome would have been different if Harris had chosen a different vice-presidential candidate, such as the governor of Pennsylvania, Josh Shapiro.\par \par \uc2 Li argued to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JacquiHeinrich/status/1854052736641212687"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News }}}\uc2  that the moderate Shapiro would have conveyed to American voters that Harris is not the \u8220\'20\'1CSan Francisco liberal\u8221\'20\'1D Trump portrayed her to be. \u8220\'20\'1CBut she went with someone actually to her left,\u8221\'20\'1D Li said, referring to the Minnesota governor, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , whom Harris chose as her vice-presidential pick.\par \par \uc2 Li also criticised the Harris campaign for not distinguishing Harris enough from Biden, a point that has been echoed by other operatives and commentators in the last few weeks.\par \par \uc2 Some pointed to Harris\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/14/kamala-harris-israel-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appearance on the talkshow The View }}}\uc2 , when she was asked if there was anything she would have done differently than Biden and responded: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is not a thing that comes to mind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 David Sirota, who was a senior adviser for Sanders\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 presidential campaign, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/davidsirota/status/1854066442016039288"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 described }}}\uc2  Tuesday night as a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery bad night\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome of us spent years warning Dems to take working-class politics more seriously & to not tout neocons,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe did so in hopes of avoiding this & yet we were vilified as traitors by Dem elites & liberal pundits. There\u8217\'20\'19s a lesson here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another former \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  staffer, Jeff Weaver, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/11/06/democrats-despair-trump-swing-states-00187722"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico }}}\uc2  that the Democratic party now needed to \u8220\'20\'1Cre-establish its relationship with the working-class people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/election-trump-harris-democrats-loss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats pick apart Trump victory: \u8216\'20\'18How do you spend $1bn and not win?\u8217\'20\'19 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nato\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s secretary general, \uc2 Mark Rutte\uc2 , said on Thursday that he aimed to work jointly with returning US leader \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in confronting the \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous new developments\u8221\'20\'1D linked to North Korea\u8217\'20\'19s entry into the Russian war on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we see more and more is that North Korea, Iran, China, and of course Russia are working together, working together against Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D Rutte told reporters at a European leaders\u8217\'20\'19 meeting in Budapest, according to Agence France-Presse (AFP).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is more and more a threat, not only to the European part of Nato, but also to the United States \u8211\'20\'13 because Russia is delivering the latest technology into North Korea,\u8221\'20\'1D he warned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI look forward to sit down with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to discuss how we can face these threats collectively,\u8221\'20\'1D Rutte said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  coasted back into the White House by a wide margin in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, with the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s bombastic style and extreme policy proposals appealing to more than 70 million voters across all 50 states.\par \par \uc2 His victory also meant misery for Democrats, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris }}}\uc2  , who was attempting to become the first woman to become president of the US, but who ultimately fell way short, crucially in the handful of swing states that decided the outcome.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/richardluscombe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe }}}\uc2  runs through the 10 key takeaways from a historic election here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/trump-election-win-10-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats suffer a drubbing: 10 key takeaways from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election win }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president, \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 , said on Thursday that she was looking forward to working with US president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  again to strengthen the transatlantic bond, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have some experience with working with President Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding it was very important that the two \u8220\'20\'1Canalyse together what our shared interests are and work on that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin said on Thursday it did not rule out the possibility that some form of contact could take place between Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , and US president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  before the latter\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration in January, Reuters reports citing the Interfax news agency.\par \par \uc2 Putin has not yet commented on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election win but is due to speak and take questions at a conference later on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin reacted cautiously on Wednesday after Trump was elected US president, saying the US was still an unfriendly state and that only time would tell if Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric on ending the Ukraine war translated into reality.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.09am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , the issue thought to be the magic bullet that would mortally wound {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s }}}\uc2  chances at a second presidency, instead failed to stop him on Tuesday. Now, two years after a conservative supermajority on the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ended federal protections for the procedure, the future of American \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is facing a new chapter of extraordinary peril.\par \par \uc2 While {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seven states passed ballot measures }}}\uc2  to amend their state constitutions and protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House means those hard-fought efforts may amount to nothing. Despite the gridlock in \uc2 US Congress\uc2 , a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could soon become a reality: anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates hope that Trump will resurrect a 19th-century anti-vice law to effectively implement a nationwide ban. Access to other forms of reproductive healthcare, such as contraception and in vitro fertilization, are also at risk.\par \par \uc2 Because he\u8217\'20\'19s barred from a third term Trump can now do whatever he wants without fear of electoral consequences, said Mary Ziegler, a professor at the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2  who studies the legal history of reproduction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s playing with house money,\u8221\'20\'1D Ziegler said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe can do whatever he\u8217\'20\'19s going to do without fear of conservative Christian voters, without fear of swing voters, without fear of anybody. And he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have Roe v Wade and he has a conservative supreme court, so that means he could do really aggressive things to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or IVF \u8211\'20\'13 or not. We don\u8217\'20\'19t know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the two years since the high court overturned Roe, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  became an issue that seemed to spell electoral promise for the Democrats. Before Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates had triumphed in all seven states that held related ballot measures. Public support surged, including in red states.\par \par \uc2 But the outrage and activism did not translate into enough votes for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who made defending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a bedrock of her campaign.\par \par \uc2 Nor did Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures necessarily boost Democratic turnout in critical swing states such as Arizona and Nevada.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/07/abortion-donald-trump-return-to-white-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to White House means \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights face new chapter of peril }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Special counsel prosecutors will shut down their criminal cases against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  before he takes office, according to two people with direct knowledge of the matter, after his stunning victory against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  meant they would not proceed to trial.\par \par \uc2 The move reflects the reality that the cases will not be completed before inauguration day. Once the former president returns to the White House, the special counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office would be prohibited from pursuing further criminal actions under justice department policy.\par \par \uc2 The justice department has long known that if Trump won, the criminal cases \u8211\'20\'13 over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s retention of classified documents and his efforts to overturn the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 would be finished because Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general would likely drop the charges.\par \par \uc2 But it is also understood to be a preemptive measure to ensure that Trump will not be able to order the dismissal of the special counsel, Jack Smith, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/trump-fire-jack-smith-hugh-hewitt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he had vowed to do if he takes office and Smith remained in his role }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That possibility had been relished by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s close aides and advisers, who privately imagined Trump ordering Smith\u8217\'20\'19s removal and his team having to vacate their office space in Washington.\par \par \uc2 The justice department is still examining how to wind down the cases, which are in different stages and are complicated. In particular, the department does not want the classified documents case, which was dismissed and currently under appeal, to go unchallenged.\par \par \uc2 Failure to pursue an appeal over the dismissal of the classified documents case on grounds that the special counsel himself was illegally appointed could set a problematic precedent and hamper the department\u8217\'20\'19s ability to use special counsels in the future.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/special-counsel-trump-criminal-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US special counsel to wind down criminal cases against Donald Trump }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.50am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/robert-f-kennedy-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr }}}\uc2  , who previously said that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had promised him control over a broad range of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/trump-tells-tucker-carlson-that-musk-and-rfk-jr-could-be-influential-figures-if-he-wins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 public health agencies }}}\uc2  if he returned to the White House, said on Wednesday that there are \u8220\'20\'1Centire departments\u8221\'20\'1D within the Food and Drug Administration (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ) that \u8220\'20\'1Chave to go\u8221\'20\'1D, reports {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4976746-robert-kennedy-potential-role-trump-administration/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Hill }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The website, citing an MSNBC interview, reports that Kennedy said:\par \par \uc2 In some categories \u8230\'20\'26 there are entire departments, like the nutrition department at the \uc2 FDA\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 that have to go, that are not doing their job, they\u8217\'20\'19re not protecting our kids.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When asked if he would eliminate any health agencies, Kennedy told MSNBC, \u8220\'20\'1Cto eliminate the agencies, as long as it requires congressional approval, I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be doing that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can get the corruption out of the agencies,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Trump on Sunday told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/trump-banning-vaccines-president-rfk-fluoride-rcna178570"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC }}}\uc2  that Kennedy, the anti-vaccine conspiracy theorist and former independent candidate who dropped out and endorsed Trump, would have a \u8220\'20\'1Cbig role in the administration\u8221\'20\'1D if he won Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump has won the election - so what happens next?\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s US election victory, here\u8217\'20\'19s what will happen next:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , spoke to Trump on Wednesday and invited him to the White House. Trump campaign spokesperson \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  said Trump \u8220\'20\'1Clooks forward to the meeting, which will take place shortly, and very much appreciated the call\u8221\'20\'1D. It would be the first time they had met since Biden\u8217\'20\'19s disastrous debate performance against Trump in June that forced him out of the race.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden will make an address to the nation on Thursday, vowing a peaceful transfer of power to Trump after his crushing election win over \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . In what promises to be an agonising moment for Biden, he will speak in the Rose Garden of the White House at 11am (4pm GMT) to \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscuss the election results and the transition\u8221\'20\'1D to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second term.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Despite Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election success being apparent pretty early on election night, the full US election results are still not in. Out of 51 states (including DC), results for 49 have been called so far. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  currently has 295 electoral votes and Harris has 226. For context, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/07/joe-biden-wins-us-election-donald-trump-loses-final-result-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declared the winner }}}\uc2  offcially four days after the election in 2020.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris }}}\uc2  will preside over a joint session of Congress in January to certify the results of the election. Harris delivered a speech conceding defeat in the presidential election to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump }}}\uc2  on Wednesday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump will be sworn in as the 47th US president on 20 January 2025.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Philippines expects US policy in the Indo-Pacific and support for its treaty ally amid South China Sea tensions to remain steady under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , driven by bipartisan resolve in Washington, its ambassador to the US said on Thursday, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Both Democrats and Republicans prioritise countering China\u8217\'20\'19s influence, including in the South China Sea, Jose Manuel Romualdez said, suggesting that military cooperation, economic ties and security commitments with the Philippines will continue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is in their interest that the Indo-Pacific region remains free, peaceful and stable, especially given the economic part of it, with trillions of dollars passing through the South China Sea,\u8221\'20\'1D Romualdez told Reuters in an interview.\par \par \uc2 US-Philippine security engagements have deepened under president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Philippine counterpart \uc2 Ferdinand Marcos Jr\uc2 , with both leaders keen to counter what they see as China\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive actions in the South China Sea and near Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 Marcos said in a congratulatory message after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory:\par \par \uc2 I am hopeful that this unshakeable alliance, tested in war and peace, will be a force of good that will blaze a path of prosperity and amity, in the region, and in both sides of the Pacific.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Under Marcos, the Philippines has increased the number of its bases accessible to US forces to nine from five, some facing the South China Sea, where China has built artificial islands equipped with runways and missile systems. The US has proposed $128m for infrastructure improvements at those bases, in addition to a $500m pledge for the Philippine military and coastguard.\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters, Romualdez expressed confidence that these commitments, including joint US-Philippine maritime exercises that began last year, would continue under Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have very strong bipartisan support in the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  where the money comes from. Every single one of our friends in the Republican side has signified their concern and strong support for whatever we\u8217\'20\'19re doing right now in relation to the challenges we face with China today,\u8221\'20\'1D Romualdez told Reuters. He suggested potential changes under Trump would be \u8220\'20\'1Cminimal\u8221\'20\'1D and could even be favourable.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Analysts say it is hard to separate the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s bluster from his actual plans but it\u8217\'20\'19s clear his priority is to bin many of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s policies, writes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roth-andrew"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Andrew Roth }}}\uc2  in this analysis piece:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-foreign-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US foreign policy }}}\uc2  establishment is set for one of the biggest shake-ups in years as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has vowed to both revamp US policy abroad and to root out the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep state\u8221\'20\'1D by firing thousands of government workers \u8211\'20\'13 including those among the ranks of America\u8217\'20\'19s diplomatic corps.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s electoral victory is also likely to push the Biden administration to speed up efforts to support Ukraine before Trump can cut off military aid, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/trump-netanyahu-victory-israel-middle-east"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hamper the already-modest efforts to restrain Israel\u8217\'20\'19s  }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/trump-netanyahu-victory-israel-middle-east"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/trump-netanyahu-victory-israel-middle-east"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in Gaza and Lebanon }}}\uc2  and lead to a fresh effort to slash and burn through major parts of US bureaucracy including the state department.\par \par \uc2 Trump backers have said he will be more organised during his second term, often dubbed \u8220\'20\'1CTrump 2.0\u8221\'20\'1D, and on the day after election day US media reported that Trump had already chosen \uc2 Brian Hook\uc2 , a hawkish state department official during the first Trump administration, to lead the transition for America\u8217\'20\'19s diplomats.\par \par \uc2 And yet analysts, serving and former US diplomats and foreign officials said that it remained difficult to separate Trump\u8217\'20\'19s bluster from his actual plans when he takes power in January. What is clear is that his priority is to bin many of the policies put in place by his predecessor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m skeptical that the transition process will be super-impactful since the natural instinct of the new team will be to toss all of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s foreign policy in the dumpster,\u8221\'20\'1D one former senior diplomat said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you go back to 2016, Mexico didn\u8217\'20\'19t pay for the wall. And, you know, it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t look like there was a secret plan to defeat Isis,\u8221\'20\'1D said Richard Fontaine, the CEO of the Center for a New American Security thinktank. \u8220\'20\'1CSome of these things didn\u8217\'20\'19t turn out the way that they were talked about on that campaign trail and we go into this without really knowing what the president\u8217\'20\'19s proposal will be for all of this \u8211\'20\'13 and what he will do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/us-election-donald-trump-foreign-policy-plans-government-purge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US diplomats brace as Trump plans foreign policy shake-up in wider purge of government }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 South Korea's Yoon praises Trump in phone call as trade officials brace for tariffs\par \par \uc2 South Korean president, \uc2 Yoon Suk Yeol\uc2 , spoke with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Thursday and congratulated him on winning the US presidency on the \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Great Again\u8221\'20\'1D slogan as officials in Seoul worked to prepare for \u8220\'20\'1Csignificant\u8221\'20\'1D economic changes, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Yoon and Trump held a 12-minute phone call and discussed the close security and economic ties of their two countries across all areas, a senior South Korean official said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the US also visited Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Mar-a-Lago home in Florida to meet with members of the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s camp, the foreign ministry said.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election has renewed attention in South Korea on his \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica First\u8221\'20\'1D foreign policy plans and how his unpredictable style will play out in his second term, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Officials worked past midnight on Wednesday to prepare for changes expected from US policies, with the Bank of Korea and thinktanks seeing a potential hit to exports if the US raises tariffs.\par \par \uc2 Meetings at the trade ministry that began in the hours after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory led to back-to-back discussions early on Thursday as South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s economic leaders weighed the impact on exports of potential tariffs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShould policy stance that has been stressed by president-elect Trump become realised, the impact on our economy is expected to be significant,\u8221\'20\'1D finance minister Choi Sang-mok said at a 7.30am (10.30pm GMT on Wednesday) meeting with trade and foreign ministers.\par \par \uc2 South Korea would probably suffer less than China, Mexico and the EU, but Asia\u8217\'20\'19s fourth-largest economy could be forced into another renegotiation of its bilateral free trade agreement with Washington, according to Kim Young-gui, an economist at the Korea Institute for International Economic Policy (KIEP).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polish prime minister Donald Tusk said on Thursday that Poland would work on strenghtening its relations with the US after Donald Trump won the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, Tusk joined other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/european-leaders-respond-to-trump-win-orban-zelenskyy-macron"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 European leaders in congratulating Trump }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump }}}\uc2  on winning the election. I look forward to our cooperation for the good of the American and Polish nations????????\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Donald Tusk (@donaldtusk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/donaldtusk/status/1854099489596071949?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Australian prime minister who vowed before the last election to herald a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/apr/01/the-closer-you-looked-at-canberra-this-week-the-uglier-it-got-especially-mps-behaviour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kinder, gentler parliament }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D has now hailed Australia\u8217\'20\'19s rowdy, robust and combative style of political debate as proof of a functioning democracy, warning \u8220\'20\'1Conly dictatorships pretend to be perfect\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In remarks to a global democracy conference in Sydney a day after the United States returned Donald Trump to the presidency eschewing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/is-trump-a-fascist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warnings }}}\uc2  about his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/trump-threats-election-enemy-within"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 autocratic style }}}\uc2 , Anthony Albanese suggested the adversarial tendencies of the Westminster political system were \u8220\'20\'1Ca virtue, not a flaw\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA fierce contest can be a good thing, as long as it\u8217\'20\'19s a contest about substance, about things that matter to people and issues that affect the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Albanese told the Commonwealth Parliamentary Association, in a speech distributed in advance.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/07/anthony-albanese-us-election-global-democracy-conference-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Only dictatorships pretend to be perfect\u8217\'20\'19: Albanese gives fiery defence of democracy after US election }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 For today\u8217\'20\'19s First Edition newsletter, my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/nimo-omer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nimo Omer }}}\uc2  spoke with Guardian US live news editor Chris Michael about what a Donald Trump presidency might look like. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a snippet:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAutocrats are rejoicing,\u8221\'20\'1D Chris says about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory. \u8220\'20\'1CThat probably tells you all you need to know\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump has on many occasions praised Russia\u8217\'20\'19s president, Vladimir Putin, and the North Korean dictator, Kim Jong-un. His admiration for other strongman leaders such as Hungary\u8217\'20\'19s Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n, China\u8217\'20\'19s Xi Jinping and Turkey\u8217\'20\'19s Recep Tayyip Erdogan is well documented and long held.\par \par \uc2 Trump has said that he would end Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Cin one day\u8221\'20\'1D, though he has not provided specific details on how. Expectations are that Ukraine will see a significant reduction in military aid from the US \u8211\'20\'13 the Trump team {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/06/ukraine-trump-victory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have made clear }}}\uc2  they have no intention of indefinitely maintaining commitment to Kyiv as the war continues to drag on.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/07/first-edition-second-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Thursday briefing: What lies ahead for the US in a second Trump administration }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 Over on the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/nov/07/bank-of-england-interest-rates-federal-reserve-trump-trade-war-eurozone-recession-business-live-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 business live blog }}}\uc2 , my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/graemewearden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Graeme Wearden }}}\uc2  writes that the a looming new trade war triggered by Donald Trump could push the eurozone economy from sluggish growth into \u8220\'20\'1Ca full-blown recession\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s according to the investment bank ING, who fear the recession could begin even before Trump \u8211\'20\'13 who has said he wants to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/donald-trump-tariffs-would-cut-uk-growth-by-half-and-push-up-inflation-thinktank-warns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 impose a 10% tariff on all non-US goods }}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 is sworn in next January.\par \par \uc2 enltrEven though Trump's tariffs might not impact Europe until late 2025, the renewed uncertainty and trade war fears could drive the eurozone economy into recession at the turn of the year. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mPyiauahuO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/mPyiauahuO }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ING Economics (@ING_Economics) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ING_Economics/status/1854231776937287766?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 China warns 'no winners' in a trade war after Trump re-election\par \par \uc2 China warned on Thursday there would be \u8220\'20\'1Cno winners in a trade war\u8221\'20\'1D after the re-election in the US of former president Donald Trump, who has pledged huge new tariffs on Chinese imports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a matter of principle, I would like to reiterate that there will be no winners in a trade war, which is also not conducive to the world,\u8221\'20\'1D foreign ministry spokesperson Mao Ning said, according to Agence France-Presse (AFP).\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 Asian equities mostly rose on Thursday, reports Agence France-Presse (AFP), while the dollar held gains and bitcoin hit a fresh record as markets try to ascertain the consequences of a second Donald Trump presidency after he pledged to cut taxes and ramp up tariffs with an eye on China.\par \par \uc2 According to AFP, bitcoin touched a new high just above $76,475 on optimism about the outlook for cryptocurrencies after the president-elect said on the campaign trail that he would make the US the \u8220\'20\'1Cbitcoin and cryptocurrency capital of the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 Iran says Trump win a chance for US to reassess 'wrong policies'\par \par \uc2 Iran on Thursday called Donald Trump \u8217\'20\'19s victory in the US presidential election an opportunity for the United States to reassess past mistakes, reports Agence France-Presse (AFP).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have very bitter experiences with the policies and approaches of different US governments in the past,\u8221\'20\'1D foreign ministry spokesperson Esmaeil Baghaei was quoted as saying by state news agency IRNA, adding Trump\u8217\'20\'19s win was a chance \u8220\'20\'1Cto review previous wrong policies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 Turkish president Recep Tayyip Erdogan has spoken by phone with US president-elect Donald Trump to discuss cooperation between the two countries, the presidency said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Erdogan \u8220\'20\'1Ccongratulated Trump on his election victory\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cexpressed his desire to develop cooperation between Turkey and the United States in the period ahead\u8221\'20\'1D, it said in a statement, reports Agence France-Presse (AFP).\par \par \uc2 Erdogan was twice hosted at the White House by Trump during his first term, but has never been received there by current President Joe Biden.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 US election results: where things stand\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump has won the election, with 295 electoral college votes, out of 270 needed for victory, and some states \u8211\'20\'13 the swing states of Nevada and Arizona \u8211\'20\'13 still to be called. Every swing state called so far has gone to Trump. Trump is also ahead in the popular vote, with 51% to Harris\u8217\'20\'19s 48%.\par \par \uc2 The Republicans also have control over the senate, after picking up three members.\par \par \uc2 The House is still in play, with neither the Republicans nor the Democrats holding the 218 members needed to gain control of the chamber. The Republicans are however ahead, with 206 House representatives.\par \par \uc2 The full results are here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/06/us-election-results-map-2024-live-donald-trump-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election 2024 results live: Donald Trump wins presidency, defeating Kamala Harris }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 China\u8217\'20\'19s outbound shipments grew at the fastest pace in over two years in October, Reuters reports, as factories rushed inventory to major export markets in anticipation of further tariffs from the US and the European Union, as the threat of a two-front trade war looms.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pre-election pledge to impose tariffs on Chinese imports in excess of 60% is likely to spur a shift in stocks to warehouses in China\u8217\'20\'19s number one export market.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tariff threat is rattling Chinese factory owners and officials, with $500bn worth of shipments annually on the line, while trade tensions with the EU, which last year took $466bn worth of Chinese goods, have intensified.\par \par \uc2 Export momentum has been one bright spot for a struggling economy as household and business confidence has been dented by a prolonged property market debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Outbound shipments from China grew 12.7% year-on-year last month, customs data showed on Thursday, blowing past a forecast 5.2% increase in a Reuters poll of economists and a 2.4% rise in September.\par \par \uc2 Imports fell 2.3%, compared with expectations for a drop of 1.5%, turning negative for the first time in four months.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can anticipate a lot of front-loading going into the fourth quarter, before the pressure kicks in come 2025,\u8221\'20\'1D Xu Tianchen, senior economist at the Economist Intelligence Unit, told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it is mainly down to Trump. The threat is becoming more real.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Kate Lamb has taken a look at this morning\u8217\'20\'19s front pages:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s sweeping victory in the US presidential election saw the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/06/us-election-results-map-2024-live-donald-trump-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 securing an unexpected majority in the popular vote }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/senate-elections-republicans-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 control of the Senate }}}\uc2 , and at least 295 electoral college votes \u8211\'20\'13 defeating vice-president Kamala Harris in a contest that dominated UK front pages on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian led with two words: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican Dread\u8221\'20\'1D, a play on the American dream, alongside a close up portrait of the president-elect.\par \par \uc2 Americans awoke to a \u8220\'20\'1Ctransformed country and a rattled world\u8221\'20\'1D as the realisation of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stunning return to power started to sink in, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/election-results-trump-presidency-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Ed Pilkington }}}\uc2 , summing up the mood.\par \par \uc2 enltrThursday\u8217\'20\'19s GUARDIAN: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican dread\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TomorrowsPapersToday?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TomorrowsPapersToday }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Xt0MSsFncU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Xt0MSsFncU }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Allie Hodgkins-Brown (@AllieHBNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AllieHBNews/status/1854289168882454719?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 The Mirror highlighted a question lingering on many minds around the world about what Trump 2.0 might bring, with the headline: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat have they done\u8230\'20\'26Again?\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory, it said, had ushered in fears the Republican leader would be even \u8220\'20\'1Cmore divisive and brutal than in his first spell in the White House\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrThursday's front page: Trump returns to power {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TomorrowsPapersToday?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TomorrowsPapersToday }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iRAWpGU48r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/iRAWpGU48r }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HRBDJXPLL3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HRBDJXPLL3 }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Mirror (@DailyMirror) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DailyMirror/status/1854294750146199772?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 See the full list here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-newspaper-front-pages-donald-trump-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18What have they done\u8230\'20\'26Again?\u8217\'20\'19: What the UK papers say after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s momentous political comeback }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 The sun is pressing through the low grey clouds above Turnberry beach in Ayrshire where Alan Ringrose is walking his dog. He shakes his head at the emerging news from across the Atlantic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think America\u8217\'20\'19s gone mad,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CHow can you elect a criminal as president?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Disbelief is his overriding emotion as the reality of a second Trump presidency sinks in. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t get it. Perhaps people were afraid to elect a black woman?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ringrose, who cares for the local bowling green in his retirement, gestures across the dunes to the terraced lawns of the five-star Trump Turnberry hotel. It is one of two luxury golfing resorts owned by the president-elect in Scotland; the other is in Aberdeenshire. \u8220\'20\'1CHe has done a lot for the area, but as a politician \u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D Ringrose trails off.\par \par \uc2 Further down the windswept beach, Elizabeth Cogan is taking her jack russell Molly for a stroll. She is also quick to acknowledge the investment Trump has made in the local economy. But as a world leader? \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a total disaster: he\u8217\'20\'19s a fascist, he\u8217\'20\'19s against women, he\u8217\'20\'19s homophobic, he\u8217\'20\'19s racist. It is a shock because I thought people would have come to their senses and realised what kind of man he is.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/disbelief-ayrshire-scotland-donald-trump-golf-course"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18America\u8217\'20\'19s gone mad\u8217\'20\'19: disbelief in Ayrshire, Scotland, near Trump\u8217\'20\'19s golf course }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 Japanese prime minister hopes to meet with Trump this month\par \par \uc2 Japanese prime minister Shigeru Ishiba hopes to meet US president-elect Donald Trump in the United States this month, four sources said, in an attempt to emulate then-prime minister Shinzo Abe\u8217\'20\'19s close ties during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term.\par \par \uc2 The US is Japan\u8217\'20\'19s most important economic and security partner, while Tokyo is a key Washington ally in Asia, providing bases that allow it to keep a large military presence on China\u8217\'20\'19s doorstep.\par \par \uc2 Ishiba told reporters he had held a five-minute phone call with Trump on Thursday morning Japan time and that they agreed to meet as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI felt that he was very friendly. So from now on, I have the impression that we can talk frankly,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Three of the people familiar with the planning, who declined to be identified due to the sensitivity of the matter, said Japan was aiming to arrange a meeting between Ishiba and Trump just after a 18-19 November summit of the Group of 20 large economies in Brazil. The fourth source said Japan was aiming to arrange the stopover \u8220\'20\'1Caround\u8221\'20\'1D the G20 meeting.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s office did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 It is approaching 1am US Eastern Time. Here is where things stand on Thursday:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/06/us-election-results-map-2024-live-donald-trump-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won every key swing state }}}\uc2  that has been called \u8211\'20\'13 Georgia, Wisconsin, North Carolina, Michigan and Pennsylvania. Nevada and Arizona haven\u8217\'20\'19t been called yet but appeared to be leaning Republican.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans now have a Senate majority, which will give Trump far more leverage to enact his legislative agenda and, crucially, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/republican-senate-majority-trump-courts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirm judicial and executive nominees }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Control of the US House of Representatives remains unclear, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/house-representatives-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many of the most competitive races still uncalled }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden, who ended his campaign for a second term in July and endorsed Kamala Harris, only to see her lose to Donald Trump yesterday, paid tribute to his vice-president in a just-released statement.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said the president-elect had spoken to Joe Biden, and accepted his invitation for a meeting to discuss transitioning between administrations at the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Initial analysis suggests that Black women remain the most reliable Democratic voters while Harris suffered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/election-trump-harris-women-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant losses among both Latino women and men }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Special counsel prosecutors will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/special-counsel-trump-criminal-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shut down their criminal cases against Donald Trump }}}\uc2  before he takes office, according to two people with direct knowledge of the matter.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/florida-abortion-ballot-ban-measure-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights supporters celebrated a handful of victories }}}\uc2  on Tuesday night, as several states voted to enshrine protections for the procedure into their constitutions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has received calls and congratulations from across the globe, including from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672be84c8f08040dded397ba#block-672be84c8f08040dded397ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Keir Starmer }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-672bb6bb8f082be82baf0dbd#block-672bb6bb8f082be82baf0dbd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emmanuel Macron }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672bab678f081ed4eda7b100#block-672bab678f081ed4eda7b100"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-672be96c8f082be82baf0fc5#block-672be96c8f082be82baf0fc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Obamas }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-672bd9da8f081ed4eda7b36f#block-672bd9da8f081ed4eda7b36f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bernie Sanders }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672bec138f082be82baf0fd5#block-672bec138f082be82baf0fd5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elizabeth Warren }}}\uc2  and other high-profile Democrats and progressives have released statements addressing the stunning loss.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The former Australian prime minister Kevin Rudd, who is now ambassador to the US, has deleted social media posts critical of president-elect Donald Trump to avoid the comments \u8220\'20\'1Cbeing misconstrued\u8221\'20\'1D, officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/07/australia-politics-live-anthony-albanese-donald-trump-peter-dutton-labor-coalition-reserve-bank-interest-rates-question-time?page=with:block-672bf9498f082be82baf104f#block-672bf9498f082be82baf104f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House speaker, Mike Johnson, is running for re-election, he announced in a letter late on Wednesday, and the House majority leader, Steve Scalise, is running for his position again. In his own letter, Scalise outlined the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 plans for their first 100 days in government. The priorities include, \u8220\'20\'1Clock in the Trump tax cuts\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cunleash American energy\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Csurge resources to the southern border\u8221\'20\'1D, among other measures, Scalise writes.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chinese President Xi Jinping on Thursday said Beijing and Washington must find a way to \u8220\'20\'1Cget along\u8221\'20\'1D in a message to Trump, state media said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Taiwan will help companies relocate production from China given the likely large impact on them from tariffs Trump has promised to impose on the country, Economy Minister Kuo Jyh-huei said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 Back to how the UK government has prepared for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s win: in opposition, several senior {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/labour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Labour }}}\uc2  MPs had vociferously criticised Trump, including David Lammy, now the foreign secretary, who labelled him a \u8220\'20\'1Cneo-Nazi sympathizing sociopath\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ca racist KKK and Nazi sympathizer\u8221\'20\'1D. Many of them also opposed the then president addressing parliament while in the UK on a state visit.\par \par \uc2 But when it became clear that Trump was going to run again, Starmer instructed his aides to start repairing relations. \u8220\'20\'1CWe all knew this election was coming and there was only one of two outcomes. The courting of both sides has been going on for a long time,\u8221\'20\'1D one insider said.\par \par \uc2 The civil service had also maintained relationships. Karen Pierce, the British ambassador in Washington, was in post last time Trump was in the White House and she and her team had stayed in close contact with Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 Whitehall also had four years of experience and contacts from that time, all there for Starmer to draw on when he arrived at No 10. \u8220\'20\'1CWe feel far better prepared this time than last time round,\u8221\'20\'1D one official said.\par \par \uc2 It was Pierce who set up the call between the prime minister and Trump after the first assassination attempt on the Republican candidate during the election campaign. Officials had suggested writing a note, but Starmer wanted to speak to Trump in person.\par \par \uc2 She was also instrumental in arranging {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/sep/26/keir-starmer-to-meet-donald-trump-in-new-york-in-push-for-good-relationship"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the dinner between the two men }}}\uc2  at Trump Tower in New York when the prime minister was at the UN in September. Trump was particularly interested in Labour\u8217\'20\'19s election success in the \u8220\'20\'1Cred wall\u8221\'20\'1D, perhaps seeing parallels with the US rust belt states.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/no-10-believes-it-has-done-its-homework-for-a-trump-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No 10 believes it has done its homework for a Trump presidency }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Rudy Giuliani will appear in a New York City courtroom on Thursday to explain to a federal judge why he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t surrendered his valuables as part of a $148m defamation judgment, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 US District Judge Lewis Liman ordered the former New York City mayor to report to court after lawyers for the two former Georgia election workers who were awarded the massive judgment visited Giuliani\u8217\'20\'19s Manhattan apartment last week only to discover it had been cleared out weeks earlier.\par \par \uc2 The judge had set an 29 October deadline for the longtime ally of once-and-future President Donald Trump to surrender many of his possessions to lawyers for Ruby Freeman and her daughter, Wandrea \u8220\'20\'1CShaye\u8221\'20\'1D Moss.\par \par \uc2 Representatives for Giuliani did not respond to an email from Reuters on Wednesday seeking comment.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 No 10 believes it has done its homework for a Trump presidency\par \par \uc2 While {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/kemi-badenoch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kemi Badenoch }}}\uc2  was the first politician since the US presidential election result to publicly challenge Keir Starmer over Labour\u8217\'20\'19s previously tense relationship with Donald Trump, she is unlikely to be the last.\par \par \uc2 Yet the UK prime minister, according to government sources, is less anxious about the return of the divisive populist to the White House than the new Tory leader, and many in his own party, might have assumed.\par \par \uc2 It is true that Starmer may have found a more natural ally in Kamala Harris had she made it to the Oval Office, but his team has spent years preparing for the possibility of a Republican victory \u8211\'20\'13 building relationships and, crucially, bridges.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re more relaxed [with the result] than people might think,\u8221\'20\'1D one senior official said. \u8220\'20\'1CKeir has already had a couple of conversations with Trump and they went very well. Trump likes winners and he sees Keir as someone who \u8216\'20\'18won big\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the election approached, the government became increasingly convinced Trump would win. \u8220\'20\'1CIt wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a huge surprise, even if it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t the outcome we hoped for,\u8221\'20\'1D a source said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe had been worried the Dems did not have enough of an economic offer to get Kamala over the line.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Downing Street had gameplanned a series of outcomes for the election, depending on whether broadcasters called the race and the numbers available at any stage. They were even ready for a scenario in which Trump declared himself the victor even though the race was too close to call.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/no-10-believes-it-has-done-its-homework-for-a-trump-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No 10 believes it has done its homework for a Trump presidency }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kuo was also asked by lawmakers about concerns Trump might cancel subsidies for TSMC, the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest contract chipmaker, which is investing $65bn in the US state of Arizona for new factories.\par \par \uc2 Kuo said there was a contingency plan, including helping more companies in the supply chain to move to the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a trend for TSMC to keep expanding its investment in the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 TSMC has not yet commented on concerns it may have about the subsidies. Its Taipei-listed shares rose about 1% on Thursday morning. Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s GlobalWafers, investing $4bn in the United States, told Reuters it expects the Chips and Science Act award aimed at encouraging investment by chipmakers in the United States would continue under the new US administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMulti-year and decadal programs like the CHIPS Act and the agreements we have signed are regularly continued from one administration to the next,\u8221\'20\'1D it said in a statement on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe expect the CHIPS programme to be no different and run smoothly in the Trump administration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Taiwan will help companies relocate production from China\par \par \uc2 Taiwan will help companies relocate production from China given the likely large impact on them from tariffs incoming US President Donald Trump has promised to impose on the country, Economy Minister Kuo Jyh-huei said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 A threat by Trump, who will take office in January, to impose 60% tariffs on US imports of Chinese goods poses major growth risks for the world\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest economy.\par \par \uc2 Taiwanese companies have invested billions of dollars in China over the past four decades, taking advantage of historically lower costs, but Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s government, wary of stepped up pressure from Beijing to accept Chinese sovereignty claims, has been encouraging its firms to move investment elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in parliament, Kuo said the impact of any Trump tariffs on China for Taiwanese firms manufacturing there would be \u8220\'20\'1Cquite large\u8221\'20\'1D, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will as soon as possible come up with help for Taiwan companies to move their production bases,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, without giving details.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris voters mourn loss after sobering concession speech: \u8216\'20\'18There\u8217\'20\'19s nothing left\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The mood was calm and sober on the Howard University campus as people waited to hear vice-president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris }}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s concession speech on Wednesday afternoon. An area that is usually the central hub of campus life, the Yard, was mostly filled with Harris campaign staff, media and members of the public.\par \par \uc2 Harris appeared about 25 minutes after her scheduled time and opened with a message on unity, building community and coalitions. \u8220\'20\'1CMy heart is full today,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CFull of heart for my country, and full of resolve.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHear me when I say that the light of America\u8217\'20\'19s promise will always burn bright. As long as we never give up and as long as we keep fighting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris encouraged young people to acknowledge their power and to believe in the impossible. \u8220\'20\'1CAt this time, it\u8217\'20\'19s necessary that people not become complacent,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut to commit to organizing and mobilizing.\u8221\'20\'1D Harris encouraged her supporters to embrace \u8220\'20\'1Cthe light of optimism\u8221\'20\'1D and of service.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHear me when I say that the light of America\u8217\'20\'19s promise will always burn bright. As long as we never give up and as long as we keep fighting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/harris-election-concession-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris voters mourn loss after sobering concession speech: \u8216\'20\'18There\u8217\'20\'19s nothing left\u8217\'20\'19 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Indonesia\u8217\'20\'19s new leader has hailed the \u8220\'20\'1Cimmense potential\u8221\'20\'1D of relations with US-president-elect Donald Trump, whose first administration dropped a visa ban imposed on the former general over alleged rights abuses.\par \par \uc2 Prabowo Subianto was inaugurated last month and committed himself to a longstanding neutral foreign policy that has allowed Indonesia to maintain ties with the United States while reaping large investments from China.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIndonesia and the United States are strategic partners who share a robust and multifaceted relationship,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote on social media platform X late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur strategic partnership holds immense potential for mutual benefit, and I look forward to collaborating closely with you and your administration to further enhance this partnership and for global peace and stability.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The 73-year-old was once barred from the US over rights abuses he allegedly committed under dictator Suharto in the late 1990s.\par \par \uc2 But the Trump administration dropped him from a visa blacklist and invited him to Washington when he was serving as defence minister in 2020, Agence France-Presse reports.\par \par \uc2 Prabowo is accused of ordering the abduction of democracy activists, some of whom were never found, but has denied any wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 The fiery nationalist said Wednesday that he had an invitation for \u8220\'20\'1Can official visit to the United States\u8221\'20\'1D as he prepares to embark on his first foreign tour, beginning Friday in China, where he will hold talks with President Xi Jinping.\par \par \uc2 He did not confirm the dates of the US visit, or if he would meet with President Joe Biden or Trump.\par \par \uc2 The presidential palace and foreign ministry did not immediately respond to AFP\u8217\'20\'19s request for comment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 Back to China: both Republican Trump and his Democratic rival Kamala Harris had pledged to get tougher on Beijing.\par \par \uc2 But Trump upped the ante, vowing to slap 60% tariffs on all Chinese goods entering the United States.\par \par \uc2 That proposal could hit $500bn worth of Chinese exports, asset managers PineBridge Investments have suggested.\par \par \uc2 In his first message to Trump since the former president secured a second term in office, Chinese leader Xi said he hoped \u8220\'20\'1Cthat both sides will uphold the principles of mutual respect, peaceful coexistence and win-win cooperation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Chinese vice-president Han Zheng also sent a message to vice president-elect JD Vance, CCTV said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat Raul Ruiz re-elected to House\par \par \uc2 Democratic Representative Raul Ruiz won reelection to a US House seat representing California on Wednesday. Ruiz was first elected to the House in 2012 when he defeated Republican incumbent Mary Bono.\par \par \uc2 His district encompasses all of Imperial County and parts of Riverside and San Bernardino counties, including the cities of Indio, Coachella, Calexico, Hemet and Needles. A physician, Ruiz worked in the emergency department at Eisenhower Medical Center in Rancho Mirage, California. He defeated Republican Ian Weeks.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 US, China must 'get along\u8217\'20\'19, Xi tells Trump\par \par \uc2 Chinese President Xi Jinping on Thursday said Beijing and Washington must find a way to \u8220\'20\'1Cget along\u8221\'20\'1D in a message to US president-elect Donald Trump, state media said.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory heralds a possible shift in US-China relations, frayed in recent years by tensions over everything from trade to the status of the self-ruled island of Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 In a congratulatory message to Trump, Xi \u8220\'20\'1Cpointed out that history has shown that China and the United States benefit from cooperation and suffer from confrontation\u8221\'20\'1D, state broadcaster CCTV said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA stable, healthy and sustainable China-US relationship is in the common interest of both countries and is in line with the expectations of the international community,\u8221\'20\'1D Xi said.\par \par \uc2 He called for Washington and Beijing to \u8220\'20\'1Cstrengthen dialogue and communication\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cproperly manage differences\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The two countries must \u8220\'20\'1Cfind a correct way \u8230\'20\'26 to get along in this new era, to benefit both countries and the world\u8221\'20\'1D, Xi said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 Opening summary\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome back to our live coverage of the US election.\par \par \uc2 After {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/election-results-trump-presidency-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decisively winning the presidential election }}}\uc2 , US president-elect Donald Trump will select personnel to serve under his leadership and enact policies that \u8220\'20\'1Cmake the life of Americans affordable, safe, and secure\u8221\'20\'1D in the days and weeks ahead, his campaign said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/kamala-harris-concession-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris conceded the election to Trump }}}\uc2 , delivering a speech at her alma mater, Howard University, telling supporters not to despair, and saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWhile I concede this election, I do not concede the fight that fuelled this campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here are the other key recent developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/06/us-election-results-map-2024-live-donald-trump-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won every key swing state }}}\uc2  that has been called \u8211\'20\'13 Georgia, Wisconsin, Michigan and Pennsylvania. Nevada and Arizona haven\u8217\'20\'19t been called yet but appeared to be leaning Republican.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans now have a Senate majority, which will give Trump far more leverage to enact his legislative agenda and, crucially, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/republican-senate-majority-trump-courts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirm judicial and executive nominees }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Control of the US House of Representatives remains unclear, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/house-representatives-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many of the most competitive races still uncalled }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden, who ended his campaign for a second term in July and endorsed Kamala Harris, only to see her lose to Donald Trump yesterday, paid tribute to his vice-president in a just-released statement.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said the president-elect had spoken to Joe Biden, and accepted his invitation for a meeting to discuss transitioning between administrations at the White House.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Initial analysis suggests that Black women remain the most reliable Democratic voters while Harris suffered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/election-trump-harris-women-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant losses among both Latino women and men }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Special counsel prosecutors will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/special-counsel-trump-criminal-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shut down their criminal cases against Donald Trump }}}\uc2  before he takes office, according to two people with direct knowledge of the matter.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/florida-abortion-ballot-ban-measure-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights supporters celebrated a handful of victories }}}\uc2  on Tuesday night, as several states voted to enshrine protections for the procedure into their constitutions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has received calls and congratulations from across the globe, including from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672be84c8f08040dded397ba#block-672be84c8f08040dded397ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Keir Starmer }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-672bb6bb8f082be82baf0dbd#block-672bb6bb8f082be82baf0dbd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emmanuel Macron }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672bab678f081ed4eda7b100#block-672bab678f081ed4eda7b100"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-672be96c8f082be82baf0fc5#block-672be96c8f082be82baf0fc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Obamas }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-672bd9da8f081ed4eda7b36f#block-672bd9da8f081ed4eda7b36f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bernie Sanders }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672bec138f082be82baf0fd5#block-672bec138f082be82baf0fd5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elizabeth Warren }}}\uc2  and other high-profile Democrats and progressives have released statements addressing the stunning loss.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The former Australian prime minister Kevin Rudd, who is now ambassador to the US, has deleted social media posts critical of president-elect Donald Trump to avoid the comments \u8220\'20\'1Cbeing misconstrued\u8221\'20\'1D, officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/07/australia-politics-live-anthony-albanese-donald-trump-peter-dutton-labor-coalition-reserve-bank-interest-rates-question-time?page=with:block-672bf9498f082be82baf104f#block-672bf9498f082be82baf104f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House speaker, Mike Johnson, is running for re-election, he announced in a letter late on Wednesday, and the House majority leader, Steve Scalise, is running for his position again. In his own letter, Scalise outlined the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 plans for their first 100 days in government. The priorities include, \u8220\'20\'1Clock in the Trump tax cuts\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cunleash American energy\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Csurge resources to the southern border\u8221\'20\'1D, among other measures, Scalise writes.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241107ekb7000mc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
