\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This victory is a mandate\u8217\'20\'19: rightwing groups ready with policy proposals for new Trump administration\b0\par\par\uc2 Rachel Leingang \par \uc2 1,079 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 November 2024\par 16:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Project 2025 and other far-right groups have outlined a blueprint for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second term\par \par \uc2 As {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump }}}\uc2  prepares to move back into the White House, he\u8217\'20\'19ll have a host of rightwing groups trying to influence his staffing choices and policy proposals, including the group behind {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025 }}}\uc2 , despite Trump\u8217\'20\'19s insistence they won\u8217\'20\'19t be involved.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats }}}\uc2  repeatedly ran attacks on Trump over Project 2025, the conservative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/01/project-2025-key-proposals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 manifesto }}}\uc2  that its writers want to guide a second Trump administration. Trump tried to distance himself from it and from the group behind it, \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 , one of DC\u8217\'20\'19s biggest thinktanks.\par \par \uc2 The Heritage president, Kevin Roberts, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.heritage.org/press/heritage-foundation-president-congratulates-president-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 congratulated }}}\uc2  Trump on his \u8220\'20\'1Chard-fought victory\u8221\'20\'1D that came despite the \u8220\'20\'1Csham\u8221\'20\'1D indictments and against a \u8220\'20\'1Crelentless leftwing machine\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe entire conservative movement stands united behind him as he prepares to secure our wide-open border, restore the rule of law, put parents back in charge of their children\u8217\'20\'19s education, restore America to its proper place as a leader in manufacturing, put families and children first, and dismantle the deep state,\u8221\'20\'1D Roberts said.\par \par \uc2 Other groups, namely the \uc2 America First Policy Institute\uc2 , have avoided the limelight that backfired on Project 2025 and instead worked behind the scenes to ally themselves with Trump and seek to influence his administration. Trump named Linda McMahon, the chair of the institute\u8217\'20\'19s board, as a co-chair of his transition team, giving the \uc2 America First Policy Institute\uc2  a critical role.\par \par \uc2 The institute, started in 2021 and stacked with Trump allies, said in a tweet that it \u8220\'20\'1Cstands ready to support bold governance that puts Americans first\u8221\'20\'1D. It also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/A1Policy/status/1854526109984928108"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shared }}}\uc2  a video clip with the former acting United States attorney general \uc2 Matt Whitaker\uc2  talking about deportations and sanctuary cities, key alignments with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policy goals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis victory is a mandate to restore our nation to a place of safety, opportunity, and prosperity rooted in freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 America First Policy Institute\uc2  said. \u8220\'20\'1CTogether, we\u8217\'20\'19ll secure borders, strengthen the economy, & uphold the freedoms that define us \u8211\'20\'13 for a stronger future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The institute has held trainings for people that could serve in the Trump White House and has a lengthy agenda published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://agenda.americafirstpolicy.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 online }}}\uc2 , complete with plans for immigration, education, energy and elections. \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/24/us/politics/donald-trump-campaign-america-first-policy-institute.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported }}}\uc2  that the group has \u8220\'20\'1Cinstalled itself as the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s primary partner in making concrete plans to wield power again\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The heads of both the \uc2 America First Policy Institute\uc2  and \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  have roots in the \uc2 Texas Public Policy Foundation\uc2 , a state-based conservative thinktank. \uc2 Brooke Rollins\uc2 , CEO of the \uc2 America First Policy Institute\uc2 , ran the Texas foundation for 15 years, and Roberts was the foundation\u8217\'20\'19s CEO before he was tapped by Heritage.\par \par \uc2 Another organization, America First Legal, is headed by former Trump adviser \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 . It has been filing lawsuits that boost Trump and other conservatives on issues like election fraud, diversity programs, public records disputes and government overreach. Miller could return to the Trump administration, but it\u8217\'20\'19s likely the group will remain an outside rightwing legal monitor to help the incoming president.\par \par \uc2 What could Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies be?\par \par \uc2 Project 2025\u8217\'20\'19s sprawling \u8220\'20\'1Cmandate for leadership\u8221\'20\'1D details in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/14/project-2025-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 900-plus pages }}}\uc2  how each government agency could be altered under a conservative president. The project includes a database of potential hires and a training program for those who could staff a Trump administration, though Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team has said none of the people associated with Heritage\u8217\'20\'19s staffing suggestions would be hired. That would be a feat, given the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/nov/04/what-is-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extensive reach }}}\uc2  the project had \u8211\'20\'13 it was signed on to by more than 100 conservative groups, and many of those who wrote chapters or otherwise contributed had played some kind of role in the previous Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 The project\u8217\'20\'19s biggest suggestion is to designate exponentially more federal government employees as political appointees rather than non-partisan civil servants. It also wants to downsize the government. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plan also involves downsizing the federal government, something he tried to start implementing near the end of his first term.\par \par \uc2 The project suggests many ways to restrict immigration, both through beefed-up border security and through limiting legal immigration programs for groups like students and low-skilled workers. That\u8217\'20\'19s another pillar for Trump, who made mass deportations a central theme of his campaign.\par \par \uc2 On education, the project wants to get rid of the Department of Education and increase the use of vouchers that use public money for private schools \u8211\'20\'13 both of which Trump has suggested as well. Conservatives have sought the dismantling of the department for decades, so far without success.\par \par \uc2 Most chapters of Project 2025 mention discarding any programs that promote LGBTQ+ rights and diversity. Trump has railed against these ideals on the campaign trail, promising to root out trans women from sports and in schools.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is one area where Trump and the project could differ, though Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been muddled. The project wants to end federal approval of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, track \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  data and root out anything that is seen as promoting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as healthcare. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t call for a direct ban on the procedure, and Trump has said he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t approve of one either, but many of these policies would make access significantly more difficult.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 America First Policy Institute\uc2  suggests many of the same policies, though it wants to go further than Project 2025 with federal employees, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/24/us/politics/donald-trump-campaign-america-first-policy-institute.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times notes }}}\uc2 , by making most federal workers at-will employees who would not receive civil service protections.\par \par \uc2 Other ideas the institute has pushed include, according to the Times, \u8220\'20\'1Chalting federal funding for \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and for mandatory ultrasounds before abortions, including those carried out with medication. It seeks to make concealed weapons permits reciprocal in all 50 states, increase petroleum production, remove the United States from the Paris Agreement, impose work requirements on Medicaid recipients and establish legally only two genders.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://americafirstpolicy.com/assets/uploads/AFPI_Biblical_Pillars_2022_Final_(1).pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 policy agenda pamphlet }}}\uc2  from the institute starts by discussing the Christian foundations of the US and imploring Christians to get involved in the government \u8220\'20\'1Cbefore it\u8217\'20\'19s too late\u8221\'20\'1D. The policy agenda for the pamphlet was written \u8220\'20\'1Cthrough the lens of their biblical foundations and applications to provide Christians more information on the issues and solutions needed for the restoration of the nation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241108ekb8001s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
