\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Thursday briefing: What lies ahead for the US in a second Trump administration\b0\par\par\uc2 Nimo Omer \par \uc2 2,480 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2024\par 07:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In today\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter: After winning Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election, America\u8217\'20\'19s first convicted president will assemble his transition team \u8211\'20\'13 here\u8217\'20\'19s what we know so far about his plans\u8226\'20\'22 Sign up here for our daily newsletter, First Edition\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  conceded the US election to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  overnight. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/kamala-harris-concession-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a speech at Howard University }}}\uc2 , the vice-president urged supporters not to lose hope, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is a time to organise, to mobilise and to stay engaged for the sake of freedom and justice and the future that we all know we can build together\u8221\'20\'1D. Harris, hoarse from the frenzied campaign that began a little over 100 days ago, contrasted sharply with Trump following his defeat in the 2020 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/trump-election-pennsylvania-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which he never formally conceded }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s speech capped a turbulent election, marked by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s dramatic political comeback. He won decisively, carrying both the electoral college and the popular vote. The Republican party also flipped control of the Senate and while the House of Representatives has not yet been called, the Republicans remain confident. With control over all three branches of government, Republicans could have a much smoother path for passing legislation.\par \par \uc2 As Democrats begin soul-searching (and the inevitable blame game), Trump\u8217\'20\'19s new GOP prepares to take power. For today\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter, I spoke with Guardian US live news editor Chris Michael about what a Trump presidency might look like. But first, the headlines.\par \par \uc2 Five big stories\par \par \uc2 Environment\par \par \uc2 | It is \u8220\'20\'1Cvirtually certain\u8221\'20\'1D that 2024 will be the hottest year on record, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/nov/07/this-year-virtually-certain-to-be-hottest-on-record-finds-eu-space-programme"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the European Union\u8217\'20\'19s space programme has found }}}\uc2 . The prognosis comes the week before diplomats meet at the Cop29 climate summit and a day after a majority of voters in the US, the biggest historical emitter of planet-heating gas, chose to make \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  president.\par \par \uc2 Middle East\par \par \uc2 | Many Israelis were reeling after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/06/netanyahus-sacking-of-defence-chief-last-thing-israel-needs-says-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s decision to dismiss }}}\uc2  his popular defence minister, Yoav Gallant, in the midst of a multifront war. The prime minister said he had fired Gallant over what he described a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrisis of trust\u8221\'20\'1D. Gallant, a member of Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s Likud party and a senior general, has been replaced by the foreign minister, \uc2 Israel Katz\uc2 , a Likud lawmaker and loyalist who has little military background.\par \par \uc2 Politics\par \par \uc2 | The Reform UK MP {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/nov/06/lee-anderson-told-to-apologise-after-swearing-at-parliament-security-guard"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lee Anderson has apologised }}}\uc2  after parliament\u8217\'20\'19s watchdog on bullying and harassment told him to do so for telling a security guard who asked for his ID to \u8220\'20\'1Cfuck off, everyone opens the door to me\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Economy\par \par \uc2 | \uc2 Rachel Reeves{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/nov/06/rachel-reeves-promises-not-increase-taxes-again-in-spring-budget"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has committed not to increase taxes }}}\uc2  at Labour\u8217\'20\'19s next budget and said the government would need to \u8220\'20\'1Clive within the means\u8221\'20\'1D of her spending plans if public services came under mounting pressure.\par \par \uc2 Health\par \par \uc2 | Doing just five extra minutes of exercise a day could help lower blood pressure, a study suggests. High blood pressure affects 1.28 billion adults worldwide and is one of the biggest causes of premature death. It can lead to strokes, heart attacks, heart failure, kidney damage and many other health problems, and is often described as a silent killer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2024/nov/07/adding-five-minutes-exercise-a-day-can-help-lower-blood-pressure-study-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 due to its lack of symptoms }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In depth: \u8216\'20\'18All bets are off\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Reproductive rights\par \par \uc2 Throughout his campaign Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cflip-flopped\u8221\'20\'1D on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Chris Michael says. Sometimes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/donald-trump-abortion-roe-v-wade-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he would brag }}}\uc2  about the singular role he played in overturning Roe v Wade; other times he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/30/trump-ivf-anti-abortion-groups"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 publicly created distance }}}\uc2  from multiple anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions and insisted that it was an issue for individual states to decide.\par \par \uc2 In Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s elections, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seven states passed measures }}}\uc2  that enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in their constitutions \u8211\'20\'13 but this will not be the end of the story. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists will likely challenge the reversal of bans in court, and will fight even harder to push legislation through before more bans are repealed.\par \par \uc2 Crucially, if Trump returns to the White House with Republican control of the Senate and House of Representatives, it could have significant implications for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump has said he would veto a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban if one reached his desk, but who knows \u8212\'20\'14he could change his mind,\u8221\'20\'1D Chris points out. As his tone suggests, few have been reassured by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s promise not to sign a federal ban. This scepticism stems not only from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s history of lying but also from accusations that his camp is playing a verbal sleight of hand, replacing the term \u8220\'20\'1Cnational ban\u8221\'20\'1D with phrases like \u8220\'20\'1Cnational minimum standard\u8221\'20\'1D, which would essentially achieve the same goal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut even if he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t do that, the GOP could theoretically use this obscure piece of law called the Comstock Act,\u8221\'20\'1D Chris adds. This 150-year-old anti-obscenity law bans mailing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related material and was outlined in Project 2025, an extreme 922-page policy document published by a rightwing thinktank as a way to bypass congress altogether and use the legislation to ban the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills \u8211\'20\'13 in effect a national ban.\par \par \uc2 Since Roe v Wade established a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Comstock Act could not be enforced. However, after Roe was overturned in 2022, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  groups have pushed the idea that the Comstock Act is valid once more.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Immigration\par \par \uc2 Border control has always been the key Trump issue. Who can forget \u8220\'20\'1CBuild the wall\u8221\'20\'1D and images of children in cages {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/sep/04/child-separation-ptsd-trump-zero-tolerance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under the child separation policy }}}\uc2 . This time around, his crackdown on immigration is set to be even more controversial \u8211\'20\'13 and wide-ranging.\par \par \uc2 As ever, much vitriol has been aimed at undocumented immigrants. But the president-elect has expanded his ire to potentially include those who legally live in the US. Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/trump-deportation-plan-economic-disaster"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has outlined a mass deportation plan }}}\uc2  that could target up to 20 million people. According to estimates, there are 11 million undocumented immigrants. There is little detail on how such an unprecedented policy would be put into practice, but as Trump appoints officials in the coming months, they will have a much easier time pushing through these changes regardless of the indirect consequences and larger fallout.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric has also become more violent, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2024/oct/28/trump-fills-madison-square-garden-with-anger-vitriol-and-racist-threats-video-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 racist }}}\uc2  and xenophobic than ever. He has warned that mass deportations will \u8220\'20\'1Cbe a bloody story\u8221\'20\'1D and claimed immigrants are \u8220\'20\'1Cpoisoning the blood of the country\u8221\'20\'1D. Such language {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/is-trump-a-fascist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 echoes the rhetoric }}}\uc2  of fascists like Mussolini and Hitler, whom Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jul/06/donald-trump-hitler-michael-bender-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly praised while in office }}}\uc2 , even lamenting that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t have commanders as loyal to him as Hitler did. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s words carry deeply troubling implications for immigrants who are fearful of reprisals from his second administration.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 The international stage\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAutocrats are rejoicing,\u8221\'20\'1D Chris says about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory. \u8220\'20\'1CThat probably tells you all you need to know\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump has on many occasions praised Russia\u8217\'20\'19s president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , and the North Korean dictator, Kim Jong-un. His admiration for other strongman leaders such as Hungary\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 , China\u8217\'20\'19s Xi Jinping and Turkey\u8217\'20\'19s Recep \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  is well documented and long held.\par \par \uc2 Trump has said that he would end Russia\u8217\'20\'19s war in Ukraine \u8220\'20\'1Cin one day\u8221\'20\'1D, though he has not provided specific details on how. Expectations are that Ukraine will see a significant reduction in military aid from the US \u8211\'20\'13 the Trump team {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/06/ukraine-trump-victory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have made clear }}}\uc2  they have no intention of indefinitely maintaining commitment to Kyiv as the war continues to drag on. \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2 , Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s president, congratulated Trump on his \u8220\'20\'1Cimpressive\u8221\'20\'1D election victory on Wednesday. \u8220\'20\'1CI appreciate President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to the \u8216\'20\'18peace through strength\u8217\'20\'19 approach in global affairs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , was among the first leaders to congratulate Trump on his victory. A Trump win is great news for Netanyahu, as Julian Borger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/trump-netanyahu-victory-israel-middle-east"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 writes in this analysis }}}\uc2 . His return to the White House \u8220\'20\'1Cremoves a substantial barrier to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s full control and potential annexation of at least part of Gaza and the West Bank\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US is an anchor for many international organisations and treaties: Nato, the Paris climate accord ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/nov/01/a-trump-presidency-could-cripple-the-paris-climate-agreement-warns-un-chief-antonio-guterres"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 again }}}\uc2  ) and other institutions could face upheaval due to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s isolationist worldview. Trump has dismissed the climate crisis as \u8220\'20\'1Ca big hoax\u8221\'20\'1D and has pledged to cut funding for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Inflation Reduction Act, which he derided as the \u8220\'20\'1Cgreen new scam\u8221\'20\'1D. Instead, Trump plans to pivot heavily toward resource extraction, prioritising oil and gas drilling \u8211\'20\'13 including on public lands and in national parks. In July, he emphasised this shift, vowing to \u8220\'20\'1Cdrill, baby, drill\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/trump-climate-change-environment-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Analysts warn }}}\uc2  that a Trump presidency could add billions of tonnes of heat-trapping gases to the atmosphere, which would have devastating global consequences.\par \par \uc2 With the Cop29 climate conference beginning next week, the pressure is even higher for decisive action.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Democratic norms\par \par \uc2 In recent months, Trump was labelled a fascist by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/trump-fascist-reaction-john-kelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his longest serving former chief of staff }}}\uc2 , retired general \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn a weird way, the one thing that isn\u8217\'20\'19t an issue, for now, is the \u8216\'20\'18stop the steal\u8217\'20\'19 movement,\u8221\'20\'1D Chris says. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump was preparing to contest the results of the election and to undermine democracy itself in order to stay in power but because he\u8217\'20\'19s legitimately won, he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have to do that. So the whole machinery that was built up around this grievance has potentially had the wind taken out of its sails.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump, a man famous for never letting go of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/12/20/us/politics/trump-republican-party-future.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grudges }}}\uc2 , will probably continue with his mission to undermine and hollow out democratic norms and institutions. Trump has said in many interviews and rallies that he would mobilise the federal government {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/08/trump-threatens-jail-adversaries"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 against his personal political enemies }}}\uc2  and the army against citizens that he called \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/trump-military-enemy-within-armed-forces-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the enemy within }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. A second Trump administration likely poses a severe threat to independence of the justice department and other institutions like the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the CIA.\par \par \uc2 Trump has also pledged to dismantle what he calls the \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep state\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 in other words the federal bureaucracy \u8211\'20\'13 by firing thousands of non-political civil servants and replacing them with loyalists. This purge \u8220\'20\'1Cposes a threat to the checks and balances system\u8221\'20\'1D that stood in the way of his most destructive instincts in his first term, says Chris.\par \par \uc2 Freedom of the press, a cornerstone for any functioning democracy, will also likely be in jeopardy. Trump has threatened to jail reporters who do not give up sources and strip broadcasting licences from news outlets as punishment for coverage that he did not agree with. A CNN review of the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s interviews and speeches over the past two years found that he has called for every major American TV news network to be punished.\par \par \uc2 Now the fevered campaigning is over, the real work begins. Trump will be appointing his top team in the coming weeks, which could even include anti-vaccine conspiracy theorist \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . For now \u8220\'20\'1Call bets are off\u8221\'20\'1D, Chris says.\par \par \uc2 For more details on the consequences of a second Trump presidency, read our Guardian series {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/the-stakes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Stakes }}}\par \par \uc2 What else we\u8217\'20\'19ve been reading\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In the second edition of our Black diaspora newsletter, The Long Wave, Nesrine Malik reflects on \uc2 Kemi Badenoch\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s ascension to leader of the Conservatives, and asks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/2024/nov/06/the-long-wave-kemi-badenoch-tory-leader-nigeria"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  if it really is a win for Nigerians }}}\uc2 . Charlie Lindlar, acting deputy editor, newsletters\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The story of the GP Thomas Kwan, sentenced to 31 years in jail yesterday for trying to poison his mother\u8217\'20\'19s partner while disguised as a nurse, is truly bizarre, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2024/nov/06/sunderland-doctor-thomas-kwan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Brown describes it }}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CAn Agatha Christie-inspired Columbo episode with a splash of Breaking Bad.\u8221\'20\'1D Toby Moses, head of newsletters\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just running free as a bird to give everyone a giggle\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2024/nov/06/it-wasnt-sexual-in-any-way-50-years-of-streaking-by-the-people-who-dared-to-bare-all"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Simon Hattenstone looks back at }}}\uc2  the rich history of streaking, meeting those who got their kit off for a cause \u8230\'20\'26 or because they just felt like it. Charlie\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As anyone who has seen the viral clips of Maggie Smith in the Nothing Like A Dame doc knows, she was a character \u8211\'20\'13 her friend {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2024/nov/06/spanx-fizz-and-travel-scrabble-30-years-of-friendship-with-maggie-smith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fiona Golfar confirms }}}\uc2  it in this lovingly told recollection. Toby\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHorrible direction, an appalling script, dreadful performances: it really does have it all\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 Catherine Bray is unfestive and unsparing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2024/nov/06/holiday-twist-review-could-this-be-the-worst-christmas-movie-ever"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in her review }}}\uc2  of the so-bad-it\u8217\'20\'19s-still-bad Christmas film Holiday Twist. Charlie\par \par \uc2 Sport\par \par \uc2 Football\par \par \uc2 | Hakan Calhanoglu scored a first-half penalty to give {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2024/nov/06/inter-arsenal-champions-league-match-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inter a 1-0 Champions League win over Arsenal }}}\uc2 , the Gunners\u8217\'20\'19 first European defeat of the season. \uc2 Aston Villa\uc2  also lost 1-0, to Belgian side Club Brugge, after Tyrone Mings gave away {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2024/nov/06/club-brugge-aston-villa-champions-league-match-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a bizarre second-half penalty }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Boxing\par \par \uc2 | Imane Khelif, who won Olympic gold in women\u8217\'20\'19s boxing amid a gender eligibility row, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2024/nov/06/olympic-boxer-imane-khelif-takes-legal-action-over-male-chromosomes-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is taking legal action }}}\uc2  over media reports allegedly detailing her leaked medical records. Reports published in France this week claimed the 25-year-old has XY (male) chromosomes.\par \par \uc2 Golf\par \par \uc2 | Rory McIlroy has suggested \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2024/nov/06/rory-mcilroy-donald-trump-elon-musk-golf-civil-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could accelerate peace talks }}}\uc2  between traditional golf tours and the Saudi Arabia-backed Liv Golf. McIlroy even floated the idea of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  becoming involved in golf\u8217\'20\'19s elongated merger plans.\par \par \uc2 The front pages\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican dread\u8221\'20\'1D says the Guardian while the Mirror asks \u8220\'20\'1CWhat have they done \u8230\'20\'26 again?\u8221\'20\'1D. The Express goes full Maga: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s been shot, convicted of a crime and branded a fascist \u8230\'20\'26 but he\u8217\'20\'19s still the people\u8217\'20\'19s choice\u8221\'20\'1D. The Times has \u8220\'20\'1CTrump promises golden age after sweeping Harris aside\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CLandslide\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s the i while the Daily Mail is a bit obvious: \u8220\'20\'1CA comeback to Trump all comebacks!\u8221\'20\'1D. The Telegraph calls it \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s clean sweep\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is back\u8221\'20\'1D reports the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2 , while in the Metro it\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica\u8217\'20\'19s golden Age\u8221\'20\'1D. And finally, the Sun goes with \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re rehired\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Today in Focus\par \par \uc2 What will Trump do in power?\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Washington bureau chief, \uc2 David Smith\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2024/nov/07/what-will-trump-do-in-power-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explains }}}\uc2  how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won a second term and what he intends to do with it.\par \par \uc2 Cartoon of the day | Ella Baron\par \par \uc2 The Upside\par \par \uc2 When Abi Wilkinson moved to the US after her partner got a new job, she assumed she could continue her work as a freelance journalist stateside. But when visa issues initially prevented her from continuing in her career, she gained a new perspective. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2024/nov/06/moment-that-changed-me-gave-up-job-journalist-found-self-esteem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 She writes for A moment that changed me }}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think I had fully understood how much my self-esteem was tied to my work and how preoccupied I was with how I was perceived by strangers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When her work permit did come through, Wilkinson \u8220\'20\'1Cdecided to prioritise mental wellbeing over status, ambition or self-aggrandising notions about significance. I found a job as a nanny. I was happier than I had been in years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/feb/12/the-upside-sign-up-for-our-weekly-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up here }}}\uc2  for a weekly roundup of The Upside, sent to you every Sunday\par \par \uc2 Bored at work?\par \par \uc2 And finally, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s puzzles are here to keep you entertained throughout the day. Until tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/quick/17007"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quick crossword }}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/cryptic/29534"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptic crossword }}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wordiply.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wordiply }}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241107ekb700108\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
