\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights supporters see victories despite major loss in Florida\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 898 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2024\par 11:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Several states vote to enshrine protections but effort to roll back Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban fell shortUS election 2024 \u8211\'20\'13 latest updatesUS election results 2024: live map and trackerTracker: where is \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the ballot?\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters celebrated a handful of victories on Tuesday night, as several states voted to enshrine protections for the procedure into their constitutions.\par \par \uc2 However, they lost what was arguably their hardest fight, after Florida voters defeated a measure to roll back the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, breaking a streak of ballot-measure victories kicked off when Roe v Wade was overturned by the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  in 2022. They also fell short in Nebraska, where voters chose to enshrine the state\u8217\'20\'19s existing 12-week ban rather than expand protections for the procedure to 24 weeks.\par \par \uc2 And they lost in South Dakota, thereby preserving a state law that makes it a felony to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  except to save the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 But \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights won in several other states, with Missouri voting to overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a post-Roe first \u8211\'20\'13 and establish a constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until fetal viability. Ballot measures in New York, Colorado and Maryland also passed, expanding their protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and cementing those states\u8217\'20\'19 status as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  havens. In Nevada, a ballot measure to enshrine the battleground state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution received its first nod of approval, though voters must also approve the ballot question in 2026 in order to amend the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Another key presidential swing state, Arizona, approved its ballot measure to establish a fundamental right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and prohibit the state from restricting or banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before 24 weeks \u8211\'20\'13 a major win for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters who sought to expand access beyond 15 weeks.\par \par \uc2 And Montana voters, too, chose to protect the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their state constitution \u8211\'20\'13 enshrining a 1999 Montana supreme court ruling that said the constitutional right to privacy protects the right to a \u8220\'20\'1Cpre-viability\u8221\'20\'1D \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 though there is no defined time frame, it typically occurs around 24 weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe people of Missouri \u8211\'20\'13 be they Democrat, Republican, or independent \u8211\'20\'13 have resoundingly declared that they don\u8217\'20\'19t want politicians involved in their private medical decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rachel Sweet, the manager of the campaign of the Missouri ballot measure, in a statement.\par \par \uc2 A total of 10 states voted on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot initiatives on Tuesday. Results are forthcoming in four more states.\par \par \uc2 Given that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of the top issues in the 2024 election, Democrats had hoped these measures would boost turnout among their base and propel \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to victory. But polls suggest many voters in effect split their votes by supporting both \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and Donald Trump, whose three supreme court appointments helped end federal protections for the procedure. In recent months, Trump backtracked on his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bona fides, but he has repeatedly flip-flopped on the issue and has many allies who would like to see a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/21/idaho-abortion-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 national ban }}}\uc2  enacted.\par \par \uc2 Out of all the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related measures, the Florida initiative \u8211\'20\'13 known as amendment 4 \u8211\'20\'13 was long considered the most difficult to pass. Unlike other measures, which only require a simple majority \u8211\'20\'13 or, in the case of Colorado, 55% of the vote \u8211\'20\'13 to pass, the Florida measure needed to garner 60% of the vote. At the time it was called by the Associated Press, the Florida measure had amassed a clear majority, with 57% of the vote.\par \par \uc2 The Florida result is a bitter pill for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters, shattering a string of successes at the ballot box. Advocates have won \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures in seven states since Roe was overturned.\par \par \uc2 After the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe  }}}\uc2  in 2022, Florida became a refuge for people fleeing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that now blanket the rest of the US south, before its six-week ban took effect in May of this year.\par \par \uc2 Had the Florida measure passed on Tuesday, it would have protected the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until fetal viability, or about 24 weeks into pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 In the weeks leading up to election day, Florida Republicans alarmed civil rights and voting rights groups by unleashing a wave of attacks on the measure. Law enforcement officials investigated people who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/13/florida-abortion-petition-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a petition to get the measure on to the ballot }}}\uc2 , while the state\u8217\'20\'19s agency for healthcare administration put up a webpage attacking the amendment. The health department also sent cease-and-desist letters to local TV stations that aired an advertisement supporting the measure, prompting the measure\u8217\'20\'19s organizers to sue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida\u8217\'20\'19s deadly \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is out of line with the values of our state,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lauren Brenzel, manager of the campaign for the amendment, Yes on 4 Florida, in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida voters sent that message loud and clear today, and despite the fact that only a minority of voters voted to retain the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban our extremist government will exploit the situation to deny its own constituents the right to decide on our bodily autonomy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more of the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 US election coverage\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/when-do-polls-close-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When do polls close? }}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/harris-trump-election-results-when"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When will we know the result? }}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Where is \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  on the ballot? }}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/us-senate-house-and-governor-elections-2024-results-from-all-50-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate, House and governor results }}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/03/us-presidential-election-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Everything you need to know }}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241106ekb6000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
