\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to White House means  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights face new chapter of peril\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 881 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2024\par 16:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could become a reality, and access to other forms of reproductive healthcare are at risk\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , the issue thought to be the magic bullet that would mortally wound {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s }}}\uc2  chances at a second presidency, instead failed to stop him on Tuesday. Now, two years after a conservative supermajority on the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  ended federal protections for the procedure, the future of American \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access is facing a new chapter of extraordinary peril.\par \par \uc2 While {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seven states passed ballot measures }}}\uc2  to amend their state constitutions and protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House means those hard-fought efforts may amount to nothing. Despite the gridlock in \uc2 US Congress\uc2 , a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could soon become a reality: anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  advocates hope that Trump will resurrect a 19th-century anti-vice law to in effect implement a nationwide ban. Access to other forms of reproductive healthcare, such as contraception and in vitro fertilization, are also at risk.\par \par \uc2 Because he\u8217\'20\'19s barred from a third term Trump can now do whatever he wants without fear of electoral consequences, said Mary Ziegler, a professor at the \uc2 University of California, Davis\uc2  who studies the legal history of reproduction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s playing with house money,\u8221\'20\'1D Ziegler said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe can do whatever he\u8217\'20\'19s going to do without fear of conservative Christian voters, without fear of swing voters, without fear of anybody. And he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have Roe v Wade and he has a conservative supreme court, so that means he could do really aggressive things to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or IVF \u8211\'20\'13 or not. We don\u8217\'20\'19t know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the two years since the high court overturned Roe, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  became an issue that seemed to spell electoral promise for the Democrats. Before Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates had triumphed in all seven states that held related ballot measures. Public support surged, including in red states.\par \par \uc2 But the outrage and activism did not translate into enough votes for Harris, who made defending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a bedrock of her campaign.\par \par \uc2 Nor did Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures necessarily boost Democratic turnout in critical swing states such as Arizona and Nevada. Instead, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/interactive/2024/politics/2020-2016-exit-polls-2024-dg/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exit polling by CNN }}}\uc2  indicates that almost half of people who believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in most cases voted for Trump \u8211\'20\'13 the man who appointed three of the supreme court justices who voted to overturn Roe and whose party spent decades dedicated to its downfall. Harris\u8217\'20\'19s support among women also fell. Compared to \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , who won with female voters by 13 points in 2016, and Joe Biden, who won with them by 15 in 2020, Harris won with female voters only by 10 points.\par \par \uc2 Trump has recently backtracked on his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  position \u8211\'20\'13 he recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/TrumpDailyPosts/status/1827007862830452738"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claimed }}}\uc2  he would be \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat for women and their \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 as public support for the procedure has mounted, and it appears that some voters bought it. \u8220\'20\'1CMost Trump voters don\u8217\'20\'19t think he\u8217\'20\'19s going to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  anymore,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tresa Undem, a pollster who has been surveying voters on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Part of the issue, Undem said, is that Republicans are not hearing about the impacts of bans, which are reportedly responsible for at least four deaths.\par \par \uc2 Whatever the reason, the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans now dotting the US map just did not seem to cost Republicans at the polls \u8211\'20\'13 a fact the right could view as an invitation to pursue a wave of new restrictions at the national level.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Outsourcing to people who care more\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Now, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the United States will largely depend on who Trump hires into his administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHistorically, even in his first administration, reproductive issues were not the thing that got him out of bed in the morning,\u8221\'20\'1D Ziegler said of Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd so a lot of the policy was outsourced to people who cared more than he did.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Project 2025, which was primarily crafted by the influential thinktank \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  but backed by more than 100 conservative groups, includes a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laundry list of anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  policies }}}\uc2 . It suggests rolling back the \uc2 FDA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s approval of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, increasing CDC \u8220\'20\'1Csurveillance\u8221\'20\'1D of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and pregnancy loss to police ban violations, and stripping federal funding from family planning providers that mention the word \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. That last proposal may also severely curtail access to family planning services, including contraception and STI testing, for low-income people.\par \par \uc2 Project 2025 also proposes using the Comstock Act, an 1873 anti-vice law that went dormant when Roe was law, to outlaw the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, which account for about two-thirds of US abortions. Other anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists say the Comstock Act can go even further and ban the mailing of all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related materials, including the equipment used by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics. Such an interpretation of the Comstock Act, which could easily be taken up by a Trump Department of Justice, would result in a de facto nationwide ban.\par \par \uc2 Deirdre Schifeling, the \uc2 ACLU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief policy and advocacy officer, said that the organization is committed to fighting a revival of the Comstock Act. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will fight with every tool that we have,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cincluding litigation, including organizing, including people in the streets.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241107ekb7001e8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
