\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrats suffer a drubbing: 10 key takeaways from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election win\b0\par\par\uc2 Richard Luscombe \par \uc2 1,041 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2024\par 17:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  fell way short as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s bombastic style and extreme proposals appealed to more than 70m votersUS election live: latest updates after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  coasted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/donald-trump-wins-us-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 back into the White House}}}\uc2  by a wide margin in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election}}}\uc2 , with the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s bombastic style and extreme policy proposals appealing to more than 70 million voters across all 50 states.\par \par \uc2 His victory also meant misery for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , who was attempting to become the first woman to become president of the US, but who ultimately fell way short, crucially in the handful of swing states that decided the outcome.\par \par \uc2 Here are 10 key takeaways from a historic election:\par \par \uc2 Racism and misogyny defeat joy and hope\par \par \uc2 Harris ran on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/11/kamala-harris-tim-walz-campaign-joy-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 platform of joy}}}\uc2  and new beginnings, but the Democratic presidential nominee was soundly defeated by a convicted felon spouting racial hatred and sexism, including accusing immigrants of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/16/trump-immigrants-new-hampshire-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poisoning the blood}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D of America and calling his opponent a \u8220\'20\'1Cbitch\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdumb as a rock\u8221\'20\'1D. Despite his outpourings of hate and disrespect, Trump looks likely to become the first Republican candidate to win the popular vote since \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  in 2004.\par \par \uc2 Democracy at a crossroads\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House comes with the promise of vengeance on his perceived enemies, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/02/trump-social-media-threats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 political opponents}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2024/nov/06/trump-calls-some-us-news-networks-the-enemy-camp-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the media}}}\uc2 . Voters passed on Harris\u8217\'20\'19s much vaunted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/harris-election-final-pitch-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to-do list}}}\uc2  in favor of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda of revenge. And while the worst of the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s wild policy excesses was largely curbed during his first term by so-called \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/dec/20/jim-mattis-resign-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 adults in the room}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, this time there will be no career professionals to act as guardrails.\par \par \uc2 World order set on fire\par \par \uc2 Prospects now appear {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/06/ukraine-trump-victory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bleak for Ukraine}}}\uc2  in standing up to Russia as Trump, who has claimed he would end the war there in 24 hours, threatens to terminate US military assistance for Kyiv. A similar fear extends to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2 , with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/trump-netanyahu-victory-israel-middle-east"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seen as a win}}}\uc2  for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 . Nato allies of the US, meanwhile, fear the next move of a man who has cozied up to adversary dictators including \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 , Kim Jong-un and \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , and encouraged Russia to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/11/donald-trump-says-he-would-encourage-russia-to-attack-nato-countries-who-dont-pay-bills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 do whatever the hell they wanted}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D to countries who were behind on Nato dues.\par \par \uc2 Climate deniers back at the controls\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has called the climate emergency \u8220\'20\'1Ca big hoax\u8221\'20\'1D, has said he will once again remove the US from the Paris climate agreement and dismantle Biden\u8217\'20\'19s climate agenda, actions experts say could \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/sep/06/presidential-election-climate-crisis-project-2025-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reverberate for a million years}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. His promises to ramp up oil production and burn more fossil fuels \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/10/trump-rallies-extreme-heat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drill, baby, drill}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, as well as weakening regulatory powers or eliminating agencies such as the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  and the \uc2 National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration\uc2 , lead some to believe the US will pose \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/trump-climate-change-environment-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a major threat to the planet}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Quackery to replace public health policy\par \par \uc2 Decades of accepted public health practices, including water fluoridation and mandatory childhood vaccinations, could end if Trump delivers on his promise to give \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , a prominent vaccine denier and opponent of pesticides, \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/election-trump-rfk-jr-vaccines-fluoride"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a big role}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D in his administration. Another assault on the Affordable Care Act is expected as one of a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/trump-healthcare-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jumble of healthcare proposals}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D following the re-election of a president who advocated for humans to take horse worming medicines and inject themselves with bleach during the Covid pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Mass deportation and immigration crackdowns\par \par \uc2 Voters overwhelmingly backed a signature and long-standing objective of the Trump campaign, namely a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/31/election-trump-immigration-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 massive crackdown on immigration}}}\uc2 , and the deportation of up to 15 million undocumented immigrants. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s re-election heralds a return to the White House of loyalist henchman \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , architect of his first-term immigration ban on Muslims and new, equally extreme proposals including the ending of birthright citizenship for children born to undocumented immigrants, and the narrowing of pathways to naturalization.\par \par \uc2 Specter of national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban appears\par \par \uc2 Several states voted to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enshrine \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  protections}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, but advocates for women\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  freedom are fearful that the Trump administration will push for a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Trump asserted during the campaign he would veto such a measure, but he has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/21/idaho-abortion-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 flip-flopped on the issue}}}\uc2 , and cast a vote in Florida on Tuesday to maintain the state\u8217\'20\'19s draconian six-week ban. Analysts speculate he will use an 1873 anti-vice law that bans the mailing of anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  materials to bypass Congress and prohibit shipping of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills.\par \par \uc2 Supreme court extremism sealed for a generation\par \par \uc2 Having hand-picked three justices in his first term who helped overturn decades of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s re-election and new Senate majority give him carte blanche to lock in the rightwing majority. Justices \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  could retire during the next four years and allow Trump to make younger picks to replace them. The next youngest justice, liberal \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 , is 70, and must stay on the bench for at least another four years to prevent Trump securing a 7-2 conservative supermajority.\par \par \uc2 Billionaires\u8217\'20\'19 bonanza as US edges closer to oligarchy\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 , the billionaire \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and X owner, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/nov/06/how-elon-musk-stands-to-benefit-from-trump-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 likely to reap rich rewards}}}\uc2  for his sycophantic campaign support for Trump with a key economic role in the White House. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  founder \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 , accused of assisting Trump by blocking his \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  newspaper from endorsing Harris, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/JeffBezos/status/1854184441511571765"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 regained his voice}}}\uc2  on Wednesday with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/trump-election-win-billionaires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 congratulatory message}}}\uc2 . And other mega-wealthy Republican campaign donors, including entrepreneur \uc2 Peter Thiel\uc2  and hotel heiress Miriam Adelson, can expect huge tax cuts and access to the next president\u8217\'20\'19s ear.\par \par \uc2 Democrats down and out\par \par \uc2 Harris and the Democratic party received an unexpected drubbing in the presidential and Senate campaigns that leaves them in a dark place, with no clear leader or agenda. It is not yet clear if they will recapture a majority in the House of Representatives, but even success there would be razor-thin. While the next presidential race is not until 2028, there are only two years until the midterms and Democrats must act quickly to rediscover their direction and purpose.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241107ekb7001gz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
