\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 This bellwether county heads to the polls \u8211\'20\'13 which way will it swing?\b0\par\par\uc2 Chris McGreal in Saginaw, Michigan \par \uc2 1,918 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2024\par 13:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 8\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Saginaw county in Michigan, a battleground state, will help decide how election falls as US voters remain largely splitUS election results 2024: live map and trackerSenate and House results 2024: live maps and tracker\par \par \uc2 They lined up in the dark and rain before the polling stations even opened across {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/deadlocked--dispatches-from-an-election-battleground"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saginaw}}}\uc2 , the bellwether county in the crucial battleground state of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some just wanted to be able to vote and get to work on time. But there was also a determination among many people that, whatever issues they cared about, this American {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election}}}\uc2  mattered more than most.\par \par \uc2 And Saginaw voters matter more than most, too. America\u8217\'20\'19s complex electoral system has created a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/swing-state-polls-pennsylvania-michigan-georgia-arizona-wisconsin-nevada-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 battleground suite of seven US states}}}\uc2  that will decide the election \u8211\'20\'13 with Michigan among them. Saginaw is one of the closest-fought patches of turf in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 From polling stations inside the Bethel AME church on the solidly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic}}}\uc2  east side of Saginaw city, one of the poorest areas of the county, to the wealthy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  -supporting city of Frankenmuth, many voters saw themselves as turning out to protect their way of life at a time of deep national division in the US.\par \par \uc2 Among those who said they voted for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , the issue of women\u8217\'20\'19s rights after the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned}}}\uc2  the constitutional right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  two years ago came up repeatedly and most often. Cheyanne Laux, who voted at the church, said it decided her vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump obviously has proven in the past that he clearly doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the rights of women in his mind. The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue, that\u8217\'20\'19s the main thing for me, so voting Democratic lines up with keeping that right,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Others who voted for the US vice-president spoke about fear of the damage Trump would do to democracy if he is returned to the White House.\par \par \uc2 For their part, supporters of Trump saw an existential threat to the US in what they regard as uncontrolled immigration and spoke about the former president as the man to bring back jobs to an area badly hit by the closure of car factories over recent years.\par \par \uc2 Tom Harris voted for \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  and then \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the last two elections. This year he cast his ballot for Trump.\par \par \uc2 Harris works at one of the few remaining car factories in Saginaw and is a longstanding member of the \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was a diehard Democrat all the way because that\u8217\'20\'19s what the union told me. It took my brother-in-law saying why he liked Trump. He says, \u8216\'20\'18I hate the man as a person but he can run the country.\u8217\'20\'19 So I started looking at Trump a little differently,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Harris said Trump as president did better on the economy and avoided involvement in foreign conflicts. He compared the global situation then with now, saying that Russia was too scared of Trump to invade Ukraine while he was in power.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss important US election coverage. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Get our free app}}}\uc2  and sign up for election alerts\par \par \uc2 For voters such as Shelley Coon in Frankenmuth, Trump was the man to protect their children from what they described as the Democratic party pushing an ungodly agenda in schools.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe final decision for me was I don\u8217\'20\'19t want our children to be taught what the Democratic party is teaching in the schools, all that 52 genders, non-binary stuff. No, that\u8217\'20\'19s just going too far. For me, that was my final decision. I know there was a whole bunch of topics but that was really the make or break,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t vote the leader. You have to go by the policies and we\u8217\'20\'19re getting too far from religion, Christianity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Michigan saw a huge surge in turnout at the last presidential election as Democrats flooded to the polls to get Trump out of the White House. Seventy-two per cent of registered voters in the state cast a ballot, the largest proportion for any election in Michigan since \uc2 John F Kennedy\uc2  won the presidency 60 years earlier.\par \par \uc2 Both recognise that turnout will again be key this year and are trying to push it to new heights. Trump told supporters at a rally in Saginaw that they needed to vote in order to make his victory \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo big to rig\u8221\'20\'1D as he continued to push his false claim that the presidency was stolen from him in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Harris ended her campaign with a flood of advertising in Michigan attacking Trump as a continuing threat to women\u8217\'20\'19s rights in the hope of getting ambivalent female voters to the polls or women who previously voted Republican to switch sides.\par \par \uc2 Saginaw county will be a litmus test of how successful that strategy has been. Trump took the county in 2016 by 1.1% of the ballot on his way to winning Michigan by just 10,704 votes and with it the election. Four years later, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vote went up in Saginaw but he still lost it to Biden by 303 votes because Democrats who stayed home in 2016 turned out in large numbers.\par \par \uc2 Chelsea la Coppola, who moved to Saginaw Township two years ago from another swing state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2 , said that her vote was primarily decided by \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen\u8217\'20\'19s rights, right to choose\u8221\'20\'1D. La Coppola said she thought the issue would drive a lot of people she knows to vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a big factor for them along with the democracy piece. Everybody\u8217\'20\'19s worried what\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen if Trump gets back in office,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Tracy Goetgeluck, voting in Saginaw city, said she had two daughters in their early 20s and that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights were \u8220\'20\'1Chuge for them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor my daughters and a lot of their friends, their main purpose for voting is because of them feeling that their own rights will be taken away if Trump were president again, and that\u8217\'20\'19s really scary to them. Even my son, because he\u8217\'20\'19s so close to his sisters, is voting because he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want his sisters to have that taken away from them,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Katherine Harris also said that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue is just huge for me\u8221\'20\'1D but as a supporter of further restrictions and a voter for Trump. She acknowledged that the issue could work against the former president, particularly among female voters angry at the supreme court stripping out their rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do think it could harm him with a lot of younger women because in our society we don\u8217\'20\'19t hold ourselves accountable for our actions, and so it\u8217\'20\'19s a lot easier to go and get the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than live up to what we did,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Erica Rapini was solidly for Trump but her first-time voting daughter, 21-year-old Mikayla, kept her views to herself, saying only that making up her mind who to vote for \u8220\'20\'1Cfelt like I was taking a test\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard to decipher what is true and what\u8217\'20\'19s not true in the media and stuff like that. So I really had to do some research,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Her mother was more certain in her views.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy biggest issue is the crime coming over the southern border and the lack of response from the current administration,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Even though Saginaw is about 1,500 miles (2,400km) from the Mexican border, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s repeated and false allegations that immigrants are driving a crime wave has hit home with many conservative voters along with the swirl of rumors and fabricated claims pushed on social media.\par \par \uc2 Katherine Harris swears that undocumented migrants were being shipped by the bus load to Bay City, about half an hour away, where her sister lives. That claim was so widespread that the mayor of Bay City issued a statement last week denying it and saying they were legal migrant workers.\par \par \uc2 Like many Trump voters, Harris said she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t bothered by the tone of his vitriolic attacks and threats against his opponents.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI tell everybody, I\u8217\'20\'19m not here to be his friend, I\u8217\'20\'19m here for him to provide for our family, the way that it should be. I don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with his \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , I don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with some of the comments he makes. But he can run the country,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 But what some Trump supporters brush aside as largely irrelevant, voters such as Goetgeluck see as disqualifying and disturbing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t want another round of Trump. He scares me a lot. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem to think of our people. He is about himself. Before him, our country was respectful of each other. Since he started campaigning against \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  things got really nasty, our elections are just nasty. That\u8217\'20\'19s not what our country is about. It didn\u8217\'20\'19t used to be anyway,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Not many voters spoke about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  with enthusiasm, saying that the important thing was to keep Trump out, and more than a few voters just wanted to get the election over.\par \par \uc2 La Coppola said that the atmosphere had been so fractious she avoided overt displays of support for the Democrat.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re worried about crazies showing up to your house, so you don\u8217\'20\'19t even want to put a sign out. You don\u8217\'20\'19t want to put a bumper sticker on your car. You don\u8217\'20\'19t want to do anything that could set the other side off,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 That concern extends to the election\u8217\'20\'19s aftermath given Trump\u8217\'20\'19s continued efforts to undermine confidence in the legitimacy of the election if it goes against him.\par \par \uc2 Goetgeluck is worried about what will happen if Trump loses and he once again refuses to accept the result as he did when he encouraged supporters to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 storm the US Capitol}}}\uc2  on 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was standing in line and two people behind me, who I could tell were going to vote for Trump, were talking about how there\u8217\'20\'19s already been false voting found in Michigan, double voting, and all this stuff and and I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that\u8217\'20\'19s true. There\u8217\'20\'19s rumours that get started and it just snowballs from there,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Joe Pratt, who voted for Trump but said he would have preferred the former president\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2 , at the top of the ticket, is one of those who believes the last election was rigged against Trump and that this one will be too.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s already people getting busted, people getting investigated. I can\u8217\'20\'19t remember where it was at, but there was a huge bust of voter fraud already. Pennsylvania maybe. It was pretty bad. So right there, it\u8217\'20\'19s already started. There is people\u8217\'20\'19s names aren\u8217\'20\'19t matching addresses. Addresses are false. People\u8217\'20\'19s names are false,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 There is no evidence for this claim. But Pratt is sanguine about what will happen if Trump loses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe all just move on with our lives. We got to ride the wave out. I mean, what else can we do at that point?\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Read more of the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 US election coverage\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/when-do-polls-close-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When do polls close}}}\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/harris-trump-election-results-when"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When will we know the result?}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/election-abortion-ballot-measures-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Where is \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  on the ballot?}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/senate-races-elections-to-watch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/nov/04/house-races-election-democrats-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House}}}\uc2  races to watch\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/election-electoral-college-votes-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 electoral college}}}\uc2  works\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/03/us-presidential-election-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Everything you need to know}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241105ekb500338\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
