\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Republicans outline \u8216\'20\'18first 100 days\u8217\'20\'19 of Trump presidency \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); Chris Stein, Sam Levin, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, Amy Sedghi and Fran Lawther (earlier) \par \uc2 22,055 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 November 2024\par 10:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is closed, you can continue to follow updates on our US politics live blog here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, but we\u8217\'20\'19re continuing our coverage of the aftermath of the US presidential election on our new live blog {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-victory-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election live: Trump to choose personnel in \u8216\'20\'18days and weeks ahead\u8217\'20\'19; Harris says \u8216\'20\'18do not despair\u8217\'20\'19 in concession speech}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Canadian prime minister \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  has spoken with Trump in a phone call during which he congratulated the president-elect on his victory and discussed trade and security in the region.\par \par \uc2 The Canada, US and Mexico trade agreement, which was negotiated in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term was among the topics discussed, Trudeau\u8217\'20\'19s office said in a statement, adding they spoke about their \u8220\'20\'1Cshared interest in secure and reliable supply chains and addressing unfair trading practices in the global economy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The pair \u8220\'20\'1Cagreed to stay in close contact\u8221\'20\'1D, the statement said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Xi Jinping congratulates Trump\par \par \uc2 Chinese President Xi Jinping has sent a congratulatory message to Trump on his win, according to Chinese state media.\par \par \uc2 In his message, Xi said China and the US must \u8220\'20\'1Cget along in the new era\u8221\'20\'1D and urged the two countries to strengthen communication and dialogue so as to properly manage their differences.\par \par \uc2 Xi reiterated that China and the US gain from cooperation and lose from confrontation and that cooperation between the two countries remained a long-term goal, the official \uc2 Xinhua\uc2  news agency said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 South Korean president congratulates Trump\par \par \uc2 South Korean President \uc2 Yoon Suk Yeol\uc2  has congratulated Trump on his \u8220\'20\'1Chuge win\u8221\'20\'1D and discussed strengthening security and economic cooperation between the allies, according to a Seoul presidential official.\par \par \uc2 Kim Tae-hyo, Yoon\u8217\'20\'19s deputy national security director, said Thursday that Yoon and Trump also discussed the growing threats posed by nuclear-armed North Korea, including its intercontinental ballistic missiles targeting the U.S. mainland, and its reported provision of troops to Russia in support of \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s war on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Kim said Trump called for expanding the countries\u8217\'20\'19 cooperation in the shipbuilding industries, highlighting South Korea\u8217\'20\'19s strengths in building warships and vessels, and called for more detailed discussions on improving U.S. competitiveness in ship exports as well as maintenance and repair.\par \par \uc2 Kim said Yoon and Trump agreed to arrange an in-person meeting soon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  warns of false videos that misuse its name and insignia\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  is warning of additional fabricated videos that misuse its name and insignia to undermine confidence in the electoral system.\par \par \uc2 One of the videos falsely claims that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  was made aware that at least 301 electors reported attempted bribery and blackmail by a political party.\par \par \uc2 Another video falsely claims that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  is investigating voter pressure at US military bases overseas, a third claims that a US social media company has seen an increase in the number of separatist groups to include a total audience of more than 40 million people and the fourth falsely claims that the \uc2 FBI\uc2  has ordered media to restrict the spread of information about the bribery of electors.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  says each of the videos contains false information.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Kate Lamb has taken a look at Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s front pages. She writes:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sweeping victory in the US presidential election saw the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/06/us-election-results-map-2024-live-donald-trump-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 securing an unexpected majority in the popular vote}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/senate-elections-republicans-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 control of the Senate}}}\uc2 , and at least 295 electoral college votes \u8211\'20\'13 defeating vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in a contest that dominated UK front pages on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  led with two words: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican Dread\u8221\'20\'1D, a play on the American dream, alongside a close up portrait of the president-elect.\par \par \uc2 Americans awoke to a \u8220\'20\'1Ctransformed country and a rattled world\u8221\'20\'1D as the realisation of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stunning return to power started to sink in, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/election-results-trump-presidency-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Ed Pilkington}}}\uc2 , summing up the mood:\par \par \uc2 enltrThursday\u8217\'20\'19s GUARDIAN: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican dread\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TomorrowsPapersToday?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TomorrowsPapersToday}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Xt0MSsFncU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Xt0MSsFncU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Allie Hodgkins-Brown (@AllieHBNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AllieHBNews/status/1854289168882454719?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The Mirror highlighted a question lingering on many minds around the world about what Trump 2.0 might bring, with the headline: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat have they done\u8230\'20\'26Again?\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory, it said, had ushered in fears the Republican leader would be even \u8220\'20\'1Cmore divisive and brutal than in his first spell in the White House\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrThursday's front page: Trump returns to power {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TomorrowsPapersToday?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TomorrowsPapersToday}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iRAWpGU48r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/iRAWpGU48r}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HRBDJXPLL3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HRBDJXPLL3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Mirror (@DailyMirror) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DailyMirror/status/1854294750146199772?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA comeback to end Trump all comebacks\u8221\'20\'1D ran the Daily Mail, noting that in the end \u8220\'20\'1Cit wasn\u8217\'20\'19t even close\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrIntroducing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TomorrowsPapersToday?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TomorrowsPapersToday}}}\uc2  from: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DailyMail?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DailyMail}}}\par \par \uc2 A comeback to Trump all comebacks\par \par \uc2 Discover more newspapers by visiting our website @ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BZkqOxi6ay"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/BZkqOxi6ay}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/buyanewspaper?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #buyanewspaper}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/buyapaper?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #buyapaper}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/pressfreedom?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #pressfreedom}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/journalist?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #journalist}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/L42HUDPBBp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/L42HUDPBBp}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 #TomorrowsPapersToday @ The TSC News Channel (@channel_tsc) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/channel_tsc/status/1854288733241041004?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 You can see the rest of the headlines here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/07/us-election-2024-newspaper-front-pages-donald-trump-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18What have they done\u8230\'20\'26Again?\u8217\'20\'19: What the UK papers say after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s momentous political comeback}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Decision Desk HQ, an organisation that uses models to project how the vote count will unfold, is predicting that Trump will win the swing state of Arizona, and its 11 electoral college votes. The Associated Press, which the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  relies on to call results, has not yet called the state for Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump to choose personnel in days and weeks ahead\par \par \uc2 US president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will select personnel to serve under his leadership and enact policies that \u8220\'20\'1Cmake the life of Americans affordable, safe, and secure\u8221\'20\'1D in the days and weeks ahead, his campaign said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is more detail on Australia\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador in Washington, \uc2 Kevin Rudd\uc2 , deleting comments he previously made about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  after the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s election win.\par \par \uc2 Rudd said on Thursday the comments did not reflect the view of the Australian government.\par \par \uc2 Rudd, a former prime minister, had previously made the comments about Trump in his capacity as the head of a US-based thinktank, a statement on his personal website said.\par \par \uc2 Among the deleted comments, Rudd had in 2020 described Trump as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most destructive president in history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COut of respect for the office of President of the United States, and following the election of President Trump, Ambassador Rudd has now removed these past commentaries from his personal website and social media channels,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said.\par \par \uc2 Rudd wanted to \u8220\'20\'1Celiminate the possibility of such comments being misconstrued as reflecting his positions as Ambassador and, by extension, the views of the Australian Government\u8221\'20\'1D, it added.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/07/australia-us-ambassador-kevin-rudd-deletes-posts-criticising-trump-after-election-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s US ambassador Kevin Rudd deletes posts criticising \u8216\'20\'18destructive\u8217\'20\'19 Trump after election win }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Japanese prime minister has held phone call with Trump\par \par \uc2 Japanese prime minister \uc2 Shigeru Ishiba\uc2  told reporters on Thursday he had held a phone call with Trump and \u8220\'20\'1Cin a nutshell, he was very friendly\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ishiba said the pair had agreed to organise a face-to-face meeting \u8220\'20\'1Cas soon as possible\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI had the impression that he is the kind of person who I will be able to talk to candidly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Back to what may lie ahead for the House if Republicans regain their majority, from Reuters:\par \par \uc2 For the past two years, members of the House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 unruly and narrow majority have repeatedly gotten in their own way, voting against bills backed by their leaders and leaving them to rely on Democratic support to approve must-pass bills, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Even a more disciplined Republican majority will face barriers, including the Senate rule known as the filibuster, which requires 60 of its 100 members to agree to pass most legislation, a threshold the new Senate will not clear with Republican votes alone.\par \par \uc2 A workaround, known as \u8220\'20\'1Cbudget reconciliation,\u8221\'20\'1D allows the Senate to pass budget-related matters with a simple majority. Republicans used this in the first two years of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, as did Democrats during the first two years of President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s term, when they had control of Congress.\par \par \uc2 Yet budget reconciliation is a limited power. Measures passed with this manoeuvre must be at least plausibly linked to revenues and spending.\par \par \uc2 In late 2021, the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s parliamentarian rejected a bid by Democrats to use reconciliation to grant work permits to millions of immigrants living in the US illegally.\par \par \uc2 Should the 60-vote filibuster rule block a Trump priority next year, he could call on Senate leaders to do away with it, as he repeatedly put pressure on them to do early in his first term, and as some Democrats urged early in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s term.\par \par \uc2 Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  upheld the filibuster against repeated Trump demands to ditch it during the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s first term.\par \par \uc2 McConnell will now step down as leader. While the top two candidates to replace him \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 John Thune\uc2  and \uc2 John Cornyn\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 have said the rule will stay, they and others who might seek the role have yet to face Trump\u8217\'20\'19s direct pressure.\par \par \uc2 And McConnell predicted on Wednesday that the filibuster will remain.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic congressman Jimmy Gomez wins re-election to House\par \par \uc2 Jimmy Gomez won re-election to a US House seat representing California on Wednesday, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 He defeated fellow Democrat and children\u8217\'20\'19s court attorney David Kim, who was running against him for the third time in a row. Gomez was first elected to Congress in 2017.\par \par \uc2 The district is almost entirely in the city of Los Angeles, and is majority Hispanic with a sizeable Asian American and white population. Roughly 20% live in poverty, and it is one of the poorest districts in the state. The Associated Press declared Gomez the winner at 8.36pm ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 House majority leader Steve Scalise, who has said he is running for the position again, told Reuters that Republicans aim to recreate the economic growth experienced early in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term, before the Covid pandemic struck in 2020 and sent the economy into a steep decline.\par \par \uc2 Republicans point to buoyant gains in federal tax receipts since 2017 as proof that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tax cuts raised revenues, and say his current agenda will bring more of the same.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHistory has shown when you reduce the overall tax burden on families, not only do their paychecks go up, but the amount of money coming into the federal government actually increases,\u8221\'20\'1D said Scalise.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs long as you\u8217\'20\'19re controlling spending, that economic growth will actually get you more money to help pay down the deficit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the revenue increase they cite is in nominal receipts driven by inflation and an expanding economy. That turns into a decline when the size of the economy is taken into account, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Trump tax cuts really did cut tax revenue, and what the Republicans are pointing to as phenomenal growth in tax receipts doesn\u8217\'20\'19t actually exist,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Marc Goldwein\uc2 , CRFB senior policy director.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 House majority leader, Steve Scalise, outlines plans for Trump's first 100 days\par \par \uc2 During Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first 100 days in office, Republicans will \u8220\'20\'1Clock in the Trump tax cuts\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cunleash American energy\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Csurge resources to the southern border\u8221\'20\'1D, among other measures, Scalise writes in his letter.\par \par \uc2 On energy, these policies include mandating lease sales, opening federal lands, including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.blm.gov/programs/energy-and-minerals/oil-and-gas/about/alaska/coastal-plain-arctic-national-wildlife-refuge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arctic national wildlife refuge}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1Cto increased energy exploration and production,\u8221\'20\'1D and repealing parts of the Inflation Reduction Act, including what Scalise calls \u8220\'20\'1Charmful slush funds\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On immigration, Scalise says his party will \u8220\'20\'1Cbuild the Trump border wall, acquire new detection technologies, bolster our border patrol and stop the flow of illegal immigration\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrMike Johnson is running for House Speaker again & Steve Scalise is running for Majority Leader, they announce to House colleagues this evening in separate letters\par \par \uc2 Scalises letter was a 4-pager outlining a first 100 days under a Republican Congress & White House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kjgE7D2MB8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kjgE7D2MB8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Liz Elkind (@liz_elkind) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/liz_elkind/status/1854318471418704074?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 Johnson running for speaker and Scalise running for majority leader\par \par \uc2 The House speaker, Mike Johnson, is running for re-election, he announced in a letter late on Wednesday, and the House majority leader, Steve Scalise, is running for his position again.\par \par \uc2 In his letter, Scalise outlined the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 plans for their first 100 days in government. We will bring the key points to you in a moment.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Two high-profile Bay Area, California politicians appeared on track for removal from office through controversial recall elections targeting progressives.\par \par \uc2 Sheng Thao, the mayor of Oakland, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s birthplace, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/sheng-thao-oakland-mayor-recall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 facing a recall election}}}\uc2  funded by wealthy tech and crypto executives and a hedge-fund manager. As of this evening, 65.1% of voters supported removing her while 34.8% have voted against the recall, according to AP results tallied by local {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kqed.org/elections/results/alameda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 news site KQED}}}\uc2  ; only 36% of votes have been counted, however, so the results could still change.\par \par \uc2 Supporters of the recall have blamed Thao for crime, homelessness and other problems. Her narrow victory in 2022 was seen as a win for progressives. She is the daughter of Hmong refugees from Laos and a domestic violence survivor who promised to fight for the city\u8217\'20\'19s most vulnerable residents, but she faced a recall within 18 months of her tenure. She also faced a mysterious \uc2 FBI\uc2  raid on her home, though has not been implicated in wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 Pamela Price, the progressive district attorney of Alameda county, which includes Oakland and Berkeley, is also facing a recall and performing poorly in initial results. With 39.1% of votes counted, 64.7% have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kqed.org/elections/results/alameda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 favored the recall}}}\uc2 , while 35.2% have opposed it. A former civil rights lawyer, Price ran on a platform of criminal justice reform, part of a wave of progressive district attorneys in the US who have prioritized police accountability and reducing mass incarceration, but she was also quickly blamed for crime and violence.\par \par \uc2 More background here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/sheng-thao-oakland-mayor-recall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An unlikely Oakland mayor is fighting for political survival amid a billionaire-backed recall}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat Sam Liccardo wins House seat\par \par \uc2 Democrat Sam Liccardo has won election to US House in California\u8217\'20\'19s 16th congressional district, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 He defeated state assemblymember Evan Low, another Democrat, in the highly competitive race. Liccardo served as San Jose mayor and council member for 16 years before winning his congressional seat.\par \par \uc2 Liccardo will succeed Democratic representative \uc2 Anna Eshoo\uc2 , who decided to not seek re-election, in the heavily Democratic 16th district. The district includes the southern half of the San Francisco Peninsula and part of San Jose. The Associated Press declared Liccardo the winner at 7.57pm ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is the video of \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  congratulating Trump on his election victory.\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president said he welcomed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s idea of \u8220\'20\'1Cpeace through strength\u8221\'20\'1D, arguing that it would bring benefits to the US and the rest of the world. During his election campaign, Trump has threatened both a withdrawal of US commitment to \uc2 Nato\uc2  and a possible end to support for Ukraine in its war with Russia:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 Australian prime minister has spoken with Trump\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Anthony Albanese, has spoken to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and congratulated him on his victory.\par \par \uc2 Albanese said on X a short while ago that he and Trump, \u8220\'20\'1Ctalked about the importance of the Alliance, and the strength of the Australia-US relationship in security, Aukus, trade and investment\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrGood to speak this morning with President Trump to personally congratulate him on his election victory.\par \par \uc2 We talked about the importance of the Alliance, and the strength of the Australia-US relationship in security, AUKUS, trade and investment.\par \par \uc2 I look forward to working\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Anthony Albanese (@AlboMP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AlboMP/status/1854320237656609027?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Thursday, Albanese and the foreign affairs minister, \uc2 Penny Wong\uc2 , responded to the victory by insisting the government is prepared to engaged with him as president, although Wong acknowledged he had campaigned on \u8220\'20\'1Cchange\u8221\'20\'1D and he may therefore do things \u8220\'20\'1Cdifferently\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 The US House contests remain a tit-for-tat fight to the finish, the Associated Press reports, with no dominant pathway to the majority for either party. Rarely if ever have the two chambers of Congress flipped in opposite directions.\par \par \uc2 Republican control of the House \u8211\'20\'13 having already won the majority of Senate seats \u8211\'20\'13 would usher in a new era of unified GOP governance in Washington.\par \par \uc2 A few individual seats, or even a single one, will determine the outcome. Final tallies will take a while, likely pushing the decision into next week \u8211\'20\'13 or beyond.\par \par \uc2 Each side is gaining and losing a few seats, including through the redistricting process, which is the routine redrawing of House seat boundary lines. The process reset seats in North Carolina, Louisiana and Alabama.\par \par \uc2 Much of the outcome hinges on the west, particularly California, where a handful of House seats are being fiercely contested, and mail-in ballots arriving a week after the election will still be counted. Hard-fought races around the \u8220\'20\'1Cblue dot\u8221\'20\'1D in Omaha, Nebraska and also in Alaska are among those being watched.\par \par \uc2 The Democrats have 190 House members to the Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 205. Either side needs a majority of 218 to have control of the chamber; 395 of 435 races have been called.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Philippines president congratulates Trump 'on victory that showed world strength of American values'\par \par \uc2 In the Philippines, president \uc2 Ferdinand Marcos Junior\uc2 , also known as Bongbong, said the American people had \u8220\'20\'1Ctriumphed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump has won, and the American people have triumphed. I congratulate them on their victory in an exercise that showed the world the strength of American values,\u8221\'20\'1D he said on X:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident Trump has won, and the American people have triumphed. I congratulate them on their victory in an exercise that showed the world the strength of American values.\par \par \uc2 We look forward to working with President Trump on a wide range of issues that will yield mutual benefits\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uaQShypkm8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uaQShypkm8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Bongbong Marcos\uc2  (@bongbongmarcos) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bongbongmarcos/status/1854100275327549573?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 Indonesian president congratulates Trump\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Kate Lamb reports that \uc2 Prabowo Subianto\uc2 , president of Indonesia \u8211\'20\'13 the world\u8217\'20\'19s third largest democracy \u8211\'20\'13 has offered \u8220\'20\'1Cheartfelt congratulations\u8221\'20\'1D to Trump, saying the two countries shared a \u8220\'20\'1Crobust and multifaceted\u8221\'20\'1D relationship:\par \par \uc2 enltrMy heartfelt congratulations to Mr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  for being elected as the 47th President of the United States of America.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia and the United States are strategic partners who share a robust and multifaceted relationship.\par \par \uc2 Our strategic partnership holds immense\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Prabowo Subianto\uc2  (@prabowo) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/prabowo/status/1854196684152332480?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is more on Eugene Vindman\u8217\'20\'19s win:\par \par \uc2 The Democrat and former Trump administration official has won his House race against the Republican and former army green beret Derrick Anderson in Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s seventh congressional district, representing a key victory for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  as they cling to the last glimmers of hope of regaining a majority in the lower chamber.\par \par \uc2 When the Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AP_Politics/status/1854304152018399559"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  the race at 6.24pm ET on Wednesday, almost 24 hours after polls closed in Virginia, Vindman led Anderson by two points in the seventh district, which stretches from the exurbs of Washington DC to more rural counties in the western and central parts of the state.\par \par \uc2 With his victory sealed, Vindman will now go on to replace the Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2 , who chose to run for governor rather than seek re-election, when the new House is seated in January. Although the seat does not represent a pick-up for Democrats, Vindman\u8217\'20\'19s defeat may have doomed the party\u8217\'20\'19s broader prospects of winning the House, where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  currently hold a narrow majority.\par \par \uc2 Vindman first gained a national profile after he and his brother, Alexander Vindman, played a central role in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment. The Vindman brothers, who both held senior roles on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s national security council, were dismissed after raising concerns about the then president\u8217\'20\'19s alleged efforts to pressure Ukraine into investigating \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and his son Hunter.\par \par \uc2 Vindman\u8217\'20\'19s name recognition helped him build a powerful fundraising operation that propelled him to victory in a crowded Democratic primary and ultimately resulted in a win on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/eugene-vindman-virginia-house-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrat and ex-Trump official Eugene Vindman wins House race}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 In the final instalment of Anywhere but Washington, Oliver Laughland and Tom Silverstone travel to Michigan to watch the final days of the race; as fervent Trump supporters hit the streets, young women mobilise behind Harris, and chaos and despair drive rival election night parties:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat Eugene Vindman, known as a Trump whistleblower, wins competitive Virginia House race\par \par \uc2 Democrat Eugene Vindman won Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s most competitive congressional race Wednesday, defeating his opponent in a blow to the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s hopes of flipping the open House seat.\par \par \uc2 In Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s seventh district, Vindman defeated the Republican Derrick Anderson by a close margin after conservatives targeted the House seat. Democrat \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2 , the district\u8217\'20\'19s three-term incumbent, has decided to run for governor in 2025 \u8211\'20\'13 presenting an opening in the battleground district.\par \par \uc2 Vindman, despite being a political newcomer, developed a national profile after blowing the whistle alongside his brother during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment. The former army officer focused his campaign on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and the threat of Maga extremism on democracy. Anderson, a fellow veteran and former Green Beret, pitched himself as the more affable candidate, and centered his campaign on the economy.\par \par \uc2 The election between Vindman and Anderson quickly became one of the most competitive in the country, with Republicans hoping to make gains in districts in which they don\u8217\'20\'19t face an incumbent. The acrimonious race was filled with insults and barbs.\par \par \uc2 Republicans steadily represented the district for nearly 50 years until Spanberger defeated former Republican congressman Dave Brat in 2018.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Australian ambassador to US deletes posts critical of Trump\par \par \uc2 The former Australian prime minister \uc2 Kevin Rudd\uc2 , who is now ambassador to the US, has deleted social media posts critical of president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to avoid the comments \u8220\'20\'1Cbeing misconstrued\u8221\'20\'1D, officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/07/australia-politics-live-anthony-albanese-donald-trump-peter-dutton-labor-coalition-reserve-bank-interest-rates-question-time?page=with:block-672bf9498f082be82baf104f#block-672bf9498f082be82baf104f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 An official with \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade\uc2  said a statement from Rudd\u8217\'20\'19s private office account confirmed the \u8220\'20\'1Cpast commentaries\u8221\'20\'1D had been removed from his personal website and social media channels \u8220\'20\'1Cout of respect\u8221\'20\'1D for the office of president of the United States and following the election of Trump.\par \par \uc2 The statement, which was read out, said:\par \par \uc2 This has been done to eliminate the possibility of such comments being misconstrued as reflecting his positions as ambassador and, by extension, the views of the Australian government. Ambassador Rudd looks forward to working with President Trump and his team to continue strengthening the US-Australia alliance.\par \par \uc2 This morning, Australia\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Anthony Albanese, said Rudd was doing a \u8220\'20\'1Cterrific job\u8221\'20\'1D as ambassador.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt says a lot about how important we regard the relationship with the United States that we appointed a former prime minister,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 In a now-deleted tweet, Rudd called Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most destructive president in history\u8221\'20\'1D and that he \u8220\'20\'1Cdrags America and democracy through the mud\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/20/donald-trump-calls-kevin-rudd-nasty-and-says-he-wont-be-there-long-as-australias-ambassador-to-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview in March}}}\uc2 , Trump called Rudd \u8220\'20\'1Cnasty\u8221\'20\'1D and claimed he \u8220\'20\'1Cwon\u8217\'20\'19t be there long\u8221\'20\'1D as ambassador.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the GOP have won the White House and control of the Senate, the Democrats are celebrating several historic wins.\par \par \uc2 In Delaware, Sarah McBride {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-sarah-mcbride-delaware-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became the first transgender person}}}\uc2  elected to Congress. With the Senate wins of \uc2 Lisa Blunt Rochester\uc2  in Delaware and Angela Alsobrooks in Maryland, the US will have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-black-women-senate-maryland-delaware"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two Black women serving as senators}}}\uc2  for the first time in history. And Andy Kim \u8217\'20\'19s win in the New Jersey Senate race made him the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/presidential-election-harris-trump-polls-results-live-updates?page=with:block-672ac4e48f08ec080b940455#block-672ac4e48f08ec080b940455"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first Korean American}}}\uc2  elected to Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 More here in this video on the historic first:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 California leaders say they are 'ready' for Trump\par \par \uc2 California is expected to be a leader in resisting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s extremist conservative policies, as it was during his first administration, and Democratic leaders in the country\u8217\'20\'19s most populous state are now saying they are \u8220\'20\'1Cready\u8221\'20\'1D for the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House.\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s concession speech, California\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , released a brief statement that praised the vice president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign and said:\par \par \uc2 California will seek to work with the incoming president \u8212\'20\'14 but let there be no mistake, we intend to stand with states across our nation to defend our Constitution and uphold the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 Federalism is the cornerstone of our democracy. It\u8217\'20\'19s the United STATES of America.\par \par \uc2 Karen Bass\uc2 , the mayor of Los Angeles and a former member of Congress, said Harris had \u8220\'20\'1Cinspired millions all over the country\u8221\'20\'1D, adding in a message to Angelenos:\par \par \uc2 No matter where you were born, how you came to this country, how you worship, or who you love, Los Angeles will stand with you. This is not a time for despair, this is a time for action. I\u8217\'20\'19ve spoken with leaders across the city, the state and the country. We are ready.\par \par \uc2 Rob Bonta\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, who could play a pivotal role in the expected legal battles over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RobBonta/status/1854246360574579138"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a post}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia will continue to move forward driven by our values and the ongoing pursuit of progress. And I\u8217\'20\'19ll use the full force of the law and the full authority of my office to ensure it. I\u8217\'20\'19ve got your back. I promise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'America is bigger than the results of any one election', Clintons say after Harris's defeat\par \par \uc2 In a joint statement, Bill and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  wished \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance well after winning the election, and acknowledged the disappointment of those who did not support them:\par \par \uc2 enltrOur statement on the result of the 2024 election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1YYdGElPMP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/1YYdGElPMP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  (@BillClinton) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BillClinton/status/1854306162247602653?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  was the first woman nominated for president by a major party, but lost to Trump in 2016, just as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  did eight years later.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New Zealand prime minister \uc2 Christopher Luxon\uc2  has congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and said he looks forward to closer relations with the incoming administration.\par \par \uc2 Luxon said the relationship between the US and New Zealand is \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong and enduring\u8221\'20\'1D and he hopes the two nations will continue to advance its shared interests: \u8220\'20\'1CThe US is one of our most important partners, our second largest export destination, and a major source of global innovation and growth. Our long-standing cooperation both bilaterally and in our region has helped ensure our prosperity and security.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The prime minister also recognised \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would like to commend the vibrant relationship between our two countries and the breadth of cooperation we have enjoyed during President Biden\u8217\'20\'19s tenure. I admire his dedication to public service and the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign says White House meeting with Biden 'will take place shortly'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign said the president-elect had spoken to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and accepted his invitation for a meeting to discuss transitioning between administrations at the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called President \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  to congratulate him on his victory and extended an invitation to the White House to ensure a smooth transition between the current administration and the incoming administration. President Trump looks forward to the meeting, which will take place shortly, and very much appreciated the call,\u8221\'20\'1D communications director \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden calls Harris 'tremendous partner and public servant' after election loss\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who ended his campaign for a second term in July and endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , only to see her lose to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  yesterday, paid tribute to his vice-president in a just-released statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat America saw today was the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  I know and deeply admire. She\u8217\'20\'19s been a tremendous partner and public servant full of integrity, courage and character,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, shortly after Harris had publicly conceded the race to Trump in a speech to supporters in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 The president signaled that he believed Harris would continue as a champion for the issues she had campaigned on:\par \par \uc2 Under extraordinary circumstances, she stepped up and led a historic campaign that embodied what\u8217\'20\'19s possible when guided by a strong moral compass and a clear vision for a nation that is more free, more just, and full of more opportunities for all Americans.\par \par \uc2 As I\u8217\'20\'19ve said before, selecting Kamala was the very first decision I made when I became the nominee for president in 2020. It was the best decision I made. Her story represents the best of America\u8217\'20\'19s story. And as she made clear today, I have no doubt that she\u8217\'20\'19ll continue writing that story.\par \par \uc2 She will continue the fight with purpose, determination, and joy. She will continue to be a champion for all Americans. Above all, she will continue to be a leader our children will look up to for generations to come as she puts her stamp on America\u8217\'20\'19s future.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand the day after the election as the world processes \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decisive win and imminent return to the White House:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672be0148f08040dded3977c#block-672be0148f08040dded3977c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris conceded}}}\uc2  at \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , where she had originally hoped to deliver a victory speech, telling supporters, \u8220\'20\'1CWhile I concede this election, I do not concede the fight that fueled this campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As votes continue to be counted, the margins in swing states appear to show a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672bd0298f082be82baf0ec9#block-672bd0298f082be82baf0ec9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decisive victory for the Republican}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/06/us-election-results-map-2024-live-donald-trump-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won every key swing state}}}\uc2  that has been called \u8211\'20\'13 Georgia, Wisconsin, Michigan and Pennsylvania. Nevada and Arizona haven\u8217\'20\'19t been called yet but appeared to be leaning Republican.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans now have a Senate majority, which will give Trump far more leverage to enact his legislative agenda and, crucially, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/republican-senate-majority-trump-courts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirm judicial and executive nominees}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Control of the \uc2 US House of Representatives\uc2  remains unclear, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/house-representatives-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 many of the most competitive races still uncalled}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Initial analysis suggests that Black women remain the most reliable Democratic voters while Harris suffered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/election-trump-harris-women-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant losses among both Latino women and men}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Special counsel prosecutors will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/special-counsel-trump-criminal-cases"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shut down their criminal cases against Donald Trump}}}\uc2  before he takes office, according to two people with direct knowledge of the matter.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/florida-abortion-ballot-ban-measure-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights supporters celebrated a handful of victories}}}\uc2  on Tuesday night, as several states voted to enshrine protections for the procedure into their constitutions.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has received calls and congratulations from across the globe, including from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672be84c8f08040dded397ba#block-672be84c8f08040dded397ba"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Keir Starmer}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-672bb6bb8f082be82baf0dbd#block-672bb6bb8f082be82baf0dbd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Emmanuel Macron}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672bab678f081ed4eda7b100#block-672bab678f081ed4eda7b100"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-672be96c8f082be82baf0fc5#block-672be96c8f082be82baf0fc5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Obamas}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-672bd9da8f081ed4eda7b36f#block-672bd9da8f081ed4eda7b36f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bernie Sanders}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672bec138f082be82baf0fd5#block-672bec138f082be82baf0fd5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elizabeth Warren}}}\uc2  and other high-profile Democrats and progressives have released statements addressing the stunning loss.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins Alaska\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has also officially won the state of Alaska, as expected, expanding his electoral college lead by three votes, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 As of around 6pm, the Republican had secured 295 electoral college votes, compared to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 226.\par \par \uc2 The key swing states of Arizona and Nevada have yet to be called, as votes are still being processed, but appeared to be leaning toward Trump.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/06/us-election-results-map-2024-live-donald-trump-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election 2024 results live: Donald Trump wins presidency, defeating Kamala Harris}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren on Trump's win: 'The far right wants us to feel powerless'\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts senator Elizabeth Warren, a progressive Democrat, has released an emotional video response to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory, acknowledging the deep pain of this outcome and reminding supporters of the successes of grassroots movements under Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first presidency.\par \par \uc2 enltrMy message about the election results: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Z1X9F6jWik"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Z1X9F6jWik}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Elizabeth Warren (@ewarren) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ewarren/status/1854280390191554775?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will not ask you to look for any silver linings,\u8221\'20\'1D she began her video. \u8220\'20\'1CI will not ask you to feel anything but grief right now. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the election, and the consequences will be real and devastating.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Warren said there will be \u8220\'20\'1Copportunities to fight back\u8221\'20\'1D moving forward:\par \par \uc2 The far right wants us to feel powerless. Extremists are counting on apathy, cynicism, heartbreak, or all of the above as their rocket fuel. They are counting on us to point fingers at each other and to lose trust in our ability to ever, ever make change. I absolutely refuse to give them that satisfaction.\par \par \uc2 When Republicans took power eight years ago, she recalled, it seemed the Affordable Care Act was doomed, but \u8220\'20\'1Cthe American people rose up \u8230\'20\'26 and saved healthcare for millions of families\u8221\'20\'1D. She also recounted Democratic successes in 2018, 2020 and 2021 elections: \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t let anyone tell you that those victories didn\u8217\'20\'19t make a real difference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She continued, \u8220\'20\'1CWe need each other. We take care of each other. And please take care of yourself. Take the time you need right now to be angry, hurt, confused. Hold your loved ones close. Find opportunities to be in community with others.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Her comments come soon after Bernie Sanders, the independent senator and leading progressive voice in Congress, issued a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672bd9da8f081ed4eda7b36f#block-672bd9da8f081ed4eda7b36f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sharp repudiation}}}\uc2  of the Democratic party, saying the failure to embrace policies that would help average Americans led to the terrible performance on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Obamas address supporters: 'Our point of view won\u8217\'20\'19t always win'\par \par \uc2 Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 , who had been rallying for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in the final stretch of the campaign, have issued a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DCC83mcP777/?igsh=YzM2Z3VkOTVyN2dn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  congratulating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance on their victory.\par \par \uc2 The statement says, in part:\par \par \uc2 This is obviously not the outcome we had hoped for, given our profound disagreements with the Republican ticket on a whole host of issues. But living in a democracy is about recognizing that our point of view won\u8217\'20\'19t always win out, and being willing to accept the peaceful transfer of power \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 As I said on the campaign trail, America has been through a lot over the last few years \u8211\'20\'13 from a historic pandemic and price hikes resulting from the pandemic, to rapid change and the feeling a lot of folks have that, no matter how hard they work, treading water is the best they can do. Those conditions have created headwinds for democratic incumbents around the world, and last night showed that America is not immune.\par \par \uc2 The good news is that these problems are solvable \u8211\'20\'13 but only if we listen to each other, and only if we abide by the core constitutional principles and democratic norms that made this country great.\par \par \uc2 Their statement also implored supporters extend \u8220\'20\'1Cgood faith and grace\u8221\'20\'1D to people they disagree with, and praised Harris and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinary public servants who ran a remarkable campaign\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Their statement comes more than eight years after Trump helped build his political career by spreading the racist \u8220\'20\'1Cbirther\u8221\'20\'1D conspiracy theory that \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  was not born in the US.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  speaks to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , offering 'hearty congratulations'\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Sir \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  told president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  he looks forward to working closely together \u8220\'20\'1Cacross all areas of the special relationship\u8221\'20\'1D as he congratulated him on his election victory, Downing Street said.\par \par \uc2 A Downing Street spokeswoman said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Prime Minister spoke to president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  this evening to congratulate him on his historic victory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Prime Minister offered his hearty congratulations and said he looked forward to working closely with president-elect Trump across all areas of the special relationship.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom defence and security to growth and prosperity, the relationship between the UK and US was incredibly strong and would continue to thrive for many years to come, the leaders agreed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Prime Minister also reflected on the situation in the Middle East and underscored the importance of regional stability \u8230\'20\'26 The leaders fondly recalled their meeting in September, and president-elect Trump\u8217\'20\'19s close connections and affinity to the United Kingdom and looked forward to working with one another.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former VP Pence congratulates Trump on his election victory\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s former vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , who fell out with the then-president after the January 6 insurrection, has congratulated him on his election victory:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe American people have spoken and Karen and I send our sincere congratulations to President-Elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his family on his election as 47th President of the United States. We also send our congratulations to Vice President-Elect J.D. Vance and his family on his\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  (@Mike_Pence) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Mike_Pence/status/1854268497926524968?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Pence made a brief and unsuccessful run for the Republican nomination, where he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/07/mike-pence-2024-republican-president-running"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized Trump for his \u8220\'20\'1Creckless\u8221\'20\'1D conduct}}}\uc2  on January 6. He later said he would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/17/mike-pence-republicans-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not endorse his former boss}}}\uc2 , who had shown little concern as a mob of his supporter attacked the Capitol while Pence was inside, but did not rule out voting for him.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris just wrapped up her speech by saying that even if the country struggles in the years to come, it will emerge stronger:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s an adage an historian once called a law of history, true of every society across the ages. The adage is: only when it is dark enough can you see the stars. I know many people feel like we are entering a dark time, but for the benefit of us all, I hope that is not the case. But here\u8217\'20\'19s the thing, America, if it is, let us fill the sky with the light of a brilliant, brilliant billion of stars.\par \par \uc2 The light, the light of optimism, of faith, of truth and service \u8230\'20\'26 and may that work guide us, even in the face of setbacks, toward the extraordinary promise of the United States of America.\par \par \uc2 Her husband, Doug Emhoff, then appeared at her side, and the couple waved at the crowd before heading off stage to the sound of Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s Freedom, a staple at events in her unsuccessful campaign for president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris tells supporters: 'Do not despair'\par \par \uc2 With a nod to future elections that could help Democrats regain political power, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  urged her supporters to stay engaged in the democratic process.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fight for our freedom will take hard work, but like I always say, we like hard work. Hard work is good work. Hard work can be joyful work. And the fight for our country is always worth it,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 She also made a point of addressing young people, who broke for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in surprisingly large numbers in the election.\par \par \uc2 To the young people who are watching, it is OK to feel sad and disappointed, but please know it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be OK. On the campaign, I would often say, \u8216\'20\'18When we fight, we win.\u8217\'20\'19 But here\u8217\'20\'19s the thing, here\u8217\'20\'19s the thing, sometimes the fight takes a while. That doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean we won\u8217\'20\'19t win. That doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean we won\u8217\'20\'19t win. The important thing is, don\u8217\'20\'19t ever give up.\par \par \uc2 Many Democrats dread Trump returning to office, but Harris encouraged them not to be overcome by grief:\par \par \uc2 So, to everyone who is watching, do not despair. This is not a time to throw up our hands. This is a time to roll up our sleeves. This is a time to organize, to mobilize and to stay engaged for the sake of freedom and justice and the future that we all know we can build together.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris concedes election to Trump, vows to keep fighting\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  made her concession to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  official, but vowed to keep fighting for the issues that she campaigned on.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile I concede this election, I do not concede the fight that fueled this campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fight for freedom, for opportunity, for fairness and the dignity of all people, a fight for the ideals at the heart of our nation, the ideals that reflect America at our best. That is a fight I will never give up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harkening back to some of the promises of her failed campaign, Harris said:\par \par \uc2 I will never give up the fight for a future where Americans can pursue their dreams, ambitions and aspirations, where the women of America have the freedom to make decisions about their own body and not have their government telling them what to do.\par \par \uc2 We will never give up the fight to protect our schools and our streets from gun violence and, America, we will never give up the fight for our democracy, for the rule of law, for equal justice and for the sacred idea that every one of us, no matter who we are or where we start out, has certain fundamental rights and freedoms. That must be respected and upheld.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris calls on supporters to accept election result, promises 'peaceful transfer of power'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said she had spoken to president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and would work with him to peacefully transfer power.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, I know folks are feeling and experiencing a range of emotions right now. I get it, but we must accept the results of this election,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEarlier today, I spoke with president-elect Trump and congratulated him on his victory. I also told him that we will help him and his team with their transition and that we will engage in a peaceful transfer of power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That would be a shift from when Trump lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020, and tried for weeks to block the Democrat from taking office, culminating in the January 6 attack on the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris then thanked everyone who worked for her campaign, which lasted just over three months.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo my beloved Doug and our family, I love you so very much. To President Biden and Dr Biden, thank you for your faith and support. To Governor Walz and the Walz family, I know your service to our nation will continue, and to my extraordinary team, to the volunteers who gave so much of themselves to the poll workers and the local election officials. I thank you. I thank you all,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Election result 'not what we wanted', Harris says after losing to Trump\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  acknowledged the disappointment of her election loss to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  yesterday, but called on her supporters to \u8220\'20\'1Ckeep fighting\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy heart is full today. Full of gratitude for the trust you have placed in me, full of love for our country and full of resolve,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe outcome of this election is not what we wanted, not what we fought for, not what we voted for, but hear me when I say, hear me when I say, the light of America\u8217\'20\'19s promise will always burn bright, as long as we never give up, and as long as we keep fighting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris makes concession speech\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has just walked on stage to make her concession speech before a crowd of supporters in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 She is speaking at her alma mater, \uc2 Howard University\uc2 . Her campaign had its election night party there yesterday, but as it became clear that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was winning, Harris canceled a planned address that evening.\par \par \uc2 She conceded to Trump in a phone call earlier in the day, an aide said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and his wife, Gwen, were just spotted in the crowd at \uc2 Howard University\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota governor was Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate in her unsuccessful bid for president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Independent senator Sanders blames Democrats for election disaster\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders, the independent senator and leading progressive voice in Congress, says Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 failure to embrace policies that would help the average American led to the party\u8217\'20\'19s terrible performance in yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt should come as no great surprise that a Democratic party which has abandoned working-class people would find that the working class has abandoned them. First, it was the white working class, and now it is Latino and Black workers as well. While the Democratic leadership defends the status quo, the American people are angry and want change. And they\u8217\'20\'19re right,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sanders, who was re-elected to a fourth term representing Vermont yesterday.\par \par \uc2 Sanders caucuses with Democrats in the Senate and campaigned for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , but has broken with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over his support for Israel, and encouraged him to adopt progressive economic policies.\par \par \uc2 In his statement, Sanders encouraged Democrats to learn lessons from a debacle that saw \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  defeat Harris, and the GOP regain control of the Senate:\par \par \uc2 Today, despite strong opposition from a majority of Americans, we continue to spend billions funding the extremist Netanyahu government\u8217\'20\'19s all out war against the Palestinian people which has led to the horrific humanitarian disaster of mass malnutrition and the starvation of thousands of children.\par \par \uc2 Will the big money interests and well-paid consultants who control the Democratic party learn any real lessons from this disastrous campaign? Will they understand the pain and political alienation that tens of millions of Americans are experiencing? Do they have any ideas as to how we can take on the increasingly powerful oligarchy which has so much economic and political power? Probably not.\par \par \uc2 In the coming weeks and months those of us concerned about grassroots democracy and economic justice need to have some very serious political discussions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a large crowd gathered at \uc2 Howard University\uc2  to see \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  speak, and among the group is former House speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She won re-election last night to her heavily Democratic district centered on San Francisco, but has handed leadership of the House Democratic caucus to \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2  of New York, who also won another term yesterday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris soon to give concession speech to supporters in Washington DC\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is due to acknowledge \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential election victory in a speech to supporters at \uc2 Howard University\uc2  in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president should be taking the stage at her alma mater in a few minutes. She has already conceded the election to Trump in a phone call earlier in the day, according to an aide.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans currently control the House, and appear favored to continue holding the majority, Cook Political Report finds.\par \par \uc2 But it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t look likely that the GOP will expand their already tiny majority by much, and with counting ongoing, there\u8217\'20\'19s still a chance that Democrats claw their way back to control:\par \par \uc2 enltrHouse state of play: Republicans have a more robust path to 218 seats than Dems. Roughly 15 races left w/ a decent amount of uncertainty, and the midpoint outcome is pretty close to the current House breakdown, 221R-214D.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dave Wasserman (@Redistrict) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Redistrict/status/1854244169503371551?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 California at center of knife-edge race for House control\par \par \uc2 If there is any good news to be had in an election that saw stinging defeats for Democrats at the presidential level and in the Senate, it may be found in the House of Representatives, and specifically the races that have yet to be called in California.\par \par \uc2 Just moments after the polls closed in the Golden state, the Democratic stronghold was called for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and the party\u8217\'20\'19s candidate for Senate, Adam Schiff, was declared the winner.\par \par \uc2 But despite a clear majority of blue votes at the top of the ticket, zooming in on the state\u8217\'20\'19s sprawling list of local races showcased deeper divisions, with many contests remaining too close to call.\par \par \uc2 Among them are important seats that could help determine which party controls the House:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As of Wednesday morning, incumbent Republican Mike Garcia was up just two points over Democratic challenger George Whitesides with 67% of votes reported in the district north of Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In the seat left open by Democratic representative \uc2 Katie Porter\uc2  after her run for Senate \u8211\'20\'13 an area considered \u8220\'20\'1CReagan country\u8221\'20\'1D that includes conservative-leaning Huntington Beach \u8211\'20\'13 Republican \uc2 Scott Baugh\uc2  and Democrat Dave Min are neck and neck with 71% of the vote reporting.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Representative \uc2 Ken Calvert\uc2 , the longest-serving House Republican from California, is up one point over Democrat Will Rollins with 69% reporting.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Incumbent Republican David Valadao has a stronger grip on his seat with 55% to Democrat Rudy Salas \u8217\'20\'19s 45%, with just over half of the votes recorded.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The rematch between Republican representative \uc2 John Duarte\uc2  and Democrat Adam Gray \u8211\'20\'13 whom he narrowly beat in 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 is close again with Duarte at 51.4% to Gray\u8217\'20\'19s 48.6% with about half of the Central valley district votes tallied.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican representative Michelle Steel leads over her challenger, Democrat Derek Tran, with 52.5% to his 47.5%, but the AP hasn\u8217\'20\'19t yet called the race.\par \par \uc2 There are also a slew of initiatives put to voters in the state that are still being decided. The \u8220\'20\'1Cno\u8221\'20\'1D votes are leading on Prop 6, which prohibits involuntary servitude as forced prison labor, Prop 32, which increases the minimum wage to $18 an hour, and Prop 5, which lowers vote thresholds required to approve bonds for affordable housing and public infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 The count can take weeks in California, where there\u8217\'20\'19s a strong reliance on mail-in ballots, which are sent out to all registered voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Among those who gathered at Howard for the vice -president\u8217\'20\'19s concession speech was Joanne Howes, a founding member of Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, an influential fundraising group that supports Democratic female candidates who back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTerrible,\u8221\'20\'1D she said when asked how she was doing. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been at this a long time and this time I really thought we were going to do it.\u8221\'20\'1D At 80, Howes said she was less hopeful now than she had ever been that she would see a female president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am so angry at white women. I thought they were going to get it this time,\u8221\'20\'1D said Howes, who is white. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd those white women who voted for those ballot measures and then went to vote for Trump \u8211\'20\'13 figure that out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After appointing the justices who overturned Roe v Wade, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was found liable for sexually abusing E Jean Carroll. Despite a campaign to remind women that their vote was a private matter that did not need to be shared with their husbands, national exit polls showed white women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-elections/exit-polls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chose}}}\uc2  Trump by a sizable margin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to feel sad and sorrowful, but then we have to get up again,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t just accept that our democracy is over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Margins in swing states underscore decisive Trump victory\par \par \uc2 When he was first elected president in 2016, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  beat \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  by less than one percentage point of the vote in the three \u8220\'20\'1Cblue wall\u8221\'20\'1D states: Michigan, Wisconsin and Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 It was a frustrating result for Democrats, leaving many with the feeling that, if only Clinton had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/nov/09/hillary-clinton-election-president-loss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 handled her campaign slightly differently}}}\uc2 , she would have been president.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are still digesting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s defeat last night, but it has become clear that voters were decisive in choosing Trump over the vice-president. As the below chart shows, he improved his margins in the blue wall states, and turned back Harris\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to win Georgia, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  had in 2020, and North Carolina. We still don\u8217\'20\'19t have the results for Nevada and Arizona yet, but he\u8217\'20\'19s leading the count in those states, too.\par \par \uc2 The chart is also a good reminder of how strong Democrats once were in the blue wall, and in Nevada. Have a look:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/datawrapper/embed/1VTxo/5/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Elissa Slotkin\uc2  wins Senate race in Michigan\par \par \uc2 Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Elissa Slotkin\uc2  will be Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s next senator, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s yet another sigh of relief for Democrats in a battleground state that gave its electoral votes to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  yesterday. Though they have already lost their majority in the Senate, Slotkin\u8217\'20\'19s victory for the open seat being vacated by Democrat \uc2 Debbie Stabenow\uc2  means they have fewer seats to retake to gain the majority in future elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Make no mistake about it \u8211\'20\'13 tens of millions of Americans voted to return \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to the White House, and are happy he has won.\par \par \uc2 In the hours since polls closed and his victory was declared, they have celebrated all over the nation. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what that looks like:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve just returned to \uc2 Howard University\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campus, where just over 12 hours ago \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s supporters learned that she would not be the next president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 Students, sorority sisters and supporters have teamed into the venue, once again amassing on the Yard.\par \par \uc2 But unlike last night, the mood is somber. There is no music playing. There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of stone-faced supporters and exhausted staff.\par \par \uc2 Harris is expected to speak here shortly, after her election night defeat to Trump, a somber end to a lightning-fast campaign that many here believed would finally catapult a woman to the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden to address nation on Thursday after Democratic disaster in presidential election\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will address the nation tomorrow, the White House said, after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the presidential election and Republicans gained control of the Senate for the first time in four years.\par \par \uc2 In his speech on Thursday, the president will \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscuss the election results and the transition\u8221\'20\'1D, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 If there\u8217\'20\'19s a glimmer of hope for Democrats after an election that counts as one of the party\u8217\'20\'19s biggest disasters in recent years, it\u8217\'20\'19s in the House of Representatives. Though Republicans appear to be holding their own in the races that will decide control of the chamber, counting is ongoing, and Democrats could still seize a majority that will probably be small.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden congratulates Trump, invites him to White House\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has called \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to congratulate him on his election victory and invite him to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The president \u8220\'20\'1Cexpressed his commitment to ensuring a smooth transition and emphasized the importance of working to bring the country together\u8221\'20\'1D, the White House said, adding that the date of the president-elect\u8217\'20\'19s visit will be announced later.\par \par \uc2 Biden also called \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and \u8220\'20\'1Ccongratulated the vice-president on her historic campaign\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Just how exactly did \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  win the White House?\par \par \uc2 With ballot counting ongoing in many parts of the country, we still do not have a complete picture of which groups broke for Trump, which declined to support \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and which decided not to vote at all. But we do have some idea from the results that have been called so far, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/538/donald-trump-won-presidency/story?id=115556511"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FiveThirtyEight has analyzed them}}}\uc2  to gain some insights into why the vice-president came up short in her bid for the White House.\par \par \uc2 The toll of inflation played a big role in souring voters on Democrats, the polling site finds:\par \par \uc2 According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Elections/exit-polls-2024-us-presidential-election-results-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exit poll}}}\uc2 , 35 percent of voters nationally rated the \u8216\'20\'18state of democracy\u8217\'20\'19 as the most important factor to their vote. Eighty-one percent of these people voted for Harris and just 17 percent for Trump. But the economy was the next-most-influential issue. Among these voters, Trump led 79 percent to 20 percent. In the end, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not rate as highly as Democrats might have hoped; only 14 percent rated it as their biggest concern.\par \par \uc2 So, too, did the increasing popularity of Republicans among voters of color:\par \par \uc2 Initial exit poll estimates also suggest Democratic support declined among non-white voters and rose among white voters (especially college-educated ones). The exit poll indicates Trump won white voters by 12 percentage points, 55 percent to Harris\u8217\'20\'19s 43 percent. Compared to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Elections/exit-polls-2020-us-presidential-election-results-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 exit poll}}}\uc2 , that is a 5-point improvement for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The Republican\u8217\'20\'19s gains with nonwhites was particularly acute among Hispanic and Latino voters. Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 vote margin with the group fell by 26 points, according to the exit poll, to just a 53-percent-to-45-percent margin. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vote share with Latinos looks like it could be the best since \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ropercenter.cornell.edu/how-groups-voted-2004"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 44 percent}}}\uc2  in 2004. Latino men moved 33 points toward Trump, one of his biggest swings.\par \par \uc2 Finally, it appears not as many Democrats came out to vote as Harris needed:\par \par \uc2 So far, around 137 million ballots have been counted for the 2024 presidential race. Predictions of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CoryMcCartan/status/1854054638972285017"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 final turnout}}}\uc2  are hovering somewhere in the neighborhood [of] 152 million votes. That would be a decrease from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fec.gov/resources/cms-content/documents/federalelections2020.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 158 million}}}\uc2  who voted in 2020 and would be equivalent to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://michaelmcdonald.substack.com/p/2024-turnout-forecast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about 61 percent of eligible voters}}}\uc2 . That would be a decline from 66 percent in 2020.\par \par \uc2 It is also likely that the drop in turnout disproportionately affected Democrats. While we can\u8217\'20\'19t be sure until we can review records of who actually voted (states will release those over the next few months), the drop-off in turnout is currently greater in the most Democratic counties across the battleground states. That is something that would uniquely hurt Harris; if you\u8217\'20\'19re a Democrat, then lower turnout in the suburbs is bad, of course, but not so bad as missing the mark in Philadelphia or Milwaukee, where you\u8217\'20\'19re relying on a lot of votes to carry you to victory.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump agreed with Harris 'on the importance of unifying the country' in phone call, campaign says\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has released details of his phone call with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  today, in which the vice-president conceded the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  and vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  spoke by phone earlier today where she congratulated him on his historic victory. President Trump acknowledged vice-president Harris on her strength, professionalism, and tenacity throughout the campaign, and both leaders agreed on the importance of unifying the country,\u8221\'20\'1D campaign communications director \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump may become first Republican in 20 years to win popular vote\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has already decisively won the electoral college but appears on course for another triumph that no Republican has pulled off in years: victory in the popular vote.\par \par \uc2 It was something Trump failed to do even when he was first elected in 2016, which heightened complaints among Democrats that the electoral college is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/18/us-election-electoral-college"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an anti-democratic enabler of unpopular candidates}}}\uc2 . But the dynamic has plagued the GOP for years \u8211\'20\'13 the last Republican to win the popular vote is \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  in 2004, when he was re-elected after winning only the electoral college four years earlier.\par \par \uc2 While all ballots nationwide have not yet been counted, Trump currently has a lead in the popular vote over \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , defying forecasts that the vice-president would be the choice of a majority of voters, even if she did not ultimately become president.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports that as of 2.11pm ET, Trump won 71,930,743 votes, or 51% of the popular vote, and Harris 67,086,484 votes, or 47.5%. The totals are expected to change as counting continues, particularly in states with lots of Democratic voters, such as California.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Macron and Trump agreed on working 'together for the return of peace and stability' \u8211\'20\'13 French president's office\par \par \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  shared a \u8220\'20\'1Cwish to work together for the return of peace and stability\u8221\'20\'1D at a time when the world faces \u8220\'20\'1Cmajor ongoing international crises\u8221\'20\'1D, the French president\u8217\'20\'19s office said on Wednesday after Macron\u8217\'20\'19s first call with the US president-elect.\par \par \uc2 The two leaders had a \u8220\'20\'1Cvery good 25-minute discussion\u8221\'20\'1D, the \u201\'00\'C9lys\u233\'00\'E9e Palace said, in which Macron \u8220\'20\'1Chighlighted the importance of Europe\u8217\'20\'19s role\u8221\'20\'1D and offered to work together on questions including Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine and the Middle East \u8220\'20\'1Conce (Trump) has taken office\u8221\'20\'1D in January.\par \par \uc2 Macron\u8217\'20\'19s entourage described the call as \u8220\'20\'1Cwarm\u8221\'20\'1D, saying the two men had known each other for a long time.\par \par \uc2 Macron was among the first world leaders to congratulate Trump on Wednesday and among the first to have a phone conversation with him.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  re-elected in Wisconsin\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  has won re-election in Wisconsin, the Associated Press reports, staving off a total disaster for the party in a swing state that was crucial in returning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to the White House.\par \par \uc2 While Democrats have already lost control of the Senate thanks to Republican victories in West Virginia, Ohio and Montana, Baldwin\u8217\'20\'19s defeat would have made it even harder for them to regain the majority in the future.\par \par \uc2 That said, things could still get worse for Democrats. Two of their incumbent senators are locked in tight races for re-election in Pennsylvania and Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 both swing states that Trump won.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris concedes to Trump in phone call\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has called \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to congratulate him on winning the 2024 presidential election, an aide to the campaign confirmed.\par \par \uc2 The call formally ends the bitter contest between the vice-president and the former president.\par \par \uc2 The aide said she emphasized the importance of a peaceful transfer of power and being a president for all Americans.\par \par \uc2 Harris is expected to deliver her concession speech at Howard later this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Americans are digesting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s decisive victory in yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, which saw him win every single swing state that has been called so far, make inroads in traditionally Democratic areas, and potentially even become the first Republican in two decades to win the national popular vote. The strength of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s comeback was further confirmed just a few minutes ago, when the Associated Press {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672bae0b8f08040dded394eb#block-672bae0b8f08040dded394eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that Trump had won the battleground state of Michigan. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is expected to announce her concession to Trump in a speech at 4pm, after a night that saw her fellow Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672b6cb18f08e1fe06250332#block-672b6cb18f08e1fe06250332"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lose control of the Senate}}}\uc2  and potentially fail in their attempt to retake the majority in the House of Representatives. Global leaders, from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672b6a578f08e1fe06250311#block-672b6a578f08e1fe06250311"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justin Trudeau}}}\uc2  in Canada to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672b618b8f08e1fe06250267#block-672b618b8f08e1fe06250267"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cyril Ramaphosa}}}\uc2  in South Africa, have spent today reaching out to welcome Trump back to power.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened so far today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672bab678f081ed4eda7b100#block-672bab678f081ed4eda7b100"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already spoken}}}\uc2  to the Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , who was one of the first world leaders to congratulate him this morning.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 , the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  billionaire who owns the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  and blocked it from endorsing Harris, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672b9ed28f08bc33caae11ad#block-672b9ed28f08bc33caae11ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 congratulated}}}\uc2  Trump on his win.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the Republican speaker of the House, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672b99ba8f08376abb057d9b#block-672b99ba8f08376abb057d9b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predicts}}}\uc2  his party will maintain its majority. While the outcome of dozens of elections for seats in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber have not been called yet, a GOP majority there and in the Senate would allow Trump to enact his legislative agenda, which may include aspects of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US support to Ukraine is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672b96668f083c4df5fc848e#block-672b96668f083c4df5fc848e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newly uncertain}}}\uc2  now that Trump is heading back to the White House. The soon-to-be-president has repeatedly said he would bring the war with Russia to a swift conclusion, if elected.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador who challenged him unsuccessfully for the Republican nomination, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672ba7108f08bc33caae1266#block-672ba7108f08bc33caae1266"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged}}}\uc2  Harris to concede.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , a Republican former congresswoman who lost her seat after breaking with Trump and later endorsed Harris, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672b72ef8f08aa3988dc35eb#block-672b72ef8f08aa3988dc35eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  on Americans to accept the election results \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether we like the outcome or not\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In a few short hours, we expect \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to concede the election to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  , a man who embraced some of the country\u8217\'20\'19s ugliest political impulses \u8211\'20\'13 racism, misogyny and nativism \u8211\'20\'13 and turned them against her, the nation\u8217\'20\'19s first female and first Black vice-president.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s 2018 memoir, The Truths We Hold, opens with a scene from election night 2016, when California chose her as the state\u8217\'20\'19s next senator as Trump won a shock election against \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harris was at dinner with her family as they awaited the results. During the meal, she said Doug let out a \u8220\'20\'1Csignature groan\u8221\'20\'1D, leaned over and showed her his phone. \uc2 The New York Times\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 probability meter showed Trump with a strong chance of winning.\par \par \uc2 By the time she arrived at her own election night party, Trump had been declared the victor. Harris said she tossed aside a draft of her acceptance speech.\par \par \uc2 Instead, she told the crowd: \u8220\'20\'1CDo we retreat or do we fight? I say we fight.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s impossible to know what Harris will say in her concession speech. After America returned Trump to power, we will see if Harris still thinks the answer is to fight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump projected to win Michigan\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won the state of Michigan, reclaiming the battleground state and its 15 electoral votes for the Republican party after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  flipped it in 2020.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press declared Trump the winner at 12.54pm EST. The Guardian relies on the Associated Press to determine the outcomes of elections across the United States.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/06/us-election-results-map-2024-live-donald-trump-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election 2024 results live: Donald Trump wins presidency, defeating Kamala Harris}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris expected to concede in afternoon speech\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will deliver a speech at 4pm EST (21.00 GMT) today, the White House has confirmed.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president is likely to concede the presidential election to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who the Associated Press declared the winner early this morning.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu says he had 'warm and cordial' call with Trump after election win\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , held a phone call with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after his election victory, his office said.\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s office said he was among the first world leaders to call Trump after his victory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe conversation was warm and cordial,\u8221\'20\'1D the Israeli prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s office said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe prime minister congratulated Trump on his election victory, and the two agreed to work together for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s security. The two also discussed the Iranian threat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats across the country were left in disbelief and searching for answers as they confronted the reality of another \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  presidency.\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning dwindled, the vice-president decided not to address her supporters gathered at \uc2 Howard University\uc2  in Washington DC on Tuesday night, instead scheduling an address for 4pm ET on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, Democratic operatives and strategists and others filled the void, expressing their disappointment and already beginning to pick apart what went wrong for Harris and the Democratic party.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/election-trump-harris-democrats-loss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats pick apart Trump victory: \u8216\'20\'18How do you spend $1bn and not win?\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  described \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory as a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat moment for America\u8221\'20\'1D on her \uc2 SiriusXM\uc2  program this morning,\par \par \uc2 Haley said Trump had \u8220\'20\'1Cliterally defied gravity\u8221\'20\'1D with his win.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe got through two assassination attempts,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe got through two impeachments, he got through numerous indictments, and America still elected him because, at the end of the day, they knew what they were getting with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And that\u8217\'20\'19s what they wanted to see.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  congratulates Trump and urges Harris to concede\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , the former South Carolina governor who ran against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the Republican presidential ticket, has congratulated Trump on a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong win\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people have spoken,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley posted to X this morning. \u8220\'20\'1CNow, it\u8217\'20\'19s time for the American people to come together, pray for our country, and start the process of a peaceful transition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat begins with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  conceding. You can\u8217\'20\'19t just talk about unity in a campaign, you have to show it regardless of the outcome,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672b8d908f085e4e6e2c8f21#block-672b8d908f085e4e6e2c8f21"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier}}}\uc2 , Harris is expected to call Trump and deliver a concession speech later today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 He was written off as a drag on the presidential ticket, mocked by political opponents as \u8220\'20\'1Cweird\u8221\'20\'1D, falsely rumored to have had sex with a couch, and pilloried as a misogynist for labelling women without children as \u8220\'20\'1Cchildless cat ladies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Now JD Vance \u8211\'20\'13 the butt of a spate of Democratic and liberal jokes for his awkward stump persona and much else \u8211\'20\'13 has turned the tables on his detractors.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s emphatic election triumph is set to put the 40-year-old Ohio senator just a heartbeat away from the presidency, serving under a chief executive who is 78 and has been the target of two failed assassination attempts.\par \par \uc2 It is a dizzying rise for a man who was elected to the Senate just two years ago and now finds himself about to become the third-youngest person in US history to hold the office of vice-president.\par \par \uc2 While Trump\u8217\'20\'19s opponents and many critics dread his return to the Oval Office and the levers of power, Vance waiting in the wings hardly gives them cause to feel reassured.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/jd-vance-trump-vp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s critics thought he was a joke. His political ruthlessness was serious}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , the outgoing Republican Senate minority leader, has told reporters it is \u8220\'20\'1Ccertainly a happy day for the GOP\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 McConnell congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on his election victory, which he credited the Trump campaign for running a \u8220\'20\'1Csmarter operation\u8221\'20\'1D than when they lost in 2020.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re looking for a simple answer, I think it was a referendum on the current administration, in part,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople were just not happy with this administration and the Democratic nominee was a part of it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McConnell also posted to X to say that \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the most gratifying results\u8221\'20\'1D of the election is that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe filibuster will stand\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThe filibuster will stand.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Outgoing Senate Minority Leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  predicts the incoming Senate GOP majority will \u8220\'20\'1Ccontrol the guardrails\u8221\'20\'1D of institutional change that some Democrats hoped to achieve. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lQKPBD1Hbk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lQKPBD1Hbk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1854201851236721013?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The head of the \uc2 US Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency\uc2  has praised the work of state and local election officials and poll workers on election day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we have said repeatedly, our election infrastructure has never been more secure and the election community never better prepared to deliver safe, secure, free, and fair elections for the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D Jen Easterly said in a statement, the Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is what we saw yesterday in the peaceful and secure exercise of democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2  congratulates Trump on 'extraordinary political comeback'\par \par \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 , the multibillionaire founder of \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and owner of the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , has offered his \u8220\'20\'1Cbig congratulations\u8221\'20\'1D to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on an \u8220\'20\'1Cextraordinary political comeback and decisive victory\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo nation has bigger opportunities,\u8221\'20\'1D Bezos wrote in a post on X, adding that he wished Trump \u8220\'20\'1Call success in leading and uniting the America we all love\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Bezos has faced intense criticism in recent weeks after his newspaper prevented its editorial team from publishing an endorsement of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The decision not to endorse has rocked the paper and seen newsroom unrest, resignations from its editorial board and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/style/media/2024/10/29/washington-post-cancellations-number/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 loss of hundreds of thousands}}}\uc2  of subscribers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kemi Badenoch\uc2 , the UK Conservative leader, made jibes about Labour\u8217\'20\'19s view of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in her first prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s questions as opposition leader on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Badenoch questioned the prime minister, \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 , on his commitment to protect Britain\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial relationship\u8221\'20\'1D with the US, and asked him about comments made by the foreign secretary, \uc2 David Lammy\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/what-uk-politicians-said-about-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 about Trump.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe prime minister did not distance himself from the remarks made by the foreign secretary, and I\u8217\'20\'19m very sure that President Trump will soon be calling to thank him for sending all of those north London Labour activists to campaign for his opponent,\u8221\'20\'1D Badenoch said.\par \par \uc2 Starmer assured the Commons he would work with Trump on issues of mutual interest, but did not directly answer Badenoch\u8217\'20\'19s questions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The UK prime minister, \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 , has not yet spoken to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after his election victory but looks forward to doing so \u8220\'20\'1Cin due course\u8221\'20\'1D, Downing Street said.\par \par \uc2 Starmer \u8220\'20\'1Cknows first-hand how busy the first couple of days are after winning an election\u8221\'20\'1D, his spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 The UK leader \u8220\'20\'1Cwould welcome\u8221\'20\'1D a visit by Trump to parliament but parliamentary matters are \u8220\'20\'1Cfor the speaker\u8221\'20\'1D, they added.\par \par \uc2 The newly elected UK Conservative leader, \uc2 Kemi Badenoch\uc2 , called on Starmer to invite Trump to address parliament on his next visit to Britain.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson predicts Republicans will keep control of House\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson, the Republican House speaker, has predicted that the party will keep its majority in the House, which would give Republicans full control of the government \u8211\'20\'13 although that race has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/us-senate-house-and-governor-elections-2024-results-from-all-50-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not yet been called}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Johnson hailed a \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric\u8221\'20\'1D election and said Republicans are \u8220\'20\'1Cpoised to have unified government in the White House, Senate, and House\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to monitor the results and ensure every legal ballot is counted throughout this process,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI look forward to working with President Trump and a Republican Senate to deliver as Speaker of the House on the mandate entrusted to us by the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement on the latest results for the U.S. House:\par \par \uc2 This historic election has proven that a majority of Americans are eager for secure borders, lower costs, peace through strength, and a return to common sense. As more results come in it is clear that, as we have predicted\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mike Johnson (@MikeJohnson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MikeJohnson/status/1854177342765035584?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukraine was plunged into gloom and uncertainty after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory amid expectations that he is likely to end US military assistance while the Kremlin said its aim of subjugating its neighbor remained unchanged.\par \par \uc2 The consequences for Ukraine of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second presidency are likely to be difficult, at a time when Russia is advancing on the battlefield {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/03/kupiansk-russian-forces-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at the quickest rate since 2022.}}}\par \par \uc2 Without US military assistance, Ukraine stands to lose further ground in Donetsk oblast, the scene of fierce fighting since \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s full-scale invasion nearly three years ago, as well as in many other frontline areas.\par \par \uc2 Trump once boasted he could end the decade-long Russo-Ukrainian war in \u8220\'20\'1C24 hours\u8221\'20\'1D. His future vice-president, JD Vance, is an outspoken Kyiv sceptic who has said he \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not really care what happens to Ukraine, one way or another\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s aides have previously sketched out a possible \u8220\'20\'1Cpeace deal\u8221\'20\'1D. It would involve giving Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s eastern regions to Russia, with the existing frontline frozen, as well as Crimea, seized in 2014. Russia controls about 20% of Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s territory.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/02/zelenskiy-trump-risks-being-loser-president-if-he-imposes-bad-deal-on-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with the Guardian in May,}}}\uc2  Zelenskyy made clear that formula was unacceptable. Nor would he be willing to accept a Russian \u8220\'20\'1Cultimatum\u8221\'20\'1D that forced Ukraine to abandon integration with Europe and future membership of \uc2 Nato\uc2 , he said.\par \par \uc2 Zelenskyy acknowledged that a re-elected Trump could, if he wanted to, impose a military defeat on his country. \u8220\'20\'1CUkraine, barehanded, without weapons, will not be able to fight a multimillion [Russian] army,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/02/zelenskiy-trump-risks-being-loser-president-if-he-imposes-bad-deal-on-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he admitted}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/nov/06/ukraine-trump-victory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A gift to the Kremlin\u8217\'20\'19: uncertainty over Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s future after Trump victory}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former president \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  congratulates Trump\par \par \uc2 Former president \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  has issued a statement congratulating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on his victory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI congratulate President Trump on his election as 47th president of the United States of America, as well as vice-president-elect JD Vance and their families,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. He also thanked \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for their \u8220\'20\'1Cservice to our country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Bush noted that election turnout was \u8220\'20\'1Ca sign of the health of our republic and the strength of our democratic institutions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said that he and his wife, Laura, \u8220\'20\'1Cjoin our fellow citizens in praying for the success of our new leaders at all levels of government\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Bush remained notably silent on the 2024 race, while his former vice-president, \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2 , and daughter, Barbara Bush, endorsed Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris to give concession speech at 4pm EST - reports\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s concession speech, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672b8c2e8f085e4e6e2c8f15#block-672b8c2e8f085e4e6e2c8f15"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 originally expected}}}\uc2  at 6pm EST, will now take place earlier at 4pm EST at \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , her alma mater, according to multiple reports.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As Arizonans are waking up, they\u8217\'20\'19re seeing a mixed picture of results \u8211\'20\'13 and still waiting for a big chunk of ballots to be counted that could sway many outstanding races.\par \par \uc2 In Maricopa county alone, there are an estimated 700,000 ballots left to count.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  now leads the state with nearly 52% of the vote, a lead that will probably hold. But Democratic US Senate candidate \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  also has the lead over Trump ally Kari Lake, though by a narrower margin of about 61,000 votes.\par \par \uc2 Two US House seats are within 5,000 votes: incumbent Republican \uc2 David Schweikert\uc2  has the edge in congressional district one, while Democratic contender Kirsten Engel is ahead over incumbent Juan Ciscomani in in the sixth district.\par \par \uc2 And on ballot measures, voters overwhelmingly approved a measure to enshrine access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state constitution while also approving a measure to allow the state to police immigration.\par \par \uc2 Several key legislative races are still very close (one Democratic state senate candidate leads by just 38 votes right now), leaving it possible that Democrats could flip a chamber.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Scranton, Pennsylvania:\par \par \uc2 In downtown Scranton, two women who declined to give their full names were chatting about the election during a cigarette break Wednesday morning.\par \par \uc2 One of the women, Suzanne S, said she had voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  but was surprised he had done so well in Scranton because there was heavy support for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in the city.\par \par \uc2 She voted for Trump, saying he was \u8220\'20\'1Cbold\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cbrazen.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CDoes he say things that he shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t say? Absolutely,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe also says things that a lot of us just say behind closed doors that aren\u8217\'20\'19t being recorded.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She started to go on before taking a long pause and saying \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know if I should say this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe whole transgender movement and stuff I don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CMy daughter has worked very hard to become a level 10 Olympic gymnast. No man should be competing against her. No man should walk into the bathroom that she\u8217\'20\'19s in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The other woman, Danielle D, said she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t surprised by the election results. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just the order of things \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re not ready for a woman president,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 She added that she hoped the fact that America had elected someone with a felony conviction would cause people to rethink broader restrictions on hiring those with felonies for work.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is expected to call \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  today to concede defeat, NBC News is reporting, citing Harris aides.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, Harris is working on her speech, according to one aide.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  also plans to call Trump today and to speak publicly about the election results, the outlet reported, citing a White House official.\par \par \uc2 Timing for both the call and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks is to be determined, it said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will deliver a speech conceding defeat in the presidential election to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at 6pm EST (23.00 GMT) on Wednesday, Reuters is reporting, citing sources.\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/06/us-presidential-election-2024-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-672b78f18f08e1fe062503c2#block-672b78f18f08e1fe062503c2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported earlier}}}\uc2 , Harris plans to deliver her speech from \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , her alma mater, according to NBC News.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  chair, \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2 , will reportedly not seek re-nomination when the party holds a leadership vote early next year.\par \par \uc2 Harrison, who came under criticism for his strong backing to keep \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the 2024 presidential race, signaled his plans to leave the position before Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election results, Reuters is reporting, citing sources.\par \par \uc2 The DNC chair is expected to hold an all-staff meeting on Wednesday to discuss the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 disappointing results and also to discuss a potential timeline for a leadership vote, which is expected to come before April, it said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Scranton, Pennsylvania:\par \par \uc2 Rick Carrick, a 69-year-old retiree was walking his dog, Elvis, outside the Lackawanna county courthouse in downtown Scranton as he processed the election results on Wednesday. He said he was ready to move out of the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just told my daughter, I said guarantee first thing he does when he\u8217\'20\'19s sworn in is he gives everybody from January 6 a full pardon,\u8221\'20\'1D said Carrick, who lives on Biden Street in Scranton.\par \par \uc2 Lackawanna county, home to Scranton, was one of several key areas in Pennsylvania where \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  improved his performance compared with 2020 . \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  carried the county by eight points in 2020, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  carried it by about three points this year. The county was once a Democratic stronghold \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  won it by nearly 28 points in 2012.\par \par \uc2 Carrick said he had no idea why Trump had been able to do so well in the county.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just looking at the big picture. OK, maybe Trump is better on the economy, and to be honest with you, the first time he ran I liked a lot of his ideas, like we can\u8217\'20\'19t be the bank for the entire world,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut then other things that he does, it\u8217\'20\'19s like he wants to be king.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic three-term congresswoman Susan Wild has conceded to her Republican challenger, Ryan Mackenzie, in Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s hotly contested seventh congressional district.\par \par \uc2 Although the race {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/us-senate-house-and-governor-elections-2024-results-from-all-50-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hasn\u8217\'20\'19t officially}}}\uc2  yet been called, Wild released a statement this morning describing the result as a \u8220\'20\'1Cbitterly disappointing outcome\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI lost this election, and my opponent won. I congratulate my opponent on winning this seat, and I am going to do everything to ensure a smooth transition, because the people of this district deserve nothing less,\u8221\'20\'1D Wild said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is how democracy works. It\u8217\'20\'19s how we move forward,\u8221\'20\'1D she continued. \u8220\'20\'1CYou cannot only recognize the results of elections you win, no matter how much you may disagree with them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMy statement on the election results ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uN2CZ1gPX8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uN2CZ1gPX8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Susan Wild (@wildforcongress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/wildforcongress/status/1854159820460359985?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 JD Vance thanks Trump for the 'opportunity to serve our country' as vice-president\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, JD Vance, has thanked him for \u8220\'20\'1Cgiving me such an opportunity to serve our country at this level\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTHANK YOU!\u8221\'20\'1D Vance wrote on X this morning, as he also thanked his \u8220\'20\'1Cbeautiful\u8221\'20\'1D wife, Usha, \u8220\'20\'1Cfor making it possible to do this\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd to the American people, for their trust. I will never stop fighting for ALL of you,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s president, Lai Ching-te, has offered his \u8220\'20\'1Csincere\u8221\'20\'1D congratulations to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on his election victory.\par \par \uc2 Lai, in a statement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ChingteLai/status/1854122825168343494?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1854122825168343494%7Ctwgr%5E1a2378269b3ea0240e6f6c0b4dc7835eeb549c50%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.reuters.com%2Fworld%2Fus-presidential-election-day-live-2024-11-05%2F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted}}}\uc2  to X, said he is \u8220\'20\'1Cconfident\u8221\'20\'1D that the Taiwan-US partnership \u8220\'20\'1Cwill continue to serve as a cornerstone for regional stability [and] lead to greater prosperity for us all\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a video timeline showing how the night of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidential comeback unfolded:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hours before it became official that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will return to the White House, his biggest supporter was already inside the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , who has been a key backer of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s return to the presidency, was in his default wind-up mode as he used his X platform to post a superimposed picture of himself \u8211\'20\'13 holding a sink \u8211\'20\'13 inside the seat of US power. \u8220\'20\'1CLet that sink in,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 enltrLet that sink in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XvYFtDrhRm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XvYFtDrhRm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  (@elonmusk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/1854034776815972649?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 It was amateurish but Musk\u8217\'20\'19s contribution to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory has been serious and will reap benefits for the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest person.\par \par \uc2 There were immediate signs of a return on that investment on Wednesday morning. Shares in \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , the electric car maker, which he leads as CEO and in which he owns a 13% stake, were up about 15% in pre-trading on Wall Street, implying a wealth gain of $15bn. There could be more to come.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/nov/06/how-elon-musk-stands-to-benefit-from-trump-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18new star\u8217\'20\'19 Elon Musk stands to benefit from his presidency}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris to address the nation from \uc2 Howard University\uc2  this afternoon \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is expected to address her supporters and the nation from \uc2 Howard University\uc2  early on Wednesday afternoon, NBC News is reporting, citing three Harris aides.\par \par \uc2 Howard University\uc2  is Harris\u8217\'20\'19s alma mater; she graduated in 1986 with a bachelor\u8217\'20\'19s degree in political science and economics.\par \par \uc2 Harris launched her first campaign on the university campus when she ran for freshman class representative, and returned in 2019 to announce her presidential run in for the 2020 election cycle. Harris also used the campus as the site to prepare for her August debate against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2 , the Florida senator, said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the election by \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamentally remaking\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I\u8217\'20\'19m most impressed by is not just the size of the victory, I know the number is still growing, but the way \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won this election,\u8221\'20\'1D Rubio told CNN this morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe won it by fundamentally remaking the Republican party, but I hope also revealing to people that for voters in the United States of America, their primary identity is not their ethnicity. It\u8217\'20\'19s not their race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s what they do for a living. It\u8217\'20\'19s who\u8217\'20\'19s who they are in their daily lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/marcorubio?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @marcorubio}}}\uc2  tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kasie?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @kasie}}}\uc2  : "What I'm most impressed by is not just the size of the victory \u8212\'20\'14 I know the number is still growing \u8212\'20\'14 but the way \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won this election. He won it by fundamentally remaking the Republican Party." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4ZtmnlGoFa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4ZtmnlGoFa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CNN This Morning with Kasie Hunt (@CNNThisMorning) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNNThisMorning/status/1854142375859237177?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Climate activists with the Just Stop Oil environmental group sprayed the US embassy in London with orange paint in protest of \u8220\'20\'1Cfascism\u8221\'20\'1D following \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election victory.\par \par \uc2 The group posted a video on X showing two men spraying paint on a section of the embassy building in south London, accompanied with the warning that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s win \u8220\'20\'1Cputs the lives of ordinary people at risk, everywhere\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 London\u8217\'20\'19s Metropolitan police arrested two men, aged 25 and 72, on suspicion of criminal damage, the force said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis activity is vandalism purporting as protest and we will continue to have a zero tolerance attitude to actions such as this,\u8221\'20\'1D a statement by Met police deputy assistant commissioner Andy Valentine said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  urges Americans to accept election results 'whether we like the outcome or not'\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , a former Republican congresswoman and prominent Trump critic, has urged Americans to accept the election results \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether we like the outcome or not\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Cheney, who campaigned for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , said Americans, the courts, members of the press, and those serving in the federal, state and local governments \u8220\'20\'1Cmust now be the guardrails of democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe now have a special responsibility, as citizens of the greatest nation on earth, to do everything we can to support and defend our Constitution, preserve the rule of law, and ensure that our institutions hold over these coming four years,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote.\par \par \uc2 enltrOur nation\u8217\'20\'19s democratic system functioned last night and we have a new President-elect. All Americans are bound, whether we like the outcome or not, to accept the results of our elections. We now have a special responsibility, as citizens of the greatest nation on earth, to do\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  (@Liz_Cheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Liz_Cheney/status/1854147758300733567?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican Tim Sheehy\u8217\'20\'19s challenge for the Montana Senate seat was considered a referendum on whether Democrats can {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/12/us/politics/jon-tester-democrats-great-plains.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 win in largely rural states}}}\uc2 , which have moved to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s far-right brand of Republicanism.\par \par \uc2 The race prompted questions about whether grassroots campaigning \u8211\'20\'13 which historically has proved successful in Montana \u8211\'20\'13 is at all effective when news coverage and campaign spending have made local politics national.\par \par \uc2 Montana, which has a population of 1.1 million, saw $280m in campaign ad spending, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/battle-for-senate-control-goes-down-to-the-wire-as-spending-shatters-records"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania and Ohio, which saw $340m and about $500m in respective spending, have about 10 times the population of the western state, further underscoring its perceived importance to both political parties.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/election-montana-senate-race-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican Tim Sheehy wins Montana Senate race over incumbent Jon Tester}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican Tim Sheehy defeats three-term Montana senator \uc2 Jon Tester\par \par \uc2 Republican Tim Sheehy is projected to defeat three-term incumbent Montana senator \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2 , flipping a closely watched Senate seat and adding to the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s newly won majority in the upper House.\par \par \uc2 Sheehy, a former Navy SEAL, ran as a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -supporting conservative in a state where he is immensely popular.\par \par \uc2 Tester \u8211\'20\'13 a moderate and the Senate\u8217\'20\'19s only working farmer \u8211\'20\'13 was considered one of the most vulnerable Democrats on the ballot nationwide. He was the only Democrat holding statewide office in Montana, which has voted for the Republican presidential candidate in every contest since 1992.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  relies on the Associated Press to determine the outcomes of elections across the United States. The New York-based global news agency has a presence in every US state and a long and authoritative history of determining the winners of elections at the presidential, congressional and state level. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/ap-race-calls-faq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here is more information}}}\uc2  about their process.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/us-senate-house-and-governor-elections-2024-results-from-all-50-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 You can keep track of the results from all 50 states as they come in here.}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/us-senate-house-and-governor-elections-2024-results-from-all-50-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate, House and governor elections 2024: results from all 50 states as Republicans win Senate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Canada's Trudeau congratulates Trump on election win\par \par \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2 , the Canadian prime minister, has congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in a post on X accompanied by a photograph of the two of them in the White House during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term in office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe friendship between Canada and the US is the envy of the world,\u8221\'20\'1D Trudeau wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CI know President Trump and I will work together to create more opportunity, prosperity, and security for both of our nations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on being elected President of the United States.\par \par \uc2 The friendship between Canada and the U.S. is the envy of the world. I know President Trump and I will work together to create more opportunity, prosperity, and security for both of our nations. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yEnL6gxyzO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/yEnL6gxyzO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Justin Trudeau\uc2  (@JustinTrudeau) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JustinTrudeau/status/1854134862921314380?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Sometimes fear triumphs over hope. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s shocking victory in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/nov/09/donald-trump-supporters-hilton-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2016 US presidential election}}}\uc2  was described as a leap into the political unknown. This time there is no excuse. America knew that he was a convicted criminal, serial liar and racist demagogue who four years ago attempted to overthrow the government. It voted for him anyway.\par \par \uc2 The result is a catastrophe for the world. It saw {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  competence and expertise, her decency and grace, her potential to be the first female president in America\u8217\'20\'19s 248-year history. It also saw Trump\u8217\'20\'19s venality and vulgarity, his crass insults and crude populism, his dehumanisation of immigrants that echoed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/22/trump-anti-immigrant-rhetoric-republican-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adolf Hitler}}}\uc2 . And the world asked: how is this race even close?\par \par \uc2 But elections hold up a mirror to a nation and the nation does not always like what it sees.\par \par \uc2 Future historians will marvel at how Trump rose from the political dead. When he lost the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/dec/08/us-election-results-2020-joe-biden-defeats-donald-trump-to-win-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2020 election to }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/dec/08/us-election-results-2020-joe-biden-defeats-donald-trump-to-win-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  , people gathered outside the White House to celebrate, brandishing signs that said, \u8220\'20\'1CBon Voyage\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CDemocracy wins!\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re fired!\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is over\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CLoser\u8221\'20\'1D. There was a tone of finality, a sense that, after four gruelling years, this particular national nightmare was over.\par \par \uc2 But Trump could do no wrong in the eyes of his cult-like following, a freakishly resilient appeal that has three main components.\par \par \uc2 First, there is the celebrity and successful businessman persona, fashioned over years by his book The Art of the Deal and the reality TV show The Apprentice. Harris recruited numerous big-name endorsers such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-endorses-kamala-harris-president-us-debate-cat-lady"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor Swift}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/beyonce-brings-star-power-to-harris-rally-in-texas-with-abortion-law-in-the-spotlight"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9}}}\uc2  ; Trump was star of his own show.\par \par \uc2 Second, Trump has understood that, whereas \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  resonated in an era of aspiration, this is an age of anxiety. The upper-working class and lower-middle class fear loss of status and yearn for a safety blanket. Young people worry they will be worse off than their parents\u8217\'20\'19 generation and unable to buy homes. Many, wrongly, perceive Trump as an economic populist because he rails against elites and \u8220\'20\'1Csays it like it is\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cspeaks how they feel\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t give a fuck\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Third, there is Trump the culture warrior. For nearly a decade he has tapped into America\u8217\'20\'19s id: a long and painful racial history of progress and backlash, stoked anew by the election of Obama and white Christians finding themselves in the minority. Xenophobia is at the heart of his political identity. In addition, his campaign spent millions on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://host2.adimpact.com/admo/viewer/8a9dc875-207e-417b-a3cf-e15362f42320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ads}}}\uc2  fuelling hysteria about transgender rights (\u8220\'20\'1CKamala\u8217\'20\'19s agenda is they/them, not you\u8221\'20\'1D).\par \par \uc2 Together, with a sinister assist from billionaire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/audio/2024/oct/25/why-elon-musk-needs-donald-trump-to-win-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2  , it was enough to eke out victory.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/how-trump-won-us-election-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fear triumphs over hope as Trump wins the presidency \u8211\'20\'13 how did it happen?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 International charity ActionAid has warned that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s re-election sends an \u8220\'20\'1Cexistential and dangerous threat to women and girls\u8217\'20\'19 rights across the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hannah Bond, Co-CEO at \uc2 ActionAid UK\uc2  said on Wednesday:\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election poses an existential and dangerous threat to women and girls rights across the world and to global peace and security.\par \par \uc2 Millions in America will be waking up to a future where their \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  and freedoms are fundamentally at risk, particularly the most marginalised people.\par \par \uc2 For women and girls facing crises across the world \u8211\'20\'13 whether in Gaza or in Ukraine \u8211\'20\'13 this is a devastating result that threatens global peace and security.\par \par \uc2 With leaders gathering at COP next week, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plans to pull out of the Paris agreement all but ends the hope of meaningful US climate action.\par \par \uc2 With the UK committed to \u8216\'20\'18standing shoulder to shoulder\u8217\'20\'19 with the new US administration, it must hold the US to account in the fight for gender equality.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 An election that barely mentioned climate could end up being the most consequential for the planet in modern history. Donald Trump is expected to pull the US out of the Paris agreement, joining just three other countries, Iran, Libya and Yemen.\par \par \uc2 The agreement\u8217\'20\'19s overarching goal is to hold \u8220\'20\'1Cthe increase in the global average temperature to well below 2C above preindustrial levels\u8221\'20\'1D and pursue efforts \u8220\'20\'1Cto limit the temperature increase to 1.5C above preindustrial levels.\u8221\'20\'1D Those countries that signed up agreed to taper off their carbon emissions by the middle of this century to achieve this.\par \par \uc2 He is also expected to cancel many of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s climate policies and, as he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cdrill, baby, drill\u8221\'20\'1D, turbocharging oil and gas production.\par \par \uc2 This will have dire consequences. CarbonBrief has estimated this will cause an additional 4bn tonnes of carbon dioxide equivalent (GtCO2e) by 2030 emitted from the US. This would negate twice over all of the savings from deploying wind, solar and other clean technologies around the world over the past five years.\par \par \uc2 Experts believe a second Trump presidency would end all hope of keeping global warming below 1.5C, the limit agreed by scientists which would avoid the worst impacts of climate breakdown. These include extreme, deadly weather events which can wipe out populations and cause mass deaths, as well as temperatures rising to make some parts of the world uninhabitable, as well as climate related severe disruptions to the food supply as fertile lands become desert.\par \par \uc2 It also has global impacts; when right wing parties falsely claim that lowering emissions and switching to a green economy is expensive, and the US is not participating in this effort, they can plausibly ask why other countries are doing that. This is likely to happen in the UK, where politicians are already falsely claiming the Labour government\u8217\'20\'19s green policies will drive up energy bills and cause rationing. To be clear, this is utterly false, but it is a message that could take hold in difficult times if there is not a proactive effort to make the positive economic case for the green transition.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 South Africa's president Ramaphosa congratulates Trump on his election victory\par \par \uc2 South Africa\u8217\'20\'19s president Cyril Ramaphosa has congratulated Trump on his election victory.\par \par \uc2 In a post on X, Ramaphosa said he was looking forward to working closely with the US during South Africa\u8217\'20\'19s G20 presidency next year. The US will succeed South Africa as president of the grouping, which includes 19 of the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest economies and the European and African unions.\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations to United States President-Elect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  on your return to the Presidency.\par \par \uc2 I look forward to continuing the close and mutually beneficial partnership between our two nations across all domains of our cooperation.\par \par \uc2 In the global arena, we look forward to\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HoQUQpp1gD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HoQUQpp1gD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Cyril Ramaphosa ???? (@CyrilRamaphosa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CyrilRamaphosa/status/1854122247968981190?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 South Africa\u8217\'20\'19s head of public diplomacy, Clayson Monyela, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://african.business/2024/11/politics/trump-declares-comeback-victory-after-swing-state-wins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deleted an earlier post on X}}}\uc2 , in which he said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll leave it to my seniors but congratulations are in order for the president-elect\u8230\'20\'26.\par \par \uc2 Historically relations between South Africa & the US thrive under a Republican White House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last year, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/may/11/us-accuses-south-africa-of-providing-arms-to-russia-reports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US ambassador to South Africa accused the country of providing arms to Russia}}}\uc2 , a claim South Africa\u8217\'20\'19s government furiously denied.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign was seen by many of her supporters, and others across the world, as having the potential of saving American democracy from an existential threat and a sign that US politics might be returning to a more normal state of affairs.\par \par \uc2 With a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  victory on Wednesday morning, that potential disappeared.\par \par \uc2 After the shock exit of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  following his disastrous debate performance raised questions about his mental acuity, Harris and her team ran a campaign that by American standards was incredibly short. Despite having had support by stars like Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 and Taylor Swift, gathering more than a billion dollars in fundraising, and crisscrossing the country in relentless rallies, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s bid to win the White House ended in defeat.\par \par \uc2 Here are some key moments, issues and events from the campaign:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/kamala-harris-key-moments-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From joy to defeat: the Kamala Harris campaign in 10 events}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin reacted cautiously on Wednesday after Donald Trump was elected US president, saying the US was still a hostile state and that only time would tell if Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric on ending the Ukraine war translated into reality, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Kremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov said Trump had made some important statements about wanting to end the Ukraine war during his campaign, but only time would tell if they led to action.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet us not forget that we are talking about an unfriendly country, which is both directly and indirectly involved in a war against our state [in Ukraine],\u8221\'20\'1D Peskov told reporters, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Peskov said he was not aware of any plans by the Russian president, Vladimir Putin, to congratulate Trump on his victory and that relations with Washington were at an historic low.\par \par \uc2 Peskov said:\par \par \uc2 We have repeatedly said that the US is able to contribute to the end of this conflict. This cannot be done overnight, but \u8230\'20\'26 the US is capable of changing the trajectory of its foreign policy. Will this happen, and if so, how \u8230\'20\'26 we will see after [the US president\u8217\'20\'19s inauguration in] January.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Russian and US diplomats say relations between the world\u8217\'20\'19s two largest nuclear powers have only been worse during the depths of the cold war. According to Reuters, Russian officials from Putin down said ahead of the election that it made no difference to Moscow who won the White House, even as Kremlin-guided state media coverage showed a preference for Trump.\par \par \uc2 The Russian Foreign Ministry said Moscow had no illusions about Trump, noting that there was what it called a bipartisan anti-Russian position among the US ruling elite designed to try to contain Russia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussia will work with the new administration when it \u8216\'20\'18takes up residence\u8217\'20\'19 in the White House, fiercely defending Russian national interests and focusing on achieving all the set objectives of the special military operation (in Ukraine),\u8221\'20\'1D the ministry said. \u8220\'20\'1COur conditions are unchanged and are well known in Washington.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kirill Dmitriev, the influential head of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s sovereign wealth fund, struck a softer note, saying a Trump victory could be a chance to repair ties, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis opens up new opportunities for resetting relations between Russia and the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D added Dmitriev, a former Goldman Sachs banker who has previously had contacts with the Trump team.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian community team would like to hear people\u8217\'20\'19s thoughts about Donald Trump having decisively won the US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 They are keen to hear from people who voted for Trump and those who did not about what shaped their vote, what they now make of the election result, and how they may now look back on the polls and the election campaigns of Trump and Kamala Harris.\par \par \uc2 Please share your story if you are 18 or over, anonymously if you wish by filling out the form at the below link:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/share-your-reactions-to-donald-trumps-seismic-victory"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Share your reactions to Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s seismic victory}}}\par \par \uc2 For more information please see our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/help/terms-of-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 terms of service}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/help/privacy-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 privacy policy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 On stage in West Palm Beach in the early hours of Wednesday morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  thanked his supporters, his family and his campaign team as he declared victory in the US presidential race. One group not on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s thank-you cards: the media, whom he referred to as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy camp\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Introducing his running mate, the Ohio senator JD Vance, Trump said:\par \par \uc2 I told JD to go into the enemy camp. He just goes: OK. Which one? CNN? MSNBC? He\u8217\'20\'19s like the only guy who looks forward to going on, and then just absolutely obliterates them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has had an antagonistic relationship with the US press for years, often labeling them as the \u8220\'20\'1Ccrooked media\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/story/trump-rally-man-attacks-journalists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 calling them }}}\uc2  the \u8220\'20\'1Cenemy of the people\u8221\'20\'1D. But as the Republican candidate in recent weeks ramped up his rhetoric against his perceived opponents, he\u8217\'20\'19s intensified his attacks on reporters as well.\par \par \uc2 The comment during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory speech come less than a week after he joked during a campaign rally he would have no concerns about reporters being shot at if there were another assassination attempt against him.\par \par \uc2 During meandering comments at a rally in Pennsylvania last week, Trump complained about gaps in the bulletproof shields surrounding him after a gunman opened fire on him at a rally in July.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo get me, somebody would have to shoot through the fake news and I don\u8217\'20\'19t mind that so much,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The press, he added, were \u8220\'20\'1Cseriously corrupt people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s communications director later claimed in a statement the comments were supposedly an effort to look out for the welfare of the news media.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/trump-media-enemy-camp-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump calls media \u8216\'20\'18the enemy camp\u8217\'20\'19 in speech declaring victory}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Voters have elected a Republican majority in the Senate. They have also been electing members of the House of Representatives and state governors.\par \par \uc2 You can keep track of the results from all 50 states as they come in here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/us-senate-house-and-governor-elections-2024-results-from-all-50-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate, House and governor elections 2024: results from all 50 states as Republicans win Senate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 Germany\u8217\'20\'19s Scholz and Italy\u8217\'20\'19s Meloni congratulate Trump on US election win\par \par \uc2 Olaf Scholz congratulated Donald Trump on Wednesday. In a post on X, the German chancellor said that Germany and the US will continue to work together to \u8220\'20\'1Csuccessfully\u8221\'20\'1D promote \u8220\'20\'1Cprosperity and freedom on both sides of the Atlantic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Scholz said:\par \par \uc2 I congratulate Donald Trump on his election as US president. For a long time, Germany and the US have been working together successfully promoting prosperity and freedom on both sides of the Atlantic. We will continue to do so for the wellbeing of our citizens.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amid the congratulations, France and Germany arranged a last-minute meeting of their defence ministers on Wednesday to discuss the results of the US elections and its implications for Ukraine and European defence, reports the Associated Press (AP).\par \par \uc2 enltrI congratulate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  on his election as US President. For a long time, Germany and the US have been working together successfully promoting prosperity and freedom on both sides of the Atlantic. We will continue to do so for the wellbeing of our citizens.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bundeskanzler Olaf Scholz (@Bundeskanzler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Bundeskanzler/status/1854093492479263186?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The Italian premier, Giorgia Meloni, also offered congratulations to Trump. According to the AP, Meloni said:\par \par \uc2 Italy and the United States are sister nations, linked by an unshakeable alliance, common values and a historic friendship. It is a strategic bond, which I am sure we will now strengthen even more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More a natural ally of Trump than many European leaders, Meloni in 2022 became the head of Italy\u8217\'20\'19s first far-right-led government since the second world war. She has forged alliances with other right-wing leaders in Europe and has made a mark cracking down on migration.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s shock {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 return}}}\uc2  to the White House has delighted his tens of millions of supporters in the US but stunned the rest of the country and much of the fearfully watching world.\par \par \uc2 Few would have imagined such a scenario when Trump left office in disgrace in January 2021, in the wake of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack}}}\uc2  on the Capitol in Washington DC and facing a long list of legal travails.\par \par \uc2 But his campaign has won back the Oval Office. It was possibly one of the most extreme campaigns in recent history, dogged by racist language, violent rhetoric and a profound sense of grievance. But it resonated with enough people in America to carve out a second Trump term and take the US into unexplored political terrain.\par \par \uc2 Here are some key moments, issues and events from the campaign:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/trump-key-moments-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Racism, snipers\u8217\'20\'19 bullets and Elon Musk: the Trump campaign in 10 moments}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 'Major blow to global climate action': climate figures react to Trump re-election\par \par \uc2 Many climate figures are horrified by the re-election of Donald Trump as president, citing his past denial of climate change and promise to drill for more fossil fuels. But they also say that the progress of cheap, clean energy is now unstoppable, and that action by states, cities and businesses can continue climate action in the US, as during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term. The UN climate summit Cop29, starting next week in Azerbaijan, will be attended by Biden officials.\par \par \uc2 Christiana Figueres, UN climate chief from 2010-2016, who oversaw the landmark Paris agreement said:\par \par \uc2 The result from this election will be seen as a major blow to global climate action, but it cannot and will not halt the changes under way to decarbonise the economy and meet the goals of the Paris agreement.\par \par \uc2 Standing with oil and gas is the same as falling behind in a fast moving world. Clean energy technologies will continue to outcompete fossil fuels. There is an antidote to doom and despair. It\u8217\'20\'19s action on the ground, and it\u8217\'20\'19s happening in all corners of the Earth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bill Hare, climate scientist and CEO of Climate Analytics, said:\par \par \uc2 The election of a climate denier to the US presidency is extremely dangerous for the world. We are already seeing extreme damages, loss of life around the globe due to human induced warming of 1.3C.\par \par \uc2 President Trump will not be above the laws of physics and nor will the country that he leads. If Trump follows through with his threat to withdraw from the Paris agreement, the biggest loser will be the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gina McCarthy, former White House national climate adviser and Environmental Protection Agency administrator, said:\par \par \uc2 No matter what Trump may say, the shift to clean energy is unstoppable and our country is not turning back. Our coalition is bigger, more bipartisan, better organised, and fully prepared to deliver climate solutions, boost local economies, and drive climate ambition.\par \par \uc2 We cannot and will not let Trump stand in the way of giving our kids and grandkids the freedom to grow up in safer and healthier communities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mitzi Jonelle Tan, from Youth Advocates for Climate Action Philippines, said:\par \par \uc2 Countries like the Philippines are already enduring life-shattering climate impacts. While the fossil fuel industry and leaders like Trump cling to a collapsing system, we cannot give in. We must continue to organise and campaign to bring the end of the fossil fuel era.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Dr Friederike Otto, co-founder of World Weather Attribution at Imperial College London, UK, said:\par \par \uc2 Climate change doesn\u8217\'20\'19t care about politics or which party is in government. The US will get hit by stronger storms and hotter heatwaves as long as the world burns oil, coal and gas.\par \par \uc2 Saying climate change isn\u8217\'20\'19t real or dismantling climate policies won\u8217\'20\'19t change that. I hope local governments will be able to step up in many places.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat Kristen McDonald Rivet won election to a US House seat representing Michigan on Wednesday, reports the Associated Press (AP).\par \par \uc2 Her victory means Democrats will retain control of a competitive district after Dan Kildee, who has represented the Flint area for about a decade, decided to retire.\par \par \uc2 McDonald Rivet currently represents a competitive state Senate district that covers Midland, Saginaw and Bay City. She defeated Republican Paul Junge, who unsuccessfully ran against Kildee in 2022 and had worked in US customs and immigration services during the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 The AP declared McDonald Rivet the winner at 6.09am EST.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ukraine's Zelenskyy congratulates Trump on an 'impressive election victory'\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian president, Volodymyr Zelenskyy, has congratulated Donald Trump on \u8220\'20\'1Chis impressive election victory\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Posting on X before the Associated Press had declared Trump the winner, Zelenskyy wrote about his hopes for the US and Ukraine working to put \u8220\'20\'1Can end to Russian aggression against Ukraine\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He wrote:\par \par \uc2 Congratulations to @realDonaldTrump on his impressive election victory!\par \par \uc2 I recall our great meeting with President Trump back in September, when we discussed in detail the Ukraine-US strategic partnership, the victory plan, and ways to put an end to Russian aggression against Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 I appreciate President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to the \u8220\'20\'1Cpeace through strength\u8221\'20\'1D approach in global affairs. This is exactly the principle that can practically bring just peace in Ukraine closer. I am hopeful that we will put it into action together.\par \par \uc2 We look forward to an era of a strong United States of America under President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s decisive leadership. We rely on continued strong bipartisan support for Ukraine in the United States.\par \par \uc2 We are interested in developing mutually beneficial political and economic cooperation that will benefit both of our nations. Ukraine, as one of Europe\u8217\'20\'19s strongest military powers, is committed to ensuring long-term peace and security in Europe and the transatlantic community with the support of our allies.\par \par \uc2 I am looking forward to personally congratulating President Trump and discussing ways to strengthen Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s strategic partnership with the United States.\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  on his impressive election victory!\par \par \uc2 I recall our great meeting with President Trump back in September, when we discussed in detail the Ukraine-U.S. strategic partnership, the Victory Plan, and ways to put an end to Russian aggression against\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Volodymyr Zelenskyy / ????????? ?????????? (@ZelenskyyUa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZelenskyyUa/status/1854073411904938032?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.13am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  has been elected the 47th president of the United States in a stunning political resurrection that sent shock waves through the country and around the world.\par \par \uc2 Trump becomes the first convicted criminal to win the White House. At 78 he is also the oldest person ever elected to the office.\par \par \uc2 The result will sound alarm bells in foreign capitals given Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chaotic leadership style and overtures to authoritarians such as Vladimir Putin of Russia and Kim Jong-un of North Korea. He was called a threat to democracy and even a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/harris-trump-fascist-hitler-comments-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fascist by his opponent}}}\uc2 , vice-president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  , and some of his own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/25/election-trump-staffers-john-kelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former White House officials}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yet the US electorate proved willing to push such concerns aside and hand the nuclear codes to the property developer turned reality TV star for a second time.\par \par \uc2 Trump defeated Harris, a Democrat who had been seeking to make history herself as the first woman, first Black woman and first south Asian American to become president in the US\u8217\'20\'19s 248-year history.\par \par \uc2 At 5.37am ET the Associated Press called Wisconsin for Trump, with the state\u8217\'20\'19s 10 electoral college votes tipping the Trump\u8217\'20\'19s total to 277 \u8211\'20\'13 well past the 270 votes that is needed to win the presidency.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/donald-trump-wins-us-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump elected US president in stunning political resurrection}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Montana voters chose to protect the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their state constitution, reports the Associated Press (AP).\par \par \uc2 The ballot initiative sought to enshrine a 1999 Montana supreme court ruling that said the constitutional right to privacy protects the right to a pre-viability \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  by a provider of the patient\u8217\'20\'19s choice. Though there\u8217\'20\'19s no defined time frame, doctors say viability is sometime after 21 weeks.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press declared the amendment was approved at 6.01am EST on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Dollar soars as markets bet that Trump would win US election\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory in the US presidential election sent the dollar soaring, even before his win was officially announced, towards its biggest one-day rise, while cryptocurrency traders pushed bitcoin to a fresh all-time high.\par \par \uc2 The likelihood that the Republicans would also grab a majority in the Senate and the House of Representatives, giving Trump sweeping powers to cut taxes and impose tariffs on imported goods, was also judged as a positive for the US currency even before some states had given their verdict.\par \par \uc2 Trump declared victory on Wednesday morning after taking the key swing state of Pennsylvania. At the time, the Republican led his Democrat rival, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  , by 267 electoral votes to her 224, with 270 electoral votes needed to win the presidency. The Associated Press declared Trump the winner at 5.34am EST.\par \par \uc2 The US currency\u8217\'20\'19s climb began after very early indications of a Republican win in Georgia and gathered pace throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2024/nov/06/us-dollar-bitcoin-bond-prices-treasury-yields-pound-euro-wall-street-business-live-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US dollar and bitcoin surge, but bond prices tumble, as investors pile into \u8216\'20\'18Trump trades\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 business live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 World leaders congratulate Trump on US election win\par \par \uc2 Even before the election was called for Donald Trump, world leaders congratulated the former president on his imminent return to office:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 France\u8217\'20\'19s president Emmanuel Macron became one of the first to tweet his congratulations, writing on X: \u8220\'20\'1CCongratulations President Donald Trump. Ready to work together as we have done for four years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu has also congratulated Donald Trump, sharing a photo of him and his wife, Sara, with the ex-president. Netanyahu wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CYour historic return to the White House offers a new beginning for America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hungarian prime minister and Trump ally Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n has welcomed the US election results. \u8220\'20\'1CGood Morning Hungary! On the road to a beautiful victory, it\u8217\'20\'19s in the bag,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/reel/1268281620965936?locale=fr_FR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on his Facebook page}}}\uc2  earlier on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 British prime minister Keir Starmer said: \u8220\'20\'1CCongratulations president-elect Trump on your historic election victory. I look forward to working with you in the years ahead. As the closest of allies, we stand shoulder to shoulder in defence of our shared values of freedom, democracy and enterprise. From growth and security to innovation and tech, I know that the UK-US special relationship will continue to prosper on both sides of the Atlantic for years to come,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 India\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister Narendra Modi offered \u8220\'20\'1Chearty congratulations to my friend Donald Trump\u8221\'20\'1D, alongside several photos of the two men tightly embracing each other and holding hands. Modi said he was \u8220\'20\'1Clooking forward to collaboration\u8221\'20\'1D between the US and India.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nato secretary-general Mark Rutte has congratulated Trump and said he showed \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong US leadership\u8221\'20\'1D in his first term in office that strengthened the alliance. In a statement Rutte said he looked forward to working with Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cto advance peace through strength through Nato\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Portugal\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Lu\u237\'00\'EDs Montenegro, Spain\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Pedro S\u225\'00\'E1nchez, Greek prime minister, Kyriakos Mitsotakis, Irish PM Simon Harris, Charles Michel, president of the European Council, also offered their congratulations.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans take Senate majority and eye unified power with Trump\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  have recaptured the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate}}}\uc2 , achieving what was billed in advance as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/jacky-rosen-nevada-democrat-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most attainable goal}}}\uc2  for the party in this year\u8217\'20\'19s elections.\par \par \uc2 The GOP regained control after it became clear that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  had lost their one-seat majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s 100-member upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 Republicans gained two Senate seats, as Trump-backed businessperson Bernie Moreno defeated three-term Democratic senator Sherrod Brown in Ohio, and Trump loyalist Jim Justice won the seat once held by Joe Manchin in West Virginia.\par \par \uc2 Republican incumbents also fought off Democratic challengers in Texas, where Ted Cruz defeated Colin Allred, and in Florida, where Rick Scott won out over Debbie Mucarsel-Powell.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/senate-elections-republicans-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans retake control of US Senate after Democrats lose majority}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 Vote counting continues and you can follow the latest presidential results as they come in with our live tracker:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/06/us-election-results-map-2024-live-donald-trump-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election results 2024 live: Donald Trump edges close to victory over Kamala Harris}}}\par \par \uc2 Here are the latest results in the House, Senate and gubernatorial races:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/us-senate-house-and-governor-elections-2024-results-from-all-50-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate, House and governor elections 2024: results from all 50 states as Republicans win Senate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans have taken control of the US Senate and are fighting to keep their majority in the US House, which would produce a full sweep of GOP power in Congress alongside president-elect Donald Trump in the White House, reports the Associated Press (AP).\par \par \uc2 A unified Republican grip on Washington would set the course for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda. Or if Democrats wrest control of the House, it would provide an almost certain backstop, with veto power over the White House.\par \par \uc2 Vote counting in some races could go on for days, and control of the House is too early to call, reports the AP.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump won the key state of Wisconsin on Wednesday, defeating vice-president Kamala Harris in a critical battleground.\par \par \uc2 The win delivers 10 electoral college votes to Trump. He narrowly won Wisconsin in 2016, becoming the first Republican since Ronald Reagan to capture the state. He lost it in 2020 to Democrat Joe Biden.\par \par \uc2 Both Harris and Trump made Wisconsin a central focus of their campaigns. In 2020, Trump attempted to overturn his loss in the state through lawsuits and recounts, but failed.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press declared Trump the winner at 5.34am EST.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump elected president of the United States\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump has won the US presidential election, the Associated Press reports, with voters overlooking his divisive speeches, felony convictions and three separate criminal indictments to send the Republican former president back to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The AP says he has reached the 270-electoral college vote threshold to return to office by winning Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The extraordinary victory will make the 78-year-old New York real estate magnate only the second former president in US history to win the White House after previously losing re-election.\par \par \uc2 He also becomes the oldest person ever elected to the presidency.\par \par \uc2 Trump was first elected in 2016, but lost his re-election bid to Joe Biden in 2020, when the Democrat was 77. Trump then spent weeks attempting to prevent his rival from taking office, culminating in the 6 January 2021 insurrection, which saw his supporters attack the US Capitol after Trump addressed them outside the White House.\par \par \uc2 In the years that followed, prosecutors at the federal level and in the states of Georgia and New York brought felony charges against him, and earlier this year, he was convicted in Manhattan on 34 counts of business fraud, while the other cases have stalled. He was also found liable in a civil court case of sexual abuse.\par \par \uc2 Trump is bound by term limits, and cannot seek re-election. The only other president to serve two non-consecutive terms was Democrat Grover Cleveland, who was in office from 1885 to 1889, and again from 1893 to 1897.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump on brink of victory after sweeping key battleground states\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump is poised to win the US presidency after an unexpected sweep through key battleground states.\par \par \uc2 The former president was set for a return to the White House after a contentious election in which democracy itself had been at stake and which is likely to take the United States into uncharted political waters.\par \par \uc2 Polls had Trump and Kamala Harris neck and neck for large stretches of the campaign \u8211\'20\'13 suggesting a nail-biting election night and potentially days of waiting for a final result. In the end, the Republican nominee took {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/northcarolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina}}}\uc2  surprisingly early, the first battleground state to be called, and later he took Georgia and then Pennsylvania. He was strongly positioned in Arizona and Nevada, other key contests.\par \par \uc2 As the mood in Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s camp turned to disappointment, a jubilant Trump took to the stage at his Florida watch party around 2am ET to declare \u8220\'20\'1Cwe made history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to chants of \u8220\'20\'1CUSA! USA!\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump told his supporters:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a movement like nobody\u8217\'20\'19s ever seen before, and frankly, this was, I believe, the greatest political movement of all time. There\u8217\'20\'19s never been anything like this in this country, and maybe beyond.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd now it\u8217\'20\'19s going to reach a new level of importance, because we\u8217\'20\'19re going to help our country. We\u8217\'20\'19ll help our country \u8230\'20\'26 we have a country that needs help, and it needs help very badly. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to fix our borders. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to fix everything about our country. And we made history for a reason tonight, and the reason is going to be just that we overcame obstacles that nobody thought possible, and it is now clear that we\u8217\'20\'19ve achieved the most incredible political thing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to thank the American people for the extraordinary honor of being elected your 47th president and your 45th president, and every citizen, I will fight for you, for your family and your future. Every single day, I will be fighting for you and with every breath in my body, I will not rest until we have delivered the strong, safe and prosperous America that our children deserve and that you deserve. This will truly be the golden age of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here is a round up of some of the key moments of the US election night:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The swing states still to be calledare Wisconsin (10 electoral college votes), Nevada (6), Michigan (15) and Arizona (11). The other states still to be called are Alaska and Maine. Alaska is considered a red state, and its three electoral college votes could deliver Trump the presidency.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Missouri, Colorado, New York and Maryland {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all passed measures to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  right}}}\uc2  s, while in Florida, an effort to roll back a six-week ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/florida-abortion-ballot-ban-measure-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell short}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans have retaken the majority in the Senate, the Associated Press reported, after picking up seats in Ohio and West Virginia, and fending off challenges to their candidates in Texas and Nebraska. Republicans will control Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber for the first time in four years. Donald Trump will be in a position to confirm his supreme court justices, federal judges and appointees to cabinet posts.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The House is still in play, but Republicans hold a strong lead, with 190 representatives to the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 168.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There were decisive victories for Democrats elsewhere in the election. The US will have two Black women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-black-women-senate-maryland-delaware"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 serving as senators for the first time in American history}}}\uc2 , with the election of Lisa Blunt Rochester from Delaware and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/maryland-senate-seat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Angela Alsobrooks}}}\uc2  of Maryland.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sarah McBride, a Delaware state senator, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-sarah-mcbride-delaware-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also made history}}}\uc2  as the first out transgender person elected to the US House of Representatives. McBride, 34, won Delaware\u8217\'20\'19s at-large House seat in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s general election against the Republican candidate John Whalen III, a former Delaware state police officer and businessman. The House seat, Delaware\u8217\'20\'19s only one, has been Democratic since 2010.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump won in Iowa despite the state\u8217\'20\'19s foremost pollster Ann Selzer on Saturday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/harris-unexpected-lead-over-trump-iowa-selzer-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 finding Harris leading by a small amount}}}\uc2  that was nonetheless within the survey\u8217\'20\'19s margin of error. The finding was viewed as a potential sign of strength for Harris in nearby Wisconsin and Michigan, two swing states that are demographically similar to Iowa. The Trump campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/trump-harris-iowa-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decried}}}\uc2  Selzer\u8217\'20\'19s poll as an outlier, which turned out to be the case.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241106ekb6001mn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
