\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Morrison and Abbott praise Trump \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Daisy Dumas and Tory Shepherd (earlier) \par \uc2 16,741 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 November 2024\par 09:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closedFormer PMs praise Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18self-belief\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18assertiveness\u8217\'20\'19 ahead of likely US election victoryGet our breaking news email, free app or daily news podcast\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 What we learned; Wednesday 6 November\par \par \uc2 What a day it\u8217\'20\'19s been! We\u8217\'20\'19re putting the live news blog to bed shortly but before we do, here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s been keeping us busy \u8211\'20\'13 besides the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/presidential-election-harris-trump-polls-results-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 monumental news coming from the US }}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The body of a boy, believed to be that of the 11-year-old who was swept out to sea on the New South Wales coast on Sunday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/06/australia-politics-live-wednesday-labor-albanese-coalition-dutton-question-time-us-election?page=with:block-672af0708f08243590db2744#block-672af0708f08243590db2744"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was found }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Nationals senator \uc2 Bridget McKenzie\uc2  disclosed 16 flight upgrades on \uc2 Qantas\uc2  and \uc2 Virgin\uc2  flights going back to 2015 \u8211\'20\'13 then apologised for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/06/australia-politics-live-wednesday-labor-albanese-coalition-dutton-question-time-us-election?page=with:block-672b0dac8f08ec080b9406ce#block-672b0dac8f08ec080b9406ce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cdeficiencies in disclosing\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  those upgrades.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/06/australia-politics-live-wednesday-labor-albanese-coalition-dutton-question-time-us-election?page=with:block-672abb8b8f08243590db2593#block-672abb8b8f08243590db2593"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposition responded }}}\uc2  to the high court\u8217\'20\'19s striking down of ankle bracelets and curfews imposed on indefinite immigration detainees. The minister for home affairs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/06/australia-politics-live-wednesday-labor-albanese-coalition-dutton-question-time-us-election?page=with:block-672af2df8f0841bfc64a8731#block-672af2df8f0841bfc64a8731"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 then claimed the measures could be used }}}\uc2  after being adjusted.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Josh Creamer, the chair of Queensland\u8217\'20\'19s truth-telling and healing inquiry, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/06/australia-politics-live-wednesday-labor-albanese-coalition-dutton-question-time-us-election?page=with:block-672ae0c08f08243590db26a3#block-672ae0c08f08243590db26a3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke about the decision }}}\uc2  to put the process on \u8220\'20\'1Chold\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Labor said a \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/06/australia-politics-live-wednesday-labor-albanese-coalition-dutton-question-time-us-election?page=with:block-672a7ef48f08ec080b9401ea#block-672a7ef48f08ec080b9401ea"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should be withdrawn }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As voting in the US was nearing a close, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/06/australia-politics-live-wednesday-labor-albanese-coalition-dutton-question-time-us-election?page=with:block-672ae7968f08243590db26e3#block-672ae7968f08243590db26e3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investors started to price in }}}\uc2  a second \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  administration.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 On the subject of Trump, prime ministers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/06/australia-politics-live-wednesday-labor-albanese-coalition-dutton-question-time-us-election?page=with:block-672b0ba18f08ec080b9406c0#block-672b0ba18f08ec080b9406c0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Scott Morrison }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/06/australia-politics-live-wednesday-labor-albanese-coalition-dutton-question-time-us-election?page=with:block-672ad1de8f0841bfc64a8612#block-672ad1de8f0841bfc64a8612"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Malcolm Turnbull }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/06/australia-politics-live-wednesday-labor-albanese-coalition-dutton-question-time-us-election?page=with:block-672b18988f0841bfc64a8840#block-672b18988f0841bfc64a8840"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tony Abbott }}}\uc2  all weighed in on his extremely likely win.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 And, Guardian Australia watched on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/06/australia-politics-live-wednesday-labor-albanese-coalition-dutton-question-time-us-election?page=with:block-672b04938f08ec080b940687#block-672b04938f08ec080b940687"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as the mood plummeted at a US elections party }}}\uc2  in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 Thank you, as ever, for joining us today. We\u8217\'20\'19ll be back with the latest news bright and early tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 Police officer seriously injured after being hit by allegedly stolen car in Melbourne\par \par \uc2 Police used \u8220\'20\'1Cstop sticks\u8221\'20\'1D after a stolen vehicle was seen on Aviation Drive in Diggers Rest at about 1.30pm.\par \par \uc2 Police said the driver and his male passenger sped off in the car and hit a male senior constable, who was taken to hospital with serious but non-life-threatening injuries.\par \par \uc2 Police said the vehicle was dumped at a shopping centre \u8211\'20\'13 understood to be Watergardens \u8211\'20\'13 in Taylors Lakes. The two men were arrested inside the shopping centre.\par \par \uc2 The incident is being investigated. Anyone with information is urged to contact Crime Stoppers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Former prime minister \uc2 Tony Abbott\uc2  has congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on his now-extremely likely presidential win.\par \par \uc2 Abbott said via X that self \u8220\'20\'1Cbelief is what the West needs right now\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations to President Trump on his return to the leadership of the free world. Self belief is what the West needs right now and Trump has that in spades\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tony Abbott\uc2  (@HonTonyAbbott) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HonTonyAbbott/status/1854060176292360423?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 Morrison says Trump \u8216\'20\'18very positive\u8217\'20\'19 about Aukus pact\par \par \uc2 Circling back to Scott Morrison \u8217\'20\'19s views on a second \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  presidency.\par \par \uc2 Speaking with the ABC a short while ago, the former prime minister said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery positive\u8221\'20\'1D about Aukus.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve never understood why people would doubt that [Trump] wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t support it. It\u8217\'20\'19s a good deal. He was very committed to the alliance.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s very clear that the US interests are heavily aligned with resisting the PRC, taking over China, taking over Taiwan \u8230\'20\'26 All the other conflicts we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing at the moment are just horrendous and awful, but in terms of their global implications, nothing compares with the fall of Taiwan to the PRC.\par \par \uc2 I mean, the point of Aukus is to resist that aggression coming out of China, amongst many other things, and if you have that strong deterrent, then you don\u8217\'20\'19t have to use it and but you have to be determined and clear about your willingness to put this in place. And weakness is not something that I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever associated with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Speaking about former PMs as ambassadors to the US, Morrison said he had \u8220\'20\'1Cno interest in taking on such a role\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 Employment agencies paid irrespective of role in finding job seeker work\par \par \uc2 Secretary of the department of employment and workplace relations Natalie James has said providers receive public funds \u8220\'20\'1Cirrespective\u8221\'20\'1D of how much they\u8217\'20\'19ve helped the jobseeker find work:\par \par \uc2 We distinguish, and a participant would definitely distinguish, between when they feel like they\u8217\'20\'19ve been helped to get the job and when they haven\u8217\'20\'19t. Our outcomes payment system doesn\u8217\'20\'19t.\par \par \uc2 Our outcomes payment system makes the payment to the providers irrespective of the contributing factors to the job being secured. It\u8217\'20\'19s always operated that way.\par \par \uc2 Payment flows irrespective of the degree of assistance provided.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 Bridget McKenzie\uc2  apologises for \u8216\'20\'18deficiencies in disclosing\u8217\'20\'19 flight upgrades\par \par \uc2 Nationals senator has now apologised for failing to disclose 16 flight upgrades she received over the last nine years, including two that came just weeks before she recently claimed to have never received a single upgrade.\par \par \uc2 After her earlier belated disclosure of 16 flight upgrades between 2015 and this August, the Nationals senator has now shared a personal statement to the media.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have never sought free upgrades, which has been affirmed by the airlines to the extent of their records,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Deficiencies in disclosing these matters do not meet the expectations of the Australian people and the parliament and were an oversight on my part, and for this I apologise.\par \par \uc2 Her statement says three flights upgraded to business class over the last two years - including in July and August this year \u8211\'20\'13 came \u8220\'20\'1Cdue to my frequent flyer status while travelling on parliamentary business, upgrades which I did not seek.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Qantas\uc2  has advised of upgrades on five personal flights to or from New Zealand between 2016 and 2018 which were not previously declared. There was also a \uc2 Qantas\uc2  domestic upgrade in January 2015,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Virgin Australia\uc2  has advised that, as a member of The Club since 2013, seven domestic flights were upgraded between 2015 and 2019.\par \par \uc2 No upgrades were issued by Rex Group to the extent of their records going back to 2013.\par \par \uc2 McKenzie said she \u8220\'20\'1Cwill continue to prosecute the Albanese Labor government\u8217\'20\'19s failure to ensure greater competition in the aviation sector on behalf of all Australian travellers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 Scott Morrison on US election: \u8216\'20\'18No doubt it\u8217\'20\'19s a Trump victory\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Speaking with the ABC, the former prime minister Scott Morrison said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would be a positive force for global security:\par \par \uc2 This was a very difficult climb for the Democrats and vice-president Harris. Then you have \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who is like unlike any other politician you will ever come across, and I can say that with some experience having dealt with both President Trump and President Biden.\par \par \uc2 I think what he brings now is an assertiveness and a strength to the role, which I think will have a very positive impact on global security issues \u8230\'20\'26 That means getting in a position of strength and then getting the right outcome, the idea of just fighting to fight tomorrow with no real intent or resource to fight to win \u8211\'20\'13 that isn\u8217\'20\'19t a good outcome for global peace and a good resolution in Ukraine, either. I think that is a recipe for calamity. I think President Trump will bring a fresh take on that. And frankly, we need a few fresh takes on some of these challenges, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s there, or in the Middle East.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 Bridget McKenzie\uc2  discloses 16 flight upgrades\par \par \uc2 The Nationals senator has just disclosed 16 flight upgrades on \uc2 Qantas\uc2  and \uc2 Virgin\uc2  flights going back to 2015, which she had failed to declare over the last four parliamentary terms.\par \par \uc2 As we brought you earlier, the opposition transport spokesperson had found more than a dozen instances where she had not disclosed flight upgrades as required by parliamentary rules on her register of interests. Her office had been expected to update the register after she had run a self-audit of her own travel schedule \u8211\'20\'13 and that update has now come, showing 16 flight upgrades, including five personal trips to or from New Zealand.\par \par \uc2 We are awaiting a statement from her office, but we understand McKenzie will stress that none of the upgrades were specifically requested by her, and that several of them came due to her membership of \uc2 Virgin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s elite airline lounge club, or her \uc2 Qantas\uc2  frequent flyer status.\par \par \uc2 However we understand also that five trips between Australia and New Zealand \u8211\'20\'13 one in 2016, four in 2018 \u8211\'20\'13 were personal trips.\par \par \uc2 McKenzie\u8217\'20\'19s update to the register, which has just arrived on the parliament\u8217\'20\'19s website, shows two \uc2 Qantas\uc2  flight upgrades in July and August 2024 which she said was due to her frequent flyer status. Just last week, McKenzie told Sky News: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never sought one [a flight upgrade] \u8230\'20\'26 I haven\u8217\'20\'19t been offered one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The update also shows seven \uc2 Virgin\uc2  flight upgrades between 2015 and 2019, which she said were \u8220\'20\'1Cprovided within membership of \uc2 Virgin\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18the club\u8217\'20\'19 allocation\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/06/bridget-mckenzie-to-update-register-after-failing-to-declare-more-than-a-dozen-flight-upgrades"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bridget McKenzie to update register after failing to declare more than a dozen flight upgrades }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 NSW Police investigate body found in car in Sydney\u8217\'20\'19s south\par \par \uc2 New South Wales Police said emergency services were called to Durham Street, Hurstville, at about 5:15 on Tuesday after reports of a concern for welfare.\par \par \uc2 Officers found a dead woman in the passenger seat of a vehicle, the police said in a statement a short time ago.\par \par \uc2 The woman, who is yet to be formally identified, is believed to be aged in her 40s.\par \par \uc2 Police established an investigation into the incident and a 46-year-old man was arrested at a home at short time later.\par \par \uc2 He was charged with contravening an AVO, taking and driving conveyance without consent of owner, Drive whilst Disqualified second offence and breach of bail. No charges have been laid over the woman\u8217\'20\'19s death.\par \par \uc2 He was refused bail and appeared in local court today, where he was refused bail to reappear on 19 November.\par \par \uc2 Anyone with information is urged to contact Crime Stoppers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Police seek information on alleged fraudsters posing as psychics\par \par \uc2 Police are re-appealing for information as investigations continue into alleged fraudsters who posed as psychics.\par \par \uc2 New South Wales Police said Strike Force Recycling was established in July 2024 to investigate after a number of people reported they had paid money to people claiming to be psychics.\par \par \uc2 Police said a woman, 48, and a man, 50, were arrested on 8 August. Both remain before the courts.\par \par \uc2 Police appealed to identify a third woman they believe may be able to assist with inquiries. They said she had a Mediterranean appearance, was believed to be aged in her 40s, about 150cm tall, had a large build and spoke with a Romanian accent.\par \par \uc2 At about 9:30am today, police executed a search warrant at a storage unit in Victoria Ave, Chatswood.\par \par \uc2 Police said that during the search, officers seized antique statues, an antique sword, crystal ball and second world war collectors\u8217\'20\'19 memorabilia, including a suitcase and a firearm magazine.\par \par \uc2 Anyone with information about the woman is urged to contact Crime Stoppers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 US Democrats in Australia \u8216\'20\'18know the drop is coming\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Nervous hope is mixing with anticipatory dread among Americans watching the US election results come in at the Kent St Hotel in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 Emily, who is visiting Sydney, says the energy has shifted at US election watch party, hosted by Democrats Abroad.\par \par \uc2 At midday, \u8220\'20\'1Cit was buzzing,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CLike before a really fun concert starts, something anticipatory.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But I think the reality is starting to set in.\par \par \uc2 It is a little bit like dread, holding your breath. It\u8217\'20\'19s like when you are on a rollercoaster, you know the drop is coming.\par \par \uc2 enltrNervous hope is mixing to anticipatory dread among Harris supporters watching the US election results come in at the Kent St Hotel in Sydney.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReality is starting to set in,\u8221\'20\'1D an American in Sydney says.\par \par \uc2 "It's like when you are on a roller coaster, you know the drop is coming." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/he2XUkpNPs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/he2XUkpNPs }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rafqa Touma (@At_Raf_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/At_Raf_/status/1854036292163801240?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 Job providers accused of harassing jobseekers over payslips\par \par \uc2 The government is investigating four job providers for regularly harassing jobseekers for payslip information.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year a Guardian Australia investigation found providers regularly harass jobseekers to get payslip information.\par \par \uc2 Under questions from Senator Penny Allman-Payne, the \uc2 Department of Employment and Workplace Relations\uc2  said the department has started investigating providers, which it would complete by mid-November. It could not name the four providers until it was finished.\par \par \uc2 Deputy Security Tania Rishniw :\par \par \uc2 One of the things that we have done now in terms of payslips is we have a specific line in terms of the customer service line that any complaint about payslips automatically gets referred to our complaints team, to be looked at, to be investigated, to make sure that those complaints are taken seriously.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve updated guidelines for providers that make it absolutely clear that there are consequences.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s red centre is roasting\par \par \uc2 A large swathe of inland Australia is sweltering today, with five states forecast to hit 44C.\par \par \uc2 Thargomindah in Queensland and White Cliffs in New South Wales surpassed that, both reaching 45.1C.\par \par \uc2 enltrCouple of hot spots in the Outback today, in the midst of an extended heatwave across much of northern Australia. (Via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BOM_au?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @bom_au }}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QHOoqn5QzK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QHOoqn5QzK }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 @phannam@mastodon.green (@p_hannam) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/p_hannam/status/1854031711333683637?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, thunderstorms are on their way for almost all of NSW:\par \par \uc2 enltr??Thunderstorm FORECAST for TOMORROW (7 Nov): Chance of thunderstorms across all of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NewSouthWales?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NewSouthWales }}}\uc2  tomorrow, except the far southwest. Thunderstorms may be severe in the northeast quarter with risks of damaging winds and large hail. Warnings as needed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HaQrNPzBsh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/HaQrNPzBsh }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5ksGuwQy2l"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5ksGuwQy2l }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Bureau of Meteorology\uc2 , New South Wales (@BOM_NSW) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BOM_NSW/status/1854026024947724545?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Greens call for ban on MPs getting free flight upgrades\par \par \uc2 The Greens say federal parliament should implement \u8220\'20\'1Ca blanket ban on MPs requesting or accepting free flight upgrades\u8221\'20\'1D, which they want to apply to both personal and work travel.\par \par \uc2 The party\u8217\'20\'19s transport spokesperson, Elizabeth Watson-Brown, claimed the move would restore trust and integrity in how politicians deal with the aviation sector.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBanning free flight upgrades would help curb any potentially inappropriate behaviour from MPs and prevent airlines from wielding undue influence over political decisions,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Watson-Brown said it was \u8220\'20\'1Ccompletely understandable for people to be questioning \uc2 Qantas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 relationship with the very same MPs and Ministers that regulate them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a cost-of-living crisis that\u8217\'20\'19s seeing people across the country struggle to pay for food and rent, MPs on generous salaries don\u8217\'20\'19t need to be getting freebies when they travel.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 Man bitten by dingo on K\u8217\'20\'19gari\par \par \uc2 Rangers have increased patrols and warned visitors to be vigilant after Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s attack, which marked the 21st dingo incident at K\u8217\'20\'19gari, formerly Fraser Island, in 2024, \uc2 AAP\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 The man was walking from his car to a picnic area at Lake McKenzie when a tagged female dingo suddenly ran at him from behind, rangers say.\par \par \uc2 The dingo bit the man on the right calf, causing a minor puncture wound. The dingo retreated when he turned around and kicked sand at it.\par \par \uc2 Rangers responded quickly and \u8220\'20\'1Cobserved the dingo continuing to walk around the car park and loiter close to vehicles and people for about an hour before it returned to the bush,\u8221\'20\'1D Queensland Parks and Wildlife Service senior ranger Linda Behrendorff said.\par \par \uc2 A four-year-old girl was flown to hospital after she was bitten on the chest while a group was fishing on the island, north of Brisbane, in August.\par \par \uc2 Behrendorff said visitors should only use fenced picnic areas when eating or preparing food and should not take food or drinks to the lake\u8217\'20\'19s shores.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVisitors and residents are also reminded to remain vigilant of their surroundings at all times, keep children within arm\u8217\'20\'19s length, never walk alone and carry a stick at all times,\u8221\'20\'1D Behrendorff said.\par \par \uc2 Fraser Coast Mayor George Seymour has previously called on the Queensland government to consider restricting families to camp inside fenced areas on K\u8217\'20\'19gari after a rise in incidents.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 A quarter of job providers underperforming\par \par \uc2 The department of employment and workplace relations is up in senate estimates where the discussion is focusing on the performance results of providers.\par \par \uc2 Job providers receive millions of dollars in public funding to help jobseekers get into work.\par \par \uc2 The most recent data has shown 44 providers out of 178 received a low-performance rating. Low means providers are \u8220\'20\'1Cnot meeting the department\u8217\'20\'19s expectations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In comparison, just 15 received a high performance.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 NSW Libertarian party\u8217\'20\'19s US election function in full swing\par \par \uc2 In his Uncle Sam outfit and sneakers, Jim Sternhell is one of the more colourful characters among the crowd at the US election watch party in New South Wales parliament.\par \par \uc2 Increasingly excited attenders at the pro-Trump crowd have sought out Sternhell for selfies as the results roll in.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s Libertarian party, hosting the event, has already called the election for Trump, but Sternhell is not yet as optimistic, fearing election interference by the Democratic party:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a whole array of tricks they can do both before, during and after.\par \par \uc2 enltrDentist Jim Sternhell is among the 50 or so at the pro-Trump watch party in NSW Parliament House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/uE9QFHrOMt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/uE9QFHrOMt }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Luca (@IttimaniL) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IttimaniL/status/1854015292198015016?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 The dentist and One Nation member has only a tangential connection to the US, spending four months in Arizona as a boy and with one of his daughters now living in the US, but he\u8217\'20\'19s concerned about the election because of what it means for climate change \u8211\'20\'13 which he says is a hoax.\par \par \uc2 Sternhell, who is mulling running for office in his local electorate of Wentworth in Sydney\u8217\'20\'19s eastern suburbs, has popped up in his distinctive outfit at past rallies for Trump and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://n/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Conservative Political Action Conference }}}\uc2 . He\u8217\'20\'19s also a regular attender at anti-climate action rallies and protests against what he describes as \u8220\'20\'1Canti-radical Islam\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 Tony Burke addresses high court ruling on ex-immigration detainee monitoring\par \par \uc2 The minister for home affairs has responded to the high court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to quash the Albanese government\u8217\'20\'19s ankle bracelet and curfew regime for former immigration detainees.\par \par \uc2 In a statement released a short time ago, Burke indicated he intended fix the problem:\par \par \uc2 The Australian government is taking immediate steps to protect community safety following the high court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling in the YBFZ case.\par \par \uc2 Regulations are now being finalised that will allow for an adjusted process for electronic monitoring devices and curfews to be used. I will sign off on these regulations later today.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow I will introduce new legislation to support those regulations. The legislation will also strengthen the government\u8217\'20\'19s power to remove people who have had their visas cancelled to third countries.\par \par \uc2 The government has also boosted personnel and resources for Operation \uc2 Aegis\uc2  in order to keep the community safe. The number of officers has been increased by 66%.\par \par \uc2 The government imposed strict conditions on the NZYQ cohort because community safety is our top priority.\par \par \uc2 We argued strongly in the high court to keep electronic monitoring and curfews in place.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s decision is not the one the government wanted \u8211\'20\'13 but it is one the government has prepared for.\par \par \uc2 Burke closed by once again assuring the public that the \u8220\'20\'1Csecurity and safety of the Australian community will always be the absolute priority for this government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/06/high-court-quashes-albanese-governments-ankle-bracelet-and-curfew-regime-for-former-immigration-detainees-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 High court quashes Albanese government\u8217\'20\'19s ankle bracelet and curfew regime for former immigration detainees }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Body found in search for boy swept out to sea in NSW\par \par \uc2 The body of a boy, believed to be that of the 11-year-old who was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/05/search-for-boy-11-swept-out-to-sea-from-nsw-coast-enters-third-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swept out to sea on New South Wales\u8217\'20\'19 Central Coast }}}\uc2  on Sunday, has been found.\par \par \uc2 A short time ago, NSW Police released a statement:\par \par \uc2 A body, believed to be that of a boy missing at The Entrance, has been located today.\par \par \uc2 About 5.15pm on Sunday, emergency services responded to reports a child had been swept into the ocean while attempting to cross The Entrance Channel.\par \par \uc2 An extensive multi-agency search for the missing boy was subsequently conducted, with ongoing taskings continuing today.\par \par \uc2 About 2.30pm today, emergency services were called to The Entrance following reports a body had been located in the water.\par \par \uc2 While the body is yet to be formally identified, it is believed to be that of the missing boy.\par \par \uc2 The boy had been visiting the Central Coast from Sydney with his father and three siblings.\par \par \uc2 The police said a report will be prepared for the Coroner.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Despite no official election outcome as of yet, New South Wales Libertarian MP John Ruddick has declared \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won the US election, getting cheers from the 50 or so attenders at his watch party in state parliament:\par \par \uc2 The NSW Libertarian party is going to make history around the world. We are calling this election for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won. And I can say this is the greatest comeback in history since the resurrection of Jesus Christ.\par \par \uc2 Ruddick told the crowd he hoped to hear from \u8220\'20\'1Cpresident-elect Trump\u8221\'20\'1D soon and asked:\par \par \uc2 Do we want to continue to watch Fox [News] or do we want to watch them cry on CNN?\par \par \uc2 The crowd cheered as the results for the key swing state Georgia, where Trump is now leading 51%, appeared on screen \u8211\'20\'13 a CNN presenter said the count in some states would not be completed today and would continue tomorrow, drawing some boos and shouts of: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a steal!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Thank you, as ever, Tory Shepherd. Let\u8217\'20\'19s get straight on with the rest of the day\u8217\'20\'19s (non-US election) news\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m going to leave you with Daisy Dumas for the rest of the afternoon. I may need a shower, some white noise (read: wine), and some dog time after that QT. See you tomorrow!\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 Question time wraps up\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s another question time over, and it had the scrappy feeling of the last day of school. But it\u8217\'20\'19s not! It\u8217\'20\'19s back on tomorrow, then there are two more sitting weeks before the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Labor \u8216\'20\'18considering a whole range of possible reforms\u8217\'20\'19 on childcare, Chalmers says\par \par \uc2 The independent MP Kylea Tink is asking the treasurer, \uc2 Jim Chalmers\uc2 , about abolishing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/may/03/labor-says-12-million-families-to-benefit-from-childcare-subsidies-in-9b-budget-boost"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 activity test for childcare }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Chalmers says:\par \par \uc2 We are big believers in the social and economic value of early childhood education and care. We see it as a gamechanger for families, and for the economy more broadly \u8230\'20\'26 we are considering a whole range of possible reforms as part of our commitment to try to get the system as close as we can to something which is a bit more universal.\par \par \uc2 He says early childhood education and care has been \u8220\'20\'1Cat the very core of our agenda\u8221\'20\'1D, that the government has invested in cheaper childcare and lifted subsidies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re also delivering a 15% pay rise for our early childhood educators,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Investors start to price in a second Trump administration\par \par \uc2 In case you\u8217\'20\'19ve strayed from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/presidential-election-harris-trump-polls-results-live-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s live US election blog }}}\uc2 , it\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that the money is moving in the direction of a victory for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The US dollar, for instance, is rising against other currencies, including the Australian dollar.\par \par \uc2 enltrAustralian dollar dropping (along with most other currencies) and investors start to price in a Trump win.\par \par \uc2 (Via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/business?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @business }}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dqGMFTEqPU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dqGMFTEqPU }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 @phannam@mastodon.green (@p_hannam) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/p_hannam/status/1853993744397398085?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 The US dollar gain against the Mexican peso is 2.5%, presumably because there\u8217\'20\'19s a greater chance of tariffs or some other punishment if Trump takes office. He\u8217\'20\'19s made various threats against the US\u8217\'20\'19s southern neighbour over the years, such as promising to get them to pay for a wall that for the most part never got built.\par \par \uc2 Part of the appeal of a Trump win is the promise of lower corporate taxes than would happen if vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  were to win a promotion to the top job. As things stand, the latter is looking a longer shot as the counting proceeds.\par \par \uc2 Australian stocks are higher, too, lifting more than 1.1% for the day.\par \par \uc2 As mentioned earlier, \uc2 Australia\u8217\'20\'19s Treasury\uc2  has provided advice to the Albanese government about what a Trump administration might mean.\par \par \uc2 Higher tariffs, particularly against China, won\u8217\'20\'19t help Australia, and they may prompt higher US interest rates than otherwise would be the case. The latter is one of the reasons why the US dollar is rising.\par \par \uc2 How to price in the effects of other Trump policies \u8211\'20\'13 such as dismantling key government agencies \u8211\'20\'13 is anybody\u8217\'20\'19s guess.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Bulk billing was \u8216\'20\'18in freefall\u8217\'20\'19 under Liberals, health minister says\par \par \uc2 The Liberal MP \uc2 Paul Fletcher\uc2  has asked about bulk billing rates, saying it was 88% under the Coalition and 74% under Labor.\par \par \uc2 The health minister, \uc2 Mark Butler\uc2 , says bulk billing was \u8220\'20\'1Cin freefall\u8221\'20\'1D when the Liberal party was coming to the end of its time in government.\par \par \uc2 He says the figures Fletcher was using included Covid vaccinations and consults for Covid vaccinations, which \u8220\'20\'1Cartificially boosted\u8221\'20\'1D the bulk billing rates under the former government:\par \par \uc2 The former government did not include transparent data on bulk billing. They artificially inflated it with Covid vaccinations and the rest. The second thing is the trajectory was clear.\par \par \uc2 And he calls Fletcher the \u8220\'20\'1Cworst health minister in the history of Medicare\u8221\'20\'1D and \uc2 Sussan Ley\uc2  the \u8220\'20\'1Csecond worst\u8221\'20\'1D for freezing Medicare.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 Promotion still sinking in for Australia\u8217\'20\'19s new defence force chief\par \par \uc2 The new chief of the defence force, David Johnston, is appearing at his first Senate estimates committee hearing since taking up the position in July, but it seems the promotion hasn\u8217\'20\'19t quite sunk in.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of making an opening statement, Johnston identified himself.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGood afternoon senators, thank you for the welcome. Vice-admiral \u8211\'20\'13 er \u8211\'20\'13 Admiral David Johnston, chief of the defence force,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, to chuckles from the committee.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSlight upgrade there, mate,\u8221\'20\'1D the committee chair, Raff Ciccone, quipped.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt takes some changing,\u8221\'20\'1D the admiral replied, before going on to talk about the difficulties in recruitment and retention of defence personnel.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 Free Tafe is doing its job, minister says\par \par \uc2 The deputy opposition leader, \uc2 Sussan Ley\uc2 , is asking about fee-free Tafe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow many have resulted in no qualification being delivered?\u8221\'20\'1D she asks.\par \par \uc2 (If you remember yesterday she asked the same question and it became a barney about how long Tafe courses went for, with Labor saying most take up to three years, so can\u8217\'20\'19t have finished because the program hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been going that long.)\par \par \uc2 The skills and training minister, Andrew Giles, says it takes four years to get the data.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat the data says is that free Tafe is doing its job,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 The treasurer, \uc2 Jim Chalmers\uc2 , is up talking about the \u8220\'20\'1Creckless arrogance of the opposition leader, and the comical cluelessness \u8230\'20\'26 of his offsider\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His major focus, he says, is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe fight against inflation\u8221\'20\'1D. And he says the \uc2 RBA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Michele Bullock\uc2  made three major points, that inflation is the highest priority, and that when it comes to inflation \u8220\'20\'1Cpublic demand is not the main game\u8221\'20\'1D. And third, that \u8220\'20\'1Cinflation has fallen substantially from its peak in 2022 and its coming back to target in a reasonable way\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s really been having a crack at Taylor all week \u8211\'20\'13 he\u8217\'20\'19s just accused him of \u8220\'20\'1Cchirping away\u8221\'20\'1D in an \u8220\'20\'1Cincoherent way\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Opposition repeats \u8216\'20\'18weak and incompetent\u8217\'20\'19 line\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the shadow treasurer, \uc2 Angus Taylor\uc2 , using the \u8220\'20\'1Cweakest and most incompetent\u8221\'20\'1D line again.\par \par \uc2 But Speaker Milton Dick \u8217\'20\'19s been doing his homework, referring to previous rulings by speakers. After looking at those precedents, he again asks Taylor to remove that part of his question (without ruling it out of order).\par \par \uc2 The opposition leader, \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2 , in the name of seeking \u8220\'20\'1Cclarification\u8221\'20\'1D, says something something \u8220\'20\'1Cweak\u8221\'20\'1D something something \u8220\'20\'1Cincompetent\u8221\'20\'1D. It\u8217\'20\'19s almost like they think the more often they say the words the more they\u8217\'20\'19ll stick (something that does, in fact, happen).\par \par \uc2 Dutton wants a ruling on \u8220\'20\'1Cweak\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cincompetent\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a personal reflection on the prime minister,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a description of the government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Also (I\u8217\'20\'19m paraphrasing): \u8220\'20\'1CThey said it first.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And Taylor. Again.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 Teal MP links US election to question about real-time donation disclosure\par \par \uc2 The independent MP Kate Chaney is up now, saying Australia \u8220\'20\'1Cis not immune to the mistrust we see in the US\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 There is increasing suspicion that politicians are acting in the interests of airlines, fossil fuels or gambling companies, unions or a political party instead of all Australians.\par \par \uc2 Voters deserve to know who is funding all political candidates before they vote. Will the government legislate real-time donation disclosure in time to make our next federal election transparent?\par \par \uc2 There was jeering and heckles from the floor, and Speaker Milton Dick intervened again.\par \par \uc2 The prime minister, Anthony Albanese, says democracy is something \u8220\'20\'1Cthat must be cherished and must be nurtured and cannot be taken for granted\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 I can confirm that I\u8217\'20\'19ve been working as the leader of the government to increase transparency, including on funding issues, and indeed, I [had] just this morning, another constructive discussion with the minister for the special minister of state, Senator Farrell, about these issues.\par \par \uc2 We believe in lower donation thresholds, and have done that and took that to an election.\par \par \uc2 He says he\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cnot picking\u8221\'20\'1D on \uc2 Clive Palmer\uc2  but that his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/feb/01/political-donations-list-australia-clive-palmer-mineralogy-united-australia-party-liberal-labor-aec-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 company\u8217\'20\'19s donations }}}\uc2  distorted the political system and says something must be done. He says some of the crossbench have \u8220\'20\'1Cvery strong views\u8221\'20\'1D about the timing of changes. He also mentions \u8220\'20\'1Csome of the backers\u8221\'20\'1D of the crossbench having opinions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Tense moment between Labor minister and Fatima Payman in Senate estimates\par \par \uc2 There was a tense moment between the Labor minister Murray Watt and former Labor senator Fatima Payman in the employment hearing of Senate estimates just before the lunch break.\par \par \uc2 Payman, who quit Labor earlier this year to sit as an independent, asked Watt \u8211\'20\'13 the employment and workplace minister \u8211\'20\'13 about salaries of administrators appointed to the \uc2 CFMEU\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reading from a \u8220\'20\'1Cleaked document\u8221\'20\'1D purporting to show the payments made to those administrators (Watt said he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t aware of their individual salaries), Payman asked:\par \par \uc2 Do you know how many fee-paying members it takes to cover the salaries of these three officials?\par \par \uc2 Watt responded:\par \par \uc2 No, but I dare say it\u8217\'20\'19s pretty similar to the members\u8217\'20\'19 contributions that were needed to pay the salaries of two former officials who are facing corruption charges in NSW right now.\par \par \uc2 Payman:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m talking about these three officials, and on my calculations it would be almost 2,000 members\u8217\'20\'19 hard-earned fees that they\u8217\'20\'19re paying their dues, just to employ your hand-picked bureaucrats. How can the government justify this program of jobs for mates at the expense of workers?\par \par \uc2 Watt responded:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure who\u8217\'20\'19s supplying these questions to you Senator Payman.\par \par \uc2 Payman interjected:\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t insult my intelligence and being able to put questions to the government, minister. That\u8217\'20\'19s really not fair.\par \par \uc2 After a brief interlude from the Labor committee chair, Tony Sheldon, the hearing got back on track. Watt referred back to his previous public statements about protecting the interests of union members.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 LNP\u8217\'20\'19s decision to pause truth-telling \u8216\'20\'18continues 165 years of government failing to listen\u8217\'20\'19: Josh Creamer\par \par \uc2 Josh Creamer, the chair of Queensland\u8217\'20\'19s truth-telling and healing inquiry, has spoken about the decision to put the process on \u8220\'20\'1Chold\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Despite repeated requests, Creamer has yet to receive a call from the minister, Fiona Simpson, or premier, David Crisafulli. The inquiry received a brief letter from Simpson at 6.49pm on Monday, he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI request further truth-telling sessions, notices, hearings and other work of the inquiry be placed on hold, until such time as the government repeals the act,\u8221\'20\'1D Simpson wrote.\par \par \uc2 Creamer will meet Simpson tomorrow, he said:\par \par \uc2 People have said to me, this is like the chief protector days, a single person deciding what\u8217\'20\'19s best for every Aboriginal and Torres Strait Island person in the state.\par \par \uc2 The government has previously signalled its intention to repeal the Pathway to Treaty Act in one of the two sitting weeks of parliament this year, making it one of the government\u8217\'20\'19s first acts. Crisafulli, who voted for the original bill, called the inquiry \u8220\'20\'1Cdivisive\u8221\'20\'1D. Creamer said:\par \par \uc2 Ceasing the inquiry\u8217\'20\'19s work in this way continues 165 years of government failing to listen to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.\par \par \uc2 Creamer said pausing the inquiry left it unable to provide \u8220\'20\'1Csupport to our participants who are no doubt hurting through this process\u8221\'20\'1D, in violation of its trauma-informed process mandated in its terms of reference.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 Liberal MP echoes \u8216\'20\'18incompetence\u8217\'20\'19 line in interest rates question\par \par \uc2 The Liberal MP Zoe McKenzie echoes Taylor\u8217\'20\'19s line on weakness and incompetence despite Dick\u8217\'20\'19s quite heartfelt plea about the language used in the house.\par \par \uc2 After more discussion over the words used, McKenzie repeats the rest of Taylor\u8217\'20\'19s earlier question about interest rates (without repeating the weakness and incompetence line).\par \par \uc2 The prime minister, Anthony Albanese, refers to comments from the \uc2 RBA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Michele Bullock\uc2 , saying \u8220\'20\'1Cwe still have inflation coming back to target in a reasonable way\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 She also went on to say \u8230\'20\'26 the fact that inflation, now for the last year, has only been 2.8% is actually real for people.\par \par \uc2 They are seeing lower petrol prices. They are seeing lower electricity prices. So this is good for people. Real incomes are rising again. As inflation is declining and wage growth is a bit higher than that, and you\u8217\'20\'19ve got the tax cuts, real incomes are rising again. That is what governor Bullock had to say yesterday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 The opposition leader, \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2 , echoes Albanese\u8217\'20\'19s words (except for a bit about Albanese being invited into Biden\u8217\'20\'19s home). \u8220\'20\'1COur relationship with the United States will endure, it will strengthen,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CWe want to see a safe environment in which people can vote and we want to see the best outcome for the US.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 Albanese pays tribute to outgoing president \uc2 Joe Biden\par \par \uc2 The prime minister, Anthony Albanese, is paying tribute to the outgoing US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , saying he met him within 48 hours of being sworn is as PM. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll never forget the genuine warmth of Joe\u8217\'20\'19s welcome,\u8221\'20\'1D he says, and talks up the future of the alliance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 Turnbull\u8217\'20\'19s little gaffe in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s favour\par \par \uc2 Another little nugget from the former prime minister \uc2 Malcolm Turnbull\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s earlier appearance on ABC television \u8211\'20\'13 while he was typically, eloquently scathing of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , he did make a little gaffe in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s favour.\par \par \uc2 Turnbull was saying the president of the day would need to certify that the US does not need the Virginia-class submarines in order for Australia to receive them, adding that the US is \u8220\'20\'1Cproducing half as many as their navy needs to sustain them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s got to say \u8211\'20\'13\u8221\'20\'1D Turnbull started.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COr she?\u8221\'20\'1D David Speers interjected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe or she has got to say it would not detract from the underwater capabilities of the \uc2 US Navy\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26,\u8221\'20\'1D Turnbull went on.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 The treasurer, \uc2 Jim Chalmers\uc2 , responding to Taylor, is giving what is by now his well-rehearsed speech that Labor \u8220\'20\'1Cturned two big Liberal deficits into two substantial Labor surpluses, and that\u8217\'20\'19s helping in the fight against inflation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re \u8220\'20\'1Ccleaning up the mess\u8221\'20\'1D of the previous government, he says, and has a crack at Taylor over the figures he\u8217\'20\'19s using:\par \par \uc2 If he was honest \u8230\'20\'26 he would say that what he\u8217\'20\'19s doing once again \u8230\'20\'26 he\u8217\'20\'19s literally trying to confuse people and trying to confuse the underlying measure and the headline measure.\par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank targets the headline measure, and they say in their new forecast that they\u8217\'20\'19ll hit the new the midpoint of the target band on the headline measure in June of 2025.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to get through this, don\u8217\'20\'19t worry,\u8221\'20\'1D the speaker, Milton Dick, says, adding that he will allow the question but wants the house to be careful with the language it\u8217\'20\'19s using.\par \par \uc2 For everyone\u8217\'20\'19s benefit, if we could reframe language to be more factual and to be on point, I think question time would be a better thing.\par \par \uc2 A point Taylor ignores, repeats his original point, and asks about Labor\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Creckless spending\u8221\'20\'1D driving up interest rates.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Question time begins\par \par \uc2 And it\u8217\'20\'19s question time! The shadow treasurer, \uc2 Angus Taylor\uc2 , is first up, calling the government \u8220\'20\'1Cthe weakest and most incompetent since the Whitlam government\u8221\'20\'1D. Speaker Milton Dick (again) calls on him to lose the \u8220\'20\'1Cdescriptors\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Dick says it\u8217\'20\'19s a \u8220\'20\'1Cslippery path and a race to the bottom\u8221\'20\'1D and puts him in a difficult position to argue for such language. The opposition leader, \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2 , wants to know what standing order Dick\u8217\'20\'19s using, but he\u8217\'20\'19s grandstanding:\par \par \uc2 If you can\u8217\'20\'19t describe a government in terms it should be described in, I don\u8217\'20\'19t understand how it is we can have a breach of the standing orders.\par \par \uc2 Dick says he was calling for dignity, rather than ruling the question out of order.\par \par \uc2 What an illuminating start.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump supporters watch US election at Parliament House\par \par \uc2 At the US election watch party in NSW Parliament House, Liberal party rank-and-file members Jamie and his wife, who preferred not to be named, are hopeful \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will win the presidency but are worried there will be electoral \u8220\'20\'1Ccheating\u8221\'20\'1D. Jamie said:\par \par \uc2 While Kamala \u8217\'20\'19s ahead in certain states, they\u8217\'20\'19ll just keep counting.\par \par \uc2 The couple were \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastated\u8221\'20\'1D by the results in 2020\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election and are happy to be watching the results with fellow Trump supporters, a few of whom are wearing Maga hats. The pair live in Sydney\u8217\'20\'19s inner west, in Anthony Albanese \u8217\'20\'19s electorate of Grayndler, where they say they feel unsafe to proclaim their support for Trump. Jamie\u8217\'20\'19s wife said:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s great we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing people walking around with Trump hats on. They\u8217\'20\'19re taking their life into their own hands in the city \u8230\'20\'26 We would probably be killed or our lives would be made a misery if people saw us in Maga hats.\par \par \uc2 The pair have been long engaged in Australian and American politics and are frustrated by Australia\u8217\'20\'19s political disengagement, citing immigration rates, the development of offshore windfarms and the nation\u8217\'20\'19s acquiescence to vaccine mandates during the pandemic. Jamie\u8217\'20\'19s wife said:\par \par \uc2 It frustrates the hell out of me \u8230\'20\'26 Australians sitting around, watching sport, drinking beer, talking about climate change, all this sort of rubbish. They\u8217\'20\'19re just not seeing what\u8217\'20\'19s really going on here, are they?\par \par \uc2 The pair heard about the watch party through an organisation called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Brit_Aus_Com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 British Australia Community }}}\uc2  , which they first encountered at an event with former Fox News host {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tucker-carlson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tucker Carlson }}}\uc2  earlier in the year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 Turnbull says Trump \u8216\'20\'18doesn\u8217\'20\'19t pay a lot of attention\u8217\'20\'19 to advisers\par \par \uc2 More from former PM \uc2 Malcolm Turnbull\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 he warned that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s behaviour with foreign leaders is different to what one might expect from a president.\par \par \uc2 Speaking with the ABC\u8217\'20\'19s David Speers just now, he said:\par \par \uc2 You know, a regular president or prime minister will have staff and advisers and a whole official system that you can interact with. Now, with Trump, he will have those people, but he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t pay a lot of attention to them. So the advocacy really is down to the prime minister or the counterpart.\par \par \uc2 When asked about ambassadors\u8217\'20\'19 roles under Trump, Turnbull again suggested things will not be in keeping with usual diplomatic modus operandi:\par \par \uc2 Joe Hockey\uc2  worked really hard, was a good ambassador. [He] tried to engage \u8230\'20\'26 but he had nothing to do with the critical negotiations with Trump. And that\u8217\'20\'19s no reflection on him. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think that any ambassador will.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 Katherine Deves\uc2  says \u8216\'20\'18angry\u8217\'20\'19 Americans will vote Trump in\par \par \uc2 At a pro-Trump watch party in New South Wales\u8217\'20\'19 Parliament House, dozens of Australians have taken their seats alongside some state politicians to watch Fox News as the US election results roll in.\par \par \uc2 A few attendees are wearing red Maga hats and one woman wears a T-shirt showing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s shooting with the words \u8220\'20\'1CGod bless President Trump\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a proud Redbubble purchase.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe NSW Libertarians have been hosting a US election watch party in the state parliament's theatrette: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MQNMoRIK0q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MQNMoRIK0q }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Luca (@IttimaniL) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IttimaniL/status/1853985310851371240?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 The Libertarian party has booked out parliament\u8217\'20\'19s theatrette, with about 200 expected to drop by over the afternoon. Libertarian MP John Ruddick, sitting in the front row, says:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m hoping that we can save western civilisation and that Trump can prevail \u8230\'20\'26 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s not a libertarian but Kamala is very much a supporter of very big government [and] the puppet of the military industrial complex.\par \par \uc2 From NSW, Liberal frontbencher \uc2 Damien Tudehope\uc2 , One Nation MP Tania Mihailuk and Libertarian party president Ross Cameron have showed up, while former federal Liberal MP \uc2 Craig Kelly\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2023/jun/01/female-only-app-giggle-for-girls-transgender-discrimination-suit-roxanne-tickle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Katherine Deves }}}\uc2 , who ran for the Liberal party in 2022, have also dropped by.\par \par \uc2 Deves predicts an \u8220\'20\'1Cangry\u8221\'20\'1D American people will vote Trump in:\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19ve got tens of millions of migrants coming in, who are unchecked, unvetted, crime is through the roof, and you\u8217\'20\'19re seeing the whole woke agenda with respect to transgenderism and critical race theory.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nacc received 3,189 referrals of suspected corrupt conduct in 2023-24\par \par \uc2 The National Anti-Corruption Commission decided not to investigate 221 instances of potential corrupt conduct in its first year of operating, while moving forward with 26 probes, acknowledging its decisions may sometimes be \u8220\'20\'1Cunpopular\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The federal integrity body\u8217\'20\'19s annual report for 2023-24 provides a snapshot of its first full year. It shows the Nacc received a total of 3,189 referrals of suspected corrupt conduct.\par \par \uc2 In 221 cases, the referral passed the triage stage but didn\u8217\'20\'19t proceed to investigation because there were \u8220\'20\'1Cinsufficient prospects of finding corrupt conduct, or the matter was already being adequately investigated by another agency, or a corruption investigation would not add value in the public interest\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The report\u8217\'20\'19s release comes a week after the Nacc\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to start a corruption investigation into robodebt royal commission referrals {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/oct/30/nacc-robodebt-investigation-misconduct-finding-commissioner-paul-brereton-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was \u8220\'20\'1Caffected by apprehended bias\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The report, which was written before the watchdog\u8217\'20\'19s watchdog made the finding, acknowledged the decision would be unpopular.\par \par \uc2 The Nacc commissioner, Paul Brereton, wrote in its foreword:\par \par \uc2 Since commencement, we have been committed to carrying out our work in good faith, with integrity and in the public interest. That does not mean that our decisions will always be popular; often they will not. Making decisions that we believe to be right, though they may be unpopular, is what integrity requires of us.\par \par \uc2 The Nacc also reported the average time for assessing referrals was 125 days. As no corruption investigations were completed within the reporting period, it could not measure the average time to finalise an investigation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Malcolm Turnbull\uc2  says Australian leaders will need to \u8216\'20\'18stand your ground\u8217\'20\'19 when dealing with Trump\par \par \uc2 Malcolm Turnbull\uc2  is giving his two-cents\u8217\'20\'19 worth on the unfolding US election results.\par \par \uc2 Speaking with the ABC in Washington DC, the former PM says the night is so far \u8220\'20\'1Cpretty much as advertised, a neck and neck race. And it\u8217\'20\'19s too early to tell.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Turnbull says that Australian leaders will need to approach \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 should he become president \u8211\'20\'13 with strength and \u8220\'20\'1Cstand your ground\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 My advice is that you should not do what everyone will tell you to do, which is to suck up to him. The newspaper columns are full of people \u8211\'20\'13 not all of them are grifters, but a lot of them are \u8211\'20\'13 who say that you have to suck up to him and flatter him and, of course, people typically do that to guys like Trump because they\u8217\'20\'19re big, bullying \u8230\'20\'26 narcissistic. So if all you want is a photo-op \u8230\'20\'26 you can do that.\par \par \uc2 If you want good outcomes, in my case for Australia, you have to stand your ground and make a case. And I did so on a number of issues and incurred his displeasure, famously, over the refugee deal. But I got the outcome Australia needed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 Severe weather warning from BoM\par \par \uc2 Heat, storms and fire: the \uc2 Bureau of Meteorology\uc2  has provided its latest severe weather update. High temperatures across much of the country\u8217\'20\'19s east over the next day or two are forecast to give way to milder conditions in the south-east towards the weekend.\par \par \uc2 enltrSevere Weather Update: Hot with storms and high fire danger in the east.\par \par \uc2 Video current as of 11:30am AEDT 6 November 2024.\par \par \uc2 Latest forecasts and warnings: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4W35o8iFmh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/4W35o8iFmh }}}\uc2  or the BOM Weather app. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/khtsUd3FTI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/khtsUd3FTI }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Bureau of Meteorology\uc2 , Australia (@BOM_au) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BOM_au/status/1853971644647383519?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Greg Jericho has cast a steely eye over Labor\u8217\'20\'19s student debt policy and says:\par \par \uc2 Governments should subsidise things that are good and which benefit society \u8211\'20\'13 and tax things that are bad and make society, the economy and the planet worse.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/nov/06/labor-cutting-hecs-debt-is-not-a-perfect-policy-but-why-the-feigned-outrage-over-fairness"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Labor cutting Hecs debt is not a perfect policy \u8211\'20\'13 but why the feigned outrage over \u8216\'20\'18fairness\u8217\'20\'19? | Greg Jericho }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ben, an American student currently at the \uc2 University of Sydney\uc2 , says he hopes no violence follows the US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 He is watching the results roll in at a Democrats Abroad watch party at Kent Street Hotel, Sydney. He says:\par \par \uc2 I thought it would just be fun to come meet other people and watch the election together in a more vibrant atmosphere.\par \par \uc2 People are a little tense. People are worried about it but, you know, its lively and people seem to be excited \u8230\'20\'26 [I] hope things go really well but I\u8217\'20\'19m still nervous.\par \par \uc2 I just, I hope it goes smoothly. I hope there\u8217\'20\'19s not violence or anything, because I\u8217\'20\'19ve heard a lot about that.\par \par \uc2 It would be really cool to see the first woman president. I\u8217\'20\'19m really excited for that. So hopefully that\u8217\'20\'19s the outcome. That\u8217\'20\'19s what I\u8217\'20\'19m hoping for.\par \par \uc2 enltrKent St Hotel, Sydney, is filling up with Australians and American expats supporting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as the US presidential election results roll in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hsoPYHdrRj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hsoPYHdrRj }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rafqa Touma (@At_Raf_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/At_Raf_/status/1853972832356610144?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Former UK prime minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/nov/06/channel-4-fired-boris-johnson-from-us-election-show-for-promoting-his-book-co-host-says"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cfired for banging on about his book\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  during a guest appearance on Channel 4\u8217\'20\'19s coverage of the US election, apparently. Yes, this is the Australian politics blog \u8211\'20\'13 but there\u8217\'20\'19s a connection \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2024/nov/01/how-to-watch-listen-us-presidential-election-results-uk-harris-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Channel 4 panellists }}}\uc2  include {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/stormy-daniels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stormy Daniels }}}\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/rufus-wainwright"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rufus Wainwright }}}\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/brian-cox"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brian Cox }}}\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/sean-spicer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sean Spicer }}}\uc2  and one \uc2 Malcolm Turnbull\uc2 , former Australian prime minister.\par \par \uc2 Now that\u8217\'20\'19s a lineup.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 American expats \u8216\'20\'18nervous\u8217\'20\'19 about US election result\par \par \uc2 Alex Webb and Jialin Wu are watching the US presidential election results roll in at the Kent Street Hotel, Sydney, wearing Harris 2024 merchandise and American flags.\par \par \uc2 Webb, an American living in Australia, says the pub feels nervously optimistic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter 2016 everybody\u8217\'20\'19s nervous,\u8221\'20\'1D Webb says. He is hoping for a \u8220\'20\'1Clandslide Kamala victory\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m looking forward to celebrating the first female president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSupporters of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are watching US election results roll in at Kent St Hotel in Sydney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2Yn4dH37Nx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2Yn4dH37Nx }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rafqa Touma (@At_Raf_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/At_Raf_/status/1853964826864939219?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Cost of living increases slowing sharply, ABS says\par \par \uc2 The ABS has issued some cost of living data this morning, and generally pressures appear to be easing.\par \par \uc2 Employee households\u8217\'20\'19 living costs rose 0.6% in the September quarter, or about half the 1.3% increase last quarter, the ABS said.\par \par \uc2 enltrCost of living indices point to a slowdown in the September quarter. (Via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABSStats?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ABSStats }}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RHenxNSnTx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/RHenxNSnTx }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 @phannam@mastodon.green (@p_hannam) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/p_hannam/status/1853960926355194070?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a range of impacts, though, with households with employees facing higher costs of living (mostly because of their exposure to higher mortgage rates). As fixed-rate loans expire and they are repriced at a higher interest, those mortgage payments have been increasing.\par \par \uc2 Against that, automotive fuel and electricity prices have been easing back \u8211\'20\'13 the former because of a slide in global oil prices, and the latter because of government rebates (especially in Queensland, Western Australia and Tasmania).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CElectricity costs for Employee households fell by 20% compared to households receiving government payments, which fell by around 10%,\u8221\'20\'1D said Michelle Marquardt, ABS head of prices statistics.\par \par \uc2 The best off, at least in terms of cost of living increases, are age pensioners and self-funded retirees. Their costs rose 0.3% in the quarter, or a quarter of the pace of the previous quarter.\par \par \uc2 As it happened, we flagged the case for the worst being over in terms of cost of living increases recently here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/oct/27/australia-inflation-figures-cpi-rba-interest-rates-abs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inflation may be about to hit a three-year low. Does that mean the cost-of-living crisis is over? }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 Coalition says legislation needed after high court quashes ankle bracelet and curfew regime\par \par \uc2 The opposition has responded to the news that the high court has struck down the harsh regime of ankle bracelets and curfews imposed on non-citizens released from indefinite immigration detention.\par \par \uc2 The shadow home affairs minister, \uc2 James Paterson\uc2 , the shadow immigration minister, \uc2 Dan Tehan\uc2 , and the shadow attorney general, Michaelia Cash, said in a statement it was an \u8220\'20\'1Cembarrassing loss for the Albanese government\u8221\'20\'1D and that the government should introduce legislation in response today, and explain what they will do to \u8220\'20\'1Ckeep the Australian people safe\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 They said the effect would be that \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous non-citizen offenders\u8221\'20\'1D would be free in the community:\par \par \uc2 This loss compounds the failure of the Albanese government to use the preventative detention powers the parliament rushed through almost 12 months ago to re-detain any high-risk offenders.\par \par \uc2 The government repeatedly assured us that the amendments they drafted were constitutionally sound, and as recently as Monday in Senate estimates promised they had comprehensive contingency plans in place if they were unsuccessful in this case.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The fate of western democracy is on the line\u8217\'20\'19: Sydney pub fills with American expats watching US election\par \par \uc2 Hope, an American-Australian dual citizen is watching the US presidential election results roll in among others at a watch party at the Kent Street Hotel, Sydney, this morning. She says:\par \par \uc2 This is a super important election, and I either wanted to celebrate with people who would be as excited as I am, or cry with people who are going to be as devastated as I will be.\par \par \uc2 The event was organised by Democrats Abroad Australia and Sydney Expat Americans. Hope, who volunteers with Democrats Abroad, says:\par \par \uc2 I really think the fate of western democracy is on the line with this election. This isn\u8217\'20\'19t just about America, but also I\u8217\'20\'19m enraged on behalf of women and minorities and the republic and the constitution and Australia as a country that always follows America culturally and politically.\par \par \uc2 Watching Australia shift over further and further to the right over the last 40 years that I\u8217\'20\'19ve been here has just been so sad.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThe fate of western democracy is on the line,\u8221\'20\'1D Hope, an American-Australian dual citizen, says. She is watching the US presidential election results roll in at a Democrats Abroad watch party in Kent St Hotel, Sydney. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PYlv0VtcG9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PYlv0VtcG9 }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rafqa Touma (@At_Raf_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/At_Raf_/status/1853958270765158534?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 Hope\u8217\'20\'19s friend Amy is visiting from America. \u8220\'20\'1CWe voted early so that we could watch this together,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 Amy says the energy in the Sydney pub is optimistic:\par \par \uc2 This could be the end of democracy. I mean, we are all voting, I never thought it would happen in my lifetime, but we are all voting to avoid an autocracy \u8230\'20\'26 but we are hopeful.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Australians and American expats gather in Sydney pub before US election results\par \par \uc2 American flags are strung up in rows to the ceiling of the Kent Street Hotel in Sydney this morning. As CNN\u8217\'20\'19s live US election coverage plays from screens throughout the pub, dozens of are gathering to watch \u8211\'20\'13 some are in shirts with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  logos, others wear badges with Democrat slogans.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds are expected to join the watch party by lunchtime, Jasper Lee, the chair of Democrats Abroad Australia, says. The event is organised by Democrats Abroad and Sydney Expat Americans.\par \par \uc2 enltrAmerican expats are filling in to watch the US election results roll in at a Democrats Abroad watch party in Kent St Hotel, Sydney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qEZDz7PCFC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qEZDz7PCFC }}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rafqa Touma (@At_Raf_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/At_Raf_/status/1853960045622632559?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024 }}}\par \par \uc2 Lee says there is an energy of excitement this morning:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s certainly anxiety, but it\u8217\'20\'19s a good kind of anxiety. We\u8217\'20\'19re all hoping for a good result.\par \par \uc2 I think that Australians, like Americans, understand the stakes of this election, what exactly \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  promises to do to the United States and the world. And I think that they feel very similarly to us.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kennedy schtum on advice over education debt cut impacts\par \par \uc2 The Liberal senator \uc2 Jane Hume\uc2  has been pressing the Treasury secretary, \uc2 Steven Kennedy\uc2 , and fellow Treasury officials in Senate estimates about the impacts of the Albanese government\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/03/student-debt-hecs-relief-young-australians-minister-jason-clare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans to cut student debt on $16bn in loans by 20% }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Hume tries to provoke a response by citing economists such as Chris Richardson, who said it was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfairness fail\u8221\'20\'1D, while others cited called the plan \u8220\'20\'1Can abominable idea\u8221\'20\'1D or that there were many good ways to spend $16bn.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy declines to take the bait, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not an economic commentator\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hume says, \u8220\'20\'1Cbut you\u8217\'20\'19re an economist\u8221\'20\'1D, to which Kennedy responds a tad sardonically: \u8220\'20\'1CI am, thank you, yes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As to the wider effects, a colleague of Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s (I missed his name) said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t think the effects are going to be substantial on inflation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ankle bracelet ruling a \u8216\'20\'18victory for fundamental freedoms\u8217\'20\'19, lawyer says\par \par \uc2 The Refugee Legal executive director, David Manne, who acted for the plaintiff YBFZ in his high court case has commented on the ruling striking down electronic monitoring and ankle bracelets.\par \par \uc2 Manne told Guardian Australia:\par \par \uc2 This is an important ruling, it underscores the bedrock principle that the government doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the power to punish people by stripping them of fundamental rights of freedom and dignity.\par \par \uc2 The invalidity of the curfew and electronic monitoring is a victory for fundamental freedoms and the rule of law. Everyone, whether citizens or non-citizens, should have the same protections of freedom and dignity under the law.\par \par \uc2 The curfew and ankle bracelets constitute punishments which seriously infringe our client\u8217\'20\'19s liberty, and the government doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have power to do that. Under our constitution only courts, and not the government, can impose punishment.\par \par \uc2 Manne said the ruling means that everyone in the cohort released from immigration detention because their removal is not practical \u8220\'20\'1Cwill no longer be able to be held in their houses eight hours a day and subject to the invasive humiliation of ankle bracelets\u8221\'20\'1D. He called on the government to abide by the ruling immediately and remove the conditions from everyone on bridging visa Rs.\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 After they are freed from immigration detention they will not be subject to further punishments, [which make] it impossible to lead ordinary lives let alone to get a job, nor be under constant fear if they\u8217\'20\'19re late home by one minute or don\u8217\'20\'19t recharge the bracelets they\u8217\'20\'19ll be imprisoned for a minimum of one year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 UBS\uc2  shifts back its guess on when the \uc2 RBA\uc2  will start cutting rates\par \par \uc2 As mentioned, the big four banks still have February as the time when they think the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  will start cutting its cash rate.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday\u8217\'20\'19s comments from the \uc2 RBA\uc2  governor, \uc2 Michele Bullock\uc2 , sounded to this correspondent as more \u8220\'20\'1Chawkish\u8221\'20\'1D than that (barring some global surprises).\par \par \uc2 Among the big four, \uc2 NAB\uc2  perhaps is the most uncertain about its February guess on a rate cut:\par \par \uc2 Overall the path to a February rate cut which had already narrowed following recent data, looks even more narrow following today\u8217\'20\'19s presser.\par \par \uc2 CBA\uc2 , which lately pushed its forecast of a December rate cut back to February, is also wondering if another shift might be needed:\par \par \uc2 Our base case sees the \uc2 RBA\uc2  on hold until the February 2025 board meeting when we expect the \uc2 RBA\uc2  to commence an easing cycle. The risk clearly sits with a later start date for the first interest rate decrease.\par \par \uc2 ANZ and \uc2 Westpac\uc2  also have February as their first \uc2 RBA\uc2  cut.\par \par \uc2 UBS\uc2 , an investment bank, has had one of the better prediction records. Its chief Australian economist, \uc2 George Tharenou\uc2 , was on a streak of about a dozen correct \uc2 RBA\uc2  rate calls, when he stumbled.\par \par \uc2 Anyway, he\u8217\'20\'19s pushed back his call until May:\par \par \uc2 Thereafter, we still see the \uc2 RBA\uc2  easing cycle to be relatively gradual with -25 basis points per quarter, to a terminal low of 3.10% in Q2-26 (was 2.85%).\par \par \uc2 So, the \u8220\'20\'1Chigher for longer\u8221\'20\'1D mantra for rates might become \u8220\'20\'1Cnot dropping as low as hoped\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Of course, a lot might happen between now and June 2026, so nobody really knows.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Encrypted messaging app Session criticises \u8216\'20\'18wildly overreaching powers\u8217\'20\'19 of Australian law enforcement\par \par \uc2 Earlier we brought you {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2024/nov/06/australia-politics-live-wednesday-labor-albanese-coalition-dutton-question-time-us-election?page=with:block-672aa19c8f08243590db24c4#block-672aa19c8f08243590db24c4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments from the Australian federal police (AFP) }}}\uc2  about its approaches to the encrypted messaging app Session that resulted in the company shifting operations to Switzerland.\par \par \uc2 The AFP said the agency was doing its job, and there was child abuse material being shared on the app.\par \par \uc2 The Session director Alex Linton has responded in a statement today. He said Session understands the AFP work and has attempted to explain the limited capacity for Session to assist in investigations \u8211\'20\'13 due to how the app works.\par \par \uc2 However, given neither the organisation nor employees have been subject to any investigation, it remains unclear how an interaction such as an unannounced visit to the home of an employee was either helpful or appropriate.\par \par \uc2 Still, the true problem stems from the wildly overreaching powers which Australian law enforcement agencies possess. These powers will intimidate and discourage anyone building or offering privacy technology to Australians, and whether it is the spectre of backdoor legislation or an actual notice forcing a company to compromise its own encryption \u8211\'20\'13 the result is these skills are leaving the country and Australians less safe online.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New Lehrmann barrister wants to remain unnamed to avoid trolling, court hears\par \par \uc2 The barrister who has agreed to represent Bruce Lehrmann in his appeal against his defamation loss wishes to remain unnamed until the court sets a date, to avoid being trolled or harassed, the federal court has heard.\par \par \uc2 In April, Justice Michael Lee found Lehrmann was not defamed by \uc2 Network Ten\uc2  and Lisa Wilkinson and last month the former Liberal staffer was granted the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/oct/23/bruce-lehrmann-appeal-defamation-case-network-ten-lisa-wilkinson-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 right to appeal }}}\uc2  against the judgment.\par \par \uc2 At a case management hearing this morning, Lehrmann\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer Zali Burrows said the barrister\u8217\'20\'19s name was confidential until a formal date was set.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUntil I have the hearing date for the appeal, and I have formally briefed him, he wishes to remain unnamed, just on the basis he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t wish to be trolled or harassed, for example, as I\u8217\'20\'19ve experienced,\u8221\'20\'1D Burrows said.\par \par \uc2 Justice Wendy Abraham asked Burrows to write his name on a piece of paper and hand it to her and to Sue Chrysanthou SC, representing Lisa Wilkinson.\par \par \uc2 The date for the appeal is yet to be determined but will be in the second half of 2025.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Following on from that story I mentioned earlier {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2024/nov/05/media-regulator-cant-bring-herself-to-read-out-revolting-kyle-jackie-o-transcripts-in-senate-estimates-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by  }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2024/nov/05/media-regulator-cant-bring-herself-to-read-out-revolting-kyle-jackie-o-transcripts-in-senate-estimates-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sarah Martin }}}\uc2  , here\u8217\'20\'19s the video of the Greens senator \uc2 Sarah Hanson-Young\uc2  on what she described as Kyle and Jackie O \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Crevolting, sexist, racist, misogynistic, divisive\u8221\'20\'1D content:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pill testing to go ahead at Schoolies despite LNP promise to drop scheme\par \par \uc2 AAP\uc2  reports that pill testing will proceed at the popular end-of-year Schoolies event on the Gold Coast after the Queensland government backflipped on its hardline stance.\par \par \uc2 The former Labor government committed $80,000 for the free and confidential service to be rolled out for the first time at the annual event attended by thousands of teenagers and young adults.\par \par \uc2 The Liberal National party vowed to dump the scheme prior to winning power at the state election in October.\par \par \uc2 The health minister, \uc2 Tim Nicholls\uc2 , confirmed on Wednesday that pill testing would go ahead given the event was just a few weeks away. A spokesperson for Nicholls said:\par \par \uc2 Our position remains that there is no safe way to take drugs and pill testing sends the wrong message.\par \par \uc2 The contract for pill testing at Schoolies this year was a contract led by the previous government.\par \par \uc2 After taking advice so close to the event, the only short-term option is for the department of health to honour the contract for this year\u8217\'20\'19s event.\par \par \uc2 The Australian Medical Association Queensland president, \uc2 Nick Yim\uc2 , welcomed the government\u8217\'20\'19s decision to allow pill testing at Schoolies. He told ABC Radio:\par \par \uc2 This demonstrates the current government is keen to seek advice on issues and pill testing was one of those issues.\par \par \uc2 He called for pill testing to become permanent at the event to prevent injury or death to curious school leavers.\par \par \uc2 Queensland, the ACT and Victoria are the only jurisdictions to have legalised pill testing, but it could be revoked in the sunshine state under the LNP government.\par \par \uc2 The former government had committed $1m over two years to fund pill testing, with fixed sites established in Brisbane and the Gold Coast.\par \par \uc2 Its first pill-testing service was rolled out at the Rabbits Eat Lettuce festival over Easter weekend in 2024, when 250 people had substances assessed.\par \par \uc2 It followed calls for increased standardised pill-testing programs at festivals after the deaths of Dassarn Tarbutt, 24, and Ebony Greening, 22, at the 2019 edition of Rabbits Eat Lettuce.\par \par \uc2 Schoolies takes place on the Gold Coast from 16 November to 1 December.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Aged care and childcare workers underpaid, Treasury boss says\par \par \uc2 The Treasury secretary, \uc2 Steven Kennedy\uc2 , says aged care and childcare workers were underpaid.\par \par \uc2 Senate estimates, so far, hasn\u8217\'20\'19t spent a lot of time on inflation, and the \uc2 RBA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s likely stance that interest rate cuts are still some way off. (See {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/05/bullock-is-sending-a-message-to-politicians-rate-cuts-or-big-spending-promises-you-can-only-have-one"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here from yesterday }}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 Markets, for instance, only estimate there\u8217\'20\'19s about a one-in-four chance of an interest rate cut by February. The big four banks have had that month \u8211\'20\'13 two \uc2 RBA\uc2  meetings away \u8211\'20\'13 as when they expect the first cut to land. (I expect they will push that back.)\par \par \uc2 Anyway, the Liberal senator \uc2 Jane Hume\uc2  has been picking up on the weak productivity growth, which is also a worry to the \uc2 RBA\uc2 . As the bank said yesterday: \u8220\'20\'1CWage pressures have eased somewhat but labour productivity is still only at 2016 levels, despite the pick-up over the past year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The finance minister, Katy Gallagher, chimed in with this response:\par \par \uc2 The lack of productivity growth over a longer time, including for the decade that you\u8217\'20\'19re in government, is something that the government is \u8230\'20\'26 also focused on.\par \par \uc2 The conversation shifts to whether Kennedy thinks there has been underpayment in the care sector, particularly aged and childcare.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes,\u8221\'20\'1D is his response:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Fair Work Commission\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s view that the relative wage cases show there has been some underpayment there.\par \par \uc2 My judgment would be that it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be difficult to attract people into those sectors, and, frankly, improve productivity in those sectors.\par \par \uc2 Therein lines some of the key challenges in the economy, and in bringing inflation down.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bridget McKenzie\uc2  to update register after failing to declare more than a dozen flight upgrades\par \par \uc2 The Nationals senator \uc2 Bridget McKenzie\uc2  did not declare more than a dozen flight upgrades she has received over the years, but is expected to update her official register of interests after a self-audit of her own travel schedule.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afr.com/politics/federal/mckenzie-failed-to-declare-more-than-a-dozen-free-flight-upgrades-20241105-p5ko4w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australian Financial Review }}}\uc2  reported overnight the shadow transport spokesperson had failed to declare more than a dozen free \uc2 Qantas\uc2  and \uc2 Virgin\uc2  flight upgrades in her time in parliament. It came after McKenzie, who has led the Coalition\u8217\'20\'19s attack on Anthony Albanese over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/oct/31/anthony-albanese-qantas-flight-upgrades"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his own dealings with Qantas }}}\uc2  and reported upgrades, was found to have received upgrades of her own.\par \par \uc2 Guardian Australia confirmed on Wednesday that McKenzie\u8217\'20\'19s office has now received correspondence from \uc2 Qantas\uc2 , \uc2 Virgin\uc2  and \uc2 Rex\uc2  airlines, after she\u8217\'20\'19d asked them for information about upgrades she may have received. We understand the senator\u8217\'20\'19s office is going through those letters, and cross-checking them against flight upgrades she has previously properly declared in her register, but that there may be more than 12 upgrades which were not properly declared.\par \par \uc2 McKenzie is likely to update her register with those outstanding upgrades in the very near future. It\u8217\'20\'19s taken this long because the last letter she was waiting for only arrived last night, we understand.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you more on this as it develops through the day.\par \par \uc2 Other politicians across the parliament are also updating their register of interests to note flight upgrades they\u8217\'20\'19ve recently received. The housing minister, Clare O\u8217\'20\'19Neil, last week disclosed she\u8217\'20\'19d received two \uc2 Qantas\uc2  upgrades last month which \u8220\'20\'1Cwere not requested\u8221\'20\'1D on Melbourne to Canberra flights, which happened \u8220\'20\'1Cwhile I was boarding the plane, as on both occasions economy was overbooked\u8221\'20\'1D; the Labor senator Lisa Darmanin similarly disclosed that a domestic ticket \u8220\'20\'1Cwas unexpectedly and unsolicited upgrade to business class\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 One Nation\u8217\'20\'19s Malcolm Roberts yesterday declared \u8220\'20\'1Ca very recent gift\u8221\'20\'1D of \u8220\'20\'1Cmembership to Chairman\u8217\'20\'19s Lounge provided by \uc2 Qantas\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 early to mid July 2024\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 High court strikes down regime of ankle bracelets and curfews imposed on released detainees\par \par \uc2 The harsh regime of ankle bracelets and curfews imposed on non-citizens released from indefinite immigration detention has been struck down by the high court.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday the court ruled in favour of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/feb/28/australia-indefinite-immigration-detention-detainee-ybfz-curfew-visa-conditions-high-court-challenge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a stateless refugee from Eritrea }}}\uc2  whose challenge argued the visa conditions breached the separation of powers and amounted to punishment.\par \par \uc2 The decision will result in ankle bracelets and curfews being lifted from more than 100 unlawful non-citizens, in a major headache for the Albanese government.\par \par \uc2 Electronic monitoring and curfews, which are usually from 10pm to 6am, were imposed on unlawful non-citizens released as a result of the high court\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/nov/08/australia-high-court-indefinite-detention-ruling-government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2023 decision that indefinite immigration detention is unlawful }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Senate estimates on Monday home affairs officials revealed that by mid-October some 215 non-citizens had been released as a result of that decision, 143 of who are subject to electronic monitoring and 126 with the curfew condition.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling is a loss for the Albanese government, which legislated the new visa conditions with Coalition support after caving to opposition {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/nov/16/labor-emergency-immigration-detention-bill-strict-visa-conditions-electronic-monitors-curfews"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demands to toughen the regime }}}\uc2  with mandatory minimum sentences for breach of visa conditions and for the conditions to be applied as a default.\par \par \uc2 The case was decided with five justices in the majority, with Justices Simon Steward and Robert Beech-Jones dissenting, and of the opinion that both visa conditions were valid.\par \par \uc2 The loss is likely to spark fresh recriminations from the Coalition about handling of those released.\par \par \uc2 On Monday the home affairs department general counsel, Clare Sharp, said the department had engaged in \u8220\'20\'1Cvery extensive planning for all possible outcomes\u8221\'20\'1D of the challenge, including possible further legislation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 AFP defends its approaches to encrypted messaging app Session\par \par \uc2 The Australian federal police (AFP) has defended its approaches to encrypted messaging app Session \u8211\'20\'13 which led to the company moving overseas \u8211\'20\'13 as \u8220\'20\'1Cdoing our job\u8221\'20\'1D and said the app was being used to share child abuse material.\par \par \uc2 Guardian Australia {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/05/session-encrypted-messaging-app-developer-moves-out-of-australia-police-visit-switzerland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported on Tuesday }}}\uc2  the Australian-based app had moved to Switzerland after approaches from police, including a visit to an employee\u8217\'20\'19s home, to ask about encryption on the app. The organisation\u8217\'20\'19s director, Alex Linton, said Australia\u8217\'20\'19s regulatory environment was hostile to privacy tools.\par \par \uc2 The AFP acting commissioner, Ian McCartney, told Senate estimates on Tuesday night:\par \par \uc2 We don\u8217\'20\'19t obviously allege any criminality on their behalf, but the app was being utilised to distribute serious child abuse material \u8230\'20\'26 the focus of our engagement with the company was identified opportunities to provide lawful assistance, including the removal of that really serious child abuse material from the platform.\par \par \uc2 McCartney said it was a productive conversation with the app company, and he said it was an independent decision they\u8217\'20\'19ve made to move overseas, largely as a policy response, rather than police actions.\par \par \uc2 The Greens senator and digital rights spokesperson, \uc2 David Shoebridge\uc2 , said senators would support the AFP identifying and removing that kind of material, but said the powers to request app developers to build capabilities to bypass encryption and the decision to move overseas did not make Australia safer:\par \par \uc2 No one\u8217\'20\'19s any safer. No benefit to Australian law enforcement, no benefit to anybody other than we lose an industry, and we lose the capability, and we lose those kinds of skills in Australia, this doesn\u8217\'20\'19t make us safer. This doesn\u8217\'20\'19t help capture these appalling offenders who are sharing this material.\par \par \uc2 The AFP revealed that, in the last financial year, it had made no requests for assistance or capability requests of app developers, but there had been 66 assistance requests issued by other agencies.\par \par \uc2 Session was contacted for comment.\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/05/session-encrypted-messaging-app-developer-moves-out-of-australia-police-visit-switzerland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Encrypted messaging app developer moves out of Australia after police visit employee\u8217\'20\'19s home }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate estimates hears Treasury thoughts on US election scenarios\par \par \uc2 The treasurer, \uc2 Jim Chalmers\uc2 , sought Treasury advice on US election scenarios, estimates has heard.\par \par \uc2 Treasury is before Senate estimates this morning, and the secretary, \uc2 Steven Kennedy\uc2 , has been pressed by the Liberal senator \uc2 Jane Hume\uc2  about what the government has asked about US election scenarios.\par \par \uc2 Now, it would be a surprise if Treasury had not done some assessment of how economic policies might change in the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest economy. That\u8217\'20\'19s especially so when there\u8217\'20\'19s a chance that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  might be elected as the 47th president.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy said he had no expertise to judge who might win (not Robinson Crusoe there), and it sounds like the analysis is in line with private economists.\par \par \uc2 Trump has promised to slap broad-based tariffs on imports, including up to 60% on those from China. (He wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t need congressional support for such a move.)\par \par \uc2 Anyway, Kennedy said such a move would have \u8220\'20\'1Cflow-on consequences\u8221\'20\'1D for Australia, not least because China accounts for about a third of our exports. Various models would need to be tweaked.\par \par \uc2 In addition, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe imposition of trade restrictions, such as tariffs, typically lead to lower growth and higher inflation\u8221\'20\'1D, Kennedy said, echoing the economic consensus.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/30/trump-biden-harris-us-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy, as it happens, is outperforming most others }}}\uc2 , and it might be a post-election puzzle to solve to understand why the incumbent Biden/Harris administration hadn\u8217\'20\'19t got more electoral support from it.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy doesn\u8217\'20\'19t talk about what a \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  wins\u8221\'20\'1D scenario looks like, but it\u8217\'20\'19s generally assumed not a lot would change.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 No matter who wins, the US has no more trusted ally than Australia, Kennedy says\par \par \uc2 The US ambassador, Caroline Kennedy, has reflected on the history of suffrage for women and African Americans in her country as she reminded guests at a US embassy election day breakfast that \u8220\'20\'1Cevery vote counts\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy told the crowd that she felt \u8220\'20\'1Cmost American\u8221\'20\'1D on election day because \u8220\'20\'1Cthe right to vote is so fundamental to our democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She said:\par \par \uc2 Every voice counts and the right to vote is not something that any of us can take for granted.\par \par \uc2 In this election, and every other, the battle is ongoing, with efforts to expand and limit voting rights. It\u8217\'20\'19s a constant struggle in our politics and in this age of disinformation that is only becoming more intense. So when I vote in the US election, I think of all the names of heroes who sacrificed to give me this right. And for those of us all who live in a democracy, it\u8217\'20\'19s something to celebrate, something to protect.\par \par \uc2 She said she returned on the weekend from meetings in the US to be in Australia on election day:\par \par \uc2 I wanted to make clear to Australians that no matter who wins, the United States has no more trusted and capable ally. And there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of rhetoric on both sides of this debate, especially on one side, the fundamentals are not in question.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Legal Aid NSW says new client portal \u8216\'20\'18a gamechanger for our clients\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 $1.6m is going to a new Legal Aid NSW client portal.\par \par \uc2 The platform will be optimised for mobile phones, to provide clients with live updates, access to correspondence, document uploads and information on court appearances and other appointments, according to a statement from the office of Jihad Dib, the customer service and digital government minister.\par \par \uc2 Legal Aid NSW provided {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.legalaid.nsw.gov.au/about-us/annual-reports/annual-report-2021-2022#:~:text=Through%20it%20all%2C%20Legal%20Aid,(including%20Wollongong%20and%20Newcastle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 half a million client services }}}\uc2  in 2022-23. More than 50% were provided in regional and rural areas.\par \par \uc2 The new portal, supported under the Digital Restart Fund, will make information more accessible and \u8220\'20\'1Cminimise the need for clients to call Legal Aid NSW because they will be directly notified of updates to their case\u8221\'20\'1D, the statement said.\par \par \uc2 The platform is expected to be operational by late 2025.\par \par \uc2 The CEO of Legal Aid NSW, Monique Hitter, said:\par \par \uc2 This portal is a gamechanger for our clients.\par \par \uc2 It enables them to easily view information about their cases, their lawyers, their appointments and court dates.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 Delivering 24/7 access to key information, this portal makes it easier for people to deal with their legal problems.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kennedy calls for special Aukus visa to promote Australia-US collaboration\par \par \uc2 The US ambassador, Caroline Kennedy, has been busy! We mentioned her media appearances below. She has also likened the Aukus nuclear submarine pact to the 1961 decision by her father, the late president John F Kennedy, to send humans to the moon within a decade and called for a special Aukus visa to facilitate industry collaboration.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/audio/2009/jul/02/kennedy-speech-moon-apollo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Audio: Kennedy sets goal of landing men on the moon }}}\par \par \uc2 Addressing the biennial Submarine Institute of Australia conference on Tuesday, Kennedy said the Aukus partners needed new measures to make it easier to work together:\par \par \uc2 We need to increase connectivity between systems, making it easier and faster for work to proceed. We need new ideas to make this possible. An Aukus visa is one way to move this along.\par \par \uc2 She invoked the audacity of her late father\u8217\'20\'19s vision, acknowledging that some Australians \u8220\'20\'1Cdoubt the complexity and boldness of Aukus\u8221\'20\'1D. She said of her father:\par \par \uc2 He obviously set our nation on the path that has created the information economy, that has benefited our country for all these years. And he did it because it was hard and because he knew it would bring out the best in us. And those kinds of challenges always do. I really feel like Australia is ready for this, is embracing this challenge.\par \par \uc2 When then President Kennedy made his moon-landing pledge on 25 May 1961, the longest space flight by US personnel had lasted just five minutes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd he committed to send a man to the moon in 10 years,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo I have absolutely no doubt \u8211\'20\'13 and I know I speak for my colleagues in the \uc2 US government\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 that this is the same kind of thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kennedy described Aukus as \u8220\'20\'1Ca critical element\u8221\'20\'1D in the collective effort to sustain peace and stability in the Indo-Pacific region:\par \par \uc2 There were a lot of people who doubted that this could be done. That it was too complicated, too bold, too revolutionary, whether the US would share its most sensitive nuclear technology, whether the three partners could reform their export control regimes to allow us to succeed \u8230\'20\'26 I think we can all say that the doubters were wrong.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy said at least 78 US-trained Australian navy personnel would eventually serve on US submarines and more than 50 civilian \uc2 Australian Submarine Corporation\uc2  personnel were currently training at the Pearl Harbor shipyard.\par \par \uc2 The ambassador urged Australian companies to undertake the US defence industry vendor training process and become component suppliers for the Virginia-class submarines.\par \par \uc2 She said the money was there to build the industrial place but \u8220\'20\'1Cmore players\u8221\'20\'1D were needed.\par \par \uc2 She called Aukus \u8220\'20\'1Ca partnership about what we stand for, not who we stand against\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bureaucrats face questions after classified cabinet documents left on plane\par \par \uc2 That sinking feeling \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 AAP\uc2  reports that, minutes after getting off a plane in Doha, an Australian government staffer urgently alerted officials a locked bag containing classified cabinet documents was missing.\par \par \uc2 The papers were being carried by the ministerial and parliamentary services staffer travelling with Senator Murray Watt, the then agriculture minister, on a flight home from the \uc2 UN Food and Agriculture Organisation\uc2  conference in July 2023.\par \par \uc2 The curious case of the missing documents was first made public in early October and has been a point of interest at the latest round of Senate estimates hearings in Canberra.\par \par \uc2 Agriculture department officials were quizzed about the international incident during a tense exchange on Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 Tim Simpson, the department\u8217\'20\'19s first assistant secretary for people, property and security, confirmed details from an internal investigation, saying the papers were left on a plane in the early hours of 7 July.\par \par \uc2 The Senator and staffers had flown from Mumbai to Doha on an Indian airline on their way back to Australia from the \uc2 UN\uc2  conference in Rome.\par \par \uc2 The staffer left the secure bag containing the cabinet documents on the aircraft, Simpson told the hearing:\par \par \uc2 What I can confirm is the documents were carried in an appropriate container \u8230\'20\'26 and secured correctly for the classification.\par \par \uc2 Australian embassy staff in India were contacted about 10 or 15 minutes after the travelling party got off the plane and staffers tried and failed to get the documents back.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the time the documents weren\u8217\'20\'19t there when they were able to get back on and look for them,\u8221\'20\'1D Simpson said.\par \par \uc2 The agriculture secretary, Adam Fennessy, said security was taken very seriously and staff were retrained after the incident.\par \par \uc2 At the end of questioning, the hearing was told the staffer worked for ministerial and parliamentary services.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope the poor devil got over it,\u8221\'20\'1D the Labor senator Glenn Sterle said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A Trump presidency would be a disaster,\u8217\'20\'19 Greens senator says\par \par \uc2 The Greens senator Steph Hodgins-May has a more emphatic position on the US election. She said in Canberra this morning:\par \par \uc2 A Trump presidency would be a disaster, a disaster for women, for people of colour, for the LGBTIQA+ community, for the climate.\par \par \uc2 He threatens our democracy and progress. It\u8217\'20\'19s incredible to think Americans might give such a vile man another chance. If Trump is elected, the prime minister must urgently cancel Aukus and reconsider Australia\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with the United States. We cannot be associated with such a dangerous demagogue like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 AAP\uc2  reports that Kennedy was on Sunrise earlier. She described the US election as historic, and said whatever the outcome Australia would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cwinner\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 In terms of our foreign policy, and especially in terms of Australia, which is our most trusted and capable ally, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it will change the fundamentals \u8230\'20\'26 no matter who wins, Australia will be the winner.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US election \u8216\'20\'18shaping up to be very close\u8217\'20\'19, ambassador Caroline Kennedy says\par \par \uc2 Caroline Kennedy, the US ambassador to Australia, says as an ambassador she\u8217\'20\'19s not supposed to talk about politics \u8230\'20\'26 but went on to say (after the ABC Breakfast host \uc2 Michael Rowland\uc2  said \u8220\'20\'1Cassuming you did vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 I think the issues that are on the ballot this time are important to women.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s made that really clear. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is focusing more on immigration.\par \par \uc2 And she points out that in the US, where voting is not compulsory, it\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Call about turnout, who shows up on election day\u8221\'20\'1D, and that they need to get young people to the polls. But she wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t change their system:\par \par \uc2 I think our system is great. It\u8217\'20\'19s so complicated, gives Australians something to talk about all year long for four years. So I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t change a thing! But the way you do it is really impressive, and I have learned a lot on that while I have been here.\par \par \uc2 She says the US has \u8220\'20\'1Can incredibly strong and transparent system despite attempts to interfere with it from abroad, as we heard from our national security agencies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd obviously some people who don\u8217\'20\'19t want to accept the result are going to start saying, you know, that there\u8217\'20\'19s a problem if it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear, but I think it\u8217\'20\'19s shaping up to be very close,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, on the potential for unrest.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Angus Taylor\uc2  bats away questions about \uc2 Bridget McKenzie\uc2  flight upgrades\par \par \uc2 The shadow treasurer, \uc2 Angus Taylor\uc2 , has been asked about reports that the shadow transport minister, \uc2 Bridget McKenzie\uc2 , did not declare more than a dozen flight upgrades. He told ABC Radio:\par \par \uc2 I don\u8217\'20\'19t know that any of that\u8217\'20\'19s been verified.\par \par \uc2 The \u8220\'20\'1Creal issue\u8221\'20\'1D, he says, is allegations about Anthony Albanese \u8217\'20\'19s upgrades.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/oct/31/anthony-albanese-qantas-flight-upgrades"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anthony Albanese says he didn\u8217\'20\'19t seek flight upgrades from anyone at Qantas }}}\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afr.com/politics/federal/mckenzie-failed-to-declare-more-than-a-dozen-free-flight-upgrades-20241105-p5ko4w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australian Financial Review }}}\uc2  is reporting that McKenzie has not updated her register of interests about the upgrades, and we\u8217\'20\'19ve asked McKenzie\u8217\'20\'19s office for a response.\par \par \uc2 Taylor also says Australia is \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely at the back of the pack\u8221\'20\'1D getting inflation to where it needs to be\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got a long way to go here. Australians are losing hope,\u8221\'20\'1D he says, adding:\par \par \uc2 Everyone is helped by lower inflation and lower interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether a possible Coalition government would wind back cost-of-living measures, Taylor says they haven\u8217\'20\'19t supported all of them, and that while they want lower debt for all Australians, they are against the government\u8217\'20\'19s policy to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/nov/05/anthony-albanese-labor-student-debt-plan-comment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reduce student debt }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He describes Labor as having \u8220\'20\'1Cmagic pudding economics\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Dutton\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/05/peter-dutton-liberal-coalition-abortion-policy-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rebuke on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , and that call from the minister for women, Katy Gallagher, for the withdrawal of the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill (mentioned below), Taylor says \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s a state issue, and we should leave this issue to the states\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 It certainly shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be politicised in the lead up to an election \u8230\'20\'26 I think it\u8217\'20\'19s incredibly insensitive.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 There was some seriously colourful language in Senate estimates yesterday, but in this case the media regulator found radio hosts\u8217\'20\'19 words were a step too far. Sarah Martin reports on what the Greens senator \uc2 Sarah Hanson-Young\uc2  described as \u8220\'20\'1Crevolting, sexist, racist, misogynistic, divisive stuff\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2024/nov/05/media-regulator-cant-bring-herself-to-read-out-revolting-kyle-jackie-o-transcripts-in-senate-estimates-hearing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Media regulator boss can\u8217\'20\'19t bring herself to read out \u8216\'20\'18revolting\u8217\'20\'19 Kyle & Jackie O transcripts in Senate estimates hearing }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Dangerous anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill\u8217\'20\'19 should be withdrawn, Labor says\par \par \uc2 A \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill\u8221\'20\'1D before the Senate should be withdrawn, if the opposition leader, \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2 , wants credibility on women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare, the minister for women, Katy Gallagher, says.\par \par \uc2 Dutton has warned his MPs on speaking out on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/23/senior-coalition-women-and-pro-life-senator-matt-canavan-reject-jacinta-prices-abortion-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comments by the Indigenous Australians spokesperson }}}\uc2 , Jacinta Nampijinpa Price, and with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/oct/29/queensland-election-lnp-kap-robbie-katter-abortion-policy-crisafulli"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 back on the agenda }}}\uc2  in the lead up to the Queensland election.\par \par \uc2 Gallagher said:\par \par \uc2 It is typical of \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2  to view this purely as a matter of winning or losing votes, rather than any genuine commitment to women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare.\par \par \uc2 If \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2  wants any credibility on women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare, he must immediately ensure Senators [Matt] Canavan and [Alex] Antic withdraw their dangerous anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bill currently before the Senate.\par \par \uc2 This is a test of \uc2 Peter Dutton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leadership, and a test of his commitment to the rights of Australian women.\par \par \uc2 She is referring to a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/article/2024/aug/28/australian-conservatives-claim-babies-are-sometimes-born-alive-after-an-abortion-whats-the-truth"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 born alive }}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D bill that has been described as misleading, and containing misinformation. A committee inquiry found there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno legal, ethical or medical basis to support the bill\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/05/peter-dutton-liberal-coalition-abortion-policy-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Peter Dutton rules out Coalition \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  policy changes and blasts MPs for stirring debate }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Labor launches pre-emptive strike over \uc2 CFMEU\uc2  ahead of Senate estimates\par \par \uc2 AAP\uc2  reports that the Albanese government has launched a pre-emptive strike as the opposition holds its feet to the fire over the \uc2 CFMEU\uc2  scandal.\par \par \uc2 The employment and workplace relations minister, Murray Watt, is expected to face a grilling when his portfolios are picked apart in a Senate estimates hearing on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The construction arm of the embattled union was placed into administration in August after allegations emerged of criminal conduct and organised crime links on job sites.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/sep/17/cfmeu-faces-fresh-investigations-into-alleged-corruption-in-queensland-nsw-and-sa-branches"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CFMEU faces fresh investigations into alleged corruption in Queensland, NSW and SA branches }}}\par \par \uc2 The Coalition has suggested Labor\u8217\'20\'19s response did not go far enough and should have included reinstating the \uc2 Australian Building and Construction Commission\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The construction watchdog was reintroduced in 2016 by the Turnbull government but abolished by Labor in February 2023, with its powers transferred to the \uc2 Fair Work Ombudsman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ombudsman has dozens of ongoing investigations into the commercial building and construction industry involving most branches of the \uc2 CFMEU\uc2 , its officials and employers.\par \par \uc2 The Liberal senator Michaelia Cash was employment minister when the commission was revived and said it would prompt \u8220\'20\'1Ccultural change\u8221\'20\'1D across the construction sector.\par \par \uc2 Watt said bringing back the body would be \u8220\'20\'1Ccomplete madness\u8221\'20\'1D, pointing out much of the union\u8217\'20\'19s alleged offending occurred under its nose. He said:\par \par \uc2 The failures of the \uc2 ABCC\uc2  to bring about change to the construction sector were plain to see.\par \par \uc2 It was politicised for the gain of [the former prime minister] \uc2 Malcolm Turnbull\uc2  and the minister who was instrumental in removing him from office, Michaelia Cash.\par \par \uc2 Under the Coalition\u8217\'20\'19s watch we saw the lowest productivity since the 1960s and higher average days lost to industrial action.\par \par \uc2 He argued the Albanese government was cleaning up the construction sector by taking the \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongest action possible\u8221\'20\'1D against the union and developing a building and construction industry blueprint.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Some more on our political editor Karen Middleton \u8217\'20\'19s piece today, which brings with it some needed nuance:\par \par \uc2 [ Anthony Albanese ] doesn\u8217\'20\'19t just need interest rates to start actually falling before he goes to the polls, he needs Australians to believe the depths of the cost-of-living crisis have passed and things are finally on the up.\par \par \uc2 And he needs them to start believing it now, not wait until they can feel it in the hip pocket.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/05/anthony-albanese-needs-interest-rates-to-fall-if-they-dont-his-reelection-chances-certainly-will"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anthony Albanese needs interest rates to fall \u8211\'20\'13 if they don\u8217\'20\'19t, his reelection chances certainly will }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Good morning, Australia, and thanks for tearing your eyes away from US politics to join me ( Tory Shepherd ) here. And muchas gracias to Martin Farrer for doing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2016/jul/19/thrushes-blackbirds-awake-sparrows-fart-country-diary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sparrow\u8217\'20\'19s fart  }}}\uc2  shift. Let\u8217\'20\'19s get started \u8211\'20\'13 estimates will continue apace, question time looms and hopefully some surprises await.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 How would Australians vote in the US election?\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s fair to say that some events in Canberra and Australia might play second fiddle to an election occurring somewhere else today. As chance would have it we have one or two Australian angles on the US election story, including an Essential poll showing that more Australian men would vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  than vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The poll shows that more Australian men would vote for Trump than Harris, and a majority of men and women support key elements of his platform including tariffs and deportation of illegal immigrants. Overall though, Harris would win the vote in Australia by 41% to 33% \u8211\'20\'13 according to the poll which you can read about here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/05/guardian-essential-poll-trump-harris-us-election-voting-australia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian Essential poll: US gender divide in support for Harris and Trump mirrored among Australians }}}\par \par \uc2 Peter Lewis analyses the poll findings and concludes that it shows progressive Australians shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be complacent.\par \par \uc2 He writes:\par \par \uc2 On the core elements of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nihilistic populism, Australians are more likely to share his disdain for the system, and even the majority of those who would vote for Harris concur.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s his full article:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/commentisfree/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-australia-impact-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australians horrified at the US election circus shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be lulled into thinking it\u8217\'20\'19s just something that happens over there | Peter Lewis }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Follow our coverage of the US election\par \par \uc2 If you want to keep up to date with the US election, check out our guide to Australian TV coverage, live results, where to watch and more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/when-is-the-us-election-2024-australia-guide-usa-presidential-day-date-results-what-time-polls-close"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election 2024 guide for Australia: when is it, what time do polls close and when will we know the results? }}}\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s more we will have unrivalled coverage of the events in the US as the day unfolds and you can follow it all here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election 2024 live updates: voting under way in most states as Harris and Trump hope to win presidency }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Fourteen people investigated for terror symbol displays\par \par \uc2 Three search warrants have been executed and 14 people are being investigated for allegedly displaying a terrorist symbol at pro-Palestinian protests, \uc2 Australian Associated Press\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 Australian federal police officers have trawled through 90 hours of CCTV and body camera footage and seized mobile phones and clothing depicting a terrorist symbol.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf relevant thresholds are met, the AFP will provide briefs of evidence to the commonwealth director of public prosecutions to determine if charges will be laid,\u8221\'20\'1D acting commissioner Ian McCartney said.\par \par \uc2 The AFP is further investigating whether rhetoric over killed terrorists or events in the Middle East reached the threshold of urging violence or advocating terrorism.\par \par \uc2 A special taskforce, codenamed ARDVARNA, was set up for the rally specifically due to the volume of evidence and referrals that had to be assessed, the AFP deputy commissioner, Krissy Barrett, said.\par \par \uc2 Police have spent some 1,100 combined hours investigating.\par \par \uc2 There were 113 reports relating to the display of prohibited hate symbols between January and October 2024, which resulted in 49 further investigations by the joint counter-terrorism team.\par \par \uc2 Of these, 28 remain active but no one has been charged since the hate symbols legislation came into effect on 8 January, Barrett confirmed yesterday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Senate told of biosecurity breaches by \uc2 United Airlines\par \par \uc2 United Airlines\uc2  has breached Australia\u8217\'20\'19s biosecurity reporting requirements three times in three years by failing to report that a dog was on a commercial flight, a Senate estimates committee heard on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Anna Brezzo, the department of agriculture\u8217\'20\'19s first assistant secretary for compliance and enforcement, said in response to questions from Victorian senator \uc2 Bridget McKenzie\uc2  that the airline had breached the pre-arrival reporting requirements on a flight into Sydney in December 2022 and a flight into Brisbane in March 2024, and had breached requirements by invalid disinfection of a plane in August 2023.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe dogs themselves were assistant dogs and they did have an import permit to arrive into Australia,\u8221\'20\'1D Brezzo said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we require however under the Biosecurity Act is that the airline lets us know ahead of time what is coming in on their airline.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Brezzo said the breach was picked up by biosecurity officers at the airports because it\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ca bit hard to miss the dog coming off the commercial airline\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 United Airlines\uc2  entered into a voluntary undertaking in August 2024 to undertake auditing, update its compliance framework and train its staff. Compliance with that undertaking will be monitored by the department of agriculture over the next 15 months, Brezzo said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShould they fail to commit or to abide by the agreement in the undertaking, we will take them to federal court and let the federal court make that decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McKenzie asked why it took three breaches to enforce the voluntary undertaking.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat looks like permissive parenting that we just let them keep getting away with a slap on the wrist,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The deputy secretary for biosecurity, operations and compliance group, Justine Saunders, said the response was \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely proportionate\u8221\'20\'1D and more effective in terms of ensuring long-term compliance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur intent is not to punish but actually to address the breach,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Welcome\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to our live Australian political coverage. I\u8217\'20\'19m Martin Farrer bringing you the best of the overnight stories and Tory Shepherd will be along to guide you through the day.\par \par \uc2 Our top story this morning is that ACT\u8217\'20\'19s former director of public prosecutions Shane Drumgold {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/law/2024/nov/05/media-hysteria-around-sofronoff-report-fuelled-mob-mentality-bruce-lehrmann-prosecutor-drumgold-says-ntwnfb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believes \u8220\'20\'1Csomething went terribly wrong\u8221\'20\'1D  }}}\uc2  with the Sofronoff report into Bruce Lehrmann \u8217\'20\'19s prosecution, which resulted in Drumgold losing his \u8220\'20\'1Cdream job\u8221\'20\'1D, a court battle over its findings and a subsequent integrity commission investigation. He says media \u8220\'20\'1Chysteria\u8221\'20\'1D over the case fuelled a mob mentality against him but will return to work at the NSW bar.\par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank\u8217\'20\'19s caution about interest rates is becoming one of the biggest obstacles to Anthony Albanese winning a second term next year. Labor needs a cut by March at the latest, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/05/anthony-albanese-needs-interest-rates-to-fall-if-they-dont-his-reelection-chances-certainly-will"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our political editor writes today }}}\uc2 , or his election chances will be much diminished. But \uc2 RBA\uc2  governor \uc2 Michele Bullock\uc2  is telling politicians that if they want a rate cut {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/nov/05/bullock-is-sending-a-message-to-politicians-rate-cuts-or-big-spending-promises-you-can-only-have-one"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 then they need to be careful with election promises }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Federal police have executed three search warrants and are investigating 14 people for allegedly displaying a terrorist symbol at pro-Palestinian protests. No one has been charged yet but we have more details coming up.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241105ekb50038p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
