\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  poised to win election after string of crucial swing state wins\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly, Joan E Greve and Lauren Gambino in Washington and David Smith in West Palm Beach, Florida \par \uc2 1,398 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 November 2024\par 14:50 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Republican nominee tells crowd \u8216\'20\'18nothing will stop me\u8217\'20\'19 after taking North Carolina, Georgia and PennsylvaniaUS election 2024 \u8211\'20\'13 latest updatesUS election results 2024: live map and trackerSenate and House results 2024: live maps and tracker\par \par \uc2 After notching a string of wins in crucial swing states, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was poised to return to the White House after a momentous presidential election in which democracy itself had been at stake and which is likely to take the United States into uncharted political waters.\par \par \uc2 The Republican nominee took North Carolina surprisingly early, the first battleground state to be called, and later he won Georgia and then Pennsylvania. He was strongly positioned in Arizona and Nevada, other key contests on Wednesday morning. Victory in one more state would see him return to the presidency.\par \par \uc2 The race between Trump, a former president, and the current Democratic vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , had been a frenetic contest and it finally approached its conclusion amid scenes of celebration in the Trump camp.\par \par \uc2 At 1.20am, at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election watch party in Palm Beach, Florida, a prolonged, almighty roar went up when Fox News called Pennsylvania for Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s over!\u8221\'20\'1D screamed one man. A young man in a black Trump hat shouted: \u8220\'20\'1CFuck \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ! Fuck her!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The euphoric crowd chanted: \u8220\'20\'1CUSA! USA!\u8221\'20\'1D They gathered near the stage, waiting for Trump to speak.\par \par \uc2 At 1.47am, Fox named Trump president-elect, though the Associated Press \u8211\'20\'13 which the Guardian follows \u8211\'20\'13 has not yet put Trump over the finish line.\par \par \uc2 The man who incited the deadly attack at the US Capitol on 6 January 2021, earning (and surviving) a second impeachment; the man who was this year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 convicted on 34 criminal charges}}}\uc2  ; the man who faces multiple other criminal counts and who has been ordered to pay millions in multiple civil lawsuits, including one over a rape claim a judge deemed \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantially true\u8221\'20\'1D; the man whom senior military aides called a fascist and a danger to the republic was preparing to head for the White House again.\par \par \uc2 Eventually, past 2am, Trump emerged to speak, to the strains of God Bless the USA, the Lee Greenwood country anthem plastered on Bibles that Trump hawks for sale. Trump was surrounded by his family, by close aides, and by JD Vance, the hard-right Ohio senator he made his vice-presidential pick.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a movement like nobody\u8217\'20\'19s ever seen before,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is I believe the greatest political movement of all time. There\u8217\'20\'19s never been anything like this in this country and now it\u8217\'20\'19s going to reach a new level of importance, because we\u8217\'20\'19re going to help our country heal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to fix our borders. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to fix everything about our country \u8230\'20\'26 I will not rest until we have delivered the strong, safe and prosperous America that our children deserve, this will truly be the golden age of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump reveled in battleground state victories and said he would win them all. He claimed to have won the popular vote, which had not yet been decided. He described \u8220\'20\'1Ca great feeling of love\u8221\'20\'1D and claimed \u8220\'20\'1Can unprecedented and powerful mandate\u8221\'20\'1D, celebrating Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/06/senate-elections-republicans-win"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retaking the Senate}}}\uc2 . He said it looked like Republicans would keep control of the House of Representatives \u8211\'20\'13 again, undecided at that point.\par \par \uc2 Trump saluted his wife, Melania, his family, and Vance, who also spoke, promising \u8220\'20\'1Cthe greatest economic comeback in American history under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leadership\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump referred to the assassination attempts against him. \u8220\'20\'1CGod spared me for a reason,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 At Harris\u8217\'20\'19s watch party, at \uc2 Howard University\uc2  in Washington, the mood {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-howard-university-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 became somber}}}\uc2 , as hopes Harris could become the first president from a Historically Black College and University began to flicker and dim. Around 1am, \uc2 Cedric Richmond\uc2 , a former congressman and Harris campaign co-chair, told supporters they would not hear from Harris that night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you for believing in the promise of America,\u8221\'20\'1D Richmond said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe still have votes to count. We still have states that have not been called yet. We will continue overnight to fight to make sure that every vote is counted, that every voice has spoken.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Attendees rushed out, their mood swinging to despair. Eight years after Trump defeated \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  in a similar fashion, few attendees seemed surprised or shocked. Many declined to comment. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat more is there to say,\u8221\'20\'1D one woman shrugged as she shuffled out.\par \par \uc2 Strewn water bottles and other litter were all that was left after the crowd was gone.\par \par \uc2 Before 1am, the Republicans had retaken the Senate. A West Virginia seat went red as expected but the die was cast when \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2 , a long-serving progressive Democrat, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-ohio-senate-race-results"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was beaten in Ohio by Bernie Moreno}}}\uc2 , a car salesperson backed by Trump. Democrats had held the chamber 51-49.\par \par \uc2 In Maryland, however, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/maryland-senate-seat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Angela Alsobrooks provided a point of light}}}\uc2  for Democrats, joining \uc2 Lisa Blunt Rochester\uc2 , of Delaware, as the third and fourth Black women ever elected to the Senate.\par \par \uc2 The House remained contested, Democrats seeking to retake the chamber, to erect a bastion against a Republican White House and Senate. The House can hold a president to account but the Senate controls federal judicial appointments. Further rightwing consolidation of control of the supreme court, to which Trump appointed three hardliners between 2017 and 2021, may be possible.\par \par \uc2 In June 2022, that Trump court removed the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Campaigns for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  fueled Democratic electoral successes after that but on Tuesday such issues seemed to fall short of fueling the wave of support from suburban, Republican-leaning women Democrats had hoped for and pundits predicted.\par \par \uc2 A measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the Florida constitution, which Democrats hoped would help boost turnout, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/florida-abortion-ballot-ban-measure-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell short}}}\uc2  of the 60% needed for approval. Nebraska, won by Trump, voted to uphold its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which outlaws the procedure after 12 weeks of pregnancy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/election-abortion-ballot-measures-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -related measures}}}\uc2 , however, did pass in New York, Maryland, Colorado, Missouri, Nevada and Arizona.\par \par \uc2 A huge gender gap opened. A CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/election/2024/exit-polls/national-results/general/president/0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exit poll}}}\uc2  showed Harris up by 11 points among female voters, Trump up 10 among male voters. Other polls showed dominant concerns over the economy and democracy. According to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/ap-votecast-elections-harris-trump-voters-d5cf4e3611f50ec4349d93ddc7f037cd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AP Votecast survey}}}\uc2 , four in 10 voters named the economy and jobs as the most important problem facing the country, a hopeful sign for Trump. Roughly half of voters cited the fate of democracy, a focal point of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday will bring jitters in foreign capitals. Victory for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica first\u8221\'20\'1D ethos can be expected to boost rightwing populists in Europe and elsewhere \u8211\'20\'13 and to place support for Ukraine in jeopardy as it fights Russian invaders.\par \par \uc2 At home, America lies divided. Harris centered her campaign on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s autocratic threat while he ran a campaign fuelled by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/02/trump-social-media-threats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 grievance}}}\uc2 , both personal and the perception of an ailing America, baselessly painting Biden and Harris as far-left figures wrecking the economy with inflation and identity politics. Though he was the subject of two assassination attempts, in Pennsylvania and Florida, he stoked huge divisions and widespread {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/election-political-violence-surge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fears of violence}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump told supporters \u8220\'20\'1CI am your retribution\u8221\'20\'1D and threatened to prosecute political foes, journalists and others. He suggested turning the US military {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/trump-military-enemy-within-armed-forces-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  against \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy from within\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 . He put immigration and border security at the heart of his pitch, painting a picture of the US overrun by illegal immigration, with language that veered into outright racism and fearmongering. He referred to undocumented people as \u8220\'20\'1Canimals\u8221\'20\'1D with \u8220\'20\'1Cbad genes \u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/16/trump-immigrants-new-hampshire-rally?CMP=twt_b-gdnnews"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poisoning the blood of our country}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He vowed to stage the biggest deportation in US history, to replace thousands of federal workers with loyalists, to impose sweeping tariffs on allies and foes alike.\par \par \uc2 On election night, he said he would govern \u8220\'20\'1Cby a simple motto: Promises made. Promises kept. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to keep our promises. Nothing will stop me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Additional reporting by Sam Levine in Allentown, Pennsylvania, Hugo Lowell in West Palm Beach, Florida, and Asia Alexander in Washington\par \par \uc2 Read more of the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 US election coverage\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/when-do-polls-close-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When do polls close?}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/harris-trump-election-results-when"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When will we know the result?}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Where is \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  on the ballot?}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/us-senate-house-and-governor-elections-2024-results-from-all-50-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate, House and governor results}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/03/us-presidential-election-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Everything you need to know}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241106ekb6001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
