\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US election 2024 live: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says \u8216\'20\'18we made history\u8217\'20\'19 as he closes in on victory with win in Pennsylvania\b0\par\par\uc2 Amy Sedghi (now); Chris Stein, Sam Levin and L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (earlier) \par \uc2 27,522 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 November 2024\par 09:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Latest results and reaction after Trump wins crucial swing states, leaving him just three delegates short of 270 neededUS election results 2024: live map and trackerSenate and House results 2024: live maps and trackerWhen will we know the result of the US presidential election?\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Portugal's PM congratulates Trump, says he 'looks forwards to working closely' with him\par \par \uc2 Portugal\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Lu\u237\'00\'EDs Montenegro, has also shared a congratualtory post on X and tagged \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Montenegro said he looked \u8220\'20\'1Cforward to working closely\u8221\'20\'1D with Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin the spirit of the longstanding and solid relationship between Portugal and the United States, bilaterally and at \uc2 Nato\uc2  and multilateral level\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations, President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 I look forward to working closely with you, within the spirit of the long standing and solid relationship between Portugal and the United States, bilaterally and at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NATO?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NATO}}}\uc2  and multilateral level.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lu\u237\'00\'EDs Montenegro (@LMontenegropm) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LMontenegropm/status/1854080900482408626?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 Spain's S\u225\'00\'E1nchez congratulates Trump\par \par \uc2 Spain\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, Pedro S\u225\'00\'E1nchez, has congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on a presumed US election victory.\par \par \uc2 In a post on X, S\u225\'00\'E1nchez wrote:\par \par \uc2 We will work on our strategic bilateral relations and on a strong transatlantic partnership.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  on your victory and your election as 47th President of the US.\par \par \uc2 We will work on our strategic bilateral relations and on a strong transatlantic partnership.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Pedro S\u225\'00\'E1nchez (@sanchezcastejon) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sanchezcastejon/status/1854083073857454171?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 Greek PM congratulates Trump, 'looks forward' to 'deepening strategic partnership' between two countries\par \par \uc2 Greek prime minister, \uc2 Kyriakos Mitsotakis\uc2 , says Athens \u8220\'20\'1Clooks forward to further deepening the strategic partnership between our two countries,\u8221\'20\'1D in a post on X congratulating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on his election victory.\par \par \uc2 At a time of regional turmoil, the centre right leader highlighted the need to continue working closely on geopolitical issues.\par \par \uc2 Nato-member Greece has increasingly emphasised its role as a \u8220\'20\'1Cpillar of stability\u8221\'20\'1D in the eastern Mediterranean \u8211\'20\'13 a role that in turn has been highlighted by the Middle East conflict.\par \par \uc2 Hours before ballot boxes opened in the US, Mitsotakis said that while the presidential elections were of \u8220\'20\'1Cparticular importance for the entire international community\u8221\'20\'1D it was \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely necessary for Europe to come of age geopolitically. The time has come for Europe to re-energize itself by launching policies that go off the beaten track\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The comments have been interpreted as speaking to the nervousness many in Europe will feel about a Trump comeback.\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  on your election victory. Greece looks forward to further deepening the strategic partnership between our two countries and working together on important regional and global issues.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Prime Minister GR (@PrimeministerGR) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PrimeministerGR/status/1854084117995897204?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 The video team have shared the below clips of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporters gathered at a watch party in Florida earlier erupting in celebration as Fox News called the 2024 race.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press, which the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  relies on for projections, has not yet called the election overall.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 Israeli government figures welcome a Trump victory while \uc2 Hamas\uc2  say he will be tested on promise to end Gaza war\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s president \uc2 Isaac Herzog\uc2  has described \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cchampion of peace\u8221\'20\'1D as senior figures in \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s government welcomed the prospect of the return of the former president to the White House.\par \par \uc2 In a post to social media Herzog said:\par \par \uc2 Congratulations to president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on your historic return to the White House. You are a true and dear friend of Israel, and a champion of peace and cooperation in our region.\par \par \uc2 I look forward to working with you to strengthen the ironclad bond between our peoples, to build a future of peace and security for the Middle East, and to uphold our shared values.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the Israeli prime minister Netanyahu himself offered congratulations, saying a Trump victory \u8220\'20\'1Coffers a new beginning for America and a powerful recommitment to the great alliance between Israel and America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s newly appointed defense minister, Israel Katz, said he believed that a Trump presidency will \u8220\'20\'1Cbring back the hostages\u8221\'20\'1D and defeat Iran, posting:\par \par \uc2 Congratulations to president-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on his historic victory. Together we\u8217\'20\'19ll strengthen the US-Israel alliance, bring back the hostages, and stand firm to defeat the axis of evil led by Iran.\par \par \uc2 Two far-right members of the Netanyahu cabinet, finance minister \uc2 Bezalel Smotrich\uc2  and national security minister \uc2 Itamar Ben-Gvir\uc2  both used social media messages to invoke blessings from God on Trump, Israel and America. The two of them head parties which are for the exansion of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s illegal settlements on the land of the occupied West Bank.\par \par \uc2 Qatar \u8217\'20\'19s Emir, Tamim bin Hamad Al Thani, also offered congratulations to Trump, saying:\par \par \uc2 I wish you all the best during your term and look forward to working together again to strengthen our strategic relationship and partnership, and to advancing our shared efforts in promoting security and stability both in the region and globally.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Qatar has been one of the nations working most closely with the US and Egypt in attempts to broker a ceasefire and hostage release deal between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . \uc2 Hamas\uc2  is believed to still be holding about 100 hostages seized from Israel on 7 October 2023, many of whom are thought to have been killed.\par \par \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , which launched the 7 October attack last year, leading to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s sustained military assault on Gaza, has also reacted to the US election.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports senior official Sami Abu Zuhri said Trump would be tested on his statements that he can stop the war within hours as US president, and told the news agency: \u8220\'20\'1CWe urge Trump to learn from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s mistakes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 Charles Michel\uc2  president of the European Council, which represents the leaders of the 27 EU member states has congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations to President-elect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ???? & ???? have an enduring alliance and a historic bond. As allies and friends, the EU looks forward to continuing our constructive cooperation.\par \par \uc2 The EU will pursue its course in line with the strategic agenda as a strong,\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Charles Michel\uc2  (@CharlesMichel) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CharlesMichel/status/1854081489157111842?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Irish PM congratulates Trump and says 'people of the US have spoken'\par \par \uc2 The prime minister of Ireland, which is the European HQ to some of the US\u8217\'20\'19s most important companies, has congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe people of the United States have spoken and Ireland will work to deepen and strengthen the historic and unbreakable bonds between our people and our nations in the years ahead,\u8221\'20\'1D said Simon Harris.\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations to US President-elect {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  on your victory. The people of the United States have spoken and Ireland will work to deepen and strengthen the historic and unbreakable bonds between our people and our nations in the years ahead.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Simon Harris TD (@SimonHarrisTD) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SimonHarrisTD/status/1854080438941188202?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Ireland\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with the US is one of its most important economically and politically given its role over the peace deal in Northern Ireland.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investment from the US is the backbone of the country\u8217\'20\'19s economy with US multinationals including tech companies \uc2 Google\uc2 , \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and Intel, employing 300,000 people in Ireland and contributing 50% of the country\u8217\'20\'19s corporate tax.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a video of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  speaking on stage in West Palm Beach, Florida, earlier where he pledgedto bring a \u8220\'20\'1Cgolden age\u8221\'20\'1D to the United States.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 The leader of the UK\u8217\'20\'19s Liberal Democrats party has called a likely \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  election victory \u8220\'20\'1Ca dark, dark day for people around the globe\u8221\'20\'1D and described the Republican as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdestructive demagogue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Ed Davey, who leads the third largest political party in the UK parliament, wrote on X:\par \par \uc2 This is a dark, dark day for people around the globe. The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy and most powerful military will be led by a dangerous, destructive demagogue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThis is a dark, dark day for people around the globe. The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy and most powerful military will be led by a dangerous, destructive demagogue.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ed Davey (@EdwardJDavey) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EdwardJDavey/status/1854078061970407860?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 In a statement recently released by the party, Davey added:\par \par \uc2 The next president of the United States is a man who actively undermines the rule of law, human rights, international trade, climate action and global security.\par \par \uc2 Millions of Americans \u8211\'20\'13 especially women and minorities \u8211\'20\'13 will be incredibly fearful about what comes next. We stand with them.\par \par \uc2 Families across the UK will also be worrying about the damage Trump will do to our economy and our national security, given his record of starting trade wars, undermining Nato and emboldening tyrants like Putin.\par \par \uc2 Fixing the UK\u8217\'20\'19s broken relationship with the EU is even more urgent than before. We must strengthen trade and defence cooperation across Europe to help protect ourselves from the damage Trump will do.\par \par \uc2 Now more than ever, we must stand up for the core liberal values of equality, democracy, human rights and the rule of law \u8211\'20\'13 at home and around the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 European Commission\uc2  president congratulates Trump, urges him to work on 'transatlantic partnership'\par \par \uc2 The president of the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2  has congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and urged him to work with her on a \u8220\'20\'1Ctransatlantic partnership\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  said the EU and US were \u8220\'20\'1Cmore than just allies\u8221\'20\'1D, but shared a deep bond \u8220\'20\'1Crooted in our shared history, commitment to freedom and democracy, and common goals of security and opportunity for all\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She said:\par \par \uc2 Let us work together on a transatlantic partnership that continues to deliver for our citizens. Millions of jobs and billions in trade and investment on each side of the Atlantic depend on the dynamism and stability of our economic relationship.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Behind the scenes von der Leyen\u8217\'20\'19s team has been preparing for a Trump victory for months, including by drawing up lists of US imports to Europe to target with tariffs, if Trump imposes punitive duties on European goods to the US.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins bellwether county in Michigan\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Saginaw county, a bellwether that bodes well for his chances of flipping the Great Lakes state \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won four years ago.\par \par \uc2 Trump is leading with 84.2% of the votes counted, picking up 50.9% support to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s 47.7%. In 2020, Biden beat Trump by winning 49.4% of the vote compared to the Republican\u8217\'20\'19s 49.1%. The county supported Trump in 2016, when he won Michigan overall.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has not yet called Michigan, but Trump currently has a lead of just under five percentage points over Harris.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-swing-state-counties"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Red or blue? The bellwether counties that could swing the US election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nato's Rutte congratulates Trump, says his leadership will 'be key' to keeping 'alliance strong'\par \par \uc2 Nato secretary-general \uc2 Mark Rutte\uc2  has congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and said he showed \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong US leadership\u8221\'20\'1D in his first term in office that strengthened the alliance.\par \par \uc2 In a statement Rutte said he looked forward to working with Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cto advance peace through strength through \uc2 Nato\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Rutte, who took office last month, referred to the challenges facing the alliance without a direct reference to the war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 We face a growing number of challenges globally, from a more aggressive Russia, to terrorism, to strategic competition with China, as well the increasing alignment of China, Russia, North Korea and Iran.\par \par \uc2 The veteran Dutch politician, reputed for knowing how to handle Trump, praised the US president-elect, while seeking to convince him of the value of the alliance.\par \par \uc2 enltrI just congratulated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  on his election as President of the United States. His leadership will again be key to keeping our Alliance strong. I look forward to working with him again to advance peace through strength through {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NATO?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NATO}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Mark Rutte\uc2  (@SecGenNATO) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecGenNATO/status/1854073276688904323?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 India's Modi offers 'hearty congratulations to my friend \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 '\par \par \uc2 India\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2  joined the ranks of world leaders congratulating \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on his presumed victory. In a post on X, Modi offered \u8220\'20\'1Chearty congratulations to my friend \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, alongside several photos of the two men tightly embracing each other and holding hands.\par \par \uc2 Modi, who has been Indian prime minister for a decade, was seen to have a close relationship with Trump during his first term in office, and Trump has repeatedly referred to \u8220\'20\'1Cmy friend Modi\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As it looked like Trump was claiming victory on Wednesday, Modi said he was \u8220\'20\'1Clooking forward to collaboration\u8221\'20\'1D between the US and India and added:\par \par \uc2 Together, let\u8217\'20\'19s work for the betterment of our people and to promote global peace, stability and prosperity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrHeartiest congratulations my friend {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  on your historic election victory. As you build on the successes of your previous term, I look forward to renewing our collaboration to further strengthen the India-US Comprehensive Global and Strategic Partnership. Together,\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/u5hKPeJ3SY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/u5hKPeJ3SY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2  (@narendramodi) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/narendramodi/status/1854075308472926675?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 At the Republican watch party in Las Vegas, the crowd is giddy.\par \par \uc2 The bar at the Ahern hotel is packed with excited, bleary-eyed supporters. In a city known for its flair and theatrics, many supporters are dressed up in their most flamboyant Maga gear. A man wearing a rubber Trump mask and a star-paneled cape draws laughs and cheers.\par \par \uc2 Sari Utschen, 57, was wearing a homemade dress that was embroidered with the word \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8221\'20\'1D down the front in huge block letters, and string of LED lights draped like a scarf.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel relieved. I feel joyous,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Utschen said she used to vote with Democrats in the 80s and 90s, but finds that the party has gone too far to the left in recent years. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been red-pilled,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, laughing. Over the past four years, she said: \u8220\'20\'1CI felt like we were being bamboozled under Biden. Nothing made sense.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 Arizona voters approve protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in state constitution\par \par \uc2 Arizonans have approved a constitutional amendment that will protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access up until fetal viability, or around 21 weeks of pregnancy, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The procedure is currently available until about 15 weeks of pregnancy. Its passage came after Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court allowed the enforcement of a near-total ban on the procedure enacted in 1864, before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/democrat-close-repeal-arizona-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the legislature repealed it}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nebraska voters reject \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights measure\par \par \uc2 Voters in Nebraska have voted down a measure that would have enshrined \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The measure would have protected the right to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until fetal viability, or later.\par \par \uc2 Voters in the state instead approved a competing measure that writes the state\u8217\'20\'19s existing ban on the procedure after 12 weeks of pregnancy into the state constitution, and allows for the passage of stricter bans.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33am GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights measure wins in Nevada, fails in South Dakota\par \par \uc2 Voters in Nevada have approved a ballot question that will set the stage to further protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state, though a similar effort in South Dakota failed, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The measure in red state South Dakota would have restored the protections of Roe v Wade, which was overturned by the supreme court two years ago. It was rejected by 61% of voters, with 39% voting in favor.\par \par \uc2 Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s measure was a bit more complicated. It will enshrine a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the swing state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution, but voters must approve it again in 2026. Abortions are already accessible in the state up until 24 weeks of pregnancy, with exceptions to protect the life or health of a mother.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Starmer congratulates Trump on 'historic election victory'\par \par \uc2 British prime minister \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on his apparent victory in the US election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCongratulations President-elect Trump on your historic election victory. I look forward to working with you in the years ahead. As the closest of allies, we stand shoulder to shoulder in defence of our shared values of freedom, democracy and enterprise. From growth and security to innovation and tech, I know that the UK-US special relationship will continue to prosper on both sides of the Atlantic for years to come,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 Hungary's Orb\u225\'00\'E1n welcomes 'beautiful victory' in US election\par \par \uc2 Hungarian prime minister and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ally \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2  has welcomed the US election results.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGood Morning Hungary! On the road to a beautiful victory, it\u8217\'20\'19s in the bag,\u8221\'20\'1D he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/reel/1268281620965936?locale=fr_FR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said on his Facebook page}}}\uc2  earlier on Wednesday\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CGood morning Hungary, on the road to a beautiful victory. It\u8217\'20\'19s in the bag\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Vote counting is under way, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Hungarian?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Hungarian}}}\uc2  PM \uc2 Viktor Orban\uc2  is certain of a Trump victory. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xQAofIc7k1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xQAofIc7k1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Vikt\u243\'00\'F3ria Serd\u252\'00\'FClt (@viktoriaserdult) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/viktoriaserdult/status/1854046760471040298?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Orb\u225\'00\'E1n, one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most loyal allies in the EU, will host leaders from across the continent in Budapest at the European Political Community summit on Thursday. For weeks European diplomats have speculated that Orb\u225\'00\'E1n would invite Trump to address the gathering by video link.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 Brazil\u8217\'20\'19s former far-right president \uc2 Jair Bolsonaro\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 one of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s biggest fans internationally \u8211\'20\'13 has hailed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe resurgence of a true warrior\u8221\'20\'1D after what he called his ally\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cepic victory\u8221\'20\'1D in the US election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAgainst all oposition [sic] from globalists and the deep state, @realDonaldTrump will return to the Presidency of the United States of America to complete his mission: restore the greatness of his nation, protect the interests of his people, and work toward a world that is freer, more peaceful, and more secure,\u8221\'20\'1D Bolsonaro wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X.\par \par \uc2 The former Brazilian president claimed the apparent result of the election marked \u8220\'20\'1Cnot only your return to the White House but also the triumph of the people\u8217\'20\'19s will over the arrogant designs of an elite who disdain our values, beliefs, and traditions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis triumph is historic\u8212\'20\'14a milestone that rekindles the flame of freedom, sovereignty, and true democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D added Bolsonarno, who will hope Trump\u8217\'20\'19s win helps revive his own political fortunes despite the fact that the Brazilian is banned from seeking office until 2030. \u8220\'20\'1CIts impact will resonate across the globe, fueling not only the strength of the United States but also empowering the rise of the right and conservative movements in countless other nations... Perhaps we will have a renewed opportunity to make Brazil a true land of freedom, where it is the Brazilian people \u8212\'20\'14 not politicians and bureaucrats \u8212\'20\'14 who are the masters of their destiny.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The populist president of El Salvador, \uc2 Nayib Bukele\uc2 , also tweeted his congratulations to Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CMay God bless and guide you,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote alongside a photo of the pair.\par \par \uc2 enltrCongratulations to the President-Elect of the United States of America, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  ????\par \par \uc2 May God bless and guide you. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kl1lr0Dwv4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kl1lr0Dwv4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nayib Bukele\uc2  (@nayibbukele) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nayibbukele/status/1854049854818853021?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 Netanyahu congratulates Trump\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  has also congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , sharing a photo of him and his wife Sara with the ex-president, who appears to also be the next president:\par \par \uc2 enltrDear Donald and Melania Trump,\par \par \uc2 Congratulations on history\u8217\'20\'19s greatest comeback!\par \par \uc2 Your historic return to the White House offers a new beginning for America and a powerful recommitment to the great alliance between Israel and America.\par \par \uc2 This is a huge victory!\par \par \uc2 In true friendship,\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/B54NSo2BMA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/B54NSo2BMA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  - ?????? ?????? (@netanyahu) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/netanyahu/status/1854070348926328965?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 Macron congratulates Trump, says 'ready to work together'\par \par \uc2 French president \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  has tweeted his congratulations to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who appears poised to be the next US president. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he said, in French:\par \par \uc2 frltrF\u233\'00\'E9licitations Pr\u233\'00\'E9sident \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Pr\u234\'00\'EAt \u224\'00\'E0 travailler ensemble comme nous avons su le faire durant quatre ann\u233\'00\'E9es. Avec vos convictions et avec les miennes. Avec respect et ambition. Pour plus de paix et de prosp\u233\'00\'E9rit\u233\'00\'E9.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  (@EmmanuelMacron) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EmmanuelMacron/status/1854069933732229240?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 Throughout the presidential campaign, and in his victory speech tonight, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  bragged that the Republican party was expanding its coalition into racial groups that typically vote for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey came from all quarters, union, non-union, African American, Hispanic, American, Asian American, Arab American, Muslim American. We had everybody. And it was beautiful. It was a historic realignment, uniting citizens of all backgrounds around a common core of common sense,\u8221\'20\'1D he said onstage just now.\par \par \uc2 And it may in fact be true, at least partially. While all the ballots have not been counted yet, early data indicates Trump may have made inroads among some groups, such as Latinos, that voted for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  four years ago.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s walking off stage now, surrounded by a number of family members and Republican bigwigs, including House speaker Mike Johnson and his running mate, JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 The Village People\u8217\'20\'19s YMCA is playing. Trump has it on at his rallies all the time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he will bring 'every ounce of energy, spirit and fighting' to White House\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  struck something of a conciliatory note to the millions of Americans who did not vote for him, saying he will devote himself to the presidency and unite the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe task before us will not be easy, but I will bring every ounce of energy, spirit and fighting that I have in my soul to the job that you\u8217\'20\'19ve entrusted to me,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will govern by a simple model, promises made, promises kept. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to keep our promises. Nothing will stop me from keeping my word. To you, the people, we will make America safe, strong, prosperous, powerful and free again. And I\u8217\'20\'19m asking every citizen all across our land to join me in this noble and righteous endeavor. That\u8217\'20\'19s what it is. It\u8217\'20\'19s time to put the divisions of the past four years behind us. It\u8217\'20\'19s time to unite, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to try.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris wins Minnesota\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has called Minnesota for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The vice-president picks up 10 electoral votes from the traditionally Democratic state, but those will not be enough to stop \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  from winning, assuming he picks up three more electoral votes from the swing states that have not been called.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump vows 'to do the best job'\par \par \uc2 More promises from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , as he stands on the verge of returning to the White House:\par \par \uc2 I want to thank the millions of hard-working Americans across the nation who have always been the heart and soul of this really great movement. We\u8217\'20\'19ve been through so much together, and today you showed up in record numbers to deliver a victory \u8230\'20\'26 this was something special. And we\u8217\'20\'19re going to, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to pay you back. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to do the best job \u8230\'20\'26 we\u8217\'20\'19re going to turn it around. It\u8217\'20\'19s got to be turned around. It\u8217\'20\'19s got to be turned around fast. And we\u8217\'20\'19re going to turn it around. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to do it in every way, with so many ways, but we\u8217\'20\'19re going to do it in every way. This will forever be remembered as the day the American people regained control of their country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump just went on an extended riff about \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the billionaire who sank millions of dollars into helping the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign win Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a character. He\u8217\'20\'19s a special guy, he\u8217\'20\'19s a super genius,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said of Musk. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to protect our geniuses. We don\u8217\'20\'19t have that many of them. We have to protect our super geniuses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump then came back to the mic, and restated his vow to crack down on undocumented people .\par \par \uc2 It was a key plank of his campaign, and appears to have worked with voters where it mattered.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to have to seal up those borders, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have to let people come into our country. We want people to come back in, but we have to, we have to let them come back in. But they have to come in legally,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 Vance says: 'We just witnessed the greatest political comeback in the history' of the US\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, just said a few words:\par \par \uc2 Well, Mr President, I appreciate you allowing me to join you on this incredible journey. I thank you for the trust that you placed in me, and I think that we just witnessed the greatest political comeback in the history of the United States of America, and under President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s leadership, we\u8217\'20\'19re never going to stop fighting for you, for your dreams, for the future of your children, and after the greatest political comeback in American history, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to lead the greatest economic comeback in American history under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leadership.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt also looks like we\u8217\'20\'19ll be keeping control of the House of Representatives,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. But we also don\u8217\'20\'19t yet know if that\u8217\'20\'19s the case, either.\par \par \uc2 The GOP has a small majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber, and races that still have not been called will determine if they keep it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump claimed victory in the popular vote, but that has not yet been determined.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you very much. Winning the popular vote was very nice, very nice, I will tell you,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 No Republican, including Trump, has won the popular vote since \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  in 2004.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says 'we made history' as election victory nears\par \par \uc2 On stage in West Palm Beach, Trump declared victory and pledged to bring a \u8220\'20\'1Cgolden age\u8221\'20\'1D to the United States.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a movement like nobody\u8217\'20\'19s ever seen before, and frankly, this was, I believe, the greatest political movement of all time. There\u8217\'20\'19s never been anything like this in this country, and maybe beyond,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd now it\u8217\'20\'19s going to reach a new level of importance, because we\u8217\'20\'19re going to help our country. We\u8217\'20\'19ll help our country \u8230\'20\'26 we have a country that needs help, and it needs help very badly. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to fix our borders. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to fix everything about our country. And we made history for a reason tonight, and the reason is going to be just that we overcame obstacles that nobody thought possible, and it is now clear that we\u8217\'20\'19ve achieved the most incredible political thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He continued:\par \par \uc2 I want to thank the American people for the extraordinary honor of being elected your 47th president and your 45th president, and every citizen, I will fight for you, for your family and your future. Every single day, I will be fighting for you and with every breath in my body, I will not rest until we have delivered the strong, safe and prosperous America that our children deserve and that you deserve. This will truly be the golden age of America.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Only three electoral votes separate Trump from the White House.\par \par \uc2 They could arrive soon, from red state Alaska, or perhaps from one of the other swing states that have not yet been called.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won Pennsylvania, the Associated Press reports, putting him on the brink of crossing the 270-electoral vote threshold to become the next president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump addresses supporters at election watch party\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just stepped onstage at his election watch party in West Palm Beach, Florida.\par \par \uc2 Things appear to be going his way this election, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not over yet. Let\u8217\'20\'19s hear what he has to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican House speaker Mike Johnson says 'we have saved America'\par \par \uc2 Mike Johnson has congratulated \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on his potential victory in the presidential race:\par \par \uc2 enltrWe have saved America. ????\par \par \uc2 The American people have spoken, and President Trump and Senator JD Vance are going to the White House.\par \par \uc2 We are ready to get to work for the American people.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Speaker Mike Johnson (@SpeakerJohnson) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SpeakerJohnson/status/1854061186142044603?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has not yet called the race.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 The former CNN anchor and Daily Beast editor \uc2 John Avlon\uc2  has fallen short in his attempt to win a congressional seat as a Democrat, losing to the incumbent Republican, Nick LaLota , in New York\u8217\'20\'19s first House district.\par \par \uc2 The contest on Long Island was a fractious one. Avlon, who once wrote speeches for \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  when he was mayor of New York City, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/25/john-avlon-cnn-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaigned}}}\uc2  on a return to the political centre and civility but the two candidates clashed repeatedly. Avlon highlighted that LaLota did not live in the district. LaLota charged Avlon with being a Manhattan elitist.\par \par \uc2 Celebrating victory, LaLota {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2024/11/05/us-news/gop-rep-nick-lalota-defeats-avlon-in-battle-for-ny-1-house-seat/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI am deeply honored that Long Islanders have entrusted me to serve in Congress for another two years. Our convincing victory reflects our commitment to tackling our nation\u8217\'20\'19s toughest challenges.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Conceding defeat, Avlon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.danspapers.com/2024/11/nick-lalota-beats-john-avlon/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a hard night in Suffolk county for us Democrats. It\u8217\'20\'19s a hard night for many Democrats in the country, but the fight continues, and it\u8217\'20\'19s really important for us to keep the energy up to understand that this is not a time for us to shirk back, but it\u8217\'20\'19s a time for folks to step up continuously, because the good fight never ends.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 Should \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory in Pennsylvania be confirmed, as it has not yet been by the Associated Press, he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t quite have the electoral votes needed to become president.\par \par \uc2 Based on states the AP has called so far, Trump would have 267 electoral votes, just shy of the 270 needed to become the next president. The remaining electoral votes may arrive soon after \u8211\'20\'13 polls closed just over an hour ago in Alaska, a red state with three electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 That would bring Trump up to exactly 270, and that\u8217\'20\'19s before the outstanding swing states Arizona, Michigan and Wisconsin are called.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump reportedly wins Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 News outlets including NBC News and CNN project that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won Pennsylvania, putting him on the verge of becoming the next president.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has not yet called the state. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  relies on the AP to determine the outcomes of elections across the United States. The New York-based global news agency has a presence in every US state and a long and authoritative history of determining the winners of elections at the presidential, congressional and state level. Here is more information about their process.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/how-associated-press-calls-election-winners"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It is a little analog\u8217\'20\'19: how the Associated Press calls election winners in the US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins bellwether county in Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 It appears that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.goerie.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/11/06/donald-trump-wins-erie-county-pa-presidential-election-2024-harris/76081763007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won the bellwether Erie county}}}\uc2  in Pennsylvania as results indicate the GOP candidate is on track to win the crucial state, and with it, the election.\par \par \uc2 Pundits have previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-swing-state-counties"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CNo county in Pennsylvania \u8211\'20\'13 and possibly in the country \u8211\'20\'13 is as consistently swingy as Erie county.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With more than 95% of votes counted, Trump appeared to have 50.3% of the votes in the county, compared with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 48.8%.\par \par \uc2 Trump previously won the working-class county in 2016, followed by a slim \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  win there in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-swing-state-counties"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Red or blue? The bellwether counties that could swing the US election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 In Las Vegas, Nevada, the crowd at a GOP watch party roared as Fox News projected \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as the winner of the election. They burst into a chant of: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump! Trump! Trump!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several states, including this swing state, remain too close to call \u8211\'20\'13 but Fox recently projected Pennsylvania for Trump, a key state for winning the White House. The Associated Press, which the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  relies on for projections, has not yet called Pennsylvania or the election overall.\par \par \uc2 Several key swing states \u8211\'20\'13 including Nevada \u8211\'20\'13 remain in play, according to the AP.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel fantastic,\u8221\'20\'1D said Yolanda Wright, 47, a former Democrat who backed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and other Republican candidates for the first time this year. Trump offers more to the African American community, she said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been a Democrat my whole life, and I haven\u8217\'20\'19t seen any benefit from that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Democrats have been sending funds to wars and resources to migrants coming in through the southern border, rather than to Americans who are struggling, added Ronda Kennedy, 51, who had run in the Republican primaries for the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI trust Trump to put us first,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins electoral vote in Maine\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won one of Maine\u8217\'20\'19s electoral votes, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 He picked up the vote in the state\u8217\'20\'19s right-leaning second congressional district, while \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  earlier won the vote in Maine\u8217\'20\'19s more liberal first district. The two other electoral votes in the state, given to the winner statewide, have not been called by the AP.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 The presidential election has not yet been called, but some Republican lawmakers are already acting as if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma Republican congressman \uc2 Kevin Hern\uc2  just issued a statement congratulating Trump for winning:\par \par \uc2 This campaign felt different from the start \u8211\'20\'13 Americans were sick and tired of the status quo under Biden-Harris and wanted the prosperity they felt under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I am thrilled to see President Trump win the electoral votes to send him back to the White House and cannot wait to work alongside him to Make America Great Again. Americans fought to win back their nation and we did it!\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 A dispatch from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/helen-davidson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Helen Davidson}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/chi-hui-lin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chi-hui Lin}}}\uc2  in Taipei:\par \par \uc2 The US election is being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/china-us-trade-harris-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 closely watched in China as well}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The country\u8217\'20\'19s relationship with the US has been swinging between competitive and hostile in recent years. China and the US were locked in a trade war during the last Trump administration, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  maintained many of the policies and sanctions put in place during that time. The continued support of Taiwan \u8211\'20\'13 which China\u8217\'20\'19s ruling Communist party has vowed to annex \u8211\'20\'13 is the primary point of friction, at least from Beijing\u8217\'20\'19s perspective.\par \par \uc2 On social media platform, Weibo, the US election is at least three of the top 10 trending topics. State media coverage of the election has so far been largely informational, with no push for one candidate over another. The Global Times, an English-language nationalistic tabloid, has a prominently placed article about fears of election-related violence.\par \par \uc2 Xinhua\uc2 , the official state media outlet, has gone through eight election issues that \u8220\'20\'1Creveal the truth about American democracy\u8221\'20\'1D, including inflation, healthcare, crime, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, and housing affordability. It also listed immigration, which it said had become a heated issue because of \u8220\'20\'1Ca shifting economic landscape that has scapegoated newcomers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The US representatives in China also welcomed Chinese people to look to their election as an example of a different governance system. The embassy in Beijing has invited people to join them at a viewing event for \u8220\'20\'1Can exciting Wednesday morning as we watch the election unfold live and witness democracy in action\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Across the Taiwan strait, the US representatives at the American Institute of Taiwan (a de facto embassy) did not hold any watch events this year. Local polling taken just a few days ago revealed overwhelming support for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  among Taiwanese people. Taiwan \u8211\'20\'13 along with Hong Kong \u8211\'20\'13 had previously been one of Asia\u8217\'20\'19s biggest pockets of Trump supporters, but it seems the tide has turned. Comments from Trump in recent months that falsely accused Taiwan of stealing US semiconductors, and separately, that Taiwan should {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jul/17/donald-trump-taiwan-pay-us-defence-china-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pay protection money to the US}}}\uc2 , didn\u8217\'20\'19t go down well.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 A prolonged, almighty roar went up at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election watch party when Fox News called Pennsylvania for him at 1.20am.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s over!\u8221\'20\'1D screamed one man amid the noise at what felt like the point of no return. A young man in a black Maga hat shouted: \u8220\'20\'1CFuck \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ! Fuck her!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The euphoric crowd chanted: \u8220\'20\'1CUSA! USA!\u8221\'20\'1D They are now gathered near the stage waiting for Trump to enter and deliver a speech. Near the front is Blake Marnell, who wears a suit styled after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s wall.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 US senator Bob Casey, a Pennsylvania incumbent Democrat in a close race with Republican \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2 , isn\u8217\'20\'19t conceding his race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have confidence in our path to victory and we are going to make sure we count every vote,\u8221\'20\'1D said Maddy McDaniel, a campaign spokesperson.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democratic officials at the party\u8217\'20\'19s Arizona election watch party kept telling supporters to wait for more results.\par \par \uc2 The ballot so far held mixed signals for the party: \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was trailing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  narrowly, while \uc2 US Senate\uc2  candidate \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  was up by several points over Republican Kari Lake, and an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access measure held a strong lead.\par \par \uc2 Gallego grew emotional as he thanked his family and recounted his upbringing as a poor kid whose single mom raised him and his sisters. He gave a shoutout to his old boss, who was in attendance, from when he used to sell hot dogs. He mentioned his fellow Marines, some of whom were there to cheer him on.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGrowing up the way I did, the son of immigrants, I would have never thought I\u8217\'20\'19d make it this far,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. When every vote in counted, he believed, \u8220\'20\'1Ca poor Latino boy who slept on the floor will be headed to the floor of the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2 , the first Latino senator in Arizona history.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The crowd was on edge as they refreshed electoral maps and saw results come in on the big screen from around the country, but they hoped Harris could still pull off a win.\par \par \uc2 Denise Dewberry, a 55-year-old Phoenix resident, said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cnauseously optimistic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She voted for the first time in 2020 and has dedicated herself to Democratic causes, doing all she could to turn out voters this year: \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t not feel optimistic. I feel so invested in what is right that I don\u8217\'20\'19t know how to not be optimistic right now. At the same time, I know what I\u8217\'20\'19m up against.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And no matter the outcome, she would get to work to keep pushing for the Democrats. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is how it starts, not how it ends.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris surrogate \uc2 Mark Cuban\uc2  congratulates Trump\par \par \uc2 Billionaire \uc2 Mark Cuban\uc2 , who acted as a surrogate for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in the final weeks of her campaign, has tweeted congratulations at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , a fellow billionaire who backed his bid to return to the White House:\par \par \uc2 enltrCongrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2 . You won fair and square.\par \par \uc2 Congrats to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @elonmusk}}}\uc2  as well. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Godspeed?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Godspeed}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Mark Cuban\uc2  (@mcuban) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mcuban/status/1854046994345382034?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has not yet called the election for Trump, but the former president has won two of the seven crucial swing states expected to determine the winner.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nebraska upholds its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Nebraska has voted to uphold its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which outlaws the procedure after 12 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Voters in Nebraska chose between two competing measures \u8211\'20\'13 one enshrining the existing 12-week ban, and another that would have amended the state constitution to protect the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until viability, or about 24 weeks.\par \par \uc2 The more restrictive measure appears to have won with just over 50% of the vote. It was only the second loss of the night for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters. An initiative to restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights fell short in Florida, but measures succeeded in four other states. Four others have yet to be called.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 California passes tough-on-crime ballot measure\par \par \uc2 California voters voted passed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/kamala-harris-proposition-36-drug-theft-crimes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Proposition 36}}}\uc2 , a tough-on-crime ballot initiative that will enact harsher penalties for retail theft, property crimes and drug offenses.\par \par \uc2 The new measure will undo parts of a landmark 2014 law that downgraded several non-violent felonies to misdemeanors as a way to reduce the state\u8217\'20\'19s prison population and redirect money to drug treatment and resources for crime victims.\par \par \uc2 While some considered the original law, known as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2014/nov/28/proposition-47-california-drug-crime"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Proposition 47}}}\uc2 , a breakthrough in criminal justice reform, for others, it was viewed as a major driver of property crime, homelessness and substance abuse.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nevada senator \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  took the stage at the Democratic watch party in Las Vegas and reminded voters that she won her re-election by 7,928 votes in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd 4,000 of those votes were ones we cured,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CListen, we feel confident that when all the votes are counted tonight and this week, however long it takes to cure and count every single vote, we will win the Silver State for Democrats up and down the ballot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans have already flipped enough seats to control the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , though in Nevada, Democrat \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2  is fighting to keep her seat and facing Republican challenger Sam Brown. Even if \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  narrowly wins here, it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear whether Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s six electoral votes would give her enough of a boost as the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s path to victory narrows.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris wins New Hampshire\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has won New Hampshire, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 She picks up four electoral votes in the state that\u8217\'20\'19s known for holding the first primaries in the presidential nomination process \u8211\'20\'13 which \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  swept earlier this year, paving the way for him to challenge the vice-president in the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 In Las Vegas, Leo Murrieta, director of Make the Road Nevada, a progressive group that has focused on turning out Latino voters and voters of color, said he was feeling \u8220\'20\'1Ca little anxious\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe did everything we could this election,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe talked to over 770,000 plus voters. We launched 475 canvassers just today. We really did everything that we possibly could to make an impact in this election, and now we just have to wait and see.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Latinos in Nevada, who make up one in five voters here, will likely play a decisive role. Polling from Make the Road suggests that economic issues and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights were the top issues for the Latino community. Murrieta said he was also closely watching Latino turnout in Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Maricopa county and other key swing districts in the west.\par \par \uc2 Polls have closed in Nevada, but snaking lines of voters were still waiting to cast their ballots at several locations across the state. Results here will only be reported once every polling place has confirmed that every voter in line has had a chance to vote. It could be days before the results are clear.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know we left no stone unturned. We persuaded hundreds and hundreds of non-partisan Brown folks to vote, and to vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , to vote for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Murrieta said. His plan for the rest of the night was to be with Make the Road members and celebrate their hard work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause regardless of the outcomes, the only thing that we can rely on is each other,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t rely on political parties to save us. Politicians won\u8217\'20\'19t save us. But our community is going to have our back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory in Georgia further expands his options for winning the White House \u8211\'20\'13 and narrow s Harris\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 Trump just needs to win Pennsylvania or Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 two states where he is currently leading in the vote count \u8211\'20\'13 to win the 270 electoral votes needed to become president.\par \par \uc2 Harris can still win, but will need to sweep the three \u8220\'20\'1Cblue wall\u8221\'20\'1D states (which aren\u8217\'20\'19t looking so blue tonight) of Michigan, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin. She could stand to lose in Wisconsin, but only if she wins Arizona.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 As Trump wins Georgia, what has happened on election night so far\par \par \uc2 As the clock ticks past 1am Eastern Time in the US on the day after the 2024 presidential election, here is where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won the swing states of Georgia and North Carolina, the only two of the seven swing state called in the race so far. Trump has 246 of 270 electoral college votes needed to win, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has 210 electoral college votes. The vice-president now cannot win the election without winning the state of Pennsylvania, in which Trump holds a lead, with 90% of the vote counted.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alaska closed its polls, ending most voting in the US presidential election. The red state was the last where voting was ongoing statewide, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to claim its three electoral votes. Voters may still be casting ballots in some counties elsewhere that saw long lines, or where courts ordered polls to be open later.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign announced that she would not be speaking on Tuesday night. Her campaign co-chair \uc2 Cedric Richmond\uc2  addressed the crowd assembled for the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s election night party, and said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe still have votes to count. We still have states that have not been called yet. We will continue, overnight, to fight to make sure that every vote is counted, that every voice has spoken. So you won\u8217\'20\'19t hear from the vice-president tonight, but you will hear from her tomorrow.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The vice-president has won the following states so far: Virginia, Hawaii, New Mexico, California, Oregon, Washington, Colorado, Connecticut, Delaware, Illinois, Massachusetts, Maryland, New Jersey, New York, Rhode Island, Vermont, Washington DC and Maine\u8217\'20\'19s first congressional district.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trumphas won the following states so far: North Carolina, Georgia, Alabama, Arkansas, Florida, Indiana, Kentucky, Louisiana, Missouri, Mississippi, Montana, North Dakota, Ohio, Oklahoma, South Carolina, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, West Virginia, Wyoming, Kansas, Idaho, Iowa and the third congressional district in Nebraska.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump won in Iowa despite the state\u8217\'20\'19s foremost pollster Ann Selzer on Saturday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/harris-unexpected-lead-over-trump-iowa-selzer-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 finding Harris leading by a small amount}}}\uc2  that was nonetheless within the survey\u8217\'20\'19s margin of error. The finding was viewed as a potential sign of strength for Harris in nearby Wisconsin and Michigan, two swing states that are demographically similar to Iowa. The Trump campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/trump-harris-iowa-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decried}}}\uc2  Selzer\u8217\'20\'19s poll as an outlier, which turned out to be the case.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans have retaken the majority in the Senate, the Associated Press reported, after picking up seats in Ohio and West Virginia, and fending off challenges to their candidates in Texas and Nebraska. Republicans will control Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber for the first time in four years.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Should \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  win, they will be in a position to confirm his supreme court justices, federal judges and appointees to cabinet posts. If Harris wins the White House, they can force hold up her appointees, or block them outright.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Missouri voters approved a ballot measure enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution, setting the state up to overturn its near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 a first in the US post-Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Colorado, New York and Maryland also passed measures to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, while in Florida, an effort to roll back a six-week ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/florida-abortion-ballot-ban-measure-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fell short}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US will have two Black women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-black-women-senate-maryland-delaware"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 serving as senators for the first time in American history}}}\uc2 , with the election of \uc2 Lisa Blunt Rochester\uc2  from Delaware and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/maryland-senate-seat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Angela Alsobrooks}}}\uc2  of Maryland.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/28/sarah-mcbride-trans-transgender-congress-run"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sarah McBride}}}\uc2 , a Delaware state senator, has made history as the first out transgender person elected to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US House of Representatives}}}\uc2 . McBride, 34, won {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/delaware"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Delaware\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  at-large House seat in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s general election against the Republican candidate John Whalen III, a former Delaware state police officer and businessman. The House seat, Delaware\u8217\'20\'19s only one, has been Democratic since 2010.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Voting in US presidential election ends as polls close in Alaska\par \par \uc2 Alaska just closed its polls, ending most voting in the US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The red state was the last where voting was ongoing statewide, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to claim its three electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 Voters may still be casting ballots in some counties elsewhere that saw long lines, or where courts ordered polls to be open later.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins Georgia\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won Georgia, the Associated Press reports, with the Republican reclaiming a state he lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  four years ago.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 With polls closed, campaign surrogates, union leaders and progressive campaigners are trickling into the Democratic watch party at the Aria hotel and casino on the Las Vegas Strip.\par \par \uc2 The mood inside is uneasy, so far. Crystal and Kiersten Madrid, twins who are 30 years old, had accompanied their friend Fabian Do\u241\'00\'F1ate, a Nevada state senator. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve just been drinking a lot of water, trying to stay hydrated,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kiersten.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it\u8217\'20\'19s good to be with loved ones and like-minded people tonight,\u8221\'20\'1D Crystal added.\par \par \uc2 Aneri Shah, 22, had canvassed in Nevada with Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, a political group focused on electing women who support \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a little nervous,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shah who had come to the event with her father, Gunjan Shah, who was wearing a \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8217\'20\'1924\u8221\'20\'1D t-shirt.\par \par \uc2 Both eyed the presidential results rolling in on the big screens. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know. Things do seem to have shifted since 2020,\u8221\'20\'1D said Aneri. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I do feel positive about Nevada.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With its six electoral votes, the state could be a decider in the election \u8211\'20\'13 especially as Harris\u8217\'20\'19s path to victory narrows.\par \par \uc2 A massive billboard just outside is showing live updates from the betting market \uc2 Kalshi\uc2 , where the presidential race is trading 83% for Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump set to soon speak from election watch party\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to speak shortly at the campaign watch party in West Palm Beach, Florida, per a person familiar, as his \u8220\'20\'1CYMCA\u8221\'20\'1D walkout song comes on and Secret Service clears the lobby area.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s aides suggest tonight ahead of his appearance that they think they could sweep all the battleground states.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris will not make speech tonight\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign co-chair \uc2 Cedric Richmond\uc2  just addressed the crowd assembled for the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s election night party, and said that she will not be speaking tonight.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe still have votes to count. We still have states that have not been called yet. We will continue, overnight, to fight to make sure that every vote is counted, that every voice has spoken. So you won\u8217\'20\'19t hear from the vice president tonight, but you will hear from her tomorrow,\u8221\'20\'1D Richmond said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election-watch party at \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , aides are yelling at camera crews to cut their lights and flip their monitors. Law enforcement officers are assembling.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s unclear what is happening but it appears someone will address the crowd, many of whom are leaving.\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s Freedom just started up, but was cut after a few chords.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 Not enough ballots left in Georgia for Harris to win \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Georgia election official \uc2 Gabriel Sterling\uc2  has told CNN that there are not enough uncounted ballots left in the state for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to overtake \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: Georgia election official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GabrielSterling?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @GabrielSterling}}}\uc2  just told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PamelaBrownCNN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PamelaBrownCNN}}}\uc2  that there are about 100,000 ballots outstanding in Georgia, where Trump is currently up by ~118,000 with 93% of the vote in.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kayla Tausche (@kaylatausche) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaylatausche/status/1854034350448210125?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Both CNN and NBC have projected that Trump has won the state, which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  carried four years ago, but the Associated Press has yet to report the winner.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  relies on the Associated Press to determine the outcomes of elections across the United States. The New York-based global news agency has a presence in every US state and a long and authoritative history of determining the winners of elections at the presidential, congressional and state level. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/ap-race-calls-faq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here is more information}}}\uc2  about their process.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 House Democrats are gaining a seat in Louisiana after Cleo Fields was projected to defeat four opponents outright to complete a congressional comeback.\par \par \uc2 Fields \u8211\'20\'13 who was a member of the US House from 1993 to 1997 \u8211\'20\'13 beat four fellow Democrats and a single Republican in a contest held under the rules of Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s open primary system by capturing 51% of the 296,011 votes cast in the race, according to election results from the state.\par \par \uc2 He ran in Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s sixth district, whose constituency changed as the state was ordered to redraw its congressional map to account for population shifts in the 2020 census. It became Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s second majority Black congressional district, encompassing parts of Shreveport, Alexandria, Lafayette and Baton Rouge.\par \par \uc2 The only other majority Black congressional district in Louisiana \u8211\'20\'13 largely based in New Orleans \u8211\'20\'13 re-elected a Democrat on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 How pivotal Fields\u8217\'20\'19s victory will be in Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to retake control of the House \u8211\'20\'13 which Republicans have held since 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 remains to be seen. The redrawn sixth district had long been seen as an opportunity for Democrats to add another of its members to the House, meaning Republicans had anticipated Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s outcome as they weighed their chances of keeping the chamber.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, on Monday, the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/supreme-court-louisiana-congressional-districts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicated}}}\uc2  it would essentially review the redrawing of Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s sixth district after a lawsuit from a group of self-described non-Black Americans challenged the constitutionality of Louisiana\u8217\'20\'19s congressional map. The map as it stands all but guarantees easy re-election paths for House speaker Mike Johnson and majority leader Steve Scalise, who are both Republicans, as long as they want them.\par \par \uc2 The seat clinched by the 61-year-old Fields, who is Black and a longtime Louisiana state lawmaker, is being vacated by Republican congressman \uc2 Garret Graves\uc2 . Graves decided against seeking re-election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats who had gathered in Milwaukee to watch the election results come in are facing a nail-bitingly close race between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m feeling super nervous \u8211\'20\'13 anxious,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sandy Solo, a truck driver who said she felt \u8220\'20\'1Cstoked\u8221\'20\'1D earlier in the day.\par \par \uc2 Erv Seheibengraber, a retired teacher, said he was feeling \u8220\'20\'1Ccautious\u8221\'20\'1D and told me he worried about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe far right, and the possibility my daughters and grandkids won\u8217\'20\'19t have the same rights as I do\u8221\'20\'1D if Trump serves another term in office.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Votes are still being counted in Pennsylvania, but there\u8217\'20\'19s yet another ominous sign for the Harris campaign. Democrats had hoped to improve on their performance in Luzerne county in northeast Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the county by nearly 20 points in 2016. In 2020, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  cut significantly into that margin and lost it by 14 points. Democrats had hoped to continue to improve on their performance this year.\par \par \uc2 But with an estimated more than 95% of the vote in, Trump is winning the county by 22 points. The county is home to the city of Hazleton, where nearly two-thirds of residents are Hispanic or Latino.\par \par \uc2 Taken together with Democratic drops compared to 2020 in Lackawanna and Northampton counties, there are clear signs Harris\u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning Pennsylvania may be slipping away.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 One key county that experts are watching in Pennsylvania is Northampton county in the Lehigh valley.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won the county in 2016 when he won Pennsylvania. In 2020, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  narrowly flipped it when he flipped the state. Tonight, with more than 90% of the vote in, Trump is leading in the county by more than 5 points.\par \par \uc2 This doesn\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily mean Harris is going to lose Pennsylvania. There\u8217\'20\'19s still a lot of votes to be counted in Philadelphia and its surrounding counties \u8211\'20\'13 the bastion of Democratic votes in the state. Those votes could make up for margins Harris has lost elsewhere in the state.\par \par \uc2 But Harris\u8217\'20\'19 performance here, combined with a decrease in her performance in Scranton\u8217\'20\'19s Lackawanna county, are not the direction Democrats had hoped to see tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris wins electoral vote in Nebraska\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has won the electoral vote in Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s second congressional district, the Associated Press reports, a potentially crucial victory for her path to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The district encompasses Omaha, and has grown increasingly Democratic in recent years. Its vote, coupled with victories in Wisconsin, Michigan and Pennsylvania and in the states that typically vote Democratic, but no other swing states, would give Harris 270 votes, precisely enough to win the White House.\par \par \uc2 Of the seven swing states, only North Carolina has been called for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , so there\u8217\'20\'19s no telling if that scenario will play out.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 In addition to picking up seats in West Virginia and Ohio, Republicans won control of the Senate through the re-election of incumbent \uc2 Deb Fischer\uc2  in Nebraska.\par \par \uc2 She faced independent Dan Osborn who put up a tougher-than-expected challenge in a state that is otherwise a GOP stronghold. But Fischer prevailed, and the Associated Press called the race for her about 10 minutes ago.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 At a watch party hosted by the Milwaukee County Republican party at an Italian restaurant in the suburbs, Dimitra Anderson, 64, and her pet boa constrictor Tarzan, watched excitedly as the early results came in.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m ecstatic,\u8221\'20\'1D said Anderson, who describes herself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cborn-again believer\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and cites her faith as her most powerful political guide. Anderson has been following numerous self-styled prophets online since 2020, when the Covid-19 pandemic jarred the world and kept her home from church. Anderson believes confidently \u8211\'20\'13 as some religious figures on the Christian far-right have prophesied \u8211\'20\'13 that Trump will win the election.\par \par \uc2 Javier Ramos, a 20-year-old first time voter in attendance at the watch party, wasn\u8217\'20\'19t so confident.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m really anxious,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramos told me. He worried that undecided voters would prefer \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and said he felt Trump had been unfairly maligned in the media. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re bashing president Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 How Trump and Harris have fared in the election so far\par \par \uc2 Here are the states where the presidential election has been called as of 12am ET:\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has won Virginia and Hawaii after previously picking up New Mexico, California, Oregon, Washington, Colorado, Connecticut, Delaware, Illinois, Massachusetts, Maryland, New Jersey, New York, Rhode Island, Vermont, Washington DC and Maine\u8217\'20\'19s first congressional district.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won Alabama, Arkansas, Florida, Indiana, Kentucky, Louisiana, Missouri, Mississippi, Montana, North Dakota, Ohio, Oklahoma, South Carolina, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, West Virginia, Wyoming, Kansas, Idaho, Iowa and the third congressional district in Nebraska.\par \par \uc2 The mood at Harris\u8217\'20\'19s watch party at \uc2 Howard University\uc2  in Washington DC has shifted throughout the night. After being jubilant earlier, the crowd is quiet. The TV is tuned to CNN, which shows Trump appearing to be in a strong position to reclaim the White House. Some people appeared to be leaving, as it remains uncertain when or whether Harris will address the crowd at Howard tonight. When CNN predicted that Trump would win North Carolina, one of the seven battleground states that Harris is contesting, there were hardly any boos, just a wave of sighs. After the North Carolina call, the TVs were muted, and the DJ started back up\u8211\'20\'13 2Pac\u8217\'20\'19s California Love. But no one seems to be in the mood for dancing \u8211\'20\'13 instead there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of stone-faced Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Trump aides, meanwhile, have expressed confidence about their chances, based on results so far, including a substantial win in a key Florida county that is considered a bellwether. Trump also won in Iowa, despite the state\u8217\'20\'19s foremost pollster Ann Selzer on Saturday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/harris-unexpected-lead-over-trump-iowa-selzer-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 finding Harris leading by a small amount}}}\uc2  that was nonetheless within the survey\u8217\'20\'19s margin of error.\par \par \uc2 The finding was viewed as a potential sign of strength for Harris in nearby Wisconsin and Michigan, two swing states that are demographically similar to Iowa. The Trump campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/trump-harris-iowa-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decried}}}\uc2  Selzer\u8217\'20\'19s poll as an outlier, which turned out to be the case.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans win majority in the Senate\par \par \uc2 The GOP has retaken the majority in the Senate, the Associated Press reports, after picking up seats in Ohio and West Virginia, and fending off challenges to their candidates in Texas and Nebraska.\par \par \uc2 Republicans will control Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber for the first time in four years. Should \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  win, they will be in a position to confirm his supreme court justices, federal judges and appointees to cabinet posts. If \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  wins the White House, they can force hold up her appointees, or block them outright.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s an air of nervousness creeping in at the Michigan Democratic watch party. There isn\u8217\'20\'19t quite the buoyancy there was earlier \u8211\'20\'13 although Harris supporters are remaining positive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m still very optimistic. I feel like we\u8217\'20\'19re still in the race. We\u8217\'20\'19re just waiting for the final numbers to come in so we can celebrate and do what we came here to do \u8211\'20\'13 and that was to win the presidency,\u8221\'20\'1D Henrietta Ivey said. \u8220\'20\'1CI still say that we still have a long way to go for the night, and those numbers can all tally up and come through like a wave.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This is Chelsea Dureseaux \u8217\'20\'19s first time voting in Michigan in 12 years \u8211\'20\'13 she just moved back to her home state after a spell living in Louisiana.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s an honor for me to come back home for this historical election and be able to cast my vote where it actually matters,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. Dureseaux said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cnervous, but also hopeful\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like the tortoise and the hare race, is how I feel about it, and I feel like she\u8217\'20\'19s gonna come out on top,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. Dureseaux said that a Harris win would have a special resonance: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you think about how far we\u8217\'20\'19ve come, and the rights that we have gained as women, and what the people in the past have fought for \u8211\'20\'13 this is that moment right here. So it\u8217\'20\'19s a pivotal moment, and I\u8217\'20\'19m praying that we actually get to write it down in the history books.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the night, the crowd erupted in cheers as the TVs at Harris HQ flipped from CNN\u8217\'20\'19s analysis to hear Angela Alsobrooks give her victory speech.\par \par \uc2 Alsobrooks will be the first Black woman to represent Maryland in the Senate, after defeating the Republican former governor, \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 . Many in the crowd live in Maryland, which neighbors Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Alsobrooks noted that in the nation\u8217\'20\'19s nearly 250-year history, \u8220\'20\'1Conly three have looked like me\u8221\'20\'1D, she said. Until tonight, only three Black women had served in the Senate, including \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to salute all of those who came before me,\u8221\'20\'1D Alsobrooks said as the crowd in Washington DC cheered. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to be celebrating this one for a moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris wins Hawaii\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has won Hawaii, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s victory was expected, and she picks up four electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m at the Arizona Democratic Party\u8217\'20\'19s election night party at a Phoenix hotel, where the crowd of liberal party faithfuls cheered as NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Steve Kornacki showed results from around the country, broadcasted on two big screens at the front of the room.\par \par \uc2 When the first drop of results from Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Maricopa county, a swing county, showed Harris with a slight edge, Democrats roared and cheered \u8211\'20\'13 but it\u8217\'20\'19s clear to all that there\u8217\'20\'19s likely a long road ahead until races are called.\par \par \uc2 enltrDemocratic US Sen \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2  and former US Rep \uc2 Gabby Giffords\uc2  say they\u8217\'20\'19re optimistic for Dems tonight but it\u8217\'20\'19ll be a while for results. Kelly stressed accuracy over speed, with Giffords adding \u8220\'20\'1Cpatience, patience, patience\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vguy65xA1P"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vguy65xA1P}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rachel Leingang (@rachelleingang) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rachelleingang/status/1853991999084634622?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Democratic US Senator \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2  and former US Representative \uc2 Gabby Giffords\uc2 , his wife, said before results dropped that they\u8217\'20\'19re optimistic for Democrats tonight, but it\u8217\'20\'19ll be a while for results.\par \par \uc2 Kelly stressed accuracy over speed, with Giffords adding, \u8220\'20\'1CPatience, patience, patience.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Democratic governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  said she was optimistic about the state\u8217\'20\'19s eventual results, but added, \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to prepare for a really long evening, a really long couple of days, and make sure all these votes are counted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls close in Hawaii\par \par \uc2 Polls have just closed in Hawaii, one of the final two states that were still voting.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a Democratic stronghold, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is expected to win its four electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 The only other state where polls remain open statewide is Alaska. Voting finishes there at 1am eastern time.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 Another dispatch from Black voters in California:\par \par \uc2 Jasmyne Cannick, a Los Angeles-based political strategist who worked as a consultant on five local campaigns, started her election day with a political activation event alongside her close friend, Nana Gyamfi, an attorney who heads Black Alliance for Just Immigration, a legal advocacy group. Cannick says she\u8217\'20\'19s excited to hopefully see \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  win the presidency but worried about the potential for subsequent protests and violence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wanna make sure this country doesn\u8217\'20\'19t act like a fool. That worries me,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen Kamala wins I hope no one pulls out the pitchforks and come for us. We saw what happened on January 6 so we know what\u8217\'20\'19s possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSpent time with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Jasmyne?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Jasmyne}}}\uc2  as she did some election day outreach in Skid Row and throughout downtown {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZhyJ6N2oa3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZhyJ6N2oa3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aben\u233\'00\'E9 Clayton (@abene_writes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/abene_writes/status/1853999775428780237?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Cannick and Gyamfi joined actresses Meagan Good and Amber Riley for stops in downtown LA, where they spoke with canvassers, handed out voter information and took people to the polls.\par \par \uc2 The work, combined with avoiding the news, had Cannick feeling excited to begin an evening of election night event-hopping that she hopes will end in celebrations for the local races she has supported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose are important: your trash, your potholes, your parks, your schools. These are critical positions that affect us quickly,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf they vote down there to raise your water bill, that\u8217\'20\'19s going to happen immediately. Sometimes we get so distracted by the noise that we just pay attention to what happened in DC. But we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to walk and chew gum at the same time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 Scenes from election watch party at Harris's alma mater\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the night, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  supporters gathered at \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s alma mater, for what they hoped would be a historic night celebrating the first Black woman elected US president. The mood has shifted over the course of the evening, but here are some photos from our photographer on the scene:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 The mood has certainly shifted at the Harris HQ. The crowd is quiet. The TV is tuned to CNN as Trump appears to be in a strong position to reclaim the White House.\par \par \uc2 Many supporters are refreshing their phones. One woman in my view is chewing her nails. A few groups appear to be leaving, as it remains uncertain when or whether Harris will address the crowd at Howard tonight.\par \par \uc2 At 11.40pm, CNN predicted that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would win North Carolina, one of the seven battleground states that Harris had contested. There were hardly any boos. Just a wave of sighs.\par \par \uc2 After the North Carolina call, the TVs were muted, and the DJ started back up, playing 2Pac\u8217\'20\'19s California Love. But no one seems to be in the mood for dancing. Instead there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of stone-faced Democrats.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris wins Virginia\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has won Virginia and its 13 electoral votes, the Associated Press Reports.\par \par \uc2 Virginia is another state that has trended blue lately, but nonetheless received a visit from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  last week \u8211\'20\'13 fruitlessly, as it turned out.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 Cruz re-elected in Texas, lowering Democrats' odds of keeping Senate\par \par \uc2 Republican Ted Cruz has been re-elected to the Senate in Texas, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The party was hoping that a victory by congressman \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2  against the incumbent, who gained notoriety for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/28/ted-cruz-cancun-airport-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vacationing in Canc\u250\'00\'FAn}}}\uc2  as a deadly cold spell struck the state, could help them keep their 51- seat majority. But Texas is a reliably Republican state, and voters there have given Cruz another six years in the office.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s another blow to Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 hopes of keeping the majority, after losing seats in West Virginia and Ohio earlier this evening.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Missouri passes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights ballot measure\par \par \uc2 Missouri voters approved a ballot measure enshrining \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution, setting the state up to overturn its near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 a first in the US post-Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 The measure protects the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up until fetal viability, or about 24 weeks of pregnancy. Its success in a ruby-red state is a stunning repudiation of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2022 overturning of Roe as well as a signal of just how powerful the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has become in US politics.\par \par \uc2 The passage of the Missouri measure does not, however, automatically overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s ban. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters must first pursue litigation or legislation to officially strike down restrictions.\par \par \uc2 A total of 10 states are voting on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot measures on Tuesday. Maryland, Colorado, and New York have all passed measures to expand protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights while Florida\u8217\'20\'19s measure fell short of the 60% it needed to pass. That failure left the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in place.\par \par \uc2 Three other states still have the chance to vote to overturn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Results are forthcoming.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris wins New Mexico\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has won New Mexico, the Associated Press reports, dashing the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  campaign\u8217\'20\'19s hopes of a surprise victory in the south-western state.\par \par \uc2 New Mexico has typically voted Democratic in recent elections, but Trump campaigned there last week, hoping to flip it to his side. He was not successful, and Harris has won its five electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 Former Trump White House strategist \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  tells me: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some Trump allies have started to filter into the Palm Beach convention center where the campaign watch party is taking place, which may be an indication that Trump may appear tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 GOP flips Senate seat in Ohio, imperiling Democratic majority\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Bernie Moreno\uc2  has defeated Democratic senator \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  in Ohio, the Associated Press reports, likely giving the GOP the majority in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 It is the second seat Democrats have lost tonight, after Republican \uc2 Jim Justice\uc2  won the seat held by retiring independent \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2  in West Virginia. Democrats will need surprise victories in Montana and Texas and a victory by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to keep control of Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris wins Oregon\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has won Oregon, the Associated Press reports, completing a sweep of the west coast\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic strongholds.\par \par \uc2 She picks up eight electoral votes from the state in a victory that was expected, given its strong Democratic tilt.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory in North Carolina is the latest instance of Democrats falling short in a state that always winds up being just out of reach.\par \par \uc2 No Democrat has won its electoral votes since \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in 2008, but \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign believed they might have a chance this year. Had they succeeded, it would have padded her margins, though she still would have had to capture several other swing states like Pennsylvania, Arizona or Georgia to take the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins North Carolina\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won North Carolina, the Associated Press reports, picking up his first of the seven swing states expected to decide the election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 Ohio voters have rejected a ballot measure that would have stripped lawmakers of their ability to draw electoral districts, a major blow to curb the practice of extreme partisan gerrymandering, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://decisiondeskhq.com/results/2024/General/races/ohio-issue-1-all-parties-ballot-question"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Decision Desk HQ is projecting}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The panel would have given redistricting power to a panel of 15 citizens \u8211\'20\'13 Democrats, Republicans, and independents to draw district lines. Citizens placed it on the ballot after the Ohio supreme court struck down maps drawn by Republicans seven times. Republicans implemented their maps anyway after control of the court changed.\par \par \uc2 Republicans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/ohio-anti-gerrymandering-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 successfully distorted}}}\uc2  the ballot language to make it confusing. They were able to approve language that said the measure would have required the panel to gerrymander districts. In reality, the measure would have outlawed gerrymandering. The news site Bolts reported that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://boltsmag.org/ohio-issue-1-gerrrymandering-misleading-language/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio voters}}}\uc2  were confused about the measure.\par \par \uc2 The defeat is a major win for Republicans, who control the Ohio state house and have a majority in the state\u8217\'20\'19s congressional delegation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COhio voters spoke loudly and clearly on Issue 1. Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s constitution is not for sale to foreign billionaires and out of state leftwing special interest groups,\u8221\'20\'1D Bob Paduchik, senior adviser to Ohio Works, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDespite Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 best efforts to deceive Ohioans into changing our constitution and rigging elections in their favor, the truth has carried the day. We are grateful to our elected Republican leaders, the Ohio Republican party, the Ohio Chamber of Commerce, Ohio Manufacturers Association and many others that took a stand to protect representational democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 Californians send Democrat Adam Schiff to the Senate\par \par \uc2 Democratic congressman Adam Schiff will be California\u8217\'20\'19s next senator, taking the seat occupied for more than 30 years by \uc2 Dianne Feinstein\uc2 , who died last year.\par \par \uc2 Schiff, a major antagonist of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and a leader of his first impeachment, takes over from Laphonza Butler, who was appointed to the seat after Feinstein\u8217\'20\'19s death, but did not stand for a full term. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about Schiff:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/adam-schiff-wins-california-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California Democrat Adam Schiff wins Dianne Feinstein\u8217\'20\'19s former Senate seat}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Colorado adopts \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights ballot measure\par \par \uc2 Colorado has passed a ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 The measure, which needed to secure 55% of the vote to pass, blocks Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s state government from denying, impeding or discriminating against individuals\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Cright to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 There is currently no gestational limit on the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in deep-blue Colorado, which has become a sanctuary for people fleeing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 A total of 10 states are also voting on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot measures on Tuesday. Maryland and New York passed measures to expand protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights while Florida\u8217\'20\'19s measure fell short of the 60% supermajority it needed to pass. Had it succeeded, the Florida initiative would have paved the way for the state to overturn its six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Four other states still have the chance to vote to overturn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. Results are forthcoming.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris wins California and Washington; Trump carries Idaho\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has won her home state of California, as well as Washington state, while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has picked up Idaho, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The two states give Harris a combined 66 electoral votes, while Idaho gives Trump four electoral votes. Oregon, the other state where polls just closed, has not yet been called.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls close in California, Oregon, Washington, Idaho\par \par \uc2 Polls have just closed in four west coast states that should give \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  a slew of electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 The most-populous state California, along with Oregon and Washington, are all reliably Democratic, and expected to be easy pick ups for the vice-president. Idaho, by contrast, is strongly Republican, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is almost certain to win its electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 I spent the day with three different Black women in Los Angeles to see how they were spending an unprecedented election day for their demographic.\par \par \uc2 The first was Kathy Evans, an LA native, who started her day with her late mother on her mind and a trove of text messages from family and friends asking for her thoughts on ballots. Evans, a longtime community activist, says that she is honored that people think highly enough of her to ask for her insights and only wishes that her mother, who died in 2000, was alive to see \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  won.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m honored, I don\u8217\'20\'19t take it lightly,\u8221\'20\'1D she said of the role she plays in her community. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t even know how I ended up with the job and it\u8217\'20\'19s important and I\u8217\'20\'19m so honored that people would trust me to be the voice of reason and the truth.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris picks up electoral vote in Maine\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has won one of Maine\u8217\'20\'19s four electoral votes, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The state is one of two, along with Nebraska, to allocate its votes by congressional district. Harris won the first congressional district, but its three other votes \u8211\'20\'13 one given to the winner of its second congressional district, and two for the winner statewide \u8211\'20\'13 have not yet been called.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 The mood at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s watch party in Florida is fairly upbeat and expectant right now.\par \par \uc2 The giant TV screens switched from Fox News to CNN, which ran through some states where Trump is leading: Georgia, North Carolina, Virginia. Each was greeted by a big cheer from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 Every now and then some young Trump supporters break into chants such as: \u8220\'20\'1CRe-elect Trump! Re-elect Trump!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A huge \u8220\'20\'1CTrump will fix it!\u8221\'20\'1D poster hangs on a far wall. Guests are helping themselves to a buffet of wine and cheese and other snacks. Thankfully, coffee is also on sale.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s early and votes are still being counted in Pennsylvania, but ominous signs have emerged for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in a key county.\par \par \uc2 Lackawanna county, home to Scranton, has reported nearly all of its votes and has Harris leading \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by three percentage points. That\u8217\'20\'19s a drop from 2020, when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  carried the county where he was born by eight points. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  won the county by three points in 2016 when she lost Pennsylvania. \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  carried it by nearly 28 points in 2012.\par \par \uc2 Harris could improve on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s margins elsewhere in the state to offset the loss in the margin here. And Trump could still slip in his performance from 2020 elsewhere. But Democrats had been hoping to build on their margin here and it was one of the key counties in the state Democrats were watching as a signal of how Harris would perform in the state and in the rust belt.\par \par \uc2 Harris campaigned in Scranton yesterday and Biden had a muted visit to the city over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins Iowa, Kansas\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won the midwestern states of Iowa and Kansas, the Associated Press reports, picking up a combined 12 electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 His victory in Kansas was expected, as was Iowa \u8211\'20\'13 until Saturday, when the state\u8217\'20\'19s foremost pollster Ann Selzer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/harris-unexpected-lead-over-trump-iowa-selzer-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found Harris leading by a small amount}}}\uc2  that was within the survey\u8217\'20\'19s margin of error. It was a surprising finding, given that the state has grown markedly Republican in recent elections, after \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  won it twice.\par \par \uc2 The finding was viewed as a potential sign of strength for Harris in nearby Wisconsin and Michigan, two swing states that are demographically similar to Iowa. The Trump campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/trump-harris-iowa-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decried}}}\uc2  Selzer\u8217\'20\'19s poll as an outlier, and that turned out to be the case.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , backer of Trump's election denialism, secures second term\par \par \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , the Missouri senator who was one of the most prominent voices in the chamber backing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s false claims of fraud in his 2020 election loss, has won re-election, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Hawley would raise his fist to the crowds that gathered outside the Capitol on January 6, only to later be seen running through the halls as they entered the building. He faced Democrat Lucas Kunce, who was not able to overcome the senator\u8217\'20\'19s appeal to voters in a state where the Republican party is strong.\par \par \uc2 Read more on Hawley here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/24/josh-hawley-republican-senator-ran-running-capitol-attack-kansas-city-star"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Josh Hawley, senator who ran from Capitol mob, mocked by home paper}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 Tarence Wheeler is among those eagerly awaiting Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s results at Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 election night party in Detroit.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s wearing a T-shirt which says: \u8220\'20\'1CVoting is my Black job\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a reference to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/KamalaHarris/videos/1164764194788225/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 frequent, but vague, claims}}}\uc2  about how he would provide Black-specific employment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is such an important election. Every election they keep saying: \u8216\'20\'18This is the most consequential election of your lifetime.\u8217\'20\'19 But this is. There\u8217\'20\'19s so much at stake in this election. We can\u8217\'20\'19t get it wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wheeler, an educator.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a momentum that\u8217\'20\'19s being built\u8221\'20\'1D - Tarence Wheeler at Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 election party in Detroit, Michigan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Q0mKzjAGDD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Q0mKzjAGDD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Adam Gabbatt (@adamgabbatt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/adamgabbatt/status/1853988631364436074?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The fact that Harris would be the first female president and the first Black woman president, adds to the historic air of the election, Wheeler said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a momentum that\u8217\'20\'19s being built. People are incentivized. They have the courage to stand in line for two hours, three hours, whatever it takes. You\u8217\'20\'19re voting for your ancestors. So for me, as a Black man, born and raised in the city of Detroit, I am immensely proud to have cast my vote,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m immensely proud that my daughters can see that. So in my lifespan, if she wins, I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen Obama and I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen Harris. That shows you that the country is making a turn. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is who America aspires to be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 Allyson DeFelice, 49, a property agent from Delray Beach, Florida, said it is \u8220\'20\'1Camazing\u8221\'20\'1D to be at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election watch party: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been waiting for this for four years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DeFelice predicted a Trump victory \u8220\'20\'1Chands down\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CSome of the main concerns for everybody over the last four years have been inflation, price of goods, gas, everything that\u8217\'20\'19s going on at the border. The Democrats destroyed what he built up in this country. Even during Covid he still managed to rebuild the economy afterwards and they just destroyed it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump infamously declared victory on election night in 2020 even as the result was slipping away from him, but DeFelice does not expect a repeat. \u8220\'20\'1CI respect that he\u8217\'20\'19s going to wait till the electoral college counts the exact votes and make sure he hits the 270 number before declaring victory.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although there is zero evidence that the 2020 election was stolen, DeFelice added: \u8220\'20\'1CThey rigged the last one but I do believe this time we have more attorneys in place beforehand able to bring any issues to the courts before they happen instead of after. That was the downfall, what happened in the 2020 election. But we\u8217\'20\'19re definitely more prepared on the ground this time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies have spent weeks talking up the accuracy of the betting market forecasts as the top platforms put the former president ahead.\par \par \uc2 After a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/presidential-election-betting-odds-polling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 significant narrowing}}}\uc2  at the weekend, Trump has rebuilt a clear lead over \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in recent hours in betting markets as the first results came in.\par \par \uc2 As of 8.54pm, Polymarket put Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chance of winning the presidential election at 75% over 26% for Harris; \uc2 Kalshi\uc2  has Trump on 70% and Harris on 30%; and PredictIt has Trump on 66% and Harris on 39%.\par \par \uc2 Betting markets, like opinion polls, have had mixed success in predicting the winner of recent presidential contests.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris wins Washington DC\par \par \uc2 Washington DC is not a state, but it has three electoral votes, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has won them, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 No Republican candidate has won the federal district\u8217\'20\'19s votes since the 23rd amendment to the constitution granted them in 1961. The victory is particularly sweet for Harris \u8211\'20\'13 she\u8217\'20\'19s an alumni of the city\u8217\'20\'19s historically Black Howard University, and her election night party is being held there.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , the US transportation secretary, is at the Michigan Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 election watch party now:\par \par \uc2 Michigan is the center of the political universe tonight \u8230\'20\'26 This isn\u8217\'20\'19t just about defending our rights and freedoms, it\u8217\'20\'19s about an opportunity to have politics get out of our face. I live and breathe politics and public policy \u8211\'20\'13 I can\u8217\'20\'19t wait for a chance to go into Thanksgiving dinner and maybe have politics be on the backburner just a little bit.\par \par \uc2 Buttigieg, a former mayor of South Bend, Indiana, moved to Michigan in 2022, and has been a high-profile figure in Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 He has regularly jousted with hosts on Fox News \u8211\'20\'13 as recently as this morning he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mediaite.com/news/is-this-an-interview-or-a-debate-pete-buttigieg-lashes-out-at-foxs-brian-kilmeade-after-barrage-of-interruptions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upsetting Brian Kilmeade}}}\uc2  on Fox and Friends \u8211\'20\'13 and recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YE1f3n_n9UA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debated 25 undecided voters}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 Presidential race calls so far - and how things are looking\par \par \uc2 Here are the states that have been called in the presidential race as of 11.08pm:\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  : California, Washington, Colorado, Connecticut, Delaware, Illinois, Massachusetts, Maryland, New Jersey, New York, Rhode Island, Vermont, Washington DC, Maine\u8217\'20\'19s second district.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  : Alabama, Arkansas, Florida, Indiana, Kentucky, Louisiana, Missouri, Mississippi, Montana, North Dakota, Ohio, Oklahoma, South Carolina, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, West Virginia, Wyoming, Kansas, Idaho and Iowa.\par \par \uc2 There haven\u8217\'20\'19t been any surprises in the presidential race so far. The swing states have all closed their polls, but none have been called yet. All eyes remain on the key battleground states \u8211\'20\'13 Arizona, Nevada, Georgia, North Carolina, Pennsylvania, Michigan and Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 where counting is ongoing.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory in Iowa had been expected \u8211\'20\'13 until Saturday, when the state\u8217\'20\'19s foremost pollster Ann Selzer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/harris-unexpected-lead-over-trump-iowa-selzer-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found Harris leading by a small amount}}}\uc2  that was within the survey\u8217\'20\'19s margin of error. The finding was viewed as a potential sign of strength for Harris in nearby Wisconsin and Michigan, two swing states that are demographically similar to Iowa. The Trump campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/trump-harris-iowa-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decried}}}\uc2  Selzer\u8217\'20\'19s poll as an outlier, and that turned out to be the case.\par \par \uc2 Trump aides have expressed confidence about their chances, based on some early results, including a substantial win in a key Florida county that is considered a bellwether. But it\u8217\'20\'19s far too soon to make a clear prediction about the final results. In previous presidential elections, pundits have described a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/harris-trump-election-results-when"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 red mirage}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D in reference to the phenomenon in which a GOP candidate appears ahead in the early evening, but loses the edge as more votes are counted.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Howard University\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s the Yard, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  supporters are dancing and cheering.\par \par \uc2 Doreen Hogans, 50, said she was feeling hopeful. She pulled a string of pearls from her pocket. The necklace belonged to her late mother. Hogans\u8217\'20\'19 eyes glistened: \u8220\'20\'1CShe would have been so proud.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Around her, students and supporters filled the Yard. They danced as the music pulsed. There were a mix of cheers and boos as CNN made a series of race calls. When CNN declared Harris the winner of Washington DC and Maryland, Chelsea Chambers clasped hands with Kelo Torres and cheered. The women wore sashes \u8211\'20\'13 Miss District of Columbia Teen USA and Miss District of Columbia USA, respectively.\par \par \uc2 enltrMiss District of Columbia(s) celebrating as CNN announces Harris won the presidential contest in DC and Maryland {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/slUDbo0X33"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/slUDbo0X33}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1853968476232175988?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Chambers, 19 and a sophomore at Howard, voted for the first time. \u8220\'20\'1CTo see a woman become president, I\u8217\'20\'19m like, I can do anything after that,\u8221\'20\'1D the aspiring sports journalist said.\par \par \uc2 Michele Fuller attended Howard at the same time as Harris \u8211\'20\'13 the future vice-president was a year ahead of her. \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels unbelievable,\u8221\'20\'1D Fuller said, as she walked into Harris\u8217\'20\'19s election night watch party at their alma mater. \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s just done so great. And she\u8217\'20\'19s more than qualified. I\u8217\'20\'19m just so excited.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked if she ever imagined Harris would one day be standing on the cusp of history, Fuller said: \u8220\'20\'1CNo \u8211\'20\'13 never. But once she became the vice-president, I knew it. I knew it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris wins Colorado\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has picked up Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s 10 electoral votes, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Though states such as Ohio and Florida have slipped away from Democrats in recent years, the party has built up its strength in Colorado, which used to be reliably Republican territory. But the GOP has not won Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s electoral votes since 2004, and won\u8217\'20\'19t this year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump aides bullish on his chances in Great Lakes swing states\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been milling around his Mar-a-Lago club tonight as the results come in, after earlier dropping in on some private dinners there.\par \par \uc2 The Trump team there has continued to be bullish on their chances. Some top advisers have told members within the last hour that they think the former president could win Pennsylvania and both of Wisconsin and Michigan, according to people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins Montana, Utah\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has won Montana and Utah, the Associated Press reports, picking up a combined 10 electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 Both results were expected. The big contest to watch of the pair is Montana Democrat \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s bid for re-election to the Senate against Republican Tim Sheehy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls close in swing state Nevada, Utah, Montana\par \par \uc2 Voting has finished in Nevada, one of the seven battleground states, as well as Utah and Montana.\par \par \uc2 All eyes will be on Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s Clark county, where Las Vegas sits, and Washoe county, home to the city of Reno. Those are the state\u8217\'20\'19s two main urban areas and turnout there will likely determine whether \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  wins the state, or if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  becomes the first Republican to triumph in Nevada in 20 years.\par \par \uc2 Utah is a solidly Republican state with no electoral surprises expected. Montana is also a red state, but there, Democratic senator \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  is running for another term against his Republican challenger Tim Sheehy. Should he lose, it\u8217\'20\'19s probably curtains for the Democratic Senate majority.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 Sarah McBride becomes first trans person elected to US House\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/28/sarah-mcbride-trans-transgender-congress-run"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sarah McBride}}}\uc2  , a Delaware state senator, has made history as the first openly transgender person elected to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/house-of-representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US House of Representatives}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank you, Delaware! Because of your votes and your values, I am proud to be your next member of Congress,\u8221\'20\'1D McBride {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SarahEMcBride/status/1853989947893862847"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  on X after the race was called.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDelaware has sent the message loud and clear that we must be a country that protects reproductive freedom, that guarantees paid leave and affordable child care for all our families, that ensures that housing and healthcare are available to everyone and that this is a democracy that is big enough for all of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McBride, 34, won {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/delaware"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Delaware}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s at-large House seat in the general election against Republican candidate John Whalen III, a former Delaware state police officer and businessman.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election, McBride spoke about what it would mean to be the first transgender person elected to Congress, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/sarah-mcbride-delaware-trans-woman-running-for-congress/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 telling}}}\uc2  CBS News: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a testament to Delawareans that the candidacy of someone like me is even possible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-sarah-mcbride-delaware-house"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sarah McBride becomes first openly trans person elected to US House}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 Several voters waiting in the snaking line to cast their ballots in Las Vegas\u8217\'20\'19 Spring Valley neighborhood were once conservatives, but are now voting with Democrats.\par \par \uc2 James, 23, who didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to give his surname because much of his family and his co-workers are staunch Republicans and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  supporters, said he was excited to cast a ballot for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of my family members are die hard conservatives. But I\u8217\'20\'19m a little bit hitting my rebellious phase right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He has been turned off by Project 2025 \u8211\'20\'13 the conservative blueprint for a second Trump term that outlines extreme policies: It\u8217\'20\'19s kind of freaky.\u8221\'20\'1D Harris seems more level-headed to him, and he likes that she is committed to protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 an important issue for him and his wife, who want children eventually but wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be able to financially support a child at the moment. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want us to be bringing someone into the world that we couldn\u8217\'20\'19t take care of,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 James said he was still reading up on some of the down ballot races \u8211\'20\'13 and was grateful he had at least an hour to read before reaching the front of the line. Sam Brown, the Republican candidate for the senate, had stopped by a few minutes back, and James said he enjoyed talking to him, but was still unconvinced. He\u8217\'20\'19s leaning toward the Democratic incumbent \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2 , who seems more moderate.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s been dismayed at how divided his community had become. \u8220\'20\'1CEven in 2020, it was divided but not like this. Bak then you could still have a civilized conversation\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is brutal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins Missouri\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the winner of Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s 10 electoral votes, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a red state and no surprises were expected there. Democrats had hoped their candidate Lucas Kunce would be able to oust Republican senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/10/capitol-attack-republican-senators-josh-hawley-ted-cruz-face-resign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a key supporter}}}\uc2  in the chamber of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baseless claims of election fraud four years ago.\par \par \uc2 But polls have shown Kunce trailing Hawley, and though the race has not yet been called, he is not expected to win.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has made congratulatory calls to a number of Democratic winners, the White House says.\par \par \uc2 The president has talked to \uc2 Lisa Blunt Rochester\uc2 , the first woman and Black senator to represent Delaware; New Jersey\u8217\'20\'19s senator-elect Andy Kim, the first Korean American to serve in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber; \uc2 John Carney\uc2 , who was elected mayor of Wilmington, Delaware; and \uc2 Josh Stein\uc2 , who was elected governor of North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 Advocates are celebrating the election of \uc2 Lisa Blunt Rochester\uc2 , who will be the first woman and first Black senator to represent Delaware in Congress.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic congresswoman will replace senator \uc2 Tom Carper\uc2  who is retiring.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Lisa Blunt Rochester\uc2  is a groundbreaking leader who has a proven track record of protecting our fundamental rights,\u8221\'20\'1D EMILYs List President Jessica Mackler said.\par \par \uc2 She will be joined in the chamber by another barrier-breaking Black female senator, Angela Alsobrooks of Maryland, who prevailed over the state\u8217\'20\'19s former Republican governor, \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 Maryland and New York pass \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights measures\par \par \uc2 New York and Maryland have both voted in support of ballot measures to amend their state constitutions to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, cementing their status as \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  havens.\par \par \uc2 The Maryland measure guarantees individuals\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Cright to reproductive freedom, including but not limited to the ability to make and effectuate decisions to prevent, continue, or end the individual\u8217\'20\'19s pregnancy\u8221\'20\'1D. There is currently no gestational limit on the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state, but the success of the measure promises to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights even in the event that anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Republicans take control of the state.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the New York measure expands the state\u8217\'20\'19s anti-discrimination laws by protecting against discrimination on the basis of \u8220\'20\'1Csex, including sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, pregnancy outcomes, and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. Although this language does not explicitly reference \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , advocates say its pregnancy-related language encompasses \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections. New York state already allows abortions until fetal viability.\par \par \uc2 Seven other states are also voting on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot measures. One of the measures \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/florida-abortion-ballot-ban-measure-amendment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Florida}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 has already failed, leaving the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in place. Four of the states with forthcoming results have the chance to overturn \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida rejects \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights measure as results in seven states still to come}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Many voters in line at the senior center in Las Vegas\u8217\'20\'19 diverse Spring Valley neighborhood were the sort of swing voters both parties have been desperate to win over this election cycle.\par \par \uc2 Some, like Kidani Perez, 32, had voted blue the past few elections. This year, he was voting for Donald Trump \u8211\'20\'13 in large part because he was disappointed by Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI grew up Democrat \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been a long term Democrat,\u8221\'20\'1D said Perez, who works in asphalt. But recently, he\u8217\'20\'19s been dismayed that Democratic leaders have been sending funds overseas to Ukraine rather than helping struggling communities in the US. \u8220\'20\'1CMy wife\u8217\'20\'19s from Hawaii and seeing Hawaii get almost no money after the fires there? And meanwhile they\u8217\'20\'19re sending millions to Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CNo that\u8217\'20\'19s our taxpayer money. And we\u8217\'20\'19re getting chump change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Maedot Apthayas, 38, agreed. The customer service representative, who voted for Biden in 2020, said she was looking forward to a Trump administration. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s going to get us out of wars,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd he\u8217\'20\'19s going to be good for the economy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Apthayas was also opposed to abortions, and appreciated Trump\u8217\'20\'19s commitment to restricting access: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s so close here, the election is very close, but I\u8217\'20\'19m praying. We\u8217\'20\'19ll see.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Fani Willis, Georgia DA prosecuting Donald Trump, is re-elected\par \par \uc2 Fani Willis, the Georgia prosecutor who charged Donald Trump over his efforts to overturn the 2020 election results, has been re-elected, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The Fulton county district attorney won her race against GOP challenger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-georgia-willis-mcafee-election-db0b3175ae1e824a5ec3d1eb17f0110a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Courtney Kramer}}}\uc2  , who had served as an intern in the White House counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office during the Trump administration. The county is home to 11% of the state\u8217\'20\'19s electorate and most of the city of Atlanta and is reliably Democratic, the AP reports.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers have tried to have Willis removed from the case, which is ongoing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 Marylanders elect Democrat Angela Alsobrooks to the Senate\par \par \uc2 Democrat Angela Alsobrooks will be Maryland\u8217\'20\'19s next senator, the Associated Press reports, with voters turning down an attempt by the popular Republican former governor Larry Hogan to win the seat.\par \par \uc2 Alsobrooks will be Maryland\u8217\'20\'19s first Black senator, and only the third Black woman to ever serve in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 Hogan was about the best candidate the GOP could hope to get in what is otherwise a strongly Democratic state. Had he won, it would have badly damaged Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 chances of keeping their Senate majority, or even regaining control in upcoming elections.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump has won one of Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s five electoral votes, the Associated Press reports, but four others have not yet been decided.\par \par \uc2 Nebraska and Maine are the only two states in the nation that dole out electoral votes by congressional district. The AP has called Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s third congressional district for Trump, and he\u8217\'20\'19s tipped to win four more in what is generally a red state.\par \par \uc2 But Nebraska\u8217\'20\'19s second congressional district, which encompasses the largest city Omaha and its suburbs, may elude him \u8211\'20\'13 and potentially send Kamala Harris to the White House. The district is viewed as Democratic leaning, and if the vice-president wins its single electoral vote along with those of Michigan, Wisconsin and Pennsylvania, it will be enough to make her president.\par \par \uc2 This post has been corrected to note that Nebraska has five electoral votes, not four.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump aides see reasons for hope in early results\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump \u8217\'20\'19s aides are expressing confidence in their chances based on some of the early results, saying they think Trump winning several key counties in Florida and Republicans defeating both \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot measures are good omens.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, Trump lost Miami-Dade county by seven points to Joe Biden. This year, Trump is currently ahead of Kamala Harris by 12 points \u8211\'20\'13 a notable turnaround that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s aides see as momentum in his favor.\par \par \uc2 When the Fox News analysis of the Miami-Dade result was played on the two massive screens here at the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s official watch party at the Palm Beach Convention Center, supporters looked up to clap and cheer over the commentary.\par \par \uc2 The atmosphere inside the convention center has been buzzing as it has started to fill up. Trump is not here himself. He is holding court at his Mar-a-Lago resort a few minutes away with a few hundred members, donors and family and friends.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters at the convention center are being well looked after. There is hot food catering, multiple snack stations with Hersheys and Snickers and marshmallow bars, as well as wine and beer on sale. Earlier in the night, staff were also handing out free Maga hats.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Alfred Vivar Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz, a political science student at the University of Nevada, Las Vegas, said he was most worried about what a Donald Trump presidency would mean for immigrants.\par \par \uc2 Vivar Mu\u241\'00\'F1oz moved to the US from Cuba as a child, and he has been especially alarmed by the former president\u8217\'20\'19s harsh, anti immigration policies, which includes a promise of mass deportations.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was Haitians, it was Mexicans, and it was Central Americans, Venezuelans. They\u8217\'20\'19re all being weaponized in this election, and I feel like that is something that we cannot have in our American politics,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CImmigrants should not be classified as a threat. We crafted this country. We have built it together with people from here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When he and his family first moved to the US, he said, he found it welcoming. But the political rhetoric about immigrants in recent years has hurt. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m an immigrant, I\u8217\'20\'19m a Democrat \u8211\'20\'13 is there a chance I\u8217\'20\'19m going to get attacked?\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut I try to contain those fears and that nervousness and just try to stay positive,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think Kamala Harris is going to win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Outside the library polling center on the University of Nevada, Las Vegas campus, Gloria-Jean Cutsforth said she was feeling cautiously optimistic about the election.\par \par \uc2 The 21-year-old student was wearing a shirt that read: \u8220\'20\'1Chysterical female voter\u8221\'20\'1D, and handing out pins, stickers and other swag to students who had stood in a snaking line to cast their ballots. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have these condoms that say \u8216\'20\'18Protect yourself from Republicans, vote Democrat\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re a big hit!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Like many students who were voting today, Cutsforth said that reproductive freedom was top of mind for her. \u8220\'20\'1CI wish we were able to spend more time on issues other than \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, noting she cared deeply about climate action, gun reform and foreign policy. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I am saddened that we are still having this debate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have to be taking up the same fight that her grandmother was fighting decades ago, she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd my grandmother should not have to be worrying about this issue again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nevada is one of 10 states with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure on the ballot, which Cutsforth has been promoting as part of a group called Vote For Equality. She has also been urging fellow students to vote for Kamala Harris and Democratic senator Jacky Rosen, both of whom have made \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  key to their campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Polls in Nevada have shown Harris and Donald Trump virtually tied, and the state\u8217\'20\'19s top pollster, John Ralston, predicts that Harris may pull through in the end with a.3% edge. Cutsforth said she was feeling nervous, but excited to just how many young people were showing up to vote. The university polling location was one of the busiest in the county.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m feeling good,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins Texas\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump has won Texas and the populous state\u8217\'20\'19s 40 electoral votes, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s his biggest victory of the night, and wholly expected, since Texas is a Republican stronghold. Democrats are holding out hope for an upset victory in the Senate race, where congressman Colin Allred is hoping to oust Republican incumbent Ted Cruz.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk says his political action committee, America Pac, will \u8220\'20\'1Ckeep going after this election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During a discussion on X this evening, the billionaire Trump backer said his Pac was \u8220\'20\'1Cpreparing for the midterms and any intermediate elections, as well as looking at elections at the district attorney level\u8221\'20\'1D, Business Insider {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/elon-musk-super-pac-america-continuing-after-election-midterms-2024-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomething has to be done to counter the damage that [George] Soros has done to the American system,\u8221\'20\'1D said Musk, referring to the billionaire philanthropist who has supported progressive prosecutors dedicated to criminal justice reform and reducing mass incarceration.\par \par \uc2 His announcement comes after Musk was sued by Larry Krasner, Philadelphia\u8217\'20\'19s DA, who has championed progressive policies and been supported by Soros. Krasner had filed a lawsuit to stop Musk\u8217\'20\'19s $1m voter prize giveaway, but a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/elon-musk-giveaway-winners-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 judge sided with Musk}}}\uc2  this week and allowed the controversial stunt to continue.\par \par \uc2 America Pac has led Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ground game efforts and was warned in September about increasing numbers of door knocks being flagged as potentially fraudulent, the Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/trump-musk-america-pac-fraudulent-door-knocks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported last week}}}\uc2 . The canvassing operation, which has funneled more than $100m into the election, was also accused of \u8220\'20\'1Cwillful violations of the California labor code\u8221\'20\'1D in a new California lawsuit. America Pac allegedly paid workers less than it promised and refused to make up the difference. More background here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/elon-musk-america-pac-labor-law-violations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s canvassing operation sued in California for alleged labor law violations}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins Ohio\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump has won Ohio, the Associated Press reports, underscoring the one-time swing state\u8217\'20\'19s shift towards the GOP.\par \par \uc2 We still do not have a result for its Senate race, which may decide whether Democrats are able to maintain their majority in the chamber. Democrat Sherrod Brown is standing for re-election against Republican challenger Bernie Moreno, and analysts view the race as a toss-up.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump supporters at his election watch party in Florida are expressing measured confidence about the final result.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWaiting for Pennsylvania,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kenneth Stewart, 47, a YouTuber from New York. \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone keeps talking about how razor thin of a margin it is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stewart does not expect Trump to declare victory prematurely as he did in 2020. \u8220\'20\'1CHe might be a little bit more cautious. There\u8217\'20\'19d be no reason to rush because we know what happened last time and we know what could happen again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stewart, who is African American, said Black voters have little faith in Kamala Harris. \u8220\'20\'1CEven in my community, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of energy behind Kamala.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump appeals to Black men, he added. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s masculine. He brings a lot of energy. He talks about things that we can understand. He talks about building. He talks about the auto industry. I\u8217\'20\'19m originally from Chicago, so he talks about a lot of stuff that people in the Rust Belt care about.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe other side, they\u8217\'20\'19re only talking about feelings. They\u8217\'20\'19re talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They\u8217\'20\'19re talking about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s bad, he\u8217\'20\'19s this or that, but come to me with tangibles. A lot of the Black men just want tangibles. We just want jobs. We want to see what our fathers had. We want to see what our grandfathers had, especially in the Rust Belt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins North and South Dakota, Louisiana, Wyoming, Harris carries New York\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris has won Democratic stronghold New York, while Donald Trump picked up both North and South Dakota along with Louisiana and Wyoming, all reliably Republican.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls close across midwestern states, including battlegrounds Arizona, Wisconsin, Michigan\par \par \uc2 More than a dozen states closed polls at 9pm, including three crucial battlegrounds: Arizona, Wisconsin and Michigan.\par \par \uc2 In addition, voting finished in Colorado, Iowa, Kansas, Louisiana, Minnesota, Nebraska, New Mexico, New York, North Dakota, South Dakota, Texas and Wyoming.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19ll be interesting to see if Kamala Harris can pull off an upset victory in Iowa, which hasn\u8217\'20\'19t supported a Democrat since Barack Obama was on the ballot in 2012. Over the weekend, an authoritative pollster found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/harris-unexpected-lead-over-trump-iowa-selzer-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris leading }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/harris-unexpected-lead-over-trump-iowa-selzer-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/harris-unexpected-lead-over-trump-iowa-selzer-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in the state}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no question Trump will win Texas\u8217\'20\'19s 40 electoral votes, but Democrats are hoping their candidate Colin Allred can oust incumbent senator Ted Cruz, and bolster their hopes of keeping the majority in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrat Josh Stein elected North Carolina governor, beating Republican Mark Robinson, who called himself 'black Nazi'\par \par \uc2 Republican Mark Robinson has lost the race for governor of North Carolina to Democrat Josh Stein, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Robinson, the state\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, was known for making controversial statements, but his campaign was badly damaged in September after reports emerged that he had previously made lewd and offensive posts on the message board of a pornography website, including calling himself a \u8220\'20\'1Cblack Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Stein, the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, will take over from fellow Democrat Roy Cooper. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more about Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s writings, which likely sunk his hopes of becoming governor:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/mark-robinson-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina Republican candidate for governor Mark Robinson called himself \u8216\'20\'18black Nazi\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 Mark Robinson is at a watch party in Raleigh tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Arizona is a narrowly divided swing state this election \u8211\'20\'13 and the Tempe campus of Arizona State University sure looked like it on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Arizona senator Mark Kelly, a Democrat, and his wife Gabrielle Giffords, a former representative turned gun control activist, showed up on campus, just feet away from a booth of Turning Point USA, a conservative group. Hundreds waiting to vote snaked around a campus fitness complex, while students in \u8220\'20\'1CSun Devils for Harris\u8221\'20\'1D t-shirts mingled with those wearing \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Great Again\u8221\'20\'1D hats.\par \par \uc2 Arizona State University student Madison Schotz, 19, wore one of those red hats \u8211\'20\'13 which matched her red sports bra \u8211\'20\'13 as she walked past the line with her best friend and roommate Zoe Bellomio, 18. Both were first time voters: Schotz had voted for Donald Trump, while Bellomio had voted for Kamala Harris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a Christian, and I see Trump upholding God\u8217\'20\'19s policies more than I see Kamala,\u8221\'20\'1D Schotz said, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Cprotection\u8221\'20\'1D is important to her. \u8220\'20\'1CI like Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies on the border.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just believe in inclusivity and I think Harris is way more inclusive,\u8221\'20\'1D Bellomio said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m Jewish so I don\u8217\'20\'19t see myself being very included in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies. But furthermore I think Harris is good for middle-class economy and lowering taxes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of the top issues in the 2024 election, especially for women under 45, it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t critical to either Schotz, who identified as \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-life\u8221\'20\'1D, or Bellomio, who identified as \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-choice\u8221\'20\'1D. Neither had voted on Proposition 139, an Arizona ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution and overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s 15-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. When asked about their friendship, Schotz and Bellomio hugged enthusiastically.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can be besties and have opposing sides!\u8221\'20\'1D Bellomio said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins Miami-Dade, a closely watched Florida county\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump is the first GOP presidential candidate to win Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Miami-Dade county since George HW Bush in 1988, the New York Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/11/05/us/trump-miami-dade-florida.html?smid=url-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Analysts have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-swing-state-counties"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 keeping a close eye on the county}}}\uc2 , which includes the city of Miami and was once a Democratic stronghold. Hillary Clinton won Miami-Dade by a 30-point margin in 2016, but the area has since moved right as Florida has transitioned from a swing state to a solidly red state. With 95% of votes in as of around 8.45pm, Trump had won 55% of the Miami-Dade vote compared with Harris\u8217\'20\'19s 44%.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden beat Trump by seven points in 2020 in the state\u8217\'20\'19s most-populous county. Some pundits have said the Miami-Dade result could be a bellwether for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s performance among Latino voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 Measure to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Florida fails\par \par \uc2 A measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the Florida state constitution fell short on Tuesday, narrowly missing the 60% vote share that it needed to become law in the red state.\par \par \uc2 The failure of the measure, which would have helped overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, is a first for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters, who have won a string of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures in the two years since the US supreme court overturned Roe v Wade in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Advocates had hoped to restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Florida, which up until May had been the only southern state to allow the procedure past six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 In the first month after the six-week ban took effect, abortions in Florida fell by roughly 30%, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/news-release/2024/new-data-show-substantial-drop-abortions-florida-after-six-week-ban-took-effect"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to data from the Guttmacher Institute}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nine other states are voting on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures on Tuesday. Results are forthcoming.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida rejects \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights measure as results in nine states remain}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris wins Illinois\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris has won Illinois, the Associated Press reports, taking the 19 electoral votes in the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 midwestern stronghold.\par \par \uc2 No Republican has won the state since 1988.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 I am at Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election watch party at the Palm Beach County Convention Center in West Palm Beach, Florida.\par \par \uc2 There are men in suits \u8211\'20\'13 often with red ties \u8211\'20\'13 and women in mostly red dresses. Other guests have gone full Maga with \u8220\'20\'1CMake America great again\u8221\'20\'1D caps and other regalia.\par \par \uc2 Most are gathered inside a black, cavernous exhibition hall, the focus of which is a giant US flag hanging from the ceiling, then a row of US flags on a stage where a lectern and microphone are set up. Unlike his 2016 party in New York, there is no sign of Maga caps displayed in glass cases like museum relics; however, a big pile of free Maga caps was on a table outside.\par \par \uc2 The hall is buzzing with conversation but dominated by giant TV screens showing Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s coverage of election results with the volume turned up loud.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, people are standing in a queue to have their photo taken against a big black canvas that says: \u8220\'20\'1CMAKE AMERICA GREAT AGAIN!\u8221\'20\'1D Steve Bannon \u8217\'20\'19s daughter Maureen is doing the rounds. And in one of the allocated press filing centres, former New York mayor Rudy Giuliani is podcasting away, providing a live commentary on events for anyone who will listen.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 A helpful reminder from Guardian US data editor Will Craft:\par \par \uc2 Votes have started coming in across the east coast. But early US vote counts are misleading.\par \par \uc2 Large numbers of early votes and vote-by-mail ballots means that the vote count will shift as the night goes on, and votes from large, urban precincts might radically shift the count with one report.\par \par \uc2 States will be reporting totals throughout the night and it\u8217\'20\'19s important to avoid the red or blue mirage.\par \par \uc2 Our results page is here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/us-election-results-2024-live-donald-trump-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election results and map 2024: Donald Trump and Kamala Harris vie to be president}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris wins Delaware, New Jersey\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris added blue states Delaware and New Jersey to her trove of electoral college wins, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The news agency has yet to call any of the three swing states where polls have closed: Pennsylvania, Georgia and North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins Arkansas\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump has won Arkansas, the Associated Press reports, gaining its six electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 The state last voted for a Democrat in 1996, when Bill Clinton, its former governor, ran successfully for a second term.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls close in Arkansas\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s closing time for polling places in Arkansas, the home state of Democratic former president Bill Clinton but otherwise a solidly red state.\par \par \uc2 Expect its six electoral votes to be quickly declared for Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 New Jersey Democrat Andy Kim becomes first Korean American elected to Senate\par \par \uc2 Andy Kim is the winner of New Jersey\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race, the Associated Press reports, making the Democratic congressman the first Korean American elected to Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 Kim takes over from fellow Democrat Robert Menendez, who resigned his seat after being convicted of bribery charges. George Helmy, also a Democrat, was appointed to replace Menendez, but did not run for a full term.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/20/bob-menendez-resignation-bribery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bob Menendez expected to resign as senator following bribery conviction}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 Lisa Blunt Rochester elected Delaware's first Black female senator\par \par \uc2 Democrat Lisa Blunt Rochester has won the race for Delaware\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat, the Associated Press said, becoming both the first woman and first African American to represent the state in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 Rochester is currently the state\u8217\'20\'19s at-large congresswoman, and broke the same barriers when first elected in 2016.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican senator Rick Scott re-elected in Florida, limiting Democrats' options for keeping majority\par \par \uc2 Republican Rick Scott has won re-election as Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Senator, the Associated Press said, blocking Democrats from an upset victory in the increasingly Republican state that could have helped them preserve their majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have a 51-seat majority in the chamber, but earlier lost the West Virginia seat held by retiring independent senator Joe Manchin. The party had hoped their candidate Debbie Mucarsel-Powell could oust Scott in the Sunshine state and give them another seat, but those hopes have been dashed.\par \par \uc2 They still have a chance to keep the majority, but it requires the re-election of Sherrod Brown in Ohio and Jon Tester in Montana, or a surprise victory by Colin Allred in Texas. All of those are red states.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump triumphs in Florida, Oklahoma, Tennessee, South Carolina, Harris wins Massachusetts, Connecticut, Rhode Island\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has called Oklahoma, South Carolina, Florida and Tennessee for Donald Trump, and Massachusetts, Rhode Island and Connecticut for Kamala Harris.\par \par \uc2 None of these results are surprising, with the two candidates winning states that have supported their respective parties for years. If there is anything to note, it\u8217\'20\'19s that Florida was called so quickly \u8211\'20\'13 when Trump first won in 2016, it was viewed as a swing state, but has since become reliably Republican.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris wins Maryland, Trump carries Mississippi, Alabama\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris has won Maryland, a Democratic stronghold, the Associated Press reports, while Donald Trump has won the very red states of Mississippi and Alabama.\par \par \uc2 Expect more race calls from the AP imminently.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls close across east coast, midwestern states, including pivotal Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Voting just finished in more than a dozen states, including Pennsylvania, which is regarded as perhaps the most vital swing state for determining the outcome of the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the Keystone state, polls closed at 8pm in Alabama, Connecticut, Delaware, Illinois, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, Mississippi, Missouri, New Jersey, Oklahoma, Pennsylvania, Rhode Island, Tennessee and the District of Columbia. Voting also finished in counties in Florida and New Hampshire that had stayed open beyond 7pm.\par \par \uc2 Beyond the presidential race, we\u8217\'20\'19ll be looking for the outcome of the Senate race in Pennsylvania, where Democratic incumbent Bob Casey is up for re-election against Republican David McCormick. Maryland is also worth watching \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s a blue state, but Democrat Angela Alsobrooks may face trouble beating Republican former governor Larry Hogan to win its Senate seat. And Democrats are hoping for a surprise in Florida, where they believe Republican senator Rick Scott could be beaten by their candidate Debbie Mucarsel-Powell.\par \par \uc2 Many of these states are otherwise solidly red or blue, and no surprises are expected at the presidential or congressional level.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s starting to pick up at Kamala HQ. The DJ has started playing music on the Yard at Howard University, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s alma mater, is beginning to fill up.\par \par \uc2 There is a whole section awash in pink and green, the colors of AKA, the sorority Harris joined at Howard. Students are dancing. The mood at this early stage in the night is joyful.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re ready to make Black history, talk to me,\u8221\'20\'1D the DJ shouted, getting cheers from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 For more on Harris and AKA:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/08/kamala-harris-and-the-political-power-of-black-sororities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris and the political power of Black sororities}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris has given one of her final interviews before the polls close, telling SiriusXM host Zerlina Maxwell that last-minute undecided voters should understand how Trump would govern if he wins.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CThe vast majority of us have so much more in common than what separates us.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  joined {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZerlinaMaxwell?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ZerlinaMaxwell}}}\uc2  this evening for an election night call to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/GOTV?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #GOTV}}}\uc2  before the polls close! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vD1aZYbT6x"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vD1aZYbT6x}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Z5VBUpl1tF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Z5VBUpl1tF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mornings With Zerlina. (@ZerlinaMornings) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZerlinaMornings/status/1853955428981330320?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The vice-president said:\par \par \uc2 On January 20th, it\u8217\'20\'19s either going to be him or me in the White House, and if it is him, he\u8217\'20\'19s going to be sitting there stewing over his enemies list, plotting his revenge, playing out all of his grievances, which are all about himself, versus what I will be doing if elected president, which is working from day one on my to-do list on behalf of the American people to make progress through common ground solutions that are common-sense solutions.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 Sister Barbara Pfarr, a member of the faith group Milwaukee Inner-City Congregations Allied for Hope (MICAH), prayed with a small group in front of the Baird Center where Milwaukee\u8217\'20\'19s central count is taking place.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re here to support the folks inside because of all of the threats and harassment,\u8221\'20\'1D said Pfarr, nodding to the increase in violent threats that election workers have faced since the 2020 election, when Donald Trump and his allies falsely claimed election workers had participated in a plot to rig the election for Joe Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re here to support the democratic process and we believe in whatever is going to come out of here,\u8221\'20\'1D said Pfarr, who said she had been stationed in front of the building since the early morning. \u8220\'20\'1CI have every confidence in [the process] and I\u8217\'20\'19m just so grateful for these folks, for what they\u8217\'20\'19re doing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Poll workers and election experts have been on high alert for security threats and voters have been telling me all day about their fears of violence no matter the outcome.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe vote is sacred, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not just the vote, it\u8217\'20\'19s what comes after,\u8221\'20\'1D said Pfarr. And then she said something that \u8211\'20\'13 following all my conversations with voters today \u8211\'20\'13 genuinely took me off guard: \u8220\'20\'1CI feel optimistic about the country and our democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican attorney general Patrick Morrisey will be West Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s next governor, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The victories are a sweep by the GOP of a state that was for decades a Democratic stronghold, but has recently become one of the most Republican in the nation and in the past two presidential elections gave Donald Trump some of his biggest margins of victory.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins West Virginia, Republicans pick up Senate seat\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump has won West Virginia, the Associated Press reports, while Republican governor Jim Justice has won its Senate seat.\par \par \uc2 enltrPolls are open until 7:30pm! Babydog says you better go vote! We need you to flip the Senate. Find a polling location here.>> {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KvWlsXzW97"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/KvWlsXzW97}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WUz9K7XeW2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WUz9K7XeW2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jim Justice (@JimJusticeWV) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JimJusticeWV/status/1853802415134232834?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Justice will replace Joe Manchin, an independent who recently left the Democratic party after acting as a spoiler to many of Joe Biden \u8217\'20\'19s economic proposals.\par \par \uc2 Manchin continues to caucus with the Democrats, and the loss of his seat brings Democrats closer to losing their control of Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber. Their hopes now hinge on victories by their candidates in Ohio, Montana and potentially Texas and Florida \u8211\'20\'13 all red states.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls close in battleground state North Carolina, West Virginia, Ohio\par \par \uc2 Voting has finished in another three states, one of which is a swing state.\par \par \uc2 At 7.30pm, polls closed in North Carolina, which has not backed a Democratic candidate since 2008, but which Kamala Harris \u8217\'20\'19s team believes she may have a chance of winning this year.\par \par \uc2 Balloting also wrapped up in deep-red West Virginia, where Democrats are expected to lose a Senate seat. But they are hopeful about Ohio, where Democratic senator Sherrod Brown is standing for re-election in a state that has grown increasingly Republican in recent years. Voting just finished there, too.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Pennsylvania chapter of the American Civil Liberties Union is seeking legal action to have voting extended past 8pm in precincts where students have been waiting hours to cast a vote.\par \par \uc2 That includes in Bethlehem, where students have been waiting as many as six-and-a-half hours to cast a ballot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe counties know from history that students come out for presidential elections, and they should have been better prepared,\u8221\'20\'1D said Witold Walczak, legal director of the ACLU of Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStill, it\u8217\'20\'19s a good problem to have. Students are participating in this election, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll take court action necessary to ensure that they get to cast their ballots.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a post on X from earlier with a clip of a voting line near the university.\par \par \uc2 enltrJaw-dropping line at the polling site near Lehigh University where the line stretches around the block multiple times & is predominately young people & students. These young people are showing UP. Amazing. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/j7iaa6Q3Va"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/j7iaa6Q3Va}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Victor Shi (@Victorshi2020) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Victorshi2020/status/1853860128153313663?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Georgia independents breaking for Trump by slim margin - exit poll\par \par \uc2 A CNN exit poll in Georgia had a potentially concerning finding for Kamala Harris : independents who backed Joe Biden in 2020 now have swung to Donald Trump, albeit by a small margin.\par \par \uc2 However, the vice-president continues to be strong among Black voters, as well as young people. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from CNN:\par \par \uc2 Roughly 86% of Black Georgia voters say they cast their ballot for Harris, as do about 6 in 10 voters younger than 30 \u8212\'20\'14 in both cases, generally similar to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s numbers in 2020.\par \par \uc2 As was the case in 2020, suburban voters are closely split. But where Biden won slightly over half of political independents in 2020, now a slim majority say they\u8217\'20\'19re backing Trump.\par \par \uc2 White voters without a college degree, who went overwhelmingly for Trump in 2020, are still predominantly in his camp, with roughly 8 in 10 picking him over Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Lara Trump, the GOP nominee\u8217\'20\'19s daughter-in-law and co-chair of the Republican National Committee, has raised alarms about slow counting in Milwaukee, saying it was \u8220\'20\'1Can unacceptable example of incompetent election administration in a key swing state\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltr?????? Throughout the day we have been monitoring slow ballot counting in Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 Now, our legal team has learned that the counting took place in unsecured conditions and the city now has to start over, wildly extending the counting timeline.\par \par \uc2 This is an unacceptable\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lara Trump (@LaraLeaTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LaraLeaTrump/status/1853942388580069736?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 As we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/presidential-election-harris-trump-polls-results-live-updates?page=with:block-672aa1828f08ec080b940320#block-672aa1828f08ec080b940320"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  earlier, a human error during Milwaukee\u8217\'20\'19s absentee vote could lead to a late night for election workers in the city. An election observer noticed panels open on multiple tabulators, which should have been locked and closed, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AlexanderShur/status/1853907144749330879"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vote Beat}}}\uc2 . The open panels revealed machines\u8217\'20\'19 on/off switches, and although officials said it appeared the machines had not been tampered, they moved to recount 30,000 votes that had already been processed.\par \par \uc2 Lara Trump\u8217\'20\'19s statement said:\par \par \uc2 We are unambiguously calling on Milwaukee\u8217\'20\'19s officials to do their jobs and count ballots quickly and effectively. Anything less undermines voter confidence.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 We also have a few race calls for House seats, with no surprises.\par \par \uc2 In Florida, the Associated Press says Republican Gus Bilirakis has been re-elected, as have Democrats Debbie Wasserman Schultz and Frederica Wilson.\par \par \uc2 In Kentucky, Republicans Hal Rogers and Thomas Massie have won themselves another term. Republican Mark Messmer has won election to a district in Indiana.\par \par \uc2 All were running in safe districts, and expected to win.\par \par \uc2 enltrU.S. Rep. Debbie Wasserman Schultz with Broward State Attorney Harold Pryor at the African American Research Library and Cultural Center in Fort Lauderdale on Sunday, Nov. 3, 2024, after a Souls to the Polls march. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/bHOypQGZjW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/bHOypQGZjW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jason Alston ???? #SaveRebeccaColton (@SoulCitySigma) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SoulCitySigma/status/1853760421557051417?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Progressive Bernie Sanders re-elected to Senate\par \par \uc2 Independent Bernie Sanders, an icon among progressives, has won a fourth term representing Vermont in the US Senate, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Republican congressman Jim Banks will be Indiana\u8217\'20\'19s next senator, replacing Mike Braun, who the AP says was just elected as the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis Election Day is one of the most consequential in the history of our country.\par \par \uc2 I was proud to cast my vote today for Kamala Harris, and I want to thank every Vermonter who has supported my candidacy for U.S. Senate.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s go forward together. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CYXnluWKdc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CYXnluWKdc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bernie Sanders (@BernieSanders) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BernieSanders/status/1853949158215868451?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Sanders posted on X on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe know why Trump should NOT be president.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s why Kamala should be.\par \par \uc2 She wants to:\par \par \uc2 - Raise the min wage to $15 per hour\par \par \uc2 - Cancel all medical debt\par \par \uc2 - Help working parents by expanding the child tax credit\par \par \uc2 - Expand Medicare to cover home health care, vision & hearing\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Bernie Sanders (@BernieSanders) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BernieSanders/status/1853245389711065255?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump wins red states Kentucky and Indiana; Harris picks up blue Vermont\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has called its first states, and there are thus far no surprises.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris became the latest Democrat to win Vermont, a party stronghold. Donald Trump has won Indiana and Kentucky, both red states.\par \par \uc2 The AP has not yet called swing state Georgia, or Virginia and South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls close in battleground Georgia and five other states\par \par \uc2 Voting just wrapped up in six states, including Georgia, one of the swing states expected to determine the winner of the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the Peach State, polls closed at 7pm in red state South Carolina, blue state Vermont and Virginia, which is expected to vote Democratic but where there are several contested races for seats in the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 Polls that had remained open in Kentucky and Indiana, both red states, have also closed.\par \par \uc2 Georgia tends to count ballots quickly, so we may know the winner there before the night is through. Joe Biden won the state in 2020 and Democrats won both of its Senate seats, despite the state\u8217\'20\'19s historically Republican tilt.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Ana Mendoza, a 19-year-old political science major at Lehigh University, got in line to vote around 11am at her polling place. She didn\u8217\'20\'19t cast her vote until six-and-a-half hours later.\par \par \uc2 She was one of many students who waited hours in line at a polling precinct that only had two working voting machines this morning, and two volunteers checking people in, according to school newspaper {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thebrownandwhite.com/2024/11/05/record-voter-turnout-on-the-south-side/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Brown and White}}}\uc2 . The county has sent three additional voting machines to the site, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lehighvalleynews.com/elections/waiting-3-to-4-hours-to-vote-line-of-hundreds-goes-for-blocks-at-this-lehigh-valley-precinct"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Allentown Morning Call.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m in Pennsylvania and it\u8217\'20\'19s a swing state so I know that every single vote matters,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Mendoza, who was voting in her first presidential election and cast her ballot for Kamala Harris, said she and those who were waiting were pretty tired by the end, but there were groups giving food and water out.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Philadelphia district attorney says Trump's 'cheating' claim 'unfounded'\par \par \uc2 Philadelphia\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic district attorney Larry Krasner had this to say about Donald Trump \u8217\'20\'19s claim that \u8220\'20\'1Ccheating\u8221\'20\'1D was happening in elections held in the city:\par \par \uc2 enltrMy response to Trump's unfounded allegation of cheating in Philly's general election:\par \par \uc2 The only talk about massive cheating has come from one of the candidates, Donald J. Trump. There is no factual basis whatsoever within law enforcement to support this wild allegation. 1/2\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 DA Larry Krasner (@DA_LarryKrasner) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DA_LarryKrasner/status/1853929895857917994?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWe have invited complaints and allegations of improprieties all day. If Donald J. Trump has any facts to support his wild allegations, we want them now. Right now. We are not holding our breath. 2/2\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 DA Larry Krasner (@DA_LarryKrasner) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DA_LarryKrasner/status/1853929897363746900?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A human error during Milwaukee\u8217\'20\'19s absentee vote count could lead to a late night for election workers in the largest city in the state, and delayed results.\par \par \uc2 According to Vote Beat, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AlexanderShur/status/1853907144749330879"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an election observer noticed}}}\uc2  panels open on multiple tabulators which should have been closed and locked \u8211\'20\'13 revealing the machines\u8217\'20\'19 on/off switches. Although election officials said it did not appear that anyone had touched the panels or tampered with the machines, the commission has moved to recount the 30,000 votes that those tabulators already processed.\par \par \uc2 The recount could mean a long night for Milwaukee election officials and lead to a possible late night boost for Kamala Harris, who will probably command a majority of the Milwaukee vote, which tends to be a Democratic party stronghold.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, Trump and his allies seized on late-night absentee votes as evidence of wrongdoing \u8211\'20\'13 a patently false claim that nonetheless contributed to a wave of misinformation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 MJ, an 18-year-old from Milwaukee, voted for the first time today \u8211\'20\'13 splitting her ballot between Donald Trump, at the top of the ticket, and Democratic candidates all the way down.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m mainly worried about economics,\u8221\'20\'1D said MJ, who cited immigration as her second top concern. She said she\u8217\'20\'19s frustrated about the possibility of non-US citizens voting in this election \u8211\'20\'13 a claim that Trump and his allies have been promoting for months, despite the fact that empirical evidence suggests non-citizens, who face steep penalties for voting illegally, including felony charges and possible deportation, rarely cast a ballot in federal elections.\par \par \uc2 Evidently, those claims have stuck \u8211\'20\'13 including influencing MJ\u8217\'20\'19s decision to vote Trump, despite preferring Democratic party candidates in general.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m gonna vote all Democrat [otherwise],\u8221\'20\'1D said MJ. She said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are a major concern for her, and said she was \u8220\'20\'1Con the fence\u8221\'20\'1D about Trump for that reason.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/ddale8/status/1853922453539467582"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to CNN}}}\uc2 , Philadelphia police don\u8217\'20\'19t know what Trump is talking about in his post alleging \u8220\'20\'1Ccheating\u8221\'20\'1D in the city, and are not aware of any issues that would call for their response.\par \par \uc2 There was a semi-viral video spreading on the rightwing internet today. James O\u8217\'20\'19Keefe, the guy who makes undercover videos that are often misleading or outright false, posted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://billypenn.com/2024/11/05/election-hidden-video-poll-worker-krasner/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2  on X claiming that an election worker in Philadelphia told voters they could cast a ballot if they were not citizens. Accounts like Libs of TikTok spread the video to their followers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Those who remember the 2020 election will recall that it took a few days before we knew for sure that Joe Biden had beaten Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 But the result of previous elections was known much sooner, as the below chart shows:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2024/11/archive-2-zip/giv-4559cgBkB108BXBT/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 The year 2000 was when a very close race between Democrat Al Gore and Republican George W Bush came down to the state of Florida and a supreme court case that was decided in Bush\u8217\'20\'19s favor, sending him to the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Fulton county, Georgia:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re stuck in a position where we have to affirm this challenge,\u8221\'20\'1D said Aaron Johnson, the Fulton County Board of Registration and Elections board\u8217\'20\'19s vice-chair.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people are getting caught up now.\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said he knew this would happen. \u8220\'20\'1CWe didn\u8217\'20\'19t make the rule. The general assembly made the rule. Whether I agree with it or not, we have to follow the rule.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been voting with this address for years,\u8221\'20\'1D said Chante Knox, whose voter registration was challenged. She was homeless when she first registered. She\u8217\'20\'19s a Republican and a Donald Trump voter, and has been skeptical of the county\u8217\'20\'19s election administration, but this issue is separate from those concerns, she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m still a Fulton County resident. I still want my vote to count,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI want a non-provisional vote for the president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jack Samuels from the Lawyer\u8217\'20\'19s Committee for Civil Rights and the ACLU, said Swanson\u8217\'20\'19s denial was the product of inadequate notice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany of the persons being challenged have not received notice,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey did not know that they needed to oppose the challenge before today. Like all of us, they have work, family, child and senior care obligations that do not generally permit people to drop everything and drive as far as 40 miles across the county to appear. A hearing on insufficient notice deprives them of the right to vote in violation of their due process rights and equal protection and should not be occurring.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Samuels demanded the right for Swanson to cast a provisional ballot, laying the groundwork for a legal appeal. \u8220\'20\'1CThis hearing is not practical\u8221\'20\'1D for voters, he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Fulton county, Georgia:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been trying to vote since eight in the morning,\u8221\'20\'1D said John Whitfield, an entertainer who goes by D C Young Fly, animatedly contesting his removal from the voting rolls in Fulton County before the elections board.\par \par \uc2 He stood. He paced the room. His indignation radiated. He \u8211\'20\'13 and dozens of others \u8211\'20\'13 packed the hearing room in south Fulton on election day, thoroughly pissed off.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just trying to exercise my right to vote. This is critical,\u8221\'20\'1D he said aloud as the hearing proceeded. \u8220\'20\'1CIf my ancestors didn\u8217\'20\'19t fight for me to vote, I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t give a damn.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Georgia legislature changed election laws after the 2020 election, to bar voters from registering at commercial addresses like UPS stores.\par \par \uc2 One by one, bewildered people who showed up to vote this morning to find that they were de-registered under this law protested their removal at the Fulton County Board of Registration and Elections, hoping to vote today.\par \par \uc2 Sheree Swanson, an actor from Sandy Springs, was challenged because she initially used a UPS store address as the address on her voter registration, the same address as a trucking company she owns, she said. Her vehicle insurance company required her driver\u8217\'20\'19s license to have the same address as the address for her vehicle registration, she said. Swanson tried to change her addresses to match her home address last week, she said. That was too late.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHer status is challenged because she listed her business as her residence,\u8221\'20\'1D said Katheryn Glenn, the board\u8217\'20\'19s registration officer. \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t swear or affirm if you don\u8217\'20\'19t live there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The board, by a 3-0 vote, denied her appeal.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 How do we know who won? A guide to calling this election\par \par \uc2 Now that the first polls have closed, it\u8217\'20\'19s a good time to talk about who the Guardian uses to determine the outcome of today\u8217\'20\'19s vote.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian relies on the Associated Press to determine the outcomes of elections across the United States. The New York-based global news agency has a presence in every US state and a long and authoritative history of determining the winners of elections at the presidential, congressional and state level. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/ap-race-calls-faq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here is more information}}}\uc2  about their process.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2024/11/archive-2-zip/giv-4559cgBkB108BXBT/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Voting finishes in parts of Kentucky and Indiana as first US polls close\par \par \uc2 The first polls have closed in the US, with voting wrapping up in most Indiana counties and in Kentucky\u8217\'20\'19s eastern half.\par \par \uc2 Voting will finish in the rest of the two red states at 7pm, at which point it will also conclude in a handful of other states \u8211\'20\'13 including swing state Georgia.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2024/11/archive-zip/giv-45592QnBeLGClCqy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 First polls soon to close in US election\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re minutes away from the first polls closing anywhere in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Most counties in Indiana and several in eastern Kentucky will wrap up voting at 6pm ET. Both generally vote Republican and not considered swing states this year. Voting in the remaining counties will finish at 7pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Milwaukee, Wisconsin:\par \par \uc2 Serina Jones, 30, pulled over her minivan in West Milwaukee and flagged down a canvasser walking down the street in a reflective jacket.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAre you all doing voter stuff?\u8221\'20\'1D she asked.\par \par \uc2 Jones, who is a mother of three, had not registered to vote yet but was determined to cast a ballot \u8211\'20\'13 and had plans to get her husband to the polls, too.\par \par \uc2 After plugging in her address and making a plan to vote, she told me she has \u8220\'20\'1Cmixed feelings\u8221\'20\'1D about the election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m fired up,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jones, who is voting for Kamala Harris and said she worried about the consequences of a second Donald Trump presidency for her three children\u8217\'20\'19s education and livelihood.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut I have a lot riding on this,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m trying to make sure we got a future for our babies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican Philadelphia official says 'no truth' to Trump's claim of election fraud\par \par \uc2 Seth Bluestein, a Republican Philadelphia city commissioner, called Donald Trump \u8217\'20\'19s claim of \u8220\'20\'1Ccheating\u8221\'20\'1D in the city \u8220\'20\'1Cdisinformation\u8221\'20\'1D, and said the vote so far has been \u8220\'20\'1Csafe and secure\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Bluestein is one of three officials on the board tasked with overseeing voting in Philadelphia. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltrThere is absolutely no truth to this allegation. It is yet another example of disinformation. Voting in Philadelphia has been safe and secure. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/wMiPnAgO17"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/wMiPnAgO17}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Seth Bluestein (@SethBluestein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SethBluestein/status/1853926611495567694?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWe have been in regular contact with the RNC. We have been responsive to every report of irregularities at the polls to ensure Philadelphians can vote safely and securely.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Seth Bluestein (@SethBluestein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SethBluestein/status/1853927878028591542?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign sees high Puerto Rican turnout in Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Philadelphia neighborhoods where many Puerto Ricans live have seen high voter turnout, the Harris campaign says, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/29/trump-rally-puerto-rico-voter-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a speaker}}}\uc2  at a Donald Trump rally last month referred to the US territory as \u8220\'20\'1Ca floating island of garbage in the middle of the ocean\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It could be a positive sign for the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning Pennsylvania, perhaps the most vital of the three \u8220\'20\'1CBlue Wall\u8221\'20\'1D swing states along the Great Lakes. Victories in the Keystone state along with Michigan and Wisconsin would probably provide enough electoral votes to make Harris the next president.\par \par \uc2 The campaign also sees high turnout by students at universities nationwide, including in Pennsylvania. In battleground state North Carolina, fewer rural Republicans appear to have voted, but many people have cast ballots in the Democratic-leaning city of Durham.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats are counting on young voters to turn out at the polls today to help deliver wins for not just Kamala Harris but congressional candidates and ballot measures across the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYoung people will decide this election. From local ballot initiatives to federal races, we know this critical bloc is showing up for their futures and making their voices heard,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cristina Tzintz\u250\'00\'FAn Ramirez, president of the youth voting group NextGen America.\par \par \uc2 According to NextGen\u8217\'20\'19s data, the group registered more than 130,000 young voters this election cycle, while more than 171,000 young voters signed pledges to vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are proud of our work this cycle on-the-ground and online to educate, mobilize, and empower young voters, contributing to a culture of civic engagement that will extend beyond this election,\u8221\'20\'1D Ramirez said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYoung people are showing up, turning out, and using their collective power to elect leaders that represent our values \u8211\'20\'13 today and into the future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Fears for democracy and state of economy top issues for voters, exit polls suggest\par \par \uc2 The state of American democracy and the economy were the top issues on voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds as they cast their ballots in the 2024 presidential election, according to an NBC News {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/nbc-news-exit-poll-voters-express-concern-democracy-economy-rcna178602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exit poll.}}}\par \par \uc2 The poll\u8217\'20\'19s preliminary results show 35% of voters said democracy mattered most to their vote, while 31% said the economy.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  (14%) and immigration (11%) ranked as the next-most important issues, while just 4% named foreign policy.\par \par \uc2 ABC News\u8217\'20\'19 preliminary {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/nbc-news-exit-poll-voters-express-concern-democracy-economy-rcna178602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  exit poll}}}\uc2  also shows that the state of democracy prevailed as the most important issue to voters. More voters said they see American democracy as threatened than secure \u8211\'20\'13 73% to 25%, the poll shows.\par \par \uc2 Voters described the economy as being in \u8220\'20\'1Cbad shape\u8221\'20\'1D by 67%-32%, with 45% of respondents saying that their own financial situation is worse now than four years ago.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Phoenix, Arizona:\par \par \uc2 Alison Folsom has cast her ballot at the same library in downtown Phoenix for years. This is the first year, Folsom said, that she had to wait in line \u8211\'20\'13 for 40 minutes.\par \par \uc2 But Folsom was delighted, especially because so many of the other people in line seemed to be between the ages of 18 and 25.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that they\u8217\'20\'19re one of the most important, consequential voting blocks, but seeing them come out and vote on election day that was special,\u8221\'20\'1D said Folsom, who wore a purple shirt that read \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 ABORTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  RIGHTS ARE HUMAN RIGHTS\u8221\'20\'1D and works for the Movement Voter Project, which helps Democratic and progressive donors give to grassroots campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Arizona State University students Joy Leon, a 19-year-old Arizona voter, and Kaya Clark, a 18-year-old Idaho voter, said that they had both voted for Kamala Harris in large part because of their support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI like having the choice. It\u8217\'20\'19s kind of strange that stuff about human rights and the choice of your body is considered controversial,\u8221\'20\'1D said Clark, who carried a handmade flag that read \u8220\'20\'1CVOTING IS BRAT\u8221\'20\'1D in green and black.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t really want to vote for a convicted felon. I\u8217\'20\'19m for the girlies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New York City mayor Eric Adams has named Kamala Harris as his candidate of choice in the presidential election, in what the New York Times said is the first time in recent memory.\par \par \uc2 enltrFor the first time in recent memory, Mayor Eric Adams explicitly named Kamala Harris as his candidate of choice in the presidential election, before voting at a Brooklyn public school. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8e2BTdFwVJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8e2BTdFwVJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dana Rubinstein (@danarubinstein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/danarubinstein/status/1853921630369517775?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Wall Street rose on a quiet last day of trading before polls close. The benchmark S&P 500 finished up 1.2% on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 While trading was broadly muted, there was a notable exception: it was another volatile day for Trump Media & Technology Group (TMTG), owner of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s tiny Truth Social media empire.\par \par \uc2 Trading in TMTG was repeatedly halted. The stock \u8211\'20\'13 which has been on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/29/truth-social-trading-suspended"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wild ride}}}\uc2  in recent weeks \u8211\'20\'13 surged by nearly 18% during early trading, before falling into the red. It finished the day down 1.2%.\par \par \uc2 The economy has taken center stage in this campaign. While the last few months have been filled with great news, according to economists, many Americans still think the economy stinks, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/america-economy-election-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as Lauren Aratani reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a disconnect that could ultimately decide who takes the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 First election result in tiny New Hampshire village sees a Trump-Harris tie\par \par \uc2 The traditional first tally of the 2024 US presidential elections in the tiny village of Dixville Notch, in New Hampshire \u8217\'20\'19s northern tip, ended in a deadlock: three votes to Kamala Harris and three for Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 It took approximately 12 minutes to count and certify the votes of the six residents of this tiny community near the Canadian border, which has been casting its ballots at midnight on election day for decades.\par \par \uc2 The result marks a significant shift from four years ago, when all five votes went to Joe Biden \u8211\'20\'13 even though this year four of the registered voters are Republicans and the other two are independents, according to the Washington Post.\par \par \uc2 Dixville Notch, in the White Mountains, started its early voting in 1960. The tradition originated in the nearby town of Hart\u8217\'20\'19s Location, to accommodate rail workers who had to be at work before normal voting hours.\par \par \uc2 Although the town\u8217\'20\'19s result doesn\u8217\'20\'19t always predict the eventual winner \u8211\'20\'13 in 2016, Hillary Clinton beat Trump here by four votes to two \u8211\'20\'13 this time the result chimes with what most polls say is an extremely close election and evenly divided electorate.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nevada is one of 10 states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is on the ballot \u8211\'20\'13 and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be a deciding issue in this key swing state.\par \par \uc2 Outside the library voting site on the University of Nevada Las Vegas campus, both Alexis Rivera-Valenzuela, 18, and his partner Jasmine Mata, 19 said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights were at top of mind as they cast their ballots.\par \par \uc2 Both voted for Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot measure, and for Kamala Harris \u8211\'20\'13 because she had promised to protect access.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump, who appointed three of the US supreme court justices who overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  and has branded himself as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most pro-life president\u8221\'20\'1D, could further restrict abortions or enact a de-facto national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban by prohibiting the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  medication and materials.\par \par \uc2 Rivera-Valenzuela said he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t too worried, as a Nevada resident. \u8220\'20\'1CIf Trump wins, he might change things at the federal level, but I think if we get the protections passed here, it won\u8217\'20\'19t matter as much what he does,\u8221\'20\'1D Rivera-Valenzuela said.\par \par \uc2 Sairy Cruz, 21, who was about to cast her first vote, said she hoped Harris would pull through in this deadlocked swing state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like a woman deserves to have the right to her own bodily autonomy, and no man should have a say in that. That\u8217\'20\'19s the bare minimum,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cruz. \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like as a person of color and also a woman, I\u8217\'20\'19d like to see another woman of color in the office.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Clark County, Nevada is a bellwether in this election \u8211\'20\'13 with polls showing Harris and Donald Trump virtually tied. About 50% of Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s electorate lives here, and they could determine the outcome in this key swing state.\par \par \uc2 Though several students said they weren\u8217\'20\'19t particularly worried. \u8220\'20\'1CTo be honest I\u8217\'20\'19m so focused on finals, so we don\u8217\'20\'19t have much time to really think about,\u8221\'20\'1D Cruz said. She had, however, avoided looking at the polls.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Las Vegas, Nevada:\par \par \uc2 The line of students waiting to vote snaked all around the third floor of the University of Nevada Lied library.\par \par \uc2 School staff were on hand to hand out candy, chips and drinks to have while they waited. The wait time was upwards of an hour, and students occasionally dipped out of line to sprint to class \u8211\'20\'13 with the intention of perhaps returning later.\par \par \uc2 Alexis Rivera-Valenzuela, 18, said it was quite a thrill when he finally cast his ballot. \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone cheered because I was a first time voter,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m feeling pretty good right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile Darcy Morales, 18, was bracing herself for the wait. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m nervous and I\u8217\'20\'19m excited,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s my first time, so I\u8217\'20\'19m just like, \u8216\'20\'18Oh am I making the right choices?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s planning on voting for Kamala Harris, as well \u8211\'20\'13 because she believes the vice president has better policies to address rising costs. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd the fact that she\u8217\'20\'19s a woman \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s also really exciting. It\u8217\'20\'19d be a really big change if she does end up winning the election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here some of the key images sent from the newswires on Election Day:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 When do the polls close tonight?\par \par \uc2 The first polls tonight will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/polls-open-close-election-day-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 close at }}}\uc2  6 pm ET and are in the eastern counties of Indiana and Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 At 7pm ET, polls will close in Georgia, South Carolina, Vermont, Virginia, parts of Florida, and the rest of Indiana and Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 Thirty minutes later, at 7:30pm ET, polls in North Carolina, Ohio and West Virginia will close.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2024/11/archive-zip/giv-45592QnBeLGClCqy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 At 8pm, polls will close in Alabama, Connecticut, Delaware, Illinois, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, the District of Columbia, Mississippi, New Hampshire, New Jersey, Oklahoma, Pennsylvania, Rhode Island, Tennessee, Missouri, parts of Michigan, North Dakota, South Dakota and Texas, and the whole of Florida.\par \par \uc2 By 9pm ET, polls will close in Arkansas, as well as Arizona, Colorado, Iowa, Kansas, Louisiana, Michigan, Minnesota, Nebraska, New Mexico, New York, Wisconsin, Wyoming, the whole of Texas, Michigan, South Dakota and North Dakota.\par \par \uc2 At 10pm ET, polls in Montana, Nevada and Utah will close. At 11pm ET, polls in California will close, as well as Idaho, Oregon and Washington.\par \par \uc2 At midnight ET, polls in Hawaii will close and finally, at 1am ET, polls will close in Alaska.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Voting enters final hours as Harris and Trump hope to win presidency\par \par \uc2 Hello {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics/all"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  readers and welcome to our live coverage of the 2024 election, where the first polls will close in about an hour on the east coast.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/when-do-polls-close-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hour-by-hour election guide }}}\uc2  for what to expect tonight and our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/03/us-presidential-election-trump-harris?utm_term=6729c276c3906b7cf98faaa95e62d016&utm_campaign=FirstEdition&utm_source=esp&utm_medium=Email&CMP=firstedition_email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 complete guide to everything you need to know}}}\uc2  about the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of the main developments so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Before the polls opened on Tuesday morning, more than 80 million Americans had already voted and cast early ballots, with just under 45 million voting early in person and about 38 million voting early by mail.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-6729b07e8f0842b343ae9fad#block-6729b07e8f0842b343ae9fad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tied with three votes}}}\uc2  each in Dixville Notch, the tiny New Hampshire town which traditionally kicks off voting on election day.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris, who voted by mail ahead of election day, made a surprise visit to the Democratic National Committee headquarters in Washington DC on Tuesday afternoon. Earlier she told a radio interview that her first order of business if elected would be \u8220\'20\'1Cbringing down the cost of living for folks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, Tim Walz, said the election was \u8220\'20\'1Crazor close\u8221\'20\'1D but said he was feeling \u8220\'20\'1Cgood about this.\u8221\'20\'1D America has \u8220\'20\'1Cthe fairest, the freest, the safest elections,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said as he visited a diner in Harrisburg, Pennsylvania earlier on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump and his wife, Melania, cast their ballots in Florida, earlier on Tuesday. Asked if he would call on his supporters not to engage in violence, Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have to tell them that there will be no violence,\u8221\'20\'1D adding his supporters \u8220\'20\'1Care not violent people\u8221\'20\'1D. He added that he felt \u8220\'20\'1Cvery confident\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, JD Vance, cast his ballot in Cincinnati, Ohio, earlier on Tuesday. Vance said his attitude \u8220\'20\'1Cis the best way to heal the rift in the country is to try to govern the country as well as we can\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The FBI said they are aware of bomb threats to polling locations in several states, many of which, they said, appear to \u8220\'20\'1Coriginate from Russian email domains\u8221\'20\'1D. The bureau said none of the threats have been determined to be credible thus far.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A man was arrested by US Capitol police officers during a screening process at the Capitol visitor center in Washington DC, police said. The man \u8220\'20\'1Csmelled like fuel\u8221\'20\'1D and had \u8220\'20\'1Ca torch\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ca flare gun\u8221\'20\'1D, police said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has been told by some advisers that he should prematurely declare victory on election night if he\u8217\'20\'19s sufficiently ahead of Harris in key battleground states like Pennsylvania, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/trump-declare-victory-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to people close to him, }}}\uc2  though whether he will heed that advice remains unclear.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241105ekb5003ph\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
