\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Millions of Americans cast their ballots \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now); Anna Betts, Hayden Vernon and Helen Livingstone (earlier) \par \uc2 22,234 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 November 2024\par 02:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 We are now closing this live blog. For all the latest news, results and reactions from US election day 2024, join us in our new live blogUS election 2024 \u8211\'20\'13 follow latest news liveUS election results 2024: live map and trackerWhen will we know the result of the US presidential election?\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Hello, election live blog readers, the country is abuzz and the first polls close at the top of the hour. Stick with the blog for all the news as this momentous evening and night unfolds, we\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you developments as they happen \u8211\'20\'13 24 hours a day.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Abbas Alawieh, one of the co-founders of the Uncommitted movement, which as a national group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/harris-uncommitted-movement-declines-endorse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to endorse}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  for the White House, has just told interviewers on MSNBC that he\u8217\'20\'19s voted for the vice-president in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this election}}}\uc2 . He said this \u8220\'20\'1Cis a moment of deep pain and frustration\u8221\'20\'1D over the war in Gaza and the ongoing sale of US weapons to Israel and yet he was \u8220\'20\'1Ctrying to do the politically savvy thing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the world\u8217\'20\'19s wealthiest person who has become \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s most prominent and powerful backer, cast his vote in Texas, in Cameron county, Texas, where his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/spacex"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SpaceX}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s headquarters are, near Hawthorne, a rural town north of Houston. Earlier in the day, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported that Musk would spend the evening of the election with Trump at Mar-a-Lago in Florida.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  made an unexpected stop at the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  headquarters in Washington DC this afternoon, where staffers and organizers were phone banking to get voters to the ballot boxes, in a last push before polls close. According to the reporters trailing her today, Harris arrived carrying a box of Doritos, her favorite campaign trail snack. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have so much work to do,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  said they are aware of bomb threats to polling locations in several states, many of which, they said, appear to \u8220\'20\'1Coriginate from Russian email domains\u8221\'20\'1D. The bureau said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fbi.gov/news/press-releases/fbi-statement-on-bomb-threats-to-polling-locations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  that none of the threats have been determined to be credible thus far. \u8220\'20\'1CElection integrity is among the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s highest priorities\u8221\'20\'1D the statement reads.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A man was arrested by US Capitol police officers at the Capitol visitor center in Washington DC, police said. The man \u8220\'20\'1Csmelled like fuel\u8221\'20\'1D and had \u8220\'20\'1Ca torch\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ca flare gun\u8221\'20\'1D when he was stopped by officers during a screening process at the center, police said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  spoke to reporters before boarding a plane from Pennsylvania to Washington DC during which the Democratic party vice-presidential nominee said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cfeeling good about this\u8221\'20\'1D election. He also pledged to \u8220\'20\'1Cshake hands and work for the winner\u8221\'20\'1D if Harris loses. Earlier he said the contest for the White House was \u8220\'20\'1Crazor close\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been told by some advisers that he should prematurely declare victory on election night if he\u8217\'20\'19s sufficiently ahead of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in key battleground states like Pennsylvania, according to people close to him, though whether he will heed that advice remains unclear. The consensus view is that Trump has nothing to lose by claiming he has won if he has a several-hundred-thousand-vote advantage in Pennsylvania or if his internal pollsters think a victory is plausible even if the results are not fully confirmed on Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Before the polls opened this morning, more than 80 million Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-672a18298f08cfd637216840#block-672a18298f08cfd637216840"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had already}}}\uc2  voted and cast early ballots, with just under 45 million voting early in person and about 38 million voting early by mail.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump and Harris have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-6729b07e8f0842b343ae9fad#block-6729b07e8f0842b343ae9fad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tied with three votes}}}\uc2  each in Dixville \uc2 Notch\uc2 , the tiny New Hampshire town which traditionally kicks off voting on election day.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trumpand his wife,Melania, voted in Florida, where he said he felt \u8220\'20\'1Cvery confident\u8221\'20\'1D. Asked if he would call on his supporters not to engage in violence, Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have to tell them that there will be no violence,\u8221\'20\'1D adding his supporters \u8220\'20\'1Care not violent people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate,JD Vance,{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-672a29da8f081ed2bfa20bd7#block-672a29da8f081ed2bfa20bd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cast his ballot}}}\uc2  in Cincinnati, Ohio, where he told reporters his attitude \u8220\'20\'1Cis the best way to heal the rift in the country is to try to govern the country as well as we can\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who voted by mail ahead of election day, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-672a3e0f8f08ec080b93fe52#block-672a3e0f8f08ec080b93fe52"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  her first order of business if elected to the White House would be \u8220\'20\'1Cbringing down the cost of living for folks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Georgia secretary of stateBrad Raffensperger said \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-credible\u8221\'20\'1D bomb threats that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-672a54308f0841bfc64a8116#block-672a54308f0841bfc64a8116"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 led to}}}\uc2  the temporary closure of two polling stations in Fulton county originated from Russia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 TheFBI warned Americans that two new fake videos bearing the agency\u8217\'20\'19s name and insignia were being \u8220\'20\'1Cmisused in promoting false narratives surrounding the election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A bipartisan coalition of 51 attorneys general across US states and territories {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-672a1fd58f08cfd63721688b#block-672a1fd58f08cfd63721688b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged}}}\uc2  people to remain peaceful and pre-emptively condemning \u8220\'20\'1Cany acts of violence related to the results\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Abbas Alawieh, one of the co-founders of the Uncommitted movement, which as a national group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/harris-uncommitted-movement-declines-endorse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to endorse}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  for the White House, has just told interviewers on MSNBC that he\u8217\'20\'19s voted for the vice-president in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this election}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrAbbas Alawieh, one of the co-founders of the Uncommitted movement, says he voted for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sH4EXVr8vd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/sH4EXVr8vd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yashar Ali ?? (@yashar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/yashar/status/1853909854295113988?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 He was also a delegate to the Democratic national convention (DNC) and was asked how he came to his decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a moment of deep pain and frustration. We are members of the Arab American, Muslim American community, for months have been oscillating between dealing with our grief, dealing with the fact that so many of our family members are there living under the bombs that the \uc2 US government\uc2  is sending \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , but also, trying to do the politically savvy thing,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CFor me personally, my decision, I see it as it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be Trump or Harris in the White House, and it\u8217\'20\'19s Harris voters, it\u8217\'20\'19s young voters, it\u8217\'20\'19s Black voters, anti-war voters all across our country who are going to be the coalition that hopefully pressures\u8221\'20\'1D the government.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  casts his vote in Texas\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s most prominent and powerful backer, cast his vote in Texas Tuesday. The billionaire CEO of \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  and \uc2 Tesla\uc2  tweeted, \u8220\'20\'1CJust voted in Cameron County, Texas, home of Starbase!\u8221\'20\'1D Starbase is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/spacex"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SpaceX}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s headquarters, near the US-Mexico border.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported that Musk would spend the evening of the election with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 enltrJust voted in Cameron County, Texas, home of Starbase! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dE8oRGlI4p"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dE8oRGlI4p}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  (@elonmusk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/1853906676476182960?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This post was amended on 5 November 2024. An earlier version misstated the location of \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s headquarters in Texas.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Democrats have been fearful of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/hamtramck-donald-trump-arab-american-muslim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 losing the vote}}}\uc2  of Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s large Arab American and Muslim American communities over the Biden-Harris administration\u8217\'20\'19s response to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel-hamas-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war on Gaza}}}\uc2 , and at a polling station in Dearborn there was some evidence that they were right to be concerned.\par \par \uc2 Although it was a small sample size, none of the Arab American voters the Guardian spoke to had voted for Harris \u8211\'20\'13 with her tepid response to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s actions clearly front of mind.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a Democrat, but I did not give my vote to Harris,\u8221\'20\'1D said Gus Tarraf, 51.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause my people are getting killed. I\u8217\'20\'19m Lebanese\u8230\'20\'26countries are being destroyed: Gaza, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/lebanon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lebanon}}}\uc2 . Why would I give my vote to her?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Arab American population in Michigan has typically voted Democratic, but Tarraf said he believes that this year Harris will only get \u8220\'20\'1C20%\u8221\'20\'1D of the community\u8217\'20\'19s vote. Tarraf has always been a Democratic voter himself \u8211\'20\'13 he voted for \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/nov/24/us-election-results-2020-joe-biden-defeats-donald-trump-to-win-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four years ago}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but he said the situation in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/middleeast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Middle East}}}\uc2  forced him to switch parties.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was a staunch supporter of Israel during his presidency, and has said little to suggest he will pursue a different strategy to Biden, but Tarraf said there was an urgency to the vote that meant the Republican could be the lesser of two evils.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now I have to think about this moment. At this moment Harris is helping with killing so why not try another one? You have one who killed your brother and sister and father. And one who they\u8217\'20\'19re saying is worse than her \u8211\'20\'13 but she killed. He hasn\u8217\'20\'19t killed yet. If he does the same thing next time, then we\u8217\'20\'19ll vote him out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Whitney Groenevelt is in an advanced placement federal government and politics class at her Florida high school, and the senior turned 18 in January.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of her first vote in a presidential election in Broward county, she has been watching \u8220\'20\'1Ca ton\u8221\'20\'1D of politics on television and the internet, and says she is excited to finally be able to take part in a process she has spent years studying.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know the way it\u8217\'20\'19s not supposed to work. There\u8217\'20\'19s not supposed to be a convicted felon in office. A convicted felon shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be able to vote,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referring to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 34 convictions}}}\uc2  from his hush money case in May.\par \par \uc2 Groenevelt, 18, said the preservation of democracy was among the two top election issues for her, the other being women\u8217\'20\'19s health and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Supporting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , she said, was the right thing to do.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI watched the debate, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve watched a ton of TV coverage from both left and right to try to get a balanced perspective,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris says 'we have so much work to do' during phone-banking session\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  made an unexpected stop at the DNC headquarters this afternoon, where staffers and organizers were phone banking in a last get out the vote push before polls close.\par \par \uc2 According to the reporters trailing her today, Harris arrived carrying a box of Doritos, her favorite campaign trail snack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is just the best, best, best and I thank you all very much,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 She walked over to a phone and picked it up.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am well,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CHave you voted already? You did? Thank you!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The room cheered.\par \par \uc2 She made another call, and it appeared a child had answered the phone.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 Waiting for you to grow 10 years more,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s so important, we have so much work to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Leaders of the Uncommitted National Movement, which has pushed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to take a tougher stance on Israel in response to the war in Gaza, described this election day as painful for anti-war voters \u8220\'20\'1Cwho feel let down by our party\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile our movement rejects a Trump presidency, the willful silence of Democratic Party leaders on Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s war crimes has left a void Trump is exploiting with dangerous lies and fraud,\u8221\'20\'1D said Layla Elabed and Abbas Alawieh, co-founders of the Uncommitted National Movement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCountless more people have been killed by the Israeli military as a result, and thousands of anti-war Democratic votes were recklessly left on the table in the process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In September, Uncommitted leaders decided {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/19/harris-uncommitted-movement-declines-endorse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 against}}}\uc2  endorsing Harris, accusing her of failing to meet their requests or do enough to push for a ceasefire in Gaza. However, they have also been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/arab-muslim-americans-vote-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urging their base}}}\uc2  to vote against Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe majority of Democrats and Harris voters oppose her stance on unrestricted weapons transfers fueling Israel\u8217\'20\'19s illegal actions,\u8221\'20\'1D the leaders said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf she wins, our plan is for this coalition to demand that she confront this moral and political catastrophe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris arrives at \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  headquarters in Washington DC\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has arrived at the headquarters of the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  in Washington DC to meet with staff and those who are phone banking for her campaign.\par \par \uc2 Harris spoke with several voters by phone, where she was overheard saying that it\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cso important that everybody participates\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Leona Green, an organizer with the Milwaukee grassroots group BLOC \u8212\'20\'14 Black Leaders Organizing Communities \u8212\'20\'14 has been knocking doors since 8 am.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDuring early voting, it was lovely \u8212\'20\'14 the line was majority young and first time voters,\u8221\'20\'1D said Green.\par \par \uc2 But she\u8217\'20\'19s been frustrated to hear from men on Election Day who \u8220\'20\'1Cfeel like a woman can\u8217\'20\'19t handle it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m getting that from a lot of males, and it\u8217\'20\'19s just crazy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Green. \u8220\'20\'1CThey think that women are too emotional, can\u8217\'20\'19t make decisions. It\u8217\'20\'19s shocking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Still, Green says she thinks young and women voters will outweigh the \u8220\'20\'1Cold school\u8221\'20\'1D views of certain men she\u8217\'20\'19s encountered while canvassing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m claiming it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  has arrested two men in Michigan in separate cases on suspicion of sending political threats online.\par \par \uc2 Isaac Sissel, 25, of Ann Arbor was arrested after allegedly threatening to commit a violent attack if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins the election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have a stolen ar15 [rifle] and a target I refuse to name so I can continue to get away with my plans,\u8221\'20\'1D Sissel allegedly wrote in a message that was sent anonymously to the \uc2 FBI\uc2  national threat operations center.\par \par \uc2 Sissel was arrested Tuesday morning and will appear in court Tuesday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Christopher Pierce, 46, of Jackson was arrested after allegedly ending threatening emails to a political action committee (PAC) fundraising for the election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Philadelphia Democratic party chair Robert Brady said turnout at the polling stations this morning was \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely high\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that a high turnout \u8220\'20\'1Cis great for us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Brady, a former Pennsylvania congressman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.insidernj.com/heavy-election-day-turnout-early-in-philadelphia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  Insider NJ that voter turnout on Tuesday morning was the \u8220\'20\'1Chighest we\u8217\'20\'19ve ever seen for this point in time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been doing elections for 50 years and I\u8217\'20\'19ve been chairman for 40 years and right now it\u8217\'20\'19s the highest we\u8217\'20\'19ve ever seen for this point in time,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 I spoke to a man gathering signatures for America PAC, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s outfit that\u8217\'20\'19s offering people $47 per person they get to sign a petition that supports the first and second amendments.\par \par \uc2 Those signers then can win a $1m prize.\par \par \uc2 The man, who said his name is Ryan Johnson, said he\u8217\'20\'19s been gathering signatures for various candidates and causes across the country for eight years, one of many traveling circulators who pop from state to state depending on who\u8217\'20\'19s paying.\par \par \uc2 He said the America PAC petition is the \u8220\'20\'1Chighest paying petition ever,\u8221\'20\'1D with a typical rate for signatures for a ballot measure or candidates being a few dollars per signature.\par \par \uc2 He claimed he has made upward of $30,000 on PAC signatures in the past 20 days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFirst of all, I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna put it in the bank and not touch it for 30 days to build the discipline of actually having it. And then once I see that it\u8217\'20\'19s there for 30 days, I\u8217\'20\'19ll allow myself to play with it a little bit,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo what I will do is I\u8217\'20\'19ll promote my business. I have a women\u8217\'20\'19s resale clothing business on \uc2 Poshmark\uc2 . I\u8217\'20\'19ll push that thing to go, because it already earns me about $40,000 a year. So if I can get that up to 100,000 a year just doing that, that\u8217\'20\'19d be super nice.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThank God for America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former New York mayor \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2  appeared outside \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s polling place in Palm Beach, Florida this morning before the Republican presidential candidate cast his ballot.\par \par \uc2 Giuliani showed up in the Mercedes convertible he was ordered to surrender to two Georgia poll workers he was found to have defamed in the aftermath of the 2020 election, the \uc2 Financial Times\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 enltrRudy Giuliani shows up to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s polling station in the Mercedes convertible he was ordered to surrender to Georgia poll workers for defaming them, acc to the driver. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/iA8D5vVL5m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/iA8D5vVL5m}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UU5CswnMQQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UU5CswnMQQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alex Rogers (@arogDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/arogDC/status/1853839248408883518?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Giuliani said Trump should go after \u8220\'20\'1Ctop people\u8221\'20\'1D if he was elected president, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d be willing to prosecute them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jocelyn Benson\uc2 , Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state, said that as of this morning, people in Michigan were already voting in record numbers.\par \par \uc2 Benson said at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MrZygyru_NI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a press conference }}}\uc2  on Tuesday that 3.3 million people in the state had already cast their ballot in this election before the polls even opened today, representing 45.8% of active registered voters in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re on track to break turnout records\u8221\'20\'1D Benson said.\par \par \uc2 Benson said unofficial results from the state of Michigan will begin to be reported shortly after 9pm ET tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  says non-credible bomb threats to polling locations appear to 'originate from Russian email domains'\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  said on Tuesday afternoon that they are aware of bomb threats to polling locations in several states, many of which, they said, appear to \u8220\'20\'1Coriginate from Russian email domains\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The bureau said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fbi.gov/news/press-releases/fbi-statement-on-bomb-threats-to-polling-locations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  that none of the threats have been determined to be credible thus far.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CElection integrity is among the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s highest priorities\u8221\'20\'1D the statement reads.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will continue to work closely with our state and local law enforcement partners to respond to any threats to our elections and to protect our communities as Americans exercise their right to vote\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Allentown, Pennsylvania:\par \par \uc2 Nearly every voter I\u8217\'20\'19ve spoken with today has said the economy is their top issue.\par \par \uc2 Tiana Peters, a 39-year-old underwriter from Allentown is a Democrat, but she voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . She also voted for Democrats in lower offices down the ticket.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe last four years, nothing really good happened,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CGiving away free money to the people that can\u8217\'20\'19t afford houses, financially that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t work, you know.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been wanting to buy a house for years now and \u8230\'20\'26 haven\u8217\'20\'19t been able to do that. It\u8217\'20\'19s just like half a million dollars for houses in the Lehigh Valley with four bedrooms. It\u8217\'20\'19s just not doable for a family making middle class money.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sharonda Casey, 47, came to vote with her son Jamel, 30, and her mother, Barbara, 72 -- three generations of her family. She said she voted for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . She {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/harris-propose-25k-payment-support-1st-time-homeowners/story?id=112877568"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited the assistance }}}\uc2  Harris has pledged for first time homebuyers as one of the reasons she voted for Harris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI got a granddaughter. I\u8217\'20\'19m not having more children unless it\u8217\'20\'19s baby Jesus \u8211\'20\'13 but I wanted to [vote] for her future and her right to go to the doctor and get care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  to spend election night with Trump \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  will spend election night with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at his Mar-a-Lago club in Palm Beach, Florida, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/11/05/us/politics/elon-musk-trump-election-night.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reporting,}}}\uc2  citing multiple sources.\par \par \uc2 The tech billionaire will be among a \u8220\'20\'1Csmall group\u8221\'20\'1D of people watching the election results with Trump as they come in, the paper writes.\par \par \uc2 Musk has spent at least $119m on a Super Pac supporting Trump and the two talk several times a week, it says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The voters in line to cast their ballots at the North Las Vegas city hall voting center Tuesday morning exemplified why Clark County, Nevada is such a bellwether in the election.\par \par \uc2 About half of all Nevada voters live in this region, in a key swing state where elections have been won and lost by exceptionally slim margins.\par \par \uc2 In a diverse city with a large proportion of non-partisan voters, locals were carrying deeply varied visions for the future with them as they headed to the polls.\par \par \uc2 Jimmy McDill, 49, who had dressed up for the occasion in a dashing lavender suit, said he was looking forward to voting for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 in large part because he believes she will help protect Medicare.\par \par \uc2 McDill, who is disabled, said he worries that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would slash medical benefits for low income and disabled Americans like him. A registered non-partisan, McDill said he has voted in every election since he was 18, and has supported candidates from both major political parties. Though he can\u8217\'20\'19t remember the last time he\u8217\'20\'19s backed a Republican for president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWas Hillary Clinton a Republican?\u8221\'20\'1D he said, laughing. \u8220\'20\'1CNo, no she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t. I just can\u8217\'20\'19t recall the last Republican, then.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Right in front of him in line, Patricia Bradley, 64, was also planning to cast a ballot for Harris. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was top of mind for her, and she was looking forward to voting for Harris and Democratic senator \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2 , both of whom have made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/21/idaho-abortion-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22reproductive rights\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  a key focus of their campaigns.\par \par \uc2 She was also planning to vote for Question 6, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/election-abortion-ballot-measures-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ballot initiative}}}\uc2  to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in the Nevada constitution. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m feeling kind of nervous,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we need to go do our parts today.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Idania Oliva, 45, who had come to vote with her mother and mother-in-law, said she was excited to vote for Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s for moral values,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. She is deeply opposed to abortions, and trusted Trump to restrict access, and secure the US southern border.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is for God,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd God is number one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Police arrest man trying to enter US Capitol who 'smelled like fuel' with 'flare gun'\par \par \uc2 A man was arrested by US Capitol police officers at the Capitol visitor center in Washington DC, police said.\par \par \uc2 The man \u8220\'20\'1Csmelled like fuel\u8221\'20\'1D and had \u8220\'20\'1Ca torch\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ca flare gun\u8221\'20\'1D when he was stopped by officers during a screening process at the center, police said.\par \par \uc2 Officials have canceled public tours of the Capitol for the remainder of the day.\par \par \uc2 enltrOur officers just arrested a man who was stopped during our screening process at the Capitol Visitor Center (CVC). The man smelled like fuel, had a torch & a flare gun.\par \par \uc2 The CVC is closed for tours for the day, while we investigate. We will provide more information when we can. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/J5geNud1h2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/J5geNud1h2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The \uc2 U.S. Capitol Police\uc2  (@CapitolPolice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CapitolPolice/status/1853869248562475086?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Allentown, Pennsylvania:\par \par \uc2 Eric Pitre Acevedo is Puerto Rican and was upset by the racist joke a comedian made at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s rally at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  late last month.\par \par \uc2 Acevedo still voted for Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel a little weird voting for him, but I still think he\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be a good president,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, standing outside a polling place in Allentown.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe believes in the family,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, expressing concern over how \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has handled transgender issues.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Harris Walz campaign says the vice-president has called into more drive-time radio stations in key battleground states, timing the interviews to the lunchtime hour to encourage Americans to vote.\par \par \uc2 Harris called into Wisconsin (101.7 The Truth in Milwaukee), Nevada (KCEP with Lady AK in Las Vegas), and Radio Campesina Network (which is based in Phoenix, Arizona, but is also carried in Nevada, among other states).\par \par \uc2 The campaign says she will do more radio call-ins later today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Walz says 'we're feeling good about this'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , spoke to reporters before boarding a plane from Pennsylvania to Washington DC during which he said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cfeeling good about this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walz said he has not spoken with Harris in the last 24 hours but praised her remarks at last night\u8217\'20\'19s final campaign rally in Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he believes that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will concede the election if he loses, Walz said he thought Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably will\u8221\'20\'1D concede.\par \par \uc2 He also pledged to \u8220\'20\'1Cshake hands and work for the winner\u8221\'20\'1D if Harris loses.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Advisers urge Trump to declare victory prematurely on election night\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been told by some advisers that he should prematurely declare victory on election night if he\u8217\'20\'19s sufficiently ahead of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in key battleground states like Pennsylvania, according to people close to him, though whether he will heed that advice remains unclear.\par \par \uc2 The consensus view is that Trump has nothing to lose by claiming he has won if he has a several-hundred-thousand-vote advantage in Pennsylvania or if his internal pollsters think a victory is plausible even if the results are not fully confirmed on Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 But even Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most pugnacious allies \u8211\'20\'13 including the former White House strategist \uc2 Steven Bannon\uc2  who spoke with him last week, one of the people said \u8211\'20\'13 have suggested he hold off making a pronouncement if the race is any closer by the time he goes to bed, lest it makes him look foolish.\par \par \uc2 In the final days of the campaign, Trump and his campaign have projected confidence. It has raised expectations among his supporters that he will win, laying the groundwork for baselessly claiming the election was stolen if he loses and Harris takes the White House. Any premature declaration of victory would also probably play into that phenomenon.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/trump-declare-victory-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Advisers urge Donald Trump to declare victory prematurely on election night}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after casting his ballot in West Palm Beach, Florida, with his wife, Melania.\par \par \uc2 Trump told reporters he felt \u8220\'20\'1Cvery confident\u8221\'20\'1D and that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cvery honored to find out the lines are long, the conservative lines, the Republican lines.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is spending the day at the Naval Observatory, the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s residence in Washington.\par \par \uc2 The public is not expected to see the Democratic nominee until later tonight, where she is poised to deliver remarks at \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , her alma mater, in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 After a sprint across Pennsylvania, Harris arrived at her residence hours before polls opened in the early hours of Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 She spent part of her day calling into radio stations in an eleventh-hour Get Out The Vote push for Americans on their way to work who hadn\u8217\'20\'19t yet cast a ballot. More radio interviews were scheduled for lunchtime and the drive home from work, before polls close.\par \par \uc2 Per her campaign, she has called into radio stations across three battleground states so far \u8211\'20\'13 Pennsylvania, Georgia and North Carolina. More are expected throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 Asked what her first order of business would be if she wins the election, Harris cited lowering costs \u8211\'20\'13 the top voting issue this cycle.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBringing down the cost of living for folks,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in an interview on NewsRadio KDKA, naming several of her economic proposals on housing, healthcare and the child tax credit. She also noted \u8220\'20\'1Cfixing what\u8217\'20\'19s going on with our broken immigration system,\u8221\'20\'1D an issues that has bedeviled presidents of both parties for decades.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Florida is no longer a swing state in terms of the presidential race, with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  holding a clear polling lead after winning it in 2016 and 2020.\par \par \uc2 But a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/19/debbie-mucarsel-powell-interview-democrat-florida-senate-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 potentially pivotal US Senate race}}}\uc2 , as well as amendments concerning the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/abortion-florida-amendment-4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 , and the legalization of recreational marijuana, are helping drive voters to the polls.\par \par \uc2 At JP Taravella high school in Coral Springs, Mackenzie Nezat, 18, was voting for the first time in a general election, and said women\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a key issue in her decision to support Democratic candidates, as well as the climate emergency and gun violence prevention.\par \par \uc2 Taravella is five miles from Marjory Stoneman Douglas high school, where 17 students and staff were killed in a 2018 mass shooting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s important to have a president that acknowledges the issue of climate change. All of us kids have to grow up with this. I want leaders who are willing to tackle it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I\u8217\'20\'19m not anti-gun, I want to be an owner for protection, but the way in which people can get them should be better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nezat, a first-year neuroscience student at Nova Southeastern University, said the character of a president was equally important to her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI care how a president talks, and that they uphold morals and positive values.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the latest images sent from the newswires across the country on election day:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 : result is 'razor close'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , said the election was \u8220\'20\'1Crazor close\u8221\'20\'1D as he visited a diner in Harrisburg, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRule of law matters, constitution matters, the American experiment matters, our neighbors matter,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd contrary to what this one guy thinks, nobody is above the damn law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStay calm. Stay with it,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, noting that America has \u8220\'20\'1Cthe fairest, the freest, the safest elections.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Nash county, North Carolina:\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ve come to talk to voters in Nash county, to the east of Raleigh, which will be closely watched tonight as it could provide one of the earliest clues as to who is prevailing.\par \par \uc2 In 2020 Nash was one of only 10 counties in the seven battleground states that flipped from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ; its count should be done by about 10.30pm ET.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m definitely pro-Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D said Randy Parrish, 65, smoking a cigarette in his car before he cast his ballot. He said he was unimpressed by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s had four years to fix things. It was just empty promises.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Asked whether he was anxious about the result, he said he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t. \u8220\'20\'1CI ain\u8217\'20\'19t that worried, because God\u8217\'20\'19s in control,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Local businessman John Tomaszewski, 55, had come to the polling place in the aptly named Spring Hope with his wife and daughter, all three of whom voted for Trump. He told a story to illustrate why he is behind the former president.\par \par \uc2 Before Trump entered the White House in 2017 he would buy plywood for the commercial cabinets he produces from China, as it was $15 per sheet cheaper. After Trump imposed tariffs on Chinese goods the sheets were only $4 cheaper and he could afford to buy American plywood.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want my man to win, of course, but I hope God will be in control of whoever wins because we need that back in our lives,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Amy Sharpe, 45, had just voted for \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . (She said she voted for Walz, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, not Harris herself, because she loves \u8220\'20\'1CCoach\u8221\'20\'1D as she called him. He\u8217\'20\'19s like everybody\u8217\'20\'19s grandpa\u8221\'20\'1D.)\par \par \uc2 As for Trump, \u8220\'20\'1Che\u8217\'20\'19s a lunatic. All that Hannibal Lecter stuff!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She works as a bar tender, and several months ago she laid down a new rule \u8211\'20\'13 no talking about politics. \u8220\'20\'1CIt has gotten physical so fast now, folk pushing and shoving and shouting. So I just said no more politics in the bar.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 Polls are open all across the country now as Americans cast their ballots for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in an election that has been cast as an existential fight for the country\u8217\'20\'19s future.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/when-do-polls-close-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hour-by-hour election guide }}}\uc2  for what to expect tonight. In the meantime, here\u8217\'20\'19s a recap of the main developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Before the polls opened this morning, more than 80 million Americans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-672a18298f08cfd637216840#block-672a18298f08cfd637216840"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had already }}}\uc2  voted and cast early ballots, with just under 45 million voting early in person and about 38 million voting early by mail.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump and Harris have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-6729b07e8f0842b343ae9fad#block-6729b07e8f0842b343ae9fad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tied with three votes}}}\uc2  each in Dixville \uc2 Notch\uc2 , the tiny New Hampshire town which traditionally kicks off voting on election day.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump and his wife, Melania, voted in Florida, where he said he felt \u8220\'20\'1Cvery confident\u8221\'20\'1D. Asked if he would call on his supporters not to engage in violence, Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have to tell them that there will be no violence,\u8221\'20\'1D adding his supporters \u8220\'20\'1Care not violent people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, JD Vance,{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-672a29da8f081ed2bfa20bd7#block-672a29da8f081ed2bfa20bd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cast his ballot}}}\uc2  in Cincinnati, Ohio, where he told reporters his attitude \u8220\'20\'1Cis the best way to heal the rift in the country is to try to govern the country as well as we can\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris, who voted by mail ahead of election day, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-672a3e0f8f08ec080b93fe52#block-672a3e0f8f08ec080b93fe52"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  said}}}\uc2  her first order of business if elected to the White House would be \u8220\'20\'1Cbringing down the cost of living for folks\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Georgia secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  said \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-credible\u8221\'20\'1D bomb threats that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-672a54308f0841bfc64a8116#block-672a54308f0841bfc64a8116"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 led to }}}\uc2  the temporary closure of two polling stations in Fulton county originated from Russia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  warned Americans that two new fake videos bearing the agency\u8217\'20\'19s name and insignia were being \u8220\'20\'1Cmisused in promoting false narratives surrounding the election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A bipartisan coalition of 51 attorneys general across US states and territories {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-672a1fd58f08cfd63721688b#block-672a1fd58f08cfd63721688b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged}}}\uc2  people to remain peaceful and pre-emptively condemning \u8220\'20\'1Cany acts of violence related to the results\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US Senate\uc2  candidate and Trump ally Kari Lake just stopped by a Scottsdale polling place and told voters waiting in line to \u8220\'20\'1Cstay in line.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Her supporters grabbed her for photos and cheered for her. \u8220\'20\'1CDid you vote?\u8221\'20\'1D she asked them. \u8220\'20\'1CDid you vote for Trump? Did you vote for Lake?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKari, you\u8217\'20\'19re the best!\u8221\'20\'1D one supporter cheered. \u8220\'20\'1CTell these jackals in the media,\u8221\'20\'1D she joked in response.\par \par \uc2 She got back on to a campaign bus emblazoned with \u8220\'20\'1Cmake Arizona grand again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrKari Lake just stopped by the Indian Bend Wash polling place. \u8220\'20\'1CStay in line!\u8221\'20\'1D she told the dozens of voters waiting to cast a ballot {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ONfxDuyz5M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ONfxDuyz5M}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rachel Leingang (@rachelleingang) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rachelleingang/status/1853851543583563945?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Allentown, Pennsylvania:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve just left a polling station in Allentown, which was much quieter than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-672a36e18f0841bfc64a7f49#block-672a36e18f0841bfc64a7f49"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the one I went to}}}\uc2  in nearby Bethlehem first thing this morning.\par \par \uc2 One the voters I spoke with was Felix Garcia, a 59-year old mechanic who is Puerto Rican. He said that the racist comments a comic made at a rally about the island wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t sway his vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI decided to vote for him because I\u8217\'20\'19m very concerned with the economy, the border. He said he can bring the companies to implement the jobs over here. I don\u8217\'20\'19t like the things they\u8217\'20\'19re teaching my kids in the school. A lot of bad things,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump didn\u8217\'20\'19t say [the racist comments about Puerto Rico at his \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally]. It\u8217\'20\'19s not coming from him. He came to work for all America, not only Puerto Ricans. Not only Black guys. All of them. And I\u8217\'20\'19m happy with that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another vocal Trump supporter was Jim Winburn, 62, who came out of the polling site and said, loudly, \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s already won.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRepublicans tell me what they\u8217\'20\'19re gonna do, they don\u8217\'20\'19t tell me what the problem with the other people is,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Georgia secretary of state says 'non-credible' bomb threats at two polling locations originated from Russia\par \par \uc2 Georgia secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  has confirmed that \u8220\'20\'1Cnon-credible\u8221\'20\'1D bomb threats made against two polling stations in Fulton county originated from Russia.\par \par \uc2 Two polling locations in Fulton county were briefly evacuated on Tuesday morning after they received false bomb threats, county election officials said. The threats targeted five polls in total, they said.\par \par \uc2 Raffensperger told reporters that the threats originated in Russia but did not elaborate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re up to mischief, it seems,\u8221\'20\'1D he said according to the Atlanta Journal-Constitution. \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t want us to have smooth, fair and accurate elections.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Voting has been extended in Cambria county, Pennsylvania, for an extra two hours, giving voters an extended time to return to cast their votes after a software malfunction earlier in the day, a court has ruled.\par \par \uc2 Cambria county commissioners filed an emergency request to extend its voting hours from 8pm ET to 10pm ET due to the malfunction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe [electronic voting system] software malfunction threatens to disenfranchise a significant number of voters,\u8221\'20\'1D the county board wrote in its court filing.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says his supporters 'are not violent people'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is asked if he will tell his supporters not to be violent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t have to tell them that there\u8217\'20\'19ll be no violence. Of course there will be no violence,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump tells reporters in Florida.\par \par \uc2 He says his supporters \u8220\'20\'1Care not violent people \u8230\'20\'26 these are people that believe in no violence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI certainly don\u8217\'20\'19t want any violence, but I certainly don\u8217\'20\'19t have to tell [these] great people,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he feels 'very confident'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , speaking to reporters after casting his ballot in Florida, was asked about the possibility that neither he nor \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  may reach 270 electoral votes by the end of tonight.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA thing like that should never happen,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican presidential candidate says. Trump says he wants to \u8220\'20\'1Cbring everybody in, we want to be very inclusive.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump says he feels \u8220\'20\'1Cvery confident\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that it looks like Republicans \u8220\'20\'1Chave shown up in force.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CI hear we\u8217\'20\'19re doing very well,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump casts ballot in Florida\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has arrived to vote in Palm Beach, Florida alongside his wife, Melania.\par \par \uc2 He told reporters he is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery honored\u8221\'20\'1D to find out that the lines are long. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the best campaign we\u8217\'20\'19ve run,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 His opponent, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , cast her vote by mail ballot to California.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2  warns over two fake videos spreading election misinformation\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  has warned Americans that two new fake videos bearing the agency\u8217\'20\'19s name and insignia are being \u8220\'20\'1Cmisused in promoting false narratives surrounding the election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fbi.gov/news/press-releases/fbi-statement-on-inauthentic-use-of-bureau-name-and-insignia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2  on Tuesday, the law enforcement agency said it is aware of a \u8220\'20\'1Cfabricated news clip purporting to be a terrorist warning issued by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D that urges Americans to \u8220\'20\'1Cvote remotely\u8221\'20\'1D, citing a high terror threat at polling stations.\par \par \uc2 The second video contains a fabricated \uc2 FBI\uc2  press release that claims \u8220\'20\'1Cfive prisons in Pennsylvania, Georgia, and Arizona rigged inmate voting and colluded with a political party,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 FBI\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Both videos are not authentic, the agency warned, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Celection integrity is among our highest priorities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAttempts to deceive the public with false content about \uc2 FBI\uc2  threat assessments and activities aim to undermine our democratic process and erode trust in the electoral system,\u8221\'20\'1D it added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The bellwether counties that could swing the election\par \par \uc2 With recent election polling showing a dead heat \u8211\'20\'13 or slim victory for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  within the statistical margin of error \u8211\'20\'13 seven swing states are all but certain to decide the race.\par \par \uc2 As pollsters scramble to make sense of these results, amid questions about reliability given bad calls over support for Trump in 2016 and 2020, analysts are taking an even more granular approach in interpreting battleground state voters, focusing on a handful of counties in these hotly contested regions.\par \par \uc2 They are often referred to as bellwether counties. This effectively means counties that could tip the scale in determining a swing state\u8217\'20\'19s outcome.\par \par \uc2 Here are the counties that analysts \u8211\'20\'13 ranging from seasoned election-watchers to Wall Street financiers \u8211\'20\'13 are focused on.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2024/11/archive-2-zip/giv-4559GLjOIEBjqpwa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-swing-state-counties"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Red or blue? The bellwether counties that could swing the US election}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This post was amended on 5 November 2024 to correct the spelling of Erie in the map.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Flooding has knocked out power to one Missouri polling site, made it hard for voters to reach another site and closed dozens of roads in the state.\par \par \uc2 More than 7in of rain have fallen in some areas over the past few days, Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Flood and flash flood warnings and watches have been issued across a large swath of Missouri, extending from its southwest corner to the St Louis area in the east.\par \par \uc2 In Jefferson county, the sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office warned that one polling site was not accessible by many people because of flooding.\par \par \uc2 In St Louis county, the weather flooded electrical equipment in one suburb, knocking out power to a church that is serving as a polling place, according to local media reports. Poll workers there are now running the elections using a generator, it said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here are some of photographs coming out of the wires as Americans head to the polls:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Scottsdale, Arizona:\par \par \uc2 Political signs littered the roadside entrance to a busy polling place in Scottsdale, Arizona, and more signs went up as voters arrived in the early morning hours to form a steady line \u8211\'20\'13 a visual representation of how coveted these voters are for races up and down the ballot.\par \par \uc2 The Indian Bend Wash polling location saw Republicans in Trump hats and shirts talking to voters outside, while Democrats handed out a voter guide to people as they walked to the line.\par \par \uc2 Turning Point USA brought out a bright pink party bus with \u8220\'20\'1CTrump train\u8221\'20\'1D signs on it, which will be used to take voters to other Scottsdale polling places if the lines become too long today. The group also put up signs imploring voters to stay in line: \u8220\'20\'1Cstay in line, don\u8217\'20\'19t leave your country behind,\u8221\'20\'1D one sign said.\par \par \uc2 A man was also gathering signatures for America Pac, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s group that is paying circulators to sign up other people who could win a $1m prize. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  needs our help,\u8221\'20\'1D the man told one voter.\par \par \uc2 We spoke to voters here who chose \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  or no one. Jesse Torrez, a 67-year-old independent, voted for Harris, both because of her ideology and because he said Trump did not have any character. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m thinking about my grandchildren and what they\u8217\'20\'19re going to need to face in the future and I just have no confidence in the Republican candidate\u8217\'20\'19s leadership or capabilities to lead this country. He\u8217\'20\'19s proven that to me,\u8221\'20\'1D Torrez said.\par \par \uc2 Jessica Mendoza, 35, voted for Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CI have two kids and I really just want to see a change for them and a better future,\u8221\'20\'1D she said \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re also Christians so we voted with our morals as well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris pledges to bring down cost of living if elected in radio interview\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.audacy.com/podcast/the-big-k-morning-show-8dd79/episodes/a-conversation-with-the-vice-president-of-the-united-states-d409f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called into}}}\uc2  The Big K Morning Show with Larry Richert on NewsRadio KDKA in Pittsburgh this morning.\par \par \uc2 Harris discussed the economy, immigration, the divide within the country, and more.\par \par \uc2 At one point, Harris said that if elected, her first order of business would be \u8220\'20\'1Cbringing down the cost of living for folks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have a package of plans that address that\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CEverything from what we need to do to create, for example of first time national ban on corporate price gouging on groceries, what we can do around tax credits for young families, tax credits and support for small businesses, including what we can do around a $25,000 down payment assistance for first time homebuyers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When asked about her plans for election day, Harris said she will be watching the results at her alma mater, \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , this evening.\par \par \uc2 Before that, she will be having dinner with her family, she said, noting that many relatives are staying with her.\par \par \uc2 Harris stated that throughout the day today she will be engaging with voters and encouraging them to make sure they get out to vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Will the Joe Rogan endorsement make a difference?\par \par \uc2 Joe Rogan has tended to present himself as receptive and open minded. He endorsed \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  in 2016, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020 and for much of this election he\u8217\'20\'19s been most receptive to the ideas of RFK Jr.\par \par \uc2 Now the most popular podcaster in history has decided to endorse \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But how much of a difference will it make?\par \par \uc2 In May, pollsters for the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 /Siena College {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/18/upshot/polls-trump-harris-young-men.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysed their data}}}\uc2  to see what were the key predictors for why a voter who supported \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020 might defect to the Republicans in 2024. They found that the No 1 predictor was whether the voter was born in the Middle East, a reflection of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 position on the war in Gaza. The No 2 predictor was whether they had a favorable view of Rogan. (Similar polling has not been done since Harris became the Democratic candidate.)\par \par \uc2 Research from the Young Men Research Initiative {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youngmenresearchinitiative.substack.com/p/new-survey-young-mens-trust-in-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from July}}}\uc2  also suggests that the timing of the endorsement \u8211\'20\'13 following a three-hour conversation with \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 could matter. 36% of young men they polled said they \u8220\'20\'1Cliked and generally trusted the views of\u8221\'20\'1D Rogan. Musk ranked even higher among the group, 45% said they liked and trusted him.\par \par \uc2 Musk appeared on Rogan\u8217\'20\'19s podcast yesterday to promote conspiracy theories about the Democratic party in a bid to convince Rogan to vote for Trump. He repeated a version of the \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat replacement\u8221\'20\'1D theory that if Democrats win the election Harris will \u8220\'20\'1Clegalize enough illegals\u8221\'20\'1D so that there will \u8220\'20\'1Cnever be another real election in the US again\u8221\'20\'1D. He said \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal migrants are literally being flown in to the swing states\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear how influential such a late endorsement will be, but there is probably a group of men who don\u8217\'20\'19t engage with traditional news sources for whom Musk\u8217\'20\'19s falsehoods \u8211\'20\'13 and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/trump-joe-rogan-interview-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appearance}}}\uc2  on the podcast last week \u8211\'20\'13 may be key to their decision.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.audacy.com/podcast/v-103-on-demand-67279/episodes/v-103s-big-tigger-morning-show-kamala-harris-e506a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  called into }}}\uc2  Atlanta radio station V-103\u8217\'20\'19s The Big Tigger Morning Show this morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe gotta get it done\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CToday is voting day and people need to get out and be active.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe wanna encourage everyone in Georgia to get out and vote,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding that her focus is \u8220\'20\'1Cmaking sure everybody knows the power of their voice through their vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from South Raleigh, North Carolina:\par \par \uc2 Lavar Turner, 46, who runs a burger joint, was also motivated to vote for Harris over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s role in overturning the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Also like Johnson, he had problems deciding.\par \par \uc2 Initially he was tempted to vote for Trump, but he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t sure. \u8220\'20\'1CSo I sat and prayed about it, and as I was praying Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s face came into my mind, and I knew she was the one.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to research her policies, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  especially, and was convinced that was the way to go. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t like them taking away women\u8217\'20\'19s rights \u8211\'20\'13 without women, men wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His wife, Beverly Turner, 51, had a more robust way of explaining her vote. \u8220\'20\'1CTrump can take his Project 2025 and shove it all the way up his ass.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Before we leave the polling station, we are given a lesson in the historical importance of the Black vote in the South. A 96-year-old Black woman walking by with the help of a frame stops to speak to us having just voted for Harris.\par \par \uc2 She is flanked by four generations of her family who have all done likewise.\par \par \uc2 The woman, who is dressed in a tweed, was too private to give her name. But she did share that she remembers growing up as a little girl under Jim Crow segregation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat was the law back then \u8211\'20\'13 being colored I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t vote,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from South Raleigh, North Carolina:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a steady flow of voters at a polling station in the Black neighborhood of South Raleigh. This is a key demographic for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 she needs to squeeze out every last vote if she is to take this neck-and-neck state.\par \par \uc2 Latoya Bailey, 38, who works in a shelter for homeless families, said she was all-in with Harris because of \u8220\'20\'1Chistory, representation and inclusion. I feel change can come if we all come together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Black women have been important to Democratic victories in recent cycles, and Bailey has done her part, holding watch parties for the presidential debates to try and engage relatives and neighbors. \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people in our community think our votes don\u8217\'20\'19t matters,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Male voters expressed having struggled with the decision. Marty A Johnson, 41, who hosts his own hip-hop {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/@themartyajohnsonshow"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 YouTube show}}}\uc2 , said until recently he was \u8220\'20\'1Cup in the air\u8221\'20\'1D about whether he would vote at all.\par \par \uc2 What swung it for him was when his son, who has just turned 18, told him he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t going to vote either. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I thought about my kid not voting, that felt wrong, and that inspired me to vote myself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He voted Harris, mainly because he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like what Trump has down to \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen and what they can do with their bodies\u8221\'20\'1D, he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Bethlehem, Pennsylvania:\par \par \uc2 At a polling site in Bethlehem, Pennsylvania, Joanne Kelchner, 77, called Trump a \u8220\'20\'1Cbig daddy\u8221\'20\'1D and said she voted for him. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19ll smack you if you\u8217\'20\'19re an asshole.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Debbie Probus, a retired 61-year-old, said she was undecided but ultimately decided to vote for Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of what\u8217\'20\'19s going on overseas. I figure he\u8217\'20\'19s a lot more authoritative. Even though he\u8217\'20\'19s not classy. He\u8217\'20\'19s a lot more authoritative and trying to keep people in line. I think Kamala is, in my opinion, too sweet, just from her way she projects on TV, she\u8217\'20\'19s always laughing like it\u8217\'20\'19s a game. It\u8217\'20\'19s not a game. And what\u8217\'20\'19s going on is terrible,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a bake sale going on at the school and lots of voters are walking out with pies and other baked goods. They are looking quite appealing this morning.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Bethlehem, Pennsylvania:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m here at a polling site in Bethlehem, Pennsylvania where voters have been coming out of a local school after counting their ballots.\par \par \uc2 Bethlehem is in Northampton county, which is considered a major bellwether of how Pennsylvania will go.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve spoken with seven voters so far, and five of them said they voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s strong. When you look at him he\u8217\'20\'19s a strong person. I mean he takes action on what he does. The way he speaks, everything about him. I feel like he\u8217\'20\'19s gonna stand up for our country and make it strong again,\u8221\'20\'1D said Stephen Super, a first-time voter.\par \par \uc2 Jake Moser, 22, another voter, said he voted for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think a large part of it is ethics. It was really tough for me to vote for somebody who had said so many negative things about the American people. I think the thing about being president is that being in that office means that you need to bring people together and not push them away. And I think dividing the country is just something that personally I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t agree with. So that\u8217\'20\'19s why I voted for Kamala,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Reporting from Saginaw, Michigan:\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign might find some satisfaction in a Guardian straw poll of voters in one part of the bellwether county of Saginaw in swing state Michigan.\par \par \uc2 More than 30 people lined up in the dark on a wet morning outside the Bethel AME church before the polls even opened, mostly to be able to vote and get to work on time.\par \par \uc2 Of the first dozen women to vote, nine said that women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, and access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in particular, was their primary issue. The other three mentioned it alongside the economy and fear about what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would do if he is returned to power.\par \par \uc2 Among them was Cheyanne Laux.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump obviously has proven in the past that he clearly doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the rights of women in his mind. The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue, that\u8217\'20\'19s the main thing for me, so voting Democratic lines up with keeping that right,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign has flooded the airwaves in Michigan and other battleground states with ads attacking Trump as a continuing threat to women\u8217\'20\'19s rights in the hope of persuading ambivalent female voters to go to the polls or women who have previously voted Republican to switch sides.\par \par \uc2 Laux said she thought the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s striking down of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights would be decisive for a lot of other female voters in this election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been seeing the repercussions from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actions against the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since it happened a couple years ago. It\u8217\'20\'19s a constant thing that I keep seeing. So I definitely think that\u8217\'20\'19ll be a driver for young women, for sure,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Deborah Adams said she was particularly disturbed that, even though Michigan recently enshrined \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution, other states have passed laws criminalising terminations in almost every case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel that a person shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have control over a woman\u8217\'20\'19s body. I got a daughter. I got granddaughters. If it\u8217\'20\'19s a matter of life or death, and they\u8217\'20\'19re stopping doctors from doing what they got to do, to me that\u8217\'20\'19s evil stuff,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 enltrPeople lined up to vote before the polls opened on a rainy Michigan morning at the Bethel AME Church in swing county Saginaw. Of the first dozen women who voted, nine told me that access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was their primary issue and the other three mentioned mentioined it as a factor. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tlwENORjP7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tlwENORjP7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris McGreal (@ChrisMcGreal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ChrisMcGreal/status/1853801166322213229?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The first election results came in early this morning, from the tiny village of Dixville \uc2 Notch\uc2 , in New Hampshire, which has a population of six residents.\par \par \uc2 The results ended in a deadlock: three votes to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and three for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Read more about Dixville \uc2 Notch\uc2  here.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/first-us-election-result-three-all-tie-trump-and-harris-dixville-notch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 First US election result is three-all tie between Trump and Harris}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Americans in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 10 states }}}\uc2  are voting this election on whether to enshrine the right to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  into their state constitutions.\par \par \uc2 The states include Florida, Colorado, Maryland, Arizona, Montana, Nebraska, Missouri, Nevada, New York and South Dakota.\par \par \uc2 Read about the proposed ballot measures in each state here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/05/abortion-ballot-results-tracker-ban-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ten states where \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights are on the ballot this election day}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 When do the polls close tonight?\par \par \uc2 The first polls tonight will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/polls-open-close-election-day-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 close at }}}\uc2  6 pm ET and are in the eastern counties of Indiana and Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 At 7pm ET, polls will close in Georgia, South Carolina, Vermont, Virginia, parts of Florida, and the rest of Indiana and Kentucky.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2024/11/archive-zip/giv-45592QnBeLGClCqy/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 Thirty minutes later, at 7:30pm ET, polls in North Carolina, Ohio and West Virginia will close.\par \par \uc2 At 8pm, polls will close in Alabama, Connecticut, Delaware, Illinois, Maine, Maryland, Massachusetts, the District of Columbia, Mississippi, New Hampshire, New Jersey, Oklahoma, Pennsylvania, Rhode Island, Tennessee, Missouri, parts of Michigan, North Dakota, South Dakota and Texas, and the whole of Florida.\par \par \uc2 By 9pm ET, polls will close in Arkansas, as well as Arizona, Colorado, Iowa, Kansas, Louisiana, Michigan, Minnesota, Nebraska, New Mexico, New York, Wisconsin, Wyoming, the whole of Texas, Michigan, South Dakota and North Dakota.\par \par \uc2 At 10pm ET, polls in Montana, Nevada and Utah will close. At 11pm ET, polls in California will close, as well as Idaho, Oregon and Washington.\par \par \uc2 At midnight ET, polls in Hawaii will close and finally, at 1am ET, polls will close in Alaska.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/when-do-polls-close-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When do polls close on election day, Tuesday, 5 November 2024?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bernard Marcus, the billionaire \uc2 Home Depot\uc2  co-founder and a Republican {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2017/05/21/politics/bernie-marcus-donor-profile/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 megadonor}}}\uc2 , has died, the company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://corporate.homedepot.com/news/company/remembering-bernie-marcus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  today.\par \par \uc2 In a statement on Tuesday from the \uc2 Home Depot\uc2  company, Marcus was described as an \u8220\'20\'1Cinspiration\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Ca master merchant\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ca genius with customer service\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1DMore than anything, he deeply believed in the company\u8217\'20\'19s core values, particularly that of giving back\u8221\'20\'1D the statement reads. \u8220\'20\'1CHe never lost sight of his humble roots, using his success not for fame or fortune but to generously help others. In business and in charity, Bernie was unparalleled in generosity and goodwill.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In recent years, Marcus has been an outspoken supporter of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Republicans.\par \par \uc2 He has donated millions of dollars to the campaigns of various Republican politicians, including the late \uc2 John McCain\uc2 , current Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , and Trump, as reported by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/11/05/business/home-depot-bernie-marcus-death/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nypost.com/2023/11/04/news/why-home-depots-bernie-marcus-says-hes-particularly-p-ssed-off/?utm_campaign=iphone_nyp&utm_source=pasteboard_app"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview last year,}}}\uc2  Marcus criticised President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , calling him the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost divisive president we\u8217\'20\'19ve ever seen\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/profile/bernard-marcus/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Forbes}}}\uc2 , Marcus\u8217\'20\'19 net worth was approximately $11bn.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 JD Vance casts his ballot in Ohio\par \par \uc2 Republican vice-presidential candidate JD Vance cast his ballot in-person {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Reuters/status/1853799746915491980"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this morning at his polling place }}}\uc2  in Cincinnati, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 CNN reported that the Ohio senator \u8220\'20\'1Cappeared in good spirits\u8221\'20\'1D as he arrived at Saint Anthony of Padua church to vote. Vance was with his wife, Usha, and their children.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do expect to win\u8221\'20\'1D Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/taylorwoodstv/status/1853804585468453170/video/1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told reporters }}}\uc2  outside the polling station. \u8220\'20\'1CBut obviously no matter who wins, half the country is gonna be at least partially disappointed, I think my attitude is the best way to heal the rift in the country is to try to govern the country as well as we can.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A coalition of current and former local, state, and national bar association presidents published a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://democracy-taskforce.org/past-bar-leaders-letter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter}}}\uc2  on Monday night ahead of the election, reminding lawyers and the public that the courtroom is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a theater for unsubstantiated claims \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The letter cautions and urges fellow lawyers filing election-related lawsuits this election against presenting false information in their court filings.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFiling election-related lawsuits without a solid factual and legal foundation endangers the very institutions lawyers are oathbound to defend\u8221\'20\'1D the letter states. \u8220\'20\'1CIn a functioning democracy, lawsuits are not weapons to spread distrust \u8211\'20\'13 they are tools for justice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After the 2020 election, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his team of lawyers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/nov/10/donald-trump-longshot-election-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  filed numerous lawsuits}}}\uc2  in various states, claiming fraud in the election.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuits were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/republicans-donald-trump-polls-us-election-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overwhelmingly unsuccessful }}}\uc2  and several lawyers connected to the cases were disbarred or had their licenses suspended, the coalition of lawyers wrote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese lawyers not only lost their licenses and tarnished their reputations, they also betrayed their communities and the American public,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter adds.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Voting under way in most of US, including all battleground states\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s just gone 9am Eastern Time, and voting is under way in most states across the country.\par \par \uc2 As of 9am ET, voting is now open in Arizona, Iowa, Oklahoma, Texas, Colorado, Wisconsin, Tennessee, Nebraska, Arkansas, New Mexico, Utah, Mississippi, some areas of Minnesota, Montana, North Dakota and South Dakota.\par \par \uc2 This is in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-672a01a78f081ed2bfa209d2#block-672a01a78f081ed2bfa209d2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 addition to the polling sites that opened earlier this morning}}}\uc2 , which included Alabama, Delaware, the District of Columbia, Florida, Georgia, New Hampshire, Illinois, Indiana, Kansas, Louisiana, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan, Missouri, Pennsylvania, Rhode Island, Rhode Island and Wyoming.\par \par \uc2 In an hour, election day voting will open in California and Idaho. At 11am ET, voting will open in Washington and Alaska, and polling stations will open in Hawaii at noon ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 This morning, some individuals are reporting delays and issues at polling stations, such as machines {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Jacob_Kaye_/status/1853789847552495701"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  not accepting ballots}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KevinLighty/status/1853780237798015115"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 systems being down}}}\uc2  at polling stations.\par \par \uc2 In Wayne county, Ohio, the local board of elections {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/WayneCoBOE/status/1853792562881908741"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  on Tuesday morning that they experienced some equipment issues at the Kidron Community Center polling station. Although voters were still processed, these problems resulted in some delays.\par \par \uc2 By 8.30am ET, Wayne county officials reported that the issues had been resolved, and the polling location was \u8220\'20\'1Cback to full force\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Attorneys general issue statement urging \u8216\'20\'18peaceful transfer of power\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A bipartisan coalition of 51 attorneys general across US states and territories released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.naag.org/press-releases/attorneys-general-issue-bipartisan-statement-condemning-possible-violence-in-response-to-election-results/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2  on Tuesday urging people to remain peaceful and pre-emptively condemning \u8220\'20\'1Cany acts of violence related to the results\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A peaceful transfer of power is the highest testament to the rule of law, a tradition that stands at the heart of our nation\u8217\'20\'19s stability. As Attorneys General, we affirm our commitment to protect our communities and uphold the democratic principles we serve.\par \par \uc2 We call upon every American to vote, participate in civil discourse and, above all, respect the integrity of the democratic process,\u8221\'20\'1D they wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CViolence has no place in the democratic process; we will exercise our authority to enforce the law against any illegal acts that threaten it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  expected to vote in person in Florida before Palm Beach watch party\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is planning to spend the day in Florida, where he is expected to vote in person, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/live/trump-harris-election-updates-11-5-2024#00000192-fc6b-dc56-a39e-fd6fe9c40000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This evening, the Trump campaign will host an election night watch party in West Palm Beach, Florida.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , along with his wife, Gwen Walz, will take part in a political event this morning in Harrisburg, Pennsylvania, according to the Harris campaign.\par \par \uc2 Later in the evening, the Harris-Walz campaign is scheduled to host an election night event at \uc2 Howard University\uc2  in Washington DC, the alma mater of Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will watch election results in the White House\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will watch the election results from the White House residence alongside first lady Jill Biden, longtime aides, and senior White House staff, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/2024-election-trump-harris#cm34fyp1v00053b6o6xh1b5jd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden does not have any public events scheduled for today and is expected to receive regular updates as races are reported nationwide.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 About 80m Americans voted early in 2024 election\par \par \uc2 Before the polls opened this morning, about 80 million Americans had already voted and cast early ballots.\par \par \uc2 According to the Election Lab at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://election.lab.ufl.edu/early-vote/2024-early-voting/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the University of Florida}}}\uc2 , 82 million Americans voted early, with just under 45 million voting early in person and about 38 million voting early by mail.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  has told \uc2 CBS\uc2  that the now infamous Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cwar room\u8221\'20\'1D will be revived at the Willard Hotel in Washington DC tonight.\par \par \uc2 Key members of the Trump campaign, including Bannon, were in the hotel on 6 January 2021, as the Capitol insurrection unfolded nearby.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jul/07/next-jan-6-hearing-trump-far-right-militias"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 That \u8220\'20\'1Cwar room\u8221\'20\'1D had specific goals}}}\uc2  : to help pressure then vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  to refuse to certify Biden\u8217\'20\'19s election win and send it to the House of Representatives in a contingent election, or failing that, delay the joint session beyond 6 January 2021.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnlike in 2020, we will secure Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory this time,\u8221\'20\'1D Bannon told \uc2 CBS\uc2  today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 An Indiana journalist reported issues with voting in Hamilton county that now appear to be fixed.\par \par \uc2 Angela Ganote said technical issues had delayed voting for about 17 minutes across the county.\par \par \uc2 enltrWe just spoke with the election board.\par \par \uc2 They told us that the Sheridan voting locations received a new code for the voting machines. It was put into and left in all machines around the county.\par \par \uc2 All someone had to do was push a button to fix it.\par \par \uc2 The issue has been fixed AT ALL\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/f006kLaVQj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/f006kLaVQj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Angela Ganote (@angelaganote) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/angelaganote/status/1853765916665790527?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania has 19 electoral votes \u8211\'20\'13 the most of any swing state \u8211\'20\'13 and the pathway to getting 270 electoral votes winning the election is more complicated for the candidate who does not win it.\par \par \uc2 Both \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  crisscrossed the state during the final week of campaigning and yesterday held rallies about an hour apart in the Lehigh valley, one of the most competitive parts of the state. Harris dedicated the entirety of the final day of the campaign to Pennsylvania, making four stops in the state.\par \par \uc2 Residents in the state have spoken about wielding the power of a vote that could decide the election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m quite terrified,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sonny Berenson, 20, a student at Muhlenberg college who attended Harris\u8217\'20\'19s rally there on Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is probably the most contentious election in American history and we\u8217\'20\'19re living in a state that can decide it. So I feel very powerful and very scared, but obviously I hope and pray Kamala wins.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Danielle Shackelford, 68, a worker for the Pennsylvania lottery from Allentown, said she was optimistic Harris would win. She said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a top issue for her and that there were many women who were silently supporting Harris over the issue. \u8220\'20\'1CThey are fighting with everything inside of them to fight against what has been put out there,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat Trump has done, he has unleashed the wrath of women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rene Diaz, Jr, a 36-year-old machinist said his top issues this election were the economy, foreign policy and the border. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are drowning in so much debt that we shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be helping fight two wars and sending countries to fight two wars and help fund other programs,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI have children and it\u8217\'20\'19s important that my children get to grow up with the life that I have.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Slaby, an 81-year-old from Allentown, arrived at Harris\u8217\'20\'19s rally in Allentown at 6.00am on Monday with her son and grandson. She said that she had been a Republican for more than 50 years but changed her registration five days after January 6.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/pennsylvania-voters-harris-trump-swing-state-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I feel very powerful and very scared\u8217\'20\'19: Pennsylvanians face pressure of voting in key swing state}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s 5 November today \u8211\'20\'13 a day when the British traditionally let off fireworks to celebrate the foiling of the plot by Guy Fawkes to blow up parliament and kill King James I over four hundred years ago.\par \par \uc2 Marina Hyde has written a bit comparing Britain\u8217\'20\'19s own insurrectionist to someone more contemporary \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/nov/05/donald-trump-us-election-fifth-november-guy-fawkes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Remember, remember, the fifth of November, when a bad guy tried to blow up a political system | Marina Hyde}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 And here is some footage of those first in-person votes getting underway:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the first images coming out of the wires as polls open:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls open in swath of states across the US\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s just gone 7am Eastern Time and voting has just begun in a number of states across the US, including in the battleground states of Georgia, Pennsylvania and Michigan (some sites open at 8am ET).\par \par \uc2 Voting has also opened in: Alabama, Delaware, District of Columbia, Florida (8am ET in parts of the Florida Panhandle on Central time), New Hampshire (Opening times vary by county with the earliest starting at 7am ET), Illinois, Indiana, Kansas (Varies by county; check with your local election office for polling hours), Louisiana, Maryland, Massachusetts, Missouri, Rhode Island (Polls in New Shoreham open at 9am ET), South Carolina and Wyoming.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Alarm grows over Trump and Musk's false voting claims\par \par \uc2 Alarm is growing over the blizzard of false voting misinformation being peddled by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his top allies, such as \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Reprising his 2020 playbook of claiming that Democrats were trying to steal the election before he lost to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and cried fraud, Trump has flatly and without evidence declared that Democrats are a \u8220\'20\'1Cbunch of cheats\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Musk has become a leading purveyor of falsehoods and conspiracies to his 200 million followers on X, the social media platform he owns.\par \par \uc2 Musk, the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man, has asserted without evidence that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign is heading for a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrushing victory\u8221\'20\'1D over Harris, and been chastised by key election officials in Arizona and Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Besides Musk, other key Trump allies such as Turning Point USA chief Charlie Kirk have reached their large rightist audiences via podcasts and public events and pushed bogus claims about Democratic election fraud.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/trump-musk-election-voter-fraud-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alarm grows over Trump and Musk\u8217\'20\'19s blizzard of baseless voter-fraud claims}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 The race to become the 47th president of the United States is on a razor-thin margin, pollster \uc2 John Zogby\uc2  writes.\par \par \uc2 Three of the final last six public polls were ties; one has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  ahead by three points; the others have \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  up by one point and two points.\par \par \uc2 My own firm, John Zogby Strategies, just released a final survey for our clients of 1,005 decided voters nationwide showing Harris leading with 49.3% of the vote and Trump polling at 45.6% of the vote \u8211\'20\'13 a margin, or difference, of 3.7 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 That is close, and even more of a squeeze because of the current relationship of the popular vote to the electoral college. Harris is certain to receive millions of \u8220\'20\'1Cexcess\u8221\'20\'1D votes in large states such as California, New York, Illinois and Massachusetts which will beef up her total popular vote nationwide but not do anything for her in key battleground states such as Arizona, Nevada, Georgia, North Carolina, Pennsylvania, Michigan and Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 all of which are too close to call as we approach election day.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/nov/05/elections-polling-data-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here is what our final polling data says about the US presidential election | John Zogby}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hindustantimes.com/topic/donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  staffer who worked as a regional field director for the western Pennsylvania Republican party was fired on Friday after it was revealed that he was a white supremacist, Lorenzo Tondo reports.\par \par \uc2 Politico reported it had identified Luke Meyer, 24, a Pennsylvania-based field staffer who worked for five months for the former president, as the online white nationalist who used the pseudonym Alberto Barbarossa.\par \par \uc2 Meyer reportedly co-hosts the Alexandria podcast with \uc2 Richard Spencer\uc2 , the organiser of the 2017 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/02/white-supremacists-unite-the-right-rally-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 white nationalist Unite the Right rally}}}\uc2  in Charlottesville, Virginia and regularly shared racist views.\par \par \uc2 After being presented with evidence by Politico linking him to the Barbarossa alias, Meyer admitted the connection and confessed that he had been concealing his online identity from fellow members of Trump Force 47, the arm of the Trump campaign overseeing volunteer mobilisation efforts.\par \par \uc2 More here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/trump-staffer-fired-from-republican-party-for-being-a-white-supremacist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump staffer fired from Republican party for being a white supremacist}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s extremely unlikely that we\u8217\'20\'19ll know the winner of the presidential contest tonight, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are virtually tied in the polls, and the odds that the race comes down to a small number of swing states is high, so when will we find out?\par \par \uc2 It depends on how close things turn out to be. Four swing states \u8211\'20\'13 Arizona, Nevada, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 have absentee ballot procedures that can require days to conclude. But if Harris has decisively won the other swing states, it is enough to declare her the victor. Any other result will take time.\par \par \uc2 Last time round, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was declared the winner on Saturday 7 November \u8211\'20\'13 four days after the election. The president crossed the electoral vote threshold that day when media outlets called Pennsylvania and Nevada. Michigan and Wisconsin were both called the day after the election, but Arizona wasn\u8217\'20\'19t called until 12 November, North Carolina until 13 November, and Georgia on 19 November, after a recount.\par \par \uc2 What about this time? According to Protect Democracy, a non-partisan group, we\u8217\'20\'19ll generally see results faster than in 2020 if the margin in a state is greater than 0.5%. They draw this conclusion because there will be significantly fewer mail ballots than in 2020, and states will be able to count them faster. Three states also expanded the pre-canvassing of mail ballots before election day that didn\u8217\'20\'19t in 2020 (Arizona, Georgia and Michigan) and three states have an earlier deadline for when mail ballots must arrive than they did in 2020 (North Carolina, Nevada and Pennsylvania).\par \par \uc2 Protect Democracy said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://protectdemocracy.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Vote-Count-Expectations-2024.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent report}}}\uc2  that its best guess was that results will be called in Michigan and Wisconsin one full day after polls closed \u8211\'20\'13 the same speed as 2020. It also guesses that Pennsylvania will be called faster than in 2020, when it took four days; Nevada will be called in the same amount of time or faster than 2020, when it took four days and Arizona will also be called in the same amount of time or faster than 2020, when it took nine days. North Carolina and Georgia will both be called faster than 2020, the organisation guesses.\par \par \uc2 You can read more about when and how we will find out who the next US president is in the story below:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/harris-trump-election-results-when"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election results: when will we know who is the next president?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 US election under way in Vermont\par \par \uc2 The US election is officially under way. Polls opened in certain locations in Vermont at 5am Eastern Time, so about 50 minutes ago.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/polls-open-close-election-day-2024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS}}}\uc2 , here\u8217\'20\'19s when polls open across the country:\par \par \uc2 6am ET \u8211\'20\'13 Connecticut, Kentucky (Polling sites in the west open at 7 a.m. ET), Maine (Polling locations open between 6 a.m. and 10 a.m. depending on town population), New Jersey, New York, Virginia.\par \par \uc2 6.30am ET \u8211\'20\'13 North Carolina, Ohio, West Virginia\par \par \uc2 7am ET \u8211\'20\'13 Alabama, Delaware, District of Columbia, Florida (8am ET in parts of the Florida Panhandle on Central time), Georgia, New Hampshire (Opening times vary by county with the earliest starting at 7am ET), Illinois, Indiana, Kansas (Varies by county; check with your local election office for polling hours), Louisiana, Maryland, Massachusetts, Michigan (Polling sites in four Upper Peninsula counties open at 8am ET), Missouri, Pennsylvania, Rhode Island (Polls in New Shoreham open at 9am ET), South Carolina, Wyoming\par \par \uc2 8am ET \u8211\'20\'13 Arizona, Iowa, Minnesota (Counties with a population of less than 500 are not required to open until 11am ET), Mississippi, Oklahoma, North Dakota (Polls start opening at 8am ET and vary by county), South Dakota (Polling locations in the west open at 9am ET), Tennessee, Texas (Polling sites in three western counties open at 9am ET), Wisconsin\par \par \uc2 8.30am ET \u8211\'20\'13 Arkansas\par \par \uc2 9am ET \u8211\'20\'13 Colorado, Montana (Polling sites in counties with less than 400 registered voters can open as late as 2pm ET), Nebraska, Nevada (Polling sites open at 10am ET with the exception of City Hall in West Wendover), New Mexico, Utah\par \par \uc2 10am ET \u8211\'20\'13 California, Idaho (Polling locations in the north open at 11am ET)\par \par \uc2 11am ET \u8211\'20\'13 Washington (Most voting is done by mail, so times vary by county), Alaska (Polling sites open at 11am ET with the exception of Adak)\par \par \uc2 12pm ET \u8211\'20\'13 Hawaii\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/when-do-polls-close-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polls then begin to close}}}\uc2  in eastern states from 6pm US Eastern Time on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Candidates close election campaign with competing visions for future of US\par \par \uc2 As the election campaign drew to a close last night, the candidates laid out their competing visions for the destiny of America. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attacked his critics and vilified migrants, while \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  laid out a positive vision for America.\par \par \uc2 Harris was in Pennsylvania, the biggest swing state and crucial to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic}}}\uc2  campaign. She held the final rally of her campaign at the steps of the \uc2 Philadelphia Museum of Art\uc2 , made famous by a scene in the film Rocky. Introduced by \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2  and Lady Gaga, Harris emphasised her message of hope. \u8220\'20\'1CWe finish, as we started, with optimism, with energy, with joy,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to get to work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump struck a darker tone in the same state, with threats to put trade tariffs on all imports from Mexico unless it stopped people from entering the US. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican}}}\uc2  candidate also held hours-long events in North Carolina and Michigan, wrapping up at about 2am local time.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a video round-up of the final campaign push by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republican lawyer seeks to unseat Georgia prosecutor who brought charges against Trump\par \par \uc2 A Republican lawyer who interned in the White House under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is challenging Fulton County district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2 , the Georgia prosecutor who brought charges against the former president over efforts to overturn the 2020 presidential election, AP reports.\par \par \uc2 Courtney Kramer worked in the White House counsel\u8217\'20\'19s office during the Trump presidency and is active in GOP organisations. She\u8217\'20\'19s the first Republican to run for district attorney in Fulton County since 2000.\par \par \uc2 Fulton County, which is home to 11% of the state\u8217\'20\'19s electorate and includes most of the city of Atlanta, is a Democratic stronghold.\par \par \uc2 Willis took office in January 2021 after beating her predecessor \u8212\'20\'14 and former boss \u8212\'20\'14 longtime district attorney Paul Howard in a bitter Democratic primary fight in 2020.\par \par \uc2 She made headlines just a month into her tenure when she announced in February 2021 that she was investigating whether Trump and others broke any laws while trying to overturn his narrow loss in the state to Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Two and a half years later, after an investigation that included calling dozens of witnesses before a special grand jury, she obtained a sprawling racketeering indictment against Trump and 18 others in August 2023.\par \par \uc2 Four people have pleaded guilty after reaching deals with prosecutors. Trump and the remaining defendants have all pleaded not guilty to the charges against them.\par \par \uc2 When she entered the district attorney\u8217\'20\'19s race in March, Kramer said the Trump prosecution was a politically motivated case and a waste of resources. She said if she becomes district attorney she will recuse herself from that case because she worked with two of the defendants.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans could take Senate, with Democrats winning control of the House\par \par \uc2 As well as who will become US president, control of the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  is at stake in today\u8217\'20\'19s elections that could flip both the House of Representatives and the Senate, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The outcome will play an important role in determining how easily the winner of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s US presidential election will govern until the next congressional elections in 2026.\par \par \uc2 Nonpartisan analysts say Republicans stand a good chance of taking back the Senate, where Democrats hold a 51-49 majority. But Republicans could also lose their grip on the House, where Democrats only need to pick up four seats to take back control of the 435-seat chamber.\par \par \uc2 As in the presidential election, the outcome will likely be determined by a small slice of voters. The battle for the Senate hinges on seven contests, while fewer than 40 House races are seen as truly competitive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s incredibly close,\u8221\'20\'1D said Erin Covey, who analyses House races for the nonpartisan Cook Political Report.\par \par \uc2 Voters do not seem to be indicating a clear preference for either party. An October Reuters/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll found 43% of registered voters would back the Republican candidate in their district, while 43% would back the Democratic candidate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 Polling guru foresees super-tight race\par \par \uc2 Leading forecaster Nate Silver released his final election forecast overnight \u8211\'20\'13 and the race looks almost as tight as it could possibly be. He said that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.natesilver.net/p/nate-silver-2024-president-election-polls-model"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris won in 40,012 out of 80,000, or 50.015% of, simulations}}}\uc2  run using his model.\par \par \uc2 Polls released on Monday found Harris had a marginal lead in Michigan but was tied with Trump in Pennsylvania and other key swing states. Trump maintained a lead over Harris in betting markets, but odds had narrowed somewhat.\par \par \uc2 Silver earned his reputation as a forecasting guru by correctly calling 49 out of 50 states in the 2008 presidential election. He also predicted the outcome of the 2012 and 2020 elections. In 2016, however, he gave eventual winner Trump just a 28.6% chance of becoming president.\par \par \uc2 enltrIt's published.\par \par \uc2 We ran 80,000 simulations tonight.\par \par \uc2 Harris won in 40,012. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vsGVG189Sa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vsGVG189Sa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nate Silver (@NateSilver538) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NateSilver538/status/1853673781350260902?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Security agencies warn of foreign interference in US election\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, several US security agencies released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fbi.gov/news/press-releases/joint-odni-fbi-and-cisa-statement-110424"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joint statement}}}\uc2  on foreign interference in the election.\par \par \uc2 The Office of the Director of National Intelligence (ODNI), the \uc2 Federal Bureau of Investigation\uc2  (\uc2 FBI\uc2 ), and the \uc2 Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency\uc2  (\uc2 CISA\uc2 ) said they had been observing foreign adversaries, particularly Russia, conducting additional influence operations intended to undermine public confidence in the integrity of US elections and stoke divisions among Americans.\par \par \uc2 The agencies warned that they expect these activities to intensify through election day and in the coming weeks, and that foreign influence narratives will focus on swing states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInfluence actors linked to Russia in particular are manufacturing videos and creating fake articles to undermine the legitimacy of the election, instill fear in voters regarding the election process, and suggest Americans are using violence against each other due to political preferences, judging from information available.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C Iran also remains a significant foreign influence threat to US elections. As noted in a prior update, we have assessed that Iran has conducted malicious cyber activities to compromise former president Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIranian influence actors may also seek to create fake media content intended to suppress voting or stoke violence, as they have done in past election cycles.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump 'should play golf' if he loses, says UK ally Farage\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should concede defeat and \u8220\'20\'1Cgo and play golf\u8221\'20\'1D in Scotland if he loses to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  , Nigel Farage has said, but added that the Democratic candidate should pardon Trump to \u8220\'20\'1Cdampen down\u8221\'20\'1D the threat of unrest.\par \par \uc2 Farage, a friend of Trump who has spoken at the former president\u8217\'20\'19s rallies in the past, said he hoped Harris would look \u8220\'20\'1Cmagnanimous\u8221\'20\'1D if she secured a \u8220\'20\'1Cclear and decisive\u8221\'20\'1D victory.\par \par \uc2 The Reform UK leader is in the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/election-day-kamala-harris-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the election}}}\uc2  but said he hoped there would be no unrest after the result. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump was convicted on 34 felony counts}}}\uc2  and is facing sentencing later in November for falsifying business records over payments to the adult film star Stormy Daniels days before his victorious 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 Farage, who has criticised Labour activists for travelling to campaign for Harris, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf she gets in on Tuesday I hope she pardons him. She could look magnanimous and it would dampen down potential tensions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf it was clear and decisive then maybe it\u8217\'20\'19s time to go and play golf at Turnberry,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s all hypothetical and I still think he is going to win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Farage attended Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally in Pennsylvania on Monday, a key swing state where both candidates held rallies the day before the election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/nov/05/donald-trump-go-play-golf-loses-us-election-nigel-farage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump should \u8216\'20\'18go and play golf\u8217\'20\'19 if he loses US election, says Nigel Farage}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 An incumbent president stepping down late in the campaign, a guilty verdict in a criminal case for one of the candidates and a couple of assassination attempts \u8211\'20\'13 this election campaign has been a wild ride.\par \par \uc2 Here are 15 moments that defined the US election campaign:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-biggest-moments-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trials, drop-outs and assassination attempts: 15 moments that defined the US election campaign}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 The influential podcast host Joe Rogan endorsed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  for president, writing on social media that his choice had been influenced by \u8220\'20\'1Cthe great and powerful \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Musk \u8220\'20\'1Cmakes what I think is the most compelling case for Trump you\u8217\'20\'19ll hear, and I agree with him every step of the way\u8221\'20\'1D, Rogan wrote on X. \u8220\'20\'1CFor the record, yes, that\u8217\'20\'19s an endorsement of Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThe great and powerful {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @elonmusk}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If it wasn't for him we'd be fucked. He makes what I think is the most compelling case for Trump you'll hear, and I agree with him every step of the way.\par \par \uc2 For the record, yes, that's an endorsement of Trump.\par \par \uc2 Enjoy the podcast {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LdBxZFVsLN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LdBxZFVsLN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joe Rogan (@joerogan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joerogan/status/1853614670764015762?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Rogan, 57, described recently by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2024-03-21/spotify-reveals-podcast-numbers-for-joe-rogan-alex-cooper-travis-kelce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg}}}\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cwidely accepted as the most popular podcaster on Earth\u8221\'20\'1D, has an overwhelmingly male audience. He {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/trump-joe-rogan-interview-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently interviewed Donald Trump}}}\uc2  on the show, and, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/joe-rogan-kamala-harris-interview-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently as last week}}}\uc2 , was negotiating for a sit-down with the Democratic presidential nominee \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , though no interview went ahead.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s interview on Rogan\u8217\'20\'19s show ten days ago currently has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hBMoPUAeLnY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 45m views}}}\uc2  on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 , while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hBMoPUAeLnY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s interview has 14m views}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/joe-rogan-endorses-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Rogan endorses Donald Trump for president}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 With a fairly hefty time difference, the US election will play out at different times of the day depending on which side of the pond you are on. Archie Bland breaks down how the race for the White House will unfold for British viewers.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/05/how-the-us-elections-trump-harris-will-unfold-overnight-for-british-viewers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How the US elections will unfold overnight for British viewers}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump tied in tiny New Hampshire town that kicks off election-day voting\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  tied with three votes each in the tiny New Hampshire town that traditionally kicks off {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voting on election day}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Since the 1960s, voters in Dixville \uc2 Notch\uc2 , close to the Canadian border, have gathered just after midnight to cast their ballots.\par \par \uc2 Votes are then counted and results announced \u8211\'20\'13 hours before other states open their polls.\par \par \uc2 According to CNN, four registered Republicans and two undeclared voters took part in the vote just after midnight on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Leslie Otten was seemingly the disaffected Republican voter that backed Harris in the six-person ballot. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been a Republican most of my life, but I find myself in conflict with the Republican Party at this time,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been loudly said by Trump that I\u8217\'20\'19m now an enemy because I don\u8217\'20\'19t back him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s video team has made an explainer on the feisty history of US political mudslinging. In it, they argue that the insults didn\u8217\'20\'19t start with Trump:\par \par \uc2 The video is part of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/@ItsComplicated"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s Complicated}}}\uc2 , a new \uc2 YouTube\uc2  channel dedicated to all forms of explanatory journalism, helping bring clarity, context and understanding in a complicated world.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 Streeting also spoke about Nigel Farage, the leader of Reform UK who was at a Trump rally last night.\par \par \uc2 Farage last night tweeted a clip from the rally where Trump was speaking about their relationship \u8211\'20\'13 which perhaps didn\u8217\'20\'19t start as a resounding endorsement of the Reform leader, but ended up there.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have a man from Europe, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if he\u8217\'20\'19s here, I saw him backstage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat he is doing is sort of what we did a few years ago. He\u8217\'20\'19s doing a great job, he\u8217\'20\'19s a fantastic \u8230\'20\'26 he\u8217\'20\'19s always been my friend for some reason. He liked me, I liked him and he\u8217\'20\'19s shaking it up pretty good over there. He was the big winner of the last election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Streeting said of the Reform leader: \u8220\'20\'1CTo be fair to Nigel Farage, the leader of the Reform Party who is currently State-side, he is a firm supporter of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe was reflecting overnight that whatever some of the noise we\u8217\'20\'19ve heard about, you know that legal action or indeed things that that we said about president Trump in the past, that we\u8217\'20\'19ll be able to work effectively together as partners and and as allies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThe special relationship. ???? ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oUh57wHDRF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oUh57wHDRF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nigel Farage MP (@Nigel_Farage) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Nigel_Farage/status/1853558745298538503?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 'We're not ideological bedfellows with Trump,' senior UK politician admits\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UK government\uc2  has been working to ensure the \u8220\'20\'1Cdeep ties\u8221\'20\'1D that bind the UK and the US will be \u8220\'20\'1Cas strong as they have ever been\u8221\'20\'1D, whatever the outcome of the US election, the UK\u8217\'20\'19s health secretary \uc2 Wes Streeting\uc2  said, PA reports.\par \par \uc2 Wes Streeting\uc2  told LBC Radio: \u8220\'20\'1CThe prime minister, the foreign secretary and others have been working hard to make sure that whatever the outcome of the US presidential election, the deep ties that bind our two nations are as strong as they have ever been.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that is particularly important in a world in which we see war on the continent of Europe, in Ukraine, war in the Middle East, wider geopolitical risks and threats where the US and the UK have common history, but also common cause in terms of the future we want to build, in the future of democracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people will decide who their president is and we will work with whoever they choose.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s fair to say that we may not be ideological bedfellows with President Trump, but if he\u8217\'20\'19s returned as president of the United States, there will be a really good working relationship.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I think we saw that with the warmth of the exchange between president Trump and the prime minister after they met recently.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 US judges have denied requests from the Republican-led states of Missouri and Texas to block the federal government from sending lawyers to their states on election day to monitor compliance with federal voting rights laws, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Both states are among the 27 that the \uc2 US Justice Department\uc2  (DOJ) said it would send staff out to monitorvoting locations, as it has done regularly during national elections.\par \par \uc2 Federal judge Matthew Kacsmaryk ordered the DOJ early on Tuesday to confirm that \u8220\'20\'1Cno observers\u8221\'20\'1D would be present in polling locations in Texas but denied issuing the restraining order the state had requested.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Court cannot issue a temporary restraining order without further clarification on the distinction between \u8216\'20\'18monitoring\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18observing\u8217\'20\'19 on the eve of a consequential election,\u8221\'20\'1D Kacsmaryk, a Trump appointee, said in the ruling.\par \par \uc2 Texas attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  had earlier said that sending monitors \u8220\'20\'1Cinfringes on States\u8217\'20\'19 constitutional authority to run free and fair elections.\u8221\'20\'1D The lawsuit argued that \u8220\'20\'1Cunder Texas law, the list of persons who may be present in voting locations or central counting stations does not include federal authorities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 District judge Sarah Pitlyk in Missouri also denied that state\u8217\'20\'19s request for a temporary restraining order, saying late last night: \u8220\'20\'1Cthe harms that the State of Missouri anticipates are speculative.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit had accused the DOJ of making an 11th-hour plan that intended to \u8220\'20\'1Cdisplace state election authorities\u8221\'20\'1D by sending poll monitors to locations throughout St. Louis.\par \par \uc2 The DOJ said two election monitors were in Missouri to monitor one polling station in St. Louis.\par \par \uc2 While some of the locations the DOJ will monitor on election day include key counties in the seven battleground states expected to help decide the election, it is also sending personnel to other locations such as counties in Massachusetts, Alaska, South Dakota, and New Jersey. Neither Missouri nor Texas are considered among the seven battleground states.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 AP reports on a tiny Indian village where \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has ancestral roots that is praying for her victory.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s little to distinguish the village of Thulasendrapuram from any other rural community in Tamil Nadu, except its connection to a woman who could become America\u8217\'20\'19s first leader with South Asian roots.\par \par \uc2 As millions of Americans vote, Harris has people rooting for her from thousands of miles away in a village surrounded by rice paddies and coconut trees, where her mother\u8217\'20\'19s family has ancestral ties. They talk about her at the local tea shop. Banners and billboards bearing her face are seen throughout the community.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur deity is a very powerful God. If we pray well to him, he will make her victorious,\u8221\'20\'1D said M. Natarajan, the temple priest that led the prayers in front of the image of Hindu deity Ayyanar, a form of Lord Shiva.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19 maternal grandfather was born in the village, about 350 kilometers (215 miles) from the southern coastal city of Chennai, more than 100 years ago. As an adult, he moved to Chennai, where he worked as a high-ranking government official until his retirement.\par \par \uc2 Harris has never visited Thulasendrapuram and she has no living relatives in the village, but people here still venerate the family that made it big in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur village ancestors\u8217\'20\'19 granddaughter is running as a US presidential candidate. Her victory will be happy news for every one of us,\u8221\'20\'1D Natarajan said.\par \par \uc2 Harris hasn\u8217\'20\'19t visited India much \u8212\'20\'14 particularly not since becoming vice president \u8212\'20\'14 but she has often spoken emotionally about her ties to her late mother\u8217\'20\'19s country of birth. On Tuesday, she released a campaign video highlighting her mother, who arrived in the US at age 19 and became a cancer researcher.\par \par \uc2 Titled \u8220\'20\'1CMother,\u8221\'20\'1D the video ends with a narrator saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThis daughter of Shyamala, this daughter of the American story, is ready to lead us forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Village residents also prayed for Harris\u8217\'20\'19 victory in 2020, and set off firecrackers when she became the US vice president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 Last night \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  reported that betting markets had narrowed on the eve of the election.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign and its supporters had been pointing to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lead over Harris at leading bookmakers as a more accurate forecast than tight polls that were too close to call in the run up to the election.\par \par \uc2 But the odds have narrowed somewhat, as the below data visualisation shows:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2024/11/archive-zip/giv-45593C2zgwrGT0OA/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 The current odds on the \uc2 Betfair\uc2  betting exchange still favour Trump \u8211\'20\'13 giving him about a 60% chance of winning the election to Harris\u8217\'20\'19 40%.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/presidential-election-betting-odds-polling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lead over Harris in betting market erodes as platforms tighten odds}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 'People say God saved me in order to save America,' Trump tells rally\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Adam Gabbatt provides some analysis on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s final rally ahead of the election \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Trump said this was his \u8220\'20\'1Clast rally\u8221\'20\'1D, and if that\u8217\'20\'19s true, it was a somewhat ignominious end. More than half the crowd left during a meandering, nearly-two hour long, speech that saw Trump attack \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , criticise the thickness of Adam Schiff\u8217\'20\'19s neck, and muse that god may have saved him from an assassin\u8217\'20\'19s bullet so that he could become president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKamala, she is a very low IQ person and we don\u8217\'20\'19t need a very low IQ individual. We\u8217\'20\'19ve had that for four years and our country is going down the drain,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said early in his rally, one of a series of typically vicious critiques on his opponent.\par \par \uc2 Trump arrived almost two hours late for the rally, and by the time he started speaking about how divine intervention saved him from an assassination attempt, people had already begun to leave.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany people say that god saved me in order to save America,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told the crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a beautiful expression and I think it might be true.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Away from the reverie on god, this \u8220\'20\'1Clast rally\u8221\'20\'1D offered up much of the grievance and doom that has characterised Trump\u8217\'20\'19s politics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome of the greatest criminals in the world are pouring into our country,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, mirroring his very first campaign rally, at Trump Tower on June 16 2015.\par \par \uc2 As well as blasting Harris, he called \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazy horrible human being\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s a sick crazy\u8230\'20\'26 oh no\u8230\'20\'26 it starts with a b but I won\u8217\'20\'19t say it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump continued: \u8220\'20\'1CThese are bad people. Adam shifty Schiff. I call him pencil neck.\u8221\'20\'1D He said of the California Democrat: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s an unattractive guy in and out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At 2.10am, with the audience bleary eyed, Trump finally left the stage after declaring, without specifics, that he would fix all America\u8217\'20\'19s ills. The now familiar sound of Village People\u8217\'20\'19s YMCA played the former president out, and now only time will tell whether he wins re-election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continued to attack \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and gave dark warnings about a dystopian future under the vice-president in the early hours of Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 Speaking in Grand Rapids, Michigan, Trump also mused that god may have saved him from an assassin\u8217\'20\'19s bullet so that he could become president, as he claimed that he has a \u8220\'20\'1C95% chance or something\u8221\'20\'1D of winning the election.\par \par \uc2 Trump has said he will not run for president again, and if this is to be Trump\u8217\'20\'19s last rally, it was a somewhat ignominious end. More than half the crowd left during a meandering, nearly-two hour long, speech that saw Trump attack \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , criticise the thickness of Adam Schiff\u8217\'20\'19s neck, and demonise immigrants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKamala, she is a very low IQ person and we don\u8217\'20\'19t need a very low IQ individual. We\u8217\'20\'19ve had that for four years and our country is going down the drain,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said early in his rally, one of a series of typically vicious critiques on his opponent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you vote for lying Kamala you\u8217\'20\'19ll have four more years of misery, failure and disaster our country may never recover from,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump added, to loud jeers.\par \par \uc2 Trump arrived almost two hours late for the rally, and by the time he started speaking about how divine intervention saved him from an assassination attempt, people had already begun to leave.\par \par \uc2 This \u8220\'20\'1Clast rally\u8221\'20\'1D offered up much of the grievance and doom that has characterised Trump\u8217\'20\'19s politics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSome of the greatest criminals in the world are pouring into our country,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, mirroring his very first campaign rally, at Trump Tower on June 16 2015.\par \par \uc2 That day the then-reality tv host descended on an escalator to announce what was seen as a long shot run for the presidency. He offered grave, racially charged warnings about immigration, characterised cities as crime-addled hellholes, made vague, hyperbolic promises about how only he could fix the country, and launched vicious attacks on political rivals.\par \par \uc2 Fast forward November 2024, and little has changed.\par \par \uc2 As well as blasting Harris, he called \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazy horrible human being\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s a sick crazy\u8230\'20\'26 oh no\u8230\'20\'26 it starts with a b but I won\u8217\'20\'19t say it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At 2am, as the rally drew to a close, he returned to the dark motifs that have been such a hallmark of his political career. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first rally and his last rally may have been nine years apart. But at this final event, held hours before voting begins in what could be one of the most consequential elections in modern history, it was clear that little has changed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris welcomed a slew of celebrities to her rallies in the closing moments of the election campaign, PA reports.\par \par \uc2 Oprah Winfrey, Katy Perry, Will.i.am, Lady Gaga, Jon Bon Jovi and Christina Aguilera were among the superstars lending their voices to support Harris.\par \par \uc2 Lady Gaga was one of the stars who performed at Harris\u8217\'20\'19 multi-city rally on the evening before the election, where she sang God Bless America before warning the audience \u8220\'20\'1Cthe country is depending on you\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, talk show host Winfrey said she travelled across the country to appear at the rally in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, wearing a t-shirt that read \u8220\'20\'1CYes she can\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we don\u8217\'20\'19t show up tomorrow, it is entirely possible that we will not have the opportunity to ever cast a ballot again,\u8221\'20\'1D the TV star warned.\par \par \uc2 Black Eyed Peas singer Will.i.am performed his Harris endorsement song titled \u8220\'20\'1CYes she can\u8221\'20\'1D, which includes the lyrics: \u8220\'20\'1CSo register and vote for your life, do it for your daughters and your sons and your wife.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It came moments after Gaga\u8217\'20\'19s performance at the rally, where she told the crowd: \u8220\'20\'1CFor more than half of this country\u8217\'20\'19s life, women did not have a voice \u8230\'20\'26 But tomorrow, women will be a part of making this decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, I am holding in my heart all the tough, tenacious women who made me who I am. I cast my vote for someone who will be a president for all Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 Crowd size has been a persistent talking point for Trump, right from the beginning of his political career more than eight years ago. But Democrats have recently been mocking him over his obsession, pointing out that people have been leaving his lengthy rallies early and that seats at some rallies have been empty. AP has this report:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump has spent nearly a decade bragging about his crowds. Lately, he\u8217\'20\'19s been making the same boasts to swaths of empty seats.\par \par \uc2 In his third presidential bid, Trump for the first time is facing an opponent who stages her own massive rallies, calling further attention to the fact that his crowds, however enthusiastic they are, sometimes have failed to fill large venues and often thinned out as he spoke.\par \par \uc2 In North Carolina this weekend, the former president and Republican nominee spoke at First Horizon Coliseum in Greensboro, where the lower level of the 22,000-seat arena remained unfilled, with the upper level blocked off altogether.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve had the biggest rallies in history of any country. Every rally\u8217\'20\'19s full,\u8221\'20\'1D he falsely claimed anyway. \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t have any seats that are empty.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He began Monday, the eve of the election, in Raleigh, North Carolina, where a late-arriving crowd came close to filling the venue but left a smattering of empty seats. In Reading, Pennsylvania, Trump took the stage in Santander Arena, where there were sections of empty seats in the 7,200-seat arena. The campaign hung a large American flag near the back of the arena, blocking the view of several seating sections that remained unfilled.\par \par \uc2 He then went to PPG Paints Arena in Pittsburgh, where the upper level seating was again blocked off.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s crowds still routinely number in the thousands and they roared regularly as he spoke. And his supporters this year remain engaged enough that his final event in Grand Rapids, Michigan, was inside a packed arena even though it started after 12:15 am Tuesday, nearly two hours late. Some rallygoers told a reporter they arrived at 7 am the day before.\par \par \uc2 But the occasional scenes of empty seats offered a notable contrast to Democratic nominee Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19 biggest events this fall \u8212\'20\'14 and to the volume and vibe of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s crowds eight years ago when he sought and won the presidency for the first time \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 The former reality television star and consummate showman clearly remains invested in the performative aspect of presidential politics and obviously concerned that Harris, unlike Democrats Hillary Clinton in 2016 or Joe Biden in 2020, can match and even exceed his signature campaign tactic. Harris, for example, recently filled the large coliseum in Greensboro.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 And as the clock approaches 2.10am in Michigan, Trump has finally ended his final rally in Grand Rapids, Michigan. After ranging further through various topics including promises to defend religious liberty, the right to keep and bear arms, \u8220\'20\'1Ckeeping men out of women\u8217\'20\'19s sports\u8221\'20\'1D and building up our borders, he says:\par \par \uc2 We will never ever surrender, together we will fight fight fight and we will win win win! \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 November 5, today, will be the most important day in the history of our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And finally, he ends:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI love you all, God bless you, God bless you Michigan, God bless the United States of America!\u8221\'20\'1D and dances out to the tune of YMCA.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump appears to be winding up and is talking about his \u8220\'20\'1Cfavourite word: tariff!\u8221\'20\'1D and repeats his threat to put \u8220\'20\'1Clarge scale\u8221\'20\'1D tariffs on goods coming from Mexico and Canada if they don\u8217\'20\'19t prevent fentanyl made by China coming into the US.\par \par \uc2 He then makes even more imflammatory comments about immigration claiming, without any evidence, that \u8220\'20\'1CCrime is plummeting all over the world\u8221\'20\'1D because they\u8217\'20\'19re sending their \u8220\'20\'1Ccriminals\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cmental patients\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cprison populations\u8221\'20\'1D and others to the US.\par \par \uc2 He also talks again about putting a missile shield around the US.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr and Eric Trump take the mic next, urging people to get out and vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou are going to save democracy in the United States and keep peace in the world,\u8221\'20\'1D Eric says of his father.\par \par \uc2 Then Tiffany says a few brief words before Trump returns. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re my kids but I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you they\u8217\'20\'19re very good people,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 After touting Joe Rogan\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement of him, Trump has invited his daughter-in-law Lara Trump, the co-chair of the National Republican Committee, to take the mic.\par \par \uc2 She says \u8220\'20\'1Cwe send a loud and clear message\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Cthe mainstream media\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe swamp\u8221\'20\'1D among other people \u8220\'20\'1Cthat it is we who get to choose the president\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She says it has been \u8220\'20\'1Ca very special night for our family\u8221\'20\'1D, adding \u8220\'20\'1Cit has been my honour to be a part of this family, to be out speaking on behalf of a man whom I love \u8230\'20\'26 who is going to save this country and is going to save the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s approaching 2am in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump has now called his family up to the stage, including his sons Eric and Donald Jr, Tiffany Trump and her husband Michael Boulos and Eric\u8217\'20\'19s wife Lara, who is the co-chair of the National Republican Committee.\par \par \uc2 His daughter Ivanka Trump, who was a White House advisor to him during his first term, and his wife Melania, are notable by their absence.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump has given shoutouts to a list of people supporting him, including Arkansas governor Sarah Huckabee Sanders and the ambassador to Germany during his time in office, Rick Grenell.\par \par \uc2 He goes into a story about former chancellor Angela Merkel, saying that when Grenell \u8220\'20\'1Cwas taken out it was the happiest day of her life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 At one point he adds as an aside, \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t let them forget that we stopped that big Chinese plant in Mexico!\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s put it this way if they build it theyre going to lose their ass\u8221\'20\'1D. It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t clear who or what plant he was referring to \u8211\'20\'13 see our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update?page=with:block-6729b20e8f083ba7acfeaba6#block-6729b20e8f083ba7acfeaba6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 The crowds are reportedly beginning to thin out at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally in Michigan. He\u8217\'20\'19s been talking for over an hour now.\par \par \uc2 enltrAs the clock ticked past 1am in Grand Rapids, the crowd at this final Trump rally began to thin. Trump has brought much more energy here than he did in Pittsburgh but it\u8217\'20\'19s getting laaaate.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Garrett Haake (@GarrettHaake) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GarrettHaake/status/1853684656006176997?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s 1.30am in Michigan and Trump has now moved back to talking about cutting energy prices and the cost of groceries again.\par \par \uc2 He tells a familiar story about an old woman going into a shop to buy three apples but only being able to afford two and having to put one back in the fridge (\u8220\'20\'1Crefrigeration\u8221\'20\'1D). It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear where or when this happened.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be happening in our country,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 After some more insults hurled at Kamala Harris and California governor Gavin Newsom, Trump begins making further inflammatory remarks about immigration, accusing Harris of wanting open borders and of allowing an \u8220\'20\'1Cinvasion\u8221\'20\'1D of immigrants including those from \u8220\'20\'1Cmental institutions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe day I take office the migrant invasion ends,\u8221\'20\'1D he says, later adding that we \u8220\'20\'1Clive in an occupied country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He also repeats his call for the death penalty for any illegal immigrant who kills and American citizen and his plan to ban sanctuary cities.\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/31/election-trump-immigration-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promised to restore and expand his most controversial immigration policies}}}\uc2 , including the travel ban aimed at mostly Muslim countries. He has consistently promised to stage the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest deportation operation in American history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump talks briefly about groceries (\u8220\'20\'1CPeople say \u8216\'20\'18groceries,\u8217\'20\'19 right? I haven\u8217\'20\'19t used tha \u8230\'20\'26 it\u8217\'20\'19s such a sort of an old term.\u8221\'20\'1D)\par \par \uc2 Then he talks for a while about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/13/trump-rally-gun-shots-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attempt to assassinate him in Pennsylvania in July}}}\uc2 . He calls his survival a \u8220\'20\'1Cmiracle\u8221\'20\'1D and at one point mentions that \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal immigration saved me\u8221\'20\'1D although I didn\u8217\'20\'19t catch how.\par \par \uc2 He then moves into an anecdote about visiting Abraham Lincoln\u8217\'20\'19s bedroom with Melania Trump. He says that the assassinated president suffered from \u8220\'20\'1Cmelancholia\u8221\'20\'1D and adds that: \u8220\'20\'1CHe was very tall, he was six foot six, that\u8217\'20\'19s the equivalent of a Barron Trump today \u8230\'20\'26 the bed was very long.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After a few asides about Melania\u8217\'20\'19s book, he returns to the theme of the attempt on his life.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump has returned to the theme of plants and Mexico, telling a convoluted story about a businessman friend and China\u8217\'20\'19s intention to build a plant in Mexico which was going \u8220\'20\'1Cto destroy Michigan\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He says that his threats to \u8220\'20\'1Cput a 100% tariff on every single car coming out of that plant\u8221\'20\'1D had led to a decision not to build the purported plant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI saved Detroit and Michigan a lot and I did that without even being president,\u8221\'20\'1D he claims.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear what plant he\u8217\'20\'19s referring to. Newsweek has previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/fact-check-trump-says-he-has-stopped-china-car-factory-plan-mexico-1973843"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  after similar remarks he made at the end of last month that his campaign could not confirm what plant it was but that it appeared to be one planned by auto manufacturer BYD and that there was no evidence the claim was true.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump and Harris get three votes each as election kicks off in New Hampshire\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris and Donald Trump have tied with three votes each in the tiny New Hampshire town which traditionally kicks off voting on election day.\par \par \uc2 Since the 1960\u8217\'20\'19s, voters in Dixville Notch, located close to the border with Canada, have gathered just after midnight to cast their ballots. Votes are then counted and results announced \u8211\'20\'13 hours before other states even open their polls.\par \par \uc2 According to CNN, four Republicans and two undeclared voters participated took part in the vote just after midnight on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump then launches into some familiar insults of Kamala Harris and Hillary Clinton of whom he says, \u8220\'20\'1CShe called me and conceded [presumably eight years ago] and then spent seven years saying how she was a good sport.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He calls Harris a \u8220\'20\'1Clow IQ person\u8221\'20\'1D and then begins on a long story about Elon Musk and his rockets.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump insults opponents at final Michigan rally\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, Trump then goes on to talk insultingly about President Joe Biden, former House Speaker Nancy Pelosi, and representative Adam Schiff, the lead investigator in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first impeachment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJoe Biden in one of his crazy moments said that we were all garbage,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump remarked adding \u8220\'20\'1CThey stole the election from a president,\u8221\'20\'1D in apparent reference to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s dropping out of the campaign to be replaced by Harris.\par \par \uc2 He then says of Pelosi \u8220\'20\'1Cshe\u8217\'20\'19s a crooked person \u8230\'20\'26 evil, sick, crazy b\u8230\'20\'26 oh no! It starts with a \u8216\'20\'18b\u8217\'20\'19 but I won\u8217\'20\'19t say it! I wanna say it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said of \u8220\'20\'1CAdam Shifty Schiff\u8221\'20\'1D: \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s got the biggest head, he\u8217\'20\'19s an unattractive guy both inside and out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, Trump claims to have done 930 rallies during his campaign, which I can\u8217\'20\'19t confirm. Then he continues:\par \par \uc2 If you make one slip up and you know I wrote a beautiful speech I haven\u8217\'20\'19t even gotten to it yet... rarely do they ever catch me making a mistake!\par \par \uc2 Those ellipses are covering for a series of meandering comments which included remarks on his use of teleprompters and the state of the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump starts his rally in Michigan apparently talking about his first election run, saying \u8220\'20\'1Cwe were given a three per cent chance\u8221\'20\'1D in Michigan and then begins a series of rambling remarks about Detroit, (\u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve heard a lot about Detroit\u8221\'20\'1D) and adds \u8220\'20\'1CWe killed the plant in Mexico\u8221\'20\'1D. It\u8217\'20\'19s not clear what he was referring to.\par \par \uc2 He then moved on to immigration, saying the US was suffering the \u8220\'20\'1Cinvasion of some of the biggest criminals in the world\u8230\'20\'26 we\u8217\'20\'19re going to end that immediately.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t have to live this way,\u8221\'20\'1D he adds.\par \par \uc2 Then he moves on to Kamala Harris, mocking her and claiming, \u8220\'20\'1CNobody knew who the hell she was.\u8221\'20\'1D He then made some more inflammatory comments about transgender people.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump has finally arrived at his final rally in Grand Rapids, Michigan, almost two and a half hours behind schedule.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 A few dozen conservative voters gathered at a Phoenix park to launch a canvass with Turning Point Action the night before the election, pulling up an app to get names and locations of voters they could talk to and convince to head to the polls.\par \par \uc2 Turning Point, the conservative youth organization, has run its \u8220\'20\'1Cchase the vote\u8221\'20\'1D program in Arizona and Wisconsin to reach low propensity voters. Monday\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csuper chase\u8221\'20\'1D canvass involved a data-driven approach to a part of town that the group says has right-leaning voters who haven\u8217\'20\'19t yet turned in ballots.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe actually modeled this program around a lot of what the Democrats have built in years prior,\u8221\'20\'1D said Andrew Kolvet, the group\u8217\'20\'19s spokesman.\par \par \uc2 People from 47 states have come to Arizona and Wisconsin to volunteer with the group to turn out voters, Kolvet said. At the Phoenix park, teams of at least two \u8211\'20\'13 often wearing red Maga hats and toting clipboards \u8211\'20\'13 set off to knock some doors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe job is not to convince a swing voter necessarily, or to convince a Democrat to vote Republican,\u8221\'20\'1D Kolvet said. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are people that we know are probably our people that just haven\u8217\'20\'19t got their vote in.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Registered Republicans have so far turned in more ballots than their Democratic counterparts in Arizona, a reversal of the last two cycles when Republicans trailed in early voting (though Republicans before 2020 often had a lead in early votes).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re feeling as good as we could feel,\u8221\'20\'1D Kolvet said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not predicting victory. I\u8217\'20\'19m just saying we have done the hard work and set the state up to have a really good day tomorrow. Anything could happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris ends campaign 'with energy, with joy' at final rally in Philadelphia\par \par \uc2 Dispatch from Philadelphia : Kamala Harris has run a remarkable 107-day presidential campaign, the shortest in modern political history.\par \par \uc2 It began on a Sunday morning with a call from the president saying he was stepping down. On election eve, hours before polls opened, she finished the final speech of a campaign she cast as a fight for American democracy.\par \par \uc2 But Harris has also sought to inject hope and optimism into her campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTonight, then, we finish, as we started with optimism with energy, with joy,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGenerations before us led the fight for freedom, and now the baton is in our hands,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to get to work and get out the vote,\u8221\'20\'1D she concluded.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Georgia poll worker arrested over bomb threat, prosecutors say\par \par \uc2 A Georgia poll worker was arrested on Monday on US charges that he sent a letter threatening to bomb election workers that he wrote to appear as if it came from a voter in the presidential election battleground state. Reuters reports:\par \par \uc2 Federal prosecutors said Nicholas Wimbish, 25, had been serving as a poll worker at the Jones County Elections Office in Gray, Georgia, on Oct. 16 when he got into a verbal altercation with a voter.\par \par \uc2 The next day, Wimbish mailed a letter to the county\u8217\'20\'19s elections superintendent that was drafted to appear as if it came from that same voter, prosecutors said. The letter complained that Wimbish was a \u8220\'20\'1Ccloseted liberal election fraudster\u8221\'20\'1D who had been distracting voters in line to cast ballots, according to charging papers.\par \par \uc2 Authorities said the letter, signed by a \u8220\'20\'1CJones county voter,\u8221\'20\'1D said Wimbish and others \u8220\'20\'1Cshould look over their shoulder\u8221\'20\'1D and warned that people would \u8220\'20\'1Clearn a violent lesson about stealing our elections!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors said the letter ended with a handwritten note: \u8220\'20\'1CPS boom toy in early vote place, cigar burning, be safe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wimbish was charged with mailing a bomb threat, conveying false information about a bomb threat, mailing a threatening letter, and making false statements to the FBI, prosecutors said. A lawyer for Wimbish could not be immediately identified.\par \par \uc2 Georgia is one of seven closely contested states expected to decide the outcome of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election match up between Republican former President Donald Trump and Democratic Vice President Kamala Harris.\par \par \uc2 Concerns about potential political violence have prompted officials to take a variety of measures to bolster security during and after Election Day.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 Dispatch from Grand Rapids, Michigan : They just showed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.si.com/extra-mustard/2017/03/30/donald-trump-vince-mcmahon-wrestlemania-hair-match"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a video}}}\uc2  here of Donald Trump shaving the head of Vince McMahon, the former CEO of WWE, during a wrestling event. It happened in 2007.\par \par \uc2 Needless to say, Trump hasn\u8217\'20\'19t arrived yet.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris emphasises her message of unity in her remarks in Philadelphia, drawing a contrast with Donald Trump without mentioning his name, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CInstead of stewing on an enemies list I will work on my to-do list.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She then lists some of the things she would do in office including banning corporate price gouging on groceries, cutting taxes for workers and middle class families and lowering the cost of health care, adding: \u8220\'20\'1Caccess to health care should be a right and not just a privilege of those who can afford it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also mentions women\u8217\'20\'19s right to control their own bodies and her determination to sign into law protections for women\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive freedom.\par \par \uc2 She then goes back to her message of unity saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI pledge to listen to those who will be impacted by the decisions I make\u8221\'20\'1D. She also repeats comments she has made previously about listening to experts and giving people who disagree with her a seat at the table.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris take the stage in Philadelphia\par \par \uc2 Harris came onstage to Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s Freedom. She hugged Oprah before beginning her remarks.\par \par \uc2 Harris said her campaign started \u8220\'20\'1Cas the underdog and climb to victory,\u8221\'20\'1D she said gesturing to the Rocky steps behind her.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis could be one of the closest races in history,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou will decide the outcome of this election Pennsylvania,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake: we will win!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The crowd begins chanting \u8220\'20\'1CWe will win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 More from the Harris rally in Philadelphia : In a white pants suit, Oprah Winfrey laid the stakes pretty bare for the audience. She told a story about meeting a woman on a hike who said she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t planning to vote this election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t get to sit this one out, Oprah said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we don\u8217\'20\'19t show up tomorrow, it is entirely possible that we will not have the opportunity to ever cast a ballot again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said those were the \u8220\'20\'1Cdangers\u8221\'20\'1D of not electing Harris on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris is taking to the stage in Philadelphia now for her final rally before election day, after an introduction by Oprah Winfrey.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 Security agencies say Russia election disinformation efforts risk inciting violence\par \par \uc2 Russia-linked disinformation operations have falsely claimed officials in battleground states plan to fraudulently sway the outcome of the extraordinarily close US presidential election, authorities have warned hours before Election Day. AFP reports:\par \par \uc2 Success in the seven swing states is key to winning the White House for rivals Kamala Harris and Donald Trump, and those states have previously been the focus of unsupported accusations of election fraud.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussia is the most active threat,\u8221\'20\'1D the Office of the Director of National Intelligence (ODNI), the FBI and the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency said Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese efforts risk inciting violence, including against election officials,\u8221\'20\'1D they added, noting the efforts are expected to intensify through Election Day and in the following weeks.\par \par \uc2 It was the latest in a series of warnings from the ODNI about foreign actors - notably Russia and Iran - allegedly spreading disinformation or hacking the campaigns during this election.\par \par \uc2 Tehran and Moscow have both denied such allegations in the past.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 More from Philadelphia, where Doug Emhoff just praised his wife, Kamala Harris as the \u8220\'20\'1Cright president for this moment in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He joked that she will lead with her \u8220\'20\'1Claugh and that look.\u8221\'20\'1D Emhoff has been crisscrossing the country for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump was supposed to start speaking at 10.30pm local time in Grand Rapids, Michigan. Well, he didn\u8217\'20\'19t - he isn\u8217\'20\'19t even here yet - and according to a police officer I just spoke to it\u8217\'20\'19s probably going to get to midnight before Trump actually appears.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime the campaign is desperately filling time. We\u8217\'20\'19ve had an appearance from a local congressman \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CWho the hell is that?\u8221\'20\'1D a Trump supporter behind me commented \u8211\'20\'13 and some lackeys just wheeled out a sort of T-shirt machine gun, which entertained people for a bit.\par \par \uc2 In contrast to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s other rallies today, the Van Andel Arena, in downtown Grand Rapids, is actually almost full. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd let me tell you,\u8221\'20\'1D one of the speakers said just now, \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s the same number of people waiting outside who couldn\u8217\'20\'19t get in!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I was a bit bored so I got up and went and looked outside. There is not a single person out there.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Lady Gaga has just arrived on stage. She takes a seat at the piano and belts God Bless America.\par \par \uc2 She said she cast her vote for Harris \u8211\'20\'13 but there is little chance Lady Gaga is a battleground state voter. Instead she encourages everyone in the audience to vote and then brings out the future \u8220\'20\'1Cfirst First Gentleman,\u8221\'20\'1D Doug Emhoff.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 Opening summary\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s live coverage as the US is set to vote in the 2024 presidential election.\par \par \uc2 With just hours to go before polls open, Kamala Harris and Donald Trump have been making their final pitch to voters, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/trump-harris-voters-us-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 honing in on the crucial battleground states}}}\uc2  of Pennsylvania and Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Polls continue to show the contest could not be closer, with both candidates tied in a number of key swing states.\par \par \uc2 The two candidates laid out starkly contrasting visions for America\u8217\'20\'19s future on the eve of election day. Trump rambled through dark and dystopian speeches painting migrants as dangerous criminals while also launching personal attacks on a number of high-profile Democratic women. Harris delivered a more positive closing argument, shifting focus away from the threat posed by the ex-president, who is not mentioned in her final ad, and insisting \u8220\'20\'1Cwe all have so much more in common than what separates us\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The polls are set to start opening on the US east coast in less than six hours time, with the rest of the country following in the hours after. Millions of Americans are set to vote across the day, but the outcome remains far from certain.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has been happening over the last 24 hours:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris put all her chips on the key battleground state of Pennsylvania on Monday, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/trump-harris-election-pennsylvania-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}\uc2  indicate an extremely close contest. She held several rallies and events including a stop at a Puerto Rican restaurant with Congresswoman Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez and directly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/nanditab1/status/1853589842266910947?s=46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined canvassing}}}\uc2  in a residential area in Reading, telling voters at one home: \u8220\'20\'1CI wanted to go door-knocking!\u8221\'20\'1D\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/trump-harris-election-pennsylvania-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought to strike a positive tone}}}\uc2 , saying she wanted to be a \u8220\'20\'1Cpresident for all Americans\u8221\'20\'1D. A sign of a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong\u8221\'20\'1D leader is someone willing to listen to the experts, the stakeholders and those who disagree, she said at a rally in Pittsburgh.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump meanwhile held rallies in Raleigh, North Carolina, two in Pennsylvania, but his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/trump-harris-election-pennsylvania-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tone was much darker}}}\uc2 , focusing on painting migrants as dangerous criminals while also launching personal attacks on a number of high-profile Democratic women. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re killing people. They\u8217\'20\'19re killing people at will,\u8221\'20\'1D he said at one rally, giving gruesome details of specific murders allegedly committed by undocumented migrants. In North Caroliana he called Democratic congresswoman Nancy Pelosi a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazyass bedbug\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/04/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-polls-latest-live-news?page=with:block-6728f9478f082a575b9e59bb#block-6728f9478f082a575b9e59bb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacked}}}\uc2  former first lady Michelle Obama, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CShe hit me the other day. I was going to say to my people, am I allowed to hit her now? They said, take it easy, sir.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The influential podcast host Joe Rogan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/joe-rogan-endorses-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed Donald Trump}}}\uc2  for president, writing on social media that his choice had been influenced by \u8220\'20\'1Cthe great and powerful Elon Musk\u8221\'20\'1D. Musk \u8220\'20\'1Cmakes what I think is the most compelling case for Trump you\u8217\'20\'19ll hear, and I agree with him every step of the way\u8221\'20\'1D, Rogan wrote on X. \u8220\'20\'1CFor the record, yes, that\u8217\'20\'19s an endorsement of Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The $1m-a-day voter sweepstakes that Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s political action committee is hosting in swing states can continue through Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/elon-musk-giveaway-winners-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Pennsylvania judge ruled}}}\uc2  on Monday. The common pleas court judge Angelo Foglietta \u8211\'20\'13 ruling after Musk\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers said the winners are not chosen by chance \u8211\'20\'13 did not immediately give a reason for the ruling.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A political action committee (Pac) linked to Elon Musk is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/election-musk-pac-michigan-ads-israel-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused of targeting Jewish and Arab American voters}}}\uc2  in swing states with dramatically different messages about Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s position on Gaza, a strategy by Trump allies aimed at peeling off Democratic support for the vice-president.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/10/31/billboards-mailers-texts-arab-american-voters-detroit-area-election-day-dearborn/75942617007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texts, mailers, social media ads and billboards}}}\uc2  targeting heavily Arab American areas in metro Detroit paint Harris as a staunch ally of Israel who will continue supplying arms to the country. Meanwhile, residents in metro Detroit or areas of Pennsylvania with higher Jewish populations have been receiving messaging that underscores her alleged support for the Palestinian cause.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican mega-donors Dick and Liz Uihlein, who are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/elections-overview/biggest-donors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the third largest donors in this year\u8217\'20\'19s US presidential election}}}\uc2 , have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/election-republican-uline-survey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought information about who employees at their company Uline will be voting for}}}\uc2  in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s ballot. A screenshot seen by the Guardian shows how employees at the private {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/wisconsin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2  paper and office products distributor were asked to take part in what was called an anonymous survey to track who the employees were voting for on 5 November.\par \par \uc2 Read more of the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 US election coverage}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/when-do-polls-close-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When do polls close}}}\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/election-electoral-college-votes-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 electoral college works}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/election-abortion-ballot-measures-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Where is \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  on the ballot?}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/senate-races-elections-to-watch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/11/house-races-2024-elections-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House}}}\uc2  races to watch\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lessons from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/swing-state-polls-pennsylvania-michigan-georgia-arizona-wisconsin-nevada-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 key swing states}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/election-trump-harris-policies-issues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump v Harris on key issues}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/03/if-trump-wins-the-election-these-11-issues-will-be-under-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s at stake}}}\uc2  in this election\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/03/us-presidential-election-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What to know about the US election}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241105ekb5000p1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
