\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18We shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be going back in time\u8217\'20\'19: Americans in swing states on who they voted for \u8211\'20\'13 and why\b0\par\par\uc2 George Chidi, Rachel Leingang and Sam Levine \par \uc2 1,459 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 November 2024\par 19:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 9\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 From \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the border and tax policies, voters explain why they cast their ballot for Trump, Harris or neither\par \par \uc2 Ryan Swingle (51) and Amy Martin (51)\par \par \uc2 Swingle: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve grown up a Democrat my whole life. So I suppose I was programmed to do it. That said, the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  world is something that I find pretty repellent. It feels very bullying-ish to me, and mean-spirited. I am disturbed by what I consider the casualness with which he lies. I\u8217\'20\'19m disturbed by the ways in which he seems to fawn over and support really awful regimes. I think we\u8217\'20\'19re on the cusp of a new and fundamentally different world with AI, and I want somebody smarter and more humble at the wheel when that happens.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Martin: \u8220\'20\'1CI just think he\u8217\'20\'19s a horrible human being, and I cannot vote for that. On \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it was right. What he did was horrible. We shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be going back in time..\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Location: Athens, Georgia\par \par \uc2 Voting for: Harris\par \par \uc2 Felix Garcia (59)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI decided to vote for him because I\u8217\'20\'19m very concerned with the economy, the border. He said he can bring the companies to implement the jobs over here. I don\u8217\'20\'19t like the things they\u8217\'20\'19re teaching my kids in the school. A lot of bad things. Trump didn\u8217\'20\'19t say [the racist comments about Puerto Rico at his \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally]. It\u8217\'20\'19s not coming from him. He came to work for all America, not only Puerto Ricans. Not only Black guys. All of them. And I\u8217\'20\'19m happy with that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Voting location: Allentown, Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Voting for: Trump\par \par \uc2 Autumn Rae Garcia (26)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m really left and so for me a Democrat is like a glorified Republican. I, at first, was really uncomfortable with the idea voting for Harris and Trump, but at the end of the day, I will not be a person that won\u8217\'20\'19t vote. Then I have no right to complain. When Harris started talking about certain policies that I really back up domestically, I appreciated that. The tax breaks for people making under $400,000: that\u8217\'20\'19s huge. I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna be honest. If Trump was coming up with actual policies instead of just the bull crap that comes out of his mouth, we would probably be having a different conversation..\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Location: Decatur, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Voting for: Harris\par \par \uc2 Josh Enders (36)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m new to Arizona so I don\u8217\'20\'19t know everything about all the people. But I made sure that I came and voted against people who were against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that were trying to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I know we\u8217\'20\'19re not in a great place and with the two candidates that we have that are potentially running the country, I don\u8217\'20\'19t feel like we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be in any better position.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Voting location: Scottsdale, Arizona\par \par \uc2 Voting for: Neither candidate\par \par \uc2 Jake Moser (22)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor me, I think a large part of it is ethics. It was really tough for me to vote for somebody who had said so many negative things about the American people. I think the thing about being president is that being in that office means you need to bring people together and not push them away. And I think dividing the country is just something that personally I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t agree with. So that\u8217\'20\'19s why I voted for Kamala.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Location: Bethlehem, Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Voting for: Harris\par \par \uc2 Brad Fogle (66) and Denise Fogle (59)\par \par \uc2 Brad: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m one of those people \u8211\'20\'13 I don\u8217\'20\'19t particularly like the personality of Trump but I like the policies. And then all the fascist comments and the negativity about Trump: you ask 90% of Americans, exactly what is a fascist, by definition? And I want to tell you something. I had to \uc2 Google\uc2  it two days ago because I\u8217\'20\'19m a 66-year-old devout voter, registered Democrat and I didn\u8217\'20\'19t exactly know. But the last Democrat I voted for was \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2 . Even though I may not be like-minded with something, whoever\u8217\'20\'19s elected, I support: that\u8217\'20\'19s our president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Denise: \u8220\'20\'1CI voted for Trump because my pocketbook is happier when he\u8217\'20\'19s in office. And I may not like all his mean, mean stuff he does, but when my pocketbook is happy, I\u8217\'20\'19m happy. Honestly, she\u8217\'20\'19s had three years in office. What have you done? What have you done? If you did something, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to listen to you, but you opened the border. You\u8217\'20\'19re going to get all the illegals in this country. I don\u8217\'20\'19t have a problem, but come in here legally.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Location: Stockbridge, Georgia\par \par \uc2 Voting for: Trump\par \par \uc2 Jesse Torrez (67)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCertainly it\u8217\'20\'19s her ideology, but most importantly it\u8217\'20\'19s the other guy who you\u8217\'20\'19d have to be insane to vote for. We will live through anything, this country\u8217\'20\'19s resilient. But I\u8217\'20\'19m thinking about my grandchildren and what they\u8217\'20\'19re going to need to face in the future, and I just have no confidence in the Republican candidate\u8217\'20\'19s leadership or capabilities to lead this country. He\u8217\'20\'19s proven that to me. I\u8217\'20\'19m registered as an independent. It\u8217\'20\'19s qualifications to me, and certainly character. Trump has displayed no character at all to me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Location: Scottsdale, Arizona\par \par \uc2 Voting for: Harris\par \par \uc2 Cyndi Keen (66)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m straight Republican all the way. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been a Republican all my life, so when it comes down to looking at having a better life for my children, for my grandkids and for myself, I like the Republican policies better. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be close. And I\u8217\'20\'19m in a house divided, my sweetie went the other way. He\u8217\'20\'19s straight Republican but he voted for Harris.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Voting location: Scottsdale, Arizona\par \par \uc2 Voting for: Trump\par \par \uc2 Rowan Allen (62) and Arlene Allen (64)\par \par \uc2 Rowan: \u8220\'20\'1CMake America safe again. Make America whole again. Her values are more aligned with mine. Somebody with moral standards and ethics versus somebody who I see has none. The things she\u8217\'20\'19s fighting for \u8211\'20\'13 the right to choose, the promotion of the middle class, making everybody pay their fair share \u8211\'20\'13 those are things that I value and that\u8217\'20\'19s what draws me to her. You need some way of unifying the country at this point, and someone who\u8217\'20\'19s not going to bring turmoil and what we had those four years. It was just chaos.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Arlene: \u8220\'20\'1CMost importantly, she\u8217\'20\'19s fighting for the Black, poor people. Women\u8217\'20\'19s rights. Those are the two most important things for me. And healthcare. Trump is a racist, and I believe that the majority of people who follow Trump are racists. Have you seen Trump say anything positive about anyone who has run for this election or the election before? There\u8217\'20\'19s always something to degrade the person who is running against him. If he loses, he\u8217\'20\'19s going to say he won. He\u8217\'20\'19s starting to set that up with the things he\u8217\'20\'19s saying right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Voting location: Ellenwood, Georgia\par \par \uc2 Voting for: Harris\par \par \uc2 Stephen Super (22)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19ll close the border, keep taxes down. I knew from the start [who I\u8217\'20\'19d for vote for]. I could see it in my everyday life. How much I pay for food. How much, like, the beef has gone up, that\u8217\'20\'19s one of the main things I buy at the grocery store. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been seeing it in my everyday life for the past three years now. Trump is strong. When you look at him he\u8217\'20\'19s a strong person. I mean he takes action on what he does. The way he speaks, everything about him. I feel like he\u8217\'20\'19s gonna stand up for our country and make it strong again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Location: Bethlehem, Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Voting for: Trump\par \par \uc2 Alexis Deville (33)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s shown herself to be a very educated woman and has an immaculate r\u233\'00\'E9sum\u233\'00\'E9. How could I vote for anybody else? Of course \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is important \u8211\'20\'13 being a healthcare worker myself, knowing that it\u8217\'20\'19s very important to be able to help our patients. As much as I\u8217\'20\'19m hoping we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have our first woman president, I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure how it will go. But I\u8217\'20\'19m hoping that America pulls together and tries something new. I\u8217\'20\'19m a little anxious, I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to lie. At the end of the day, this is a democracy and I\u8217\'20\'19d like to keep it that way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Voting location: Scottsdale, Arizona\par \par \uc2 Voting for: Harris\par \par \uc2 Interviews have been edited for length and clarity\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241105ekb50035y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
