\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Democrats are scrambling to keep the Senate. Could an old-school bipartisan help save it?\b0\par\par\uc2 Maanvi Singh in Reno, Nevada \par \uc2 1,912 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 November 2024\par 18:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2 , the Democratic Nevada senator, is running a re-election campaign on local issues in the key swing state\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEverybody\u8217\'20\'19s got their comfy shoes?\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2  scanned the room full of union workers who were preparing canvas for her in Reno, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nevada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nevada}}}\uc2 . The room erupted in response.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose gym shoes are going to be worn out,\u8221\'20\'1D the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic}}}\uc2  senator told the crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CBut that\u8217\'20\'19s OK. Those holes in the bottom mean you\u8217\'20\'19re doing the good work \u8230\'20\'26 helping return the Democratic majority in the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rosen has been wearing out her own shoes \u8211\'20\'13 crisscrossing the state and running one of the most aggressive and persistent re- {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 election}}}\uc2  campaigns in the country as she fights to preserve her own career, and a precarious party advantage in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate}}}\uc2 . Her campaign message has matched her practical footwear.\par \par \uc2 Her platform has focused on a few big, national issues \u8211\'20\'13 including the cost of living and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 but also many small ones specific to her geographically vast, politically enigmatic state. She touts her record preserving a local postal hub in northern Nevada, bringing in money for a solar facility.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re trying to take care of what we have here, and we want our kids to have a good place to grow up,\u8221\'20\'1D she told members of Culinary Workers Union Local 226 \u8211\'20\'13 a powerful organisation representing tens of thousands of hospitality workers in the state. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what everyone wants.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/20/us-elections-2024-early-voting-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 early voting}}}\uc2  in Nevada already underway, Rosen holds an eight-point lead in polling averages. But she\u8217\'20\'19s not letting up or taking any chances. Armies of volunteers from unions and a coalition of moderate and progressive political groups are knocking on doors on her behalf. And a barrage of advertisements, on the radio and television, in English and Spanish \u8211\'20\'13 are tearing down her opponent Sam Brown, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  -backed Republican that Rosen has characterised as extreme.\par \par \uc2 The race will be a test of whether candidates like her \u8211\'20\'13 a pragmatic, old-school bipartisan focused on local issues \u8211\'20\'13 can prevail in a politically polarised country. The outcome in Nevada will help determine which party controls the closely divided Senate, with the power to either impede of enable the agenda of Trump or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In April, the non-partisan Cook Political Report had ranked the race a \u8220\'20\'1Ctoss-up\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 in a swing state that appeared {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/10/21/nevada-independent-voters-swing-state-2024-election-00184609"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasingly inscrutable}}}\uc2  to pollsters. In 2022, the Democratic senator \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  won her seat by fewer than 8,000 votes.\par \par \uc2 And Rosen\u8217\'20\'19s challenger, Sam Brown, a military veteran and Purple Heart recipient, had the makings of a model candidate \u8211\'20\'13 one who could help Republicans pick up a Senate seat and flip the chamber for the party. But by August, the polling agency had moved the race to \u8220\'20\'1Cleaning Democrat\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 citing growing enthusiasm for Democrats following Harris\u8217\'20\'19s entry into the race, as well as Brown\u8217\'20\'19s failure to drum up much enthusiasm.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSam Brown just didn\u8217\'20\'19t turn out to be the candidate that I think Republicans hoped he would be \u8211\'20\'13 in terms of energy, in terms of fundraising, in terms of just doing what\u8217\'20\'19s needed,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Byler, chief of research at the polling firm Noble Predictive Insights. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd then you have a Democratic incumbent who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have any obvious flaws.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Paradoxically, Rosen\u8217\'20\'19s unobtrusive temperament and heads-down approach to her first term could become her greatest asset. In Las Vegas and Reno, dozens of voters told the Guardian they weren\u8217\'20\'19t particularly familiar with Rosen\u8217\'20\'19s record \u8211\'20\'13 but she seemed to be doing just fine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe does what she says she\u8217\'20\'19s gonna do,\u8221\'20\'1D said Vivian Jackson, 69, of Las Vegas. \u8220\'20\'1CThey try to attack her, but she\u8217\'20\'19s not like that. She\u8217\'20\'19s a real person.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s occasionally said some stuff that\u8217\'20\'19s given me pause,\u8221\'20\'1D said her neighbour Kenneth Logan, 65, a retired bartender and veteran who lives in west Las Vegas. On several issues, his politics are to the left of Rosen\u8217\'20\'19s. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I\u8217\'20\'19m probably going to vote for her. She\u8217\'20\'19s doing fine, and I can\u8217\'20\'19t think of a candidate I\u8217\'20\'19d vote for instead of her.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rosen is a former computer programmer and synagogue president who was hand-picked to run for Congress, and then the Senate \u8211\'20\'13 seemingly out of nowhere \u8211\'20\'13 by Harry Reid, the former Democratic senate leader from Nevada who helped reshape the state\u8217\'20\'19s politics over his long political career. In 2018 \u8211\'20\'13 after serving just two years in Congress \u8211\'20\'13 she unseated Republican senator Dean Heller with a five-point margin, largely relying on support from the state\u8217\'20\'19s powerful labour unions and by emphasising her support for the Affordable Care Act and immigration reform. Heller had embraced Trump and voted to repeal the popular health care law.\par \par \uc2 Six years later, Nevada \u8211\'20\'13 like the US at large \u8211\'20\'13 is much more politically polarised. Canvassers for the Libre Initiative, a conservative group affiliated with mega-donor \uc2 Charles Koch\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s political network, have been messaging to mostly Latino voters that Rosen is closely tied with the Biden administration. \u8220\'20\'1CShe voted 94% of the time with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Eddie Diaz, a strategic director at Libre in Nevada. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd people are not better off than they were before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But unlike many of her colleagues, Rosen has shied away from a national profile, forgoing the Democratic national convention in August in favour of staying in Nevada to campaign there.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think she\u8217\'20\'19s done a decent job so far, and that\u8217\'20\'19s largely because she\u8217\'20\'19s moderate, and bipartisan,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kim, 66, a mental health and wellness educator who said she didn\u8217\'20\'19t want to share her full name because many of her family and clients are staunch Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Her partner, Luis, 55, used to belong to the same synagogue as Rosen. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a small world,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Gladis Blanco, a political organiser with the Culinary Workers Union in Reno, said she credits Rosen for working with the administration to lower the cost of asthma medication. A single mother of three, Blanco said both she and several of her children have asthma \u8211\'20\'13 and new price caps on inhalers have transformed her family\u8217\'20\'19s monthly budget. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I tell voters about that they get so excited,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile Miguel Martinez, a Reno city council member who has been canvassing on behalf of Rosen and Harris, said he was especially impressed that Rosen successfully fought against the US postal service plan to move all mail processing from its Reno facility to California, which locals, especially in remote regions of rural northern Nevada, worried would result in delayed medication deliveries and mail ballot processing. \u8220\'20\'1CThat was a really big win in our community,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 And much like her mentor Reid, who was famous for funnelling funds to the state, Rosen has managed to win allies by delivering federal aid to the state\u8217\'20\'19s cities and rural communities.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, several rural Republican officials have backed Rosen over Brown \u8211\'20\'13 noting, simply, that they\u8217\'20\'19re happy with the incumbent\u8217\'20\'19s record. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2  helped bring Democrats and Republicans together to pass the largest infrastructure investment in a generation,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nathan Robertson, the Republican mayor of the small eastern Nevada town of Ely. \u8220\'20\'1CThat law is now leading to better and safer roads for our residents, including $24m in federal transportation funding to improve Ely\u8217\'20\'19s streets and sidewalks and revitalise our downtown.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ed Lawson \u8211\'20\'13 the Republican mayor of Sparks, a small city just outside Reno \u8211\'20\'13 similarly cited all the funding she has brought to his region. Just a day prior to his endorsement, Rosen and Cortez Masto announced that they had secured $275m in federal funding to enhance a major highway corridor east of Sparks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m a lifelong Republican who has never voted for a Democrat, but this November I\u8217\'20\'19ll be voting for \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 It has helped Rosen\u8217\'20\'19s cause that Brown has floundered though the election cycle.\par \par \uc2 With early voting underway, the Senate Leadership Fund \u8211\'20\'13 the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s main outside group supporting Senate races \u8211\'20\'13 announced it would spend an addition $6.2m on TV, radio and digital ads for Brown. But it\u8217\'20\'19s unclear if the funds will come too late.\par \par \uc2 Brown has often leaned on his personal story in appeals to voters. In 2008, when he was a US army officer in Afghanistan, his Humvee hit a roadside bomb. The explosion caused third-degree burns and Brown had to endure dozens of reconstructive surgeries. The experience was transformative, Brown has said. \u8220\'20\'1CGod saved me for a purpose,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote in a recent campaign email.\par \par \uc2 But while he has made clear why he\u8217\'20\'19s running for office, he has struggled to define how for voters he would govern.\par \par \uc2 Trump endorsed Brown just days before the primary elections and since then Brown has clung tightly to the former president and his platform. Brown said he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have supported the Bipartisan Infrastructure Law or the Inflation Reduction Act \u8211\'20\'13 Biden administration programs that have brought unprecedented federal dollars into the state and help fund a range of projects. His past support for storing nuclear waste in Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s Yucca Mountain \u8211\'20\'13 a third rail of politics in the state \u8211\'20\'13 has also left the impression that he is out of touch with Nevada.\par \par \uc2 Such missteps have opened the opportunity for an easy critique \u8211\'20\'13 that Brown is a newcomer, one who moved from Dallas to Reno in 2018, and simply doesn\u8217\'20\'19t know enough about the state.\par \par \uc2 His muddled stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also played badly. In attack ads, Rosen has called Brown a \u8220\'20\'1CMaga extremist\u8221\'20\'1D who would take away \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. And though Brown has responded by saying he supports Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/29/abortion-laws-bans-by-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 current law}}}\uc2 , which allows abortions up to 24 weeks \u8211\'20\'13 he has repeatedly dodged questions on whether he\u8217\'20\'19ll support the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/20/nevada-signatures-abortion-vote-november"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state\u8217\'20\'19s \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ballot initiative}}}\uc2 , which aims to enshrine Nevada\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution.\par \par \uc2 Nearly 70% of Republicans and 90% of Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thenevadaindependent.com/article/poll-nevada-voters-want-expanded-birth-control-access-oppose-abortion-criminalization"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said they opposed}}}\uc2  criminalising \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to a recent poll by the Program for Public Consultation at the University of Maryland.\par \par \uc2 Diane Gutierrez, a 65-year-old real estate agent based in Reno, said she is personally opposed to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , due to her faith, but believes it should remain protected. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that that should be taken away from any woman,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just not OK to go backwards.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A registered non-partisan, Gutierrez said she\u8217\'20\'19s voted for both Republican and Democratic candidates in the past. But in recent years, she has gotten more involved in volunteering with the Democratic party \u8211\'20\'13 and has largely steered clear of Republicans. \u8220\'20\'1CThe party has had time, but they haven\u8217\'20\'19t selected good candidates,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding they\u8217\'20\'19ve failed to make a good case to voters. Initially, she thought Brown bucked the trend.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBeing from a military family \u8211\'20\'13 my dad was a marine \u8211\'20\'13 I appreciate Sam Brown and thank him for his service because obviously he paid a huge price,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you\u8217\'20\'19re in the military, you have respect.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But his failure to define a platform of his own has been disappointing, she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI would like him to speak up more,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhere\u8217\'20\'19s Sam Brown? Is he in Nevada? It\u8217\'20\'19s like, \u8216\'20\'18Sam \u8211\'20\'13 say something.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241105ekb5002xq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
