\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18If Harris wins, it\u8217\'20\'19s because of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19: election tests fallout from Roe reversal\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman in Phoenix \par \uc2 1,096 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 November 2024\par 17:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 7\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Arizona is one of 10 states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a top voting issue, on ballots. Could a Trump presidency unravel measures?Ten states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on the ballot this election dayUS election results 2024: live map and tracker\par \par \uc2 Leslie Lemus\u8217\'20\'19s top issue in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 election}}}\uc2  is probably the economy. But she has a close second: \u8220\'20\'1CThem fucking with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Really, for the 26-year-old {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2  native, the two issues are one and the same. On Monday, she got an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Camelback Family Planning, one of the last \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in Arizona, in large part because Lemus feels like she can\u8217\'20\'19t financially care for a child right now.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI look at the world and it\u8217\'20\'19s not very pretty. I\u8217\'20\'19m not ready for that yet, to bring a child into the world right now, where the economy is not OK,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lemus, who said she lived paycheck to paycheck. Some months, she has to choose between making her car payments and paying off her credit card debt. \u8220\'20\'1CEverybody\u8217\'20\'19s struggling left and right.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lemus is registered to vote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/arizona-political-violence-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maricopa county}}}\uc2 , which is home to 60% of the Arizona electorate and may determine whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  wins the valuable swing state. Harris has made access to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  a key part of her policy platform \u8211\'20\'13 particularly as a contrast to Trump, who appointed three of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices who overturned {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  and who has toggled between branding himself as a champion of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  and as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most pro-life president\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lemus is a passionate supporter of Harris, who she calls \u8220\'20\'1Cmy homegirl\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Majorities of Americans have backed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and Roe v Wade for decades, but it was rarely their top issue in the voting booth. Now that the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has overturned Roe, permitting more than a dozen states to ban almost all abortions and several more to ban it at six, 12, or \u8211\'20\'13 as in Arizona \u8211\'20\'13 15 weeks, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  may become the deciding issue of the 2024 election. It is now the most important issue for women under 45, like Lemus.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Harris wins the election, it will be because of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and women voting for her in large part because of that issue,\u8221\'20\'1D said Tresa Undem, a pollster who\u8217\'20\'19s been surveying people about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for more than two decades.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Camelback had about 40 patients to see; at least one had traveled in from Texas, which bans almost all abortions. Visitors to the lobby were greeted by a sign urging them to register to vote while they waited for their \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The sign advised: \u8220\'20\'1CThe health of our democracy is in our hands.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18That gives me hope\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Arizona will become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/election-abortion-ballot-measures-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of 10 states}}}\uc2  where voters will decide whether to amend their state constitutions to add or expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections. (In one of those states, Nebraska, voters will vote on both a ballot measure that could expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and on the nation\u8217\'20\'19s sole anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measure.) Five of those states, including Arizona, have some kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban on the books. If any of the measures supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights pass, it would be the first time that a state has overturned a post-Roe v Wade ban.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have long hoped these measures would boost turnout among their base, but the rosy polling for the measures in steadfastly red states indicates that a significant swath of voters are essentially splitting their votes by supporting both \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and Republicans, the party that helped engineer Roe\u8217\'20\'19s downfall. Although the measure looks likely to pass in Arizona, for example, polling suggests that Trump will win the state.\par \par \uc2 Julio Morera helped collect signatures at the Arizona state fair in order to get the measure on the ballot. His group\u8217\'20\'19s booth, he recalled, was set up next to a man who was hawking rightwing memorabilia adorned with eagles, guns and the slogan \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t Tread On Me\u8221\'20\'1D. When asked to sign the petition, the man demurred. \u8220\'20\'1CI got customers to think about,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 But at the very end of the fair, Morera said, the man added his signature.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat gives me hope that this is gonna pass,\u8221\'20\'1D Morera said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are quite a few people that may not be Democrats or left-leaning who would support this access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A vote for Trump, however, may ultimately cancel out a vote for a ballot measure. If {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/21/idaho-abortion-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump wins the presidency}}}\uc2 , he will be able to skirt Congress and use a 19th-century anti-vice law known as the Comstock Act to ban the mailing of all \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related materials \u8211\'20\'13 which would result in a de facto national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and render these measures\u8217\'20\'19 successes moot.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2 , an influential policy playbook for the next conservative administration, suggests using the Comstock Act to at least ban the mailing of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pills, which account for roughly two-thirds of US abortions. It also suggests rolling back privacy protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients and reshaping the nation\u8217\'20\'19s largest family planning program, which would curtail access to contraception, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/project-2025-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 among a bevy of other anti-\b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  policies}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harris, meanwhile, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/19/harris-abortion-rights-early-voting-atlanta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 forcefully defended \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1COver these past two years, the impact of Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans has been devastating,\u8221\'20\'1D she told a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/beyonce-brings-star-power-to-harris-rally-in-texas-with-abortion-law-in-the-spotlight"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally in Texas}}}\uc2  in October. \u8220\'20\'1CWe see the horrific reality that women and families face every single day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For Lemus, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans all come down to one thing: \u8220\'20\'1CMen being in control of women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The economy was not the only reason that Lemus sought an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday. She is also worried about the mental toll of having a child. At 18, Lemus gave birth to a son who was born prematurely and died just a month after birth.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was there with all the medical stuff, seeing my child in the incubator until he passed away,\u8221\'20\'1D she said quietly. Eight years later, Lemus is not ready to have another one.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe fought so hard to have choices,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy do they feel like we can\u8217\'20\'19t have a choice?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more of the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s 2024 US election coverage\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/when-do-polls-close-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When do polls close}}}\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/election-electoral-college-votes-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  electoral college works}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/election-abortion-ballot-measures-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Where is \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  on the ballot?}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/senate-races-elections-to-watch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/11/house-races-2024-elections-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  House}}}\uc2  races to watch\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lessons from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/swing-state-polls-pennsylvania-michigan-georgia-arizona-wisconsin-nevada-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  key swing states}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/election-trump-harris-policies-issues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump v Harris on key issues}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/03/if-trump-wins-the-election-these-11-issues-will-be-under-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s at stake}}}\uc2  in this election\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/03/us-presidential-election-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What to know about the US election}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN00002