\par\par \uc2 Australia news\par \b \uc2 Guardian Essential poll: US gender divide in support for Harris and Trump mirrored among Australians\b0\par\par\uc2 Paul Karp Chief political correspondent \par \uc2 752 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 November 2024\par 05:59 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 There was strong support for legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  among respondents surveyed about the US election, but almost 60% agreed with key elements of former president\u8217\'20\'19s platformUS election 2024 live: latest polls, results and updatesUS election guide for Australia: dates, polls, times, results and moreGet our breaking news email, free app or daily news podcast\par \par \uc2 More Australian men would vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  than vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and a majority of men and women support key elements of his platform including tariffs and deportation of illegal immigrants.\par \par \uc2 Those are the results of the latest Guardian Essential poll of 1,131 voters finding that the strong gender divide in Trump and Harris\u8217\'20\'19 support is mirrored in Australia.\par \par \uc2 Overall, more Australians (41%) would vote Harris for president, if they were eligible, than would support Trump (33%). A further 7% would vote for \u8220\'20\'1Canother candidate\u8221\'20\'1D, 13% \u8220\'20\'1Cwould not vote\u8221\'20\'1D and 7% are unsure.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=copyembed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up for Guardian Australia\u8217\'20\'19s breaking news email}}}\par \par \uc2 Among Australian men, Trump leads by 44% to Harris\u8217\'20\'19 36%; while among women Harris leads 45% to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 23%.\par \par \uc2 More respondents said that if Harris were elected president of the United States this would be good for Australia (32%) than said it would be bad (26%).\par \par \uc2 If Trump were victorious in the election, to be held Tuesday in the US with results on Wednesday Australian time, more said this would be bad (44%) than good (28%) for Australia.\par \par \uc2 A majority of respondents agreed with statements summarising Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies (without mentioning him by name), including \u8220\'20\'1Cglobalisation has gone too far, we need to protect local workers with tariffs on foreign goods\u8221\'20\'1D (60% agree).\par \par \uc2 Almost 60% of respondents agreed with each of the statements that \u8220\'20\'1Cgovernment is fundamentally corrupt and politics has been taken over by vested interests\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Ca deep state of unelected officials has too much control\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal immigrants should be deported\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Opposition to the Indigenous voice and politicisation of Palestinian visas has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/article/2024/aug/26/jim-chalmers-calls-peter-dutton-most-divisive-leader-in-modern-australian-history"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 led to Labor labelling the Liberal leader, Peter Dutton, \u8220\'20\'1Cdivisive\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theconversation.com/can-a-trumpist-approach-to-politics-work-in-australia-241780"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 progressive commentators likening his tactics to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the Albanese government\u8217\'20\'19s bill to force unlawful non-citizens to cooperate with their deportation and black-ban visa applications from countries that don\u8217\'20\'19t accept involuntary removals has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/mar/28/labor-deportation-bill-blacklist-entire-countries-citizens-visas-australia-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attracted comparisons to Trump from the Greens}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Australia, Trump has support from sections of the Liberal-National Coalition including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/article/2024/may/31/anthony-albanese-donald-trump-hush-money-trial-guilty-verdict-no-comment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Matt Canavan}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.skynews.com.au/australia-news/politics/liberal-senator-alex-antic-praises-donald-trump-for-shifting-us-political-discourse-and-calls-out-wokeness-in-speech-at-cpac/news-story/0f0d04751840681937aa368b4036cd90"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alex Antic}}}\uc2 , and rightwing minor parties including One Nation and the United Australia party senator, Ralph Babet.\par \par \uc2 The poll found Labor and Greens supporters were much more likely to support Harris than Trump, with Harris up 55% to 22% among Labor and 54% to 18% among Greens voters.\par \par \uc2 Trump enjoyed a lead over Harris among Coalition voters, 47% to 33%, and minor parties and independents, 44% to 27%.\par \par \uc2 However, the poll could spell trouble for importation of US-style culture wars over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Essential found that most respondents wanted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be legal \u8220\'20\'1Cin all cases\u8221\'20\'1D (41%) or \u8220\'20\'1Cmost cases\u8221\'20\'1D (38%). Only about one-in-five wanted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be illegal \u8220\'20\'1Cin most cases\u8221\'20\'1D (14%) or \u8220\'20\'1Cin all cases\u8221\'20\'1D (7%).\par \par \uc2 On Monday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afr.com/politics/federal/rudd-wong-scramble-to-shore-up-trump-ties-in-coin-flip-election-20241030-p5kmjp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Australian Financial Review reported}}}\uc2  that the foreign minister, \uc2 Penny Wong\uc2 , and defence minister, \uc2 Richard Marles\uc2 , have been contacting Trump contacts to prepare for the possibility of a Trump victory.\par \par \uc2 The prime minister, Anthony Albanese, appeared to confirm the report by saying \u8220\'20\'1Cwe engage with people across the US political system\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I was in the United States, I met with the Republicans, I met with the Democrats, I met with people in Congress, people in the Senate,\u8221\'20\'1D he told ABC Radio.\par \par \uc2 Asked if Australia would need to replace former prime minister \uc2 Kevin Rudd\uc2  as ambassador if Trump were elected, Albanese replied: \u8220\'20\'1CAustralia decides who our ambassador is and Mr Rudd is doing a terrific job.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In May, Trump was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found guilty of all 34 counts of falsifying business records}}}\uc2  in a criminal hush-money scheme to influence the outcome of the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 Read more of the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 US election coverage}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election 2024 live updates: latest polls, results and news}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/when-do-polls-close-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When do polls close}}}\uc2  ?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/election-electoral-college-votes-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 electoral college works}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/election-abortion-ballot-measures-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Where is \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  on the ballot?}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/senate-races-elections-to-watch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/11/house-races-2024-elections-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House}}}\uc2  races to watch\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lessons from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/swing-state-polls-pennsylvania-michigan-georgia-arizona-wisconsin-nevada-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 key swing states}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/election-trump-harris-policies-issues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump v Harris on key issues}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/03/if-trump-wins-the-election-these-11-issues-will-be-under-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s at stake}}}\uc2  in this election\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/03/us-presidential-election-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What to know about the US election}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241105ekb5000ry\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
