\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump and Harris hold final rallies in Pennsylvania \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Livingstone (now); Lois Beckett, L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong, Chris Stein and Yohannes Lowe (earlier) \par \uc2 22,331 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 November 2024\par 04:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed, you can follow the latest on our 2024 US election day live blog here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed, but you can follow the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/05/us-election-2024-live-updates-donald-trump-vs-kamala-harris-results-presidential-elections-day-latest-news-polls-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest updates on our 2024 US election day live blog here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 A dispatch from Philadelphia : Sonya Harris, 53, a sales manager in Montgomery County, said she plans to vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as soon as polls open on Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 Harris, no relation to the woman she hopes is the next president of the United States, came to the Philadelphia rally with her son because she believes that the vice president will help bring an end to the \u8220\'20\'1Cdivision, hate and chaos\u8221\'20\'1D fanned by Trump over the last decade.\par \par \uc2 Harris has gotten involved for the first time. This year, she volunteered to canvas and phonebank for Harris \u8211\'20\'13 something she has never done for a political candidate before.\par \par \uc2 She fears what Trump would do if given four more years, especially to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. She said:\par \par \uc2 I think he\u8217\'20\'19s going to roll back women\u8217\'20\'19s rights to way back when.\par \par \uc2 But Harris is not feeling anxious about the results tomorrow, quite the opposite.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m feeling joy and happiness. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think the world is as dire as the other side says... And [vice president Harris] has run a very happy campaign. It\u8217\'20\'19s been very positive, it\u8217\'20\'19s been very motivating and inspirational. You feel, we\u8217\'20\'19re not stuck where we think we are, and the world is not coming to an end.\par \par \uc2 Her neighbor leaned over and chimed in: \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s gonna win in a landslide.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was supposed to start speaking at 10.30pm local time in Grand Rapids, Michigan. Well, he didn\u8217\'20\'19t - he isn\u8217\'20\'19t even here yet - and according to a police officer I just spoke to it\u8217\'20\'19s probably going to get to midnight before Trump actually appears.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime the campaign is desperately filling time. We\u8217\'20\'19ve had an appearance from a local congressman \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CWho the hell is that?\u8221\'20\'1D a Trump supporter behind me commented \u8211\'20\'13 and some lackeys just wheeled out a sort of T-shirt machine gun, which entertained people for a bit.\par \par \uc2 In contrast to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s other rallies today, the Van Andel Arena, in downtown Grand Rapids, is actually almost full. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd let me tell you,\u8221\'20\'1D one of the speakers said just now, \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s the same number of people waiting outside who couldn\u8217\'20\'19t get in!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I was a bit bored so I got up and went and looked outside. There is not a single person out there.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Security agencies say Russia election disinformation efforts risk inciting violence\par \par \uc2 Russia-linked disinformation operations have falsely claimed officials in battleground states plan to fraudulently sway the outcome of the extraordinarily close US presidential election, authorities have warned hours before Election Day. AFP reports:\par \par \uc2 Success in the seven swing states is key to winning the White House for rivals \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and those states have previously been the focus of unsupported accusations of election fraud.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRussia is the most active threat,\u8221\'20\'1D the Office of the Director of National Intelligence (ODNI), the \uc2 FBI\uc2  and the \uc2 Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency\uc2  said Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese efforts risk inciting violence, including against election officials,\u8221\'20\'1D they added, noting the efforts are expected to intensify through Election Day and in the following weeks.\par \par \uc2 It was the latest in a series of warnings from the ODNI about foreign actors - notably Russia and Iran - allegedly spreading disinformation or hacking the campaigns during this election.\par \par \uc2 Tehran and Moscow have both denied such allegations in the past.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re expecting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on stage in Philadelphia in a few minutes for her final rally of the campaign.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Grand Rapids, Michigan, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was due on stage half an hour ago but is running late after his last rally in Pittsburgh went way over .\par \par \uc2 A succession of surrogates \u8211\'20\'13 including the mayor of Dearborn Heights, Bill Bazzi, congressman John Moolenaar, congressman Bill Huizenga, and former Trump ambassador to Germany \uc2 Rick Grenell\uc2 , have instead been stumping for Trump.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you updates on these final rallies as they come in.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Blue Wall governors are rallying for Harris in Pennsylvania. From the stage set at the iconic \u8220\'20\'1CRocky Steps\u8221\'20\'1D at the Philadelphia Museum of the Arts, Pennsylvania governor \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  invoked the city\u8217\'20\'19s legacy as the birthplace of American democracy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C248 years ago, it was here in Philly just down the street that we declared our independence from a king, and hear me on this. We are not going back to a king in this country,\u8221\'20\'1D Shapiro said in a rousing speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBig Gretch is calling on you to get out and vote,\u8221\'20\'1D Michigan governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  told voters in a speech from Detroit, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 As Trump and his surrogates have increased talk of election fraud, fears are growing among some that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters could again turn to violence in the aftermath of a defeat.\par \par \uc2 At the Trump rally in Grand Rapids, Michigan, however, many are convinced that it would actually be Democrats who would cause trouble, should they get an unwanted result.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think Republicans take loss better than the Democrats do. So I think if we win, if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins, the Democrats will cause more harm than if the Republicans lose,\u8221\'20\'1D said Payton VanSickle, a 25-year-old Michigander who said he had already cast his vote for Trump.\par \par \uc2 Asked to square that view with what happened after Trump losing in 2020, when he attempted to overturn the result and hundreds of his supporters staged a violent insurrection at the US Capitol, VanSickle said that \u8220\'20\'1Csome shenanigans\u8221\'20\'1D had occurred during the election, and suggested the reaction to the January 6 insurrection was exaggerated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t condone it, but I believe they blew it up bigger than what it was. I think there was obviously bad actors, but from what I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen, I think there was a few people here and there that were starting things, and it was kind of follow the leader,\u8221\'20\'1D VanSickle said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 A dispatch from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 final rally in Philadelphia : \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s all about pride,\u8221\'20\'1D Fat Joe said, a proud \u8220\'20\'1CBoricua\u8221\'20\'1D. He said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s xenophobia was evident from the moment he descended the golden staircase to announce his presidential campaign in 2015.\par \par \uc2 He recalled Trump throwing paper towels at Puerto Ricans after Hurricane Maria, and insulting Haitian Americans, and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden rally, when a shock jock comedian called Puerto Rico a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Addressing \u8220\'20\'1Cmi gente Latino\u8221\'20\'1D, he asked: \u8220\'20\'1CWhere\u8217\'20\'19s your pride?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t know who you\u8217\'20\'19re voting for? You gotta be kidding me at this point,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Then Fat Joe introduced Puerto Rican Ricky Martin and the crowd went wild.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re just joining us now, here\u8217\'20\'19s a quick roundup of where we stand as we wait for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to hold their final rallies in Grand Rapids, Michigan and Philadelphia, Pennsylvania respectively.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  put all her chips on the key battleground state of Pennsylvania on Monday, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/trump-harris-election-pennsylvania-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}\uc2  indicate an extremely close contest. She held several rallies and events including a stop at a Puerto Rican restaurant with Congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  and directly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/nanditab1/status/1853589842266910947?s=46"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined canvassing}}}\uc2  in a residential area in Reading, telling voters at one home: \u8220\'20\'1CI wanted to go door-knocking!\u8221\'20\'1D\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/trump-harris-election-pennsylvania-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought to strike a positive tone}}}\uc2 , saying she wanted to be a \u8220\'20\'1Cpresident for all Americans\u8221\'20\'1D. A sign of a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong\u8221\'20\'1D leader is someone willing to listen to the experts, the stakeholders and those who disagree, she said at a rally in Pittsburgh.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  meanwhile held rallies in Raleigh, North Carolina, two in Pennsylvania, but his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/trump-harris-election-pennsylvania-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tone was much darker}}}\uc2 , focusing on painting migrants as dangerous criminals while also launching personal attacks on a number of high-profile Democratic women. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re killing people. They\u8217\'20\'19re killing people at will,\u8221\'20\'1D he said at one rally, giving gruesome details of specific murders allegedly committed by undocumented migrants. In North Caroliana he called Democratic congresswoman \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazyass bedbug\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/04/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-polls-latest-live-news?page=with:block-6728f9478f082a575b9e59bb#block-6728f9478f082a575b9e59bb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacked}}}\uc2  former first lady \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 , saying: \u8220\'20\'1CShe hit me the other day. I was going to say to my people, am I allowed to hit her now? They said, take it easy, sir.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The influential podcast host Joe Rogan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/joe-rogan-endorses-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed Donald Trump}}}\uc2  for president, writing on social media that his choice had been influenced by \u8220\'20\'1Cthe great and powerful \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. Musk \u8220\'20\'1Cmakes what I think is the most compelling case for Trump you\u8217\'20\'19ll hear, and I agree with him every step of the way\u8221\'20\'1D, Rogan wrote on X. \u8220\'20\'1CFor the record, yes, that\u8217\'20\'19s an endorsement of Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The $1m-a-day voter sweepstakes that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s political action committee is hosting in swing states can continue through Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/elon-musk-giveaway-winners-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Pennsylvania judge ruled}}}\uc2  on Monday. The common pleas court judge Angelo Foglietta \u8211\'20\'13 ruling after Musk\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers said the winners are not chosen by chance \u8211\'20\'13 did not immediately give a reason for the ruling.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A political action committee (Pac) linked to \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/election-musk-pac-michigan-ads-israel-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused of targeting Jewish and Arab American voters}}}\uc2  in swing states with dramatically different messages about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s position on Gaza, a strategy by Trump allies aimed at peeling off Democratic support for the vice-president.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/10/31/billboards-mailers-texts-arab-american-voters-detroit-area-election-day-dearborn/75942617007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texts, mailers, social media ads and billboards}}}\uc2  targeting heavily Arab American areas in metro Detroit paint Harris as a staunch ally of Israel who will continue supplying arms to the country. Meanwhile, residents in metro Detroit or areas of Pennsylvania with higher Jewish populations have been receiving messaging that underscores her alleged support for the Palestinian cause.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Republican mega-donors Dick and \uc2 Liz Uihlein\uc2 , who are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/elections-overview/biggest-donors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the third largest donors in this year\u8217\'20\'19s US presidential election}}}\uc2 , have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/election-republican-uline-survey"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought information about who employees at their company Uline will be voting for}}}\uc2  in Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s ballot. A screenshot seen by the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  shows how employees at the private {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/wisconsin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2  paper and office products distributor were asked to take part in what was called an anonymous survey to track who the employees were voting for on 5 November.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Betting markets {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/presidential-election-betting-odds-polling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have narrowed significantly}}}\uc2  on the eve of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, eroding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s lead over \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as Americans cast their vote. The former president and his allies have touted the betting market forecasts as more accurate than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/04/presidential-polls-today-election-donald-trump-kamala-harris-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 traditional polling}}}\uc2  in recent weeks, as the top platforms put him way ahead of Harris. As election day nears, however, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory odds have faded, and Harris even retook the lead on one platform this weekend.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 At the \uc2 MGM\uc2  Grand on the Las Vegas strip, Democratic senator \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2 , congresswoman Susie Lee and a number of party and local officials were riling up a modest crowd ahead of a performance by Christina Aguilera later tonight.\par \par \uc2 Many in the crowd \u8211\'20\'13 like most everyone at the Grand and out on the Strip \u8211\'20\'13 were from out of town. Some had come to help get out the vote. Louis LeGrand, a field director with the \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2  (\uc2 Seiu\uc2 ) had come from California \u8211\'20\'13 to make sure that Nevada workers knew how important their votes were in this crucial swing state. \u8220\'20\'1CI think we\u8217\'20\'19ve turned out a lot of folks,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CJust by talking to people and making them realize this is a battleground, it makes a difference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Others in attendance were tourists. Damian DJ Jackson of Georgia was staying at the \uc2 MGM\uc2  hotel, and wandered over after spotting signs for the rally and concert. He had already voted early for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Clayton County \u8211\'20\'13 a key district in another key swing state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m excited, just because she\u8217\'20\'19ll be the first African American, as well as the first woman to do it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI believe a woman who knows what she\u8217\'20\'19s doing, that can be, that can be a leader, will lead us to the water. That\u8217\'20\'19s what we need in the US.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 From a watch party in Atlanta, Avery Davis Bell shared her deeply personal and still raw story of being delayed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care under her state\u8217\'20\'19s ban after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Two weeks ago, Davis Bell, a genetics researcher and mother of one, was 18 weeks pregnant with her \u8220\'20\'1Cvery wanted second baby\u8221\'20\'1D. Then she began hemorraging.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the hospital my doctors were clear. My water had broken prematurely. My baby would not survive and what was happening could kill me,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, her voice catching.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sorry,\u8221\'20\'1D someone shouted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban my doctors had to ignore their years of training and wait until I was near enough to death to intervene. No doctor should be put in that situation. No mother, no family should either. An \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban nearly took my life,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is one of the most salient issues this election, and it appears to be driving high turnout. Across the country, women have been speaking out and sharing their stories to raise awareness of the harm caused when \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is inaccessible.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis loss is so very fresh for me and my family but I am here anyway because our lives depend on it,\u8221\'20\'1D she concluded, as the crowd started chanting \u8220\'20\'1CNever again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Key event\par \par \uc2 Returning to the news that Joe Rogan has endorsed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  here\u8217\'20\'19s a bit of background, courtesy of Reuters:\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s recent interview with Rogan lasted about 3 hours and was released on \uc2 YouTube\uc2  and \uc2 Spotify\uc2  in late October. The two discussed a range of topics and the interview got over 45 million views on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former president criticized Rogan in August on Truth Social, his social media platform, after the podcaster praised then-independent candidate Robert Kennedy Jr. Kennedy has since pulled out of the race and endorsed Trump. Trump later called Rogan a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood guy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump and Harris have courted voters with appearances on podcasts, in addition to more traditional rallies and media interviews.\par \par \uc2 Spotify\uc2  said in March \u8220\'20\'1CThe Joe Rogan Experience\u8221\'20\'1D had 14.5 million followers, almost triple the platform\u8217\'20\'19s second most popular program. Rogan also has more than 19 million followers on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  and 18 million followers on \uc2 YouTube\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A poll by \uc2 YouGov\uc2  last year found that 81% of his listeners are male and 56% are under 35 years old, a demographic that tends to support Trump over Harris.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19 team had been in touch with Rogan\u8217\'20\'19s program about a possible appearance but her campaign said in late October she would not appear on his podcast.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 At an election eve concert for Harris and Walz supporters at the \uc2 MGM\uc2  Grand on the Las Vegas strip, Iesha James, 34, said she was sending out some last minute texts to people she knew had not yet voted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI just need to feel like I\u8217\'20\'19m doing something,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, in the minute before the band Los Tigres del Norte took the stage. This election, more than any other she remembers, feels \u8220\'20\'1Cterrifying\u8221\'20\'1D, she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never been so afraid that a Republican will win office and all my rights will be taken away,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 James, a physician\u8217\'20\'19s assistant, said she was most worried about the consequences a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  presidency would have on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and healthcare over all. The former president spent much of his term trying to tear down the Affordable Care Act.\par \par \uc2 James said she also felt Harris would be the better of the two presidential candidates on Gaza. \u8220\'20\'1CAs vice president she\u8217\'20\'19s only able to say so much,\u8221\'20\'1D James said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut at least she has signaled that she\u8217\'20\'19s going to try to get more aid and do more to stop the suffering in Gaza.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Having grown up in Vegas, in a state that had voted for the Democratic presidential candidate in every race since 2004, James said she was shocked that the race was so close. But the sprawling, diverse state was hard to poll, she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m hoping it won\u8217\'20\'19t be as close as the polls say.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 James had come to the concert with her mother, Carol James, who had also cast her ballot for Harris. Her 94-year-old grandmother who lives in Alabama, she said, was also excited to vote for a woman of color for president for the first time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 At his Pittsburgh rally, Trump has returned to the auto-cue and is delivering what appears to be the closing argument of his Pennsylvania rally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis nation belongs to you. It was hard-working patriots like you that built our country and tomorrow, it is hard-working patriots like you who are going to save our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After almost two hours of speaking, Trump ends the rally to the strains of YMCA, waving to supporters and bopping about on stage with his signature dance moves.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump has now been speaking for more than an hour and a half in Pittsburgh. He is now speaking about the brother of one of his supporters who was killed in the September 11 attacks on the World Trade Centre.\par \par \uc2 The Republican candidate is still set to speak in Michigan later this evening.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 In Pittsburgh, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  declared: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica is ready for a fresh start.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is time for a new generation of leadership in America and I am ready to offer that leadership as the next president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, speaking from the Carrie Furnace, an outdoor historical landmark.\par \par \uc2 But she said the election wasn\u8217\'20\'19t over yet. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve still got some work to do,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, encouraging everyone who hasn\u8217\'20\'19t voted yet to do so tomorrow and to bring a friend.\par \par \uc2 Harris reminded the crowd of the stakes, as she has laid them out over the last 100 days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are fighting for our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said at the high-energy rally. A sign of a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong\u8221\'20\'1D leader is someone willing to listen to the experts, the stakeholders and those who disagree, she said. She pledged never to vilify those who disagree with her, instead she said she would give them a seat at the table.\par \par \uc2 It was time to move past the\u8221\'20\'1Dfear and division\u8221\'20\'1D of the past decade \u8211\'20\'13 an implicit but not explicit \u8211\'20\'13 reference to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe are done with that. We\u8217\'20\'19re done,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re exhausted with it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris was introduced at the Pittsburgh event by Cedric the Entertainer who said Harris was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a demagogue and yet she is not demure.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Pittsburgh, Trump is still speaking. He\u8217\'20\'19s been calling out prominent supporters at his rally, including \uc2 Mike Pompeo\uc2  (\u8220\'20\'1CHe lost all that weight, he\u8217\'20\'19s so thin now\u8221\'20\'1D), \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  (\u8220\'20\'1CA woman of great common sense\u8221\'20\'1D) and \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  (\u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s doing a great job\u8221\'20\'1D).\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMomentum is on our side\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has said at her penultimate rally in Pittsburgh, and without naming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , immediately sought to draw a contrast with her Republican rival.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInstead of stewing on an enemies list I will spend everyday working on my to-do list\u8221\'20\'1D she said, adding \u8220\'20\'1Cours if not a fight against something it is a fight for something.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will listen to people who disagree with me\u8221\'20\'1D and in fact \u8220\'20\'1CI will give them a seat at the table\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 Other soundbites included \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen you know what you stand for you know what to fight for\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cyour vote is your voice and your vote is your power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also highlighted the right of women to make decisions about their own bodies, but other than that stayed away form particular policies or themes.\par \par \uc2 Then, after just 10 minutes, she made her exit to the sound of Beyonce\u8217\'20\'19s Freedom and Katy Perry took the stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 In an election that has been defined by deep gender divides, former Fox News anchor Megyn Kelly spoke directly to these concerns: \u8220\'20\'1CHe will not look at our boys like their second class citizens,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Kelly warmed up her brief guest appearance at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Pittsburgh rally by talking about the dangers of open borders and reciting a list of anti-trans talking points. But she also got big cheers by talking about what Trump will do for boys and men.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe will look out for our boys too, our forgotten boys and our forgotten men,\u8221\'20\'1D Kelly said. \u8220\'20\'1CGuys like you, guys like these guys, who have got the calluses on their hands, who work for a living with the beards and the tats\u8230\'20\'26 [men who] don\u8217\'20\'19t want to be judged by people like Oprah and Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9, who will never have to face the consequences of her disastrous economic policies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd ladies out there who want a bit of girl power in this election, let me tell you something: How can you win when the sons and the husbands and the brothers and the dads you love are losing It\u8217\'20\'19s not a win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is speaking from Milwaukee, where his speech is being broadcast live at Harris\u8217\'20\'19s rally in Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 He told the crowd that a Harris-Walz presidency would make the country \u8220\'20\'1Cmore free\u8221\'20\'1D but that they couldn\u8217\'20\'19t let up yet. They needed to keep pushing to get out the vote in battleground Wisconsin until polls closing on Tuesday night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis thing\u8217\'20\'19s tied but we got the damn ball,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz, a former football coach, told the crowd.\par \par \uc2 He remarked that Harris had transformed the race in just over three months. \u8220\'20\'1CImagine what she\u8217\'20\'19ll do in four years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added of Harris: \u8220\'20\'1CShe has brought back the joy to our politics,\u8221\'20\'1D the crowd in Philadelphia erupted in applause.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 In Nevada, where one in five potential voters are Latino, the progressive group Make the Road Nevada had dispatched canvassers all over Las Vegas as part of their final efforts to get out the vote.\par \par \uc2 Josie Rivera, an organizer and communications associate for the organization, which focuses on turning out Latino voters, said he was feeling cautiously optimistic ahead of Election Day.\par \par \uc2 Polls ahead of the election suggested that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had more support among Latino voters, especially men, than in previous elections. Anecdotally, he said, swing voters here have been upset after a comedian at a Trump rally in New York made a joke about Puerto Rico being a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know why it took so long,\u8221\'20\'1D Rivera said, for voters to pay attention to Trump and his allies\u8217\'20\'19 offensive comments about Latinos and immigrants. \u8220\'20\'1CBut this seems to have made an impact.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  told supporters in Pittsburgh: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just come over the wires that Joe Rogan endorsed me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The crowd erupted in a huge roar.\par \par \uc2 Minutes earlier the rally heard a speech from rightwing media personality Megyn Kelly, who said she had voted for Trump because of immigration and keeping boys out of girls\u8217\'20\'19 sports.\par \par \uc2 Kelly added: \u8220\'20\'1CHe got mocked by the left for saying he would be a protector of women. He will be a protector of women, and that\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m voting for him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Rogan endorses Trump\par \par \uc2 Trump celebrated the endorsement from the powerful podcaster, who has a massive male audience, at his Pittsburgh rally.\par \par \uc2 Rogan tweeted that he agreed with \u8220\'20\'1Cthe great and powerful \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe great and powerful {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @elonmusk}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If it wasn't for him we'd be fucked. He makes what I think is the most compelling case for Trump you'll hear, and I agree with him every step of the way.\par \par \uc2 For the record, yes, that's an endorsement of Trump.\par \par \uc2 Enjoy the podcast {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LdBxZFVsLN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LdBxZFVsLN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joe Rogan (@joerogan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joerogan/status/1853614670764015762?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has taken the stage in Pittsburgh, where she\u8217\'20\'19s holding her penultimate rally of the day.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 In Philadelphia, Nicole Hinton said she is channeling \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s confidence and feeling good about the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s prospects.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn my mind, it\u8217\'20\'19s like she\u8217\'20\'19s won already,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hinton, carrying a poster with a photo of MLK, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The 21-year-old said she\u8217\'20\'19s already cast her ballot for Harris and because she wants \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen to have the right to do whatever they want with their body\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Hinton worries that a second Trump presidency would erode \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access even further and would make it even more difficult for women to access reproductive healthcare.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s historic candidacy is important, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not why Hinton is supporting the vice-president, Hinton said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about whoever brings us all together and what is best for us as a whole,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had a rare moment of self-reflection in Pittsburgh as he summoned sons Don Jr and Eric, daughter Tiffany, daughter-in-law \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2  and son-in-law Michael Boulos to the stage.\par \par \uc2 The former president sounded wistful as he recalled the hundreds of rallies he had done and how this is the penultimate one (he finishes in Grand Rapids, Michigan, tonight). He insisted that son Barron and daughter Ivanka were watching.\par \par \uc2 But what might have been a heartwarming family moment for any other candidate inevitably veered off track as Trump, wildly digressing from topic to topic, launched a bitter attack on \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cdivisive\u8221\'20\'1D and scorned his wife Michelle.\par \par \uc2 Then he let rip at Democratic congressman Adam Schiff, describing him as \u8220\'20\'1Cevil\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Chuman scum\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cwatermelon head\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s children laughed, as did the crowd. It was hardly an uplifting closing argument at the end of a long campaign.\par \par \uc2 As it approaches 9pm in Pittsburgh, there is now a steady flow of people leaving the rally.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 One of the viral comments from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Pittsburgh rally tonight is when he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/third-party-election-votes-jill-stein-rfk-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 referenced thi}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/third-party-election-votes-jill-stein-rfk-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rd party presidential candidate Jill Stein}}}\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cone of my favorite politicians \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: "I love the Green Party. Jill Stein. I've never met her but she may be one of my favorite politicians." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JWhRUEDApT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JWhRUEDApT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1853605428178919816?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 A Reuters journalist shares a Reuters photo from Washington, DC today:\par \par \uc2 enltrA person eats inside of a restaurant with plywood covering the windows near the White House in Washington, U.S., November 4, 2024. REUTERS/Nathan Howard {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tGub73IPuX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tGub73IPuX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Idrees Ali (@idreesali114) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/idreesali114/status/1853579312634404943?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 If you\u8217\'20\'19re on X, the social media platform formerly known as \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , you\u8217\'20\'19re probably seeing cascades of misinformation about the election, some of it shared by the platform\u8217\'20\'19s owner, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 NBC News did an analysis of Musk\u8217\'20\'19s own posts, and found that what he shared got more attention when it undermined trust in the integrity of the voting process:\par \par \uc2 enltrElon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s posts on his social media platform X get far more attention when they cast doubt on the integrity of the electoral process, an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NBCNews}}}\uc2  analysis finds. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1FNAMms4n3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/1FNAMms4n3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NBC News (@NBCNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCNews/status/1853516354491490796?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 My colleague Johana Bhuiyan has more context on this issue:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/oct/31/elon-musk-election-integrity-community-misinformation-disinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18election integrity community\u8217\'20\'19 on X is full of baseless claims}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 In Pittsburgh, Trump is now ranting about his frustrations with Democratic congressman Adam Schiff, who led the first Trump impeachment trial. Schiff is expected to cruise to victory in the US senate race in California, running against a Republican former baseball player with no political experience.\par \par \uc2 Schiff\u8217\'20\'19s opponent in California, Steve Garvey, is no close Trump ally: he refused to say whether or not he was voting for Trump in the California primary.\par \par \uc2 It seems likely there are some Republican members of Congress who wish Trump were using this primetime speech to talk about their very close races, not about an un-winnable US senate race in California.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump calls Adam Schiff "evil," "scum," "watermelon head," and fantasizes about him being decapitated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tnmvtfJEWT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tnmvtfJEWT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1853612098502135839?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 A veteran correspondent with an estimate of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s crowd side in Pittsburgh:\par \par \uc2 enltrWith the upper deck of this 19,000 capacity venue in Pittsburgh closed off, I\u8217\'20\'19d estimate Trump will speak to 10-12k supporters at this final rally of his Pennsylvania campaign. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mje280E4dJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mje280E4dJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Garrett Haake (@GarrettHaake) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GarrettHaake/status/1853585196680962305?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.27am GMT\par \par \uc2 In Pittsburgh, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , sounding hoarse and looking more orange-faced than ever, kicked off his final Pennsylvania rally by returning to his pet obsession: crowd sizes.\par \par \uc2 The Republican presidential nominee, speaking to a near capacity crowd in Pittsburgh, noted that rival \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  also has a rally in the city tonight.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s event had not yet started but Trump brazenly lied: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s quite embarrassing, it\u8217\'20\'19s all over the internet, she\u8217\'20\'19s screaming and the people \u8211\'20\'13 there\u8217\'20\'19s about a 100 people \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re not moving, they just want to go home, just be done with it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stretching his arms wide, he added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not quite this!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also mocked Harris\u8217\'20\'19s recent joint appearance in Houston with singer Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9, whose name elicited angry boos from the crowd. The former president said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere were no songs, there was no happiness, it was just like, \u8216\'20\'18Give me my cheque, I want to get out of here.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He falsely claimed: \u8220\'20\'1CThey booed both of them the hell out of the stadium.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s not much sympathy for the press here at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Grand Rapids, Michigan, with responses to his comments that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/trump-election-pennsylvania-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t mind if an assassin shot his way through the media to reach him}}}\uc2  varying from indifference to actual endorsement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter people lie so long and so much you\u8217\'20\'19re bound to get to where you don\u8217\'20\'19t care. And I agree with him,\u8221\'20\'1D said Doug Ayers, 73. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause they don\u8217\'20\'19t tell the truth. And if somebody can\u8217\'20\'19t write a true story and tell the truth to people about what\u8217\'20\'19s going on, I\u8217\'20\'19ll back him [Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments] 100%.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ayers, a Vietnam war veteran, lives in Ionia, a 40-minute drive from Grand Rapids. He has already cast his vote for Trump, whose chances he rated as 50-50. Ayers lamented that the US has gone \u8220\'20\'1Cdown the wrong path with our leadership\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the borders are open this much and everything else \u8230\'20\'26 I fought in Vietnam, we fought our hearts off for this country to eliminate communism. [Now] we got more going on in the United States than what we ever did in our life,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now saying he would like to stage a wrestling match between \uc2 Penn State\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s college wrestlers or UFC champions and the im migrants he has accused of stealing jobs from US citizens.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COh, those \uc2 Penn State\uc2  guys, I wanted them to wrestle the migrants,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says, referencing a campaign visit to \uc2 Penn State\uc2 , which has a famous wrestling team.\par \par \uc2 He also referenced Ultimate Fighting Championship CEO Dana White: \u8220\'20\'1CI told Dana, you ought to set up your league of champions \u8211\'20\'13 unbelievable, best fighters in the world \u8211\'20\'13 and a migrant league.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the end I want the migrant to go against the champions, and I think the migrant might actually win. That\u8217\'20\'19s how nasty some of those guys are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump went back and forth between reminiscing about his \uc2 Penn State\uc2  visit and dreaming of a wrestling match involving immigrants to the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI felt very comfortable with those big \uc2 Penn State\uc2  wrestlers,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CI said to them, \u8216\'20\'18Fellas, you might be the only guys in the country who could beat the hell out of the migrants. It\u8217\'20\'19s true. They\u8217\'20\'19re the only ones who could beat the migrants in the fight.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 At the penultimate rally of his campaign, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now complaining that TV stations covering his live campaign rallies do not air the videos that he plays. \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t put it on television,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t treat me good.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a terrible thing \u8211\'20\'13 a terrible thing,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to get them to straighten out. Without a free and fair press, it\u8217\'20\'19s very hard to do what we want to do \u8230\'20\'26 it\u8217\'20\'19s a very hard thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 In his speech, Trump is now repeating debunked claims about the Olympic women\u8217\'20\'19s boxing event this summer.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  has a fact-check of how Trump\u8217\'20\'19s final election ad featured similar debunked claims:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump\u8217\'20\'19s closing ad features debunked claim about Olympic boxer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fQdKdn5tmv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/fQdKdn5tmv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joseph Trento (@JosephTrento) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JosephTrento/status/1853534160373088729?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 More than two dozen states have indicated they are willing to send national guard troops to Washington in the coming weeks following the election and in the run-up to the inauguration, national guard officials said.\par \par \uc2 Col Jean Paul Laurenceau, chief of future operations for the National Guard Bureau, said it was not yet clear how many Guard troops will be needed or requested this year, Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 Washington DC has not yet made any formal request for guard troops.\par \par \uc2 But officials across the government have been meeting and preparing for the possibility that the US Capitol could once again be rocked by violence around the certification of the election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump is now comparing the crowd numbers at his rally versus \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Pittsburgh rally tonight, saying hers is a \u8220\'20\'1Clittle rally going on \u8211\'20\'13 and when I say little, I mean little.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 (Harris is not due to speak at her Pittsburgh rally for at least another hour.)\par \par \uc2 The Trump crowd boos at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s mention of Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 Knowles-Carter, and her endorsement of Harris, which Trump suggests she did \u8220\'20\'1Cfor a check\u8221\'20\'1D. (Forbes estimated the singer\u8217\'20\'19s net worth at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/profile/beyonce-knowles/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than $700m}}}\uc2 .)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t need a star,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump goes on. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t need a star, because we have policy. We have great policy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 Candace Valenzuela, 40, had flown in from Texas to canvass in Las Vegas, she said, to make sure women here don\u8217\'20\'19t lose their \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  here the way they have in Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m the mother of two young sons. I have a five-year-old and a nine-year-old,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I\u8217\'20\'19ve also had a couple of miscarriages.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since Texas enacted its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, with the threat of prison time for medical interventions that end a fetal heartbeat, Valenzuela has been afraid to try for a third child, she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNevada is a key to making sure that laws like we have in Texas don\u8217\'20\'19t become the law of the land,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, before heading out to door-knock for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Democratic senator \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Harris and Rosen have both promised to help restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, emphasizing that Republicans could further restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access if they gain control of the White House and Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf they win in Nevada, maybe we can reverse the atrocious things happening to women all over the country,\u8221\'20\'1D Valenzuela said.\par \par \uc2 Last week, a pregnant teenager died in Valenzuela\u8217\'20\'19s home state after being denied proper care at two emergency room visits. Doctors insisted on two ultrasounds to confirm her fetus had died before intervening.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is canvassing for her own presidential campaign in Reading, Pennsylvania, a sign of just how critical the commonwealth\u8217\'20\'19s 19 electoral votes are to her prospects of becoming the next president.\par \par \uc2 According to a pool report, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s motorcade pulled into a residential neighborhood in the city. She was joined at the door by two campaign volunteers holding signs and a clipboard.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wanted to go door-knocking!\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told the man, woman and their adult son, who came to the door.\par \par \uc2 Harris then walked to a second home a few doors down. At that house the vice-president rang the doorbell. A woman answered and hugged Harris and enthusiastically told her that she had already voted for her. She indicated that her husband planned to cast his ballot for her tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 Her team has been leading a remarkable get-out-the-vote operation, part of the reason they feel confident heading into the final days of the election.\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, the campaign said it knocked 807,000 doors in Pennsylvania \u8211\'20\'13 more than 10 times Biden\u8217\'20\'19s margin of victory in the state.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor a person that they hate, they sure do show up,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says, referencing the \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D journalists in Pittsburgh there to cover the major pre-election speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt shows that ratings are more important than hatred, I\u8217\'20\'19ve always said that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMany people say that God saved me in order to save America,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says, revisiting the assassination attempt against him in Butler, Pennsylvania, in July. \u8220\'20\'1CMany, many people are saying that, and with your help, we will fulfill that extraordinary mission together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Pittsburgh crowd tonight booed when Trump first mentioned the assassination attempt, which left one of his supporters dead.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat brush with death did not stop us. It only made us more determined to finish the job,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, of himself and his movement.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COnly one day \u8211\'20\'13 does that sound nice \u8211\'20\'13 one day from now,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says, of tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s election, and the victory he\u8217\'20\'19s anticipating. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve been waiting four years for this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTomorrow\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump says, to cheers. He is standing in front of a crowd of people in plastic hard hats.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now on stage at his rally in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, and will begin speaking shortly. Both he and Harris will be rallying supporters in Pittsburgh tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 Among the crowd at the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 East Las Vegas office was Regina Houston, 60 \u8211\'20\'13 she had come out to see senators \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2  and \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m nervous and anxious. I\u8217\'20\'19m nervous about this election, because there\u8217\'20\'19s so much on the line,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI came down here by myself, because it\u8217\'20\'19s better than sitting home and watching the news.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Houston votes in every election, but this year has felt especially \u8220\'20\'1Cheavy,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Polls show that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are locked in a tight race, and even seasoned analysts have been struggled to predict the outcome in this key swing state.\par \par \uc2 Nevada has gone for the Democratic candidate in every presidential race since \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  in 2004, but in recent years, Trump appears to have gained support.\par \par \uc2 Houston said she has her fingers crossed that her state will go blue once again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t imagine America operating and functioning at the level that candidate Trump wants to take us to,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.28am GMT\par \par \uc2 How active are the Proud Boys ahead of another furiously contested election?\par \par \uc2 Top leaders of the Proud Boys are still in prison for the far-right group\u8217\'20\'19s key role in storming the US capitol on 6 January. But the violent group, known for misogyny, street fighting, and receiving the instruction from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2020 to \u8220\'20\'1Cstand back and stand by,\u8221\'20\'1D has not collapsed since 2020. NBC News\u8217\'20\'19 Ryan Reilly reports that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/proud-boys-claim-polling-places-trump-ups-violent-rhetoric-election-fr-rcna178386"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Proud Boys are weakened, but still \u8220\'20\'1Cclearly active}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D ahead of the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 On Telegram, at least 30 channels run by Proud Boys chapters are sharing pro-Trump election information, according to nonprofit Advance Democracy, Reilly reports.\par \par \uc2 While most chapters of the Proud Boys and other active militia groups had not made explicit calls to interfere with the election as of Monday, NBC News reports, there were two notable exceptions.\par \par \uc2 Two Ohio-based Proud Boys chapters have posted that \u8220\'20\'1Cthey\u8217\'20\'19ll be watching the polls on Election Day,\u8221\'20\'1D with the Proud Boys of Columbus recently posting \u8220\'20\'1Ca claim that they had enrolled members as poll watchers and poll workers,\u8221\'20\'1D Reilly reports, citing posts reviewed.\par \par \uc2 enltr"Two Proud Boys chapters, both based in Ohio, say they'll be watching the polls on Election Day, according to posts reviewed by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NBCNews}}}\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 "The Proud Boys of Columbus posted a claim that they had enrolled members as poll watchers and poll workers." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1QNZaXbtTF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/1QNZaXbtTF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lois Beckett (@loisbeckett) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/loisbeckett/status/1853593297370968220?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not clear whether claims that they are watching the polls or are embedded as election volunteers will result in any real-world action,\u8221\'20\'1D Reilly notes. Far-right groups often make exaggerated public claims about the actions that they\u8217\'20\'19re going to take, or the access that they have, and don\u8217\'20\'19t follow through. Making the public afraid of what they might could is sometimes victory enough.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 On election eve, Democrats in Nevada are doubling down on door knocking efforts \u8211\'20\'13 making last pitches to get out the vote.\par \par \uc2 In East Las Vegas, Democratic senator \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2  gave canvassers one last pep talk. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re at the finish line now, and whatever you do, it makes a difference,\u8221\'20\'1D Rosen said. \u8220\'20\'1COne last call, one last door knock.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rosen is leading in polls as she fights for reelection against Republican Sam Brown. But more Republicans than expected have voted early, and a PAC associated with Senate Republican leader \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2  has recently spent $6m on ads to promote Brown.\par \par \uc2 Canvassers for Rosen and the Harris/Walz campaign have been deployed across the state to make final pleas to voters.\par \par \uc2 Rosen appeared alongside her fellow Nevada senator, \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2 , at an afternoon canvass launch.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is how we win in Nevada, Because of all of you!\u8221\'20\'1D Said Cortez Masto. \u8220\'20\'1CWe organize our way to victory, right?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The few dozen canvassers cheered. And a few who were standing near a call in the campaig office knocked on wood.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has been canvassing in Pennsylvania this evening, where she went door knocking in Reading in an attempt to win over voters just hours before polls open on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the day before the election and I just wanted to come by and say I hope to earn your vote,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told one person, who informed the Democratic candidate \u8220\'20\'1Cyou already got my vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrLate-night door knocking in Reading, PA. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WvL0yXmYm3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WvL0yXmYm3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Akayla Gardner (@gardnerakayla) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/gardnerakayla/status/1853586507916771798?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Harris visited a Puerto Rican restaurant in Reading earlier on Monday, joined by Pennsylvania governor \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  and New York congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harris initially said she wanted to order a \u8220\'20\'1Cspicy taquito\u8221\'20\'1D but later said she also wanted the rice, plantains, pork and cassava, Associated Press reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m very hungry. I don\u8217\'20\'19t get to eat as often as I like,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Jazmine Sullivan, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2021/feb/03/jazmine-sullivan-heaux-tales-ep-r-and-b-great-observer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the R&B star}}}\uc2 , just took the stage at the \uc2 Philadelphia Museum of Art\uc2 , addressing supporters: \u8220\'20\'1CAre we ready to make history tomorrow?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She encouraged Pennsylvanians to vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  when polls open tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel safer when there\u8217\'20\'19s a woman in leadership,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights were under assault across the country, she said, dedicating her rendition of Marvin Gaye\u8217\'20\'19s What\u8217\'20\'19s Going On to the cause.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause what\u8217\'20\'19s going on?\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 JD Vance is once again being condemned for misogyny after repeatedly calling \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18trash\u8217\'20\'19 at campaign rallies.\par \par \uc2 The Republican vice-presidential nominee compared Harris with trash at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bostonglobe.com/2024/11/03/metro/jd-vance-trump-rally-derry-nh-kamala-harris-immigration-taxes-housing-trash/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a New Hampshire rally}}}\uc2  yesterday, then did it again today in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bostonglobe.com/2024/11/03/metro/jd-vance-trump-rally-derry-nh-kamala-harris-immigration-taxes-housing-trash/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Flint, Michigan}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/harris-trump-election-11-03-04-24/card/jd-vance-calls-kamala-harris-trash-at-new-hampshire-rally-DUygS3ukLwbsFfQxDKK6?mod=mhp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Atlanta, Georgia}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 enltrJD Vance: "The trash's name is \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8QMtRoSoiV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8QMtRoSoiV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1853562375271481653?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Mainstream political commenters have not been complimentary to Vance\u8217\'20\'19s choice to make the closing argument for the Trump campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/sbg1/status/1853562679438221587"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so explicitly \u8220\'20\'1Cnasty\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COh, JD Vance, you just effed up in a way that I\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen in my political life, and I worked for \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/deadline-white-house/watch/-in-my-humble-view-lights-out-nicolle-wallace-reacts-to-jd-vance-calling-vp-harris-trash-223539781512"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MSNBC\u8217\'20\'19s Nicole Wallace said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrWatch "JD Vance you just f'ed up in a way I've never seen in my pollical life and I worked for \uc2 Sarah Palin\uc2 " - Nicole Wallace\par \par \uc2 JD Vance just called \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  TRASH at his final rally in Atlanta, Georgia. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xjJHQ0KRPC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xjJHQ0KRPC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Chris Borkowski (@cborkowski) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cborkowski/status/1853581610844598782?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Hours before election day, a crowd has amassed at the \uc2 Philadelphia Museum of Art\uc2 , where \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will hold the last rally of her lightning-fast presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala Harris will hold the final rally of her 100+ day campaign in Philadelphia later tonight, with a view of the \u8220\'20\'1CRocky Steps\u8221\'20\'1D illuminated in blue {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/9TSgT7e4nS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/9TSgT7e4nS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1853577677615095821?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The 72 \u8220\'20\'1CRocky Steps\u8221\'20\'1D were illuminated in blue lights with scrolling LED signs that say Vote for Freedom and Vote. The DJ is spinning Taylor Swift\u8217\'20\'19s Cruel Summer.\par \par \uc2 The lines to get in wrapped for ages and people came prepared for a long night. Harris will appear at a rally in Pittsburgh before landing in the city of Brotherly Love for what is expected to be a star-studded event.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  became the Democratic candidate, TikTok and \uc2 Instagram\uc2  saw the emergence of a particularly vicious kind of misinformation \u8211\'20\'13 that Harris stole someone\u8217\'20\'19s husband, specifically Willie Brown, a former mayor of San Francisco.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/kamala-harris-willie-brown-mistress/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This is false}}}\uc2 . But these rumors were soon translated into Chinese and posted on X, with the language becoming \u8220\'20\'1Ceven more inflammatory\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the Chinese factchecking group, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.piyaoba.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 PiYaoBa}}}\uc2 . One Chinese influencer, whose tweet garnered more than 60,000 views, translated \u8220\'20\'1Cstole a woman\u8217\'20\'19s husband\u8221\'20\'1D as \u8220\'20\'1Cmistress\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 This translation spread to other Chinese platforms like \uc2 WeChat\uc2 , accumulating more than 100,000 views and leading some users to refer to her using the word \u8220\'20\'1Cchicken\u8221\'20\'1D, which in Mandarin is often a slur for sex workers.\par \par \uc2 It suggests how English-language misinformation is not only spreading in other languages \u8211\'20\'13 it also takes new, culturally specific forms.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2024/nov/04/chinese-americans-election-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the full story here: }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2024/nov/04/chinese-americans-election-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chinese Americans targeted with \u8216\'20\'18misogynistic and insulting\u8217\'20\'19 election misinformation}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2024/nov/04/chinese-americans-election-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Chinese Americans targeted with \u8216\'20\'18misogynistic and insulting\u8217\'20\'19 election misinformation}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump ally Nigel Farage says ex-president should accept result and 'play golf' if he loses\par \par \uc2 Nigel Farage, the leader of the UK\u8217\'20\'19s Reform party, said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should accept the result of the election and \u8220\'20\'1Cgo play golf\u8221\'20\'1D if he loses decisively to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.telegraph.co.uk/us/politics/2024/11/04/nigel-farage-donald-trump-play-golf-if-kamala-harris-wins/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  with the Telegraph at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s home in Palm Beach, Florida, Farage said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf it was clear and decisive then maybe it\u8217\'20\'19s time [for Trump] to go and play golf at Turnberry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Farage said he has \u8220\'20\'1Cnever gone along with\u8221\'20\'1D Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 stolen election narrative, adding that \u8220\'20\'1Clet\u8217\'20\'19s hope and pray that is not an issue this time. If it [the outcome] was clear then Republicans have to accept the result.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He suggested that Harris could move to quell any potential unrest if she wins the election by pardoning Trump once in office. \u8220\'20\'1CIf she gets in on Tuesday I hope she pardons him. She could look magnanimous and it would dampen down potential tensions,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 However, he added: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s all hypothetical and I still think he is going to win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Farage attended Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally earlier today in Reading, Pennsylvania, where he hailed his \u8220\'20\'1Cspecial relationship\u8221\'20\'1D with the Republican presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe special relationship. ???? ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oUh57wHDRF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oUh57wHDRF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nigel Farage MP (@Nigel_Farage) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Nigel_Farage/status/1853558745298538503?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As Shasta county, California, grapples with a thriving election denialism movement that has amplified conspiracy theories about voter fraud and made life increasingly difficult for election workers, residents of one of California\u8217\'20\'19s most conservative counties are bracing for a contentious election.\par \par \uc2 In recent weeks, some residents of Shasta county, home to 180,000 people in the state\u8217\'20\'19s far north, have urged the county not to certify the election results while one official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/election-office-georgia-arizona-michigan-pennsylvania-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  that if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Ccheated\u8221\'20\'1D out of the election, there would be \u8220\'20\'1Ca price\u8221\'20\'1D to pay.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/california-shasta-county-election-residents-divided"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Residents of conservative California county brace for tumultuous elections }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The first Muslim woman elected to public office in North Carolina has shared a thread on why she is voting for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and how the tone of her brief conversations with Harris about Gaza have changed over the course of this year.\par \par \uc2 Nida Allam, the chair of the Durham Board of county commissioners, and an organizer in the state Democratic party, wrote today about why she is voting for Harris over Jill Stein.\par \par \uc2 Allam\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bittersoutherner.com/2020/nida-allam-durham-north-carolina-county-comissioner-muslim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 engagement with politics}}}\uc2  began when three Muslim college students, her friends, were murdered by a white man in a horrific {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jun/12/craig-stephen-hicks-north-carolina-chapel-hill-pleads-gu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2015 shooting in Chapel Hill, North Carolina}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrAs Chair of the BOCC I was invited again to meet with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  as she arrived in NC last week.\par \par \uc2 Every opportunity with her I have used my limited time to advocate for Gaza & the West Bank.\par \par \uc2 This time I was surprised.\par \par \uc2 - A rambling thread of my thoughts & processing /?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YGY4uKPO2l"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YGY4uKPO2l}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nida Allam ?? (@NidaAllam) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NidaAllam/status/1853503841708523805?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the latest images from the newswires on election eve from across the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nevada county puts panic buttons in polling places after threats\par \par \uc2 After threats, one county in Nevada has put panic buttons in all polling places\par \par \uc2 Threats against election workers have gotten so bad that all polling places in Washoe County, Nevada, have a \u8220\'20\'1Cpanic button\u8221\'20\'1D that workers can hit to automatically call 911, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/live/election-2024-harris-trump-updates-11-4-2024#00000192-f93b-dcda-ab92-f9fb528b0000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But Andrew McDonald, the deputy registrar of voters in the swing county of half a million people, says there\u8217\'20\'19s only been one incident in nearly two weeks of in-person early voting that required someone to hit the panic button.\par \par \uc2 That incident, McDonald said at a press conference, involved a voter at one of the county\u8217\'20\'19s 24 early voting sites who would not remove his hat when asked by a worker, who was following state law prohibiting campaign signs or paraphernalia within 100 feet (30 meters) of a polling station.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA few other voters in line sort of ganged up on the site manager,\u8221\'20\'1D McDonald said. But when police arrived, he added, \u8220\'20\'1Cthey calmed down and were able to vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Washoe has become a hotbed for election conspiracy theorists who believe Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lies that the 2020 election was stolen from him. Still, \uc2 McDonald\uc2  noted that the panic button incident is the only significant one that\u8217\'20\'19s happened during the early vote period, when 90,000 people cast their ballots.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI get an incident report daily,\u8221\'20\'1D McDonald said, \u8220\'20\'1Cand there haven\u8217\'20\'19t been that many incidents.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The intense international attention on Maricopa county, Arizona \u8211\'20\'13 one of the few swing counties in a swing state \u8211\'20\'13 was made clear during a press conference today, whe n officials said they had given media credentials to more than 600 journalists from around the world and a reporter from Estonia asked about democracy issues.\par \par \uc2 The county\u8217\'20\'19s elections officials detailed how they would count a long, two-page ballot and report results, reminding voters that as more ballots are tabulated, leaders in races can change.\par \par \uc2 Given the close nature of races here and large amounts of lengthy ballots, it\u8217\'20\'19s likely we\u8217\'20\'19ll be watching results from Maricopa well beyond election night.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also no stranger to mis- and disinformation campaigns. Several of the county\u8217\'20\'19s elections officials have seen threats against them prosecuted by the federal government.\par \par \uc2 Knowing this environment, assistant county manager Zach Schira said the county would be aggressive in correcting any bad information that affects a person\u8217\'20\'19s ability to vote, but that overall, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe will not be playing whack-a-mole\u8221\'20\'1D with every piece of misinformation.\par \par \uc2 The county has nearly 2.6 million registered active voters and has received more than 1.5m early ballots turned in already, most of which came by mail though others voted in person early at the polls.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jon Ralston, a Nevada journalist with a track record of accurately predicting state election results, says he believes \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will narrowly win Nevada, but that the results will not be clear until after election night.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe great {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RalstonReports?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @RalstonReports}}}\uc2  has Sen. \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2  (D-Nev.) defeating Sam Brown by 5 points, and Harris beating Trump ever so slightly: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ev47byT2yj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Ev47byT2yj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Andrew Desiderio (@AndrewDesiderio) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AndrewDesiderio/status/1853526404643590215?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrJon Ralston, the seer of Nevada, predicts that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will pull out a very slim victory over Trump. He also warns that "it will not be clear who won on Election Night here, so block out the nattering nabobs of election denialism." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Wve0u3mBx6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Wve0u3mBx6}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8WD7adK6bm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8WD7adK6bm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Justin Baragona (@justinbaragona) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/justinbaragona/status/1853535374527611235?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Ralston\u8217\'20\'19s full explanation here:\par \par \uc2 enltrPredictions! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6LUYzarArw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/6LUYzarArw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jon Ralston (@RalstonReports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RalstonReports/status/1853524385694699922?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US readers: share which issues have shaped your vote the most in this election\par \par \uc2 As we cover the outcome of the 2024 election, we\u8217\'20\'19re interested in hearing from \uc2 Guardian\uc2  readers across the US about what issues influenced how you think about voting, and what decisions you\u8217\'20\'19ve made when it comes to your vote.\par \par \uc2 Have recent developments or events \u8211\'20\'13 in the world or in your personal life \u8211\'20\'13 affected your thinking? Have your existing views hardened? Have you become more ambivalent about certain issues?\par \par \uc2 Whatever your politics and how they\u8217\'20\'19ve changed, we want to know.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/male-and-female-us-voters-share-which-issues-have-shaped-your-vote-the-most"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Male and female US voters: share which issues have shaped your vote the most}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Philadelphia rapper and prison reform activist Meek Mill released a track saying he will vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , even as he invoked her record as a prosecutor in an unjust criminal justice system, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/live/election-2024-harris-trump-updates-11-4-2024#00000192-f941-df8c-a7fb-fd4bf3f90000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meek Mill surprise released the new track, \u8220\'20\'1CWho You Voting For\u8221\'20\'1D on Monday afternoon, sharing a snippet of the song with the caption, \u8220\'20\'1CI made this last night \u8230\'20\'26 who you voting for???\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@meekmill/video/7433483466114665759"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on TikTok}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy homie say vote for Trump / You want that stimulus / I wanted two from him but the way he movin\u8217\'20\'19 venomous,\u8221\'20\'1D he starts the song. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going probably vote Kamala.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMeek Mill - WHO YOU VOTING FOR (Official Visualizer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Qm55AUYBsX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Qm55AUYBsX}}}\uc2  via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/YouTube?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @YouTube}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MeekMill (@MeekMill) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MeekMill/status/1853537582644380029?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt ain\u8217\'20\'19t fair when your lawyer look like Trump / DA lookin\u8217\'20\'19 like Kamala,\u8221\'20\'1D he continues, critiquing Harris\u8217\'20\'19s past as a prosecutor. \u8220\'20\'1CWe Thanksgiving to the system / They\u8217\'20\'19ve been eating us for lunch / And it\u8217\'20\'19s the last supper / Hope you be with us for once, Mrs Harris.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The $1m-a-day voter sweepstakes that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s political action committee is hosting in swing states can continue through Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania}}}\uc2  judge ruled on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Common pleas court Judge Angelo Foglietta \u8211\'20\'13 ruling after Musk\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers said the winners are not chosen by chance \u8211\'20\'13 did not immediately give a reason for the ruling.\par \par \uc2 More details on this news from my colleague Richard Luscombe:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/elon-musk-giveaway-winners-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania judge declines to block Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s $1m voter prize giveaway}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s highest court on Monday ruled ballots in the state\u8217\'20\'19s third-largest county must be returned by election day, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 A previous lower court ruling would have allowed certain voters in Cobb county who received their absentee ballots late to return them after the deadline as long as they were postmarked by Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The county, just north of Atlanta, didn\u8217\'20\'19t mail out absentee ballots to some voters who had requested them until late last week. Georgia law says absentee ballots must be received by the close of polls on election day.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: Georgia Supreme Court sides with the \uc2 RNC\uc2  in a fight over 3K absentee ballots sent out last-minute in Cobb County -- court says ballots can only be counted if they arrive by election day (a lower court judge had extended deadline) Late-arriving ballots will be set aside for\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AkVavi9zzS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AkVavi9zzS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Zoe Tillman (@ZoeTillman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ZoeTillman/status/1853533152188289517?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The Georgia supreme court ruling means the affected residents must vote in person on election day, or get their absentee ballots to the county elections office by 7 p.m. that day.\par \par \uc2 The high court ruling instructs county election officials to notify the affected voters by email, text message and in a public message on the county election board\u8217\'20\'19s website. And it orders officials to keep separate and sealed any ballots received after the election day deadline but before 5pm on Friday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  brought some of his children on stage during his rally in Reading, Pennsylvania, where he said \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is our last time now, for forever \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s children Don Jr, Eric and Tiffany, as well as Eric\u8217\'20\'19s wife and \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  co-chair, \uc2 Lara Trump\uc2 , and Tiffany\u8217\'20\'19s husband, Michael Boulos, all appeared on stage on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The Republican presidential candidate\u8217\'20\'19s youngest daughter, Tiffany, made a rare speech during the Reading event, hours after she posted to X that her father \u8220\'20\'1Cwill NOT sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrA few points to reiterate as you head to the voting booth:\par \par \uc2 1. Project 2025 is NOT my father\u8217\'20\'19s plan. He has not read it and does not endorse it.\par \par \uc2 2. My father will NOT sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 3. My father greatly supports IVF and wants to make it accessible to anyone who\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tiffany Ariana Trump (@TiffanyATrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TiffanyATrump/status/1853498101019099554?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Despite it being a work day, a long queue formed outside the PPG Paints Arena in Pittsburgh for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s final Pennsylvania rally.\par \par \uc2 There was the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1853552871658135805"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 usual Maga paraphernalia}}}\uc2  including T-shirts saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m voting for the outlaw and the hillbilly\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CJesus is my savior, Trump is my president\u8221\'20\'1D, plus a photo of Trump with the legend \u8220\'20\'1CPet Lives Matter\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Michael Barringer, 55, a fifth generation coalminer, was standing in line wearing a miner\u8217\'20\'19s helmet. I asked why he supports Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy grandfather was a the second world war vet,\u8221\'20\'1D Barringer replied. \u8220\'20\'1CHe served in the navy from 1942 to \u8216\'20\'1845. He taught me to love this country, pledge allegiance to your flag \u8211\'20\'13 the greatest country in the world. I love this country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve got millions and millions of illegal aliens crossing the border. They don\u8217\'20\'19t speak English. They don\u8217\'20\'19t say a pledge allegiance to the flag. They freeload off of us. I\u8217\'20\'19m all for legal immigration but not coming across the border illegally, taking American jobs, undercutting us.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that Trump, his first term in office, he renegotiated Nafta, he\u8217\'20\'19s for the American people and that\u8217\'20\'19s why I vote him. I think he\u8217\'20\'19s one of the greatest presidents ever to run for office and hold office.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 I wondered if Barringer had read the reports of Trump calling Americans who died in war \u8220\'20\'1Csuckers\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Closers\u8221\'20\'1D. He insisted: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s all garbage. I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe a word of it. Listen, my grandfather\u8217\'20\'19s rolling over in his grave today to hear these people kneeling for the flag and everything else.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow about the fake news media? They call Trump Hitler. His son-in-law is a Jew. His grandchildren are Jewish. He\u8217\'20\'19s the first president ever to put an embassy in Jerusalem. They call him a fascist. Do I believe he\u8217\'20\'19s for America first? Absolutely. That\u8217\'20\'19s who I want running my country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania judge rejects legal challenge of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s $1m giveaway\par \par \uc2 A Pennsylvania judge has rejected an attempt to shut down \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s $1m giveaway scheme, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports from Philadelphia:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING FROM PHILLY:\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  wins in Pennsylvania court.\par \par \uc2 The judge just ruled that Musk CAN continue his $1 million sweepstakes, declining to issue an injunction against America PAC.\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s team had argued that their paid spokespeople were not lottery winners. Larry\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/AObJ2o2v5l"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/AObJ2o2v5l}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Teddy Schleifer (@teddyschleifer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/teddyschleifer/status/1853555200759562252?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 More from the Associated Press:\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/musk-1-million-giveaway-trump-voters-petition-b4e48acbfe04fde735e60b1911ad0197"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1 million-a-day voter sweepstakes}}}\uc2  that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/hub/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18s political action committee is hosting in swing states can continue through Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, a Pennsylvania judge ruled Monday.\par \par \uc2 Common Pleas Court Judge Angelo Foglietta \u8212\'20\'14 ruling after Musk\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers said the winners are not chosen by chance \u8212\'20\'14 did not immediately give a reason for the ruling.\par \par \uc2 Philadelphia District Attorney \uc2 Larry Krasner\uc2  had called the sweepstakes a scam that violates state election law and asked that it be shut down.\par \par \uc2 The winners of the sweepstakes did not win by chance but are instead paid spokespeople for the group, Musk\u8217\'20\'19s lawyers said in court Monday.\par \par \uc2 Musk lawyer Chris Gober said the final two recipients before Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election will be in Arizona on Monday and Michigan on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe $1 million recipients are not chosen by chance,\u8221\'20\'1D Gober said Monday. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know exactly who will be announced as the $1 million recipient today and tomorrow.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to finish this strong,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says during her rally in Allentown.\par \par \uc2 Harris has just wrapped up her remarks, which lasted a little under 30 minutes here.\par \par \uc2 She has two more rallies in Pennsylvania scheduled today.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A demonstrator just interrupted \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech and staffers quickly got the section around the woman to start chanting \u8220\'20\'1CUSA\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The protester was escorted out by staff.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are fighting for our democracy right now. We love our democracy and democracy can be a bit complicated sometimes. But that\u8217\'20\'19s OK,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 These demonstrations, many over the war in Gaza, have become common at Harris\u8217\'20\'19s rallies in the last week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In Allentown, speakers are focusing hard on a pro-Trump comedian\u8217\'20\'19s racist comments about Puerto Rico and Latinos at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden rally in New York.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/estrongbeauty/?hl=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elizabeth Strong}}}\uc2 , a Latino Affairs Commissioner for Pennsylvania governor \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , just introduced \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Allentown as \u8220\'20\'1Csomeone who will be president for all Americans \u8211\'20\'13 including Puerto Ricans!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris: 'I will be a president for all Americans'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has taken to the stage here in Allentown .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI stand here proud of my longstanding commitment to Puerto Rico and her people and I will be a president for all Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 Harris opens her speech by saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have momentum on our side. Can you feel it?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The crowd here in a gymnasium at Muhlenberg college hasn\u8217\'20\'19t sat down since she walked in.\par \par \uc2 Harris is tearing into Trumpism without mentioning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  himself by name.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the opportunity in this election to turn the page on a decade of politics that has been driven by fear and division \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19re done with that,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica is ready for a fresh start.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'Where's your pride as a Latino?' Rapper Fat Joe condemns Trump rally 'joke' at Harris event\par \par \uc2 The rapper Fat Joe just took the stage and is ripping into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his treatment of Puerto Ricans and urging Latino voters to support \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhere\u8217\'20\'19s your pride? If you\u8217\'20\'19re still out there talking about, you might be voting somebody or you\u8217\'20\'19re not decided, where\u8217\'20\'19s your pride as a Latino,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe man went and blocked the aid for Puerto Rico for Hurricane Maria, what are we do here? The man blocked aid for Puerto Rico,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf I\u8217\'20\'19m speaking to some undecided Puerto Ricans, especially in Pennsylvania, what more do they have to do to show you who they are?\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Fat Joe\u8217\'20\'19s comments are the latest in a series of speakers today to appeal to Allentown\u8217\'20\'19s heavily Latino population.\par \par \uc2 enltrFat Joe takes the stage and is ripping into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s treatment of Puerto Ricans {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BeXQG4Sx1u"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BeXQG4Sx1u}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1853543020781555886?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  speaks in Allentown, Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Watch \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  speak live in Allentown, Pennsylvania, as the Democrat focuses her attention on turning out supporters in what her campaign believes is their must-win swing state.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is expected to speak soon in Allentown, Pennsylvania. More soon from my colleague Sam Levine on Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 focus on the anti-Puerto Rican remarks at a Trump rally.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe gym at Muhlenberg college is filling up here in Allentown ahead of Harris\u8217\'20\'19 rally. A chant of \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re not going back\u8221\'20\'1D just broke out in the crowd. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5u3APTORDg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5u3APTORDg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1853536197001236872?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , delivered remarks at a campaign event in Stevens Point, Wisconsin, where said Americans were about to elect a \u8220\'20\'1Cnew generation of leadership with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , a new way forward\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust tell yourself how great it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said, as he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/04/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-polls-latest-live-news?page=with:block-67291a4c8f0842b343ae9b09#block-67291a4c8f0842b343ae9b09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 again}}}\uc2  reiterated his confidence in the US electoral infrastructure. \u8220\'20\'1COur system is secure, our elections are safe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Minnesota governor spoke about the \u8220\'20\'1Cincredible journey\u8221\'20\'1D that he has been on since he was invited to join as Harris\u8217\'20\'19s ticket.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook at the movement, and look at the energy that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has built in 107 days,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. \u8220\'20\'1CImagine what she can do for the next eight years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on stage in Reading, Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now on stage in Reading, Pennsylvania, his second of four campaign rallies planned for today.\par \par \uc2 His speech thus far has focused on his claims that migrants are dangerous, and that he will deport them, if elected:\par \par \uc2 November 5, 2024 will be Liberation Day in America. And on day one, I will launch the largest deportation program of criminals in American history. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to get them out.\par \par \uc2 Trump heads to Pittsburgh after this, then to Grand Rapids, Michigan, for his last appearance of the day.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 How will the vice -president spend her election day?\par \par \uc2 With her ballot already posted and her campaign stops finished, Harris will return to Number One Observatory Circle in Washington in the wee hours of Tuesday morning, following a late-night rally in Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 Throughout the rest of the day, the campaign said she will be \u8220\'20\'1Con the airwaves\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 calling into local radio stations in the seven battleground states.\par \par \uc2 The eleventh-hour calls are about \u8220\'20\'1Cmaking sure that those final voters who are on their way to work, on their way home, taking a lunch break, understand the stakes, but understand her vision for where she wants to take this country over the course of the next four years,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris\u8217\'20\'19s communications director, Michael Tyler, told reporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd most importantly, make sure that they understand when, where and how to vote \u8230\'20\'26 she\u8217\'20\'19s going put in the work that it takes to hit 270, and that\u8217\'20\'19s until polls close tomorrow.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 This is the second \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  rally I\u8217\'20\'19ve attended this week in Pennsylvania, and I have noticed that speakers are bringing up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/29/trump-rally-puerto-rico-voter-reaction"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the racist joke about Puerto Ricans}}}\uc2  made at a recent Trump rally much more often than they were before.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want a president of the United States who looks to the 500,000 Puerto Ricans who live in our communities and strengthens our neighborhoods,\u8221\'20\'1D Pennsylvania governor \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  said to loud cheers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign also says it\u8217\'20\'19s prepared to combat any attempts by Trump to challenge the election results.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have hundreds of lawyers across the country ready to protect election results against any challenge that Trump might bring,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Dana Remus\uc2 , a senior campaign adviser and outside counsel. \u8220\'20\'1CThis will not be the fastest process, but the law and the facts are on our side.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Remus said the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s legal efforts were designed to undermine faith in the electoral process.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKeep in mind that the volume of cases does not equate to a volume of legitimate concerns. In fact, it just shows how desperate they\u8217\'20\'19re becoming,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign expects 'near complete results' from Georgia, North Carolina, Michigan on election night\par \par \uc2 Jen O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon\uc2 , chair of the Harris campaign, offered a rundown of when the team is expecting to learn the results from key states on election night.\par \par \uc2 By the end of election night, the campaign expects to have \u8220\'20\'1Cnear complete results\u8221\'20\'1D from Georgia, North Carolina and Michigan, and \u8220\'20\'1Cpartial results from Pennsylvania, Wisconsin and Arizona\u8221\'20\'1D, she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy Wednesday morning, we expect most results in from Wisconsin and additional results from Pennsylvania and potentially Michigan,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. More results from Pennsylvania, Arizona and Nevada will come after that.\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania is seen as an all-but-must-win for Harris, who is spending the final day before the election barnstorming the commonwealth.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania governor \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  gets loud ovation when he takes stage\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania governor \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2  just received a loud ovation when he took to the stage a little after 3 pm.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis race is about something deeper that a policy or a bill,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about the character of this great nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The last time battleground state Nevada went red was in 2004, when \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  was on the ballot. But Republicans hope that this year, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will end Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 streak.\par \par \uc2 As with all the other swing states in this election, polls have shown Trump neck and neck with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Nevada \u8211\'20\'13 an encouraging sign for the GOP, considering its recent history of Democratic strength. But Jon Ralston, a veteran political forecaster and editor of the Nevada Independent, released his projections for the year, and does not think Trump can pull it off.\par \par \uc2 From {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thenevadaindependent.com/article/editor-jon-ralstons-2024-nevada-election-predictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his article}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The key to this election has always been which way the non-major-party voters break because they have become the plurality in the state. They are going to make up 30 percent or so of the electorate and if they swing enough towards Harris, she will win Nevada. I think they will, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you why: Many people assume that with the GOP catching up to the Democrats in voter registration that the automatic voter registration plan pushed by Democrats that auto-registers people as nonpartisans (unless they choose a party) at the DMV had been a failure for the party. But I don\u8217\'20\'19t think so. There are a lot of nonpartisans who are closet Democrats who were purposely registered by Democrat-aligned groups as nonpartisans. The machine knows who they are and will get them to vote. It will be just enough to overcome the Republican lead \u8211\'20\'13 along with women motivated by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and crossover votes that issue also will cause. I know some may think this reflects my well-known disdain for Trump, heart over data. But that is not so. I have often predicted against my own preferences; history does not lie. I just have a feeling she will catch up here, but I also believe \u8211\'20\'13 and please remember this \u8211\'20\'13 it will not be clear who won on Election Night here, so block out the nattering nabobs of election denialism. It\u8217\'20\'19s going to be very, very close. Prediction: Harris, 48.5 percent; Trump 48.2 percent; others and None of These Candidates, 3.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Allentown mayor Matthew Tuerk is the first speaker at this rally.\par \par \uc2 He is the city\u8217\'20\'19s first Latino mayor and is laying into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after a speaker at his rally called Puerto Rico an island of garbage.\par \par \uc2 There is a huge Puerto Rican population in Allentown, and there were loud boos in the crowd, and then cheers, when some people in the audience held up a big Puerto Rican flag.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C Puerto Rico se respeta, Allentown se respeta,\u8221\'20\'1D Tuerk said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.17pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  holds a slight lead over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the final national PBS News/NPR/Marist poll {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/harris-has-4-point-lead-over-trump-in-final-pbs-news-npr-marist-election-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  today, just hours before election day.\par \par \uc2 The poll shows Harris holding a four-point lead over Trump, with the support of 51% of likely voters compared with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 47%. The lead lies just outside the study\u8217\'20\'19s 3.5-point margin of error.\par \par \uc2 A little more than half of independents support Trump, a 5-point lead over Harris, according to the poll.\par \par \uc2 Mostly notably, the poll shows that the gender gap has shrunk significantly in the last month of the campaign. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lead over Harris among male voters has dropped to just 4 points, down from the 16-point advantage in October.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, 55% of women said they will back Harris in the latest poll, meaning that her lead among women has dropped from 18 points to 11 points since last month.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Before \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  took the stage here at Muhlenberg college in Allentown, I chatted with Elizabeth Slaby, an 81-year-old, who was the first person in line this morning.\par \par \uc2 She said she got here at 6am \u8211\'20\'13 so early that she had to circle the block before getting in line.\par \par \uc2 She was a registered Republican for more than 50 years. But after the attack on the US Capitol on 6 January 2021 she changed her voter registration.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s her with her son and grandson. \u8220\'20\'1CI never thought I\u8217\'20\'19d see a woman president and now I\u8217\'20\'19m so so excited,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'Let's get this done': Harris rallies supporters in Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  sought to reassure her supporters during a campaign stop in Scranton, Pennsylvania, telling them \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re good\u8221\'20\'1D and urging them to \u8220\'20\'1Cenjoy this moment\u8221\'20\'1D during the final 24 hours of her campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m telling you guys, we\u8217\'20\'19re good,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris addressed Democratic canvassers. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re good. So we\u8217\'20\'19re going to keep doing this work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris recalled campaigning with her ironing board when she first ran for office as district attorney for San Francisco. \u8220\'20\'1CNo one thought I could win,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI like to say that when you love something, you fight for it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She told her supporters she could \u8220\'20\'1Cfeel the energy\u8221\'20\'1D and called for them to go and knock on neighbors\u8217\'20\'19 doors, \u8220\'20\'1Ceven if you\u8217\'20\'19ve not met them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs we\u8217\'20\'19re getting out the vote, let\u8217\'20\'19s be intentional about building community, about building coalitions and reminding people, we all have so much more in common than what separates us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe love our country and that\u8217\'20\'19s what this fight is about,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s get this done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/04/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-polls-latest-live-news?page=with:block-6729055c8f082a575b9e5a77#block-6729055c8f082a575b9e5a77"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also }}}\uc2  appeared at a rally in La Crosse, Wisconsin, on Monday where he said the decisions made over the next days \u8220\'20\'1Cwill shape not just the next four years, they will shape the coming generations \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Walz, who was joined at the rally by his wife, Gwen, and Minnesota senator \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2 , said the election \u8220\'20\'1Cquite literally could be won through the state of Wisconsin\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a generational opportunity for us to turn the page for us to take this momentum going forward,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Walz also spoke about his confidence in the country\u8217\'20\'19s election security, arguing that the US has \u8220\'20\'1Cthe fairest, the most secure elections in the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will count the votes. We will win on the votes, and we will be able to know, too, that we have a part in not only moving on from nine years of what we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen, but charting, truly, a new way forward. The rest of the world is watching, so I have one request: win this for America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While we\u8217\'20\'19re {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/04/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-polls-latest-live-news?page=with:block-672910ea8f0842b343ae9ab2#block-672910ea8f0842b343ae9ab2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on the subject}}}\uc2  of Katy Perry, the pop star posted to X to say that she has officially voted for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrThis is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2 . She\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be\u8230\'20\'26 well\u8230\'20\'26 We\u8217\'20\'19re the only ones who can finish this sentence ??????? VOTE! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zrEcSH1fah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zrEcSH1fah}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 KATY PERRY (@katyperry) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/katyperry/status/1853487317656175029?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will close out the final day of campaigning with a series of star-studded events featuring Oprah, Lady Gaga and \u8230\'20\'26 Katy Perry.\par \par \uc2 For anyone at the Javits Center in New York City on Election Night 2016 \u8211\'20\'13 and for those who were not, picture a glass-ceilinged convention hall with hordes of women and young girls blissfully unaware that the US was not, in fact, about to elect its first female president \u8211\'20\'13 Perry\u8217\'20\'19s election eve appearance may be jarring.\par \par \uc2 Not just because her solo Woman\u8217\'20\'19s World debuted this summer to brutal reviews \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/jul/12/katy-perry-womans-world-review"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Guardian asked:}}}\uc2  what regressive, warmed-over hell is this? \u8211\'20\'13 but because Perry\u8217\'20\'19s song Roar was the anthem of Hillary Clinton \u8217\'20\'19s doomed presidential bid in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Perry was due to perform at the Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s election night watch party in 2016. But as the results began to turn irrevocably against Clinton, Perry arrived on stage, not to sing but to implore voters in California to stay in line if they had not voted yet. The urgency in the pop star\u8217\'20\'19s voice, especially about votes in a deep blue state, shattered hopes in the room and confirmed what few had even considered at the beginning of the evening: that the \u8220\'20\'1Chighest, hardest\u8221\'20\'1D glass ceiling would not shatter \u8211\'20\'13 at least not that night.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps Perry\u8217\'20\'19s presence on the campaign trail on its final day will prove cathartic.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Transportation secretary \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2  appeared on the popular Jubilee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YE1f3n_n9UA&ab_channel=Jubilee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 YouTube }}}\uc2  channel where he attempted to win over 25 undecided Michigan voters.\par \par \uc2 In one clip {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/p/DB70VSVpZxd/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  posted }}}\uc2  on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , Buttigieg faced a young voter who said they were trying to decide between voting for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  or the Green party presidential candidate, Jill Stein. \u8220\'20\'1CI want to see something different,\u8221\'20\'1D the undecided voter said.\par \par \uc2 Buttigieg argued that neither the Democratic nor Republican party is \u8220\'20\'1Cperfect\u8221\'20\'1D but that \u8220\'20\'1CJill Stein is not going to become the president of the United States. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is, or \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom an environmental perspective \u8230\'20\'26 you\u8217\'20\'19ve got one side that is saying climate change is a hoax,\u8221\'20\'1D Buttigieg said, adding that Trump would \u8220\'20\'1Ctear up\u8221\'20\'1D the Clean Water Act if he is re-elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou keep mentioning stuff about Trump, but I\u8217\'20\'19m trying to tell you that I\u8217\'20\'19m between Jill and Kamala,\u8221\'20\'1D the voter responded. \u8220\'20\'1CI I have lost a lot of faith in our two party system, and I want to see something different.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Prior to the debate, six of the 25 voters said they were leaning toward Harris, four toward Trump, five leaning third parties and 11 said they were leaning toward not voting at all.\par \par \uc2 After hearing from Buttigieg, 12 of the participants said they planned to vote for Harris. Five said they would vote for Trump, six for third parties and three said they did not intend to vote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Arizona senate race: Democrat \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  polling ahead of Republican Kari Lake\par \par \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  is polling well ahead of his competitor, Kari Lake, while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is slightly ahead of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in most polls in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve spoken with people who are voting for both Trump and Gallego, who is a progressive member of the US House \u8211\'20\'13 an unlikely voting combination.\par \par \uc2 Gallego told me this morning that he\u8217\'20\'19s winning over Republicans and independents because he\u8217\'20\'19s been showing up for nearly two years in places they didn\u8217\'20\'19t expect to see him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe went to rural Arizona. We went to the boardrooms. We went to the rodeos,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI reached out to my veterans out there and made sure for them to understand that no matter what party I am, I\u8217\'20\'19m still a Marine Corps veteran first, and that I would be here to fight for them.\par \par \uc2 As far as the Trump-Gallego voter? \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s not a sizeable amount of people, but they\u8217\'20\'19re there, and we\u8217\'20\'19re proud to have them part of our coalition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At a house in the suburbs outside Phoenix this morning, US representative \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  fired up his supporters for one more day of getting out the vote for Democrats in Arizona as he seeks the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  seat, one of the crucial races nationally to keep the chamber.\par \par \uc2 The group of a dozen or so volunteers circled up with Gallego to first chant \u8220\'20\'1C si se puede,\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cyes we can\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CThe other side does not have this,\u8221\'20\'1D he told them. The Republicans aren\u8217\'20\'19t hitting the doors for dozens of canvasses every day like Democrats are, he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTheir IE is being funded by billionaires like \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . Ours is being funded by people. We have people, and that\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s going to win the day,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Voters say they\u8217\'20\'19re most concerned about three issues, Gallego said: \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access (the state has a measure to restore Roe on the ballot), cost of living and border security.\par \par \uc2 enltrRuben Gallego arrives to give a pep talk to canvassers launching from Avondale this morning. Canvassers are going out around the city today for last-minute GOTV {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/BiTvR6QWnT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/BiTvR6QWnT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rachel Leingang (@rachelleingang) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rachelleingang/status/1853479127283867795?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 I just got on a shuttle bus from the parking area for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Allentown and you can already feel the excitement.\par \par \uc2 People are cheering as strangers get on the bus bringing their children to the rally (schools in Allentown are closed today because of the visit).\par \par \uc2 Harris earlier stopped by a canvas in Scranton and is set to hold two more rallies in Pennsylvania today.\par \par \uc2 The fact that she\u8217\'20\'19s spending the entire last day of the campaign in Pennsylvania underscores how important the state\u8217\'20\'19s 19 electoral votes are to the race.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While in La Crosse, Wisconsin, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate JD Vance stopped by a set of giant storage tanks billed as the \u8220\'20\'1Cworld\u8217\'20\'19s largest six-pack\u8221\'20\'1D of beer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a six pack under the leadership of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said in a clip posted to his X account, while holding a six-pack of a beer.\par \par \uc2 Pointing to the 54ft-tall tanks, Vance said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a six pack under the leadership of \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2 . Let\u8217\'20\'19s make America great again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMake Six Packs Great Again.\par \par \uc2 Vote for \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cXGP7T5H6y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cXGP7T5H6y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 JD Vance (@JDVance) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JDVance/status/1853476540056543614?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, Ohio senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2 , made one final visit to the key swing state of Wisconsin before election day where he urged voters to back the Republican ticket even if \u8220\'20\'1Cyou don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with everything that Trump says.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur message to the swing voters of the state of Wisconsin is very simple: it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have to be like this,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance addressed supporters in La Crosse on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t have to agree with everything that I say, every policy proposal that we have. But what we know is that when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was president, you could afford to pay your bills.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance delivered a tight speech about border security and the economy, arguing that Americans were \u8220\'20\'1Cplaying by the rules\u8221\'20\'1D but have been \u8220\'20\'1Cfalling farther and farther behind\u8221\'20\'1D thanks to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s policies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is president, we get back to an old age of American prosperity,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 The final day of campaigning before Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election is here, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , JD Vance and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will be on the road rallying voters all day. We already heard from the former president, who told supporters in North Carolina that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/04/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-polls-latest-live-news?page=with:block-6728f02b8f08b3d97c36532d#block-6728f02b8f08b3d97c36532d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he would put tariffs on Mexico}}}\uc2  to force them to stop migrants from entering the United States, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/04/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-polls-latest-live-news?page=with:block-6728fe038f083ba7acfea54a#block-6728fe038f083ba7acfea54a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 distorting his economic record}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/04/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-polls-latest-live-news?page=with:block-6728f9478f082a575b9e59bb#block-6728f9478f082a575b9e59bb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacking}}}\uc2  Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 . Harris, meanwhile, will be spending her time in Pennsylvania, and has so far today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/04/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-polls-latest-live-news?page=with:block-6728e61b8f080a1fc5f96459#block-6728e61b8f080a1fc5f96459"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 avoided talking about her opponent}}}\uc2  in what will be one of her last chances to reach the voters who could send her to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has been going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 We can expect to see some of the final polls of the presidential race released today. One survey that came out, from Emerson College and The Hill, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/04/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-polls-latest-live-news?page=with:block-6728d9b98f0869c6d52e5f5f#block-6728d9b98f0869c6d52e5f5f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirms}}}\uc2  that the two candidates are ties in the swing states.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Election administrators{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/04/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-polls-latest-live-news?page=with:block-6728bc4d8f080a1fc5f961f0#block-6728bc4d8f080a1fc5f961f0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have stepped up their security}}}\uc2  as they face threats and harassment connected to Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s vote.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 If recent history is any guide, tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s election may take days to call \u8211\'20\'13 or merely hours. Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/04/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-polls-latest-live-news?page=with:block-67287b358f080a1fc5f95f0b#block-67287b358f080a1fc5f95f0b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a look}}}\uc2  at why calling election winners can be so unpredictable.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 An official in Washoe has raised concerns about a new voter registration system in Nevada.\par \par \uc2 Cari-Ann Burgess, the former interim Washoe County registrar who has been on administrative leave since September and is facing charges of insubordination and poor job performance, has said that the county\u8217\'20\'19s new voter registration and management system that went live eight days before the early voting in Nevada started has issues that still needs to be worked out. Her complaints are detailed in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/nevada-voter-registration-election-management-system-concerns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent article by ProPublica.}}}\par \par \uc2 Burgess has alleged that the new system lacked safeguards to keep non-citizens from voting, and that issues with transferring data from the old to the new system could have left some registered voters off.\par \par \uc2 But the secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office has strongly denied any issues, and noted that a lack of issues with early voting are a sign that things are working well.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Early voting ballots are being tallied in Washoe County, Nevada \u8211\'20\'13 and observers from both major parties have been holed up in the plexiglass observation room to watch the count.\par \par \uc2 Washoe, which includes the mountain city of Reno, is what many locals call the \u8220\'20\'1Cswingiest\u8221\'20\'1D county in a key swing state, one that could help determine the outcome of the presidential election. During the midterms this year, the county\u8217\'20\'19s Republican commissioners {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/washoe-county-cisco-aguilar-aaron-ford-427cb4cbb840f6f9d995403d52e63419"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted against certifying}}}\uc2  the election, spurring legal action, before reversing course.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of Election Day, the office has been fielding a deluge of questions and public information requests, working to reassure the public that the vote count is coming along smoothly.\par \par \uc2 Bob Blackstock, who is one among several observers with the local Democratic Party, said he was compelled to get involved in the elections process in 2022. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not even that I\u8217\'20\'19m so passionate about being a Democrat, it\u8217\'20\'19s that I\u8217\'20\'19m passionate about democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Blackstock, who is an organizer with the Washoe Democrats, but was speaking from his personal capacity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we lose our democracy I don\u8217\'20\'19t know what is left.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Blackstock anticipates that his biggest responsibility will be to testify at the commission\u8217\'20\'19s vote to approve the canvass \u8211\'20\'13 and providing a counterpoint to election deniers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt really seems like people have already made up their minds,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. Even though those who believe there is fraud have been able to watch the count and ask officials detailed questions, he worries that those looking for anything suspicious will think they see it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s self-confirmation bias,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Despite presiding over mass layoffs, Trump makes false claim about employment\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just told a whopper of a lie about the economy, saying that the most recent employment numbers were \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst \u8230\'20\'26 in modern history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In fact, that distinction goes to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/archives/empsit_05082020.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 2020\u8217\'20\'19s data}}}\uc2 , which showed more than 20 million people had lost their jobs and unemployment had skyrocketed to 14.7% due to the outbreak of Covid-19. Who was president then? Trump, whose administration was roundly criticized for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/mar/28/trump-coronavirus-politics-us-health-disaster"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mishandling the pandemic}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last month\u8217\'20\'19s jobs report was indeed weak, though it remains to be seen if the trend will persist, or if the data was just reflecting the impact of an industrial strike and two major hurricanes:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/nov/01/us-october-jobs-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US adds only 12,000 jobs in October in final report before election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In something of a throwback to his first presidential campaign (and many years of Republican attacks before that), Trump made a point to mention \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s middle name, and also attacked former first lady \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Barack Hussein Obama\uc2 , I call him the great divider,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said during his ongoing speech in Raleigh, North Carolina. Hussein is Obama\u8217\'20\'19s middle name, but Republicans, including Trump, have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/aug/11/donald-trump-calls-barack-obama-the-founder-of-isis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made a point of mentioning it while}}}\uc2  simultaneously propagating baseless claims that he is Muslim, or was born outside the United States.\par \par \uc2 Trump then complained that \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  insulted him: \u8220\'20\'1CMichelle hit me there. I was so nice to her, out of respect. I was saying she hit me the other day. I was going to say to my people, am I allowed to hit her now? They said, take it easy, sir.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  recently appeared with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at a rally in swing state Michigan:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/michelle-obama-kamala-harris-michigan-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michelle Obama blasts Trump for \u8216\'20\'18gross incompetence\u8217\'20\'19 at Harris\u8217\'20\'19s Michigan rally}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As he has campaigned this year, Trump has become known for his lengthy speeches that typically run around 90 minutes.\par \par \uc2 The former president is clearly aware that much has been written about his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/07/election-trump-speeches"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 penchant to go on and on}}}\uc2 , saying at his rally in Raleigh, North Carolina: \u8220\'20\'1CBy the way, the press will say, Oh, he rambled.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat was genius,\u8221\'20\'1D he said of his speech. \u8220\'20\'1CThe rest of it I don\u8217\'20\'19t really even have to talk about.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has dubbed his rambling speaking style \u8220\'20\'1Cthe weave\u8221\'20\'1D, and called his speech in Raleigh \u8220\'20\'1Cthe ultimate weave\u8221\'20\'1D. He added: \u8220\'20\'1CAnd think of it, isn\u8217\'20\'19t it nice that you can have a president that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t need to use a teleprompter?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump definitely uses a teleprompter, but often does not follow what\u8217\'20\'19s on it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump threatens Mexico with tariffs if they don't stop migrants from entering US\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has finally taken the stage in Raleigh, North Carolina, and announced a new policy: he would impose tariffs on Mexico if the United States\u8217\'20\'19s southern neighbor does not stop migrants from crossing their shared border.\par \par \uc2 Referring to Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s recently inaugurated president \uc2 Claudia Sheinbaum\uc2 , Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CI haven\u8217\'20\'19t met her, and I\u8217\'20\'19m going to inform her on day one or sooner, that if they don\u8217\'20\'19t stop this onslaught of criminals and drugs coming into our country, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to immediately impose a 25% tariff on everything they send in to the United States of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s only got a 100% chance of working, because if that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t work, I\u8217\'20\'19ll make it 50, and [if] that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t work, I\u8217\'20\'19ll make it 75. For the tough guys, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll make it 100,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, predicting Mexico will deploy soldiers to its southern border with Guatemala and Belize to stop migrants heading north.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, their southern border\u8217\'20\'19s where they come in, they come right through. And by the way, there\u8217\'20\'19s 100% chance of working. It\u8217\'20\'19s only a question,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. He called Mexico America\u8217\'20\'19s top trading partner, which isn\u8217\'20\'19t quite right \u8211\'20\'13 according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ustr.gov/countries-regions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US trade representative}}}\uc2 , it is the number-two supplier and purchaser of American goods.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a bit late to his rally in Raleigh, North Carolina, but his son \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  just came onstage to give voters a pep talk, one angled on encouraging them to look for the voter fraud that Republicans claim, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/03/trump-republicans-non-citizen-voters-myth-stolen-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 without much evidence}}}\uc2 , mars elections in the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo, you guys, at this point is up to each and every one of you. So, whatever you would do if you woke up on November 6 and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was president-elect, whatever you would do to stop that disaster for our country, for the world and for Western civilization, whatever you would do, do it now,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump Jr said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo it till the polls close tomorrow night, and then start calling your friends on the west coast to make sure they\u8217\'20\'19re doing it, too. Get in line, dear friends, stay in line. If you see nonsense, video it, show it to everyone. Do not let them play their games.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Conspicuously absent from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s closing argument? \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At least in name. In the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s closing ad and in the final days on the campaign trail, the vice-president has made no explicit reference to her opponent, instead opting to end on a positive, forward-looking note.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur campaign has not been about being against something, it is about being for something,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said at a high-energy rally in Michigan on Sunday night. \u8220\'20\'1CA fight for a future with freedom and opportunity and dignity for all Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At a Black church in Detroit, Harris appealed to \u8220\'20\'1CAmericans from so-called red states to so-called blue states who are ready to bend the arc of history toward justice\u8221\'20\'1D and declared the country ready to \u8220\'20\'1Cturn the page and write the next chapter of our history.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a shift from just a few days ago, when the vice-president focused on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s threat to American democracy and agreed with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former aides who said he was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfascist.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But in the final days, the Harris campaign is betting that the slice of undecided voters left need an affirmative reason to vote for Harris. If they were scared of the threat Trump poses, they\u8217\'20\'19d likely have made up their minds long ago.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump to rally in North Carolina, first of four events in final day of campaigning\par \par \uc2 We expect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to soon take the stage in Raleigh, North Carolina, kicking off his final sprint of campaigning before polls open in tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The former president has four events scheduled today. After Raleigh, he\u8217\'20\'19s set to appear in Reading, Pennsylvania at 2pm, then in Pittsburgh at 6pm, and finally in Grand Rapids, Michigan at 10.30pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The presidential election is being held tomorrow, but it may take days to count the ballots necessary to determine the winner, and the story may not end there. Evidence is mounting that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies are planning to once again cast doubt on the result, should he lose. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levine}}}\uc2  explains how:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has left little doubt that he will contest the results of the 2024 election if he loses.\par \par \uc2 Election lawyers and voting rights experts are bracing for an aggressive effort by the former president in the days after the election to challenge the results while votes are still being counted. But unlike 2020, when Trump\u8217\'20\'19s effort after the election seemed a bit haphazard, experts say they\u8217\'20\'19re seeing a much more organized effort that stretches from the courts to local groups organizing election deniers to work the polls.\par \par \uc2 Here are a few key ways Trump is preparing to contest the 2024 vote:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/trump-2024-election-subversion-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fraud, lawsuits, chaos: how Trump is preparing to contest the 2024 election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 We can also expect some final polls of the presidential race to be released today, though what has come out doesn\u8217\'20\'19t show much.\par \par \uc2 The Hill and Emerson College surveyed all seven swing states and found, as many, many other polls before it have shown, that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are in an effective tie:\par \par \uc2 enltrFINAL SWING STATE POLLS with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/thehill?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @thehill}}}\par \par \uc2 2024 Presidential Election\par \par \uc2 AZ: Trump 50%, Harris 48%\par \par \uc2 GA: Trump 50%, Harris 49%\par \par \uc2 MI: Harris 50%, Trump 48%\par \par \uc2 NC: Trump 49%, Harris 48%\par \par \uc2 NV: Harris 48%, Trump 48%\par \par \uc2 PA: Trump 49%, Harris 48%\par \par \uc2 WI: Trump 49%, Harris 49% {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/axSc58DgwM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/axSc58DgwM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Emerson College Polling (@EmersonPolling) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EmersonPolling/status/1853437395711963570?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 We will soon hear from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , when he holds his first campaign event of the day in Raleigh, North Carolina at 10am.\par \par \uc2 And we may also see some of his supporters turn up wearing trash bags, as they have started doing recently:\par \par \uc2 If you missed this latest bizarre turn in the presidential campaign \u8211\'20\'13 which could have real impacts on the allegiances of a key voters group \u8211\'20\'13 the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Richard Luscombe explains what it is and why it matters in the below piece:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/trump-final-week-campaign-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Threats, racism, misogyny: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s disturbing final week of campaigning}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Walz to campaign in Minnesota, Wisconsin and Michigan\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  also has a busy day of campaigning ahead of him.\par \par \uc2 He starts in St Paul, Minnesota, capital of the state he governs, where he and his wife Gwen Walz will greet their neighbors, before heading to Wisconsin for rallies in La Crosse, Stevens Point and Milwaukee. At that last rally, they\u8217\'20\'19ll have Eric Ben\u233\'00\'E9t as their musical guest, the campaign says.\par \par \uc2 They finish the day with a rally in Detroit where they will have even more musical guests, specifically the Detroit Youth Choir, Jon Bon Jovi, and The War and Treaty.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate JD Vance will campaign in four different swing states today.\par \par \uc2 Specifically Wisconsin, Michigan, Georgia and Pennsylvania. His press secretary just posted a video of him dressed all casual and he and his wife set out for the day:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JDVance?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JDVance}}}\uc2  and Usha board TF2 for a full day on the campaign trail today!\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re headed to:\par \par \uc2 ?? La Crosse, WI\par \par \uc2 ?? Flint, MI\par \par \uc2 ?? Atlanta, GA\par \par \uc2 ?? Newtown, PA {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xK0VaOqn61"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xK0VaOqn61}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Taylor Van Kirk (@taylorvankirk) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/taylorvankirk/status/1853428548461121784?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris spends final campaign day blitzing Pennsylvania with events\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is spending all day campaigning in Pennsylvania, which is seen as potentially the most important state to win this election.\par \par \uc2 Her first stop is in Scranton, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s childhood hometown, where she\u8217\'20\'19ll participate in a kickoff for canvassers, he campaign said. After that, she heads to Allentown, Pittsburgh and Philadelphia before finally returning to Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 Biden is not scheduled to join her in Scranton. He\u8217\'20\'19s spent the weekend at his home in Wilmington, Delaware, and is heading to the White House this morning, where he will have a private call with military members involved in fighting the Islamic State in Iraq and Syria.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 US election offices increase security measures amid ongoing threats\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/the-election-office"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elections offices}}}\uc2  in the US have hardened their security measures this year, anticipating potential violence based on experience since 2020 and during an ongoing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/election-political-violence-surge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rise in threats}}}\uc2  and harassment focused on election workers.\par \par \uc2 Many offices have now trained their workers on de-escalation tactics. They\u8217\'20\'19ve run drills for active shooters or other disturbances. They have a process for flagging the threats that could be criminal and seeking law enforcement help when needed.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of election offices have been reinforced with bulletproof glass and steel doors. Some have increased their security details or locked down their social media in case people come looking into their lives. And new laws and added enforcement of prohibitions on such harassment have added to the response to the increased hostility.\par \par \uc2 Authorities are concerned about the rise of the right-wing election denial movement, which originated in 2020 following Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rejection of his defeat to Joe Biden. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s propagation of unfounded theories regarding the election mobilized large crowds to participate in \u8220\'20\'1CStop the Steal\u8221\'20\'1D protests, which reached a climax on January 6, 2021, when supporters stormed the US Capitol in a bid to impede Congress\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation of the election outcomes.\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/09/08/trump-election-threats/?itid=lk_inline_manual_6&itid=lk_inline_manual_15"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not committed to accepting the outcome}}}\uc2 , claiming without evidence that Democrats will cheat to install his opponent, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/kamala-harris/?itid=lk_inline_manual_15"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Michigan secretary of state Jocelyn Benson, a Democrat, said her concern for her personal safety increased after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 , the owner of X, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/elon-musk-michigan-election-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacked her online}}}\uc2 . Before she responded to his claims about Michigan voting and her office, she called her security team to \u8220\'20\'1Cmake sure my family was safe,\u8221\'20\'1D she said on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KXV-Nj7qkNI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story by my colleague, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rachel-leingang"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rachel Leingang}}}\uc2 , here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/election-office-security-threats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election offices increase security measures amid ongoing threats}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 What would a Trump victory mean for the UK-US 'special relationship'?\par \par \uc2 Eleni Coureais a political correspondent for the Guardian:\par \par \uc2 A Trump victory would be awkward for the Labour party, which has close links with the Democrats and has seen droves of members voluntarily head to the US in recent months to campaign for Kamala Harris.\par \par \uc2 Last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/trump-complaint-uk-labour-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign filed a formal complaint}}}\uc2  accusing Labour of foreign interference in the US election after a social media post by the party\u8217\'20\'19s head of operations Sofia Patel said nearly 100 current and former staffers were travelling over to support Harris and offered to help them with accommodation.\par \par \uc2 The row was deeply frustrating for Keir Starmer, who has sought to build a good working relationship with Trump since becoming prime minister in July and was one of a few world leaders to speak directly to the former president after he suffered an assassination attempt in mid-July. The pair met in person in September for a two-hour dinner while Starmer was in New York for the UN General Assembly.\par \par \uc2 David Lammy, the UK\u8217\'20\'19s foreign secretary, was present at the dinner in New York and has actively been developing links with Republican politicians. But there are questions over whether Lammy can remain in his role if Trump wins, given his strident criticism of the former president in past years \u8212\'20\'14 he has branded him a \u8220\'20\'1Cneo-Nazi sympathizing sociopath,\u8221\'20\'1D a \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous clown\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ca racist KKK and Nazi sympathizer\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 If Trump is elected, Starmer would need to try and convince him of the importance of supporting Ukraine in its defence against the Russian invasion. Trump has censured Ukrainian president Volodymyr Zelenskyy for not making concessions to Russia and has made clear he wants to see a quick end to the war.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 Secretaries of state ask social media companies for moderation plans on election day\par \par \uc2 Rachel Leingang is a democracy reporter focused on misinformation for Guardian US\par \par \uc2 A group of Democratic secretaries of state are calling on social media companies to detail their plans to moderate inflammatory content and artificial intelligence on their platforms during and after election day.\par \par \uc2 Seven secretaries of state \u8211\'20\'13 representing Maine, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/rhode-island"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rhode Island}}}\uc2 , Illinois, Oregon, Vermont, Washington and New Mexico \u8211\'20\'13 sent the letters to Google, X and Meta on Friday. Secretaries of state typically play some role in overseeing elections in their states.\par \par \uc2 The officials note that violent threats against election officials and disinformation about elections are already spreading online, saying they are \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply concerned about the failure of major social media companies to clearly lay out their plans to moderate inflammatory claims and AI-generated election-related content ahead of, during and following election day\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Throughout the 2024 election, false and misleading claims about elections have spread widely, playing on frequent myths like that noncitizens are voting en masse or that tabulation machines aren\u8217\'20\'19t secure. Donald Trump often elevates these claims, as does X owner Elon Musk, as part of an ongoing narrative that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  can only win the election if they cheat.\par \par \uc2 Republicans in Congress and in the courts continue to go after attempts to flag misinformation during previous elections and call it censorship. In response, many platforms have taken a less active approach to moderating or removing content, and some have far fewer staff dedicated to trust and safety than they did in previous years.\par \par \uc2 Some of those signed on to the letters have been targets of threats and harassment personally for doing their jobs.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/secretaries-of-state-social-media-companies-election-plans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Secretaries of state ask social media companies for moderation plans on election day}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Reuters news agency has pulled together a list of people Donald Trump has suggested he would investigate or prosecute if he is reelected for a second presidential term (having lost a reelection bid in 2020 against Joe Biden \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/04/trump-2024-election-subversion-explainer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a result he still falsely claims was rigged against him}}}\uc2  ):\par \par \uc2 The \u8216\'20\'18enemy from within\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Asked on Fox News last month whether he expected chaos on Election Day, Trump responded that the bigger problem was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy from within\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have some sick people, radical left lunatics... and it should be very easily handled by, if necessary, by National Guard, or if really necessary, by the military.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Political adversaries\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has called for investigations into Kamala Harris, President Joe Biden, former President Barack Obama and Liz Cheney, a former Republican congressman and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/liz-cheney-kamala-harris-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vocal Trump opponent}}}\uc2 . Trump has shared posts on his Truth Social media platform calling for military tribunals to try Cheney and Obama.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At a September rally in Pennsylvania, Trump said Harris, the US vice president, was responsible for the \u8220\'20\'1Cbiggest crime story of our time,\u8221\'20\'1D referring to illegal border crossings. \u8220\'20\'1CShe should be impeached and prosecuted for her actions,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Election workers\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump and his allies have been laying the groundwork to contest a potential loss in November by stoking doubts about the election\u8217\'20\'19s legitimacy. Trump has portrayed Democrats as cheaters, called mail-in ballots corrupt and urged supporters to vote in such large numbers to render the election \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo big to rig\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPlease beware that this legal exposure extends to Lawyers, Political Operatives, Donors, Illegal Voters, & Corrupt Election Officials,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump posted on Truth Social last month. \u8220\'20\'1CThose involved in unscrupulous behavior will be sought out, caught, and prosecuted at levels, unfortunately, never seen before in our country,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Protestors\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Following pro-Palestinian protests on college campuses across the USs this year, Trump told Fox News in July that anyone who desecrates the American flag should get a one-year jail sentence. \u8220\'20\'1CNow, people will say: \u8216\'20\'18Oh it\u8217\'20\'19s unconstitutional.\u8217\'20\'19 Those are stupid people who say that,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, adding that he wants to work with Congress to allow the jail sentences. Trump has said he would arrest \u8220\'20\'1Cpro-Hamas thugs\u8221\'20\'1D who engage in vandalism, an apparent reference to the college student protesters.\par \par \uc2 Tech sector\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has also warned Meta CEO Mark Zuckerberg and Google over what he claims is potential election interference on their tech platforms. Trump has accused Meta of suppressing content that would have hurt Joe Biden in the 2020 election, and has also criticised Zuckerberg\u8217\'20\'19s donations to bolster election infrastructure. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are watching him closely, and if he does anything illegal this time he will spend the rest of his life in prison,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote his recently published Save America coffee table book, according to media reviews of the book.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has also threatened to instruct the Department of Justice to criminally investigate Google for \u8220\'20\'1Conly revealing and displaying bad stories about Donald J. Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a Truth Social post last month. \u8220\'20\'1CI will request their prosecution, at the maximum levels, when I win the Election,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump wrote, without providing evidence for his assertion about Google.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump said earlier this month that if elected he would fire Jack Smith, the federal prosecutor leading the criminal probes into his attempts to overturn his 2020 election defeat and alleged mishandling of classified documents after leaving office. That follows an April 2023 speech by Trump - after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/mar/30/who-is-alvin-bragg-donald-trump-indictment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Manhattan District Attorney Alvin Bragg}}}\uc2  convinced a New York grand jury to bring the first criminal charges ever against a former US president, in which he said Bragg was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe criminal\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CHe should be prosecuted or at a minimum he should resign,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 Memorable images from the 2024 US presidential campaign\par \par \uc2 Here is a look back at some of the more memorable pictures of the 2024 US presidential campaign:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/trump-banning-vaccines-president-rfk-fluoride-rcna178570"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In an interview with NBC News}}}\uc2 , Donald Trump did not rule out banning certain vaccines if he was elected to a second presidential term.\par \par \uc2 Trump told the outlet in a phone interview that he is open to some of the more controversial ideas of Robert F Kennedy Jr, a nephew of President John F Kennedy and son of the US attorney general and New York senator Robert F Kennedy.\par \par \uc2 Trump said recently that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/from-joy-and-jlo-to-insults-and-alpha-males-harris-and-trump-zero-in-on-nevada"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he wants}}}\uc2  the vaccine skeptic Robert F Kennedy Jr \u8220\'20\'1Cto take care of health\u8221\'20\'1D, including \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen\u8217\'20\'19s health\u8221\'20\'1D if the former president wins back the White House in this election.\par \par \uc2 Asked on Sunday whether banning certain vaccines would be an option if he was elected, Trump told NBC News: \u8220\'20\'1CWell, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to talk to [Kennedy] and talk to other people, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll make a decision, but he\u8217\'20\'19s a very talented guy and has strong views.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump refused to say what specific role Robert F Kennedy Jr may play in his administration but sources close to his campaign told NBC News he might play a prominent role in battling \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/rfk-jr-lead-trump-efforts-chronic-childhood-disease-rcna178293"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 chronic childhood disease}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It comes as Robert F Kennedy Jr, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/robert-f-kennedy-jr-drops-out-endorses-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who ended his independent White House bid in August}}}\uc2  and endorsed Trump, said the former Republican president would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/rfk-jr-trump-remove-fluoride-drinking-water"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 push to remove fluoride from drinking water}}}\uc2  on his first day in office if elected. He said fluoride was \u8220\'20\'1Can industrial waste\u8221\'20\'1D linked to a variety of health conditions.\par \par \uc2 enltrOn January 20, the Trump White House will advise all U.S?. water systems to remove fluoride from public water. Fluoride is an industrial waste associated with arthritis, bone fractures, bone cancer, IQ loss, neurodevelopmental disorders, and thyroid disease. President\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert F. Kennedy Jr (@RobertKennedyJr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RobertKennedyJr/status/1852812012478398923?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Where does Donald Trump stand on some of the key election issues?\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the stances former Republican president Donald Trump has on key election issues. You can read more in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/election-trump-harris-policies-issues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this explainer}}}\uc2  by my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Economy\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Much of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s inflation-reduction plan hinges on his vow to slash energy costs by expanding oil and gas drilling and deregulation. He has also been highly critical of high interest rates, the Federal Reserve\u8217\'20\'19s main inflation-fighting tool.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-08-08/trump-wants-presidents-to-have-some-say-over-fed-policy?sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  recently that he thinks the president should have a say in decisions made by the Fed, which traditionally operates independently from politics.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has vowed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/markets/us/tariffs-tax-cuts-core-trumps-economic-pitch-voters-2024-09-24/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 extend and expand}}}\uc2  a suite of tax cuts he signed into law in 2017, while pledging to cut the corporate tax rate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-09-05/trump-vows-15-corporate-tax-and-taps-musk-for-federal-audit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to 15% from 21%}}}\uc2  for companies that make their products in the US. He has also said he would exempt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/social-security-tax-trump-election-2024-9f911216"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Social Security benefits}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-taxes-social-security-overtime-tariffs-989016ef41dc1533b05d1871d69c03ff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and overtime pay}}}\uc2 , in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/09/trump-las-vegas-rally-heat-medics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 addition to tips}}}\uc2 , from income taxes.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 He has suggested an across-the-board {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/markets/us/trumps-plan-hike-tariffs-would-spike-shipping-costs-just-like-2018-experts-say-2024-09-12/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 levy}}}\uc2  of perhaps 10% and up to 20% on virtually all foreign-made goods, as well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2024/02/04/trump-floats-more-than-60percent-tariffs-on-chinese-imports.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slapping tariffs of 60%}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 or more \u8211\'20\'13 on goods from China.\par \par \uc2 Abortion\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access should be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/08/trump-abortion-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left to the states}}}\uc2 , and has vowed that as president he would not sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban (weeks before making that pledge, he refused to say whether he would veto such a ban).\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has said that if he wins he would make IVF free for women, though has provided few specifics and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  in Congress have repeatedly blocked legislation that would protect the treatment.\par \par \uc2 Immigration and \u8216\'20\'18border security\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has promised to carry out the largest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/trump-mass-deportations-detention-camps-military-migrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 domestic deportation}}}\uc2  operation in US history, a policy that would face many logistical, legal and financial hurdles.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has said he would reinstate several controversial policies from his first term, including the Remain in Mexico program, Title 42 and a travel ban targeting several Muslim-majority nations.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 He has vowed to rescind programs that shield undocumented immigrants from deportation, including children, while revoking the legal status of potentially hundreds of thousands of immigrants in the US under the federal temporary protected status program.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has also suggested he would end birthright citizenship for the US-born children of undocumented immigrant.\par \par \uc2 Climate and energy policies\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump has questioned established climate science, previously dismissing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/oct/02/donald-trump-climate-change-michael-mann-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate crisis}}}\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cmythical\u8221\'20\'1D and an \u8220\'20\'1Cexpensive hoax\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As president, Trump claims he will prioritize clean air and water for Americans. Yet he has also promised to continue to roll back environmental regulations, including all of the ones put in place by the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a May meeting with oil bosses, he reportedly offered to dismantle Biden\u8217\'20\'19s environmental rules and requested $1bn in contributions to his presidential campaign. He is especially opposed to wind power \u8211\'20\'13 falsely claiming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/trump-whale-wind-turbine-renewable-energy-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wind turbines}}}\uc2  kill birds and cause cancer.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 Where does Kamala Harris stand on some of the key election issues?\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2 , a political correspondent for Guardian US, has done {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/election-trump-harris-policies-issues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this useful explainer}}}\uc2  about where the two presidential candidates stand on key issues. Here are some extracts from the piece:\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\par \par \uc2 Economy\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris says she wants to build up the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/16/kamala-harris-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Copportunity economy,\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , focused on the middle class, with plans to combat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/14/kamala-harris-economic-policy-aides"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 price gouging}}}\uc2 , boost housing development, aid first-time homebuyers, expand tax credits for parents and expand Medicare to cover {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/harris-home-health-care-sandwhich-generation-098a7ed48dfd94d11fb0efcd5d63b42b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in-home senior care}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris has pledged to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/16/kamala-harris-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut taxes }}}\uc2  for tens of millions of middle- and low-income families, while saying she supports {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/antoniopequenoiv/2024/09/04/harris-proposes-50000-small-business-tax-deduction-for-startup-expenses-heres-what-to-know/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tax breaks}}}\uc2  for entrepreneurs and small business owners. She also backs a proposal championed by Trump to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/10/harris-walz-las-vegas-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminate taxes on tips}}}\uc2 . Harris has called for the corporate tax rate to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/business/4835444-harris-proposes-corporate-tax-increase/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raised to 28%}}}\uc2 , up from 21%.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris is expected to maintain the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s approach, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/may/14/joe-biden-tariff-chinese-made-electric-vehicles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relying on tariffs}}}\uc2  and export controls to boost domestic competitiveness with China.\par \par \uc2 Abortion\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris has called on Congress to pass legislation to restore the protections of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade,}}}\uc2  which the supreme court overturned in 2022. Doing so would reinstate the Roe-era status quo, in effect blocking states from banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability, or about 24 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 As president, Harris has vowed she would veto any nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, Harris has pledged to protect the full spectrum of reproductive healthcare, including access to contraception and other fertility treatments such as in vitro fertilization ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/ivf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 IVF}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 Immigration and \u8216\'20\'18border security\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 During a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/27/harris-immigration-border-visit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visit to the border in September}}}\uc2 , Harris laid out a plan to enact stricter penalties for people who attempt to claim asylum between lawful ports of entry.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris has long championed comprehensive immigration reform, including pathways to citizenship for undocumented immigrants, especially those who were brought to the US as children.\par \par \uc2 Climate and energy policies\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris has walked back her support for the progressive Green New Deal proposal and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/sep/11/fracking-debate-explained-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fracking ban}}}\uc2 . She is a proponent of electric vehicles \u8211\'20\'13 though does not support a mandate \u8211\'20\'13 and backs clean-energy tax credits.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.57am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 In the 60th {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US presidential election}}}\uc2 , all 435 seats in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_House_of_Representatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives}}}\uc2  are up for grabs along with 34 of the 100 seats in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Senate}}}\uc2 , which together will decide the membership of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/119th_United_States_Congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 119th Congress}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republicans hold a majority in the House, while Democrats control the Senate, both by narrow margins. But the polls \u8211\'20\'13 if to be believed \u8211\'20\'13 suggest Democrats could win back the House and Republicans retake the Senate.\par \par \uc2 The Republican House majority leader, Steve Scalise, has told Axios that multiple GOP members have been \u8220\'20\'1Cangling\u8221\'20\'1D for senior posts in a potential administration led by Donald Trump.\par \par \uc2 Scalise, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/03/steve-scalise-house-speaker-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a hardline conservative}}}\uc2  representing Louisiana, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/11/03/house-republicans-scalise-trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the outlet}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve heard from a number of members that have been having conversations whether they\u8217\'20\'19re on a short list or a long-short list.\par \par \uc2 And we saw it in 2017 where a number of House colleagues got pulled into Cabinet secretary positions and other positions, and so I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t expect anything different this time.\par \par \uc2 Hopefully we have a large enough majority where that option is available to them, but that\u8217\'20\'19s going to be up to President Trump.\par \par \uc2 Scalise said he is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery confident\u8221\'20\'1D House Republicans will hold or grow their majority, adding that a margin of 8-12 seats would be a good one for the party (Democrats need to flip only four seats to win back a House majority this year).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, with the way redistricting is, these aren\u8217\'20\'19t the days we can get a 30-seat majority anymore. So whatever majority we have is going to be slim,\u8221\'20\'1D Scalise told Axios.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump said with two days until the presidential election that he should never have left the White House after his defeat in 2020 and joked darkly he would be fine with reporters getting shot, dredging up grievances that overshadowed his attack lines against Kamala Harris.\par \par \uc2 The closing themes of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign at a rally in Lititz in the battleground state of Pennsylvania brought him full circle with his 2016 campaign that went after the news media and his 2020 campaign that was defined by his attempts to overturn the result.\par \par \uc2 Trump stayed on message for the first part of his remarks but could not resist reverting to resentments he has held on to for years, describing Democrats as demonic and lamenting the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 an issue that polls badly and his aides privately said they thought he had been convinced to drop.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe had the safest border in the history of our country the day that I left,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CI shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have left, I mean honestly, we did so well, we had such a great \u8211\'20\'13 \u8221\'20\'1D he said before abruptly cutting himself off.\par \par \uc2 The remark reflected what Trump told aides and allies in the aftermath of his 2020 election defeat, a loss he has never conceded, and how he sat in at least one meeting at the end of his first term where he mused about refusing to leave the White House, a person familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story by my colleague, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2 , here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/trump-election-pennsylvania-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump says \u8216\'20\'18I shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have left\u8217\'20\'19 White House, despite losing 2020 election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.32am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/04/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-polls-latest-live-news?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-672847a28f08b3d97c364c41#block-672847a28f08b3d97c364c41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As we mentioned in the opening summary}}}\uc2 , the US vice president and Democratic presidential hopeful, Kamala Harris, pledged to \u8220\'20\'1Cdo everything in my power to end the war in Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D in her final rally in Michigan on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Many Democratic voters, including Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s large Arab American and Muslim American population, have expressed anger at the Biden administration over its support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war on Gaza (and now Lebanon).\par \par \uc2 The US continues to be the biggest arms supplier to Israel and is its most powerful diplomatic ally. Harris has not signalled a significant shift from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s policy. Both have condemned the high civilian death toll (according to Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s health ministry over 43,000 Palestinian people have been killed in Israeli airstrikes since last October) but continue to insist on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right \u8220\'20\'1Cto defend itself\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris said at the Michigan rally:\par \par \uc2 We are joined today by leaders of the Arab American community, which has deep and proud roots here in Michigan, and I want to say this year has been difficult, given the scale of death and destruction in Gaza and given the civilian casualties and displacement in Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 It is devastating, and as president, I will do everything in my power to end the war in Gaza, to bring home the hostages, end the suffering in Gaza, ensure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  is secure and ensure the Palestinian people can realize their right to dignity, freedom, security and self-determination.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 How long it will take to know the winner and where to find early clues about how the contest might unfold\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Election Day in the US}}}\uc2  is now often considered election week as each state follows its own rules and practices for counting ballots that can delay the results. There is also the possibility of legal challenges to counts that could cause delays.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, The Associated Press declared Joe Biden the winner on Saturday afternoon \u8212\'20\'14 four days after polls closed. But even then, The AP called North Carolina for Donald Trump 10 days after Election Day and Georgia for Biden 16 days later after hand recounts.\par \par \uc2 Four years earlier, the 2016 election was decided just hours after most polls closed. The Associated Press declared Trump the winner on election night at 2:29 a.m.\par \par \uc2 The tightness of the race this year makes it hard to predict when a winner could be declared \u8211\'20\'13 but North Carolina and Georgia could give an early indication as results in these swing states come in relatively quickly.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press has pinpointed areas in swing states that could give us a clue on how the race will unfold:\par \par \uc2 In North Carolina, Harris\u8217\'20\'19 margins in Wake and Mecklenburg counties, home to the state capital of Raleigh and the state\u8217\'20\'19s largest city, Charlotte, respectively, will reveal how much Trump will need to squeeze out of the less-populated rural areas he has dominated.\par \par \uc2 In Pennsylvania, Harris needs heavy turnout in deep blue Philadelphia, but she\u8217\'20\'19s also looking to boost the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 advantage in the arc of suburban counties to the north and west of the city.\par \par \uc2 She has campaigned aggressively in Bucks, Chester, Delaware and Montgomery counties, where Biden improved on Clinton\u8217\'20\'19s 2016 winning margins. The Philadelphia metro area, including the four collar counties, accounts for 43 percent of Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s vote.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere in the Blue Wall, Trump needs to blunt Democratic growth in Michigan\u8217\'20\'19 s key suburban counties outside of Detroit, especially Oakland County. He faces the same challenge in Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s Waukesha County outside of Milwaukee.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 What is the current state of the polls?\par \par \uc2 The Guardian US has been averaging national and state polls to see how the two candidates are faring. Nationally, Kamala Harris has a one-point advantage, 48% to 47%, over Donald Trump, virtually identical to last week.\par \par \uc2 The election will be decided in the seven battleground states: Arizona, Georgia, Michigan, Nevada, North Carolina, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin. In these states, the polls are too close to call.\par \par \uc2 Harris has an 8% lead among those who have already voted, while Trump is ahead among those who say they are very likely to vote but have not yet done so. The poll, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/11/03/us/politics/harris-trump-times-siena-poll.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 from the New York Times and Siena College}}}\uc2 , also found Harris was slightly ahead in Nevada, North Carolina and Wisconsin, with Trump up in Arizona and the other three too close to call.\par \par \uc2 Many Democrats are worried Trump is setting the stage for a series of legal challenges to poll results, in a sign the former president thinks Harris may win on election day tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/03/presidential-polls-today-donald-trump-kamala-harris-election-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 US presidential polls tracker: Trump v Harris latest national averages}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump begin blitz of rallies across battleground states on election day eve\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s continuing coverage of the 2024 US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris and Donald Trump will begin a blitz of rallies and media appearances across the vital battleground states in the rust belt, as the final day of campaigning gets under way.\par \par \uc2 Harris is set to appear in the Pennsylvania cities of Allentown, Pittsburgh and Philadelphia, in a sign of how crucial the state will be to securing victory. Trump will start his day in North Carolina before making appearances in Pennsylvania and Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Opinion polls show the pair locked in a tight race. More than 78m Americans have already voted, according to the University of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Election Lab, approaching half the total 160 million votes cast in 2020, in which US voter turnout was the highest in more than a century.\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the latest developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris pledged to \u8220\'20\'1Cdo everything in my power to end the war in Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/kamala-harris-michigan-arab-muslim-americans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her final rally}}}\uc2  in Michigan on Sunday, as she attempted to appeal to the state\u8217\'20\'19s large Arab American and Muslim American population two days out from the election. Michigan is home to about 240,000 registered Muslim voters, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/election-muslim-voters-michigan-kamala-harris-donald-trump-1966507"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a majority}}}\uc2  of whom voted for Joe Biden in 2020, helping him to a narrow victory over Donald Trump. But Arab Americans and Muslim Americans in the state have expressed dissatisfaction over the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s stance on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war on Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris was making her fourth stop of the day in Michigan, having earlier spoken at a church in Detroit and stopped by a barber shop in Pontiac. Trump is holding his final rally of the campaign in Michigan on Monday night.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/trump-election-pennsylvania-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he should never have left the White House}}}\uc2  after his defeat in 2020 and joked darkly he would be fine with reporters getting shot. \u8220\'20\'1CWe had the safest border in the history of our country the day that I left,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said at a rally in Lititz, Pennsylvania. \u8220\'20\'1CI shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have left, I mean honestly, we did so well, we had such a great \u8211\'20\'13 \u8221\'20\'1D he said before abruptly cutting himself off. In other comments, as he denigrated the media, he said: \u8220\'20\'1CTo get to me, somebody would have to shoot through fake news, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t mind that much, because, I don\u8217\'20\'19t mind. I don\u8217\'20\'19t mind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump again suggested {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/nov/03/donald-trump-kamala-harris-iowa-poll-us-presidential-election-live?page=with:block-67281d978f0869c6d52e58d1#block-67281d978f0869c6d52e58d1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he would give a role on health policy}}}\uc2  to Robert F Kennedy Jr at a rally in Macon, Georgia. \u8220\'20\'1CI told a great guy, RFK Jr., Bobby \u8212\'20\'14 I said, \u8216\'20\'18Bobby, you work on women\u8217\'20\'19s health, you work on health, you work on what we eat. You work on pesticides. You work on everything,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. Kennedy, a well known vaccine sceptic, on Saturday said that the former president would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/31/election-trump-immigration-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 push to remove fluoride from drinking water}}}\uc2  on his first day in office if elected.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/kamala-harris-proposition-36-drug-theft-crimes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dodged a question}}}\uc2  on whether she voted for California\u8217\'20\'19s Proposition 36, which would make it easier for prosecutors to send repeat shoplifters and drug users to jail or prison, after submitting her ballot. The measure would roll back provisions of Proposition 47, which downgraded low-level thefts and drug possession to misdemeanors.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign claimed that recent polling by the New York Times and the Des Moines Register is designed to suppress Trump voter turnout by presenting a bleak picture of his re-election prospects. The memo claims that the Times\u8217\'20\'19s polls have biased samples and overrepresent Democratic voters compared with actual voter registration and turnout trends.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/03/trump-harris-iowa-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also disputed}}}\uc2  a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/harris-unexpected-lead-over-trump-iowa-selzer-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shock Iowa poll}}}\uc2  that found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  leading the former president in the typically red state 47% to 44%. \u8220\'20\'1CNo President has done more for farmers, and the Great State of Iowa, than Donald J. Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in a post on the Truth Social network on Sunday morning. \u8220\'20\'1CIn fact, it\u8217\'20\'19s not even close! All polls, except for one heavily skewed toward the Democrats by a Trump hater who called it totally wrong the last time, have me up, by a lot\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241104ekb4000uv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
