\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US politics live: Women\u8217\'20\'19s marches hit the streets in support of Harris as both candidates target east coast \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell (now) and Tom Ambrose (earlier) \par \uc2 12,856 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 November 2024\par 01:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Harris leading Trump in new Iowa poll in startling reversal, pulling ahead of Trump 47% to 44%\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Thanks for joining us today. This has been Cecilia Nowell reporting on the latest US elections headlines this Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a summary of the day:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In a startling reversal, a Des Moines Register/Mediacom Iowa poll shows \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  ahead of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  47% to 44% among likely voters as the presidential race comes down to its final days.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Vaccine skeptic \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 who was recently reported to be up for a role in US health and food safety in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration \u8211\'20\'13 said in a social media post that he would remove fluoride from all public water if Trump wins the election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump criss-crossed the country today, as both candidates tried to drum up support in the final weekend ahead of the presidential election. Both candidates began the day in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, before Harris departed for Atlanta and then Charlotte, North Carolina. Trump also traveled to North Carolina, before heading to a rally in Virginia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Both candidates\u8217\'20\'19 running mates appeared at events in Nevada and Arizona. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  knocked on doors in Henderson, Nevada, before speaking alongside Indigenous leaders in Flagstaff and then courting Latino voters in Tucson. Meanwhile, JD Vance spoke in Las Vegas before heading to a gun store in Scottsdale.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Americans took to the streets in cities across the country for a day of women\u8217\'20\'19s marches. Marches were planned in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.womensmarch.com/newsroom/there-are-438-marches-happening-tomorrow-find-the-one-closest-to-you"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all 50 states}}}\uc2  for the eighth annual gathering, which began the day after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was inaugurated in 2017.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  spoke at a carpenters\u8217\'20\'19 union in his hometown of Scranton, Pennsylvania, where he was joined by his granddaughter, a sophomore at the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The national guard is on standby in at least three states \u8211\'20\'13 Washington, Oregon and Nevada \u8211\'20\'13 and Washington DC as the election approaches, as fears of civil unrest grow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A record number of wealthy Americans are planning to leave the country as election day approaches, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/business/personal-finance/record-numbers-wealthy-americans-are-making-plans-leave-us-election-rcna178450"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2  reports, citing fears that the election could spur political and social unrest regardless of its outcome.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 In Tucson, Arizona, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  has pulled out his \u8220\'20\'1Cmind your own damn business\u8221\'20\'1D mantra again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis guy is not \uc2 John McCain\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Republican party,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, referring to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies. \u8220\'20\'1CHe means government should have the freedom to be in your exam room, to be in your bedroom, to tell you what books to read and make those decisions. If they just mind their own damn business, we\u8217\'20\'19ll mind our own damn business and we\u8217\'20\'19ll all be better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris now leads Trump in new Iowa poll\par \par \uc2 The latest Des Moines Register/Mediacom Iowa poll shows \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  leading \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a startling reversal for political analysts who had all but written off the state as a win for Republicans.\par \par \uc2 The poll shows Harris ahead of Trump 47% to 44% among likely voters as the presidential race comes down to its final days.\par \par \uc2 enltrIowa Poll: \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  pulls ahead in state \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won twice\par \par \uc2 This is a stunning poll. But Ann Seltzer has as stellar a record as any pollster of forecasting election outcomes in her state.\par \par \uc2 Women are powering this surge. Portents for the country?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CNJfcQKXja"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/CNJfcQKXja}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 David Axelrod (@davidaxelrod) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/davidaxelrod/status/1852855309208875098?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s hard for anybody to say they saw this coming,\u8221\'20\'1D pollster \uc2 J Ann Selzer\uc2 , president of Selzer & Co, said to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/iowa-poll/2024/11/02/iowa-poll-kamala-harris-leads-donald-trump-2024-presidential-race/75354033007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Des Moines Register}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CShe has clearly leaped into a leading position.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The poll of 808 likely Iowa voters, which include those who have already voted as well as those who say they definitely plan to vote, was conducted by Selzer & Co from 28-31 October. It has a margin of error of plus or minus 3.4 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  has taken the stage at a rally in Montgomery county in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 She was preceded by musician Alicia Keys, who encouraged the crowd to keep fighting for feminist causes. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not some dystopian \uc2 Netflix\uc2  show I\u8217\'20\'19m talking about. This is the platform the other side is running on. They want to turn back the clock,\u8221\'20\'1D Keys said, hinting at the points in Project 2025.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  is campaigning again for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  this afternoon alongside singer Alicia Keys at an event in Norristown, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m excited to be back out on the campaign trail for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  !\par \par \uc2 Today, I\u8217\'20\'19ll be with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aliciakeys?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @AliciaKeys}}}\uc2  in Norristown, Pennsylvania, making my closing argument about why this election is so important to the progress we seek. With only three days left, we\u8217\'20\'19ve all got to organize,\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qZEoeNkuRt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qZEoeNkuRt}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  (@MichelleObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MichelleObama/status/1852791820805132771?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, supporters were gathered outside the local high school where Obama will appear.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe line to see \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  campaigning for VP Harris snakes around the lot and a field in Norristown, PA. Event itself is taking place in a HS gym {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/U6Kghr9Uah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/U6Kghr9Uah}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sarah Ewall-Wice (@EwallWice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/EwallWice/status/1852819233635271080?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump has wrapped up his speech in Salem, Virginia, in his usual manner, reciting his Maga chants that have come to mark the ends of his rallies: \u8220\'20\'1CWe will make America great again \u8230\'20\'26 we will make America strong again!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This time, he has pointedly added a new chant before leaving the stage: \u8220\'20\'1CWe will make America healthy again!\u8221\'20\'1D, perhaps in reference to recent reports that \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  could assume some control over US health and food safety in a second Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 According to the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , Kennedy has met with Trump transition officials to help draw up an agenda for a new administration and could take a broad \u8220\'20\'1Chealth tsar\u8221\'20\'1D position that would not require confirmation by the Senate.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  has made his fifth visit to Arizona for a final campaign pitch for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as the US 2024 presidential race enters its final days.\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump are locked in a fierce battle for the swing state and have made several trips to court voters. According to the website FiveThirtyEight, Trump leads Harris by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/president-general/2024/arizona/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2.2 points}}}\uc2  in the state. More than 1.2 million Arizonans have already cast their ballots in this election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As the candidates continue a busy day of events, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  are still expected to make at least one more appearance each this evening. Trump is returning to North Carolina, where he\u8217\'20\'19ll speak at a rally in Greensboro at 7.30pm ET while Walz heads to Tucson, Arizona.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr vows to remove fluoride from public water\par \par \uc2 In a post on X, \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  has said that he would remove fluoride from all public water if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is elected and gives him responsibility over the nation\u8217\'20\'19s health agencies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFluoride is an industrial waste associated with arthritis, bone fractures, bone cancer, IQ loss, neurodevelopmental disorders, and thyroid disease,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy wrote.\par \par \uc2 enltrOn January 20, the Trump White House will advise all U.S?. water systems to remove fluoride from public water. Fluoride is an industrial waste associated with arthritis, bone fractures, bone cancer, IQ loss, neurodevelopmental disorders, and thyroid disease. President\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Robert F. Kennedy Jr\uc2  (@RobertKennedyJr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RobertKennedyJr/status/1852812012478398923?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Although fluoride is associated with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/society/article/2024/aug/23/fluoride-water-study"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some health issues}}}\uc2 , dentists strongly recommend adding it to public water to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2016/sep/14/fluoride-in-water-safe-tooth-decay-iq-cancer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prevent tooth decay}}}\uc2 . Fluoride is naturally occurring in drinking water at varying levels.\par \par \uc2 US district judge \uc2 Edward Chen{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.courtlistener.com/docket/6201332/445/food-water-watch-inc-v-environmental-protection-agency/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruled}}}\uc2  on 24 September that the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  must take action regarding fluoride in drinking water, claiming his finding does not \u8220\'20\'1Cconclude with certainty\u8221\'20\'1D any harmful effects but that there is evidence of the risk of cognitive decline.\par \par \uc2 The ruling stems from an August {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ntp.niehs.nih.gov/publications/monographs/mgraph08"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from the Department of Health and Human Service\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 National Toxicology Program\uc2 , which found that drinking water that contained more than twice the recommended limit of fluoride was \u8220\'20\'1Cconsistently associated\u8221\'20\'1D with lower IQ in children.\par \par \uc2 Despite this ruling, the \uc2 American Dental Association\uc2  said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adanews.ada.org/ada-news/2024/september/judge-orders-epa-to-address-impacts-of-fluoride-in-drinking-water/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  in September that it remains \u8220\'20\'1Cstaunchly in support\u8221\'20\'1D of adding fluoride to community drinking water to help prevent tooth decay.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking to the crowd in Virginia, Trump is once again fixated on his hair. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m having a bad hair day! I have to have a bad hair day in front of Virginia? That\u8217\'20\'19s not good,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, turning around presumably to look into a monitor that shows the back of his head.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s hair \u8211\'20\'13 and his appearance, in general \u8211\'20\'13 has lately become a standard talking point during his long and rambling campaign speeches \u8211\'20\'13 although he insists he does not ramble but employs a style of speech he calls \u8220\'20\'1Cthe weave\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has implied that elections are rigged in blue states such as California and New York, falsely claiming that election officials will be executed if they ask to see voter ID.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we had an honest election in California, we would win California,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking at his rally in Salem, Virginia, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has denounced a trans woman who was allowed to join \uc2 Roanoke College\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s women\u8217\'20\'19s swim team last year. He said that seven members of the college\u8217\'20\'19s swim team had joined him backstage, before welcoming the teammates to the stage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  have advocated for and pushed for this anti-woman sex-based discrimination to continue all over this country,\u8221\'20\'1D swimmer Lily Mullens said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are so lucky to have a leader like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with common sense,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, thanking the ex-president for \u8220\'20\'1Cstanding with women\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  takes the stage at a rally in Virginia\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has taken the stage at his second rally of the day, this time in Salem, Virginia \u8211\'20\'13 a state that his rival \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is leading by a wide margin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe win Virginia, we win the whole thing without question,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very possible that without winning Virginia we\u8217\'20\'19re going to win the whole thing too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump was introduced by Virginia governor \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2 , who led attendees in a prayer before the ex-president began speaking.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Campaigning in Scottsdale, Arizona, JD Vance has called on voters to \u8220\'20\'1Cmake this thing too big to rig \u8221\'20\'1D. He focused much of his remarks on immigration, an issue that is central to many Arizona voters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In a new video, actor Harrison Ford has endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook, I\u8217\'20\'19ve been voting for 64 years. Never wanted to talk about it very much,\u8221\'20\'1D Ford said, before referencing the former Trump administration officials who\u8217\'20\'19ve denounced the ex-president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve got one vote \u8211\'20\'13 same as anyone else \u8211\'20\'13 and I\u8217\'20\'19m going to use it to move forward. I\u8217\'20\'19m going to vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWATCH >> Harrison Ford lays it out\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe truth is this, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will protect your right to disagree with her about policies or ideas, and then, as we have done for centuries, we\u8217\'20\'19ll debate them. We\u8217\'20\'19ll work on them together, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll move forward.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/8jsWg3Z655"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/8jsWg3Z655}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 James Singer (@Jemsinger) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Jemsinger/status/1852798584766541840?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump Jr\uc2  has concluded speaking ahead of JD Vance in Scottsdale, Arizona. In his remarks, the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s son echoed misinformation his father has spread regarding Fema relief efforts following hurricanes Helene and Milton, Haitian immigrants, \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  and the media. He also implied that Democrats had tried to assassinate his father in July, and encouraged attendees to make sure their friends voted Republican down-ballot.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 rally in Charlotte, North Carolina has otherwise proceeded much like her other campaign events, with the vice-president delivering a familiar version of her stump speech. She\u8217\'20\'19s encouraged attendees to make a plan for voting if they haven\u8217\'20\'19t done so already.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need everyone to vote, North Carolina. You all will make the difference in this election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 JD Vance is currently campaigning at a gun store in Scottsdale, Arizona alongside \uc2 Donald Trump Jr.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the opportunity to put not just my father in the White House, but have you seen the team around him,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said from the stage at Dillon Precision, touting roles his father has promised \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrThe scene here in Scottsdale, Arizona where JD Vance and Don Jr are set to speak to several hundred fans and make a final pitch to voters in this crucial swing state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UOz6ykWu5h"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UOz6ykWu5h}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Christal Hayes (@Journo_Christal) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Journo_Christal/status/1852792614166180263?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pro-Palestine protestors interrupt Harris's rally in Charlotte\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Charlotte was briefly interrupted by pro-Palestine protestors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of the reasons we are here is because we are fighting for a democracy, and the right of people to speak their mind, but right now I am speaking,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CDemocracy can be complicated, it\u8217\'20\'19s all right. This is what democracy looks like.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSeveral protestors just escorted out of the Harris rally here yelling "STOP BOMBING ISRAEL."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kellie Meyer (@KellieMeyerNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KellieMeyerNews/status/1852817720984629346?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is speaking at her second rally of the day, this time in Charlotte, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of her appearance, Roy Cooper, the state\u8217\'20\'19s governor, urged Republicans and independents to vote for the vice-president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CListen to the ultraconservative, well-respected leaders who worked with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Cooper said, referencing longtime Republicans like \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  who\u8217\'20\'19ve endorsed Harris. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is a danger to our country, and he should never be president again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 National guard on standby across the country \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Preparing for potential social unrest ahead of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election, the national guard is on standby in at least three states and Washington DC, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 In Washington, governor \uc2 Jay Inslee\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://governor.wa.gov/news/2024/inslee-activates-some-washington-national-guard-members-support-public-safety-activities-related"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that the national guard is on standby following recent ballot box fires there. Meanwhile, in neighboring Oregon, governor Tina Kotek {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ktvz.com/news/crime-courts/2024/11/01/portland-police-gear-up-for-potential-election-violence-and-national-guard-on-standby/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  the national guard is prepared to respond to potential uncertainty, following another ballot box fire in Portland. And in Nevada, governor Joe Lombardo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gov.nv.gov/Newsroom/PRs/2024/2024-10-28_election-preparedness-update/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  60 troops are prepared to oversee a \u8220\'20\'1Csafe and smooth election day\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, law enforcement is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JabcdbOJWZc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 preparing}}}\uc2  for election day in Washington DC, where more than 3,000 police officers will work in 12-hour shifts.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is campaigning this afternoon in Flagstaff, Arizona, alongside interior secretary \uc2 Deb Haaland\uc2 . The city, which is located just outside the borders of the Navajo Nation, is also home to \uc2 Northern Arizona University\uc2 . Walz, whose lieutenant governor, Peggy Flanagan, will become the first female Indigenous governor in the United States if he and Harris are elected Tuesday, has focused many of his campaign stops on Native voters in Arizona, including by visiting the capital of the Navajo Nation last week.\par \par \uc2 enltrReady to rally in Flagstaff!\par \par \uc2 Take a look at this crowd of folks ready to vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2 , \uc2 Jonathan Nez\uc2 , and Dems across the ballot!\par \par \uc2 Tune in: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vglBV9mjLQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/vglBV9mjLQ}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EgVX7tKe6M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EgVX7tKe6M}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Deb Haaland\uc2  (@DebHaalandNM) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DebHaalandNM/status/1852804311224602947?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Speaking ahead of Walz, Haaland evoked her childhood growing up in a pueblo household and encouraged attendees to \u8220\'20\'1Cas Coach would say, leave it all on the field\u8221\'20\'1D. Navajo Nation president \uc2 Jonathan Nez\uc2  was also in attendance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe sovereignty of our Indigenous tribes is paramount,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said, noting his recent visit to Window Rock, Arizona, before encouraging voters to get to the polls. \u8220\'20\'1CWe get to shape not just the next four years, but generations to come.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Women's march begins in Washington DC\par \par \uc2 As the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March in Washington DC kicks off, women and supporters are gathering across the country in the 8th annual march since the 21 January 2017 march spurred by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s inauguration and the Access Hollywood tapes.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest from around the country:\par \par \uc2 enltrHuge crowd for the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March on Freedom Plaza {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QFj1gBNWde"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/QFj1gBNWde}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joe Flood (@joeflood) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joeflood/status/1852792730059202801?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWaiting for the Monroe (MI) Marches Forward Women's March to start! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DemCastMI?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DemCastMI}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/WomensMarch?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #WomensMarch}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NotGoingBack?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NotGoingBack}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/YesWeKam?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #YesWeKam}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UqfD1IlDLA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UqfD1IlDLA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jill ??????? #DemCastMI (@WhitchMI) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhitchMI/status/1852778747931295855?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going back!!! Had a great time at the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March in Tuscaloosa rallying to get out the vote. Great to meet this future voter who knows what's possible when we as women and girls use our power! ??? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/E3BGH9roJa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/E3BGH9roJa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Terri A. Sewell\uc2  (@Sewell4Congress) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Sewell4Congress/status/1852797051760763225?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrAt the Women\u8217\'20\'19s March in Boston {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jsWhkLq0eK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jsWhkLq0eK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aline Boucher Kaplan (@AlineKaplan) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AlineKaplan/status/1852772631231008923?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 After starting the morning side by side on the tarmac in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s planes are now lined up once again in Charlotte, North Carolina. Both candidates are criss-crossing the country in a final blitz of campaign stops before Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 enltrAir Force Two and Trump Force One are seen on the tarmac in Charlotte, NC. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RCI5UQRjsG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/RCI5UQRjsG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Doug Mills\uc2  (@dougmillsnyt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dougmillsnyt/status/1852796622964433384?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrGood morning from the Milwaukee airport, where Trump\u8217\'20\'19s plane and Air Force Two are parked quite close to each other on the tarmac {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/omp3kOVdkh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/omp3kOVdkh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kate Sullivan (@KateSullivanDC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KateSullivanDC/status/1852689252179493326?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Visiting the carpenter\u8217\'20\'19s union in Scranton this afternoon, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  used some of the unvarnished language that has come to endear him to many Americans (and gotten him in some hot water lately).\par \par \uc2 Speaking about Republicans who want to repeal the Affordable Care Act and the Chips Act, as well as cut social security, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CThese are the kinds of guys you like to smack in the ass,\u8221\'20\'1D according to a White House pool report.\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2 , back at the Carpenters Hall in Scranton, warns GOP wants to repeal the ACA & CHIPS, cut Social Security so they can cut taxes for wealthy again. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are the kinds of guys you like to smack in the ass.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/waBLjnXuWc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/waBLjnXuWc}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mike Memoli (@mikememoli) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/mikememoli/status/1852767425122513286?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 This week, Florida will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/election-abortion-ballot-measures-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 one of 10 states}}}\uc2  where voters will weigh in on measures to expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. The debate in Florida \u8211\'20\'13 which has turned from purple to red in recent years \u8211\'20\'13 has been particularly intense as Republican party leadership campaigns against Amendment 4.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Carter Sherman with more:\par \par \uc2 As she stood in the parking lot of an auto supply store on Friday evening, Brittany Robinson was practically vibrating. With just a few days left before the 2024 presidential election, the 32-year-old Floridian needed an outlet for her anxiety.\par \par \uc2 So Robinson decided to go knock on strangers\u8217\'20\'19 doors in support of Amendment 4, a ballot measure that, if passed, would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into Florida\u8217\'20\'19s constitution and overturn the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wish I started earlier,\u8221\'20\'1D said Robinson, a native of the Tampa Bay area who had never before canvassed for a political campaign. Living under Florida\u8217\'20\'19s ban, she said, is \u8220\'20\'1Cterrifying\u8221\'20\'1D. When she was a freshman in college 13 years ago, Robinson discovered she was seven weeks pregnant and had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  a week later.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have been able to do that now,\u8221\'20\'1D Robinson said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/florida-amendment-4-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I try not to get my hopes up\u8217\'20\'19: campaigners make final push to save \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights in Florida}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Marches planned as presidential candidates make final push to earn women's votes\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  make their closing arguments ahead of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s election, Americans are preparing to take to the streets in cities across the country for a day of Women\u8217\'20\'19s marches. Marches are planned in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.womensmarch.com/newsroom/there-are-438-marches-happening-tomorrow-find-the-one-closest-to-you"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all 50 states}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNo matter where you\u8217\'20\'19re voting, we are in a choice between freedom and fascism,\u8221\'20\'1D Rachel O\u8217\'20\'19Leary Carmona, executive director of Women\u8217\'20\'19s March, told ABC News Live today.\par \par \uc2 enltrWomen's March protesters will rally in Washington, D.C. at 4 p.m. today, voicing support for VP \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "No matter where you're voting, we are in a choice between freedom and fascism," Women's March executive director Rachel O'Leary Carmona says. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IDTA54rzqW"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IDTA54rzqW}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ABC News Live (@ABCNewsLive) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABCNewsLive/status/1852754559111700853?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump have taken different approaches to earning female voters\u8217\'20\'19 support, with Harris campaigning largely on issues of reproductive freedom and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, while Trump says he will be a \u8220\'20\'1Cprotector\u8221\'20\'1D of women.\par \par \uc2 Here are some photos from marches across the country \u8211\'20\'13 we\u8217\'20\'19ll keep you updated on any developments as the largest march in Washington DC kicks off:\par \par \uc2 enltrWaiting for the Monroe (MI) Marches Forward Women's March to start! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DemCastMI?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DemCastMI}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/WomensMarch?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #WomensMarch}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/NotGoingBack?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #NotGoingBack}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/YesWeKam?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #YesWeKam}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UqfD1IlDLA"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UqfD1IlDLA}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jill ??????? #DemCastMI (@WhitchMI) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhitchMI/status/1852778747931295855?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrPlymouth MA Women\u8217\'20\'19s March visibility on Saturday. Nov. 2 in support of women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Harris?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Harris}}}\uc2  /Walz and down ballot Democrats, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/OncxTmMk2u"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/OncxTmMk2u}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ??Tracy on Thee MTA ???????????? ?? (@SeelyeTracy) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SeelyeTracy/status/1852755748649947584?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrGreat turnout for the women's rights rally and march in New Milford today! Thanks to the organizers and to all who came out! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/H4HlkJC1lj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/H4HlkJC1lj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Justin Potter for State Senate (@justinpotter24) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/justinpotter24/status/1852776926919999630?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In the final days of the election, Taylor Swift\u8217\'20\'19s fans are trying to get out the vote among \u8220\'20\'1Clow propensity Swiftie voters across Pennsylvania \u8221\'20\'1D. The pop star {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-endorses-kamala-harris-president-us-debate-cat-lady"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed}}}\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  shortly after the September presidential debate.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Swifties4Kamala?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Swifties4Kamala}}}\uc2  has launched its first-ever targeted fandom mail program to turn out low propensity Swiftie voters across Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Potential voters across PA have started receiving these in their mailboxes over the past few weeks. ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zeCkNsuGmd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zeCkNsuGmd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Annie Wu (all socials: @annie_wu_22) (@Annie_Wu_22) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Annie_Wu_22/status/1852728693765894604?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSwifties for Kamala (S4K) sent over 250,000 mail pieces encouraging Pennsylvania voters to vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for President and take a pledge to vote. Included in 50,000 of the mailers was an exclusive \u8216\'20\'18Voting Era\u8217\'20\'19 friendship bracelet,\u8221\'20\'1D the press release reads. \u8220\'20\'1CAs of this release, over 4,600 pledges to vote have been submitted because of the mailer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FBI\uc2  is working to dispel misinformation about the election, saying today that two videos circulating on social media are false. One claims that the bureau had \u8220\'20\'1Capprehended three linked groups committing ballot fraud\u8221\'20\'1D and another concerns second gentleman Doug Emhoff.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese videos are not authentic, are not from the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , and the content they depict is false,\u8221\'20\'1D the \uc2 FBI\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 etltrFBI Statement on False Videos. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UJzjDLd8p2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/UJzjDLd8p2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 FBI\uc2  (@\uc2 FBI\uc2 ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FBI/status/1852743285711761791?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  campaign on the east coast today, their running mates are hosting events out west.\par \par \uc2 JD Vance spoke at a rally in Las Vegas this morning while \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  campaigned in Henderson, Nevada. This afternoon, both candidates will travel to Arizona, where Vance will speak in Scottsdale and Walz will attend events in Flagstaff and Tucson.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking in Atlanta this afternoon, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  delivered a familiar version of her stump speech, addressing the future of the Affordable Care Act, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s proposed tariffs, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and contraception, Project 2025 and bipartisanship.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI pledge to you to listen to experts and to listen to people who disagree with me, because unlike \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that people who disagree with me are the enemy,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe wants to put them in jail, I will give them a seat at the table. That\u8217\'20\'19s what real leaders do. That\u8217\'20\'19s what strong leaders do.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI pledge to you to always put country above party and self and I pledge to you to be a president for all Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris will speak again in North Carolina later this afternoon \u8211\'20\'13 where Trump is currently holding a rally.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Jen O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon\uc2 , chair of the Harris-Walz campaign, said the team was \u8220\'20\'1Cfeeling very good about where we are right now\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She pointed to the release of a new ad that draws from Harris\u8217\'20\'19s interactions with voters she met on the trail during her 100-day campaign, as an opportunity to create a \u8220\'20\'1Chigh impact moment\u8221\'20\'1D in the final days of the election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are continuing to operate on this very broad map of the battleground states, where all seven of our battleground states are within the margin of error, completely in play,\u8221\'20\'1D she told reporters on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon repeated what the campaign has been saying for days, that late-deciding voters have been \u8220\'20\'1Cbreaking\u8221\'20\'1D decisively in Harris\u8217\'20\'19s favor. Her campaign has pointed to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vitriol-filled \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally as a key factor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese undecided voters, we believe, over the course of the last week, have been breaking in our direction,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The campaign also said that Harris was planning to vote by mail but were not sure if she had submitted her ballot yet.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has been introduced by Justin Martinez Posadas, a first-time voter and high school senior, at her Atlanta rally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m the son of a factory worker and the child of immigrants. Vice-President Harris is the daughter of a single mother from a middle-class family,\u8221\'20\'1D Martinez Posadas said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why I was honored to cast my first ever ballot for Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D He added that his grandparents, who recently became US citizens, also cast their first ballots for Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is speaking in his home town of Scranton, Pennsylvania, where he has been joined by his granddaughter Natalie, who is a sophomore at the \uc2 University of Pennsylvania\uc2  and the daughter of his deceased son, Beau.\par \par \uc2 Addressing members of the carpenters union, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of politicians have trouble saying the word union, but I\u8217\'20\'19m not one of them.\u8221\'20\'1D Following a chorus of cheers, the president added: \u8220\'20\'1CBy the way, neither does Kamala.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump addresses North Carolina as Harris prepares to take stage in Atlanta\par \par \uc2 Director Spike Lee and Georgia senator \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2  have begun speaking at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Atlanta, as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  addresses supporters at a rally in Gastonia, North Carolina .\par \par \uc2 Tapping into current fears that there will be voter suppression in this election, Ossoff told attendees in Atlanta: \u8220\'20\'1C[Trump] tried to throw out your votes. You all remember the phone call.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know what has been given for the struggle for voting rights in the state of Georgia, and across the American south,\u8221\'20\'1D Ossoff added.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Trump is speaking about the support he\u8217\'20\'19s received from customs and border patrol agents (saying agents have told him \u8220\'20\'1Che\u8217\'20\'19s the greatest president in the history of our country\u8221\'20\'1D), the economy and the election (\u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re just three days away from the greatest political victory in world history\u8221\'20\'1D).\par \par \uc2 JD Vance is expected to begin speaking soon in Las Vegas, Nevada, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will be addressing a carpenters union in his home town of Scranton, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign has released a new closing ad titled \u8220\'20\'1CBrighter Future\u8221\'20\'1D that will air tomorrow afternoon during \uc2 NFL\uc2  games on \uc2 CBS\uc2  and Fox. In the two-minute ad, Harris pledges to be \u8220\'20\'1Ca president for all Americans\u8221\'20\'1D and promises to \u8220\'20\'1Cbuild a brighter future for our nation\u8221\'20\'1D as her campaign seeks to draw out the differences between the vice-president and her opponent in the final days of the election cycle.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Michigan congresswoman \uc2 Rashida Tlaib\uc2  declined to endorse \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at a \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  rally yesterday. The only Palestinian American in Congress, Tlaib has criticized the Biden-Harris administration\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the war in Gaza. Her non-endorsement comes as a voter survey published on Friday suggested that 43% of Muslim American voters support the Green party candidate, Jill Stein.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  with more on Tlaib:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/rashida-tlaib-decline-endorsement-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan congresswoman Rashida Tlaib declines to endorse Kamala Harris}}}\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/erum-salam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Erum Salam}}}\uc2  with more on the Arab and Muslim Americans campaigning for Harris despite the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/arab-muslim-americans-vote-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18It can get worse\u8217\'20\'19: Arab and Muslim Americans make final push for Harris}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As election day approaches, state and federal officials are preparing for social unrest and political upheaval that could suppress votes. Yesterday, the justice department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/justice-department-monitor-polls-27-states-compliance-federal-voting-rights-laws"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  it will send election monitors to 86 jurisdictions, the most in two decades. Meanwhile, Washington state governor \uc2 Jay Inslee{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://governor.wa.gov/news/2024/inslee-activates-some-washington-national-guard-members-support-public-safety-activities-related"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  that the state will put national guard members on standby this week to support law enforcement and protect key infrastructure in the event of social unrest. The Washington state announcement comes just days after someone set fire to a ballot drop box there and in neighboring Portland, Oregon, damaging hundreds of ballots.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign struggled to balance chaos and discipline - report\par \par \uc2 A deep dive inside \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign published today in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2024/11/trump-2024-campaign-lewandowski-conway/680456/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Atlantic}}}\uc2  shows how the ex-president has struggled to balance his chaotic tendencies with running a disciplined campaign. The report notes that after \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  replaced \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on the Democratic ticket, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s advisers encouraged him to stick to planned criticism of the Biden-Harris administration while the ex-president instead longed to attack Harris personally. As a result, Trump began communicating with two of his 2016 campaign managers, Kellyanne Conway and \uc2 Corey Lewandowski\uc2 , citing fears that he was being overly \u8220\'20\'1Cmanaged\u8221\'20\'1D by his current advisors.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW \u8212\'20\'14 and several months in the making \u8212\'20\'14 my final look beneath the hood of Trump 2024.\par \par \uc2 Pour a cup of coffee and find a comfy chair.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInside the Ruthless, Restless Final Days of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Campaign\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aWTijBQqH4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/aWTijBQqH4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tim Alberta (@TimAlberta) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TimAlberta/status/1852690274767581245?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The report includes two other notable asides: Trump wanted to start calling the current president \u8220\'20\'1CRetarded \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D but was dissuaded by current aides, and broke ties with far-right activist Laura Loomer when he learned she\u8217\'20\'19d had significant plastic surgery.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has filed a complaint against the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  with the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2 , alleging that the paper made illegal in-kind contributions to the Harris-Walz campaign through its advertising, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/style/media/2024/11/01/donald-trump-campaign-violations-washington-post-advertising-fec-complaint/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Post reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A copy of the complaint released by the Trump campaign cites a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/10/30/2024/washington-post-pays-to-boost-stories-critical-of-trump-as-subscribers-flee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Semafor}}}\uc2  article that suggests the Post purchased ads to increase readership of articles it had published that were critical of the ex-president \u8211\'20\'13 after the newspaper\u8217\'20\'19s announcement that it would not endorse a candidate sparked backlash and a wave of unsubscriptions.\par \par \uc2 In the complaint, the Trump campaign calls the advertising a \u8220\'20\'1Cdark money corporate campaign in opposition to President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. In response, a \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  spokesperson said the allegations were \u8220\'20\'1Cwithout merit\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Cpromoted posts across social media platforms reflect high-performing content across all verticals and subjects\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A rally for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is filling Atlanta Civic Center on Saturday, \u8220\'20\'1Cthree days before we remind the world that the south has something to say \u8221\'20\'1D, said U S representative \uc2 Nikema Williams\uc2 , quoting the iconic Atlanta hip -hop group Out Kast.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis election is too important to sit out,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is battleground Georgia.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Just over 4 million Georgia voters have already cast a ballot, about 80% of the 2020 figure and 55.3% of registered voters in the state, according to the Georgia secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office. Fulton and DeKalb counties, the two counties with the largest number of Democratic voters in Georgia, are slightly ahead of state averages for early turnout, but the election remains too close to call judging by early voting turnout. Errors in polling models are likely to be larger than the ultimate margin.\par \par \uc2 Harris is expected to appear at 1pm. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  today announced a rally in Macon for Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Morehouse College graduate Spike Lee and recording artist Pastor Troy opened the rally, with Troy performing Vice Versa.\par \par \uc2 enltrPastor Troy, performing Vice Versa at the Atlanta Civic Center rally for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ds3bhVpsYz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ds3bhVpsYz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 George Chidi (@neonflag) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/neonflag/status/1852734028140486979?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A record number of wealthy Americans are planning to leave the country as election day approaches, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/business/personal-finance/record-numbers-wealthy-americans-are-making-plans-leave-us-election-rcna178450"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2 , citing fears that the election could spur political and social unrest regardless of its outcome.\par \par \uc2 Immigration attorneys at high-powered firms such as Lesperance and Associates and Henley & Partners told NBC that they\u8217\'20\'19re seeing greater demand for services regarding possible moves overseas than ever before.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA survey by Arton Capital, which advises the wealthy on immigration programs, found that 53% of American millionaires say they\u8217\'20\'19re more likely to leave the US after the election, no matter who wins,\u8221\'20\'1D the outlet added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 President Biden is set to land in Scranton, the city where he was born, for a visit shortly and I spotted this truck parked on Biden street downtown.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis truck is parked on Biden Street in downtown Scranton this morning (President Biden is visiting the city today) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4M0gbQOILu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4M0gbQOILu}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1852727213025554793?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Scranton is a key piece in Democratic hopes to win Pennsylvania, a key battleground state this election. \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  lost tremendous ground here in 2016 when she lost the state, but \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  improved on that in 2020. Democrats are hoping to build even further on those gains this year, or at least not lose ground.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump grows anxious as election approaches\par \par \uc2 In the final days before the 2024 election, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is growing increasingly anxious, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/11/02/trump-anxiety-builds-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reports}}}\uc2 . Although the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign is projecting confidence, a campaign official close to Trump tells Axios that the ex-president is asking more questions about polling and demanding more work from his aides in late-night and early morning calls.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Trump is getting anxious, asking more questions and demanding more work from his aides. His restlessness is evident in late-night/early-morning calls in which he peppers aides w/ Qs on how things are going \u8212\'20\'14 and whether they think he'll win. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dDj57JWOr3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/dDj57JWOr3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sophia Cai (@SophiaCai99) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SophiaCai99/status/1852709244010647582?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Before heading to North Carolina today, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will rally voters in Atlanta alongside director Spike Lee, rapper Monica and singer Victoria Mon\u233\'00\'E9t. The vice-president will also be joined by senators \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2  and \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , and will be introduced by a first-time voter, according to the campaign.\par \par \uc2 Then Harris will head to Charlotte, North Carolina \u8211\'20\'13 a state that both she and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are visiting today. It\u8217\'20\'19s the fourth day in a row that both candidates will appear in the same state on the same day, as they attempt to swing through the most important battleground states one last time before Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 At Harris\u8217\'20\'19s rally in Charlotte, her campaign says, Harris will be joined by actor Kerry Washington and again introduced by a first-time voter. The event will also feature performances by Brittney Spencer, Jon Bon Jovi, Khalid and the War and Treaty.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Good morning, Cecilia Nowell here taking over from my colleague Tom Ambrose.\par \par \uc2 As the final weekend before election day gets under way, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  called into Fox & Friends Weekend to comment on the state of the race \u8211\'20\'13 and criticize a recent Harris campaign ad telling women they don\u8217\'20\'19t have to tell their husbands whom they vote for.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCan you imagine a wife not telling a husband who she\u8217\'20\'19s voting for? Did you ever hear anything like that? Even if you have a \u8230\'20\'26 bad relationship, you\u8217\'20\'19re going to tell your husband. That\u8217\'20\'19s a ridiculous ad. So stupid,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 During the call, Trump also critiqued \uc2 Mark Cuban\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s recent comments that the ex-president avoids \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong, intelligent women\u8221\'20\'1D, said he didn\u8217\'20\'19t know the comedian who made an offensive joke about Puerto Rico at the \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally last week and responded to concerns regarding his comments about shooting former congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He also shared that he has sued \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C60 Minutes\u8221\'20\'1D and thought the outlet should lose its broadcasting license.\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump explains on Fox & Friends that he's suing \uc2 CBS\uc2  and thinks their license should be taken away {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HaWdYMagyx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HaWdYMagyx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1852720368986861892?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 2, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democrat {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  head to North Carolina on Saturday to try to clinch support in the south-eastern battleground state just three days before Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s US presidential election. It will be the fourth day in a row that vice-president Harris and former president Trump visit the same state on the same day, underlining the critical importance of the seven states likely to decide the race, which opinion polls show to be on a knife\u8217\'20\'19s edge, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris}}}\uc2  battled to woo voters in the key swing states of Michigan and Wisconsin on Friday, as the presidential campaign enters its final stretch. Harris made several appearances in Wisconsin on Friday, including one that featured the musician Cardi B, while Trump visited both {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2  and Wisconsin. At his rally in Warren, Michigan, on Friday afternoon, Trump tried to energize his voters, delivering an address replete with his characteristic fear-mongering about immigrants and tangents including musings about his hair.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At a Wisconsin rally on Friday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  called \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Clow-IQ person\u8221\'20\'1D and vowed to save the economy \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom total obliteration\u8221\'20\'1D in a 1.5 hour-long meandering speech that touched on top campaign issues including the economy and foreign policy \u8211\'20\'13 but also featured threats to curb press freedoms and a lengthy discussion of his own rhetorical style. \u8220\'20\'1CI will stop the criminal invasion of this country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump during his opening remarks, promising to usher in a new \u8220\'20\'1Cgolden age\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CCan you imagine if Kamala won? You would go down to a 1929 style depression,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Top Republicans have called on the White House to produce all documents and internal communications regarding president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s statement earlier this week in which he appeared to take a swipe at supporters of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 . White House press officials altered the official transcript of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s statement, drawing objections from the federal workers who document such remarks for posterity, according to two \uc2 US government\uc2  officials and an internal email obtained on Thursday by the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The office of Arizona Democratic attorney general Kris Mayes is \u8220\'20\'1Clooking into\u8221\'20\'1D whether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  broke state law when he said on Thursday that \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  should face rifles \u8220\'20\'1Cshooting at her\u8221\'20\'1D to see how she feels about sending troops to fight. \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 Arizona attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office\uc2  is looking into whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments about \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  violated Arizona law,\u8221\'20\'1D Richie Taylor, communications director for the AG\u8217\'20\'19s office, said in a statement on Friday. \u8220\'20\'1CThe office has no additional comments to make at this time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Officials in the US battleground state of Michigan said they worry that the Democratic-leaning city of Warren could lag behind the rest of the state in reporting the results of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, raising early doubts about the state\u8217\'20\'19s vote count. Warren, unlike Detroit and most other cities in Michigan, opted not to take advantage of changes enacted in a 2022 state law allowing for up to eight days of pre-processing of absentee ballots, Reuters reported. Instead, the city of 135,000 people will wait until election day to verify and tabulate more than 20,000 mail-in ballots.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s troubled canvassing operation on behalf of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and the Republican party is now facing a lawsuit in southern California filed by two women who say they were cheated out of wages and expenses as they knocked on doors for an embattled Republican congresswoman. The suit accuses Musk\u8217\'20\'19s America PAC, which has poured more than $100m into this year\u8217\'20\'19s election campaign, of \u8220\'20\'1Cwillful violations of the California labor code\u8221\'20\'1D by paying the plaintiffs less than it promised and refusing to make up the difference.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US presidential election campaign enters its final weekend with polls showing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  in seemingly permanent deadlock and few clues as to which of them will prevail on Tuesday. At the end of another unruly week that began with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s racially charged rally in New York\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Guardian and was punctuated by celebrity endorsements, misogynistic comments and insults about \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D being levelled left and right, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s 10-day polling average tracker showed little change from seven days earlier, with voter loyalty to their chosen candidate appearing relatively impervious to campaign events, however seismic.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s all from me, Tom Ambrose, for today. My colleague Cecilia Nowell will be along shortly to continue bringing you all the latest from the US election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 On the second to last Sunday in July, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  had just finished making pancakes and bacon for her grandnieces at the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s residence in Washington, and was sitting down with them to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.siriusxm.com/blog/kamala-harris-howard-stern"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 work on}}}\uc2  a jigsaw puzzle when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  called.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI got up to take the call, and then life changed,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?app=desktop&v=pNbwMrBMGgE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recounted}}}\uc2  later. Biden, isolating with Covid at his vacation home in Rehoboth Beach, Delaware, and facing calls from all corners of his party to step aside, had reached the history-altering decision to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 end his bid}}}\uc2  for re-election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAre you sure?\u8221\'20\'1D Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/theviewabc/reel/DA3kYW2RKp2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  she asked the US president. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause what a big decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With Biden\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, Harris, still wearing her workout clothes and hooded sweatshirt from her alma mater, \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , leapt into action. Time was of the essence. Over the next 10 hours, with pizza boxes littered around her, she placed 100 calls to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  whose support she would need to secure the nomination.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/harris-election-final-pitch-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris pitches self as a unifier with a \u8216\'20\'18to-do list\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 is it enough for knife-edge race?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A year punctuated by two assassination attempts, high levels of threats and harassment, and a number of troubling, violent incidents in the lead-up to election day will culminate on Tuesday with an election deemed existential by all sides.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the first presidential election since the January 6 insurrection, a reminder of the ways political violence can manifest that leaves Americans with a fear that such an attack could happen again. Those who study the attack and its participants say they aren\u8217\'20\'19t convinced criminal convictions against them will fully deter those involved on January 6 from future political violence, but that the biggest threat is a lone actor, not a large, coordinated event.\par \par \uc2 In the last few weeks, a man in Arizona was allegedly stockpiling weapons and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/man-jeffrey-michael-kelly-held-over-democratic-office-shootings-may-have-planned-act-of-mass-casualty"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plotting}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cmass casualty\u8221\'20\'1D event, according to police who arrested him for shooting at Democratic party offices. The person behind explosive devices that burned hundreds of ballots in two drop boxes in Oregon and Washington is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.12newsnow.com/article/news/nation-world/ballot-box-arsons-suspect-description/507-381cbca5-1176-46cd-a701-4242825b367b?utm_medium=social"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspected}}}\uc2  to be a metalworker who could be planning more attacks. Arguments at polling places over political paraphernalia, banned at the polls in some places, have become physical. A young man waved a machete at a polling place in Florida.\par \par \uc2 The risk of political violence only increases after election day, experts say, once races are called. Certain places could become targets of people or groups upset about results or who claim fraud.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/political-violence-election-january-6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Political violence has marked the 2024 race \u8211\'20\'13 but risks rise after election day}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In the last week, the US saw numerous attacks on the voting process and threats of violence, and extremism experts are bracing for what comes after voting has ended.\par \par \uc2 The goal of people committing these acts is often to create fear and distrust around voting or to sabotage the functioning of democracy. Still, election officials stress that voting is safe, and voters should not be deterred from voting because of any threats to the process, which are rare.\par \par \uc2 Here is a timeline of the political violence seen so far during the voting period in the US.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/us-election-violence-timeline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bomb threats, ballot-box arson: a timeline of US election violence}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s canvassing operation sued in California for alleged labor law violations\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s troubled canvassing operation on behalf of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the Republican party is now facing a lawsuit in southern California filed by two women who say they were cheated out of wages and expenses as they knocked on doors for an embattled Republican congresswoman.\par \par \uc2 The suit accuses Musk\u8217\'20\'19s America PAC, which has poured more than $100m into this year\u8217\'20\'19s election campaign, of \u8220\'20\'1Cwillful violations of the California labor code\u8221\'20\'1D by paying the plaintiffs less than it promised and refusing to make up the difference.\par \par \uc2 The women, Tamiko Anderson and Patricia Kelly, say they were hired last month and promised an hourly wage \u8211\'20\'13 about $25, according to their lead lawyer \u8211\'20\'13 to help turn out votes for Michelle Steel, who represents a closely contested swing district in Orange county, south of Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 It was only once the women started working, the suit alleges, that they found out they were being paid instead by the number of houses they visited. The suit further alleges that they were not reimbursed for work-related expenses, including the use of personal cellphones to track their movements along their designated routes.\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s ground-game operation has come under repeated scrutiny in recent days following a report in the Guardian that canvassers may have skipped as many as a quarter of the houses they claimed to have visited in Arizona and Nevada, and a second report in Wired that revealed hired canvassers in Michigan were not told which campaign they were working for until they had already signed on.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/elon-musk-america-pac-labor-law-violations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s canvassing operation sued in California for alleged labor law violations}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 If {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  re-enters the White House on 20 January he will do so emboldened by a power that no previous incoming president has ever enjoyed: immunity from criminal prosecution for any act carried out in his official capacity.\par \par \uc2 The protection, awarded in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jul/01/supreme-court-decision-trump-immunity-ruling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a July ruling}}}\uc2  from the far-right supermajority of the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 , changes fundamentally the dynamics of the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe justices wrote a how-to guide for a president who wants to break the law,\u8221\'20\'1D said Michael Waldman, president of the non-partisan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.brennancenter.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Brennan Center for Justice}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIn practical terms, if you are a president who wants to break the law, make sure your co-conspirators are also government employees \u8211\'20\'13 then you\u8217\'20\'19re off the hook.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The immunity ruling, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/23pdf/23-939_e2pg.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump v United States}}}\uc2 , is the clearest example yet of the judicial feedback loop that the former president established during his 2017 to 2021 presidency. With the active support of Republicans in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , then President Trump appointed three new hard-right justices to the country\u8217\'20\'19s top court, creating a 6-3 conservative-to-liberal supermajority.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/02/trump-immunity-election-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 If Trump wins the election, he could seize control of America\u8217\'20\'19s courts}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Is it any surprise that \u8220\'20\'1Cphoto op\u8221\'20\'1D is a phrase imported into British English from the United States? Of course it came from there, the land where the visual image sits right at the centre of the culture, with politics no exception.\par \par \uc2 It was the Nixon White House that came up with it, specifically a press aide by the name of Bruce Whelihan. According to Washington legend, whenever the president was meeting a visiting dignitary, \uc2 Richard Nixon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hardball press secretary, Ron Ziegler, would turn to his underling with an order to summon the snappers. \u8220\'20\'1CGet \u8217\'20\'19em in for a picture,\u8221\'20\'1D Ziegler would say.\par \par \uc2 Too polite to put it that way himself, Whelilan would clear his throat and announce to the ladies and gentlemen of the Washington press corps, \u8220\'20\'1CThere will be a photo opportunity in the Oval Office.\u8221\'20\'1D) The photo op was born.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/33-pivotal-us-presidential-moments-captured-on-camera"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18There are images no leader ever wants to be seen\u8217\'20\'19: 33 pivotal US presidential moments captured on camera}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  promised a \u8220\'20\'1Crecovery for everybody\u8221\'20\'1D as he prepared to take over an economy ravaged by the pandemic four years ago. Few predicted what would follow.\par \par \uc2 One of two candidates \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , his vice-president, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his predecessor \u8211\'20\'13 will succeed Biden in January. As millions prepare to elect the next US president, here is how the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest economy fared under Biden.\par \par \uc2 The shock waves unleashed by Covid-19 were still rippling across the world when Biden took office in January 2021. In the US, and many other economies, they set the stage for an extraordinary rise in inflation.\par \par \uc2 For months, the White House and Federal Reserve insisted the factors driving this surging price growth were \u8220\'20\'1Ctransitory\u8221\'20\'1D. By the time the consumer price index peaked, reaching its highest level in a generation in June 2022, officials had changed their minds.\par \par \uc2 The Fed embarked upon an aggressive campaign to tackle inflation in March 2022. Interest rates \u8211\'20\'13 cut to close to zero at the outset of the pandemic \u8211\'20\'13 were increased at 11 meetings, to a two-decade high.\par \par \uc2 Suddenly the central fear looming over the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/useconomy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US economy}}}\uc2  was not runaway inflation, but the specter of recession. As the Fed scrambled to cool activity in an attempt to tackle prices, warnings of a prolonged downturn cast a shadow.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/joe-biden-economy-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Did Bidenomics work? How the US economy fared over the last four years}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s one story of the 2024 presidential contest that says that this election is all about men, and their anger.\par \par \uc2 Men, in this account, have gotten a raw deal: the decline of the industrial economy in the years since the postwar boom means that many of the jobs that gave dignity, structure, and steady paychecks to their fathers are now gone, and some men, especially those without college degrees, have fallen into a cycle of desperation and despair, unable to make the kind of living for which they could respect themselves.\par \par \uc2 This economic argument about men is usually followed by a cultural one: that women aren\u8217\'20\'19t as nice to men as they should be, or maybe not as nice to men as they used to be. On one end of this conversation, there are paeans to male loneliness and discussions of the male suicide rate, quasi-poetic odes to their depths of despair and acute feeling: women just don\u8217\'20\'19t understand what it\u8217\'20\'19s like to be sad the way that men are sad.\par \par \uc2 On the other end, writers and commentators point to more recent cultural trends that they say have alienated men, making them feel attacked or unnecessary. They point, apparently seriously, to the fact that some young feminists online have used the term \u8220\'20\'1Ctoxic masculinity,\u8221\'20\'1D which they say makes men feel bad, bad enough that their feelings are an emergency for the nation. They point to those t-shirts that were popular in 2017 that said, \u8220\'20\'1CThe Future Is Female.\u8221\'20\'1D This, too, is reflective of a great social pathology, a sign that we as a nation have failed men and boys. Why, they plead, can\u8217\'20\'19t the future be male?\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/nov/02/this-tight-race-is-in-part-about-sexist-backlash-but-feminists-can-lash-back-too"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 This tight race is, in part, about sexist backlash. But feminists can lash back, too | Moira Donegan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump and Harris head to North Carolina in campaign's final weekend\par \par \uc2 Democrat \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  head to North Carolina on Saturday to try to clinch support in the south-eastern battleground state just three days before Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 It will be the fourth day in a row that vice-president Harris and former president Trump visit the same state on the same day, underlining the critical importance of the seven states likely to decide the race, which opinion polls show to be on a knife\u8217\'20\'19s edge, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 More than 70 million Americans have already cast ballots, according to the Election Lab at the \uc2 University of Florida\uc2 , below the record early-voting pace in 2020 during Covid-19, but still indicating a high level of voter enthusiasm.\par \par \uc2 Saturday also marks the last day of early voting in North Carolina, where over 3.8m votes have been cast, while the state\u8217\'20\'19s western reaches are still recovering from Hurricane Helene\u8217\'20\'19s deadly flooding.\par \par \uc2 Harris plans appearances with rock star Jon Bon Jovi in Charlotte, the biggest city in North Carolina, which is tied with Georgia for the second-biggest prize of the swing states. Each has 16 votes in the Electoral College, where 270 are needed to secure the presidency.\par \par \uc2 North Carolina backed Trump in 2020 but elected a Democratic governor on the same day, giving hope to both parties.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Losing an election for the highest office is a crushing blow that no candidate forgets. But when the American electorate delivers its verdict next week, the personal stakes for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  will be uniquely high. His fate will hover between the presidency and the threat of prison.\par \par \uc2 If he claims victory, Trump will be the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first convicted criminal}}}\uc2  to win the White House and gain access to the nuclear codes. If he falls short, the 78-year-old faces more humiliating courtroom trials and potentially even time behind bars. It would be the end of a charmed life in which he has somehow always managed to outrun the law and duck accountability.\par \par \uc2 For Trump, Tuesday is judgment day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe branded himself as the guy who gets away with it,\u8221\'20\'1D said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://journalism.columbia.edu/directory/gwenda-linda-blair"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gwenda Blair}}}\uc2 , a Trump biographer, adding that, should he lose, \u8220\'20\'1Che is facing a lot of moments of reckoning. He could go to jail. He could end up considerably less wealthy than he is . No matter what happens, and no matter whether he wins or loses, there will be a reckoning over his health. Death, ill health, dementia \u8211\'20\'13 those are things even he can\u8217\'20\'19t escape.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The property developer and reality TV star has spent his career pushing ethical and legal boundaries to the limit, facing countless investigations, court battles and hefty fines. Worthy of a novel, his has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/20/us/politics/trump-scandals.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a life of scandal on a gargantuan scale}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/trump-trial-election-loss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He could go to jail\u8217\'20\'19: for Donald Trump, election day is also judgment day}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 Michigan city of Warren in focus amid worries about delayed election results\par \par \uc2 Officials in the US battleground state of Michigan said they worry that the Democratic-leaning city of Warren could lag behind the rest of the state in reporting the results of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election, raising early doubts about the state\u8217\'20\'19s vote count.\par \par \uc2 Warren, unlike Detroit and most other cities in Michigan, opted not to take advantage of changes enacted in a 2022 state law allowing for up to eight days of pre-processing of absentee ballots, Reuters reported. Instead, the city of 135,000 people will wait until election day to verify and tabulate more than 20,000 mail-in ballots.\par \par \uc2 The potential delay from Warren has worried some Democratic leaders that it could leave the results appearing artificially high for Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on Tuesday evening, and that the former president would seek to exploit the situation by falsely declaring victory in the state before all votes were in.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the state is close at all and we don\u8217\'20\'19t have returns from Warren, which is our third-largest city, it\u8217\'20\'19s going to create all kinds of concerns,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mark Brewer, an attorney and the former chair of the Michigan Democratic Party. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very, very worrisome.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Are the polls 'improbably tight'? Some experts think so\par \par \uc2 The US presidential election campaign enters its final weekend with polls showing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  in seemingly permanent deadlock and few clues as to which of them will prevail on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 At the end of another unruly week that began with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s racially charged rally in New York\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden and was punctuated by celebrity endorsements, misogynistic comments and insults about \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D being levelled left and right, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s 10-day polling average tracker showed little change from seven days earlier, with voter loyalty to their chosen candidate appearing relatively impervious to campaign events, however seismic.\par \par \uc2 Nationally, Harris, the Democratic nominee, has a one-point advantage, 48% to 47%, over her Republican opponent, virtually identical to last week. Such an advantage is well with the margin of error of most polls.\par \par \uc2 The battleground states, too, remain in a dead heat. The candidates are evenly tied at 48% in Pennsylvania, often seen as the most important swing state because it has the most electoral votes (19). Harris has single-point leads in the two other blue-wall states, Michigan and Wisconsin, while Trump is marginally ahead in the Sun belt: up by 1% in North Carolina and 2% in Georgia and Arizona. In Nevada, his average advantage in the polls is less than a percentage point.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/state-poll-results-show-ties-are-tied-voters-pollsters-rcna177703"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Writing on NBC\u8217\'20\'19s website}}}\uc2 , Josh Clinton, a politics professor at \uc2 Vanderbilt University\uc2 , and John Lapinski, the network\u8217\'20\'19s director of elections, pondered whether the tied race reflected not the sentiments of the voters, but rather risk-averse decision-making by pollsters. Some, they suggested, may be wary of findings indicating unusually large leads for one candidate and introduce corrective weighting.\par \par \uc2 Of the last 321 polls in the battlegrounds, 124 \u8211\'20\'13 nearly 40% \u8211\'20\'13 showed margins of a single point or less, the pair wrote. Pennsylvania was the most \u8220\'20\'1Ctroubling\u8221\'20\'1D case, with 20 out of 59 polls showing an exact tie, while another 26 showed margins of less than 1%.\par \par \uc2 This indicated \u8220\'20\'1Cnot just an astonishingly tight race, but also an improbably tight race\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Clinton and Lapinski.\par \par \uc2 Read the full piece here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/what-polls-mean-so-far-trump-harris-election-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dead-heat poll results are astonishing \u8211\'20\'13 and improbable, these experts say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 Around a month before the US elections, in the Kharkiv region, I sat down with a group of Ukrainian infantry soldiers together with the American historian Timothy Snyder. I suggested they ask questions of him not only as an American historian, but also as an American citizen.\par \par \uc2 The servicemen were curious about the upcoming election, but mainly the chances of receiving significant military aid any time soon. They expressed pity that many Americans still don\u8217\'20\'19t understand that the Ukrainian fight is not just about us. It\u8217\'20\'19s in the world\u8217\'20\'19s interests to support the fight against blatant breaches of the international order.\par \par \uc2 The anxiety of the American elections is felt more strongly in Kyiv among Ukrainian officials and civil society leaders because Ukraine has become a partisan issue, and part of US domestic politics. These groups have been trying for years to be on good terms with both Democrats and Republicans in the US. This was especially true during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/20/us-house-vote-foreign-aid-ukraine-support"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long delays in Congress}}}\uc2  over the vote for security assistance to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 But engaging with the Maga camp has become difficult. This only got worse when it was revealed what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s vice-presidential candidate, JD Vance, said in 2022: \u8220\'20\'1CI gotta be honest with you, I don\u8217\'20\'19t really care what happens to Ukraine one way or another.\u8221\'20\'1D During the race, Vance has characterised \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  as an \u8220\'20\'1Cadversary\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ccompetitor\u8221\'20\'1D, rather than an enemy, and has generally argued that the US should be focusing on China, not Russia.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/nov/02/ukraine-us-elections-war-russia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukrainians ask what I'm hearing about our country on the US campaign trail. The truth? We're all but forgotten | Nataliya Gumenyuk}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 This is what happens when successive US governments fail to tackle inequality. While millions of people live in poverty, a handful grow unimaginably rich. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/inequality/2024/jan/15/worlds-five-richest-men-double-their-money-as-poorest-get-poorer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wealth begets wealth}}}\uc2 , and they acquire political power to match. It was inevitable that one of them \u8211\'20\'13 now the richest man on Earth \u8211\'20\'13 would launch what looks like a bid for world domination.\par \par \uc2 A vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  next week is a vote for \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . Just as Trump is using Musk, Musk could be using Trump as a springboard to perhaps even greater power than the US president can wield. Musk\u8217\'20\'19s secret conversations with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/russia/musk-putin-secret-conversations-37e1c187"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported by the Wall Street Journal}}}\uc2  last week, and his contacts with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/18/elon-musk-trump-election-influence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 other extremist world leaders}}}\uc2 , suggest a pattern of power-seeking that could be even more alarming than the prospect of a second Trump presidency.\par \par \uc2 Trump, if he wins, will do to the nation what Musk did to \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : the US will be e-Muskulated. What this means is that those with the power to swarm, harass and crush people who do not share their noxious ideology will be unleashed.\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  claims to be a \u8220\'20\'1Cfree speech absolutist\u8221\'20\'1D. But his absolutism seems to extend only to his allies. Since he bought \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and renamed it X, the platform has complied with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://restofworld.org/2023/elon-musk-twitter-government-orders/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 83% of requests by governments}}}\uc2  for the censorship or surveillance of accounts. When the Turkish president, \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 , demanded the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/news/2023/05/twitter-musk-censors-turkey-election-erdogan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 censorship of his opponents}}}\uc2  before the last general election, the platform obliged. When Indian government officials asked it to remove a hostile BBC documentary, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theintercept.com/2023/01/24/twitter-elon-musk-modi-india-bbc/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 X did as they asked}}}\uc2 , and later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/apr/05/twitter-accused-of-censorship-in-india-as-it-blocks-modi-critics-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deleted the accounts}}}\uc2  of many critics of the prime minister, \uc2 Narendra Modi\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/nov/02/elon-musk-donald-trump-us-presidential-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Can democracy survive now the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man has it in his sights? | George Monbiot}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Republicans want documents released in Biden 'garbage' comment row\par \par \uc2 Top Republicans have called on the White House to produce all documents and internal communications regarding president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s statement earlier this week in which he appeared to take a swipe at supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 White House press officials altered the official transcript of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s statement, drawing objections from the federal workers who document such remarks for posterity, according to two \uc2 US government\uc2  officials and an internal email obtained on Thursday by the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 The Republican lawmakers said they question whether the decision to create \u8220\'20\'1Ca false transcript and manipulate or alter the accurate transcript\u8221\'20\'1D produced for the \uc2 National Archives and Records Administration\uc2  was a violation of federal law.\par \par \uc2 Representative James Comer, Republican chair of the House Committee on Oversight and Accountability, and House Republican conference chair \uc2 Elise Stefanik\uc2  demanded the White House produce the records.\par \par \uc2 They also called on the White House to make available for a briefing the top supervisor of its stenography office.\par \par \uc2 Comer and Stefanik said:\par \par \uc2 The White House cannot simply rewrite president Biden\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric.\par \par \uc2 We are concerned with the latest reporting of the White House\u8217\'20\'19s apparent political decision to protect the Biden-Harris administration, instead of following longstanding and proper protocols.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  repeats anti-immigrant threads at Milwaukee rally\par \par \uc2 At a Wisconsin rally on Friday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  called \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Clow-IQ person\u8221\'20\'1D and vowed to save the economy \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom total obliteration\u8221\'20\'1D in a 1.5 hour-long meandering speech that touched on top campaign issues including the economy and foreign policy \u8211\'20\'13 but also featured threats to curb press freedoms and a lengthy discussion of his own rhetorical style.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will stop the criminal invasion of this country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump during his opening remarks, promising to usher in a new \u8220\'20\'1Cgolden age\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCan you imagine if Kamala won? You would go down to a 1929 style depression,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump.\par \par \uc2 On immigration, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s message was characteristically dark. The campaign played a painful video of a mother describing her daughter\u8217\'20\'19s murder and blaming Harris for allowing the accused to enter the US without authorization. Studies overwhelmingly refute Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim that immigrants are disproportionately responsible for crime in the US, but such claims are a feature of his campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe day I take office, the migrant invasion ends,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump. He vowed to launch the \u8220\'20\'1Clargest deportation program in American history\u8221\'20\'1D and said cities and towns had been \u8220\'20\'1Cconquered\u8221\'20\'1D by immigrants, whom he referred to as \u8220\'20\'1Canimals\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Since his \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally \u8211\'20\'13 which showcased racist and misogynistic comments from a lineup of speakers, including comedian Tony Hinchcliffe, who called Puerto Rico a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 Trump and his allies have sought to recast the former president and his Maga base as unfairly maligned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKamala has spent the final week of her campaign comparing her political opponents to the most evil mass murderers in history,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump at the Wisconsin rally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVice-president Harris thinks you are Nazis, fascists,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Wisconsin senator Ron Johnson, who spoke at the rally.\par \par \uc2 Johnson praised Trump for bringing into his campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/robert-f-kennedy-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr}}}\uc2 , who ended his presidential bid as a third party candidate in August; and \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , a former Democratic congresswoman who announced she had left the party in 2022. Johnson accused Democrats of \u8220\'20\'1Cdestroying America\u8221\'20\'1D and credited Trump with making \u8220\'20\'1Cthe Republican Party the party of the working men and women of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/donald-trump-repeats-anti-immigrant-threads-at-milwaukee-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump repeats anti-immigrant threads at Milwaukee rally }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Arizona officials probing whether Trump broke the law after Cheney remarks\par \par \uc2 The office of Arizona Democratic attorney general Kris Mayes is \u8220\'20\'1Clooking into\u8221\'20\'1D whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  broke state law when he said on Thursday that \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  should face rifles \u8220\'20\'1Cshooting at her\u8221\'20\'1D to see how she feels about sending troops to fight.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 Arizona attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office\uc2  is looking into whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments about \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  violated Arizona law,\u8221\'20\'1D Richie Taylor, communications director for the AG\u8217\'20\'19s office, said in a statement on Friday. \u8220\'20\'1CThe office has no additional comments to make at this time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump made the comments about Cheney, one of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s biggest Republican critics and the daughter of former vice-president \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2 , to former Fox News Host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  at a campaign event in Glendale on Thursday, AP reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s put her with a rifle standing there with nine barrels shooting at her,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s see how she feels about it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He repeated his aggressive attack at his rally in Warren, Michigan, on Friday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s tough one. But if you gave {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/liz-cheney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Cheney}}}\uc2  a gun, put her into battle facing the other side with guns pointing at her. She wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have the courage or the strength or the stamina to even look the enemy in the eye,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why I broke up with her,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump commented, prompting some laughs.\par \par \uc2 In an interview on Friday with 12News, a local television station in Arizona, Mayes said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments were \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply troubling.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have already asked my criminal division chief to start looking at that statement, analyzing it for whether it qualifies as a death threat under Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s laws,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayes told 12News.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not prepared now to say whether it was or it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t, but it is not helpful as we prepare for our election and as we try to make sure that we keep the peace at our polling places and in our state,\u8221\'20\'1D she continued.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Opening summary\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to the US politics live blog. I\u8217\'20\'19m Tom Ambrose and I will be bringing you all the latest from the campaign trail throughout this morning.\par \par \uc2 We start with news that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  battled to woo voters in the key swing states of Michigan and Wisconsin on Friday, as the presidential campaign enters its final stretch.\par \par \uc2 Harris made several appearances in Wisconsin on Friday, including one that featured the musician Cardi B, while Trump visited both {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan}}}\uc2  and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 At his rally in Warren, Michigan, on Friday afternoon, Trump tried to energize his voters, delivering an address replete with his characteristic fear-mongering about immigrants and tangents including musings about his hair.\par \par \uc2 He repeated his aggressive attack on \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , one day after he first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/liz-cheney-donald-trump-dictator"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the former Republican US representative should be under fire with rifles \u8220\'20\'1Cshooting at her\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris meanwhile sought to draw a contrast, emphasizing at a rally in Wisconsin in the afternoon that she is looking to be a political consensus builder.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere is my pledge to you. Here is my pledge to you as president. I pledge to seek common ground and commonsense solutions to the challenges you face,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CI pledge to listen to those who will be impacted by the decisions I make. I will listen to experts. I will listen to the people who disagree with me. Because, you see, unlike {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 , I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that people who disagree with me are the enemy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe wants to put them in jail,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, repeating a line she\u8217\'20\'19s has frequently invoked of late. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll give them a seat at the table.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During his appearance in Warren in the afternoon and in Milwaukee in the evening, Trump repeatedly stoked fears about immigrants. In Warren, he said: \u8220\'20\'1Cevery state is a border state\u8221\'20\'1D and falsely claim immigrants were being flown into the south-west.\par \par \uc2 He repeated some of his most racist tropes, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CAll of our jobs are being taken by the migrants that come into our country illegally and many of those migrants happen to be criminals, and some of them happen to be murderers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For more on last night\u8217\'20\'19s events, see our full report here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/trump-rally-warren-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris and Trump tour key swing states as end of campaign draws close}}}\par \par \uc2 In other news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris told her crowd at the Wisconsin State Fair Park Exposition Center that with four days to go, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/trump-rally-warren-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 there was }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/trump-rally-warren-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 still work to do, but \u8220\'20\'1Cwe like hard work\u8221\'20\'1D}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/trump-rally-warren-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 .}}}\uc2  Minutes beforehand, during a raucous warmup, the rapper Cardi B referred to Trump as \u8220\'20\'1CDonnie Dunk\u8221\'20\'1D and told the crowd: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump says he\u8217\'20\'19s going to protect women whether they like it or not. Well, if his definition of protection is not the freedom of choice, if his definition of protection is making sure our daughters have fewer rights than our mothers, then I don\u8217\'20\'19t want it! I don\u8217\'20\'19t want it! I don\u8217\'20\'19t want it! \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Harris said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s violent rhetoric about Cheney \u8220\'20\'1Cmust be disqualifying\u8221\'20\'1D as far as his suitability for the presidency is concerned. \u8220\'20\'1CRepresentative Cheney is a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/liz-cheney-donald-trump-dictator"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 true patriot who has shown extraordinary courage in putting country above party}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D Cheney for her part warned the public against dictatorship and a presidential candidate who \u8220\'20\'1Cwants to be a tyrant\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 latest offensive and misogynistic comments have boosted Democratic hopes of turning out women on election day in a contest where the rights of women have been a central issue for the Harris campaign.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/02/donald-trump-repeats-anti-immigrant-threads-at-milwaukee-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Milwaukee rally on Friday}}}\uc2 , Trump called Harris a \u8220\'20\'1Clow-IQ person\u8221\'20\'1D and vowed to save the economy \u8220\'20\'1Cfrom total obliteration\u8221\'20\'1D in a 1.5-hour-long meandering speech that touched on the economy and foreign policy but also featured threats to curb press freedoms and a lengthy discussion of his own rhetorical style. \u8220\'20\'1CI will stop the criminal invasion of this country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump, promising to usher in a new \u8220\'20\'1Cgolden age\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CCan you imagine if Kamala won? You would go down to a 1929-style depression.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters are laying the ground for rejecting the result of the election if he loses, according to warnings from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  as well as anti-Maga {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2 . As well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/republicans-supreme-court-pennsylvania-ballots"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 baseless and/or failed lawsuits}}}\uc2 , suspicions have been voiced over partisan polls run by groups with Republican links in battleground states that mainly show Trump leading \u8211\'20\'13 the idea being that if Trump loses, the polls can be proferred as \u8220\'20\'1Cevidence\u8221\'20\'1D that he was cheated out of the win.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The New York author and journalist Michael Wolff has released audio tapes that appear to detail how Trump had a close social relationship with the late sex trafficker \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  that he has long denied. Wolff says the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/trump-jeffrey-epstein-tapes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recordings were made during a 2017 discussion}}}\uc2  with Epstein about writing his biography. Epstein {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/aug/10/jeffrey-epstein-dead-prison-report-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 died by suicide}}}\uc2  while awaiting trial on sex-trafficking charges two years later. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said the claims, made on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/fire-and-fury-the-podcast/id1750757108"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wolff\u8217\'20\'19s podcast Fire and Fury}}}\uc2 , amounted to \u8220\'20\'1Coutlandish false smears\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge rejected an attempt by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s America Pac to have charges of running an illegal lottery heard in federal court, instead of the courts of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/elon-musk-giveaway-lawsuit-state-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania, where Musk is running the sweepstakes}}}\uc2  to help Trump get re-elected. The case has been sent back to the Pennsylvania state court for a further hearing on Monday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Racism and misogyny ; a firing squad {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/liz-cheney-donald-trump-dictator"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 death threat}}}\uc2  to a former congresswoman; the Republican candidate for president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2024/oct/31/donald-trump-stages-garbage-truck-stunt-in-bid-to-turn-tables-over-puerto-rico-backlash-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dressing up as a sanitation worker}}}\uc2 in the cab of a garbage truck. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s final full week on the campaign trail was as unedifying as it was bizarre \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/trump-final-week-campaign-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Richard Luscombe sums it up}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A valuable Republican voting bloc in Arizona is seeing a shift of its members towards Harris in numbers that Democrats believe could make the difference for them in an election where the latest polls have Trump slightly ahead. That bloc is the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/arizona-mormons-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints \u8211\'20\'13 the Mormons}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241102ekb2000xd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
