\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris pitches self as a unifier with a \u8216\'20\'18to-do list\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 is it enough for knife-edge race?\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino \par \uc2 2,332 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 November 2024\par 00:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s historic campaign has aligned stars and positioned itself as an antidote to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s threat but contest remains deadlocked\par \par \uc2 On the second to last Sunday in July, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  had just finished making pancakes and bacon for her grandnieces at the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s residence in Washington, and was sitting down with them to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.siriusxm.com/blog/kamala-harris-howard-stern"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 work on}}}\uc2  a jigsaw puzzle when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  called.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI got up to take the call, and then life changed,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?app=desktop&v=pNbwMrBMGgE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recounted}}}\uc2  later. Biden, isolating with Covid at his vacation home in Rehoboth Beach, Delaware, and facing calls from all corners of his party to step aside, had reached the history-altering decision to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 end his bid}}}\uc2  for re-election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAre you sure?\u8221\'20\'1D Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/theviewabc/reel/DA3kYW2RKp2/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  she asked the US president. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause what a big decision.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With Biden\u8217\'20\'19s endorsement, Harris, still wearing her workout clothes and hooded sweatshirt from her alma mater, \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , leapt into action. Time was of the essence. Over the next 10 hours, with pizza boxes littered around her, she placed 100 calls to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  whose support she would need to secure the nomination.\par \par \uc2 By the time Harris walked into her inherited campaign headquarters in Wilmington, Delaware, to the strains of Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s hard-charging anthem Freedom, her ascension seemed suddenly \u8211\'20\'13 and unexpectedly \u8211\'20\'13 inevitable.\par \par \uc2 In the roughly 100 days since, Harris has enthralled her party, which had been all but resigned to defeat with Biden as its nominee. She {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/kamala-harris-running-mate-tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 selected}}}\uc2  a running mate, the affable Minnesota governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  ; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/kamala-harris-democratic-nomination-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accepted}}}\uc2  the nomination at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/18/democratic-national-convention-chicago"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  joy-filled }}}\uc2  convention; supercharged volunteer sign-ups and on-the-ground organizing; raised a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/10/harris-funding-swing-state-concerns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staggering billion dollars}}}\uc2  ; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/trump-harris-debate-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dominated}}}\uc2  the contest\u8217\'20\'19s only presidential debate against her opponent, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 . She secured endorsements from a host of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/25/election-trump-staffers-john-kelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 former advisers and aides}}}\uc2 , as well as several of the planet\u8217\'20\'19s biggest stars. She appeared on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2024/oct/19/trump-harris-podcasts-election-strategy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 popular podcasts}}}\uc2 , daytime TV and news networks and delivered a closing argument that blended the economic and the existential anxieties driving Americans\u8217\'20\'19 choice in November.\par \par \uc2 But has it all been enough? The race has built to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/nov/01/presidential-polls-latest-donald-trump-kamala-harris-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deadlocked finale}}}\uc2 , with each of the seven battleground states \u8211\'20\'13 and the nation \u8211\'20\'13 virtually tied just days before the final votes of the 2024 election are cast. Along the way, some of that early shine has worn off. Trump has crept back in the polls. Critics have carped at the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s traditionalism, and a perception among some that she has focused too much on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s threat and not offered enough of a vision of her own for Americans to be inspired by.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/us-presidential-election-trump-harris-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delivered}}}\uc2  her last major speech of the campaign from the Ellipse in Washington, a direct appeal to the vanishingly small slice of Americans who have yet to make up their minds.\par \par \uc2 The significance of the site, an oval-shaped park south of the White House, was twofold. It was intended as a stark reminder of the violent forces Trump inflamed from that very spot nearly four years ago, when he implored supporters to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2021/02/10/966396848/read-trumps-jan-6-speech-a-key-part-of-impeachment-trial"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fight like hell}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D before a mob of them {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stormed}}}\uc2  the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 And it was meant to underline the possibility of a Harris presidency.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss important US election coverage. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Get our free app}}}\uc2  and sign up for election alerts\par \par \uc2 With the White House illuminated behind her, Harris declared: \u8220\'20\'1CFor too long, we have been consumed with too much division, chaos and mutual distrust. And it can be easy to forget a simple truth: it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have to be this way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She cast the election as a contest between herself, a unifier with a \u8220\'20\'1Cto-do list\u8221\'20\'1D and Trump, a \u8220\'20\'1Cpetty tyrant\u8221\'20\'1D seeking a return to \u8220\'20\'1Cunchecked power\u8221\'20\'1D. In 90 days, one of them would take the oath of office. \u8220\'20\'1CKamala! Kamala!\u8221\'20\'1D chanted the crowd, her largest to date with an estimated 75,000 people who spilled beyond the park, toward the Washington Monument.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Harris is running the shortest presidential campaign in modern US history. If she wins, she will have persuaded Americans to do something unprecedented in the country\u8217\'20\'19s 248-year history: elect a woman and woman of color to the presidency.\par \par \uc2 At 18, could she have ever imagined this would be her life, Pro Football Hall of Famer Shannon Sharpe asked the 60-year-old during a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Vu5yD3fu6A8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  recent appearance}}}\uc2  on his podcast. \u8220\'20\'1CNever,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, shaking her head. \u8220\'20\'1CNever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The daughter of an endocrinologist from India and an economist from Jamaica, Harris said an \u8220\'20\'1Cinstinct to protect\u8221\'20\'1D propelled her career as a prosecutor, and was central to her opening pitch against Trump. From the courtroom, Harris took on \u8220\'20\'1Cpredators\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cfraudsters\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cscammers\u8221\'20\'1D, she would begin, building to the line: \u8220\'20\'1CSo hear me when I say: I know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s type.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In an election defined by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/25/us-presidential-election-trump-harris-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 striking gender gap}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 with women powering Harris and men turning toward Trump \u8211\'20\'13 the central question may be who Americans trust to protect them \u8211\'20\'13 and what they believe they need protecting from.\par \par \uc2 Harris has vowed to protect Americans\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamental freedoms\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, clean air, decades-old alliances, and democracy itself. Trump has cast himself, by contrast, as the protector of a nation under \u8220\'20\'1Cinvasion\u8221\'20\'1D, overrun by illegal immigration and crime. At a recent rally, he crassly suggested he would protect women, whether they \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/donald-trump-women-protector-wisconsin-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 like it or not}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s critics \u8211\'20\'13 even those who will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/29/opinion/trump-conservative-harris-election.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 begrudgingly}}}\uc2  vote for her \u8211\'20\'13 knock her as a maddeningly scripted politician who lacks an ideological core and who has struggled to articulate a serious policy agenda.\par \par \uc2 At a CNN {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/kamala-harris-cnn-town-hall-pennsylvania-john-kelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 town hall}}}\uc2 , she hewed closely to a set of talking points, offering circular responses to pointed questions. And yet, during the 80-minute segment, she delivered her most forceful warning about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/trump-threats-election-enemy-within"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 authoritarian tendencies}}}\uc2 . Yes, she agreed, her opponent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/harris-trump-fascist-hitler-comments-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was a fascist}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harris has waved off any criticism, calling herself disciplined.\par \par \uc2 At a rally with Harris, \uc2 Michelle Obama{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/michelle-obama-kamala-harris-michigan-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 defended her further}}}\uc2  by suggesting critics were holding the nation\u8217\'20\'19s first female and first Black vice-president to a \u8220\'20\'1Chigher standard\u8221\'20\'1D than Trump, who often {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/07/election-trump-speeches"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rambles}}}\uc2  incoherently, had threatened to jail his political opponents, and would be the first convicted felon elected to the White House if he wins.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope you\u8217\'20\'19ll forgive me if I\u8217\'20\'19m a little frustrated that some of us are choosing to ignore \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s gross incompetence while asking Kamala to dazzle us at every turn,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said in Kalamazoo, Michigan. \u8220\'20\'1CPreach!\u8221\'20\'1D a woman shouted from the audience.\par \par \uc2 Over the course of her abbreviated campaign, Harris has laid out a broad strokes economic agenda with proposals for first-time homebuyers, caregivers, new parents, and the \u8220\'20\'1Csandwich\u8221\'20\'1D generation of adults caring for their children and their parents. She has, meanwhile, backed away from her past support for progressives policies on immigration and fracking, which helped fuel the San Francisco liberal caricature, though it never quite suited the former \u8220\'20\'1Ctop cop\u8221\'20\'1D of California. Drawing on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/28/kamala-harris-moderates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support from anti-Trump Republicans}}}\uc2 , she has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/aug/29/trump-kamala-harris-interview-poll-election-latest-updates?page=with:block-66d0d83f8f08b036ea3f5500#block-66d0d83f8f08b036ea3f5500"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed}}}\uc2  to put a Republican in her cabinet, and insisted she would be a president for \u8220\'20\'1Call Americans\u8221\'20\'1D, including Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters.\par \par \uc2 Along the way, many stars have aligned for her. Oprah sang her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/22/oprah-winfrey-democratic-national-convention-speech-trump-harris-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 praise}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CKamaaaaala\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 in a DNC speech. Taylor Swift {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/article/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-endorses-kamala-harris-president-us-debate-cat-lady"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed}}}\uc2  Harris after her debate performance against Trump. Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/beyonce-brings-star-power-to-harris-rally-in-texas-with-abortion-law-in-the-spotlight"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 embraced}}}\uc2  Harris at an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights focused event in Texas. Bad Bunny {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/27/bad-bunny-supports-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged}}}\uc2  support for her after a shock jock {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/27/trump-madison-square-garden-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disparaged}}}\uc2  Puerto Rico as an \u8220\'20\'1Cisland of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D at a Trump rally. She has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/19/mark-cuban-supporting-kamala-harris-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won support}}}\uc2  from the billionaire \uc2 Mark Cuban\uc2 , who has traveled the country making the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/31/kamala-harris-mark-cuban-fundraising"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case}}}\uc2  that Harris would be better for business than the man who made his name as a Manhattan builder.\par \par \uc2 Tory Gavito, the president of Way to Win, a hub for liberal donors and organizers, likened Harris\u8217\'20\'19s dizzying \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything, everywhere, all at once\u8221\'20\'1D campaign to the Wizard of Oz. The vice-president was thrust to the forefront of American politics and quickly assembled an unlikely coalition that includes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/12/gen-z-kamala-harris-youth-vote-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gen Z}}}\uc2  meme-makers and the former Republican vice-president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/06/dick-cheney-vote-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dick Cheney}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow here we are. This is the end of the road,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI just can\u8217\'20\'19t imagine it having been done any other way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Although Harris has served as the vice-president for nearly four years, she nevertheless arrived at the top of the Democratic ticket relatively unknown. But in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/favorability/kamala-harris/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stark reversal of fortunes}}}\uc2 , she defied skeptics of her political skill, and her popularity soared.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe has not put a foot wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D said Paul Begala, a veteran Democratic strategist and former adviser to \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 . If he had to identify a misstep, it would be during an appearance on ABC\u8217\'20\'19s The View, where, when asked how she would distinguish herself from Biden, Harris responded: \u8220\'20\'1CNot a thing that comes to mind.\u8221\'20\'1D The Trump campaign seized on the line, tying Harris to the unpopular president.\par \par \uc2 Begala marveled at the way Harris has \u8220\'20\'1Csquared the circle\u8221\'20\'1D between Democrats who believed her closing message should be centered around Trump\u8217\'20\'19s threats to democracy \u8211\'20\'13 as the party did in the 2022 midterms when they blunted the anticipated red wave \u8211\'20\'13 and those who argued she should conclude with an economic-focused message, highlighting Americans\u8217\'20\'19 top voting issue. Trump would arrive in office \u8220\'20\'1Cobsessed with revenge\u8221\'20\'1D against an ever-growing enemies list, Harris says, while she would focused on her \u8220\'20\'1Cto-do\u8221\'20\'1D list: lowering costs and fighting to protect what\u8217\'20\'19s left of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in America.\par \par \uc2 Since the supreme court overturned Roe in 2022, Harris has been a powerful messenger {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/19/harris-abortion-rights-early-voting-atlanta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 , framing it as a matter of bodily autonomy. On the campaign trail, she has been joined by women whose lives have been put a risk by their state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/harris-trump-georgia-abortion-death-amber-nicole-thurman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as well as}}}\uc2  by the family of Amber Thurman, the 28-year-old mother from Georgia who died of sepsis in 2022 after being denied timely medical care to treat a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to make sure that we know who is responsible for those deaths, and that is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his supreme court, and all of the Maga Republicans who have voted for legislation up and down the ballot across the country,\u8221\'20\'1D said Silvina Alarc\u243\'00\'F3n, political director at \uc2 Reproductive Freedom for All\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harris has also had to navigate, as she has her entire career, a torrent of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/24/republican-leaders-avoid-racist-and-sexist-attacks-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 racist and sexist abuse}}}\uc2 , including from her opponent, who has insulted her intelligence, calling her \u8220\'20\'1Cdumb as a rock\u8221\'20\'1D and an \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely low IQ person\u8221\'20\'1D. During a live interview with members of the \uc2 National Association of Black Journalists\uc2 , Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/31/trump-lies-questions-kamala-harris-racial-identity-nabj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacked}}}\uc2  her racial identity and asked when she \u8220\'20\'1Chappened to turn Black\u8221\'20\'1D. The remark drew gasps in the room.\par \par \uc2 Christina Reynolds, a senior vice-president of communications for Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, the influential political group that backs female candidates who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, said Harris has faced all of the obstacles that have long burdened women, and especially women of color, who seek high political office. But she has also helped blaze her own trail, demonstrating leadership as the vice-president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s had to stack up to the division and hate and lies, while building the plane,\u8221\'20\'1D Reynolds said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think that when she wins, it will be historic and epic and truly a testament to her and the people around her and the work that they\u8217\'20\'19ve done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Support for Harris has slightly fallen as the Trump campaign sharpened its attacks. Looming over a race that appears to be teetering on a razor\u8217\'20\'19s edge is whether Harris can stitch together her own diverse coalition, similar to the one that elevated Biden in 2020, while polls show Trump making inroads with voters of color and young people, especially men.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are closely watching places such as Dearborn, Michigan, where Democratic emissaries from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/11/01/kamala-harris-gaza-clinton-obama-arab-americans/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Barack Obama}}}\uc2  and the independent senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/30/bernie-sanders-israel-gaza-harris-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bernie Sanders are working}}}\uc2  to stave off a mass defection of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/arab-americans-harris-trump-vote-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arab and Muslim American voters}}}\uc2  furious at the administration over the deadly war in Gaza. At nearly every stop, Harris is heckled by pro-Palestinian protesters, many of whom have said they plan to vote for a third party candidate or not at all.\par \par \uc2 John Zogby\uc2 , an author and pollster who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aaiusa.org/library/press-release-new-poll-arab-american-voters-evenly-divided-in-race-for-white-house-f989m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  studies the Arab American }}}\uc2  electorate, said the scale of the devastation in Gaza and now Lebanon, and the depth of these voters\u8217\'20\'19 discontent, have reached a \u8220\'20\'1Cpoint of almost no return\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt really is different this time,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 In the final days, Harris will circle between all seven battleground states, searching for any last wells of support that might tip the balance. Until the end, she is attempting to make the affirmative case for herself, while arguing that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vilification of his most prominent critics, using increasingly violence rhetoric, \u8220\'20\'1Cmust be disqualifying\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Election eve will be spent in Pennsylvania, whose 19 electoral college votes are seen as a must-win for Harris. On Tuesday, the Harris campaign will host an election night party at Howard, the historically Black college where the vice-president won her first election: freshman class representative.\par \par \uc2 While Democrats remain fearful a second Trump presidency will usher in a dark era for American democracy, and of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/trump-2024-election-subversion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pre-emptive efforts to deny}}}\uc2  an election loss, those on the ground say they see signs that Harris\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cjoyful warrior\u8221\'20\'1D campaign will prevail. Maxwell Alejandro Frost, the gen Z congressman from Florida, told reporters on Friday: \u8220\'20\'1CA bellwether for me in an election is when you\u8217\'20\'19re going to events and you\u8217\'20\'19re seeing people who are not political, who don\u8217\'20\'19t like politics but are there because \u8211\'20\'13 sometimes they can\u8217\'20\'19t even articulate it \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re there because they felt like they needed to be there.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the difference between a political candidate and a movement candidate. And we have a movement candidate, and this is a movement right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 David Smith\uc2  contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241102ekb2001jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
