\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Jennifer Lopez campaigns with Harris in Las Vegas \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now), Maanvi Singh, Erum Salam, Anna Betts and Daniel Lavelle (earlier) \par \uc2 16,118 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 November 2024\par 06:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is closed now, thanks for following along. You can find all of our US elections coverage here.Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss important US election coverage. Get our free app and sign up for election alerts\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. You can find all of our US elections coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 The comments by Trump come as he has struggled to connect with female voters and as Harris courts women in both parties with a message centered on freedom. She\u8217\'20\'19s making the pitch that women should be free to make their own decisions about their bodies and that if Trump is elected, more restrictions will follow as both campaigns sprint toward Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 At a rally Wednesday evening near Green Bay, Wisconsin, Trump told his supporters that aides had urged him to stop using the term protector because it was \u8220\'20\'1Cinappropriate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Then he added a new bit to the protector line. He said he told his aides: \u8220\'20\'1CWell, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to do it whether the women like it or not. I am going to protect them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Those comments shaped much of Harris\u8217\'20\'19 Thursday as the two campaigns jostled over the remarks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 More detail on Harris\u8217\'20\'19s remarks: she said that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comment that he would protect women whether they \u8220\'20\'1Clike it or not\u8221\'20\'1D shows that the Republican presidential nominee does not understand women\u8217\'20\'19s rights \u8220\'20\'1Cto make decisions about their own lives, including their own bodies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s offensive to everybody, by the way,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said before she set out to spend the day campaigning in the western battleground states of Arizona and Nevada.\par \par \uc2 She followed up those remarks at her rally in Phoenix: \u8220\'20\'1CHe simply does not respect the freedom of women or the intelligence of women to know what\u8217\'20\'19s in their own best interests and make decisions accordingly. But we trust women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Arizona, we\u8217\'20\'19re now taking quite the trip down political memory lane, as Trump recounts his opposition to the Iraq war, and takes a swipe at \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , the last Republican to occupy the White House before he got in.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnybody that went into the Middle East, I thought was stupid,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBush, oh, he was just, he was another beauty,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued, appearing to hold himself back from insulting the ex-president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 There are five days left, and \u8220\'20\'1Cno one can sit on the sidelines\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 People should reach out to friends and family and neighbours and co-workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn these next days let us please be intentional about building community,\u8221\'20\'1D she says\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris reminds supporters in Las Vegas that she has spent her life fighting for people who \u8220\'20\'1Chave been hurt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She has lived the promise of America, she says, and sees it in everyone there tonight.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in Arizona, is now insulting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , saying she isn\u8217\'20\'19t as smart as \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The invective came as he recounted his path to the White House in 2016, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CAll of a sudden I\u8217\'20\'19m fighting against crooked \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , who\u8217\'20\'19s a smart woman, much smarter than Kamala, but doesn\u8217\'20\'19t lie as much. Hillary was a liar, a horrible scoundrel, but this one lies so much, and she\u8217\'20\'19s a low IQ individual.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another one about Harris, from Trump: \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s dumb as a rock. And you can\u8217\'20\'19t have that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 At the Harris event, the crowd is chanting \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going back! We\u8217\'20\'19re not going back!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going back because ours is a fight for the future, and a fight for freedom. The freedom for a woman to make decisions about her own body.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She reminds voters that changes to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws under Trump mean that one in three women now lives in a state with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  then teed-up a question about the CIA and \uc2 FBI\uc2  conspiring against Trump, but the former president didn\u8217\'20\'19t seem interested in answering it.\par \par \uc2 Instead, he proposed firing anyone involved in the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s withdrawal from Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou mentioned the enemy within.. \u8230\'20\'26 It\u8217\'20\'19s a fact that the CIA and the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , which are absolutely not allowed by law to have any influence in American politics, because that\u8217\'20\'19s the end of democracy. Both of them and a bunch of other intel agencies worked against you on behalf of the Democratic Party from the minute you got elected in 2016 and they\u8217\'20\'19re still doing it. They\u8217\'20\'19re working against you. Now, what will you do about that?\u8221\'20\'1D Carlson asked.\par \par \uc2 Trump didn\u8217\'20\'19t quite say, instead talking about how succeeding in Washington was all about finding the right people. Then he brought up the chaotic withdrawal from Afghanistan, the point at which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s approval ratings began dropping to levels from which they have not recovered.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy the way, every one of those people having to do with Afghanistan should be fired immediately. Every general should be fired immediately. You know, Biden doesn\u8217\'20\'19t fire anybody,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s event:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doubled down on his insistence that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy from within\u8221\'20\'1D, as he called his political opponents, are a true threat to the country.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has seized on his remarks to argue that he is a fascist looking for \u8220\'20\'1Cunchecked power\u8221\'20\'1D, but Trump doesn\u8217\'20\'19t appear bothered.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe do have an enemy from within. We have some very bad people, and those people are also very dangerous. They would like to take down our country. They\u8217\'20\'19d like to have our country be a nice communist country or fascist in any way they can, and we have to be careful of that. But they\u8217\'20\'19re the greatest con artists, because [as] soon as I said an enemy from within, they said \u8230\'20\'26 oh, he\u8217\'20\'19s saying an enemy from within. These are sick puppies, I\u8217\'20\'19m telling you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 More detail on J Lo\u8217\'20\'19s appearance a few moments ago, from the press pool report:\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Lopez took to the stage at 9.02, wearing a long olive-colored dress. The crowd sounded very pleased.\par \par \uc2 The event is being livestreamed but here are a couple of quotes:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou are the ones who are going to send a message \u8211\'20\'13 that Las Vegas is Harris country\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  gets it \u8230\'20\'26. As president of the United States Kamala will fight for us \u8230\'20\'26 And the freedom to choose to do what we do with our bodies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On Trump and \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt wasn\u8217\'20\'19t just Puerto Ricans who were offended that day. It was every Latino\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Shouts of \u8216\'20\'18thank you\u8217\'20\'19 and \u8216\'20\'18we love you J-Lo\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris takes to the stage and, smiling, says what she has said before: She\u8217\'20\'19s not afraid of hard work, and nor are those present, she is a new generation of leadership, she has a record of being tough on criminals, and if elected, \u8220\'20\'1Cthere is nothing that will stand in my way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.17am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s do this Las Vegas,\u8221\'20\'1D J Lo says, and introduces Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s get loud,\u8221\'20\'1D J Lo says, using a line from the chorus of one of her hits.\par \par \uc2 Then she says she promised herself she wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t get emotional, but that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe should get emotional.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She calls on voters to encourage their loved ones to vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey love it when you do nothing,\u8221\'20\'1D J Lo says, and that a non-vote is an agreement.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t just Puerto Ricans who were offended by the comments made at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden event, J Lo says, \u8220\'20\'1CIt was every Latino in this country. It was humanity and anyone of decent character.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris has \u8220\'20\'1Cshown up every day\u8221\'20\'1D for the people, and it is time for them to \u8220\'20\'1Cshow up for\u8221\'20\'1D Harris.\par \par \uc2 J Lo reminds the audience that her parents are children of Puerto Rico.\par \par \uc2 She says she likes Hollywood endings, she likes it when the good girl or good guy wins.\par \par \uc2 And she\u8217\'20\'19ll be voting for Harris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t even spell American without \u8216\'20\'18Rican\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D J Lo says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile at the Trump event in Arizona:\par \par \uc2 At least once per rally, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tries to give his supporters the opportunity to boo reporters in attendance.\par \par \uc2 This evening\u8217\'20\'19s moment just came as he complained about how news outlets had pursued stories about his potential ties to Russia following his 2016 election victory: \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a hoax. It was made up to justify why \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  lost the election, which he wasn\u8217\'20\'19t supposed to lose \u8230\'20\'26 it was made up by [congressman Adam] Schiff and Hillary and some \u8230\'20\'26 just total sleaze balls. And what happened is, the fake news media, which is back there, you do know that, they\u8217\'20\'19re always around someplace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And at that, the crowd got their moment to boo.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris has \u8220\'20\'1Conly ever had one client: you, the people,\u8221\'20\'1D J Lo says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no candidate in the history of the presidency that is more qualified, and there is no job that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  can\u8217\'20\'19t do,\u8221\'20\'1D J Lo says, somewhat hyperbolically.\par \par \uc2 She repeats: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  gets it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe in the power of women,\u8221\'20\'1D J Lo says. \u8220\'20\'1CWomen have the power to make the difference in this election. I believe in the power if Latinos,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe in the power of all our votes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 J Lo is on stage now at the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  event in Las Vegas, Nevada.\par \par \uc2 She says that America faces a choice between \u8220\'20\'1Cdivided and united\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And that if you believe that any child in America, if they \u8220\'20\'1Cwork their ass off\u8221\'20\'1D, will be able to make it in America, the choice is clear.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNot just some Americans, but all Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 When she started in TV and film, she could get roles playing \u8220\'20\'1Cthe maid or the loud-mouthed Latina,\u8221\'20\'1D but she knew she could do more.\par \par \uc2 A lot of Americans have had that experience, she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  gets it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Should Trump lose, it\u8217\'20\'19s widely expected that he will claim fraud, as he did in 2020.\par \par \uc2 To that effect, he says: \u8220\'20\'1CI think we\u8217\'20\'19re leading by a lot, and \u8230\'20\'26 we can keep that cheating down, because there are a bunch of cheats. If we can keep that cheating down, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have a tremendous victory \u8230\'20\'26 I think it\u8217\'20\'19ll go down as one of the greatest victories of all time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 More now from the start of the Trump portion of the Carlson-Trump event in Arizona :\par \par \uc2 After Carlson\u8217\'20\'19s introduction, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  arrived onstage to Lee Greenwood\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CGod Bless the USA\u8221\'20\'1D, his customary entry music.\par \par \uc2 First question from \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CWhat motivates you to keep going?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters often point to the fact that he\u8217\'20\'19s rich, thus doesn\u8217\'20\'19t stand to benefit from being president, and therefore must be running for some altruistic reason.\par \par \uc2 This is a friendly crowd, and Trump gave them the answer they wanted to hear: \u8220\'20\'1Chell knows. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know \u8230\'20\'26 I just want to be with people like this \u8230\'20\'26 so much love in this room, so much love, right? It\u8217\'20\'19s pretty easy \u8230\'20\'26 I have a lot of alternatives. [I] could be in a beautiful beach with the waves hitting me in the face and all that boring stuff. And I\u8217\'20\'19ve been there, and you get very bored pretty easily. I have one thing in mind: It\u8217\'20\'19s called Make America Great Again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump is now in stage with \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 . He repeats his very well-worn line that he could be doing anything right now \u8211\'20\'13 he could be on the beach, he says this time \u8211\'20\'13but has instead chosen to do this.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 In addition to praising Trump, \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  is also swiping at his enemies.\par \par \uc2 He just took aim at congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , an influential progressive who conservatives like Carlson have no time for.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAOC, that would be \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , I love that she\u8217\'20\'19s this revolutionary who\u8217\'20\'19s named after a Conquistador and doesn\u8217\'20\'19t even know it. Your last name is Cortez, honey, sit this one out,\u8221\'20\'1D Carlson said. \u8220\'20\'1CLike, Larry Mussolini shows up and is, like, no, I\u8217\'20\'19m against fascism, really. All right, got it. What a moron.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He segued into an attack on second gentleman Doug Emhoff: \u8220\'20\'1CShe was at a rally in Vegas yesterday, and she goes, Doug emhoff is the model of masculinity. Oh man, yeah, memo to any unmarried women here, do not date a feminist man. They\u8217\'20\'19ll smack you around.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is the full report from the Associated Press on the Biden apostrophe question:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/nov/01/joe-biden-donald-trump-garbage-comment-white-house-transcript"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 White House press officials altered transcript of Joe Biden \u8216\'20\'18garbage remark\u8217\'20\'19 call: report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 No sign of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  yet, but \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  is now onstage at the Republican candidate\u8217\'20\'19s Arizona event, singing the former president\u8217\'20\'19s praises.\par \par \uc2 Carlson is set to sit down with Trump in what has been billed as a fundraiser for Hurricane Helene relief, but is now giving something of a warm-up speech.\par \par \uc2 Referring back to how Trump was received when he launched his campaign in 2015, Carlson said: \u8220\'20\'1CEverything he said was kind of moderate and sensible, like, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know, we should have a border, and if we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have \uc2 Nato\uc2 , maybe that countries in Nato should help pay for it. If we\u8217\'20\'19re going to defend Europe, maybe they could, you know, pony up a little bit. Why are we paying the entire bill? That didn\u8217\'20\'19t seem crazy to me, boy, they treated Trump like he was a dangerous freak, like he just escaped from the state mental institution, shackles on his arm and a butcher knife in his hand, stop this man.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He left out the part about how, as he launched his campaign, Trump called Mexicans rapists \u8211\'20\'13 the sort of offensive comment that turned off swathes of the electorate, but didn\u8217\'20\'19t prevent him from winning in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/jun/16/donald-trump-mexico-presidential-speech-latino-hispanic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s tirade on Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18drugs and rapists\u8217\'20\'19 outrages US Latinos}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 The former independent presidential candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  is speaking now at the Trump rally in Arizona, and appeared to describe a conversation with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  where he asked him to play a role in his administration.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy, a conspiracy theorist known for his opposition to vaccines, dropped out of the presidential race in August and endorsed the former president, and there\u8217\'20\'19s lately been talk of Trump appointing him to lead an agency or department, if re-elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs soon as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  started talking about giving me the power, he asked me to do three things. He asked me to root out the corruption, and end the conflicts of interest in our regulatory agencies, and end this corporate capture that has turned our regulatory agencies into sock puppets [of] the industries they\u8217\'20\'19re supposed to regulate. And he asked me to restore the tradition of gold-standard, empirically based, evidence-based science in medicine in our regulatory agencies, and to restore the transparency so that these agencies have to must stop hiding science from us when it clashes with the commercial ambitions of the pharmaceutical industry,\u8221\'20\'1D Kennedy said, adding that Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t want me to take vaccines away from people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe asked me to do that, and then he asked me to end the chronic disease epidemic in this country. And he said, and he said, I want to see results, measurable results, in the diminishment of chronic disease within two years. And I said, Mr President, I will do that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 Employees for Arizona \u8217\'20\'19s most populous county are taking on extra shifts to help election workers with an around-the-clock operation to process early ballots that are an unusually long two pages, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 Election officials in Maricopa County must verify each voter\u8217\'20\'19s signature on early ballot envelopes and then remove the ballot pages so they can be prepared for actual counting. The county was unsure how long it would need to keep up the 24-hour operation, which kicked off Thursday night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs predicted, the first two-page ballot since 2006 has affected election administration, especially for the hard-working bipartisan boards who are separating the ballot pages from the affidavit envelopes,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jennifer Liewer, Maricopa County deputy elections director for communications.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn addition to election workers already on staff, county workers are stepping up to assist with the process,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Liewer said early Thursday evening that the number of people helping out would fluctuate as they are trained, but that eventually between 150 and 200 people are expected to be used for the additional shifts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe county employees who are assisting with the night shifts are doing so outside of their normal job responsibilities,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are also utilizing Maricopa County Public Health Medical Reserve Corps members.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Maricopa County Recorder Stephen Richer said earlier this week that ballots have been received from 1 million voters, a number approaching 40% of the nearly 2.6 million people registered.\par \par \uc2 Election officials in the presidential battleground state have urged people to vote early, or make a plan if they opt to cast their ballots in person on Election Day, which is Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Early voting, particularly by mail, has long been popular in Arizona, where nearly 80% of voters submitted their ballots before Election Day in 2020, according to the secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s Office.\par \par \uc2 Arizona was the first of the presidential battleground states to open early in-person voting sites on Oct. 9, with a scattering of traditional voting centers.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Just spotted at Tucker Carlson \u8216\'20\'18s Hurricane Helene fundraiser in Phoenix with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  : a man wearing a garbage bag.\par \par \uc2 He had cut holes in it so it fit sort of like a vest over his shirt. The costume is plainly a reference to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18s statement, which he says was misinterpreted, that people who vote for Trump are \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump has seized on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s gaffe to argue that Democrats are insincere when they say they want to unify the country, holding a rally in Wisconsin yesterday where he was dressed in an orange reflective vest, like a garbage man would wear.\par \par \uc2 It does happen to be Halloween night, but costumes aren\u8217\'20\'19t unusual at Trump campaign events, no matter the time of year. At the Republican national convention in July, there were people wearing brick-patterned suits to represent the wall Trump wants to build along the Mexican border, and fake bandages on their ears, as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s was at the time after the Butler, Pennsylvania assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will soon take the stage at a Hurricane Helene relief fundraiser in Phoenix, Arizona, where he\u8217\'20\'19s billed to chat with star conservative broadcaster \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former president hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been sighted yet, but the crowd did get a pep talk from Charlie Kirk, founder of conservative youth group Turning Point USA.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won Arizona, and Kirk entreated the crowd to do everything they can to prevent \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  from winning the swing state again.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want you to recreate the anger that you felt, I want you to recreate that pit of the stomach for those you that lived through your whole life and you thought this state would never, ever, ever send its votes to a Democrat as president,\u8221\'20\'1D Kirk said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can all do more to make sure that will never happen again, and in the coming days that will be determined.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kirk told the crowd: \u8220\'20\'1CThere are hundreds of thousands of Trump supporters right now in the valley that have received mail-in ballots that have not yet submitted them. We need to find those people and get them the system. There are hundreds of thousands of Trump supporters that may or may not show up. These are plumbers, electricians and welders. These are people that we love and that we cherish might say, oh, my vote won\u8217\'20\'19t matter. You need to convince them to go to the polls and get their vote in and bring two friends with them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also noted that Republicans have improved their early voting response rate since 2020. However, early voting is not predictive of election results, and the Trump campaign is this year encouraging voters to submit ballots early, after downplaying it in 2020.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Nerves are particularly stretched in Maricopa, the Arizona county in which Phoenix sits, and which will probably decide whether Harris or Trump, who has a narrow lead in recent polls, wins Arizona.\par \par \uc2 After Trump\u8217\'20\'19s loss in the state in 2020, his supporters staged demonstrations in Phoenix\u8217\'20\'19s streets. This time around, election officials in Maricopa county {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/22/arizona-election-security-measures-maricopa-county"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plan to have}}}\uc2  a Swat team and mounted sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s deputies ready at the building where they tabulate ballots. Last week, Phoenix police {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/phoenix-mailbox-fire-ballots-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested a man}}}\uc2  for setting fire at a postal box that damaged some mail-in ballots, though said the suspect said his actions were not politically motivated.\par \par \uc2 At Harris\u8217\'20\'19s speech in Phoenix on Thursday, the vice-president told voters to prepare for \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the most consequential elections of our lifetime\u8221\'20\'1D and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/election-harris-trump-women-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized the former president}}}\uc2  for saying he\u8217\'20\'19d protect women \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether the women like it or not\u8221\'20\'1D. But the question of what the former president\u8217\'20\'19s supporters would do if he loses was on attendees\u8217\'20\'19 mind.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would say that I definitely worry about that since he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t conceded the last election,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bethany Hagen, 34, as she waited for a ride in the parking lot of the amphitheater where Harris spoke.\par \par \uc2 While no one the Guardian spoke to predicted imminent violence, many acknowledged that life in a swing state made participating in, or even discussing, politics a fraught experience.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is hard to talk to people here,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hagen, a Colorado native who had moved to the state.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/arizona-political-violence-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18People are scared\u8217\'20\'19: Arizonans fear political violence as election looms}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 Pearl Hubbard picked up some yard signs for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s speech in Phoenix, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2 , on Thursday afternoon, but wasn\u8217\'20\'19t yet sure whether she\u8217\'20\'19d risk displaying them outside her home in a city that sits in some of the most hotly contested political territory in the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m scared to put them up,\u8221\'20\'1D Hubbard said. \u8220\'20\'1CAs I drive \u8230\'20\'26 I only saw one place that had a [Harris] sign. Just don\u8217\'20\'19t see them. I think people are scared to put them up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  became the first Democrat since 1996 to win the state four years ago, Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s capital and most-populous city, Phoenix, saw tense confrontations between local officials and Trump supporters who believed his baseless claims that the election was stolen from him.\par \par \uc2 With the 5 November presidential election days away, Trump still refuses to publicly acknowledge his defeat in 2020, and has already suggested that if he loses this year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/trump-2024-election-subversion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he will once again claim fraud}}}\uc2 . The allegations have changed life for formerly low-key election offices and secretaries of state nationwide, as they regularly face threats, hoaxes and harassment, especially in the seven swing states that are expected to decide the election:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/arizona-political-violence-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18People are scared\u8217\'20\'19: Arizonans fear political violence as election looms}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 The AP story goes on to say that according to the email the news organisation obtained, the press office had asked the stenographers to quickly produce a transcript of the call amid the firestorm:\par \par \uc2 Biden himself took to social media to say that he was not calling all Trump supporters garbage and that he was referring specifically to the \u8220\'20\'1Chateful rhetoric about Puerto Rico spewed by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporter at his \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The stenographers office is charged with preparing accurate transcripts of public and private remarks of the president for preservation by the National Archives and distribution to the public.\par \par \uc2 The two-person stenography team on duty that evening \u8211\'20\'13 a \u8220\'20\'1Ctyper\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cproofer\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 said any edit to the transcript would have to be approved by their supervisor, the head of stenographers\u8217\'20\'19 office.\par \par \uc2 The supervisor was not immediately available to review the audio, but the press office went ahead and published the altered transcript on the White House website and distributed it to press and on social media in an effort to tamp down the story.\par \par \uc2 White House senior deputy press secretary Andrew Bates that evening also posted on X the edited version of the quote and wrote that Biden was referring \u8221\'20\'1Dto the hateful rhetoric at the \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally as \u8216\'20\'18garbage.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The supervisor, a career employee of the White House, raised the concerns about the press office action \u8211\'20\'13 but did not weigh in on the accuracy of the edit \u8211\'20\'13 in an email to White House communications director Ben LaBolt, press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  and other press and communications officials.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRegardless of urgency, it is essential to our transcripts\u8217\'20\'19 authenticity and legitimacy that we adhere to consistent protocol for requesting edits, approval, and release,\u8221\'20\'1D the supervisor wrote.\par \par \uc2 The supervisor declined to comment to The AP and referred questions about the matter to the White House press office.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 AP reports White House officials altered official transcript of Biden's 'garbage' remarks\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports, citing two \uc2 US government\uc2  officials and an internal email obtained on Thursday, that White House press officials altered the official transcript of a call in which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  appeared to take a swipe at supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , drawing objections from the federal workers who document such remarks for posterity:\par \par \uc2 Biden created an uproar earlier this week with his remarks to Latino activists responding to racist comments at a Trump rally made by the comedian Tony Hinchcliffe, who referred to the US island territory of Puerto Rico as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden, according to a transcript prepared by the official White House stenographers, told the Latino group on a Tuesday evening video call, \u8220\'20\'1CThe only garbage I see floating out there is his supporters \u8211\'20\'13 his \u8211\'20\'13 his demonisation of Latinos is unconscionable, and it\u8217\'20\'19s un-American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The transcript released by the White House press office, however, rendered the quote with an apostrophe, reading \u8220\'20\'1Csupporter\u8217\'20\'19s\u8221\'20\'1D rather than \u8220\'20\'1Csupporters,\u8221\'20\'1D which aides said pointed to Biden criticizing Hinchcliffe, not the millions of Americans who are supporting Trump for president.\par \par \uc2 The change was made after the press office \u8220\'20\'1Cconferred with the president,\u8221\'20\'1D according to an internal email from the head of the stenographers\u8217\'20\'19 office that was obtained by The AP. The authenticity of the email was confirmed by two government officials who spoke on condition of anonymity to discuss internal matters.\par \par \uc2 The supervisor, in the email, called the press office\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the matter \u8220\'20\'1Ca breach of protocol and spoilation of transcript integrity between the Stenography and Press Offices.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf there is a difference in interpretation, the Press Office may choose to withhold the transcript but cannot edit it independently,\u8221\'20\'1D the supervisor wrote, adding, \u8220\'20\'1COur Stenography Office transcript \u8211\'20\'13 released to our distro, which includes the National Archives \u8211\'20\'13 is now different than the version edited and released to the public by Press Office staff.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has wrapped up a rally in Henderson, near Las Vegas in Nevada, a swing state where Latino people make up about 30% of the population.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re especially excited to have the support of record numbers of Hispanic Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, \u8220\'20\'1Cand right here in Nevada we\u8217\'20\'19re going to win a record share of the Hispanic American vote at a level that nobody\u8217\'20\'19s ever seen before for the party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign was forced into damage control mode over the weekend when a comedian speaking at his big New York rally called Puerto Rico a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D, prompting criticism from Latino activists.\par \par \uc2 But the Republican nominee argued that he has a winning agenda. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s pretty simple: Hispanics want great jobs, they want rising wages and they want safe communities. They\u8217\'20\'19re great people. Energy \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19re very entrepreneurial. I know\u8217\'20\'19em well, they\u8217\'20\'19re really hard workers, they\u8217\'20\'19re great people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t want vicious gang members getting dumped into your state and you don\u8217\'20\'19t want Kamala teaching your children that they can change their gender anytime they\u8217\'20\'19d like.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also used the rally to recycle election lies, promise that \uc2 Robert Kennedy Jr\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to work on women\u8217\'20\'19s health\u8221\'20\'1D and lavish praise on \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  for space rockets and campaigning in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 He hurled insults at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as lacking \u8220\'20\'1Cintellect\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cstamina\u8221\'20\'1D, a \u8220\'20\'1Ctrain wreck\u8221\'20\'1D and incapable of running a kindergarten. And in a bizarre riff against Democrats, Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t want windows. They don\u8217\'20\'19t want cows. They don\u8217\'20\'19t want anything. They don\u8217\'20\'19t know what they want, actually.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Historian Simon Schama {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/simon_schama/status/1852161468609048712"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 responded on Twitter/X}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18they dont want windows, they dont want cows\u8217\'20\'19 how moronically dumb do you have to be to think this creature is fit to be President?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.56am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 The cast of Marvel\u8217\'20\'19s Avengers movies have come out in support of Democratic presidential candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  less than a week before the US election.\par \par \uc2 In a video posted first on Vanity Fair on Thursday evening, actors Robert Downey Jr, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/scarlettjohansson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Scarlett Johansson}}}\uc2  , Mark Ruffalo, Don Cheadle, Chris Evans, Danai Gurira and Paul Bettany playfully riffed on their respective characters in the Marvel Cinematic Universe while encouraging viewers to vote for Harris.\par \par \uc2 The video, which runs for just over 90 seconds, opens with the actors taking an incoming video call from Johansson. On screen, they brainstorm ideas for a catchphrase for Harris, landing on the dubious \u8220\'20\'1CDown with Democracy\u8221\'20\'1D, which they spin into a brief Marvel-style Harris-Walz campaign video with dramatic music and comic-style graphics. The final frame of the video encourages viewers to vote on 5 November.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/MarkRuffalo/status/1852086652753035272"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sharing the video on Twitter/X}}}\uc2 , Ruffalo, a vocal Democratic supporter who is best known for his role as the Hulk, wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t sit this one out. It\u8217\'20\'19s the one where we will lose big: Project 2025, women\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , climate change, LGBTQIA+ rights, public education, student debt relief, Affordable Care Act, Social Security, and as of today, life saving vaccines. This shit is real and it\u8217\'20\'19s going to come for you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2024/nov/01/us-election-avengers-cast-kamala-harris-endorsement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Avengers stars assemble to endorse Kamala Harris \u8211\'20\'13 by brainstorming an election catchphrase}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump will be campaigning with far-right personality \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  in about 90 minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time in Phoenix, Arizona.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.22am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is the pool report on Harris\u8217\'20\'19s speech in Reno:\par \par \uc2 VP Harris wrapped up at 5.46pm and did a bit of ropeline.\par \par \uc2 Her comments were similar to her earlier speech although targeted to Nevada at the start. There was a lot of placard waving, stamping of feet, booing at mentions of Trump, and chants of Kamala. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need you to vote, Nevada, you are going to make the difference in this election and I thank you,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Protesters interrupted Harris again at least three times, by pool\u8217\'20\'19s count. At least one could be heard shouting about Gaza. Harris drowned out the most vocal protesters when she said \u8220\'20\'1CLet me say something about this \u8211\'20\'13 we are here because we\u8217\'20\'19re fighting for a democracy\u8221\'20\'1D, drawing loud cheers from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 Pool was rushed back at motorcade and now about to roll as of 5.54pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 Pop icon Jennifer Lopez and the Mexican band Man\u225\'00\'E1 are performing at Harris\u8217\'20\'19s event in Las Vegas, in about two hours\u8217\'20\'19 time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris ends her speech with the call: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we fight, we win!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She is shortly heading to Las Vegas, where she will appear at a campaign rally and concert.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 Georgia secretary of state addresses false election video\par \par \uc2 Cutting away from the rally for a moment, the Georgia secretary of state, \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2 , has released a statement in which he says that a video that claimed to show a Haitian immigrant claiming to have voted multiple times is \u8220\'20\'1Cfalse\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ctargeted disinformation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said:\par \par \uc2 Earlier today, our office became aware of a video purporting to show a Haitian immigrant with multiple Georgia ID\u8217\'20\'19s claiming to have voted multiple times.\par \par \uc2 This is false, and is an example of targeted disinformation we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen this election. It is likely foreign interference attempting to sow discord and chaos on the eve of the election.\par \par \uc2 We are working to combat this and identify the origin of it with our state and federal partners. CISA is currently investigating. In the meantime, we ask \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and the leadership of other social media platforms to take this down. This is obviously fake and part of a disinformation effort. Likely it is a production of Russian troll farms.\par \par \uc2 As Americans we can\u8217\'20\'19t let our enemies use lies to divide us and undermine our faith in our institutions \u8211\'20\'13 or each other.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo, Nevada, I am here asking for your vote. I am asking for your vote. And here is my pledge to you,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 Someone yells: \u8220\'20\'1CWe got your back,\u8221\'20\'1D and Harris responds: \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I got your back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She promises to find commonsense solutions, reach common ground, listen to experts and to those who disagree with her.\par \par \uc2 She repeats her line that Trump wants to put those who disagree with him in jail, and that she wants to give them a seat at the table.\par \par \uc2 She promises to be a president for all Americans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause we love our country. And when you love something, you fight for it,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, to loud cheers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.24am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris: 'We're here because we're fighting for a democracy'\par \par \uc2 Harris says forcefully, and with seriousness: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re here because we\u8217\'20\'19re fighting for a democracy!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She gets huge cheers.\par \par \uc2 Then she appears to be heckled, though I could not make it out. She says: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s OK. It\u8217\'20\'19s OK. You know what, democracy can be complicated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re fighting for the right for people to be heard and not jailed because they speak their mind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.41am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris talks about her plans for small business owners, and asks any small business owners to make some noise: there is a lot of enthusiastic noise in response.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 From the pool report at the event:\par \par \uc2 ?Motorcade stopped at 5pm and pool was ushered into a packed Reno Expo Center, an indoor arena with tiered seating and with crowds standing in the middle, in front of the VP\u8217\'20\'19s lectern. There\u8217\'20\'19s a large red sign saying Reno Votes Harris-Walz with two large US flags above one tier and a blue one saying When We Vote We Win. Uplifting music is booming \u8211\'20\'13 the crowd waved their signs in time to Katy Perry\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18Firework.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 ?At 5.21pm VP Harris emerged from behind a curtain in a doorway beneath a large sign saying \u8216\'20\'18Reno Votes\u8217\'20\'19, and walked 50 yards or so along a runway to the lectern.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris tells Nevada: 'Make no mistake \u8211\'20\'13 we will win'\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake: we will win,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is time for a new generation of leadership in America,\u8221\'20\'1D says Harris. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I am ready to offer that leadership.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris, who recently turned 60, is a generation younger than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , her opponent, who is 78, and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , 81, who she replaced on the Democratic ticket.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris starts by saying: \u8220\'20\'1CHappy Nevada day!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need you to vote, Nevada: you are going to make the difference in the outcome of this election and I thank you, I thank you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.30am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris has taken to the stage now in Reno, Nevada. She and Trump are tied in the state according to the latest polling:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/26/presidential-polls-latest-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 US presidential polls tracker: Trump v Harris latest national averages}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s event in Reno, Nevada has started. She is not yet on stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.14am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump is still speaking in Nevada:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump on \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CIn terms of computer, I would say he\u8217\'20\'19s probably about as good as you get\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/5GJKDdETr7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/5GJKDdETr7}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1852140092489347174?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November 1, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a rally in Arizona earlier on Thursday, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t believe women should \u8220\'20\'1Cmake decisions over their own bodies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris made the comment after Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appearance in Wisconsin, when he declared he would protect them \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether the women like it or not\u8221\'20\'1D. Harris said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a saying that you gotta listen to people when they tell you who they are. He does not believe women should have the agency and authority to make decisions about their own bodies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Stormy Daniels honored at witches\u8217\'20\'19 ceremony in Salem, Massachusetts\par \par \uc2 Practising witches from around the world gathered in Salem by the hundreds on Thursday night to honour {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/stormy-daniels"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stormy Daniels}}}\uc2  at their annual \u8220\'20\'1Cmagic circle\u8221\'20\'1D ceremony recognizing loved ones who have died.\par \par \uc2 Daniels \u8211\'20\'13 the adult film actor who allegedly had an affair with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and was at the center of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 May criminal trial}}}\uc2  that led to the former president\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/30/trump-trial-hush-money-verdict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conviction on 34 felonies}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 was chosen to be honored in the Halloween ceremony as the organisers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www2.bostonglobe.com/2024/10/30/metro/stormy-daniels-salem-witches/?fbclid=IwY2xjawGQbjJleHRuA2FlbQIxMQABHX_47WM8mrjihnkFpjHM9qAI4NMFAtpgKOyoHktUssiHo5wFvXj4Xlm_WQ_aem_Z47Tq8rdzTHnXYCKWRsoFg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 believe}}}\uc2  that she has been the victim of a modern-day witch-hunt.\par \par \uc2 The event, which started at 5pm at Salem Common in Salem, Massachusetts, was part of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.festivalofthedead.com/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Festival of the Dead}}}\uc2 , an annual event series exploring \u8220\'20\'1Cdeath\u8217\'20\'19s macabre customs, heretical histories and strange rituals\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The magic circle ceremony is intended to be a time to \u8220\'20\'1Crenew connections, mourn those you miss and to celebrate all that these cherished souls brought to your life\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.festivalofthedead.com/magiccircle.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 event details}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/stormy-daniels-salem-witches"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stormy Daniels honored at witches\u8217\'20\'19 ceremony in Salem, Massachusetts}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is talking again about Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D gaffe, saying he thinks it is \u8220\'20\'1Cworse than \u8216\'20\'18deplorables\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 am I right?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd how did that go for Hillary?\u8221\'20\'1D he asks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has taken the stage in Henderson, Nevada, to the familiar strains of Lee Greenwood\u8217\'20\'19s song God Bless the USA as supporters snap pictures on their phones. Big screens say \u8220\'20\'1CBetter off with Trump\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CTrump will fix it!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19d like to start with a very simple question: are you better off now than you were four years ago?\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican nominee asked. \u8220\'20\'1CNo!\u8221\'20\'1D roared the crowd.\par \par \uc2 Trump was quick to lambast his opponent \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CShe is the worst vice-president in the history of our country. Kamala, you\u8217\'20\'19re fired! Get the hell out of here. She is horrible. And she lies. Every time she gets up she tells a lie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CShe lies about everything. She\u8217\'20\'19s worse than Crooked Hillary, actually.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump trotted out his familiar lines, accusing Harris of violating her oath, eradicating the border and unleashing an army of gangs and criminals from prisons, jails, \u8220\'20\'1Cinsane asylums and mental institutions from all around the world, from Venezuela to the Congo\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He is now playing a video about the murder of a 12-year-old girl, allegedly by undocumented immigrants. The crowd is lapping it up.\par \par \uc2 Some fans are wearing yellow vests to resemble garbage collectors, a reference to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s recent alleged gaffe. When Trump asked who had already voted, a big cheer went up. But he has failed to draw a capacity crowd: there are a few rows of empty seats behind me.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 David Smith\uc2  is at the Trump rally in Nevada, where the Republican nominee asked the crowd if they felt they were better off now than they were four years ago.\par \par \uc2 The crowd yelled: \u8220\'20\'1CNo!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrAt \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  campaign rally in Henderson, Nevada. Trump: \u8220\'20\'1CFive days!\u8230\'20\'26 We\u8217\'20\'19re doing great in Nevada\u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19d like to start with a very simple question: are you better off now than you were four years ago?\u8221\'20\'1D (Crowd yells, \u8220\'20\'1CNo!\u8221\'20\'1D) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xqNmQyAcJQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xqNmQyAcJQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 David Smith\uc2  (@SmithInAmerica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SmithInAmerica/status/1852127290978972006?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Coming up\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what\u8217\'20\'19s coming up over the next few hours:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will hold a campaign rally in Reno, Nevada in the early evening.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris will also a campaign rally and concert in Las Vegas.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump will attend a \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  tour event in Glendale, Arizona.\par \par \uc2 This is Helen Sullivan taking over the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s live US politics coverage \u8211\'20\'13 my colleagues and I will bring you the latest from those events, and any other breaking news.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 There are five days left until the US election. Here are the key recent developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has taken the stage in Phoenix, telling supporters: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have five days left in one of the most consequential elections of our lifetime.\u8221\'20\'1D She emphasized the threats a Trump administration would pose to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CDid everyone hear what he just said yesterday, that he will do what he wants, whether the women like it or not?\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referencing his appearance in Wisconsin, when he declared he would protect them \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether the women like it or not\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Keller, the mayor of Albuquerque, where Trump is holding a rally, said last Friday that the Republican presidential candidate owes the city hundreds of thousands of dollars in bills from his last visit. The Trump campaign owed the city $200,000 for when he hosted his last rally at its convention center in 2019, which has climbed to almost $445,000 with interest. The costs covered police coverage, barricades and other expenses. Trump is banned from rallying in the city over the unpaid bill \u8211\'20\'13 his event is being held instead at a private hangar owned by CSI Aviation near the Albuquerque international sunport.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Billionaires have flushed the election with cash \u8211\'20\'13 roughly $1.9b to be exact, largely to the benefit of republican candidates like Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CBillionaire campaign spending on this scale drowns out the voices and concerns of ordinary Americans. It is one of the most obvious and disturbing consequences of the growth of billionaire fortunes, as well as being a prime indicator that the system regulating campaign finance has collapsed,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Kass, ATF\u8217\'20\'19s executive director.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Voter enthusiasm is at a historical high for a presidential election, a Gallup poll found. Similar to November 2020, 70% of registered voters nationwide said that they were more enthusiastic than usual about voting now compared to March, when only 56% expressed enthusiasm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former attorney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/trump-lawyer-kenneth-chesebro-suspended"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kenneth Chesebro}}}\uc2  has been suspended from practicing law in New York. Chesboro was indicted on state racketeering and conspiracy charges over efforts to overturn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defeat in the 2020 election in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris has received more endorsements today. Former New York mayor and 2020 presidential candidate \uc2 Michael Bloomberg\uc2  and the Economist have publicly expressed their support.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris}}}\uc2  said on Thursday that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s comment that he would protect women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/donald-trump-women-protector-wisconsin-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether the women like it or not\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  showed that the Republican presidential nominee does not understand women\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cagency, their authority, their right and their ability to make decisions about their own lives, including their own bodies\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/election-harris-trump-women-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s offensive to everybody, by the way,\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  Harris said before she set out to spend the day campaigning in the western swing states of Arizona and Nevada.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris will be joined by Jennifer Lopez for her rally in Las Vegas, Nevada - a critical swing state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ex-Fox News anchor \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  will interview Trump in Arizona before the former president heads to his own rally in Nevada.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state, \uc2 Adrian Fontes\uc2 , was ordered to turn over a list of 98,000 voters who may not have provided proof of citizenship.\par \par \uc2 The list was sought by a group called Stronger Communities Foundation. A county judge ordered Fontes to hand over the list of voters by Monday.\par \par \uc2 Fontes argued that he was entitled to withhold the information to protect the safety of the voters, which includes a small group of people who may hold pre-1996 drivers licenses and, due to some complex bureaucracy, may not have been asked to provide proof of citizenship at voter registration as required by a later, 2004 law.\par \par \uc2 The judge who made the order said there was \u8220\'20\'1Clack of any evidence that any individual life was in danger,\u8221\'20\'1D but also forbade Stronger Communities from using the list to contact voters before Election day.\par \par \uc2 Hannah Fried, executive director of All Voting Is Local, wrote that the order to release the list got her attention, but that laws protect voters from intimidation, regardless.\par \par \uc2 enltrOrdering election officials to release a list of voters' names gets my attention this close to Nov 5 - and not in a good way. But state & federal law protects against intimidation, + impacted voters can cast a full ballot without concern in this election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/yTurFmxnG5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/yTurFmxnG5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hannah Fried (@HannahKFried) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HannahKFried/status/1852106955625762883?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  launched an \u8216\'20\'18election integrity community\u8217\'20\'19 on X, full of baseless claims\par \par \uc2 While {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2  faces his own election integrity questions offline, the X owner has deputized his followers to spot and report any \u8220\'20\'1Cpotential instances of voter fraud and irregularities\u8221\'20\'1D. The community he spawned is rife with unfounded claims passed off as evidence of voter fraud.\par \par \uc2 Musk opted not to show up to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/elon-musk-court-hearing-voter-lottery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 required court appearance}}}\uc2  Thursday in Philadelphia to respond to a lawsuit challenging his political action committee\u8217\'20\'19s daily $1m voter giveaway. Meanwhile, online, he has started a dedicated {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/i/communities/1848518910653415584"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 community space}}}\uc2  on X, formerly \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , where he\u8217\'20\'19s asked users to share any issues they see while voting. Users posting on the self-contained feed, the \u8220\'20\'1Celection integrity community\u8221\'20\'1D, quickly began pointing out what they deemed as evidence of fraud and election interference.\par \par \uc2 Tweets showing everything from ballots that arrived ripped, an ABC news system test, a postal worker doing his job and dropping off mail-in ballots were all presented as evidence that the upcoming presidential election had been compromised. Some users posted videos of individuals they deemed suspicious, despite providing little or no proof of suspicious activity and asked others in the community to help identify them.\par \par \uc2 Among the tweets are attempts at doxxing and identifying people who users falsely accuse of ballot box stuffing or preventing Trump supporters from voting. In one case, a post with 14,000 shares and 31,000 likes includes a video of a postal worker bringing ballots into a polling location in Northampton county, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/oct/31/elon-musk-election-integrity-community-misinformation-disinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18election integrity community\u8217\'20\'19 on X is full of baseless claims}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Los Angeles Lakers\uc2  star LeBron James has endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , writing: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I think about my kids and my family and how they will grow up, the choice is clear to me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWhat are we even talking about here?? When I think about my kids and my family and how they will grow up, the choice is clear to me. VOTE KAMALA HARRIS!!! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tYYlTmQS6e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tYYlTmQS6e}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 LeBron James (@KingJames) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KingJames/status/1852093996350275595?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The endorsement isn\u8217\'20\'19t a surprise \u8211\'20\'13 James has supported Democrats before, and been critical of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , gathering for a campaign rally in Henderson, near Las Vegas in Nevada, are confident that he will win next week\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election \u8211\'20\'13 and some refuse to contemplate defeat.\par \par \uc2 Bob Diaz, 69, who is Latino and teaches at a college, said Trump is doing \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot better\u8221\'20\'1D with Latino voters this time. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople will be blown away about how much he actually won by,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s going to get the electoral votes and the popular vote as well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His wife, Audrey, also 69, a homemaker and mediator, added: \u8220\'20\'1CPolls are just polls. I believe he\u8217\'20\'19s going to win. I\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen anything like this. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been involved with other campaigns. I\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen so many age groups, so many cultures, so many countries, so many languages. I\u8217\'20\'19ve never, ever seen this before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She believes that border security is a winning issue for the Republican nominee. \u8220\'20\'1CI wish he didn\u8217\'20\'19t cuss, I wish he didn\u8217\'20\'19t say weird things, but he\u8217\'20\'19s going to protect our borders and clean it up from the inside and protect it from the outside. Bottom line.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Some here say they would not accept a Trump defeat. Kathy Holesapple, 56, an entrepreneu, pilot and aircraft mechanic, said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t. None of us will. We know he didn\u8217\'20\'19t lose in 2020 either.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGod\u8217\'20\'19s going to bring it in and take down the wicked. The righteous will be lifted up and the wicked will fall and those who support the death of innocent children in America and around the world will not survive in this nation. They will not be in power for much longer.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Enrique Lopez, 32, a physical therapy student and military veteran, warned: \u8220\'20\'1CNo matter what happens, there\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a lot of chaos on both sides. Whether Trump wins or loses, there\u8217\'20\'19s going to be so much chaos.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris says Trump doesn't believe women should 'make decisions over their own bodies'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has taken the stage in Phoenix, telling supporters: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have five days left in one of the most consequential elections of our lifetime.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She emphasized the threats a Trump administration would pose to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CDid everyone hear what he just said yesterday, that he will do what he wants, whether the women like it or not?\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referencing his appearance in Wisconsin, when he declared he would protect them \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether the women like it or not\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a saying that you gotta listen to people when they tell you who they are,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe does not believe women should have the agency and authority to make decisions about their own bodies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has baselessly claimed that Democrats are acting like the \u8220\'20\'1Cgestapo\u8221\'20\'1D in forcing people to adopt electric vehicles, during a rally in New Mexico today.\par \par \uc2 In his latest broadside against electric cars, the former president said that trucks made 50 years ago are better than electric versions today but that people are being forced to switch by a \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  administration that is using tactics he likened to Nazi Germany.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo, I said, did you explain that to the authorities as they burst into your office to demand that you go all electric?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, in reference to a conversation he\u8217\'20\'19d had with someone. \u8220\'20\'1CHe said: \u8216\'20\'18I explained it.\u8217\'20\'19 \u8216\'20\'18What did they say?\u8217\'20\'19 \u8216\'20\'18We don\u8217\'20\'19t give a damn. We want you to go all electric.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is what we\u8217\'20\'19re dealing with. It\u8217\'20\'19s like gestapo stuff, OK? They use that term. It\u8217\'20\'19s like gestapo stuff. What they\u8217\'20\'19re doing to our country is unbelievable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s accusation is based on a falsehood \u8211\'20\'13 there is no obligation to switch to electric cars nor any ban on gasoline or diesel cars. Despite this, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has repeatedly claimed otherwise, assailing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://host2.adimpact.com/admo/viewer/0619f435-d06f-4d00-8da3-94eb9a30d85f/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TV adverts}}}\uc2  for adopting an \u8220\'20\'1CEV mandate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Electric cars have long stirred antipathy in Trump, who has said incentives to buy them are \u8220\'20\'1Clunacy\u8221\'20\'1D and that their supporters should \u8220\'20\'1Crot in hell\u8221\'20\'1D even as \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , the billionaire chief of electric car giant \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , has become one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s most prominent backers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/05/trump-endorses-electric-vehicles-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The president acknowledged this incongruity in August}}}\uc2  when he said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m for electric cars, I have to be because Elon endorsed me very strongly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The ceasefire against electric vehicles now appears to be over, however. Should he win next week\u8217\'20\'19s election, Trump is expected to roll back vehicle pollution standards that nudge people to buy electric alternatives, as well as repeal tax rebates for people to buy electric models.\par \par \uc2 Gasoline cars, trucks and other forms of transport are the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epa.gov/greenvehicles/fast-facts-transportation-greenhouse-gas-emissions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest sectoral contributor}}}\uc2  of planet-heating gases in the US, as well as a major source of the air pollution that routinely causes tens of thousands of respiratory and cardiovascular health problems, and deaths, among Americans each year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Trump campaign is quite present at this Quakertown voting location, where there\u8217\'20\'19s a long line of people waiting to vote.\par \par \uc2 They have a table set up with coffee and donuts, and volunteers are going up and down the line giving voters the forms they need to fill out to request their mail-in ballots on demand.\par \par \uc2 I chatted with Betsy Cross, a Trump campaign volunteer from New Jersey who was handing out forms to people in line to request their mail-in ballots on demand. She had been there since 2.30 and estimated people were waiting two hours to vote. Was she surprised that so many people were there? \u8220\'20\'1CNo,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople want to bank their vote for president Trump.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 I just stopped by a voting location in Bucks county, a Pennsylvania battleground where a local judge extended the deadline for voters to cast ballots after a Trump campaign lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Voters here can request and return an absentee ballot on the spot \u8211\'20\'13 Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s clunky version of early, in-person voting \u8211\'20\'13 until Friday. The deadline for the rest of the state was Tuesday, but the Trump campaign successfully sued the county to get voting extended until Friday. Residents had been blocked from voting even though they were in line by 5pm, the daily cutoff.\par \par \uc2 I arrived a little after 3pm at the government offices in Quakertown and saw that there was a pretty long line stretching around the corner. Just before he went into vote, a man at the front of the line told me he had been waiting about an hour.\par \par \uc2 One of the people in the back of the line was Phil Haegele, a 47-year-old plumber who was celebrating his sixth wedding anniversary. He said he was supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and that he\u8217\'20\'19d heard about voting being extended on the radio yesterday and got \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably 50 text messages\u8221\'20\'1D encouraging him and his wife to come vote.\par \par \uc2 Haegele usually votes on election day but said that he had decided to come out and cast his ballot early.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe had saw that on a lot of the news agencies that we follow, they were saying that they were trying to get as many Trump supporters to vote early to try and ward off as much fraud as they could,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He predicted that the election would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cblowout\u8221\'20\'1D, even though the polls show an extremely tight race in Pennsylvania and across the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf they call the election on election day, it\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be a blowout,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf they need to take a week to print more ballots, then yes, it\u8217\'20\'19s gonna be tough.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump voters unmoved by controversy over protecting women remarks\par \par \uc2 Supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Henderson, near Las Vegas in Nevada, are giving short shrift to a controversy over his remark on Wednesday that he would protect women \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether the women like it or not\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Awaiting a Trump campaign rally, Patty Periva, 74, a retired education worker, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t care. The Democrats do not protect women. They allow abortions. How many of those abortions are women? They\u8217\'20\'19re killing women and they don\u8217\'20\'19t protect women. It\u8217\'20\'19s a lie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Lisa Consigilo, 60, a retired personal trainer, added: \u8220\'20\'1CMy family\u8217\'20\'19s from New York. Some things he says people take literally but I know how he speaks: it\u8217\'20\'19s how my dad spoke. You don\u8217\'20\'19t need to take stuff so literally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll their campaign is running on lies. He\u8217\'20\'19s not going to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the country. You can\u8217\'20\'19t: it\u8217\'20\'19s impossible. He\u8217\'20\'19s not for that. Everything that they\u8217\'20\'19re running on is not true about Project 2025. He\u8217\'20\'19s a dad, he\u8217\'20\'19s a grandfather, it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t literal like: \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19m going to protect women.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Opinion polls suggest a historic gender gap in the presidential election, with women supporting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  by a wide margin. But Kathy Holesapple, 56, an entrepreneur, pilot and aircraft mechanic, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve weaponised the women against this party but the truth is that they\u8217\'20\'19ve also held down the women in this nation by calling us Karens.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not allowed to stand up and speak for our beliefs. They call us a Karen every time we speak up. So the American woman needs to stand up \u8211\'20\'13 and they will \u8211\'20\'13 and they\u8217\'20\'19re going to realise that Trump is for American women. He\u8217\'20\'19s for women all over the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Stakes: mass deportations\par \par \uc2 Raids and mass deportations lie at the heart of the former president\u8217\'20\'19s second-term vision \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/trump-mass-deportations-detention-camps-military-migrants"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a web of policies so vast}}}\uc2  that critics say their collective implementation would challenge the very ideal of the United States as a nation of immigrants.\par \par \uc2 Should he win in November, the Republican nominee has vowed not only to restore many of his most controversial immigration policies, but to go even further. While a number of his first-term plans were stymied by the courts and Congress, immigration rights leaders believe a second Trump administration would likely be more sophisticated and strategic.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is different this time. There\u8217\'20\'19s a plan. There is a sense of urgency that they\u8217\'20\'19ve created around this issue,\u8221\'20\'1D said Vanessa C\u225\'00\'E1rdenas, executive director of the immigration advocacy group America\u8217\'20\'19s Voice. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd they know how to use the levers of government in a way they didn\u8217\'20\'19t in 2016.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would also be operating in a changed political landscape. Since leaving office, the political center of gravity has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/10/15/2024/no-matter-who-wins-the-country-is-moving-to-the-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shifted rightward}}}\uc2 , amid a post-pandemic rise in global migration that saw a record number of people arriving at the southern border and claiming asylum. Americans have become {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2024/06/06/immigration-attitudes-and-the-2024-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less tolerant}}}\uc2  of illegal immigration while a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/508520/americans-value-immigration-concerns.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing minority}}}\uc2  is increasingly concerned about its impact on the country\u8217\'20\'19s economy and national identity.\par \par \uc2 Though border crossings have plummeted this year following the president\u8217\'20\'19s asylum clampdown, a sense of disorder persists. Voters continue to broadly disapprove of the Biden-Harris administration\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the situation. Trump and his team are confident immigration remains a potent political issue for voters \u8211\'20\'13 and one that he has long played to his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/trump-leads-harris-wsj-poll-779f8516?st=RAtQf6&reflink=desktopwebshare_permalink?mod=WSJ_WNPOD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advantage}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 When Trump first descended {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/jun/13/donald-trump-presidential-campaign-speech-eyewitness-memories"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a golden escalator}}}\uc2  in 2015, he pledged to construct a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat wall\u8221\'20\'1D along the south-west border with Mexico to keep out immigrants he disparaged as \u8220\'20\'1Crapists\u8221\'20\'1D and drug dealers. Now, in the final weeks of his third presidential race, Trump has again escalated his threats against immigrants, but this time he is turning his vitriol inward toward those already here.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe United States is now an occupied country,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump claimed recently at a rally in Atlanta. \u8220\'20\'1CBut on November 5, 2024, that will be liberation day in America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/31/election-trump-immigration-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 If Trump wins the election, mass deportations could wreak havoc on immigrants}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris to rally voters in Phoenix and Las Vegas\par \par \uc2 The vice-president will be appearing in Phoenix alongside the musical group Los Tigres del Norte.\par \par \uc2 Then, she\u8217\'20\'19ll be heading to Las Vegas, where she will be campaigning alongside Jennifer Lopez and Mana\u180\'00\'B4.\par \par \uc2 In both cities, Harris will seek to energize Latino voters, who could help decide the outcome of the race in the key swing states of Arizona and Nevada.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 Happy Halloween! There are barely five days left in the 2024 US presidential election and polls show the candidates \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 remain neck and neck in swing states like Pennsylvania, Michigan and North Carolina. More than 60 million Americans have cast ballots so far.\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump are traveling across the western half of the country in states like New Mexico, Nevada and Arizona in the final days of their campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a summary of the day so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Keller, the mayor of Albuquerque, where Trump is holding a rally, said last Friday that the Republican presidential candidate owes the city hundreds of thousands of dollars in bills from his last visit. The Trump campaign owed the city $200,000 for when he hosted his last rally at its convention center in 2019, which has climbed to almost $445,000 with interest. The costs covered police coverage, barricades and other expenses. Trump is banned from rallying in the city over the unpaid bill \u8211\'20\'13 his event is being held instead at a private hangar owned by CSI Aviation near the Albuquerque international sunport.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Billionaires have flushed the election with cash \u8211\'20\'13 roughly $1.9b to be exact, largely to the benefit of republican candidates like Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CBillionaire campaign spending on this scale drowns out the voices and concerns of ordinary Americans. It is one of the most obvious and disturbing consequences of the growth of billionaire fortunes, as well as being a prime indicator that the system regulating campaign finance has collapsed,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Kass, ATF\u8217\'20\'19s executive director.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Voter enthusiasm is at a historical high for a presidential election, a Gallup poll found. Similar to November 2020, 70% of registered voters nationwide said that they were more enthusiastic than usual about voting now compared to March, when only 56% expressed enthusiasm.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former attorney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/trump-lawyer-kenneth-chesebro-suspended"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kenneth Chesebro}}}\uc2  has been suspended from practicing law in New York. Chesboro was indicted on state racketeering and conspiracy charges over efforts to overturn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defeat in the 2020 election in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris has received more endorsements today. Former New York mayor and 2020 presidential candidate \uc2 Michael Bloomberg\uc2  and the Economist have publicly expressed their support.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris}}}\uc2  said on Thursday that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s comment that he would protect women {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/donald-trump-women-protector-wisconsin-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether the women like it or not\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  showed that the Republican presidential nominee does not understand women\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cagency, their authority, their right and their ability to make decisions about their own lives, including their own bodies\u8221\'20\'1D. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/election-harris-trump-women-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s offensive to everybody, by the way,\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  Harris said before she set out to spend the day campaigning in the western swing states of Arizona and Nevada.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris will be joined by Jennifer Lopez for her rally in Las Vegas, Nevada - a critical swing state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Ex-Fox News anchor \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  will interview Trump in Arizona before the former president heads to his own rally in Nevada.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Of the more than 60 million Americans who have gone to the polls early \u8211\'20\'13 some 32 million and counting did so in person. Here are some of the best pictures of early voting from the newswires:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Albuquerque mayor says Trump owes town where he is holding rally nearly $500,000\par \par \uc2 Tim Keller, the mayor of Albuquerque, where Trump is holding a rally, said last Friday that the Republican presidential candidate owes the city hundreds of thousands of dollars in bills from his last visit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump now owes almost a half a million dollars to the city of Albuquerque \u8230\'20\'26 We\u8217\'20\'19ve had collection agencies calling and so forth for about two years now,\u8221\'20\'1D Keller said.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign owed the city $200,000 for when he hosted his last rally at its convention center in 2019, which has climbed to almost $445,000 with interest. The costs covered police coverage, barricades and other expenses. Since the Trump campaign still allegedly hasn\u8217\'20\'19t paid its bills, he was banned from rallying there. Instead, the rally is being held at a private hangar owned by CSI Aviation near the Albuquerque international sunport.\par \par \uc2 The general manager for the Albuquerque convention center, Ray Roa, confirmed to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.abqjournal.com/election/tempers-flare-between-city-council-president-and-mayor-over-trumps-visit-records-show/article_dc26daee-96fb-11ef-9b90-873040b5d364.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Albuquerque Journal}}}\uc2  on Monday that members of the Trump campaign contacted them to try to rent the convention center but were denied.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump called his supporters smarter than \u8220\'20\'1Ccrooked Joe\u8217\'20\'19s or lyin\u8217\'20\'19 Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s\u8221\'20\'1D and denounced \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  over his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/joe-biden-puerto-rico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  remark.\par \par \uc2 Trump took several digs at his opponent, telling his crowd that Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t have the stamina, the intellect or that special quality\u8221\'20\'1D that certain leaders have.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump called the US \u8220\'20\'1Can occupied country\u8221\'20\'1D of illegal immigrants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn day one, I will launch the largest deportation program in American history,\u8221\'20\'1D he told the crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will put these vicious and bloodthirsty criminals in jail or kick them the hell out of our country, and fast.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also promised to end sanctuary cities across the country.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been holding a rally in Albuquerque, New Mexico, a region he said \u8220\'20\'1Chas some of the worst border problems\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1DIf you voted against me, shame on you,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told his crowd.\par \par \uc2 In addition to calling \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cgrossly incompetent\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump falsely said Harris imports criminals and mental institute patients into the US. He said \u8220\'20\'1Crough and tough hombres\u8221\'20\'1D were coming across the border, a callback to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AneeacsvNwU&ab_channel=CNN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 comment he made in 2016}}}\uc2  during a debate with the then Democratic presidential nominee \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  about male drug dealers allegedly crossing the southern border illegally: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have some bad hombres here and we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna to get \u8216\'20\'18em out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has rebuked Harris-Walz surrogate \uc2 Mark Cuban\uc2  for comments he made about women on Thursday during an appearance on The View.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 you never see him around strong, intelligent women ever,\u8221\'20\'1D Cuban said when discussing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former primary opponent \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  and the women working Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign and in his former administration. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just that simple: they\u8217\'20\'19re intimidating to him. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like to be challenged by them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign said in a statement in response: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  called Trump supporters garbage, and now, Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s top surrogate \uc2 Mark Cuban\uc2  insinuated female Trump supporters are \u8216\'20\'18weak and dumb.\u8217\'20\'19 This is extremely insulting to the thousands of women who work for President Trump, and the tens of millions of women who are voting for him. These women are mothers, entrepreneurs, and industry leaders and they are, indeed, strong AND intelligent, despite what \uc2 Mark Cuban\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  say.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Michael Bloomberg\uc2 , former New York mayor, endorses Harris\par \par \uc2 Michael Bloomberg\uc2  has announced he voted for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former New York City mayor, who governed as a Republican and as an independent, and who was also a Democratic presidential candidate in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2024-10-31/michael-bloomberg-why-i-m-voting-for-kamala-harris?srnd=opinion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote in an article}}}\uc2  for his own news media company, Bloomberg News, that he voted for Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cwithout hesitation\u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  said that although he disagreed with Harris on some issues, he applauded a number of her policies including women\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , immigration, gun safety, and the climate crisis.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  called the US \u8220\'20\'1Cthe world\u8217\'20\'19s greatest nation\u8221\'20\'1D and said Trump made it \u8220\'20\'1Clook like a banana republic\u8221\'20\'1D when he tried to overturn the results of the election and incite violence on 6 January at the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  added: \u8220\'20\'1CMost Americans never thought we\u8217\'20\'19d witness such a shameful episode. Trump, rather than apologizing for it \u8211\'20\'13 as some of those convicted of January 6-related crimes have done \u8211\'20\'13 celebrates it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  concluded with an ask to \u8220\'20\'1Cundecided voters of all political stripes\u8221\'20\'1D to join him in voting for Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Where are the presidential and vice-presidential candidates campaigning today?\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is campaigning in Nevada and Arizona, with rallies planned in Reno, Las Vegas, and Phoenix, according to her campaign.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  delivered remarks at a campaign event in Bucks County, Pennsylvania this morning and then will make a local stop in Erie, Pennsylvania, per the campaign.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be hosting rallies in New Mexico, Nevada, Arizona today, per his campaign.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  attended a town hall at \uc2 High Point University\uc2  in North Carolina this morning.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Economist endorses \uc2 Kamala Harris\par \par \uc2 The Economist magazine announced {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.economist.com/in-brief/2024/10/31/why-the-economist-endorses-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 their endorsement }}}\uc2  of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 In the statement, editors at the Economist wrote:\par \par \uc2 Tens of millions of Americans will vote for Mr Trump next week. Some will be true believers. But many will take a calculated risk that in office his worst instincts would be constrained. We see that as recklessly complacent.\par \par \uc2 By making Mr Trump leader of the free world, Americans would be gambling with the economy, the rule of law and international peace.\par \par \uc2 Ms Harris\u8217\'20\'19s shortcomings, by contrast, are ordinary. And none of them are disqualifying. If The Economist had a vote, we would cast it for her.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New poll shows presidential race pretty much deadlocked in North Carolina, Pennsylvania and Michigan.\par \par \uc2 The surveys, conducted by \uc2 UMass Lowell\uc2 /\uc2 YouGov\uc2  and released today, found that in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uml.edu/docs/2024-Oct31-NC-Topline_tcm18-392299.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina}}}\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was leading \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  47% to 45%.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uml.edu/docs/2024-Oct31-PA-Topline_tcm18-392293.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania,}}}\uc2  Harris is leading Trump, 48% to 47%, and in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uml.edu/docs/2024-Oct31-MI-Topline_tcm18-392302.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan, }}}\uc2  Harris received 49% of the support among likely voters surveyed compared with 45% for Trump, well within the survey\u8217\'20\'19s margin of error.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former Trump attorney Kenneth Chesebro suspended from practicing law in New York\par \par \uc2 A state appeals court in New York ruled on Thursday that Kenneth Chesebro \u8211\'20\'13 the attorney who allegedly devised the \u8220\'20\'1Cfake electors\u8221\'20\'1D plan to prevent \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from winning the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 will have his law license suspended.\par \par \uc2 Last year, in August, Chesebro was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/aug/14/donald-trump-georgia-indictment-2020-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicted}}}\uc2 , along with Trump and 17 others in Georgia on state racketeering and conspiracy charges over efforts to overturn Trump\u8217\'20\'19s defeat in the 2020 election there.\par \par \uc2 In October, Chesebro {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/20/kenneth-chesebro-plea-deal-fulton-county-racketeering-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accepted a plea deal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 With just days before the US presidential election, Guardian reporters Oliver Laughland and Joel Van Haren visited communities in Pennsylvania with the most on the line.\par \par \uc2 Watch here:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Election enthusiasm up from 56% to 70% among registered voters, poll says\par \par \uc2 Voter enthusiasm is high for this presidential election, according to a new Gallup poll.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/652853/half-votes-likely-cast-election-day.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2 , released on Thursday, found that 70% of registered voters nationwide said that they were more enthusiastic than usual about voting, up from 56% in March.\par \par \uc2 The increase was largely a result of Democrats and Democratic-leaning independents expressing heightened enthusiasm for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  dropped out of the race, the survey states.\par \par \uc2 70% enthusiasm is also one percentage point higher than what Gallup measured at the close of the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Americans\u8217\'20\'19 attention to the election is also relatively high, the poll writes, with 83% of registered voters and 77% of US adults saying they have given \u8220\'20\'1Cquite a lot of thought\u8221\'20\'1D to the election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More than 60m Americans have voted already\par \par \uc2 More than 60 million Americans have already voted in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 With just five days until election day, 60.9 million people in the US have voted early as of Thursday at noon, according to the Election Lab at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://election.lab.ufl.edu/early-vote/2024-early-voting/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the University of Florida.}}}\par \par \uc2 Of the nearly 61 million, just over 32 million voted early in person and about 28 million voted early by mail.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Cardi B will join \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at a rally in Wisconsin on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign announced today that rapper Cardi B will be delivering remarks to voters in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, tomorrow. It is unclear whether she will perform, or just talk.\par \par \uc2 The rally in Milwaukee will also feature performances by GloRilla, Flo Milli, MC Lyte, the Isley Brothers and DJ Gemini Gilly.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is hitting back at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  after she said that he wanted to end the Affordable Care Act, also known as \u8216\'20\'18\u8220\'20\'1CObamacare\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Truth Social on Thursday, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/113402752841810552"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that he \u8220\'20\'1Cnever mentioned\u8221\'20\'1D ending the Affordable Care Act, adding that he has \u8220\'20\'1Cnever even thought about such a thing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But, during his presidency, Trump repeatedly tried to terminate and replace the Affordable Care Act.\par \par \uc2 In 2017, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/realDonaldTrump/status/890820505330212864"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted }}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Clet ObamaCare implode\u8221\'20\'1D after the Senate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2017/jul/28/healthcare-bill-us-senate-votes-down-obamacare-skinny-repeal-revolt-by-john-mccain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to pass a trimmed-down Affordable Care Act repeal bill}}}\uc2  that Trump had supported.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration asked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/jun/26/trump-administration-asks-supreme-court-axe-obamacare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for the supreme court}}}\uc2  to terminate the Affordable Care Act, and in 2019, the justice department {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/mar/26/trump-administration-pushes-to-completely-gut-obamacare-in-dramatic-escalation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 under Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration backed}}}\uc2  a Texas judge\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/dec/14/judge-rules-obama-healthcare-law-unconstitutional"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2  that Obamacare was unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 And more recently, during the presidential debate with Harris, Trump called Obamacare \u8220\'20\'1Clousy\u8221\'20\'1D adding: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to replace it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  hit back at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments last night about how he will \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect\u8221\'20\'1D women, \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether the women like it or not \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CIt actually is, I think, very offensive to women in terms of not understanding their agency, their authority, their right and their ability to make decisions about their own lives, including their own bodies.\par \par \uc2 Harris said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments were \u8220\'20\'1Cjust the latest on a series of reveals by the former president on how he thinks about women and their agency\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CWhether he has said, as he has, that women should be punished for their choices, whether he has talked about his pride is taking away a fundamental right of women, whether it be how he has actually created a situation in America where one in three women lives in a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban state.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a Saturday afternoon at Al Madina Halal market and restaurant in Norcross, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 , and the line is four people deep for shawarma sandwiches or leg of lamb with saffron rice and two sides.\par \par \uc2 A television on the wall by a group of tables has Al Jazeera correspondents reporting from several countries on a split screen about Israel\u8217\'20\'19s attack on Iranian military targets the day before.\par \par \uc2 Mohammad Hejja is drinking yogurt, surveying the bustle in the store he bought in 2012. There are shoppers and employees from Sudan, Ethiopia, Iran, Pakistan, Morocco and other countries \u8211\'20\'13 a clear sign of what makes surrounding Gwinnett county, with nearly a million residents, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usnews.com/news/health-news/slideshows/the-15-most-diverse-counties-in-the-us?slide=17"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most diverse}}}\uc2  in the south-east.\par \par \uc2 Hejja has Jordanian and US citizenship, but his family is Palestinian. Soldiers of the nascent nation of Israel drove his grandparents out of Palestine in the 1948 Nakba \u8211\'20\'13 the Palestinian catastrophe caused by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s creation.\par \par \uc2 Asked about how he expects his community to vote when Americans head to the polls next week, he says: \u8220\'20\'1CEverybody is confused about this election.\u8221\'20\'1D His No 1 concern is to \u8220\'20\'1Cstop the war\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ongoing bombardment of Gaza and recent attacks on Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 The issue is top of mind for Arab American voters nationwide. Some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/arab-americans-poll-trump-harris-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}\uc2  suggest Arab Americans could abandon the Democrats in droves over the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel; elsewhere, advocates and community leaders are urgently organizing to prevent a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  victory, warning about impacts in the Middle East and on domestic issues such as immigration if the GOP candidate is re-elected.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/arab-americans-harris-trump-vote-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Five days out, Arab Americans are split on Harris v Trump: vote \u8216\'20\'18strategically\u8217\'20\'19 or \u8216\'20\'18morally\u8217\'20\'19?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Abdullah Hammoud, mayor of Dearborn, Michigan, wrote on X in response to Clinton\u8217\'20\'19s speech: \u8220\'20\'1CDo us a favor \u8211\'20\'13 stop sending surrogates who have no respect or regard for this community. You\u8217\'20\'19re only inflicting more damage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrRumor has it the Dems want to send \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  to Dearborn to rally the Arab vote this weekend.\par \par \uc2 Do us a favor - stop sending surrogates who have no respect or regard for this community. You\u8217\'20\'19re only inflicting more damage. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UYcJOOo9Gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/UYcJOOo9Gi}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Abdullah H. Hammoud (@AHammoudMI) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AHammoudMI/status/1851982829212647793?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Georgia state representative and Palestinian American Ruwa Romman said in response to Clinton\u8217\'20\'19s speech she was \u8220\'20\'1Cso ready for this generation to step aside\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Romman hoped to speak at the Democratic national convention this summer as a representative of the Palestinian American community but that request was ultimately denied, a move that upset Arab and Muslim American political groups. Shortly after Romman was denied a speaking slot, Muslim Women for Harris-Walz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/22/muslim-women-kamala-harris-disbands"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 withdrew their support}}}\uc2  for Harris and disbanded.\par \par \uc2 enltrFor no reason whatsoever randomly remembering \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  speaking at Georgetown and telling Muslims to \u8220\'20\'1Cstay here and fight\u8221\'20\'1D as if we were just here for vacation. Anyway, I\u8217\'20\'19m so ready for this generation to step aside. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Uh8U3Uz8np"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Uh8U3Uz8np}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rep. Ruwa Romman (@Ruwa4Georgia) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Ruwa4Georgia/status/1851961293965541862?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 31, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Polls show \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are neck and neck in Michigan, a state home to the one of the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest Arab populations, many of whom are mourning the losses of family members killed by Israeli forces abroad in Palestine and Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 Former president \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  made a speech in support of Harris in the key swing state last night addressing these voters, and said: \u8220\'20\'1CI understand why young Palestinian and Arab Americans in Michigan think too many people have died \u8211\'20\'13 I get that,\u8221\'20\'1D Clinton said before adding: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Hamas\uc2  makes sure that they\u8217\'20\'19re shielded by civilians. They\u8217\'20\'19ll force you to kill civilians if you want to defend yourself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/arab-americans-poll-trump-harris-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent poll}}}\uc2  showed Arabs favor Trump slightly more than Harris, a likely reaction to the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s Middle East policy and \u8220\'20\'1Crock solid\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cunwavering\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/14/biden-israel-backing-israel-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ironclad}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D support for Israel.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pictures of the ballots that were set on fire in Washington and Oregon earlier this week have been released. Election staff in Washington\u8217\'20\'19s Clark county identified the 488 voters with damaged ballots, 345 of whom have requested new ballots. The remaining 143 replacement ballots will be mailed out today.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ClarkCoWA?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ClarkCoWA}}}\uc2  Auditor Greg Kimsey has released photos and updated information on the damaged ballots from the Oct. 28 drop box fire. Elections staff have been able to identify 488 damaged ballots retrieved from the ballot box. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/53cyLFNFqK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/53cyLFNFqK}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Clark County WA (@ClarkCoWA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ClarkCoWA/status/1851717433578656022?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Officials fear the suspect, a white man of medium or thin build between 30 and 40 years old, who is balding or has very short hair, may intend to strike again. Bob Day, the police chief of Portland, Oregon, said the said the welding on the incendiary devices found inside the ballot boxes is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery detailed \u8230\'20\'26 it\u8217\'20\'19s really quality, so this person obviously has some skills in that area\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is one of the billionaires who shelled out large sums of money in support of the Republican party.\par \par \uc2 The tech billionaire known for \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  and \uc2 Tesla\uc2  gave $133m to America Pac, a Super Pac he created to support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But Musk\u8217\'20\'19s campaign tactics have gotten him into trouble.\par \par \uc2 The America Pac has been giving a $1m cash prize away each day until election day on 5 November to a person in a swing state if they pledged to support the first and second amendments.\par \par \uc2 The justice department warned Musk that offering a monetary incentive to voters was illegal and he might be breaking the law. \uc2 Larry Krasner\uc2 , the Democratic district attorney of Philadelphia, brought the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/28/election-elon-musk-petition-giveaway-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first legal action against Musk}}}\uc2 , arguing it is an illegal lottery which violates state consumer protection laws.\par \par \uc2 Musk on Wednesday night sought to have the case brought to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/31/politics/elon-musk-sweepstakes-filing-pennsylvania/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 federal court}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Billionaires spent $1.9bn on US election contributions\par \par \uc2 A lot of money has been spent on this year\u8217\'20\'19s elections.\par \par \uc2 Only 150 billionaire families have contributed $1.9bn in support of presidential and congressional candidates, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1nsUJbTHDK4nnHqDLVkK9sk26ShoFWpi2bWLkK8W5LHE/edit?gid=1535161183#gid=1535161183"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new report}}}\uc2  from Americans for Tax Fairness.\par \par \uc2 Of this giant figure 72% went to support Republicans compared with the 22% spent on Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBillionaire campaign spending on this scale drowns out the voices and concerns of ordinary Americans. It is one of the most obvious and disturbing consequences of the growth of billionaire fortunes, as well as being a prime indicator that the system regulating campaign finance has collapsed,\u8221\'20\'1D said David Kass, ATF\u8217\'20\'19s executive director.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to rein in the political power of billionaire families by better taxing them and by effectively limiting their campaign donations. Until we do both, we can only expect the influence of the super-rich over our politics and government to escalate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump deadlocked in swing state Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  poll\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/tablet/2024/10/31/oct-24-28-2024-washington-post-poll-michigan-voters/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new Washington Post poll}}}\uc2  has found that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are tied in toss-up state Michigan. Harris has 47% support among likely voters while Trump has 46% support.\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1DBoth margins are within the poll\u8217\'20\'19s margin of error of 3.7 percentage points, indicating either candidate could hold a lead,\u8221\'20\'1D the newspaper said.\par \par \uc2 With 50.6% of the vote, \uc2 Joe Biden{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/election-results/michigan-2020/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 won}}}\uc2  the midwest state in 2020 compared to the 47.8% who voted for Trump. Trump narrowly won Michigan in 2016 by a little less than 11,000 votes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 After the January 6 attack on the US Capitol, America\u8217\'20\'19s business leaders came out strongly in their criticism of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2 . Now \u8211\'20\'13 as the Harris campaign brands Trump a \u8220\'20\'1Cfascist\u8221\'20\'1D and Trump threatens retribution against \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy within\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 there appears to be a conspiracy of silence.\par \par \uc2 In fact, as the nation heads to the polls in an election that is too close to call, some of America\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful chief executives appear to be cozying up to Trump again.\par \par \uc2 In public, only a small handful of business leaders are backing Trump. In private it\u8217\'20\'19s a different story. At least, that\u8217\'20\'19s how Trump is telling it.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/business-leaders-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Business leaders keep quiet on Trump \u8211\'20\'13 what are they saying in private?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 Most gamblers might want to sit out the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election}}}\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s too close to call with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  neck and neck, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to official polls}}}\uc2 . But the former president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has latched on to signs he says prove he\u8217\'20\'19s actually \u8220\'20\'1Cleading\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In a close race, Trump and his allies claim some \u8220\'20\'1Cgambling polls\u8221\'20\'1D, as he described them last week, put him significantly ahead of Harris. \u8220\'20\'1CLike, 65 to 35, or something like that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The irony of touting an apparent lead in betting markets at a Believers and Ballots {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Cjb6BB1lYY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign event}}}\uc2  in Georgia aimed at Christian voters was not lost on Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CBut nobody here gambles,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued. \u8220\'20\'1CDoes anybody here gamble? No, no, no, no. Great Christians don\u8217\'20\'19t gamble, do they? Oh no.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/election-betting-presidential-odds-polling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Opinion polls have Harris and Trump locked in a tight race. \u8216\'20\'18Gambling polls\u8217\'20\'19 say otherwise}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Lots of memes and tweets and posts and videos are popping up, assuring women that they can keep their votes secret from their husbands and boyfriends. The unspoken assumption is that lots of women are bullied, intimidated or controlled by their partners, specifically in straight couples when she wants to vote for Harris and he supports Trump. The messages assure these intimidated voters that they can vote in peace and privacy at a polling place. But a lot of Americans now vote by mail, which generally means they fill out their ballots at home, where that privacy may not be available.\par \par \uc2 On the one hand, I\u8217\'20\'19m glad there\u8217\'20\'19s outreach to those voters. On the other, the way these messages are framed seem to regard the grim reality that a lot of women live in fear of their spouses as a given hardly worth stating outright, let alone decrying \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/31/why-are-so-many-women-hiding-their-voting-plans-from-their-husbands"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why are so many women hiding their voting plans from their husbands? | Rebecca Solnit}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.46am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says he will \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect women\u8221\'20\'1D if he wins power, but previous remarks and behaviour suggest otherwise :\par \par \uc2 Since the 1970s, about 26 women have accused \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of sexual misconduct. The allegations include: rape, intruding on naked teenage pageant contestants, kissing and groping without consent, and looking under women\u8217\'20\'19s skirts.\par \par \uc2 Trump was found liable for sexually abusing and defaming E Jean Carroll. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s counterclaim was rejected by a judge in New York, Lewis A Kaplan, who said that the allegation that Trump raped Carroll was \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantially true\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As well as being an adjudicated rapist, Trump has made a litany of sexist comments throughout his public life. In an interview with Esquire Magazine in 1991, Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t really matter what [the media] write as long as you\u8217\'20\'19ve got a young and beautiful piece of ass.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a leaked recording from 2005, Trump told Billy Bush that, \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen you\u8217\'20\'19re a star, they let you do it. You can do anything.\u8221\'20\'1D He adds seconds later: \u8220\'20\'1CGrab them by the pussy. You can do anything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On a 2013 episode of Celebrity Apprentice, Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt must be a pretty picture, you dropping to your knees\u8221\'20\'1D to a female contestant.\par \par \uc2 His tendency to make misogynistic remarks does not seem to be abating. Only in August did the former president suggest Harris had traded sexual favours to advance her political career.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.19am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump to campaign in western swing states days before election\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will travel out west in the US election race on Thursday, as opportunities to edge ahead are running out.\par \par \uc2 Both candidates are trying to get Latino voters to support them. Harris has secured the star power of Jennifer Lopez for her rally in Las Vegas, Nevada, a critical swing state. Meanwhile, ex-Fox News anchor \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  will interview Trump in Arizona before the former president heads to his own rally in Nevada.\par \par \uc2 A stand-up comedy set performed at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  is still reverberating throughout this campaign. Comedian Tony Hinchcliffe likened Puerto Rico to a floating island of garbage, which Harris\u8217\'20\'19 campaign has seized upon, claiming that it reveals the racism of Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 This was gaining traction, but President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  still managed to make it backfire on his party when he appeared to describe all Trump supporters as \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage.\u8221\'20\'1D This prompted Trump, who has also branded Harris\u8217\'20\'19 supporters as garbage, to use a garbage truck in a publicity stunt in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Trump is due to deviate slightly from campaigning in battleground states with a trip to New Mexico on Thursday, a state pollsters forecast will go to Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.38am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 The concept of \u8220\'20\'1Celite overproduction\u8221\'20\'1D was developed by social scientist Peter Turchin around the turn of this century to describe something specific: too many rich people for not enough rich-person jobs. It\u8217\'20\'19s a byproduct of inequality: a ton of poor people, sure, but also a superfluity of the wealthy, without enough positions to house them in the influence and status to which they think themselves entitled. In a modern context, that would mean senior positions in the government and civil service, along with the top tier of finance and law, but Turchin tested the hypothesis from ancient Rome to 19th-century Britain. The names and nature of the contested jobs and titles changed; the pattern remained. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2023/jun/10/how-to-avoid-a-civil-war-by-the-man-who-predicted-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Turchin predicted }}}\uc2  in 2010 that by the 2020s it would be destabilising US politics \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/31/elon-musk-an-excess-of-billionaires-is-destabilising-politics-just-as-academics-predicted"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An excess of billionaires is destabilising politics \u8211\'20\'13 just as academics predicted}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.21am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49am GMT\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  may never have visited Thulasendrapuram, a sleepy village in south India, but its residents claim to be some of her most devoted fans.\par \par \uc2 It was here, in among the verdant rice paddies and groundnut farms of rural Tamil Nadu, that Harris\u8217\'20\'19s grandfather PV Gopalan was born. Though more than a century has passed since then, residents have proudly claimed Harris as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdaughter of the land\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The outcome of the US election next week, where Harris is running as the Democrat party\u8217\'20\'19s presidential nominee, has the community on edge. At the local tea shop, gossip has been pushed to one side to make way for chatter over the challenges posed by Harris\u8217\'20\'19s opponent \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and the trends from crucial swing states.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/31/india-village-kamala-harris-support-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Village in India where Harris is \u8216\'20\'18daughter of the land\u8217\'20\'19 on edge as US election looms}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump make final pitches to voters as millions vote early\par \par \uc2 Good morning. It is less than a week before polls close at the 2024 US election and more than 57.5 million Americans have already checked their ballots, according to the Election Lab at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://election.lab.ufl.edu/early-vote/2024-early-voting/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the University of Florida}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Presidential candidates \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are still hot on the campaign trail in a fiercely contested race that is too close to call.\par \par \uc2 Trump made an appearance in a high-vis vest at the wheel of a garbage truck before heading off to a rally in Wisconsin, a key battleground state. Trump promised to protect women \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether they liked it or not\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris was also in Wisconsin offering platitudes on climate change, gun control and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She said those issues were \u8220\'20\'1Cnot political\u8221\'20\'1D but one\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Clived experience\u8221\'20\'1D. She was speaking shortly after the latest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/30/kamala-harris-donald-trump-joe-biden-us-election-news-updates?page=with:block-6722e0528f0821f410faa8d5#block-6722e0528f0821f410faa8d5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  CNN poll}}}\uc2  showed her six points ahead of Trump in the state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump take their nail-biting White House race west later, seeking supremacy on border security and aiming to woo crucial Latino voters days ahead of the US election. Pop singer Jennifer Lopez will bring her star power to the stage for Harris in Las Vegas, as the candidates battle through the seven swing states expected to decide the next president. Meanwhile, Trump has scheduled an interview in Arizona with ex-Fox News host \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  and a rally in Nevada.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/harris-pennsylvania-battleground-state-election-closing-argument"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke in Harrisburg, the Pennsylvania state capital}}}\uc2 , one of few counties that voted for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020.{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polls show a tied race}}}\uc2  in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/arnold-schwarzenegger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arnold Schwarzenegger}}}\uc2  has announced that he is backing Harris in next week\u8217\'20\'19s election. Schwarzenegger, 77, said that while he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Creally do endorsements\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2024/oct/30/arnold-schwarzenegger-endorses-kamala-harris-i-will-always-be-an-american-before-i-am-a-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he felt compelled to formally endorse Harris and her pick for vice-president, Tim Walz}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/trump-puts-on-high-vis-vest-to-trash-bidens-garbage-gaffe-at-wisconsin-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to apologise for the comments made about Puerto Rico}}}\uc2  at his \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a comedian, what can I tell you? I know nothing about him. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know why he\u8217\'20\'19s there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Pennsylvania judge on Wednesday sided with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/trump-lawsuit-ballot-bucks-county-pennslyvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  agreed to extend an in-person voting option in suburban Philadelphia}}}\uc2 , where long lines on the final day led to complaints voters were being disfranchised by an unprepared election office.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A majority of voters in swing states {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/trump-defeat-voter-swing-state"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 do not believe Trump will accept defeat}}}\uc2  if he loses next week\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election and fear that his supporters will turn to violence in an attempt to install him in power, a new poll suggests.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241031ekav001mn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
