\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Amazon donates to group backing hardline anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  Republican\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in Washington \par \uc2 982 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 October 2024\par 18:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 DoorDash\uc2  and CVS also contributing funds to Raga group trying to re-elect \uc2 Todd Rokita\uc2 , who favors total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Amazon, \uc2 DoorDash\uc2  and \uc2 CVS Health\uc2  are among major US companies publicly committed to supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have nonetheless contributed this year to a group supporting the re-election of \uc2 Todd Rokita\uc2 , the Republican attorney general of Indiana who supports a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wthr.com/article/news/politics/indiana-attorney-general-hopeful-for-abortion-restriction-ahead-of-special-session-exceptions/531-623b630a-1dc5-4d70-b5c0-cf1772774a83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 total \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He was also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2023/11/03/1210440222/indiana-abortion-todd-rokita-reprimand-caitlin-barnard"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reprimanded}}}\uc2  by his state supreme court for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/jul/10/indiana-abortion-doctor-10-year-old-child-rape"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticizing}}}\uc2  a doctor who provided an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for 10-year-old rape victim from Ohio.\par \par \uc2 The corporate donations, detailed in publicly available filings, were made to the Republican Attorneys General Association, or Raga, a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.opensecrets.org/527s/basics.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 527 committee}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a tax-exempt political campaign group so-called in reference to the US tax code. It exists to funnel nationally donated funds into key state races.\par \par \uc2 In 2024, Amazon, Doordash and \uc2 CVS Health\uc2  between them have donated $425,000 to Raga. And Raga has given $255,000 to Rokita, who has also participated in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tn.gov/content/dam/tn/attorneygeneral/documents/pr/2024/pr24-38EEOC.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suit}}}\uc2  against the \uc2 Equal Employment Opportunity Commission\uc2  over accommodations for workers receiving abortions; signed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/23/23-235/301853/20240229123329431_Nos.%2023-235%2023-236%20States%20Merits-Stage%20Amici%20Brief.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 amicus briefs}}}\uc2  in a \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/jun/13/supreme-court-abortion-pill-access"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenge}}}\uc2  to Food and Drug Administration approval of mifepristone, an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill; and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mississippifreepress.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/657773029-Mississippi-AG-opposes-reproductive-care-privacy-rule.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought access}}}\uc2  to private health records, in order to prosecute women seeking abortions.\par \par \uc2 Altria\uc2 , \uc2 AT&T\uc2  and \uc2 Comcast\uc2  are also among major public companies that publicly support \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  while donating to Raga , which supports campaigns for attorney general across the US. (In 2024, \uc2 Altria\uc2  has given $450,000, \uc2 AT&T\uc2  $125,000 and \uc2 Comcast\uc2  $125,000.)\par \par \uc2 Donations to Republican and Democratic 527 committees have long been tracked by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politicalaccountability.net/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Center for Political Accountability}}}\uc2 , a Washington thinktank, which highlighted the donations to Raga and Rokita.\par \par \uc2 In August, in an introduction to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politicalaccountability.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Corporate-Underwriters-Where-the-Rubber-Hits-the-Road.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a CPA report}}}\uc2 , Bruce Buchanan, a professor of business ethics at the Stern School of Business at \uc2 New York University\uc2 , said of 527 committees: \u8220\'20\'1CTheir power far exceeds their media presence. The American citizenry has little awareness of their influence, and even less of their funding and methods. This is unfortunate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\u8230\'20\'26 As major corporations open their checkbooks to these 527s \u8211\'20\'13 and especially to the Republican Attorney Generals Association (Raga) \u8211\'20\'13 these funds are going to elect and re-elect state officials that are actively advancing policies antithetical to stakeholder groups across society.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many major US companies made public statements about support for employees in light of Dobbs v Jackson, the 2022 \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2  that removed the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the ensuing state bans.\par \par \uc2 In May 2022, after Dobbs was leaked, Amazon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/retail-consumer/amazon-reimburse-us-employees-who-travel-treatments-including-abortions-2022-05-02/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told}}}\uc2  employees it would pay up to $4,000 in travel expenses for non-life-threatening treatment including abortions, if an operation was not available within 100 miles of an employee\u8217\'20\'19s home. In 2024, with stringent post-Dobbs bans in place in Republican-run states including Indiana, where Rokita has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wthr.com/article/news/politics/indiana-attorney-general-hopeful-for-abortion-restriction-ahead-of-special-session-exceptions/531-623b630a-1dc5-4d70-b5c0-cf1772774a83"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 advocated}}}\uc2  for a total ban, Amazon has given Raga $150,000.\par \par \uc2 In June 2022, shortly after Dobbs, a \uc2 DoorDash\uc2  spokesperson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.restaurantbusinessonline.com/workforce/these-restaurant-companies-will-pay-employees-travel-abortions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the company would cover \u8220\'20\'1Ccertain travel-related expenses\u8221\'20\'1D for employees forced to travel out of state for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s paramount that all \uc2 DoorDash\uc2  employees and their dependents covered on our health plans have equitable, timely access to safe healthcare.\u8221\'20\'1D This year, Doordash has paid $150,000 to Raga.\par \par \uc2 CVS Health\uc2  has said it is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.managedhealthcareexecutive.com/view/cvs-health-cigna-signal-support-for-coverage-of-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 committed}}}\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cmaking out-of-state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  healthcare services more accessible and affordable\u8221\'20\'1D for employees in states with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. In 2024, it has given Raga $125,000.\par \par \uc2 The pattern of companies donating through Raga to Rokita \u8211\'20\'13 and other politicians at odds with professed corporate values \u8211\'20\'13 is repeated regarding climate policy. Amazon, Doordash and \uc2 CVS Health\uc2  are also publicly committed to action to combat climate change. In Indiana, Rokita has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wthitv.com/news/indiana-attorney-general-leads-lawsuit-against-epas-climate-change-mandate/article_f2789390-6ee8-11ef-a987-3f94b014ae20.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prominently}}}\uc2  involved in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.ag.ky.gov/Press%2520Release%2520Attachments/2024-03-06%2520Petition%2520for%2520Review.pdf&sa=D&source=docs&ust=1730155924638875&usg=AOvVaw043Bs0EyrXfJ6YlfDpMBDD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuits}}}\uc2  against the \uc2 US Environmental Protection Agency{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ago.wv.gov/Documents/SEC%20Climate%20Disclosure%20Petition%20for%20Review.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and}}}\uc2  the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  over carbon emissions standards.\par \par \uc2 None of the companies responded to requests for comment. Last year, in response to \uc2 Guardian{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/03/anti-abortion-lawmakers-donation-amazon-google-comcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reporting}}}\uc2  about donations to 527 committees used for efforts to pass a strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in North Carolina, a spokesperson for the software giant \uc2 Intuit\uc2  outlined one corporate defense.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur financial support does not indicate a full endorsement of every position taken by an individual policymaker or organization,\u8221\'20\'1D the spokesperson said. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Intuit\uc2  is non-partisan and works with policymakers and leaders from both sides of the aisle to advocate for our customers. We believe engagement with policymakers is essential to a robust democracy and political giving is just one of the many ways \uc2 Intuit\uc2  engages on behalf of its customers, employees, and the communities it serves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the same report, a \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  spokesperson {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2023/jun/03/anti-abortion-lawmakers-donation-amazon-google-comcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  527 committees could only use its donations for \u8220\'20\'1Coperational and administrative purposes, not to support any candidates or ballot initiatives\u8221\'20\'1D. The CPA argued that given 527 committees exist to elect governors, attorneys general and other state officials, that is a distinction without a difference.\par \par \uc2 In a statement to the Guardian about donations to Raga by companies publicly committed to supporting rights Republican attorneys general have attacked, Bruce Freed, president of CPA and a co-author of the 2024 report, said: \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s political environment makes it even more important that companies have policies and a framework in place for approaching, managing and evaluating the risks of political spending.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey need this to give them control over their spending and to protect themselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mike Schmul, the chair of the Indiana Democratic party, said his party\u8217\'20\'19s candidate against Rokita, Destiny Wells, was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe only candidate in the race for AG who has received the support of Hoosiers first, not special interests and out-of-state mega-donors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Todd Rokita\uc2  is out of touch with the issues that matter, attacking women and doctors, and threatening the medical privacy of Hoosiers. The choice is clear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241031ekav002pj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
