\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US elections live: Harris addresses first-time voters as Trump performs \u8216\'20\'18garbageman\u8217\'20\'19 stunt \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); with Maanvi Singh, Maya Yang and Daniel Lavelle (earlier) \par \uc2 12,243 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 October 2024\par 02:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. You can find all of our US elections coverage here.Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss important US election coverage. Get our free app and sign up for election alerts\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now \u8211\'20\'13 thanks for following along. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a summary of day:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 57.5 million people have already voted in US election. With six days until the 2024 election, more than 57.5 million Americans have already voted as of Wednesday afternoon, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://election.lab.ufl.edu/early-vote/2024-early-voting/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Election Lab}}}\uc2  at the \uc2 University of Florida\uc2 . Of the 57 million, just over 30 million voted early in-person and about 27 million voted by early mail.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/30/politics/cnn-polls-michigan-wisconsin-pennsylvania-blue-wall/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new CNN poll}}}\uc2  shows \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  leading over Trump by six points in Wisconsin and five points in Michigan, key battleground states. Harris leads Trump by 48% to 43% among likely voters in Michigan and 51% to 45% in Wisconsin. The candidates are tied at 48% in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Puerto Rican reggaeton singer Nicky Jam has withdrawn his support for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  after comedian Tony Hinchcliffe called Puerto Rico a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden rally on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CNever in my life did I think that a month later a comedian would come to criticize my country, to speak poorly of my country, and therefore I renounce any support to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and move aside from any political situation. Puerto Rico deserves respect,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump and Harris each held rallies in Wisconsin. Trump riffed on his appearance in a garbage truck earlier, and wore a reflective vest of the kind often worn by sanitation workers. The crowd laughed as he said that he liked the vest because it was flattering. Harris spoke to a hugely enthusiastic crowd and seemed at ease and energetic. The strongest part of her speech was when she addressed first-time voters, specifically, telling them that issues including the climate crisis, gun control and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions weren\u8217\'20\'19t political to them: these were their lived experience.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/30/bernie-sanders-israel-gaza-harris-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an op-ed for the Guardian}}}\uc2 , Bernie Sanders, the independent senator from Vermont, addresses progressives\u8217\'20\'19 concerns about voting for Harris given the administration\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  held a campaign rally in Raleigh, North Carolina, this afternoon. \u8220\'20\'1CUnlike \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe people who disagree with me are the enemy,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris said that she strongly disagrees with criticisms of people based on who they voted for. Speaking on the tarmac at Joint Base Andrews on Wednesday following \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D remarks, Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/kamala-harris-says-strongly-disagrees-criticism-people-based-vote-rcna178013"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that Biden had \u8220\'20\'1Cclarified his comments\u8221\'20\'1D, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI strongly disagree with any criticism of people based on who they voted for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arnold Schwarzenegger, the actor and former California governor, has announced he is endorsing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 . He joins a running list of Republicans crossing party lines to vote against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  has paused the ruling by a lower court that would have restored voting rights to approximately 1,600 voters in Virginia. In its brief order, the supreme court wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CThe application for stay presented to The Chief Justice and by him referred to the Court is granted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  has hailed the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cvictory for common sense and election fairness\u8221\'20\'1D. Youngkin had ordered state officials to identify and cancel the voter registration of alleged non-citizens unless they could prove their citizenship in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  appeared on Good Morning America, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CWe know it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be close, but we\u8217\'20\'19re going to win this thing.\u8221\'20\'1D Speaking to host George Stephanopoulos, Walz said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got the better ground game, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got the excitement, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got the momentum on our side.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Many Puerto Ricans who have moved to the mainland will be able to make their voices heard on 5 November, with large communities in Pennsylvania and Florida being targeted by both campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Those who remain in the territory meanwhile, have made numerous efforts to become a state in their own right. The island has more people than the five smallest states combined and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/20/puerto-rico-washington-dc-statehood-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statehood is supported}}}\uc2  by many, but the final decision lies with Congress \u8211\'20\'13 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jul/20/puerto-rico-statehood-independent-free-association-debate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent efforts have stalled}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Those delays and persistent disfranchisement means some Puerto Ricans are eager to leave the US orbit altogether.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, alongside elections for local politicians and an informal straw poll for their favoured presidential candidate, they will vote in their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2017/jun/10/puerto-rico-vote-statehood-us-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seventh non-binding referendum on status}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 this time putting full and partial independence up against statehood.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not fair that that all of these decisions are being made as if we were savages, as if we were people who can\u8217\'20\'19t have self determination,\u8221\'20\'1D Betancourt says. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t want to vote for the United States \u8211\'20\'13 I want to vote for the president of Puerto Rico.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/us-election-puerto-rico-joe-biden-donald-trump-comedian-comments-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I feel robbed\u8217\'20\'19: the millions of residents in US territories like Puerto Rico who can\u8217\'20\'19t vote in presidential race}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 Residents have no say over Washington\u8217\'20\'19s decisions that control their everyday lives, according to Karina Claudio Betancourt, a student in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/puerto-rico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Puerto Rico}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s capital city, San Juan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CElections impact us because the president decides what to do or not to do with Puerto Rico right now,\u8221\'20\'1D they say.\par \par \uc2 Betancourt points to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/22/hurricane-maria-puerto-rico-trump-delayed-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 response to Hurricane Maria}}}\uc2 , which devastated the island, and the Obama administration\u8217\'20\'19s imposition of a board controlling government funding.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBasic transportation and health services and things that impact us day-to-day are decided by the \uc2 Congress of the United States\uc2  and by this fiscal oversight board, but we don\u8217\'20\'19t get to vote for any of that,\u8221\'20\'1D they say. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are fed up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/us-election-puerto-rico-joe-biden-donald-trump-comedian-comments-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I feel robbed\u8217\'20\'19: the millions of residents in US territories like Puerto Rico who can\u8217\'20\'19t vote in presidential race}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden rally was meant to be a triumphant return to the city that made his name. Instead, the event has reheated simmering tensions on the island territory of Puerto Rico, where locals say they feel like second-class citizens, days out from a historic US election.\par \par \uc2 Comments from a comedian at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/27/trump-madison-square-garden-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally}}}\uc2  this week, describing Puerto Rico as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D, might have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/puerto-rico-republican-chief-demands-trump-apology-rally-racist-remarks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired up local resentment against the Republican candidate}}}\uc2 , but those who live there will be unable to show their anger through the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 Residents of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/puerto-rico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Puerto Rico}}}\uc2  are among the more than 3 million Americans whose votes won\u8217\'20\'19t count, when the country elects its president next week.\par \par \uc2 Most residents of the US territories \u8211\'20\'13 Puerto Rico, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/guam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guam}}}\uc2 , American Samoa, the US Virgin Islands and the Northern Marianas \u8211\'20\'13 are citizens and pay federal taxes. Many have family on the mainland.\par \par \uc2 But the territories have no votes in the electoral college that ultimately decides the president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re just basically captive to whatever Congress and the president want to do to them,\u8221\'20\'1D says Luis Fuentes-Rohwer, a law professor at \uc2 Indiana University\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CTo be a citizen means to be a member of the political community. Not in the US.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s one of the few things uniting the disparate territories, which range from Puerto Rico, home to 3 million citizens in the Caribbean, to American Samoa, closer to Australia than America with a population of just 50,000.\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/31/us-election-puerto-rico-joe-biden-donald-trump-comedian-comments-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I feel robbed\u8217\'20\'19: the millions of residents in US territories like Puerto Rico who can\u8217\'20\'19t vote in presidential race}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42am GMT\par \par \uc2 One reason for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s energy: as we reported earlier, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/30/politics/cnn-polls-michigan-wisconsin-pennsylvania-blue-wall/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new CNN poll}}}\uc2  shows \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  leading over Trump by six points in the state.\par \par \uc2 Harris leads Trump by 51% to 45% among likely voters in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 A tale of two Wisconsin rallies: Trump kept his relatively tight, for him \u8211\'20\'13 it was just over 60 minutes \u8211\'20\'13 while Harris spoke for her usual 20 minutes.\par \par \uc2 Trump riffed on his appearance in a garbage truck earlier, and wore a reflective vest of the kind often worn by sanitation workers. The crowd laughed as he said that he liked the vest because it was flattering.\par \par \uc2 Harris spoke to a hugely enthusiastic crowd and seemed at ease and energetic. The strongest part of her speech was when she addressed first-time voters, specifically, telling them that issues including the climate crisis, gun control and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions weren\u8217\'20\'19t political to them: these were their lived experience.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris ends that hugely energetic speech, in response to which she received very loud cheers from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.23am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris addresses first-time voters: 'This is not political. This is your lived experience'\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe love our country. And when you love something, you fight for it,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s speech tonight, unsurprisingly, is a combination of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/kamala-harris-turn-the-page-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 last night\u8217\'20\'19s major address}}}\uc2  in Washington DC and her previous speeches.\par \par \uc2 Her speech was interrupted near the start by a person calling for a ceasefire in Gaza, and she responded quickly. If that person continued shouting \u8220\'20\'1CCeasefire!\u8221\'20\'1D the sound was drowned out by the crowd cheering when Harris said: \u8220\'20\'1CI am speaking now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris addresses young, first-time voters: \u8220\'20\'1CYou, who grew up with active shooter drills, are fighting to keep this country safe. You, who have fewer rights than your mothers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also addressed the climate crisis, an issue that has been on the backburner for the Democrats during this campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not political,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is your lived experience\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris repeats her line: if Trump is elected, \u8220\'20\'1Con day one he will walk into the Oval Office with an enemies list,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CI will walk in with a to-do list focused on your needs. And at the top of my list will be bringing down your cost of living.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.09am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is time for a new generation of leadership in America,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 Harris repeats her record as a prosecutor, saying she isn\u8217\'20\'19t afraid of a tough fight.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you give me the chance to fight on your behalf as president, there is nothing in the world that will stand in my way of fighting for you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo Madison, early voting has started [\u8230\'20\'26] you can vote through November 3rd. And we need you to vote early, Wisconsin,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd make no mistake: we will win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris is energetic, the crowd is energetic.\par \par \uc2 Someone in the crowd is chanting: \u8220\'20\'1CCeasefire now!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris stops her speech. \u8220\'20\'1CListen,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, \u8220\'20\'1Cwe all want the war in Gaza to end.\u8221\'20\'1D She says she will do everything in her power to make that happen. Everyone has a right to be heard, she says. \u8220\'20\'1CBut right now, I am speaking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 There is a sustained and very loud cheer from the crowd \u8211\'20\'13 this is one of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s most famous lines.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.12am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris holds rally in Madison, Wisconsin\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is on stage now in Madison, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s good to be back,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd many of you may know when I was five years old, my parents taught at the \uc2 University of Wisconsin\uc2 , Madison.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 In the days leading up to the election, mysterious monuments continue to pop up in cities across the US poking fun at candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his supporters, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Olivares reports:\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday in Maja Park in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/philadelphia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Philadelphia}}}\uc2 , a large statue of Trump was propped up. Titled \u8220\'20\'1CIn Honor of a Lifetime of Sexual Assault\u8221\'20\'1D, the monument, showing Trump smiling and holding his hand in a suggestive manner, quotes from the infamous 2005 recording \u8211\'20\'13 leaked in 2016 \u8211\'20\'13 in which Trump is heard bragging about sexually assaulting women.\par \par \uc2 The monument was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.phillyvoice.com/donald-trump-statue-philly-maja-park/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quickly removed}}}\uc2 , Philly Voice reported.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, a similar satirical statue was found in Portland, Oregon. It was beheaded that day and further damaged by a Portland city council candidate and Trump supporter, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.koin.com/news/portland/city-council-candidate-removes-sexual-assault-plaque-from-pop-up-trump-statue/?utm_campaign=socialflow&utm_source=t.co&utm_medium=referral"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filmed himself}}}\uc2  chipping away at the base of the statue.\par \par \uc2 Read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/donald-trump-comical-statues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mysterious statues poking fun at Trump pop up in US cities}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 Alice Herman\par \par \uc2 There are 13,000 people at the Harris event in Madison, according to the Harris-Walz campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is expected to speak in 40 minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time in Madison, in the swing state of Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump is wrapping up. \u8220\'20\'1CJust in conclusion\u8221\'20\'1D, he says, and repeats various falsehoods, mainly about Harris, whom he earlier criticised for speaking about him too much.\par \par \uc2 Trump begins with various things he will make America again. These include \u8220\'20\'1Chealthy\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cproud\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Csafe\u8221\'20\'1D, and, of course, \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump is once again played off by Village People \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2018/jul/06/ymca-bloom-charting-evolution-gay-anthem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gay anthem}}}\uc2 , YMCA.\par \par \uc2 Village People sent Trump a cease and desist letter in 2023 asking him to stop using the song at campaign events.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.50am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Alice Herman is in Madison, Wisconsin for the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  event. She reports:\par \par \uc2 Mumford & Sons, the British folk-pop band, is now performing \u8211\'20\'13 an offering to the elder millennial rallygoers, who seem way more into this set than Gracie Abrams\u8217\'20\'19s younger fans. (The young woman who sobbed throughout Abrams\u8217\'20\'19s set appears unmoved by Mumford & Sons so far).\par \par \uc2 Harris has rolled out a series of celebrity endorsers and performers during her rallies so far this year, from Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9, who appeared at a Harris rally in Texas, to Jennifer Lopez, who is scheduled to make an appearance at a Nevada rally later this week.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Alice Herman is in Madison, Wisconsin, for the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  event.\par \par \uc2 She reports: Gracie Abrams, a popular gen Z singer-songwriter, is performing in Madison at the Alliant Energy Center, where Harris is scheduled to speak soon. Her performance was likely a draw for some in the crowd \u8211\'20\'13 including the young woman in the risers to my left who has been sob-singing every lyric during Abrams\u8217\'20\'19s performance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump plays a video about Jocelyn Nungaray, who was killed in Texas when she was 12 yeas old by two Venezuelan men who reportedly entered the country illegally.\par \par \uc2 The video features Nungaray\u8217\'20\'19s mother talking about her daughter and what happened, and is incredibly sad.\par \par \uc2 Trump has talked about Nungaray before. During Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate against then presumptive Democratic nominee \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , Trump repeatedly brought up her murder and assault.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.10am GMT\par \par \uc2 As Trump began speaking about his \u8220\'20\'1Cfavorite chart\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the one about illegal immigration that he was talking about on stage in Butler, Pennsylvania when a gunman tried to kill him \u8211\'20\'13 a woman in the audience began shouting: \u8220\'20\'1CFight! Fight! Fight!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s what Trump shouted that July afternoon as the Secret Service hustled him away, and become a rallying cry for his supporters.\par \par \uc2 The audience picked up the chant, and Trump paused to soak it in, before saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s an aggressive youngster. He\u8217\'20\'19s going to go places.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Apparently he didn\u8217\'20\'19t get a good look at who started the chant.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.13am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump is repeating his well-worn, racist and false statements about immigration.\par \par \uc2 He claims he wants to \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect the women of our country\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 from immigrants.\par \par \uc2 He says he is going to protect women \u8220\'20\'1Cwhether they like it or not\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It is a statement with menacing undertones, given that Trump has boasted about limiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access for women: a procedure that can be key to keeping women safe. He has done this despite the majority of Americans supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 More than 60% of Americans now believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe broke Roe v Wade,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump has bragged:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/donald-trump-abortion-roe-v-wade-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump boasts \u8216\'20\'18We broke Roe v Wade\u8217\'20\'19 as \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  dogs GOP election hopes}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has touched down in Wisconsin, where she will be speaking in 90 minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time.\par \par \uc2 Her stepdaughter, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/fashion/2021/feb/18/ella-emhoff-kamala-harris-debut-new-york-fashion-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fashion world darling}}}\uc2  Ella Emhoff, is with her, per the pool report. In a profile published this week, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  called her the \u8220\'20\'1Csecond daughter of New York\u8217\'20\'19s downtown\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump says he has sold 10,000 black Maga hats \u8211\'20\'13 it is unclear whether this is true.\par \par \uc2 The red Maga hat is the most recognisable Trump supporter accessory, and was the subject \u8211\'20\'13 or inciting incident \u8211\'20\'13 of a Curb Your Enthusiasm episode.\par \par \uc2 And more recently:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2024/oct/30/two-women-removed-from-ba-flight-after-altercation-over-maga-cap"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Two women removed from BA flight \u8216\'20\'18after altercation over Maga cap\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump claims that his profession is \u8220\'20\'1Cvery dangerous\u8221\'20\'1D but that if he had to do it again he would, \u8220\'20\'1Cevery time\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump was injured during an assassination attempt in July during which the shooter, Thomas Matthew Crooks, was killed. In September, a second man, Ryan Wesley Routh, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/24/man-charged-trump-assassination-attempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged}}}\uc2  with attempted assassination of a major presidential candidate. Authorities said he spent 12 hours camped outside \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s golf course before the Secret Service spotted him with a rifle. He pleaded not guilty to attempting to assassinate the former president as well as other federal charges.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The orange reflective vest \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is wearing has made him appear even more orange, at least on the Resch Center jumbotron.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s orange-tinged skin tone is a signature part of his appearance, something the left often mocks, and which the right has mocked back with its \u8220\'20\'1Corange man bad\u8221\'20\'1D meme directed at liberal outrage.\par \par \uc2 Trump rarely wears anything but a suit (unless he\u8217\'20\'19s golfing), but is clearly trying to make the most of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comment yesterday in which the president appeared to describe his supporters as \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 something the White House disputes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump is doing a bit now about being reluctant to wear the vest on stage, wondering whether he could wear it over a suit, and so on.\par \par \uc2 He says his campaign staff told him it would make him look thinner, at which point he was sold on the idea. That gets laughs and applause from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI may never wear a blue jacket again,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The audience in Green Bay\u8217\'20\'19s Resch Center stood up for the first 10 minutes or so of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech, but now they\u8217\'20\'19re in their seats.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s worth settling in for a Trump speech \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19ve stretched to about the 90-minute mark lately (about the length of a movie) with the ex-president riffing on all kinds of things.\par \par \uc2 He just played a video of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  mentioning his name in her speeches, which draw a huge applause.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump plays a recording of about 15 times \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has used his name while making speeches during an election in which he is her opponent.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s all she talks about because she and Joe have absolutely no achievements,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says, falsely.\par \par \uc2 He continues talking about Harris.\par \par \uc2 Then Trump talks garbage.\par \par \uc2 One of his advisers said: \u8220\'20\'1CSir, the hottest word right now is garbage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He then says his campaign staff managed to organise the garbage truck on short notice, and that he felt uncomfortable driving it while wearing a suit. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd then they said sir, we have a vest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.35pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trum says the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost beaautiful words to me\u8221\'20\'1D are \u8220\'20\'1Creligion, number one and love number two\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He pauses, then says: \u8220\'20\'1Cand tariffs, number three\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He has said this before.\par \par \uc2 Trump is promising to levy tariffs on all imports in a bid to boost American manufacturing, a proposal that economists say would probably mean higher prices for consumers while angering US allies.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  warned this week that the tariffs could hurt global growth, as it upgraded its forecast for the UK economy.\par \par \uc2 The Washington-based organisation said tariffs trigger tit-for-tat trade wars that impoverish the economies involved in the dispute and the wider global economy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.33pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A reminder of what it is Trump is riffing on:\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday Biden appeared to call supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/joe-biden-puerto-rico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 garbage}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The president clarified that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t mean Trump supporters, but rather the attitude of a comedian who performed at a Trump rally and made several racist statements \u8211\'20\'13 including calling Puerto Rico a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 towards Latinos. The official transcript had Biden saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThe only garbage I see floating out there is his supporter\u8217\'20\'19s \u8211\'20\'13 his \u8211\'20\'13 his \u8211\'20\'13 his demonization of Latinos is unconscionable, and it\u8217\'20\'19s un-American.\u8221\'20\'1D The comment nevertheless set off echoes of Hillary Clinton \u8217\'20\'19s infamous \u8220\'20\'1Cbasket of deplorables\u8221\'20\'1D put-down of a section of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters in 2016.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd by the way, I want to thank all of our incredible sanitation workers across America,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says, in a continuation of his garbage-truck-driver schtick.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.29pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Here is the scene my colleague Chris Stein referred to earlier \u8211\'20\'13 Trump answering questions from reporters while seated in a garbage truck.\par \par \uc2 He falsely stated that Harris was responsible for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s use of the word \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cthe comment made by really both of them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He also wildly overstated his support, calling the remark about his supporters an insult to \u8220\'20\'1Cmaybe 250 million people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump got 74.2m votes in 2020 (to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s 81.2m):\par \par \uc2 enltrArriving in Green Bay, Wisconsin, Trump answers reporters questions while sitting in a garbage truck.. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xegSclxY0q"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xegSclxY0q}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Howard Mortman (@HowardMortman) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HowardMortman/status/1851758007534915987?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re done with their hatred, we\u8217\'20\'19re done with their hysteria,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says of the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments were the direct result of Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to portray everyone who is not voting for her as \u8230\'20\'26 subhuman,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says. This statement is false \u8211\'20\'13 Harris has been careful not to insult Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Just before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  took the stage in Green Bay, a video played showing him in shirtsleeves with a reflective vest on, declaring: \u8220\'20\'1CHello everybody, this is \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2 . Two hundred fifty million people are not garbage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It then cut to his photo op earlier today, where he took questions while sitting in the driver\u8217\'20\'19s seat of a garbage truck and honking its horn.\par \par \uc2 Now he\u8217\'20\'19s on stage, in the same reflective vest.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is on stage. He starts by saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI have to say 250 million Americans are not garbage\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ambiguous comments yesterday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Turnout at rallies is no guarantee of election victory, but the Trump campaign must be pleased with the sight in Green Bay tonight.\par \par \uc2 Just about every seat in the approximately 10,000-seat Resch Center is full, with the former president yet to take the stage.\par \par \uc2 Brown county, of which Green Bay is the seat, is friendly GOP territory, voting for Republican presidents in every recent election, with the exception of when \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  was first elected in 2008, and when \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  was re-elected in 1996.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to speak soon at a rally in Green Bay, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 This is Helen Sullivan taking over our live US politics coverage. I\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you any key developments from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech in Wisconsin in two-and-a-half hours\u8217\'20\'19 time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a wrap-up of the day\u8217\'20\'19s key events:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/30/politics/cnn-polls-michigan-wisconsin-pennsylvania-blue-wall/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new CNN poll}}}\uc2  shows \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  leading over Trump by 6 points in Wisconsin and 5 points in Michigan, key battleground states. Harris leads Trump by 48% to 43% among likely voters in Michigan and 51% to 45% in Wisconsin. The candidates are tied at 48% in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Puerto Rican reggaeton singer Nicky Jam has withdrawn his support for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  after comedian Tony Hinchcliffe called Puerto Rico a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden rally on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CNever in my life did I think that a month later a comedian would come to criticize my country, to speak poorly of my country, and therefore I renounce any support to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and move aside from any political situation. Puerto Rico deserves respect,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  held a campaign rally in Raleigh, North Carolina, this afternoon. \u8220\'20\'1CUnlike \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe people who disagree with me are the enemy,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said that she strongly disagrees with criticisms of people based on who they voted for. Speaking on the tarmac at Joint Base Andrews on Wednesday following \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D remarks, Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/kamala-harris-says-strongly-disagrees-criticism-people-based-vote-rcna178013"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that Biden had \u8220\'20\'1Cclarified his comments\u8221\'20\'1D, adding, \u8220\'20\'1CI strongly disagree with any criticism of people based on who they voted for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arnold Schwarzenegger, the actor and former California governor, has announced he is endorsing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 . He joins a running list of Republicans crossing party lines to vote against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has paused the ruling by a lower court that would have restored voting rights to approximately 1,600 voters in Virginia. In its brief order, the supreme court wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CThe application for stay presented to The Chief Justice and by him referred to the Court is granted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  has hailed the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cvictory for common sense and election fairness\u8221\'20\'1D. Youngkin had ordered state officials to identify and cancel the voter registration of alleged non-citizens unless they could prove their citizenship in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  appeared on Good Morning America, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe know it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be close but we\u8217\'20\'19re going to win this thing.\u8221\'20\'1D Speaking to host George Stephanopoulos, Walz said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got the better ground game, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got the excitement, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got the momentum on our side.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is taking questions from reporters while sitting in a garbage truck branded with his campaign logo.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis truck is in honor of Kamala and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s quite a move, days after his campaign caught flack for platforming a comedian who compared Puerto Rico with an island of garbage.\par \par \uc2 Asked about reports that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , who has become a close ally, has been in communication with Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , Trump responded: \u8220\'20\'1CElon is a great guy, he\u8217\'20\'19s one of our geniuses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Chris Stein is in Green Bay, reporting on the Trump rally there.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is holding a rally this evening in Green Bay, Wisconsin, and booked himself perhaps the best warm-up speaker he could hope to get in the football-mad city: Brett Favre, a legendary former quarterback for the Green Bay Packers NFL team.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have not done an event like this before, but I\u8217\'20\'19ve decided it\u8217\'20\'19s time,\u8221\'20\'1D Favre told the crowd at an indoor arena next to the football stadium, where quite a few people had forgone wearing Maga hats and Trump shirts in favor of Packers jerseys. One of the last small cities with an \uc2 NFL\uc2  team in the United States, Green Bay sits in Brown county, a Republican-leaning area of a swing state that\u8217\'20\'19s regarded as one of the most evenly divided in the country.\par \par \uc2 After lamenting the financial damage done by inflation and the human toll of fentanyl overdoses, Favre said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve already had President Trump once. We\u8217\'20\'19ve already seen Kamala in action. We can compare, and we know this is better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo, it\u8217\'20\'19s time to pitch Kamala, and put in the star quarterback,\u8221\'20\'1D Favre said. \u8220\'20\'1CUSA, it\u8217\'20\'19s a great country. We all know that. Kamala broke it, Trump will fix it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Canvassers for \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s America PAC in Michigan were subjected to poor working conditions, unreasonable quotas, and in some cases were misled about the fact that they would be promoting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Wired reports.\par \par \uc2 From {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wired.com/story/elon-musk-america-pac-blitz-canvassing-michigan-uhaul/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wired}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 In Michigan, canvassers and paid door knockers for the former president, contracted by a firm associated with America PAC, have been subjected to poor working conditions: A number of them have been driven around in the back of a seatless U-Haul van, according to video obtained by WIRED, and threatened that their lodging at a local motel wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be paid for if they didn\u8217\'20\'19t meet canvassing quotas. One door knocker alleges that they didn\u8217\'20\'19t even know they were signing up for anything having to do with Musk or Trump.\par \par \uc2 A representative for Musk and America PAC did not return a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Labor grievances and disputes have been a common thread across Musk\u8217\'20\'19s companies. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has reported on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2017/may/18/tesla-workers-factory-conditions-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 injuries and safety issues}}}\uc2  at \uc2 Tesla\uc2 . Black workers at the company have also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/tesla-must-face-class-action-claims-by-6000-workers-race-bias-case-2024-02-29/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alleged}}}\uc2  race discrimination and harassment. A pregnant worker at \uc2 Neuralink{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fortune.com/2024/06/16/elon-musk-neuralink-herpes-monkeys-pregnant-employee-lawsuit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alleges}}}\uc2  she was forced to work with a monkey that was carrying herpes. Employees at \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.space.com/former-employees-suing-spacex-elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued}}}\uc2  Musk and the company for sexual harassment and whistleblower retaliation, among other wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bernie Sanders: 'We cannot sit this election out'\par \par \uc2 In an op-ed for the Guardian, Bernie Sanders, the independent senator from Vermont, addresses progressives\u8217\'20\'19 concerns about voting for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  given the administration\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war.\par \par \uc2 He writes:\par \par \uc2 I understand that there are millions of Americans who disagree with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  on the terrible war in Gaza. I am one of them.\par \par \uc2 While Israel had a right to defend itself against the horrific \uc2 Hamas\uc2  terrorist attack of 7 October 2023, which killed 1,200 innocent people and took 250 hostages, it did not have the right to wage an all-out war against the entire Palestinian people.\par \par \uc2 It did not have the right to kill 42,000 Palestinians, two-thirds of whom were children, women and the elderly, or injure over 100,000 people in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2 . It did not have the right to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/10/how-a-year-of-war-laid-waste-the-gaza-strip-visualised"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 destroy Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s infrastructure}}}\uc2  and housing and healthcare systems. It did not have the right to bomb every one of Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s 12 universities. It did not have the right to block humanitarian aid, causing massive malnutrition in children and, in fact, starvation.\par \par \uc2 And that is why I am doing everything I can to block US military aid and offensive weapons sales to the rightwing extremist Netanyahu government in Israel. And I know that many of you share those feelings. And some of you are saying, \u8220\'20\'1CHow can I vote for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  if she is supporting this terrible war?\u8221\'20\'1D And that is a very fair question.\par \par \uc2 And let me give you my best answer. And that is that even on this issue, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his rightwing friends are worse. In the Senate and in Congress Republicans have worked overtime to block humanitarian aid to the starving children in Gaza. The president and vice-president both support getting as much humanitarian aid into Gaza as soon as possible.\par \par \uc2 Trump has said that Netanyahu is doing a good job and that Biden is holding him back. He has suggested that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  Strip would make excellent beachfront property for development. It is no wonder Netanyahu prefers to have \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in office.\par \par \uc2 But even more importantly, and this I promise you, after Harris wins we will, together, do everything we can to change US policy toward Netanyahu \u8211\'20\'13 including an immediate ceasefire, the return of all hostages, a surge of massive humanitarian aid, the stopping of settler attacks on the West Bank, and the rebuilding of Gaza for the Palestinian people.\par \par \uc2 Read the full piece here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/30/bernie-sanders-israel-gaza-harris-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How can I vote for Kamala Harris if she supports Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war? Here is my answer | Bernie Sanders}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A Pennsylvania judge on Wednesday sided with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign and agreed to extend an in-person voting option in suburban Philadelphia, where long lines on the final day led to complaints voters were being disenfranchised by an unprepared election office.\par \par \uc2 A lawsuit demanding an extension of Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s 5pm deadline in Bucks county until today was filed this morning after long queues outside the county\u8217\'20\'19s election offices on the last day for applications led to security guards cutting off the line and telling some of those waiting they would not be able to apply.\par \par \uc2 Videos of the scenes were widely circulated on social media, fuelling rumours of voter suppression.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign was joined by the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  (\uc2 RNC\uc2 ) and the GOP Senate candidate \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2  in the lawsuit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/pennsylvania-early-voting-problems-bucks-lehigh-county-2916b3bf337d39635d63f642435aa1f9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alleging}}}\uc2  that voters waiting outside election offices for mail ballots were turned away empty-handed and ordered to leave after the deadline expired at 5pm on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a direct violation of Pennsylvanians\u8217\'20\'19 rights to cast their ballot \u8211\'20\'13 and all voters have a right to STAY in line,\u8221\'20\'1D the Trump campaign said.\par \par \uc2 Judge Jeffrey Trauger said in a one-page order that Bucks county voters who want to apply for an early mail ballot now have until Friday.\par \par \uc2 The queues for late mail ballots were a result of Pennsylvania not having an early on-site voting system at designated spots, as is the case in some other states. Instead, voters can apply for ballots on-demand at election offices before filling them out and submitting them on the spot, a procedure that takes about 10 minutes.\par \par \uc2 The flood of late applicants overwhelmed electoral workers in Bucks county\u8217\'20\'19s administration building in Doylestown, leading to a long queue which was cut off at around 2.45pm on Tuesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/philadelphia/news/early-voting-mail-ballot-pennsylvania-how-county/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to CBS}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Protesters interrupted Harris about 8 minutes into her remarks here.\par \par \uc2 It was difficult to hear what they were saying, but I could hear the word \u8220\'20\'1Cgenocide\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The crowd began chanting \u8220\'20\'1CUSA!\u8221\'20\'1D and Harris reminded the crowd that democracy was on the line in this election. \u8220\'20\'1COurs is about a fight for democracy and your right to be heard. That is what is on the line in this election,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CLook, everybody has a right to be heard, but right now I am speaking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 After another protester interrupted a few minutes later, she said: \u8220\'20\'1CAt this particular moment it should be emphasized that unlike \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe people who disagree with me are the enemy from within. He wants to put them in jail. I\u8217\'20\'19ll give them a seat at the table.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Shawna Barnes, a 45-year old healthcare worker from Philadelphia, said she\u8217\'20\'19s concerned that men aren\u8217\'20\'19t supporting Harris in this election. When she\u8217\'20\'19s knocked on doors, she\u8217\'20\'19s noticed that the women are often all in, but the men are \u8220\'20\'1Ciffy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBlack and brown women are going to come out and support. White women of course are going to support. The men are just kind of like afraid,\u8221\'20\'1D she said as Mr Brightside by The Killers blasted on the sound system. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s about gender, I just think it\u8217\'20\'19s fear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris in Harrisburg, Pennsylvania, promotes her economic plan\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is speaking at the Pennsylvania Farm Show Complex & Expo Center in Harrisburg, where she is promoting her economic proposals.\par \par \uc2 "We stand for working people, we stand for middle class growth and strength,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 She derided \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tariff proposals, and warned that he would dismantle the popular Affordable Care Act. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know what\u8217\'20\'19s on the line. We know that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will try, like he has so many times to get rid of the Affordable Care Act, which would throw, millions of Americans off of their health care and take us back to when insurance companies could deny people with pre-existing conditions,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s team is reportedly considering withholding federal grants from police departments that decline to work with \uc2 Immigration and Customs Enforcement\uc2  (Ice) to ease deportations.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/trump-considering-halting-federal-grants-police-decline-conduct-mass-d-rcna177541"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2  that the former president\u8217\'20\'19s team is working on plans to force sanctuary cities such as Chicago, and states such as California to work with the federal government to help Trump deliver on his promise of mass deportations.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has not independently verified NBC\u8217\'20\'19s reporting.\par \par \uc2 Withholding funding from police departments who decline to work with Ice will undoubtedly face legal challenges. During Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, several states sued the administration after it cut off grants to sanctuary cities, and appealed a court decision that sided with Trump \u8211\'20\'13 running out the clock on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s term before the supreme court could issue a final decision on the matter.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.27pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 57.5m people have already voted in US election\par \par \uc2 With six days until the 2024 election, more than 57.5 million Americans have already voted as of Wednesday afternoon, according to the Election Lab at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://election.lab.ufl.edu/early-vote/2024-early-voting/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the University of Florida}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Of the 57 million, just over 30 million voted early in-person and about 27 million voted by early mail.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 I spotted Minerva Ortiz-Garcia, 68, walking around with a small Puerto Rican flag before the rally started so I stopped her to ask what she thought of the racist joke a speaker made before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel horrible. I\u8217\'20\'19m Puerto Rican, I actually started to cry,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CHow could someone say that about an island that is trying to survive [Hurricane] Maria?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ortiz-Garcia, a flight attendant, lives in Easton, which is in eastern Pennsylvania, a part of the state that is extremely competitive and has a huge Latino population. She said she thought many Latino voters in her part of the state were waiting for Harris to reach out to them directly.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that people want her to say something directly,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been chatting to a few voters at a \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  rally here at the Farm expo building in Harrisburg, where there\u8217\'20\'19s a vague smell of horses as the crowd swag surfs and dances to Motown hits such as We Are Family and Aretha Franklin\u8217\'20\'19s Respect.\par \par \uc2 I just spoke with Corine Wherley, a 38-year-old librarian from Harrisburg who is attending her first political rally ever. She said she decided to come to the rally because she was so alarmed by what she heard during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of it was the rhetoric around \u8216\'20\'18this secret\u8217\'20\'19 and other things like that they\u8217\'20\'19re planning on doing,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referring to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comment that he has a \u8220\'20\'1Clittle secret\u8221\'20\'1D with House speaker Mike Johnson, that many took to be a plan to contest the election. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re like: \u8216\'20\'18I can do whatever I want,\u8217\'20\'19 and I think that\u8217\'20\'19s what scares me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Puerto Rican reggaeton singer Nicky Jam has withdrawn his support for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  after comedian Tony Hinchcliffe called Puerto Rico a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden rally on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the singer posted a video on social media saying: \u8220\'20\'1CThe reason I supported \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is because I believed it was what\u8217\'20\'19s best for the economy in the United States, where a lot of Latinos live \u8230\'20\'26 a lot of immigrants that are suffering over the state of the economy \u8230\'20\'26 With [Trump] being a businessman, I felt it was the right move.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to add: \u8220\'20\'1CNever in my life did I think that a month later a comedian would come to criticize my country, to speak poorly of my country, and therefore I renounce any support to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and move aside from any political situation. Puerto Rico deserves respect.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrNicky Jam walks back on his endorsement of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in new video:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI retract any support to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 Puerto Rico deserves respect\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mafI7LDDcP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/mafI7LDDcP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Pop Base (@PopBase) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PopBase/status/1851699475183739217?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 In September, Nicky Jam made an appearance at one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally during which he was misgendered by the former president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo you know Nicky? She\u8217\'20\'19s hot!\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said to the crowd, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CWhere\u8217\'20\'19s Nicky? Where\u8217\'20\'19s Nicky? Thank you, Nicky. Great to be having you here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump: Latin music superstar Nicky Jam. Do you know Nicky? She\u8217\'20\'19s hot\par \par \uc2 (Nicky Jam is a man) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/njv0MxAgEB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/njv0MxAgEB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1834995678113599539?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The battleground states for the White House overlap significantly with the states where Democrats are fighting to keep or gain majorities in state legislative chambers, noted Heather Williams, president of the Democratic Legislative Campaign Committee (DLCC).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the overlap has opened some opportunities for unprecedented collaboration, this environment has also produced steep challenges for state legislative candidates to get their message out, especially through paid communication,\u8221\'20\'1D Williams told reporters on a press call today.\par \par \uc2 Williams noted that the Harris campaign was now spending more on paid ads each week than the DLCC\u8217\'20\'19s entire budget for this election cycle, which is $60m. The gap in resources could heighten the risk of \u8220\'20\'1Cballot rolloff\u8221\'20\'1D, the phenomenon of voters only filling out the top of their ballot without continuing down to lower-level races.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur historical data indicates that, in presidential years, we face the challenge of ballot rolloff most acutely,\u8221\'20\'1D Williams said. \u8220\'20\'1CCommunicating and educating voters on who their state legislative candidates are is incredibly important to mitigate underperforming the top of the ticket.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Although much of the country is focused on the presidential and congressional races, the results of this year\u8217\'20\'19s state legislative elections will have vast consequences on Americans\u8217\'20\'19 everyday lives.\par \par \uc2 On a press call today, the Democratic Legislative Campaign Committee (DLCC) reported that state legislative control appears to be a true toss-up in several battleground states, reflecting the neck-and-neck nature of the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, just 12 legislative seats are deciding six legislative majorities in the biggest battleground states across the country, and all our polling shows that this election will be incredibly close,\u8221\'20\'1D said Heather Williams, president of the DLCC.\par \par \uc2 Democrats are looking to maintain their narrow majorities in state legislative chambers in Michigan, Minnesota and Pennsylvania while attempting to regain majorities in Arizona and New Hampshire. The new legislative maps in Wisconsin also represent a key opportunity for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe stakes couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be higher, as nearly half of Americans currently have their rights protected by Democratic majorities in state legislatures,\u8221\'20\'1D Williams said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDecisions on fundamental freedoms are happening in the states, and many of the dangers of Project 2025 and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s MAGA [\u8217\'20\'19Make America Great Again\u8217\'20\'19] agenda will continue to advance through our statehouses no matter the outcome at the top of the ticket.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris takes lead over Trump in Wisconsin and Michigan - poll\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/30/politics/cnn-polls-michigan-wisconsin-pennsylvania-blue-wall/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new CNN poll}}}\uc2  shows \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  leading over Trump by 6 points in Wisconsin and 5 points in Michigan, key battleground states.\par \par \uc2 Harris leads Trump by 48% to 43% among likely voters in Michigan and 51% to 45% in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The candidates are tied at 48% in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 The vice president\u8217\'20\'19s slim advantage is due in part to \u8220\'20\'1Crelatively strong performance among White voters and White voters without college degrees, two groups which traditionally break Republican,\u8221\'20\'1D CNN said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Interim Summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  held a campaign rally in Raleigh, North Carolina, this afternoon. \u8220\'20\'1CUnlike \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe people who disagree with me are the enemy,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said that she strongly disagrees with criticisms of people based on who they voted for. Speaking on the tarmac at Joint Base Andrews on Wednesday following \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D remarks, Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/kamala-harris-says-strongly-disagrees-criticism-people-based-vote-rcna178013"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that Biden had \u8220\'20\'1Cclarified his comments\u8221\'20\'1D, adding, \u8220\'20\'1CI strongly disagree with any criticism of people based on who they voted for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arnold Schwarzenegger, the actor and former California governor, has announced he is endorsing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 . He joins a running list of Republicans crossing party lines to vote against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has paused the ruling by a lower court that would have restored voting rights to approximately 1,600 voters in Virginia. In its brief order, the supreme court wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CThe application for stay presented to The Chief Justice and by him referred to the Court is granted.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  has hailed the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cvictory for common sense and election fairness\u8221\'20\'1D. Youngkin had ordered state officials to identify and cancel the voter registration of alleged non-citizens unless they could prove their citizenship in two weeks.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  appeared on Good Morning America, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe know it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be close but we\u8217\'20\'19re going to win this thing.\u8221\'20\'1D Speaking to host George Stephanopoulos, Walz said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got the better ground game, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got the excitement, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got the momentum on our side.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI see the promise of America in all the young leaders who are voting for the first time,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve only known the climate crisis and are leading the charge to protect our planet and our future. You young leaders who grew up with active shooter drills, who are trying to keep our schools safe, you who have known fewer rights than your mothers and grandmothers and are standing up to fight for freedom to make your own decisions about your own bodies. None of this for you young leaders is theoretical. This is not theoretical for you. It is not political for you. For our young leaders, this is your lived experience, and I see you, and I see your power, and I am so proud of you,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnlike \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe people who disagree with me are the enemy,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe wants to put them in jail. I\u8217\'20\'19ll give them a seat at the table,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have an opportunity in this election to turn the page on a decade of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who has been trying to keep us divided and afraid of each other. We know that is who he is but, North Carolina, that is not who we are,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is time for a new chapter where we stop with the pointing fingers at each other, and instead let us lock arms with one another, knowing we have so much more in common than what separates us,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is now on stage in Raleigh, North Carolina, for a campaign rally.\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned as we bring you the latest updates.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is claiming \u8211\'20\'13 without evidence \u8211\'20\'13 that Pennsylvania is cheating and has filed a lawsuit against Bucks county.\par \par \uc2 In a post on Truth Social, Trump wrote that the state is \u8220\'20\'1Ccheating, and getting caught, at large-scale levels rarely seen before\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He did not specify what constituted the state\u8217\'20\'19s cheating.\par \par \uc2 In a separate statement, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign announced on Wednesday that it has filed a lawsuit against Buck county for \u8220\'20\'1Cturning away voters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Again, without evidence, the campaign claimed that voters were being turned away early, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://email.press.donaldjtrump.com/c/eJxMk01v4jAQhn9NuDXyt51DDhQ2Fajp11Jouawc24E0iZ1NDCz8-lUMqnqZ5B0_885oZMu2a6rynEb8PkJoX-khQijC0wihj5civzyYc_FyR0-X5s5tnTvuxmM0u7FH9E1bJV_zXtV_z-_bwQ3i6elzd4TftD935pu9NY1NK6tmzPL5RKdUU63MxKSQY4AB4JRO9imWHJY0KbmSSBSSqsIwTBJTCiaIYHRSpQggAgEGkAKMRQw0IZgipoDiVCUmIqDrzTDE2lnZ6C_fH9ouVq6dNOne-24IQ2URyqxsIYwHWZqmsvUQd73zRvnK2dgdfONcPZaNLM4OfRPh-bUe0dGBjh4UZf-uEEVZJwcvvdGm80GP6jCEXygoxJBwRinGCQcJFqNNFszmhI0Q80Eou_mgDd3Ub2jhX7i8PGqSTyPEtPQywnNAI0T5DKDwWb25nelHGwJ2rrvNwmfUlAIzA1liECHcCMUREFqVwjAjAAkQkUAgJWBCgSQQ6IRBQRiSieJEM2kCBK_tQmRYMCoSyAUBCeAiufq829q6k70OtMm64mE7FFgLc15uFl-uymfk9Pg1PeXzafU4W76OuTVqDvllMer7VbVgixru5eY06o_1bMFyC8I6fnT_GdhwW8fzwy_d9nmJV2u3qi-zui7Dxr1aAwrLbfO8twSvP3evW7Xcft482R_bVDrC8-00U8t8Ne3eQzK8CDxHpzP-Tdo2f5r0qbRWxoXxfogI8HuzO8heV9KGO3VM0f8AAAD__7Qf-Lo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania Department of State made clear}}}\uc2  if voters are in line at a county elections office by 5:00PM, the counties MUST give voters the opportunity to apply for their mail-in ballot. Pennsylvania voters were turned away as early as 2:30PM.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s democracy reporter Rachel Leingang reports on the most pervasive myths and lies about US elections:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/30/election-harris-trump-myths-lies-fact-checkfalse-claims-include-that-noncitizens-are-voting-in-broad-numbers-and-attacks-on-the-voting-and-counting-process"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Factchecking the most pervasive myths and lies about US elections}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris rejects criticizing Americans based on who they vote for after Biden 'garbage' remarks\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said that she strongly disagrees with criticisms of people based on who they voted for.\par \par \uc2 Speaking on the tarmac at Joint Base Andrews on Wednesday following \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D remarks, Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/kamala-harris-says-strongly-disagrees-criticism-people-based-vote-rcna178013"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that Biden had \u8220\'20\'1Cclarified his comments\u8221\'20\'1D, adding, \u8220\'20\'1CI strongly disagree with any criticism of people based on who they voted for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response to whether she is worried that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments could increase the country\u8217\'20\'19s political divisiveness ahead of the elections, Harris said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been very clear with the American public \u8211\'20\'13 I respect the challenges that people face, I respect the fact that we all have so much more in common than what separates us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Arnold Schwarzenegger, the actor and former California governor, has announced he is endorsing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He joins a running list of republicans crossing party lines to vote against Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to tune out. But I can\u8217\'20\'19t. Because rejecting the results of an election is as un-American as it gets,\u8221\'20\'1D Schwarzenegger wrote on X. \u8220\'20\'1CTo someone like me who talks to people all over the world and still knows America is the shining city on a hill, calling America a trash can for the world is so unpatriotic, it makes me furious.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I will always be an American before I am a Republican. That\u8217\'20\'19s why, this week, I am voting for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added that electing Trump as president would be \u8220\'20\'1Cfour more years of bullshit with no results that makes us angrier and angrier, more divided, and more hateful\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrI don\u8217\'20\'19t really do endorsements. I\u8217\'20\'19m not shy about sharing my views, but I hate politics and don\u8217\'20\'19t trust most politicians.\par \par \uc2 I also understand that people want to hear from me because I am not just a celebrity, I am a former Republican Governor.\par \par \uc2 My time as Governor taught me to\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Arnold (@Schwarzenegger) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Schwarzenegger/status/1851627802027758005?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The legal dispute centers on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.governor.virginia.gov/media/governorvirginiagov/governor-of-virginia/pdf/eo/EO-35-Comprehensive-Election-Security-Ensuring-Legal-Voters-and-Accurate-Counting---vF---8.7.24.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 7 August executive order}}}\uc2  by the Republican Virginia governor, \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2 , ordering the state to run its voter registration rolls against DMV data on a daily basis to check for non-citizens.\par \par \uc2 The justice department and civil rights groups sued, saying that the state was violating a federal law that prohibits systematic removals of voters within 90 days of a federal election.\par \par \uc2 The US district judge Patricia Giles {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/25/virginia-voter-non-citizen-eligible"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 granted an injunction}}}\uc2  request last week to restore the voters.\par \par \uc2 Voting experts have long warned that comparing voting rolls to DMV data is not a reliable way to find non-citizens on the rolls because there may be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25260010-full-analysis-non-citizens-veris-review"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paperwork errors}}}\uc2  and people can become naturalized after getting their driver\u8217\'20\'19s license. The plaintiffs in the lawsuit said they had identified several people who were in fact citizens but had their registrations wrongly canceled.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and allies had distorted the removals, saying that the lower court decision meant that non-citizens were going to be placed back on the voter rolls. But the state had not provided conclusive evidence that many of those removed were non-citizens.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/supreme-court-virginia-voter-registration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court rules Virginia can continue removing voters from rolls}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The supreme court made the ruling to pause the lower court ruling on its emergency docket and did not give a rationale for its decision, which is customary for rulings on an expedited basis.\par \par \uc2 All three liberal justices on the court \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2 , \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  and \uc2 Ketanji Brown Jackson\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 said they would not have halted a lower court ruling earlier in October ordering the state to restore the voter registrations.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Virginia attorney general welcomes supreme court ruling\par \par \uc2 Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general \uc2 Jason Miyares\uc2  has also lauded the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to strip away voting rights from approximately 1,600 people, saying:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am pleased to announce that the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  granted Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s emergency stay to keep noncitizens off our voter rolls.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr????BREAKING: I am pleased to announce that the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  granted Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s emergency stay to keep noncitizens off our voter rolls.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Jason Miyares\uc2  (@JasonMiyaresVA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JasonMiyaresVA/status/1851626618147495997?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Virginia Republican governor claims supreme court ruling is 'victory for election fairness'\par \par \uc2 Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  has hailed the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling that allowed the state to proceed with its removal of approximately 1,600 voter registrations, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Cvictory for common sense and election fairness\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Youngkin, who ordered state officials to identify and cancel the voter registration of alleged non-citizens unless they could prove their citizenship in two weeks, said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClean voter rolls are one important part of a comprehensive approach we are taking to ensure the fairness of our elections. Virginians also know that we have paper ballots, counting machines not connected to the internet, a strong chain of custody process, signature verification, monitored and secured drop boxes, and a \u8216\'20\'18triple check\u8217\'20\'19 vote counting process to tabulate results. Virginians can cast their ballots on Election Day knowing that Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s elections are fair, secure, and free from politically-motivated interference.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWe are pleased by the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s order today. This is a victory for commonsense and election fairness. I am grateful for the work of Attorney General {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JasonMiyaresVA?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @JasonMiyaresVA}}}\uc2  on this critical fight to protect the fundamental rights of U.S. citizens. Clean voter rolls are one\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Glenn Youngkin\uc2  (@GlennYoungkin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GlennYoungkin/status/1851631305353482681?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme court rules Virginia can stop 1,600 people from voting\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has paused the ruling by a lower court that would have restored voting rights to approximately 1,600 voters in Virginia.\par \par \uc2 In its brief order, the supreme court wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe application for stay presented to The Chief Justice and by him referred to the Court is granted. The October 25, 2024 order of the United States District Court for the Eastern District of Virginia \u8230\'20\'26 is stayed pending the disposition of the appeal in the United States Court of Appeals for the Fourth Circuit and disposition of a petition for a writ of certiorari, if such a writ is timely sought. Should certiorari be denied, this stay shall terminate automatically. In the event certiorari is granted, the stay shall terminate upon the sending down of the judgment of the Court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: The \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  has paused a lower court ruling that orders Virginia to restore some 1,600 registered voters that a state program purged too close to this fall\u8217\'20\'19s election in violation of the National Voter Registration Act {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7OzDN8eGg2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/7OzDN8eGg2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hansi Lo Wang (he/him) (@hansilowang) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hansilowang/status/1851624138323939539?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Last week, Virginia was asked to permit more than 1,600 people to the vote after a federal judge ruled that the state had illegally revoked those rights.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s voting rights reporter Sam Levine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/25/virginia-voter-non-citizen-eligible"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  then that the plaintiffs who brought forth the lawsuit said that many people were being incorrectly identified as non-citizen by the Department of Motor Vehicles by checking the wrong box on a form.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In a new interview with CBS Mornings, \uc2 Tim Walz{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/tim-walz-unity-kamala-harris-speech-ellipse/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said,}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are hungry to come back together \u8230\'20\'26 They\u8217\'20\'19re hungry for us to find solutions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walz, who spoke to Good Morning America earlier this morning, said: \u8220\'20\'1COne that\u8217\'20\'19s talking about unifying us, one that\u8217\'20\'19s talking about bringing folks to the table \u8230\'20\'26 The American tradition of disagreeing and debating but still doing it in a respectful manner.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He went on to add that one of the most important campaign issues was restoring federal \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  across the country, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CRestoration of Roe \u8211\'20\'13 that\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re looking for.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response to Arab American voters in Michigan who have voiced their disapproval towards \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  over her support of Israel, Walz said, \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s one ticket here that is going to find the pathway to stabilization in the Middle East, but also one that is going to respect their human rights here \u8211\'20\'13 push back against Islamophobia \u8211\'20\'13 make sure that they have the right to fully engage in our system here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A former Republican congressional candidate has been charged with stealing ballots in Indiana.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports:\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican}}}\uc2  former congressional candidate was charged with stealing ballots during a test of a voting system in Madison county, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/indiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Indiana}}}\uc2 , state police said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 During the test on 3 October, which involved four voting machines and 136 candidate ballots marked for testing, officials discovered that two ballots were missing, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/indiana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Indiana}}}\uc2  state police.\par \par \uc2 Voter fraud is rare in the United States, and courts dismissed multiple lawsuits of alleged electoral fraud brought by former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/donald-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and some of his Republican allies who accused Democrats of stealing the 2020 election. Trump faces the Democratic vice-president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/kamala-harris/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , in a 5 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/elections/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November presidential election}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/indiana-republican-ballot-theft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican former congressional candidate charged with stealing ballots in Indiana}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Walz says election will be close but hails Democrat ground game\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  appeared on Good Morning America, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe know it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be close but we\u8217\'20\'19re going to win this thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speaking to host George Stephanopoulos, Walz said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve got the better ground game, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got the excitement, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got the momentum on our side.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added that his biggest concern was that \u8220\'20\'1Cthat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has brought up a pessimism to folks, that folks don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that their vote matters. Those votes do matter \u8230\'20\'26 Make sure you participate in this democracy. I think you\u8217\'20\'19re going to see \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continue to spiral downward in this really difficult and hateful rhetoric.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D remark, Walz said, \u8220\'20\'1CThe president\u8217\'20\'19s clarified his remarks, but let\u8217\'20\'19s be very clear: the vice-president and I have made it absolutely clear that we want everyone as a part of this. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s divisive rhetoric is what needs to end \u8230\'20\'26 and what I say is, there\u8217\'20\'19s a place for all of us here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 With the election just a few days away, here is what the presidential and vice-presidential candidates are going to be up to today, according to Politico:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will hold a rally in Rocky Mount, North Carolina, at 1pm ET then a rally in Green Bay Wisconsin at 7pm ET.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JD Vance will hold a town hall with Democrat-turned-Republican \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  in Bedford, Pennsylvania at 5.30pm ET.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will hold rallies in Raleigh, North Carolina, Harrisburg, Pennsylvania, and Madison, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will make appearances on Good Morning America and CBS Mornings before holding campaign events in Charlotte, Greensboro and Asheville, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.22pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 : 'not a time to have anyone criticize Puerto Rico or Latinos'\par \par \uc2 In a new interview on Fox News, \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  critic-turned ally, said now was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a time to have anyone criticize Puerto Rico or Latinos \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Haley, who ran against Trump earlier this year before dropping out the presidential race, added:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve got Americans who are absolutely not going to vote for Trump. And then you\u8217\'20\'19ve got a percentage in the middle who like Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies but don\u8217\'20\'19t like his style. That is what they need to focus on. So when you look at these things, it has got to be a story of addition. This is not a time to have anyone criticize Puerto Rico or Latinos. This is not a time for them to get overly masculine with this bromance thing that they\u8217\'20\'19ve got going. 53% of the electorate are women with will vote. They care about how they\u8217\'20\'19re being talked to, and they care about the issues \u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr"This is not a time to have anyone criticize Puerto Rico or Latinos. This is not a time for them to get overly masculine with this bromance thing they've got going."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  says she hasn't spoken to Trump since June but remains "on standby" if the campaign needs her help {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HlHtSiau9n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HlHtSiau9n}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1851438233638289478?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.45am GMT\par \par \uc2 When Yadira Caraveo, a Democratic party member, won the race to represent Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s eighth district in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/colorado/news/speaker-house-mike-johnson-colorado-8th-congressional-race-impact/?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axioslatino&stream=science"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House of Representatives}}}\uc2  in 2022, she eked out a victory, winning by the narrowest margin of any Democrat in the country. This November, Caraveo is facing yet another close race \u8211\'20\'13 one that could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/colorado/news/speaker-house-mike-johnson-colorado-8th-congressional-race-impact/?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axioslatino&stream=science"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 determine the balance of Congress}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a district where {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.census.gov/mycd/?cd=08&st=08"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly 40% of residents}}}\uc2  identify as Hispanic or Latino, the community will be decisive in crowning a winner. The battle for their votes is mostly playing out not on TV or in town halls, but on social media and local radio.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[Latino voters] are listening to social media and the radio,\u8221\'20\'1D said Sonny Subia, Colorado\u8217\'20\'19s volunteer state director for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lulac.org/about/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lulac}}}\uc2 , the \uc2 League of United Latin American Citizens\uc2 , the largest and oldest Hispanic organization in the country \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/colorado-eighth-district-latino-votes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In a key Colorado county, the local radio plays a pivotal role in securing Latino votes}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.34am GMT\par \par \uc2 Local newspapers are just as relevant as ever this election, as the DNC takes out attack ads.\par \par \uc2 The adverts that paint \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cunhinged, unstable, unchecked\u8221\'20\'1D are running in 25 local newspapers in the seven battleground states. The papers include the Delco Times and Erie Times-News in Pennsylvania or the Macomb Daily and Northern Express in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 On of the ads takes up a full page and is plastered with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s infamous mugshot snapped during his indictment on racketeering charges in Georgia. The ad calls the former president \u8220\'20\'1Cunhinged, unstable, unchecked\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cunfit to lead\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the final week of the election, Democrats are not leaving any stone unturned, reminding voters in key battleground states that their vote means the difference between chaos and revenge with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , or a New Way Forward with Vice President Harris,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Jaime Harrison\uc2 , the chair of the DNC, told the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 Fears grow over Trump's threats to political foes\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s extremist attacks on top Democrats as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy from within\u8221\'20\'1D and talk of deploying the military against political foes if he wins the election are stark signs Trump will endanger the rule of law in America, say former US justice department officials and scholars.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s threats \u8211\'20\'13 singling out ex-speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , Adam Schiff and others as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy from within\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cmore dangerous than China [and] Russia\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 jibe with his earlier incendiary talk of using a return to the White House to seek \u8220\'20\'1Crevenge\u8221\'20\'1D against political foes led by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . He also suggested the military could be used to quell violence at the polls from \u8220\'20\'1Cradical left lunatics\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Those comments, along with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s adamant refusal to say clearly he will accept the election results if he is defeated, prompt critics to say Trump poses unprecedented dangers to the US constitution \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/30/trump-threats-election-enemy-within"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Frightening to consider\u8217\'20\'19: fears grow over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s threats to political foes}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.06am GMT\par \par \uc2 Election too close to call less than a week from polling day\par \par \uc2 The latest polls show \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  enjoys a small lead over her rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . However, the election is still too close to call and a small margin of error could see either candidate in the White House.\par \par \uc2 The key battleground states, so named because there is no entrenched support for Democrats or Republicans and could swing either way, are Wisconsin, Nevada, Arizona, Georgia, Pennsylvania, Michigan and North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 US presidential polls tracker: Trump v Harris latest national averages}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.47am GMT\par \par \uc2 Comedian Tony Hinchcliffe\u8217\'20\'19s controversial set continues to be used as a political football by both sides of the aisle as election night draws closer.\par \par \uc2 The joke that got everyone\u8217\'20\'19s back up was when Hinchcliffe compared Puerto Rico to a floating island of garbage.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said Puerto Ricans are \u8220\'20\'1Cgood, decent honorable people. The only garbage I see floating out there is his supporters \u8212\'20\'14 his, his demonization of Latinos is unconscionable, and it\u8217\'20\'19s un-American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans seized on the president\u8217\'20\'19s line, comparing it to \uc2 Hilary Clinton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cbasket of deplorables,\u8221\'20\'1D comment during the 2016 election campaign.\par \par \uc2 Senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2  of Ohio, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is disgusting. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her boss \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  are attacking half of the country.\u8221\'20\'1D Just one day earlier, Vance brushed off the Puerto Rico island-of-garbage comment, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to stop getting so offended at every little thing in the United States of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden backpedalled somewhat on social media: \u8220\'20\'1CEarlier today I referred to the hateful rhetoric about Puerto Rico spewed by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporter at his \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally as garbage \u8211\'20\'13 which is the only word I can think of to describe it,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CHis demonization of Latinos is unconscionable. That\u8217\'20\'19s all I meant to say. The comments at that rally don\u8217\'20\'19t reflect who we are as a nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33am GMT\par \par \uc2 If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins next week\u8217\'20\'19s election, it would be the first time in US history that a candidate wins based on such a huge lie \u8211\'20\'13 his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/watch/?v=836424705310494"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 falsehood}}}\uc2  that we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2024/09/26/biden-record-republicans-improvements/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst economy ever\u8221\'20\'1D. The former president\u8217\'20\'19s Big Lie has distorted the views of millions of Americans, wrongly convincing many that the US economy is in bad shape.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no denying that many Americans are struggling economically and that inflation was painfully high back in 2022, but inflation is far lower now, and most economists agree that our economy is strong. The unemployment rate is low, inflation is way down, economic growth is solid, and job growth has been remarkably strong. Indeed, the country has added {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/PAYEMS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly 18m jobs}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a record \u8211\'20\'13 under the Biden-Harris administration. Not only that, median household income has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.statista.com/statistics/200838/median-household-income-in-the-united-states/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climbed to $80,610}}}\uc2 , higher than it was in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s last year in office\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/30/trump-biden-harris-us-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump wants you to believe that the US economy is doing terribly. It\u8217\'20\'19s untrue | Steven Greenhouse}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden clarifies \u8216\'20\'18garbage\u8217\'20\'19 comments as Harris makes closing speech in Washington\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our ongoing coverage of the US election campaign as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continue to make their pitches to voters with less than a week to go to election day.\par \par \uc2 Current president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was forced to clarify comments he made on Tuesday after he was seen in an edited video clip saying \u8220\'20\'1Cthe only garbage I see floating out there is his supporters\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said that a pro-Trump comedian\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Chateful rhetoric\u8221\'20\'1D about Puerto Rico was \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Republican politicians and rightwing media outlets quickly picked up the clip to argue that Biden had called Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters garbage, comparing his remarks with \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s labeling of half of Trump supporters as belonging in \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/sep/10/hillary-clinton-basket-of-deplorables-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a basket of deplorables}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Urged by some allies to apologise for racist comments made by speakers at his weekend rally, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  took the opposite approach on Tuesday, saying it was an \u8220\'20\'1Chonour to be involved\u8221\'20\'1D in such an event and calling the scene a \u8220\'20\'1Clovefest\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the same term he has used to describe the 6 January insurrection at the US Capitol.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris will spend election night at her alma mater, \uc2 Howard University\uc2 , in Washington, according to a person familiar with the matter. The person spoke on the condition of anonymity to discuss her campaign\u8217\'20\'19s plans. If elected, Harris would be the first graduate of a historically Black university to occupy the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  took the stump in Georgia. The former first lady\u8217\'20\'19s organisation When We All Vote hosted a rally for more than 2,000 people at an arena in College Park, near Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s airport \u8211\'20\'13 a slickly produced event that was dominated by earnest pleas to vote from a star-studded roster.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2  hit back at those who say Trump is a fascist, accusing Harris and her allies of disrespecting second world war veterans as he campaigned on Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/jd-vance-michigan-trump-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in one of the most hotly contested regions of battleground Michigan}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241030ekau001jn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
