\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Texas woman died after being denied miscarriage care due to  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban, report finds\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 779 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2024\par 22:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Josseli Barnica died days state passed six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and doctors delayed treatment, \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  reports\par \par \uc2 Just days after Texas banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past six weeks of pregnancy, a woman died after doctors in the state delayed treating her miscarriage for 40 hours, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/josseli-barnica-death-miscarriage-texas-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica reported on Wednesday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Experts told \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  that the September 2021 death of Josseli Barnica, a 28-year-old mother, was \u8220\'20\'1Cpreventable\u8221\'20\'1D. Barnica is the third woman reported by \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  to have died in recent years after being unable to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legally or having her medical care delayed.\par \par \uc2 Although US \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans \u8211\'20\'13 which more than a dozen states have enacted in the two years since the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 technically permit the procedure in medical emergencies, doctors across the country have said that the laws are worded so vaguely that they don\u8217\'20\'19t know when they can legally intervene. Instead, many physicians say they have been forced to wait until a patient is on the brink of death \u8211\'20\'13 then attempt to pull them back.\par \par \uc2 Barnica went to the hospital with cramps when she was just over 17 weeks pregnant on 2 September 2021, the day after the Texas six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban took effect, according to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 . (Texas enacted the ban almost a year before Roe was overturned; it now bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  from conception.) When her bleeding worsened the following day, Barnica returned to the hospital, where a doctor concluded that a miscarriage was \u8220\'20\'1Cin progress\u8221\'20\'1D. Another soon concluded that a miscarriage was \u8220\'20\'1Cinevitable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Barnica\u8217\'20\'19s cervix was dilated at nearly 9cm, a condition that left her vulnerable to fast-acting infections, \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  reported. Normally, in cases like Barnica\u8217\'20\'19s doctors will offer medication to speed up labor or perform a procedure to empty the uterus.\par \par \uc2 But Barnica\u8217\'20\'19s fetus still had a heartbeat. And under the Texas ban, doctors could not intervene unless a \u8220\'20\'1Cmedical emergency\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a term that was not defined in the law \u8211\'20\'13 developed.\par \par \uc2 About 40 hours after Barnica\u8217\'20\'19s second arrival at the hospital, doctors stopped being able to detect a fetal heartbeat, according to the report. A doctor expedited her labor using medications and delivered Barnica\u8217\'20\'19s fetus. But after she returned home, Barnica\u8217\'20\'19s bleeding continued and worsened.\par \par \uc2 Within days, she was back at the hospital, where she died of sepsis involving \u8220\'20\'1Cproducts of conception\u8221\'20\'1D, according to her autopsy report. Her widowed husband is now raising their four-year-old daughter, \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 Multiple experts, including OB-GYNs and maternal fetal medicine specialists, told \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  that delaying Barnica\u8217\'20\'19s care ran against the medical standard of care due to the risk of infection. Had she been given options earlier, they told the outlet, Barnica might have survived.\par \par \uc2 Doctors involved in Barnica\u8217\'20\'19s case did not respond to \uc2 ProPublica\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s requests for comment. In a statement, \uc2 HCA Healthcare\uc2 , the hospital chain that treated Barnica, told \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  that doctors exercised independent judgment and \u8220\'20\'1Cour responsibility is to be in compliance with applicable state and federal laws and regulations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the consequences of banning the procedure have become one of the top issues in the US election, as support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has surged in the years since Roe fell and dozens of women have come forward to say they were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/21/idaho-abortion-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied medically necessary care}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has made protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a key plank of her policy platform, while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and other Republicans have tried to evade discussion of it or flip-flopped on the issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy heart breaks for the Barnica family,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2 , a US representative from Dallas running for a Senate seat, posted on X on Wednesday. Allred is running against Ted Cruz, the avowedly anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  senator, and has made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a centerpiece of his campaign. \u8220\'20\'1CJosseli Barnica should be alive today but because of Ted Cruz\u8217\'20\'19s cruel \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, Texas women have been denied the life-saving health care they need. We can\u8217\'20\'19t afford six more years of Ted Cruz.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cruz has recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.texastribune.org/2024/10/07/ted-cruz-texas-abortion-colin-allred/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kept quiet on \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 . He declined a \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  request from comment, as did the Texas governor, Greg Abbott, and the state attorney general, \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the weeks since \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  first reported on two Georgia women, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amber Nicole Thurman}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/candi-miller-abortion-ban-death-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Candi Miller}}}\uc2 , who died after being unable to access legal abortions in their home state, Trump has also largely avoided commenting on their specific cases. However, during a Fox News townhall, the host Harris Faulkner told Trump that Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s family was holding a press call.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll get better ratings, I promise,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/KamalaHQ/status/1846571615498232032"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump joked}}}\uc2 . The crowd laughed.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241030ekau002jw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
