\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  delivers \u8216\'20\'18closing argument\u8217\'20\'19 in Washington \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); with Maanvi Singh, Anna Betts and Daniel Lavelle (earlier) \par \uc2 16,734 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2024\par 03:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is closed now, thanks for following along. Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss important US election coverage. Get our free app and sign up for election alerts\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following. Here is our full story on \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s major address to the nation \u8211\'20\'13 referred to by her campaign as her \u8220\'20\'1Cclosing argument\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/kamala-harris-turn-the-page-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris calls for a \u8216\'20\'18new generation of leadership\u8217\'20\'19 in Washington speech}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.43am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden clarifies 'garbage' remark\par \par \uc2 US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has now clarified his remarks in a post on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X.\par \par \uc2 Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CEarlier today I referred to the hateful rhetoric about Puerto Rico spewed by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporter at his \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally as garbage\u8211\'20\'13which is the only word I can think of to describe it. His demonization of Latinos is unconscionable. That\u8217\'20\'19s all I meant to say. The comments at that rally don\u8217\'20\'19t reflect who we are as a nation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrEarlier today I referred to the hateful rhetoric about Puerto Rico spewed by Trump's supporter at his \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally as garbage\u8212\'20\'14which is the only word I can think of to describe it. His demonization of Latinos is unconscionable. That's all I meant to say. The\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  (@JoeBiden) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JoeBiden/status/1851436643498037614?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 He says that he was referring specifically to \u8220\'20\'1Chateful rhetoric\u8221\'20\'1D made by \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s supporter\u8221\'20\'1D Tony Hinchcliffe (who he does not name) as \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D and not to Trump supporters in general.\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a Trump event at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2 , Hinchliffe called Puerto Rico \u8220\'20\'1Ca floating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Conservatives claimed that Biden was referring to Trump supporters in general as garbage.\par \par \uc2 Biden said, according to one transcript,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe only garbage I see floating out there is his supporters \u8211\'20\'13 his, his demonization of Latinos is unconscionable and it\u8217\'20\'19s un-American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to another, he said, \u8220\'20\'1CThe only garbage I see floating out there is his supporter\u8217\'20\'19s \u8211\'20\'13 his, his demonization of Latinos is unconscionable and it\u8217\'20\'19s un-American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 From the video of Biden speaking, it is unclear which was his meaning, but he has now clarified, saying he was referring specifically to the person and his remarks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.49am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 There is some debate going on online over the transcript of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks \u8211\'20\'13 and whether his use of the word \u8220\'20\'1Csupporters\u8221\'20\'1D contained an apostrophe.\par \par \uc2 Here is one version of the transcript, where Biden appears to refer to the floating garbage being that of a single \u8220\'20\'1Csupporter\u8221\'20\'1D or his supporter\u8217\'20\'19s floating garbage.\par \par \uc2 This could refer specifically to the comedian who made multiple racist remarks, including saying Puerto Rico was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 his garbage being, presumably, the remarks he made.\par \par \uc2 So: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporter\u8217\'20\'19s remarks demonizing Latinos are the only garbage Biden sees:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe full Biden quote from the Zoom tonight, which is being taken out of context: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fHT9PvVjiO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/fHT9PvVjiO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jonathan Lemire (@JonLemire) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JonLemire/status/1851423968583942519?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 However, if what Biden said contained no apostrophe, then he was saying that it was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters (plural) as a whole, who were themselves floating garbage.\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s transcript reads as follows: \u8220\'20\'1CThe only garbage I see floating out there is his supporters, his, his demonization of Latinos is unconscionable and it\u8217\'20\'19s un-American.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 So: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters are the only floating garbage Biden sees.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has contacted Voto Latino, which hosted the event during which Biden made the remarks, for the full video.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am GMT\par \par \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  has claimed that if elected, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has promised to give him \u8220\'20\'1Ccontrol\u8221\'20\'1D of multiple health and other agencies, including the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 (\uc2 HHS\uc2 ) \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC) Food and Drug Administration (\uc2 FDA\uc2 ), \uc2 National Institutes of Health\uc2  (\uc2 NIH\uc2 ), as well as the \uc2 United States Department of Agriculture (USDA)\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr is an anti-vaccination activist or anti-vaxxer. He became fixated on a belief that vaccines are not safe more than 15 years ago.\par \par \uc2 He emerged as one of the leading voices in the anti-vaccine movement and his work has been described by public health experts and members of his own family as misleading and dangerous.\par \par \uc2 RFK Jr dropped out of the presidential race to support Trump.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear whether the claim is true, but Trump has said at multiple rallies, including as recently as Sunday, that he plans to give RFK Jr a role overseeing health agencies if elected.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy has said he would expect any role would involve healthcare and food and drug policy, and reportedly sought a post overseeing health and medical issues under any new Trump administration in exchange for his support.\par \par \uc2 Here is a clip of the comments from HuffPost\u8217\'20\'19s Yashar Ali :\par \par \uc2 enltrRobert Kennedy Jr. says former President Trump has promised him control of the public health agencies.\par \par \uc2 According to him, that includes but is not limited to:\par \par \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  (\uc2 HHS\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  (CDC)\par \par \uc2 Food and Drug\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Y8blzGw3eI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Y8blzGw3eI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Yashar Ali ?? (@yashar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/yashar/status/1851358276937794015?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.36am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden has made many gaffes, though the timing of this one \u8211\'20\'13 a week out from the election, and as the Harris campaign appears to be gaining support as a result of the Trump campaign going low and insulting an important group of voters \u8211\'20\'13 is inopportune, to say the least.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, two months before she lost the election to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, to just be grossly generalistic, you could put half of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters into what I call the basket of deplorables. Right?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The comments were seized on by Trump supporters as evidence of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 contempt for some Americans. And conservatives on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X are seizing on this as a similar remark.\par \par \uc2 Here is a history of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s slips:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/05/joe-biden-verbal-decline-warning-signs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Warning signs: a history of Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s verbal slips}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.16am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58am GMT\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments appearing to compare Trump supporters to \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage [\u8230\'20\'26] floating\u8221\'20\'1D was made during a Zoom webinar with Voto Latino, a non-profit that encourages young Latino voters to vote.\par \par \uc2 Biden was criticising racist comments made by comedian Tony Hinchcliffe at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally at Madison Square Garden, including describing Puerto Rico was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In the crucial swing state of Pennsylvania, most of the 580,000 eligible Latino voters are of Puerto Rican descent.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.54am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump, in his rally in Allentown, Pennsylvania, compared America to a garbage can.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like we\u8217\'20\'19re a giant garbage can,\u8221\'20\'1D he said:\par \par \uc2 enltrHarris at the Ellipse moments ago: "I've lived the promise of America and I see the promise of America in all of you."\par \par \uc2 Trump: "We are a giant garbage can."\par \par \uc2 Quite the contrast. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lWhUZizECN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/lWhUZizECN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Polly Sigh (@dcpoll) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dcpoll/status/1851423060747837653?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has responded to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech \u8211\'20\'13 in which she repeatedly said \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re not going back\u8221\'20\'1D and called on Americans to \u8220\'20\'1Cturn the page and start writing the next chapter\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 as \u8220\'20\'1Cclinging to the past\u8221\'20\'1D, according to a statement from Trump campaign national press secretary, Karoline Leavitt.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.51am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.44am GMT\par \par \uc2 Conservatives are sharing a clip of Biden appearing to cal Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters garbage on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X.\par \par \uc2 In the clip from an interview on CNN, Biden says: \u8220\'20\'1CThe only garbage I see floating out there is his supporters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign spokesperson \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  has just shared the clip, along with unfounded and false claims saying that Harris and Biden will \u8220\'20\'1Chate Americans and will do everything to crush us if they every hold power again\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 enltr2016: "Basket of deplorables"\par \par \uc2 2024: "Garbage... supporters"\par \par \uc2 Kamala and Biden HATE Americans and will do everything to crush us if they ever hold power again.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jAGNuZ0T2Y"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jAGNuZ0T2Y}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  (@TheStevenCheung) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheStevenCheung/status/1851424264978612441?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.53am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.39am GMT\par \par \uc2 NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Gabe Gutierrez reports that the White House has sought to walk back Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks, saying that he was referring specifically to comedian Tony Hinchcliffe, who made the racist remark referring to Puerto Rico as an \u8220\'20\'1Cisland of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D, as himself being floating garbage \u8211\'20\'13 and not Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters.\par \par \uc2 A transcript of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s remarks has not been published by the White House.\par \par \uc2 enltrPres. Biden tonight:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has no character. He doesn't give a damn about the Latino community\u8230\'20\'26just the other day, a speaker at his rally called Puerto Rico a floating island of garbage?\u8230\'20\'26The only garbage I see floating out there is his supporters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Gabe Gutierrez (@gabegutierrez) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/gabegutierrez/status/1851407148535750873?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26am GMT\par \par \uc2 The US president addressed comments made by Trump and his supporters about Puerto Rico and Puerto Ricans, saying that the only garbage he sees \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating out there is his [Trump\u8217\'20\'19s] supporters\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign has called Trump supporters \u8220\'20\'1Cweird\u8221\'20\'1D but has otherwise been careful to avoid insulting the Republican nominee\u8217\'20\'19s base as they try to avoid a repeat of Hillary Clinton \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cdeplorables\u8221\'20\'1D comments.\par \par \uc2 enltrPres. Biden tonight:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has no character. He doesn't give a damn about the Latino community\u8230\'20\'26just the other day, a speaker at his rally called Puerto Rico a floating island of garbage?\u8230\'20\'26The only garbage I see floating out there is his supporters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Gabe Gutierrez (@gabegutierrez) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/gabegutierrez/status/1851407148535750873?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.25am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 After an event in Baltimore and a nearby fundraiser, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  returned home to the White House as the crowd gathered outside for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally.\par \par \uc2 According to the reporters trailing the president today, cheers could be heard from the driveway as his motorcade returned to the White House, one week from an election he expected to be running in. The music is throbbing, with another 45 minutes before Harris is expected to give remarks.\par \par \uc2 According to the \u8220\'20\'1Cpool report\u8221\'20\'1D, Biden was in for the night, meaning there is little chance he would make a surprise appearance at the rally.\par \par \uc2 A report in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/10/27/harris-biden-distance-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios}}}\uc2  suggested the Harris campaign has been trying to keep its distance from Biden, viewing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/biden-approval-rating/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unpopular}}}\uc2  president as a liability in the final days.\par \par \uc2 Biden will campaign for the Democratic ticket on Saturday, in his home town of Scranton, Pennsylvania. But there are no events scheduled for him to campaign alongside Harris, who he effectively elevated after stepping aside in July.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.55am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Allentown, Pennsylvania, Trump distorted an ongoing voter fraud investigation in Lancaster county, Pennsylvania. Officials there are investigating a batch of 2,500 voter registration forms after flagging suspicious similarities between them. Some of the registrations are legitimate.\par \par \uc2 Trump falsely said at his rally just now that there have been fraudulent votes, which isn\u8217\'20\'19t true. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve already started cheating, 2,600 votes, he said. Every vote was written by the same person. It must be a coincidence,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The comment is an example of how Trump is priming supporters to believe there was fraud in the election to prepare for contesting a possible loss.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.52am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.18am GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's national address: summary\par \par \uc2 With that, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s speech is over.\par \par \uc2 Harris, speaking at the National Mall in Washington, which leads to the Capitol where the 6 January 2021 insurrection happened, invoked Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actions that day to portray him \u8211\'20\'13 not for the first time \u8211\'20\'13 as a dangerous leader who cared only about himself.\par \par \uc2 She contrasted that with her history as a prosecutor and protector of all Americans, especially those who are vulnerable.\par \par \uc2 She portrayed herself as pragmatic, a leader focused on uniting Americans, and part of a new generation of leadership \u8211\'20\'13 Harris, who just turned 60, is a generation younger than her rival, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who she replaced on the Democratic ticket.\par \par \uc2 She also sought to portray herself as somebody who is in touch with the struggles and aims of ordinary Americans \u8211\'20\'13 she watched her mother work hard to save up for a house, and watched her mother worry about bills, she said at different points.\par \par \uc2 Harris also said she has \u8220\'20\'1Calways had an instinct to protect. There is something about people being treated unfairly or overlooked that frankly just gets to me. I don\u8217\'20\'19t like it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said that Trump would walk into the Oval Office with a list of enemies, whereas she would walk in with a \u8220\'20\'1Cto-do list\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Finally, she branded Trump a \u8220\'20\'1Cpetty tyrant\u8221\'20\'1D, comparing the moment that faces Americans next week to the war of independence that saw America become independent from the British:\par \par \uc2 enltrVP: "Nearly 250 years ago America was born when we wrested freedom from a petty tyrant. Across the generations Americans have preserved that freedom." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/KamalaDefendsDemocracy?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #KamalaDefendsDemocracy}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/n9ZfzQQslN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/n9ZfzQQslN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CAP Action (@CAPAction) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CAPAction/status/1851417309450997860?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 30, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.20am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.08am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris calls on Americans to 'turn the page and start writing the next chapter'\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn seven days, we have the power, each of you has the power, to turn the page and start writing the next chapter in the most extraordinary story ever told. I thank you and God bless you, and God bless the United States of America,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris calls Trump a 'petty tyrant'\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am in this race to fight for the people, just like I always have,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNearly 250 years ago America was born when we wrested power from a petty tyrant,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 And since then, America has proved that a \u8220\'20\'1Cgovernment for and by the people is strong and can endure\u8221\'20\'1D, she says.\par \par \uc2 The patriots at Selma, Seneca Falls and Stonewall \u8220\'20\'1Cdid not struggle and lay down their lives only to see us cede our fundamental freedoms. They did not do that only to see us submit to the will of another petty tyrant,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.11am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.05am GMT\par \par \uc2 She sees the promise of America in women who refuse to see a future without reproductive freedom and the men who support her, for Republicans who vote Democrat, she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI love our country with all my heart, and I believe in its promise, because I lived it,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 She was a child of the civil rights era, and was taken to marches by her parents when she was still in a stroller.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGrowing up I was blessed to have family by blood, and family by love, who instilled in me the values of community, compassion and faith that have always defined our nation at its best. I\u8217\'20\'19ve lived the promise of America. I\u8217\'20\'19ve spent my life fighting for the people who have been hurt and counted out, but never stopped believing,\u8221\'20\'1D in the promise of America, she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere is my pledge to you: I pledge to seek common ground and common-sense solutions,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI pledge to listen to experts, to those who will be impacted by the decisions I make, and to those who disagree with me,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 Trump wants to put those who disagree with him in jail, she says, and she will \u8220\'20\'1Cgive them a seat at the table\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI pledge to be a president for all Americans, and to always put country above party and self.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.04am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.01am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump is, \u8220\'20\'1Ceasy to manipulate with flattery or favour\u8221\'20\'1D, Harris says. She says the Russian and North Korean leaders want Trump to win.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica, we know what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has in mind: more chaos, more division, and policies that help those at the very top and hurt everyone else.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.02am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00am GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris moves onto the border.\par \par \uc2 She has prosecuted drug smugglers, she says. As president, she will deport criminals. She will work to end cartels.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut at the same time, we must acknowledge that we are a nation of immigrants,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. She will work to help dreamers: a group of people who get their name from the Dream Act, a bill that aimed to grant legal status to young immigrants living in the United States unlawfully \u8211\'20\'13 because they were brought into the country by their parents who were not citizens.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.03am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris moves on to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe idea that a woman who survives the crime of a violation to her body should not have the power to decide what happens to her body next is immoral,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 She repeats her message that people do not have to let go of their deeply held beliefs to agree that the government should not have permission to tell a woman what to do with her body.\par \par \uc2 She will sign \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  into law as president, she says, to huge cheers from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Pro-Palestinian protesters removed from venue\par \par \uc2 Several pro-Palestinian protesters are being removed from the venue. Harris is often interrupted by protests over her refusal to call for an arms embargo against Israel following its devastating invasions of Gaza and Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 Harris did not appear to hear the protesters and kept speaking without disruption.\par \par \uc2 One woman carrying the red, black and green Palestinian flag was removed. \u8220\'20\'1CFree Palestine,\u8221\'20\'1D she shouted and was drowned out by chants of \u8220\'20\'1CUSA! USA!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.55pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris repeats her policies about care giving at home. She will change medicare so that it will cover the costs of home-based medical care, she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm GMT\par \par \uc2 She will work to make sure \u8220\'20\'1Chard-working Americans can afford a place to live\u8221\'20\'1D, she says. She remembers her own mother saving up to buy a home.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about the pride of your hard work,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 There is an obvious contrast here with Trump, who inherited wealth from his property mogul father.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 So far this speech is specific and practical. Harris has sought to portray herself as someone down-to-earth and in touch, a protector who gets things done, who will walk into the Oval Office \u8220\'20\'1Cwith a to-do list\u8221\'20\'1D, and who will work to unite Americans.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur top priority as a nation four years ago was to end the pandemic and rescue the economy. Now our priority is to bring down costs,\u8221\'20\'1D says Harris.\par \par \uc2 She says she remembers her mother sitting at a \u8220\'20\'1Cformica table\u8221\'20\'1D, worrying about bills.\par \par \uc2 Trump, she says, is going to impose a Trump sales tax on everything that is important. It would cost the average family nearly $4,000 a year.\par \par \uc2 Families will pay even more if \u8220\'20\'1CTrump finally gets his way and repeals the affordable care act\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not going back,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are not going back,\u8221\'20\'1D and the crowd goes wild.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'Trump will walk in with an enemy list. I will walk in with a to-do list,' says Harris\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn less than 90 days, either \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or I will be in the Oval Office,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, and the crowd erupts into chants of \u8220\'20\'1CKamala! Kamala!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd on day one of being elected, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will walk in with an enemy list. I will walk in with a to-do list,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will always tell you the truth, even if it is difficult to hear,\u8221\'20\'1D says Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  acknowledges that some voters may not \u8220\'20\'1Cknow who I am\u8221\'20\'1D, and she introduces herself as a prosecutor who has \u8220\'20\'1Calways had an instinct to protect. There is something about people being treated unfairly or overlooked that frankly just gets to me. I don\u8217\'20\'19t like it,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'It is time for a new generation of leadership,' says Harris\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is time for a new generation of leadership in America,\u8221\'20\'1D says Harris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I am ready to offer that leadership as the next president of the United States of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris, who just turned 60 years old, is 18 years younger than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 'For too long we have been consumed by division,' says Harris\par \par \uc2 Harris says that America\u8217\'20\'19s motto, E pluribus unum, which is Latin for \u8220\'20\'1COut of many, one\u8221\'20\'1D, signifies that debate, and disagreement, are important: the fact that a person disagrees with you does not make them your enemy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs Americans we rise and fall together,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica, for too long, we have been consumed by division,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have to be this way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have to stop pointing fingers and start linking arms,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is who \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says, but she is here to remind America: \u8220\'20\'1CThat is not who we are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris is highlighting Trump describing those who disagree with him as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy within\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump is \u8220\'20\'1Cunstable, obsessed with revenge, consumed with grievance and out for unchecked power\u8221\'20\'1D, she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris invokes January 6 storming of Capitol, 'at this very place'\par \par \uc2 Harris says the vote will be between chaos and division, or freedom.\par \par \uc2 Harris says: \u8220\'20\'1CAt this very place, [Trump] sent an armed mob to overturn a free and fair election, an election that he lost. Americans died as a result of that attack,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 She reminds the crowd that Trump was told that the mob wanted to kill \u8220\'20\'1Chis own vice-president\u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , and responded with \u8220\'20\'1Ctwo words: \u8216\'20\'18So what?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.39pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris says next week will be, 'the most important vote you ever cast'\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo listen: one week from today you will have the chance to make a decision that directly impacts your life, the life of your family, and the future of this country that we love,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it will probably be the most important vote you ever cast.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.40pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  takes stage at National Mall in Washington for major 'closing argument' address\par \par \uc2 The US vice-president and Democratic presidential nominee is walking onto the stage now at Washington DC\u8217\'20\'19s National Mall.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGood evening America,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, over the roars of the crowd.\par \par \uc2 The crowd starts to chant: \u8220\'20\'1CKamala! Kamala!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The event is now starting with a performance of the American national anthem, the Star-Spangled Banner.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Washington\u8217\'20\'19s metropolitan police department chief, Pamela Smith, said in a press conference earlier on Tuesday that as many as 52,000 people were expected to attend this evening\u8217\'20\'19s address, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox5dc.com/news/kamala-harris-ellipse-rally-crowd-could-top-52000-people-police-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  Fox5DC.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re trying to confirm how many are there \u8211\'20\'13 but are seeing reports that it is now so full that people are being turned away.\par \par \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Robert Costa reports that at least 1,000 people were turned away at one entrance:\par \par \uc2 enltrEnormous crowd here at Harris event in DC. At least a thousand or so being turned away now at west entrance due to lack of space.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert Costa (@costareports) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/costareports/status/1851400170535059502?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The sun has gone down over \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Washington DC. The stage is set, as promised with a view of the White House behind her, a site her campaign hopes will remind Americans of the gravity of their choice. The crowd stretches from the Ellipse, the park outside the White House nearly to the Washington monument behind us.\par \par \uc2 The crowd just heard from a group of battleground state voters who represent parts of the broad coalition she has built. Amanda and Josh Zurawski, a young Texas couple shared their trauma after Amanda developed complications with her pregnancy and had to wait until she was at risk of losing her life before she received a life-saving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They have been traveling the country on Harris\u8217\'20\'19s behalf, warning about the threat Trump poses to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Bob and Kristina Lange, farmers from Pennsylvania who previously supported Trump, said they would \u8220\'20\'1Cproudly support Harris this year\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe deserve better,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bob Lange, who was met with groans when he admitted to having twice voted for Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CIt made sense because I was a Republican.\u8221\'20\'1D His wife, he noted, was \u8220\'20\'1Cway ahead of the curve\u8221\'20\'1D and only voted for him once.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEnough is enough,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Jenny Poon, a small business owner and mom of two young kids in Phoenix, said she and her husband mailed in their ballots before coming to DC to speak at the rally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday women run our homes. They run our businesses. They run our cities.\u8221\'20\'1D Poon said, surrounded by her family. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd soon they\u8217\'20\'19ll run this country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As supporters were lined up to get into the arena for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally here, a small protest descended on the street just outside the arena.\par \par \uc2 Some waved Puerto Rican flags and held signs that said Latinos for Harris-Walz.\par \par \uc2 enltrA protest outside of the Trump rally in Allentown is being met with chants of \u8220\'20\'1CTrump Trump Trump! Across the street {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/F5XryzMTFs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/F5XryzMTFs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Levine (@srl) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/srl/status/1851361680711704879?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 One of the people marching was Luis Gonzalez, a retired 65-year-old truck driver from Allentown. He wore a sweater with the Puerto Rican flag stitched on it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe guy has no idea what he\u8217\'20\'19s talking about,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI was born in Puerto Rico. That island as well as all the other islands around it are beautiful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor anybody to say that it\u8217\'20\'19s a garbage island \u8211\'20\'13 they\u8217\'20\'19ve never been to the Caribbean.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ve been chatting to a few voters here at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally about their reaction to the racist joke about Puerto Rico a comic made on Sunday at his rally at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some hadn\u8217\'20\'19t heard of the joke and one woman laughed when I told her. And those who had heard it didn\u8217\'20\'19t think it would matter much in the election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was made in poor taste, I have to admit. But \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mark Melendez, 55, who is Puerto Rican and traveled to the rally from New Jersey. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it will affect him, it might.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Several speakers at the rally emphasized their Puerto Rican background and gave the crowd a reason to vote for Trump. Allentown and the surrounding Lehigh valley has a huge Latino population and their remarks signaled how serious an effort the campaign is to court the Latino vote.\par \par \uc2 At least one audience member is holding a sign that says \u8220\'20\'1CBoricuas for Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D using the term to that describes people of Puerto Rican dissent.\par \par \uc2 Jackie Beller, 60, who lives near Allentown thought the joke was funny.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you take a comedian out of context and you look at it as a serious thing, yes you would be offended,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.30pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to address nation in major, 'closing argument' speech\par \par \uc2 With the presidential race deadlocked a week before election day, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  will call on voters to \u8220\'20\'1Cturn the page\u8221\'20\'1D on the Trump era, in remarks delivered from a park near the White House where the former president spoke before a mob of his supporters stormed the US Capitol in a last effort to overturn his 2020 loss.\par \par \uc2 Harris, a former prosecutor, will deliver what her campaign has called her \u8220\'20\'1Cclosing argument\u8221\'20\'1D intended to persuade the vanishing slice of undecided voters, in a location she hopes will remind them precisely why Americans denied Trump a second term four years ago. The Democrat is expected to cast her opponent as a divisive figure who will spend his term consumed by vengeance, leveraging the power of the presidency against his political enemies rather than in service of the American people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that there are still a lot of voters out there that are still trying to decide who to support or whether to vote at all,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Jennifer O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon\uc2 , Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign\u8217\'20\'19s chair, told reporters on a call previewing the remarks on Tuesday morning. She said many Americans were \u8220\'20\'1Cexhausted\u8221\'20\'1D by the tribalism and polarization Trump has exacerbated since his political rise in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/kamala-harris-turn-the-page-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris to urge voters to \u8216\'20\'18turn the page\u8217\'20\'19 on era of Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 While we wait for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to address the nation in 20 minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time \u8211\'20\'13 in a major speech that her campaign has described as her '\u8220\'20\'1Cclosing argument\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 here is a summary of the key recent developments. This is Helen Sullivan taking over our live US elections coverage.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will warn that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cunstable\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cobsessed with revenge\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1Cconsumed with grievance\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cout for unchecked power\u8221\'20\'1D during her speech at the Ellipse on Tuesday night, according to excerpts of her remarks released by the campaign.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New polls show \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  leading \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by one percentage point in Arizona, and Trump leading Harris in Nevada by the same margin. In the polls, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/25257085/cnn-polls-harris-and-trump-locked-in-close-races-in-arizona-and-nevada-as-pool-of-persuadable-voters-shrinks.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published by CNN and conducted by SSRS polling}}}\uc2  between 21 October and 26 October, Harris received 48% support in Arizona among likely voters, while Trump received 47%.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The United States Postal Service\uc2  issued an alert on Tuesday urging voters who choose to vote by mail to send their ballots in by today. In the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.usps.com/newsroom/national-releases/2024/1028-us-postal-service-is-ready-to-deliver-the-nations-election-mail.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  message}}}\uc2 , USPS said that they \u8220\'20\'1Canticipate an uptick of ballots in the mail over the coming days\u8221\'20\'1D and recommended that voters who want to mail their ballots do so at least a week before their election office needs them to ensure it arrives in time. \u8220\'20\'1CIf a ballot is due on Election Day, the Postal Service recommends mailing the ballot by this Tuesday\u8221\'20\'1D 29 October, the postal service said. USPS said that in 2020, 99.9% of ballots were delivered within seven days and 98.3% of ballots were delivered within three days.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Grammy-winning Puerto Rican artist, Bad Bunny, posted a video on his \uc2 Instagram\uc2  on Tuesday in celebration of Puerto Rican culture. The post comes in response to the insulting remarks made at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally on Sunday against the island, where a comedian called Puerto Rico a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D. Bad Bunny\u8217\'20\'19s eight-minute long {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/badbunnypr/?utm_source=ig_embed&ig_rid=cc80a7da-d4b5-40d9-9478-a9f92b5b67ce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2 , posted to his more than 45 million followers on Tuesday, is captioned \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D and highlights Puerto Rican culture, history and people over inspirational music.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Puerto Rico\u8217\'20\'19s Largest Newspaper, El Nuevo D\u237\'00\'EDa, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.elnuevodia.com/english/editorial/puerto-ricans-should-vote-for-kamala-harris/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed }}}\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for President as of Tuesday morning. \u8220\'20\'1COn Sunday, continuing a pattern of contempt and misinformation that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has maintained for years against the eight million of us American citizens who are Puerto Ricans, comedian Tony Hinchcliffe insulted us during a Republican Party event by referring to Puerto Rico as \u8216\'20\'18an island of garbage in the ocean\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D the statement from the newspaper reads.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barbara Pierce Bush, the daughter of \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  and granddaughter of \uc2 George HW Bush\uc2 , has revealed that she is campaigning for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . In an interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://people.com/george-w-bush-s-daughter-barbara-breaks-silence-on-election-to-campaign-for-kamala-harris-exclusive-8735810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 People Magazine}}}\uc2 , Pierce Bush said that she is \u8220\'20\'1Chopeful\u8221\'20\'1D that Harris and her running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will \u8220\'20\'1Cmove our country forward and protect women\u8217\'20\'19s rights\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  held a press conference at his Florida residence and described the marathon New York rally that he held at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  in Manhattan two days ago \u8211\'20\'13 which has been widely condemned for racist remarks from speakers - as a \u8220\'20\'1Clove fest\u8221\'20\'1D. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe love in that room, it was breathtaking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, the GOP vice-presidential candidate, has been rallying in Saginaw in the swing state of Michigan, 100 miles north of Detroit, and criticized opposing politicians calling Trump a fascist in the last week. That includes Harris, whom Vance, a US Senator from Ohio, called unqualified to be president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Lopez will join \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at a rally in Las Vegas on Thursday, the Harris campaign has announced. Lopez will speak on the importance of voting, what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake for the country with this election, and why she is endorsing Harris and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Harris campaign said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House announced that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will travel to his childhood home town of Scranton, Pennsylvania for political engagements on Saturday. The US president has campaigned often in the city as a way of reminding the electorate of his working class roots and pro-union politics.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rapper 50 Cent said that he turned down a $3m offer to perform at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s controversial rally in New York City\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden on Sunday, according to Variety magazine. Deadline also reported that 50 Cent also confirmed that he was also offered money to perform at the Republic National Convention in the summer, but turned it down because he prefers to stay away from party politics.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New polling has found that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s support among young Black men has decreased since August, while Harris\u8217\'20\'19s has grown. A new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://naacp.org/articles/new-naacp-data-displays-progress-reaching-black-male-voters-shifts-key-attitudes-and"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NAACP survey}}}\uc2 , conducted between 11 and 17 October, found that 21% of Black men under 50 years old said they would for the former president, down from 27% in August. Harris\u8217\'20\'19s support among this group jumped from 51% to 59 % over that same time frame, the researchers said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , the longtime Trump Maga ally, is back on air hosting his podcast after being released from prison this morning. He served a four-month sentence for defying a congressional subpoena related to the investigation into the January 6 attack on the US Capitol by extremist supporters of Trump who were intent on overturning his loss to Biden in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Most Americans are prepared to accept the election results as legitimate, according to a new ABC/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll released today. And more than 48.6 million Americans have reportedly voted early in this year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In Allentown, Pennsylvania, the Trump campaign is doing damage control after a comedian made racist comments about Puerto Rico at the former president\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden rally this weekend.\par \par \uc2 Several speakers in Allentown were Puerto Rican: pastor Robert Albino, Shadow US senator from Puerto Rico Zoraida Bux\u243\'00\'F3 Santiago and former mayoral candidate Tim Ramos.\par \par \uc2 About a quarter of Allentown\u8217\'20\'19s population is Puerto Rican and voters there could play a decisive role in the election in this swing state.\par \par \uc2 At Trump rally in Madison Square Garden, Tony Hinchcliffe, a podcaster with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://chartable.com/podcasts/kill-tony/reviews"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a history}}}\uc2  of racist remarks, described Puerto Rico, home to 3.2 million US citizens, as an \u8220\'20\'1Cisland of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will call on voters to 'turn the page' in Washington DC speech\par \par \uc2 With the presidential race deadlocked a week before election day, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  will call on voters to \u8220\'20\'1Cturn the page\u8221\'20\'1D on the Trump era, in remarks delivered from a park near the White House where the former president spoke before a mob of his supporters stormed the US Capitol in a last effort to overturn his 2020 loss.\par \par \uc2 Harris, a former prosecutor, will deliver what her campaign has called her \u8220\'20\'1Cclosing argument\u8221\'20\'1D intended to persuade the vanishing slice of undecided voters, in a location she hopes will remind them precisely why Americans denied Trump a second term four years ago. The Democrat is expected to cast her opponent as a divisive figure who will spend his term consumed by vengeance, leveraging the power of the presidency against his political enemies rather than in service of the American people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that there are still a lot of voters out there that are still trying to decide who to support or whether to vote at all,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Jennifer O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon\uc2 , Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign\u8217\'20\'19s chair, told reporters on a call previewing the remarks on Tuesday morning. She said many Americans were \u8220\'20\'1Cexhausted\u8221\'20\'1D by the tribalism and polarization Trump has exacerbated since his political rise in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Although the vice-president frames the stakes of the 2024 election as nothing less than the preservation of US democracy, her speech is expected to strike an optimistic and hopeful tone, standing in stark contrast to the dark, racist themes that animated Trump\u8217\'20\'19s grievance-fueled rally at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why people are exhausted with him,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said before boarding Air Force Two, where she worked on the speech with advisers on the plane. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are literally ready to turn the page.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12pm GMT\par \par \uc2 How a rightwing machine stopped Arkansas\u8217\'20\'19s effort to roll back one of the strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans\par \par \uc2 In July, a dedicated network of about 800 grassroots organizers in Arkansas had collected the necessary signatures to get a measure on the 5 November ballot that \u8211\'20\'13 if passed \u8211\'20\'13 would have changed Arkansas\u8217\'20\'19s constitution to protect the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for any reason up to 18 weeks of pregnancy. It also would have legalized exceptions for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after 18 weeks, including in cases involving rape, incest, fatal fetal anomalies, and life and health of the mother.\par \par \uc2 The measure did not provide the same rights that existed under Roe \u8211\'20\'13 which protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  until viability, or around 24 weeks \u8211\'20\'13 a fact that organizers said kept national organizations like \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and the \uc2 ACLU\uc2  from getting involved in the effort. But organizers believed that it was a measure that even conservative voters would support. After all, voters in neighboring Kansas, another Republican stronghold, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/03/kansas-abortion-vote-state-constitution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overwhelmingly voted to protect \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2  when its ballot was put to voters in a referendum in 2022.\par \par \uc2 To the dismay and shock of the grassroots organizers, however, the Arkansas initiative was ultimately quashed before it ever reached voters. A paperwork error by organizers prompted a legal challenge by Arkansas\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state, John Thurston, who rejected the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  amendment. On 22 August, the Arkansas supreme court upheld his decision.\par \par \uc2 For Arkansas women, there is no end in sight.\par \par \uc2 A Guardian investigation into the ballot\u8217\'20\'19s demise tells a more complicated story than just a bureaucratic screw-up, revealing a confluence of rightwing actors working in parallel to ensure it never got to voters: a reclusive donor who has helped shape the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement across the US; the inner circle of the Arkansas governor, \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 , who has proclaimed Arkansas \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most pro-life state in the country\u8221\'20\'1D; and judges who are supposed to be non-partisan but are deeply aligned with the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican party.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/arkansas-abortion-ban-ballot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How a rightwing machine stopped Arkansas\u8217\'20\'19s ballot to roll back one of the strictest \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  bans}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.16pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The Stakes: if Trump wins the election, \uc2 Nato\uc2  can expect more turbulence ahead\par \par \uc2 Politeness and convention dictate that European leaders try to sound noncommittal when asked whether a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  presidency would hurt Nato. But despite the rhetoric about \u8220\'20\'1CTrump-proofing\u8221\'20\'1D, Nato cohesion will be at risk from a hostile or isolationist Republican president, who has previously threatened to leave the alliance if European defence spending did not increase.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe truth is that the US is Nato and \uc2 Nato\uc2  is the US; the dependence on America is essentially as big as ever,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jamie Shea, a former Nato official who teaches at the \uc2 University of Exeter\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CTake the new Nato command centre to coordinate assistance for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ukraine}}}\uc2  in Wiesbaden, Germany. It is inside a US army barracks, relying on US logistics and software.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 US defence spending will hit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nato.int/nato_static_fl2014/assets/pdf/2024/6/pdf/240617-def-exp-2024-en.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a record $968bn}}}\uc2  in 2024 (the proportion the US spends in Europe is not disclosed). The budgets of the 30 European allies plus Canada amount to $506bn, 34% of the overall total. It is true that 23 out of 32 members expect to spend more than 2% of GDP on defence this year, but in 2014, when the target was set, non-US defence spending in Nato was 24%. Lower than now but not dramatically so.\par \par \uc2 There are more than 100,000 US personnel stationed in Europe, more than the British army, a figure increased by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/29/us-to-increase-military-forces-across-europe-joe-biden-announces"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 20,000 by Joe Biden}}}\uc2  in June 2022 in response to Russia\u8217\'20\'19s attack on Ukraine. US troops have long been based in Germany, but a 3,000-strong brigade was moved by Biden into Romania, a forward corps command post is based in Poland, and US troops contribute to defending the Baltic states, while fighter and bomber squadrons are based in the UK and five naval destroyers in Spain.\par \par \uc2 Boris Pistorius, Germany\u8217\'20\'19s defence minister, was recently asked whether \uc2 Nato\uc2  was ready for Trump. \u8220\'20\'1CElections will have a result whatever,\u8221\'20\'1D he began, before acknowledging that much of Europe had been slow to increase defence budgets, missing the warning of Russia\u8217\'20\'19s capture of Crimea in Ukraine in 2014 and only reacting substantively in 2022 after Russia\u8217\'20\'19s full invasion. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we did was push the snooze button and turn around,\u8221\'20\'1D Pistorius said.\par \par \uc2 Read the full analysis here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/if-trump-wins-the-election-nato-can-expect-more-turbulence-ahead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 If Trump wins the election, Nato can expect more turbulence ahead}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s case, Kennedy had asked the supreme court to remove him from the ballot by covering his name with stickers, which officials said would be a herculean task.\par \par \uc2 The state\u8217\'20\'19s law prohibits the removal of a nominee\u8217\'20\'19s name from the ballot, stating that \u8220\'20\'1Cany person who files nomination papers and qualifies to appear on the ballot may not decline nomination\u8221\'20\'1D, with the only exception being in the case of that candidate\u8217\'20\'19s death.\par \par \uc2 Similarly, in Michigan, officials said that Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s request would be impossible to fulfill, requiring counties reprint and distribute new ballots, which would cause delays.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s arguments to have his named removed from swing state ballots run contrary to his assertions in a New York case, where he fought to remain on the ballot after he was disqualified for listing a friend\u8217\'20\'19s address as his residence.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Supreme court rejects appeal to remove \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  from swing state ballots\par \par \uc2 The highest court rejected an emergency appeal to remove \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , a third-party presidential candidate that has dropped out of the race and endorsed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , from the ballots in Wisconsin and Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy wanted to have himself remove from the ballots in these key swing states, arguing that keeping him on would violate his first amendment rights. But with early voting already under way, Wisconsin and Michigan said that removing him from the ballot now would be impossible.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear how Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s presence on the ballot will affect the election, and how many voters might choose to cast votes for Kennedy who would otherwise have voted for Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.45pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.09pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At the business roundtable in Pennsylvania, a woman from Puerto Rico who worked as a Medicare provider asked Trump about his plans for the health program.\par \par \uc2 The campaign\u8217\'20\'19s emphasis on the questioner\u8217\'20\'19s Puerto Rican heritage was, no doubt, a way to manage the fallout from a comedian\u8217\'20\'19s racist comments about the island during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally this weekend. She told the former president that Puerto Ricans stand behind him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think no president said more for Puerto Rico than I have,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump responded, noting that the administration had approved aid for the island after Hurricane Maria. (It\u8217\'20\'19s worth noting that his administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2021/apr/22/hurricane-maria-puerto-rico-trump-delayed-aid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cunnecessarily\u8221\'20\'1D delayed}}}\uc2  $20bn in aid to Puerto Rico due to bureaucratic obstacles, according to an internal review)\par \par \uc2 The roundtable is being hosted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theverge.com/2024/10/29/24282957/progress-2028-elon-musk-building-americas-future-ads-pac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Building America\u8217\'20\'19s Future}}}\uc2 , an \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 -funded Super Pac that has been putting out misleading campaign ads about Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At a business roundtable in Pennsylvania, where he was billed to discuss issues impacting senior citizens, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is repeating a stump speech about migrants at the US border.\par \par \uc2 He told the crowd of supporters that he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t believe polls showing that the economy and inflation are the top issues for voters. \u8220\'20\'1CI think this is the biggest senior issue,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said about migration. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re destroying our country, they\u8217\'20\'19re ruining our country,\u8221\'20\'1D he said of migrants.\par \par \uc2 As his campaign seeks to manage the fallout from this Madison Square rally, where a comedian\u8217\'20\'19s racist joke about Puerto Rico has unleashed angry backlash, Trump has not scaled back any of the anger, vitriol or racist rhetoric that has been at the core of his message to voters.\par \par \uc2 In his rambling comments, Trump also touched on transgender rights, lying that Democrats \u8220\'20\'1Cwant transgender operations for almost everybody in the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Deterioration of the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s subscriber base continued on Tuesday, hours after its proprietor, \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 , defended the decision to forgo formally endorsing a presidential candidate as part of an effort to restore trust in the media.\par \par \uc2 The publication has now shed 250,000 subscribers, or 10% of the 2.5 million customers it had before the decision was made public on Friday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/davidfolkenflik/status/1851309625125081336"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the NPR reporter David Folkenflik}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A day earlier, 200,000 had left {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/10/28/nx-s1-5168416/washington-post-bezos-endorsement-president-cancellations-resignations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the same outlet}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The numbers are based on the number of cancellation emails that have been sent out, according to a source at the paper, though the subscriber dashboard is no longer viewable to employees.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  has not commented on the reported numbers.\par \par \uc2 The famed \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  journalist Bob Woodward said on Tuesday he disagreed with the paper\u8217\'20\'19s decision, adding that the outlet was \u8220\'20\'1Can institution reporting about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and what he\u8217\'20\'19s done and supported by the editorial page\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Bezos framed the decision as an effort to support journalists and journalism, noting that in \u8220\'20\'1Csurveys about trust and reputation, journalists and the media have regularly fallen near the very bottom, often just above Congress\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But in this election year, he noted, the press had fallen below Congress, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/651977/americans-trust-media-remains-trend-low.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup poll}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have managed to fall below Congress. Our profession is now the least trusted of all. Something we are doing is clearly not working,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2024/oct/29/washington-post-subscriber-cancellations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post cancellations hit 250,000 \u8211\'20\'13 10% of subscribers}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 In her remarks this evening, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is also expected to say that returning Trump to power will bring \u8220\'20\'1Cmore chaos\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cmore division\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI offer a different path,\u8221\'20\'1D she will say, in a speech dedicated to the still-undecided slice of US voters. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I ask for your vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris will pledge to \u8220\'20\'1Cseek common ground and commonsense solutions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnlike \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe people who disagree with me are the enemy. He wants to put them in jail. I\u8217\'20\'19ll give them a seat at my table,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris is expected to say.\par \par \uc2 The Democrat has built a broad coalition that includes conservative anti-Trump Republicans such as \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the former Wyoming congresswoman and her father, the former vice-president \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI pledge to be a President for all Americans,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris will say, \u8220\'20\'1Cto always put country above party and above self.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris to warn Trump is 'unstable' and 'out for unchecked power' in Tuesday speech\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will warn that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cunstable \u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cobsessed with revenge\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1Cconsumed with grievance\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cout for unchecked power \u8221\'20\'1D during her speech at the Ellipse on Tuesday night, according to excerpts of her remarks released by the campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has spent a decade trying to keep the American people divided and afraid of each other. That\u8217\'20\'19s who he is,\u8221\'20\'1D she will say. \u8220\'20\'1CBut America, I am here tonight to say: that\u8217\'20\'19s not who we are.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris is attempting to cast herself as a unifying figure who will work for \u8220\'20\'1Call Americans\u8221\'20\'1D as president, regardless of who they voted for in the November election, drawing a sharp contrast with Trump who has threatened a campaign of retribution against his political enemies. It\u8217\'20\'19s a similar approach Biden took in the waning days of the 2020 election, but healing the tribalism and polarization proved elusive.\par \par \uc2 Harris suggests that her election would \u8220\'20\'1Cturn the page\u8221\'20\'1D on the Trump era entirely, though there are plenty of reasons to be skeptical that Trump would accept his defeat and retreat from the national stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.59pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.42pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At his press conference, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  also flirted with the idea that Democrats would try to steal the 2024 election from Trump.\par \par \uc2 He also continued to deny the results of the 2020 election, though there is no credible evidence of misconduct that undermines the legitimacy of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2020 victory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWere going to have a reprise of 2020 where they\u8217\'20\'19re going to do everything humanly possible to nullify\u8221\'20\'1D Trump\u8217\'20\'19s victory and \u8220\'20\'1Cdelegitimize his second term\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe working-class people in this country that support \uc2 Donald John Trump\uc2  are not going to let that happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe 2020 election was stolen,\u8221\'20\'1D Bannon said later.\par \par \uc2 During a question-and-answer session, some sort of apparent interloper \u8211\'20\'13 it was unclear whether this was a comedian or performance artist or someone else entirely \u8211\'20\'13 asked Bannon: \u8220\'20\'1CWhen\u8217\'20\'19s the next insurrection, and can we storm the \uc2 Burger King\uc2  after this?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 This person appears to have been escorted out of the press conference.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm GMT\par \par \uc2 At a press conference Tuesday afternoon, about 12 hours after his release from prison, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  railed against Democrat \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , attorney general \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  and Harris, again claiming that he was a \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical prisoner \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe system is broken,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, claiming the justice department was \u8220\'20\'1Cweaponized\u8221\'20\'1D to punish Trump supporters and gut his popular podcast, in an effort to thwart Maga\u8217\'20\'19s influence.\par \par \uc2 Bannon also claimed that he met a lot of \u8220\'20\'1Cworking class minorities\u8221\'20\'1D behind bars, saying he listened to, and learned from, them. They disliked Harris, he claimed, referring to the former prosecutor as the \u8220\'20\'1Cqueen of mass incarcerations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Doubling down on his War Room statements this morning, where Bannon insisted that prison had empowered him, he also said: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , suck on that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bannon also thanked the prison for giving him the opportunity to teach civics to about 100 students, noting that he had Puerto Rican and Dominican students. Bannon discussed his encounters with people of color at several points today, in an apparent effort to deflect anti-Latino commentary from Trump supporters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Nearly 3.2 million voters have cast ballots in the 2024 general election in North Carolina as of Tuesday at noon.\par \par \uc2 The North Carolina state board of elections made the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncsbe.gov/news/press-releases/2024/10/29/north-carolina-tops-3-million-ballots-cast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcement}}}\uc2  on Tuesday, adding that 3.2 million voters represents a turnout of 40.7% of registered voters in the state.\par \par \uc2 Just over 3m of the votes were cast in-person, and about 170,000 were cast via mail in ballot.\par \par \uc2 Through the end of the day on Monday, more than 2.9 million voters had cast ballots in person during the first 12 days of the early voting period, which the elections officials said was an increase of 11.9% compared with 2020.\par \par \uc2 Interestingly, turnout in the 25 western North Carolina counties affected by Hurricane Helene continue to outpace statewide turnout, the election board added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 JLo to rally with Harris in Las Vegas\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Lopez will join \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at a rally in Las Vegas on Thursday, the Harris campaign has announced.\par \par \uc2 Lopez will speak on the importance of voting, what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake for the country with this election, and why she is endorsing Harris and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Harris campaign said.\par \par \uc2 Mexican pop band Man\u225\'00\'E1, will also perform at that rally.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Bad Bunny posts apparent response to racist Puerto Rico joke at Trump rally\par \par \uc2 Grammy-winning Puerto Rican artist, Bad Bunny, posted a video on his \uc2 Instagram\uc2  on Tuesday in celebration of Puerto Rican culture.\par \par \uc2 The post comes in response to the insulting remarks made at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally on Sunday against the island, where a comedian called Puerto Rico a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Bad Bunny\u8217\'20\'19s eight-minute long {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/badbunnypr/?utm_source=ig_embed&ig_rid=cc80a7da-d4b5-40d9-9478-a9f92b5b67ce"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2 , posted to his more than 45 million followers on Tuesday, is captioned \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage\u8221\'20\'1D and highlights Puerto Rican culture, history and people over inspirational music.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Bad Bunny, whose official name is Benito Antonio Mart\u237\'00\'EDnez Ocasio, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/27/bad-bunny-supports-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signalled his support for Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , sharing a video of the vice-president on his \uc2 Instagram\uc2  just moments after the comedian Tony Hinchcliffe made the remarks about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/puerto-rico"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Puerto Rico}}}\uc2  at the Trump rally.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vanessa C\u225\'00\'E1rdenas, the executive director of the pro-immigration group America\u8217\'20\'19s Voice, said the speakers at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally on Sunday makes clear that his nativist movement will never see \u8220\'20\'1CLatinos or immigrants are real Americans.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 C\u225\'00\'E1rdenas pointed to comments made by \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , an influential immigration adviser to Trump. Speaking at the same Sunday rally, Cardenas pointed to Miller\u8217\'20\'19s declaration: \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica is for Americans and Americans only.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese words reveal their thinking. In their eyes we are not real Americans, and as far as Trump and his team are concerned, we will never be,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt foreshadows the sort of administration they would run.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.56pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Puerto Ricans are heavily concentrated in the battleground states of Pennsylvania and Georgia but they have a presence in all 50 states Hispanic leaders and Activists said on a call on Tuesday responding to the racist remark about Puerto Rico made at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Alex Gomez, executive director of LUCHA based in Arizona, said there were approximately 64,000 Puerto Ricans living in the state, which was decided by 10,000 votes in 2020.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is showing us who he is,\u8221\'20\'1D Gomez said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is our warning signal of the types of policies and what he and the people that follow him believe and so our communities are not going to stand for that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She said her organization has a goal of knocking on 500,000 doors before election day, next Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will make sure that our communities know what he has said,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A racist remark about Puerto Rico made at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden rally on Sunday was the \u8220\'20\'1COctober surprise for the Latino community\u8221\'20\'1D, said Gustavo Torres, head of CASA in Action, a Latino and immigrant organization.\par \par \uc2 Torres said his organization would work to inform Latino voters every day for the next week until election day. Trump, he said, \u8220\'20\'1Chumiliate[s] and \u8230\'20\'26 underestimate[s] the Puerto Rican Community and the Latino community.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Polls suggest Trump has made notable inroads with Latino voters, particularly men and young people, despite his persistent attacks on immigrant communities and his pledge of mass deportations. The Hispanic leaders and activists on Tuesday\u8217\'20\'19s call predicted a backlash that could cost Trump not only his support among Latinos but possibly the election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to see what is going to happen on November 5,\u8221\'20\'1D Torres told reporters on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUntil he apologises and directly disavows those comments, it will leave a stain of racism and bigotry on him and his campaign for the Latino community,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Janet Murguia\uc2 , President, UnidosUS Action Fund. \u8220\'20\'1CIf he understands the importance of Puerto Rican voters in Pennsylvania and Georgia in particular, it would be in his interest to at least make that effort.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.51pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Puerto Rico\u8217\'20\'19s largest newspaper endorses \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president\par \par \uc2 Puerto Rico\u8217\'20\'19s Largest Newspaper, El Nuevo D\u237\'00\'EDa, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.elnuevodia.com/english/editorial/puerto-ricans-should-vote-for-kamala-harris/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed }}}\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for President as of Tuesday morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn Sunday, continuing a pattern of contempt and misinformation that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has maintained for years against the eight million of us American citizens who are Puerto Ricans, comedian Tony Hinchcliffe insulted us during a Republican Party event by referring to Puerto Rico as \u8216\'20\'18an island of garbage in the ocean\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D the statement from the newspaper reads.\par \par \uc2 It continues, \u8220\'20\'1CIs that what Trump and the Republican Party think about Puerto Ricans? Politics is not a joke and hiding behind a comedian is cowardly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The newspaper said that Trump \u8220\'20\'1Chas for years maintained a discourse of contempt and misinformation against the island\u8221\'20\'1D pointing out the time Trump, as president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/sep/12/trump-puerto-rico-maria-hurricane-claim-fact-check-reality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threw paper towels }}}\uc2  into a crowd after Hurricane Maria, \u8220\'20\'1Cwhile we suffered without electricity for months.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Later in the lengthy piece, the newspaper asks readers, \u8220\'20\'1CIs this the great America we want?\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn Sunday, as insults rained down on Puerto Rico, the Democratic candidate offered a message of hope, promising to maintain the interagency group dedicated exclusively to strengthening and creating new opportunities\u8221\'20\'1D the piece states.\par \par \uc2 In its conclusion, the newspaper writes: \u8220\'20\'1Ctoday we urge all those who love our beautiful island, the land of the sea and the sun, not to lend their vote to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . To all Puerto Ricans who can vote in this upcoming United States election and represent those of us who cannot: Vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Former Michigan GOP Chair Rusty Hills has spoken out against Trump in a new opinion piece in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/opinion/contributors/2024/10/29/trump-michigan-gerald-ford-ronald-reagan-or-george-bush/75891532007/?taid=6720c0396ae5f900011ec0e5&utm_campaign=trueanthem&utm_medium=social&utm_source=twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Detroit Free Press}}}\uc2  published on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 In the article, titled \u8216\'20\'18Trump\u8217\'20\'19s no Gerald Ford. He\u8217\'20\'19s not even \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Hills outlines the ways in which Trump is different from former Republican candidates for president.\par \par \uc2 Hills pointed to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s character, rhetoric, offensive insults toward political opponents, praise of Russia, and language regarding immigrants, among other differences he sees between Trump and former GOP candidates.\par \par \uc2 He then asks the readers:\par \par \uc2 Why would any Republican in Michigan who voted for Gerald Ford \u8211\'20\'13 or \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 , \uc2 George HW Bush\uc2  or \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , Sens. \uc2 John McCain\uc2  or \uc2 Mitt Romney\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 ever cast a ballot for someone like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Hills, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fordschool.umich.edu/faculty/gerald-hills"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  teaches}}}\uc2  at the Gerald R Ford School of Public Policy at the \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2 , then writes:\par \par \uc2 The answer is clear \u8211\'20\'13 they shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm GMT\par \par \uc2 New polling shows Harris and Trump deadlocked in Arizona and Nevada\par \par \uc2 New polls show \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  leading \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  by one percentage point in Arizona, and Trump leading Harris in Nevada by the same margin.\par \par \uc2 In the polls, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.documentcloud.org/documents/25257085/cnn-polls-harris-and-trump-locked-in-close-races-in-arizona-and-nevada-as-pool-of-persuadable-voters-shrinks.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published by CNN and conducted by SSRS polling}}}\uc2  between 21 October and 26 October, Harris received 48% support in Arizona among likely voters, while Trump received 47%.\par \par \uc2 In Nevada, Trump received 48% support among likely voters, and Harris received 47%.\par \par \uc2 It is important to point out that these numbers are within the margins of error for these polls.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Send your mail-in ballot today, USPS tells voters\par \par \uc2 The United States Postal Service\uc2  issued an alert on Tuesday urging voters who choose to vote by mail to send their ballots in by today.\par \par \uc2 In the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://about.usps.com/newsroom/national-releases/2024/1028-us-postal-service-is-ready-to-deliver-the-nations-election-mail.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  message}}}\uc2 , USPS said that they \u8220\'20\'1Canticipate an uptick of ballots in the mail over the coming days\u8221\'20\'1D and recommended that voters who want to mail their ballots do so at least a week before their election office needs them to ensure it arrives in time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf a ballot is due on Election Day, the Postal Service recommends mailing the ballot by this Tuesday\u8221\'20\'1D 29 October, the postal service said.\par \par \uc2 USPS said that in 2020, 99.9% of ballots were delivered within seven days and 98.3% of ballots were delivered within three days.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.06pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Obama says he tells young American men voting is their birthright\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  has posted a clip on X of himself on The Pivot podcast where he recalls how he regularly talks to young men and tells them \u8220\'20\'1Cdo not let people think you do not belong.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said that he tells them that people with power, \u8220\'20\'1Cfancy\u8221\'20\'1D titles and wealth are just the same as everyone else when you get up close to them. \u8220\'20\'1CThey just folk,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The former US president, who is currently campaigning to get \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  elected to the White House next month, said that such young men are amazed when he tells them of some of the struggles of his youth and that \u8220\'20\'1CI was getting high, screwing around\u8221\'20\'1D and understands they are sometimes \u8220\'20\'1Cnot doing what they are supposed to do\u8221\'20\'1D. But then he tells them they have the power to make choices.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no reason why you cannot pursue the dreams you want, and politics is part of that and voting is part of that. That\u8217\'20\'19s your birthright as a citizen, do not give it away,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltrVoting is a part of your birthright as a citizen. Don't give it away.\par \par \uc2 Make sure you\u8217\'20\'19re registered and have a plan to vote at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/NKXRGNgJPv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/NKXRGNgJPv}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JCKSgiqgB5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JCKSgiqgB5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Barack Obama (@BarackObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BarackObama/status/1851304766242242712?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.46pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A federal judge today threw out a lawsuit by six Republican members of Congress seeking to make Pennsylvania election officials institute new checks confirming the identity of soldiers, sailors, and others who vote from overseas and to make sure they\u8217\'20\'19re eligible.\par \par \uc2 US district judge Christopher Conner said he agreed with the defendants \u8211\'20\'13 Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s secretary of state, Al Schmidt, and one of his top deputies \u8211\'20\'13 who argued there were no grounds to sue and that the case was launched too late and too close to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Election Day}}}\uc2 , the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The Pennsylvania congressmen:\par \par \uc2 Provide no good excuse for waiting until barely a month before the election to bring this lawsuit,\u8221\'20\'1D Conner wrote.\par \par \uc2 More than 25,000 overseas ballots had already been sent out when the case was filed in late September, the judge noted.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit was filed by six of the state\u8217\'20\'19s eight Republican members of the US House: Representatives \uc2 Guy Reschenthaler\uc2 , \uc2 Dan Meuser\uc2 , GT Thompson, Lloyd Smucker, Mike Kelly and Scott Perry. The other plaintiff is PA Fair Elections, a group led by Heather Honey, an election researcher whose work has fueled right-wing attacks on voting procedures.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  falsely said Democrats had staged a \u8220\'20\'1Ccoup\u8221\'20\'1D to force \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/21/joe-biden-withdraw-running-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drop his re-election bid}}}\uc2 , as his Democratic rival, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , planned a rally in Washington DC, that will remind voters of the violent attack on the US Capitol by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters.\par \par \uc2 At an event at his Florida estate, his accusation that Democrats had unfairly forced Biden out of the race recalled Trump\u8217\'20\'19s false claims that he had lost the 2020 election due to fraud, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 They stole the presidency of the United States. You can call it a coup, you can call it whatever. But they stole it. The way they took that away from him was not right,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Harris is due to hold a rally this evening at the Ellipse, a park near the White House where on 6 January 2021, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/05/fight-like-hell-grievance-and-denialism-rule-at-trump-georgia-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 once again}}}\uc2  urged supporters to \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/28/january-6-committee-session-new-evidence"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fight like hell}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D and march to the US Capitol, where lawmakers were due to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/congress-certify-election-biden-republicans-object"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certify his loss}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Four people died in the ensuing riot, and one police officer who defended the Capitol died the following day. Trump has said if he is re-elected he would pardon the more than 1,500 participants who have been charged with crimes.\par \par \uc2 Harris will call on Americans tonight to \u8220\'20\'1Cturn the page\u8221\'20\'1D on Trump while stressing her plans to lower costs and make the economy work for middle-class Americans, campaign chair \uc2 Jen O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon\uc2  told reporters.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.07pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Hello, US election live blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s a packed day on the campaign trail for all the candidates, with just a week left before election day next Tuesday. We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you the news as it happens.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barbara Pierce Bush, the daughter of \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  and granddaughter of \uc2 George HW Bush\uc2 , has revealed that she is campaigning for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . In an interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://people.com/george-w-bush-s-daughter-barbara-breaks-silence-on-election-to-campaign-for-kamala-harris-exclusive-8735810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 People Magazine}}}\uc2 , Pierce Bush said that she is \u8220\'20\'1Chopeful\u8221\'20\'1D that Harris and her running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will \u8220\'20\'1Cmove our country forward and protect women\u8217\'20\'19s rights\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  held a press conference at his Florida residence and described the marathon New York rally that he held at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  in Manhattan two days ago \u8211\'20\'13 which has been widely condemned for racist remarks from speakers - as a \u8220\'20\'1Clove fest\u8221\'20\'1D. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe love in that room, it was breathtaking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, the GOP vice-presidential candidate, has been rallying in Saginaw in the swing state of Michigan, 100 miles north of Detroit, and criticized opposing politicians calling Trump a fascist in the last week. That includes Harris, whom Vance, a US Senator from Ohio, called unqualified to be president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House announced that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will travel to his childhood home town of Scranton, Pennsylvania for political engagements on Saturday. The US president has campaigned often in the city as a way of reminding the electorate of his working class roots and pro-union politics.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Rapper 50 Cent said that he turned down a $3m offer to perform at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s controversial rally in New York City\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden on Sunday, according to Variety magazine. Deadline also reported that 50 Cent also confirmed that he was also offered money to perform at the Republic National Convention in the summer, but turned it down because he prefers to stay away from party politics.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 New polling has found that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s support among young Black men has decreased since August, while Harris\u8217\'20\'19s has grown. A new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://naacp.org/articles/new-naacp-data-displays-progress-reaching-black-male-voters-shifts-key-attitudes-and"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NAACP survey}}}\uc2 , conducted between 11 and 17 October, found that 21% of Black men under 50 years old said they would for the former president, down from 27% in August. Harris\u8217\'20\'19s support among this group jumped from 51% to 59 % over that same time frame, the researchers said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , the longtime Trump Maga ally, is back on air hosting his podcast after being released from prison this morning. He served a four-month sentence for defying a congressional subpoena related to the investigation into the January 6 attack on the US Capitol by extremist supporters of Trump who were intent on overturning his loss to Biden in the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Most Americans are prepared to accept the election results as legitimate, according to a new ABC/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll released today. And more than 48.6 million Americans have reportedly voted early in this year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and her allies have lately stepped up their accusations that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a fascist.\par \par \uc2 They were aided last week by his former chief of staff \uc2 John Kelly\uc2  saying publicly that he believes his ex-boss met the definition of a politician who believes in the governing philosophy typically associated with the Nazis.\par \par \uc2 In Saginaw, Michigan on Tuesday, JD Vance accused Democrats of being disrespectful with that accusation, comparing it to the experience of a World War II veteran who had led the pledge of allegiance earlier in the event.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRather than persuade their fellow Americans, they\u8217\'20\'19ve decided that they\u8217\'20\'19re going to call their fellow Americans Nazis and fascists. And I think it\u8217\'20\'19s disgusting... and a person who would close out her campaign by running and attacking her fellow Americans has no business leading the greatest nation on Earth,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt occurs to me that when they attack us as Nazis, it\u8217\'20\'19s so disgraceful because there are people in this room right now who have grandparents, who have parents, or who they themselves fought in World War II.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.31pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Barbara Pierce Bush, the daughter of former Republican president \uc2 George W Bush\uc2  and granddaughter of former president \uc2 George HW Bush\uc2 , has revealed that she is campaigning for vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://people.com/george-w-bush-s-daughter-barbara-breaks-silence-on-election-to-campaign-for-kamala-harris-exclusive-8735810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 People Magazine}}}\uc2 , Pierce Bush said that she is \u8220\'20\'1C hopeful\u8221\'20\'1D that Harris and her running mate Minnesota Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will \u8220\'20\'1Cmove our country forward and protect women\u8217\'20\'19s rights.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added that over the weekend, she campaigned in Pennsylvania for the Harris-Walz campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was inspiring to join friends and meet voters with the Harris-Walz campaign in Pennsylvania this weekend,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.32pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A woman in Minnesota has been charged with three felonies for allegedly attempting to submit a mail in ballot for her recently deceased mother, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/voter-fraud-mail-minnesota-dead-mother-07728368892dad330e1c5b058289c4f2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Associated Press}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The probable cause statement reported by AP revealed that during an interview with a sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant, the woman admitted to filling out her mother\u8217\'20\'19s ballot after her death and that her mother was an \u8220\'20\'1Cardent\u8221\'20\'1D Trump supporter who had wanted to vote for him before she died.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.startribune.com/northern-minnesota-woman-faces-felonies-after-signing-late-moms-name-to-absentee-ballots/601170823"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Star Tribune}}}\uc2  also reported that the woman signed her late mother\u8217\'20\'19s signature on two absentee ballots.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump defends \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally as 'love fest'\par \par \uc2 During his speech on Tuesday, former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  described his New York rally, which has been widely condemned for racist remarks, as a \u8220\'20\'1Clove fest\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think anybody has ever seen anything like what happened the other night at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26\u8221\'20\'1D Trump told a crowd at his Mar-a-Lago resort in Florida. \u8220\'20\'1CThe love in that room, it was breathtaking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPoliticans that have been doing this for a long time said there\u8217\'20\'19s never been an event so beautiful, it was like a love fest, an absolute love fest, and it was my honor to be involved.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump calls his hate filled rally at MSG a \u8220\'20\'1Clovefest.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/MqKDq1iYUR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/MqKDq1iYUR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Republican Voters Against Trump (@AccountableGOP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AccountableGOP/status/1851297347143409957?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.21pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.10pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been underwater in public opinion polls for most of his presidency, a problem that came to a head in his disastrous debate against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in June, which set off a chain of events that led to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  taking his place atop the Democratic ticket.\par \par \uc2 JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s message to voters in Saginaw today \u8211\'20\'13 he\u8217\'20\'19s focusing most of his time talking about Harris and not her running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , who he debated earlier this month \u8211\'20\'13 is that Harris and Biden are substantively the same \u8211\'20\'13 and the vice-president has nothing new to offer.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the fact that so many of our fellow citizens are telling us they\u8217\'20\'19re worse off, and they\u8217\'20\'19re telling us that because they are, that explains why \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is going around running as far away as she can from the policies of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 He continued, \u8220\'20\'1Cin fact, you know, between her copying \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policies and her pretending that she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t even know who \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is, I\u8217\'20\'19m half convinced that tomorrow on the campaign trail, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is going to show up in a long red tie and a red Maga hat, realizing that the American people just haven\u8217\'20\'19t had it anymore.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance mocked Harris, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CShe\u8217\'20\'19s copying all of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policy, she might as well copy [his] style too. You know, just complete the bit Kamala. It\u8217\'20\'19s not working so far. Just lean into it a little bit more.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.05pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Poll after poll has shown that Americans feel the country is on the wrong path, and are looking for change. Speaking in Saginaw today, JD Vance sought to convince voters in the seat of a county that voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2016 then \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  four years later that the Democratic vice-president would not transform the country in the ways that they want:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs much as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  pretends that she is the candidate of change, she is the sitting vice president, she signed off, she bragged about being the last person in the room after the disastrous policies the last four years were made\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 He continued: \u8220\'20\'1CYou cannot, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , pretend that you had nothing to do with the Biden administration when you are the sitting vice president. You can\u8217\'20\'19t pretend you had nothing to do with the trillions of dollars in new spending when you cast the tie-breaking vote on trillions of dollars in new spending, you cannot pretend to be the candidate of change when your party has been running the show for the last four years, and the American people have suffered because of it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 JD Vance was never involved with \u8220\'20\'1CThe Apprentice\u8221\'20\'1D, the reality show that made \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  even more of a household name before he entered politics.\par \par \uc2 But in his speeches, the Ohio senator and vice-presidential nominee has adopted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cyou\u8217\'20\'19re fired\u8221\'20\'1D catchphrase from the show.\par \par \uc2 During his remarks on Tuesday in Michigan , Vance said:\par \par \uc2 I think in seven days, the great state of Michigan is going to tell \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , we don\u8217\'20\'19t want any more [of] your word salad. We don\u8217\'20\'19t even want any more of your broken policies. You are fired. Go back to California, where [you] already belong. We want a real president who fights for the American people.\par \par \uc2 Michigan, along with Pennsylvania and Wisconsin, are all swing states that helped put Trump in the White House eight years ago, but which \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  reconquered in 2020. This year, polls show voters in all three are essentially evenly divided between Trump and Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 JD Vance continued on with one of several attacks he would make on the Democratic vice-president over the course of his speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen anything like it in my life where, when you ask \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  what she wants to do for the American people, ask specifically \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , how do you plan to fix the inflation that your policies have caused, how do you plan to make it more affordable for our fellow citizens to be able to buy groceries, for example? How are you going to fix the very problems that your policies created? She\u8217\'20\'19ll say, Well, I grew up in a middle class family\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said.\par \par \uc2 He continued \u8220\'20\'1Cand when you ask her, you know about the terrible chaos at the southern border, or the chaos that we have all over the globe, how are you going to address the problems that your policies cause? She\u8217\'20\'19ll say, well, you know, when I worked at \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 , I was really good at making the hash browns. And I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if I even buy that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 JD Vance just took the stage here at a city recreation center in Saginaw, Michigan, where he explained to the crowd why he believes \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is not qualified to lead the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe all agree, in this room, that politics is a little absurd from time to time, and sometimes we ought to poke fun at the absurdity of our political process. But you know what\u8217\'20\'19s the most absurd thing about American politics in 2024? That a person like \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  thinks she can actually lead the United States of America,\u8221\'20\'1D the Ohio senator told the crowd as he campaigns in one of the \u8220\'20\'1CBlue Wall\u8221\'20\'1D swing states that Republicans are hoping to win this year.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm GMT\par \par \uc2 The White House has announced that president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will travel to his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/09/21/statement-by-president-joe-biden-on-the-passing-of-thomas-bell/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 childhood home }}}\uc2  town of Scranton, Pennsylvania for political engagements on Saturday, 2 November.\par \par \uc2 Biden last visited Scranton {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wnep.com/article/news/local/lackawanna-county/president-biden-visits-scranton-avoca-airforceone-funeral-childhood-friend/523-e210b8ab-6e7f-43c1-9e35-72fbbe1fbf25"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in September}}}\uc2  to attend the funeral of one of his childhood friends.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign will become the first political campaign to advertise on the Las Vegas Sphere.\par \par \uc2 The news was first reported on Tuesday by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.8newsnow.com/news/politics/kamala-harris-campaign-to-advertise-on-las-vegas-sphere-a-political-first/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 8 News Now }}}\uc2  in Las Vegas, which added that the ads will coincide with Harris\u8217\'20\'19s visit to Las Vegas on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The campaign hopes the imagery will reach millions of voters in Nevada and online, a spokesperson for the Harris campaign told the outlet.\par \par \uc2 Josh Marcus Blank, who does communications for the Harris campaign also posted the news on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew: \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  campaign to advertise on Las Vegas Sphere, a political first {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kcDkrBkJ0B"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/kcDkrBkJ0B}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Josh Marcus-Blank (@jmarcusblank) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jmarcusblank/status/1851281149332492495?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 29, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.34pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump addresses crowd at Mar-a-Lago\par \par \uc2 Trump is now speaking to a crowd at Mar-a-Lago in Florida.\par \par \uc2 The former president opened his remarks by referring to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/pennsylvania-voter-registration-investigation-8380686817ed4d4eb16dc303d01b2a76"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  story out of Pennsylvania }}}\uc2  this week where hundreds of ballot applications are being investigated for potential fraud.\par \par \uc2 Trump then quickly moved on to attacking vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and is now discussing the issue of immigration in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Trump so far not addressed the controversial remarks made by a comedian at the Trump rally on Sunday at New York City\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden, where Puerto Rico was described as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 American rapper 50 Cent said that he turned down a $3m offer to perform at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s controversial rally in New York City\u8217\'20\'19s Madison Square Garden on Sunday, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://variety.com/2024/music/news/50-cent-turned-down-trump-3-million-offer-madison-square-garden-rally-1236193527/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Variety}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an interview on Tuesday morning on \u8220\'20\'1CThe Breakfast Club\u8221\'20\'1D host DJ Envy asked the rapper whether it\u8217\'20\'19s true that Trump offered him money to endorse him, to which he responded yes, adding \u8220\'20\'1CI got a call, but they wanted me [for] Sunday.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey offered three million dollars to do it,\u8221\'20\'1D 50 Cent added.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2024/10/50-cent-donald-trump-trump-three-million-msg-the-breakfast-club-charlamagne-tha-god-dj-envy-kanye-west-1236160878/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Deadline}}}\uc2  also reported that 50 Cent also confirmed that he was also offered money to perform at the Republic National Convention, but turned it down because he prefers to stay away from politics.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 As we wait for former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to take the stage for his press conference at Mar-a-Lago in Florida \u8211\'20\'13 where he is more than an hour behind schedule \u8211\'20\'13 a new poll of voters in Michigan was released today showing how Trump and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are neck and neck in the key battleground state.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://emersoncollegepolling.com/october-2024-michigan-poll-trump-49-harris-48/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey,}}}\uc2  conducted by Emerson College Polling/RealClearWorld between October 25-27, found that among Michigan voters 49% support Trump, while 48% support Harris.\par \par \uc2 2% were undecided and 1% plan on voting for a third party.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith one week until Election Day, the race remains a toss-up,\u8221\'20\'1D Spencer Kimball, executive director of Emerson College Polling, said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Harris support among young Black men grows as Trump's dips, poll suggests\par \par \uc2 New polling has found that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s support among young Black men has decreased since August, while \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s has grown.\par \par \uc2 A new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://naacp.org/articles/new-naacp-data-displays-progress-reaching-black-male-voters-shifts-key-attitudes-and"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NAACP survey}}}\uc2 , conducted between Oct. 11-17, found that 21% of Black men under 50 years old said they would for the former president, down from 27% in August.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s support among this group jumped from 51% to 59 % over that same time frame, the researchers said.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, during a press briefing, the \uc2 NAACP\uc2  unveiled its final pre-election round of polling results outlining shifting attitudes and issue priorities of millions of Black voters.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 NAACP\uc2  is proud to see the results of our $20 million investment as we continue to increase Black\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 NAACP (@NAACP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NAACP/status/1851011308910436673?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 28, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.47pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 JD Vance {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/hugolowell/status/1851267356535754944"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will sit for an interview}}}\uc2  with Joe Rogan tomorrow for his podcast.\par \par \uc2 The interview is expected to drop later this week, and will be taped in Rogan\u8217\'20\'19s studio in Austin, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/alaynatreene/status/1851266637174903185"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to CNN}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This comes just several days after the popular {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/trump-joe-rogan-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 podcast host interviewed }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/trump-joe-rogan-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday morning, Rogan said on social media \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has not \u8220\'20\'1Cpassed on doing the podcast\u8221\'20\'1D but that they only offered one hour, and he would have to travel to her.\par \par \uc2 Rogan said that he feels \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly\u8221\'20\'1D that the best way to do the interview is in his studio in Austin, Texas and that his wish was just to \u8220\'20\'1Chave a nice conversation\u8221\'20\'1D with Harris and \u8220\'20\'1Cget to know her as a human being.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI really hope we can make it happen\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.20pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump set to deliver remarks to press at Mar-a-Lago\par \par \uc2 Any moment, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is set to deliver remarks to the press from his Mar-a-Lago resort in Palm Beach, Florida.\par \par \uc2 The event was scheduled for 10am ET but appears to be running 20 or so minutes behind.\par \par \uc2 The press conference on Tuesday morning comes as Trump and his campaign continue to face {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/27/trump-madison-square-garden-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backlash for racist and vulgar comments}}}\uc2  made at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s New York City campaign rally on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 If Trump opens up the room to questions on Tuesday, it is likely that Trump will face questions about the comments at this press conference.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 After being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/steve-bannon-released-from-prison-early-a-week-before-us-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 released from prison}}}\uc2  this morning, \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 , the longtime \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ally, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Bannons_WarRoom/status/1851263411352408274"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  back on air }}}\uc2  hosting his podcast \u8211\'20\'13 War Room.\par \par \uc2 The live-stream podcast episode \u8220\'20\'1CThe Return of \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D began at 10 am ET this morning, just hours after his release.\par \par \uc2 Bannon is also reportedly planning to hold a press conference later on Tuesday in Manhattan.\par \par \uc2 Bannon spent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/steve-bannon-released-from-prison-early-a-week-before-us-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 four months behind bars }}}\uc2  after he was convicted on two counts of contempt of Congress.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 40,000 people expected for Harris speech in Washington, DC\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Park Service\uc2  has said that it is expecting about 40,000 people in attendance for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s speech this evening on the Ellipse in Washington DC, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2024/10/29/us/harris-trump-election/fb52d455-03a5-5571-bf77-a025a6e4a7bc?smid=url-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will lay out her vision for the presidency in a speech this evening near the White House to underscore the \u8220\'20\'1Cgravity\u8221\'20\'1D of the choice before Americans this November, her campaign chair \uc2 Jen O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon\uc2  told reporters in a call previewing the speech.\par \par \uc2 A former prosecutor, Harris will lay out the speech as she would a closing argument, with the American people as the jury, campaign co-Chair \uc2 Cedric Richmond\uc2 . She has been laying out the evidence for the last 100 days, and now she is prepared to rest her case.\par \par \uc2 Richmond said Harris will use the speech, from a site where Trump spoke to his supporters before they stormed the Capitol on January 6, to remind Americans that the former president is \u8220\'20\'1Cso all-consumed by his grievances and his power and his endless desire for revenge that he is not focused on the needs of the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris is also expected to lay out her personal story and her vision for building up the economy and working across party lines to serve \u8220\'20\'1Call Americans\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 including, in contrast to Trump, she will argue, those who did not support her.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon said the speech is dedicated to reaching voters who have yet to make up their minds- or aren\u8217\'20\'19t sure they will vote \u8211\'20\'13 young people, those who haven\u8217\'20\'19t tuned in and suburban women, and independents. O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric in the final weeks and especially his \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  rally appears to have created even more openings for the campaign to reach these voters. Support among their targeted Puerto Rican voters is growing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know that there are still a lot of voters out there that are still trying to decide who to support or whether to vote at all,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Malley Dillon said. The campaign, she said, considers the contes a \u8220\'20\'1Cmargin-of-error race.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.58pm GMT\par \par \uc2 USA Today has joined the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  and LA Times in not endorsing a candidate for this election \u8212\'20\'14 report\par \par \uc2 USA Today has reportedly joined the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  and the LA Times in deciding not to endorse a presidential candidate in the 2024 election.\par \par \uc2 USA Today, which has over 200 US news outlets under it, including the Arizona Republic, The Des Moines Register, and the Detroit Free Press, is one of the largest daily newspapers by circulation in the country.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the company said it would not be backing candidates \u8220\'20\'1Cin presidential or national races\u8221\'20\'1D this year, a spokesperson told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/media/4958134-300-gannett-outlets-not-endorsing-presidential-national-races/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Hill}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last election, USA Today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2020/oct/20/usa-today-supports-joe-biden-first-ever-presidential-endorsement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed Joe Bien for president}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The spokesperson said on Monday that while the company will not endorse for president, \u8220\'20\'1Clocal editors at publications across the \uc2 USA TODAY Network\uc2  have the discretion to endorse at a state or local level.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.01pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump claims that he didn't hear comedian's Puerto Rico comment \u8212\'20\'14 report\par \par \uc2 Former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has reportedly told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/live-updates/2024-election-updates-harris-make-closing-argument-amid/?id=115252538&entryId=115254897"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC News}}}\uc2  that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t hear any of the comments made by comedian Tony Hinchcliffe at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally in New York on Sunday, including when the comedian called Puerto Rico an \u8220\'20\'1Cisland of floating garbage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When asked about the comments, Trump allgedly did not denounce them but rather repeated that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t hear them.\par \par \uc2 Trump also said that he didn\u8217\'20\'19t know Hinchcliffe, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know him; someone put him up there. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know who he is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.49pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Podcast host Joe Rogan, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/trump-joe-rogan-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interviewed Donald Trump}}}\uc2  on Friday, said on social media today that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has not \u8220\'20\'1Cpassed on doing the podcast\u8221\'20\'1D but that they only offered one hour, and he would have to travel to her.\par \par \uc2 In a post on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/joerogan/status/1851118464447971595?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1851118464447971595%7Ctwgr%5E673807c59aad5b0125bb358a72768ec69da45199%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2Flive%2F2024%2F10%2F29%2Fus%2Fharris-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 X}}}\uc2  early Tuesday morning, Rogan said that he feels \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly\u8221\'20\'1D that the best way to do the interview is in his studio in Austin, Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy sincere wish is to just have a nice conversation and get to know her as a human being,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI really hope we can make it happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.04pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will do five interviews today ahead of her Closing Argument speech in Washington DC this evening, according to her campaign.\par \par \uc2 The interviews will include four battleground state television interviews to reach voters in Detroit, Milwaukee, Philadelphia, and Pittsburgh, as well as a Spanish radio interview with Rumba in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is set to deliver remarks from Mar-a-Lago at 10am ET today.\par \par \uc2 Later in the day, he is scheduled to travel to Drexel Hill, Pennsylvania, to attend a roundtable with senior citizens there where he will be joined by former Arkansas Governor \uc2 Mike Huckabee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This evening, Trump is scheduled to speak at a campaign rally in Allentown, Pennsylvania, at 7 pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.54pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Most Americans are prepared to accept the election results as legitimate, according to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ipsos.com/en-us/most-americans-are-prepared-accept-election-results-legitimate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC/Ipsos poll }}}\uc2  released on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The poll, conducted between 18 October to 22, 2024, states 83% of Americans surveyed and 86% of registered voters surveyed are prepared to accept the outcome of the presidential election as legitimate, regardless of which candidate they support.\par \par \uc2 About 15% of Americans and 12% of registered voters say they are not prepared to accept the outcome of the presidential election as legitimate.\par \par \uc2 In addition, most Americans think that vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is prepared to accept the outcome of the presidential election as legitimate, while only 30% feel \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is prepared to do the same.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50pm GMT\par \par \uc2 More than 48 million Americans have voted early as of Tuesday morning\par \par \uc2 As of 8:45am ET on Tuesday, more than 48.6 million Americans have voted early in this year\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election that\u8217\'20\'19s just a week away, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://election.lab.ufl.edu/early-vote/2024-early-voting/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Election Lab at the University of Florida}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Of the total number of early votes, 25,257,519 were cast in person and 23,469,957 were returned by mail.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Puerto Rico Republican chief demands that Trump apologises for rally\u8217\'20\'19s racist remarks\par \par \uc2 As outrage continues over the remarks from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s Sunday rally in New York, Angel M Cintr\u243\'00\'F3n, the president of the Republican party\u8217\'20\'19s branch in Puerto Rico, has said that he will not vote for Trump unless Trump apologises for the racist remarks made at his rally, where a speaker referred to Puerto Rico as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfloating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now we have no business and no relationship with Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D Cintr\u243\'00\'F3n said on Monday during a Puerto Rican talkshow. \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t apologise, we won\u8217\'20\'19t vote for him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/puerto-rico-republican-chief-demands-trump-apology-rally-racist-remarks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Puerto Rico Republican chief demands Trump apology for rally\u8217\'20\'19s racist remarks}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.36pm GMT\par \par \uc2 A senior campaign adviser for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/28/politics/trump-offensive-rally-overshadowed-message/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  told CNN }}}\uc2  that the speeches from Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/27/trump-madison-square-garden-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Madison Square Garden Rally}}}\uc2 , which included racist remarks and dangerous threats about immigrants, were vetted beforehand.\par \par \uc2 But, the senior campaign official, who was not named, insisted that the more offensive remarks were \u8220\'20\'1Cadlibbed\u8221\'20\'1D and not on any draft given to the campaign.\par \par \uc2 Many of the remarks from Sunday appeared to be read from teleprompters, CNN reported, indicating they had been approved by someone within the event\u8217\'20\'19s planning team.\par \par \uc2 Another Trump campaign adviser told the broadcaster that they were uncertain as to how the overtly racist language had made it to the stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Tony Hinchcliffe workshopped offensive Puerto Rico joke the night before Madison Square Garden Rally \u8212\'20\'14 report\par \par \uc2 Tony Hinchcliffe \u8211\'20\'13 the comedian who delivered offensive and racist jokes during the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  rally on Sunday in New York where he referred Puerto Rico as \u8220\'20\'1Ca floating island of garbage\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 reportedly practised the line the night before at a Manhattan comedy club, according to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/latino/tony-hinchcliffe-trump-rally-racist-puerto-rico-remarks-rcna177587"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News}}}\uc2  report.\par \par \uc2 At the comedy club, the joke did not draw laughs, NBC reports, instead prompting only a few \u8220\'20\'1Cawkward chuckles.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During his set, Hinchcliffe reportedly mentioned to the audience that he was going to be performing at the \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  Trump rally the next day.\par \par \uc2 Hinchcliffe allegedly stated multiple times throughout his routine that he expected to receive a better reaction \u8220\'20\'1Ctomorrow at the rally.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump rally speaker: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s literally a floating island of garbage in the middle of the ocean right now. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s called Puerto Rico\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pbw88p5PhI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pbw88p5PhI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1850616657477095712?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 27, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.28pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  set to give her closing argument address in Washington DC later today\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will give her closing argument speech later today at the Ellipse in Washington DC, just one week before election day.\par \par \uc2 She is expected to deliver {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/kamala-harris-turn-the-page-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a hopeful and optimistic message }}}\uc2  that\u8217\'20\'19s focused on moving forward.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/29/kamala-harris-turn-the-page-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris to urge voters to \u8216\'20\'18turn the page\u8217\'20\'19 on era of Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 Democratic vice-presidential candidate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is scheduled to deliver remarks in Georgia today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.43pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.02pm GMT\par \par \uc2 Key event\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania is investigating potential voter fraud after an \u8220\'20\'1Coverabundance\u8221\'20\'1D of voter registration forms and requests for mail ballots were sent to the York County elections office.\par \par \uc2 The York County elections office received a \u8220\'20\'1Clarge delivery containing thousands of election-related materials from a third-party organization,\u8221\'20\'1D including voter registration forms and mail-ballot applications, York County President Commissioner Julie Wheeler said in a statement to the York Daily Record.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C As with all submissions, our staff follows a process for ensuring all voter registrations and mail-in ballot requests are legal. That process is currently underway. If suspected fraud is identified, we will alert the District Attorney\u8217\'20\'19s Office, which will then conduct an investigation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Wheeler told Fox 43 on Monday: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not unusual to get large stacks of voter registrations or large stacks of requests for mail-in ballots; it\u8217\'20\'19s just this was an overabundance of registrations from one particular organization.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to do our homework before we go and make accusations when we don\u8217\'20\'19t have the data to back it up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.03pm GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48am GMT\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  are fending off a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican}}}\uc2  offensive aimed at overturning their tiny majority in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Retaking control of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-congress"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Congress}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber may represent the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s best opportunity of success in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 November\u8217\'20\'19s election}}}\uc2 , according to analysts, surpassing their chances of retaking the White House or even retaining control of the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 But with a burst of enthusiasm from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  campaign, Democrats are still competitive\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/senate-races-elections-to-watch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The key US Senate races that could determine who controls the chamber}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump ally \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  released from prison week before election\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  ally \uc2 Steve Bannon\uc2  has been released from prison after serving a four-month sentence.\par \par \uc2 Bannon, 70, was jailed for defying a subpoena in the congressional investigation into the attack on the US Capitol on 6 January 2021. When he began serving his sentence in July, Bannon called himself a \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical prisoner\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am proud of going to prison,\u8221\'20\'1D he said at the time, adding that he was standing up to the attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , and a \u8220\'20\'1Ccorrupt\u8221\'20\'1D justice department.\par \par \uc2 Bannon will have to answer further charges at trial in New York. He is accused of tricking donors who gave money to help build Trump\u8217\'20\'19s notorious wall along the US-Mexico border. Bannon has pleaded not guilty to money laundering, conspiracy, fraud and other charges. The trial begins in December.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.59am GMT\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37am GMT\par \par \uc2 Trump claims he's 'the opposite of a Nazi' as rally fallout continues\par \par \uc2 Campaigning is ramping up in the race to the White House as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continue to exchange barbs on the campaign trail. Only seven days remain until Americans head to the polls on Tuesday, 5 November. On Monday, Harris and Tim Waltz courted young voters in Michigan, while \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and Bruce Springsteen spoke in Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in Atlanta, Georgia, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  railed against being compared to Hitler, telling voters that he was the \u8220\'20\'1Copposite of a Nazi\u8221\'20\'1D in response to Democratic opponents, who likened him to the Nazi dictator after a slew of racist remarks were made at his rally in Madison Square Garden on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Trump will hold a news conference at Mar-a-Lago at 10am ET \u8211\'20\'13 where he is likely to face questions about racist remarks about Puerto Rico at the New York event.\par \par \uc2 He is then heading to Allentown, Pennsylvania \u8211\'20\'13 home to tens of thousands of Puerto Ricans.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Campaigning for Harris in Wisconsin, Bernie Sanders said: \u8220\'20\'1CYou have \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  saying I can\u8217\'20\'19t support the guy I worked with for four years\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CWe cannot allow someone to be president of the United States who is a pathological liar and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/28/alexandria-ocasio-cortez-bernie-sanders-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  who is working night and day to undermine American democracy}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Sanders also released a video addressing voter concerns over the Biden-Harris administration\u8217\'20\'19s record on Gaza, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CAfter Kamala wins, we will together do everything that we can to change US policy towards Netanyahu.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/28/obama-bruce-springsteen-rally-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 performing at a rally with Obama in Pennsylvania}}}\uc2 , Bruce Springsteen said: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m Bruce Springsteen and I\u8217\'20\'19m here today to support \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and to oppose \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance \u8230\'20\'26 I want a president who reveres the constitution, who does not threaten but wants to protect and guide our great democracy, who believes in the rule of law and the peaceful transfer of power, who will fight for women\u8217\'20\'19s rights \u8230\'20\'26 [and] create a middle-class economy that works for all our citizens.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2021/sep/28/anita-hill-on-sexual-harassment-and-survival-you-have-to-think-what-is-my-life-for"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anita Hill}}}\uc2 , a former clerk to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/clarence-thomas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Clarence Thomas}}}\uc2 , has said \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/01/kamala-harris-texas-rally-donald-trump-racial-identity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 racist}}}\uc2 , misogynist and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/29/donald-trump-kamala-harris-sexist-post"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sexist}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/24/kamala-harris-doug-emhoff-sexist-antisemitic-attacks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 insults}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D aimed at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cmust sting\u8221\'20\'1D. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/28/opinion/kamala-harris-dignity.html?smid=nytcore-android-share"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times opinion piece}}}\uc2  published on Monday, the \uc2 Brandeis University\uc2  professor \u8211\'20\'13 who was famously brought before Thomas\u8217\'20\'19s confirmation hearings only to have her sexual harassment allegations against him picked apart by sitting senators \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/28/anita-hill-harris-op-ed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote that she sympathises with the US vice-president}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.40am GMT\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241029ekat001rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
