\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18A Trojan horse\u8217\'20\'19: how the right is using \u8216\'20\'18parental rights\u8217\'20\'19 to fight  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ballot measures\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 1,382 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 October 2024\par 14:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 With 10 states set to vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related measures, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists are trying to disrupt a streak of wins\par \par \uc2 A Maryland ballot measure to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state constitution is, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wjla.com/news/local/trojan-horse-tactic-new-md-group-fights-reproductive-rights-amendment-health-not-harm-maryland-md-reproductive-rights-abortion-annapolis-ballot-initiative"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Maryland activist claims}}}\uc2 , a \u8220\'20\'1CTrojan horse to trick pro-choice Marylanders into voting away parental rights\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Opponents of a New York referendum, which is meant to cement protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/nbc-out/out-politics-and-policy/ny-ballot-measure-abortion-transgender-culture-wars-rcna174845"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have started calling it}}}\uc2  the \u8220\'20\'1CParent Replacement Act\u8221\'20\'1D and claim it would expand rights for transgender minors.\par \par \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2 , the Republican senator from Missouri, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kansascity.com/news/politics-government/article292624044.html#storylink=cpy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said}}}\uc2  that his state\u8217\'20\'19s ballot measure would \u8220\'20\'1Cmandate constitutionally, all \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  services, and that includes transgender treatments for minors\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In the two years since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights has soared. Seven states have voted on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures, and in every state, voters have sided with supporters of the procedure, including in deep-red states like Kentucky and Ohio. Now, in the run-up to election day, 10 states are set to vote on their own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures \u8211\'20\'13 and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists across the country are trying to disrupt that streak using the specter of \u8220\'20\'1Cparental rights\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 These measures, they say, could strip parents of their right to make decisions for their children \u8211\'20\'13 an argument that, in the years since the Covid pandemic broke out, has become an increasingly potent weapon in US culture wars.\par \par \uc2 Legal experts say these claims are overblown.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a vast oversimplification of what\u8217\'20\'19s happening,\u8221\'20\'1D said Nicole Huberfeld, a professor who leads the Boston University School of Law\u8217\'20\'19s reproductive law program.\par \par \uc2 More than 30 states say minors cannot obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  without notifying a parent or obtaining their consent. If a state with such a law \u8211\'20\'13 called a \u8220\'20\'1Cparental involvement law\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 passes a measure expanding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the law would not immediately be struck down, according to Huberfeld. Instead, a court would need to rule on the issue. And, although the exact wording of each measure would ultimately determine how it was interpreted, Huberfeld said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t see these issues as being real issues.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She continued: \u8220\'20\'1CThey are fear and confusion campaigns. There are efforts to try to confuse the people who will be voting on these ballot initiatives, to make it so that they don\u8217\'20\'19t understand what they\u8217\'20\'19re voting on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, because some forms of gender-affirming care can affect people\u8217\'20\'19s ability to reproduce, opponents have suggested that measures to protect reproductive healthcare would also protect minors\u8217\'20\'19 access to gender-affirming care. But experts say that it has not been firmly established that gender-affirming care legally falls under the banner of \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven if you accept that it could have this wild, expansive meaning, there still are ways within the text of the amendment that allow the government to pass laws around this topic,\u8221\'20\'1D one law professor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://missouriindependent.com/2024/10/16/missouri-abortion-gender-affirming-health-care-amendment-3/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the Missouri Independent}}}\uc2  after Hawley\u8217\'20\'19s comments.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, touting these claims has become a go-to strategy in the anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  playbook. Michigan and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/03/ohio-abortion-vote-misinformation-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2 , which respectively passed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures in 2022 and 2023, were both hit with messaging around parental rights and warnings from anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists that the measures would erase parental involvement laws around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gender-affirming care. Both states still require minors to obtain consent from their parents before undergoing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . And while Michigan permits gender-affirming care for minors \u8211\'20\'13 and did so before the ballot measure passed \u8211\'20\'13 a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/transgender-health-ohio-ruling-70a054af6729c06a3d892edfa004caed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 judge recently upheld Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s ban}}}\uc2  on it.\par \par \uc2 Kelly Hall, executive director of the Fairness Project, which is backing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights measures in several states, believes claims about parental rights are a calculated distraction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt does reveal that our opponents really do understand that the electorate is not with them on the core, fundamental issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Hall said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s no other reason they would be trying to change the subject so dramatically.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Florida invented this playbook\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 The most heated and high-profile \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related measure of the election is playing out in Florida, which currently bans the procedure after six weeks of pregnancy \u8211\'20\'13 and is arguably the headquarters of the modern-day parental rights movement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmendment 4 would remove the requirement for parental consent for minors seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/RonDeSantis/status/1847304317809852695"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted on X last week}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAmendment 4 would undermine the foundation of parental rights in Florida.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also shared an ad featuring Dr Grazie Christie, a radiologist, calling Amendment 4 \u8220\'20\'1Ctoo extreme and not what it seems\u8221\'20\'1D. In the ad, Christie says: \u8220\'20\'1CAmendment 4 would make \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  the only medical procedure a minor could undergo without parental consent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since the pandemic ignited debates around Covid safety measures in schools, the idea of parental rights has become a rallying cry among activists who claim government institutions are intruding on parents\u8217\'20\'19 rights to make decisions for their children. Moms for \uc2 Liberty\uc2 , the far-right group that advocates for book bans and limiting discussions about race and LGBTQ+ identities, calls Florida home. The state also passed the nation\u8217\'20\'19s first \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t say gay\u8221\'20\'1D bill, which aims to block teachers from speaking about sexual orientation and gender identity. (A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/11/florida-dont-say-gay-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settlement later allowed teachers}}}\uc2  to talk about these topics as long as the discussion is not part of formal instruction.)\par \par \uc2 Now, Florida is a battlefield over Amendment 4, which would roll back the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. More than $70m has been poured into the fight over the amendment, which needs to garner 60% of the vote to pass \u8211\'20\'13 a threshold that no post-Roe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measure has met.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida did invent this playbook, and I\u8217\'20\'19m hoping that this is a time where we get to put this playbook to bed,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lauren Brenzel, the campaign director of Floridians Protecting Freedom, the coalition spearheading the campaign for the amendment.\par \par \uc2 Floridians Protecting Freedom has sued Florida officials at least twice \u8211\'20\'13 once for attempting to block a TV ad in support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and once over a state-run website that suggested that, among other things, Amendment 4 could \u8220\'20\'1Copen discussions about the role of parental involvement in a minor\u8217\'20\'19s decision to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. Aaron Bos-Lun, the Florida-based deputy executive director of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/20/abortion-rights-dobbs-men"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -rights group Men4Choice}}}\uc2 , said he had recently been barraged by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ads that talk about Amendment 4 and its alleged impact on Florida\u8217\'20\'19s parental consent law requirements.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we canvass, when we talk with voters \u8211\'20\'13 whether that\u8217\'20\'19s on the phones or at the doors \u8211\'20\'13 there\u8217\'20\'19s definitely been an uptick of people who have heard some piece of misinformation about the ballot initiative,\u8221\'20\'1D Bos-Lun said.\par \par \uc2 Parental involvement laws involving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  have long been popular with American voters. In 2022, 70% of Americans said they supported laws requiring minors to notify their parents about their decisions to get abortions, including 57% of self-identified Democrats, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/05/16/democrats-gop-parental-notification-abortion-laws-00097245"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Pew Research Center found}}}\uc2 . Even since Roe fell, boosting support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2023/05/16/democrats-gop-parental-notification-abortion-laws-00097245"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 activists have struggled}}}\uc2  to get even their allies in state legislatures to consider repealing them.\par \par \uc2 Amendment 4 explicitly declares that it \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not change the legislature\u8217\'20\'19s constitutional authority to require notification to a parent or guardian before a minor has an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D. Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists claim the amendment would permit Florida minors to only notify their parents that they want an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not to obtain their consent, as Florida law currently requires.\par \par \uc2 But Floridians Protecting Freedom says the amendment does not aim to change Florida\u8217\'20\'19s parental consent law. Louis Virelli, a professor of constitutional law at Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Stetson University College of Law, agreed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmendment 4 leaves enough space for courts to say: \u8216\'20\'18Yes, legislature, you can regulate parental consent.\u8217\'20\'19 That is a certainty,\u8221\'20\'1D Virelli said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no good-faith argument that says it absolutely, unequivocally prohibits them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With parental rights being invoked in some of the United States\u8217\'20\'19 biggest culture-war issues \u8211\'20\'13 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , LGBTQ+ rights, vaccines \u8211\'20\'13 Huberfeld sees a clear through-line.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a new tool in the toolbox of anti-medicine, anti-public health campaigns,\u8221\'20\'1D Huberfeld said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is just another feature of how that\u8217\'20\'19s playing out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241028ekas001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
