\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris and Trump lean into their faith in appeals to Christian voters in Georgia\b0\par\par\uc2 George Chidi in Atlanta \par \uc2 1,643 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 October 2024\par 14:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Religious voters on both the right and the left are a powerful force in Georgia. In a race this close, they may be decisive\par \par \uc2 Two Georgia megachurches hosted presidential candidates last week, highlighting the stark differences between how \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  speak about faith and what Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Christian religious congregations expect of them.\par \par \uc2 Though Trump and Harris communicate differently to the public about their faith, religious leaders on the left and the right are casting this election in apocalyptic terms. And both candidates know religious voters will be essential to winning swing states like Georgia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is so good to be here with everyone today and to worship with you,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said from the pulpit to thousands gathered at New Birth Missionary Baptist church in south DeKalb county last Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1COn this day, then, I am reminded, with everything that we reflect on, on the parable from the Gospel of Luke.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Four thousand people packed the pews of the predominantly Black megachurch outside of Atlanta, one of the most prominent and powerful Black churches in America \u8211\'20\'13 a point of which pastor Jamal Bryant regularly reminds his congregation. New Birth owns more land than any Black church in America. It gave away $83m in college scholarships last year, he said.\par \par \uc2 It wields its political clout deftly. New Birth\u8217\'20\'19s congregants include many of Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful political figures \u8211\'20\'13 mayors, sheriffs, members of Congress. Bryant said it has hosted appearances by five presidents.\par \par \uc2 But people who attend New Birth aren\u8217\'20\'19t there for a stump speech. And Harris didn\u8217\'20\'19t give one.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t want to give political speeches in a sanctuary, because you\u8217\'20\'19re there to worship God,\u8221\'20\'1D said state senator Emanuel Jones, a DeKalb Democrat who attended church at New Birth last week. \u8220\'20\'1CTo me, it is not a good use of a sanctuary to try and politicize \u8211\'20\'13 particularly on a Sunday, by the way \u8211\'20\'13 to try and mix politics with religion. I think she does a really good job of keeping them separate. She did that today, and we all should.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris campaigned in Georgia with her pastor Rev Dr \uc2 Amos Brown\uc2 , pastor at Third Baptist Church of San Francisco and a contemporary of \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr\uc2  and other luminaries in Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s civil rights history. She told a CNN town hall a few days later that her first call after learning that Biden would be withdrawing was to Brown.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do pray every day,\u8221\'20\'1D she told Anderson Cooper. \u8220\'20\'1CSometimes twice a day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris will discuss her faith when it comes up, but doesn\u8217\'20\'19t go out of her way to portray her campaign as religiously motivated. Conversely, she never mentioned her campaign directly while speaking at New Birth. She shied away from the political themes common to her political rhetoric \u8211\'20\'13 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, the cost of living and the general unfitness of her opponent. She used the word \u8220\'20\'1Cfaith\u8221\'20\'1D 16 times in her 14-minute address.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFaith is a verb,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe show it in action, in our deeds and in our service.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Though she had not come to deliver a political speech, in a church with the flags of dozens of countries lining the balconies, the subtext was clear enough \u8211\'20\'13 a repudiation of conservative xenophobia about immigrants.\par \par \uc2 Elaine Montgomery heard it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLike she said, when you don\u8217\'20\'19t help people like my neighbors and we all in this world,\u8221\'20\'1D Montgomery said. \u8220\'20\'1CEverything belongs to God.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Montgomery, 69, from Stone Mountain, Georgia, was wearing a pink hat big enough to see from space that Sunday. She was on her way to vote. Her disdain for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s expression of faith was plain.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s a man speaking on a level that\u8217\'20\'19s below God, I will say that,\u8221\'20\'1D Montgomery said. Her voice lowered. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t really think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had faith. I really don\u8217\'20\'19t. I\u8217\'20\'19m serious, you know, because if he had faith and he believed in Jesus Christ, he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be doing the things he does.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Faith matters in Georgia. White Christian evangelical beliefs correlate with the strongest support for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and about 38% of Georgians fall into that category, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religious-landscape-study/database/state/georgia/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew Research Center}}}\uc2 . Black voters in Georgia are also much more likely to be religious than the baseline, and Black voters represent about 30% of the electorate.\par \par \uc2 Georgia, in the heart of the Bible belt, has one of the highest rates of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/religious-landscape-study/database/compare/attendance-at-religious-services/by/state/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 regular church attendance}}}\uc2  in America at 42%.\par \par \uc2 Last Sunday, 42,694 voters cast a ballot in Georgia, many going in a \u8220\'20\'1Csouls to the polls\u8221\'20\'1D push regularly organized by churches, particularly in metro Atlanta. In the flurry of conservative election legislation that followed the 2020 election in Georgia, a plan to eliminate Sunday early voting floated through the legislature. Outcry from pastors across the state ended that gambit. Mobilizing religiously motivated voters is a necessary, if insufficient, requirement for any candidate to win a Georgia election.\par \par \uc2 Trump found himself in Zebulon, Georgia, last week, doing just that.\par \par \uc2 He was 45 minutes late to the faith town hall held at Christ Chapel church. Thousands of people packed its hall and sprawled into a parking lot ringed by semi-truck trailers with snipers on the roofs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, without religion, it\u8217\'20\'19s like the \u8211\'20\'13 it\u8217\'20\'19s like the glue that holds it all together. This would be a different country,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, noting a declining trend in religious participation, suggesting that \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople started thinking a little bit differently and they got used to a different way of life\u8221\'20\'1D after the pandemic. He spoke about how Christians \u8211\'20\'13 particularly Catholics \u8211\'20\'13 faced unspecified \u8220\'20\'1Cpersecution\u8221\'20\'1D today in America.\par \par \uc2 But most of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments at the \u8220\'20\'1CBelievers and Ballots\u8221\'20\'1D town hall were campaign fodder about illegal immigration, how great his rallies have been and attacks on Harris and the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 About 1,100 people live in Zebulon, about an hour and a half south of Atlanta. Christ Chapel has about 1,600 members, with more at satellite campuses in middle Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Brian Hood, a congregant at Christ Chapel, said he expected Trump to speak about the border and inflation, but also freedom of religion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDonald J Trump professes to be a born-again Christian. Does that mean that he\u8217\'20\'19s perfect? Of course not. None of us are. Anybody who says they are is a liar. He appeals to, not just Christians, but all the American people. He loves God and loves people, all walks of life.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, Burt Jones, a Republican and ally of the former president, asked Trump about coping with the assassination attempts and the pressure of the campaign. \u8220\'20\'1CHow do you lean into your faith and your family to deal with this?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI say this. Faith \u8211\'20\'13 when you have faith, when you believe in God, it\u8217\'20\'19s a big advantage over people that don\u8217\'20\'19t have that. It\u8217\'20\'19s a big advantage,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump replied.\par \par \uc2 It was the only substantial reference Trump made to his own faith in the abbreviated 40-minute forum for faith voters.\par \par \uc2 Ralph Reed\uc2 , chairman of the Faith & Freedom Coalition and a longtime activist on the Christian right, succinctly laid out the stakes for antiabortion conservatives as he warmed up the crowd before Trump\u8217\'20\'19s arrival.\par \par \uc2 Harris is \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to pass a federal law to impose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on demand on all 50 states\u8221\'20\'1D, Reed said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd when she\u8217\'20\'19s done doing that, she\u8217\'20\'19s going to repeal the filibuster and then she\u8217\'20\'19s going to pass a federal law imposing term limits on the supreme court which will instantly remove justices \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 , \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  and \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  from the court and she\u8217\'20\'19s going to replace them with the most leftwing radical extremist justices ever nominated. That\u8217\'20\'19s her agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The first accomplishment listed on the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://believers.donaldjtrump.com/accomplishments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Believers for Trump}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D website is how Trump appointed three supreme court justices, \u8220\'20\'1Cwhich led to the end of Roe v Wade and broader protections for religious liberties\u8221\'20\'1D. Ending legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is central to the religious conservatism of many of his supporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe that life begins in conception. I cannot follow the dictates of being able to abort at any time,\u8221\'20\'1D said Carol Whitcomb of Stockbridge, a conservative who attended the Trump forum.\par \par \uc2 But it also may be a losing political position, even in Georgia. In every state where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights have been a ballot referendum since the end of federal protections, voters have taken the more pro-choice position. Trump has generally avoided talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the campaign trail, with no mention of it at all in a later appearance in Georgia last week.\par \par \uc2 Sandra Stargel of McDonough, Georgia, who attended the forum, has registered a change in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s posture toward \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut, you know, I believe God has been talking to him, too. God has him here for a reason. I understand that women want to be in charge of their bodies. I get that. But in that case, they make birth control. Use it. Don\u8217\'20\'19t just keep killing babies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reed highlighted the stakes of the election: \u8220\'20\'1CWe gather in this sanctuary 13 days before not only the most important election of our lifetimes but one of the most important elections in American history,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 While Harris was at New Birth a few days earlier, the church\u8217\'20\'19s pastor Bryant used similar rhetoric, likening this political moment to the biblical story of Esther and her obligation to save Jews from death. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you are silent in this moment, your family will not survive,\u8221\'20\'1D Bryant said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not the time for y\u8217\'20\'19all to be bougie and stuck up. Generations of your unborn family are waiting to see what you do next.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241027ekar001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
