\par\par \uc2 Music\par \b \uc2 Stevie Nicks says Fleetwood Mac would have been \u8216\'20\'18done\u8217\'20\'19 without 1977  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Ramon Antonio Vargas \par \uc2 743 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 October 2024\par 13:43 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Legendary singer-songwriter tells Rolling Stone new song was inspired by battle to reinstate federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/stevie-nicks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stevie Nicks}}}\uc2  thrust herself into the ongoing fight for access to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in the US because she had \u8220\'20\'1Cbeen there, done that\u8221\'20\'1D, the legendary singer-songwriter says in a new interview.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI tell a good story,\u8221\'20\'1D Nicks remarked in an interview conducted by CBS News Sunday Morning, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSSunday/status/1849808225043873795"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clip}}}\uc2  of which was circulated by the network in advance. \u8220\'20\'1CSo maybe I should try to do something.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was also there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nicks\u8217\'20\'19 comments come after the release in September of her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2024/sep/27/stevie-nicks-song-abortion-rights-the-lighthouse-fleetwood-mac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new single}}}\uc2  The Lighthouse, which was inspired by progressives\u8217\'20\'19 battle to reinstate federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the US.\par \par \uc2 She wrote the rock song after three \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  justices appointed by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  White House voted to essentially overturn the 1973 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  ruling that gave Americans a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-features/stevie-nicks-fleetwood-mac-kamala-harris-new-music-1235140437/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a recent Rolling Stone interview}}}\uc2 , Nicks discussed her certainty that if she had not gotten an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the 1970s, it would have marked the end of the renowned band {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/fleetwood-mac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fleetwood Mac}}}\uc2  that she ultimately helped launch to rock immortality.\par \par \uc2 Nicks at the time had a contraceptive intrauterine device but nonetheless became pregnant by the singer Don Henley after breaking up her prior relationship with Lindsey Buckingham, her Fleetwood Mac bandmate, she told Rolling Stone. She said she decided to terminate the pregnancy in about 1977, or going into 1978, as Fleetwood Mac sat atop the world after its album Rumours.\par \par \uc2 Rumours won Fleetwood Mac the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/grammys"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Grammy}}}\uc2  for album of the year in 1978, a year that saw the band play 18 live {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fleetwoodmac-uk.com/concerts/Rumours-Tour/rumours-tour.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shows}}}\uc2  in 11 US states. Three of the album\u8217\'20\'19s singles \u8211\'20\'13 Go Your Own Way, Don\u8217\'20\'19t Stop and You Make Loving Fun \u8211\'20\'13 reached the top 10 on the charts. Dreams, with Nicks\u8217\'20\'19 vocals, went No 1 as Rumours eventually finished seventh on \uc2 Rolling Stone\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s list of the 500 greatest albums of all time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow what the hell am I going to do?\u8221\'20\'1D Nicks said to Rolling Stone about her thought process at the time of her aborted pregnancy. \u8220\'20\'1CI cannot have a child. I am not the kind of woman who would hand my baby over to a nanny, not in a million years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo we would be dragging a baby around the world on tour, and I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t do that to my baby. I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t say I just need nine months. I would say I need a couple of years, and that would break up the band period.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nicks, 76, said she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Creally care\u8221\'20\'1D if people become upset with her over having decided to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CMy life was my life, and my plan was my plan and had been since I was in the fourth grade,\u8221\'20\'1D Nicks said to Rolling Stone, adding that Fleetwood Mac would have been \u8220\'20\'1Cdone\u8221\'20\'1D if she had decided otherwise.\par \par \uc2 Nicks\u8217\'20\'19 remarks to Rolling Stone about her personal experience with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  elaborate on ones she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2020/oct/14/stevie-nicks-on-art-ageing-and-attraction-botox-makes-it-look-like-youre-in-a-satanic-cult"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 delivered}}}\uc2  to the Guardian in 2020, when she said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s just no way that I could have had a child then, working as hard as we worked constantly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, after the reversal of Roe v Wade as Trump set his sights on a second presidency in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 5 November election}}}\uc2 , Nicks said she heard everywhere around her that \u8220\'20\'1Csomebody has to do \u8230\'20\'26 [and] say something\u8221\'20\'1D to support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I\u8217\'20\'19m like: \u8216\'20\'18Well I have a platform,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Nicks said after the \uc2 CBS\uc2  Sunday Morning correspondent Tracy Smith asked the singer about the courage needed to \u8220\'20\'1Cstep into the waters of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  debate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The result was The Lighthouse, a rare new release for Nicks, whose last album of entirely fresh material was put out in 2011. The single casts her as a lighthouse guiding women to campaign for their rights as voters choose between {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and Trump, whose supporters include a conservative thinktank that is urging him to step up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/fact-sheet/how-project-2025-seeks-obliterate-srhr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacks against sexual and \b  \highlight22reproductive health\b0 \highlight22  and rights}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ll take your soul, take your power, unless you stand up, take it back,\u8221\'20\'1D Nicks sings on the track. \u8220\'20\'1CTry to see the future and get mad/It\u8217\'20\'19s slipping through your fingers, you don\u8217\'20\'19t have what you had/And you don\u8217\'20\'19t have much time to get it back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241027ekar000ji\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
