\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris in Texas, Trump in New York: rivals campaign in surprise spots\b0\par\par\uc2 Adam Gabbatt \par \uc2 824 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 October 2024\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The candidates have taken detours from the critical swing states into unfriendly territory \u8211\'20\'13 what\u8217\'20\'19s in it for them?\par \par \uc2 Texas is not a usual stop for a Democratic presidential candidate, yet 11 days out from the election, that\u8217\'20\'19s where \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  could be found.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president held a campaign rally in the traditionally Republican state on Friday, appearing alongside Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 and the Senate candidate \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2 . But it is not just Democrats who are venturing into uncharted territory \u8211\'20\'13 on Sunday \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will appear at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2 , in the deep blue New York.\par \par \uc2 Both candidates will be visiting key swing states including Michigan and Pennsylvania in the coming days, but these extra-curricular visits give them a chance to tap into key messages, in moments the Harris and Trump campaigns will be eagerly capturing and distributing online.\par \par \uc2 In an election which will essentially be decided by voters in seven or fewer states, it\u8217\'20\'19s also a chance to demonstrate inclusiveness, said Shannon Bow O\u8217\'20\'19Brien, a politics professor at the \uc2 University of Texas at Austin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of things people criticize the Democrats for, and I think rightly so, is they frequently treat the interior of the country like flyover country, and they routinely ignore these types of places,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think maybe also going down here, is signaling that she\u8217\'20\'19s gonna pay attention to these areas too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For Harris, the visit to Texas was an opportunity for her to drive home the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which she has made one of the key issues of her campaign. Trump has bragged about being responsible for the overturning of Roe v Wade, which guaranteed the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the US.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign launched a series of new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4zNmmiYjDgQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -related ads}}}\uc2  this week, telling the story of a Texas woman who contracted a life-threatening infection when was denied proper medical care after miscarrying at 16 weeks pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTexas is symbolically really important, because \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  for Harris is a strong issue, and Texas has been the origin of a number of really heartbreaking stories about the consequences of an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. And any meaningful challenges to the ban in front of the supreme court have come from women out of Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mona Kleinberg, a professor of political communication at the \uc2 City University of New York\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Texas stop created another thing: content. Aided by the star power of Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9, the Harris campaign will hope that their message about Trump and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  can gain a wide audience online, including in swing states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObviously the most important decision a presidential campaign makes is where their principal is spending time,\u8221\'20\'1D David Plouffe, a Harris senior adviser, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/2024/10/24/beyonce-kamala-harris-houston-rally/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CSo the fact that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to Texas means we really believe that will help us in those seven battleground states.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Kleinberg said the presence of Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 added a level of excitement that Harris may be struggling to generate, while also guaranteeing coverage on national news shows.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CObama was such a good orator, he had all this charm, he generated a lot of excitement. Harris hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been able to do the same: in part because she has had less time, in part because she\u8217\'20\'19s a woman, she has this double burden, but I think she needs that. That\u8217\'20\'19s why Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 is important,\u8221\'20\'1D Kleinberg said.\par \par \uc2 The Texas trip came as Trump prepared to visit New York, where he lived for decades before departing after his first pugnacious election campaign. His appearance, at the famous arena in midtown, has same thinking as Harris\u8217\'20\'19s Texas visit, Kleinberg said: highlight a key campaign issue while drawing eyeballs. States including Texas have sent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/20/us/abbott-texas-migrant-buses.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 45,000 undocumented}}}\uc2  migrants on buses to New York, and Trump will likely be aiming to play on fear around the issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about creating enthusiasm, and lots of anger. Anger is the number one mobilizing emotion, political psychology research shows this over and over again. Anger makes people not think but act. And so that\u8217\'20\'19s what they\u8217\'20\'19re going to be trying to generate,\u8221\'20\'1D Kleinberg said.\par \par \uc2 For a born-and-raised New Yorker who has spent a lifetime seeking the spotlight, an attraction will also be simply the thrill of appearing at one of the most famous venues in the world \u8211\'20\'13 which is also a mile from Trump Tower, where Trump still has an apartment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s going to get a big crowd. He loves the adulation. He\u8217\'20\'19s going to get a lot of attention. Everybody\u8217\'20\'19s going to be talking about him. That\u8217\'20\'19s nectar to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ears,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Brien said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it\u8217\'20\'19s a hell of a lot easier just to go there and then go to bed at Trump Tower than it is to be rigorously campaigning around the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241027ekar000un\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
