\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  introduces \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at Michigan rally; across state, Trump joined by Arab and Muslim leaders \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell \par \uc2 7,835 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2024\par 23:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Obama urges crowd to \u8216\'20\'18turn the page on the ugliness\u8217\'20\'19 as Michigan voters pledge support for Trump because \u8216\'20\'18he promised to end war\u8217\'20\'19. This blog is now closed.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now \u8211\'20\'13 thanks for following along. You can read our US elections coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . Here are the major developments from today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  joined \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for a rally focused on reproductive freedom in Kalamazoo, Michigan (or as Obama called it, \u8220\'20\'1CKamala-zoo\u8221\'20\'1D). The former first lady and the vice-president emphasized the stakes for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and reproductive healthcare if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is re-elected. Earlier in the day, Harris spoke with reproductive healthcare providers at a clinic in Portage, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 On the first day of early voting in Michigan, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also held a rally in Michigan. At an event in Novi, the ex-president was joined on stage by several imams and other leaders of the state\u8217\'20\'19s large Muslim and Arab American community, who denounced \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s handling of the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Later in the evening, Trump spoke at a second event in State College, Pennsylvania, where he again promised to ban sanctuary cities and launch a massive deportation program all while unleashing more personal attacks against Harris.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , who has become a vocal critic of \u8220\'20\'1Copen borders\u8221\'20\'1D, worked illegally in the United States early in his career, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2024/10/26/elon-musk-immigration-status/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 . After arriving in the United States for a graduate program at Stanford, Musk never attended classes and did not have work authorization when he started building the company that became Zip2.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  campaigned for Harris across Pennsylvania today, speaking with the \uc2 Laborers\u8217\'20\'19 International Union of North America\uc2  in Pittsburgh.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nika Soon-Shiong, whose family owns the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2 , says the paper\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to endorse a presidential candidate was made by her family due to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s position on the war in Gaza. Her father, Dr \uc2 Patrick Soon-Shiong\uc2 , who owns the paper, said his daughter was speaking in her personal capacity.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senator Bob Casey addressed members of the Carpenters Union in Philadelphia and attacked his Republican opponent, \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2 , over allegations that he fostered a toxic work environment as CEO of the hedge fund Bridgewater, describing the claims as \u8220\'20\'1Cdisqualifying\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris is expected to campaign across Philadelphia tomorrow while Trump gears up for a rally at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.18am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.06am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump ends his rally begging supporters to deliver a 'landslide'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  concluded his roughly hour-long rally in State College, Pennsylvania, with a request for all of his supporters to go to the polls on 5 November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith your vote this November, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to fire Kamala, and we are going to save America,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Again raising the specter of Democratic election meddling despite no evidence of such fraud in the 2020 presidential race, Trump implored his supporters to deliver a \u8220\'20\'1Clandslide\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe must defeat \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and stop a radical left agenda with a landslide that is too big to rig,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe will never ever back down, and we will never surrender.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump then walked off the stage with the sound of YMCA by the Village People playing in the background.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  unleashed more personal attacks against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at his Pennsylvania rally, dismissing her as a \u8220\'20\'1Cradical left lunatic\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He then gave a detailed account of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global/video/2024/oct/21/donald-trump-makes-fries-during-staged-campaign-event-at-mcdonalds-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 photo opp}}}\uc2  at \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s last week to recirculate baseless claims that Harris lied about working at the fast-food chain when she was in high school.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  again promised to ban sanctuary cities and launch a massive deportation program if he wins the presidential race, making xenophobic comments about how US towns have been \u8220\'20\'1Cconquered\u8221\'20\'1D by immigrants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are dangerous people. These are really dangerous people,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s nothing you\u8217\'20\'19re going to do about it to make them less dangerous.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanimmigrationcouncil.org/research/mass-deportation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  compiled by the \uc2 American Immigration Council\uc2  estimated the annual cost of deporting one million immigrants per year to be roughly $88bn.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  briefly touched on his baseless claims of widespread fraud in the 2020 presidential election as he addressed supporters in State College, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Trump noted that he won more votes in 2020 than any president in US history. That statement is true, but crucially, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 74m votes fell short of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 81m votes in the 2020 race. Trump unsurprisingly sidestepped that fact in his remarks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI got the most votes in the history of our country for a sitting president. Can you imagine? But they say they beat us,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1C[Biden] got a few more votes \u8211\'20\'13 sitting in his basement, not talking \u8211\'20\'13 and it\u8217\'20\'19s a disgrace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump then repeated his boast that he would easily defeat \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to pull this off. It\u8217\'20\'19ll be the greatest victory in the history of our country for all of us \u8211\'20\'13 not for me, for all of us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  griped about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/beyonce-brings-star-power-to-harris-rally-in-texas-with-abortion-law-in-the-spotlight"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign rally}}}\uc2  with Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 in Houston last night, mocking the event as a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisaster\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 endorsed Harris at the rally, telling the 30,000 people assembled at Shell Energy stadium: \u8220\'20\'1CFor all the men and women in this room, and watching around the country, we need you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite some speculation that Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 would perform, she did not, prompting ridicule from Trump.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe people went there because they thought they\u8217\'20\'19re going to hear Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 sing,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said at his rally in State College. \u8220\'20\'1CThen she turned around [and] she left.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should \u8220\'20\'1Cnever again\u8221\'20\'1D serve as president of the United States, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says, evoking the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s authoritarian tendencies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomeone who suggests we should terminate the Constitution of the United States should never again stand behind the seal of the President of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, before leading the crowd in a chorus of \u8220\'20\'1Cnever again\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo love our country is to know that one of the highest forms of patriotism, I believe, is to then fight for the ideals of our country,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric against \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has turned increasingly vitriolic in the final days of the presidential race, and he continued that trend at his rally in State College, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Promising a \u8220\'20\'1Cnew golden age\u8221\'20\'1D for the nation if he wins, Trump lambasted Harris and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leadership over the past four years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPennsylvania, you have to stand up and you have to tell Kamala that you\u8217\'20\'19ve had enough. You\u8217\'20\'19re not going to take it anymore. You\u8217\'20\'19re the worst vice-president,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re just horrible, Kamala. You\u8217\'20\'19re fired. Get out of here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Echoing \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is trying to draw a through-line between her ancestors in the civil rights movement, her work to preserve reproductive freedom and gen Z\u8217\'20\'19s advocacy around a host of issues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou, who have only known the climate crisis, are leading the charge to protect our planet and our future. You, who grew up with active shooter drills, are fighting to keep our schools safe. You, who now know fewer rights than your mothers and grandmothers, are standing up for reproductive freedom. And for you, all these issues are not, they\u8217\'20\'19re not political. They\u8217\'20\'19re your lived experience. And I want to tell you I see you, and I see your power,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is lauding the Affordable Care Act and speaking about reproductive freedom at her Kalamazoo rally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe healthcare should be a right and not a privilege of those who have the money to afford it. On the other hand, we\u8217\'20\'19ve got \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who intends to end the Affordable Care Act, or as we like to call it, Obamacare,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI did an event in Texas last night in Houston and if you saw it, you probably saw some of the stories about what has been happening in our country, the suffering,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, refering to women and families who shared their stories of struggling to access medical care under \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Noting that Michigan has protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, Harris added, \u8220\'20\'1Cif there\u8217\'20\'19s a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, nobody is safe.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  takes stage in State College, Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Arriving about an hour-and-a-half late, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has taken the stage for his campaign rally in State College, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 In his typical boasting manner, Trump claimed he is \u8220\'20\'1Cleading in all the polls\u8221\'20\'1D. even as surveys suggest the presidential race is a true toss-up with just 10 days left before election day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re leading, but we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to close it out,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1COn November 5, America will be bigger, better, bolder, richer, safer and stronger than ever before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Bob Casey attacked his Republican opponent, \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2 , over allegations that he fostered a toxic work environment as CEO of the hedge fund Bridgewater, describing the claims as \u8220\'20\'1Cdisqualifying\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve always placed a priority on combating sexual harassment in the workplace, and apparently at Bridgewater, it was just a whole different story,\u8221\'20\'1D Casey told reporters this morning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo he\u8217\'20\'19s being held accountable for that, and he should be held accountable. I think that alone is disqualfiying. If you\u8217\'20\'19ve engaged in that kind of activity in the private sector, you should not be a public official at any level.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Casey campaign released an ad this week highlighting claims that McCormick attempted to silence or retaliate against female employees of Bridgewater who came forward with harassment claims.\par \par \uc2 Casey\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager also penned a letter calling on McCormick to demand that Bridgewater release employees who reported harassment from their non-disclosure agreements.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is your responsibility to ensure the voters of Pennsylvania have complete information about your record before casting their votes,\u8221\'20\'1D Tiernan Donohue, Casey\u8217\'20\'19s campaign manager, wrote in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://bobcasey.com/wp-content/uploads/Letter-to-Dave-McCormick_Bridgewater-NDAs.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the letter}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey deserve the full story.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters after his event with the Carpenters Union, Senator Bob Casey said he believes the momentum and enthusiasm on the ground in Pennsylvania will lift Democrats to victory in 10 days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it is close. There\u8217\'20\'19s no question about that,\u8221\'20\'1D Casey said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat energy and intensity on the ground is starting to uplift our side. I\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen the number of volunteers that we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen in this state. Every weekend they\u8217\'20\'19re breaking another record.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrAsked about how close the race feels 10 days out, Casey said momentum is on Dems\u8217\'20\'19 side.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat energy and intensity on the ground is starting to uplift our side. I've never seen the number of volunteers we've seen in this state. Every weekend, they're breaking another record.\u8220\'20\'1C\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1850179869314814187?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Asked specifically about whether young voters will turn out to vote for him and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , Casey expressed confidence that they would.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the turnout is going to be high,\u8221\'20\'1D Casey said. \u8220\'20\'1CYoung voters might engage a little late, but I think they\u8217\'20\'19re ready to vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is drawing out the personal and political differences between her and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI grew up in a middle class neighborhood with a working mother who kept a strict budget and did everything she could to make sure my sister and I had all that we needed. I come from the middle class, and I will never forget where I come from,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cagenda is all laid out in Project 2025, which I still must say, I cannot believe they put that in writing,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, before going on to talk about her plan for a child tax credit and to lower housing and healthcare costs.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senator Bob Casey addressed members of the Carpenters Union in Philadelphia this morning, as the three-term Democrat enters the final 10 days of his race against Republican \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Casey, whose race has grown {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/analysis/senate/senate-overview/two-weeks-go-pennsylvania-senate-shifts-toss-nebraska-senate-moves"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasingly close}}}\uc2  in recent weeks, again criticized McCormick over his leadership of the hedge fund Bridgewater and his recent residency in Connecticut.\par \par \uc2 enltrSenator Bob Casey is speaking to the Carpenters Union in Philadelphia this morning.\par \par \uc2 With 10 days left until Election Day, Casey is hitting his opponent, Republican \uc2 Dave McCormick\uc2 , for his record as a hedge fund manager and his recent residency in Connecticut. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PZcV8VKsyS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PZcV8VKsyS}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Joan Greve (@joanegreve) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/joanegreve/status/1850165771906822187?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe was investing in Chinese oil companies, investing in Chinese steel companies and betting against \uc2 US Steel\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 hurting our workers, hurting our companies. That is his record as a hedge fund CEO,\u8221\'20\'1D Casey said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll put my record \u8211\'20\'13 fighting for families in this state, investing in communities in this state and fighting for working men and women \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19ll put that record up against his record any day of the week.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Thanking the union for its support throughout his political career, Casey added, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to work night and day for the next 10 days, like I\u8217\'20\'19ve been working my whole life, to earn your votes and to earn your trust.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gaza protesters interrupt Harris rally\par \par \uc2 Protesters demonstrating against the war in Gaza briefly interrupted \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Kalamazoo.\par \par \uc2 The crowd chanted over the protesters before Harris continued, \u8220\'20\'1CAnd listen on the topic of Gaza, we must end that war, and we must end the war and bring the hostages home, but now I am speaking about 2024.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  has welcomed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to the stage in Kalamazoo.\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  has welcomed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to the stage in Kalamazoo.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe stakes are high, because, as [\uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 ] reminds us, as my mother taught me, don\u8217\'20\'19t just complain about injustice, do something,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  says \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will defend reproductive freedom \u8220\'20\'1Cnot because she\u8217\'20\'19s a woman, but because she\u8217\'20\'19s a decent human being.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe will usher in a new generation of American leadership and send the ugliness of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his politics, back where it belongs. The past,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said, before encouraging the crowd in Kalamazoo to \u8220\'20\'1Cdo something\u8221\'20\'1D and talk to their family and community about voting.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  is painting a picture of what restricted \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care could look like across the United States if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is re-elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will see more doctors hesitating or shying away from providing life saving treatments because they are worried about being arrested. More medical students reconsidering even pursuing women\u8217\'20\'19s health at all. More OB-GYN clinics without enough doctors to meet demand, closing their doors, leaving untold numbers of women in communities throughout this country without a place to go for basic gynecological care, which in turn, will leave millions of us at risk of undiagnosed medical issues like cervical and uterine cancers,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo the men who love us, let me just try to paint a picture of what it will feel like if America, the wealthiest nation on Earth, keeps revoking the basic care from its women, and how it will affect every single woman in your life,\u8221\'20\'1D she continued.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am asking y\u8217\'20\'19all, from the core of my being, to take our lives seriously,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CDo not put our lives in the hands of politicians, mostly men, who have no clue or do not care about what we as women are going through.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  is asking the crowd at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Kalamazoo to consider which presidential candidate they think will look out for their civil and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19ve ever been out there marching and weeping for justice, who do you think is going to have your back? Is it \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who once took out a full-page ad to demonize innocent young Black teenagers in New York City, who has dreamed openly about his own version of a purge, where, in his words, he has said for one day, one real rough, nasty day, he says he will allow cops to use violence indiscriminately?\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s more at stake than just protecting a woman\u8217\'20\'19s choice to give birth, and sadly, we as women and girls have not been socialized to talk openly about our \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We\u8217\'20\'19ve been taught instead to feel shame and to hide how our bodies work,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, describing the stigma many women feel discussing everything from menstruation to menopause.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd look, I don\u8217\'20\'19t expect any man to fully grasp how vulnerable this makes us feel, to understand the complexities of our \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  experiences. In all honesty, most of us as women don\u8217\'20\'19t fully understand the breadth and depth of our own reproductive lives,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a huge disparity in research funding for women\u8217\'20\'19s health, and if you happen to look like me and report pain, you\u8217\'20\'19re more likely to be ignored even by your own doctors,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, to a chorus of agreement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf we keep dismantling parts of our reproductive care system piece by piece, as Trump intends to do, I want folks to understand the chilling effect, not just on critical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, but on the entirety of women\u8217\'20\'19s health.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  urges Michigan crowd to 'turn the page on the ugliness'\par \par \uc2 Still speaking in Kalamazoo, \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  has criticized \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s handling of the pandemic and January 6 attack.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the American people fired him from a job that was too big for him to begin with, he tried to steal it,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said. Referencing the growing list of former Trump administration officials who have noted the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s authoritarian tendencies, Obama added, \u8220\'20\'1CThese folks know that nothing this man says or does is funny in any way. So I hope you\u8217\'20\'19ll forgive me if I\u8217\'20\'19m a little frustrated that some of us are choosing to ignore \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s gross incompetence while asking Kamala to dazzle us at every turn.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope that you will forgive me if I am worried that we will blow this opportunity to finally turn the page on the ugliness once and for all, because, believe me, if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is president again at some point or another, that ugliness will touch all of our lives.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Meet the Press, JD Vance has tried to explain \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy from within .\par \par \uc2 Vance told moderator Kristen Welker: \u8220\'20\'1CI think what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said is that those folks pose a greater threat to United States\u8217\'20\'19 peace and security because America is strong enough to stand up to any foreign adversary.\u8221\'20\'1D The full interview will air tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Although she says she hates politics, \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  says the stakes of this election were too high for her to sit it out.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI wanted to do everything in my power to remind the country that I love that there\u8217\'20\'19s too much we stand to lose if we get this one wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D the former first lady said.\par \par \uc2 Obama also called out the higher standards that Black women are held to as some have criticized Harris. \u8220\'20\'1CThey accuse her of not providing enough policy detail. Some wonder, do we really know her? Is she too aggressive? Is she not aggressive enough? There are folks sowing seeds of doubt about whether she\u8217\'20\'19s who she appears to be,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said. \u8220\'20\'1CNow, don\u8217\'20\'19t get me wrong, voters have every right to ask hard questions of any candidate seeking office, but can someone tell me why we are once again holding Kamala to a higher standard than her opponent?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor Trump, we expect nothing at all, no understanding of policy, no ability to put together a coherent argument, no honesty, no decency, no morals.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking at the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s rally in Kalamazoo, \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  seeks to draw a stark comparison between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is \u8220\'20\'1Cshowing us what a sane, stable leader looks like,\u8221\'20\'1D the former first lady said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s because \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is a grown-up. And Lord knows we need a grown-up in the White House.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is someone who understands you, all of you, someone from a middle class family raised mostly by her mom, like so many of us, leaning on her neighbors, like we all do, that\u8217\'20\'19s what you want in a president,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith all that being said, I got to ask myself, well, why on earth is this race even close?\u8221\'20\'1D she added \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s clear to me that the question isn\u8217\'20\'19t whether Kamala is ready for this moment, because by every measure, she has demonstrated that she\u8217\'20\'19s ready. The real question is, as a country, are we ready for this moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  speaks at Harris rally in Michigan\par \par \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  is speaking now at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 rally in Kalamazoo, Michigan. The former first lady, who was welcomed onstage to uproarious applause, called the city \u8220\'20\'1CKamala-zoo\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrHello, Michigan! Who\u8217\'20\'19s ready to elect the next President of the United States, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KamalaHarris}}}\uc2  ? I hope you\u8217\'20\'19ll tune in as I talk about the importance of voting in this election: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JsLhXpMe6M"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/JsLhXpMe6M}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  (@MichelleObama) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MichelleObama/status/1850276510315266282?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  prepare to make their closing arguments in the final week of the presidential election, the \uc2 National Park Service\uc2  has just approved a permit request for an estimated 20,000 people to attend Harris\u8217\'20\'19 Tuesday rally at The Ellipse. The park just south of the White House was where Trump rallied his supporters on January 6 before they stormed the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 enltrJUST IN: The \uc2 National Park Service\uc2  has approved a permit request for the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  campaign to host an event Tuesday night on the Ellipse, next to the White House. Estimated total attendees: 20,000. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LvVDS0Ac1P"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LvVDS0Ac1P}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Dennis Reports (@broadcastben_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/broadcastben_/status/1850252343133999386?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Daughter of LA Times owner says decision not to endorse Harris due to Gaza\par \par \uc2 Nika Soon-Shiong, whose family owns the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2 , says the paper\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to endorse a presidential candidate was made by her family due to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s position on the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a citizen of a country openly financing genocide, and as a family that experienced South African Apartheid, the endorsement was an opportunity to repudiate justifications for the widespread targeting of journalists and ongoing war on children,\u8221\'20\'1D Soon-Shiong said in a statement to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/26/us/los-angeles-times-endorsement-soon-shiong.html?searchResultPosition=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On X, she elaborated in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/nikasoonshiong/status/1849671252052439145"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a post}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CFor my family, Apartheid is not a vague concept. My father was an emergency surgeon at Baragwanath Hospital in Soweto. He treated students shot by the police during the Soweto Uprisings \u8211\'20\'13 where 176 died protesting the brutal system of racial segregation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Her father, Dr \uc2 Patrick Soon-Shiong\uc2 , who owns the paper, said his daughter was speaking in her personal capacity. Mariel Garza, who resigned from the paper on Tuesday following the announcement that it would not endorse a candidate, said that explanation had not been communicated to the editorial board.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the family\u8217\'20\'19s goal was to \u8216\'20\'18repudiate justifications for the widespread targeting of journalists and ongoing war on children,\u8217\'20\'19 remaining silent did not accomplish that,\u8221\'20\'1D Garza said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris will speak at another packed rally, this time at an event center in Kalamazoo, where the local ice hockey team plays.\par \par \uc2 The Saturday afternoon event featuring Mich elle Obama is drawing thousands of people, many of them women sporting all kinds of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s merchandise that, like the campaign, has grown ever more targeted in the final days of the election.\par \par \uc2 A group of women wore shirts emblazoned with \u8220\'20\'1CKamalazoo\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a play on the name of the host city. Others were more blunt: \u8220\'20\'1CFeminists vs Fascists\u8221\'20\'1D was printed across one woman\u8217\'20\'19s sweatshirt.\par \par \uc2 Pink pussy hats came out of the closet, and pearl necklaces were the accessory du jour.\par \par \uc2 Cousins Teressa Randle and Kisha McAllister of Kalamazoo said they were ecstatic to have the vice-president visit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity to see the first woman, first Black woman and first south Asian woman president,\u8221\'20\'1D Randle said. \u8220\'20\'1CI couldn\u8217\'20\'19t stay home.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Both women had already cast their ballots and said they could not understand anyone who had not yet made up their minds. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19ve been paying attention to anything that\u8217\'20\'19s happened over the last eight years, it should not be a question,\u8221\'20\'1D Randle said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pro-Palestinian activists protest outside Harris event\par \par \uc2 Outside the Harris event, pro-Palestinian activists protested the Biden-Harris administration\u8217\'20\'19s policy toward Israel. Waving Palestinian flags and holding signs that read \u8220\'20\'1Cnot another bomb \u8221\'20\'1D, they called on Harris to support an arms embargo.\par \par \uc2 The protesters stood in line, linked by a chain of baby clothes that they said represents the thousands of Palestinian and Lebanese children who have been killed by Israeli airstrikes over the course of the yearlong war.\par \par \uc2 enltrA group of pro-Palestinian demonstrators protest outside of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s rally in Kalamazoo. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qoMqcHfqoL"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qoMqcHfqoL}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1850244841805918679?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Michigan is home to a sizeable population of Arab and Muslim voters furious over the president\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the war. Many say they will skip the election or vote for the Green party candidate, Jill Stein, as a way of expressing their discontent that Harris has refused to meaningfully separate herself from Biden.\par \par \uc2 Polls show the race in Michigan deadlocked, suggesting that even the smallest defections could swing the result.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  visited with reproductive healthcare providers and medical students in Portage, Michigan, en route to her rally in Kalamazoo this evening.\par \par \uc2 Harris spoke with six female providers at the offices of Dr Rockelle Rogers and Dr Amanda Henry, according to White House pool reports.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe represent not only a safety net for our region here in the Midwest, but over the last 18 months, we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen an influx of patients that are coming, particularly from the south,\u8221\'20\'1D one of the doctors told Harris.\par \par \uc2 Asked how \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are affecting where they decide to practice medicine, one medical student told the vice-president: \u8220\'20\'1CI think as medical students, we kind of found ourselves in this sort of limbo. You know, we put all this hard work and time into doing what we want to but we\u8217\'20\'19re supposed to be excited about that, but there is this decision to make on November 5 that has this chance to monumentally impact our careers before they even start.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s event in Kalamazoo, Liz Morley of Oxford, Michigan, sells homemade pearl necklaces with a Chuck Taylor \u8211\'20\'13 two of the vice -president\u8217\'20\'19s favorite accessories.\par \par \uc2 enltrOutside of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s event in Kalamazoo today, Liz Morley sells homemade pearl necklaces with a Chuck Taylor - a nod to two of the vice presidents favorite accessories. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Tozr9lQaEJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Tozr9lQaEJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1850235427115905375?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 In the battleground state, where the election has divided neighborhoods and families, Morley said she\u8217\'20\'19s found that some Harris voters prefer more subtle displays of support.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA lot of people are afraid to put lawn signs out and bumper stickers, and they feel better putting something on their person,\u8221\'20\'1D Morley said. Even in her own town, loyalties were split \u8220\'20\'1C50-50\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like every other house,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Both Harris and Trump will be in the state today, one of their many stops in an effort to claim Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s (potentially decisive) 15 electoral votes.\par \par \uc2 Morley began making the necklaces in August after Harris ascended to the top of the Democratic ticket. Competing with vendors selling Harris T-shirts and hats, Morley said her wares stood apart. Plus, at $10 a necklace, buying one was more affordable than buying a new pair of Converse or strand of pearls, she said with a smile.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 In response to our reporting earlier this week, former model Stacey Williams says she has been attacked by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s online supporters. On Wednesday, the Guardian exclusively reported that Williams, who says she met {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  through the late sexual abuser {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein}}}\uc2 , has accused the former president of groping and sexually touching her in an incident in Trump Tower in 1993.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump and his angry, divisive followers have attacked Stacey with the usual playbook of insults and lies,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mariann Wang of Wang Hecker, a representative of Stacey Williams. \u8220\'20\'1CAs Stacey has courageously reported, Trump groped her breasts and entire body in front of his good friend \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  as part of some kind of twisted game. Stacey was just 24 and Trump was almost twice her age. Stacey\u8217\'20\'19s report is supported by the evidence, including a polygraph finding, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s own handwriting on a postcard he sent her, and multiple witnesses she reported to over the years. Trump wants you to ignore Stacey \u8211\'20\'13 the most recent of dozens of women who have come forward to describe his assaults \u8211\'20\'13 and sweep all these women under the rug. Trump and his friend Epstein are one of a kind \u8211\'20\'13 men who believe their wealth and fame gives them power over young women and their bodies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/donald-trump-accuser-stacey-williams-jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump groped me in what felt like a \u8216\'20\'18twisted game\u8217\'20\'19 with Jeffrey Epstein, former model alleges}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will play Madden NFL on Twitch with New York representative \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  tomorrow. Earlier this month, the Harris-Walz campaign livestreamed one of Walz\u8217\'20\'19s rallies during a World of Warcraft stream. Ocasio-Cortez has previously made news for her video game streams, which she\u8217\'20\'19s used to engage with young male voters.\par \par \uc2 enltr????This is a TWITCH Public Service Announcement ????\par \par \uc2 Me versus {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tim_Walz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Tim_Walz}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Madden. ??\par \par \uc2 TOMORROW 3pm EST on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/u9zNReAauY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/u9zNReAauY}}}\par \par \uc2 You ready Gov? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4h9tEPyZNG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4h9tEPyZNG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (@AOC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1850247473794527385?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrTim Walz and AOC are going to play Madden together on Twitch (!) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tOYZiMu9Rx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/tOYZiMu9Rx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kevin Munoz (@munozka315) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/munozka315/status/1850230676206854397?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris addresses Israel\u8217\'20\'19s pre-dawn strikes on Iran\par \par \uc2 Moments ago, Harris took a handful of questions from reporters on the tarmac in Michigan about the situation in the Middle East. She said she had a \u8220\'20\'1Clengthy and important\u8221\'20\'1D conversation with Biden and members of the national security team earlier on Saturday, following Israel\u8217\'20\'19s pre-dawn strikes on Iran.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe maintain the importance of supporting Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to defend itself,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice president said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we are also very adamant that we must see de-escalation in the region going forward and that will be our focus.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Underscoring her dual roles as vice president and candidate, Harris was briefed on the situation before stepping on the stage in Houston for a rally with Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 on Friday night.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis war must end. We must get the hostages out and work toward a two-state solution,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the views of the US\u8217\'20\'19s Arab allies, Harris said there was a \u8220\'20\'1Cconsensus among leaders in the region, and certainly it is the strong perspective of the United States that there must be the de-escalation and not an escalation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She stressed the US would always defend Israel against an attack by Iran.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been joined on stage by Bill Bazzi, the current and first Muslim mayor of Dearborn Heights, at his rally in Novi, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have never seen the devastation that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Bazzi said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen President Trump was president, there was no wars.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  joined on Michigan stage by Arab and Muslim leaders\par \par \uc2 At his rally in Novi, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was joined on stage by leaders of the state\u8217\'20\'19s Arab and Muslim communities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe as Muslims stand with President Trump because he promises peace. He promises peace, not war. We are supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  because he promised to end war in the Middle East and Ukraine,\u8221\'20\'1D one member of the coalition said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe support \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  for his commitment to promoting family values and protected our children well-being, especially when it comes to curriculums and schools.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Speaking to Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s large Muslim community, which has expressed marked dissatisfaction with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s handling of the war in Gaza, Trump decried Harris for campaigning alongside former Republican senator \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKamala is campaigning with Muslim-hating warmonger \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , who wants to invade practically every Muslim country on the planet,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, implying that the October 7 attack in Israel wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have happened if he\u8217\'20\'19d been president.\par \par \uc2 Adding that he\u8217\'20\'19d met with a coalition of local imams earlier in the day, Trump said that his campaign is \u8220\'20\'1Cwinning overwhelming support from the Muslim and Arab voters here in Michigan\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/hamtramck-donald-trump-arab-american-muslim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They will vote against Harris\u8217\'20\'19: Arab Americans in Michigan desert Democrats over Gaza}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/24/michigan-democrats-failed-gaza-voices-from-the-swing-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here in Michigan, we know the Democrats have failed on Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 and they\u8217\'20\'19ll pay dearly for it | Mona Mawari}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 With just over a week left until election day, our latest polling shows that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are locked in a nail-bitingly close race.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  with more analysis:\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 10-day polling tracking average shows Harris, the Democratic nominee and US vice-president, maintaining the single-point advantage over her Republican rival she had a week earlier, 47% to 46%.\par \par \uc2 Surveys for the seven battleground states are equally cliffhanging and provide little obvious clue as to who will reach the threshold of 270 electoral votes essential for victory.\par \par \uc2 According to poll averages, Harris leads by a single point in Michigan and by less than 1% in Pennsylvania, Georgia, Wisconsin and Nevada. Trump has a two-point lead in North Carolina and a one-point lead in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/presidential-election-polls-close"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats panicking for no reason, pollsters say \u8211\'20\'13 US race nail-bitingly close}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is campaigning for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  today at a voter turnout event with the \uc2 Laborers\u8217\'20\'19 International Union of North America\uc2  in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe choice couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be more stark,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said of the current election. \u8220\'20\'1CThe only picket line Trump ever looks at is when he can cross, not walk, cross.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t give a damn about union work. He views unions as getting in the way of the accumulation of wealth,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Liuna, which previously backed Biden, has endorsed Harris for president.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is currently campaigning in Novi, Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 a Detroit suburb \u8211\'20\'13 while his rival, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , visits the Kalamazoo area.\par \par \uc2 Trump kicked off his remarks by denouncing Harris\u8217\'20\'19 rally in Houston last night. \u8220\'20\'1CBeyonc\u233\'00\'E9 went up, spoke for a couple of minutes, and then left, and the place went crazy. They booed the hell out of everybody,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19 rally in Houston \u8211\'20\'13 where she spoke alongside Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 and various women and families impacted by Texas\u8217\'20\'19 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 was the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s largest to date, drawing 30,000 people.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Our latest polling}}}\uc2  shows Harris is leading in Michigan by a narrow one-point margin.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will continue to highlight \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access as she campaigns in Michigan on Saturday. Before rallying with \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  later this afternoon, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said the vice president will meet with healthcare providers and medical students at a doctor\u8217\'20\'19s office in Portage to make the case that their work could be threatened by a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, even in a state where access is protected under the constitution.\par \par \uc2 On Friday night, Harris held a rally in deeply conservative Texas to elevate the stories of residents who have been harmed by the state\u8217\'20\'19s harsh \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. She made the case there that Trump should not be believed when he says he would not sign a federal ban. In her remarks, Harris name-checked battleground Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Harris stopped in Portage earlier this year before \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  stepped aside for a moderated conversation on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a Republican voter and a former Trump official who has endorsed her.\par \par \uc2 In a social media post, Trump claimed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was losing salience, though polls show it remains one of voters top concerns. He repeated his preference that the matter be left to the states and that he supports exceptions for rape, incests and instances where the life of the mother is at risk.\par \par \uc2 But Harris is arguing that this approach has created the current \u8220\'20\'1Chealthcare crisis\u8221\'20\'1D in which women in red states are falling gravely ill and in some cases dying because they have been denied an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fueled by anger over the loss of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, women powered Democratic wins up and down the ballot in Michigan in the 2022 midterm elections. They also voted to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access into the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is expected to campaign across Philadelphia tomorrow while \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  gears up for a rally at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Harris is expected to focus her tour of Philadelphia on Sunday on the city\u8217\'20\'19s Black and Latino neighborhoods. She\u8217\'20\'19ll begin by attending service at a Black church in west Philadelphia before traveling to north Philadlphia to visit a local Puerto Rican restaurant.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Trump will be joined by the who\u8217\'20\'19s who of far-right political figures at his rally in New York. A lineup released by his campaign includes many of the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s most loyal associates, such as \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 , \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  and \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Trump campaign released a list of 29 people who will speak/perform at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally at \uc2 Madison Square Garden\uc2  tomorrow. The list ranges from Mike Johnson to \uc2 Rudy Giuliani\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Not on the list: The 7 Republicans running in New York's competitive House races and Melania/Barron\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nptdofTNiC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nptdofTNiC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Libbey Dean (@LibbeyDean_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LibbeyDean_/status/1850186869541130435?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  talks tariffs and RFK Jr on Joe Rogan's podcast\par \par \uc2 Over the course of a three-hour interview last night, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  told Joe Rogan about his plans to eliminate income taxes and appoint \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  to tackle health care issues if he is elected president. He also shared that the biggest mistake he made during his presidency was hiring \u8216\'20\'18disloyal people \u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 While discussing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s planned tariffs, Rogan asked Trump if he was open to replacing income taxes with tariffs. \u8220\'20\'1CWell, OK,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CYeah, sure. Why not? Because, we, ready, our country was the richest in the, relatively, in the 1880s and 1890s. A president who was assassinated named McKinley \u8211\'20\'13 he was the tariff king. He spoke beautifully of tariffs. And then around in the early 1900s, they switched over stupidly to frankly an income tax.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also spoke about his relationship with Kennedy \u8211\'20\'13 whom he has not agreed with on every issue. Trump said he has told Kennedy: \u8220\'20\'1CFocus on health, you can do whatever you want.\u8221\'20\'1D The two have released an agenda titled \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Healthy Again\u8221\'20\'1D which focuses on processed foods and the pharmaceutical industry.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/edwardhelmore"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Edward Helmore}}}\uc2  with more on the interview:\par \par \uc2 Trump used his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hBMoPUAeLnY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview with Rogan}}}\uc2  on Friday to repeat his claim that his defeat in the 2020 presidential election against \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was a \u8220\'20\'1Crigged\u8221\'20\'1D outcome. But Trump changed the subject when Rogan asked him if he was ever going to release evidence proving the election was \u8220\'20\'1Cstolen\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/trump-joe-rogan-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump says on Joe Rogan podcast his biggest White House mistake was hiring \u8216\'20\'18disloyal people\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 shows up for Harris in Texas last night\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 lent her star power to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  at a high-octane rally in Texas on Friday, declaring that the US was on the \u8220\'20\'1Cbrink of history\u8221\'20\'1D as the vice-president warned that the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could become the law of the land if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  were to be elected, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  reported from the event.\par \par \uc2 In an apparent reaction to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign rally in Houston \u8211\'20\'13 which 30,000 people attended, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has posted on Truth Social, saying that \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dropped way down as an issue\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a Harris campaign staffer sharing the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s Truth Social post:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump is clearly worried about Vice President Harris\u8217\'20\'19 powerful event in Texas last night with survivors of the consequences of the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Insists \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dropped way down as an issue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It hasn\u8217\'20\'19t.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s about to find out next Tuesday just how much it hasn\u8217\'20\'19t. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cCLhsWbySj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cCLhsWbySj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ian Sams (@IanSams) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IanSams/status/1850180390243180738?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 26, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s Lauren with more from Houston:\par \par \uc2 With the presidential race effectively deadlocked, Harris detoured briefly from the seven battleground states to appear in deep-red {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/texas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas}}}\uc2 . Here in a place she called \u8220\'20\'1Cground zero for the fight for reproductive freedom\u8221\'20\'1D, Harris sought to lay out the stakes in November for voters who have yet to make up their minds about the candidates \u8211\'20\'13 or whether to cast a ballot at all.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/26/beyonce-brings-star-power-to-harris-rally-in-texas-with-abortion-law-in-the-spotlight"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 brings star power to Harris rally in Texas with \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law in the spotlight}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Report: \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  worked illegally in the US early in his career\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , who has become a vocal critic of \u8220\'20\'1Copen borders\u8221\'20\'1D, worked illegally in the United States early in his career, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2024/10/26/elon-musk-immigration-status/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 . After arriving in the United States for a graduate program at Stanford, Musk never attended classes and did not have work authorization when he started building the company that became Zip2.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 When the venture capital firm Mohr Davidow Ventures poured $3 million into Musk\u8217\'20\'19s company in 1996, the funding agreement \u8211\'20\'13 a copy of which was obtained by The Post \u8211\'20\'13 stated that the Musk brothers and an associate had 45 days to obtain legal work status. Otherwise, the firm could reclaim its investment.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTheir immigration status was not what it should be for them to be legally employed running a company in the U.S.,\u8221\'20\'1D said Derek Proudian, a Zip2 board member at the time who later became chief executive. Investors agreed, Proudian said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t want our founder being deported.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning, with just over a week left before election day, the race is nail-bitingly close. We\u8217\'20\'19ll be bringing you the latest headlines and analysis today as the campaigns continue.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This morning, we\u8217\'20\'19re expecting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to deliver remarks at a rally in Novi, Michigan, before traveling to State College, Pennsylvania. His running mate, JD Vance, will similarly speak in Atlanta, Georgia, before heading to Erie, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In her first event of the campaign, \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  will hold a get-out-the-vote rally alongside \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Kalamazoo, Michigan. M, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will travel to Phoenix and Window Rock, Arizona \u8211\'20\'13 the capital of the Navajo Nation.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Houston yesterday, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was joined on stage by superstar singer Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9, congressman \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2 , musician Willie Nelson, actor Jessica Alba, several Texas-based OB-GYNs and families affected by the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in what her campaign is calling their largest rally to date. Harris focused her remarks on the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which sparked a slew of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions nationwide.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Traverse City, Michigan, was delayed several hours last night after the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s interview with podcast host Joe Rogan lasted three hours.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump are tied at 48% each for the popular vote for the US presidential election, according to the final New York Times/Siena College national poll published on today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  declined to endorse a presidential candidate for the first time since the 1980s. Some staffers and reporters have said the decision was allegedly made by the Post\u8217\'20\'19s owner, billionaire \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241026ekaq001me\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
