\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 brings star power to Harris rally in Texas with  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  law in the spotlight\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino in Houston \par \uc2 1,292 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2024\par 13:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Singer says America is on the \u8216\'20\'18brink of history\u8217\'20\'19 as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said Trump would seek to make state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban nationwide\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 lent her star power to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at a high-octane rally in Texas on Friday, declaring that the America was on the \u8220\'20\'1Cbrink of history\u8221\'20\'1D as the vice-president warned the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could become the law of the land if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor all the men and women in this room, and watching around the country, we need you,\u8221\'20\'1D Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 told a roaring crowd of 30,000 people at the open-air Shell Energy stadium in her native Houston.\par \par \uc2 With the presidential race effectively deadlocked, Harris detoured briefly from the seven battleground states to appear in deep-red Texas. Here in a place she called \u8220\'20\'1Cground zero for the fight for reproductive freedom\u8221\'20\'1D, Harris sought to lay out the stakes in November for voters who have yet to make up their minds about the candidates \u8211\'20\'13 or whether to cast a ballot at all.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet us be clear: If \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins again, he will ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told the audience, her largest to date. She walked on to the stage, as she has ever since she became the presumptive nominee roughly 100 days ago, to Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s hard-charging anthem, Freedom.\par \par \uc2 Harris has framed her campaign on the theme of freedom, painting Trump as a threat to hard-won progress advancing personal liberties and to American democracy itself. Earlier this week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/harris-trump-fascist-hitler-comments-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris agreed that Trump was a \u8220\'20\'1Cfascist\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The crowd that turned out for Harris on Friday night was exuberant. Thousands lined up for hours in the sticky Houston heat to attend. Rally-goers wore flashing wristbands in all different colors added to the concert-like atmosphere. A group of women in cowboy hats and boots danced and sang as a DJ spun pop ballads before the event began.\par \par \uc2 But the message Harris came to deliver was sobering. In her remarks, she detailed the cascading effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans like the one in Texas, which prohibits physicians from performing abortions after cardiac activity is detected, as early as six weeks. Doctors were being driven out of states, leaving women, particularly in the south, with fewer healthcare options. But it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t just Republican-led states at risk, she said, warning that a second Trump administration would seek to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in every state, even New York, Michigan and California, where it legal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll that to say, elections matter,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Despite the speculation, the megastar did not perform, but she did offer her endorsement of Harris, a woman \u8220\'20\'1Cstanding in her power\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m here as a mother,\u8221\'20\'1D Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 said. A mother who cares deeply about the world my children, and all of our children, live in. A world where we have the freedom to control our bodies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the final days before the election, the Harris campaign is tapping the star power of the party\u8217\'20\'19s most popular figures and celebrity supporters. On Friday night, Willie Nelson, the country music star who was introduced as a \u8220\'20\'1CTexas voter\u8221\'20\'1D, performed a handful of his best-known songs, including On the Road Again and actor Jessica Alba urged women to vote. Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 was joined by her mother, Tina Knowles, and her former bandmate Kelly Rowland, who gave a rousing call to action on Harris\u8217\'20\'19s behalf.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are grabbing back the pen from those who are trying to write an American story that would deny the right for women to make our own decisions about our bodies,\u8221\'20\'1D Rowland said. \u8220\'20\'1CToday that means grabbing that pen and casting my vote for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The night before, Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/kamala-harris-obama-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held her first campaign event with Barack Obama}}}\uc2 . They were joined onstage in Atlanta by rocker Bruce Springsteen, who played a three-song set and branded Trump an \u8220\'20\'1CAmerican tyrant.\u8221\'20\'1D On Saturday, Harris will rally with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/18/us/politics/kamala-harris-michelle-obama-barack-obama.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michelle Obama}}}\uc2  in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Trump was also in Texas on Friday, where he taped a lengthy podcast interview with Joe Rogan. And, at an earlier stop, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/trump-arizona-rally-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeated his assertion}}}\uc2  that migration had turned the US into a \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage can for the world\u8221\'20\'1D. Before sitting for her own podcast interview with vulnerability researcher Bren\u233\'00\'E9 Brown, Harris responded to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remark, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Canother example of how he really belittles our country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris does not expect to win Texas. But Democrats here are suddenly hopeful after polls suggest an unexpectedly close senate race between the Republican incumbent, Ted Cruz, and the Democrat, Dallas-area congressman \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Senate Democrats face a daunting map this cycle. With a loss in West Virginia all but certain, and Montana slipping away, their hopes of maintaining narrow-control of the chamber increasingly rest on an upset in the Lone Star state.\par \par \uc2 In his remarks, Allred taunted his opponent for supporting Trump\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to overturn the 2020 election, which led to the January 6 assault on the US Capitol, and for fleeing to Canc\u250\'00\'FAn, Mexico, during a winter storm that devastated the state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEverything is bigger in Texas. But Ted Cruz is too small for Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D Allred said, holding his hand low for emphasis.\par \par \uc2 The emotional heart of the evening was the personal stories of Texas women who had nearly died from pregnancy-related complications because they did not receive proper care.\par \par \uc2 Ondrea Cummings, a Texas woman who appeared in a new Harris campaign, became emotional as she shared her harrowing experience after a miscarriage at 16 weeks and needing an emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that she was denied under the state\u8217\'20\'19s law. A video played before her remarks showed her with a wound and scars that stretched down her body, from her breast to her pelvis, after a six-hour surgery in which she said doctors had to cut open her torso in order to save her life.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTexas\u8217\'20\'19 \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans unleashed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  almost cost me my life and have left me with physical and emotional scars,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Amanda and Josh Zurawski, residents of Austin, Texas, also shared their story. At 18 weeks pregnant with a girl she planned to name Willow, Amanda Zurawski began to suffer complications and needed an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There was no chance the fetus would survive, but doctors refused to terminate the pregnancy until she eventually developed sepsis, days later.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was finally close enough to death to deserve healthcare in Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D said Amanda Zurawski, who has been a powerful surrogate for Harris on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 Todd Ivey, an OB-GYN in Houston, addressed the crowd surrounded by a team of doctors and medical professionals in white coats. He emphasized the challenges of administering care to patients under a law that threatens physicians with jail time for performing abortions. Since the Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law took effect the state\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/24/texas-abortion-ban-infant-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 infant mortality has risen}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese laws are designed to handcuff me \u8211\'20\'13 literally,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, declaring: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no place for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in my exam room.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among those in the crowd was Sara Gonzales, of Splendora, Texas, who rescheduled her work schedule so that she could drive straight to the stadium after finishing an early-morning shift at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 . The 32-year-old said she considers herself an independent and in 2020, wrote in a candidate for president. But the political stakes changed, Gonzales said, the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade, and Texas enacted its near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . She plans to vote for Harris in the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBeing a woman in Texas right now, it\u8217\'20\'19s not OK,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI should have freedom over my own body.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241026ekaq000e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
