\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Location tracking, meet  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  bans \u8211\'20\'13 authoritarians have too much power\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,238 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2024\par 13:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Babel Street\u8217\'20\'19s people-tracking service allows customers \u8211\'20\'13 including government agencies \u8211\'20\'13 to track mobile users\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  surveillance state\par \par \uc2 Ever heard of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.babelstreet.com/babel-street-analytics?gad_source=1&gclid=CjwKCAjwg-24BhB_EiwA1ZOx8vteK2NWjHvnitxTx8f1Orl8uu3HWpU-QIgh5hnUML7bOmt_TvyIAxoC5j0QAvD_BwE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Babel Street}}}\uc2  ? Unless you\u8217\'20\'19re a data and analytics enthusiast, it\u8217\'20\'19s likely you haven\u8217\'20\'19t. The Virginia-based technology company isn\u8217\'20\'19t a household name the way that \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 Facebook\uc2  are. And yet the company most likely knows a hell of a lot about you and everyone else in your household.\par \par \uc2 Babel Street, you see, has a people-tracking service called Locate X, that allows customers to track individual mobile users by their Mobile Advertising ID: a string of characters that uniquely identifies your phone or other smart device. Where it gets really creepy is that, according to recent reporting from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://krebsonsecurity.com/2024/10/the-global-surveillance-free-for-all-in-mobile-ad-data/?ref=404media.co"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Krebs on Security}}}\uc2  and other outlets, Babel Street allows its customers, which include government agencies, to \u8220\'20\'1Cdraw a digital polygon around nearly any location on a map of the world, and view a slightly dated (by a few days) time-lapse history of the mobile devices seen coming in and out of the specified area\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 What does this mean? Well, among many other disturbing things, it means that you could use Locate X to zoom in on an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic and see exactly who is going in and out of it. In fact, this is exactly what a group of privacy advocates recently did. They looked at an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic in Florida and tracked one individual leaving it. Then they leaked a video of the demonstration to media outlets including 404 Media.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis phone started at a residence in Alabama in mid-June,\u8221\'20\'1D 404 Media says in a description of the demonstration. \u8220\'20\'1CIt then went by a Lowe\u8217\'20\'19s Home Improvement store, traveled along a highway, went past a gas station, visited a church, crossed over into Florida, and then stopped at the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic for approximately two hours.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It wasn\u8217\'20\'19t immediately obvious who the individual being tracked was. However, 404 Media notes that \u8220\'20\'1Cit would be trivial for US authorities, some of which already have access to this tool, to go one step further and unmask this or other \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic visitors\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Locate X\u8217\'20\'19s location-tracking capabilities aren\u8217\'20\'19t new news: the service has popped up in various headlines over the years. In 2020, for example, it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/secret-service-phone-location-data-babel-street/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was reported}}}\uc2  that the \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  (\uc2 USSS\uc2 ) had signed a contract to use Locate X. And last year \uc2 Guardian\uc2  reported that Australia\u8217\'20\'19s Home Affairs had had access to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2023/nov/06/home-affairs-locate-x-paying-mobile-phone-tracking-tool"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Locate X since at least 2021}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While details of Locate X\u8217\'20\'19s capabilities aren\u8217\'20\'19t entirely new, what is new is the political and legal climate in which the platform operates. A number of states, including Alabama (which has effectively banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), are trying to criminalize anyone who helps a woman leave the state to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/08/23/nx-s1-5082217/can-alabama-prosecute-someone-for-helping-people-travel-out-of-state-for-an-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 get an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  elsewhere}}}\uc2 . The terms of service for Locate X state the product \u8220\'20\'1Cmay not be used as the basis for any legal process in any country, including as the basis for a warrant, subpoena, or any other legal or administrative action\u8221\'20\'1D, but you can very easily see how the technology could be misused.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe best minds of my generation are thinking about how to make people click ads,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Jeff Hammerbacher\uc2 , one of \uc2 Facebook\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s first employees, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2011/04/quote-ad-generation/349689/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lamented back in 2011}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThat sucks.\u8221\'20\'1D It certainly does. But what is far more depressing is the fact that the technology used to make people click on ads has grown into a vast, and largely unregulated, web of surveillance. All around the world, authoritarianism is on the rise. And thanks to technology originally designed to encourage you to buy more cereal, authoritarian leaders have never had so much power.\par \par \uc2 Infant death rates in the US increased after Roe was overturned\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/baby-deaths-roe-wade-abortion-bans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A new study}}}\uc2 , published by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamapediatrics/article-abstract/2825201"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JAMA Pediatrics}}}\uc2 , found hundreds more babies died than expected after Roe v Wade was overturned and more than a dozen states implemented near-total {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  bans. The increase was particularly pronounced among infants with congenital anomalies, the study notes: \u8220\'20\'1C[P]otentially owing to frail fetuses more often being carried to term following the implementation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Judge strikes down Ohio \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as unconstitutional\par \par \uc2 Judge Christian Jenkins {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/ohio-abortion-ban-judge"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said last year\u8217\'20\'19s voter-approved amendment}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cunequivocally protects the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Stevie Nicks thinks we should all get off the internet\par \par \uc2 Rolling Stone\uc2  has a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-features/stevie-nicks-fleetwood-mac-kamala-harris-new-music-1235140437/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 very entertaining interview}}}\uc2  with Stevie Nicks. It\u8217\'20\'19s full of gems but I particularly enjoyed this quote: \u8220\'20\'1CAbout 10 years ago, Katy Perry was talking to me about the internet armies of all the girl singers, and how cruel and rancid they were. I said, \u8216\'20\'18Well, I wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t know because I\u8217\'20\'19m not on the internet.\u8217\'20\'19 She said, \u8216\'20\'18So, who are your rivals?\u8217\'20\'19\u8230\'20\'26 I said, \u8216\'20\'18Katy, I don\u8217\'20\'19t have rivals. I have friends. All the other women singers that I know are friends. Nobody\u8217\'20\'19s competing. Get off the internet and you won\u8217\'20\'19t have rivals either.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Evergreen advice.\par \par \uc2 Texas pastor suggests executing \u8216\'20\'18a few women\u8217\'20\'19 to end false rape accusations\par \par \uc2 Joel Webbon, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.chron.com/culture/religion/article/christian-pastor-rape-accusations-death-19848806.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas pastor and Christian nationalist}}}\uc2 , has a history of misogynistic, racist and downright disturbing statements. As well as fantasizing about executing women he reckons God doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want women to vote and has said he needs to approve every book his wife reads. Rather than being an isolated extremist, Webbon is part of a group of extremely online young Christian men that have been termed the TheoBros. \u8220\'20\'1CThe TheoBros\u8217\'20\'19 strategy is bottom-up: They aim to convert small American towns into Christian enclaves,\u8221\'20\'1D Kiera Butler {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2024/09/theobros-jd-vance-christian-nationalism/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently wrote for Mother Jones}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CBut it is also top-down: Some are working to position themselves close to the locus of federal power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Pregnancy is now a death sentence in Gaza\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe targeting of maternity hospitals and the blockade that limits essential medical supplies, such as anaesthetics and maternity kits, from entering Gaza have turned pregnancy into a life-threatening condition for thousands of women,\u8221\'20\'1D a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(24)02249-9/fulltext?rss=yes&s=09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter in the Lancet notes}}}\uc2 . Innocent babies in Gaza are being \u8216\'20\'18born into hell\u8217\'20\'19, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.unicef.org/press-releases/born-hell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Unicef puts}}}\uc2  it, and deprived of any hope of a future. All with the help of our tax dollars.\par \par \uc2 Did Jeff Bezos order the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  not to endorse a candidate in the presidential race?\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  editorial page has decided {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/10/25/nx-s1-5165353/washingon-post-presidential-endorsement-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not to make a presidential endorsement}}}\uc2  for the first time in 36 years . According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/davidfolkenflik/status/1849842968921805119"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NPR\u8217\'20\'19s media correspondent}}}\uc2 , it is not clear whether Bezos, who owns the Post, or whether CEO \uc2 Will Lewis\uc2  made the call. However, there are rumours that \u8220\'20\'1CBezos ordered the decision and Lewis carried it out\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2  is fantasizing about \u8216\'20\'18daddy\u8217\'20\'19 Donald Trump spanking teenage girls\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s even more {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/tucker-carlson-speech-trump-spanking"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gross than it sounds}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The week in porktriarchy\par \par \uc2 Thanks to the climate crisis and various other man-made issues, boars are invading the beach resorts of southern Spain and other areas with increasing frequency, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/oct/23/the-wild-boars-of-the-costa-del-sol-do-these-sun-loving-pigs-really-need-to-be-culled"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian reports}}}\uc2 . (Although some may say they are not invading, they are conducting targeted ground operations.) This is causing all manner of problems, but is also providing some very memorable photos. None as great as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2020/aug/07/german-nudist-chases-wild-boar-that-stole-laptop-berlin-teufelssee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this classic photo of a nudist bather}}}\uc2  who chased a wild boar near a Berlin lake after it stole his laptop. The nudist managed to recover it, by the way: in the end, all was swine.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241026ekaq001ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
