\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  rally says \u8216\'20\'18time for America to sing a new song\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell (now); Maya Yang and Tom Ambrose (earlier) \par \uc2 13,389 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2024\par 03:05 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing Summary\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. You can read our US elections coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . Here are the major developments from today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Houston, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was joined onstage by superstar singer Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9, congressman \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2 , musician Willie Nelson, actress Jessica Alba, several Texas-based OB-GYNs and families impacted by the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in what her campaign is calling their largest rally to date. Harris focused her remarks on the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, which sparked a slew of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions nationwide, and was joined on stage by Amanda and Josh Zurawski, a Texas couple who sued the state after Amanda was unable to access treatment for a life-threatening pregnancy complication.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Traverse City, Michigan was delayed several hours after the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s interview with podcast host Joe Rogan lasted three hours. Trump\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump are tied at 48% each for the popular vote for the US presidential election, according to the final New York Times/Siena College national poll published on today.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chinese hackers have targeted phones used by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/25/us/politics/trump-vance-hack.html?smid=nytcore-ios-share&referringSource=articleShare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on Friday, citing people familiar with the matter. According to the sources, investigators are trying to determine what communication data may have been taken or observed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 On Friday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  formally apologized for the \uc2 United States government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in running at least 523 Indian boarding schools. His remarks were given at the Gila Crossing community school outside Phoenix, Arizona, and marked his first visit to Indian Country as president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  declined to endorse a presidential candidate for the first time since the 1980s . Senior Democratic figure Susan Rice, who was US ambassador to the United Nations and national security adviser under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and then director of the US domestic policy council under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , made a blistering post on X about the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CSo much for \u8216\'20\'18Democracy Dies in Darkness\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referring to the newspaper\u8217\'20\'19s slogan.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Two Senate Democrats have written {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.welch.senate.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/20241025-Welch-Blumenthal-Letter-DOJ-Musk-Federal-Campaign-Finance-Law.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a letter}}}\uc2  urging the justice department to investigate, and if necessary prosecute, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  over his potentially illegal $1m giveaway for registered voters. And another top Democrat is calling for an investigation into Musk for the tech billionaire\u8217\'20\'19s ties to Russia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 During his rally in Scranton tonight, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  took a moment to express his appreciation for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who was born in the Pennsylvania city and remains a popular figure there. \u8220\'20\'1CThis country owes a huge debt to you and a huge debt to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris raised $97m in the first half of October, compared with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s $16m, according to reports filed with the Federal Election commission.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In an appearance on the Cats & Cosby podcast, a conservative talk radio show, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  should be deported. Trump made news yesterday when he said he would fire Smith, the justice department official who is prosecuting him for allegedly plotting to overturn the 2020 election and hide classified documents, \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin two seconds\u8221\'20\'1D of becoming president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris has concluded her rally in Houston, calling on voters to cast their ballots in the next 11 days.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo we trust women? Do we believe in reproductive freedom? Do we believe in the promise of America, and are we ready to fight for it?\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, before concluding, \u8220\'20\'1CAnd when we fight, we win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know weeping may endure for a night, but joy cometh in the morning,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says, quoting Psalm 30:5 and encouraging voters to get out to the polls before 5 November.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking to Gen Z voters in the audience, Harris says that she \u8220\'20\'1Csees your power \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt ain\u8217\'20\'19t right that you may have fewer rights than your mother or your grandmother,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, before asking the crowd: \u8220\'20\'1CCan we applaud our leaders who are voting for the first time?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris vows to restore reproductive freedom\par \par \uc2 Seeking to cast herself in contrast to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , Harris said she will restore reproductive freedom if elected president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen Congress passes the bill to restore reproductive freedom, I will proudly sign it into law,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince Roe was overturned, every time reproductive freedom has been on the ballot, from Kansas to California to Kentucky and Michigan, Montana, Vermont and Ohio, the people of America have voted for freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.51am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris is continuing, speaking about the stakes of the supreme court if Trump is re-elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd now the attorney general of Texas is suing the \uc2 United States government\uc2  so that Texas prosecutors can get their hands on private medical records of women who leave the state to get care,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1COn the one hand, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won\u8217\'20\'19t let anyone see his medical records. I gave up mine. And on the other hand, they want to get their hands on your medical records.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet us be clear, if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins again, he will ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  nationwide,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CNo one is protected if there is a Trump national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is president again, he will likely get to appoint at least one justice\u8221\'20\'1D to the Supreme court, Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CAt which point \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will have packed the court with five out of nine justices.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is continuing to excoriate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , sharing the stories of women who\u8217\'20\'19ve been denied healthcare since Roe was overturned.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTexas, what is happening across this state, in our country, is a health care crisis. And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the architect of it,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 She went on to share the story of Ryan Hamilton, who found his wife alone and bleeding after being denied care for a miscarriage. \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s be clear, men across America, this needs to be said, men across America do not want to see their sisters and mothers put at risk because their rights have been taken.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has just shared the story of Kate Cox, a Texas woman who was denied emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care by the Texas Supreme Court, and is introducing Shanette Williams, the mother of Amber Nicole Thurman.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAmber Nicole Thurman, I promised her mother, I would speak her name, a vibrant 28 year old mother of a six year old son who died of preventive death because of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris has continued, denouncing Republican leaders who have neglected maternal and infant healthcare while denying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care across the US.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor decades, these extremist leaders, who have neglected prenatal care, maternity care and postpartum care, and who now continuously failing support women and children, claim to care of women and children. I have a question for them, where you been?\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhere have you been when it comes to helping pregnant women and new mothers? Where have you been when it comes to affordable child care?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe hypocrisy abounds,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, before showing a video combining testimony of families who\u8217\'20\'19ve suffered under \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans alongside \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  saying he did \u8220\'20\'1Ca great thing\u8221\'20\'1D by appointing the Supreme court justices who overturned Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking onstage at her rally in Houston, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is making a powerful call for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou are ground zero in the fight for reproductive freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe know what\u8217\'20\'19s happening here in Texas, doctors and nurses could go to prison for life simply for providing reproductive care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTexas has a law now that offers a cash bounty for turning in someone who merely helps a friend or a family member get the care they need,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris added. \u8220\'20\'1CIn some counties in Texas, they have passed travel bans to prevent women from going to other states to receive care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was president, he hand selected the \uc2 United States Supreme Court\uc2  with the intention that they would undo the protections of Roe v Wade, and as he intended, they did. And now more than 20 states have a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, one in three American women live in a state with a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd let us agree, one does not have to abandon their faith or deeply help to agree the government should not be telling her what to do with her body.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 has welcomed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on stage, with her song Freedom playing in the background.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time to sing a new song,\u8221\'20\'1D Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 said. \u8220\'20\'1COur generations of loved ones before us are whispering a prophecy, a quest, a calling, an anthem, our moment right now. It\u8217\'20\'19s time for America to sing a new song.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 and Kelly Rowland appear at Houston rally\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 and Kelly Rowland are speaking onstage at the Harris rally in Houston.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are grabbing back the pen to write a new American story, a story of community, of equality, strength, of kindness and of hope,\u8221\'20\'1D Rowland said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen I was a little girl and I pledged allegiance to the United States of America, that flag meant something to me, and today that means grabbing that pen and casting my vote as I already did two days ago, for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not here as a celebrity. I\u8217\'20\'19m not here as a politician. I\u8217\'20\'19m here as a mother,\u8221\'20\'1D Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 said. \u8220\'20\'1CImagine our daughters growing up seeing what\u8217\'20\'19s possible with no ceilings, no limitations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYour voice has power and magnitude. Your vote is one of the most valuable tools. And we need you. Your freedom is your God given right, your human right,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Tina Knowles, an American businesswoman, fashion designer and mother of Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9, is speaking now at Harris\u8217\'20\'19 rally in Houston.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been so blessed to have many careers, many Black jobs,\u8221\'20\'1D Knowles opened, referencing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s statement that immigrants are going to take so-called \u8220\'20\'1CBlack jobs\u8221\'20\'1D from Black Americans. \u8220\'20\'1CThe best job that I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever had is being a mother.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m so proud to be here with two of my daughters,\u8221\'20\'1D Knowles said, before welcoming her daughter Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 and good friend Kelly Rowland.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.09am BST\par \par \uc2 After a long intermission, Ondrea Cummings has begun speaking at the Harris rally in Houston. Cummings, a resident of San Antonio, is featured in a new ad that the Harris campaign released earlier this week, telling her story of nearly dying after a pregnancy complication.\par \par \uc2 enltrNew ad from the Harris campaign on reproductive freedom, ahead of the VP's speech in Texas on Friday. This is a very tough one to watch, but it's incredibly important to. Thank you so much to Ondrea and Ceasar for trusting us to share their story. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ytJQg2ONiv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ytJQg2ONiv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Hitt (@LaurenHitt) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/LaurenHitt/status/1849105617450848456?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the fall of 2022, after many prayers, my husband and I found out that we were expecting. Everything changed when my one evening far too early into my pregnancy, after going to the ER and my OB GYN, and learning that my pregnancy was not viable, I was given no options. Despite being at high risk for infection because of Texas extreme laws, I was told I had to wait, which I did in the hospital for days,\u8221\'20\'1D Cummings said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy baby girl, Emery J, was born five days after my water broke. She lived only for a few minutes, but I hold my baby close to my heart,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, describing how she developed a severe infection that left her hospitalized for three weeks afterward.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday is the first time I\u8217\'20\'19m sharing my story. It\u8217\'20\'19s taken many months of physical and emotional healing to get where I am today,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Cummins\uc2  said. \u8220\'20\'1CTexas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans unleashed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  almost cost me my life,\u8221\'20\'1D she added before noting that Black and brown womens\u8217\'20\'19 pain is often ignored.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37am BST\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign reports that 30,000 people are at her Houston rally tonight, the largest crowd to date for her campaign.\par \par \uc2 Follow along here:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2 , the Democratic congressman running to unseat Texas senator Ted Cruz, is speaking at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 rally in Texas, denouncing his opponent and recalling his experience in Congress on January 6.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe in a very different Texas than Ted Cruz does,\u8221\'20\'1D Allred said. \u8220\'20\'1CMy time in Congress, I\u8217\'20\'19ve been the exact opposite of Ted Cruz, because I never forgot where I came from, never forgot the folks who gave me a chance. I\u8217\'20\'19ve been the most bipartisan Texan in Congress, because that\u8217\'20\'19s how you get things done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTed Cruz is too small for Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D Allred said, recalling how Cruz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/24/ted-cruz-supply-closet-january-6-riot-book"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took refuge in a supply closet}}}\uc2  during the January 6 attack on the Capitol while Allred prepared to defend his colleagues, using the strength he says he built as an \uc2 NFL\uc2  linebacker, and how Cruz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/feb/18/ted-cruz-cancun-flight-texas-storms-holiday-senator-reports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fled the state}}}\uc2  during a deadly winter storm.\par \par \uc2 He went on to lead the crowd in a chant of \u8220\'20\'1CYou gotta lose your job.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21am BST\par \par \uc2 Amanda and Josh Zurawski, a Texas couple who sued the state after Amanda was unable to access treatment for a life-threatening pregnancy complication, are speaking now at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 rally in Houston.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter 18 months of grueling fertility treatments in the spring of 2022 we were thrilled to find out that she was pregnant with our first baby, a girl. We were over the moon,\u8221\'20\'1D Josh said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy first trimester was smooth sailing, but suddenly at 18 weeks, I suffered complications we were, with 100% certainty going to lose our baby girl. We were devastated. What I needed at that point was an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  so that I could safely and with dignity, deliver our daughter and begin the healing process,\u8221\'20\'1D Amanda added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut this was Post Roe Texas, the near total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban had gone into effect just two days after Amanda\u8217\'20\'19s water broke, ending the pregnancy would have been illegal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the Texas ban, our doctor risked losing her license and even face jail time,\u8221\'20\'1D Josh continued. \u8220\'20\'1CEventually, Amanda\u8217\'20\'19s temperature spiked. She was shaking and disoriented. We rushed to the emergency room, and by this time, Amanda had developed an infection, which had become septic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was finally close enough to death to deserve health care in Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D Amanda said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is unthinkable to me that anyone could cheer on the cruel \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that nearly took Amanda\u8217\'20\'19s life, but that\u8217\'20\'19s exactly what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Ted Cruz have done,\u8221\'20\'1D Josh said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe decision about if and when to start a family should be ours to make. Not \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s, not Ted Cruz\u8217\'20\'19s. That\u8217\'20\'19s why we need to elect vice president Harris, representative \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2  and Democrats up and down the ballot to restore our reproductive freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/20/trump-abortion-ban-zurawski-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas woman denied \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  decries \u8216\'20\'18cruelty\u8217\'20\'19 of Trump 15-week ban proposal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Lifelong Texan and beloved musician Willie Nelson is on stage at the rally performing Mammas Don\u8217\'20\'19t Let Your Babies Grow Up to Be Cowboys and On the Road Again.\par \par \uc2 The 91-year-old Texan wore his signature braids and red bandana as he performed on stage with a band.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Yesenia Gamez Gamboa, a Tucson-area immigration lawyer, is sharing her experience healing from an ectopic pregnancy and pursuing IVF in order to conceive a family with her husband.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAccess to a safe and quick \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was what saved my life and preserved my fertility and now those very same protections are gone,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, on stage at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 Houston rally.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI trust women to make decisions over their own bodies, and I trust Texas Women to tell men like Ted Cruz. JD Vance and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  that they are done, their turn is over.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign is playing another ad between speakers at its Houston rally. This one features a woman who recalls being impregnated by her abusive stepfather at the age of 12.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI didn\u8217\'20\'19t know what to do. I was a child. I didn\u8217\'20\'19t know what it meant to be pregnant at all. But I had options,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CBecause \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, girls and women all over the country have lost the right to choose, even for rape or incest. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did this. He took away our freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Todd Ivey, a Houston-based OB-GYN, is speaking now at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 rally in Texas, and is joined on stage with several colleagues in their white coats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday in Texas, because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , I could be thrown in prison for life for providing \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care,\u8221\'20\'1D Ivey said. \u8220\'20\'1CAs a result, many of my patients with tragic pregnancy complications have been forced to flee up to get the health care that they need and that they deserve.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNearly 7 in 10 OB-GYNs say that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans have worsened their ability to manage pregnancy related emergencies, and here in Texas, three and four OBGYNs have said they simply can no longer practice evidence based medicine,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CTens of thousands of Texas women traveled out of state for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care last year, leaving their jobs, leaving their homes and leaving their families just to get medical care.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was shocked when Roe was overturned, but I\u8217\'20\'19ve never been more shocked to hear \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  continue to brag about them,\u8221\'20\'1D Ivey said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo let me be clear about one thing, there is no place for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in my exam room.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46am BST\par \par \uc2 Between speakers at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 rally in Houston, the campaign briefly displayed an ad featuring the family of Amber Nicole Thurman, a Georgia woman who died because of the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the result of what happens when you try to control a woman\u8217\'20\'19s body. My daughter is gone because of what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did. She would be here had they helped her,\u8221\'20\'1D Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s mother, Shanette Williams, said in the video.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  rally in Houston gets under way\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Houston has gotten under way this evening, with actor Jessica Alba kicking off the event.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was here in Texas that I learned the importance of looking out for your neighbors, lending a hand without hesitation and treating people the way you would want to be treated,\u8221\'20\'1D Alba said, noting that she spent a portion of her childhood living in Del Rio, Texas.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a woman, I know we need a leader like \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  who is dedicated to protecting reproductive freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D she added, also noting her support for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s proposed child tax credit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo let\u8217\'20\'19s hear it Houston, We are not going back,\u8221\'20\'1D Alba concluded.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Leonard Sanchez is attending the Harris rally with other members of his Local UFCW455, which represents grocery and retail workers in southern Texas and Louisiana. Being a long-time Democrat in a perennially red state can be \u8220\'20\'1Crough,\u8221\'20\'1D he conceded. But he hopes Harris\u8217\'20\'19s star-studded event in the final stretch of the campaign jolt apathetic voters in the state, who feel their vote matters. But he said so much is on the line, especially in Texas, which has a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 While Sanchez is supportive of Harris, he also fears a return of \u8220\'20\'1Cthe other guy\u8221\'20\'1D to the White House. \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s too anti-immigrant,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that Trump was not a real ally of labor.\par \par \uc2 Sanchez said he is baffled by union members who are abandoning Democrats for Republicans, especially in a right-to-work state like Texas. He is hopeful Harris will take on big corporations and fight for better wages, but progress will also depend on changing the state\u8217\'20\'19s politics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery year we get a little bit closer and closer,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanchez said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34am BST\par \par \uc2 Among the crowd at the Harris rally in Houston, many said they waited for hours to get in, as temperatures climbed to 90F, just shy of a record for late October.\par \par \uc2 Sara Gonzales, 32, of Splendora, Texas, rearranged her work schedule and drove to the stadium as soon as she finished her early-morning shift at \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 . Gonzales said she was an independent and and wrote-in a candidate for president in 2020. But the political stakes changed when the Supreme Court overturned Roe, and Texas enacted a near-total ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBeing a woman in Texas right now, it\u8217\'20\'19s not ok. I should have freedom over my own body,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. She views Harris as a protector of hard-fought \u8220\'20\'1Cfreedoms\u8221\'20\'1D from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access to LGBTQ+ rights.\par \par \uc2 Seated in the front row behind the stage, Tiffany Hiza, 48, and her mother Joyce Hiza, 80, wore green shirts touting their Jamaican ancestry, which they\u8217\'20\'19re proud to share with Harris.\par \par \uc2 enltrTiffany Hiza and her mother Joyce Hiza are feeling \u8220\'20\'1Chopeful\u8221\'20\'1D - they both voted on the first day of early voting in Texas. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nF7klRD15a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nF7klRD15a}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1849962696692715739?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Being a Democrat in Texas can feel like \u8220\'20\'1Cswimming against the tide,\u8221\'20\'1D Tiffany Hiza said. She and her mother voted on the first day of early voting this week for Harris, a poignant moment for her mother, who had come to fear she might never see a woman president after \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  lost in 2016.\par \par \uc2 In the final stretch, they\u8217\'20\'19ve tuned out the polls and the analysis. Both said they feel sanguine about Harris\u8217\'20\'19s chances.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Traverse City, Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 originally scheduled for 7:30pm ET \u8211\'20\'13 has been postponed several hours following the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s interview with podcast host Joe Rogan.\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign spokesman \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  posted on X that the former president\u8217\'20\'19s interview lasted three hours, delaying his departure from Austin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re coming now, Michigan!\u8221\'20\'1D Cheung wrote. He posted the message at 7:19 pm ET.\par \par \uc2 enltrEPIC: President Trump just wrapped a 3 HOUR episode of the Joe Rogan Podcast!\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re coming now, Michigan! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/qmJrgJKCFy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/qmJrgJKCFy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  (@TheStevenCheung) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheStevenCheung/status/1849954000109699180?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The Upper Michigan Source {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uppermichiganssource.com/2024/10/25/watch-trump-hold-rally-traverse-city-friday-evening/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that Trump is now expected to arrive in the state around 10:30pm ET.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.12am BST\par \par \uc2 During his rally in Scranton tonight, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  took a moment to express his appreciation for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who was born in the Pennsylvania city and remains a popular figure there.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis country owes a huge debt to you and a huge debt to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. \u8220\'20\'1C[Presidents] have always put this country above themselves, no matter the cost to their personal ambitions or what happened to them. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has secured his place in history by upholding that tradition.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Scranton crowd erupted into cheers of \u8220\'20\'1CJoe!\u8221\'20\'1D as Walz spoke. Michael McNulty, a 47-year-old voter from Scranton, lives down the street from Biden\u8217\'20\'19s childhood home and expressed gratitude for the president but said he felt invigorated by the Harris-Walz ticket.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think there\u8217\'20\'19s a real sense of optimism and hope here. It\u8217\'20\'19s not just against Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D McNulty, wearing a Harris-Walz camo hat, said after the Scranton rally. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re sharing a vision for the future of the country that is one I want to live in. It\u8217\'20\'19s one that I want to raise my children in and that I\u8217\'20\'19m really proud to go out and contribute to make happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden won Pennsylvania by 1.2 points in 2020, four years after Trump carried the state by 0.7 points. Although polls show a tied race, McNulty is confident that Harris will win the Keystone State this time around.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to push this over the finish line here for the Harris-Walz ticket,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CPA is going to deliver, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to have Madame President.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Thousands awaiting start of Harris rally in Houston\par \par \uc2 Thousands of fans waited for hours to attend \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s event in Houston. Inside Shell Energy stadium, the crowd buzzed in anticipation of a performance by Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 in her native Houston. Lots of cowboy boots and cowboy hats. Some wore shirts that said \u8220\'20\'1CMy president is a Black Woman\u8221\'20\'1D. One man wore a sequined white blazer over a \u8220\'20\'1Ccomma la\u8221\'20\'1D T-shirt.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s been decades since a Democratic presidential nominee stopped in the Lone Star state this close to Election Day and the Democrats here are ecstatic to be on the receiving end of some political love.\par \par \uc2 The DJ just encouraged the crowd to let loose. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s your American right,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 enltrFans out in force at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sticky Houston rally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hfuOKRFNbP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hfuOKRFNbP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Lauren Gambino (@laurenegambino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/laurenegambino/status/1849946048103330103?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.36am BST\par \par \uc2 The fifth circuit court of appeals ruled today that Mississippi violated federal law by counting mail ballots that are postmarked by election day, but arrive after that. The ruling, which was issued by a panel of three judges, does not require the state to make any changes before the election.\par \par \uc2 The court\u8217\'20\'19s decision is a victory for the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 , which brought the lawsuit, and a loss for Democrats and voting rights advocates, who worry the case will impact other states. Although the court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling is only binding in three states under the fifth circuit\u8217\'20\'19s jurisdiction (and not in effect for the current election), Democrats fear the decision could impact the outcome of elections in other states that allow ballots to be counted after election day \u8211\'20\'13 such as Nevada, Ohio, Virginia and Maryland \u8211\'20\'13 especially if the election is contested.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.39am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Eight Washington Post columnists have issued {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2024/10/25/post-columnist-no-endorsement-2024-trump-harris/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a response}}}\uc2  to their paper\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to endorse a presidential candidate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAn independent newspaper might someday choose to back away from making presidential endorsements. But this isn\u8217\'20\'19t the right moment, when one candidate is advocating positions that directly threaten freedom of the press and the values of the Constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D they write.\par \par \uc2 The letter\u8217\'20\'19s signatories include Perry Bacon Jr, EJ Dionne Jr, David Ignatius, Ruth Marcus, Dana Milbank, Eugene Robinson, Jennifer Rubin and Karen Tumulty.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 A San Antonio election clerk was assaulted at a polling site yesterday \u8211\'20\'13 in what is believed to be the first instance of violence against an election worker this fall, The Texas Tribune reports. The suspect has been arrested on suspicion of injury to an elderly person, a felony.\par \par \uc2 According to a Bexar County sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s report, the suspect, 63-year-old Jesse Lutzenberger, entered the polling location wearing a Make America Great Again hat. Displaying political slogans in polling sites is considered electioneering. The poll worker asked Lutzenberger to remove his hat and Lutzenberger proceeded to vote, but put the hat back on after. As the poll worker escorted Lutzenberger out of the building (after he cast his ballot), Sheriff Javier Salazar said a surveillance video showed Lutzenberger throw \u8220\'20\'1Cseveral punches right at the face of the victim.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The poll worker received emergency medical treatment and Lutzenberger was booked into jail before being released on a $30,000 bond today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis has been an especially contentious elections cycle,\u8221\'20\'1D Salazar said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/BexarCoSheriff/videos/1091412052629745"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at a Friday briefing}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve had several incidents where people show up wearing inappropriate clothing,\u8221\'20\'1D that qualifies as electioneering.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is currently campaigning in \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hometown of Scranton, Pennsylvania. The vice presidential nominee has praised Biden, saying \u8220\'20\'1CThis country owes a huge debt to you and a huge debt to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D Current Guardian {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling}}}\uc2  shows Harris leading Trump by less than a point in the crucial swing state.\par \par \uc2 enltrHuddle up, Scranton \u8212\'20\'14 we\u8217\'20\'19re in the final stretch of this race with just 11 days to go.\par \par \uc2 This is a tied game, but we\u8217\'20\'19ve got the right team to win this. Watch now. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KUFLMWKjtE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/KUFLMWKjtE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  (@Tim_Walz) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Tim_Walz/status/1849931945318191162?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, former president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  is in North Carolina campaigning for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . The Democratic Party has not won the swing state since 2008, when Obama was elected president. Our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling}}}\uc2  shows Harris trailing Trump by two points in the Tar Heel state.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Another top Democrat is calling for an investigation into \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 this time for the tech billionaire\u8217\'20\'19s ties to Russia. Rep. \uc2 Adam Smith\uc2 , the ranking Democrat on the \uc2 House Armed Services Committee\uc2 , has called for the defense department to investigate a report that Musk has been in regular contact with Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/10/25/musk-putin-conversations-investigated-00185543"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe should investigate what \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is up to to make sure that it is not to the detriment of the national security of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith said.\par \par \uc2 Senator Jeanne Shaheen, a senior member of the Senate Foreign Relations Committee and Armed Services Committee, echoed Smith. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14who has billions in contracts that support some of our most sensitive military operations\u8212\'20\'14reportedly has an open line to Putin,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/SenatorShaheen/status/1849879192583696542"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shaheen said}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s spacecraft company \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  has multiple contracts with the defense department and \uc2 NASA\uc2 . According to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/world/russia/musk-putin-secret-conversations-37e1c187"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wall Street Journal report}}}\uc2  published yesterday, the billionaire has had previously unreported discussions with Putin since 2022. Musk has been one of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s greatest supporters this election cycle, donating $118m to his pro-Trump super Pac. Trumphas long been a vocal admirer of Putin\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 After concluding his remarks in Austin this afternoon, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  spoke with executives from \uc2 Blue Origin\uc2 , the aerospace company owned by \uc2 Jeff Bezos\uc2 . Bezos, the billionaire founder of \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , also owns the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , which announced today that it wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t endorse a candidate for president.\par \par \uc2 The Washington Post Guild, the union that represents many of the paper\u8217\'20\'19s staffers, said that according to the paper\u8217\'20\'19s reporters and Guild members, the endorsement for Harris was already drafted and the decision not to publish was made by Bezos himself.\par \par \uc2 According to the Associated Press, Trump spoke briefly with \uc2 Blue Origin\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s CEO, David Limp, and vice-president of government relations, Megan Mitchell, as he left a hangar where he spoke to supporters and journalists at the Austin airport.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/anna-betts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anna Betts}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/25/washington-post-endorsement-president-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post says it will not endorse candidate for first time in 30 years}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Although \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  refused to appear in a CNN townhall alongside Kamala Harrris this week, his running mate JD Vance will appear on the network this weekend. The vice presidential nominee will appear on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union with Jake Tapper and Dana Bash, alongside former Wyoming congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , a longtime Republican who has endorsed Harris.\par \par 