Tune in on ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @CNN}}}\uc2 , ?????? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cnni?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @cnni}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/StreamOnMax?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @StreamOnMax}}}\uc2 , ???? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Audacy?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Audacy}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tunein?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @tunein}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SIRIUSXM?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SIRIUSXM}}}\uc2  Ch. 116 & ??????? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/FhaqYPemhI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/FhaqYPemhI}}}\uc2  ! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/gN0uVSTEBw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/gN0uVSTEBw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 State of the Union (@CNNSOTU) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNNSOTU/status/1849911308398764435?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to hold major rally in Houston later this evening\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is expected to discuss the \u8220\'20\'1Cfundamental fight for the freedom of women to make decisions about their own body\u8221\'20\'1D at her Houston rally this evening.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19ll appear alongside families that have been affected by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans like Texas\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 including Amanda and Josh Zurawski, a Texas couple who sued the state after Amanda was unable to access treatment for a life-threatening pregnancy complication, and Shanette Williams, the mother of Amber Nicole Thurman, a Georgia mother who died from an infection she feared seeking treatment for under the state\u8217\'20\'19s restrictive laws.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSadly, the elected leaders of Texas, a lot of them, have made Texas ground zero in this fundamental fight for the freedom of women to make decisions about their own body,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told reporters earlier today. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not just some theoretical concept. Real harm has occurred in our country, a real suffering has occurred. People have died.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At a rally in Austin earlier today, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said Harris was only campaigning in Texas in order to \u8220\'20\'1Crub shoulders with woke celebrities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Excerpts of Harris\u8217\'20\'19 prepared remarks show that the vice-president also intends to criticize Texas attorney general \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  (who sued the federal government \u8220\'20\'1Cso that Texas prosecutors can get their hands on the private medical records of women who leave the state to get care\u8221\'20\'1D) and Trump (\u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won\u8217\'20\'19t let anyone see his medical records. But these guys want to get their hands on yours?\u8221\'20\'1D). Harris is also expected to argue that no state will be safe if Trump is re-elected and imposes a nationwide \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban \u8211\'20\'13 a policy Trump has fluctuated on despite nominating three of the conservative supreme court justices who ruled to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat happens in this election will determine the future of reproductive freedom for generations to come,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris is expected to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Two Senate Democrats have written a letter urging the justice department to investigate, and if necessary prosecute, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  over his potentially illegal $1m giveaway for registered voters. On Wednesday, the justice department sent a letter to Musk\u8217\'20\'19s America Super Pac warning that a $1m-a-day sweepstake the billionaire and \uc2 Tesla\uc2  CEO began last week may violate federal elections law. Despite the warning, Musk has continued the giveaway, naming two winners yesterday.\par \par \uc2 In their letter to the attorney general, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , Vermont senator Peter Welch and Connecticut senator Richard Blumenthal urge that the justice department to hold Musk accountable:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPermitting this scheme to proceed without consequences makes a mockery of democracy and the law,\u8221\'20\'1D the senators wrote in a letter first obtained by CNN. \u8220\'20\'1CWe urge you to investigate whether \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s cash prizes are prohibited payments for voter registration and take appropriate enforcement action, including prosecution, if his actions prove to be illegal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Musk, who has endorsed Trump, has donated more than $118m to his pro-Trump political action committee and has recently begun campaigning for the ex-president in person.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/elon-musk-justice-department-giveaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US warns Musk\u8217\'20\'19s Super Pac $1m-a-day giveaways may be illegal, reports say}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally this evening with superstar singer Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 will be far from her last appearance alongside a celebrity musician.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Harris and her running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/10/25/harris-walz-campaign-ann-arbor-maggie-rogers/75846636007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign}}}\uc2  in Ann Arbor, Michigan, with singer-songwriter Maggie Rogers. Then, on Wednesday, Harris will rally voters at the \uc2 University of Wisconsin\uc2 , Madison, alongside performances by Mumford & Sons, two members of the band the National, Gracie Abrams and Remi Wolf.\par \par \uc2 The performances come in the final days of a high-stakes election season, as both Democrats and Republicans urge voters to get out to the polls.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump doubles down on threats against \uc2 Jack Smith\par \par \uc2 In an appearance on the Cats & Cosby podcast, a conservative talk radio show, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  should be deported. Trump made news yesterday when he said he would fire Smith, the justice department official who is prosecuting him for allegedly plotting to overturn the 2020 election and hide classified documents, \u8220\'20\'1Cwithin two seconds\u8221\'20\'1D of becoming president.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Hugo Lowell has more:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump says Special Counsel should be deported on the Cats and Cosby podcast: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  should be considered mentally deranged and he should be thrown out of the country\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1849893284199485723?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Thirteen \u8220\'20\'1Clifelong Republican\u8221\'20\'1D former Trump administration staffers released a letter today echoing former Trump chief of staff \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s warnings about the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s authoritarian tendencies.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/joannawalters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joanna Walters}}}\uc2  with more:\par \par \uc2 A fresh group of \u8220\'20\'1Clifelong Republican\u8221\'20\'1D former aides to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  added their voices on Friday to the chorus of criticism of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican}}}\uc2  nominee\u8217\'20\'19s character and fitness for the White House, speaking out in support of \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 , who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/us-presidential-election-trump-harris-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier this week called}}}\uc2  his old boss a fascist.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe revelations General Kelly brought forward are disturbing and shocking. But because we know Trump and have worked for and alongside him, we were sadly not surprised by what General Kelly had to say,\u8221\'20\'1D a letter from more than a dozen staffers who worked in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s administration says, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/10/25/never-trump-former-officials-back-kelly-warning-00185435?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=00000168-5c87-d6fb-a77d-fdb72f6a0000&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported}}}\uc2  by Politico.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/25/election-former-officials-denounce-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 More \u8216\'20\'18lifelong Republican\u8217\'20\'19 former Trump aides denounce ex-president in letter}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Chinese hackers have targeted phones used by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/25/us/politics/trump-vance-hack.html?smid=nytcore-ios-share&referringSource=articleShare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on Friday, citing people familiar with the matter. According to the sources, investigators are trying to determine what communication data may have been taken or observed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 On Friday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  formally apologized for the \uc2 United States government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in running at least 523 Indian boarding schools. His remarks were given at the Gila Crossing community school outside Phoenix, Arizona, and marked his first visit to Indian Country as president.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The new publisher of the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , controversial British journalist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/willlewis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Will Lewis}}}\uc2 , squashed the paper\u8217\'20\'19s plans to endorse {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  for the White House in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this election}}}\uc2 , according to a report. The Columbia Journalism Review has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cjr.org/political_press/the-washington-post-opinion-editor-approved-a-harris-endorsement-a-week-later-the-papers-publisher-killed-it.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just published}}}\uc2  an article saying that senior figures at the Post had been preparing to publish the announcement that the Post was endorsing Harris, the Democratic nominee for president \u8211\'20\'13 but there were delays.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Senior Democratic figure Susan Rice, who was US ambassador to the United Nations and national security adviser under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and then director of the US domestic policy council under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , has made a blistering post on X about the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CSo much for \u8216\'20\'18Democracy Dies in Darkness\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referring to the newspaper\u8217\'20\'19s slogan.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has formally apologized for the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in running more than 500 Indian boarding schools.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Adria R Walker reports:\par \par \uc2 On Friday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  formally apologized for the \uc2 United States government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in running at least 523 Indian boarding schools. His remarks were given at the Gila Crossing community school outside Phoenix, Arizona, and marked his first visit to Indian Country as president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAfter 150 years, the \uc2 United States government\uc2  eventually stopped the program,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut the federal government has never, never formally apologized for what happened \u8211\'20\'13 until today. I formally apologize, as president of the United States of America, for what we did. I formally apologize. That\u8217\'20\'19s long overdue.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFederal Indian boarding school policy, the pain it has caused, will always be a significant mark of shame, a blot on American history,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CFor too long, this all happened with virtually no public attention.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/25/biden-apologizes-indian-boarding-schools"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden formally apologizes for Indian boarding schools: \u8216\'20\'18a blot on US history\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Chinese hackers targeted phones used by Trump and Vance \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Chinese hackers have targeted phones used by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/25/us/politics/trump-vance-hack.html?smid=nytcore-ios-share&referringSource=articleShare"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  on Friday, citing people familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 According to the sources, investigators are trying to determine what communication data may have been taken or observed.\par \par \uc2 They added that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s and Vance\u8217\'20\'19s teams have been alerted this week and that the two men were \u8220\'20\'1Camong a number of people inside and outside the government whose phone numbers had been targeted through the infiltration of Verizon phone systems\u8221\'20\'1D, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reports.\par \par \uc2 It added that Trump campaign spokesperson \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  did not directly address whether the phones used by Trump and Vance have been targeted. The outlet did however report that Cheung blamed the Biden-Harris administration for allowing a foreign adversary to target the campaign.\par \par \uc2 In August, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  said that Iranian hackers targeted the Trump campaign and sent documents to the Biden campaign.\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s efforts include \u8220\'20\'1Cthefts and disclosures\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Care intended to influence the US election process\u8221\'20\'1D, a joint statement by the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , the office of the director of national intelligence and the \uc2 Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency\uc2  said at the time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joining \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on stage was Alexis Nungaray, the mother of 12-year old Jocelyn, who was murdered earlier this summer.\par \par \uc2 The people accused of killing Jocelyn are Franklin Pena and Johan Jose Martinez Rangel, two undocumented men from Venezuela.\par \par \uc2 Addressing the crowd, Nungaray said:\par \par \uc2 She was just being a child and due to the Biden-Harris policies we have here are why she\u8217\'20\'19s not here any more. She was taken from her vulnerability and they made her a target, and ran with that and now I will for ever be a grieving mother and my son will for ever be a grieving brother who will no longer get to grow up with his sister.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has never reached out to me, just even as a human to give her condolences as a humane person running this country. I think it\u8217\'20\'19s very sad that she can\u8217\'20\'19t even just give me an open apology, sincere apology.\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s attempted to apologize to me just days before this election. I find it very inconvenient and convenient for her. I appreciate everything \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Senator Ted Cruz have done for me. They\u8217\'20\'19ve been a tremendous amount of help for me and my family during this incredibly hard, hard journey.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has taken the stage at a campaign rally in Austin, Texas.\par \par \uc2 Addressing the latest decision from a federal judge that Virginia must restore voter eligibility to more than 1,600 people after their eligibility was illegally removed, Trump said:\par \par \uc2 The outrageous decision goes against the very bedrock of our democracy.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has also falsely claimed that the 2020 election was stolen from him, called the decision \u8220\'20\'1Cblatantly non-American, it\u8217\'20\'19s election interference\u8221\'20\'1D, and went on to baselessly accuse \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  of being \u8220\'20\'1Cbehind it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris slams Trump for comments that 'belittle' US\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is talking to reporters in Houston, in one of her new, impromptu quick comments on camera at short notice and willingness to take questions on the hop.\par \par \uc2 She has just criticized \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/trump-arizona-rally-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 for his comments}}}\uc2  on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign trail}}}\uc2  last night when he called the country a \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage can\u8221\'20\'1D because of immigration policies under the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just another example of how he really belittles our country,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. The Democratic nominee for president is standing against a backdrop of American flags, shortly after arriving in Houston, Texas, which, despite being a strongly Republican-voting state, is a place her campaign thinks is a powerful springboard for a national message. Harris is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2024/oct/24/kamala-harris-beyonce-houston-rally-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appearing with Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9}}}\uc2  and Willy Nelson tonight.\par \par \uc2 Harris continued on about Trump, the Republican nominee, about him enjoying a bully pulpit.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd this is how he uses it? To tell the rest of the world that the United States is trash?\u8221\'20\'1D she said. She said it was not how the president of the United States should behave.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether she has voted yet, she said no, not yet. Asked if she could get pro-choice legislation through Congress to restore the rights of Roe v Wade \u8211\'20\'13 taken away by a \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  stacked by Trump to the right \u8211\'20\'13 she pointed out, revealingly, that if Democratic candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2024/oct/24/kamala-harris-beyonce-houston-rally-abortion-rights"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Colin Allred}}}\uc2  can unseat GOP Senator Ted Cruz in Texas, it will boost her party\u8217\'20\'19s hopes of keeping control of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , which is crucial to pass legislation.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  publisher reversed plan to endorse Harris \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 The new publisher of the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , controversial British journalist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/willlewis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Will Lewis}}}\uc2  , squashed the paper\u8217\'20\'19s plans to endorse {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  for the White House in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this election}}}\uc2 , according to a report.\par \par \uc2 The Columbia Journalism Review has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cjr.org/political_press/the-washington-post-opinion-editor-approved-a-harris-endorsement-a-week-later-the-papers-publisher-killed-it.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just published}}}\uc2  an article saying that senior figures at the Post, including in the opinion section and on the board, had been preparing to publish the announcement that the Post was endorsing Harris, the Democratic nominee for president \u8211\'20\'13 but there were delays.\par \par \uc2 Then earlier today, the publication announced it would not endorse either Harris or her Republican rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and that the plan to back Harris had been reversed by Lewis.\par \par \uc2 It quoted a democracy expert, Ian Bassin, from a previous CJR article calling the decision by the Post \u8211\'20\'13 and also this week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2024/oct/23/la-times-editor-resigns-presidential-endorsement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 by the Los Angeles Times}}}\uc2 , which is also owned by a billionaire \u8211\'20\'13 not to endorse {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cjr.org/analysis/anticipatory-obedience-bassin-potter-scheppele-orban-trump-hungary-media-punish.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Canticipatory obedience\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  in trying to appease \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in case he wins. Trump has called the mainstream media \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy of the people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Susan Rice calls \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  refusal to endorse a nominee 'chicken shit'\par \par \uc2 Senior Democratic figure Susan Rice, who was US ambassador to the United Nations and national security adviser under \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and then director of the US domestic policy council under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , has made a blistering post on X about the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo much for \u8216\'20\'18Democracy Dies in Darkness\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, referring to the newspaper\u8217\'20\'19s slogan.\par \par \uc2 She continued: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the most hypocritical, chicken shit move from a publication that is supposed to hold people in power to account.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSo much for \u8220\'20\'1CDemocracy Dies in Darkness\u8221\'20\'1D. This is the most hypocritical, chicken shit move from a publication that is supposed to hold people in power to account. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xnQMuR4kIJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/xnQMuR4kIJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Susan Rice (@AmbassadorRice) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AmbassadorRice/status/1849869496456184179?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 There is welling disquiet over the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s announcement that it will decline to endorse either \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in this election.\par \par \uc2 A former long-serving senior editor from the paper called it \u8220\'20\'1Cappalling\u8221\'20\'1D, especially \u8220\'20\'1Cgiven the choice this year\u8221\'20\'1D. Robert McCartney has previously speculated that the Post would endorse Harris and also had heard on the grapevine that they would dodge. Here\u8217\'20\'19s his reaction on X now:\par \par \uc2 enltrOmigod, it\u8217\'20\'19s apparently true: NPR reports \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  will not endorse for president. First time since 1988. Given the choice this year, it\u8217\'20\'19s appalling. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HoDjKcKYnQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/HoDjKcKYnQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Robert McCartney (@McCartneyWP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/McCartneyWP/status/1849867274255204802?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 McCartney had posted yesterday: \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s speculation in newsroom that owner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/jeff-bezos"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeff Bezos}}}\uc2  may want to avoid risk of endangering \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s government contracts if Trump wins.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Publisher {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/willlewis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Will Lewis}}}\uc2  was a controversial choice by Bezos at the Post, which the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  mogul owns. A British police special enquiry team {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/article/2024/jul/31/police-set-up-special-enquiry-team-to-examine-role-of-washington-post-chief-in-email-deletions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is examining}}}\uc2  allegations that Lewis presided over the deliberate destruction of emails at \uc2 Rupert Murdoch\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s UK newspaper business when he worked for the company 13 years ago. \uc2 Sally Buzbee\uc2 , the editor who took over from Marty Baron, was forced out last year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/article/2024/jun/03/sally-buzbee-washington-post-executive-editor-steps-down-replacement-robert-winnett"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a move instigated}}}\uc2  by Lewis, who wanted to replace her with fellow Brit Robert Winnett, but he shortly after backed out amid uproar at the Post.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  editor calls non-endorsement 'cowardice'\par \par \uc2 Marty Baron, the distinguished former editor of the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , has excoriated his old employer\u8217\'20\'19s decision not to endorse either \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  or \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in next month\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Baron, who was editor of the \uc2 Boston Globe\uc2  before he moved to the capital to run the Post in 2013 \u8211\'20\'13 both of which publications have won Pulitzer prizes under his leadership \u8211\'20\'13 has called the Post\u8217\'20\'19s move to avoid picking a favored nominee for the White House \u8220\'20\'1Ccowardice\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He posted on X that it represented: \u8220\'20\'1CDisturbing spinelessness at an institution famed for courage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrOn political endorsement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/e5OTZhylIE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/e5OTZhylIE}}}\par \par \uc2 This is cowardice, with democracy as its casualty. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realdonaldtrump}}}\uc2  will see this as an invitation to further intimidate owner {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JeffBezos?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @jeffbezos}}}\uc2  (and others). Disturbing spinelessness at an institution famed for courage.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Marty Baron (@PostBaron) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PostBaron/status/1849847940761657353?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Baron {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/mar/01/marty-baron-washington-post-ultimate-old-school-editor-retires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 retired}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  in 2021. You can read the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s profile of him then, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2021/mar/01/marty-baron-washington-post-ultimate-old-school-editor-retires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  prepares to take the stage in Philadephia for a campaign rally event, here\u8217\'20\'19s a look at where things stand in the world of US politics:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 For the first time since the 1980s, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  has said it will not endorse any US presidential candidate this year nor in any future presidential elections. A note from publisher \uc2 Will Lewis\uc2  that was posted on X on Friday said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe recognize that this will be read in a range of ways, including as a tacit endorsement of one candidate, or as a condemnation of another, or as an abdication of responsibility. That is inevitable. We don\u8217\'20\'19t see it that way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are tied at 48%, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/10/25/us/elections/times-siena-poll-crosstabs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  a new poll by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Siena College. Published on Friday, the poll also revealed that 31% of registered voters view Trump as very favorable while 29% view Harris as very favorable.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More young Americans favor \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the 2024 presidential race, according to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iop.harvard.edu/youth-poll/latest-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Harvard Youth Poll}}}\uc2  published today by the \uc2 Institute of Politics\uc2  at \uc2 Harvard Kennedy School\uc2 . The poll, which surveyed 2,001 voters under the age of 30 between 3 and 14 October, found that Harris leads Trump by 20 points among registered voters under 30 and by 28 points among likely voters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has issued a statement ahead of his presidential apology for the federal Indian boarding school era, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the darkest chapters of American history\u8221\'20\'1D. In his statement, Biden said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe Federal Indian Boarding School Era is one of the darkest chapters of American history. The trauma experienced in those institutions haunts our conscience to this very day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden is set to campaign alongside Gwen Walz in Michigan and Wisconsin next week. In a press release issued on Friday, the Harris-Walz campaign said that the two educators will campaign in Michigan and Wisconsin, marking the first time they campaign together.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 With just a few days away from the election, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign continues to raise significantly more funds than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s. In the first half of October, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign reported $97m raised, according to reports filed on Thursday with the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2 , Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2024/10/24/2024-elections-live-coverage-updates-analysis/harris-trump-fundraising-campaign-finance-reports-00185469"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reports}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign raised $16m during this time period.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are taking a detour from barnstorming the battleground states that will decide November\u8217\'20\'19s election with Friday stops in Texas, a conservative state that was the first to implement a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Superstar singer Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 is expected to join Harris at her Houston stop and perform, two sources told Reuters. Harris has made Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s song Freedom her campaign anthem.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  won't make presidential endorsement for first time since 1980s\par \par \uc2 For the first time since the 1980s, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  has said it will not endorse any US presidential candidate this year nor in any future presidential elections.\par \par \uc2 A note from publisher \uc2 Will Lewis\uc2  that was posted on X on Friday said:\par \par \uc2 We recognize that this will be read in a range of ways, including as a tacit endorsement of one candidate, or as a condemnation of another, or as an abdication of responsibility. That is inevitable. We don\u8217\'20\'19t see it that way. We see it as consistent with the values The Post has always stood for and what we hope for in a leader: character and courage in service to the American ethic, veneration for the rule of law, and respect for human freedom in all its aspects. We also see it as a statement in support of our readers\u8217\'20\'19 ability to make up their own minds on this, the most consequential of American decisions \u8211\'20\'13 whom to vote for as the next president.\par \par \uc2 Our job at \uc2 The Washington Post\uc2  is to provide through the newsroom non-partisan news for all Americans, and thought-provoking, reported views from our opinion team to help our readers make up their own minds. Most of all, our job as the newspaper of the capital city of the most important country in the world is to be independent.\par \par \uc2 And that is what we are and will be.\par \par \uc2 enltrnew: \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  publisher \uc2 Will Lewis\uc2  explains why The Post won\u8217\'20\'19t be endorsing for president: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Zn0o655UIz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Zn0o655UIz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Mullin (@BenMullin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BenMullin/status/1849843723636531540?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has released the following statement to mark one year since the Lewiston shootings in Maine when 18 people were killed and another 13 were injured by a gunman who stormed a bowling alley and a restaurant:\par \par \uc2 One year ago, an act of senseless violence carried out with a weapon of war took the lives of 18 loved ones and injured 13 others in Lewiston, Maine. Doug and I join all Mainers in remembering those who lost their lives on that fall night, standing with their families, and thinking of the survivors of this horrific mass shooting.\par \par \uc2 In the 12 months since this tragedy took place at a local restaurant and a bowling alley, the Lewiston community has shown incredible unity, resilience and strength. They have responded by reminding the nation of the unacceptable fact that far too many families have experienced the tremendous pain and trauma caused by the epidemic of gun violence. This is exactly why I have worked to take action to address this issue with the urgency it demands and keep our loved ones safe \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 I continue to call on Congress to pass universal background checks, red flag and safe storage laws, a ban on bump stocks, and a renewal of the assault weapons ban.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a new tweet on Friday, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  warned of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s threats of using the justice department against his enemies, saying:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been very clear that he would weaponize the Department of Justice against his political enemies. You know who does that?\par \par \uc2 Dictators do that.\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump has been very clear that he would weaponize the Department of Justice against his political enemies. You know who does that?\par \par \uc2 Dictators do that.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@KamalaHarris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris/status/1849808884744999115?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 More young Americans favor \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the 2024 presidential race, according to a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iop.harvard.edu/youth-poll/latest-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Harvard Youth Poll}}}\uc2  published today by the \uc2 Institute of Politics\uc2  (IOP) at \uc2 Harvard Kennedy School\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The poll, which surveyed 2,001 voters under the age of 30 between 3 and 14 October, found that Harris leads Trump by 20 points among registered voters under 30 and by 28 points among likely voters.\par \par \uc2 In the seven key swing states, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s lead narrows to 9 points among registered voters under 30.\par \par \uc2 Interestingly, the survey found that peer influence might play a crucial role in voter turnout for those under 30. When young Americans believe their friends will vote, 79% say they plan to vote as well, per the survey, compared with just 35% for those who think peers will not participate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe social dynamic of youth voting has never been more clear: when young Americans believe their friends will vote, they\u8217\'20\'19re nearly two and a half times more likely to cast a ballot themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D John Della Volpe, the polling director of the \uc2 Institute of Politics\uc2 , said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s peer influence, not just politics, that could determine youth turnout this year \u8211\'20\'13 and ultimately who becomes the next president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the live stream of \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign event in Philadelphia:\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned as we bring you the latest updates.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  to hold campaign event in Philadelphia\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is scheduled to attend a campaign rally in Philadephia later this morning.\par \par \uc2 The vice-presidential candidate\u8217\'20\'19s visit to the City of Brotherly Love comes as part of his campaign stops across Pennsylvania, which will also include Allentown and Scranton.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of his Philadelphia rally, Walz spoke to Philadephia-based radio station WHYY on which he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://whyy.org/articles/tim-walz-interview-trump-fascist/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said:}}}\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tendencies now are fascist tendencies, he has a long history of his racial comments. His running mate, JD Vance, said voters just don\u8217\'20\'19t like the racist part of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Walz\u8217\'20\'19s comments about Trump follow a slew of similar comments made by Democrats and former Trump allies in recent days who have likened the former president to a fascist.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 The ongoing elections in Ohio could decide control of the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stephen Starr reports for the Guardian:\par \par \uc2 When the Democrat \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  was first elected to the \uc2 US Senate\uc2  in 2006, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ohio"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ohio}}}\uc2 , with its large urban populations and manufacturing industries, was fairly reliable territory for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  claimed the state in 2008 and 2012 on his way to the White House. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  boasted strong representation in Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s politics. Analysts zealously watched its voting patterns, such was its prominence as a bellwether state.\par \par \uc2 In the years since, the state has become older, whiter and more conservative. Manufacturing has shrunk and population has stagnated.\par \par \uc2 Brown is now the only Democrat holding a statewide seat in Ohio. And he is weeks out from a crucial Senate election against former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/bernie-moreno-ohio-senate-candidate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 luxury car dealer Bernie Moreno}}}\uc2 , a contest that could reshape US politics for years to come,\par \par \uc2 For one, keeping Brown\u8217\'20\'19s seat is crucial if Democrats hope to maintain their control of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/25/ohio-senate-election-power-balance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How the battle for Ohio could decide control of the US Senate}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has issued a statement ahead of his presidential apology for the federal Indian boarding school era, calling it \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the darkest chapters of American history \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In his statement, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 The Federal Indian Boarding School Era is one of the darkest chapters of American history. The trauma experienced in those institutions haunts our conscience to this very day.\par \par \uc2 Today, I\u8217\'20\'19m in Arizona to issue a long overdue presidential apology for this era \u8211\'20\'13 and speak to how my Administration has worked to invest in Indian Country and our relationships with Tribal Nations, advance Tribal sovereignty and self-determination, respect Native cultures, and protect Indigenous sacred sites.\par \par \uc2 On my watch, we\u8217\'20\'19ll remain committed to ushering in a new era between our government and nation-to-nation relationships \u8211\'20\'13 one that is grounded in dignity and respect. We must remember our full history, even when it\u8217\'20\'19s painful. That\u8217\'20\'19s what great nations do. And we are a great nation.\par \par \uc2 enltrThe Federal Indian Boarding School Era is one of the darkest chapters of American history. The trauma experienced in those institutions haunts our conscience to this very day.\par \par \uc2 Today, I'm in Arizona to issue a long overdue presidential apology for this era \u8211\'20\'13 and speak to how my\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1849803486361202758?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden is set to campaign alongside Gwen Walz in Michigan and Wisconsin next week.\par \par \uc2 In a press release issued on Friday, the Harris-Walz campaign said that the two educators will campaign in Michigan and Wisconsin, marking the first time they campaign together.\par \par \uc2 In Bay City, Michigan, they will attend a Women for Harris-Walz event which will focus on reproductive freedoms. In Traverse City, Michigan, the two women will join Harris-Walz campaign supporters for a volunteer mobilization event.\par \par \uc2 In La Crosse, Wisconsin, they will attend an Educators for Harris-Walz event.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former model Stacey Williams says \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18coordinated \u8217\'20\'19 the groping incident at Trump Towers in 1993.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Jessica Glenza reports:\par \par \uc2 Former model Stacey Williams said she thought \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  groped her to show off to her then boyfriend, the late financier and sexual abuser {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein}}}\uc2 , when the couple dropped by to visit him in Trump Tower in New York in 1993.\par \par \uc2 In her first detailed, on-camera interview since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/donald-trump-accuser-stacey-williams-jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 discussing assault allegations with the Guardian}}}\uc2 , Williams late on Thursday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/10/24/politics/stacey-williams-donald-trump-jeffrey-epstein/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN}}}\uc2  that she recalled the former president and Epstein smiled at each other as the property mogul was feeling her up, which gave her the impression the entire incident was a \u8220\'20\'1Ccoordinated\u8221\'20\'1D game between the two men.\par \par \uc2 Her account comes just weeks before the presidential election, in which Trump and Democratic nominee \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 essentially tied}}}\uc2 , according to polls. Trump has denied Williams\u8217\'20\'19s accounts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe second he was in front of me, he pulled me into him and his hands were just on me and didn\u8217\'20\'19t come off,\u8221\'20\'1D Williams told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/cnn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2 , echoing her account to the Guardian.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThen the hands started moving on the side of my breasts, on my hips, back down to my butt, back up, sort of \u8211\'20\'13 they were just on me the whole time, and I froze,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/25/stacey-williams-trump-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stacey Williams says Donald Trump and Jeffrey Epstein \u8216\'20\'18coordinated\u8217\'20\'19 groping incident}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris raises $97m in first half of October, compared with Trump's $16m\par \par \uc2 With just a few days away from election day, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign continues to raise significantly more funds than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \uc2 In the first half of October, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign reported $97m raised, according to reports filed on Thursday with the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2 , Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2024/10/24/2024-elections-live-coverage-updates-analysis/harris-trump-fundraising-campaign-finance-reports-00185469"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reports}}}\uc2 . Meanwhile, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign raised $16m during this time period.\par \par \uc2 The outlet reports:\par \par \uc2 The picture looked slightly better for Trump when looking at his overall political operation, including money raised through joint fundraising committees, but Harris still maintained a significant advantage, with $176 million raised across her network compared to $97 million for Trump when including his affiliated fundraising groups.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It also added that in the first 16 days of October, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign outspent Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign significantly \u8211\'20\'13 $166m compared with $99m. For both candidates, paid media was the largest category, with Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign spending $127m and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign spending $88m.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump tied at 48% in new poll\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are tied at 48%, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/10/25/us/elections/times-siena-poll-crosstabs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to}}}\uc2  a new poll by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and Siena College.\par \par \uc2 Published on Friday, the poll, the poll also revealed that 31% of registered voters view Trump as very favorable while 29% view Harris as very favorable.\par \par \uc2 Ms Harris\u8217\'20\'19s position, if anything, may have declined among likely voters since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/08/us/politics/harris-trump-poll-national.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the last Times/Siena College poll}}}\uc2 , taken in early October. At the time, she had a slight lead over Mr Trump, 49 percent to 46 percent. The change is within the margin of error, but The Times\u8217\'20\'19s national polling average has registered a tightening in polls over the past few weeks as well, suggesting at the very least that this contest has drawn even closer.\par \par \uc2 In response to which candidate would do a better job of handling the issue voters regard as most important, 46% said Harris while 49% said Trump.\par \par \uc2 Additionally, 45% said they believe Harris would do a better job on the economy, compared to 52% who indicated their preference for Trump.\par \par \uc2 On \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , 55% indicated Harris as the candidate who would do a better job to address the issue, compared to 40% who chose Trump.\par \par \uc2 On immigration, 43% chose Harris while 54% chose Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking on CNN in response to what she thinks \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  needs to do to avoid repeating the 2016 loss to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  said:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think she has \uc2 Jim Comey\uc2  in the wings waiting to kneecap her so that\u8217\'20\'19s good.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Clinton made the comment in reference to then-\uc2 FBI\uc2  director who reopened the investigation into her private email server days before the 2016 election.\par \par \uc2 Clinton went on to add:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think she is doing what she needs to do, and\u8230\'20\'26a number of the voters who were at [the CNN] town hall have said she convinced them, that she had shown the kind of empathy and concern about their problems, that she had come forward with her ideas, her suggested policies. So, I think she\u8217\'20\'19s doing what she needs to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr"I don't think she has \uc2 Jim Comey\uc2  in the wings waiting to kneecap her, so that's good."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  when asked what \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  needs to do to avoid repeating 2016 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/HU9QGlYqV3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/HU9QGlYqV3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1849623995408060726?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 25, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 expected to join \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at Houston rally today\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are taking a detour from barnstorming the battleground states that will decide November\u8217\'20\'19s election with Friday stops in Texas, a conservative state that was the first to implement a near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Superstar singer Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 is expected to join Harris at her Houston stop and perform, two sources told Reuters. Harris has made Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s song \u8220\'20\'1CFreedom\u8221\'20\'1D her campaign anthem.\par \par \uc2 Texas hasn\u8217\'20\'19t backed a Democratic president since 1976, and Republican Trump is almost certain to win the state\u8217\'20\'19s 40 electoral college votes, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 But Democrats are betting it will provide a powerful backdrop for vice-president Harris to talk about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the final days before the election.\par \par \uc2 Harris will speak about the danger former president Trump and Republicans could present to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights across the country if he\u8217\'20\'19s elected, a campaign source said, and be joined by women who have suffered after Texas\u8217\'20\'19 anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations were passed and their family members.\par \par \uc2 Texas implemented a first-of-its kind law in September 2021 that banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks and allowed anyone to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients in violation and those who assisted them.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former model who alleges Trump groped her, says it was 'one of the strangest moments of my life'\par \par \uc2 A former model has said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and the late sexual abuser {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein}}}\uc2  were \u8220\'20\'1Clooking at each other and smiling\u8221\'20\'1D while the former president groped her body.\par \par \uc2 Stacey Williams {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/donald-trump-accuser-stacey-williams-jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused the former president}}}\uc2  of groping and sexually touching her in an incident in Trump Tower in 1993, in what she believed was a \u8220\'20\'1Ctwisted game\u8221\'20\'1D between the two men.\par \par \uc2 Williams, who worked as a professional model in the 1990s, said she first met Trump in 1992 at a Christmas party after being introduced to him by Epstein, who she believed was a good friend of the then New York real estate developer. Williams said Epstein was interested in her and the two casually dated for a period of a few months.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/10/24/politics/stacey-williams-donald-trump-jeffrey-epstein/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2  yesterday, she said Trump greeted them outside his office:\par \par \uc2 The second he was in front of me, he pulled me into him, and his hands were just on me and didn\u8217\'20\'19t come off. And then the hands started moving, and they were on the, you know, on the side of my breasts, on my hips, back down to my butt, back up, sort of then, you know \u8211\'20\'13 they were just on me the whole time.\par \par \uc2 And I froze. I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t understand what was going on.\par \par \uc2 I think I probably was trying to smile and go through the motions of being engaged the way you would in a social situation. But it was an out of body experience.\par \par \uc2 So, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if I spoke, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if I answered questions, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know. It was one of the strangest moments of my life.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than 80 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/nobelprizes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nobel prize}}}\uc2  winners have endorsed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  for the presidency, warning that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  would \u8220\'20\'1Cjeopardize any advancements in our standards of living\u8221\'20\'1D given his earlier proposals for enormous cuts to science funding.\par \par \uc2 In an open letter, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/24/science/kamala-harris-nobel-winners.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a copy of which was obtained by The New York Times}}}\uc2 , 82 Nobel prize winners from the US in the fields of physics, chemistry, economics and medicine, said \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is the most consequential presidential election in a long time, perhaps ever, for the future of science and the United States\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The letter, which commends Harris for recognizing that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enormous increases in living standards and life expectancies over the past two centuries are largely the result of advances in science and technology\u8221\'20\'1D, called Trump a potential threat to progress who could \u8220\'20\'1Cjeopardize any advancements in our standards of living and impede our responses to climate change\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Nobel laureates range from a physicist involved in the discovery of remnant light from the Big Bang, to an immunologist instrumental in the development of a specific type of Covid-19 vaccine.\par \par \uc2 They include signatories who won Nobels {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2024/oct/07/nobel-prize-in-medicine-awarded-to-scientists-for-work-on-microrna-victor-ambros-gary-ruvkun"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this month}}}\uc2  such as molecular biologist Gary Ruvkun, chemist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2024/oct/09/google-deepmind-scientists-win-nobel-chemistry-prize"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Baker}}}\uc2 , physicist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2024/oct/08/nobel-prize-physics-john-hopfield-geoffrey-hinton-machine-learning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 John Hopfield}}}\uc2  and economist Daron Acemoglu.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/25/nobel-prize-winners-endorse-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nobel prize winners endorse Harris and warn Trump would endanger future of science}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , campaigning in the border swing state of Arizona on Thursday, called the country a \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage can\u8221\'20\'1D because of immigration policies under the Biden administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re like a garbage can, you know, it\u8217\'20\'19s the first time I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever said that,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in Tempe, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/arizona"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona}}}\uc2 , the home of \uc2 Arizona State University\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAnd every time I come up and talk about what they\u8217\'20\'19ve done to our country, I get angry. First time I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever said garbage can, but you know what, it\u8217\'20\'19s a very accurate description.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Candidates and their surrogates for both presidential campaigns are blitzing swing states like Arizona in the final two weeks before election day. The Republican vice-presidential candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/jd-vance-arizona-voters-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held two campaign rallies}}}\uc2  in Arizona earlier this week. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  and the former president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  are set to visit this week, as is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2 , the Democratic vice-presidential pick.\par \par \uc2 A banner behind the stage said, \u8220\'20\'1CVote early!\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 a change in strategy for Republicans and Trump, who have cast doubt on early and mail-in voting by falsely claiming it is an avenue for widespread fraud. He said of Arizona voting: \u8220\'20\'1CThey got a problem. Gotta make it too big to rig.\u8221\'20\'1D An image of Trump, raised fist and bloodied ear after his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-pennsylvania-rally-shooting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assassination attempt in Butler, Pennsylvania}}}\uc2 , showed before he came out. Early on, he displayed on screens behind him the chart of migration that he has attributed with saving his life.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/trump-arizona-rally-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump calls US a \u8216\'20\'18garbage can\u8217\'20\'19 in diatribe against immigration in Arizona}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic candidate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are tied at 48% each for the popular vote for the US presidential election, according to the final New York Times/Siena College national poll published on Friday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  shared the stage at her Georgia rally on Thursday night. Our video editors have put together this clip from the event:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Bruce Springsteen urged voters to back \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in the presidential election, warning that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a would-be \u8220\'20\'1Ctyrant\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want a president who reveres the constitution, who does not threaten but wants to protect and guide our great democracy, who believes in the rule of law and the peaceful transfer of power, who will fight for a woman\u8217\'20\'19s right to choose, and who wants to create a middle-class economy that will serve all our citizens,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2024/10/kamala-harris-bruce-springsteen-rally-georgia-1236157889/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Springsteen said}}}\uc2  at the Thursday evening rally.\par \par \uc2 The rally at James R Hallford Stadium in Clarkston, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 , drew about 20,000 people, according to the Democratic nominee\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, which would make it her largest political rally yet, besting the 17,000 Harris drew in Greensboro, North Carolina, in early September.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is only one candidate in this election who holds those principles dear: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 . She\u8217\'20\'19s running to be the 47th president of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Born in the USA singer is among the many celebrities stumping for Harris; directors Spike Lee and Tyler Perry, as well as actor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/samuel-l-jackson"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Samuel L Jackson}}}\uc2 , were also in attendance.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/bruce-springsteen-trump-american-tyrant-harris-georgia-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Springsteen calls Trump an \u8216\'20\'18American tyrant\u8217\'20\'19 at Harris\u8217\'20\'19s star-studded rally}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  tell crowd election is 'fight for the future' at joint Georgia rally\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to the US election live blog. I\u8217\'20\'19m Tom Ambrose and I\u8217\'20\'19ll be bringing you all the latest from the campaign trail over the next couple of hours.\par \par \uc2 We start with news that vice-president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  appeared with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  for the first time, offering closing arguments targeting Black voters in Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s eastern suburbs, a vibrant, symbolic part of Georgia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COurs is a fight for the future,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said at the rally in Clarkston. She touched on familiar themes \u8211\'20\'13 reducing the costs of drugs, housing and groceries. \u8220\'20\'1CI come from the middle class, and I will never forget where I come from.\par \par \uc2 Harris said she believes \u8220\'20\'1Chealthcare should be a right and not just a privilege for those who can afford it\u8221\'20\'1D, and said Trump would gut the Affordable Care Act and roll back the $35 cap on insulin.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic nominee also reaffirmed her support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, referring to the death of Amber Nicole Thurman, a Georgia woman whose death was recently found to be a result of the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. Harris said: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  still refuses to acknowledge the pain and suffering he has caused \u8230\'20\'26 women are being denied care during miscarriages.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For more on the rally, see George Chidi\u8217\'20\'19s full report here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/kamala-harris-obama-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Ours is a fight for the future\u8217\'20\'19: Harris and Obama share stage for first time at Georgia rally}}}\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in other news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The family of Amber Nicole Thurman, a Black 28-year-old mother who died just weeks after Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ban went into effect, was in attendance at the Harris rally. Harris is expected to make another high profile appearance today, this time alongside Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 in Houston, where the vice-president hopes to rally support for Senate candidate \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  rallied supporters in Tempe, Arizona, where he spoke alongside Senate candidate Kari Lake. Earlier in the day, Trump made news when he vowed that, if elected, he would immediately fire \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2 , the justice department special counsel who is prosecuting him for allegedly plotting to overturn the 2020 election and hide classified documents.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump called the country a \u8220\'20\'1Cgarbage can\u8221\'20\'1D because of immigration policies under the Biden administration. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re like a garbage can, you know, it\u8217\'20\'19s the first time I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever said that,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said in Tempe, the home of \uc2 Arizona State University\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAnd every time I come up and talk about what they\u8217\'20\'19ve done to our country, I get angry. First time I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever said garbage can, but you know what, it\u8217\'20\'19s a very accurate description.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Phoenix police arrested a man suspected of setting fire to a mailbox there, damaging mail-in ballots. The news comes just days after Tempe police arrested another man in connection with three shootings at Democratic party campaign offices in Tempe. An Arizona prosecutor said the second man had more than 120 guns and more than 250,000 rounds of ammunition in his home, leading law enforcement to believe he may have been planning a mass casualty event.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris picked up the endorsement of two Republicans, one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a43a28f08791c139f6a05#block-671a43a28f08791c139f6a05"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a former congressman from Michigan}}}\uc2 , the other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a48368f08e8a9846d1797#block-671a48368f08e8a9846d1797"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a mayor in a pivotal county in Wisconsin}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced he will issue an apology for the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in forcing thousands of Indigenous American children to attend Indian boarding schools \u8211\'20\'13 a policy which has been widely recognized as an element of genocide. The news comes as Harris is trailing in the polls in Arizona, a state that Biden famously won in 2020, largely due to the support of Indigenous American voters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 29 million people have voted already in the 2024 election, at least partly driven by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  embracing early voting at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  direction. So far, Republicans have cast 32% of ballots, up from 27% at this point in 2020. Whereas Democrats have cast 42% of the votes, down from 47% at this point in the last presidential election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241025ekap001e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
