\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Hundreds more babies in US died than expected in months after Roe was overturned\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 474 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 October 2024\par 15:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Study shows an average of 247 more infant deaths a month in October, March and April after supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling\par \par \uc2 In the 18 months after the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, leading more than a dozen states to implement near-total {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  bans, hundreds more babies died than expected, new research has found.\par \par \uc2 The study, which was conducted by researchers from the \uc2 Ohio State University\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jamapediatrics/fullarticle/2825201"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published on Monday in Jama Pediatrics}}}\uc2 , compared data on infant mortality from the months before Roe\u8217\'20\'19s downfall with data from afterward. Overall infant mortality, they found, rose by 7% in October 2022, March 2023 and April 2023.\par \par \uc2 On average, in those months, researchers found that there were roughly 247 more infant deaths a month than expected. In six out of those 18 months, mortality among infants with congenital anomalies rose by 10%. In those months, there were about 210 more deaths a month than expected.\par \par \uc2 Infant mortality rates never dropped lower than expected.\par \par \uc2 This study is the latest to examine how Roe\u8217\'20\'19s demise has affected babies\u8217\'20\'19 health. In June, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/24/texas-abortion-ban-infant-deaths"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 another study estimated that}}}\uc2 , after Texas outlawed abortions past roughly six weeks of pregnancy, the number of infants who died in their first year of life rose by 13%.\par \par \uc2 The researchers behind that study also found that deaths among infants with congenital anomalies spiked.\par \par \uc2 These conditions can frequently be detected in utero and, in states where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still legal, lead people to terminate their pregnancies, especially since they may be incompatible with life. However, that may no longer be an option for people living under \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny infant death is tragic, but then layering on top of that, this pregnant person\u8217\'20\'19s situation where they know that they\u8217\'20\'19re carrying a fetus that is incompatible with life, whereas before, they maybe would have had the option to terminate,\u8221\'20\'1D Alison Gemmill, the lead author of the June study and an assistant professor at the \uc2 Johns Hopkins Bloomberg School of Public Health\uc2 , told the Guardian after her study was released.\par \par \uc2 The study released on Monday did not break down infant mortality rates by state.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans have also threatened pregnant women\u8217\'20\'19s health. Dozens of women from across the country have said that, due to highly restrictive bans, they were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/21/idaho-abortion-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied medically necessary abortions}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Two women, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amber Nicole Thurman}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/candi-miller-abortion-ban-death-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Candi Miller}}}\uc2 , died in Georgia after being unable to access legal abortions due to the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  has reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This article was amended on 22 October 2024. The stated rise in the number of infant deaths to 247 more than expected refers to three specific months \u8211\'20\'13 October 2022, March 2023 and April 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 not every month following the supreme court decision.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241022ekam0028o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
