\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris holds rally in Georgia with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and celebrities \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Cecilia Nowell (now); Chris Stein, Victoria Bekiempis and Amy Sedghi (earlier) \par \uc2 13,977 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 October 2024\par 01:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closedTell us: is the looming election stressing you out?Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss important US election coverage. Get our free app and sign up for election alerts\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing Summary\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. You can read our US elections coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 . Here are the major developments from today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  campaigned alongside \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at a star-studded rally in Atlanta today. The ex-president and vice-president were joined on stage by Samuel L Jackson, Spike Lee, senators \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and Jon Ossof, Bruce Springsteen and Tyler Perry. Over the course of the evening, speakers repeatedly criticized \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for comments made by past members of his administration who said Trump fits the definition of fascist.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The family of Amber Nicole Thurman, a Black 28-year-old mother who died just weeks after Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ban went into effect, was in attendance at the rally. Tomorrow, Harris is expected to make another high profile appearance, this time alongside Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 in Houston, where the vice-president hopes to rally support for Senate candidate \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  rallied supporters in Tempe, Arizona, today, where he spoke alongside Senate candidate Kari Lake. Earlier in the day, Trump made news when he vowed that, if elected, he would immediately fire \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2 , the justice department special counsel who is prosecuting him for allegedly plotting to overturn the 2020 election and hide classified documents.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Phoenix police arrested a man suspected of setting fire to a mailbox there, damaging mail-in ballots. The news comes just days after Tempe police arrested another man in connection with three shootings at Democratic party campaign offices in Tempe. An Arizona prosecutor said the second man had more than 120 guns and more than 250,000 rounds of ammunition in his home, leading law enforcement to believe he may have been planning a mass casualty event.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris picked up the endorsement of two Republicans, one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a43a28f08791c139f6a05#block-671a43a28f08791c139f6a05"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a former congressman from Michigan}}}\uc2 , the other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a48368f08e8a9846d1797#block-671a48368f08e8a9846d1797"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a mayor in a pivotal county in Wisconsin}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced he will issue an apology tomorrow for the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in forcing thousands of Indigenous American children to attend Indian boarding schools \u8211\'20\'13 a policy which has been widely recognized as an element of genocide. The news comes as Harris is trailing in the polls in Arizona, a state that Biden famously won in 2020, largely due to the support of Indigenous American voters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 More than 29 million people have voted already in the 2024 election, at least partly driven by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  embracing early voting at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  direction. So far, Republicans have cast 32% of ballots, up from 27% at this point in 2020. Whereas Democrats have cast 42% of the votes, down from 47% at this point in the last presidential election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28am BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, who is currently speaking with Chris Cuomo on News Nation, called \uc2 John Kelly\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cdisgrunted ex-employee\u8221\'20\'1D at a campaign event in Waterford, Michigan earlier today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 John Kelly\uc2  was fired by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and he\u8217\'20\'19s pissed off about it and won\u8217\'20\'19t stop talking about it,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve got three or four people who were allegedly in the room when it happened saying he\u8217\'20\'19s making it up. Even \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff said that \uc2 John Kelly\uc2  is making up a bunch of crap about \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has concluded her rally in Atlanta by evoking the legacy of the late Congressman \uc2 John Lewis\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs the great Congressman \uc2 John Lewis\uc2  reminded us, Democracy is not a state, it is an act,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. Georgia senators \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and \uc2 Jon Ossoff\uc2 , who spoke earlier in the evening, were close confidants of Lewis. Warnock was Lewis\u8217\'20\'19 pastor and Ossoff served as an intern in Lewis\u8217\'20\'19 office early in his career.\par \par \uc2 Lewis, who represented Georgia in the House, was a civil rights leader most famous for organizing the March on Washington.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Family of Amber Nicole Thurman attends Harris's rally in Atlanta\par \par \uc2 The family of Amber Nicole Thurman is in attendance at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 rally in Atlanta. Thurman, a Black 28-year-old mother to a young son, died just weeks after Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ban went into effect. Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s death was only recently identified as a result of the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in September when {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ProPublica}}}\uc2  published an investigation into her death.\par \par \uc2 For more on Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s death:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/harris-trump-georgia-abortion-death-amber-nicole-thurman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris blames Trump for Georgia \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 -related death: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s what we feared\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/sep/19/georgia-abortion-ban"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amber Thurman was killed by Georgia's \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban. There will be others | Moira Donegan}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.23am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has praised ex-president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  throughout her speech in Atlanta, tapping into their close friendship and the Obamas\u8217\'20\'19 cast ing of Harris as their political heir.\par \par \uc2 Early in her speech, Harris led the crowd in a chant of \u8220\'20\'1CYes we can,\u8221\'20\'1D evoking Obama\u8217\'20\'19s own campaign for presidency. Later, she began a chant of \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going back.\u8221\'20\'1D She also noted the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s signature achievement, the Affordable Care Act. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  intends to end the Affordable Care Act, or like we like to call it Obamacare,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/21/barack-michelle-obama-dnc-speech-harris-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Obamas cast Kamala Harris as their heir and \u8216\'20\'18flip script on Trump\u8217\'20\'19, says ex-aide}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.01am BST\par \par \uc2 At a campaign event in North Carolina today, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  praised former vice-president \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2  for endorsing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 while also acknowledging his own past criticism of Cheney.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrust me on this. I have expressed my opinions over the years very strongly toward former vice-president Cheney on where I felt. But when the time came to protect the constitution, he\u8217\'20\'19s making the right decision,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I have no illusion on this. \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2  is protecting the Constitution, but the minute he gets to vote for a true Republican, he will vote for a true Republican. And we will welcome that. The minute that they do that \u8211\'20\'13 he will do that, and he will not vote for me \u8211\'20\'13 and I understand that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  takes the stage after \uc2 Barack Obama\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is now speaking at her rally in Atlanta. The vice-president was introduced by \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harris has begun her remarks by recalling her early friendship with Obama. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was over 17 years ago when I took a trip to Springfield. It was a cold February day, and I went there to support this brilliant young senator who was running for president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Harris also thanked Samuel L Jackson, Spike Lee, Tyler Perry and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe great American poet Bruce Springsteen\u8221\'20\'1D before launching into a familiar version of her stump speech.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.18am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  has reiterated many of the points he has made in previous stump speeches for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 including denouncing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s handling of the pandemic and economy \u8211\'20\'13 while also criticizing the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s comments following Hurricane Helene.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lies about about hurricane aid,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said, adding that Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cdeliberately circulate[d] rumors that that money is being given to illegal aliens, illegal immigrants, as opposed to people who are desperate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am BST\par \par \uc2 New filings with the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2  show that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  gave $10m to campaigns for Senate Republicans in October. Musk has donated millions to political action committees working to elect Republican candidates this election cycle, including about $75m to his pro-Trump America Pac. This latest filing shows that Musk donated $10m to the Senate Leadership Fund, a super Pac working to flip the Senate to Republican control. The fund has spent at least $210m supporting Repubican candidates for Senate this year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  has referenced \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s authoritarian tendencies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe other day, General \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff, said that Trump told him he wanted his generals be like Hitler\u8217\'20\'19s generals,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn politics, a good rule of thumb is don\u8217\'20\'19t say you want to do anything like Hitler.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are serious people,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama added, speaking of Kelly and \uc2 Mark Meadows\uc2 , who both served as Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chiefs of staff. \u8220\'20\'1CThey are not, quote, unquote, woke liberals. They are people who have never in the past even talked about politics, because they believe that the military should be above politics. But the reason they\u8217\'20\'19re speaking up is because they have seen that in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s mind, the military does not exist to serve the constitution or the American people. He doesn\u8217\'20\'19t see being commander in chief as a solemn, sacred responsibility, just like everything else. He thinks the military exists to do his bidding, to serve his interests.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  takes the stage to encourage the crowd to vote\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  is now speaking at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 rally in Atlanta. The ex-president acknowledged the line-up of celebrity guests that preceded him and then encouraged the crowd to go vote, before giving a version of the stump speech he has given at other Harris campaign events.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow we know this election is going to be tight because a lot of Americans are still struggling,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo I get why people are looking to shake things up. What I cannot understand is why anybody would think that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will shake things up in a way that is good for you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 rally in Atlanta, actor Tyler Perry has denounced \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and says that today he voted for Harris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI watched [Trump] from the Central Park Five to Project 2025. What I realized is in this \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s America, there is no dream that looks like me. We want a president who believes the American dream is for everyone. That president is \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Perry said. Noting the close margin of votes in Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 presidential election, Perry added: \u8220\'20\'1CEvery vote counts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26am BST\par \par \uc2 A star-studded line-up of politicians and celebrities have rallied attendees of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign event in Atlanta, Georgia, this evening. Harris and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  are expected to speak at 7.30 ET. Ahead of them, actor Samuel L Jackson, director Spike Lee, senators \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2  and Jon Ossof, and actor Tyler Perry have spoken to voters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet me say that I do not believe that significant numbers of Black men are going to vote for the likes of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Warnock said, referencing data that has shown young Black men are increasingly leaning toward the ex-president. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that. Now, we are not a monolith. There will be some. But there won\u8217\'20\'19t be this wave. After all, we know who \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier, Bruce Springsteen \u8211\'20\'13 who has endorsed Harris - performed Land of Hope and Dreams and Dancing in the Dark. The musician warned the audience that Trump was running to become \u8220\'20\'1Can American tyrant\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.36am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Navajo Nation President Buu Nygren \u8211\'20\'13 whose grandmother was taken to an Indian boarding school in Riverside, California \u8211\'20\'13 has released a statement thanking President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  for his expected apology for the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in the boarding school system.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor generations, Native children, including many from the Navajo Nation, were subjected to an education system that sought to erase our languages, cultures and identities,\u8221\'20\'1D Nygren said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy recognizing this tragic legacy, President Biden honors the resilience of the survivors and their families, many of whom carry the weight of these experiences. He sends a message that healing and truth are central to building a just future. The Navajo Nation stands ready to work with his administration, as well as the next administration, to continue uncovering the truth, honoring those who were lost, and ensuring that these atrocities are never repeated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than 29 million people have voted already in the 2024 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/live-news/harris-trump-election-10-24-24/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2 , as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  calls for his supporters to vote ahead of election day. So far, Republicans have cast 32 percent of ballots, up from 27 percent at this point in 2020. Whereas Democrats have cast 42 percent of the votes, down from 47 percent at this point in the last presidential election. In recent weeks, Trump and his supporters have increasingly called for Republicans to vote early \u8211\'20\'13 a strategy Republicans have not typically embraced.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance published an essay in The \uc2 Pittsburgh Post-Gazette\uc2  today calling \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Canti-Catholic\u8221\'20\'1D. The news comes just a day after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attended a campaign event at a church in Zebulon, Georgia yesterday, where he claimed Catholics are \u8220\'20\'1Cthreated worse than anybody.\u8221\'20\'1D Later, at a CNN town hall yesterday evening, Harris spoke openly about her Christian faith, noting that she prays every day.\par \par \uc2 In the Post-Gazette {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.post-gazette.com/opinion/guest-columns/2024/10/24/jd-vance-kamala-harris-prejudice-bigotry-catholics/stories/202410240035"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 essay}}}\uc2 , Vance argues that Harris and other Democrats have \u8220\'20\'1Cmocked\u8221\'20\'1D Catholics and that her support of progressive policies \u8211\'20\'13 like same-sex marriage and gender-affirming healthcare \u8211\'20\'13 is anti-Catholic.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is polling slightly ahead of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the swing state of Michigan, according to recently released {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ippsr.msu.edu/sites/default/files/soss/soss_election_mini_report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey results}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Michigan State University\uc2 . As of 17 October, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our polling}}}\uc2  showed Trump leading the state by a narrow one-point margin.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Michigan State University\uc2 , Harris is leading Trump at 52 percent to 48 percent among likely voters. Michigan, which holds 16 electoral votes, voted for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 but the state is hotly contested this year, in part as the state\u8217\'20\'19s large Arab American community grapples with which candidate to support following the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/24/michigan-democrats-failed-gaza-voices-from-the-swing-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Here in Michigan, we know the Democrats have failed on Gaza \u8211\'20\'13 and they\u8217\'20\'19ll pay dearly for it | Mona Mawari}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/13/democrats-michigan-saginaw-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats on edge in critical Michigan amid fears of waning enthusiasm}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Celebrities rally at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  event in Georgia\par \par \uc2 Actor Samuel L Jackson and director Spike Lee \u8211\'20\'13 two graduates of Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s Morehouse college \u8211\'20\'13 spoke to a crowd of thousands at a stadium in Clarkston, G eorgia ahead of the appearance of vice -president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and former president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo not wait until election day to show your support,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson said, exhorting voters to go to the polls early. \u8220\'20\'1CShowing up at the polls is the only way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Early voting totals have been breaking records in Georgia, with about 30% of the electorate having already cast a ballot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve heard her favorite curse word is a favorite of mine too,\u8221\'20\'1D Jackson said, pointedly avoiding the use of the actual offensive term he is famous for. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s the kind of president I can stand behind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Spike Lee reminded people that he is a \u8220\'20\'1CGrady baby\u8221\'20\'1D, born at Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s Grady Memorial hospital and three generations deep in the city.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPower is knowing your past,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CGeorgia is where the future is being written. Georgia is showing up and showing out, no matter what kind of shenanigans, skullduggery and subterfuge.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Referring to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Cagent orange\u8221\'20\'1D, Lee said that \u8220\'20\'1Ctoday, we cannot be hoodwinked, bamboozled, led astray\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Opening his rally in Tempe, Arizona, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he watched \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 town hall on CNN last night and called her performance \u8220\'20\'1Cpathetic\u8221\'20\'1D. Later, he denounced reporters in the building for focusing their cameras on his face and not the charts he shows at his rallies. His comments that journalists are \u8220\'20\'1Cbad people\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy of the people\u8221\'20\'1D spurred a chorus of chants from his supporters, who booed the reporters in the building.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the final days of the 2024 presidential campaign, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is gearing up for another podcast interview, this time with former \uc2 NFL\uc2  player Shannon Sharpe for his show Club Shay Shay . The interview, which will tape in Atlanta, will air on Monday, 28 October.\par \par \uc2 Harris has embraced podcast interviews in the final weeks of the election, with appearances on Call Her Daddy and All The Smoke. \uc2 Guardian\uc2  reporter {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/jesse-hassenger"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jesse Hassenger}}}\uc2  has more on Harris\u8217\'20\'19 and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s podcast appearances:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2024/oct/19/trump-harris-podcasts-election-strategy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Call Her Daddy to Theo Von: how podcasts became a vital election tool}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Tempe, Arizona , is starting late. Meanwhile, his running mate JD Vance is expected to take the stage shortly at a separate event in Waterford, Michigan. We\u8217\'20\'19ll alert you of any developments as the events get underway. Trump is expected to hold another rally in Las Vegas, Nevada, this evening after \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  campaigns alongside ex-president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and Bruce Springsteen in Atlanta this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a rare post on X, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is denouncing his former chief of staff \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 , who recently made news for saying Trump meets the definition of a fascist. In the post, Trump calls Kelly a \u8220\'20\'1Cbad general\u8221\'20\'1D, an apparent reference to a separate interview Kelly gave the Atlantic where he described Trump lamenting that he did not have generals who were loyal in the way he believed German military commanders had been to Hitler.\par \par \uc2 enltrThank you for your support against a total degenerate named \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 , who made up a story out of pure Trump Derangement Syndrome Hatred! This guy had two qualities, which don\u8217\'20\'19t work well together. He was tough and dumb. The problem is his toughness morphed into weakness,\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  (@realDonaldTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump/status/1849537439720931529?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Robert Tait has more on Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s comments about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s authoritarian leanings:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/trump-fascist-reaction-john-kelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump slams John Kelly for calling him a \u8216\'20\'18fascist\u8217\'20\'19 after Harris lauds comments}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  travels to Arizona and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  prepares to take the stage at two rallies there today, Phoenix police have arrested a man suspected of setting fire to a mailbox there where mail-in ballots were damaged this morning. The news comes just days after Tempe police arrested a separate man in connection with three shootings at Democratic party campaign offices in Tempe.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.azcentral.com/story/news/local/phoenix/2024/10/24/ballots-damaged-phoenix-mailbox-fire/75824504007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Arizona Republic reports}}}\uc2  that Phoenix police arrested Dieter Klofkorn, who told investigators he lit the fire because he wanted to be arrested, this morning. Before firefighters could extinguish the fire, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/live/2024/10/24/us/harris-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the New York Times reports}}}\uc2 , approximately 20 ballots were damaged. Arizona secretary of state \uc2 Adrian Fontes\uc2  told the paper that voters whose ballots were damaged will receive a new ballot.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Phoenix PD says 35-year-old Dieter Klofkorn is in custody.\par \par \uc2 "Klofkorn stated that he committed the arson because he wanted to be arrested and that his actions were not politically motivated and not related to anything involving the upcoming election." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2TQUiRrTUC"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/2TQUiRrTUC}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sasha Hupka ?? (@SashaHupka) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SashaHupka/status/1849535617824071860?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be taking the stage at his rally in Tempe, Arizona, shortly, where he is expected to return to the issue that has defined his campaign: immigration. According to his prepared remarks, Trump will argue that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s handling of the border should disqualify her from the presidency.\par \par \uc2 Trump will be joined on stage by Kari Lake, a former television news anchor and dedicated follower of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s who is running for the state\u8217\'20\'19s open Senate seat. Ahead of her appearance in Tempe, Lake told the Associated Press that she would use the CBP One app, which allows migrants to request asylum at the south-west border, to deport people if elected.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat app works both ways,\u8221\'20\'1D Lake said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn January 2025, we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna control that app and we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna find the people who invaded our country and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to send them home.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hilary Clinton\uc2  will appear on CNN this evening in an interview with Kaitlan Collins, host of The Source. The interview comes just a day after the network aired its town hall with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , an event that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  declined to attend.\par \par \uc2 enltrComing up tonight at 9 p.m. ET. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VA6VWibhYE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/VA6VWibhYE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1849528117854982285?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden to issue apology for \uc2 US government\uc2  role in Native American boarding schools\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will travel to Arizona today and is expected to formally apologize tomorrow for the \uc2 US government\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s role in forcing thousands of Native American children to attend Indian boarding schools \u8211\'20\'13 a policy which has been widely recognized as an element of genocide. The news comes as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is trailing in the polls in Arizona, a state that Biden famously won in 2020, largely due to the support of Native American voters.\par \par \uc2 enltr.? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @POTUS}}}\uc2  ? tells reporters he is heading to Arizona to make a formal apology to Native Americans/Indian nation about how their children were treated. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/siRpqYSV1G"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/siRpqYSV1G}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeff Mason (@jeffmason1) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeffmason1/status/1849539643676451053?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would never have guessed in a million years that something like this would happen,\u8221\'20\'1D the secretary of interior, \uc2 Deb Haaland\uc2 , a member of the Pueblo of Laguna, told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/indian-border-schools-apology-biden-haaland-701872132d7f191973d54cd05286ef75"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a big deal to me. I\u8217\'20\'19m sure it will be a big deal to all of Indian Country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 As the first Native American to lead the Department of the Interior, Haaland launched an investigation into the boarding school system, which found that at least 18,000 children were removed from their parents and forced to attend the schools, which sought to assimilate them into white American culture. The investigation documented about 1,000 deaths of children that occurred at the boarding schools.\par \par \uc2 On Indigenous Peoples\u8217\'20\'19 Day, the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  announced that it had launched a \u8220\'20\'1Csix-figure ad campaign\u8221\'20\'1D aimed at turning out Native American voters in Arizona, North Carolina, Montana and Alaska. It is the party\u8217\'20\'19s third Native-focused campaign this year, and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most the DNC has ever spent on a campaign targeting Native voters\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Phoenix mayor \uc2 Kate Gallego\uc2  has announced the arrest of a suspect involved in setting a fire at a USPS mailbox that damaged a small number of mail-in ballots:\par \par \uc2 enltrThanks to swift action by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PhoenixPolice?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PhoenixPolice}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PHXFire?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PHXFire}}}\uc2  and federal partners, we have arrested the suspect involved in this incident. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DRkqz06All"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/DRkqz06All}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Mayor \uc2 Kate Gallego\uc2  (@MayorGallego) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MayorGallego/status/1849515749942944222?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Phoenix is the largest city in swing state Arizona, and many residents are returning ballots by mail. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more of what we know about the incident:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/phoenix-mailbox-fire-ballots-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mail-in ballots damaged after USPS collection box was set on fire in Arizona}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Things aren\u8217\'20\'19t looking terrible everywhere for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 The party grew nervous earlier this year in Maryland when Republican former governor \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  jumped into the race for the open Senate seat in what is typically a Democratic bastion. Maryland voters had twice elected Hogan to the governor\u8217\'20\'19s mansion, and he is viewed as perhaps the only Republican in the state with a shot at winning the Senate seat.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/dc-md-va/2024/10/24/maryland-senate-race-poll-results/?utm_source=twitter&utm_campaign=wp_main&utm_medium=social"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a poll from the Washington Post and the University of Maryland}}}\uc2  released today shows the Democratic nominee, Prince George\u8217\'20\'19s county executive Angela Alsobrooks, with a commanding lead of 52% among likely voters, and Hogan at a mere 40%. That\u8217\'20\'19s sure to quell some jitters in the party, though winning the seat, which is currently occupied by Democrat Ben Cardin, is not enough to get the party the majority in the chamber.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic senator \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bid for re-election in Montana is a mirror of the party\u8217\'20\'19s wider struggles to maintain the support of voters in rural areas across the country, which have grown increasingly Republican in recent years, threatening the party\u8217\'20\'19s ability to win races up and down the ballot. The Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/davidsmith"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Smith}}}\uc2  traveled to Big Sky Country to see if Tester\u8217\'20\'19s circumstances are as dire as they appear from afar:\par \par \uc2 He was a young and little-known underdog. So Max Baucus, candidate for Congress, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://helenair.com/baucus-begins-630-mile-trek/article_19482b00-f58e-5193-84f1-0022ca0e0681.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decided to trek 630 miles}}}\uc2  across Montana and listen to people talk about their problems. \u8220\'20\'1CAs luck would have it, on the first day, I walked into a blizzard,\u8221\'20\'1D he recalls, pointing to a photo of his young self caked in snow. \u8220\'20\'1CIt was cold! But the blizzard didn\u8217\'20\'19t last that long .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Baucus shed 12lb during that two-and-a-half month journey in 1974. He also made friends. The Democrat defeated a Republican incumbent and would soon go on to serve as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://baucusinstitute.org/about-max-baucus/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Montana senator for 36 years}}}\uc2 . He never lost an election but saw his beloved home state undergo many changes. Among them is the prospect that Democrats like him are now facing political extinction.\par \par \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2 , a moderate Democrat who is one of Montana\u8217\'20\'19s current senators, is fighting for his political life in the 5 November election. Opinion polls suggest that he is trailing his Republican rival, Tim Sheehy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/senate-races-elections-to-watch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Control of the closely divided Senate}}}\uc2 , and the ability to enable or stymie the ambitions of a President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  or President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , could hinge on the outcome.\par \par \uc2 The Senate race in Montana is widely seen as a litmus test of whether Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/12/us/politics/jon-tester-democrats-great-plains.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 can still win in largely rural states}}}\uc2  that have embraced Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Republican party. It is also a study in whether the type of hyperlocal campaigning that Baucus practised half a century ago can outpace shifts in demographics, media and spending that have rendered all politics national.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/montana-senate-race-jon-tester-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Can Democrats still win in rural states? Montana\u8217\'20\'19s Senate race offers high-stakes litmus test}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats are fighting to keep their majority in the Senate, and evidence continues to mount that \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2 , the Montana senator whose re-election is viewed as essential to doing that, is struggling.\par \par \uc2 The party has already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/18/election-west-virginia-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conceded a seat}}}\uc2  in deep-red West Virginia, but is hoping \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s victory combined with those of Tester and \uc2 Sherrod Brown\uc2  in Ohio, along with several other incumbents, will renew its majority.\par \par \uc2 Polls have lately shown Tester trailing his Republican opponent, and the political advertising trackers at Medium Buying report a Republican group has cancelled television ads in Montana \u8211\'20\'13 a sign the party views the seat as theirs for the taking:\par \par \uc2 enltrFLASH: R group American Crossroads is canceling TV ad schedules it had booked in Montana markets for 10/29-11/4 flight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/MTSen?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #MTSen}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Medium Buying (@MediumBuying) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MediumBuying/status/1849472968344101060?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on the calculations behind the quest for control of Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/senate-races-elections-to-watch"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The key US Senate races that could determine who controls the chamber}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris then took a few questions from the press, but didn\u8217\'20\'19t make news.\par \par \uc2 Asked for more details of the Philadelphia concert scheduled for Monday where Bruce Springsteen will perform and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  will speak in support of her candidacy, Harris demurred.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have nothing to report at this moment. Stay tuned,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said, after noting that Springsteen was \u8220\'20\'1Can American icon\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She dodged a question about whether she would allow construction of a wall on the border with Mexico, and how she would vote on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/16/california-governor-crime-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a California ballot proposition}}}\uc2  to heighten penalties for shoplifters and drug dealers.\par \par \uc2 Harris did share some thoughts on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a833d8f08e8a9846d1ade#block-671a833d8f08e8a9846d1ade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the gender divide}}}\uc2  pollsters say they are observing ahead of the election, with women breaking for Democrats and men for Republicans by increasingly wide margins:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not what I see, in terms of my rallies, in terms of interactions I\u8217\'20\'19m having with people in communities and on the ground. What I\u8217\'20\'19m seeing is, in equal measure, men and women talking about their concerns about the future of our democracy, talking about the fact that they want a president who leads with optimism and takes on the challenges that we face, whether it be grocery prices or investing in small businesses or home ownership.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris calls Republican endorsements a sign that leaders 'understand what's at stake'\par \par \uc2 In brief remarks to the press in Philadelphia before departing for a campaign event in Georgia, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  thanked the two Republican politicians who announced they would be voting for her.\par \par \uc2 Former congressman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a43a28f08791c139f6a05#block-671a43a28f08791c139f6a05"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fred Upton}}}\uc2  of Michigan and Waukesha, Wisconsin mayor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a48368f08e8a9846d1797#block-671a48368f08e8a9846d1797"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shawn Reilly}}}\uc2  both cited their concerns with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in announcing their endorsement of Harris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis continues to be, I think, evidence of the fact that people who have been leaders in our country, regardless of their political party, understand what\u8217\'20\'19s at stake. And they are weighing in courageously, in many cases, in support of what we need to have, which is a president of the United States who understands the obligation to uphold the constitution of the United States and our democracy,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 She also hit out at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who declined to participate in a second debate with Harris hosted by CNN that would have happened last night. Instead, the vice-president to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/kamala-harris-cnn-town-hall-pennsylvania-john-kelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared solo at a town hall}}}\uc2  the network organized with undecided voters in Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Harris said:\par \par \uc2 As for last night, yet again, Trump not showing up, refused to be a part of a CNN debate, and clearly his staff has been saying he\u8217\'20\'19s exhausted. And the sad part about that is, he\u8217\'20\'19s trying to be president of the United States, probably the toughest job in the world, and he\u8217\'20\'19s exhausted.\par \par \uc2 I said last night what I mean, which is the American people are being presented with a very serious decision, and it includes what we must understand will happen starting on January 20, in this choice. Either you have the choice of a \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will sit in the Oval Office stewing, plotting revenge, retribution, writing out his enemies list, or what I will be doing, which is responding to folks like the folks last night with a to-do list, understanding the need to work on lifting up the American people, whether it be through the issue of grocery prices and bringing them down, or investing in our economy, investing in our small businesses, investing in our families.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Voto Latino, a top civic engagement non-profit aimed at empowering Latino voters, has launched a new campaign to raise awareness about what {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/14/project-2025-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2  means for Latinos.\par \par \uc2 The organization identified parts of Project 2025 that would have the most negative effect on the Latino community, and translated these portions into Spanish. Voto Latino is launching paid ads in Arizona, North Carolina, Nevada, Pennsylvania and Michigan to publicize this initiative, in a $3.5m campaign.\par \par \uc2 Remember: Trump has tried to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/17/trump-team-project-2025-banned-staffers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 distance himself}}}\uc2  from \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 -backed initiative to overhaul the \uc2 US government\uc2 , which includes plans to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fire civil servants en masse, as polling indicated it was a political liability for him. The Vera Institute for Justice {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vera.org/news/project-2025-is-a-pathway-to-mass-deportations-and-family-separation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that provisions relating to immigration were \u8220\'20\'1Cdesigned to initiate mass deportations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs much as former President Trump tries to distance himself from Project 2025, we will not be fooled: We know that he will implement this extremist agenda if he wins. It is clear that Project 2025 will set us back by dismantling the fabric of our country through extreme conservative efforts to impose a regressive vision for our nation,\u8221\'20\'1D Maria Teresa Kumar, Voto Latino President and Co-Founder, said in a press release announcing the campaign.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe threats posed to our community by Project 2025 are clear and present. Latino voters and other voters of color will be affected the most by Project 2025.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the power to ensure that an extremist agenda does not go into place by making our voices heard at the ballot box in November,\u8221\'20\'1D Kumar also said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn this election, over 36 million Latinos are eligible to vote. We have a responsibility to inform one another of the potential dangers related to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s agenda as seen in Project 2025, and the impact that it will have on ourselves, our communities, and our families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been working tirelessly to win over male voters and by some measures, his efforts appear effective.\par \par \uc2 Trump is besting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  among men 53 to 37 percent, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/opinion/columnist/2024/10/23/harris-trump-men-women-voters-election/75776154007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USA Today/Suffolk University poll}}}\uc2 , while the vice president is winning women 53 percent to his 36 percent.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s far-right politics seem especially appealing to white male voters, and there have been various explanations for this trend. Some have opined that it\u8217\'20\'19s sheer sexism; others believe that it\u8217\'20\'19s due to a purported male loneliness epidemic and uncertainty about their role in American society.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Oliver Laughland and Tom Silverstone {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2024/oct/24/bro-culture-how-gender-is-defining-us-election-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke with residents of Middletown}}}\uc2 , Ohio--GOP vice presidential candidate JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s hometown-- in an effort to learn why gender is a watershed issue in this election.\par \par \uc2 Here is their eye-opening report.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 With less than two weeks to go before election day, data {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/us-presidential-election-trump-harris-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicates}}}\uc2  that early voting has hit massive numbers in several key swing states.\par \par \uc2 Some 25 million Americans have already cast their ballots. At least part of this surge was prompted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  deciding to vote early due to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  direction.\par \par \uc2 In the battleground state of Georgia, which Trump lost by just 11,779 votes in 2020, more than 1.9 million Americans have either cast their votes via mail-in ballots or in person. North Carolina saw 1.7 million voting early {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/18/election-north-carolina-early-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  in spite of the disastrous Hurricane Helene}}}\uc2  in September.\par \par \uc2 While Trump has emphatically urged his supporters to hit the polls, saying at a Georgia rally \u8220\'20\'1Cjust vote \u8211\'20\'13 whichever way you want to do it,\u8221\'20\'1D Democrats and progressives are also encouraging early voting. Senate Democrats on Tuesday released a report urging Americans to vote as early as possible, and to answer questions about why the results might not be known on election night.\par \par \uc2 On college campuses, advocates are working to increase early voting access for students. At the \uc2 University of Minnesota\uc2  on Tuesday, for example, the undergraduate student government organized a one-day pop-up {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/college-students-voters-polling-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling site}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made clear that he would end the effort to hold him legally accountable for allegedly trying to overturn the 2020 election and hide classified documents, saying in an interview that he would fire special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a6ba48f081d096f9f84eb#block-671a6ba48f081d096f9f84eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 within two seconds}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, if elected. The comment {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a6eef8f08791c139f6c67#block-671a6eef8f08791c139f6c67"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drew an uproar}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign, which is seeking to convince voters that Trump would govern as a dictator in a second term. Meanwhile, the vice-president is gearing up for her rally in Houston tomorrow, where she will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a5aa18f08e8a9846d185b#block-671a5aa18f08e8a9846d185b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  be joined by Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a39a68f081d096f9f8248#block-671a39a68f081d096f9f8248"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 We will see}}}\uc2  her later today in Georgia at a campaign event scheduled for 7pm, while Trump holds a rally in Arizona at 4pm.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has been going on today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris picked up the endorsement of two Republicans, one {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a43a28f08791c139f6a05#block-671a43a28f08791c139f6a05"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a former congressman from Michigan}}}\uc2 , the other {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a48368f08e8a9846d1797#block-671a48368f08e8a9846d1797"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a mayor in a pivotal county in Wisconsin}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Yet another former Trump administration official has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a51038f08e8a9846d17eb#block-671a51038f08e8a9846d17eb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly warned}}}\uc2  of his dictatorial streak, specifically his \u8220\'20\'1Cauthoritarian tendencies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A thorough poll from Bloomberg News and \uc2 Morning Consult{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/24/donald-trump-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-democrats-republicans?page=with:block-671a63978f081d096f9f843e#block-671a63978f081d096f9f843e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 finds}}}\uc2  the same thing many before it has: the race is too close to call.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Later on in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interview with conservative broadcaster \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2 , the former president attacked special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Ca scoundrel\u8221\'20\'1D, and says he does not think he would be impeached for firing him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, they will impeach you again on day one if you fire \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  or you pardon yourself. Are you prepared to be impeached again and again and again if they have the House, because they just will?\u8221\'20\'1D Hewitt asked, referring to the Democrats who could recapture that majority in Congress\u8217\'20\'19s lower chamber in the upcoming election.\par \par \uc2 Trump responded:\par \par \uc2 No, I don\u8217\'20\'19t think they will impeach me if I fire \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2 . \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  is a scoundrel, he\u8217\'20\'19s a very dishonest man in my opinion, very dishonest man, and he\u8217\'20\'19s a mean man, a mean man, but his problem is he\u8217\'20\'19s so mean that he always goes too far, like the raid of Mar-a-Lago.\par \par \uc2 The latter part is a reference to the second case Smith brought against Trump, for allegedly hiding classified materials at his properties, including Mar-a-Lago in south Florida. Over the summer, Aileen Cannon, a Trump-appointed federal judge who was assigned to the case, threw out Smith\u8217\'20\'19s indictment, which the special counsel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/26/special-counsel-appeals-trump-classified-document-case-dismissal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is appealing}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In his interview with Hewitt, Trump said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe had a brave, brilliant judge in Florida\u8221\'20\'1D, apparently a reference to Cannon. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/judge-tossed-trumps-classified-docs-case-list-proposed/story?id=114997807"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC News reports}}}\uc2  that his feelings go deeper than that: Cannon\u8217\'20\'19s name is on a list of potential attorney general candidates for his second administration, and was added after she dismissed the classified documents indictment.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for allegedly conspiring to overturn the 2020 election was delayed for months as the supreme court dealt with the former president\u8217\'20\'19s claim of immunity, and is only now getting back on track. As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2  reported earlier this month, Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team appears to want to center its case on how Trump\u8217\'20\'19s vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  handled the then-president\u8217\'20\'19s effort to keep \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  out of the White House. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 Special counsel prosecutors intend to make {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s vice-president \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  and efforts to recruit fake Trump electors the centerpiece of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donald-trump-trials"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criminal prosecution}}}\uc2  against the former president, according to a sprawling legal brief that was partly unsealed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The redacted brief, made public by the presiding US district judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 , shows prosecutors are relying extensively on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s pressure campaign against Pence to support the charge that Trump conspired to obstruct the January 6 certification of the election results.\par \par \uc2 And prosecutors used an equally voluminous portion of the 165-page brief to express their intent to use evidence of Trump trying to get officials in seven key swing states to reverse his defeat to support the charges that he conspired to disenfranchise American voters.\par \par \uc2 The brief\u8217\'20\'19s principal mission was to convince Chutkan to allow the allegations and evidence buttressing the superseding indictment against Trump to proceed to trial, arguing that it complied with the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s recent ruling that gave former presidents immunity for official acts.\par \par \uc2 As part of the ruling, the court ordered Chutkan to sort through the indictment and decide which of the allegations against Trump should be tossed because of the immunity rules and which could proceed to trial.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/02/jack-smith-pence-trump-election-interference-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Special counsel pushes to use Pence against Trump in 2020 election case}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Democrats have been loudly condemning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for rhetoric they call dictatorial, as well as steering voters\u8217\'20\'19 attention to his former White House chief of staff \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comment that he meets the definition of a fascist.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newrepublic.com/article/187481/transcript-harris-harsh-takedown-trumps-hitler-stunner-nails"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with the New Republic}}}\uc2 , Ben Wikler, who as chair of the Wisconsin Democratic Party is hoping to deliver the electoral votes of one of the swingiest swing states to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , explains why he believes such allegations may tip the scales in the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s favor:\par \par \uc2 This is critical because this is the genuine article that stakes in this election. Now we\u8217\'20\'19ve got \uc2 Mark Milley\uc2 , the former head of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 , former President Trump\u8217\'20\'19s chief of staff, who was a four-star general\u8212\'20\'14and Harris amplifying it\u8212\'20\'14making clear that the nation\u8217\'20\'19s cameras are pointed directly at this reality. For the voters that are on the fence, who often feel deeply conflicted in the final weeks of this election, people who maybe have voted Republican in the past, but are not quite sure if they can vote for Trump again, this gives them a very clear reason to break against Trump. And that could be the entire ball game.\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin is a jump ball right now. There\u8217\'20\'19s a poll today that finds 2 percent of Wisconsin, or 4 percent of Wisconsin voters, undecided, and 48-48 for Harris and for Trump. That means that the decisions made by those last 4 percent could tip the entire election here and probably, frankly, in all the other battleground states. There\u8217\'20\'19s seven states that are jump balls in the final stretch. And what we know\u8212\'20\'14I know this from directly knocking on doors and talking to voters; we know this from polls; we know this from models; we know this from focus groups; we know from every method of research that we have\u8212\'20\'14is that there\u8217\'20\'19s a share of the undecided electorate who have been traditionally Republican, who can\u8217\'20\'19t stand the idea of Trump and are trying to decide for themselves whether they can overcome their aversion to Trump and still vote for him, or whether that is just so unacceptable that even if they disagree with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  about a bunch of stuff, they\u8217\'20\'19re going to vote for her in the final stretch. That is probably the election-defining question.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign says latest Trump comments proof of his plans for dictatorship\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s comment about firing \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  and his brags about the supreme court giving presidents immunity is proof he would govern as a dictator.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  thinks he\u8217\'20\'19s above the law, and these latest comments are right in line with the warnings made by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former Chief of Staff that he wants to rule as a dictator with unchecked power,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ammar Moussa, the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s director of rapid response.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA second Trump term, where a more unstable and unhinged Trump has essentially no guardrails and is surrounded by loyalists who will enable his worst instincts, is guaranteed to be more dangerous. America can\u8217\'20\'19t risk a second Trump term.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 If elected, Trump says he will fire \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  'within two seconds'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has vowed that if he returns to the White House, he will swiftly fire \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2 , the justice department special counsel who is prosecuting him for allegedly plotting to overturn the 2020 election and hide classified documents.\par \par \uc2 In an interview today, conservative broadcaster \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2  asked Trump if he would pardon himself or fire Smith. Trump meandered in his reply, before saying:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s so easy. I would fire him within two seconds.\par \par \uc2 Trump also noted that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe got immunity at the Supreme Court,\u8221\'20\'1D a reference to the ruling by the court\u8217\'20\'19s conservative majority this summer finding that presidents are immune from prosecution for official acts. That complicated Smith\u8217\'20\'19s election meddling case against the former president, and played a part in it not going to trial prior to the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Perhaps more interesting is this survey that the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  wrote up yesterday showing that Arab Americans are now narrowly leaning towards \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , after strongly backing \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020. That shift is likely a consequence of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza following the 7 October attack, and could imperil \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning the White House. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 Arab Americans are slightly more likely to vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , according to a new poll, in a worrying sign for the Democratic nominee\u8217\'20\'19s chances of carrying the battleground state of Michigan, which is home to a large Arab American population.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cdn.sanity.io/files/ifn0l6bs/production/7c56e606b1909778e15af5643bff9346a1d76bd8.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The survey}}}\uc2 , conducted by the Arab News Research and Studies Unit along with \uc2 YouGov\uc2 , shows 43% supporting Trump compared with 41% for Harris, and 4% backing the Green Party candidate, Jill Stein.\par \par \uc2 The figures are broadly in line with a previous poll carried out this month by \uc2 the Arab American Institute\uc2 . Together they suggest that Harris\u8217\'20\'19s support in the community has been undermined by the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s backing for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s year-long war against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The latest poll also shows Trump leading Harris by 39% to 33% on the question of which candidate would be most likely resolve the Israeli-Palestinian conflict, while the candidates were tied at 38% apiece on who would be \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter for the Middle East in general\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Support for Trump is particularly striking given that the same poll shows twice as many respondents \u8211\'20\'13 46% to 23% \u8211\'20\'13 think anti-Arab racism and hate crimes are likely to increase under a Trump presidency compared with under Harris.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/arab-americans-poll-trump-harris-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arab Americans slightly favor Trump over Harris, says new poll}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/features/2024-10-23/new-poll-has-trump-harris-tied-in-key-states-just-12-days-to-election?utm_source=google&utm_medium=bd&cmpId=google&sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloomberg News and Morning Consult}}}\uc2  released polling that found, like so many before it have, an essentially tied race between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The survey heard from voters in all seven swing states, and found Trump leading by 1.5 percentage points in Georgia, 1.2 percentage points in North Carolina and 0.3 percentage points in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Harris was up by 0.4 percentage points in Arizona, 3.1 percentage points in Michigan, 0.5 percentage points in Nevada and 1.7 percentage points in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Many of these findings are within the poll\u8217\'20\'19s one percentage point margin of error.\par \par \uc2 Should the swing states end up voting the way they are leaning in this poll \u8211\'20\'13 and there\u8217\'20\'19s no telling that they will \u8211\'20\'13 Harris would win.\par \par \uc2 For more of what polls are telling us, or not telling us, check out our tracker:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 US presidential polls tracker: Trump v Harris latest national averages}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 NBC News has a little more detail on Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s event with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Houston tomorrow, specifically that she will be performing:\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NBCNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @NBCNews}}}\uc2  confirms: Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 is expected to appear with Vice President Harris in Houston Friday evening, three sources familiar with the planning tell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KellyO?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @KellyO}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Yamiche?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @Yamiche}}}\uc2  & myself. One of the people said Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 plans to PERFORM as well. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/tylerpager?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @tylerpager}}}\uc2  scooped the ?? news first.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Monica Alba (@albamonica) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/albamonica/status/1849462604357353637?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 to campaign with Harris in Houston on Friday - report\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 will appear with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Houston on Friday, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reports, when the vice-president visits the pop star\u8217\'20\'19s hometown to rally with Democratic Senate candidate \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2  and attack \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans passed by Republicans.\par \par \uc2 Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s song \u8220\'20\'1CFreedom\u8221\'20\'1D is regularly played at Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign events, though the singer has not appeared with the vice-president since she launched her campaign.\par \par \uc2 Harris has been picking up the endorsements of a number of prominent musicians in recent weeks, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/11/taylor-swift-harris-endorsement-reactions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taylor Swift}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2024/oct/04/bruce-springsteen-endorses-kamala-harris-for-president-while-criticising-dangerous-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bruce Springsteen}}}\uc2  , who will do concerts with the campaign starting today in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 In addition to attempting to impeach \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , House Republicans have fixated on his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/05/hunter-biden-guilty-plea-tax-avoidance-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legally troubled}}}\uc2  son \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 , looking for evidence of corruption by the president.\par \par \uc2 They have not turned up much, despite issuing a flurry of subpoenas to Biden administration officials that have led to lengthy and complex litigation. Yesterday, one of the last outstanding matters came before a federal judge who became so frustrated with the squabble she invoked her dog. The hearing led to an agreement that will likely delay the release of any new information the Republicans are seeking until next year \u8211\'20\'13 at which point, there will be a new Congress, and Biden will no longer be in the White House.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/10/23/subpoena-fight-hunter-biden-00185119?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico was at the hearing}}}\uc2 , and explains more:\par \par \uc2 A highly unusual ultimatum from a frustrated judge caused House Republican investigators to postpone their demand for testimony from two Justice Department tax attorneys in a probe of \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s finances.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m willing to bet everything I own, plus my dog Scout, that these two line attorneys are going to have zero information to confirm your suspicion,\u8221\'20\'1D U.S. District Judge Ana Reyes told a lawyer representing the House GOP on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Reyes threatened to order Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  and \uc2 House Judiciary Committee\uc2  Chairman Jim Jordan (R-Ohio) to show up next week in her Washington courtroom for legal arguments on the dispute.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t test me on this \u8230\'20\'26 I\u8217\'20\'19m not bluffing,\u8221\'20\'1D said Reyes, an appointee of President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  who is often seen around the federal courthouse with her golden retriever.\par \par \uc2 The fight emerged from House Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 long-running search for evidence that the White House exerted political pressure on officials who investigated the younger Biden\u8217\'20\'19s failure to pay income taxes. As part of that inquiry, the \uc2 House Judiciary Committee\uc2  tried to obtain testimony from two Justice Department tax lawyers who worked on the case.\par \par \uc2 When the Justice Department resisted the House GOP\u8217\'20\'19s subpoenas to the two lawyers, the fight ended up before Reyes, who has been refereeing the dispute for months with increasing exasperation.\par \par \uc2 During a two-hour hearing on Wednesday, she pressed lawyers for both sides to punt the dispute until next year. If they refused, she said, she would summon their bosses into court.\par \par \uc2 After a brief recess, the House\u8217\'20\'19s top lawyer, Matthew Berry, and veteran Justice Department lawyer Elizabeth Shapiro told the judge they had agreed to shelve the matter until early next year. By that point, a new Congress and a new president will have been sworn in \u8212\'20\'14 developments likely to diminish both sides\u8217\'20\'19 appetite for a fight linked to an all-but-defunct effort to impeach \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 You don\u8217\'20\'19t hear so much about Congress these day, and there\u8217\'20\'19s a good reason for that.\par \par \uc2 Both houses are in recess, and many lawmakers are back in their districts campaigning for re-election. But the Republican-led House judiciary committee will today convene in Milwaukee for a hearing titled \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://judiciary.house.gov/committee-activity/hearings/biden-harris-border-crisis-wisconsin-perspectives-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Biden-Harris Border Crisis: Wisconsin Perspectives}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not an accident that they are focusing on one of the issues \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is campaigning on in one of the swing states he needs to win. Led by his ally Jim Jordan, the committee has been at the forefront of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/house-republicans-biden-impeachment-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ultimately fruitless}}}\uc2  effort to impeach \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and quickly shifted to attacking \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  when she became the Democratic candidate in July. Expect this hearing to be a continuation of that offensive.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, another former Trump administration official {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/10/23/elizabeth-neumann-john-kelly-trump-warnings-00185181"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told Politico}}}\uc2  that she agrees with \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s assessment that the former president is a fascist, and said he has \u8220\'20\'1Cauthoritarian tendencies\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDoes he have authoritarian tendencies? Yes,\u8221\'20\'1D said Elizabeth Neumann, a former deputy chief of staff in the homeland security department.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIs he kind of leaning towards that ultra-nationalism component? Absolutely. That is kind of his brand, right? He\u8217\'20\'19s made nationalism the new definition of the Republican Party.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Neumann has already endorsed his opponent, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 After ex-chief of staff call him 'fascist', Trump lobs insults at Harris\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign spent yesterday hitting back at \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 , his former White House chief of staff who went public with his thoughts that his one-time boss was a fascist.\par \par \uc2 While the president angrily condemned Kelly as \u8220\'20\'1Ca bad general\u8221\'20\'1D in a Truth Social post, he didn\u8217\'20\'19t bring the subject up much at a Georgia rally in the evening, instead publicly insulting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis woman is crazy,\u8221\'20\'1D he told an arena full of supporters in the Atlanta suburb of Duluth. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re the worst ever. There\u8217\'20\'19s never been anybody like you. You can\u8217\'20\'19t put two sentences together. The world is laughing at us because of you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 And more:\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s not a smart person. She\u8217\'20\'19s a low IQ individual.\par \par \uc2 It was all part of a campaign speech that was, in typical Trump 2024 form, lengthy and meandering, touching on everything from \uc2 Richard Nixon\uc2  to \uc2 McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2 . \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/sam-levin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Levin}}}\uc2  watched the whole thing, so you don\u8217\'20\'19t have to:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/trump-harris-insults-georgia-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump escalates insults against Harris as he faces scrutiny over alleged praise of Hitler}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris picks up endorsement from Republican mayor in key Wisconsin county - report\par \par \uc2 A Republican city mayor in a Wisconsin county that has often swung elections in the battleground state has endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fox6now.com/news/waukesha-mayor-endorses-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FOX6 News Milwaukee reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Shawn Reilly is the mayor of Waukesha, the largest city in the county of the same name, which is also the most-populous Republican-voting county in the state that is viewed as crucial to Harris\u8217\'20\'19s hopes of winning the White House. He told the broadcaster that he\u8217\'20\'19s voting for the vice-president because he does not want \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to return to the White House:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s difficult. The easy thing to do is just not say anything and cast my vote the way I want, but I think we\u8217\'20\'19re at a crossroads now,\u8221\'20\'1D Reilly said. \u8220\'20\'1CI feel in my heart that this is something that I need to come out and say: I am going to be voting for Vice President Harris to become our next president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Reilly voted third party in 2016 and for President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in 2020 but kept that to himself. For other officers, he said he votes Republican \u8220\'20\'1Cmore often than not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Now this red city mayor is publicly endorsing blue for president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a vote against Trump,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI am terrified of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  becoming our next president for all the reasons I have indicated: he\u8217\'20\'19s already been impeached twice. He\u8217\'20\'19s been convicted of felonies and this is not what the United States needs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The chair of the state Democratic party, Ben Wikler, cheered Reilly\u8217\'20\'19s break from the GOP:\par \par \uc2 enltrThis\par \par \uc2 is\par \par \uc2 a\par \par \uc2 big\par \par \uc2 deal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7eTwMlqkhI"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7eTwMlqkhI}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ben Wikler (@benwikler) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benwikler/status/1849306765902450736?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican former Michigan congressman endorses Harris - report\par \par \uc2 Fred Upton\uc2 , a Republican former congressman who represented a western Michigan district for 36 years, has endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/politics/2024/10/24/gops-upton-backs-harris-presidential-campaign/75810489007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Detroit News reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Upton, who was one of 10 Republicans to vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s impeachment after January 6, said he had voted Democratic in a presidential election for the first time in his life because he is turned off by the former president\u8217\'20\'19s extremism and believes Harris will be more successful at governing with bipartisan support.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWatching Trump day after day, he\u8217\'20\'19s ignored the advice of many senior, respected Republicans to stay on the issues,\u8221\'20\'1D Upton said in an interview with the Detroit News.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInstead, he\u8217\'20\'19s still talking about the election being stolen, trashing women left and right. He\u8217\'20\'19s just totally unhinged. We don\u8217\'20\'19t need this chaos. We need to move forward, and that\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m where I am.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The endorsement comes as Harris steps up her outreach to Republicans who she believes can be swayed against voting for Trump. Earlier this week, she campaigned alongside \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , another Republican former congresswoman who lost her seat after breaking with the former president:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/liz-cheney-kamala-harris-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Cheney urges conservatives to back Kamala Harris over \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 When he speaks in Tempe, Arizona later today, one wonders if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will address the allegation made by former model Stacey Williams in an interview with the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/stephanie-kirchgaessner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stephanie Kirchgaessner}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lucy-osborne"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lucy Osborne}}}\uc2  that he groped her in 1993. She\u8217\'20\'19s the latest woman to come forward and say the then-real estate mogul put his hands on her without permission. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 A former model who says she met {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  through the late sexual abuser {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein}}}\uc2  has accused the former president of groping and sexually touching her in an incident in Trump Tower in 1993, in what she believed was a \u8220\'20\'1Ctwisted game\u8221\'20\'1D between the two men.\par \par \uc2 Stacey Williams, who worked as a professional model in the 1990s, said she first met Trump in 1992 at a Christmas party after being introduced to him by Epstein, who she believed was a good friend of the then New York real estate developer. Williams said Epstein was interested in her and the two casually dated for a period of a few months.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt became very clear then that he and Donald were really, really good friends and spent a lot of time together,\u8221\'20\'1D Williams said.\par \par \uc2 The alleged groping occurred some months later, in the late winter or early spring of 1993, when Epstein suggested during a walk they were on that he and Williams stop by to visit Trump at Trump Tower. Epstein was later convicted on sex offenses and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2019/aug/10/jeffrey-epstein-dead-prison-report-latest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed himself in prison}}}\uc2  in 2019.\par \par \uc2 Moments after they arrived, she alleges, Trump greeted Williams, pulled her toward him and started groping her. She said he put his hands \u8220\'20\'1Call over my breasts\u8221\'20\'1D as well as her waist and her buttocks. She said she froze because she was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply confused\u8221\'20\'1D about what was happening. At the same time, she said she believed she saw the two men smiling at each other.\par \par \uc2 Karoline Leavitt, the press secretary for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign, provided a statement denying the allegations, which said in part: \u8220\'20\'1CThese accusations, made by a former activist for \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and announced on a Harris campaign call two weeks before the election, are unequivocally false. It\u8217\'20\'19s obvious this fake story was contrived by the Harris campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/donald-trump-accuser-stacey-williams-jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump groped me in what felt like a \u8216\'20\'18twisted game\u8217\'20\'19 with Jeffrey Epstein, former model alleges}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris heads to Georgia, Trump to Arizona as campaign grinds to finish\par \par \uc2 The two lead actors in US politics (soon there will be only one) are scheduled to make a single appearance each today, as they look to clinch the support of swing state voters with little time left before the election.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will head to Georgia for a campaign event in Clarkston, outside Atlanta, at 7pm ET. She flies from there to Houston, Texas, where tomorrow, she\u8217\'20\'19s set to attack \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in a state that is not a swing state, but which moved swiftly to ban the procedure after Roe v Wade was overturned. She will also campaign with \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2 , the Democratic Senate candidate whose victory could allow the party to maintain its control of Congress\u8217\'20\'19s upper chamber, which the GOP is otherwise viewed as having a good shot at taking.\par \par \uc2 As for Trump, he\u8217\'20\'19s having one of his usual rallies in a Tempe, Arizona arena at 4pm. Based on how his campaign advertised it, the former president will attack Harris and the Democrats over inflation, but Trump, of course, rarely stays on topic.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 An Arizona prosecutor said the man arrested in the shooting of a Democratic national committee office in suburban Phoenix had more than 120 guns and more than 250,000 rounds of ammunition in his home, leading law enforcement to believe he may have been planning a mass casualty event.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press (AP) reports that Maricopa county prosecutor Neha Bhatia said at Jeffrey Michael Kelly\u8217\'20\'19 s initial court appearance on Wednesday that federal agents told her about the large seizure made after Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s arrest. Scopes, body armour and silencers were also found, she said. A machine gun was discovered in the car he was driving.\par \par \uc2 The sheer size of the cache led authorities to believe \u8220\'20\'1Cthis person was preparing to commit an act of mass casualty,\u8221\'20\'1D Bhatia said.\par \par \uc2 Police said Kelly, 60, allegedly fired BB pellets and then gunshots at the glass front door and a window of the Arizona Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 field office in Tempe. Police found three.22-caliber bullet casings while searching Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s trash, according to court documents, reports the AP.\par \par \uc2 Nobody was inside during the shootings in the early morning hours of 16 September, 23 September and 6 October.\par \par \uc2 The Tempe location was one of 18 Harris field offices in Arizona where Democrats gathered to organise Harris campaign efforts. It was shut down after the last shooting, police said.\par \par \uc2 Kelly is also accused of hanging several political signs lined with razor blades on Tuesday in Ahwatukee, an affluent suburb of Phoenix where most voters have chosen Democrats in recent elections. Authorities said he also hung plastic bags holding a white powder labeled \u8220\'20\'1Cbiohazard\u8221\'20\'1D from those signs.\par \par \uc2 The AP reports that authorities said the hand-painted signs were attached to palm trees and appeared to criticise Democrats and their presidential nominee, vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kelly was being held on three felony counts of acts of terrorism and four other counts related to the shootings, according to police. A $500,000 cash bond was set with a requirement for house arrest and an ankle monitor in the event he is able to raise that amount.\par \par \uc2 His attorney Jason Squires said Kelly was a retired aerospace engineer who at one time had top security clearance, had no criminal record and was not a flight risk. Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s next appearance was set for the morning of 29 October in Maricopa county superior court.\par \par \uc2 Political violence has already marred the campaign season, with the Republican presidential nominee being targeted by assassination attempts at a campaign rally and at one of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Florida golf courses.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris praises \uc2 John Kelly\uc2  for sending \u8216\'20\'18911 call\u8217\'20\'19 to the US over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fitness to serve\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  praised \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff for sending a \u8220\'20\'1C911 call\u8221\'20\'1D to the nation about the former president\u8217\'20\'19s unfitness to serve a second term, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/harris-trump-fascist-hitler-comments-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attacking her opponent as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfascist\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  who would send the nation down a dangerous path.\par \par \uc2 Harris participated in a CNN town hall with undecided voters in Delaware county, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania}}}\uc2  , on Wednesday, as the battleground state appears poised to play a potentially decisive role in the presidential race. While taking voters\u8217\'20\'19 questions on everything from the cost of living to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, Harris repeatedly steered the conversation back to questions over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fitness for office.\par \par \uc2 The town hall came a day after the Atlantic published {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theatlantic.com/politics/archive/2024/10/trump-military-generals-hitler/680327/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a story}}}\uc2  detailing former Trump advisers\u8217\'20\'19 accounts of the then president expressing a wish for \u8220\'20\'1Cthe kind of generals that Hitler had\u8221\'20\'1D. The article {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/us-presidential-election-trump-harris-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quoted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff, }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/us-presidential-election-trump-harris-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 John Kelly}}}\uc2  , who described the former president\u8217\'20\'19s consistent pattern of demeaning members of the military. The Trump campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/trump-harris-insults-georgia-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has denied these accounts}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do believe that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is unstable, increasingly unstable, and unfit to serve,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told the CNN anchor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/anderson-cooper"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anderson Cooper}}}\uc2  at the town hall. She added:\par \par \uc2 The people who know \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  best, the people who worked with him in the White House \u8230\'20\'26 they have said explicitly he has contempt for the constitution of the United States. They have said he should never again serve as president of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris predicted that, if elected to a second term, Trump would not have advisers like Kelly who might help put guardrails around the former president\u8217\'20\'19s behaviour in office.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[Kelly] is just putting out a 911 call to the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd this time, we must take very seriously, those folks who knew him best and were career people are not going to be there to hold him back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When asked explicitly by Cooper whether she considered Trump to be a fascist, Harris said, \u8220\'20\'1CYes, I do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/kamala-harris-cnn-town-hall-pennsylvania-john-kelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris praises John Kelly for sending \u8216\'20\'18911 call\u8217\'20\'19 to the US over Trump\u8217\'20\'19s fitness to serve}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some of the latest images on the newswires:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Project 2025 will \u8216\'20\'18upend\u8217\'20\'19 the lives of Black Americans, new report shows\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2 , the 900-page ultra-conservative roadmap that details how the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his allies would restructure the \uc2 US government\uc2  if he is elected, has specific implications for Black Americans, according to a new report.\par \par \uc2 The Legal Defense Fund (LDF), an organisation that fights for racial justice, recently released the most in-depth legal analysis of Project 2025 \u8217\'20\'19s impact on Black communities. It highlights how Black Americans would be harmed due to policies that would weaken anti-discrimination laws; dismantle the Department of Education ; threaten Black political power; increase the use of the death penalty (which disproportionately affects Black people); and exacerbate health disparities caused by environmental racism.\par \par \uc2 Karla McKanders, the director of the LDF\u8217\'20\'19s Thurgood Marshall Institute (TMI), the in-house research thinktank that produced the report, said she wanted people to understand the \u8220\'20\'1Clarger impact that Project 2025 will have on our democracy and undermining our democracy\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The report is written in plain language and has been shared on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/naacpldf/photos/project-2025-will-eliminate-key-safeguards-that-protect-black-workers6-and-bar-f/979747910847968/?_rdr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media}}}\uc2 , McKanders said, as the organization wants it to be available to a wide audience. \u8220\'20\'1CThe most important part of the report is how Project 2025 will have an impact on individual lives and how those individual lives will be upended through the policy proposals.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Of note, she said, are the report\u8217\'20\'19s chapters on education equity and political participation.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/project-2025-black-americans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025 will \u8216\'20\'18upend\u8217\'20\'19 the lives of Black Americans, new report shows}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  tells supporters to 'just vote' at Georgia rally organized by Charlie Kirk\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  implored supporters at a Georgia rally to vote for him \u8211\'20\'13 with an early ballot or in-person on election day \u8211\'20\'13 in a state that will be crucial in the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust vote \u8211\'20\'13 whichever way you want to do it,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said at the event on Wednesday organised by conservative provocateur Charlie Kirk and the group he founded, reports the Associated Press (AP).\par \par \uc2 But the rest of former president\u8217\'20\'19s speech and the lineup that preceded him framed the 2024 presidential election in stark terms. The Republican nominee insulted \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  while Kirk and other speakers used religious references and described the vice-president and her Democratic party as evil, reports the AP.\par \par \uc2 Democrats \u8220\'20\'1Cstand for everything God hates,\u8221\'20\'1D Kirk said, calling the Trump v Harris choice \u8220\'20\'1Ca spiritual battle\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a Christian state. I\u8217\'20\'19d like to see it stay that way,\u8221\'20\'1D Kirk told the 10,000 or so Georgians, who at one point, the AP reports, joined Kirk in a deafening chant of \u8220\'20\'1CChrist is King! Christ is King!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris, who is a Baptist, used a CNN town hall in Philadelphia to describe Trump as fascistic, further crystallizing the nation\u8217\'20\'19s polarized posture with less than two weeks before the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign strategy of encouraging supporters to consider every voting method is a turn from when blamed his 2020 election loss to Democrat \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on mail ballots; the number of people voting early has surged this year.\par \par \uc2 Over 1.9 million voters have cast early ballots in Georgia, where Trump lost by a mere 11,779 votes four years ago to Biden. Voters nationwide have returned more than 23 million advance ballots in the 2024 general election. That has broken records in multiple states, partly driven by Republicans embracing early voting at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s direction.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou need to go to every single person you know and say, \u8216\'20\'18Are you voting for Trump?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Kirk told the crowd.\par \par \uc2 The AP reports that the 31-year-old Kirk has an outsize role in this year\u8217\'20\'19s election, using his online presence and the organisation he founded, Turning Point Action, to make himself one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s most recognisable conservatives and a central part of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s operation. The former president has put a particular emphasis on courting younger men, the \u8220\'20\'1Cbro vote,\u8221\'20\'1D trying to reach them through podcasts, social media and influencers such as Kirk.\par \par \uc2 The rally, at the Gas South arena in Duluth, was filled with Turning Point\u8217\'20\'19s signature pyrotechnics, reports the AP. Trump used it to feature three figures who represent the populist coalition he is trying to assemble: \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , who ran his own campaign for president this year before endorsing Trump; former Rep. \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 , a former Democrat who announced this week that she is joining the Republican Party; and \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , the former Fox News commentator who has attracted millions of followers with his bravado-heavy social media presence. He added country music singer Jason Aldean, whose Try That in a Small Town single was a reaction to urban protests.\par \par \uc2 Carlson whipped the crowd into a frenzy by reassuring them that liberals and political elites were the \u8220\'20\'1Cbizarre minority\u8221\'20\'1D in US politics, while Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CMake America Great Again\u8221\'20\'1D supporters comprise a \u8220\'20\'1Cgentle, tolerant\u8221\'20\'1D movement.\par \par \uc2 According to the AP, Carlson cast Trump as America\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CDad\u8221\'20\'1D and said a Trump victory over Harris would mean \u8220\'20\'1CDad\u8217\'20\'19s home! And he\u8217\'20\'19s pissed!\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 while also being a \u8220\'20\'1Cbig middle finger wagging\u8221\'20\'1D at \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst people in the English-speaking world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Later in the night as Trump spoke, some in the crowd shouted out, \u8220\'20\'1CDaddy\u8217\'20\'19s home!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43am BST\par \par \uc2 With less than two weeks until the US election, Madeleine Finlay speaks to climate activist and author \uc2 Bill McKibben\uc2  for the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/series/science"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Science Weekly}}}\uc2  podcast to find out what a win for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  could mean for the environment and the world\u8217\'20\'19s climate goals.\par \par \uc2 You can listen to it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/audio/2024/oct/24/whats-at-stake-for-the-climate-if-trump-wins-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s at stake for the climate if Trump wins? \u8211\'20\'13 podcast}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s hopes of meeting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  before the US presidential election have faded, Downing Street has said.\par \par \uc2 The UK prime minister said last month he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/sep/24/keir-starmer-heads-to-us-for-summit-at-un-as-aides-seek-meetings-with-harris-and-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aimed to meet both presidential candidates}}}\uc2  before American voters go to the polls on 5 November.\par \par \uc2 He told reporters who had travelled with him to New York that it would be \u8220\'20\'1Cvery good to meet both [Trump and Harris] at some stage\u8221\'20\'1D before the US election. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ll just have to see what\u8217\'20\'19s possible,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Starmer did secure a meeting with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  while in New York for the \uc2 UN\uc2  general assembly in September. He and the former US president had a two-hour dinner, where they were joined by \uc2 David Lammy\uc2 , the foreign secretary.\par \par \uc2 A government source said on Thursday that hopes of arranging a meeting between Starmer and Harris had faded. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re obviously a number of days out from the campaign and I suspect both candidates are focused on the election,\u8221\'20\'1D they said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/oct/24/keir-starmer-unlikely-meet-kamala-harris-us-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Keir Starmer unlikely to meet Kamala Harris before US election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.34am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.22am BST\par \par \uc2 LA Times editor resigns after owner blocks presidential endorsement\par \par \uc2 Patrick Soon-Shiong\uc2 , the billionaire owner of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/los-angeles-times"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles Times}}}\uc2 , refused to allow the newspaper\u8217\'20\'19s editorial board to endorse \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president, the former editor of the paper\u8217\'20\'19s opinion section told a media news outlet on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Mariel Garza, a veteran California journalist who has worked for the Times\u8217\'20\'19 editorial board for nearly a decade, resigned from the paper in protest of Soon-Shiong\u8217\'20\'19s decision, she told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cjr.org/business_of_news/los-angeles-times-editorials-editor-resigns-after-owner-blocks-presidential-endorsement.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Columbia Journalism Review}}}\uc2  (CJR).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn dangerous times, honest people need to stand up. This is how I\u8217\'20\'19m standing up,\u8221\'20\'1D Garza told CJR.\par \par \uc2 Harris is the first presidential nominee from California in any political party since \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/DrPatSoonShiong/status/1849217132183060705"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 long social media post}}}\uc2  on X, apparently written in response to Garza\u8217\'20\'19s comments, Soon-Shiong wrote that the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2  editorial board had rejected a proposed alternative to a typical presidential endorsement editorial, which he described as \u8220\'20\'1Ca factual analysis of all the POSITIVE AND NEGATIVE policies by EACH candidate during their tenures at the White House, and how these policies affected the nation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrSo many comments about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/latimes?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @latimes}}}\uc2  Editorial Board not providing a Presidential endorsement this year. Let me clarify how this decision came about.\par \par \uc2 The Editorial Board was provided the opportunity to draft a factual analysis of all the POSITIVE AND NEGATIVE policies by EACH\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dr. Pat Soon-Shiong (@DrPatSoonShiong) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DrPatSoonShiong/status/1849217132183060705?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Soon-Shiong wrote that the paper\u8217\'20\'19s opinion editors, who typically endorse one candidate each for a range of local and national offices and explains why each candidate is the best pick, were asked to instead present \u8220\'20\'1Cclear and non-partisan information side-by-side, [so] our readers could decide who would be worthy of being President for the next four years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInstead of adopting this path as suggested, the Editorial Board chose to remain silent and I accepted their decision,\u8221\'20\'1D Soon-Shiong wrote. He ended with the words: \u8220\'20\'1CPlease {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/hashtag/vote?src=hashtag_click"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #vote}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/los-angeles"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Los Angeles}}}\uc2  Times did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2024/oct/23/la-times-editor-resigns-presidential-endorsement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LA Times editor resigns after owner blocks presidential endorsement}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Nearly 25 million Americans have already voted, less than two weeks out from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election}}}\uc2 , with records broken in multiple battleground states, at least partly driven by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  embracing early voting at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  direction.\par \par \uc2 Either through in-person early voting or mail-in ballots, more than 1.9 million voters have cast early votes in Georgia, where Trump lost by a mere 11,779 votes four years ago to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrat}}}\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , while North Carolina also set a new record of more than 1.7m {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/18/election-north-carolina-early-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 despite the chaos caused by Hurricane Helene}}}\uc2  last month.\par \par \uc2 At an event in Georgia, Trump celebrated the state\u8217\'20\'19s record-breaking vote levels, and at a separate rally urged his supporters to \u8220\'20\'1Cjust vote \u8211\'20\'13 whichever way you want to do it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to address \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s economic policy at an afternoon rally in Tempe, Arizona, his campaign announced in a statement that said the vice-president had \u8220\'20\'1Cmade the American Dream of home ownership unreachable for young Americans and families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to Agence France-Presse (AFP), the pro-Trump Turning Point political action committee will then host the Republican ex-president at a Las Vegas rally aimed at recruiting volunteers and celebrating the Asian American and Pacific Islander community.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are voters whose values closely align with the conservative platform but have been given too little attention by our movement,\u8221\'20\'1D Turning Point founder Charlie Kirk said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 AFP reports that Trump told supporters in North Carolina on Tuesday that former president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1Ca real jerk\u8221\'20\'1D and shrugged off his support for Harris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver the last couple of days I\u8217\'20\'19ve watched him campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Republican, who held a spate of stops across Georgia on Wednesday. Trump said:\par \par \uc2 What a divider he is. He divides this country. He couldn\u8217\'20\'19t care less, him and his little group of people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris and former first lady \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  are set to hold a rally this Saturday in Kalamazoo, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris showcases Springsteen in star-studded swing state stop\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will stage a star-studded rally on Thursday alongside \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and Bruce Springsteen, as she launches a series of battleground state concerts to juice support in the final days of a nail-biting US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The Atlanta rally, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s first campaign stop with the only black president in US history, comes as an already bitter campaign is reaching new heights with the Democrat openly calling her Republican rival, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a \u8220\'20\'1Cfascist\u8221\'20\'1D who presents a clear and present danger to US national security, reports Agence France-Presse (AFP).\par \par \uc2 The contest remains a toss-up, with polling in all the swing states within the margin of error, and both campaigns have been pulling out the stops to win over undecided Americans and bank early votes ahead of 5 November.\par \par \uc2 According to AFP, the Harris campaign said it planned gigs in all seven of the swing states expected to determine who wins the White House, with Springsteen back out on the campaign trail Monday in Philadelphia with Obama.\par \par \uc2 The rock legend, whose socially conscious paeans to working-class struggle have made him one of the most popular artists in the US, has long lent his blue-collar appeal to Democratic campaigns.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  walked out to the Springsteen song \u8220\'20\'1CWe Take Care of Our Own\u8221\'20\'1D when he accepted victory in the 2020 election. The rocker \u8211\'20\'13 known as \u8220\'20\'1CThe Boss\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 has campaigned for \uc2 John Kerry\uc2 , \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  and Obama in the past.\par \par \uc2 Obama has been making his own headlining appearances in support of Harris and other Democrats in Arizona, Nevada, Pennsylvania, Wisconsin and Michigan, five of the country\u8217\'20\'19s most closely-fought states.\par \par \uc2 Party officials hope the former president, still one of the most popular Democrats on the national stage eight years after leaving office, will reverse eroding support among black voters, which is behind where it was for Biden in 2020.\par \par \uc2 In other developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nearly 25 million Americans have already voted, less than two weeks out from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election}}}\uc2 , with records broken in multiple battleground states, at least partly driven by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  embracing early voting at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  direction.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s highest court allowed people whose mail ballots were rejected on technicalities to cast provisional ballots, likely affecting thousands of early voters. The decision was another defeat for the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s legal campaign, after it argued some provisional ballots cast during the April primary should have been rejected.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A former model who says she met \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  through the late sexual abuser {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jeffrey Epstein}}}\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/donald-trump-accuser-stacey-williams-jeffrey-epstein"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused the former president of groping and sexually touching her}}}\uc2  in an incident in Trump Tower in 1993, in what she believed was a \u8220\'20\'1Ctwisted game\u8221\'20\'1D between the two men. The Trump campaign called the allegations by Stacey Williams \u8220\'20\'1Cunequivocally false\u8221\'20\'1D, calling it a fake story \u8220\'20\'1Ccontrived by the Harris campaign\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump appeared {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/23/kamala-harris-donald-trump-us-election-2024-latest-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-671956938f085af2d344e9df#block-671956938f085af2d344e9df"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in Zebulon}}}\uc2 , Georgia, with lieutenant governor and 2020 election denierBurt Jones, at a faith-focused event his campaign dubbed a \u8220\'20\'1CBelievers and Ballots town hall\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump praised tech mogul \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , for providing hurricane relief where he claimed the federal government did not.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Writing on Truth Social, Trump assailed \uc2 John Kelly\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Ca bad general\u8221\'20\'1D gripped by \u8220\'20\'1Cpure Trump Derangement Syndrome Hatred\u8221\'20\'1D. Kelly, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff and a retired Marine general, on Tuesday said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/us-presidential-election-trump-harris-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he believed Trump met the definition of \u8220\'20\'1Cfascist\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  and was \u8220\'20\'1Ccertainly an authoritarian\u8221\'20\'1D. Two retired army officers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/23/kamala-harris-donald-trump-us-election-2024-latest-news?page=with:block-67191c238f08509e45b96735#block-67191c238f08509e45b96735"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  they agreed with Kelly, while Republicans including the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/23/kamala-harris-donald-trump-us-election-2024-latest-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-67198c388f087245fd856d74#block-67198c388f087245fd856d74"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 governor of New Hampshire}}}\uc2  dismissed the comments.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harrisdenounced Trump as a \u8220\'20\'1Cfascist\u8221\'20\'1D who wants \u8220\'20\'1Cunchecked power\u8221\'20\'1D and a military personally loyal to him. In a surprise speech from her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/washington-dc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington DC}}}\uc2  residence, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democratic}}}\uc2  nominee jumped on Kelly\u8217\'20\'19s claims. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , said the president also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/23/kamala-harris-donald-trump-us-election-2024-latest-news?CMP=share_btn_url&page=with%3Ablock-6719459e8f085af2d344e925#block-6719459e8f085af2d344e925"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed with those calling Trump a fascist}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris repeated the fascist claim during a televised town hall with undecided voters in Delaware County, outside Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. In response to CNN moderator Anderson Cooper asking her: \u8220\'20\'1CLet me ask you tonight, do you think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a fascist?\u8221\'20\'1D, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/kamala-harris-cnn-town-hall-pennsylvania-john-kelly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris answered: \u8220\'20\'1CYes, I do.\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  Trump was invited to attend the same town hall but declined.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump stayed in Georgiafor a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/trump-harris-insults-georgia-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rally in Duluth }}}\uc2  with guests \uc2 Tucker Carlson\uc2 , \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2 , and former congresswoman \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 . He escalated his personal insults against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , saying she was \u8220\'20\'1Ccrazy\u8221\'20\'1D and inviting voters to tell his opponent: \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18You\u8217\'20\'19re the worst ever. There\u8217\'20\'19s never been anybody like you. You can\u8217\'20\'19t put two sentences together. The world is laughing at us because of you.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 China-linked social media bots are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/24/taizi-flood-china-social-media-bots-marco-rubio-targeting-republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 targeting Republicans including Marco Rubio,}}}\uc2  according to new research from \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 , while a senior US intelligence official said groups in Russia created and helped spread {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/tim-walz-russia-disinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 viral disinformation targeting Tim Walz.}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US justice department warned Musk\u8217\'20\'19s Super Pac that the billionaire and \uc2 Tesla\uc2  CEO\u8217\'20\'19s $1m-a-day giveaways {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/elon-musk-justice-department-giveaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 may violate federal law}}}\uc2 , according to multiple reports. Musk, who has thrown his support behind Trump, announced on Saturday while speaking before a crowd in Pennsylvania that he was giving away $1m each day until election day to someone who signs his online petition supporting the US constitution.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign announced she willdeliver a major \u8220\'20\'1Cclosing argument\u8221\'20\'1D address next week in the same location that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  rallied January 6 rioters before they stormed the US Capitol in 2021.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Democratic vice-presidential nominee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2  voted early along with his wife, Gwen, and son, Gus. Leaving the voting booth in St Paul, Minnesota, Walz said his vote was \u8220\'20\'1Can opportunity to turn the page on the chaos of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and a new way forward\u8221\'20\'1D .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Second gentleman Doug Emhoff, Harris\u8217\'20\'19shusband, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/23/doug-emhoff-florida-rally-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rallied Democrats in Florida}}}\uc2 , marking a break from his recent stumping in more competitive states including Wisconsin, North Carolina and Pennsylvania. Both parties expect the Sunshine state to once more swing for Trump, but the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s rare foray drew attention to the close Senate race between the Republican incumbent and Democratic challenger.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2  opinion editor resigned after the newspaper\u8217\'20\'19s owner blocked the masthead from endorsing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for president. Mariel Garza said she was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/2024/oct/23/la-times-editor-resigns-presidential-endorsement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 standing up against the decision}}}\uc2  by Patrick Soon-Shiong, the paper\u8217\'20\'19s billionaire owner. In a social media post, Soon-Shiong wrote that the \uc2 Los Angeles Times\uc2  editorial board had rejected a proposed alternative to a typical presidential endorsement editorial, which he described as \u8220\'20\'1Ca factual analysis of all the POSITIVE AND NEGATIVE policies by EACH candidate during their tenures at the White House\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241024ekao001h0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
