\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Obama ridicules Trump\u8217\'20\'19s boasts on economy as Walz dismisses Republican nominee\u8217\'20\'19s McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18stunt\u8217\'20\'19 \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin (now); Maanvi Singh, Chris Stein, Tom Ambrose and Victoria Bekiempis (earlier) \par \uc2 12,375 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 October 2024\par 12:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can find more of our US elections coverage here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re ending our live coverage for the day, just two weeks out from election day. Here are some key events and stories from the day:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and Tim Walz{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/obama-walz-wisconsin-early-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 baited the Trump campaign at a Wisconsin rally}}}\uc2  as part of an early voting push.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  told NBC that she has no doubt that the US was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/kamala-harris-nbc-interview-female-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ready for a female president}}}\uc2 , insisting that Americans care more about what candidates can do to help them, rather than their gender.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/trump-complaint-uk-labour-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed an extraordinary complaint against the UK\u8217\'20\'19s }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/trump-complaint-uk-labour-party"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Labour party}}}\uc2  for what it claims is \u8220\'20\'1Cinterference\u8221\'20\'1D in the US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US army has been ordered to release documents about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/trump-arlington-ceremony-records-release"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s pugnacious visit to Arlington national cemetery}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Scrutiny is growing about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/montana-tim-sheehy-business-scrutiny-senate-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Montana aerial firefighting company once led by }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/montana-tim-sheehy-business-scrutiny-senate-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Sheehy}}}\uc2 , the former Navy Seal and Republican Senate candidate who could oust the Democrat incumbent \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/arab-americans-poll-trump-harris-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arab Americans are slightly more likely to vote for }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/arab-americans-poll-trump-harris-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/arab-americans-poll-trump-harris-"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  than \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , according to a new poll, in a worrying sign for the Democratic nominee\u8217\'20\'19s chances of carrying the battleground state of Michigan.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s top elections official defended the state\u8217\'20\'19s elections after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/elon-musk-michigan-election-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeated attacks on Twitter/X from }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/elon-musk-michigan-election-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2 , who spread false claims about inactive voters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff said the Republican candidate meets the definition of a \u8220\'20\'1Cfascist\u8221\'20\'1D and reiterated that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/22/donald-trump-christian-voters-kamala-harris-election-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-67183a318f08da124b607b7d#block-67183a318f08da124b607b7d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump previously praised Hitler}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  promotes small business loans for Latinos\par \par \uc2 In an interview with Telemundo earlier today, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  pledged to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/harris-trump-latinos-economic-policies-18e99a491ba6df73f61a8c6cca004fd7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drive more funds to community banks}}}\uc2  to help Latino men access small business loans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to construct a strong economy that supports the working class, the vice-president said, AP reported. She continued:\par \par \uc2 I know that Hispanic men often have more difficulty securing loans from banks because of their connections and the fact that things aren\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily set up so that they will qualify \u8230\'20\'26 For that reason, I\u8217\'20\'19m focused on seeing what we can do to bring more capital to community banks that better understand the community so we can give them that kind of loans.\par \par \uc2 In a Trump event in Florida courting Latino voters, the former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-kamala-lazy-trope-stereotype-4c2ded1046e492c5d24c7382245d0f7b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denigrated Harris}}}\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1Clazy as hell\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Clow IQ\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Obama rallies in Michigan: 'She didn't pretend to work at \uc2 McDonald's\uc2 '\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  is rallying in Detroit after he was introduced by Eminem. The former president mocked Trump for his meandering rallies and inability to coherently answer questions:\par \par \uc2 Have you seen Mr Trump lately? \u8230\'20\'26 He\u8217\'20\'19ll give two-and-a-half-hour speeches, just a word salad, you don\u8217\'20\'19t know what the heck he\u8217\'20\'19s saying. The other day he had a town hall meeting.. about 45 minutes into it, he says: \u8216\'20\'18You know what? I don\u8217\'20\'19t feel like taking questions no more,\u8217\'20\'19 and then he just played music for half an hour.\par \par \uc2 Praising \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , Obama took another swipe at Trump for his publicity stunt at a \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s:\par \par \uc2 This is a leader who has spent her life fighting on behalf of people who need a voice, need a champion \u8211\'20\'13 somebody who was raised in the middle class. She worked at \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s when she was in college to pay her expenses. She did not pretend to work at \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s when it was closed.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.03am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 : US is 'absolutely' ready for a female president\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said that she has no doubt the US is ready for a female president, insisting that Americans care more about what candidates can do to help them, rather than a presidential contender\u8217\'20\'19s gender.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s statement came during an interview with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/nbc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC}}}\uc2  News\u8217\'20\'19s Hallie Jackson, who asked whether she thought the country was ready for a woman, and a woman of color, to be in the Oval Office. \u8220\'20\'1CAbsolutely,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CAbsolutely.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn terms of every walk of life of our country,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, \u8220\'20\'1Cpart of what is important in this election is really, not really turning the page \u8211\'20\'13 closing a chapter, on an era that suggests that Americans are divided.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/kamala-harris-nbc-interview-female-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The US is \u8216\'20\'18absolutely\u8217\'20\'19 ready for a female president, Harris says in NBC interview}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Eminem rallies for \uc2 Kamala Harris\par \par \uc2 Rapper Eminem took the stage at the Detroit rally for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s important to use your voice, so I\u8217\'20\'19m encouraging everybody to get out and vote, please \u8230\'20\'26 I also think that people shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be afraid to express their opinions, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t think anyone wants an America where people are worried about retribution \u8230\'20\'26 if you make your opinion known.\par \par \uc2 Vice-President Harris supports a future for this country where these freedoms and many others will be protected and upheld.\par \par \uc2 Eminem then introduced \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , who started his speech by reciting Eminem lyrics.\par \par \uc2 enltrRapper Eminem introduces former President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  at a Detroit rally for Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SGURWEGAMw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SGURWEGAMw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MSNBC (@MSNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC/status/1848884149555192199?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 23, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.02am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump's former chief of staff says he's a 'fascist'\par \par \uc2 John Kelly\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former chief of staff, told the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  that he believes his former boss meets the definition of \u8220\'20\'1Cfascist\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: In an interview with \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  -- the audio of which we have published online --- former White House chief of staff \uc2 John Kelly\uc2  answers the question of whether he thinks Trump is a fascist. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/RrSdanoNKz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/RrSdanoNKz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Michael S. Schmidt (@nytmike) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nytmike/status/1848862618439848284?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Kelly, a retired Marine general who was Trump\u8217\'20\'19s longest-serving chief of staff, has publicly condemned the former president over his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/03/trump-john-kelly-chief-of-staff"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contempt for wounded and killed soldiers}}}\uc2 . In a new interview with the Times, Kelly was asked whether he considered Trump a fascist. Kelly responded:\par \par \uc2 Looking at the definition of fascism: It\u8217\'20\'19s a far-right authoritarian, ultranationalist political ideology and movement characterized by a dictatorial leader, centralized autocracy, militarism, forcible suppression of opposition, belief in a natural social hierarchy \u8230\'20\'26 Certainly, in my experience, those are the kinds of things that he thinks would work better in terms of running America.\par \par \uc2 Certainly the former president is in the far-right area, he\u8217\'20\'19s certainly an authoritarian, admires people who are dictators \u8211\'20\'13 he has said that. So he certainly falls into the general definition of fascist, for sure.\par \par \uc2 Kelly said Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cprefers the dictator approach to government\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Kelly also confirmed past reports that Trump privately made admiring comments about Hitler: \u8220\'20\'1CHe commented more than once that, \u8216\'20\'18You know, Hitler did some good things, too.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  rallies in North Carolina\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now speaking at a rally in North Carolina, mocking \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and other Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re close to a nuclear war, and we don\u8217\'20\'19t know who the hell is running our country,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president said, before an audience member shouted: \u8220\'20\'1CObama!\u8221\'20\'1D Trump continued: \u8220\'20\'1CObama, that\u8217\'20\'19s another beauty. Obama, he did great, didn\u8217\'20\'19t he? He did great, if you like a divided country. He was a great, he was fabulous. Obama, he was a real beauty. But under the Trump administration, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to take back what is ours.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 : 'We gotta lock him up... politically'\par \par \uc2 Speaking at a Democratic campaign office in New Hampshire, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  outlined the threat posed by a second \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  term :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe is talking about doing away with the entire Department of Education. He means it, this is not a joke. This is a guy who also wants to replace every civil servant, every single one, [who] thinks he has a version of the supreme court ruling on immunity to be able... to actually eliminate, physically eliminate, shoot, kill someone who is, he believes, to be the threat to him. I know this sounds bizarre. It sounds like, if I said this five years ago, you\u8217\'20\'19d lock me up. We got to lock him up \u8211\'20\'13 politically lock him up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The president paused after he echoed the \u8220\'20\'1Clock him up\u8221\'20\'1D chants of Trump critics, and then added \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitically\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden in NH lists what Trump would do as president and says: \u8220\'20\'1Cwe gotta lock him up\u8221\'20\'1D and then, appearing to realize how his comments would be taken, adds: \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitically, lock him up.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cw3X8RzKn2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cw3X8RzKn2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alex Thompson (@AlexThomp) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AlexThomp/status/1848846678138183726?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  supporters have shouted \u8220\'20\'1Clock him up\u8221\'20\'1D, she has generally not encouraged the chants and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AlexThomp/status/1848854010201313688"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said the courts will handle his criminal cases}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s the thing about that. The courts are going to take care of that,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/news/2024/10/what-kamala-harris-said-about-trump-when-crowd-chanted-lock-him-up.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  at a rally.\par \par \uc2 Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2024/06/07/biden-trump-case-connections-no-evidence/73983572007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 falsely claimed}}}\uc2  that Biden was behind his prosecution and conviction in his New York hush-money case and has repeatedly blamed Democrats for his various criminal cases.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  talks Trump pardon and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  in new interview\par \par \uc2 In her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/now/video/harris-full-interview-absolutely-the-country-is-ready-for-a-woman-president-222411845750"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC interview}}}\uc2 , Hallie Jackson asked \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  whether she would consider pardoning \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  if she were elected, citing the argument some have made that clemency would \u8220\'20\'1Chelp unify the country and move on\u8221\'20\'1D. The vice-president responded:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to get into those hypotheticals, I\u8217\'20\'19m focused on the next 14 days \u8230\'20\'26 Let me tell you what\u8217\'20\'19s gonna help us move on: I get elected president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 Harris also said the Democrats \u8220\'20\'1Chave the resources and the expertise\u8221\'20\'1D in the case of Trump trying to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/live/2024-election-trump-harris-news-updates#00000192-b642-dd3b-abfa-beeabfcb0000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subvert}}}\uc2  the election or declare early victory. She added:\par \par \uc2 This is a person, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who tried to undo the free and fair election, who still denies the will of the people, who incited a violent mob to attack the United States Capitol, and some 140 law enforcement officers were attacked. Some were killed. This is a very serious matter.\par \par \uc2 Asked about \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/tim-walz-elon-musk-trump-giveaway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pledge}}}\uc2  to give away $1m to random voters as he campaigns for Trump, Harris said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m not about doing gimmicks and all of that. I think that what we have to do, and what I\u8217\'20\'19m going to continue to do, is to be out in the communities.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 JD Vance campaigns in Arizona\par \par \uc2 Two weeks out from election day, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2  told supporters at a rally in swing state Arizona that they need to pull their friends to the polls because the race could go either way.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s the scenario that I want you to consider, and I don\u8217\'20\'19t mean to give you nightmare fuel here, but I\u8217\'20\'19m going to do it,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance said to the crowd in Peoria, Arizona. \u8220\'20\'1CWe wake up on November the sixth, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  is barely elected president of the United States by a 700-vote margin in the state of Arizona. Think about that. And ask yourself what you can do from now until then to make sure it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Vance visited Arizona on Tuesday, stopping in Peoria, part of the suburban metro around Phoenix, and is scheduled to stop in Tucson, in southern Arizona, later in the day. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  plans to rally in the state on Thursday. Democrats have a host of campaign surrogates, including former president \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  and current president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , on the schedule this week in the final stretch before 5 November.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/jd-vance-arizona-voters-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance urges Arizona crowd to \u8216\'20\'18work our rear ends off\u8217\'20\'19 to help Trump win}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to NBC: \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  'cannot be negotiable'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has done an interview with NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Hallie Jackson, as part of her ongoing media blitz. The interview is airing in full at 6.30 ET, but here are some initial highlights.\par \par \uc2 Jackson asked which concessions could be on the table on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as religious exemptions. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/atrupar/status/1848844260562399474"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris responded}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think we should be making concessions when we\u8217\'20\'19re talking about a fundamental freedom to make decisions about your own body.\u8221\'20\'1D She declined to entertain hypotheticals about possible compromises with Republicans, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CA basic freedom has been taken from the women of America, the freedom to make decisions about their own body. And that cannot be negotiable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris also said she is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/turning-page-harris-says-america-ready-black-female-president-rcna176329"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not concerned}}}\uc2  with sexism impacting the race:\par \par \uc2 My challenge is the challenge of making sure I can talk with and listen to as many voters as possible and earn their vote. And I will never assume that anyone in our country should elect a leader based on their gender or their race, instead that that leader needs to earn the vote based on substance.\par \par \uc2 Asked if the \u8220\'20\'1Ccountry is ready for a woman and a woman of color to be president\u8221\'20\'1D, Harris responded: \u8220\'20\'1CAbsolutely \u8230\'20\'26 Part of what is important in this election is really not only turning the page, but closing the page and the chapter on an era that suggests that Americans are divided.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 Scrutiny is growing about the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/montana"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Montana}}}\uc2  aerial firefighting company once led by Tim Sheehy, the former Navy Seal and Republican Senate candidate who could oust the Democrat incumbent \uc2 Jon Tester\uc2  in next month\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/senate-candidate-tim-sheehys-firm-promised-jobs-montana-county-s-still-rcna176439"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 According to NBC News}}}\uc2 , Sheehy\u8217\'20\'19s Bridger Aerospace, a company he founded in 2013, negotiated a deal with Gallatin county in eastern Montana to use its pristine credit rating to raise $160m in bonds. The county was meant to benefit from Bridger\u8217\'20\'19s plans to hire more workers and build two new aircraft hangers.\par \par \uc2 But the company used most of the money, or $134m, from the 2022 bond issue to pay back previous investment from \uc2 Blackstone\uc2 , a New York-based investment giant.\par \par \uc2 Bridger\u8217\'20\'19s finances have been complicated by the fact that there were fewer wildfires to fight this year and thus less revenue for Bridger. As of Tuesday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nifc.gov/fire-information/nfn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the National Interagency Fire Center}}}\uc2  reported 42,603 wildfires nationwide this year compared with the 10-year average of 48,689 for the same period.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/ix?doc=/Archives/edgar/data/1941536/000162828024036974/baer-20240630.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 financial filings}}}\uc2  for the quarterly period that ended 30 June 2024, Bridger said it had \u8220\'20\'1Ca substantial amount of debt\u8221\'20\'1D and that failure to service that debt \u8220\'20\'1Ccould prolong the substantial doubt about our ability to continue as a going concern\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A victory for Sheehy in November could hand {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans}}}\uc2  control of the Senate, making his connections to Bridger a vital topic as voters head to the polls.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/montana-tim-sheehy-business-scrutiny-senate-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Scrutiny of Republican Tim Sheehy\u8217\'20\'19s business grows amid US Senate race}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 Election day is exactly two weeks away, and today has been a frenzy of campaign activity.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Eminem{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/22/donald-trump-christian-voters-kamala-harris-election-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6717ce9b8f08deab319f3a09#block-6717ce9b8f08deab319f3a09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  will introduce Barack Obama when he appears in Detroit tonight, and Bruce Springsteen will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/22/donald-trump-christian-voters-kamala-harris-election-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6717d51e8f08deab319f3a7e#block-6717d51e8f08deab319f3a7e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 headline two concerts}}}\uc2  as part of a series that will hit every swing state.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Obama also campaigned with \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JD Vance dodged a question about whether he would strip immigrants with legal authorization of their status, at an event in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be in North Carolina, where Walz is holding a second event this evening.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump held a roundtable with Latino leaders but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/22/donald-trump-christian-voters-kamala-harris-election-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6717ca758f08da124b607758#block-6717ca758f08da124b607758"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took his time}}}\uc2  in getting to issues of importance to the voting bloc.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/22/donald-trump-christian-voters-kamala-harris-election-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6717af8f8f08da124b6075f3#block-6717af8f8f08da124b6075f3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will campaign}}}\uc2  in Houston on Friday, with an eye towards picking up Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat and highlighting how \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans have affected women in the Republican bastion.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US economy{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/22/donald-trump-christian-voters-kamala-harris-election-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6717abac8f08da124b6075cf#block-6717abac8f08da124b6075cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is poised}}}\uc2  for stronger growth than many wealthy nations, the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  said in forecasts released today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in New Hampshire, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  appeared alongside Vermont Senator Bernie Sanders to discuss his administration\u8217\'20\'19s work on lowering prescription drug prices.\par \par \uc2 But the president also took a chance to issue a warning that Trump and Vance were extreme. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not your father\u8217\'20\'19s Republican party,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said, referencing Strom Thurmond, the late senator from South Carolina who famously conducted the longest speaking filibuster in opposition to the Civil Rights Act of 1957. Thurmond later moderated his stance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople change, but these guys just keep getting worse,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said of the party now. \u8220\'20\'1CGet to the vote. Because the nation\u8217\'20\'19s democracy depends on it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He shared an embrace with Sanders.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 At an early voting pop-up location at the \uc2 University of Minnesota\uc2 , hundreds of students waited in line to cast ballots on Tuesday \u8211\'20\'13 a sign of youth enthusiasm for the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 The early voting location at the campus\u8217\'20\'19 Weisman Art Museum, a one-day on-campus polling place for any Minneapolis voter, was a first-time occasion made possible by recent changes in state law to allow for pop-up polling places to help voters who can be harder to reach, like college students.\par \par \uc2 enltrI\u8217\'20\'19m out at the \uc2 University of Minnesota\uc2  today for a pop-up early voting site - tons of traffic among students to cast a ballot {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7cnsPA4UFE"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/7cnsPA4UFE}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rachel Leingang (@rachelleingang) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rachelleingang/status/1848775530608566678?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe brought the polls to them,\u8221\'20\'1D said Riley Hetland, a sophomore and undergraduate student government civic engagement director who helped plan the event. Hetland said the group has been going to classrooms and hosting tables around campus for weeks to get people registered to vote and help them make a plan to cast ballots. So far, they have gotten 12,000 voters to pledge to vote, double their goal of 6,000.\par \par \uc2 Madelyn Ekstrand finished her class for the day and waited about an hour, all told, to cast her ballot. The 21-year-old senior said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and climate change were important to her, so she was voting for Harris. She thought she\u8217\'20\'19d vote early to get it done, but didn\u8217\'20\'19t realize how popular the choice would be \u8211\'20\'13 she was glad it was so busy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m happy to see people my age getting out and voting and being proactive and not waiting till the last second,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia's supreme court has rejected a Republican effort reinstate last-minute election rule changes\par \par \uc2 The ruling upholds another order by a Fulton county judge, who invalidated last-minute rules made by Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s state election board this year.\par \par \uc2 The rules, which were approved by Trump-aligned members of the board, would have required all ballots to be counted by hand on election night \u8211\'20\'13 a feat that would probably yield results that are far less accurate than a count done by ballot scanners. The changes would also have allowed officials investigate discrepancies in vote totals and conduct \u8220\'20\'1Creasonable inquiries\u8221\'20\'1D into irregularities, without clarifying what such an inquiry entailed.\par \par \uc2 The unanimous ruling by the conservative-majority supreme court did not touch on the legality of the seven rules \u8211\'20\'13 rather, it dismissed a request to hold a decision issued by a lower-court judge.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s an arresting split screen: \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , in Madison, tells voters that when Trump and Vance are pressed to elaborate on their policies, \u8220\'20\'1Cthey\u8217\'20\'19ll fall back on one answer: blame immigrants\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe wants you to believe that if you let him round up whoever he wants and ships them out, all your problems will be solved,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama says.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in Arizona, JD Vance dodges a question about whether he would strip immigrants of their legal status.\par \par \uc2 enltrJD Vance on Arizona doesn't directly answer a question about if supports stripping legal status from some migrants who are here legally and deporting them but it is pretty clear that he's fine with it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rhAdsb7mQy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rhAdsb7mQy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1848823030857793811?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Obama tells voters: 'Don't be nostalgic for Trump economy. It was mine'\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  is hitting on a key issue for voters: the economy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t have nostalgia for what his economy was. Because it was mine,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said.\par \par \uc2 Polls show voters tend to favor Trump on the economy, yearning for the time, early in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency, pre-pandemic, when housing and grocery costs were lower.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI spent eight years cleaning up the mess that Republicans left,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  has wrapped up his speech, after introducing \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Democratic former president apologized for being late, saying he had an issue with his plane that forced him to drive to Madison from Chicago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo we board the plane \u8230\'20\'26 and then the pilot comes in and says: \u8216\'20\'18Sir, there\u8217\'20\'19s a pile of oil leaking out of the back of the plane.\u8217\'20\'19 Now, I do not know anything about planes, except for the fact that it should not leak oil. So we had a nice road trip instead, and I am glad I made it,\u8221\'20\'1D Obama said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz warns that Trump could retaliate against him, if elected\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  encouraged the crowd not to grow sanguine about the possibility of a second Trump term, saying the Republican could retaliate against him if he returns to the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHere\u8217\'20\'19s another reason that the stakes are so high in this election, something that I don\u8217\'20\'19t think many of us have seen. You hear some version of this from the people in your life, neighbors, relatives, brothers, in some cases, who said, look, we made it through the first Trump term, we\u8217\'20\'19ll get through a second. This \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8230\'20\'26 is far more dangerous \u8230\'20\'26 He is not the 2016 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . This is a brand-new version,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said.\par \par \uc2 He elaborated on why he believes that:\par \par \uc2 As Kamala says, he is a very unserious person, but the consequences of putting him back in office are deadly serious. He\u8217\'20\'19s talking about sending the military against people who don\u8217\'20\'19t support him. He\u8217\'20\'19s naming names. Look, I recognize I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be at the top of that list. You think he\u8217\'20\'19s stopping with me? He\u8217\'20\'19s talking about you. He\u8217\'20\'19s talking about using the United States military to go after people who disagree with his idiotic ideas, his unpatriotic ideas, his traitorous ideas. And he\u8217\'20\'19s talking about using the military. He talks about the enemy from within.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Taking a page from Trump's book, Walz insults \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  with vulgarity\par \par \uc2 After \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  recently called \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/20/us-presidential-election-trump-harris-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shit vice-president}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  just used similar language to describe \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s enthusiastic campaigning for the former president.\par \par \uc2 Musk bounded on stage and briefly got airborne at a Trump rally in the Pennsylvania town where the former president nearly lost his life in an assassination attempt in July.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Walz had to say about that:\par \par \uc2 So look, Elon is on that stage, jumping around, skipping like a dipshit on these things. You know it. Think about it \u8230\'20\'26 that guy is literally the richest man in the world spending millions of dollars to help \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  buy an election.\par \par \uc2 Now, look, they\u8217\'20\'19re saying the quiet parts out loud now, because \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has already promised that he would put Elon in charge of government regulations that oversee the businesses that Elon runs.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s a hell of a buy. He could spend billions to make more than $10bn on the back end. So in other words, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in front of the eyes of the American public, is promising corruption. That\u8217\'20\'19s what he\u8217\'20\'19s promising you. And you know what? I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe, I don\u8217\'20\'19t believe he keeps many promises, but he\u8217\'20\'19ll keep that one.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz says Trump's McDonald's appearance nothing but a 'stunt'\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  then took \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to task for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global/video/2024/oct/21/donald-trump-makes-fries-during-staged-campaign-event-at-mcdonalds-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staged campaign event}}}\uc2  he held at a Pennsylvania McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s over the weekend, saying the appearance amounted to a \u8220\'20\'1Cstunt\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe went to a McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s and dressed up as the drive-thru worker. They found him an apron his size and put it on him. And I was thinking, it is possible he mixed up his weekends and thought that it was Halloween already. He\u8217\'20\'19s been forgetting things lately, as you might have noticed,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said.\par \par \uc2 Pressing the attack, the Minnesota governor continued:\par \par \uc2 That restaurant, that restaurant wasn\u8217\'20\'19t even open. It was a stunt \u8211\'20\'13 fake orders for fake customers. They even staged the drive thru. We know that they won\u8217\'20\'19t let you walk through the damn drive thru. We knew that. They saw that happening.\par \par \uc2 But look, everything about this guy is fake. Everything he does is fake. Next, he\u8217\'20\'19s going to be telling you he\u8217\'20\'19s a cop or a construction worker because {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/15/trump-dancing-pennsylvania-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he dances to the Village People}}}\uc2 , so he knows the YMCA. And I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you this: so that five minutes he stood next to the deep fryer, I\u8217\'20\'19ll guarantee you that\u8217\'20\'19s the hardest that guy\u8217\'20\'19s ever worked in his life. And that\u8217\'20\'19s not a joke.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz attacks Trump for saying no to second debate with Harris, saying he 'does not have stamina'\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  laid into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the meandering tone of his recent speeches and for declining to debate \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for a second time.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt takes stamina to run for president. It takes stamina to be president, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  does not have stamina,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz began. \u8220\'20\'1CHe has been rambling more than the normal rambling.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Noting that Trump has lately taken to describing his speaking style as \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/07/election-trump-speeches"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the weave}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, Walz said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe know there\u8217\'20\'19s only one weave that you know anything about, and it is not this. It is not this \u8230\'20\'26 He\u8217\'20\'19s ducks debates, but you can\u8217\'20\'19t blame him. When you get your ass whipped that hard, you don\u8217\'20\'19t come back for seconds.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 After the customary playing of Beyonc \u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s Freedom \u8211\'20\'13 the song used at just about every Harris campaign event \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  strolled on stage.\par \par \uc2 He shouted out all the Democrats who introduced him, as well as the rally attendees: \u8220\'20\'1CBut each of you, huge thank-you. Took time out of your busy lives, you came here, you came here because you believe in the promise of America and you believe in the democracy. Thank you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 Next up was \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2 , the state Democratic senator who is locked in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cookpolitical.com/senate/race/306306"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasingly tight}}}\uc2  re-election battle against Republican \uc2 Eric Hovde\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Like \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  before her on the lineup, Baldwin centered her appeal to voters on her support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and the Affordable Care Act.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust a little bragging here: I wrote the provision in the Affordable Care Act that allows young people to stay on their parents\u8217\'20\'19 health insurance until they turn 26 and I will never stop fighting until all Americans have the quality, affordable healthcare that they need and deserve,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 , one of the early speakers at the Walz-Obama rally in Madison, didn\u8217\'20\'19t hold back when describing what a second \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  presidency would mean.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know Trump and Vance will try to pass a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, roll back access to birth control, emergency contraception and even fertility treatments. We know that they\u8217\'20\'19re going to repeal the Affordable Care Act and deny coverage to folks like me and so many others here in the audience, and people you care about who have a pre-existing condition,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 The governor continued:\par \par \uc2 What Trump said about that \u8211\'20\'13 he\u8217\'20\'19s got the concept of a plan. Now you take that concept for a plan and go pay a bill, it ain\u8217\'20\'19t going to work. And they\u8217\'20\'19re going to give more tax breaks for the ultra-rich and the big corporations instead of helping working families get ahead. And we know that a second Trump term would mean unchecked power with no guardrails to hold them back. That\u8217\'20\'19s just bullshit.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Actor Bradley Whitford \u8211\'20\'13 you may remember him from The West Wing or the many movies and television shows he\u8217\'20\'19s appeared in since that series concluded \u8211\'20\'13 is giving a lengthy introduction for \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in his home town Madison, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMake sure five people who you may assume are with you, make sure they make a plan and make sure they vote,\u8221\'20\'1D Whitford told the crowd.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause I got news for you. If we spend the next two weeks knocking doors, manning phones, doing everything we can to get out every vote, with your help, we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna win. We\u8217\'20\'19re not, we\u8217\'20\'19re not, we\u8217\'20\'19re not moving back, we\u8217\'20\'19re not going back, we\u8217\'20\'19re moving forward. We\u8217\'20\'19re gonna win with your help. We\u8217\'20\'19re gonna hold this country up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Obama and Walz to hold joint rally in Wisconsin\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is soon to take the stage along with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in Madison, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the only joint appearance the two men will make today, though Obama will head to Detroit this evening, while Walz will hold a second event in Racine, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The rally comes as Obama steps up his campaigning for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , with the general election two weeks away. The vice-president is meanwhile in Washington DC, where she has taped interviews with NBC News and Noticias Telemundo that will air in the evening.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know what Walz and Obama have to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a small lead among likely voters in Georgia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/trump-has-a-slight-edge-in-georgia-over-harris-latest-ajc-poll-finds/LVP66TCGKJCF5CEDNUBAYU3EW4/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Atlanta Journal-Constitution reports in a new poll}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He leads \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  with 47% support to the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s 43%, just outside the survey\u8217\'20\'19s 3.1 percentage point margin of error.\par \par \uc2 However, all signs point to a race that remains either candidate\u8217\'20\'19s to win. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Journal-Constitution:\par \par \uc2 But with 8% of likely voters indicating they\u8217\'20\'19re still undecided, the race could break either way as early voting enters its second week.\par \par \uc2 Among the most telling takeaways of the poll is the stability of the race. As both campaigns pour time and treasure into Georgia, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s support remains {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/ajc-poll-finds-kamala-harris-and-donald-trump-are-locked-in-a-tight-race-in-georgia/C5CQ6742V5AHVIDUVQ77LQ7YMY/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 virtually unchanged }}}\uc2  since the AJC\u8217\'20\'19s last poll in September. Harris\u8217\'20\'19 dropped a fraction of a percentage point. The number of undecided voters has hardly budged.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a really close race. Neither side has this in the bag,\u8221\'20\'1D said University of Georgia political scientist Trey Hood, who oversaw the poll. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that makes the next two weeks even more important.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The poll suggests that Harris may still be struggling to woo Black voters, the bulwark of the Democratic coalition. About three-quarters of Black voters say they\u8217\'20\'19ll vote for her, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/election/2020/exit-polls/president/georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 far behind the 88% }}}\uc2  that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won in 2020 when he narrowly flipped Georgia.\par \par \uc2 That doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean those voters are gravitating toward Trump. One in 5 Black voters are undecided, while only 8% say they will cast their ballot for Trump. It indicates that Harris\u8217\'20\'19 campaign, which has stepped up efforts to bolster her Black support, should be more worried about apathy than losing those voters to the GOP.\par \par \uc2 In another sign of concern for Harris, 11% of Democrats say they\u8217\'20\'19re undecided. While few back third-party candidates \u8212\'20\'14 the Green Party\u8217\'20\'19s Jill Stein and others registered minimal support \u8212\'20\'14 the poll suggests she has more work to do to consolidate her base and little time to do so.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 CBS News reports that Republican former prosecutors have asked the justice department to investigate \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s effort to pay voters to cast ballots for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: Justice Dept confirms to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CBSNews?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @cbsnews}}}\uc2  that it has received inquiry from former federal prosecutors and GOP appointees to \u8220\'20\'1Crequest that (Justice Dept) review payments that are being made by the \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 -founded America PAC to voters in Pennsylvania and other states that\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Scott MacFarlane (@MacFarlaneNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MacFarlaneNews/status/1848711232573874240?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltrJustice Dept confirms receipt of the letter... but declines to comment further\par \par \uc2 The former GOP-appointed officials want a DOJ review of Musk's effort\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Scott MacFarlane (@MacFarlaneNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MacFarlaneNews/status/1848714427551338765?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor Josh Shapiro made a similar suggestion over the weekend:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/election-shapiro-musk-1-million-giveaway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania governor says law enforcement should investigate Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s $1m voter ploy}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s freewheeling, stream-of-consciousness style of delivering speeches doesn\u8217\'20\'19t always hit the mark. The latest example is the daughter of golf legend Arnold Palmer, who did not like the way the former president talked about her late father\u8217\'20\'19s penis, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/ramon-antonio-vargas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ramon Antonio Vargas}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/arnold-palmer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arnold Palmer}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s daughter says \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  disrespected her late father\u8217\'20\'19s memory by fawning over the size of the champion golfer\u8217\'20\'19s penis at a campaign rally over the weekend.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHackneyed anecdotes from the locker room \u8230\'20\'26 seemed disrespectful and inappropriate to me,\u8221\'20\'1D Peg Palmer Wears told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/arnold-palmers-daughter-calls-trumps-remarks-father-disrespectful/story?id=115008367"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ABC News}}}\uc2  on Monday, two days after the former president publicly suggested her father was well endowed.\par \par \uc2 Wears added that \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople coming to these rallies\u8221\'20\'1D hosted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2  as he seeks a second presidency \u8220\'20\'1Cdeserve substance about plans [he] has as a candidate\u8221\'20\'1D. She specifically called on him to address \u8220\'20\'1Csome of the threats he\u8217\'20\'19s made to people\u8221\'20\'1D, an apparent reference to how he recently suggested sending the US military against his political adversaries when voters go to the polls during the 5 November presidential election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are important issues that should be discussed for people when they\u8217\'20\'19re getting ready to vote, and using my dad to cover over the important things just seems unacceptable to me,\u8221\'20\'1D Wears said.\par \par \uc2 Trump was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/20/kamala-harris-campaigns-trump-arnold-palmer"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speaking}}}\uc2  to his supporters in Palmer\u8217\'20\'19s home town of Latrobe, Pennsylvania, on Saturday at a regional airport named after him when the former president suddenly invoked the genitals of the renowned golfer, an old acquaintance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CArnold Palmer was all man,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump remarked. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen he took showers with other pros, they came out of there \u8211\'20\'13 they said, \u8216\'20\'18Oh my God. That\u8217\'20\'19s unbelievable.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/donald-trump-rally-arnold-palmer-penis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump rebuked by Arnold Palmer\u8217\'20\'19s daughter for fawning over late golf legend\u8217\'20\'19s penis size}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  says Trump's McDonald's shift was 'making fun' of workers\par \par \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , a Democratic representative from New York, did not hold back in criticizing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s minutes-long stint as a fry cook at a Pennsylvania McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s on Sunday, saying he was \u8220\'20\'1Cmaking fun\u8221\'20\'1D of workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve got {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/people/donald-trump/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  putting on a little McDonald\u8217\'20\'19s costume because he thinks that\u8217\'20\'19s what people do,\u8221\'20\'1D she said Monday at a \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  event, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4946673-alexandria-ocasio-cortez-donald-trump-mcdonalds-visit/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 per the Hill}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re not trying to empathize with us. They are making fun of us.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  thinks that people who work at \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s are a joke.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump stopped by the fast-food restaurant for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global/video/2024/oct/21/donald-trump-makes-fries-during-staged-campaign-event-at-mcdonalds-video"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staged campaign event}}}\uc2  where employees showed him how to make fries. He then served pre-approved customers at the drive-through window.\par \par \uc2 Trump used the event to needle \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , whom he has claimed lied about her time working at \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s during college. Trump has made these claims without providing any evidence whatsoever.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Top Senate Democrats released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.klobuchar.senate.gov/public/_cache/files/5/c/5cd4e6b2-a0c1-47e7-8d34-d14fe16aeb76/FC36526E37BB5D613B0A3E03F4A7BEBDCFAF19161B90821B130259F0DFA0EC0E.2024.10.22-election-night-report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  today urging voters to cast their ballots as early as possible. The document also sought to answer questions about the election process.\par \par \uc2 The lawmakers \u8211\'20\'13 which include New York Senator \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , Vermont Senator Bernie Sanders and Minnesota Senator \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 reminded voters that the outcome might not be known on 5 November as different states have varying timelines for accepting and processing mail-in ballots.\par \par \uc2 Their document also emphasizes that voter intimidation, as well as violence, \u8220\'20\'1Cis never acceptable and any attempts to suppress the vote will not be tolerated\u8221\'20\'1D. The report notes that under federal law, \u8220\'20\'1Cit is illegal to intimidate, threaten, or coerce anyone in order to interfere with their right to vote\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn our democracy, every eligible citizen should be able to freely cast a ballot in the way that works best for them and should not face restrictions or barriers to voting,\u8221\'20\'1D the report says.\par \par \uc2 The document also appears to try addressing voters\u8217\'20\'19 concerns about whether votes were safe from interference, noting that officials from both political parties have \u8220\'20\'1Cconfirmed the security of recent elections\u8221\'20\'1D and that the infrastructure \u8220\'20\'1Chas never been more secure\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 These statements come as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who still makes the false claim that the 2020 election was stolen from him, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/fact-checking-trumps-false-claims-about-voter-fraud-and-rigged-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that election fraud is unfolding in this race. (There is no evidence of massive voter fraud, including alleged irregularities surrounding mail-in ballots or non-citizens casting votes.)\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere have been efforts to stoke fear and chaos about the election with false allegations of voter fraud,\u8221\'20\'1D the report said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people should beware of election misinformation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Election day is exactly two weeks away. Gulp. While there\u8217\'20\'19s no telling who is going to win, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/22/donald-trump-christian-voters-kamala-harris-election-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6717b7118f087dde7205e250#block-6717b7118f087dde7205e250"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News and CNN reported}}}\uc2  this morning that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign is bracing for a very close election that could potentially see the \u8220\'20\'1Cblue wall\u8221\'20\'1D swing states not vote as a bloc for the first time in decades. They are deploying a variety of surrogates on the campaign trail to make the case for the vice-president in the final two weeks, with Eminem {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/22/donald-trump-christian-voters-kamala-harris-election-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6717ce9b8f08deab319f3a09#block-6717ce9b8f08deab319f3a09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  set to introduce Barack Obama when he appears in Detroit tonight, and Bruce Springsteen to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/22/donald-trump-christian-voters-kamala-harris-election-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6717d51e8f08deab319f3a7e#block-6717d51e8f08deab319f3a7e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 headline two concerts}}}\uc2  as part of a series that will hit every swing state. Obama will also campaign with \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  in Wisconsin later today, JD Vance will hold two events in Arizona, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will campaign in North Carolina, and Walz will hold a second event in the Badger state before the evening is through.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump held a round table with Latino leaders but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/22/donald-trump-christian-voters-kamala-harris-election-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6717ca758f08da124b607758#block-6717ca758f08da124b607758"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took his time}}}\uc2  in getting to issues of importance to the voting bloc.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/22/donald-trump-christian-voters-kamala-harris-election-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6717af8f8f08da124b6075f3#block-6717af8f8f08da124b6075f3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will campaign}}}\uc2  in Houston on Friday, with an eye towards picking up Texas\u8217\'20\'19s Senate seat and highlighting how \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans have affected women in the Republican bastion.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US economy{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/22/donald-trump-christian-voters-kamala-harris-election-us-politics-latest-updates?page=with:block-6717abac8f08da124b6075cf#block-6717abac8f08da124b6075cf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is poised}}}\uc2  for stronger growth than many wealthy nations, the \uc2 IMF\uc2  said in forecasts released today.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bruce Springsteen to appear with Harris, Obama as campaign launches battleground state concert series\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign will hold concerts in the seven swing states, with legendary performer Bruce Springsteen to appear alongside the vice-president and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  on Thursday in Georgia, a senior campaign official said.\par \par \uc2 The Atlanta concert is the first of what the campaign is calling the When We Vote We Win series, and is aimed at whipping up voter enthusiasm ahead of 5 November. It will continue on Monday of next week in Philadelphia, when Springsteen and Obama will appear together, and concerts in the five other swing states will be announced soon, the official said.\par \par \uc2 Springsteen has backed Democrats before, and endorsed Harris earlier this month:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2024/oct/04/bruce-springsteen-endorses-kamala-harris-for-president-while-criticising-dangerous-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bruce Springsteen endorses Kamala Harris for president while criticising \u8216\'20\'18dangerous\u8217\'20\'19 Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s round table with Latino leaders in Doral, Miami, has just concluded. The audience livened a little as the former president turned his attention, briefly, to immigration.\par \par \uc2 He repeated baseless and often-aired claims that foreign countries, especially Venezuela, were opening their prisons to send \u8220\'20\'1Cviolent gang members\u8221\'20\'1D and drug dealers into the US with military weapons. He called \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ca stupid person\u8221\'20\'1D as he falsely labeled her \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cborder tsar\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His remarks segued quickly into an attack on Democrats for allegedly allowing transgender women to play women\u8217\'20\'19s sports and a somewhat fanciful tale of a \u8220\'20\'1Ca man who transitioned into, congratulations, a woman\u8221\'20\'1D smashing a baseball so hard it hit a female player on the head and \u8220\'20\'1Cthese young ladies said they\u8217\'20\'19d never seen anything like it\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps sensing things were going off topic, event host Jennifer Korn, a former White House aide and executive director of the Hispanic Leadership Network, attempted to interrupt with a \u8220\'20\'1CMr President \u8230\'20\'26 \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ll leave it at that,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CDoes anyone else have anything to say?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Robert Unanue\uc2 , the president of \uc2 Goya Foods\uc2 , the largest Hispanic-owned food company in the US, took the microphone for a lengthy speech praising Trump, then the event wound down with a prayer session.\par \par \uc2 Honduran televangelist Guillermo Maltonado, founder of Miami megachurch the King Jesus International Ministry, said Trump would be re-elected because \u8220\'20\'1Cthere\u8217\'20\'19s a higher assignment for him to finish with this nation\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 God sets up kings. We\u8217\'20\'19re praying for the will of God to make [Trump] the 47th president.\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This post was amended on 23 October 2024; an earlier version said \u8220\'20\'1Ctransgender men\u8221\'20\'1D instead of transgender women.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Eminem to introduce Obama at Detroit rally tonight \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Detroit\u8217\'20\'19s own Eminem will introduce \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  during his rally in support of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  this evening in Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s largest city, and likely weigh in on the presidential election, CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a rare public appearance by the rapper who has been synonymous with the Motor City throughout his career, and who has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2018/aug/31/eminem-donald-trump-surprise-album-kamikaze"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 occasionally condemned}}}\uc2  Harris\u8217\'20\'19s opponent, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The vice-president is not scheduled to attend the event, which begins at 7.45pm and is one of two appearances Obama is making for her campaign today. The former president is also rallying with \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  in Madison, Wisconsin, at 2.30pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hasn\u8217\'20\'19t yet turned his attention to issues affecting Latino voters at his round table in Miami.\par \par \uc2 Instead he\u8217\'20\'19s on a tear about the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s policies that encourage the use of electric vehicles:\par \par \uc2 They want to go to all-electric cars. A charging station is the equivalent of a gas pump \u8230\'20\'26 They spent $8b for nine charging stations. It\u8217\'20\'19s so out of control. They don\u8217\'20\'19t want to change.\par \par \uc2 He was referring to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.autoweek.com/news/a60702457/federal-funds-yield-only-8-ev-charging-stations/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 slow-moving $7.5bn federal program}}}\uc2  that by May had yielded a small number of charging stations, but has ramped since with more than 1,000 new installations nationwide each week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.transportation.gov/briefing-room/investing-america-number-publicly-available-electric-vehicle-chargers-has-doubled"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to government figures}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump is promising that if he is re-elected US businesses would continue to benefit from tax cuts he enacted in his first term:\par \par \uc2 We gave you the biggest cut in taxes in the history of the country. We have a great foundation to build on a lot of companies coming in very fast.\par \par \uc2 At one point Trump confused \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the vice-president and his Democratic opponent, with \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , whom he beat in 2016, calling the nonexistent Biden-Clinton administration \u8220\'20\'1Cthe worst ever\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is telling a roundtable of Latino leaders at his golf resort in Doral, Florida, that he expects Hispanic voters to help sweep him to victory on 5 November.\par \par \uc2 He claimed falsely that \u8220\'20\'1Call the polls\u8221\'20\'1D show him ahead among Hispanic voters in swing states, despite surveys showing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/latino/4944585-harris-leads-trump-battleground-latino-voters-poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exactly the opposite}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He kicked off the event by addressing the devastation caused by Hurricane Helene in North Carolina, where he was campaigning yesterday. It was a \u8220\'20\'1Chorrible event\u8221\'20\'1D he said, repeating debunked claims about the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s emergency response.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFema responded not well, the White House has done a poor job. They should be ashamed of themselves,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Numerous politicians, including some prominent Republicans, have praised the speed at which federal resources and help reached the hardest-hit areas.\par \par \uc2 Trump has yet to start answering questions, instead delivering a lengthy monologue with familiar attacks on \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , whom he beat in 2016.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the second time in a week that the former president has addressed Latino voters in Miami.\par \par \uc2 In a town hall hosted by Univision, the largest US Spanish-language network, on Thursday, Trump mostly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/17/donald-trump-miami-town-hall-migrants-eating-pets-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dodged awkward questions about immigration}}}\uc2 , and repeated debunked claims that Haitians in Springfield, Ohio, were eating pets and \u8220\'20\'1Cother things too that they\u8217\'20\'19re not supposed to\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, senator Ted Cruz\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has hit out at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  after it was announced she would visit Texas and appear alongside his opponent \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2  on Friday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Colin Allred\uc2  is \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . They have spent the last four years working hand-in-hand against Texans and the American people with their radical policies, whether those be pushing to allow boys in girls\u8217\'20\'19 sports, allowing dangerous illegal aliens to come into our country or trying to destroy the oil and gas industry in Texas,\u8221\'20\'1D a Cruz campaign spokesperson said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CColin and Kamala share an agenda, and now they\u8217\'20\'19ll share a stage for all Texans to see.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to meet with Latino leaders in Florida\par \par \uc2 The first campaign event of the day is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s round table with Latino leaders, which is scheduled to begin now at his golf resort in Doral, Florida.\par \par \uc2 Latinos are a voting bloc whose support is expected to be crucial to deciding the election, both in swing states and in states and congressional districts that will determine which party controls the Senate and House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the event, Miami\u8217\'20\'19s Trump-supporting Republican mayor, \uc2 Francis Suarez\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://video.snapstream.net/Play/7JNvB90DOPS4j96KGzJPEk?accessToken=bpu4l1t8bd12n"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told CNN in an interview}}}\uc2  that he does not believe the former president\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/17/donald-trump-miami-town-hall-migrants-eating-pets-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vows}}}\uc2  to carry out mass deportations and impose draconian policies against undocumented migrants will hurt his support with Hispanic voters:\par \par \uc2 Law-abiding Hispanics care more about having a prosperous future for themselves and their children than they do about people who are in this country illegally. And so I think there\u8217\'20\'19s a misperception that all they care about is, you know, immigration. And I think \u8230\'20\'26 that is, frankly, somewhat racist.\par \par \uc2 You know, I think Hispanics care more about making sure that they have an opportunity to succeed, making sure that inflation doesn\u8217\'20\'19t crush them every single day as it\u8217\'20\'19s done under this administration. And they\u8217\'20\'19re law-abiding people, like my parents are, who came to this country at 12 and seven from \u8211\'20\'13 from Cuba, which is a communist country and has \u8211\'20\'13 and has only produced misery and poverty for its people. And they see a lot of the same rhetoric being, unfortunately, espoused by the Democratic party and that\u8217\'20\'19s something that concerns them.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign reportedly bracing for tight election, fears 'blue wall' could crumble\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign expects \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to put up a strong performance in the 5 November presidential election that could break apart the \u8220\'20\'1Cblue wall\u8221\'20\'1D swing states for the first time in decades, according to two reports published this morning.\par \par \uc2 While neither story suggests that the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign does not think it has a path to victory, the reports underscore the potency of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s bid for office and the fact that the race remains essentially tied despite weeks of vigorous campaigning and fundraising by Harris and her surrogates.\par \par \uc2 Citing people with knowledge of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign strategy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/democrats-brace-crack-blue-wall-signs-north-carolina-slipping-rcna176046"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reports}}}\uc2  that they are concerned that the blue wall of Michigan, Wisconsin and Pennsylvania could, for the first time since 1988, not vote as a bloc in November, imperiling the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s path to the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 The campaign is also concerned that Hurricane Helene\u8217\'20\'19s ravages in North Carolina and the struggles of the controversial Republican candidates for governor are undermining Harris\u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning that state. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 Recent discussions have centered on the possibility of an anomaly happening this year with just part of the blue wall breaking its way. The conversations have focused on whether Michigan or Wisconsin \u8220\'20\'1Cfall\u8221\'20\'1D to former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  while the two other states go blue, according to three sources with knowledge of the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s strategy.\par \par \uc2 Losing Wisconsin or Michigan would mean that even if Harris secures Pennsylvania \u8211\'20\'13 where both Harris and Trump have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/trump-harris-pennsylvania-battleground-visits-map-rcna175691"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent the most time}}}\uc2  and resources \u8211\'20\'13 she would not reach the necessary 270 electoral votes to win the White House without winning another battleground state or possibly two.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere has been a thought that maybe Michigan or Wisconsin will fall off,\u8221\'20\'1D said a senior Harris campaign official, who stressed that the bigger concern is over Michigan. Two other people with knowledge of campaign strategy \u8211\'20\'13 who, like others in this article, were granted anonymity to speak candidly \u8211\'20\'13 also underscored deep concern about Michigan. Those people still believe that all the states are close and that there are alternative routes to victory.\par \par \uc2 A Harris campaign spokesperson pushed back against the notion about deep concerns over Michigan, pointing to recent public polling. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.detroitnews.com/story/news/politics/2024/10/07/kamala-harris-donald-trump-michigan-poll-slight-lead-presidential-race-white-house-rfk-kennedy/75552929007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Detroit News poll conducted 1-4 October}}}\uc2  found Harris, who was campaigning in Michigan on Monday, holding a slight lead in the state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/10/21/harris-trump-post-schar-school-poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as did a Washington Post poll on Monday}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 While North Carolina is still in the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s sights and Democrats maintain strong organization and leadership there, the Harris team is far less bullish about victory, four people with knowledge of the dynamics said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf all of the seven [states], that one seems to be a little bit slipping away,\u8221\'20\'1D the Harris campaign official said of North Carolina.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/22/politics/kamala-harris-campaign-final-weeks/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN}}}\uc2 , meanwhile, heard from top Harris adviser David Plouffe, who acknowledged that the race may very well remain tight right down to election day:\par \par \uc2 Historically, it would be unusual to have seven states come down to a point or less,\u8221\'20\'1D David Plouffe, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2008 campaign manager who now serves as a senior adviser to Harris, said of the battleground landscape. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I think at this point, you have to assume that\u8217\'20\'19s a distinct possibility.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Plouffe and other Harris advisers do not believe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/04/politics/trump-campaign-ground-game/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s largely outsourced}}}\uc2  door-knocking and other on-the-ground outreach operations can match what the national Democrats and the Harris campaign \u8211\'20\'13 which inherited some of the same team from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/politics/joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 President Joe Biden}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 spent a year putting together. But they believe this advantage can only take them so far.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDemocrats wish \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t get more than 46% of the vote,\u8221\'20\'1D Plouffe said, referring to the national popular vote percentage the former president secured in his previous campaigns. But in the battleground states, \u8220\'20\'1Cthat\u8217\'20\'19s not reality. He\u8217\'20\'19s going to get up to 48% in all of these states. And so we just have to make sure we\u8217\'20\'19re hitting our win number, which depending on the state, could be 50, could be 49.5.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign just announced that the vice-president will campaign in Philadelphia on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 The announcement was light on details, but needless to say it\u8217\'20\'19s difficult for Harris to win the White House without carrying Pennsylvania, and many Democratic voters live in and around Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to campaign in Texas with eye towards pulling off Senate surprise\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will return to Texas in the final days of the presidential campaign for an event that will highlight the stories of women harmed by the state\u8217\'20\'19s strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 In Houston on Friday, she will appear alongside the Democratic nominee for Senate, \uc2 Colin Allred\uc2 , who is locked in an unexpectedly tight race with the Republican incumbent, Ted Cruz.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have turned their attention to the Texas Senate race, despite a long history of falling short in the Republican-dominated state. With Democrats poised to lose a seat in West Virginia and Montana appearing to slip away, their best opportunity to keep control of the Senate may run through the Lone Star state.\par \par \uc2 According to a senior campaign official, Harris will travel to Texas from Georgia, two states with the most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in the country. The Democrat has repeatedly assailed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for appointing the three supreme court justices who voted to overturn Roe v Wade and paved the way for a wave of new restrictions and near-total bans in Republican-led states.\par \par \uc2 Harris has made \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights the centerpiece of her short campaign for the White House. At campaign stops, and the party\u8217\'20\'19s convention, she has shared the stories of women and families affected by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans, among them Texas resident Amanda Zurawski, who nearly died {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/20/trump-abortion-ban-zurawski-response"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after being denied}}}\uc2  an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the state\u8217\'20\'19s law.\par \par \uc2 Zurawski, along with the family of Amber Thurman, a Georgia woman who died after her medical care was delayed under the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, have become powerful surrogates for Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a central issue in the Texas Senate race. Allred has made Cruz\u8217\'20\'19s staunch anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  views a central plank of his campaign. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/senate/2024/texas/general/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Polls}}}\uc2  show Cruz with a steady lead, though the race has appeared to tighten in recent weeks.\par \par \uc2 While in Houston, Harris will also sit for an interview with academic turned Ted talks host and popular podcaster Bren\u233\'00\'E9 Brown.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/03/ted-cruz-texas-senate-election-abortion-record"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How Ted Cruz\u8217\'20\'19s \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  record could cost him a historic election in Texas}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Despite campaign rhetoric, \uc2 IMF\uc2  projections show US economy better than most\par \par \uc2 On the campaign trail, you\u8217\'20\'19ll hear \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/15/trump-tariffs-price-hikes-warnings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assail the state of the economy}}}\uc2  and say \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is to blame. And you\u8217\'20\'19ll hear Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/25/harris-opportunity-economic-plan-middle-class"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vow to lower prices}}}\uc2  for everything from housing to healthcare.\par \par \uc2 There is no doubt that Americans have suffered from the wave of inflation that racked the country over the past three years, but has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/10/september-inflation-declines"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recently subsided}}}\uc2 . What\u8217\'20\'19s less discussed is that the US economy is, in fact, far healthier than many others.\par \par \uc2 Just-released forecasts from the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , the Washington-based crisis lender whose economic data is closely watched from Wall Street to the White House, shows that the US economy is poised for some of the strongest growth among wealthy nations in the years to come, beating out the United Kingdom, Japan and many European nations:\par \par \uc2 enltrIMF Growth Forecast: 2024\par \par \uc2 ????US: 2.8%\par \par \uc2 ????Germany: 0.0%\par \par \uc2 ????France: 1.1%\par \par \uc2 ????Italy: 0.7%\par \par \uc2 ????Spain: 2.9%\par \par \uc2 ????UK: 1.1%\par \par \uc2 ????Japan: 0.3%\par \par \uc2 ????Canada: 1.3%\par \par \uc2 ????China: 4.8%\par \par \uc2 ????India: 7.0%\par \par \uc2 ????Russia: 3.6%\par \par \uc2 ????Brazil: 3.0%\par \par \uc2 ???? Mexico: 1.5%\par \par \uc2 ????KSA: 1.5%\par \par \uc2 ????Nigeria: 2.9%\par \par \uc2 ????\uc2 RSA\uc2 : 1.1% {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/sDv9tK6YQb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/sDv9tK6YQb}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/epCi3VT13o"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/epCi3VT13o}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 IMF\uc2  (@IMFNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IMFNews/status/1848711419002556747?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 22, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 These are, of course, just projections, and as the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/22/imf-upbeat-global-growth-dangers-lurk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Larry Elliott}}}\uc2  reports, various things could undercut them \u8211\'20\'13 including some of the policies Trump is campaigning on:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/22/imf-upbeat-global-growth-dangers-lurk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  While the IMF is upbeat about global growth it knows where dangers lurk}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lauren-gambino"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lauren Gambino}}}\uc2  earlier this month took the political pulse of young voters nationwide, particularly when it came to the question of which presidential candidate to support. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what she found:\par \par \uc2 It was the height of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/07/22/kamala-harris-campaign-coconut-memes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brat summer}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/style/story/kamala-harris-chappell-roan-femininomenon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 femininomenon}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, electrifying a high-stakes presidential race that many of the country\u8217\'20\'19s youngest voters had been dreading: a rematch between the two oldest candidates in American history.\par \par \uc2 Chartreuse-blocked memes and coconut emojis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/25/kamala-harris-tiktok-memes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filled}}}\uc2  social media feeds. The tidal wave of young \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/27/kamala-harris-young-voters-israel-gaza-jayapal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamalove}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D sparked a rush of small-dollar donations and volunteer sign-ups for her days-old campaign. For an extremely online generation of young Democrats, the vibes were so good.\par \par \uc2 On the ground in St Louis, a cadre of young progressives were gathering for an entirely different election \u8211\'20\'13 one with virtually no bearing on the balance of power in Washington, but one they believed mattered deeply. There in Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s first congressional district, representative \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  was fighting for her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/03/cori-bush-wesley-bell-missouri-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 political survival}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many of the twentysomethings had traveled from out of state, sacrificing summer jobs and sleeping on yoga mats to campaign for Bush in the sticky August heat. \u8220\'20\'1CWe just stopped our lives and went to St Louis,\u8221\'20\'1D said John Paul Mejia, a 22-year-old student and climate activist.\par \par \uc2 Mejia was there as part of Protect Our Power (Pop), a youth coalition that came together earlier this year for what he described as a \u8220\'20\'1CDavid-and-Goliath\u8221\'20\'1D mission to defend leftwing members of Congress against a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/20/pro-israel-groups-gaza-us-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 well-funded effort}}}\uc2  to unseat them.\par \par \uc2 To them, Bush, the nurse turned racial justice activist, was one of the few elected leaders who shared their sense of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/29/cori-bush-interview-midterms-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urgency}}}\uc2  about everything from the country\u8217\'20\'19s affordability crisis to safeguarding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 As a newly elected member of Congress, Bush had slept on the steps of the US Capitol to protest against the expiration of a federal eviction moratorium. The action paid off: the Biden administration extended the pause. In warning about the threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bush {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/cspan/status/1443592081218277381?lang=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 testified}}}\uc2  before a House panel that she had had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 18 after becoming pregnant by rape. In 2023, she emerged as one of the strongest critics of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza, a stance that reflected a groundswell of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/10/05/gen-z-israel-pro-palestinian-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 youth dissent}}}\uc2  but ultimately imperiled her congressional career.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s pretty much nobody else, even members of Congress who are closer to our age, in some instances, who actually represent what our generation cares about,\u8221\'20\'1D Vincent Vertuccio, a 21-year-old college student and an activist with Pop, said of the progressive Squad members. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we lose these people, even one or two, it\u8217\'20\'19s a direct diminishment of our power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/12/gen-z-kamala-harris-youth-vote-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gen Z and Kamala Harris: is the meet-cute enough to bring her to the White House?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris matching Biden's 2020 margin with young voters as support grows \u8211\'20\'13 poll\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has a significant advantage over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  among young voters, matching the lead \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ended up taking in the 2020 election, a new poll finds.\par \par \uc2 The survey from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2024/10/22/harris-trump-young-voters-cnbc-generation-lab-election.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNBC Generation Lab}}}\uc2  shows Harris up 20 percentage points with voters aged 18 to 34, with 60% support compared with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 40%. That\u8217\'20\'19s about the same margin by which Biden won the group four years ago.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s also an improvement from July, when the vice-president was at 46%, Trump at 34% and independent candidate \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr\uc2  picking up 21%. Kennedy has since dropped out of the race and endorsed Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll see \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  around 11am, when he holds a round table with Latino leaders at his golf resort in Doral, Florida.\par \par \uc2 Then he\u8217\'20\'19ll head to battleground state of North Carolina for a rally in Greensboro at 7pm, making his second visit to the state in as many days.\par \par \uc2 His running mate, JD Vance, will be in Arizona, campaigning in Peoria, outside Phoenix, at 4pm, then again in Tucson at 7.30pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Obama, Walz to stump for Harris in swing states\par \par \uc2 Democrats are deploying one of their best-known figures as they seek an edge against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the final weeks of the campaign, with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  holding two events today in swing states \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign covets most.\par \par \uc2 The former president will at 2.30pm appear in Madison, Wisconsin, alongside \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , then hold a solo event in Detroit at 7.45pm. Walz will stay in Wisconsin, where he has an event in Racine at 7.30pm.\par \par \uc2 The pair\u8217\'20\'19s visit to Wisconsin is to mark the start of early voting in the state, one of three in the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1Cblue wall\u8221\'20\'1D along the Great Lakes that are crucial to Harris\u8217\'20\'19s White House hopes.\par \par \uc2 Expect to see a lot more of both Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  before this election is through:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/18/election-michelle-barack-obama-harris-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Obamas to bring star power to campaign appearances alongside Kamala Harris}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 After a busy day of campaigning with \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  on Monday, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is having a comparably quiet one today.\par \par \uc2 She has no public campaign events scheduled, but will sit for two interviews. The first is with NBC News\u8217\'20\'19s Hallie Jackson and will air at 6.30pm ET, and the second with Noticias Telemundo\u8217\'20\'19s Julio Vaqueiro, which will be broadcast at 7pm.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president has been doing a lot more interviews and media appearances lately as the election enters the home stretch. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/19/kamala-harris-trump-voters-media-blitz-call-her-daddy-fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From Fox News to Call Her Daddy: how Kamala Harris turned up election heat in pivot to media blitz }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Thomas Klingenstein, chairperson of the rightwing Claremont Institute, has cemented his place in the pantheon of Republican megadonors with a more than $10m spending spree so far in the 2024 election cycle, according to campaign contributions recorded by the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2  (\uc2 FEC\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 Klingenstein has been one of Claremont\u8217\'20\'19s largest donors for decades. As the institute has made its hard-right, pro-Trump drift in recent years, Klingenstein has continued to publicly describe US politics with extremist rhetoric, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Ccold civil war\u8221\'20\'1D, and has encouraged rightwingers to join the fight to defeat what he calls \u8220\'20\'1Cthe woke regime\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 His spending puts him at the forefront of a class of donors who are explicitly supporting more extreme and polarizing politics in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Republican party.\par \par \uc2 The largesse has already dwarfed his contributions in previous election seasons. The money has gone exclusively to Republicans, and has included seven-figure donations to at least four pro-Trump Pacs in recent months.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  emailed Klingenstein for comment on this reporting but received no reply.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/thomas-klingenstein-megadonor-pro-trump-pac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The far-right megadonor pouring over $10m into the US election to defeat \u8216\'20\'18the woke regime\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the second year of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, a young lawyer with crisply shorn blond hair approached the podium at a gathering for Texas members of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f-_5bPKuIRg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federalist Society}}}\uc2 , a conservative legal group that wields immense power in the US judicial system. As vice-president of the group\u8217\'20\'19s Fort Worth chapter, Matthew Kacsmaryk had the honor of presenting the first speaker.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are blessed to have Judge Edith Jones,\u8221\'20\'1D Kacsmaryk announced. Jones, a longtime judge on the US fifth circuit court of appeals, stepped on stage to introduce the evening\u8217\'20\'19s guest, her friend, the supreme court justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2 . In her introduction, Jones also hailed the four new conservative judges Trump had appointed to join her on the appeals court.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve raised the bar for the fifth circuit since I got on,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd that\u8217\'20\'19s thanks to the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2 , to Leonard.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Leonard Leo\uc2  needed no last name in his introduction to this crowd as he took his seat in a black leather chair across from Thomas. The justice was the featured speaker but Leo may have been the most important person in the American legal system in that room \u8211\'20\'13 a conservative activist who had built the \uc2 Federalist Society\uc2  into a political powerhouse and helped Trump create the supreme court majority that, in 2022, erased federal protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 His influence continues to be on display now in one of the most consequential cases moving through the American legal system \u8211\'20\'13 one that seeks to strike another blow to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and could possibly bankrupt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/planned-parenthood"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood}}}\uc2 , one of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s leading providers of healthcare for women. It\u8217\'20\'19s a lawsuit that has been filed by an anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activist tied to Leo and heard by judges \u8211\'20\'13 from the lower courts to the fifth circuit appeals court \u8211\'20\'13 who are also linked to Leo.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/22/maga-courts-planned-parenthood-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Maga legal networks that could topple Planned Parenthood and gut women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Dustin Guastella, research associate at the Center for Working-Class Politics and the director of operations for Teamsters Local 623, writes:\par \par \uc2 The 2024 campaign has entered the final stretch and, as polls tighten, it seems \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  plans to lean into attacking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as a threat to democracy.\par \par \uc2 Over the past week the Wall Street Journal, the Associated Press, the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2 , the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  and even the conservative National Review have all reported or commented on the messaging pivot. In a newly unveiled official campaign ad, a disembodied voice warns gravely that a second Trump term \u8220\'20\'1Cwould be worse. There would be no one to stop his worst instincts. No guard rails.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At a recent rally in Erie, Pennsylvania, Harris reminded her supporters of Project 2025, the \u8220\'20\'1Cdetailed and dangerous plan\u8221\'20\'1D that she believes an \u8220\'20\'1Cincreasingly unstable and unhinged\u8221\'20\'1D Trump will follow to cement \u8220\'20\'1Cunchecked power\u8221\'20\'1D. She sounded the alarm about the dire threat Trump poses to \u8220\'20\'1Cyour fundamental freedoms\u8221\'20\'1D and how in his second term he would be \u8220\'20\'1Cessentially immune\u8221\'20\'1D from oversight.\par \par \uc2 This is hair-raising stuff. And the campaign thinks that menacing warnings like these will motivate some urgency to march to the polls for Harris. The only problem is that voters, especially working-class voters, seem uniquely uninspired by the appeal.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/22/harris-working-class-voters-poll-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 To win, Harris should talk more about working-class needs and less about Trump | Dustin Guastella}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Democratic US vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  held a marginal 46% to 43% lead over Republican former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , with a glum electorate saying the country is on the wrong track, a new Reuters/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll found.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19 lead in the six-day poll, which closed on Monday, differed little from her 45% to 42% advantage over Trump in a Reuters/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll conducted a week earlier, reinforcing the view that the contest is extraordinarily tight with just two weeks left before the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reported:\par \par \uc2 Both polls showed Harris with a lead within the margin of error, with the latest poll showing her ahead just 2 percentage points when using unrounded figures.\par \par \uc2 The new poll showed that voters have a dim view of the state of the economy and immigration \u8211\'20\'13 and they generally favour Trump\u8217\'20\'19s approach on these issues.\par \par \uc2 Some 70% of registered voters in the poll said their cost of living was on the wrong track, while 60% said the economy was heading in the wrong direction and 65% said the same of immigration policy.\par \par \uc2 Voters also said the economy and immigration, together with threats to democracy, were the country\u8217\'20\'19s most important problems. Asked which candidate had the better approach on the issues, Trump led on the economy \u8211\'20\'13 46% to 38% \u8211\'20\'13 and on immigration by 48% to 35%.\par \par \uc2 Immigration also ranked as the number one issue when respondents were asked what the next president should focus on most in their first 100 days in office. Some 35% picked immigration, with 11% citing income inequality and equal 10% shares citing healthcare and taxes.\par \par \uc2 But Trump fared poorly on the question of which candidate was better to address political extremism and threats to democracy, with Harris leading 42% to 35%. She also led on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and on healthcare policy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , a former Republican congresswoman and longtime opponent of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, on Monday condemned Republican-imposed bans on the procedure and urged conservatives to support Democrat \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for US president.\par \par \uc2 Cheney was speaking during three joint events with the vice-president in three swing states aimed at prising suburban Republican voters away from party nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . She has become the Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s most prominent conservative surrogate and is rumoured to be in contention for a seat in a potential Harris cabinet.\par \par \uc2 At the final event in Waukesha, Wisconsin, against a blue backdrop patterned with the words \u8220\'20\'1Ccountry over party\u8221\'20\'1D, Cheney, 58, suggested that Republican-led states have overreached in restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 2022 Dobbs decision ended it as a constitutional right.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pro-life and I have been very troubled, deeply troubled by what I have watched happen in so many states since Dobbs,\u8221\'20\'1D said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/16/wyoming-republican-primary-liz-cheney-donald-trump-harriet-hageman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  former Wyoming congresswoman}}}\uc2  and daughter of former vice-president \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI have been troubled by the extent to which you have women who \u8211\'20\'13 as the vice-president said, in some cases have died \u8211\'20\'13 who can\u8217\'20\'19t get medical treatment that they need because providers are worried about criminal liability.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/liz-cheney-kamala-harris-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Liz Cheney urges conservatives to back Kamala Harris over \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Opening summary\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to the US politics live blog. I\u8217\'20\'19m Tom Ambrose and I\u8217\'20\'19ll be bringing you all the latest from the campaign trail, with polling day now just two weeks away.\par \par \uc2 We start with the news that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has urged Christian voters on Monday to participate in the 2024 election, claiming that a \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  administration would restrict religious freedoms and casting himself as a protector of Christians.\par \par \uc2 During an event in North Carolina billed as an \u8220\'20\'1C11th-Hour Faith Leaders Meeting\u8221\'20\'1D, a series of conservative pastors warmed up for Trump, including Guillermo Maldonado, an \u8220\'20\'1Capostle\u8221\'20\'1D and longtime Trump ally who cast the election in perilous terms.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, we\u8217\'20\'19re now in spiritual warfare,\u8221\'20\'1D said Maldonado, alluding to the idea that Christians are at war on the supernatural plane against dark forces that affect the real world. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s beyond warfare between the left and the right. It\u8217\'20\'19s between good and evil. There\u8217\'20\'19s a big fight right now that is affecting our country and we need to take back our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Introducing Trump, Ben Carson, the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s National Faith Chairman for the 2024 election, openly rejected the idea of secular society.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis election is about whether we are a secular nation or one nation under God,\u8221\'20\'1D said Carson, echoing the aims of Christian nationalists who view the US as a Christian nation that must return to God.\par \par \uc2 In other news:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , former Republican congresswoman and longtime opponent of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, condemned Republican bans on the procedure and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/liz-cheney-kamala-harris-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged conservatives on Monday}}}\uc2  to support \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden acknowledged on Monday that her husband {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/jill-joe-biden-dropping-out"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made \u8220\'20\'1Cthe right call\u8221\'20\'1D by stepping down}}}\uc2  from his run for re-election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Democratic vice-presidential candidate, said \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/tim-walz-elon-musk-trump-giveaway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plan to give away $1m a day}}}\uc2  in support of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a reflection of a ticket with \u8220\'20\'1Cno plan\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Central Park Five{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/central-park-five-trump-defamation-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued Trump for defamation}}}\uc2  after he falsely said during the presidential debate that they had pleaded guilty to a brutal rape 35 years ago, despite the fact that they had their convictions overturned.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Republican county supervisor in Arizona who refused to certify the 2022 midterm election has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/peggy-judd-pleads-guilty-arizona-election-denier"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded guilty to a misdemeanor}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The politics writer Olivia Nuzzi and New York magazine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/olivia-nuzzi-leaves-new-york-magazine-rfk-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have parted ways}}}\uc2  after she was placed on leave following the disclosure that she had engaged in a \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonal\u8221\'20\'1D relationship with \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Key rightwing legal groups tied to Trump and his allies have banked millions of dollars from conservative foundations and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/trump-maga-swing-states-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed multiple lawsuits challenging voting rules in swing states}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump doubled down on false claims about the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s hurricane recovery efforts and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/trump-visit-north-carolina-hurricane-conspiracy-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promoted baseless conspiracy theories}}}\uc2  about immigration.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241022ekam001gu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
