\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  questions Trump\u8217\'20\'19s stamina: \u8216\'20\'18Is he fit to do the job?\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Ethan Meyers in Grand Rapids, Michigan \par \uc2 765 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 October 2024\par 10:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democratic nominee suggests at Michigan rally that rival does not have stamina to handle another presidential term\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  used a rally in Grand Rapids, Michigan, on Friday to seize on reports that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had been canceling media interviews to question whether he has the stamina for a second presidency if voters choose him over her in November\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf he can\u8217\'20\'19t handle the rigors of the campaign trail, is he fit to do the job?\u8221\'20\'1D the Democratic vice-president, 59, told rallygoers about the 78-year-old {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She said: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump is unfit for office.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris and her Republican opponent were in Michigan as the weekend began while trying to shore up support in a battleground state that could decide their 5 November race. Polling suggests Michigan as well as its fellow \u8220\'20\'1Cblue wall\u8221\'20\'1D states of Pennsylvania and Wisconsin remain in play for both candidates as the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s waning days arrive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the place that is going to decide the election, right here,\u8221\'20\'1D Democratic representative Hillary Scholten told Friday\u8217\'20\'19s audience as she opened the event.\par \par \uc2 Among the crowd, some Harris supporters struck a hopeful tone. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s about time for a woman to lead,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jenifer Lake, who took her daughter Adeline Butts to the rally for a chance to \u8220\'20\'1Csee history in the making\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Butts, who will be old enough to vote for the first time this election, described herself as mostly concerned about the cost of living, tuition and housing affordability. Her fellow attendee Bill Bray, who came to the rally from Adrian, Michigan, said he believed Harris would better promote economic opportunity for those situated like him than Trump would.\par \par \uc2 Bray grew up \u8220\'20\'1Cin a poor neighborhood\u8221\'20\'1D but said he is doing well thanks to benefits from his prior military service as well as his long career at \uc2 Ford Motor Company\uc2 . He said he wants other people to have a chance at that same trajectory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump doesn\u8217\'20\'19t understand equality,\u8221\'20\'1D said Bray, a veteran of the Vietnam war who also accused the former president of dodging the military draft that would have sent him to the same conflict.\par \par \uc2 Bray also said he supports stronger federal gun control after seeing \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat guns do to people\u8221\'20\'1D and has no faith in Trump \u8211\'20\'13 who is widely supported by the firearms industry \u8211\'20\'13 taking that issue seriously.\par \par \uc2 Other attendees said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access was at the top of their mind. Harris has campaigned on preserving \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access while three of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appointees to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  helped eliminate federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in 2022.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19d be nice to have control of my body back, and then I\u8217\'20\'19ll think about listening to the other side,\u8221\'20\'1D Kim Osborn said.\par \par \uc2 Lauren Rockel said she would like to see Harris fight to reinstate the Roe v Wade protections that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court appointees helped strip away.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are people dying\u8221\'20\'1D as a result of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions that have since gone into effect in many states, Rockel said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s awful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 To them, Harris said it was \u8220\'20\'1Ctime to turn the page\u8221\'20\'1D on Trump.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/13/gretchen-whitmer-doritos-chip"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer}}}\uc2 , the Democratic governor of Michigan, spoke before Harris took the stage. Four other Democratic state governors joined her.\par \par \uc2 Her presence and that of the other governors \u8220\'20\'1Cshows how important you are, Michigan\u8221\'20\'1D, Whitmer said. She told the crowd that they would be the ones to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake our country forward\u8221\'20\'1D if they helped send Harris to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic US senator \uc2 Debbie Stabenow\uc2  also spoke before Harris, alluding to how it got \u8220\'20\'1Cscarier and scarier\u8221\'20\'1D the more she thought about the proposed policies of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters. The former president has sought to distance himself from the far-right Heritage Foundation, whose Project 2025 plan calls for the mass firings of civil servants and exalts the idea of outlawing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  altogether during a second Trump presidency.\par \par \uc2 But he has struggled to effectively do that, with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jd-vance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 JD Vance}}}\uc2 , having written the foreword for a book by \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s president. And, echoing Stabenow, many attenders said they were fearful of what a return to the Oval Office for Trump may produce.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic nominee\u8217\'20\'19s message resonated with Richard Bandstra, who described himself as a \u8220\'20\'1Cformer Republican\u8221\'20\'1D. Bandstra said he came to the rally to hear a message of hope \u8211\'20\'13 and, as he saw it, to fight for what he called the most important issue of the race: preserving American democracy.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241022ekam002k4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
