\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  urges conservatives to back \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  over  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 David Smith in Washington \par \uc2 1,516 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 October 2024\par 15:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 26\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ex-Republican congresswoman, longtime \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights opponent, campaigns with vice-president in swing statesUS politics \u8211\'20\'13 live updates\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , a former Republican congresswoman and longtime opponent of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, on Monday condemned Republican-imposed bans on the procedure and urged conservatives to support the Democrat \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  for US president.\par \par \uc2 Cheney was speaking during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?539381-1/vice-president-harris-campaigns-liz-cheney-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three joint events}}}\uc2  with the vice-president in three swing states aimed at prising suburban Republican voters away from the party nominee, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . She has become the Democrat\u8217\'20\'19s most prominent conservative surrogate and is rumoured to be in contention for a seat in a potential Harris cabinet.\par \par \uc2 At the final event in Waukesha, Wisconsin, against a blue backdrop patterned with the words \u8220\'20\'1Ccountry over party\u8221\'20\'1D, Cheney, 58, suggested that Republican-led states had overreached in restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s 2022 Dobbs decision ended it as a constitutional right.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m pro-life and I have been very troubled, deeply troubled by what I have watched happen in so many states since Dobbs,\u8221\'20\'1D said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/16/wyoming-republican-primary-liz-cheney-donald-trump-harriet-hageman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  former Wyoming congresswoman}}}\uc2  and daughter of the former vice-president \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI have been troubled by the extent to which you have women who \u8211\'20\'13 as the vice-president said, in some cases have died \u8211\'20\'13 who can\u8217\'20\'19t get medical treatment that they need because providers are worried about criminal liability.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The current situation is \u8220\'20\'1Cuntenable\u8221\'20\'1D, Cheney said, and America needs a president \u8220\'20\'1Cwho understands how important compassion is, who understands that these shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be political issues, that we ought to be able to have these discussions and say, \u8216\'20\'18You know what? Even if you are pro-life, as I am, I do not believe, for example, that the state of Texas ought to have the right, as they\u8217\'20\'19re currently suing to do, to get access to women\u8217\'20\'19s medical records.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are some very fundamental and fundamentally dangerous things that have happened and so I think that it\u8217\'20\'19s crucially important for us to find ways to have the federal government play a role and protect women from some of the worst harms that we\u8217\'20\'19re seeing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cheney went on to draw a contrast with Trump, who as president appointed three supreme court justices instrumental in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/may/10/divided-america-roe-v-wade-supreme-court-cold-civil-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturning the 1973 Roe v Wade precedent}}}\uc2  and whose rhetoric continues to alienate many suburban women. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at one point called for criminal penalties for women,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s been now trying to sort of be all over the place on this issue, although he expresses great pride for what\u8217\'20\'19s happened and I think the bottom line on this, as on so many other issues, is you just can\u8217\'20\'19t count on him. You cannot trust him. We\u8217\'20\'19ve seen the man that he is. We\u8217\'20\'19ve seen the cruelty and America deserves much better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The remarks echoed comments that Cheney made earlier in the day in Malvern, a suburb of Philadelphia in Pennsylvania, in a striking effort to build a permission structure for conservatives to back Harris, who has made reproductive freedom {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/19/harris-abortion-rights-early-voting-atlanta"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a centrepiece of her campaign}}}\uc2 . Cheney, by contrast, has an A rating from Susan B Anthony Pro-Life America, a group that grades members of Congress based on their anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  credentials.\par \par \uc2 Monday\u8217\'20\'19s three events in Pennsylvania, Michigan and Wisconsin, a show of unity designed to cast Trump as a threat to the constitution, were held in counties won by \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  in the Republican presidential primary. Haley, a former South Carolina governor and US ambassador to the United Nations, had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/01/23/haley-abortion-new-hampshire/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sought to neutralise \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  as an election issue by supporting states\u8217\'20\'19 autonomy and rejecting calls for a national ban.\par \par \uc2 Cheney has vocally opposed Trump since the January 6 insurrection at the US Capitol. Her recent endorsement of Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.newsweek.com/liz-cheney-responds-kamala-harris-cabinet-rumor-1955664"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fuelled speculation}}}\uc2  that she could play a part in a future Harris administration.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss important US election coverage. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.apple.com/us/app/the-guardian-live-world-news/id409128287?mt=8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Get our free app}}}\uc2  and sign up for election alerts\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, appearing on the popular {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/13/kamala-harris-shortest-presidential-campaign-trail"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 daytime talkshow The View}}}\uc2 , Harris said she would differ from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  by including a Republican in her cabinet. She was asked by the radio host Howard Stern if that might be Cheney but avoided a direct answer. Appointing Cheney would carry considerable political risks given her hawkish foreign policy and her father\u8217\'20\'19s role in instigating the Iraq war.\par \par \uc2 Trump has frequently tried to paint Harris, who is from deep blue California, as a radical liberal but she struck a moderate tone during her appearances with Cheney, who lost her House seat after she co-chaired a congressional committee that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/jun/09/january-6-hearings-sketch-liz-cheney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 investigated the January 6 attack}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harris promised to \u8220\'20\'1Cinvite good ideas from wherever they come\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ccut red tape\u8221\'20\'1D, and she said \u8220\'20\'1Cthere should be a healthy two-party system\u8221\'20\'1D in the country. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to be able to have these good intense debates about issues that are grounded in fact,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CImagine!\u8221\'20\'1D Cheney responded.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s start there!\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said as the audience clapped. \u8220\'20\'1CCan you believe that\u8217\'20\'19s an applause line?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Foreign policy loomed large over the three conversations as Harris and Cheney described Trump as chaotic, erratic and unfit to lead. In Waukesha, at an event moderated by the conservative author and broadcaster {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/audio/2023/jun/09/will-too-many-cooks-spoil-the-republican-broth-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Charlie Sykes}}}\uc2 , Cheney highlighted Trump\u8217\'20\'19s admiration for autocrats such as \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  of Russia, Kim Jong-un of North Korea and Xi Jinping of China.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you listen to him, he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t just praise those people generally,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe praises them for their cruelty, for their tyranny. That\u8217\'20\'19s not who we are as a nation. It\u8217\'20\'19s not who we are and the world needs us to be better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris criticised Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim that he would end the Russia-Ukraine war in a day as tantamount to \u8220\'20\'1Csurrender\u8221\'20\'1D, explaining: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  would be sitting in Kyiv if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  were president and understand what that means, as our allies understand, and that\u8217\'20\'19s why they\u8217\'20\'19re concerned about this election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf Putin were to get away with invading the sovereignty and territorial integrity of Ukraine \u8230\'20\'26 you think he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t march next right into Poland and the rest of Europe? Because \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants to please somebody that he considers to be a strongman who he admires? So on this, and so many issues, the stakes are extremely high.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But some observers questioned the wisdom of campaigning with Cheney in Michigan, which has the highest concentration of Arab Americans in the country, given her hawkish foreign policy and her father\u8217\'20\'19s role in instigating the Iraq war. Many such voters are now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/hamtramck-donald-trump-arab-american-muslim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wavering or abstaining}}}\uc2  because of the Biden-Harris administration\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the crisis in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Trump weighed in on Monday, writing on his Truth Social platform: \u8220\'20\'1CArab Voters are very upset that Comrade \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the Worst Vice President in the History of the United States and a Low IQ individual, is campaigning with \u8216\'20\'18dumb as a rock\u8217\'20\'19 War Hawk, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , who, like her father, the man that pushed Bush to ridiculously go to War in the Middle East, also wants to go to War with every Muslim Country known to mankind.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?539383-1/vice-president-harris-campaigns-liz-cheney-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michigan event}}}\uc2  was held in Royal Oak, outside Detroit, and moderated by Maria Shriver, a journalist and former first lady of California.\par \par \uc2 In a nod to the concept of shy Harris voters who would rather not share their views publicly, Cheney said: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re at all concerned, you can vote your conscience and not ever have to say a word to anybody and there will be millions of Republicans who do that on November 5.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In a lighter moment, Shriver asked Harris \u8211\'20\'13 who turned 60 on Sunday \u8211\'20\'13 about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/atrupar/status/1848478563814486268"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 what she is doing to de-stress}}}\uc2 , noting that Americans say they are turning off the news, doing yoga, \u8220\'20\'1Ceating gummies, all sorts of things\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris replied: \u8220\'20\'1CNot eating gummies!\u8221\'20\'1D and burst into laughter. She admitted: \u8220\'20\'1CI wake up in the middle of the night usually these days, just to be honest with you, but I work out every morning. I think that\u8217\'20\'19s really important to just kind of \u8211\'20\'13 you know, mind, body and spirit \u8230\'20\'26 My family grounds me in every way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But Harris counselled against despair: \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s not feel powerless \u8230\'20\'26 because then we have been defeated and that\u8217\'20\'19s not our character as the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More than 100 former Republican officeholders and officials {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2024/10/16/remarks-by-vice-president-harris-at-a-campaign-event-washington-crossing-pa/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 joined Harris last week}}}\uc2  in Washington Crossing, Pennsylvania, not far from where general George Washington led hundreds of troops across the Delaware River to a major victory in the revolutionary war. At a rally there, Cheney told Republican voters that the patriotic choice was to vote for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 She and Harris appeared to have a good chemistry during their swing state tour. At one point in Wisconsin, Cheney observed: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t hire somebody to babysit your kids, you shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t make that guy the president of the United States.\u8221\'20\'1D The audience laughed. And no one seemed more amused than Harris herself.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241021ekal002ux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
