\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris and Cheney talk economy, women\u8217\'20\'19s health and Trump in Michigan campaign event \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Sam Levin (now); Chris Stein and Yohannes Lowe (earlier) \par \uc2 9,844 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 October 2024\par 00:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. You can find more of our US elections coverage here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.05am BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re ending our live coverage for the day, thanks for following along. Some links and key events from the day:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , former Republican congresswoman and longtime opponent of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, condemned Republican bans on the procedure and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/liz-cheney-kamala-harris-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urged conservatives on Monday}}}\uc2  to support \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden acknowledged on Monday that her husband {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/jill-joe-biden-dropping-out"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 made \u8220\'20\'1Cthe right call\u8221\'20\'1D by stepping down}}}\uc2  from his run for re-election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the Democratic vice-presidential candidate, said \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/tim-walz-elon-musk-trump-giveaway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plan to give away $1m a day}}}\uc2  in support of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is a reflection of a ticket with \u8220\'20\'1Cno plan\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Central Park Five{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/central-park-five-trump-defamation-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sued Trump for defamation}}}\uc2  after he falsely said during the presidential debate that they had pleaded guilty to a brutal rape 35 years ago, despite the fact that they had their convictions overturned.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Republican county supervisor in Arizona who refused to certify the 2022 midterm election has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/peggy-judd-pleads-guilty-arizona-election-denier"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded guilty to a misdemeanor}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The politics writer Olivia Nuzzi and New York magazine {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/olivia-nuzzi-leaves-new-york-magazine-rfk-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have parted ways}}}\uc2  after she was placed on leave following the disclosure that she had engaged in a \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonal\u8221\'20\'1D relationship with \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Key rightwing legal groups tied to Trump and his allies have banked millions of dollars from conservative foundations and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/trump-maga-swing-states-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed multiple lawsuits challenging voting rules in swing states}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump doubled down on false claims about the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s hurricane recovery efforts and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/trump-visit-north-carolina-hurricane-conspiracy-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promoted baseless conspiracy theories}}}\uc2  about immigration.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.50am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  campaigns in North Carolina\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is now on stage at a campaign event in Concord, North Carolina, with faith leaders. His former housing secretary, Ben Carson, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/live/2024-election-trump-harris-news-updates#00000192-b150-deb3-ab9f-bbd1715f0000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spoke}}}\uc2  before the ex-president arrived, saying the election would determine whether the US is a secular nation or one under God: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re as close to losing it right now as we have been at any point in time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The former president leaned into religious messaging, saying of his assassination attempt, \u8220\'20\'1CGod saved me for a purpose.\u8221\'20\'1D He also said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe embrace followers of Jesus,\u8221\'20\'1D and later added:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m here tonight to deliver a simple message to Christians across America. It\u8217\'20\'19s time to stand up and save your country.\par \par \uc2 Throughout his campaign, Trump has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/wireStory/trump-boosts-hard-christian-worldview-paints-election-spiritual-114970078"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 embraced a rightwing Christian worldview}}}\uc2 , working with evangelical leaders who have claimed he is \u8220\'20\'1Canointed\u8221\'20\'1D to fight \u8220\'20\'1Cspiritual warfare\u8221\'20\'1D against Democrats, the AP recently reported.\par \par \uc2 Read more here form the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s past reporting on Christian nationalists\u8217\'20\'19 embrace of Trump during the election:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/07/christian-nationalists-embrace-trump-as-their-savior-will-they-be-his"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Christian nationalists embrace Trump as their savior \u8211\'20\'13 will they be his?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  gave a shoutout to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at a ceremony honoring winners of the National Medals of Arts and National Humanities Medals, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/live/2024-election-trump-harris-news-updates#00000192-b13f-d913-afff-bf3f2e0b0000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AP reports}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know the power of the women in this room to get things done\u8221\'20\'1D and boost the next generation, Biden told the crowd, which included singer and actor Queen Latifah and poet Joy Harjo. He added that female winners were \u8220\'20\'1Cproving a woman can do anything a man can do, and then some, that includes being president of the United States of America\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s nod to the vice-president was met with a standing ovation, according to the AP. Hollywood heavyweights were in attendance, including Spike Lee, Steven Spielberg and Aaron Sorkin.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona GOP official who refused to certify election pleads guilty\par \par \uc2 A Republican county supervisor in rural Arizona who refused to certify the 2022 midterm election has agreed to a plea deal, becoming the first person criminally sanctioned for refusing to certify an election since 2020.\par \par \uc2 Peggy Judd, a Republican supervisor in Cochise county, Arizona, agreed to plead guilty to a misdemeanor charge for failing or refusing to perform an official duty by an election officer. She will serve an unsupervised probation of at least 90 days and pay a maximum $500 fine, Arizona\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic attorney general, Kris Mayes, said in a press release announcing the plea deal on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Judd, who is still in office, will preside over the presidential election next month and be required to certify its results. The attorney general\u8217\'20\'19s office said in court on Monday that the probation term lasted through the 2024 certification and that if Judd again refused, she would be in violation of her probation and would face up to 30 days in jail for the violation, the local outlet Capitol Media Services {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tucson.com/news/local/government-politics/elections/cochise-county-election-interference-canvass-peggy-judd-plea/article_2148d208-8fd1-11ef-b4ba-5f78104a0bc6.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/peggy-judd-pleads-guilty-arizona-election-denier"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona Republican official who refused to certify 2022 midterm election pleads guilty}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Judges reject Republican challenges to overseas ballots\par \par \uc2 Judges in Michigan and North Carolina have ruled against two Republican lawsuits today seeking to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/10/21/nx-s1-5159996/uocava-overseas-voters-military-lawsuit-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenge the legitimacy}}}\uc2  of ballots from Americans overseas, NPR reports.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25244950-michigan-republican-party-v-benson-2024-10-21-opinion-and-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 state judge in Michigan}}}\uc2  dismissed a recent \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  legal complaint that alleged certain overseas voters from the state were not eligible to cast ballots. The Michigan judge said the law \u8220\'20\'1Cbars this 11th hour attempt to disenfranchise these electors\u8221\'20\'1D and that Republicans were seeking to challenge language from the state secretary of state\u8217\'20\'19s office that is \u8220\'20\'1Cconsistent with federal and state law, and the Michigan constitution\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 And a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25244966-kivett-2024-10-21-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina judge}}}\uc2  rejected a \u8220\'20\'1Crequest for the court to order that returned ballots of some overseas voters be set aside and not counted until the voters\u8217\'20\'19 eligibility can be confirmed\u8221\'20\'1D, NPR reported. That judge said there was \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely no evidence\u8221\'20\'1D that anyone had taken advantage of the overseas rules and cast a fraudulent ballot.\par \par \uc2 From 2023 through September 2024, the committee and its affiliates have filed or been involved in 72 election lawsuits, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/republican-litigation-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 major legal blitz}}}\uc2  that experts say is designed to sow doubt about the results if Trump loses.\par \par \uc2 More background on those cases here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/republican-litigation-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Inside the Republican legal blitz to sow election doubt: \u8216\'20\'18The claims are garbage\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fact-checking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's hurricane claims\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/trump-visit-north-carolina-hurricane-conspiracy-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeated a litany of falsehoods}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/21/politics/fact-check-trump-fema-hurricane-response/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conspiracy theories}}}\uc2  about Hurricane Helene and the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s response while campaigning in North Carolina today.\par \par \uc2 The former president falsely suggested, once again, that federal money meant for hurricane relief was \u8220\'20\'1Cspent \u8230\'20\'26 on illegal migrants\u8221\'20\'1D. There is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/21/politics/fact-check-trump-fema-hurricane-response/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no basis}}}\uc2  for the claim that disaster funding was reallocated to services related to immigration. The \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema) is part of the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 , which also oversees the major US immigration agencies. But money allocated for a program to help migrants is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/21/politics/fact-check-trump-fema-hurricane-response/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 separate}}}\uc2  and unrelated to disaster response funds.\par \par \uc2 Trump also falsely implied that the Democrats were spending money on undocumented people so that they could \u8220\'20\'1Cvote in the election\u8221\'20\'1D, reiterating his frequently cited baseless claim about election fraud.\par \par \uc2 He also claimed Fema\u8217\'20\'19s money is \u8220\'20\'1Call gone\u8221\'20\'1D. But this is false, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/21/politics/fact-check-trump-fema-hurricane-response/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN noted}}}\uc2 , as the federal agency told the network last week that its disaster relief fund had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/15/politics/sba-loan-program-out-of-money/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 roughly $8.5bn remaining}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 More here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/trump-visit-north-carolina-hurricane-conspiracy-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump uses North Carolina visit to reiterate hurricane relief conspiracies}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Michigan rally with \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  comes to a close, moderator Maria Shriver asks the vice-president how she copes with the stress of the race and what her message is to voters who are struggling with anxiety over the election.\par \par \uc2 Harris says, \u8220\'20\'1CI wake up in the middle of the night usually these days \u8230\'20\'26 but I work out every morning. I think that\u8217\'20\'19s really important [for] mind, body and spirit \u8230\'20\'26 I try to eat well. I love my family, and I make sure that I talk to the kids and my husband every day \u8230\'20\'26 My family grounds me in every way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The vice-president adds:\par \par \uc2 We cannot despair \u8230\'20\'26 Every individual has the power to make a decision about what this will be \u8230\'20\'26 so let\u8217\'20\'19s not feel powerless. I get the overwhelming nature of this all makes us feel powerless \u8230\'20\'26 That\u8217\'20\'19s not our character as American people. We are not one to be defeated. We rise to a moment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the former Republican congresswoman now campaigning with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Michigan, outlines Trump\u8217\'20\'19s threats on foreign policy :\par \par \uc2 He heaps praise on the world\u8217\'20\'19s most evil people, while he attacks with venom his political opponents here at home \u8230\'20\'26 If you look at where the Republican party is today, there\u8217\'20\'19s been a really dangerous embrace of isolationism, a dangerous embrace of tyrants \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t think that Congress can stop him \u8230\'20\'26 all he has to do is what he\u8217\'20\'19s doing and say, I won\u8217\'20\'19t fulfill our Nato treaty obligations, and \uc2 Nato\uc2  begins to unravel.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , campaigning with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Michigan, criticizes commentators who assert that the vice-president isn\u8217\'20\'19t ready to be president:\par \par \uc2 She is supremely qualified to be president of the United States. There sometimes are some men who suggest that she\u8217\'20\'19s not, but if you look at her qualifications, there\u8217\'20\'19s no question that she\u8217\'20\'19s somebody that I know I can count on, who will put the good of this country first.\par \par \uc2 Cheney also emphasizes her conservative credentials while explaining her support for Harris: \u8220\'20\'1CThe very first campaign I ever volunteered in was for President Gerald Ford \u8230\'20\'26 and ever since then, I have been voting for Republicans. I\u8217\'20\'19ve never voted for a Democrat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 : 'Vote your conscience... vote him out'\par \par \uc2 Maria Shriver asks \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  if they ever imagined they would be campaigning together. Harris says she has long worked with Republicans, and given the threat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  poses, she is not surprised to be standing with the former Republican congresswoman:\par \par \uc2 What is at stake in this election is so fundamental for us as Americans \u8230\'20\'26 Do we take seriously the importance of a president who obeys the oath to be loyal to the constitution of the United States? Do we prioritize a president \u8230\'20\'26 who cares about the rule of law?\par \par \uc2 Cheney says: \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone who watched January 6th knows what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is willing to do.\u8221\'20\'1D She adds:\par \par \uc2 I could have just said I\u8217\'20\'19m going to do everything I can to work against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , and there are a lot of Republicans who have said that \u8230\'20\'26 I have decided, and I am very proud, and I\u8217\'20\'19m honored to have made the decision to endorse Vice-President Harris \u8230\'20\'26 As a mother, I want my children to know that there is someone sitting in the Oval Office that they can look up to, someone who can be a role model.\par \par \uc2 Shriver asks Cheney if she was afraid to endorse Harris, knowing the backlash she\u8217\'20\'19d face. Cheney shares a message to Republicans who want to support the Democratic ticket, but are afraid: \u8220\'20\'1CYou can vote your conscience and not ever have to say a word to anybody \u8230\'20\'26 Vote him out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Maria Shriver hosts discussion with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Liz Cheney\par \par \uc2 Maria Shriver, former first lady of California, has taken the stage at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign event in Royal Oak, Michigan, with \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Shriver starts off by making a pitch for bipartisanship, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI served as a Democratic first lady in a Republican administration in California. So I get this bipartisan thing. I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen it up close. And now I\u8217\'20\'19m a proud independent \u8230\'20\'26 People of both parties used to get along really well.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Cheney to appear together again for town hall event\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will soon make another appearance with \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?539383-1/vice-president-harris-campaigns-liz-cheney-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign event in Royal Oak, Michigan}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, the vice-president and former conservative congresswoman made their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/21/kamala-harris-donald-trump-rallies-us-election-politics?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-671680408f08556b4172daf4#block-671680408f08556b4172daf4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pitch in Pennsylvania}}}\uc2 , geared toward Republican voters. Cheney said:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m a conservative, and I know that the most conservative of all conservative principles is being faithful to the constitution. And you have to choose in this race between someone who has been faithful to the constitution, who will be faithful, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who is not just us predicting how he will act. We watched what he did after the last election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump then went on to insinuate that he had been told he was a better president than George Washington and \uc2 Abraham Lincoln\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He was harping on the border and the alleged ills of undocumented people, before going on to say that the border patrol had endorsed him. That\u8217\'20\'19s not quite true \u8211\'20\'13 the government agency has not endorsed him, but its union, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/BPUnion/status/1845835750224597096"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Border Patrol Council has}}}\uc2 . Undeterred, Trump went on:\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19re great. They endorsed your favorite president. They didn\u8217\'20\'19t only endorse me, saying I\u8217\'20\'19m the greatest president there\u8217\'20\'19s ever been \u8230\'20\'26 What about George Washington? No, you\u8217\'20\'19re better. What about Lincoln? What about \uc2 Abraham Lincoln\uc2 ? No, you\u8217\'20\'19re better, they said, I\u8217\'20\'19m tougher on the border than \uc2 Abraham Lincoln\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 The former president appeared to try to hit back at claims that, at the age of 78, he is \u8220\'20\'1Ccognitively impaired\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But Trump raised more questions than he answered by jumbling his words.\par \par \uc2 The moment came as he told the crowd in North Carolina, in a somewhat confusing anecdote, that he was talking to someone from the state on the phone, but was then distracted by watching one of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  rockets land.\par \par \uc2 He told the person on the phone to wait while he watched the rocket, then forgot he was on the phone. \u8220\'20\'1CI forgot he was on the phone because, and now they, all these idiots back there, will say he\u8217\'20\'19s cognitively impaired because he put he\u8217\'20\'19s cognitively impaired,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, apparently referring to reporters in attendance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, I do this stuff, five, six, seven times a day for 52 days without a break,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, by way of explanation for his misstatements. He appeared to then lose his train of thought:\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll tell you what they are, really not all of them, not all of them. I\u8217\'20\'19d say about 92% couple of good ones. That\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of cameras going on. There are a couple of good ones back there. Now it is crazy in the crazy what they do, and the level of meanness.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is now onstage in Greenville, North Carolina, where he\u8217\'20\'19s been whipping up the crowd with his usual attacks on \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, he took note of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaigning alongside \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 . On Truth Social, Trump implied that Arab voters \u8211\'20\'13 significant communities of which live in Michigan, a battleground state \u8211\'20\'13 are unlikely to look kindly on the vice-president associating with the daughter of \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2 , who, as vice-president under \uc2 George W Bush\uc2 , was an architect of the US invasion of Iraq:\par \par \uc2 enltrArab Voters are very upset that Comrade \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the Worst Vice President in the History of the United States and a Low IQ individual, is campaigning with \u8220\'20\'1Cdumb as a rock\u8221\'20\'1D War Hawk, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , who, like her father, the man that pushed Bush to ridiculously go to War in the\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  Posts From His Truth Social (@TrumpDailyPosts) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TrumpDailyPosts/status/1848377254000181260?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Arab voters are indeed a source of concern for Democrats, though mostly over the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on that, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Stephen Starr:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/hamtramck-donald-trump-arab-american-muslim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They will vote against Harris\u8217\'20\'19: Arab Americans in Michigan desert Democrats over Gaza}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump rallies in swing state North Carolina\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is scheduled to soon take the stage in North Carolina, which hasn\u8217\'20\'19t voted for a Democratic presidential candidate since 2008 but where polls have indicated \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  may have a fighting chance this year.\par \par \uc2 Trump earlier in the day visited western parts of the state damaged by Hurricane Helene, and is now rallying in Greenville, on North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s eastern side. He was introduced by adviser \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , who was the architect of the hardline immigration policies Trump allowed during his presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor eight long years, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been fighting for us in the arena. What he has endured, what he has been through on this journey,\u8221\'20\'1D Miller said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey came after him, they came after his family, they came after his children, they came after his businesses, they came after his freedom, and they came after his life, and he\u8217\'20\'19s still standing strong. He is still standing tall. And with your help, North Carolina, \uc2 Donald J Trump\uc2  is going to save the United States of America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 The former president then invited Adam Smith, a former Green Beret who has helped relief efforts in the Asheville area since Hurricane Helene devastated the area just over three weeks ago, to speak.\par \par \uc2 At the podium, Smith thanked Trump for coming to the area.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe biggest fear that western North Carolina is sitting on right now, at least in the communities we\u8217\'20\'19ve talked to, is being forgotten,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTo have you here and have an opportunity to have this conversation at a national level, will keep western North Carolina on the map, and not leave the communities holding the bag on the back end of this, so we\u8217\'20\'19re very grateful that you\u8217\'20\'19ve shown up,\u8221\'20\'1D Smith said to the former president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump continued his remarks by accusing the federal government of leaving North Carolinians \u8220\'20\'1Chelpless and abandoned\u8221\'20\'1D after Hurricane Helene.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the wake of this horrible storm, many Americans in this region felt helpless and abandoned and left behind by their government, and yet, in North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s hour of desperation, the American people answered the call much more so than your federal government, unfortunately,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCitizens poured into western North Carolina from all over the country, bringing food, water, fuel, medical aid, even helicopters.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNothing is more inspiring than to see the American spirit triumph over adversity with the most selfless acts of generosity and love\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump again attacks Hurricane Helene response in North Carolina visit\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  held a press conference in western North Carolina, where he surveyed the damage wrought by Hurricane Helene and attacked the federal government\u8217\'20\'19s recovery efforts.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDriving up here you see the kind of destruction, actually incredible\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe power of nature, nothing you can do about it but you got to get a little bit better crew in to do a better job than has been done by the White House, because it\u8217\'20\'19s not good, not good.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m here today in western North Carolina to express a simple message to the incredible people of the state, I\u8217\'20\'19m with you and the American people are with you all the way\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to continue to be with you, we will see what happens with the election and on January 20th I think you are going to have a new crew coming in to do it properly and help you in a proper manner.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also addressed those who had lost family members and loved ones to the storm. \u8220\'20\'1CTo everyone who has lost a loved one... we ask God to give you comfort and peace,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been a terrible ordeal and this area was hit about as hard as anyone has ever seen....the communities were ravaged and destroyed, we are praying for you and we will not forget about you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s repeated criticisms of the federal response to Hurricane Helene comes as the director of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/07/hurricane-helene-trump-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fema condemned}}}\uc2  the former president and his supporters for spreading misinformation about the hurricane and the response by the federal disaster agency, which, the director said, has hampered the government\u8217\'20\'19s ability to get people the help they need.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has long drawn criticism before over his statements about the Central Park Five, a group of men who were exonerated after being wrongly convicted for a crime and who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/21/kamala-harris-donald-trump-rallies-us-election-politics?page=with:block-671693418f0832d15c5fd599#block-671693418f0832d15c5fd599"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 earlier today sued}}}\uc2  him.\par \par \uc2 After the jogger\u8217\'20\'19s assault, he spoke out about the case and took out a full-page ad in several New York newspapers calling for the reinstatement of the death penalty, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Trump in 2019 stood by his prior comments about the Central Park Five, and declined to apologize.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  adds that at the debate with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  last month, Trump said of the men: \u8220\'20\'1CThey pled guilty\u8230\'20\'26They killed a person, ultimately.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The five then-boys, who were tried as adults, actually {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2016/feb/17/central-park-five-donald-trump-jogger-rape-case-new-york"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pleaded not guilty}}}\uc2 . And the victim, Trisha Meili, although almost killed, was found unconscious in the park, survived and testified in court.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/13/central-park-five-dnc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yusef Salaam}}}\uc2  watched the debate in Philadelphia, afterwards telling the \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  in an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/2024/09/10/presidential-debate-live-updates/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CHere we are right now, full-circle moment, being able to be participants in this great democracy on the cusp of everything really powerfully supporting \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 . I\u8217\'20\'19m ready for it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Central Park Five sue Trump\par \par \uc2 The five Black and Hispanic teenagers who were wrongfully convicted for the 1989 rape of a white jogger in New York\u8217\'20\'19s Central Park have sued \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for defamation over statements he made at last month\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/trump-harris-debate-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US presidential debate}}}\uc2 , Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Known widely as the Central Park Five, the defendants spent between five and 13 years in prison before they were cleared in 2002 based on new DNA evidence and the confession of another person.\par \par \uc2 Trump falsely said at the September 10 debate with presidential rival \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  that the Central Park Five had killed a person and pleaded guilty.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, filed in federal court in Philadelphia by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/nov/07/yusef-salaam-nyc-council-seat-central-park-five"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yusef Salaam}}}\uc2  , Raymond Santana, Kevin Richardson, Antron Brown and Korey Wise, called Trump\u8217\'20\'19s statements \u8220\'20\'1Cdemonstrably false.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign called the case \u8220\'20\'1Cjust another frivolous, election interference lawsuit, filed by desperate left-wing activists.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A lawyer for the plaintiffs, Shanin Specter, said in a statement that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remarks \u8220\'20\'1Ccast them in a harmful false light and intentionally inflicted emotional distress on them.\u8221\'20\'1D The plaintiffs are seeking unspecified monetary damages for reputational and emotional harms as well as punitive damages.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is on tour of the three Great Lakes swing states with \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , a Republican former congresswoman who broke with her party over their support for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . In their first event together in a Philadelphia suburb, Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/21/kamala-harris-donald-trump-rallies-us-election-politics?page=with:block-67167cfd8f0832d15c5fd444#block-67167cfd8f0832d15c5fd444"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned voters}}}\uc2  to take Trump seriously, while Cheney {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/21/kamala-harris-donald-trump-rallies-us-election-politics?page=with:block-671680408f08556b4172daf4#block-671680408f08556b4172daf4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  she came around to backing the Democrats because she does not think the former president will stand up for American allies. They will appear together in metro Detroit and then Milwaukee before the day is through. Meanwhile, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  was on daytime talk staple \u8220\'20\'1CThe View\u8221\'20\'1D, where he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/21/kamala-harris-donald-trump-rallies-us-election-politics?page=with:block-671673728f0832d15c5fd386#block-671673728f0832d15c5fd386"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments about deploying the national guard against his political enemies was a sign that he planned to bend the country\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cconstitutional guardrails\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/21/kamala-harris-donald-trump-rallies-us-election-politics?page=with:block-6716454a8f08ec51ad9b1f02#block-6716454a8f08ec51ad9b1f02"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed}}}\uc2  an expansion of contraception coverage under the Affordable Care Act (aka Obamacare) that will allow women to access birth control without a prescription.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/21/kamala-harris-donald-trump-rallies-us-election-politics?page=with:block-671663ff8f0832d15c5fd2b1#block-671663ff8f0832d15c5fd2b1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has scheduled}}}\uc2  an interview with NBC News from her home at the Naval Observatory in Washington DC on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A new poll{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/21/kamala-harris-donald-trump-rallies-us-election-politics?page=with:block-67165d588f0832d15c5fd25c#block-67165d588f0832d15c5fd25c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2  Trump may have lost his edge among voters when it comes to handling the economy, while Harris is viewed more favorably overall.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s push for the support of Republican voters won her the support of the daughter of Gerald Ford, the late Republican former president who served from 1974 to 1977.\par \par \uc2 Susan Ford Bales \u8217\'20\'19s endorsement is perhaps most consequential in Michigan, the ex-president\u8217\'20\'19s home and also a swing state coveted by both candidates. The Detroit News has Bales\u8217\'20\'19s statement:\par \par \uc2 enltrSusan Ford Bales, daughter of Republican former President Gerald Ford, endorses Democrat \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , according to the Harris campaign: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Lyqip1IFlR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Lyqip1IFlR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Craig Mauger (@CraigDMauger) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CraigDMauger/status/1848384310510080046?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 As they wrapped up their joint event in Pennsylvania, \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  was asked to give something of a closing argument to her fellow Republicans for why they should support \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former congresswoman said:\par \par \uc2 I think that in this election, and especially here in Pennsylvania, we have the opportunity to tell the whole world who we are, and we have the chance to say, you know, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to reject cruelty. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to reject the kind of vile vitriol that we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . We\u8217\'20\'19re going to reject the misogyny from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance. And we have the chance in this race to elect somebody who, you know is going to defend the rule of law.\par \par \uc2 You know, vice-president Harris is going to defend our constitution. We have the chance to remind people that we are a good country. We are a good and honorable people. We are a great nation and in this race, we have the opportunity to vote for and support somebody you can count on. We\u8217\'20\'19re not always going to agree, but I know vice-president Harris will always do what she believes is right for this country. She has a sincere heart, and that\u8217\'20\'19s why I\u8217\'20\'19m honored to be here.\par \par \uc2 Thus concluded the first of three joint events the pair will do today. They now fly to Michigan for an event in the Detroit suburbs, followed by another in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 All three states are part of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1CBlue Wall\u8221\'20\'1D of swing states along the Great Lakes where voters traditionally back the party, but where polls show Harris is locked in a tight race against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Cheney explains Harris support: Trump 'won't defend this nation'\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s support for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is somewhat inexplicable.\par \par \uc2 She was a conservative Republican in Congress who supported almost none of the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 legislative priorities, but her break with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  led to her falling out with the party, and losing her seat. She is also the daughter of \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2 , the former vice-president who was an ardent supporter of the US invasion of Iraq.\par \par \uc2 Asked at the event alongside Harris about how she came around to backing Democratic national security priorities, Cheney noted that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/22/national-security-officials-endorse-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hundreds of national security officials}}}\uc2  have endorsed the vice-president, and said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies were too dangerous to tolerate:\par \par \uc2 The choice here, with respect to national security policy, is a man who has proven, he\u8217\'20\'19s absolutely proven, that he will not stand up, he won\u8217\'20\'19t defend this nation with respect to our own constitution and rule of law. And vice-president Harris, who has been clear in terms of support for Ukraine, in terms of recognizing and understanding across the board that America cannot maintain our own freedom and security if we walk away from our allies around the world.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris's message to voters: take Trump seriously\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has taken an almost humorous tack to his campaign lately, including holding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/us-presidential-election-2024-updates-kamala-harris-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a staged campaign event}}}\uc2  at a \uc2 McDonald\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s over the weekend that saw him work the drive-thru window.\par \par \uc2 Speaking alongside \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  warned voters not to fall for his jokes:\par \par \uc2 In many, many ways, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is an unserious man, but the consequences of him being president of the United States are brutally serious. There are things that he says that will be the subject of skits and laughter and jokes, but words have meaning coming from someone who aspires to stand behind the seal of the president of the United States. These are the things that are at stake.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Cheney\u8217\'20\'19s event in Malvern, Pennsylvania is set up as a moderated conversation with Sarah Longwell, the publisher of the Bulwark and the leader of a group called Republican Voters Against Trump.\par \par \uc2 Longwell began by asking Harris and Cheney about their unusual decision to campaign together. Harris replied:\par \par \uc2 I think that this moment, with the choice that the American people have in this election, in two weeks and one day, this election is presenting, for the first time, probably in certainly recent history, a very clear choice and difference between the two nominees.\par \par \uc2 And I think that is what, as much as anything, is bringing us as Americans together who are understanding that we cannot, with such fundamental stakes being presented, afford to be mired in ideological differences without really staking our claim to the most fundamental ideals upon which our country stands.\par \par \uc2 And here\u8217\'20\'19s Cheney\u8217\'20\'19s answer:\par \par \uc2 For me, every single thing in my experience and in my background has played a part in my decision to endorse vice-president Harris. And, you know, that that begins with the fact that I\u8217\'20\'19m a conservative, and I know that the most conservative of all conservative principles is being faithful to the constitution. And you have to choose in this race between someone who has been faithful to the constitution, who will be faithful, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who is not just us predicting how he will act. We watched what he did after the last election.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to campaign with \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  in battleground state Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is soon to take the stage in Malvern, Pennsylvania, where she will be campaigning with Republican former congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s one of three events in each of the Great Lakes battleground states she will do today with Cheney, who lost her primary two years ago after falling out with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . The push is part of the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to win over moderate voters in key areas who they believe can be persuaded not to back the former president.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll let you know what the vice-president has to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz warns Trump bending 'constitutional guardrails' with attacks on 'enemy within'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s running mate is being interviewed on ABC daytime talk staple \u8220\'20\'1CThe View\u8221\'20\'1D right now, where he warned that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s recent comments about sending {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/trump-military-enemy-within-armed-forces-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the national guard}}}\uc2  after \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy within\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 as he has taken to calling his political enemies \u8211\'20\'13 is a sign that he is willing to bend America\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cconstitutional guardrails\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe guardrails are off with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  right now,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m an optimist, but our systems are strained, and the ability to politicize the military has never been tried in this country. He\u8217\'20\'19s trying it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walz also took a crack at answering the question of what Harris would do differently as president than \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign attacked the vice-president last week after she said she wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t do anything differently, comments she then had to walk back. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Walz said:\par \par \uc2 enltrTim Walz tells "The View" what \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  would have done differently than Biden:\par \par \uc2 "This expansion on Medicare is something that I wished would have been proposed sooner. But look, they're tackling the issues that they needed to." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ufLDidrr7F"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ufLDidrr7F}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1848385093498511425?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  squabbled by text with Mike Johnson over election certification - report\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will be joined on the campaign trail today by \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , a Republican former congresswoman who lost her primary because of her opposition to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Cheney, who was the top Republican on the January 6 committee, expressed doubts that Republican House speaker and Trump ally Mike Johnson would certify Harris\u8217\'20\'19s election win. \u8220\'20\'1CI do not have faith that Mike Johnson will fulfill his constitutional obligations,\u8221\'20\'1D she said on NBC.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/10/20/mike-johnson-liz-cheney-text-messages-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Axios reported yesterday}}}\uc2  that Johnson reached out to Cheney by text message to object to her comments. \u8220\'20\'1CWe had a little debate in conversation, on text message, back and forth and agreed to disagree,\u8221\'20\'1D the speaker told Axios, adding that he told Cheney \u8220\'20\'1Chow disappointed I was in that, to make things personal, because I\u8217\'20\'19ve not done that.\u8221\'20\'1D He continued:\par \par \uc2 You know the idea that President Trump is somehow a danger to the Republic, and that any of us who support him are a danger or would not fulfill our constitutional obligations, all these things that have been said are it\u8217\'20\'19s just nonsense.\par \par \uc2 She knows, she knows me. She used to know me well and knows that I\u8217\'20\'19m a constitutional conservative, and I take all matters at this level very seriously, and I will fulfill my constitutional oath. And to say otherwise is just dishonest.\par \par \uc2 In her own statement to Axios, Cheney said: \u8220\'20\'1CMike knows this is a conscious choice between right and wrong and can\u8217\'20\'19t honestly rationalize supporting Trump on this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor Josh Shapiro has suggested that law enforcement should investigate \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s handout of checks to encourage people to vote for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/anna-betts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anna Betts}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Josh Shapiro, the governor of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania}}}\uc2 , said law enforcement should look into \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/oct/20/elon-musk-promises-to-award-1m-every-day-to-voters-as-he-steps-up-campaigning-for-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ploy to give $1m}}}\uc2  to a registered voter who signs a petition supporting free speech in key swing states each day until the US presidential election.\par \par \uc2 Legal experts have said it appears to violate laws that prohibit giving incentives to people to register to vote. On Sunday, Shapiro expressed similar concerns. Monday is Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s deadline to register to vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think there are real questions with how he is spending money in this race, how the dark money is flowing, not just into Pennsylvania, but apparently now into the pockets of Pennsylvanians,\u8221\'20\'1D Shapiro told NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is deeply concerning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Later in the interview Shapiro added: \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s something that law enforcement should take a look at. I\u8217\'20\'19m not the attorney general any more of Pennsylvania, I\u8217\'20\'19m the governor, but it does raise serious questions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/election-shapiro-musk-1-million-giveaway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania governor says law enforcement should investigate Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s $1m voter ploy}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to sit for NBC News interview on Tuesday\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will sit for an interview with NBC News tomorrow from her home at the Naval Observatory in Washington DC, the network {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nbcuniversalnewsgroup.com/nbcnews/2024/10/20/nbc-news-exclusive-hallie-jackson-to-interview-vice-president-kamala-harris-on-tuesday/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The vice-president will speak to Hallie Jackson as she steps up her interviews and media appearances ahead of the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 The interview is set to air at 6.30pm on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Poll finds Harris viewed more favorably than Trump, former president losing edge on economy\par \par \uc2 An Associated Press-NORC Center for Public Affairs Research poll released this morning contained some positive news for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , though there\u8217\'20\'19s no telling if it is predictive of the election outcome.\par \par \uc2 The survey found that Harris is viewed more favorably than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , including among the independent voters that could decide the seven swing states. It also reported that Trump no longer appears to have the advantage he once did on handling of economic issues, even though the former president has made that a centerpiece of his campaign with accusations that Democratic policies have driven up prices. That\u8217\'20\'19s one of two main messages he\u8217\'20\'19s been pushing, along with promises to crack down on migrants \u8211\'20\'13 an area on which the poll finds Trump maintains his advantage.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what it found about the two candidates\u8217\'20\'19 favorability:\par \par \uc2 Registered voters\u8217\'20\'19 opinions of the candidates have not changed much since last month. In general Harris and her running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , are viewed more positively than Trump or JD Vance. A large majority of Democratic voters have positive views of Harris and Walz, and Republicans voters feel favorably toward Trump and Vance. Independent voters are closely divided in their opinion of Harris while most have a negative view of Trump. Independent voters have similar opinions about both vice-presidential candidates.\par \par \uc2 When it comes to economic issues, 40% of registered voters trust Harris to handle the cost of groceries and gas, and 42% trust Trump. Six percent trust both equally, and 12% neither. On the cost of housing, Harris is more trusted with 42% support to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 37%, while 7% truth both and 14% trust neither.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  released a comprehensive new poll this morning that tells us \u8230\'20\'26 not much new.\par \par \uc2 For weeks, surveys of swing states have found \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  effectively tied, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/10/21/harris-trump-post-schar-school-poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Post\u8217\'20\'19s poll}}}\uc2 , conducted with George Mason University\u8217\'20\'19s Schar School of Policy and Government, is no different. The two candidates are neck-in-neck nationally, and within the poll\u8217\'20\'19s margin of error in the seven states that are expected to decide the election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what they found:\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/tablet/2024/10/21/sept-29-oct-15-washington-post-schar-school-deciders-poll-seven-swing-states/?itid=lk_inline_manual_4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post-Schar School poll}}}\uc2  of more than 5,000 registered voters, conducted in the first half of October, finds 47 percent who say they will definitely or probably support Harris while 47 percent say they will definitely or probably support Trump. Among likely voters, 49 percent support Harris and 48 percent back Trump.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s support is little changed from the 48 percent he received in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/06/17/deciders-2024-election-poll/?itid=lk_inline_manual_6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  spring survey}}}\uc2  of six key states using the same methodology, but Harris\u8217\'20\'19s standing is six percentage points higher than the 41-percent support registered for President {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/candidates/joe-biden-2024/?itid=lk_inline_manual_6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2 , who was then a candidate.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Among these key-state voters, Harris runs strongest in Georgia, where she has an advantage of six percentage points among registered voters and four points among likely voters, which is within the margin of error of plus or minus 4.5 percentage points. Harris also is slightly stronger than Trump in the three most contested northern states \u8212\'20\'14 Michigan, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin \u8212\'20\'14 but by percentages within the margin of error.\par \par \uc2 The seventh battleground state, Nevada, is tied among likely voters though Harris is three points stronger than Trump among registered voters.\par \par \uc2 Our own poll tracker reaches much the same conclusion:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 US presidential polls tracker: Trump v Harris latest national averages}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 We reported earlier that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has a huge advantage in campaign cash over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But the former president has his own deep-pocketed backer in the former of \uc2 Tesla\uc2  boss \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , who held a strange town hall in swing state Pennsylvania this weekend where he started handing out mammoth checks to voters to get them to back Trump. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/laughland-oliver"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Oliver Laughland}}}\uc2  witnessed the spectacle in person:\par \par \uc2 Standing before a large US flag, which spanned the breadth of a vast stage, the world\u8217\'20\'19s richest man told an assembled crowd that he loved them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis kind of energy lights a fire in my soul,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, having just made one of the crowd a millionaire after everyone chanted his name.\par \par \uc2 His love \u8211\'20\'13 and that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/oct/20/elon-musk-promises-to-award-1m-every-day-to-voters-as-he-steps-up-campaigning-for-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $1m}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 of course, was contingent on them all doing exactly as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/elon-musk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Elon Musk}}}\uc2  wanted: signing a petition tied to his political action committee (Pac) , which is dedicated to sending {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  back to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The spectacle was both surreal and potentially {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://electionlawblog.org/?p=146397"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 illegal}}}\uc2 . But no one here, not least Musk himself, seemed to care in the slightest.\par \par \uc2 The billionaire was in Pittsburgh on his final stop across the vital swing state of Pennsylvania, having {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/oct/16/elon-musk-donald-trump-donation-america-pac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 donated $75m to help get Trump}}}\uc2  re-elected, and seemingly willing to accept a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/05/trump-musk-efficiency-commission"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 job offer in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s government}}}\uc2  should he win.\par \par \uc2 Musk\u8217\'20\'19s latest ploy to assist Trump to attain more political power, has been to give away $1m every day to a member of the public, provided they also live in a swing state and are registered to vote.\par \par \uc2 The stunt is prohibited and akin to buying votes, in the view of some experts, as it violates federal election {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title52/pdf/USCODE-2023-title52-subtitleI-chap103-sec10307.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 law}}}\uc2  preventing payments for registering to vote. The state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/02/josh-shapiro-kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Josh Shapiro}}}\uc2 , on Sunday described it as \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply concerning\u8221\'20\'1D and encouraged law enforcement to \u8220\'20\'1Ctake a look at\u8221\'20\'1D. Musk\u8217\'20\'19s America Pac did not respond to a list of questions from the Guardian after the Pittsburgh town hall.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/election-elon-musk-trump-pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Conspiracy theories and a $1m check: a night at Elon Musk\u8217\'20\'19s surreal election giveaway}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 In a statement released as his administration announced a proposed rule that would allow women to receive birth control without a prescription under the Affordable Care Act, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  signaled that the move was part of an effort to highlight the differences between the two parties on the issue.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSince Roe v Wade was overturned more than two years ago, Republican elected officials have made clear they want to ban or restrict birth control, defund federal programs that help women access contraception, and repeal the Affordable Care Act. And Congressional Republicans have repeatedly blocked federal legislation to safeguard the fundamental right to birth control for women in every state. It\u8217\'20\'19s unacceptable,\u8221\'20\'1D the president said, continuing:\par \par \uc2 Today, my Administration is taking a major step to expand contraception coverage under the Affordable Care Act. This new action would help ensure that millions of women with private health insurance can access the no-cost contraception they need. Vice President Harris and I have worked tirelessly to protect and build on the Affordable Care Act. We lowered costs for Marketplace coverage by an average of $800 per year for millions of Americans, and more Americans than ever before have signed up for health insurance through the law.\par \par \uc2 At a time when contraception access is under attack, Vice President Harris and I are resolute in our commitment to expanding access to quality, affordable contraception. We believe that women in every state must have the freedom to make deeply personal health care decisions, including the right to decide if and when to start or grow their family. We will continue to fight to protect access to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care and call on Congress to restore reproductive freedom and safeguard the right to contraception once and for all.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 While the Biden administration has moved to expand contraception access, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , if returned to the White House, will likely pursue policies that make it harder to access reproductive care, particularly abortions. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 When Jennifer Adkins and her husband were considering having a second child in Idaho, they vaguely thought how the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban could affect them. But Adkins\u8217\'20\'19 first pregnancy had gone so smoothly, she didn\u8217\'20\'19t even use an epidural when she gave birth. Her next pregnancy, she expected, would be similar.\par \par \uc2 But in April 2023, 12 weeks into her second pregnancy, an ultrasound scan shattered that hope.\par \par \uc2 The ultrasound indicated a litany of issues with the fetus, whom Adkins and her husband had taken to calling \u8220\'20\'1CSpooky\u8221\'20\'1D, since Adkins\u8217\'20\'19 due date was Halloween. Spooky, Adkins learned, showed multiple signs of a chromosomal disorder as well as dangerously severe swelling. Together, these conditions usually lead to a miscarriage or death shortly after delivery, Adkins\u8217\'20\'19 doctors told her. And if the pregnancy continued, Adkins herself was at risk of developing life-threatening pre-eclampsia and swelling.\par \par \uc2 As the mother of a toddler son, Adkins was not willing to take that chance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think that you understand, until you are in that situation, how scary and how awful that actually is,\u8221\'20\'1D Adkins said during a recent interview at a coffee shop outside Boise.\par \par \uc2 Under Idaho law, abortions are permitted in medical emergencies. But although Adkins\u8217\'20\'19 health was in jeopardy, her doctors didn\u8217\'20\'19t believe her case was enough of an emergency to legally end the pregnancy. They were too afraid of Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s ban to even refer her to an out-of-state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic.\par \par \uc2 So Adkins and her husband frantically called clinics in Washington, Oregon and Utah, trying to find somewhere within driving distance that was not booked up for weeks with other patients fleeing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans now blanketing the US. The couple also scrambled for financial support to pay for the procedure and travel. If they had to shoulder all those costs on their own, the family would be at risk of being unable to afford their mortgage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re thinking about all these logistics when all you want to think about is grieving the loss of a baby that you really wanted,\u8221\'20\'1D Adkins said. \u8220\'20\'1CNone of us feel good about making that decision. But it is a loving choice that we should be able to make for our family.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/21/idaho-abortion-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Life-threatening crises, frantic calls: Idaho offers glimpse of what \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  could look like under Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris cheers proposal to expand contraception coverage under Obamacare\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration has proposed allowing women with private health insurance to receive birth control without a prescription, in a major expansion of contraception access.\par \par \uc2 The rule is under the Affordable Care Act, also known as Obamacare, and comes as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Democrats nationwide seek to make voters aware of their support for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Harris had to say about the proposed rule:\par \par \uc2 Today, our Administration is proposing the largest expansion of contraception coverage in more than a decade. This new proposed rule will build on our Administration\u8217\'20\'19s work to protect reproductive freedom by providing millions of women with more options for the affordable contraception they need and deserve. That includes coverage for no-cost over-the-counter contraception without a prescription for the first time in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history. These lower contraception costs would be in addition to the billions of dollars that women have already saved on contraception under the Affordable Care Act which President Biden and I have strengthened since taking office.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, former Democratic US President, \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , is expected to campaign with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Georgia, a state \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  narrowly won in 2020. \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  plans to join Harris for a rally - to encourage people to get out and vote - in Michigan on Saturday as early voting begins in the state that helped propel \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to victory in 2016, before Biden took it back in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , who become America\u8217\'20\'19s first black president when he was elected in 2008, campaigned for Harris for the first time, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/10/obama-kamala-harris-pennsylvania-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appearing alone}}}\uc2  in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, in early October. He held a rally for Harris in Las Vegas over the weekend on the first day of early voting in Nevada.\par \par \uc2 As my colleague {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/michael-sainato"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Michael Sainato}}}\uc2  notes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/18/election-michelle-barack-obama-harris-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in this story}}}\uc2 , the Obamas and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris}}}\uc2  have a friendship stretching over two decades.\par \par \uc2 Harris was an early supporter of Obama\u8217\'20\'19s presidential campaign in the closely contested 2008 Democratic presidential primaries, and one of the few elected officials in California to back him over \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  for the party\u8217\'20\'19s nomination.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump allies spending millions to dissuade voters in key states from polls\par \par \uc2 Key rightwing legal groups with ties to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and his allies have banked millions of dollars from conservative foundations and filed multiple lawsuits challenging voting rules in swing states that are already sowing distrust of election processes and pushing dangerous conspiracy theories, election watchdogs warn.\par \par \uc2 They also warn that the groups appear to be laying the groundwork for a concerted challenge to the result of November\u8217\'20\'19s presidential election if Trump is defeated by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 America First Legal and the Public Interest Legal Foundation together reaped more than $30m dollars from the Wisconsin based Bradley Impact Fund and its parent, the Lynde and Harry Bradley Foundation, from 2017 through 2022, according to a financial analysis from the \uc2 Center for Media and Democracy\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Lawsuits filed by the groups, which overlap with some Republican party litigation, focus in part on conspiratorial charges of non-citizen voting, which is exceedingly rare, and bloated voter rolls, and pre-sage more lawsuits by Trump if his presidential run fails, in an echo of his 2020 election-denialist claims, say watchdogs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt seems clear that the lawsuits these rightwing groups are bringing attacking the integrity of the voting rolls, methods of voting and how the ballots are counted are an attempt to make it harder for people to vote, disenfranchise and intimidate legitimate voters, and create confusion,\u8221\'20\'1D said Larry Noble, a former general counsel at the \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Noble added: \u8220\'20\'1CAt the same time, they also appear to be laying the groundwork to challenge the results of the election after November 5, if Trump loses.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can read the full story here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/21/trump-maga-swing-states-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump allies spending millions to dissuade voters in key states from polls}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to campaign in North Carolina as Harris visits three swing states\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/21/kamala-harris-donald-trump-rallies-us-election-politics?filterKeyEvents=false&page=with:block-67161c4c8f08c6f693b79db0#block-67161c4c8f08c6f693b79db0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As we mentioned in the opening summary}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be campaigning in North Carolina \u8211\'20\'13 a crucial swing state \u8211\'20\'13 today.\par \par \uc2 The Republican presidential nominee is visiting the city of Asheville to survey the damage Hurricane Helene brought last month.\par \par \uc2 Communities in western North Carolina have been reeling since the storm ravaged the region, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wxii12.com/article/north-carolina-helene-missing-death-toll-update/62611910"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killing about 100 people}}}\uc2  and destroying homes and causing widespread power outages.\par \par \uc2 Trump has falsely accused \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/113227266617485932"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deliberately diverting assistance away from Republican areas}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As well as visiting Asheville, Trump will be holding a rally in Greenville this afternoon, before attending a meeting of 11th Hour Faith leaders, alongside his son Eric and Dr Ben Carson, the retired {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/lifestyle/style/the-story-of-the-surgery-that-made-ben-carson-famous--and-its-complicated-aftermath/2015/11/13/15b5f900-88c1-11e5-be39-0034bb576eee_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 neurosurgeon}}}\uc2 , former US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/feb/28/ben-carson-housing-department-furniture-inquiry"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 housing secretary}}}\uc2 , in Concord. You can keep up-to-date with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign schedule {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.donaldjtrump.com/events"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , meanwhile, will join Republican Congresswoman and vocal Trump opponent \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  in Chester County, Pennsylvania, for a campaign event before heading to Waukesha County, Wisconsin, and Oakland County, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 There are mounting concerns from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Republican allies that crippling damage from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hurricane-helene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Helene}}}\uc2  will depress turnout in the battleground state\u8217\'20\'19s conservative mountain regions.\par \par \uc2 Trump won about 62% of the vote in 2020 in the 25 counties declared to be a disaster area after Helene, while Biden won about 51% in the remainder of the state. New emergency {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncsbe.gov/news/press-releases/2024/10/07/bipartisan-state-board-unanimously-approves-measures-help-wnc-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voting arrangements}}}\uc2  have been put in place by the state board of election covering some of the most devastated counties.\par \par \uc2 The Hill/Decision Desk HQ\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://elections2024.thehill.com/forecast/2024/president/north-carolina/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling average}}}\uc2  shows North Carolina is too tight to call with confidence, with Harris, the US vice president and Democratic nominee, trailing behind Trump by 0.7 percentage points.\par \par \uc2 More than one million North Carolinians have already voted in the November general election, according to estimates. More than 400 early voting sites opened as scheduled on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37am BST\par \par \uc2 New finance filings show Harris campaign's huge financial advantage in presidential race\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign reported raising $221.8m (\u163\'00\'A3170.4m) in September, compared to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign raising $62.7m (\u163\'00\'A348.2m), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/10/21/kamala-harris-trump-fundraising-advantage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reported}}}\uc2  after new federal campaign finance filings showed her huge financial advantage in the final weeks of the presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2  filings, released yesterday, also showed that the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  raised $98.6m (\u163\'00\'A376m) last month, compared to the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2  raising $37.8m (\u163\'00\'A329m).\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  reported:\par \par \uc2 New reports filed on Tuesday showed that Harris\u8217\'20\'19s primary fundraising vehicle for big-dollar donations, the Harris Victory Fund, brought in a staggering $633m (\u163\'00\'A3486m) during the third quarter. That was more than four times as much as the $145m (\u163\'00\'A3111m) that the victory fund\u8217\'20\'19s GOP counterpart, the Trump 47 committee, brought in, according to reports filed last week.\par \par \uc2 Despite that huge spending edge and Harris\u8217\'20\'19s sprawling ground game, her campaign has still struggled to significantly outpace Trump in key swing state polls. The vice president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has a much larger footprint than Trump\u8217\'20\'19s, which relies on outside groups to help it turn out voters, and her advisers are worried about whether they will have enough money to secure victory. Harris\u8217\'20\'19s advisers believe that the race remains close in all of the key swing states, and point to the high cost of targeting hard-to-reach and infrequent voters in seven very different states.\par \par \uc2 Harris is running a campaign that is about three times the size of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s operation, spending more money on ads and having more staff, volunteers and a larger surrogate operation than her Republican opponent, according to a \uc2 Washington Post\uc2  analysis of campaign spending.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.18am BST\par \par \uc2 The US defence secretary, \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2 , is making an unexpected visit to Ukraine today to reaffirm Washington\u8217\'20\'19s support of Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  when he meets him later.\par \par \uc2 Austin is also expected to meet his Ukrainian counterpart, Rustem Umerov. US backing is crucial if Kyiv is to get support from other allies for proposals Zelenskyy believes are necessary to strengthen Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s position on the battlefield and ahead of any peace negotiations.\par \par \uc2 There are concerns that a second Trump administration could suspend military support for Kyiv, at a time when Ukraine is in desperate need for financial support and military equipment, much of which is supplied by the US. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  seems set to follow \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policy towards Ukraine, supplying Kyiv with military aid and supporting them diplomatically. She has ruled out meeting one-on-one with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  to negotiate an end to the war in Ukraine unless leaders from Kyiv are involved.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been absolutely remarkable that Ukraine has been able to do what it\u8217\'20\'19s done,\u8221\'20\'1D Austin told reporters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been able to do that, of course, because of the fact that we have supported them from the very beginning, and we\u8217\'20\'19ve rallied some 50 countries to be a part of that support,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 enltrKYIV\u8212\'20\'14Secretary Austin has just arrived in Kyiv for meetings with President Zelensky and Defense Minister Umerov. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/B3d8BaVCoO"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/B3d8BaVCoO}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Natasha Bertrand (@NatashaBertrand) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NatashaBertrand/status/1848237986111950854?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 21, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's language 'demeans office of the presidency'\par \par \uc2 Good morning, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2  readers.\par \par \uc2 There are now only 15 days to go until voting day and the attacks traded between the two presidential candidates \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (D) and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  (R) \u8211\'20\'13 are intensifying. On Sunday, Harris celebrated her 60th birthday and gave an interview with Rev \uc2 Al Sharpton\uc2  on MSNBC.\par \par \uc2 Sharpton asked her about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/20/us-presidential-election-trump-harris-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump calling her a \u8220\'20\'1Cshit vice-president\u8221\'20\'1D at a rally in Latrobe}}}\uc2 , Pennsylvania, on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Harris, who became the first black vice-president and woman in the role after \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  defeated Trump in the 2020 presidential election, responded:\par \par \uc2 The American people deserve so much better. That is how I come at it. And to your point, the President of the United States must set a standard \u8211\'20\'13 not only for our nation but understanding the standard we as a nation must set for the world.\par \par \uc2 We representing the United States of America walk into rooms around the world with the earned and self-appointed authority to talk about the importance of democracy, of rule of law and have been thought of as a role model \u8230\'20\'26 of what it means to be committed to certain standards, including international rules and norms, but also standards of decorum.\par \par \uc2 And what you see in my opponent, a former President of the United States, demeans the office. And I have said \u8211\'20\'13 and I am very clear about this \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should never again stand behind the seal of the President of the United States. He has not earned the right \u8230\'20\'26 and that is why he is going to lose.\par \par \uc2 enltrVice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheRevAl?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @TheRevAl}}}\uc2  during an exclusive interview that the president of the United States must set a standard for the world and what we see in Trump, "demeans the office."\par \par \uc2 Watch the full interview today at 5pm ET on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PoliticsNation?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @PoliticsNation}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/SXhha8ibGw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/SXhha8ibGw}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 MSNBC (@MSNBC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MSNBC/status/1848081356145807762?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 20, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The presidential race is essentially deadlocked, both nationally and in so-called battleground states. The contest on 5 November will be decided by the slimmest of margins. In order to appeal to voters in the critical swing states (Arizona, Georgia, Michigan, Nevada, North Carolina, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin), both Trump and Harris are trying to appeal to moderate, swing voters and ensure their bases are enthused enough to go out and vote.\par \par \uc2 Later today, Harris will be targeting suburban Pennsylvania, Michigan and Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 holding a series of conversations with Republican \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  that will be moderated by Republican strategist Sarah Longwell and conservative radio host Charlie Sykes.\par \par \uc2 Trump has three North Carolina stops on Monday, including a visit to see storm damage in Asheville. He beat Biden in the state by 1.3% in 2020, but the polls this year are extremely tight, giving the Democrats a rare chance of winning the state.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241021ekal0018w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
