\par\par \uc2 Global development\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18One-man anti- \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  army\u8217\'20\'19: shadow of US global gag rule looms over Nepal\u8217\'20\'19s family planning services\b0\par\par\uc2 Pete Pattisson in Beni \par \uc2 1,074 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 October 2024\par 04:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Since the country legalised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , maternal mortality rates have plummeted. But US-funded programmes and a Trump victory could reverse that progress, warn experts\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne, two, three,\u8221\'20\'1D says Soman Rai slowly, to the click of his fingers. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery three seconds a baby dies by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . One, two, three,\u8221\'20\'1D he repeats. Behind him, the word \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D is projected on to a screen in a red font that drips down the slide to resemble blood. Underneath is written: \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is world history\u8217\'20\'19s greatest genocide.\par \par \uc2 It is an uncompromising message in an unlikely location; a church in a remote valley in Nepal.\par \par \uc2 A self-proclaimed \u8220\'20\'1Cone-man army\u8221\'20\'1D, Rai says he has been taking his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  message to more than 30,000 people across Nepal since he founded his organisation, Voice of Fetus Nepal, in 2009.\par \par \uc2 As an audience of about 65 gathers for his talk in the church in Beni, a small town in the foothills of the Himalayas, they greet each other with \u8220\'20\'1C Jay Mashiah \u8221\'20\'1D, meaning \u8220\'20\'1Cpraise the Lord\u8221\'20\'1D, instead of the traditional namaste. While Rai speaks to schools and colleges, the focus of his work is among Nepal\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2017/aug/15/they-use-money-to-promote-christianity-nepal-battle-for-souls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 growing Christian community}}}\uc2 , who eagerly embrace his anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pitch.\par \par \uc2 Rai speaks with the fluency and confidence of an evangelical preacher, taking his mostly female audience on an emotional journey. His message is built on the belief that life begins at the moment of conception, and underpinned by the teachings of the Bible. Instead of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Rai promotes parenting, adoption and abstinence.\par \par \uc2 If his argument sounds familiar it is because his work is \u8211\'20\'13 at least partly \u8211\'20\'13 funded by anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Christian groups in the US and draws heavily on their messaging and methods.\par \par \uc2 Rai\u8217\'20\'19s preaching comes at a time when providers of women\u8217\'20\'19s healthcare around the world are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/article/2024/aug/16/global-health-charities-warning-threat-global-gag-rule-abortion-rights-family-planning-women-trump-project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 preparing for potentially disastrous consequences}}}\uc2  should Donald Trump win the US presidential election in November. When he last took office in 2017, one of his first acts was to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2017/jul/21/trump-global-death-warrant-women-family-planning-population-reproductive-rights-mexico-city-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reinstate, and later expand, an order known as the Mexico City policy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 US law has long prohibited the use of foreign aid for abortions, but the policy also bars foreign organisations that receive US family planning funds from providing advice on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services or advocating for the liberalisation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws, even if they do so using funds from other sources.\par \par \uc2 Trump greatly expanded the policy so it applies to any organisation receiving US healthcare funding. Foreign organisations wishing to access this funding must sign up to the policy, which is often referred to as the global gag rule (GGR) because of the restrictions it places on organisations to even discuss the option of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Nepal first legalised \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2002 and today women have the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to 12 weeks of pregnancy and in limited circumstances up to 28 weeks. The legalisation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been credited with contributing to a 72% fall in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://mohp.gov.np/uploads/Resources/Final%20Report-26%20March-%202023-UPDATED.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 maternal mortality rates}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 from 539 deaths for every 100,000 live births in 1996 to 151 in 2022.\par \par \uc2 It takes guts for a woman to come here. Some communities believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is wrong. Pre-marital sex is not acceptable\par \par \uc2 Puja Karki, MSI Nepal\par \par \uc2 Those gains are being put at risk by the GGR, say experts. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://crehpa.org.np/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/Impacts-of-PLGHA-Policy-in-Nepal_CREHPA-2020-2021.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study on the impact of the policy in Nepal}}}\uc2  by the Center for Research on Environment, Health and Population Activities (Crehpa), a Nepali organisation, found that it had \u8220\'20\'1Ccreated a major obstacle to improving women\u8217\'20\'19s lives\u8221\'20\'1D, in particular among \u8220\'20\'1Cmarginalised and underserved populations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Since the GGR was first introduced by Ronald Reagan in 1984, successive Republican administrations have imposed it, while the Democrats have revoked it, leaving family planning organisations such as MSI Nepal (formerly \uc2 Marie Stopes International\uc2 ) \u8211\'20\'13 which refuses to sign it \u8211\'20\'13 caught in a cycle of funding and defunding.\par \par \uc2 The consequences have been dire, says Tushar Niroula, the executive director of MSI Nepal. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can\u8217\'20\'19t strengthen the health system in four years and then stop for four years. Next time you have to start from scratch.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Niroula says his organisation had to shut down projects soon after the Trump administration took office, due to cuts in funding. \u8220\'20\'1CThere was a huge gap overnight,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 The prospect of a Trump victory in November is already hampering MSI Nepal\u8217\'20\'19s work. Members of a consortium bidding for US healthcare funding have been reluctant to collaborate with MSI Nepal because its refusal to sign the GGR could put the whole bid at risk, says Niroula.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 US government\uc2  funding is huge and extends for five to six years, which is enough time to build systems and make them sustainable. That is why the global gag rule is such a barrier,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 Puja Karki sees what is at stake every day in her role as team leader at MSI Nepal\u8217\'20\'19s clinic in Pokhara, a city about a three-hour drive from Beni.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a big deal for a woman to come here, it takes guts,\u8221\'20\'1D says Karki. \u8220\'20\'1CSome communities do not accept family planning and they believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is wrong. Pre-marital sex is not acceptable, so unmarried women are afraid of taking up the service.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Karki says a combination of social stigma, lack of awareness and difficulties accessing family planning services puts women at severe risk. Some turn to \u8220\'20\'1Cunsafe and unauthorised places for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D, says Karki, or attempt to abort themselves using traditional herbs or a sharpened stick.\par \par \uc2 While there is limited accurate and recent data, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5568822/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a study by Crehpa}}}\uc2  estimated that in 2014 almost 60% of abortions in Nepal were carried out illegally, meaning they took place at unapproved facilities in potentially unsafe conditions. Another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nepal.ipas.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/Research-brief-4-NEW-June-7-2023.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study put the figure at 52%}}}\uc2  in 2021.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe main challenge is they lack awareness of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in rural areas. They do not know how to access proper services,\u8221\'20\'1D says Karki. \u8220\'20\'1CMany are not even aware that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That challenge is only likely to grow under a second Trump presidency, but that does not seem to concern Rai. Although he says he does explain the law in his talks, he adds that if Nepali women do not know that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is legal, \u8220\'20\'1Cthat is good news for me\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Asked if he would prefer Donald Trump to win the election, Rai replies, \u8220\'20\'1COf course.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241021ekal000b8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
