\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  hold dueling rallies in swing-state Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Johana Bhuiyan, Chris Stein, Anna Betts and Daniel Lavelle \par \uc2 9,630 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 October 2024\par 01:37 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog has now closed. Read our latest story hereDon\u8217\'20\'19t miss important US election news. Get our free app and sign up for election alerts\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35am BST\par \par \uc2 That's it for today\par \par \uc2 With just 18 days until election day, both presidential candidates had a busy day campaigning across Michigan. The day ended with Trump taking the stage at a Detroit rally and Harris speaking from Oakland County, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, a federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-67127f788f08d025c3e953ad#block-67127f788f08d025c3e953ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed the release}}}\uc2  of hundreds of documents used in special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election subversion case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but the majority of them are redacted. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-671284958f08d025c3e9542f#block-671284958f08d025c3e9542f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What we can see}}}\uc2  mostly concerns the legal strategy Trump and his allies concocted to block \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from taking the White House, which may be presented to jurors whenever the case goes to trial. Meanwhile, reports have emerged that Trump has canceled interviews because he is \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-671262f38f08c6f693b783c7#block-671262f38f08c6f693b783c7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exhausted}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 something his campaign denies \u8211\'20\'13 and is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-671250b88f08ea656ca1cedf#block-671250b88f08ea656ca1cedf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considering holding a town hall}}}\uc2  with one-time rival \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  in a bid to woo female voters.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-67127cc28f08d025c3e9537a#block-67127cc28f08d025c3e9537a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that some of the jokes he told at last night\u8217\'20\'19s Al Smith dinner were written by employees of conservative network Fox \u8211\'20\'13 a breach of ethics, if confirmed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Frank-Walter Steinmeier\uc2 , the president of Germany, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-671271d18f08d025c3e952ab#block-671271d18f08d025c3e952ab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  in unusually direct terms of the threat Trump could pose if returned to the White House, during a visit by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to the country.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-671277698f08156d15775acb#block-671277698f08156d15775acb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enlisted}}}\uc2  singer-songwriter Marc Anthony for a campaign ad aimed at Latino voters in which he condemns Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments about Puerto Rico.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A House oversight committee report accused Trump of exploiting tax payer money by charging Secret Service agents and other federal officials higher-than-normal rates at his DC hotel.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump hit back on reports that he\u8217\'20\'19s too tired to attend events.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An unnamed White House employee told an investigator for the January 6 committee that Trump watched the attack on the Capitol unfold from a White House dining room while drinking a Diet Coke. The detail was included in hundreds of pages of mostly redacted documents in the federal case against Trump for trying to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 Signing off.\par \par \uc2 Johana Bhuiyan, Diana Ramirez-Simon, Chris Stein, Anna Betts and Daniel Lavelle\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris wrapped up her speech reminding her Detroit audience of about 3,500 to vote. In Michigan, early voting for most jurisdictions begins 26 October. For Detroit, it begins on 19 October. \u8220\'20\'1COur vote is our voice and your voice is your power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is concluding his rally with a reminder of his campaign promises.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn conclusion, with your vote this November we are going to fire Kamala and we are going to save America. We will teach our children to love our country honor our history\u8230\'20\'26we will cut your taxes, crush inflation, slash your prices, raise your wages and create the greatest job boom the world has ever seen\u8230\'20\'26we will do that very easily.\par \par \uc2 We will hire American, buy American, build American, grow American and show the whole world the American dream is back.\par \par \uc2 I will stop the global theft of American jobs. I will turn America into the manufacturing superpower of the world. I will end the war in Ukraine immediately\u8230\'20\'26stop the chaos in the Middle East and prevent World War 3. We are very close to World War 3\u8230\'20\'26because we have incompetent people.\par \par \uc2 I will crush violent crime and give our police the\u8230\'20\'26support that they so dearly deserve. We will strengthen and modernize our military\u8230\'20\'26you know I rebuilt our military. We will build a missile defense shield all made in the USA. And we will put the stars and stripes on the surface of Mars and maybe with the help of Elon we\u8217\'20\'19ll get it done quickly. We\u8217\'20\'19ll rebuild our cities including our capital in Washington DC. We will get\u8230\'20\'26and remember this one, we will get critical race theory and transgender insanity the hell out of our schools.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut for that to happen we must defeat \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8230\'20\'26we want a landslide and it looks like that could be happening,\u8221\'20\'1D he ended.\par \par \uc2 He closed out his rally by clapping and dancing to YMCA by the Village People.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.16am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says she will 'proudly sign in to law' a bill restoring reproductive freedoms\par \par \uc2 Harris went in on outlining her other policies and criticizing Trump for having only \u8220\'20\'1Cconcepts of a plan\u8221\'20\'1D to which the audience echoes \u8220\'20\'1CConcepts!\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She emphasizes her fight for freedom, especially in relation to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, describing the downfall of Roe v Wade and vowing that when a bill restoring national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights comes across her desk she will \u8220\'20\'1Cproudly sign it in to law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris rehashed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s job losses in Michigan, calling him \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the biggest losers of manufacturing jobs in American history\u8221\'20\'1D. She reminded her supporters of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s broken promises over losing auto plants during his presidency, resulting in \u8220\'20\'1Cthousands of Michigan auto workers losing their jobs\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She says Trump is making the same empty promises that he made before. \u8220\'20\'1CBut we\u8217\'20\'19re not falling for the okey doke. And we won\u8217\'20\'19t be fooled!\u8221\'20\'1D she said as the crowd hollers \u8220\'20\'1CNooo!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris vows to her Detroit audience to invest in American manufacturing and industry such as steel, iron and the auto industry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd contrary to what my opponent is suggesting, I will never tell you what kind of car you have to drive\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, addressing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claim that her administration would \u8220\'20\'1Cmandate\u8221\'20\'1D electric vehicles.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump called for the death penalty for any migrant who kills an American citizen or a law enforcement officer.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump said that his administration will also restore the US borders.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s the worst thing that has happened to us. 21 million people. When I win on November 5, the migrant invasion ends and the restoration of our country begins. I have no choice.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/06/28/nx-s1-5021996/presidential-debate-fact-check-immigration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2  about the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s immigration policies have been previously debunked. For instance, Trump claims the Biden administration opened the borders but in fact the administration increased the number of expedited removals and added more sections to the U.S. Southern border walls.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.northwestern.edu/stories/2024/03/immigrants-are-significantly-less-likely-to-commit-crimes-than-the-us-born/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 study}}}\uc2  that looked at 150 years of census data has also shown that despite Trump\u8217\'20\'19s claims, the vast majority of immigrants do not commit crimes and are significantly less likely to commit crimes than those born in the US.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump has addressed a few topics in a span of a few minutes. Trump addressed what he calls an electric vehicle \u8220\'20\'1Cmandate\u8221\'20\'1D that the Biden administration has set. However, the administration has set no such requirement. They have set a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2023/04/17/fact-sheet-biden-harris-administration-announces-new-private-and-public-sector-investments-for-affordable-electric-vehicles/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 goal}}}\uc2  of having 50% of car sales be electric vehicles by 2030.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn day 1 of the Trump administration I will terminate Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s insane electric vehicle mandate and we will end the green new scam once and for all. We will quickly become energy independent and we will frack, frack, frack and drill, baby, drill. I will cut your energy prices in half within 12 months of taking office. That\u8217\'20\'19s going to bring everything down. I will massively cut taxes for workers and we will also have no tax on tips, no tax on overtime and no tax on social security benefits for our seniors.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Back at the Harris rally, she says, \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m gonna just go off script for a moment.\u8221\'20\'1D She begins to talk about the difficulties of taking care of an aging relative and the financial toll it can take.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy plan is to fix Medicare to cover the home health costs for seniors because it\u8217\'20\'19s about dignity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.06am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the worst mic I\u8217\'20\'19ve ever had in my life,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump quipped.\par \par \uc2 After playing two campaign videos, Trump calls \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  the \u8220\'20\'1Ctax queen\u8221\'20\'1D and claims her tax proposals will kill \u8220\'20\'1Calmost a million full-time jobs\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CIt will be economic armageddon for Detroit,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s microphone is working again.\par \par \uc2 He\u8217\'20\'19s talking about his \u8220\'20\'1Cbuild it in America plan\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen CEOs call me to complain about my tariffs, my answer will be very simple, build it in America. And to be specific, build it in Detroit, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll give you good electricity.\par \par \uc2 His plan is to impose tariffs on companies to discourage them from building manufacturing plants outside of America.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe centerpiece of his plan will be a 15% made in America corporate tax rate. So we brought the rate down from close to 40% to 21%\u8230\'20\'26now we\u8217\'20\'19re going to get it down to 15% but only if they build it in America,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CFor those who don\u8217\'20\'19t make their product in America they will be forced to pay tariffs.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris is back.\par \par \uc2 She begins again, starting with addressing the devastation in Gaza and Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI know this year has been very difficult, given the scale of death and destruction in Gaza and given the civilian casualties and displacement in Lebanon. It is devastating. And now Sinwar\u8217\'20\'19s death must be a turning point. Everyone must seize this opportunity to end the war in Gaza. Bring the hostages home. And end the suffering once and for all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  takes the stage at Oakland County rally\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  began by thanking the members of the Arab- American communities at the rally.\par \par \uc2 Harris, however, suddenly stopped her remarks to call for a medic. Harris made a few comments about it being warm in the room.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.11am BST\par \par \uc2 While Trump waits for the technical difficulties to be fixed, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is taking the stage at her dueling rally in Oakland County, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is indeed on stage at the rally but there are technical difficulties with the microphone it turns out. He began speaking but the sound cut out and he\u8217\'20\'19s now standing around as the crowd cheers for him.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump takes stage in Detroit, days after criticizing the city\par \par \uc2 Trump takes the stage in Michigan with his usual self-confidence, acknowledging the cheers of the crowd who are waving \u8220\'20\'1CMake Detroit Great Again\u8221\'20\'1D signs. \u8220\'20\'1CWe win Michigan, we win the whole ballgame,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, as he\u8217\'20\'19s promised every other city he\u8217\'20\'19s visited lately.\par \par \uc2 However on his previous visit to the city, he bashed it as a \u8220\'20\'1Cmess\u8221\'20\'1D and a \u8220\'20\'1Cdeveloping nation\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1COur whole country will end up being like Detroit if she\u8217\'20\'19s your president. You\u8217\'20\'19re going to have a mess on your hands,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, referring to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump surrogates who have spoken before \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  takes the stage have all hit on talking points we\u8217\'20\'19ve heard repeatedly throughout his campaign. In addition to getting back jobs for American workers, including auto workers, and rising costs of living, nearly everyone who has taken the stage has decried what they describe as mass illegal immigration. They also made promises to Detroit residents specifically.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDetroit once was the city that powered the entire world, every car worth driving in the entire world was manufactured here,\u8221\'20\'1D said former Trump adviser \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CNot in Mexico, not in China, not in Japan. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a plan to make Detroit and to make Michigan the economic center of the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 However, just last week, Trump criticized the city during a speech at the Detroit Economic Club.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe whole country will be like \u8212\'20\'14 you want to know the truth? It\u8217\'20\'19ll be like Detroit,\u8221\'20\'1D the Republican presidential nominee said. \u8220\'20\'1COur whole country will end up being like Detroit if she\u8217\'20\'19s your president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the time, Detroit\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic mayor \uc2 Mike Duggan\uc2  responded and cited the city\u8217\'20\'19s recent drop in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/detroit-crime-homicides-partnership-67d34ceeec87b9d3aecd35884cbd5c5e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 crime}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLots of cities should be like Detroit. And we did it all without Trump\u8217\'20\'19s help,\u8221\'20\'1D Duggan said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.34am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is slated to speak at a rally in Detroit in a few minutes. Follow along {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Wn4j7E66vU8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  spent the last few minutes of his round table in Michigan talking about returning jobs to American auto workers , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is reminding auto workers what he\u8217\'20\'19s previously said about their work.\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/live-updates/2024/10/15/2024-elections-live-coverage-updates-analysis/harris-in-michigan-00184456"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Politico}}}\uc2 , at a campaign event at the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  Local 652 in Lansing, Harris played the room full of auto workers remarks Trump made earlier this week at the Economic Club of Chicago. In addition to saying a child could do their jobs, Trump said car manufacturers \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t build cars\u8221\'20\'1D and just \u8220\'20\'1Ctake them out of a box, and they assemble them\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Both candidates are fighting to win over auto workers as well as working class voters in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 The round table has concluded. He ended the event by talking about tariffs in response to a \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  member. He said he plans to use tariffs to discourage people from building plants in other countries and taking jobs from American workers.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be speaking at a rally in Detroit at 7pm. Stay tuned for more updates.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is hearing from audience members in Michigan. Among them have been a Teamster representative as well as a holistic wellness practitioner and the president of the Police Officers Association of Michigan.\par \par \uc2 Jim Tignanelli\uc2 , the group\u8217\'20\'19s president, described what he says is the loss of honor for police. He said three officers were shot in Michigan over the last 90 days.\par \par \uc2 In response, Trump said he wants to call for the death penalty for anyone killing a police officer. Trump also called for qualified immunity for police. \u8220\'20\'1COne thing we\u8217\'20\'19re going to be doing is \u8230\'20\'26 immunity for some of these police,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf police officers are doing their job \u8230\'20\'26 if they make a mistake, and that happens \u8230\'20\'26 we have to help people out now. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to do the immunity thing. We have to stop being politically correct. You\u8217\'20\'19re always going to have some bad apples but very few of them,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is speaking at a roundtable in Auburn Hills, Michigan\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  started the conversation by again criticizing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19 decision not to attend the \uc2 Alfred E Smith Memorial Foundation\uc2  Dinner, which raises funds for Catholic charities.\par \par \uc2 You can follow along {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?539309-1/president-trump-holds-roundtable-detroit-michigan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Upon landing in Michigan, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  touted the support he\u8217\'20\'19s received from the Arab-American community after many have expressed disappointment in how the Biden administration has responded to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s assault on Gaza. Just last month, Trump was endorsed by Amer Ghalib, the Democratic mayor of Michigan suburb, Hamtramck. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/hamtramck-donald-trump-arab-american-muslim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Forty percent}}}\uc2  of Hamtramck\u8217\'20\'19s residents are of Middle Eastern or North African descent.\par \par \uc2 But minutes later, Trump said that he planned to speak with the Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  and tell him that \u8220\'20\'1Che\u8217\'20\'19s doing a good job\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[Biden] is trying to hold him back,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said to reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CThey probably should be doing the opposite. I\u8217\'20\'19m glad that Bibi decided to do what he had to do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump says he's about to speak to Netanyahu and says, "Biden is trying to hold him back... he probably should be doing the opposite, actually." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/i12koY0z1s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/i12koY0z1s}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1847354656273334780?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 A new investigation by 404 Media found that an \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  -funded PAC called Future Coalition is targeting Muslim and Jewish populations in Michigan and Pennsylvania with extremely contradictory ads.\par \par \uc2 The ads are being delivered to \uc2 Snapchat\uc2  users and targeting them by zip code. Those who live in an area with a large Muslim population in Michigan are being served ads that paint \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as pro-Israel while those who live in parts of Pennsylvania that have a high percentage of Jewish residents are seeing ads that says Harris stands with Palestine.\par \par \uc2 You can read the investigation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.404media.co/this-is-exactly-how-an-elon-musk-funded-pac-is-microtargeting-muslims-and-jews-with-opposing-messages/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump rejects claim he is exhausted and has canceled events\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile in Michigan, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  answered questions from the press and denied reports that he\u8217\'20\'19s exhausted and canceling events.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat event did I cancel,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/TrumpWarRoom/status/1847362851234861341"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI haven\u8217\'20\'19t canceled. She doesn\u8217\'20\'19t go to any events. She\u8217\'20\'19s a loser. She didn\u8217\'20\'19t even show up for the Catholics last night at the hotel. It was insulting. All they are is soundbites.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump said he has gone 48 days without a rest. \u8220\'20\'1CTell me when you\u8217\'20\'19ve seen me take even a little bit of a rest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 According to a new House oversight committee report that accuses \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  of fleecing tax payers and exploiting the presidency, former president Trump charged secret service agents who were staying at his hotel while protecting him far more than the hotel charged private patrons.\par \par \uc2 The report says Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cturned the \uc2 U.S. Secret Service\uc2  into an ATM for his personal enrichment\u8221\'20\'1D by charging the agency, in at least one case, more than 5 times the rate approved by the government. \u8220\'20\'1CAmazingly, that same night, the Trump International Hotel in Washington, D.C., rented out more than 200 rooms to private parties at just $125 or $170 each.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The report goes onto say that at least five people who received pardons from Trump as well as four federal judges who Trump nominated and were later given lifetime appointments also stayed at the hotel.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversightdemocrats.house.gov/sites/evo-subsites/democrats-oversight.house.gov/files/evo-media-document/2024-10-18COA-DEM-Staff-Report-Domestic-Emoluments.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  also details startling instances in which state and federal officials, as well as individuals actively seeking federal jobs and presidential pardons, used the D.C. hotel as a channel to put money into the Commander-in-Chief\u8217\'20\'19s pocket,\u8221\'20\'1D Rep resentative Jamie Raskin said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hey all, Johana Bhuiyan taking over from my colleague, Chris.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19ll be tuning into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s speech in Michigan which starts at 5pm ET but in the meantime I\u8217\'20\'19m going through a new {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://oversightdemocrats.house.gov/news/press-releases/oversight-democrats-new-report-proves-trump-used-his-dc-hotel-take"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  from the House committee on oversight and accountability.\par \par \uc2 Citing hotel guest logs, the report claims Trump used his DC hotel to take \u8220\'20\'1Cethically questionable payments\u8221\'20\'1D from the \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2 , federal and state officials, federal job seekers as well as people seeking a federal pardon during his presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese payments demonstrate how \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  violated the Constitution\u8217\'20\'19s Domestic Emoluments Clause as he used the Secret Service as his personal ATM and repeatedly took payments that raise the specter of pay-to-play corruption from individuals who sought and, in many cases obtained, favors from the Commander-in-Chief,\u8221\'20\'1D the press release read.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris announces events with Barack, \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  as early voting begins in key states\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will campaign alongside \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  in two separate events next week aimed at encouraging voting in swing states, the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s campaign said.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Harris and \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  will campaign in Atlanta, with the goal of encouraging supporters to take advantage of the early voting period. The vice-president will then head to Michigan on Saturday, the first day of early voting in that state, for an event with \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has meanwhile arrived in Michigan, ahead of his 5pm campaign event in Detroit.\par \par \uc2 His campaign is sharing photos and video of him taking questions from reporters upon his arrival, saying it\u8217\'20\'19s not the sort of thing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  would do:\par \par \uc2 enltrPresident {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  lands in Michigan and takes questions from the press ????\par \par \uc2 You\u8217\'20\'19ll never see Kamala do this! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ij7iOI8vKZ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Ij7iOI8vKZ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Margo Martin (@margommartin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/margommartin/status/1847356849324015908?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Reporters traveling with the vice-president to Grand Rapids said she spoke to them before going onstage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 A key message of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to voters in Michigan today was encouraging them to cast ballots when early voting begins next Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CElection Day is in 18 short days, okay? And here in Michigan, early voting starts on Saturday, October 26, which is one week from tomorrow,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said as she concluded her speech.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow is the time to make your plan to vote. Make a plan.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Unions have long played an outsized role in Michigan, particularly when it comes to its automotive industry.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has focused much of her speech on how she would be more friendly to organized labor than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMake no mistake, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is no friend of labor,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president said. She continued:\par \par \uc2 He encouraged automakers to move their plants out of Michigan so he could pay they could pay their workers less. Understand what that was about, so they could pay their workers less. And when the [\uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2 ] went on strike to demand the higher wages they deserved, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  went to a non-union shop and attacked the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , and he said, he said, striking and collective bargaining don\u8217\'20\'19t make \u8216\'20\'18a damn bit of sense\u8217\'20\'19.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CStrong unions mean higher wages, better healthcare and greater dignity for union members and for everyone, whether or not you are part of a union: get that straight,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris whacks Trump over reports he canceled interviews due to 'exhaustion'\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  seized on reports that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had backed out of interviews because he was \u8220\'20\'1Cexhausted\u8221\'20\'1D, saying that they were proof he is not up to the job of being president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe has no plan for how he would address the needs of the American people, and he is, as we have seen, only focused on himself, and now he is ducking debates and canceling interviews,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told the crowd in Grand Rapids, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd check this out. His own campaign team recently said it is because of exhaustion. Well, if you are exhausted on the campaign trail, it raises real questions about whether you are fit for the toughest job in the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is on stage now, with familiar walk-out song Freedom by Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9 playing.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president was introduced by carpenters union official Brian Hein, who decried \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as someone \u8220\'20\'1Cwho has never done a hard day\u8217\'20\'19s work in his life\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to campaign in hotly contested Michigan\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is soon to begin speaking in Grand Rapids, Michigan, as she looks for an edge among voters in a swing state that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is looking to reclaim.\par \par \uc2 The western Michigan city lies in historically Republican territory where Democrats have only recently begun showing strength. From a stage set up in a park, the vice-president was introduced by Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic governor \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 , who said:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has shown us that he is incapable of handling a crisis. He is a petty man who tells dangerous lies and is always looking for someone else to blame. We don\u8217\'20\'19t need that. We need leaders who are going to put politics aside and work together to solve problems. As our next commander-in-chief, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will ask, what do you need? How can I help you? Are you okay? That\u8217\'20\'19s what a leader does.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House employee said Trump watched January 6 attack while drinking Diet Coke\par \par \uc2 An unnamed White House employee told an investigator for the January 6 committee that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  watched the attack on the Capitol unfold from a White House dining room while drinking a Diet Coke.\par \par \uc2 The detail was included in hundreds of pages of mostly redacted documents in the federal case against Trump for trying to overturn the 2020 election, which a federal judge allowed to be released today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re rioting down at the Capitol\u8221\'20\'1D, the employee recalls telling Trump in an interview with an unnamed investigator.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COh, really?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump replied.\par \par \uc2 The employee recalls going with Trump to the dining room where he often spent time, and where a television was set up:\par \par \uc2 And then we walked back to the back. I\u8217\'20\'19m taking off his outer coat that he\u8217\'20\'19s wearing right now, and I get the TV, like, ready for him, and I hand him over the remote, and he starts watching it. And I stepped out to get him a Diet Coke, come back in and that\u8217\'20\'19s pretty much it for me as he\u8217\'20\'19s watching and, like, seeing it for himself.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 A federal judge blocked an effort by authorities in Florida to keep off the air a television advertisement in support of the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access ballot initiative, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/carter-sherman"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Carter Sherman}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s health department\uc2  can\u8217\'20\'19t block a TV advertisement in support of a ballot measure that would protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a federal judge ruled on Thursday, after the department sent letters to local TV stations commanding them to stop airing the ad or risk criminal consequences.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe government cannot excuse its indirect censorship of political speech simply by declaring the disfavored speech is \u8216\'20\'18false\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D US district judge Mark E Walker wrote in his ruling. \u8220\'20\'1CTo keep it simple for the State of Florida: it\u8217\'20\'19s the First Amendment, stupid.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/election-abortion-ballot-measures-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida is one of 10 states}}}\uc2  set to vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures in November. If enacted, Florida\u8217\'20\'19s measure would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution and roll back the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban on the procedure, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/florida-abortion-ban-clinic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which took effect in May}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s health department{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/09/florida-news-abortion-ballot-coverage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent cease-and-desist letters}}}\uc2  to TV stations running an ad by Floridians Protecting Freedom, the campaign behind the measure. In the ad, a woman named Caroline speaks about being diagnosed with cancer while pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe doctors knew if I did not end my pregnancy, I would lose my baby, I would lose my life and my daughter would lose her mom,\u8221\'20\'1D Caroline says in the ad. \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida has now banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even in cases like mine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/18/florida-abortion-ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge slaps down Florida effort to ban \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ad: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s the first amendment, stupid\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will be hosting a campaign rally in Atlanta, Georgia on Saturday, where she will be joined by singer Usher, her campaign said.\par \par \uc2 This comes as the \uc2 Democratic National Committee{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://democrats.org/news/dnc-rolls-out-youth-voter-campaign-at-taylor-swifts-miami-concert-and-in-the-battlegrounds-with-new-snapchat-filter-and-ads-directing-to-iwillvote-com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced }}}\uc2  today that it is launching a \uc2 Taylor Swift\uc2 -themed \u8220\'20\'1CI Will Vote\u8221\'20\'1D campaign to increase engagement among young voters in battleground states.\par \par \uc2 The campaign will kick off in Miami, the DNC said, with billboards around the city, a mobile billboard on a boat near Taylor Swift\u8217\'20\'19s concert venue in Miami where the singer is playing this weekend, and exclusive \uc2 Snapchat\uc2  filters.\par \par \uc2 Rosemary Boeglin, DNC Communications Director, said in a statement that Democrats \u8220\'20\'1C are reaching out to young voters where they are, from concert venues to social media platforms, to make sure they have the resources they need to cast their ballot.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrForever & always reaching voters where they are ?? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ThDJKpibik"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ThDJKpibik}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Democrats (@TheDemocrats) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheDemocrats/status/1847303414436266212?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will be visiting Asheville, North Carolina on Monday to see the devastation of Hurricane Helene first-hand and deliver remarks, his campaign announced on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Hurricane Helene made landfall in Florida three weeks ago, before moving across parts of the south-east, quickly becoming the deadliest hurricane to hit the US mainland since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hurricane-katrina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Katrina}}}\uc2  in 2005.\par \par \uc2 Parts of western North Carolina, including Asheville, were among the hardest-hit areas.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the first day of early in-person voting for the 2024 election in the battleground state of North Carolina, more than 350,000 voters North Carolinians cast their ballots, setting a new state record, officials announced.\par \par \uc2 Election officials in the state {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wral.com/north-carolina-sets-record-for-first-day-of-early-voting/21678861/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said }}}\uc2  on Friday that a record 353,166 voters turned out statewide on Thursday, surpassing the previous record for the first day of early voting of 348,559 voters set in 2020.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYesterday\u8217\'20\'19s turnout is a clear sign that voters are energized about this election, that they trust the elections process, and that a hurricane will not stop North Carolinians from exercising their right to vote,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncsbe.gov/news/press-releases/2024/10/18/north-carolina-sets-turnout-record-first-day-early-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 Karen Brinson Bell\uc2 , executive director of the State Board of Elections.\par \par \uc2 This comes as earlier this week, Georgia voters shattered Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s early voting record, casting 328,000 ballots on the first day of early voting, which is more than double the previous record of 136,000, set in 2020.\par \par \uc2 You can read more about that here.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/us-election-briefing-georgia-shatters-early-voting-record-as-more-than-300000-cast-ballots"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election briefing: Georgia shatters early voting record as more than 300,000 cast ballots }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fox News has reportedly denied that any of its employees or freelancers assisted in writing the jokes that former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  told at last night\u8217\'20\'19s Al Smith dinner.\par \par \uc2 This comes as the former president appeared on Fox News this morning and said that some of his jokes were written by \u8220\'20\'1Ca couple people from Fox\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrFox News says in a statement it's not true: "Fox News confirmed that no employee or freelancer wrote the jokes.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zjjL5M9Vt0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/zjjL5M9Vt0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jeremy Barr (@jeremymbarr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jeremymbarr/status/1847312593045606750?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 A federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-67127f788f08d025c3e953ad#block-67127f788f08d025c3e953ad"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed release}}}\uc2  of hundreds of documents used in special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s election subversion case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but the majority of them are redacted. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-671284958f08d025c3e9542f#block-671284958f08d025c3e9542f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 What we can see}}}\uc2  mostly concerns the legal strategy Trump and his allies concocted to block \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from taking the White House, which may be presented to jurors whenever the case goes to trial. Meanwhile, reports have emerged that Trump has canceled interviews because he is \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-671262f38f08c6f693b783c7#block-671262f38f08c6f693b783c7"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 exhausted}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 something his campaign denies \u8211\'20\'13 and is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-671250b88f08ea656ca1cedf#block-671250b88f08ea656ca1cedf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considering holding a town hall}}}\uc2  with one-time rival \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  in a bid to woo female voters.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-67127cc28f08d025c3e9537a#block-67127cc28f08d025c3e9537a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  that some of the jokes he told at last night\u8217\'20\'19s Al Smith dinner were written by employees of conservative network Fox \u8211\'20\'13 a breach of ethics, if confirmed.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Frank-Walter Steinmeier\uc2 , the president of Germany, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-671271d18f08d025c3e952ab#block-671271d18f08d025c3e952ab"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warned}}}\uc2  in unusually direct terms of the threat Trump could pose if returned to the White House, during a visit by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to the country.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/18/us-election-news-joe-biden-berlin-kamala-harris-donald-trump-ukraine?page=with:block-671277698f08156d15775acb#block-671277698f08156d15775acb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 enlisted}}}\uc2  singer-songwriter Marc Anthony for a campaign ad aimed at Latino voters in which he condemns Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments about Puerto Rico.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interestingly included among the documents are copies of the envelopes used to mail electoral vote tallies from states \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  targeted to overturn the election result.\par \par \uc2 CBS News took a screenshot:\par \par \uc2 enltrA third batch of \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  court exhibits (500+ pages)\par \par \uc2 includes actual highlighted sections of \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 's book (sections about pre-Jan 6)\par \par \uc2 And the mailing envelopes of electoral votes from states from which Trump baselessly claimed fraud\par \par \uc2 ====> {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/fi2lvSY4ky"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/fi2lvSY4ky}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LbQilNfmLh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/LbQilNfmLh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Scott MacFarlane (@MacFarlaneNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MacFarlaneNews/status/1847307410823672111?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 The portions of the documents that are not redacted include statements by Republican swing state lawmakers and officials in late 2020, around the time that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies were pressing them to cooperate with his attempts to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election victory.\par \par \uc2 As has been documented by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/23/the-17-findings-in-the-january-6-committees-final-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the January 6 committee}}}\uc2  and other investigations, Trump and his allies attempted to convince Republicans in states like Arizona and Georgia to cast doubt on the validity of their state\u8217\'20\'19s votes for Biden \u8211\'20\'13 largely without success.\par \par \uc2 Also visible in the documents are portions of \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s memoir, where he described how his former boss leaned on him to go along with his plans to throw Biden\u8217\'20\'19s election victory into doubt:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/books/2022/nov/14/pence-trump-book-2024-republican-presidential-primary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pence risks Trump\u8217\'20\'19s wrath by piling on criticisms of ex-president in new book}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 The documents released thus far consist of hundreds of blank pages, interspersed occasionally with what appear to be snippets of emails, text messages and interviews, parts of which are, themselves, redacted.\par \par \uc2 From what can be gleaned, much of it appears to relate to Trump and his allies\u8217\'20\'19 strategy to create a legal basis to prevent \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  from taking office \u8211\'20\'13 which is at the heart of special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s case against the former president.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Federal court releases more evidence in Trump election subversion case\par \par \uc2 A federal court has unsealed hundreds of pages of evidence in the case against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for trying to overturn the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The release comes as special prosecutor \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s team moves to get its case back on track after the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s ruling earlier this year that presidents have immunity from charges related to official acts.\par \par \uc2 Much of the documents released have been redacted, but we will let you know if any news emerges. Meanwhile, here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest in the legal wrangling over the case:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/03/trump-january-6-court-filing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump January 6 case: five key points in the latest filing against former president}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says Fox employees helped write jokes for Al Smith dinner\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was on Fox News earlier this morning, and was asked about his jokes at last night\u8217\'20\'19s Al Smith dinner.\par \par \uc2 He replied that some of them were written by \u8220\'20\'1Ca couple people from Fox\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 which, if true, would be quite the breach of media ethics, even for the right-leaning network. CNN captured a clip:\par \par \uc2 enltrDoocy: Your material at the Al Smith dinner "was real funny, who helped you with it?" Trump: "I had a lot of people helping, a lot of people, a couple people from Fox \u8211\'20\'13 actually, I shouldn't say that, but they wrote some jokes. For the most part, I didn't like any of them." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hQSFzPNDkd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hQSFzPNDkd}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brian Stelter (@brianstelter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brianstelter/status/1847250996235252118?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Here is our coverage of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s zingers and insults from last night\u8217\'20\'19s get-together:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/17/donald-trump-january-6-riot-kamala-harris-us-election-politics-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump speaks at Al Smith dinner \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has enlisted singer songwriter Marc Anthony to appear in a new ad in which he slams \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for comments he made about Puerto Rico during his presidency:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s part of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s push to win the diverse group of Latino voters who could make the difference between winning and losing key swing states.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 German president warns of threat of Trump's return as Biden visits\par \par \uc2 In a speech during \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s visit to Germany, president \uc2 Frank-Walter Steinmeier\uc2  was unusually frank about the threat posed by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  if he returns to the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn this friendship, there have been and always will be times of proximity and greater distance, times of agreement and times of discord. Even recently, just a handful years ago, the distance had grown so wide that we almost lost each other,\u8221\'20\'1D Steinmeier said.\par \par \uc2 He noted that the outcome of the election could impact an array of American and European foreign policy priorities, including the defense of Ukraine:\par \par \uc2 The choice on November the 5th is only Americans\u8217\'20\'19 choice to make but we as Europeans have a choice too. We have the choice to do our part, to be unwavering in our support for Ukraine. To invest in our common security. To invest in our shared future. And as you have done sir, to stand by the transatlantic alliance no matter what.\par \par \uc2 From the bottom of my heart, in this time when democracy is under strain all around the western world, you Mr President have been the beacon of democracy...\par \par \uc2 Decency is maybe what we are most at risk of losing.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Which is not to say \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has not been doing any interviews at all.\par \par \uc2 He spoke with Fox News personality and ex-professional wrestler Tyrus for an episode of his Outkick podcast released today, in which he repeated his comments warning of \u8220\'20\'1Can enemy from within\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip, shared by the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  campaign:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump says Americans who don\u8217\'20\'19t support him are the \u8220\'20\'1Cenemy\u8221\'20\'1D and are a bigger \u8220\'20\'1Cproblem\u8221\'20\'1D than \u8220\'20\'1CChina and Russia\u8221\'20\'1D: \u8220\'20\'1CThese are bad people. These are sick people\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/a9shBYeB9g"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/a9shBYeB9g}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1847273867485512026?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Democrats have said the former president\u8217\'20\'19s usage of the terminology to describe his political enemies is a dangerous escalation of rhetoric, and a sign that he is out for \u8220\'20\'1Cunchecked power\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/fox-news-trump-town-hall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump doubles down on \u8216\'20\'18enemy from within\u8217\'20\'19 comments at Fox town hall}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Case in point: \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has turned down an invitation from CNN for a televised town hall just days before the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has said yes to the invitation, CNN reports, and her town hall is set for 23 October. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 enltrThe window has closed on CNN's offer to hold a town hall with Trump and voters. Last week the network proposed back to back town halls on October 23, and Harris accepted the invite, but Trump did not. (1/2)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brian Stelter (@brianstelter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brianstelter/status/1847256515679330316?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr"His campaign has not committed to participate, so we are moving forward with a Town Hall event with VP Harris taking questions from a live audience of Pennsylvania voters who are still undecided or persuadable in this election," CNN said in a statement this morning. (2/2)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brian Stelter (@brianstelter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brianstelter/status/1847256524604756304?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump canceling interviews because he's 'exhausted' - report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has uncharacteristically been backing out of media interviews lately, and Politico has learned the reason why: the former president is \u8220\'20\'1Cexhausted\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what they found:\par \par \uc2 It happened just this week to planned Trump sit-downs with NBC in Philadelphia and CNBC\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CSquawk Box\u8221\'20\'1D \u8212\'20\'14 and that\u8217\'20\'19s on the heels of him backing out of a \u8220\'20\'1C60 Minutes\u8221\'20\'1D episode earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 Why does this keep happening? Another outlet was recently given an explanation by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s team for why their own interview wasn\u8217\'20\'19t coming to fruition: exhaustion.\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign had spent weeks in conversations with The Shade Room, a site that draws a largely young and Black audience \u8212\'20\'14 a demographic where Trump has been making inroads. It hosted an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5WWnKBnHAP8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interview with Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  just last week.\par \par \uc2 But no interview has materialized. As Shade Room staff began feeling that feet were being dragged inside Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, they pressed earlier this week to set a date for a sit-down.\par \par \uc2 In response, a Trump adviser told Shade Room producers that Trump was \u8220\'20\'1Cexhausted and refusing [some] interviews but that could change\u8221\'20\'1D at any time, according to two people familiar with the conversations.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s spokeswoman has denied the report:\par \par \uc2 Trump national press secretary Karoline Leavitt, while making clear she wasn\u8217\'20\'19t part of the back-and-forth for the Shade Room interview, said last night that the idea that Trump was exhausted \u8220\'20\'1Cis unequivocally false.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Trump is running laps around \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on the campaign trail,\u8221\'20\'1D Leavitt said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd has done media interviews every day this week. He has more energy and a harder work ethic than anyone in politics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Evidence in Trump election subversion case to be unsealed today - report\par \par \uc2 The federal judge handling \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s trial on charges related to subverting the 2020 election has allowed a new batch of evidence against the former president to be made public today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/dc-md-va/2024/10/17/trump-jan-6-appendix-jack-smith/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The evidence underpins a brief filed by special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  that argues Trump\u8217\'20\'19s conduct is not covered by a recent supreme court ruling that gave presidents immunity from prosecution for official acts. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from the Post on what we can expect to see when the evidence is released:\par \par \uc2 In a five-page order Thursday, U.S. District Judge Tanya S. Chutkan said Trump had failed to address the legal system\u8217\'20\'19s presumption in favor of public access to criminal court proceedings, and rejected the former president\u8217\'20\'19s assertion that it could appear the court was trying to impact the election by making public potentially unflattering material about Trump in an appendix to Smith\u8217\'20\'19s brief.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the court withheld information that the public otherwise had a right to access solely because of the potential political consequences of releasing it, that withholding could itself constitute \u8212\'20\'14 or appear to be \u8212\'20\'14 election interference,\u8221\'20\'1D Chutkan wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CThe court will therefore continue to keep political considerations out of its decision-making, rather than incorporating them as Defendant requests.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys earlier Thursday had asked Chutkan to postpone the release of the material, much of which was expected to be redacted, until nine days after the Nov. 5 election. That would fall after the former president is set to file his own blockbuster brief of up to 180 pages with its own appendix of sources arguing why he should not still face trial after the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s July ruling establishing that presidents have broad immunity from criminal prosecution for their official acts.\par \par \uc2 While Trump argued that release of the materials would poison the jury pool, Chutkan said that both sides\u8217\'20\'19 filings ultimately would be available to potential jurors, any taint could be rooted out in jury selection, and Trump was free to make his own legal arguments in court and to the public.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 While \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is believed to have made gains among Black and Hispanic voters, a new poll shows the \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  continues to lead among the former group, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/anna-betts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anna Betts}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par \uc2 A new poll has revealed that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  continues to lead \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  among Black likely voters in battleground states.\par \par \uc2 The poll, conducted by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gs.howard.edu/sites/gs.howard.edu/files/2024-10/HIPO_Battleground_African_American_Survey_Wave_2_LV_Toplines_2024_10_10_10152024.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Howard University\u8217\'20\'19s Initiative on Public Opinion}}}\uc2  from 2 October to 8 October, surveyed 981 Black likely voters in the states of Arizona, Georgia, Michigan, Nevada, North Carolina, Pennsylvania and Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The results show that 84% of respondents said they planned to vote for the vice-president, while only 8% said they would support Trump for president in November, and another 8% remained undecided.\par \par \uc2 The survey also identified the most important issues for the respondents, with \u8220\'20\'1Cdemocracy/voting rights/elections\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D ranked as a top priority, followed by the economy and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/17/harris-trump-black-swing-state-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris maintains lead over Trump among Black swing state voters \u8211\'20\'13 poll}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll hear more from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at 7pm today, when he holds a rally in Detroit.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s the largest city in swing state Michigan, and a Democratic stronghold. Don\u8217\'20\'19t be surprised if he presses his case to the city\u8217\'20\'19s large African American population, a demographic where the Trump campaign is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/25/harris-trump-election-black-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trying to make inroads}}}\uc2 , that they would be better off voting for him.\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , meanwhile, will also be in Michigan. She rallies in Grand Rapids at 2.30pm, then has another event in the state capital Lansing at 5.25pm, and a final event in suburban Detroit\u8217\'20\'19s Oakland county at 8.10pm. Busy day!\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump campaign considering holding town hall with \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2  - report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign is pondering arranging a town hall with \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , his former \uc2 UN\uc2  ambassador turned rival for the Republican nomination, who has since endorsed his candidacy, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thebulwark.com/p/trump-world-in-talks-with-haley-for"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Bulwark reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The joint appearance, which could be held with conservative commentator \uc2 Sean Hannity\uc2  on Fox News, is a bid to shore up his standing with women voters, who polls indicate are less enthusiastic about returning Trump to the White House than are men. Haley and Trump were at-times bitter rivals in the GOP primaries earlier this year, but she later endorsed him during a speech at the Republican national convention in July.\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, Haley has lately noted that she still has her differences with Trump. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what the Bulwark reports:\par \par \uc2 Since then, however, Haley and Trump have not appeared together. And she hinted that tensions still linger on her new \uc2 SiriusXM\uc2  satellite radio show last month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t agree with Trump 100 percent of the time,\u8221\'20\'1D Haley said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have not forgotten what he said about me. I\u8217\'20\'19ve not forgotten what he said about my husband or his, you know, deployment time or his military service. I haven\u8217\'20\'19t forgotten about his or his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s tactics from, you know, putting a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/MarcACaputo/status/1708497618425303171"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bird cage}}}\uc2  outside our hotel room to calling me \u8216\'20\'18bird brain,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Haley {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/media/4900682-nikki-haley-trump-personality-sirusxm/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  on her show, adding that she\u8217\'20\'19s still for Trump because she thinks he \u8220\'20\'1Cwill make the country better.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Those comments garnered some attention in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s orbit. One confidant of the ex-president privately joked that talk like that is usually taboo in his circles because \u8220\'20\'1Cif you\u8217\'20\'19re with him 99 percent of the time, you\u8217\'20\'19re a fucking traitor in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s eyes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 Fox News anchor Bret Baier says he made \u8220\'20\'1Ca mistake\u8221\'20\'1D when he failed to include a clip of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  referring to the \u8220\'20\'1Cenemy from within\u8221\'20\'1D about his rivals during an interview with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Baier showed a clip that came from a town hall broadcast earlier in the day via Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CThe Faulkner Focus\u8221\'20\'1D, in which Trump said he is \u8220\'20\'1Cnot threatening anybody.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat clip was not what he has been saying about the enemy from within. \u8230\'20\'26 That\u8217\'20\'19s not what you just showed,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said to the Fox News anchor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou didn\u8217\'20\'19t show that, and here is the bottom line: He has repeated it multiple times, and you and I both know that, and you and I both know he has talked about turning the military on the American people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Baier said on \u8220\'20\'1CSpecial Report\u8221\'20\'1D on Thursday that he \u8220\'20\'1Cdid make a mistake\u8221\'20\'1D when it came to clips shown in the interview.\par \par \uc2 Trump brushed off concerns from President Biden about Election Day not being peaceful, saying, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe bigger problem is the enemy from within, not even the people that have come in and destroyed our country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the bigger problem are the people from within,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have some very bad people. We have some sick people, radical left lunatics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  appeared at the Al Smith charity dinner, a bi-partisan fundraising event traditionally attended by presidential candidates to trade lighthearted jokes at each other, via a pre-recorded video link.\par \par \uc2 Actress and former SNL cast member Molly Shannon appeared in the sketch, playing her fictional Catholic school pupil character Mary Katherine Gallagher.\par \par \uc2 Harris asked for advice; Shannon-as-Gallahgher suggests she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t lie, as it is a sin. Harris replies you shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t lie, especially, about \u8220\'20\'1Cthy neighbour\u8217\'20\'19s election results\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She would never insult Catholics, Harris said \u8211\'20\'13 taking another jibe at Trump: \u8220\'20\'1CThat would be like insulting Detroiters when you\u8217\'20\'19re in Detroit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19 sketch received a lukewarm reception by those in attendance at the dinner.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs I watched that I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t help but think now I know how my kids felt when I face-timed into a piano recital they were at,\u8221\'20\'1D Jim Gaffigan, the comedian who hosted the dinner, said.\par \par \uc2 The crowd cheered \u8211\'20\'13 not hugely enthusiastically, but more than just politely \u8211\'20\'13 following Harris\u8217\'20\'19s appearance.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Electioneering places a cost burden on local police forces. As the candidates descend on Michigan, a key battleground state in the upcoming election, local forces scramble to provide support to the Secret Service and other agencies.\par \par \uc2 The Detroit Free Press reports that by late last month, Kent County, home of Grand Rapids, had incurred more than $300,000 in expenses.\par \par \uc2 Assistant County Administrator Lori Latham said:\par \par \uc2 We anticipate additional expenses as we expect more visits leading up to the election.\par \par \uc2 Although we do not have a dedicated fund for these unforeseen costs, we use overtime and contingency funds to manage such unexpected expenditures.\par \par \uc2 Bob Stevenson, executive director of the Michigan Association of Chiefs of Police, said some areas feel the burden more than others:\par \par \uc2 The degree of the burden sometimes depends on the size of the city and their experience with it,\u8221\'20\'1D Stevenson said. \u8220\'20\'1CYou take a town like Dearborn or Detroit or Battle Creek.\par \par \uc2 They have lots of people, they can probably divert a lot of their working people for that short period of time, and it\u8217\'20\'19s not a problem. But you take some of the smaller cities, not only are they already short staffed, but now you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to somehow come up with people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Security concerns have been the theme of this campaign, with two attempts on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s life taking place in less than three months.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is preparing for her first campaign appearances with Barack and \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  this month in Georgia and Michigan.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press reports that the vice president will appear with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in Georgia on October 24, and with \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  in Michigan on October 26.\par \par \uc2 The Obamas endorsed Harris in July and spoke at the Democratic National Convention in August in Chicago.\par \par \uc2 The rally is being hosted by When We All Vote, a nonpartisan civic engagement organisation founded my \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  to encourage people to engage with politics.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump insults Harris in jibe-filled speech at Catholic charity dinner\par \par \uc2 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  did not attend the Al Smith charity dinner in New York in person, appearing via a pre-recorded video sketch, instead. Her jokes didn\u8217\'20\'19t appear to land with the audience.\par \par \uc2 The white-tie dinner raises millions of dollars for Catholic charities and traditionally candidates from both parties have attended.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s jokes were crude but seemed to be well received by those in attendance.\par \par \uc2 Trump mocked transgender people, aiming a jibe at vice-presidential nominee \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He also took aim at migrants and New York, saying he had to wrap up his speech so New York can \u8220\'20\'1Cturn the room into an illegal migrant shelter\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Regarding Harris\u8217\'20\'19 absence, he posted on his Truth Social network:\par \par \uc2 Just found out that Lyin\u8217\'20\'19 Kamala is doing a video message tonight instead of being at the Al Smith Dinner. She shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be allowed to do a video message.\par \par \uc2 Kamala should be there like almost every other Presidential Candidate in their History, except \uc2 Walter Mondale\uc2 , who lost 49-1. They didn\u8217\'20\'19t give me the option of a video message, nor would I have done it. This is very disrespectful to everyone involved. She should be here, or lose the Catholic Vote!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Germany honours Biden for restoring 'Europe's hope in the trans-Atlantic alliance'\par \par \uc2 Germany have awarded US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  the highest class of the Grand Cross of the Order of Merit of the Federal Republic of Germany for his work improving the German-American friendship and the transatlantic alliance.\par \par \uc2 He was presented the award by Germany\u8217\'20\'19s President \uc2 Frank-Walter Steinmeier\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Steinmeier said the friendship with the US is \u8220\'20\'1Cand will always be existentially important\u8221\'20\'1D for Germany, but there have always been \u8220\'20\'1Ctimes of proximity and greater distance.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1DEven recently, just a handful of years ago, the distance had grown so wide that we almost lost each other,\u8221\'20\'1D Steinmeier said, alluding to tense relations during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s earlier presidency.\par \par \uc2 He said Biden \u8220\'20\'1Crestored Europe\u8217\'20\'19s hope in the trans-Atlantic alliance literally overnight.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the months to come, I hope that Europeans remember: America is indispensable for us,\u8221\'20\'1D he added. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I hope that Americans remember: Your allies are indispensable for you. We are more than just \u8216\'20\'18other countries\u8217\'20\'19 in the world \u8212\'20\'14 we are partners, we are friends.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump accuses Zelenskyy of helping to start war in extraordinary attack\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to our coverage of the run-up to the US election as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has claimed Ukrainian president \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2  helped to start his country\u8217\'20\'19s war with Russia.\par \par \uc2 The Republican presidential candidate\u8217\'20\'19s extraordinary criticism \u8211\'20\'13 the war started when Russia invaded Ukrainian sovereign territory \u8211\'20\'13 comes as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  arrives in Europe for closed-door discussions with allies with Ukraine high on the agenda.\par \par \uc2 As Reuters reports, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments indicate he is likely to radically shift US policy toward Russia if he wins the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 The Republican former president has frequently criticized Zelenskyy on the campaign trail, repeatedly calling him \u8220\'20\'1Cthe greatest salesman on Earth\u8221\'20\'1D for having solicited and received billions of dollars of US military aid since the war broke out in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Trump has also slammed the Ukrainian leader for failing to seek peace with Moscow, and he has suggested Ukraine may have to cede some of its land to Russia to make a peace deal, a concession Kyiv considers unacceptable.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments on the PBD Podcast on Thursday with Patrick Bet-David went a step further than his previous criticism. He said Zelenskyy was to blame not just for failing to end the war, but for helping start it. \u8220\'20\'1CThat doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to help him because I feel very badly for those people. But he should never have let that war start. The war\u8217\'20\'19s a loser,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile on Friday, Biden will seek to cement cooperation with key European partners on issues from the Ukraine war to conflict in the Middle East during a swift swansong trip to Berlin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re wheels down in Berlin,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden wrote in a post on X overnight. \u8220\'20\'1CReady to greet old friends and strengthen our close alliance as we stand together for freedom and against tyranny around the world.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrWe\u8217\'20\'19re wheels down in Berlin.\par \par \uc2 Ready to greet old friends and strengthen our close alliance as we stand together for freedom and against tyranny around the world. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/zaTFtTOFMT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/zaTFtTOFMT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 President Biden (@POTUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/POTUS/status/1847075258596983276?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 More on this shortly. In other developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  laid into \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and other Democrats on Thursday in a pointed and at times bitter speech as he headlined the annual Al Smith charity dinner in New York. The Republican nominee repeatedly criticised his Democratic campaign rival over her decision to skip the event. She sent a video instead.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Billionaire \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  launched five nights of campaign events in Pennsylvania in support of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign last night. \u8220\'20\'1CThis election, I think, is going to decide the fate of America and, along with the fate of America, the fate of Western civilization,\u8221\'20\'1D he said at a town hall event in Folsom, on the outskirts of Philadelphia. He also reportedly pushed the debunked narrative that voting machines had been used in a plot to rig the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump will both be scouring for votes in Michigan on Friday as they try to lock down support in this key political battleground. Harris is scheduled to begin her day in Grand Rapids before holding events in Lansing and Oakland County, which is northwest of Detroit. Trump has his own event in Oakland County in the afternoon before holding a rally in Detroit in the evening.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241018ekai001mj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
