\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Judge slaps down Florida effort to ban  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ad: \u8216\'20\'18It\u8217\'20\'19s the first amendment, stupid\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 587 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 October 2024\par 16:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 State health department sent letter to stations demanding they not air TV ad backing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access ballot measureUS politics \u8211\'20\'13 live updates\par \par \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s health department\uc2  can\u8217\'20\'19t block a TV advertisement in support of a ballot measure that would protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a federal judge ruled on Thursday, after the department sent letters to local TV stations commanding them to stop airing the ad or risk criminal consequences.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe government cannot excuse its indirect censorship of political speech simply by declaring the disfavored speech is \u8216\'20\'18false\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D US district judge Mark E Walker wrote in his ruling. \u8220\'20\'1CTo keep it simple for the State of Florida: it\u8217\'20\'19s the First Amendment, stupid.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/election-abortion-ballot-measures-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida is one of 10 states}}}\uc2  set to vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures in November. If enacted, Florida\u8217\'20\'19s measure would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution and roll back the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban on the procedure, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/florida-abortion-ban-clinic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 which took effect in May}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s health department{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/09/florida-news-abortion-ballot-coverage"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent cease-and-desist letters}}}\uc2  to TV stations running an ad by Floridians Protecting Freedom, the campaign behind the measure. In the ad, a woman named Caroline speaks about being diagnosed with cancer while pregnant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe doctors knew if I did not end my pregnancy, I would lose my baby, I would lose my life and my daughter would lose her mom,\u8221\'20\'1D Caroline says in the ad. \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida has now banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even in cases like mine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The letters said the claim that women can\u8217\'20\'19t get life-saving abortions in Florida was \u8220\'20\'1Ccategorically false\u8221\'20\'1D, since Florida\u8217\'20\'19s ban permits abortions in medical emergencies. \u8220\'20\'1CThe fact is these ads are unequivocally false and detrimental to public health in Florida,\u8221\'20\'1D Jae Williams, the Florida department of health communications director, said in an email late on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 However, doctors across the country have said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans are worded so vaguely as to force them to deny people medically necessary abortions. A New York doctor recently said that she had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/30/whole-womans-health-abortion-clinic-virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 treated a woman with an ectopic pregnancy}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which is nonviable and potentially life-threatening if left untreated \u8211\'20\'13 who had been turned away from a Florida hospital.\par \par \uc2 In response to the letters, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/florida-pro-abortion-ad-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Floridians Protecting Freedom sued}}}\uc2  the Florida surgeon general, Joseph Ladapo, and John Wilson, the former general counsel for the state health department. At least one TV station stopped airing the ad, the coalition\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit alleged.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Walker granted a temporary restraining order blocking Ladapo from taking any further action against broadcasters or other media outlets that might air ads by Floridians Protecting Freedom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COf course, the surgeon general of Florida has the right to advocate for his own position on a ballot measure,\u8221\'20\'1D Walker wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CBut it would subvert the rule of law to permit the state to transform its own advocacy into the direct suppression of protected political speech.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Over the last several weeks, Florida\u8217\'20\'19s government, run by \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Republican governor, has sent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/13/florida-abortion-petition-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 law enforcement officials to investigate people}}}\uc2  who signed a petition to get the measure on the ballot, set up a webpage urging people not to vote for it, and issued a report suggesting the measure got on the ballot due to \u8220\'20\'1Ca large number of forged signatures or fraudulent petitions\u8221\'20\'1D. Floridians Protecting Freedom has denied wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 Anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://floridaphoenix.com/2024/10/16/anti-abortion-suit-against-amendment-4/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since filed a lawsuit}}}\uc2  to remove the measure from the ballot or nullify votes cast for it.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241018ekai002e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
