\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump speaks at Al Smith dinner \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); with Maanvi Singh ,Maya Yang, Erum Salam and Amy Sedghi (earlier) \par \uc2 12,987 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 October 2024\par 02:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live coverage has ended, thanks for following along. Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss important US election coverage. Get our free app and sign up for election alerts\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.38am BST\par \par \uc2 This live coverage is ending for the day. Thanks for following along.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s speech ends and he receives warm applause from the crowd. We will end our coverage of this event now.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.38am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says he will bring back the SALT tax deduction. Some context from NBC\u8217\'20\'19s Sahlil Kapur:\par \par \uc2 enltrBizarro World \u8212\'20\'14> At the Al Smith dinner in New York, Trump calls for bringing back the SALT deduction that he capped in his signature tax law with the support of nearly every Republican, a deduction that Democratic leaders are pushing to restore but can\u8217\'20\'19t due to GOP opposition.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sahil Kapur (@sahilkapur) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/sahilkapur/status/1847096287663214955?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump makes another transphobic joke.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump repeats claims that he has been treated worse than any other president.\par \par \uc2 He takes a jab at Gaffigan, saying that hopefully his role as \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will be short-lived.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump makes a joke to boos, then says, \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s nasty. I told the idiots who gave me this stuff.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The joke was about Harris\u8217\'20\'19s support for childcare and was directed at her husband, Dough Emhoff and paid child care workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast time I did this I was wondering against crooked Hillary\u8230\'20\'26I had the meanest guy you\u8217\'20\'19d ever seen write stuff up and man was the room angry,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says.\par \par \uc2 They said \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s too much, but I did it anyway.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump jokes that he is meant to make self-depracating jokes, then says, \u8220\'20\'1CSo here goes. Nope! I got nothing\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.15am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  is here looking very glum, Trump says. \u8220\'20\'1CBut look on the bright side chuck, considering how woke your party has become, if Kamala loses you still have the chance to become the first woman president,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says \u8211\'20\'13 it is a transphobic joke.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump again refers to Harris not appearing in person, and says she is \u8220\'20\'1Creceiving communion from \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D to claps and cheers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf the Democrats really wanted someone to not be with us this evening, they would have just sent \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says.\par \par \uc2 Trump claims \u8211\'20\'13 not clear if joking \u8211\'20\'13 that Biden is having second thoughts and wants to come back. There is no evidence of this.\par \par \uc2 Trump says the term \u8220\'20\'1Cfake news\u8221\'20\'1D is no longer in vogue.\par \par \uc2 He refers to President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  as \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Barack Hussein Obama\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 dog whistling for the baseless \u8216\'20\'18birther\u8217\'20\'19 conspiracy theory that Obama is secretly a Muslim born in Kenya.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump says of Harris, \u8220\'20\'1CI like her a lot, but now I can\u8217\'20\'19t stand her.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCatholics you gotta vote for me,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m here and she\u8217\'20\'19s not.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump lists good deeds done by Catholics.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you wanted Harris to accept your invitation you should have told her the funds were going to bail out the rioters and looters in Minneapolis,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says, to loud whoops and cheers.\par \par \uc2 Trump is referring to the George Floyd protests that took place in the historically Catholic city of Minneapolis in 2020.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.03am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe last Democrat not to attend this important event was \uc2 Walter Mondale\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says, \u8220\'20\'1CAnd it did not go very well for him. He lost 49 states and he won one: Minnesota. So I said there\u8217\'20\'19s no way I\u8217\'20\'19m missing it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mondale \u8220\'20\'1Cwas expected to do well, then it didn\u8217\'20\'19t work out,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump jokes. \u8220\'20\'1CIt shows you there is a god.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump then says that Harris is weird and it is weird that Harris isn\u8217\'20\'19t here tonight \u8211\'20\'13 saying the word several times, referring to the insult Harris and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  direct at Trump and his supporters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.01am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlways: It\u8217\'20\'19s a rule, you gotta go to the dinner, you gotta do it, otherwise bad things are going to happen to you from up there,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump jokes, getting a laugh \u8211\'20\'13 he is referring to God.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut my opponent feels that she does not have to be here which is disrespectful to the event and in particular to our Catholic community,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says. The crowd claps.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve gone after me. Mr Mayor, you\u8217\'20\'19re peanuts compared to what they did to me,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.58am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMayor Adams, good luck with everything, they went after you,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says to a big laugh.\par \par \uc2 More on New York Mayor Eric Adams, the first mayor in city history to be indicted on federal corruption charges:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/02/eric-adams-corruption-scandals"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Show me the money\u8217\'20\'19: how Eric Adams made it to the top \u8211\'20\'13 and fell back down}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is receiving a warm response from the crowd.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey told me under no circumstances are you allowed to use a teleprompter and I get up here and see there is a beautiful teleprompter,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 Unclear if that is a joke or more of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s obsession with whether Harris is using teleprompters or not.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.55am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, here\u8217\'20\'19s the thing that\u8217\'20\'19s so amazing about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . It is impossible not to have a strong opinion about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . You either think he is endearingly outspoken and brash. Or you think he is a sociopath and you\u8217\'20\'19d like to be his running mate,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaffigan jokes. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and I have a lot in common. We both have five children and we both have a lush mane of golden hair. And we both try to travel as much possible to get away from our families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gaffigan then turns to Trump: \u8220\'20\'1CI want you to know if you are re-elected, I always liked you. And I\u8217\'20\'19m not saying that because I don\u8217\'20\'19t want to be sent to a labour camp. Well, I guess that\u8217\'20\'19s the reason, sir,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaffigan says.\par \par \uc2 He invites Trump to the stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52am BST\par \par \uc2 The crowd boos that joke. Someone to Gaffigan\u8217\'20\'19s right said, \u8220\'20\'1CWe talked about leaving that out.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was gonna leave that out,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaffigan says, to laughter.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs I watched that I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t help but think now I know how my kids felt when I face-timed into a piano recital they were at,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaffigan says.\par \par \uc2 The crowd cheered \u8211\'20\'13 not hugely enthusiastically, but more than just politely \u8211\'20\'13 following Harris\u8217\'20\'19s appearance.\par \par \uc2 Gaffigan says, \u8220\'20\'1CShortly I will introduce President Trump, who will likely talk about how vice president Harris\u8217\'20\'19s absence likely proves she hates Catholics, Americans, and babies. Then CNN and MSNBC will say he went to far, and \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and Fox News will say he was pitch perfect.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Gaffigan turns to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baseless claims about immigrants eating cats and dogs. \u8220\'20\'1CYou know this is the second time grabbing a kitty has been a campaign issue,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 He is referring to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8211\'20\'13 much talked about in the 2016 election \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cgrab em by the pussy\u8221\'20\'1D comments.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47am BST\par \par \uc2 As Harris turns to face the screen, she says the dinner \u8220\'20\'1Cprovides a rare opportunity to set aside politics\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She lists various philanthropic activities achieved by the church.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the spirit of tonight\u8217\'20\'19s dinner, let us commit to reaching across the divide,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.46am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a very important dinner, and an important tradition to be a part of,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says in her video.\par \par \uc2 Actress and former SNL cast member Molly Shannon appears, playing her fictional Catholic school pupil character Mary Katherine Gallagher.\par \par \uc2 She makes a speech from House of Dragons, about the need for a woman leader.\par \par \uc2 Harris asks for advice: Shannon-as-Gallahgher suggests she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t lie, as it is a sin.\par \par \uc2 Harris says you shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t lie, especially, about \u8220\'20\'1Cthy neighbour\u8217\'20\'19s election results\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 She would never insult Catholics, Harris says \u8211\'20\'13 taking another jibe at Trump: \u8220\'20\'1Cthat would be like insulting Detroiters when you\u8217\'20\'19re in Detroit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's virtual appearance at the Al Smith charity dinner \u8211\'20\'13 video\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s video appearance is being played now at the dinner. Here it is:\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  speech at Al Smith dinner\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe Democrats have been telling us Trump\u8217\'20\'19s re-election is a threat to democracy. In fact, they were so concerned of this threat, they staged a coup, ousted their democratically elected incumbent, and installed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . In other words, all her dreams have come true. It really makes me consider the power of prayer, right Cardinal. Sometimes prayers takes three and a half years and a \uc2 George Clooney\uc2  op-ed,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaffigan jokes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.39am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is of course a historic race for many reasons. If vice-president Harris wins this election, not only would she be the first female president \u8211\'20\'13 a Black woman would be occupying the White House, a former Trump residence,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaffigan says.\par \par \uc2 Addressing Trump, he adds, \u8220\'20\'1CObviously, you wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be renting to her. I mean that would never happen anyway.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.55am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHarris\u8217\'20\'19s trajectory has been astounding. In the course of just a couple of months, she went from a mediocre vice-president to everyone\u8217\'20\'19s mamala,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaffigan says, to a very muted response.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris will be the first to (virtually) address the room, he says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have to admit, the Democrats have done an amazing job rebranding vice-president Harris. The term joyful warrior was used so many times at the Democratic convention I felt like I was at a yoga retreat,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaffigan jokes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s start off in a joyful warrior pose, and go straight into a downward-facing Doug Emhoff pose. Now laugh uncontrollably.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.54am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.34am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe live in divided times, and I hope whoever is elected in November, they establish an initiative to heal the divide that exists in this country. And I have a great name for this. It could be called, \u8216\'20\'18Project 2025\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaffigan jokes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32am BST\par \par \uc2 The media has begun discussing the phenomenon of secret Trump voters. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if you\u8217\'20\'19ve heard about this: people who publicly say they would never vote for Trump, but when they go in the booth, they do. It\u8217\'20\'19s a small group, it\u8217\'20\'19s called the Biden family,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaffigan jokes. That one gets a pretty big laugh, including from Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 This election is \u8220\'20\'1Cbeing left up to American voters and four billionaires\u8221\'20\'1D, Gaffigan jokes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is one group that baffles me. And I think it baffles most everyone in this country. And I\u8217\'20\'19m talking about the undecided voter. Are you kidding me? Are you kidding me? You don\u8217\'20\'19t know who you\u8217\'20\'19re voting for?\u8221\'20\'1D Gaffigan says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t see a difference between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Like nobody has ever thought, \u8216\'20\'18Wait, is that a Trump quote or a Harris quote?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here is Gaffigan, with Trump and Melania Trump seated to his left.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.53am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.26am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would probably be less loyal to RFK [Jr] than he would be to KFC,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaffigan says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s virtual appearance tonight will feature a cameo from actress and former SNL cast member Molly Shannon, playing her fictional Catholic school pupil character Mary Katherine Gallagher.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.21am BST\par \par \uc2 The Alfred E Smith Memorial Foundation Dinner is named for the former New York governor, a Democrat who was the first Catholic to receive a major party nomination for president when he unsuccessfully ran for the White House in 1928.\par \par \uc2 The event has become a tradition for presidential candidates since \uc2 Richard Nixon\uc2  and \uc2 John F Kennedy\uc2  appeared together in 1960. In 1996, the archdiocese of New York decided not to invite then president \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  and his Republican challenger, \uc2 Bob Dole\uc2 , reportedly because Clinton vetoed a late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19am BST\par \par \uc2 A brief history of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s appearances at this event, from the Associated Press:\par \par \uc2 In 2016, Trump was booed when he appeared at the dinner with his Democratic rival, \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , and unleashed a particularly nasty speech, calling her \u8220\'20\'1Ccorrupt\u8221\'20\'1D and accusing her of \u8220\'20\'1Cpretending not to hate Catholics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Both Trump and President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who is Catholic, spoke at a virtual version of the fundraiser in 2020, which was moved online due to concerns over large gatherings at the height of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Both candidates used their speeches not to tell jokes, but to appeal to Catholic voters, with Biden speaking about how his faith had guided him through moments of tragedy and Trump emphasizing his nomination of \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  to the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Gaffigan takes aim at Harris for not appearing: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m sorry, why is vice-president Harris not here? Consider this, this is a room full of Catholics and Jews from New York City, this is a lay-up for vice-president Harris.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.20am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.13am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be here tonight, the DNC made sure of that,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaffigan jokes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris will not be appearing in person at the event, but will appear virtually. Trump has criticised her for this, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CThey didn\u8217\'20\'19t give me the option of a video message, nor would I have done it. This is very disrespectful to everyone involved\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.10am BST\par \par \uc2 American comedian Jim Gaffigan, the actor who, among other things, plays \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  on SNL, is speaking now at the Al Smith charity dinner, where Trump is also expected to speak.\par \par \uc2 Gaffigan promises to be balanced, joking that the will make jokes about both Trump and his running mate, JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.58am BST\par \par \uc2 In comments to reporters after landing in Germany, the US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he had congratulated the Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  on \uc2 Hamas\uc2  leader \uc2 Yahya Sinwar\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s death and that \u8216\'20\'18now was the time to move on\u8217\'20\'19. He called the killing an opportunity to free Israeli hostages held by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and end the yearlong war in Gaza. US officials have expressed measured optimism that Sinwar\u8217\'20\'19s death might breathe new life into ceasefire talks that have so far failed to produce a breakthrough:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.05am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.38am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are the clips Harris played at the rally of Trump talking about women and their \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala Harris in Green Bay plays clips of Trump claiming he'll be a protector of women, taking credit for overturning Roe, and claiming he's "the father of IVF." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jX8fcgsfRf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jX8fcgsfRf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1847069402635579819?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are Harris\u8217\'20\'19s comments on Trump declaring himself \u8220\'20\'1Cthe father of IVF\u8221\'20\'1D on a Fox News town hall.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI mean it just gets more unbelievable sometimes. And now the man calls himself \u8216\'20\'18the father of IVF,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, to laughter from the crowd. \u8220\'20\'1CI mean what does that even mean,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, laughing. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd all of that while he is the one who by the way is responsible for it being at risk in the first place,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat is sadly interesting, I think, when you listen to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  talk, it becomes increasingly clear, I think, he has no idea what he\u8217\'20\'19s talking about when it comes to the healthcare of women in America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is expected to speak in 45 minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time.\par \par \uc2 Trump will headline the annual Al Smith charity dinner on Thursday night.\par \par \uc2 Eight years ago, he was jeered by attendees while delivering an especially pointed speech.\par \par \uc2 Harris is skipping attending the event in person as she campaigns in battleground states, breaking with presidential tradition. But she will appear on screen in a recorded video, organisers said.\par \par \uc2 The white-tie dinner in New York raises millions of dollars for Catholic charities and has traditionally offered candidates from both parties the chance to trade light-hearted barbs and show that they can get along \u8211\'20\'13 or at least pretend to \u8211\'20\'13 for one night in the election\u8217\'20\'19s final stretch.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s often the last time the two nominees share a stage before election day.\par \par \uc2 Trump will be joined at the dinner by his wife, Melania, who has been an infrequent presence on the campaign trail, according to a seating chart shared by organizers.\par \par \uc2 He is expected to speak at 9.15pm ET \u8211\'20\'13 in about 45 minutes.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.28am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.23am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s speech has ended.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRemember, Wisconsin has same-day voter registration,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says. \u8220\'20\'1CYou can vote early.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYour vote is your voice, and your voice is your power,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CEach individual has the power to weigh in on this.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.26am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.20am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the clip of Harris talking about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cfather of IVF\u8221\'20\'1D comments:\par \par \uc2 enltrHarris: Now the man calls himself 'the father of IVF.' What does that even mean? He's the one responsible for it being at risk in the first place! What's sadly interesting is that when you listen to Trump talk it becomes increasingly clear he doesn't know what he's talking about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4UYV6xMTmJ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4UYV6xMTmJ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1847070100429455644?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 18, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.19am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSomeone who suggests we should terminate the constitution of the United States should never again stand behind the seal of the president of the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNever again. Never again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.18am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo much is on the line in this election,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 She brings up the supreme court immunity ruling: \u8220\'20\'1CNow just imagine Trump with no guard rails.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.26am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.17am BST\par \par \uc2 'The man calls himself the father of IVF? I mean what does that even mean?' Harris says of Trump\par \par \uc2 Women \u8220\'20\'1Cdid not want this\u8221\'20\'1D, Harris says, explaining that they are dying of sepsis and having fertility treatment cut off.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI mean it just gets more unbelievable sometimes. And now the man calls himself the father of IVF? I mean, what does that even mean?\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you listen to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  talk, it becomes increasingly clear, I think, he has no idea what he\u8217\'20\'19s talking about when it comes to the healthcare of women in America.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris plays a series of clips of Trump saying things including: \u8220\'20\'1CSo the women thing, I did a great thing, long term, on the Roe v Wade, and I think they\u8217\'20\'19ll understand.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It also includes Trump saying he is the \u8220\'20\'1Cfather of IVF\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During a Fox News town hall taped Tuesday, Trump declared that he is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe father of IVF\u8221\'20\'1D, despite acknowledging during his answer that he had needed an explanation of IVF in February, after the Alabama supreme court ruled that frozen embryos can be considered children under state law.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he instructed the Alabama senator Katie Britt, a Republican, to \u8220\'20\'1Cexplain IVF very quickly\u8221\'20\'1D to him in the aftermath of the ruling.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris turns to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying: \u8220\'20\'1COne in three women live in a state with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban. And you\u8217\'20\'19ve heard the stories. Painful stories.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI come from the middle class, and I will never forget where I come from,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  to unseal new dossier on Trump tomorrow - report\par \par \uc2 Just stepping away from the rally for a moment: Politico reports that a judge has denied \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s effort to block a new dossier of \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s evidence from becoming public, as the special counsel seeks to argues that the former US president is not entitled to immunity from prosecution, in the wake of a July supreme court ruling:\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Judge Chutkan has denied Trump's effort to block a new dossier of \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2 's evidence from becoming public.\par \par \uc2 She says she will unseal it tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kyle Cheney (@kyledcheney) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kyledcheney/status/1847061785347604647?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The decision comes as federal prosecutors said in a court filing that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cresorted to crimes\u8221\'20\'1D in a failed bid to cling to power after losing the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 The filing unsealed in early October argued that the former US president is not entitled to immunity from prosecution.\par \par \uc2 It was submitted by Smith\u8217\'20\'19s team following a supreme court opinion that conferred broad immunity on former presidents and narrowed the scope of the prosecution.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/02/trump-crimes-2020-election-unsealed-filing"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Special counsel reveals new details of Trump bid to overturn 2020 election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the press pool report from the rally:\par \par \uc2 Motorcade pulled into Green Bay rally site at 6.22pm CT. Uneventful ride, though poolers note a beautiful moon on the horizon leaving the airport.\par \par \uc2 Rally is at the Resch Expo, which is adjacent to Lambeau Field.\par \par \uc2 Signs around the interior include \u8220\'20\'1CA NEW WAY FORWARD FOR WISCONSIN,\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CGREEN BAY\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cvote.\u8221\'20\'1D Stage podium features fall colored mums and pumpkins.\par \par \uc2 Handheld signs include references such as \u8220\'20\'1CCHEESEHEADS\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CWISCONSIN\u8221\'20\'1D for \u8220\'20\'1CHARRIS WALZ.\u8221\'20\'1D Also some of the camo \u8220\'20\'1CHarris Walz\u8221\'20\'1D signs, and the blue version.\par \par \uc2 Speakers haven\u8217\'20\'19t started as of 6.40pm CT.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLast night you may have seen that I went on Fox News. Meanwhile Trump joined the Univision town hall\u8230\'20\'26where a voter asked him about January 6th.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She says, \u8220\'20\'1CAs we all know, January 6th was a tragic day\u8230\'20\'26 and what did Dobald Trump say about January 6th? He called it, quote: \u8216\'20\'18a day of love\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Americans are \u8220\'20\'1Csick of his gaslighting\u8221\'20\'1D, she says. \u8220\'20\'1CWe are ready to turn the page\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The crowd chants \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re not going back! We\u8217\'20\'19re not going back!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo Green Bay, we have 19 days until the election. 19 days. So we are entering the home stretch,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo many of you may know, when I was five years old we lived in Wisconsin,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says. Every time she lands in the state the governor, \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 , says \u8220\'20\'1CWelcome home\u8221\'20\'1D, she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Wisconsin is a swing state with 10 electoral college votes. Democrats call it the \u8220\'20\'1Cland of the nail-biter\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.54am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is walking onto the stage in Green Bay, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.46am BST\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the League of Women Voters of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/wisconsin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2  has called on the Department of Justice to investigate text messages they say targeted and threatened to discourage young people from voting in the November election.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 League of Women Voters\uc2  says it initially learned of the alleged text campaign on 10 October, when the group received numerous complaints from voters who had received the text. Two people in their 20s who work with the \uc2 League of Women Voters\uc2  also received the message, which reads: \u8220\'20\'1CWARNING: Violating WI Statutes 12.13 & 6.18 may result in fines up to $10,000 or 3.5 years in prison. Don\u8217\'20\'19t vote in a state where you\u8217\'20\'19re not eligible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The rules governing voter eligibility for college students are no different than for any other Wisconsin residents, who are required to have lived at their current address for at least 28 days before the election to vote there.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/election-wisconsin-voter-texts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Malicious\u8217\'20\'19 texts sent to Wisconsin youths to discourage them from voting}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the crowd in Green Bay, Wisconsin, where Harris is expected to speak shortly:\par \par \uc2 enltr??I\u8217\'20\'19m in Green Bay, Wisconsin, where \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is hosting a rally with just 19 days to go before Election Day. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/kjYS3kodB1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/kjYS3kodB1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dan Shafer (@DanRShafer) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanRShafer/status/1847045568016928854?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump will headline the annual Al Smith charity dinner, on Thursday night.\par \par \uc2 Eight years ago he was jeered by attendees while delivering an especially pointed speech.\par \par \uc2 Harris is skipping attending the event in person as she campaigns in battleground states, breaking with presidential tradition. But she will appear on screen in a recorded video, organisers said.\par \par \uc2 The white tie dinner in New York raises millions of dollars for Catholic charities and has traditionally offered candidates from both parties the chance to trade light-hearted barbs and show that they can get along \u8211\'20\'13 or at least pretend to \u8211\'20\'13 for one night in the election\u8217\'20\'19s final stretch.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s often the last time the two nominees share a stage before Election Day.\par \par \uc2 Trump will be joined at the dinner by his wife, Melania, who has been an infrequent presence on the campaign trail, according to a seating chart shared by organizers.\par \par \uc2 He is expected to speak at 9.15pm EDT \u8211\'20\'13 in about an hour and a half\u8217\'20\'19s time.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.26am BST\par \par \uc2 ICYMI: Trump called himself the 'father of IVF'\par \par \uc2 In case you missed those comments from Trump: during a Fox News town hall taped Tuesday, Trump declared that he is \u8220\'20\'1Cthe father of IVF\u8221\'20\'1D, despite acknowledging during his answer that he needed an explanation of IVF in February, after the Alabama supreme court ruled that frozen embryos can be considered children under state law.\par \par \uc2 Trump said he instructed Katie Britt, a Republican senator from Alabama, to \u8220\'20\'1Cexplain IVF very quickly\u8221\'20\'1D to him in the aftermath of the ruling.\par \par \uc2 As concerns over access to fertility treatments rose, Trump pledged to promote IVF by requiring health insurance companies or the federal government to pay for it. Such a move would be at odds with the actions of much of his own party.\par \par \uc2 Even as the Republican party has tried to create a national narrative that it is receptive to IVF, these messaging efforts have been undercut by GOP state lawmakers, Republican-dominated courts and anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  leaders within the party\u8217\'20\'19s ranks, as well as opposition to legislative attempts to protect IVF access.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to play clips of Trump talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Green Bay, Wisconsin rally\par \par \uc2 Tonight in Green Bay, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  plans to spotlight \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including showing the Wisconsin voters what Trump has been saying about women on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 She will respond to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s baffling comments calling himself the \u8220\'20\'1Cfather of IVF\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That event is expected to start any minute \u8211\'20\'13 we will bring it to you live.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 A former funeral home owner from Long Island, New York, pleaded guilty today to spraying wasp killer at police officers and assaulting two journalists, including an Associated Press photographer, during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 riot at the US Capitol}}}\uc2  almost four years ago.\par \par \uc2 Peter Moloney, 60, of Bayport, is now scheduled to be sentenced on February 11 by US district judge Carl Nichols, AP reports.\par \par \uc2 Moloney answered the judge\u8217\'20\'19s routine questions as he pleaded guilty to two assault charges stemming from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/trump-capitol-american-carnage-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 January 6}}}\uc2 , 2021, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/09/us-capitol-insurrection-white-supremacist-terror"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack on Congress}}}\uc2  by a mob of supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as they aspired to overturn his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/nov/24/us-election-results-2020-joe-biden-defeats-donald-trump-to-win-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 loss to Joe Biden}}}\uc2  in the presidential election the previous November.\par \par \uc2 enltrA former co-owner of Moloney Family Funeral Homes pleaded guilty to a pair of assault charges related to his participation in the Jan. 6, 2021, riot at the U.S. Capitol, the U.S. Attorney\u8217\'20\'19s Office for the District of Columbia announced.\par \par \uc2 Peter Moloney, 60, of Bayport, admitted to\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/POF4HIlPW9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/POF4HIlPW9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Newsday (@Newsday) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Newsday/status/1846975011107622975?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Moloney, who co-owned Moloney Family Funeral Homes, was arrested in June 2023. Moloney appears to have come to the Capitol \u8220\'20\'1Cprepared for violence,\u8221\'20\'1D equipped with protective eyewear, a helmet and a can of insecticide, according to an \uc2 FBI\uc2  agent\u8217\'20\'19s affidavit. Video shows him spraying the insecticide at officers, the agent wrote.\par \par \uc2 Video also captured Moloney participating in a vicious attack on an AP photographer who was documenting the unfolding situation. Moloney pleaded guilty to charges including a felony assault. Congress returned to session and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/congress-certify-election-biden-republicans-object"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 certified Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victory}}}\uc2  in the early hours of January 7, 2021.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 The overwhelming majority of young Americans worry about the climate crisis, and more than half say their concerns about the environment will affect where they decide to live and whether to have children, new research finds.\par \par \uc2 The study comes just weeks after back-to-back hurricanes, Helene and Milton, pummeled the south-eastern US. Flooding from Helene caused more than 600 miles of destruction, from Florida\u8217\'20\'19s west coast to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/15/asheville-arts-community"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 mountains of North Carolina}}}\uc2 , while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/12/florida-hurricane-milton-helene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Milton}}}\uc2  raked across the Florida peninsula less than two weeks later.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne of the most striking findings of the survey was that this was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/us-election-hurricanes-climate-voter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 across the political spectrum}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said the lead author, Eric Lewandowski, a clinical psychologist and associate professor at the \uc2 NYU Grossman School of Medicine\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThere was no state sample where the endorsement of climate anxiety came in less than 75%.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The study was published in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lanplh/article/PIIS2542-5196(24)00229-8/fulltext"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lancet Planetary Health}}}\uc2 , and follows a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2021/sep/14/four-in-10-young-people-fear-having-children-due-to-climate-crisis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2021 study}}}\uc2  covering 10 countries. Both the previous and current study were paid for by \uc2 Avaaz\uc2 , an advocacy group.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2024/oct/17/young-americans-climate-change"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Overwhelming majority of young Americans worry about climate crisis}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says death of \uc2 Yahya Sinwar\uc2  is chance to finally end Israel-Gaza war\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has hailed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/17/israeli-military-says-it-may-have-killed-hamas-leader-yahya-sinwar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the death of Yahya Sinwar}}}\uc2  as an opportunity to finally end the war in Gaza and prepare for \u8220\'20\'1Cthe day after\u8221\'20\'1D when \uc2 Hamas\uc2  no longer dominated the territory.\par \par \uc2 The US vice-president and Democratic nominee said \u8220\'20\'1Cjustice has been served\u8221\'20\'1D with the death of the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  leader, adding that the US, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  and the wider world were \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter off as a result\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Locked in a titanic election contest with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to win the battleground state of Michigan, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/hamtramck-donald-trump-arab-american-muslim"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 home to a large Arab-American voting bloc sympathetic to the Palestinian cause,}}}\uc2  Harris also pressed for an end to the year-long hostilities that have killed more than 42,000 people in Gaza and left a trail of destruction in the territory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Hamas\uc2  is decimated and its leadership is eliminated,\u8221\'20\'1D she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.msnbc.com/msnbc/watch/harris-delivers-statement-on-death-of-hamas-leader-yahya-sinwar-222005829607"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CThis moment gives us an opportunity to finally end the war in Gaza.\u8221\'20\'1D The end of the conflict had to be accompanied by security for Israel, the release of the remaining hostages and an end to suffering in Gaza, she said.\par \par \uc2 She also hinted at her support for Palestinian statehood by saying it should herald Palestinians\u8217\'20\'19 rights to \u8220\'20\'1Cdignity, security, freedom and self-determination\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Her comments chimed with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/10/17/statement-from-president-joe-biden-on-the-death-of-yahya-sinwar/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 those of Joe Biden}}}\uc2 , who has been criticised by progressives for unstinting support for Israel even while Netanyahu had ignored his entreaties to avoid civilian casualties and ease humanitarian suffering in the tiny coastal territory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael has had every right to eliminate the leadership and military structure of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/hamas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hamas}}}\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in comments that appeared designed to answer criticisms of his support.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/17/kamala-harris-yahya-sinwar-death-reactions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris says death of Yahya Sinwar is chance to finally end Israel-Gaza war}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump has said he received a call from the \uc2 Apple\uc2  CEO \uc2 Tim Cook\uc2  over concerns about the financial penalties that have been imposed by the \uc2 European Union\uc2  on the iPhone maker, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Apple\uc2  did not respond to the agency\u8217\'20\'19s request seeking confirmation of the authenticity of the phone call.\par \par \uc2 European regulators have launched a series of investigations into big tech firms in recent years, with the aim of curbing their power and ensuring a level playing field for smaller rivals.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTwo hours ago, three hours ago, he (Cook) called me,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said, while speaking with podcaster Patrick Bet-David in a program that was released on Thursday. \u8220\'20\'1CHe said the \uc2 European Union\uc2  has just fined us $15bn \u8230\'20\'26 then on top of that they got fined by the \uc2 European Union\uc2  another $2bn,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump added, quoting his call with Cook.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 At a rally earlier in Wisconsin \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  responded to hecklers in the crowd, saying: \u8220\'20\'1COh you guys are at the wrong rally. I think you meant to go to the smaller one down the street.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here is that clip:\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala Harris: Oh, you guys are at the wrong rally. I think you meant to go to the smaller one down the street {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/tjhbDB9m3R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/tjhbDB9m3R}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1847024907521347765?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today so far\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/10/17/statement-from-president-joe-biden-on-the-death-of-yahya-sinwar/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2  on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s killing of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief \uc2 Yahya Sinwar\uc2 . In his statement, Biden called the killing a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood day for Israel, for the United States, and for the world\u8221\'20\'1D, adding that he planned to speak to \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  and other Israeli leaders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  also commented on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s killing of Sinwar while on the campaign trail in Milwaukee, Wisconsin. \u8220\'20\'1CThis moment gives us an opportunity to end the war in Gaza,\u8221\'20\'1D the US vice-president and Democratic nominee for president in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this election}}}\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  told the audience at the Univision town hall last night that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe can\u8217\'20\'19t destroy our country\u8221\'20\'1D in order to save the planet from the climate crisis. Answering a question from a veteran construction worker, who had seen first-hand \u8220\'20\'1Cthe devastating impacts of climate change\u8221\'20\'1D, whether he still believed global warming was a hoax, Trump launched into a lengthy tirade.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At a rally in Durham, North Carolina, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  delivered a fiery criticism of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWhen Trump is talking about bringing back stop-and-frisk policies, those are harassment that went on to the Black community, specifically Black males, and put a disproportionate number of them into incarceration,\u8221\'20\'1D he told supporters.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden announced today further student debt relief for public servants \u8211\'20\'13 amounting to about $4.5bn. The action affects about 60,000 borrowers across the country, said the White House, touting the efforts of the US president and Harris to improve loan forgiveness since taking office.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Surrogates for the Harris-Walz campaign, meanwhile, are questioning Trump\u8217\'20\'19s cognitive abilities, pointing to his recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/15/trump-dancing-pennsylvania-rally"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 40-minute musical interlude}}}\uc2  at a town hall where he was meant to be answering voters\u8217\'20\'19 questions.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Mark Cuban\uc2 , the billionaire executive and TV personality who appeared alongside Harris in Wisconsin:\par \par \uc2 enltr"I don't know what happened to him" -- Cuban highlights Trump's decline from the 1990s to today {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vshjjS9pQb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vshjjS9pQb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1847012296213545058?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 , who appeared with \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  in North Carolina, quipped: \u8220\'20\'1CHeck, I\u8217\'20\'19m only two months younger than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . But the good news for you is I will not spend 30 minutes swaying back and forth to music.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says Americans done with Trump's 'gaslighting' as she criticizes January 6 remarks\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, in LaCrosse, Wisconsin, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  slammed Trump\u8217\'20\'19s performance at the Univision town hall yesterday, when he referred to 6 January 2021, when rioters stormed the capitol and injured over 140 police officers, \u8220\'20\'1Ca day of love\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe American people are exhausted with his gaslighting. Enough. We are ready to turn the page. We\u8217\'20\'19re done,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 During the Univision town hall, a Republican voter told Trump the former president had lost his vote due to his response to the January 6 riots and the coronavirus pandemic. Trump responded: \u8220\'20\'1CNothing done wrong at all.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere were no guns down there. We didn\u8217\'20\'19t have guns. The others had guns, but we didn\u8217\'20\'19t have guns,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd when I say we, these are people that walked down \u8211\'20\'13 this was a tiny percentage of the overall which nobody sees and nobody, nobody shows. But that was a day of love.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  condemnds Trump's stop-and-frisk pledge at campaign rally in North Carolina\par \par \uc2 At a rally in Durham, North Carolina, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  delivered a fiery criticism of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen Trump is talking about bringing back stop-and-frisk policies, those are harassment that went on to the Black community, specifically Black males, and put a disproportionate number of them into incarceration,\u8221\'20\'1D he told supporters.\par \par \uc2 Walz also slammed the idea that Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cunderstood\u8221\'20\'1D the needs of voters. \u8220\'20\'1CIf any of our relatives \u8230\'20\'26 tells us \u8216\'20\'18\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  understands us\u8217\'20\'19, that\u8217\'20\'19s bullshit. He does not understand us. He does not understand you,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said, noting that the former president didn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Cgive a damn\u8221\'20\'1D if social security checks cleared.\par \par \uc2 He appeared at the rally alongside former president \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 enltrWalz: "Let's us start saying the quiet part out loud about Trump... when Trump is talking about bringing back stop and frisk policies, those are harassment that went on to the Black community, specifically Black males, and put a disproportionate number of them into incarceration" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aEOF2hRmBN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/aEOF2hRmBN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1847014695745548765?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 The stakes: US cities are preparing to defend themselves if Trump wins\par \par \uc2 Senior Democrats in US cities are preparing to defend their communities in the event of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s return to the White House after the former president has repeated threats that he would use presidential powers to seize control of major urban centers.\par \par \uc2 Trump has proposed deploying the military inside major cities largely run by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  to deal with protesters or to crush criminal gangs. He has threatened to dispatch large numbers of federal immigration agents to carry out mass deportations of undocumented people in so-called \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary\u8221\'20\'1D cities.\par \par \uc2 He also aims to obliterate the progressive criminal justice policies of left-leaning prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn cities where there has been a complete breakdown of law and order \u8230\'20\'26 I will not hesitate to send in federal assets including the national guard until safety is restored,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says in the campaign platform for his bid to become the 47th US president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.donaldjtrump.com/agenda47/agenda47-president-trump-announces-plan-to-end-crime-and-restore-law-and-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Agenda47}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/trump-military-enemy-within-armed-forces-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provoked uproar}}}\uc2  earlier this week when he called for US armed forces to be deployed against his political rivals \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy within\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 on election day next month. But his plans to use national guard troops and military personnel as a means to attack those he sees as his opponents go much wider than that, spanning entire cities with Democratic leadership.\par \par \uc2 Mayors and prosecutors in several US cities are collaborating over strategies to minimize the fallout. \uc2 Levar Stoney\uc2 , the Democratic mayor of Richmond, Virginia, a city of more than 220,000, said he was aware how difficult it would be to resist Trump given the enormous powers at a president\u8217\'20\'19s disposal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very difficult to autocrat-proof your city,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut you have to have backstops, and mayors are working in coalition to ensure they can be a backstop against these divisive policies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/17/trump-wins-elections-outcomes-stakes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 If Trump wins the election, US cities are at risk of military takeovers and mass deportations}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Newly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.azcourts.gov/highprofilecases/Cases/FileList?id=Gallego%20and%20Gallego"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unsealed divorce records}}}\uc2  show Arizona congressman \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2 , the Democratic nominee for an open Senate seat, petitioned a court to end his marriage with \uc2 Kate Gallego\uc2 , Phoenix\u8217\'20\'19s mayor, just before she gave birth to their son. But it contained none of the potentially damaging details conservatives had hoped to uncover.\par \par \uc2 Gallego\u8217\'20\'19s opponent, Kari Lake, has long alluded to the filings, making insinuations that their contents would tarnish his public persona. Ahead of the release, one of her advisers sought to distance the campaign from the effort to unseal the documents, an effort brought by the conservative outlet, Washington Free Beacon.\par \par \uc2 The couple split in 2016 after six years of marriage. The congressman has previously said that his post-traumatic stress disorder from serving in Iraq contributed to the demise of their marriage.\par \par \uc2 The Gallegos had fought the release, expressing concern that the public disclosure could endanger their son, Michael. The effort to keep the records sealed fanned rightwing speculation about what was in them.\par \par \uc2 Kate Gallego\uc2  has endorsed her husband\u8217\'20\'19s Senate bid.\par \par \uc2 In June, Yavapai superior court judge John Napper, who originally presided over the Free Beacon\u8217\'20\'19s case, tempered expectations well in advance, according to a video obtained by 12 News.\par \par \uc2 enltrUPDATE 'One of the most garden variety divorce files I've ever seen': At June hearing, Yavapai County Judge John Napper saw nothing striking in court files for Congressman \uc2 Ruben Gallego\uc2  & Mayor \uc2 Kate Gallego\uc2 's 2017 divorce. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/12News?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @12News}}}\uc2  has learned unsealed docs do redact info on son. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nRUsq1UtWD"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nRUsq1UtWD}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brahm Resnik (@brahmresnik) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brahmresnik/status/1846768465631220203?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEveryone\u8217\'20\'19s going to be rather deflated with the results of it,\u8221\'20\'1D Napper said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m not a politician, and maybe this will be very, very important information but this looks to me like one of the most garden-variety divorce files I have ever seen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US has granted temporary protected status to Lebanese nationals amid Israel\u8217\'20\'19s deadly war on the country.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Michael Sainato reports:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Department of Homeland Security\uc2  (DHS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dhs.gov/news/2024/10/17/dhs-offers-protections-lebanese-nationals-currently-united-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  a new \u8220\'20\'1Ctemporary protected status\u8221\'20\'1D allowing Lebanese nationals in the US to remain in the country and apply for work permits, as the \u8220\'20\'1Congoing armed conflict\u8221\'20\'1D in Lebanon continues with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/what-to-know-about-the-israel-hezbollah-conflict"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/14/israeli-airstrike-kills-christian-town-northern-lebanon-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expanding its invasion}}}\uc2  and its attacks on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/hezbollah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hezbollah}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As of July 2024, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/news/politics/2024/07/26/lebanese-citizens-united-states-biden/74558502007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 around 11,500 Lebanese nationals}}}\uc2  were believed to be in the US on nonimmigrant visas for business, tourism, temporary work or other opportunities, with California and Michigan hosting the most. About 11,000 of them will probably now be eligible to apply for temporary protected status, as well as for deferred enforced departure \u8211\'20\'13 in other words, protection from deportation. An additional 1,740 students from Lebanon may also be eligible for special student relief.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/17/temporary-protected-status-lebanon-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US grants temporary protected status to Lebanese nationals amid Israel war}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , has also weighed in on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s killing of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  chief \uc2 Yahya Sinwar\uc2 , saying in a statement on Thursday:\par \par \uc2 Sinwar has the blood of countless innocents in Israel and Gaza on his hands and the world is a much better place without him \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Sinwar in his beliefs and actions have caused so much pain to the Israeli and Palestinian people; and I pray that his elimination from the scene will clear a path to urgently and immediately bring home all the hostages \u8211\'20\'13 including the seven Americans \u8211\'20\'13 and negotiate an end to hostilities that will ensure the security of the Israeli people and provide full humanitarian relief and a new path forward for the people of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Schumer made no mention of Palestinians\u8217\'20\'19 right to self-determination.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US will try to push forward a ceasefire and hostage -release proposal following Israel\u8217\'20\'19s killing of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  chief \uc2 Yahya Sinwar\uc2 , Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 Speaking during a press briefing on Thursday, state department spokesperson \uc2 Matthew Miller\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1COver the past few weeks, there have been no negotiations for an end to the war because Sinwar has refused to negotiate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden hails Sinwar death as 'good day for Israel'\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has released a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2024/10/17/statement-from-president-joe-biden-on-the-death-of-yahya-sinwar/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement }}}\uc2  on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s killing of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Gaza chief \uc2 Yahya Sinwar\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In his statement, Biden called the killing a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood day for Israel, for the United States, and for the world\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Biden went on to add, \u8220\'20\'1CAs the leader of the terrorist group \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , Sinwar was responsible for the deaths of thousands of Israelis, Palestinians, Americans, and citizens from over 30 countries.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver 1,200 people were killed on that day, the deadliest day for Jews since the Holocaust, including 46 Americans. More than 250 were taken hostage, with 101 still missing. That number includes seven Americans, four of whom are believed to still be alive and held by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  terrorists. Sinwar is the man most responsible for this, and for so much of what followed,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden continued in his statement.\par \par \uc2 He added that he will be speaking soon with Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  and other Israeli leaders to \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscuss the pathway for bringing the hostages home to their families, and for ending this war once and for all, which has caused so much devastation to innocent people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Notably, Biden made no mention of the 42,400 Palestinians \u8211\'20\'13 including healthcare workers and journalists \u8211\'20\'13 that Israeli forces killed since October or the nearly 2 million survivors who Israeli forces have forcibly displaced across the narrow strip.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says 'justice has been served' over death of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  leader Sinwar\par \par \uc2 Moments ago, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  stepped up to a podium while on the election trail in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, and commented on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s stating that it killed \uc2 Yahya Sinwar\uc2 , the leader of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , in a battle in Gaza today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis moment gives us an opportunity to end the war in Gaza,\u8221\'20\'1D the US vice-president and Democratic nominee for president in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this election}}}\uc2 , said.\par \par \uc2 She said \u8220\'20\'1Cjustice has been served\u8221\'20\'1D over the reported killing of the leader of the Islamist militants that control Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Harris reiterated the administration\u8217\'20\'19s stance that \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael has the right to defend itself and called for the remaining hostages held by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  since it led an attack on southern Israel on October 7, 2023, to be released.\par \par \uc2 But she added that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe suffering must end\u8221\'20\'1D in Gaza and said it was \u8220\'20\'1Ctime for the day after to begin without \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in power\u8221\'20\'1D. Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  has not pledged a ceasefire.\par \par \uc2 We are live blogging all the developments in Gaza, Lebanon and Israel, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/oct/17/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-israel-iran-lebanon-gaza-war#top-of-blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the Middle East, the government of Israel has announced its military forces have killed \uc2 Yahya Sinwar\uc2 , the leader of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , in a battle in Gaza. This comes less than three weeks after Israel also killed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/sep/29/hassan-nasrallah-obituary"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hassan Nasrallah}}}\uc2 , the head of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 , during air strikes on the outskirts of Beirut in Lebanon.\par \par \uc2 Confirmation on Sinwar\u8217\'20\'19s death is awaited from the Palestinian side. If verified that means the heads of Iran\u8217\'20\'19s two most powerful proxy forces opposed to Israel have been wiped out. We are following all the developments on this live in our international blog and you can find all that news {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/oct/17/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-israel-iran-lebanon-gaza-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Interim summary\par \par \uc2 Hello, US politics blog readers, it\u8217\'20\'19s another lively day on the campaign trail with less than three weeks to go before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the election}}}\uc2 . There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot more news to come and we\u8217\'20\'19ll keep up with developments as they happen.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  told the audience at the Univision town hall last night that \u8220\'20\'1Cwe can\u8217\'20\'19t destroy our country\u8221\'20\'1D in order to save the planet from the climate crisis. Answering a question from a veteran construction worker, who had seen first-hand \u8220\'20\'1Cthe devastating impacts of climate change\u8221\'20\'1D, whether he still believed global warming was a hoax, Trump launched into a lengthy tirade.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  posted that \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  incited an attack on our nation\u8217\'20\'19s democracy because he didn\u8217\'20\'19t like the outcome of the election. If January 6 [2021] was a bridge too far, there is a place for you in our campaign.\u8221\'20\'1D This is further outreach from the Democratic nominee for president herself, including to hammer home facts about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/trump-capitol-american-carnage-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the insurrection}}}\uc2  at the US Capitol that day. It came a day after she did an interview with rightwing Fox News and led a rally attended by more than 100 prominent Republicans.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, will campaign in Durham and Winston-Salem in North Carolina with Common today, to mark the first day of early voting in that important swing state. The Emmy-winning rapper and voting rights activist is to join Walz in Winston-Salem, in a push to get out the vote.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris is on a swing through two vital \u8220\'20\'1Cblue wall\u8221\'20\'1D states today, with campaign stops including Milwaukee, La Crosse and Green Bay in Wisconsin, then heading to Grand Rapids, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced today further student debt relief for public servants \u8211\'20\'13 amounting to about $4.5bn. The action affects about 60,000 borrowers across the country, said the White House, touting the efforts of the US president and Harris, his vice-president and successor as presidential nominee, to improve loan forgiveness since taking office.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has released some details about his rally schedule for the coming days.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, Trump will hold a town hall in Lancaster, Pennsylvania, at 5pm.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, he will deliver remarks at a rally in Greenville, North Carolina, at 3pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 In another state hit hard by hurricanes recently, early voting is underway.\par \par \uc2 Many voters had to relocate after Hurricane Helene hit North Carolina, where \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is making a campaign stop. But the state\u8217\'20\'19s board of elections is ensuring those displaced or who live in an area under the federal disaster declaration can still vote via an absentee ballot.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you had to relocate due to the storm, you do not have to return to your county to vote. You can request to have your ballot delivered to your temporary housing location or wherever you can receive mail,\u8221\'20\'1D the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncsbe.gov/helene#AbsenteeVoting-4063"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 website}}}\uc2  of North Carolina state board of election reads.\par \par \uc2 Absentee ballots can be requested at a local county board of elections office during business hours, or online at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://votebymail.ncsbe.gov/app/home"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina absentee ballot portal}}}\uc2  until 5pm on 29 October and must be received no later than 7.30pm on 5 November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 Hurricanes like Milton and Helene, which recently battered US states in the south, is top of mind for many voters. Those who live in natural disaster-prone areas increasingly at risk due to the climate crisis have even more at stake.\par \par \uc2 Despite this, many of these residents are still choosing to back \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , a vocal climate denier. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Oliver Laughland and Tom Silverstone travelled to south-west Louisiana to speak to some of these communities.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump told town hall: 'We can't destroy our country' to save climate\par \par \uc2 During \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Univision town hall, the former president pushed back on the climate crisis, telling an audience member at one point : \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t destroy our country\u8221\'20\'1D in order to save the climate.\par \par \uc2 Answering a question from a veteran construction worker who had seen first-hand \u8220\'20\'1Cthe devastating impacts of climate change\u8221\'20\'1D on whether he still believed global warming was a hoax, Trump launched into a lengthy tirade, saying:\par \par \uc2 I get awards, environmental awards, for the way I build it for the water, the way I use the water, the sand, the mixing of the sand and the water, I mean, many different, but I\u8217\'20\'19ve had many awards over the years for environmental, the way I\u8217\'20\'19ve built because you know about building, that\u8217\'20\'19s what you do \u8230\'20\'26 \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrQ: Given the amount of the mounting evidence of climate change, do you still believe it's a hoax?\par \par \uc2 Trump: I get awards environmental awards for the way I build it for the water, the way I use the water, the sand, the mixing of the sand and the water, I mean, many different, but\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/CPEBBdxXFl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/CPEBBdxXFl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1846747316633411673?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s team will ban Project 2025 affiliates from a future administration, according to Politico.\par \par \uc2 Robert Tait reports for the Guardian:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  transition team is reportedly preparing a blacklist of potential officials to be banned from a future administration, with special emphasis being placed on those with links to the radical {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2  plan to overhaul the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s eldest son, Donald Jr, is spearheading the drive to compile the list of barred staffers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/10/16/trump-transition-hiring-staffer-ban-00183208"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to Politico}}}\uc2 , citing a former official in the first Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClearly people working on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2  are blacklisted,\u8221\'20\'1D another ex-official told the site.\par \par \uc2 The Republican nominee publicly disowned the 922-page document, prepared by \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  thinktank, after polls showed that its ideologically driven prescriptions \u8211\'20\'13 including mass firings of civil servants and plans to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 were an electoral liability.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/17/trump-team-project-2025-banned-staffers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump team to ban Project 2025 affiliates from future administration \u8211\'20\'13 report}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris hits out at Trump's 'day of love' comment\par \par \uc2 In response to a video of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  answering a question from an audience member during a Univision town hall in which he said the January 6 riot was a \u8220\'20\'1Cday of love \u8221\'20\'1D, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  wrote on X:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  incited an attack on our nation\u8217\'20\'19s democracy because he didn\u8217\'20\'19t like the outcome of the election.\par \par \uc2 If January 6 was a bridge too far, there is a place for you in our campaign.\par \par \uc2 enltrDonald Trump incited an attack on our nation\u8217\'20\'19s democracy because he didn\u8217\'20\'19t like the outcome of the election.\par \par \uc2 If January 6 was a bridge too far, there is a place for you in our campaign. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YWmubEBHkg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/YWmubEBHkg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@KamalaHarris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris/status/1846905096790999427?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 17, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump has repeatedly said that he did not lose the 2020 election \u8211\'20\'13 a baseless claim which his running mate JD Vance doubled down on this week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/17/jd-vance-trump-2020-election-lost"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  saying}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CDid \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lose the election? Not by the words that I would use.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will travel to Atlanta, Georgia, this weekend for a campaign rally.\par \par \uc2 According to her campaign, Harris will use the rally to encourage Georgians to vote early.\par \par \uc2 The US vice-president has visited the crucial battleground state at least 8 times this year. Her upcoming visit to Atlanta will follow a rally that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  held in the city on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz to campaign in North Carolina with the rapper Common\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will campaign in Durham and Winston-Salem in North Carolina today to mark the first day of early voting.\par \par \uc2 The Emmy-winning rapper and voting rights activist Common will join Walz in Winston-Salem where the two will speak to North Carolinians about the importance of voting, according to the Harris-Walz campaign.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 When Lauren Miller found out she was pregnant with twins in the summer of 2022, she was shocked and excited. But an early scan revealed that one of the twins was not developing at the same pace as the other. He had severe abnormalities, and a rare chromosomal disorder called trisomy 18.\par \par \uc2 Lauren lives in Dallas, Texas, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is illegal unless the pregnancy places the woman at risk of death or \u8220\'20\'1Csubstantial impairment of a major bodily function\u8221\'20\'1D. Carter Sherman, the Guardian US \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  and justice reporter, explains why this exception does not necessarily reassure women wanting treatment:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2024/oct/17/how-abortion-became-a-battleground-issue-of-the-us-election-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  became a battleground issue of the US election \u8211\'20\'13 podcast}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to campaign in three Wisconsin cities today\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is set to travel through Wisconsin today, Politico reports.\par \par \uc2 Her stops include Milwaukee, La Crosse and Green Bay, as well as a college business class. The US vice-president will also hold two rallies before heading to Grand Rapids, Michigan.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here are some key takeaways from \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Fox News interview, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Helen Sullivan reports:\par \par \uc2 1. Immigration\par \par \uc2 Harris was asked about the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/04/biden-us-mexico-border-asylum-seekers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tackle a surge in illegal immigration}}}\uc2  at the southern border, and laid the blame on Republicans for failing to pass a border bill.\par \par \uc2 Harris was asked to defend the administration\u8217\'20\'19s early decision to reverse some of her Republican rival \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s restrictive policies, and to respond to a mother who testified in Congress about the loss of her child at the hands of an illegal immigrant.\par \par \uc2 2. The Biden-Harris record\par \par \uc2 Harris was questioned over her recent comment that there was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a thing\u8221\'20\'1D she would change about the actions of the Biden administration, responding: \u8220\'20\'1Clet me be very clear, my presidency will not be a continuation of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency,\u8221\'20\'1D but she did not elaborate.\par \par \uc2 Harris was asked when she first noticed that Biden\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cmental faculties appeared diminished\u8221\'20\'1D, but the vice-president responded by saying that the president had the judgment and experience to do what needs to be done on behalf of the American people.\par \par \uc2 For the full story, click here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/17/kamala-harris-fox-news-interview-key-takeaways"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Key takeaways from Fox News interview: Harris grilled on immigration, the Middle East and Biden\u8217\'20\'19s record }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , said Tuesday that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  would \u8220\'20\'1Ccut her own path\u8221\'20\'1D if elected, as the Democratic nominee tries to convince voters she would bring change to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Agence France-Presse reports:\par \par \uc2 Harris came under fire from her Republican rival, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , last week after saying there was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot a thing comes to mind\u8221\'20\'1D when asked what she would have done differently from Biden.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery president has to cut their own path. That\u8217\'20\'19s what I did. I was loyal to \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  but I cut my own path as president,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden told a Democratic party dinner in Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s going to do. She\u8217\'20\'19s been loyal so far but she\u8217\'20\'19ll cut her own path.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden added: \u8220\'20\'1CKamala\u8217\'20\'19s perspective on our problems will be fresh and new. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s perspective is old and failed and quite frankly thoroughly totally dishonest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Senior Democrats in US cities are preparing to defend their communities in the event of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2  return to the White House after the former president has repeated threats that he would use presidential powers to seize control of major urban centers.\par \par \uc2 Trump has proposed deploying the military inside major cities largely run by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats}}}\uc2  to deal with protesters or to crush criminal gangs. He has threatened to dispatch large numbers of federal immigration agents to carry out mass deportations of undocumented people in so-called \u8220\'20\'1Csanctuary\u8221\'20\'1D cities.\par \par \uc2 He also aims to obliterate the progressive criminal justice policies of left-leaning prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn cities where there has been a complete breakdown of law and order \u8230\'20\'26 I will not hesitate to send in federal assets including the national guard until safety is restored,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump says in the campaign platform for his bid to become the 47th US president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.donaldjtrump.com/agenda47/agenda47-president-trump-announces-plan-to-end-crime-and-restore-law-and-order"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Agenda47}}}\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/trump-military-enemy-within-armed-forces-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 provoked uproar}}}\uc2  earlier this week when he called for US armed forces to be deployed against his political rivals \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy within\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 on election day next month. But his plans to use national guard troops and military personnel as a means to attack those he sees as his opponents go much wider than that, spanning entire cities with Democratic leadership.\par \par \uc2 Mayors and prosecutors in several US cities are collaborating over strategies to minimize the fallout. \uc2 Levar Stoney\uc2 , the Democratic mayor of Richmond, Virginia, a city of over 220,000, said he was aware how difficult it would be to resist Trump given the enormous powers at a president\u8217\'20\'19s disposal.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s very difficult to autocrat-proof your city,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut you have to have backstops, and mayors are working in coalition to ensure they can be a backstop against these divisive policies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 You can read more of Ed Pilkington\u8217\'20\'19s news feature here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/oct/17/trump-wins-elections-outcomes-stakes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 If Trump wins the election, US cities are at risk of military takeovers and mass deportations}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US Republican candidate, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , on Tuesday said that companies will drop plans to build factories overseas when faced with the threat of high tariffs on shipping goods to the US, reports Agence France-Presse (AFP).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe higher the tariff, the more likely it is that the company will come into the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president told an audience at the Economic Club of Chicago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou make it so high, so horrible, so obnoxious\u8221\'20\'1D companies will \u8220\'20\'1Ccome right away,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 The economy has emerged as one of the main issues ahead of the 5 November US election, where Trump is in a dead heat with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , according to polls.\par \par \uc2 The former president has vowed a 10% to 20% across-the-board tariff on imports and a 60% rate on Chinese goods \u8211\'20\'13 and more recently threatened a 200% levy on vehicles made in Mexico.\par \par \uc2 AFP reports that during the hour-long interview, Trump pushed back at arguments that tariffs would hike costs for consumers and punish businesses faced with higher-priced imports. \u8220\'20\'1CTo me, the most beautiful word in the dictionary is tariff,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden approves $4.5 bn in student debt relief as vote nears\par \par \uc2 The US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , announced on Thursday further student debt relief for public servants \u8211\'20\'13 amounting to about $4.5bn \u8211\'20\'13 with just over two weeks to go until the presidential election, reports Agence France-Presse (AFP).\par \par \uc2 The action affects about 60,000 borrowers across the country, said the White House, touting Biden and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to improve loan forgiveness since taking office.\par \par \uc2 AFP reports that the announcement comes as US households feel the weight of higher costs of living since the Covid-19 pandemic, with voters citing the economy as a crucial concern in polls.\par \par \uc2 Biden said in a statement that with the latest move, more than one million people have had their debt cancelled under Public Service Loan Forgiveness.\par \par \uc2 The promise of the programme \u8211\'20\'13 supporting teachers, nurses and others \u8211\'20\'13 involved student debt forgiveness after 10 years of public service and 10 years of payments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut for too long, the government failed to live up to its commitments, and only 7,000 people had ever received forgiveness,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said. \u8220\'20\'1CI will never stop working to make higher education affordable,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 Biden has embarked on efforts to cancel student debt for millions of Americans, after a student loan payment freeze instituted by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  during the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Americans hold $1.6tn in student loans, and some end up repaying them over decades as they start jobs and families.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , will spend Friday in Berlin with the German chancellor, \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2 , reports the Associated Press (AP).\par \par \uc2 There is also a planned meeting with other leaders in the \u8220\'20\'1CEuropean quad\u8221\'20\'1D, a group that in addition to Biden and Scholz includes the French president, \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , and the UK prime minister, \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The White House press secretary, \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2 , described Biden as having a \u8220\'20\'1Cclose relationship\u8221\'20\'1D with Scholz, who early this year helped broker a multi-country prisoner swap that brought back to the US the journalist \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2  and former marine Paul Whelan. The German leader told Biden before the deal in words to the effect: \u8220\'20\'1CFor you, I will do this,\u8221\'20\'1D reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have worked together closely to strengthen our economies for both our people and provide critical support for Ukraine as it continues to defend itself against Russian aggression,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said at Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s White House briefing. \u8220\'20\'1CThe president really wanted to make sure to go to Germany to thank chancellor Scholz directly.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The US and Germany have been the largest two sources of aid to Ukraine as it fights to repel a Russian invasion. And with less than three weeks before the US presidential election, Biden also feels obliged to ready allies for the possible return to the White House of the Republican Trump, who has antagonized US friends while displaying an appreciation for the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , reports the AP.\par \par \uc2 The administration said Biden has no plans while in Europe to meet with the Ukrainian president, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2 , but the two spoke on Wednesday about additional military aid, with the White House announcing $425m in assistance, bringing the total support to more than $64bn over two and a half years.\par \par \uc2 In addition to Ukraine, Biden and Scholz plan to discuss EU relations, democratic values, trade and technology issues, global supply chains, tensions in the Middle East and security issues in the Indo-Pacific region, reports the AP. While in Germany, Biden will also meet with its president, \uc2 Frank-Walter Steinmeier\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, Biden delayed a trip planned to Germany and Angola in order to oversee relief efforts ahead of Hurricane Milton making landfall in Florida. He now plans to go to Angola in December.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43am BST\par \par \uc2 At Wednesday\u8217\'20\'19s Miami town hall, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sidestepped a question on immigration, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 One town hall participant, a Mexican-born California farm worker who spoke of picking strawberries and broccoli for years, asked who would do hard farm labor if Trump goes through with his plans to deport millions of people who are in the US illegally, and how that would impact food prices.\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters, Trump did not answer directly and instead claimed African Americans and Hispanic Americans were losing their jobs because of illegal immigration. He also repeated baseless claims that Latin American countries were emptying out mental institutions and jails to send people to the US.\par \par \uc2 Trump has previously used dehumanizing terminology to describe immigrants in the US illegally, calling them \u8220\'20\'1Canimals\u8221\'20\'1D when talking about alleged criminal acts, and saying they are \u8220\'20\'1Cpoisoning the blood of our country\u8221\'20\'1D, a phrase that has drawn criticism as xenophobic and echoing Nazi rhetoric.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.29am BST\par \par \uc2 In the final weeks before the 5 November election, the Republican candidate, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , is increasingly resorting to darker and more violent language about illegal immigration, an issue that opinion polls show resonates with many voters, especially Republicans, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 He is competing against the Democratic candidate, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , for key votes from the growing Latino population. Latino voters have typically backed Democrats, but the Trump campaign is hoping to win over more, especially men, on the back of economic discontent.\par \par \uc2 Harris led Trump by eight percentage points \u8211\'20\'13 47% to 39% \u8211\'20\'13 among Hispanic voters in Reuters/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  polling conducted between 11 September and 7 October.\par \par \uc2 Harris held her own Latino town hall last week in Nevada, a battleground state with a significant Hispanic population.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.16am BST\par \par \uc2 'Just saying what was reported' - Trump stands by debunked Ohio immigrants eating pets claims\par \par \uc2 The Republican presidential candidate, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , on Wednesday stood by debunked claims that immigrants in Ohio were eating pets, telling Latino voters during a town hall he was \u8220\'20\'1Cjust saying what was reported\u8221\'20\'1D, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Trump in recent weeks has amplified a false claim that has gone viral that Haitian immigrants in Springfield, Ohio, were stealing residents\u8217\'20\'19 pets or taking wildlife from parks for food.\par \par \uc2 There have been no credible reports of Haitians eating pets, and officials in Ohio \u8211\'20\'13 including Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 have repeatedly said the story is untrue.\par \par \uc2 At a town hall hosted by the Spanish-language television network Univision, an undecided Mexican-born Latino Republican voter from Arizona, a battleground state, asked Trump in Spanish whether he truly believed that immigrants were eating pets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was just saying what was reported \u8230\'20\'26 And eating other things too that they\u8217\'20\'19re not supposed to be. All I do is report,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump replied during the event held in Miami. \u8220\'20\'1CI was there, I\u8217\'20\'19m going to be there and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to take a look.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to Reuters, Trump added that \u8220\'20\'1Cnewspapers\u8221\'20\'1D had also reported on the claim, without naming any or providing any details.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has not yet traveled to Springfield, has previously said he would conduct mass deportations of Haitian immigrants from the Ohio city, even though the majority of them are in the US legally.\par \par \uc2 The city has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/17/bomb-threats-springfield-schools-highway-patrol"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 faced bomb threats}}}\uc2  since Trump began repeating the false accusations about Haitians.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/17/donald-trump-miami-town-hall-migrants-eating-pets-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump stands by debunked claims immigrants are eating pets at event for Hispanic voters}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  describes 6 January Capitol riots as 'day of love' during Miami town hall\par \par \uc2 The Republican presidential candidate, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , on Wednesday described 6 January 2021, when thousands of his supporters attacked the Capitol in Washington DC in a bid to stop formal certification of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election defeat, as a \u8220\'20\'1Cday of love\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During a town hall with a Latino audience, hosted by Spanish-language television network Univision yesterday, Trump was told by a participant that he wanted to give the former US president a chance to \u8220\'20\'1Cwin back his vote\u8221\'20\'1D given his concerns over the 6 January 2021 Capitol riot, reports Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of Trump supporters attacked the Capitol in Washington DC that day causing millions of dollars in damage. Four people died on the day of the attack, and one \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  officer who fought against the rioters died the next day.\par \par \uc2 At the town hall in Miami, Trump gave a lengthy response in which he described 6 January 2021 as a \u8220\'20\'1Cday of love\u8221\'20\'1D and said former administration officials who had turned against him were angry about having been fired.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope someday maybe we\u8217\'20\'19ll get your vote,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said as he wrapped up. \u8220\'20\'1CSounds like maybe I won\u8217\'20\'19t, but that\u8217\'20\'19s OK too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also stood by debunked claims that immigrants in Ohio were eating pets, telling Latino voters during a town hall he was \u8220\'20\'1Cjust saying what was reported\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Trump in recent weeks has amplified a false claim that has gone viral that Haitian immigrants in Springfield, Ohio, were stealing residents\u8217\'20\'19 pets or taking wildlife from parks for food.\par \par \uc2 There have been no credible reports of Haitians eating pets, and officials in Ohio \u8211\'20\'13 including Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 have repeatedly said the story is untrue.\par \par \uc2 More on this story in a moment, but first, here are the latest updates:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Surrounded by more than 100 former Republican officeholders and officials, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  urged GOP voters on Wednesday to put \u8220\'20\'1Ccountry first\u8221\'20\'1D and abandon Trump. Trump is \u8220\'20\'1Cunstable\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cunhinged\u8221\'20\'1D and would eviscerate democratic norms if given a second White House term, she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica must heed this warning\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In her interview on Fox News, Harris was asked about the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to tackle illegal immigration at the southern border, and laid the blame on Republicans for failing to pass a border bill. Harris said Trump told Republicans to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/23/senate-democrats-immigration-border-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reject the bill}}}\uc2  because \u8220\'20\'1Che preferred to run on a problem instead of fixing a problem.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In the Fox interview, Harris singled out Iran when asked which foreign country she considers to be America\u8217\'20\'19s greatest adversary. The interviewer, Bret Baier, questioned whether the Biden-Harris administration was \u8220\'20\'1Cacting like Iran is the number one threat\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, JD Vance answered \u8220\'20\'1Cno\u8221\'20\'1D when asked if Trump lost the 2020 election, at a Pennsylvania rally. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat message do you think it sends to independent voters when you do not directly answer the question \u8216\'20\'18Did \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lose in 2020?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D the reporter asked, eliciting boos from the crowd. Vance said, \u8220\'20\'1CNo. I think there were serious problems in 2020\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump doubled down on his controversial comments about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy from within\u8221\'20\'1D made over the weekend. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/fox-news-trump-town-hall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Before an all-female audience in Cumming, Georgia}}}\uc2 , Trump mocked Harris and her allies as \u8220\'20\'1Csick\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cevil\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ca party of soundbites\u8221\'20\'1D. He told the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/fox-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fox News}}}\uc2  anchor Harris Faulkner: \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re very dangerous. They\u8217\'20\'19re Marxists and communists and fascists. They\u8217\'20\'19re the threat to democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 In Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Univision town hall he was asked to name three virtues possessed by Harris, which he did, before again attacking her. He said that \u8220\'20\'1Cshe seems to have an ability to survive,\u8221\'20\'1D that \u8220\'20\'1Cshe seems to have some pretty longtime friendships\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Cshe seems to have a nice way about her.\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, I like the way some of her statements, some of her \u8211\'20\'13 the way she behaves, in a certain way. But in another way, I think it\u8217\'20\'19s very bad for our country,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  judge has declared that seven new election rules recently passed by the state election board are \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal, unconstitutional and void\u8221\'20\'1D. The Fulton county superior court judge, Thomas Cox, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/georgia-election-rules-trump-board-unconstitutional"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued the order on Wednesday}}}\uc2  after holding a hearing on challenges to the rules. The rules that Cox invalidated included three that had garnered a lot of attention: one that required that the number of ballots be hand-counted after the close of polls and two that had to do with the certification of election results.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2 , the centenarian former Democratic president, has voted in the 2024 presidential election, his representatives confirmed on Wednesday. A statement from the \uc2 Carter Center{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/election-jimmy-carter-votes-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 did not reveal who he voted for}}}\uc2 , but it is assumed the 100-year-old, who is in hospice care, cast his ballot for the Democratic candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Alabama cannot remove thousands of people from its voter rolls on the eve of the presidential election,{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/election-alabama-voting-rolls-registration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a federal judge ruled on Wednesday}}}\uc2 . The US district judge Anna Manasco, an appointee of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump}}}\uc2 , issued a preliminary injunction halting an effort by Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s top election official to try to remove more than 3,200 people from the voter rolls who it suspected of being non-citizens until at least after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential election}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The League of Women Voters of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/wisconsin"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wisconsin}}}\uc2  has called on the Department of Justice to investigate text messages they say targeted and tried to discourage young people from votingin the November election. The \uc2 League of Women Voters\uc2  says it initially learned of the alleged text campaign on 10 October, when the group {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/election-wisconsin-voter-texts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received numerous complaints}}}\uc2  from voters who had received the text. Two people in their 20s who work with the \uc2 League of Women Voters\uc2  also received the message, which reads: \u8220\'20\'1CWARNING: Violating WI Statutes 12.13 & 6.18 may result in fines up to $10,000 or 3.5 years in prison. Don\u8217\'20\'19t vote in a state where you\u8217\'20\'19re not eligible.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.16pm BST\par \par 