E5B91CE38CE3BD145007FFD9}}
\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 US election live: Trump holds rally in Atlanta \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); Maanvi Singh , Chris Stein and Vicky Graham (earlier) \par \uc2 12,889 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 October 2024\par 14:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss important election coverage. Get our free app and sign up for election alerts\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59am BST\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re going to end this live coverage now. Thanks for following along. You can find all of the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s US elections coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is thanking various supporters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is Vermont senator Bernie Sanders on CNN a short while ago. He spoke about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s actions on and in the lead up to the January 6 storming of the Capitol:\par \par \uc2 enltrSen. Bernie Sanders: "There is a reason why his own Vice President \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , who sat by his side for four years, is not supporting him. Why \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2 , the most maybe conservative vice president in the modern history of this country, is not supporting them.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xdtOrgdFTf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xdtOrgdFTf}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1846366826147512596?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.00am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.44am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump has been speaking for 40 minutes.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is now repeating racist and baseless claims about immigrants.\par \par \uc2 Here is further reading on the impacts of his rhetoric:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/13/trump-anti-immigrant-racism-hate-white-supremacy-springfield"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18He gives them the green light\u8217\'20\'19: Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric revives hate groups across US}}}\par \par \uc2 And the Guardian view on his attacks:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/sep/22/the-guardian-view-on-trumps-attacks-on-migrants-smirking-racism-is-no-less-dangerous"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Guardian view on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on migrants: smirking racism is no less dangerous | Editorial}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.37am BST\par \par \uc2 How China sees its future with the US after the election\par \par \uc2 Speaking of China, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Amy Hawkins, Helen Davidson and Chi Hui Lin have this report on how China sees its future with the US after the election:\par \par \uc2 Deciphering the obscure machinations of elite politics is a pursuit that western China-watchers are all too familiar with. But as the US election approaches, it is analysts in China who are struggling to read the tea leaves on what differentiates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  when it comes to their stance on the US\u8217\'20\'19s biggest geopolitical rival.\par \par \uc2 Commentators are calling it the vibes election. For Beijing, despite the cheers and whoops of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign, her vibes are largely similar to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHarris will continue Biden\u8217\'20\'19s policies\u8221\'20\'1D on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/china"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 China}}}\uc2 , says Wang Yiwei, a professor of international studies at Renmin University in Beijing. What are Biden\u8217\'20\'19s policies? He is a \u8220\'20\'1CTrumpist without the Trump\u8221\'20\'1D, says Wang.\par \par \uc2 Harris has done little to dispel the belief that her stance on China will be largely the same as Biden\u8217\'20\'19s, should she win the election in November. In her headline speech at the Democratic national convention on 22 August, China was mentioned just once: she promised to ensure that \u8220\'20\'1CAmerica, not China, wins the competition for the 21st century\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris has little foreign policy record to be judged on. But in an economic policy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2024/08/16/remarks-by-vice-president-harris-at-a-campaign-event-in-raleigh-nc/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 speech}}}\uc2  on 16 August, she emphasised her goal of \u8220\'20\'1Cbuilding up our middle class\u8221\'20\'1D, a vision that Biden has used to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2024/05/14/remarks-by-president-biden-remarks-by-president-biden-on-his-actions-to-protect-american-workers-and-businesses-from-chinas-unfair-trade-practices/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 justify}}}\uc2  placing high tariffs on Chinese imports, extending \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s trade war.\par \par \uc2 Beijing fundamentally does not see there being much difference between a Democratic- or Republican-controlled White House. Indeed, hawkishness on China has become one of the few bipartisan issues in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.foreignaffairs.com/united-states/does-china-prefer-harris-or-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent piece}}}\uc2  for Foreign Affairs, leading foreign policy commentators Wang Jisi, Hu Ran and Zhao Jianwei wrote that \u8220\'20\'1CChinese strategists hold few illusions that US policy toward China might change course over the next decade \u8230\'20\'26 they assume that whoever is elected in November 2024 will continue to prioritise strategic competition and even containment in Washington\u8217\'20\'19s approach to Beijing.\u8221\'20\'1D The authors predicted that although Harris\u8217\'20\'19s policymaking would likely be more \u8220\'20\'1Corganised and predictable\u8221\'20\'1D than Trump\u8217\'20\'19s, both would be \u8220\'20\'1Cstrategically consistent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/16/china-us-trade-harris-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Taiwan and trade: how China sees its future with the US after the election}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump again complains about electric cars that \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t go very far\u8221\'20\'1D and are \u8220\'20\'1Cmade in China\u8221\'20\'1D. Then he walks that back to say that electric cars can be good and that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  makes them.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump veers from thoughts on public speaking to say we will \u8220\'20\'1Cfrack, frack, frack and drill, drill, drill\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He seems to forget where he is, and says, \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t forget, Pennsylvania\u8221\'20\'1D. He is in Georgia. He was in Pennsylvania yesterday.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is patting himself on the back for not using a teleprompter.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is now griping about the \u8220\'20\'1Cwoke military\u8221\'20\'1D. He plays a series of clips that I can\u8217\'20\'19t see \u8211\'20\'13 more soon.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is now saying that he is reluctant to talk about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s record in San Francisco because it could bring down the value of property he owns.\par \par \uc2 He then plays a series of media clips and clips of Harris about taxes; it includes Harris saying that corporate taxes should be raised.\par \par \uc2 Trump wants to lower corporate tax rates to 15%, Harris wants to increase them to 28%.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/25/harris-opportunity-economic-plan-middle-class"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris says cost of living \u8216\'20\'18still too high\u8217\'20\'19 as she lays out economic agenda}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.29am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is speaking to a large audience in Atlanta, and despite the long wait, they are clapping and cheering during the speech, which is littered with false and unsubstantiated claims, especially about immigration.\par \par \uc2 enltra look at Trump's crowd tonight {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lcbBtYTbSx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lcbBtYTbSx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1846357190476529883?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump claims that \u8220\'20\'1Cstarting on day one I will quickly defeat inflation \u8230\'20\'26 we will bring down energy costs. Liquid gold\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.18am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI got a lot of rich friends. They go here, they go there ,they\u8217\'20\'19re boring as hell,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 Then Trump pivots to his misleading claim that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  did not pass her bar exam.\par \par \uc2 From factchecking site Verify This: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump\u8217\'20\'19s claims are misleading. Harris failed the bar exam on her first attempt, but passed on her second try.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.24am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is encouraging people to vote. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t want to take a chance, we can\u8217\'20\'19t lose this country,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 He claims, without evidence, that the American standard of living \u8220\'20\'1Cis in a freefall\u8221\'20\'1D and that \u8220\'20\'1Cnothing works\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He says \u8220\'20\'1Cwe\u8217\'20\'19re teetering on the brink of World War Three\u8221\'20\'1D and lists other well-worn problems, including his claims that \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal aliens are pouring into the country.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But other than that we\u8217\'20\'19re doing well, he says.\par \par \uc2 He promises that if he wins it will be a \u8220\'20\'1Cgolden time\u8221\'20\'1D. He thanks \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  for giving him \u8220\'20\'1Cthe greatest endorsement\u8221\'20\'1D. He talks about Space X\u8217\'20\'19s latest rocket test, which he says he watched while on a call with someone \u8220\'20\'1Cwho couldn\u8217\'20\'19t have been that interesting\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.16am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump arrives at Atlanta event 90 minutes late\par \par \uc2 Trump has finally appeared \u8211\'20\'13 90 minutes late \u8211\'20\'13 at his event in Atlanta. We have not yet seen an explanation for why he is so late. He is expected to being speaking shortly, though, given the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/15/us-election-briefing-harris-airs-clips-of-her-opponents-interviews-at-rally-while-trump-hosts-a-musical-fest"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cmusical fest\u8221\'20\'1D he chose to hold yesterday}}}\uc2  after cutting his town hall short, who knows.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.11am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is now running an hour and 20 minutes late for his speech in Atlanta, Georgia.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46am BST\par \par \uc2 CNN reports that the number of people who voted early in Georgia today has now risen to 300,000.\par \par \uc2 The previous record for the number of votes cast on the first day of early voting was 136,000 in 2020.\par \par \uc2 enltrUpdate: More than 300,000 people cast their votes today during the first day of early voting in Georgia, per \uc2 Gabriel Sterling\uc2 . The number is 123% higher than the previous record for the first day of voting. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Ymy33D55xb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/Ymy33D55xb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1846348674873311697?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 16, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41am BST\par \par \uc2 A campaign to restore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Missouri so far has raised close to $22m, the Associated Press reports, citing finance reports filed on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The campaign reported bringing in more than $14m between July and the end of September.\par \par \uc2 Missourians for Constitutional Freedom seeks to undo the state\u8217\'20\'19s near-total \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and is one of nine statewide campaigns to enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into state constitutions.\par \par \uc2 The campaign had close to $11m in the bank at the beginning of the month to spend on advertising in the final weeks before the election.\par \par \uc2 Donors to the Missouri campaign include model Karlie Kloss, who gave $50,000, and the former New York mayor \uc2 Michael Bloomberg\uc2 , who last month chipped in $1m. Other big funders include \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2 , Sixteen Thirty Fund and The Fairness Project, among others.\par \par \uc2 A Missouri political action committee opposing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights amendment has raised about $212,000 and had less than $5,000 left at the beginning of October. The political action committee of the powerful anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  group Missouri Right to Life so far has spent at least $637,000 opposing the amendment.\par \par \uc2 Initiative petition campaigns tend to cost a lot of money in Missouri, and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ballot measures in other states have been hugely expensive.\par \par \uc2 A 2022 fight over protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in Ohio cost a combined $70m, with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters pitching in nearly $40m and opponents spending more than $30m. The \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  amendment passed with almost 57% of the Ohio vote.\par \par \uc2 This year, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights groups have out raised opponents by a nearly eight-to-one margin in campaigns for ballot measures across the US.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.25am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.36am BST\par \par \uc2 CNN has an interesting story on the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s approach to \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , where, according to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/10/15/politics/daily-scroll-facebook-harris-campaign-ads/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN report}}}\uc2 , it has spent $11m to promote a page, maintained by the campaign, called The Daily Scroll.\par \par \uc2 The social media ads, which are adorned with a nondescript logo resembling a pair of checkmarks, have promoted news articles from mainstream outlets including CNN, ABC and NBC, showing easing US inflation, cheaper insulin prices, and the consequences of state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Overall, the Harris campaign has far outspent the Trump campaign on Meta\u8217\'20\'19s platforms, spending nearly $80 million on ads since this summer, compared with about $9.4 million from Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign and associated fundraising committees.\par \par \uc2 Unlike the Harris campaign\u8217\'20\'19s main \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2  accounts, the ads run by The Daily Scroll and Headlines 2024 aren\u8217\'20\'19t soliciting donations, and most of them aren\u8217\'20\'19t directing users to the campaign\u8217\'20\'19s website. Instead, the Harris team is using the ads to promote select news stories from major media outlets that reflect well on the Democratic presidential nominee and poorly on Trump.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.39am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.25am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is more on Biden\u8217\'20\'19s speech.\par \par \uc2 Biden said \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  would \u8220\'20\'1Ccut her own path\u8221\'20\'1D once she wins the 2024 election, allowing for more daylight between him and his vice-president as she works to win over skeptical voters three weeks before election day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKamala will take the country in her own direction, and that\u8217\'20\'19s one of the most important differences in this election,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CKamala\u8217\'20\'19s perspective on our problems will be fresh and new. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s perspective is old and failed and quite frankly, thoroughly totally dishonest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 AP reports:\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments may give Harris more licence to stake out her own political and policy stances in the critical closing phase of the presidential race, and appear to go further to distance the two than Harris has herself. The vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s aides have privately expressed some frustration that the 81-year-old president has been too focused on his own legacy \u8211\'20\'13 and not the race to succeed him.\par \par \uc2 But Harris has of late faced increasing pressure to articulate how she\u8217\'20\'19d govern differently from Biden, a question trickier than it seems on the surface.\par \par \uc2 While Biden\u8217\'20\'19s favorability ratings remain underwater, some of the biggest pieces of his legislative agenda, from infrastructure to lowering the costs of some prescription drugs, are popular, and signaling any daylight with the president on foreign policy at a time of global crises could be seen as reckless.\par \par \uc2 Harris herself has been loathe to do anything that could be perceived as disloyal to Biden, who elevated her from a first-term senator to the vice-presidency, and then handed the reins of his political operation over to her, endorsing Harris when he dropped out of the race in July.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.26am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.14am BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 US Justice Department\uc2  will send election monitors to an Ohio county where a sheriff was recently accused of intimidating voters in a social media post, federal officials announced Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 AP reports that the justice department said it will monitor Portage county\u8217\'20\'19s compliance with federal voting rights laws during early voting and on election day. The agency said it regularly sends staff to counties around the US to monitor compliance with the federal Voting Rights Act and other civil rights statutes related to elections and voting.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CVoters in Portage County have raised concerns about intimidation resulting from the surveillance and the collection of personal information regarding voters, as well as threats concerning the electoral process,\u8221\'20\'1D the justice department said in a news release.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is so far running almost 40 minutes late to his rally in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.02am BST\par \par \uc2 Biden spoke a short while ago on behalf of Harris in Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 He said of Trump that he used to hide is racism, but that now it is \u8220\'20\'1Cout front\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe has the same ideas on race as the 1930s. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ideas on economy are from the \u8217\'20\'1920s. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ideas on women are from the \u8217\'20\'1950s. Folks, this is 2024, we can\u8217\'20\'19t go back.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrBiden: "He has the same ideas on race as the 1930s. Trump's ideas on economy are from the '20s. Trump's ideas on women are from the '50s. Folks, this is 2024 -- we can't go back." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DGXpMEJMpM"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DGXpMEJMpM}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1846339829803438444?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.14am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is expected to hold a rally shortly in Atlanta, Georgia. We will bring you any key developments from that live.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.48am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris was asked why people \u8220\'20\'1Care acting like this is going to be a free and fair election\u8221\'20\'1D, given the events of 6 January 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 and those leading up to it \u8211\'20\'13 and the conservative-leaning supreme court.\par \par \uc2 She said: \u8220\'20\'1CSo it will be a free and fair election if we, the American people, stand up for that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris was asked by a caller about Trump saying he would use a law from 1798 to carry out mass deportations.\par \par \uc2 She responded: \u8220\'20\'1CSo you\u8217\'20\'19ve hit on a really important point and expressed it, I think so well, which is he is achieving his intended effect to make you scared. He is running full time on a campaign that is about instilling fear, not about optimism, not about the future, but about fear. And so this is yet another example.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.22am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Charlamagne tha God said to Harris: \u8220\'20\'1CI had a politician tell me once that if you\u8217\'20\'19re running for a national election, it\u8217\'20\'19s bad electoral strategy to say you are going to do things for Black people, which is why a lot of politicians don\u8217\'20\'19t speak directly to their plans for Black people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris responded: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t know that that\u8217\'20\'19s true. I think that what is true is that I am running to be president for everybody, but I\u8217\'20\'19m clear-eyed about the history and the disparities that exist for specific communities, and I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to shy away from that. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean that my policies aren\u8217\'20\'19t going to benefit everybody, because they are \u8211\'20\'13everything I just talked about will benefit everybody.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.44am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.11am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris was asked about her stance on reparations, too.\par \par \uc2 She said, \u8220\'20\'1CIt has to be studied. There\u8217\'20\'19s no question about that, and I\u8217\'20\'19ve been very clear about that position.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris, in that response on her town hall, also pointed out that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is selling bibles for $60 (\u163\'00\'A346).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his followers spend full time trying to suggest that the measure of the strength of a leader is based on who you beat down, which is absolutely contrary to the church,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhere our church, and my church, is about saying true leadership, the measure of that is based on who you lift up and right. And then he\u8217\'20\'19s selling $60 bibles or tennis shoes and trying to play people as though that makes him more understanding of the Black community. Come on.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.13am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.07am BST\par \par \uc2 In her interview with Charlamagne tha God on Tuesday, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was asked whether she had engaged enough with the Black church.\par \par \uc2 Harris said that allegations she had not engaged with the Black church \u8220\'20\'1Ccomes from the Trump team \u8230\'20\'26 they are trying to disconnect me from the people I have worked with and that I\u8217\'20\'19m from,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI grew up in the Black church. I grew up attending 23rd Avenue Church of God in Oakland, California. That\u8217\'20\'19s church. My pastor is Amos C Brown, of Third Baptist Church in San Francisco, California. I have, throughout my career and as vice-president and recently, been actively engaged in the church and church leaders, not only so we can share in fellowship, but so we can share in what we can do together that is about supporting the community,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.12am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is a bit more on the record early voting numbers in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Voters in Georgia turned out in record numbers as the battleground state opened early voting for the 5 November presidential election between Democrat \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Republican \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , state officials said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 At least 252,000 voters had cast ballots at early-voting sites as of 4pm ET (8pm GMT), nearly double the 136,000 who participated in the first day of early voting in the 2020 election, said \uc2 Gabriel Sterling\uc2 , Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s No2 election official. \u8220\'20\'1CSpectacular turnout,\u8221\'20\'1D he wrote on social media.\par \par \uc2 Early voting, either in person or by mail, has become increasingly popular with US voters. Nearly one in seven voters cast their ballots ahead of election day in 2020, according to the University of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Election Lab. However, many Republicans opposed the dramatic expansion of mail voting that year, saying it was less secure than in-person voting, and Trump cited false claims of mail ballot fraud as he sought unsuccessfully to overturn his defeat byJoe Biden in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans continue to insist that voters should be able to cast their ballots only in person on election day, though party officials are encouraging supporters to vote ahead of time.\par \par \uc2 Nationwide, 5.5 million Americans have already voted this year, according to Election Lab. By contrast, 27 million people had cast their ballots at this point in the 2020 election as voters sought to avoid crowded polling places during the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Like some other states, Georgia has tightened its mail-in voting laws since then, requiring voters who want to cast an absentee ballot to provide proof of identity and limiting the number of places they can deposit their ballots.\par \par \uc2 Georgia, with 16 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/11/us-election-2024-trump-harris-terms-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 electoral college}}}\uc2  votes, is one of the seven competitive battleground states expected to play a decisive role in deciding the election.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/11/us-election-2024-trump-harris-terms-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sun belt to October surprise: US election terms explained}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris defends record as a prosecutor as she attempts to shore up support with black voters\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  defended her record as a prosecutor and pledged to decriminalize marijuana as president in Detroit on Tuesday, as she aims to shore up support among Black men in an interview with radio host Charlamagne tha God.\par \par \uc2 Charlamagne, a Black comedian and author who hosts radio program The Breakfast Club, is known for his blunt interviews of celebrities.\par \par \uc2 Although he is a Harris supporter, he has been critical of her and \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in the past and called Democrats \u8220\'20\'1Ccowards\u8221\'20\'1D for ineffectively prosecuting a case against Republican presidential candidate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . One of his first questions was asking Harris to address a common rumour \u8211\'20\'13 that she disproportionately locked up Black men over her more than a dozen years as San Francisco\u8217\'20\'19s district attorney.\par \par \uc2 Harris said she was \u8220\'20\'1Cone of the most progressive prosecutors\u8221\'20\'1D on marijuana cases, and would work to decriminalise it, because she knows how that has hurt certain populations, especially Black men.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is holding a town hall in Detroit hosted by Charlamagne tha God.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CSo can you imagine you go to a city and you say you want the votes of those people and you disparage that city,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris is saying now. She is referring to Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments last week in Detroit.\par \par \uc2 The former US president and Republican nominee was speaking on Thursday at the Detroit Economic Club in the city, which is the biggest city in Michigan \u8211\'20\'13 one of the most crucial swing states in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 US election}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But Trump, whose speeches are frequently rambling and lengthy discourses rather than set piece deliveries, could not stop himself from lambasting the city in which he was speaking by pointing to Detroit\u8217\'20\'19s recent history of economic decline from its heyday as the home of American car production.\par \par \uc2 As he was speaking about China being a developing nation, Trump said: \u8220\'20\'1CWell, we\u8217\'20\'19re a developing nation too, just take a look at Detroit. Detroit\u8217\'20\'19s a developing area more than most places in China.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He later returned to the theme, warning of an economic disaster if his Democratic opponent, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , wins in November\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur whole country will end up being like Detroit if she\u8217\'20\'19s your president. You\u8217\'20\'19re going to have a mess on your hands,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 This is Helen Sullivan taking over the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s live US elections coverage.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.24pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Early voting has begun in several states including Georgia, where a record number of voters are casting ballots.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  spoke at Economic Club of Chicago, where he dodged questions about the peaceful transfer of power, refused to say whether he had spoken with Russia\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  since the election and promoted his tariff-heavy proposals that economic expects say will do little to address inflation and will likely push prices higher.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  joined a town hall in Detroit hosted by Charlemagne Tha God.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump was scheduled to appear on CNBC this week, but backed out unexpectedly. It was the second time the former president canceled an interview recently, after declining to appear on the popular CBS News show 60 Minutes\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 There are many theories about why presidential polls have moved so little since Harris entered the race in July. In an interview today with CNN, veteran Republican pollster Frank Luntz said the atmosphere is beginning to remind him of 2016, when \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  lost to Trump, despite winning the popular vote.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  spent the day in the key swing state of Pennsylvania. Wearing a plaid shirt, Walz spoke at a farm in Volant, Pennsylvania \u8211\'20\'13 a small town with a population of just 125 \u8211\'20\'13 to tout his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s agenda for rural America.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 More than a quarter-million Georgia voters cast ballots by 4 pm on the first day of early voting Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Lines stretched as much as two hours at some locations in Atlanta at peak times. For context, about 130,000 people cast early ballots in person on the first day of early voting in 2020. So far, about 260,000 Georgians have requested an absentee ballot.\par \par \uc2 Voters at the Buckhead branch of the Fulton county library said they were concerned about the economy, the tone of the election and attacks on immigrants, but particularly \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 John Dodson, an orchestra conductor from Atlanta, said he voted for Harris.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think she\u8217\'20\'19s enormously capable, and I believe that she understands this moment, that she is the right person to lead us from this moment,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThis moment is unique. We are divided as we have not been since the time just before the civil war. And while I hope it wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8211\'20\'13 and don\u8217\'20\'19t think it would \u8211\'20\'13 rise to those kinds of outcomes, the foundations of the public are being shaken. Frankly, the way we have seen ourselves is being re-evaluated in ways I could never have imagined. So I think this is a very important moment for us to re-establish norms and return to what made us the \u8216\'20\'18shining city on the hill\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With regard to the \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  quote Dodson referenced, he said Reagan \u8220\'20\'1Cwas quoting someone else, and that is the point. He and I could disagree with a policy, and would have, but that isn\u8217\'20\'19t what we\u8217\'20\'19re discussing. We\u8217\'20\'19re now talking about the functioning of the democracy and whether we simply seize power by hook or crook, or whether we actually allow people a voice in their governance. That\u8217\'20\'19s the real issue underneath this contest.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think that election day plus one will be a very difficult day for a lot of people, and election day plus two, and election day plus three, but also Thanksgiving, and also December, at Christmas, or at the New Year\u8217\'20\'19s party or at Hanukkah. I mean, I think that when you really think about it, one half of this country will be very, very unhappy with the results. But the question is, and you spoke about the tenor of this conversation, the conversation has degraded to a point of coarseness, and fear is ruling a huge amount of this discourse. And under fear comes this feeling of being threatened. And when you get threatened, people get angry. And so then, now we\u8217\'20\'19ve filled a country with weapons, and I, too, worry that there are people who really do seem to feel that an outcome that is OK here is a violent outcome, So, this is the point: this is not the great experiment that has been us. And we\u8217\'20\'19ve got to try to find our north star again and return.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris has spent the town hall addressing very specific policies, focusing on a list of plans to boost the middle class, and help Americans though an affordability crisis.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m going to extend tax deductions to $50,000. Every first-time homeowner, wherever they are, whatever their race, will benefit if they are [a] first-time homebuyer with a $25,000 down-payment assistance. Everyone is going to benefit from my plan to extend the child tax [credit to] $6,000 for the first year of their child\u8217\'20\'19s life,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 In a substantive discussion, Harris also repeatedly emphasized that policies that will benefit Black Americans will help everybody.\par \par \uc2 Charlemagne: \u8216\'20\'18I had a politician tell me once that if you\u8217\'20\'19re running for a national election, it\u8217\'20\'19s bad electoral strategy to say you are going to do things for Black people, which is why a lot of politicians don\u8217\'20\'19t speak directly to their plans for Black people.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Harris: \u8216\'20\'18I don\u8217\'20\'19t know that that\u8217\'20\'19s true. I think that what is true is that I am running to be president for everybody, but I\u8217\'20\'19m clear eyed about the history and the disparities that exist for specific communities.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  joins town hall hosted by Charlamagne tha God\par \par \uc2 The vice-president has joined a town hall in Detroit, hosted by Charlamagne tha God. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a margin-of-error race. It\u8217\'20\'19s tight. I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna win. I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna win, but it\u8217\'20\'19s tight,\u8221\'20\'1D she told him.\par \par \uc2 The event is being livestreamed on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iheartradio.com/WeThePeople"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 iHeartRadio}}}\uc2 . Prior to the town hall, Harris stopped by the Norwest Gallery of Art for a conversation with Black men about entrepreneurship.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 As early voting begins in Georgia, a county judge in the state has ruled that local officials cannot refuse to certify election results.\par \par \uc2 The ruling from judge Robert McBurney on Monday night rebukes an argument from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies that local election officials should have the discretion to deny the certification of election results.\par \par \uc2 McBurney found that \u8220\'20\'1Cthe superintendent must certify and must do so by a certain time\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 with no exemptions. The ruling could help protect the election against rogue officials, encouraged by Republicans who have falsely alleged widespread fraud in elections.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhile the [election official] must investigate concerns about miscounts and must report those concerns to a prosecutor if they persist after she investigates, the existence of those concerns, those doubts, and those worries is not cause to delay or decline certification,\u8221\'20\'1D McBurney wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CThat is simply not an option for this particular ministerial function in the superintendent\u8217\'20\'19s broader portfolio of functions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is spending the day in the key swing state of Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Wearing a plaid shirt, Walz spoke at a farm in Volant, Pennsylvania \u8211\'20\'13 a small town with a population of just 125 \u8211\'20\'13 to tout his campaign\u8217\'20\'19s agenda for rural America.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen people think rural America, farm policy matters,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. \u8220\'20\'1CCrop insurance matters. Trade matters, tariff matters. But you\u8217\'20\'19re bigger than that. Your families, your healthcare matters, your education matters, your roads matter, your retirement matters, all those things matter.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also tried to push an optimistic message, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI saw the Wall Street Journal said: \u8216\'20\'18Joyfulness isn\u8217\'20\'19t a plan.\u8217\'20\'19 Well, no one said it\u8217\'20\'19s a plan. But it\u8217\'20\'19s a hell of a lot better to be joyful than to be angry and terrible like they\u8217\'20\'19re doing on the other side.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump cancels CNBC interview \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was scheduled to appear on CNBC this week, but backed out unexpectedly, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/15/media/trump-cancel-cnbc-interview-media/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It was the second time the former president had canceled an interview recently, after declining to appear on the popular CBS News show 60 Minutes. He has instead given interviews to rightwing news outlets, and earlier today had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/15/us-election-live-kamala-harris-donald-trump?page=with:block-670e9e298f088ef416005719#block-670e9e298f088ef416005719"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a live conversation}}}\uc2  on economic policy moderated by Bloomberg News.\par \par \uc2 CNN reports that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign cited a scheduling conflict as the reason he could not appear on CNBC\u8217\'20\'19s Squawk Box show.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump canceled, and he was going to come on,\u8221\'20\'1D co-anchor Joe Kernen announced on air earlier today. He added that the network had also asked \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to appear but that \u8220\'20\'1Cshe\u8217\'20\'19s not coming on\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 There are many theories about why presidential polls have moved so little since \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  entered the race in July.\par \par \uc2 In an interview today with CNN, veteran Republican pollster Frank Luntz says the atmosphere is beginning to remind him of 2016, when \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  lost to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , despite winning the popular vote and polls generally showing her with the edge. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what Luntz had to say:\par \par \uc2 enltr"I began to look at this as quite similar to 2016 when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  surprised voters and beat \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 ." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FrankLuntz?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @FrankLuntz}}}\uc2  weighs in on the Trump debate debacle, Harris' narrow lead, the 3 groups to watch for, and why authenticity matters in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Election2024?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Election2024}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/dk3i9dorJ9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/dk3i9dorJ9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Julia Chatterley (@jchatterleyCNN) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jchatterleyCNN/status/1846268205255565695?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 In other swing state news, Mark Robinson, the Republican candidate for governor of North Carolina, is suing CNN after the network revealed his history of lewd and offensive remarks on pornography websites, the Associated Press reports:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/20/mark-robinson-north-carolina-governor-race"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Robinson}}}\uc2 , North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s lieutenant governor, announced a lawsuit Tuesday against CNN over its recent report alleging he made explicit racial and sexual posts on a pornography website\u8217\'20\'19s message board, calling the reporting reckless and defamatory.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, filed in Wake county superior court, comes less than four weeks after a television report that led many fellow GOP elected officials and candidates, including \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , to distance themselves from Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s gubernatorial campaign. Robinson announced the lawsuit at a news conference in Raleigh.\par \par \uc2 CNN \u8220\'20\'1Cchose to publish despite knowing or recklessly disregarding that Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s data \u8211\'20\'13 including his name, date of birth, passwords, and the email address supposedly associated with the NudeAfrica account \u8211\'20\'13 were previously compromised by multiple data breaches\u8221\'20\'1D, the lawsuit states.\par \par \uc2 CNN declined to comment, spokesperson Emily Kuhn said in an email.\par \par \uc2 Polls at the time of the CNN report already showed \uc2 Josh Stein\uc2 , Robinson\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic rival and the sitting attorney general, with a lead over Robinson. Early in-person voting begins Thursday statewide, and well over 50,000 completed absentee ballots have been received so far.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/15/mark-robinson-cnn-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mark Robinson sues CNN over report he wrote racist posts on porn website}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia sees record amount of early voting - report\par \par \uc2 The day is not over, but the Atlanta Journal-Constitution reports that Georgia has seen a record amount of early voting on the first day polls have been open:\par \par \uc2 enltrMore than 200,000 voters have cast ballots in Georgia during the first day of in-person early voting according to state elections officials, shattering the state's record. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mrjIq41dx2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/mrjIq41dx2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Greg Bluestein (@bluestein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bluestein/status/1846257677900697923?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 This is not necessarily indicative of how the swing state, where many polls have shown \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with a narrow lead, will end up voting in November.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 On the first day of early voting in battleground Georgia, one of the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senators, \uc2 Raphael Warnock\uc2 , warned that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was a \u8220\'20\'1Cdangerous\u8221\'20\'1D choice for the country.\par \par \uc2 He urged Black men to consider how Trump would govern, as Harris works to shore up support from this traditionally Democratic-leaning voting bloc.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t buy this idea that there will be huge swaths of Black men voting for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . That\u8217\'20\'19s not going to happen,\u8221\'20\'1D said Warnock, a Baptist pastor, who preaches from the same Atlanta pulpit as \uc2 Martin Luther King\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I would urge folks to do is to show up, to understand that if you don\u8217\'20\'19t vote, that is a vote \u8211\'20\'13 for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , that\u8217\'20\'19s the concern.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Warnock spoke on the call organized by the Harris campaign ahead of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s visit to the state today. Warnock acknowledged the work Democrats still needed to do to mobilize their \u8220\'20\'1Cbroad coalition\u8221\'20\'1D ahead of next month\u8217\'20\'19s election, as polls show Harris drawing notably less support among Black men than past Democratic nominees.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDo you think when the George Floyds and all of those cases emerge again that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s going to do something about it? No, he\u8217\'20\'19s going to do just the opposite,\u8221\'20\'1D Warnock said. \u8220\'20\'1CAn unhinged \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will give these officers who have behaved with brutality a free pass and immunity, and this could literally mean death in our communities. You need to vote like your life depends on it \u8211\'20\'13 it does.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Amber Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s mother wants Americans to know that her daughter was not a statistic.\par \par \uc2 Thurman, a young mother and aspiring nurse, developed sepsis and died after being unable to access legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and routine medical care in Georgia.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CShe was loved by a family, a family that would have done anything had we known when I looked at her and reassured her that she was in the best care,\u8221\'20\'1D Shanette Williams said on a call organized by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign. \u8220\'20\'1CI had no clue. I had no clue that this could have been prevented, and when I found that out, everything changed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the line in November, Thurman\u8217\'20\'19s mother has become a reluctant but powerful surrogate for Harris in the battleground state, where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is banned after six weeks of pregnancy. Harris has said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Republicans should be held accountable for ushering in the post-Roe bans that ultimately led Thurman to wait.\par \par \uc2 The campaign call was timed in advance of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s visit to Georgia today for a town hall on \u8220\'20\'1Cwomen\u8217\'20\'19s issues\u8221\'20\'1D hosted by Fox News.\par \par \uc2 Williams was with her daughter at the hospital, where she waited for more than 20 hours for a routine medical procedure known as a D&C that removes remaining tissue. She developed sepsis and died in August 2022, leaving behind her young son, now eight.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInitially, I wasn\u8217\'20\'19t a political person. I\u8217\'20\'19m independent. Because of August the 19th, we\u8217\'20\'19ve been thrown into an arena where we have to do something to honor Amber,\u8221\'20\'1D Williams said through tears. \u8220\'20\'1CI just need to make sense of it all. My baby is not here, and it\u8217\'20\'19s left us so much pain and trauma.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  talked more about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-capitol-breach"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 6 January 2021}}}\uc2 , and said that there was a term \u8220\'20\'1Cpeaceful and patriotic\u8221\'20\'1D and said \u8220\'20\'1Ca lot of strange things\u8221\'20\'1D happened on that day, mentioning \u8220\'20\'1Cpeople being waved into the Capitol\u8221\'20\'1D by police.\par \par \uc2 He said only \u8220\'20\'1Ca tiny fraction\u8221\'20\'1D of people who came to Washington that day {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/trump-capitol-american-carnage-washington"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went down to the US Capitol}}}\uc2  after his rally close to the White House and \u8220\'20\'1Cnot one of those people had a gun\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cno one was killed\u8221\'20\'1D. He then, as he has done many times before, criticized the shooting by a law enforcement official of rioter Ashli Babbitt as she tried to break into the House chamber as part of the mob that had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/09/us-capitol-insurrection-white-supremacist-terror"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 violently invaded}}}\uc2  the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 In fact, the insurrectionists smashed their way into the Capitol against outnumbered police, as they tried to stop the certification by Congress of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory over Trump in the previous November\u8217\'20\'19s election.\par \par \uc2 At least {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/apr/30/marjorie-taylor-greene-accused-lying-capitol-attack-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seven deaths}}}\uc2 , and perhaps {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/01/05/us/politics/jan-6-capitol-deaths.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 as many as}}}\uc2  nine deaths, have been linked to the January 6 riots, including suicides among police officers some time after the event.\par \par \uc2 After fleeing for their lives, the \uc2 US Congress{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/jan/06/congress-certify-election-biden-republicans-objec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reconvened}}}\uc2  in the early hours of 7 January 2021, to certify {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2020/nov/24/us-election-results-2020-joe-biden-defeats-donald-trump-to-win-presidency"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump dodges question about peaceful transfer of power if he loses election\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was asked about a peaceful transfer of power after this November\u8217\'20\'19s election. He dodged.\par \par \uc2 The interviewer on stage at the Economic Club of Chicago, Bloomberg News editor-in-chief John Micklethwait, said, moments ago: \u8220\'20\'1CIf you look at the events of January 6, 2021, it showed to many people that America\u8217\'20\'19s democracy was unruly and violent. Only three weeks to go to the election, will you commit now to respecting and encouraging a peaceful transfer of power?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Instead of answering the question about this election cycle, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Acyn/status/1846245361964536074"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said that}}}\uc2  the US had a peaceful transfer of power.\par \par \uc2 enltrMicklethwait: Will you commit to respecting and encouraging a peaceful transfer of power?\par \par \uc2 Trump: You had a peaceful transfer of power. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XCou8CMAEl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XCou8CMAEl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1846245361964536074?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 There was a smattering of applause in the audience. Micklethwait said: \u8220\'20\'1CCome on, President Trump, you had a peaceful transfer of power compared with Venezuela but it was by far the worst transfer of power for a long time,\u8221\'20\'1D then added: \u8220\'20\'1CWould you respect the decision?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump digresses with some criticism of Micklethwait. Then he comes back to the topic, but again talking about 2021.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just claimed that, if he became president again, he would have the right to instruct the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  about interest rates \u8211\'20\'13 while saying he would not actually order the US central bank what to do.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think I have the right to say, \u8216\'20\'18I think you should go up or down a little bit\u8217\'20\'19. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think I should be allowed to order it, but I think I have the right to put in comments as to whether or not the interest rates should go up or down,\u8221\'20\'1D he said at the Chicago Economic Club moments ago.\par \par \uc2 The president of the US traditionally does not weigh in on interest rates, allowing the Fed to make its own decisions. This doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean that the bank is not susceptible to political pressure in the wider sense, but the bank expects and is expected to make monetary policy and related decision autonomously.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump refuses to say if he has talked to Russia's Putin since leaving office\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has just declined to comment when asked directly in an event he\u8217\'20\'19s appearing at in Chicago if he has had conversations with Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  since he left the White House in 2021 after being voted out of office.\par \par \uc2 The former president was asked if he had talked to Putin \u8220\'20\'1Csince you stopped being president\u8221\'20\'1D, as has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/08/trump-putin-covid-test-machines-bob-woodward"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stated in a book}}}\uc2  by veteran journalist and author Bob Woodward, reported last week. He asked by Bloomberg News editor-in-chief John Micklethwait moments ago, who is interviewing Trump in an appearance at the Economic Club of Chicago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will not comment,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 However, he then hinted maybe he had when he added: \u8220\'20\'1CBut if I did it\u8217\'20\'19s a smart thing. If I have a good relationship with people, that\u8217\'20\'19s a good thing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Woodward said that Trump has held several private calls with Putin since his single-term presidency.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/08/trump-putin-covid-test-machines-bob-woodward"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump secretly gave Putin Covid test machines, Bob Woodward book says}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Bloomberg News editor-in-chief John Micklethwait is busy pushing back on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s insistence that imposing what the former president boasts would be \u8220\'20\'1Cobnoxious\u8221\'20\'1D levels of tariffs on imports will have a positive effect on the US economy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCritics say tariffs would end up being like a sales tax,\u8221\'20\'1D Micklethwait said, saying that it will push up costs for US consumers.\par \par \uc2 The two men talked over each other a bit, and Trump insisted that high tariffs would force overseas manufacturers to build their products in the US to sell to American consumers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe higher the tariff, the more likely it is that company will come into the US and build factories here. You make the tariffs so obnoxious that they come in straight away,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump argues for higher tariffs in Chicago economic speech\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just took the stage at the Economic Club in Chicago, where he\u8217\'20\'19s repeating his familiar campaign promise to enact high import tariffs to spur domestic manufacturing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to bring the companies back. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to lower taxes still, further, for companies that are going to make their product in the USA. We\u8217\'20\'19re going to protect those companies with strong tariffs, because I\u8217\'20\'19m a believer in tariffs,\u8221\'20\'1D the former president told his interviewer, Bloomberg News editor-in-chief John Micklethwait.\par \par \uc2 The ex-president added:\par \par \uc2 To me, the most beautiful word in the dictionary is tariff, and it\u8217\'20\'19s my favorite word. It needs a public relations firm.\par \par \uc2 Economists have been skeptical that tariffs would help American manufacturers:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/trump-economy-inflation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18This just isn\u8217\'20\'19t going to add up\u8217\'20\'19: experts warn Trumponomics would hurt US}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/15/us-election-live-kamala-harris-donald-trump?page=with:block-670e82a98f08ff54487bd94c#block-670e82a98f08ff54487bd94c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is expected}}}\uc2  to soon take the stage at the Economic Club of Chicago, where we can expect him to outline his plans to lower prices for US consumers. But the Associated Press reports that his tariff-heavy proposals and ideas for meddling with the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  are unlikely to undo the impact of inflation, and may instead push prices higher. Meanwhile, \uc2 Kamala Harris{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/15/us-election-live-kamala-harris-donald-trump?page=with:block-670e5d9b8f0838b423b50a41#block-670e5d9b8f0838b423b50a41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has seized on}}}\uc2  his strange behavior at a campaign event yesterday, where Trump spent more than a half-hour swaying to the music onstage. The former president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/15/us-election-live-kamala-harris-donald-trump?page=with:block-670e791f8f088ef4160054c2#block-670e791f8f088ef4160054c2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said this morning}}}\uc2  that he was reacting to a pair of medical emergencies that occurred in the audience, but the Harris campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/15/us-election-live-kamala-harris-donald-trump?page=with:block-670e7e848f088ef416005505#block-670e7e848f088ef416005505"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has implied}}}\uc2  it is a sign that he is not as healthy as he appears.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today so far:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign rejected an allegation of plagiarism brought against the vice-president by a conservative activist, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/15/us-election-live-kamala-harris-donald-trump?page=with:block-670e617a8f088cd0c5e1cf1c#block-670e617a8f088cd0c5e1cf1c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Early voting begins today in Georgia, and long lines of voters {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/15/us-election-live-kamala-harris-donald-trump?page=with:block-670e87d08f08ff54487bd986#block-670e87d08f08ff54487bd986"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 were spotted}}}\uc2  in at least one Atlanta-area county. Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/15/us-election-live-kamala-harris-donald-trump?page=with:block-670e97708f0898da3e0b4eb6#block-670e97708f0898da3e0b4eb6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 encouraged}}}\uc2  his supporters to vote by whatever method they chose.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nathan Wade, a former prosecutor in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s election meddling case in Georgia, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/15/us-election-live-kamala-harris-donald-trump?page=with:block-670e70198f088ef416005423#block-670e70198f088ef416005423"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is testifying}}}\uc2  behind closed doors to a Republican-led House committee.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/12/trump-anti-mail-in-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blamed absentee ballots}}}\uc2  (among other things, real and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/10/trump-voters-republican-new-hampshire-cnn-town-hall"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 imagined}}}\uc2  ) for his 2020 election loss.\par \par \uc2 But on the day early voting begins in Georgia in this year\u8217\'20\'19s election, his campaign is calling on people to get their ballots in using whatever method they choose.\par \par \uc2 That includes absentee ballots, as the below tweet shows:\par \par \uc2 enltr?? GEORGIA! Early voting has started!\par \par \uc2 This is the most important election of our lifetime.\par \par \uc2 Whether you're voting in person or sending in your absentee ballot, make sure your voice is heard. Let's make it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/TooBigToRig?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #TooBigToRig}}}\uc2  ! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/1B6VUcO6YK"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/1B6VUcO6YK}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/EarlyVote?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #EarlyVote}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/SwampTheVote?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #SwampTheVote}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/vOxm75ZZxy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/vOxm75ZZxy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Team Trump (Text TRUMP to 88022) (@TeamTrump) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TeamTrump/status/1846204338353422496?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 How might swing states like Michigan, Georgia and North Carolina vote on election day, which is three weeks from now?\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no way to know for sure, and recent polls have shown \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  essentially neck-in-neck across the board. At Sabato\u8217\'20\'19s Crystal Ball, an outfit affiliated with the University of Virginia\u8217\'20\'19s Center for Politics that is one of several well-regarded poll watchers nationwide, they view all seven swing states as toss-ups. But in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://centerforpolitics.org/crystalball/three-weeks-to-go-has-anybody-seen-our-crystal-ball-anywhere/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an analysis released this morning}}}\uc2 , they offer some thoughts on how the states may end up voting \u8211\'20\'13 though do not predict a winner of the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 Their thoughts on Michigan:\par \par \uc2 We still think Michigan is likeliest to be Harris\u8217\'20\'19s best state out of this group, as it was for Biden in 2020, and it generally has been the most Democratic of these seven states over the past couple of decades.\par \par \uc2 And North Carolina:\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, North Carolina is the one state among the seven that Biden did not carry in 2020, and we remain somewhat skeptical of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s ability to actually win it.\par \par \uc2 One thing that is preventing us from being confident enough to move it to Leans Republican is the devastation wrought by Hurricane Helene in western North Carolina, which could have impacts on turnout in what is on balance a Republican-leaning area. In 2020, the 25 counties that FEMA currently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ncsbe.gov/voting/upcoming-election/helene-recovery-and-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 considers}}}\uc2  to be the disaster zone favored Trump by 25 percentage points while Biden carried the rest of the state by 3.5 points. The state has taken efforts to keep {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ncnewsline.com/briefs/nearly-all-early-voting-sites-in-western-nc-are-ready-to-open-next-week/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 early voting on track}}}\uc2  in western North Carolina; giving voters additional opportunity to make their voices heard in the midst of an unforeseen disaster is probably the best argument there is for offering robust absentee and early voting options.\par \par \uc2 And finally Georgia and Arizona, two states that generally vote Republican, but which Trump lost four years ago:\par \par \uc2 Trump has generally, although not always, led polling in Arizona and Georgia, the two typically Republican-leaning states that fell out of his grasp in 2020. Forced to choose, one might also be inclined to tilt those states to Trump. It seems possible that a critical mass of \u8220\'20\'1Csofter\u8221\'20\'1D Republican voters in those states who dislike Trump personally are expressing some buyer\u8217\'20\'19s remorse after they took a chance on Biden in 2020. It wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t take all that many of them to flip Arizona and Georgia back to Republicans after Biden won each by less than half a percentage point.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking of Georgia, an attempt by a Republican voting official to get out of certifying election results was rejected by a court, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/george-chidi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Chidi}}}\uc2  reports:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Election}}}\uc2  certification is a mandatory duty, not discretionary, for county election officials in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2 , a judge ruled on Tuesday, rejecting assertions made by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican}}}\uc2  elections official that elections board members could refuse to certify an election based on their suspicions of fraud or error.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jun/04/republican-julie-adams-georgia-election-integrity-network"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Julie Adams}}}\uc2 , a Republican member of the Fulton county board of registration and elections, brought the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/10/georgia-election-board-member-lawsuit-dismissed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suit}}}\uc2  earlier this year after abstaining from a vote to certify the May primary election. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://americafirstpolicy.com/issues/afpi-announces-lawsuit-against-georgia-election-process"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 America First Policy Institute}}}\uc2 , a legal thinktank that was formed by former {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  advisers in the wake of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s 2020 election loss to help lay legal groundwork for his potential return to office, joined the suit.\par \par \uc2 Adams refused certification after claiming she had been denied access to a long list of elections documents. But Robert McBurney, Fulton county superior court judge, ruled that Adams was entitled to review documents quickly, but failing to provide those documents was not grounds for denying the certification of an election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf election superintendents were, as plaintiff urges, free to play investigator, prosecutor, jury, and judge and so \u8211\'20\'13 because of a unilateral determination of error or fraud \u8211\'20\'13 refuse to certify election results, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  voters would be silenced,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote McBurney in his ruling. \u8220\'20\'1COur Constitution and our election code do not allow for that to happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/15/georgia-election-certification-denier-republican"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia counties are mandated to certify elections, judge rules}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s the first day of early voting in Georgia, one of the swing states expected to decide the election, and NBC News reports a long line of people are waiting to cast ballots in DeKalb county, outside of Atlanta:\par \par \uc2 enltrVoter enthusiasm appears high on day one of early voting here in battleground Georgia.\par \par \uc2 Take a look at the *very long* line outside of a polling precinct in DeKalb County. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/R7xzpycVLT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/R7xzpycVLT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nnamdi (@NnamEgwuon) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NnamEgwuon/status/1846198726009724948?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won Georgia four years ago, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  carried it in 2016. This year, our poll tracker shows it leaning towards Trump, but only narrowly. We\u8217\'20\'19ll know the answer for sure in three weeks:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2024 US presidential polls tracker: Trump v Harris latest national averages}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump to speak at Economic Club of Chicago\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will speak at the Economic Club of Chicago at noon, where you can expect to hear him argue that his policies will tame inflation.\par \par \uc2 Prices rose at levels not seen in four decades under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and though the rate of increase has declined in recent months, polls have shown inflation remains one of the issues voters are most concerned about.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-inflation-tariffs-taxes-immigration-federal-reserve-a18de763fcc01557258c7f33cab375ed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2  that, based on what Trump has proposed, it\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely he would be able to unilaterally bring prices down. In fact, he might make them go up:\par \par \uc2 Last month, the \uc2 Peterson Institute for International Economics\uc2  predicted that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies \u8211\'20\'13 the deportations, import taxes and efforts to erode the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s independence \u8211\'20\'13 would drive consumer prices sharply higher two years into his second term. Peterson\u8217\'20\'19s analysis concluded that inflation, which would otherwise register 1.9% in 2026, would instead jump to between 6% and 9.3% if Trump\u8217\'20\'19s economic proposals were adopted.\par \par \uc2 Many economists aren\u8217\'20\'19t thrilled with Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 economic agenda, either. They dismiss, for example, her proposal to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/kamala-harris-price-gouging-ban-inflation-65dc8844bb41159d76886f752b6cab28"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 combat price gouging}}}\uc2  as an ineffective tool against high grocery prices. But they don\u8217\'20\'19t regard her policies as particularly inflationary.\par \par \uc2 Mark Zandi\uc2 , chief economist at \uc2 Moody\u8217\'20\'19s\uc2  Analytics, and two colleagues have estimated that Harris\u8217\'20\'19 policies would leave the inflation outlook virtually unchanged, even if she enjoyed a Democratic majority in both chambers of Congress. An unfettered Trump, by contrast, would leave prices higher by 1.1 percentage points in 2025 and 0.8 percentage points in 2026, they concluded.\par \par \uc2 Taxes on imports \u8211\'20\'13 tariffs \u8211\'20\'13 are Trump\u8217\'20\'19s go-to economic policy. He argues that tariffs protect American factory jobs from foreign competition and deliver a host of other benefits.\par \par \uc2 While in office, Trump started a trade war with China, imposing high tariffs on most Chinese goods. He also raised import taxes on foreign steel and aluminum, washing machines and solar panels. He has still grander plans for a second term: Trump wants to impose a 60% tariff on all Chinese goods and a \u8220\'20\'1Cuniversal\u8217\'20\'19\u8217\'20\'19 tariff of 10% or 20% on everything else that enters the United States.\par \par \uc2 Trump insists that the cost of taxing imported goods is absorbed by the foreign countries that produce those goods. The truth, though, is that U.S. importers pay the tariff \u8211\'20\'13 and then typically pass along that cost to consumers in the form of higher prices, which is how Americans themselves end up bearing the cost of tariffs.\par \par \uc2 What\u8217\'20\'19s more, as tariffs raise the cost of imports, the weakened competition from foreign products makes it easier for U.S. producers to raise their own prices.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been prolific on Truth Social, the social network he owns and uses most frequently.\par \par \uc2 He made several late-night posts this morning and yesterday, insisting he is healthy enough to serve as president for another four-year term. But Trump has not released his medical records, something \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has seized on:\par \par \uc2 enltrTRUMP at 1am: ranting on Truth Social about how sane he is.\par \par \uc2 Just today, he "swayed" and appeared lost in a "bizarre" town hall and said the election is in January (it's not).\par \par \uc2 Over 230 doctors called on him to release his medical records.\par \par \uc2 What is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realDonaldTrump}}}\uc2  hiding? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XGhWBjtBGk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/XGhWBjtBGk}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sarafina Chitika (@SarafinaChitika) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SarafinaChitika/status/1846069595033018381?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, the vice-president released her own medical report, which says she is in \u8220\'20\'1Cexcellent health\u8221\'20\'1D:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/12/kamala-harris-to-release-health-report-saying-she-is-fit-for-presidency-aide"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris releases medical report saying she is in \u8216\'20\'18excellent health\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump offers explanation for lengthy dance interlude at Pennsylvania event\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  raised a lot of eyebrows last night, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/15/us-election-live-kamala-harris-donald-trump?page=with:block-670e5d9b8f0838b423b50a41#block-670e5d9b8f0838b423b50a41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 including }}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/15/us-election-live-kamala-harris-donald-trump?page=with:block-670e5d9b8f0838b423b50a41#block-670e5d9b8f0838b423b50a41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/15/us-election-live-kamala-harris-donald-trump?page=with:block-670e5d9b8f0838b423b50a41#block-670e5d9b8f0838b423b50a41"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s}}}\uc2 , after he spent a significant part of his town hall in Oaks, Pennsylvania, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/15/us-election-live-kamala-harris-donald-trump?page=with:block-670e3c688f088cd0c5e1ccd8#block-670e3c688f088cd0c5e1ccd8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swaying to music}}}\uc2  on stage.\par \par \uc2 On {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/113311732586143252"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Truth Social}}}\uc2 , the former president has offered an explanation for the campaign event that could, charitably, be described as unorthodox. Here\u8217\'20\'19s what he said:\par \par \uc2 I had a Town Hall in Pennsylvania last night. It was amazing! The Q and A was almost finished when people began fainting from the excitement and heat. We started playing music while we waited, and just kept it going. So different, but it ended up being a GREAT EVENING!\par \par \uc2 For more updates on the US election, tune in to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://linktr.ee/todayinfocus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Today in Focus US Election Extra podcast}}}\uc2 . Join Lucy Hough, breaking down every essential development in the presidential race every weekday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2024/oct/15/us-election-extra-dj-trump-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US election extra: DJ Trump \u8211\'20\'13 podcast}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 After launching her presidential campaign in July, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  waited weeks before having a proper sit-down interview with a news outlet.\par \par \uc2 But she has stepped up the tempo of her media appearances lately, and will tomorrow appear on Fox News, the top conservative network in the country. As you can see below, her campaign is trying to turn the tables on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , accusing him of avoiding interviews, including with \u8220\'20\'1C60 Minutes\u8221\'20\'1D, the popular \uc2 CBS\uc2  Sunday evening news program:\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW >> VP Harris will do an interview with Fox News on Wednesday\par \par \uc2 As of today, it has been **one month** since Trump\u8217\'20\'19s been interviewed by a mainstream media outlet, as he has backed out of 60 Minutes and refuses to debate again\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile Harris is willing to even go on Fox {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/A9VvW0MoeX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/A9VvW0MoeX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ian Sams (@IanSams) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IanSams/status/1845862212037996606?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nathan Wade, a former prosecutor in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s election meddling case in Georgia who is a key figure in the legal wrangling that has prevented it from moving forward, will testify in private to a House of Representatives panel today, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/nathan-wade-will-testify-before-the-us-house-judiciary-committee/5N5WUGXD5BFO3L2K2IDB7RNPVA/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Atlanta Journal-Constitution reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The case against Trump and several other defendants brought by Atlanta-area district attorney \uc2 Fani Willis\uc2  was upended after it was revealed that she had a romantic relationship with Wade, who has since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/15/nathan-wade-resigns-fani-willis-trump-georgia-case"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 resigned}}}\uc2  from the prosecution team. Nonetheless, arguments over his role and whether it created a conflict of interest has prevented the case from moving forward, while the House GOP has launched its own investigation of Willis.\par \par \uc2 The Journal-Constitution reports that Wade will answer questions about the case behind closed doors. Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 Wade\u8217\'20\'19s attorney Andrew Evans said Tuesday that his client will sit for questions in a closed-door session before the \uc2 House Judiciary Committee\uc2  on Oct. 15. It comes after weeks of back-and-forth over whether he\u8217\'20\'19d comply with the panel\u8217\'20\'19s subpoena.\par \par \uc2 Wade is expected to field queries related to Willis\u8217\'20\'19 office\u8217\'20\'19s use of grant funding as well as their meetings with the White House and the panel that investigated the Jan. 6, 2021 pro-\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  mob that ransacked the U.S. Capitol, Evans said.\par \par \uc2 The Judiciary Committee\u8217\'20\'19s investigators {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ajc.com/politics/the-us-house-judiciary-committee-is-looking-for-nathan-wade-it-cant-find-him/7MU36EVEIVDILJKQ5GD3G6KEWI/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 had not been able to find}}}\uc2  Wade for several days in September before succeeding in serving him a summons that required him to appear in Washington.\par \par \uc2 Even so, Wade\u8217\'20\'19s legal counsel bristled at the demands by Republican U.S. Rep. Jim Jordan\u8217\'20\'19s committee. Former Gov. \uc2 Roy Barnes\uc2 , one of Willis\u8217\'20\'19 attorneys, fired off a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25196803-barnes-letter-to-jordan-9-30-24"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Sept. 30 letter}}}\uc2  that objected to the \u8220\'20\'1Cvitriol and anger\u8221\'20\'1D directed at his client.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you have calmed down and attended the anger management class,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote Barnes, \u8220\'20\'1CI will be glad to discuss this matter with you in a logical, dispassionate manner.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At Jordan\u8217\'20\'19s direction, the panel has been investigating Willis for more than a year over her handling of the prosecution of Trump and his allies. The Ohio Republican is a Trump loyalist.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 In an interview with conservative broadcaster \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2  earlier today, Fox News anchor Bret Baier said his interview with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will have no commerical breaks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C For everybody who\u8217\'20\'19s been asking, it is as live. In other words, we roll the tape, but it\u8217\'20\'19s running just as \u8230\'20\'26 we do it. So, from beginning to end, you\u8217\'20\'19ll see every second and it will be unedited, and we will run it without commercial straight through the first half hour of my show,\u8221\'20\'1D Baier said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is in his home town of Wilmington, Delaware, this morning, but will in the evening head to nearby Philadelphia for an unspecified political event.\par \par \uc2 The White House has not yet made public any details of that event, scheduled for 6.45pm, but the president has frequently traveled to Philadelphia during his presidency. It\u8217\'20\'19s an especially good investment of his time right now \u8211\'20\'13 Pennsylvania is one of the swing states expected to decide the election, and Democratic turnout in Philadelphia and its suburbs is expected to be crucial to determining if \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  can win.\par \par \uc2 After that event wraps up, the president will return to the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign denies plagiarism allegations from conservative activist \u8211\'20\'13 report\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has rejected allegations made by conservative activist Christopher Rufo that she plagiarized parts of a book she co-authored shortly before being elected California\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/14/politics/kamala-harris-plagiarism-allegation/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Citing the work of Stefan Weber, an Austrian \u8220\'20\'1Cplagiarism hunter\u8221\'20\'1D, Rufo {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://christopherrufo.com/p/kamala-harriss-plagiarism-problem"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 wrote}}}\uc2  that Harris\u8217\'20\'19s 2009 book Smart on Crime: A Career Prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19s Plan to Make Us Safer co-authored with Joan O\u8217\'20\'19C Hamilton contains sections that were plagiarized.\par \par \uc2 CNN took a closer look at the claim, and this is what they found:\par \par \uc2 Rufo, in his post, refers to six specific paragraphs from Harris\u8217\'20\'19 roughly 200-page book.\par \par \uc2 CNN reviewed several of the passages highlighted by Rufo and found that Harris and O\u8217\'20\'19C. Hamilton failed to properly attribute language to sources.\par \par \uc2 Plagiarized works include using someone else\u8217\'20\'19s work without giving them proper and appropriate credit for their ideas and words. Even if the source of the information is cited, it is still considered plagiarism if the ideas are not paraphrased or quoted in the correct place, experts told CNN late last year.\par \par \uc2 In one instance, Harris and O\u8217\'20\'19C. Hamilton appear to have lifted some language from a John Jay College of Criminal Justice press release without proper attribution. The book copies exact language and sections of the press release but fails to use quotation marks in several sentences, according to an analysis of the book and the press release.\par \par \uc2 The authors do, however, cite the press release as a source in a footnote next to the text.\par \par \uc2 They also properly attribute other quotes from parts of the press release.\par \par \uc2 In response to Rufo\u8217\'20\'19s allegations, Harris campaign spokesperson James Singer told CNN:\par \par \uc2 Rightwing operatives are getting desperate as they see the bipartisan coalition of support Vice President Harris is building to win this election, as Trump retreats to a conservative echo chamber refusing to face questions about his lies. This is a book that\u8217\'20\'19s been out for 15 years, and the Vice President clearly cited sources and statistics in footnotes and endnotes throughout.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 He might be \u8220\'20\'1CDJ Trump\u8221\'20\'1D to his campaign, but \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is taking the former president\u8217\'20\'19s lengthy musical interlude as a sign that he might not be well.\par \par \uc2 Reacting to a clip of his rally yesterday in Oaks, Pennsylvania, during which Trump spent a considerable amount of time onstage swaying and rocking to the music, the vice-president said:\par \par \uc2 enltrHope he's okay. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WGhGteFpjm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/WGhGteFpjm}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@KamalaHarris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris/status/1846049221369024700?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 US anti-missile system begins arriving in Israel, says Pentagon\par \par \uc2 The Pentagon said components for an advanced anti-missile system began arriving in Israel yesterday and that it would be fully operational in the near future, according to a statement this morning. About 100 troops will accompany the system.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver the coming days, additional US military personnel and THAAD battery components will continue to arrive in Israel,\u8221\'20\'1D Pentagon spokesperson Major General Pat Ryder said. \u8220\'20\'1CThe battery will be fully operational capable in the near future, but for operations security reasons we will not discuss timelines.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 THAAD is designed to defend against ballistic missiles, and will line up alongside Israel\u8217\'20\'19s Arrow 2 and 3 and David\u8217\'20\'19s Sling long- and medium-range defence systems.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what our defence editor, Dan Sabbagh, had to say about the THAAD deployment when it was announced:\par \par \uc2 Bringing THAAD to bear suggests the US believes that whatever Israel is planning to do will invite a fresh response from Iran, and that it could test existing air defences seriously.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 California and Nevada voters will decide in November whether to ban forced prison labor by removing language from their state constitutions rooted in the legacy of chattel slavery.\par \par \uc2 The measures aim to protect incarcerated people from being forced to work under the threat of punishment in the states, writes Associated Press. It is not uncommon for prisoners to be paid less than $1 an hour to fight fires, clean prison cells, make license plates or do yard work at cemeteries.\par \par \uc2 Nevada incarcerates about 10,000 people. All prisoners in the state are required to work or be in vocational training for 40 hours each week, unless they have a medical exemption. Some of them make as little as 35 cents hourly.\par \par \uc2 Voters will weigh the proposals during one of the most historic elections in modern history, said Jamilia Land, an advocate with the Abolish Slavery National Network who has spent years trying to get the California measure passed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCalifornia, as well as Nevada, has an opportunity to end legalized, constitutional slavery within our states, in its entirety, while at the same time we have the first Black woman running for president,\u8221\'20\'1D she said of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s historic bid.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Men injured in Trump shooting accuse Secret Service of negligence\par \par \uc2 Two men who were shot during the first assassination attempt on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  this summer say the \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1Cnegligent\u8221\'20\'1D in protecting the former president and other bystanders at the campaign rally in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 David Dutch, 57, an ex-marine, and James Copenhaver, 74, a retired liquor store manager, told NBC News in an exclusive interview yesterday they were excited to be sitting in the bleachers behind the Republican nominee at the fairgrounds in Butler on 13 July when gunshots rang out and they were hit.\par \par \uc2 Another man, Corey Comperatore, 50, was killed in the shooting while shielding his family. Trump was wounded in the ear.\par \par \uc2 The interview was the two men\u8217\'20\'19s first public statements since 20-year-old shooter Thomas Matthew Crooks of Bethel Park, Pennsylvania, opened fire in July from an unsecured rooftop nearby before he was fatally shot by sharpshooters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was like getting hit with a sledgehammer right in the chest,\u8221\'20\'1D said Dutch. He said he could see chunks of the bleacher and metal \u8220\'20\'1Cflying all around\u8221\'20\'1D until the shooting stopped.\par \par \uc2 He said he was still \u8220\'20\'1Cangry that the whole situation even happened. It should have never happened.\u8221\'20\'1D NBC News reported the two men\u8217\'20\'19s attorneys said they were looking into possible litigation over what they view as negligence by the Secret Service.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz says Trump and Vance 'don't think like us' in pitch for rural votes\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  will unveil the Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 plans to improve the lives of rural voters later today while he stars in a new radio ad attacking his Republican rivals.\par \par \uc2 Associated Press reports it will include a focus on improving rural healthcare with plans to recruit 10,000 new healthcare professionals in rural and tribal areas through scholarships, loan forgiveness and new grant programs, as well as economic and agricultural policy priorities.\par \par \uc2 It marks a concerted effort by the Democratic campaign to win over rural votes. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  carried rural voters by a nearly two-to-one margin in 2020, according to AP VoteCast.\par \par \uc2 The vice-presidential nominee is set to announce the plan during a stop in rural Lawrence County in western Pennsylvania, one of the marquee battlegrounds of the 2024 contest. Walz is also starring in a new radio ad for the campaign highlighting his roots in a small town of 400 people and his time coaching football, while attacking Trump and his running mate, JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn a small town, you don\u8217\'20\'19t focus on the politics, you focus on taking care of your neighbors and minding your own damn business,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz says in the ad. \u8220\'20\'1CNow \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance, they don\u8217\'20\'19t think like us. They\u8217\'20\'19re in it for themselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The plan calls on Congress to permanently extend telemedicine coverage under Medicare, a pandemic-era benefit that helped millions access care that is set to expire at the end of 2024. They are also calling for grants to support volunteer EMS programs to halve the number of Americans living more than 25 minutes from an ambulance.\par \par \uc2 It also urges Congress to restore the Affordable Connectivity Program, a scheme launched by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  that expired in June that provided up to $30 off home internet bills, and for lawmakers to require equipment manufacturers to grant farmers the right to repair their products.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.52am BST\par \par \uc2 Press secretary hails 'DJ Trump' after 40 minutes of music at town hall event\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s town hall in the Philadelphia suburbs turned into an impromptu concert last night after the former president was twice interrupted by medical emergencies in the room.\par \par \uc2 As Associated Press reports, the Republican presidential nominee paused during a question-and-answer session as a doctor attended to the first person to have a medical issue. After a second emergency halted the discussion moderated by South Dakota governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , Trump stopped taking questions. He and Noem mentioned it was hot in the venue, and Trump asked about air conditioning.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey probably can\u8217\'20\'19t afford it, sir, in this economy,\u8221\'20\'1D Noem quipped.\par \par \uc2 Once Noem announced the second person was up and moving, Trump spoke for a few more minutes before suggesting the audience could enjoy some music rather than hearing him answer more questions.\par \par \uc2 He called for the Village People\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CYMCA\u8221\'20\'1D and it blasted through the loudspeakers, the usual signal that Trump is done speaking and is ready to leave. But he remained onstage. \u8220\'20\'1CNobody\u8217\'20\'19s leaving,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s going on?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 More music played \u8212\'20\'14 and for roughly 40 minutes, it didn\u8217\'20\'19t stop.\par \par \uc2 Trump bopped and shimmied onstage to an eclectic playlist of songs that included Sinead O\u8217\'20\'19Connor\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CNothing Compares 2 U,\u8221\'20\'1D Rufus Wainwright\u8217\'20\'19s cover of \u8220\'20\'1CHallelujah\u8221\'20\'1D and Guns N\u8217\'20\'19 Roses\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1CNovember Rain.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Finally, Trump left the stage as \u8220\'20\'1CMemory\u8221\'20\'1D from the musical \u8220\'20\'1CCats\u8221\'20\'1D played.\par \par \uc2 Karoline Leavitt, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s national press secretary, published on the social media site X a photo of Trump from the side of the stage. \u8220\'20\'1CDJ TRUMP!\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote.\par \par \uc2 enltrDJ TRUMP! ?????? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DvvSS1b9s1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DvvSS1b9s1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Karoline Leavitt (@kleavittnh) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kleavittnh/status/1845982377698373691?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Trump spokesperson \uc2 Steven Cheung\uc2  wrote on X that \u8220\'20\'1Csomething very special is happening in Pennsylvania\u8221\'20\'1D as the scene unfolded, adding Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cis unlike any politician in history, and it\u8217\'20\'19s great.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump 'out for unchecked power,' says Harris\par \par \uc2 Vice president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has hit out at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8216\'20\'18s comments suggesting the US military could be used to deal with \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy from within\u8221\'20\'1D as the two presidential nominees took the fight for battleground Pennsylvania to opposite ends of the state last night.\par \par \uc2 Harris, at her rally in northwestern Pennsylvania, called Trump a serious threat to American democracy who is \u8220\'20\'1Cout for unchecked power\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe considers anyone who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t support him or who will not bend to his will an enemy of our country,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said after playing a clip of the comment on the jumbo screen at her rally at an Erie arena.\par \par \uc2 Harris argued that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments in a Fox News \u8220\'20\'1CSunday Morning Futures\u8221\'20\'1D interview are the latest example of threatening rhetoric from the former president that should concern Americans about what a potential second Trump term could look like.\par \par \uc2 Trump made the comment in response to a question about \u8220\'20\'1Coutside agitators\u8221\'20\'1D potentially disrupting Election Day.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the bigger problem is the enemy from within,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. He added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have some very bad people. We have some sick people, radical left lunatics. And I think they\u8217\'20\'19re the big \u8212\'20\'14 and it should be very easily handled by, if necessary, by National Guard, or if really necessary, by the military, because they can\u8217\'20\'19t let that happen.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump held his own town hall event last night in suburban Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Opening summary\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to what is likely to be another turbulent day in the run-up to the US election amid anger over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments suggesting the military could be used to deal with \u8220\'20\'1C the enemy from within \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Both candidates were in Pennsylvania last night and while the Democratic hopeful, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , used her event in Erie to call Trump a serious threat to American democracy who is \u8220\'20\'1Cout for unchecked power\u8221\'20\'1D, her Republican rival treated the crowds in Oaks to an impromptu playlist as he bopped and shimmied onstage to an eclectic playlist of songs that included Sinead O\u8217\'20\'19Connor\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CNothing Compares 2 U,\u8221\'20\'1D Rufus Wainwright\u8217\'20\'19s cover of \u8220\'20\'1CHallelujah\u8221\'20\'1D and Guns N\u8217\'20\'19 Roses\u8217\'20\'19 \u8220\'20\'1CNovember Rain\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 More on last night\u8217\'20\'19s events shortly. In other developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  has admitted she still has not spoken to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  since her crucial intervention in July led to his decision to drop out of the presidential race. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/audio/2024/oct/15/i-said-his-name-i-hope-i-dont-burn-in-hell-nancy-pelosi-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian podcast with columnist Jonathan Freedland}}}\uc2  she also addressed how she feels about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CI hardly ever say his name,\u8221\'20\'1D she said of the former Republican president and the GOP\u8217\'20\'19s current nominee, instead describing him as \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat\u8217\'20\'19s-his-name\u8221\'20\'1D. You can read our story {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/pelosi-biden-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  could sit down for an interview with popular podcaster Joe Rogan, whose audience leans heavily towards young men, as she works to shore up support with male voters, sources said on Monday. Reuters reports that Harris campaign officials met Rogan\u8217\'20\'19s team this week but an appearance has not been confirmed yet, said two of the sources, who have knowledge of the matter.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House said on Monday that the US has been closely tracking Iranian threats against Trump for years and it warned of \u8220\'20\'1Csevere consequences\u8221\'20\'1D if Tehran was to attack any of its citizens. \u8220\'20\'1CWe consider this a national and homeland security matter of the highest priority, and we strongly condemn Iran for these brazen threats. Should Iran attack any of our citizens, including those who continue to serve the United States or those who formerly served, Iran will face severe consequences,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 White House National Security Council\uc2  spokesperson Sean Savett.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump will be interviewed by Bloomberg News and the Economic Club of Chicago at an event on today from 11am \u8211\'20\'13 12pm CDT. Bloomberg Editor-in-Chief John Micklethwait will interview Trump in downtown Chicago. It will be carried live on Bloomberg News platforms and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/live/api9V-jaxYg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Economic Club of Chicago\u8217\'20\'19s YouTube channel}}}\uc2 . This evening he will be speaking at an event in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile Harris will be in Detroit later for a live conversation with radio host and comedian Charlamagne tha God, which will air on iHeartRadio at 5pm EDT.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241015ekaf0018n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
