\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is \u8216\'20\'18increasingly unstable and unhinged\u8217\'20\'19, says \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); with Cecilia Nowell andHayden Vernon (earlier) \par \uc2 9,701 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 October 2024\par 00:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is closed now, thanks for following along. You can read our US elections coverage here.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.39am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. You can read our US elections coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.33am BST\par \par \uc2 After standing on stage swaying while various songs play for more than 20 minutes, Trump finally leaves the stage. It is unclear what that was about, although we are trying to find explanation that makes sense.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.22am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump has already answered questions at this town hall in Oaks, Pennsylvania \u8211\'20\'13 it is unclear whether he plans to speak again, or just stand on stage listening to his rally playlist.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.20am BST\par \par \uc2 The large screen behind Trump on stage says \u8220\'20\'1CTrump was right about everything.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is that clip from Harris a short while ago:\par \par \uc2 enltrAt her Erie, PA rally, Harris plays multiple clips of Trump's threats, then says "he considers anyone who doesn't support him, or who will not bend to his will, an ENEMY of our country." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/j9KBMZ1qHR"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/j9KBMZ1qHR}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Brian Stelter (@brianstelter) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/brianstelter/status/1845980658180518127?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.16am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is also in Pennsylvania, in Oaks.\par \par \uc2 At the moment he is standing on stage swaying side to side as Sin\u233\'00\'E9ad O\u8217\'20\'19Connor\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CNothing Compares 2 U\u8221\'20\'1D plays.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris has finished speaking. She makes her way through the crowd, shaking hands with supporters.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris reminds the crowd that the way people from Erie county vote \u8220\'20\'1Coften predicts the national vote\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 People start chanting \u8220\'20\'1CErie! Erie!\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 where Harris is speaking.\par \par \uc2 She reminds the crowd that they can vote early.\par \par \uc2 Erie is a bellwether county \u8211\'20\'13 the way it has voted has been the way the country voted in the last four elections:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 2008 Presidential Election : Erie County voted for \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , who won the presidency.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 2012 Presidential Election : Erie County voted for \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , who won re-election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 2016 Presidential Election : Erie County voted for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who won the presidency.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 2020 Presidential Election : Erie County voted for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , who won the presidency.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump meanwhile, according to MSNBC:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump is just standing at his rally swaying as hallelujah (jeff buckley) plays. He's tapping his chair. The crowd is standing. just listening to music\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sam Stein (@samstein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/samstein/status/1845980329632247945?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 15, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.10am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen freedom is on the line, Americans always answer the call,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 The crowd chants \u8220\'20\'1CVote! Vote!\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump is 'Increasingly unstable and unhinged', Harris says\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve said for a while now, watch his rallies, listen to his words. He tells us what he is, he tells us what he will do if he is elected president,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 Harris plays clips from several Trump events, including, \u8220\'20\'1CThe worst people are the enemies from within \u8230\'20\'26 those people are more dangerous than Russia and China \u8230\'20\'26 Now if you had one really violent day, one rough hour, and I mean really rough\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe\u8217\'20\'19s talking about the enemy from within Pennsylvania,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says, and anyone who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t agree with him.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe is saying that he would use the military to go after them,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we know who he would target, because he has attacked them before. Journalists whose stories he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t like. Election officials who refuse to cheat \u8230\'20\'26 Judges who follow the law instead of bending to his will,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA second Trump term would be a huge risk for America, and dangerous,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is increasingly unstable and unhinged. And he is out for unchekced power,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.04am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris now takes aim at Trump calling for the \u8220\'20\'1Ctermination\u8221\'20\'1D of the constitution of the United States.\par \par \uc2 The crowd chants \u8220\'20\'1Clock him up\u8221\'20\'1D and Harris says, \u8220\'20\'1CThe courts will handle that,\u8221\'20\'1D and that voters must handle 5 November \u8211\'20\'13 voting day.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.03am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris turns now to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne in three women lives in a state with a Trump \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also be on the ballot in at least ten states on 5 November:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/election-abortion-ballot-measures-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Where will \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  be on the ballot in the 2024 US election?}}}\par \par \uc2 These measures are known as down-ballot measures. Here is an explainer:\par \par \uc2 Measures on the ballot other than the vote for US presidential ticket are down-ballot measures, and a third or more of the roughly half of Americans who usually turn up to vote don\u8217\'20\'19t fill out the entire ballot, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usvotefoundation.org/downballot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the US Vote Foundation}}}\uc2 . Voters do not have to vote for any down-ballot measures for their ballots to count.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou gotta read the plan.\u8221\'20\'1D says Harris, \u8220\'20\'1CI mean the fact that they put it in writing is a whole other thing to be discussed,\u8221\'20\'1D she says, referring to the Project 2025 document.\par \par \uc2 More on this subject:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/14/project-2025-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 I read the full 900-page Project 2025 manifesto \u8211\'20\'13 here\u8217\'20\'19s why it matters}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris turns now to Project 2025.\par \par \uc2 She repeats her criticism of Trump as an \u8220\'20\'1Cunserious man\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 but that the consequences of him being president again are very serious.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Some trivia: \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t forget healthcare\u8221\'20\'1D was one of the three rules Democrat campaign veteran James Carville came up with for the 1992 Clinton-Gore campaign \u8211\'20\'13 along with \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the economy, stupid\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CChange vs. more of the same.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris is talking about taking care of her mother when she was diagnosed with cancer.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s about trying to cook something for them that they might enjoy eating, trying to find something for them to wear that won\u8217\'20\'19t irritate their skin, trying to find something that will make them smile or laugh, it\u8217\'20\'19s about dignity, she says, to applause.\par \par \uc2 She says her plan is that Medicare (not Medicaid) helps pay for home healthcare.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.49am BST\par \par \uc2 The election is about two very different visions, one focused on the past, one on the future, Harris says. It has been one of her key messages this campaign.\par \par \uc2 So far, she is repeating well-worn messaging. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need a president who works for all the American people,\u8221\'20\'1D she says.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19re expecting this rally to portray \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as a potential tyrant-in-waiting who wants to jail his political opponents by seizing on his threat to use US armed forces against those he has branded \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy within\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.47am BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are the underdogs, we have some hard work ahead of us, but here\u8217\'20\'19s the thing: we like har work,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn 22 days, we will win.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Just over three weeks left\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.45am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on stage in Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 The Democratic presidential nominee and US vice-president is on stage in Erie, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 Here is the pool report on the number of people there \u8211\'20\'13 about 7,000:\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign is using about three-quarters of the arena, which has a total concert capacity of about 9400, and appears to have filled it, except for the obstructed seats directly behind the media riser and the space on the floor set aside for press.\par \par \uc2 The crowd is chanting \u8220\'20\'1CKamala! Kamala!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.43am BST\par \par \uc2 And here is a refresher on the electoral college:\par \par \uc2 The electoral college is a group of 538 people, called electors, who officially cast their votes for the US president after citizens have voted. This is a requirement outlined in the US constitution. The electors are chosen by political parties in each of the US\u8217\'20\'19s 50 states ahead of the election.\par \par \uc2 Different states have different numbers of electoral college votes, with the number decided based on the census. The number of votes is equal to its total congressional delegation: the number of senators plus the number of representatives. While not a state, the District of Columbia \u8211\'20\'13 as in Washington DC \u8211\'20\'13 is allocated three electoral college votes.\par \par \uc2 This is why the total is 538: 100 senators plus 435 representatives plus three for DC.\par \par \uc2 A candidate needs more than half \u8211\'20\'13 or at least 270 \u8211\'20\'13 of the electoral college votes to win. In most states, all of the electoral college votes from the state go to the same candidate. The exceptions are Maine and Nebraska, which allocate two electoral votes to the state popular vote winner, and then one electoral vote to the popular vote winner in each congressional district.\par \par \uc2 The party that wins a state has its electors formally vote for its candidate. This happens a few weeks after the November election \u8211\'20\'13 and after US states have certified their election results \u8211\'20\'13 on the first Monday after the second Wednesday in December.\par \par \uc2 In 2020 \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/dec/14/what-is-electoral-college-vote-explainer-electors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tried to remove electors}}}\uc2  in some states before the electoral college vote but the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  rejected that attempt the week before.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is a refresher on swing states \u8211\'20\'13 Pennsylvania is the largest of the swing states:\par \par \uc2 A red state is a one that tends to vote Republican, a blue state one that tends to vote Democrat, and a swing state one that swings between the two major parties from one election to the next.\par \par \uc2 Swing states, or battleground states, are where campaigns tend to spend the most money trying to win over undecided voters, or voters who they hope might be convinced to switch from supporting the other team to theirs.\par \par \uc2 Voters in the seven swing states are likely to decide the election this year. The states, and the number of electoral college votes up for grabs, are Arizona (11), Georgia (16), Michigan (15), Nevada (6), North Carolina (16), Pennsylvania (19) and Wisconsin (10). Together they account for 93 electoral college votes, or more than a third of what a candidate needs to win.\par \par \uc2 Swing states are less commonly referred to as \u8220\'20\'1Ctoss-up\u8221\'20\'1D or \u8220\'20\'1Cpurple\u8221\'20\'1D states \u8211\'20\'13 the latter referring to a mix of blue and red.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.39am BST\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign event in Erie, Pennsylvania has started, but she is not yet on stage.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.36am BST\par \par \uc2 In case you missed this earlier:\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has revealed a plan to give Black men more economic opportunities, as anxiety mounts among her supporters that some in the Black community are less enthused by the Democratic presidential ticket than in recent elections, and may sit this one out \u8211\'20\'13 or support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s plan includes forgivable business loans for Black entrepreneurs, creating more apprenticeships, and studying sickle cell and other diseases that disproportionately affect African American men. It also includes ensuring that Black men have more access to shaping a national cannabis industry and to invest in cryptocurrency.\par \par \uc2 Harris presented the so-called \u8220\'20\'1Copportunity agenda for Black men\u8221\'20\'1D on Monday, before speaking in the north-west corner of Erie, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania}}}\uc2 , the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest battleground state. It will be Harris\u8217\'20\'19s 10th visit to Pennsylvania this election season.\par \par \uc2 Political support among Black men for the Harris-Walz campaign has been wavering somewhat. Last week, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/barack-obama"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Barack Obama}}}\uc2  suggested that some Black men \u8220\'20\'1Caren\u8217\'20\'19t feeling the idea of having a woman as president\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/harris-black-men-economic-opportunities-plan-weed-crypto"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris reveals \u8216\'20\'18opportunity agenda for Black men\u8217\'20\'19 in efforts to shore up support}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will be speaking in a few minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time in Pennsylvania. We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring that to you live.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.32am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , is speaking now in Wisconsin, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/11/us-election-2024-trump-harris-terms-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 swing state}}}\uc2  with 10 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/11/us-election-2024-trump-harris-terms-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 electoral college}}}\uc2  votes.\par \par \uc2 He is talking about the cost of insulin, small business tax credits, and the sandwich generation \u8211\'20\'13 people who are sandwiched between caring for their children and their parents.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.34am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.20am BST\par \par \uc2 When asked about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comment on the possibility of election day \u8220\'20\'1Cchaos\u8221\'20\'1D, Trump dismissed them, saying the real threat comes from within the country, specifically from radical leftists. \u8220\'20\'1CThe enemy from within, in my opinion, is more dangerous than China, Russia and all these countries,\u8221\'20\'1D said Trump.\par \par \uc2 Here is the video clip of those remarks:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13am BST\par \par \uc2 While we wait for that Harris rally to start in Pennsylvania, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Tom Breihan argues that if you want to understand Trump, you should watch 80s action movies.\par \par \uc2 He writes:\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s a real possibility that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  sees no distinction between the terms \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongman\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong man\u8221\'20\'1D. At the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/11/prosecutor-kamala-harris-put-trump-on-trial-but-the-court-of-public-opinion-can-be-fickle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential debate last month}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said world leaders were \u8220\'20\'1Claughing\u8221\'20\'1D at Trump. In response, Trump brought up his endorsement from the autocratic Hungarian prime minister, \uc2 Viktor Orb\u225\'00\'E1n\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1COne of the most respected men \u8211\'20\'13 they call him a strong man. He\u8217\'20\'19s a tough person, smart.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Two months before that debate, the Republican national convention played host to a strong man \u8211\'20\'13 or, at least, to a man who exemplified a certain 80s-kitsch version of strength.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2024/oct/15/donald-trump-macho-movie-action-hero-for-votes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Want to understand Donald Trump? Then watch macho 80s action movies}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who has embarked on a late-campaign round of high-profile interviews after being accused for weeks of avoiding the media, is seeking to highlight the increasingly authoritarian tone Trump has been striking at his rallies.\par \par \uc2 At a speech in Coachella in California on Saturday, he referred to Democratic opponents as \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy within\u8221\'20\'1D, saying they posed a bigger threat to the US than the country\u8217\'20\'19s foreign foes, and targeted Adam Schiff, a Democratic congressman who is running for the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an interview on Fox News the following day, he repeated the phrase to describe those he claimed were planning to create \u8220\'20\'1Cchaos\u8221\'20\'1D on the day of the presidential election. He said the military should be deployed against them.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s use of extreme language has coincided with an increase in his vitriol to describe Harris, who he last week described as \u8220\'20\'1Cmentally impaired\u8221\'20\'1D. He called her \u8220\'20\'1Cretarded\u8221\'20\'1D while addressing Republican fundraisers in September, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign is also trying to draw attention to what it says a dearth of mainstream interviews given by Trump, who instead has chosen to make himself available to sympathetic interviewers, such as the rightwing radio host \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs of today, it has been **one month** since Trump\u8217\'20\'19s been interviewed by a mainstream media outlet, as he has backed out of 60 Minutes and refuses to debate again,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/4932702-trump-harris-media-interviews/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris campaign spokesperson Ian Sams}}}\uc2  posted on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X.\par \par \uc2 By contrast, Harris is due {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/kamala-harris-fox-news-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to be interviewed on Wednesday}}}\uc2  by Bret Baier on Fox News, an outlet that is usually a go-to platform for Trump but unfriendly terrain for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/harris-trump-enemy-within-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris to portray Trump as tyrant-in-waiting after his \u8216\'20\'18enemy within\u8217\'20\'19 remarks}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28pm BST\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  will this evening seek to portray {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  as a potential tyrant-in-waiting who wants to jail his political opponents by seizing on his threat to use US armed forces against those {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/trump-military-enemy-within-armed-forces-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he has branded \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy within\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The US vice-president and Democratic nominee will hone in on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s darkening campaign rhetoric at a rally in Erie, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/pennsylvania"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pennsylvania}}}\uc2 , widely deemed the most crucial battleground state in a presidential race that multiple polls suggest will go down to the wire.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign is releasing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YQnugO8SEx0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new campaign advert}}}\uc2 , titled The Enemy Within, featuring some of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s recent ominous comments about his adversaries and warnings from two former members of his presidential administration about the danger he would pose if elected president again.\par \par \uc2 The 30-second video, complete with footage of Trump walking in front of a row of helmeted riot officers and showing troops on the street during his presidency, tries to concentrate voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds with contributions from \uc2 Olivia Troye\uc2 , a one-time national security adviser to \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , and Kevin Carroll, a former senior counsel in the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI do remember the day that he suggested that we shoot people on the streets,\u8221\'20\'1D Troye says in the ad, which is accompanied with a dramatic musical soundtrack.\par \par \uc2 Carroll adds: \u8220\'20\'1CA second term will be worse. There will be no stopping his worst instincts. Unchecked power to no guard rails. If we elect Trump again, we\u8217\'20\'19re a terrible danger.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/harris-trump-enemy-within-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris to portray Trump as tyrant-in-waiting after his \u8216\'20\'18enemy within\u8217\'20\'19 remarks}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will be speaking at a rally in the all-important state of Pennsylvania (the swing state with the highest number of electoral college votes \u8211\'20\'13 19) in just over an hour and fifteen minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time, or 7.35pm ET.\par \par \uc2 This is Helen Sullivan taking over our live US politics coverage, and I\u8217\'20\'19ll bring that to you as it happens.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Today So Far\par \par \uc2 Here are the major developments so far today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  unveiled new policy proposals aimed at black men that include forgivable small business loans and access to a new legal recreational marijuana industry. She\u8217\'20\'19ll speak about that policy in greater detail at her rally in Erie, Pennsylvania shortly \u8211\'20\'13 where she\u8217\'20\'19s also expected to denounce \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 s statements calling for military force against \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy within.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Trump is also expected to speak in Pennsylvania today, at a rally just outside Philadelphia. The former president\u8217\'20\'19s social media company, Truth Social, is also experiencing a resurgence as its stock value soars ahead of the election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris will appear on Fox News for her first formal sit-down interview with the network on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  campaigned today in Wisconsin, with senators \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2  and \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  and governors \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  and \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2 . At a stop at the \uc2 University of Wisconsin\uc2 , Walz warned students that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s threats against the \u8220\'20\'1Cenemy from within\u8221\'20\'1D meant them.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gwen Walz, an educator and wife of the Democratic vice-presidential nominee \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , shared the couple\u8217\'20\'19s fertility journey today in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.womenshealthmag.com/health/a62578686/gwen-walz-fertility-journey-iui-essay/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 On Indigenous Peoples\u8217\'20\'19 Day, the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  announced that it will launch a \u8220\'20\'1Csix-figure ad campaign\u8221\'20\'1D aimed at turning out Native American voters in Arizona, North Carolina, Montana and Alaska. It is the party\u8217\'20\'19s third Native-focused campaign this year, and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most the DNC has ever spent on a campaign targeting Native voters\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is continuing his tour of Wisconsin today with Michigan and Wisconsin governors \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  and \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, Walz spoke with students at the \uc2 University of Wisconsin\uc2  in Eau Claire, before touring Lambeau Field, where the Packers play, and meeting with a small contingent of Oneida Nation members.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to warn of Trump presidency targeting "the enemy from within"\par \par \uc2 As \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 rally in Erie, Pennsylvania gets under way, the vice-president is expected to warn voters of what a future Trump presidency could look like, seizing upon the former president\u8217\'20\'19s recent comments that he would deploy military force against \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy from within\u8221\'20\'1D, according to a senior campaign official.\par \par \uc2 On that theme, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign is also releasing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YQnugO8SEx0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new ad}}}\uc2 , featuring \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s former national security aides \uc2 Olivia Troye\uc2  and Kevin Carroll. Troye recounts an instant where Trump suggested \u8220\'20\'1Cwe shoot people in the streets\u8221\'20\'1D and Carroll concludes \u8220\'20\'1Cthe second term would be worse.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/roberttait"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert Tait}}}\uc2  with more:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/harris-trump-enemy-within-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris to portray Trump as tyrant-in-waiting after his \u8216\'20\'18enemy within\u8217\'20\'19 remarks}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 As the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  announces its largest ad campaign focused on turning out Native American voters, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has shared her own message on Indigenous Peoples\u8217\'20\'19 Day. Her post on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X shows a meeting she held with young Indigenous leaders while campaigning in Arizona last week.\par \par \uc2 enltrThis Indigenous Peoples\u8217\'20\'19 Day, I am thinking about the young Indigenous leaders I met in Arizona last week.\par \par \uc2 I am counting on their leadership and looking forward to our partnership. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jZbWxeHEkQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/jZbWxeHEkQ}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@KamalaHarris) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHarris/status/1845916348318163037?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Our latest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polling}}}\uc2  indicates that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  holds a two-point lead over the vice-president in Arizona. In 2020, Native voters were largely credited for swinging the long-red state blue for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s America Pac has spent $10.1 million supporting Republican candidates across 18 competitive House races, Business Insider reports. The political action committee has spent more than $100 million this election cycle in total, the majority towards supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s candidacy.\par \par \uc2 enltrElon Musk's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/america?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @America}}}\uc2  super PAC has now hit the $10 million it planned to spend across 18 different House races.\par \par \uc2 More than $100 million spent on the election overall (mostly on Trump/Harris).\par \par \uc2 Highest sum in one district was $1.2 million in NY-17 (Lawler vs. Jones). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/WMdXNNLSP1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/WMdXNNLSP1}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 bryan metzger (@metzgov) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/metzgov/status/1845910077124861998?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 According to Business Insider, which cites \uc2 FEC\uc2  filings, the top three races that the Pac has funded are in New York\u8217\'20\'19s 17th district, where Republican Rep. Mike Lawler faces former Democratic Rep. \uc2 Mondaire Jones\uc2 ; California\u8217\'20\'19s 41st district, where Republican Rep. \uc2 Ken Calvert\uc2  faces Democratic candidate Will Rollin, and Ohio\u8217\'20\'19s 13th district, where Democratic Rep. Emilia Sykes faces Republican candidate Kevin Coughlin.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 New York congresswoman \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  has called out the Biden administration for arming Israel as increasingly dire images emerge from northern Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe horrors unfolding in northern Gaza are the result of a completely unrestrained Netanyahu gov, fully armed by the Biden admin while food aid is blocked and patients are bombed in hospitals,\u8221\'20\'1D she wrote on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a genocide of Palestinians. The US must stop enabling it. Arms embargo now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrThe horrors unfolding in northern Gaza are the result of a completely unrestrained Netanyahu gov, fully armed by the Biden admin while food aid is blocked and patients are bombed in hospitals.\par \par \uc2 This is a genocide of Palestinians. The US must stop enabling it. Arms embargo now.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2  (@AOC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AOC/status/1845915520098267299?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has differentiated herself from \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  by expressing more sympathy for Palestinians since she joined the presidential race in July, but she\u8217\'20\'19s also maintained strong support for Israel.\par \par \uc2 Here are Guardian columnists Moira Donegan and Mohamad Bazzi on how Harris should position herself on Gaza:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/14/kamala-harris-israel-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Time is running out for Kamala Harris to break with Biden on the Gaza catastrophe | Moira Donegan}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/article/2024/sep/06/kamala-harris-israel-arms-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris should do what Joe Biden won\u8217\'20\'19t: commit to actually reining in Israel | Mohamad Bazzi}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Walz: Trump 'crossed a line' by saying army should be used against his enemies\par \par \uc2 Speaking in Eau Claire, Wisconsin, today, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  denounced \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments that armed forces should be deployed against his opponents, who he called \u8220\'20\'1Cthe enemy within \u8221\'20\'1D, after the election. Trump made the statement on Fox News yesterday.\par \par \uc2 enltrGov. Walz: Trump just crossed a line that I have to tell you, in my lifetime, I would have never imagined. He said he would deploy the military against Americans who disagree with him. He called it the 'enemy within.' To \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , anybody who doesn't agree with him is the\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aL37tWX7yz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/aL37tWX7yz}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1845902972749750739?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Speaking to students at the \uc2 University of Wisconsin\uc2 , Walz said: \u8220\'20\'1CTrump just crossed a line that I have to tell you, in my lifetime, I would have never imagined. He said he would deploy the military against Americans who disagree with him. He called it the \u8216\'20\'18enemy within\u8217\'20\'19. To \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , anybody who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t agree with him is the enemy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Read more about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s comments here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/trump-military-enemy-within-armed-forces-election-day"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump sparks outrage after calling for army to handle enemies on election day}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 As news of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s upcoming appearance on Fox News broke this morning, another headline from the network passed more quietly: former friend of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s and Fox News commentator Geraldo Rivera announced he will be voting for Harris.\par \par \uc2 enltrSore Loser\par \par \uc2 With three weeks to go until Election Day, \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  stands a reasonable chance of becoming the 47th President of the United States. Despite assassination attempts, impeachments, special counsels, felony convictions and hundreds of millions in civil penalties,\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Geraldo Rivera (@GeraldoRivera) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GeraldoRivera/status/1845830234710438103?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 On \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X, Rivera shared a long post explaining his decision:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs President [Trump] was a loyal friend, who allowed regular access. My resulting coverage gave him the benefit of most doubts. His presidency was underrated. Throughout his first big scandal in office, the 2017-2019 Mueller Investigation into allegations Trump conspired with Russia to undermine our political process, I stuck with him, deeply suspicious of constant efforts to undermine his Administration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf you are a Republican, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has made a liar of you. He has coaxed and intimidated tens of millions into pretending he was reelected in 2020, and that the election was stolen,\u8221\'20\'1D Rivera continued. \u8220\'20\'1CFormer President Trump is a sore loser who cannot be trusted to honor the Constitution. That is why I am voting for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to be our 47th President.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 With both \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  traveling to Pennsylvania today, CNN reports that one -fifth of all advertising money that has been spent on the race since Harris became the nominee has targeted the state.\par \par \uc2 enltrOut of a total of nearly $1.5B that has been spent on presidential advertising since Harris became the Democratic nominee, more than 1/5 \u8211\'20\'13 about $312M \u8211\'20\'13 has targeted the PA. That\u8217\'20\'19s almost $90M more than the state that has seen the next most ad spending, MI, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DavidWright_7?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DavidWright_7}}}\uc2  reports\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alayna Treene (@alaynatreene) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/alaynatreene/status/1845910278136865026?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 According to Guardian polling, Harris holds a narrow one-point lead in the state, while a recent \uc2 New York Times\uc2  report shows her four points ahead of her opponent there.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is campaigning today in Eau Claire, Wisconsin, with senators \uc2 Amy Klobuchar\uc2  and \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Joking about the support from across the political spectrum that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has received in recent weeks, Klobuchar told students at the \uc2 University of Wisconsin\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re gonna see like a bus going through western Wisconsin with \u8211\'20\'13 I want you to picture this \u8211\'20\'13 \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  and \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2  together holding a sign that says brat fall.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrSens. Klobuchar & Baldwin have joined Gov. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  for a students event at UW Eau Claire.\par \par \uc2 Klobuchar: \u8220\'20\'1CWe're gonna see like a bus going through Western Wisconsin with \u8212\'20\'14 I want you to picture this \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  & \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2  together holding a sign that says brat fall.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/cdpIFQ6rIV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/cdpIFQ6rIV}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Dylan Wells (@dylanewells) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dylanewells/status/1845882383511245272?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 If you were looking for a break from the election cycle this weekend, you may have taken a trip to the movies \u8211\'20\'13 only to find no such break to be had. The Apprentice, a two-hour biopic focused on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s early life, hit theaters on Friday. Here\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/victoria-bekiempis"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Victoria Bekiempis}}}\uc2  on the former president\u8217\'20\'19s less-than-thrilled reaction:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  railed against a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/2024/oct/05/apprentice-trump-movie-ali-abbasi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 just released biopic}}}\uc2  about his life in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/113303964855794908"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 social media screed}}}\uc2  early on Monday, calling it a \u8220\'20\'1Ccheap, defamatory, and politically disgusting hatchet job\u8221\'20\'1D meant to thwart his presidential candidacy.\par \par \uc2 The Apprentice portrays how Trump created his real estate empire under the tutelage of Roy Cohn, a notoriously cutthroat attorney and power-broker in 1970s and 1980s New York City, Intelligencer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/article/trump-movie-the-apprentice-drama-guide.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notes}}}\uc2 . Trump is played by the Marvel actor Sebastian Stan and Cohn by the Succession star Jeremy Strong.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s ex-wife \uc2 Ivana Trump\uc2  is played by Maria Bakalova \u8211\'20\'13 whose breakout role in Borat Subsequent Moviefilm landed her an Academy award nomination. There is a disclaimer at the beginning of The Apprentice indicating that portions were \u8220\'20\'1Cfictionalized for dramatic purposes\u8221\'20\'1D, Intelligencer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nymag.com/intelligencer/article/trump-movie-the-apprentice-drama-guide.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 notes}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In his rant Trump described the film as \u8220\'20\'1Cfake and classless\u8221\'20\'1D. Trump said he hoped it would \u8220\'20\'1Cbomb\u8221\'20\'1D and alleged that it was \u8220\'20\'1Cput out right before the 2024 Presidential Election, to try and hurt the Greatest Political Movement in the History of our Country, \u8216\'20\'18MAKE AMERICA GREAT AGAIN!\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/donald-trump-apprentice-film-attacks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump pens 1am screed against controversial biopic The Apprentice}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 This Indigenous Peoples\u8217\'20\'19 Day, the \uc2 Democratic National Committee\uc2  has announced that it will launch a \u8220\'20\'1Csix-figure ad campaign\u8221\'20\'1D aimed at turning out Native American voters in Arizona, North Carolina, Montana and Alaska. It is the party\u8217\'20\'19s third Native-focused campaign this year, and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most the DNC has ever spent on a campaign targeting Native voters\u8221\'20\'1D, according to the committee.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, Native voters were crucial to swinging Arizona \u8211\'20\'13 a traditionally Republican state \u8211\'20\'13 for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNative American people will absolutely help decide the results of this election,\u8221\'20\'1D Minnesota Lt Gov Peggy Flanagan, a member of the White Earth Band of Ojibwe, said in a statement announcing the ads. If \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  wins the election, making Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  her vice-president, Flanagan would become the first Native American woman to serve as a state\u8217\'20\'19s governor.\par \par \uc2 Democratic and Republican leaders have celebrated today\u8217\'20\'19s holiday in markedly different ways. While the Trump campaign has tweeted \u8220\'20\'1CHappy Columbus Day\u8221\'20\'1D while saying \u8220\'20\'1CRadical left Marxist \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  thinks that this holiday celebrating the discovery of the Americas and the birth of western civilization is a bad thing,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president has yet to make any statement on the holiday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 A Gallup News poll released today found that Americans\u8217\'20\'19 trust in the media is still at record lows, as has been the case since 2016. For the third year in a row, Gallup found that more adults have no trust at all in the media than trust it a great deal or fair amount. The news is particularly profound as election day approaches: Gallup found the media is the least trusted group among 10 civic and political institutions involved in the democratic process, such as state and local governments, the judiciary and Congress.\par \par \uc2 enltrFor the third consecutive year, more U.S. adults have no trust at all in the media (36%) than trust it a great deal or fair amount. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Eg1Xy1ZHCa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Eg1Xy1ZHCa}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Gallup (@Gallup) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Gallup/status/1845838672333000866?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 In the 1970s, Gallup first reported that trust in the media hovered around 70% \u8211\'20\'13 though that percentage began to fall in the late 1990s and early 2000s, as about 50% of Americans reported trusting the news. Only about a third of Americans said they trusted the media in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Trust in the media correlates with party affiliation and age, Gallup reports. Currently, 54% of Democrats, 27% of independents and 12% of Republicans say they have a great deal or fair amount of trust in the media. Meanwhile, older Americans trust the media at higher rates than their younger peers (only 31% of Democrats between the ages of 18 and 29, versus 74% of those 65 and older).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ex-president \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  has been campaigning for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Georgia this weekend. At a campaign stop today, he told voters: \u8220\'20\'1CYou have to realize it is literally possible that the whole election could be decided here.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrFormer President \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  is in Columbus today trying to fire up Georgia Democrats ahead of the first day of early voting tomorrow. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19ve just got to decide how bad you want this.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/gapol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #gapol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/YTrSMohxG9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/YTrSMohxG9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jill Nolin (@jillnolin) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jillnolin/status/1845851055248068853?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 our most recent polling}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is currently leading \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  by one point in the Peach state. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/us/elections/polls-president-georgia.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent poll}}}\uc2  from the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  shows the same. The state\u8217\'20\'19s elections have been in the spotlight since 2020, when then Georgia secretary of state \uc2 Brad Raffensperger\uc2  refused to change the election results in Trump\u8217\'20\'19s favor.\par \par \uc2 For more on the state of the election, and election interference, in Georgia, consider:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/10/fulton-county-georgia-election-board"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fulton county brawl with Georgia state election board escalates as election approaches}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/18/trump-election-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Network of Georgia election officials strategizing to undermine 2024 result}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/georgia-board-of-elections-election-deniers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The election deniers with a chokehold on Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s state election board}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris agrees to first-ever sit-down interview with Fox News\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will appear on Fox News for her first formal sit-down interview with the network on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 enltrBIG! VP Harris to sit down with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BretBaier?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BretBaier}}}\uc2  on Weds, her first with FOX (and something Biden hasn\u8217\'20\'19t ever done). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xIkn0f30Zg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xIkn0f30Zg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jacqui Heinrich (@JacquiHeinrich) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JacquiHeinrich/status/1845861715231031542?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The interview, with the network\u8217\'20\'19s chief political anchor Bret Baier, will air Wednesday at 6pm ET.\par \par \uc2 enltrNEW: \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has agreed to her first-ever Fox News sit-down interview on Wednesday with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BretBaier?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @BretBaier}}}\uc2 , outside Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 Tapes in afternoon & airs at 6 p.m. Eastern. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/UV7jJwK5wN"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/UV7jJwK5wN}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Michael M. Grynbaum (@grynbaum) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/grynbaum/status/1845857264759926982?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 14, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Although the conservative outlet generally airs content that supports Republican nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s appearance signals the inroads she is attempting to make among Republicans. In campaign events across the country, Harris has spoken in front of banners reading \u8220\'20\'1CCountry Over Party\u8221\'20\'1D and alongside guests such as \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 . Her running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , has appeared on Fox News Sunday twice this month, and other Democratic proxies such as \uc2 Josh Shapiro\uc2 , the governor of Pennsylvania, and \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , the transportation secretary, have spoken on the network in recent weeks as well.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/02/democrats-buttigieg-sanders-fox-news-appearances-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why are so many Democratic politicians appearing on Fox News?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 5.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 With election day nearing, both the Harris and Trump campaigns are closely tracking every potential vote in hotly contested swing states such as Pennsylvania and Arizona. But, according to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/hugo-lowell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hugo Lowell}}}\uc2 , there\u8217\'20\'19s an issue with the Trump campaign\u8217\'20\'19s software that\u8217\'20\'19s made it difficult for them to know whether their ground game operation is reaching target voters. Here\u8217\'20\'19s Hugo:\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign this cycle is targeting so-called low propensity Trump voters, who are often in rural areas, as part of their bet that hitting those people who don\u8217\'20\'19t typically vote but would cast a ballot for Trump if they did, could make a difference in a close election.\par \par \uc2 But the Trump campaign and the \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 -backed America Pac, which is now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/trump-voter-turnout-elon-musk-pac"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 doing an outsized portion of the Trump ground game}}}\uc2 , use a management app called Campaign Sidekick that struggles in areas with slow internet and means canvassers have to use an offline version.\par \par \uc2 The Campaign Sidekick app effectively forces canvassers who have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://vimeo.com/458710648"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less than 40mbps of internet}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 sufficient to stream 4K video \u8211\'20\'13 to use \u8220\'20\'1Coffline walkbooks\u8221\'20\'1D which have no geo-tracking feature and do not always upload after a route is completed, the people said.\par \par \uc2 As a result, the Trump campaign and America Pac then have little way to know whether canvassers are actually knocking on doors or whether they are cheating \u8211\'20\'13 for instance, by \u8220\'20\'1Cspeed-running\u8221\'20\'1D routes where they literally throw campaign materials at doors as they drive past.\par \par \uc2 For more, continue reading here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/trump-ground-game-smartphone-app"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump ground game undercut by slow internet that crashes app}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 Black lawmakers are calling for an investigation of Tom Barrett , a Republican running for Michigan\u8217\'20\'19s vacant seat in the House of Representatives, after his campaign published an ad in a Black-owned newspaper incorrectly listing election day as 6 November.\par \par \uc2 The complaint, filed by the Michigan Legislative Black caucus, accuses Barrett of purposely attempting to mislead Black voters to suppress their vote: \u8220\'20\'1CAt best, Tom Barrett and his Campaign have committed a shocking oversight which will undoubtedly lead to confusion by Black voters in Lansing. And, at worst, this ad could be part of an intentional strategy to \u8216\'20\'18deter\u8217\'20\'19 Black voters by deceiving them into showing up to vote on the day after the 2024 election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Barrett\u8217\'20\'19s campaign told {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/2024/10/14/tom-barrett-michigan-election-misleading-ad/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Washington Post}}}\uc2  the mistake was \u8220\'20\'1Cnothing but a proofing error\u8221\'20\'1D, noting other mailers it has sent to Black voters with the correct date.\par \par \uc2 Barrett is currently running against Democrat Curtis Hertel to fill the seat left vacant by \uc2 Elissa Slotkin\uc2 , a Democrat who is running for Senate. The outcome of the race could determine which party controls the House in the new year.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 Gwen Walz, an educator and wife of the Democratic vice-presidential nominee \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , is sharing the couple\u8217\'20\'19s fertility journey today in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.womenshealthmag.com/health/a62578686/gwen-walz-fertility-journey-iui-essay/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Women\u8217\'20\'19s Health}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s never easy to tell this story, and I think all of us who speak about our reproductive challenges wish we didn\u8217\'20\'19t have to,\u8221\'20\'1D Gwen Walz told the magazine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEarlier this year, Tim and I were in his office at the Minnesota State Capitol, getting ready to do a press conference, when we heard the news that the \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court\uc2  had ruled that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.womenshealthmag.com/health/a46905045/alabama-supreme-court-ruling-frozen-embryo-ivf-patients-questions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 embryos have personhood}}}\uc2 , which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.womenshealthmag.com/life/a60029416/alabama-women-affected-ivf-embryo-supreme-court-ruling/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 effectively halted IVF treatments in the state}}}\uc2  as clinics and hospitals tried to figure out what to do. We looked at each other, and we were both just right back there, all those years ago, when we were trying to start our own family and going through our own fertility treatments.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Walz goes on to describe the couple\u8217\'20\'19s experience trying intrauterine insemination (a fertility treatment that her husband incorrectly referred to as IVF earlier in the campaign) and the joy they felt when they learned they had conceived their daughter Hope, who today is 23. She concludes by speaking about her sadness that Hope will not have the same reproductive freedoms, and worry that that will worsen if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is re-elected in November, before urging readers to vote for the Harris-Walz ticket.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are both returning to Pennsylvania today \u8211\'20\'13 a state they and their proxies have frequented over the past month. Last week, former president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  rallied voters in Pittsburgh to vote blue downballot, while also specifically calling on Black men to support the vice-president. Meanwhile, earlier on 5 October, Trump held one of his largest rallies in Butler, the site of his near-assassination in July.\par \par \uc2 Today, Harris will rally voters in Erie \u8211\'20\'13 in the state\u8217\'20\'19s far north-west corner \u8211\'20\'13 while Trump speaks just outside Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 Although the state\u8217\'20\'19s leadership is largely Democratic \u8211\'20\'13 Pennsylvania has elected a Democratic governor three times in a row, and both of the state\u8217\'20\'19s senators are also Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 the margin for victory in Pennsylvania is narrow. The state\u8217\'20\'19s natural gas industry could sway the election in a state that holds 19 electoral votes \u8211\'20\'13 the most of any swing state.\par \par \uc2 Current {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/23/presidential-polls-kamala-harris-donald-trump-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Guardian polling}}}\uc2  shows Harris leading the state by a narrow one-point margin, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/12/upshot/harris-trump-polls-election.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a recent New York Times poll}}}\uc2  shows the vice-president leading in the Keystone state by four points.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be following both campaigns\u8217\'20\'19 appearances in Pennsylvania today and keep you apprised of any developments.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/10/obama-kamala-harris-pennsylvania-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Obama tells men to drop \u8216\'20\'18excuses\u8217\'20\'19 and support Kamala Harris over Trump}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/05/us-politics-donald-trump-kamala-harris-joe-biden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump repeats false anti-immigrant claims at Pennsylvania rally as Musk urges everyone to vote \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House press aides scrap \u8211\'20\'13 Axios\par \par \uc2 Take a break for a moment from the endless campaign coverage and feverish polls speculation and enjoy an old fashioned gossipy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/10/14/white-house-briefings-karine-jean-pierre-john-kirby"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  on in-house bickering at the White House.\par \par \uc2 The protagonists are \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  and national security spokesperson John Kirby. Apparently, Axios gleefully reports, KJP has been \u8220\'20\'1Cblocking\u8221\'20\'1D Kirby from appearances at the press podium.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHaving both of them at the podium was what Biden wanted, but Jean-Pierre thought that Kirby\u8217\'20\'19s presence gave the impression she needed a chaperone, people familiar with her thinking told Axios.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Full details {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/10/14/white-house-briefings-karine-jean-pierre-john-kirby"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Truth Social stock rallies\par \par \uc2 CNN is reporting on a recent stock market rally in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s social media platform Truth Social. Truth Social has far more often been the subject of mockery and schadenfreude as its value has largely headed downwards since its stock market debut.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/14/investing/trump-stock-truth-social-election/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CNN reports}}}\uc2  that recently it has soared.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUp until very recently, \uc2 Trump Media & Technology Group\uc2  had been in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/09/11/investing/trump-stock-debate-truth-social/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 meltdown mode}}}\uc2 . Its share price dropped to a record low of $12.15 on September 23, marking a stunning 82% crash from its high.\par \par \uc2 But the owner of Truth Social is enjoying a massive rebound, more than doubling its share price in less than three weeks. It spiked nearly 50% last week alone. It\u8217\'20\'19s a remarkable turnaround, even for a notoriously-volatile stock that has been described as a meme stock on steroids.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The reason? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/10/14/investing/trump-stock-truth-social-election/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Market speculation }}}\uc2  that Trump could be heading back to the White House.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Voter registration worries for Harris in key swing states\par \par \uc2 The incredibly right races in the seven crucial battleground states have been a feature of the 2024 election almost from the start \u8211\'20\'13 and especially since \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  entered the race.\par \par \uc2 But Democratic jitters \u8211\'20\'13 already at peak intensity \u8211\'20\'13 are unlikely to be soothed by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4929781-voter-registration-democrats-pennsylvania-nc-nevada/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hill report}}}\uc2  showing worrying signs re \u8211\'20\'13 Democrat voter registration.\par \par \uc2 Key points: \u8220\'20\'1C Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 voter registration advantage has dropped in three key battleground states \u8211\'20\'13 Pennsylvania, North Carolina and Nevada \u8211\'20\'13 raising a red flag for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/people/kamala-harris/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vice President Harris }}}\uc2  as experts cite a lack of enthusiasm for the Biden administration brand and the Democratic Party, generally, as problems.\par \par \uc2 In Arizona, another key battleground state, Republicans have seen their voter registration advantage increase substantially, which could make it tougher for Harris to carry a state that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/people/joe-biden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 President Biden }}}\uc2  narrowly won in 2020.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A full report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4929781-voter-registration-democrats-pennsylvania-nc-nevada/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.34pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good news for Democrats in Senate\par \par \uc2 Suffice to say, that in recent days the mood among many Democrats has turned a little sour as November\u8217\'20\'19s election date gets ever closer. There is deep nervousness about the state of the race between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , especially as poll after poll shows the crucial swing states are on a knife-edge.\par \par \uc2 But Politico has a little cheer for Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/10/13/senate-republican-poll-memo-00183570"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with an internal memo}}}\uc2  from a Repuplican Super Pac showing the party\u8217\'20\'19s chances of extending power in the Senate is looking grim.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe new round of October polling from the Senate Leadership Fund shows all but one Republican candidate running behind \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in battleground states, a pattern that could sharply limit their ability to build a sizable majority unless they can force a change in the final weeks of the election,\u8221\'20\'1D the memo says.\par \par \uc2 More details and a full report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/10/13/senate-republican-poll-memo-00183570"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump making regular appearances in key battleground state of Pennsylvania\par \par \uc2 Harris and Trump have both been making regular appearances in Pennsylvania, the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest battleground state. Today will be Harris\u8217\'20\'19s 10th visit to Pennsylvania this campaign, and just last week Trump made stops in both Scranton and Reading in the state.\par \par \uc2 AP provides some background on the key battleground state where both candidates will speak today:\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s energy industry and natural gas fracking are likely topics as they compete for the fraction of the state\u8217\'20\'19s voters who have not made up their minds. Mail-in voting is well underway in the state where some 7 million people are likely to cast votes in the presidential race.\par \par \uc2 Trump beat \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  by more than 40,000 votes in Pennsylvania on his way to winning the presidency in 2016, but native Scrantonian \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  edged Trump by about 80,000 votes in the state four years ago.\par \par \uc2 Harris will be holding a rally in Erie, a Democratic majority city of about 94,000 people bordered by suburbs and rural areas with significant numbers of Republicans. Erie County is often cited as one of the state\u8217\'20\'19s reliable bellwether regions, where the electorate has a decidedly moderate voting record. Trump visited Erie on Sept. 29.\par \par \uc2 Trump plans a town hall Monday at the Greater Philadelphia Expo Center and Fairgrounds in suburban Oaks, hoping to drive up turnout among his supporters.\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania\u8217\'20\'19s 19 electoral votes, the most of any swing state, have long made it a center of presidential electioneering. Democrats have won three straight elections for governor and both current U.S. senators are Democrats, but its legislature is closely divided and both parties have had recent success in statewide contests.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Three polls released yesterday show the candidates locked in a close battle for the White House.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/10/13/us/elections/times-siena-poll-hispanic-likely-electorate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A New York Times poll}}}\uc2  found that Harris is underperforming the last three Democratic candidates for the White House among Latino voters.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/dead-heat-trump-pulls-even-harris-nbc-news-poll-rcna174201"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 An NBC News poll}}}\uc2  showed the candidates in a \u8220\'20\'1Cdead heat\u8221\'20\'1D nationally at 48% support. The poll found that voters are reassessing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s first term more favourably \u8211\'20\'13 but also that voters view \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a top motivating issue, which could hurt the former president after three of his \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  appointees eliminated the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-harris-poll-how-information-beliefs-shape-tight-2024-campaign/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A CBS News poll}}}\uc2  found that the presidential race is more than just two conflicting ideologies \u8211\'20\'13 but about a fundamental disconnection.\par \par \uc2 Each poll contained positive signs for Harris, including a five-point advantage on \u8220\'20\'1Clooking out for middle class\u8221\'20\'1D (ABC); \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  being \u8220\'20\'1C#1 motivating issue\u8221\'20\'1D (NBC), with Democrat up 19 points on the issue over Trump (\uc2 New York Times\uc2 ); Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Latino support at the same level from 2020 (\uc2 CBS\uc2 ), and also Harris matching Biden in 2020 with Black voters.\par \par \uc2 You can read more analysis of the latest polls by Edward Helmore in the story below.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/13/harris-trump-election-race-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris and Trump, locked in tight race, seek edge among undecided voters}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 In the Middle East, Iran has said it sees \u8220\'20\'1Cno grounds\u8221\'20\'1D for indirect talks with the US via Oman.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CCurrently we don\u8217\'20\'19t see any ground for these talks, until we can get past the current crisis,\u8221\'20\'1D Iran\u8217\'20\'19s foreign minister \uc2 Abbas Araghchi\uc2  said on Monday, adding the process had been halted \u8220\'20\'1Cdue to the specific conditions of the region\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It comes amid expectations that Israel could launch an attack on Iran.\par \par \uc2 On Sunday it was announced that the US will send an antimissile system to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  as well as a crew of US military personnel to operate the system. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.defense.gov/News/Releases/Release/Article/3934493/statement-by-pentagon-press-secretary-maj-gen-pat-ryder-on-the-deployment-of-a/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  released on Sunday, Pentagon press secretary Maj Gen Pat Ryder said that the US will send an \u8220\'20\'1Cassociated crew of US military personnel to Israel to help bolster Israel\u8217\'20\'19s air defenses\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  offer two starkly different visions for the country with much at stake \u8211\'20\'13 from pocketbook economic issues and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the strength of the country\u8217\'20\'19s global alliances and existential questions about the future of American democracy and the planet.\par \par \uc2 As they compete for the White House, both candidates have laid out their plans in speeches, campaign ads and media interviews. Most of it amounts to a wish list, sketched out in broad strokes and lacking concrete details about how they would be implemented or paid for. A number of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s proposals raise legal questions, while some of Harris\u8217\'20\'19s would probably require Democratic control of Congress.\par \par \uc2 You can see where they stand on the key issues here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/14/election-harris-trump-issues-policies"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Where do Harris and Trump stand on the key election issues?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Like Trump, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will be in Pennsylvania this evening. The vice-president will attend an evening campaign rally in Erie, where she is to appear with Democratic senator \uc2 John Fetterman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.56am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  unveiled new policy proposals aimed at black men on Monday that include forgivable small business loans and access to a new legal recreational marijuana industry, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign and Democrats \u8211\'20\'13 including former president \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 have expressed deep concern about whether black males will turn out on 5 November in numbers seen in past elections and whether they will support Harris or her Republican rival.\par \par \uc2 The new policies, directly pitched at the black male electorate, include one million loans that are fully forgivable of up to $20,000 to entrepreneurs in underserved communities, and a promise to legalise recreational marijuana and help ensure black entrepreneurs have access to the new industry.\par \par \uc2 Other proposals include boosting access to the cryptocurrency industry for black Americans and launching a national health equity initiative focused on black men that addresses diseases like sickle cell, which disproportionately impacts the community.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters provides more detail on the man who was arrested at a security checkpoint near a Trump rally on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Riverside County\uc2  Sheriff Chad Bianco said he believed his department halted an assassination attempt, though he acknowledged that was \u8220\'20\'1Cspeculation\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The man faces gun charges after he was found in possession of loaded firearms, multiple passports and a fake license plate. The suspect was released on bail on Saturday, jail records showed. A federal official said on Sunday that a federal investigation was underway.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we do know is he showed up with multiple passports with different names, an unregistered vehicle with a fake license plate and loaded firearms,\u8221\'20\'1D the sheriff said at a news conference yesterday. \u8220\'20\'1CI truly do believe that we prevented another assassination attempt.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The 49-year-old man, identified as Las Vegas resident Vem Miller, was stopped in a black SUV by sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s deputies around 5pm local time on Saturday and taken into custody without incident, according to the sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office. Trump had not yet taken the stage.\par \par \uc2 Jail records show Miller was released on $5,000 bail on Saturday after being charged with possession of a loaded firearm and a high-capacity magazine.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe incident did not impact the safety of former President Trump or attendees of the event,\u8221\'20\'1D the sheriff\u8217\'20\'19s office said in a press release.\par \par \uc2 The US Attorney\u8217\'20\'19s Los Angeles office, in a statement on its web site on Sunday, also said Trump was not in danger, citing the \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.43am BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will speak in Oaks, Pennsylvania, later today. News of the event, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.donaldjtrump.com/news/7dc11697-2f4f-4603-88e1-b63d4f200363"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 posted on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s website}}}\uc2 , gives a flavour of what the candidate might speak about:\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania voters are no stranger to the disastrous policies of the Harris-Biden administration. Pennsylvanians are paying nearly $1,000 extra per month for the same basket of goods due to Kamala\u8217\'20\'19s inflation crisis. At the same time hardworking Pennsylvanians are bringing home real wages worth less and racking up more credit card debt. Gas and diesel prices hit historic highs thanks to the Harris-Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s crackdown on American energy and Pennsylvania fracking.\par \par \uc2 More broadly, Pennsylvania has been on the receiving end of America\u8217\'20\'19s lopsided trade deals that have allowed foreign adversaries to hollow out our industry. Countless factories have shuttered, and countless more quality American jobs have been lost thanks the nonsensical dogma of \u8216\'20\'18free trade.\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 A Trump-Vance administration will pick up where the first Trump administration left off to fuel an American revival of strong job growth, low inflation, and prosperity for everyday Pennsylvanians. President Trump will unleash Pennsylvania energy and get back to re-writing America\u8217\'20\'19s faulty trade agreements to support the Pennsylvania industrial prowess that built America.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.28am BST\par \par \uc2 US officials said they were monitoring China\u8217\'20\'19s military drills around Taiwan.\par \par \uc2 China launched its latest war games around the democratically-governed island in response to a speech made by Taiwan\u8217\'20\'19s president Lai Ching-te last week. Lai said China and Taiwan are not \u8220\'20\'1Csubordinate to each other\u8221\'20\'1D and China has \u8220\'20\'1Cno right to represent Taiwan\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe call on the PRC to act with restraint and to avoid any further actions that may undermine peace and stability across the Taiwan Strait and in the broader region, which is essential to regional peace and prosperity and a matter of international concern,\u8221\'20\'1D State Department spokesperson \uc2 Matthew Miller\uc2  said, using the initials for the People\u8217\'20\'19s Republic of China, China\u8217\'20\'19s official name.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.12am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump pledges an extra 10,000 border agents if elected\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  pledged on Sunday to hire an extra 10,000 border patrol agents if he is reelected as president as he steps up his hardline rhetoric on immigration, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The Republican presidential candidate said he would meet the goal by asking Congress to fund a 10% pay rise for border patrol agents and a $10,000 retention and signing bonus, at a rally in the border state of Arizona, an election battleground. There are currently about 20,000 border patrol officers, so the pledge would see a sizeable increase in the force.\par \par \uc2 Flanked on stage by leaders of the Border Patrol union, who have endorsed Trump, the former president said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis will ensure that we can hire and keep the Border Patrol agents that we need.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has noticeably hardened his anti-immigration rhetoric in the final weeks of the campaign. Last month he called immigrants in the US illegally who commit violent crimes \u8220\'20\'1Cmonsters,\u8221\'20\'1D \u8220\'20\'1Cstone-cold killers\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cvile animals.\u8221\'20\'1D On Friday he called for the death penalty for \u8220\'20\'1Cany migrant\u8221\'20\'1D who kills a US citizen.\par \par \uc2 Critics say Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric reinforces racist tropes \u8211\'20\'13 studies generally find there is no evidence immigrants commit crimes at a higher rate than native-born Americans.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.17am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.58am BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning and welcome to the US elections blog with a little over three weeks to go until Americans head to the polls.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  were speaking last night and are back on the campaign trail today with both expected to hold events later in the swing state of Pennsylvania. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a round-up of what happened overnight in the US.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A man with a shotgun, loaded handgun, ammunition and several fake passports in his vehicle was arrested at a security checkpoint outside \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally Saturday night in the Southern California desert, police said. He was released the same day on $5,000 bail. The suspect, a 49-year-old resident of Las Vegas, was driving an unregistered black SUV with a \u8220\'20\'1Chomemade\u8221\'20\'1D license plate that was stopped by deputies assigned to the rally in Coachella, east of Los Angeles, \uc2 Riverside County\uc2  Sheriff Chad Bianco said at a news conference.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  spent Sunday trying to shore up political support among what they perceived to be must-have voting blocs. Polls show them locked in a tight 5 November presidential race.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump pledged on Sunday to hire an extra 10,000 border patrol agents if he is reelected as president. The Republican presidential candidate said he would meet the goal by asking the \uc2 US Congress\uc2  to fund a 10% pay rise for border patrol agents and a $10,000 retention and signing bonus, at a rally in the border state of Arizona, an election battleground.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris held a rally in Greenville, North Carolina, where she attacked her rival for spreading misinformation related to hurricanes Helene and Milton. \u8220\'20\'1CFrom him, we are just hearing from that same, old tired playbook,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe has no plan for how he would address the needs of the American people. He is only focused on himself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Both Harris and Trump will be in Pennsylvania later today. Harris is speaking in the city of Erie and Trump is on the stump in Oaks, a small community about 20 miles from Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Speaker Mike Johnson said that passing additional hurricane aid for states impacted by hurricanes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hurricane-helene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Helene}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hurricane-milton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Milton}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ccan wait\u8221\'20\'1D until Congress is back in session after the election.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Three major polls were released Sunday, showing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  either ahead of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or running a head-to-head race.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241014ekae001e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
