\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Monday briefing: The battlegrounds that could define the final weeks of the US election\b0\par\par\uc2 Nimo Omer \par \uc2 2,356 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 October 2024\par 05:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In today\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter: The Republican and Democrat nominees have ramped up their media appearances and rhetoric in recent days to try and gain an advantage ahead of the election in three weeks\u8226\'20\'22 Sign up here for our daily newsletter, First Edition\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 As the US election slowly builds to its crescendo, there is little time left for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to convince the remaining undecided voters to pick them in this coin-toss race.\par \par \uc2 To try to pull ahead, Harris went on an uncharacteristic media blitz last week. Largely avoiding traditional media, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s team opted to focus their strategy on talkshows like Howard Stern and The Late Show with Stephen Colbert and podcasts like Call Her Daddy and All the Smoke, to reach audiences who are less likely to vote.\par \par \uc2 The Democrat campaign has pushed hard to characterise Harris as the change candidate despite being the incumbent vice-president. Trump, meanwhile, has been holding at least two rallies a week during the election cycle, which have grown in terms of length and vitriol.\par \par \uc2 With just three short weeks to go before US voters head to the polls, today\u8217\'20\'19s newsletter breaks down the state of the race. That\u8217\'20\'19s right after the headlines.\par \par \uc2 Five big stories\par \par \uc2 Scotland\par \par \uc2 | Alex Salmond, the former first minister of Scotland, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/oct/13/alex-salmond-had-huge-political-impact-says-john-swinney-scotland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has died at the age of 69}}}\uc2 . \uc2 John Swinney\uc2 , the incumbent first minister, has paid tribute to Salmond\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ccolossal contribution\u8221\'20\'1D to Scottish and UK politics, as allies of the former first minister mourned his sudden death on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Middle East\par \par \uc2 | A \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  drone attack on an army base in central Israel killed four soldiers and severely wounded seven others on Sunday, the Israeli military said, in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/oct/14/hezbollah-drone-attack-on-israel-army-idf-base"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deadliest strike by the militant group}}}\uc2  since Israel launched its ground invasion of Lebanon nearly two weeks ago.\par \par \uc2 Politics\par \par \uc2 | \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/oct/14/keir-starmer-promise-slash-red-tape-investment-summit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 promise to slash red tape}}}\uc2  and \u8220\'20\'1Crip out the bureaucracy that blocks investment\u8221\'20\'1D as he hosts hundreds of global business executives for a major summit in central London.\par \par \uc2 US\par \par \uc2 | A man {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/13/las-vegas-man-arrested-trump-assassination-attempt-coachella-california"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 armed with guns and false press and VIP passes}}}\uc2  was apprehended by authorities at a campaign rally in California on Saturday being held by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Water industry\par \par \uc2 | Small companies in Suffolk that manufacture drinks have been told to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/oct/14/water-supply-small-companies-drinks-makers-suffolk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 keep a lid on their water usage for most of the next decade}}}\uc2 , amid concerns at their supplier that it will be unable to meet rising demand.\par \par \uc2 In depth: The issues shaping the campaign\par \par \uc2 The Democrats sent out their most iconic figures to throw their weight behind Harris last week, with \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  beginning his swing state tour in Pennsylvania and \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  travelling through the south. This is an existential election, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign argues, so they are throwing everything they have at it.\par \par \uc2 Trump, meanwhile, has only grown more agitated and profane. His insults against Harris have become more personal \u8211\'20\'13 during a rally Trump described his rival as \u8220\'20\'1Cmentally impaired\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cmentally disabled\u8221\'20\'1D. In equally hyperbolic language, Trump is promising voters an \u8220\'20\'1Ceconomic boom\u8221\'20\'1D if he wins the election. Conversely, he said that a Harris victory would turn the US into a hellhole \u8220\'20\'1Clike Detroit\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 during a speech in Detroit.\par \par \uc2 The tone and mood of the race will likely only sour as we get closer to polling day.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Too close to call\par \par \uc2 Despite Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign raising a record-breaking \u163\'00\'A31bn in 80 days, the race in key battleground states remains extremely tight. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://emersoncollegepolling.com/october-2024-state-polls-mixed-movement-across-swing-states-shows-dead-heat/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A poll by Emerson College and the Hill}}}\uc2  found that in Georgia, North Carolina and Pennsylvania, 49% support Trump and 48% Harris. In Michigan and Wisconsin, 49% support both candidates. In Nevada, 48% support Harris, 47% Trump, and in Arizona, 49% support Trump and 47% Harris.\par \par \uc2 Other polls similarly show that the candidates are neck and neck in many major swing states. A national poll published by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://today.yougov.com/politics/articles/50661-kamala-harris-lead-vp-debate-hurricanes-health-care-pete-rose-october-6-7-2024-economist-yougov-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 YouGov/the Economist}}}\uc2  found that Harris pulled ahead by four points, and another by the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/campaign/4921203-kamala-harris-donald-trump-national-new-york-times-poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times/Siena College}}}\uc2  found that she took a slim three-point lead. And this past weekend alone {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/economic-discontent-issue-divisions-add-tight-presidential-contest/story?id=114723390"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2024-election/dead-heat-trump-pulls-even-harris-nbc-news-poll-rcna174201"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 major}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/trump-harris-poll-how-information-beliefs-shape-tight-2024-campaign/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 polls}}}\uc2  showed that Harris was either ahead of former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or running a head-to-head race. Both teams are dashing across the country to scoop up every vote they can, in a final frenzied attempt to pull just ahead of the other.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 The immigration \u8216\'20\'18issue\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Trump has long blamed many of the country\u8217\'20\'19s ills on immigration, including unemployment, unaffordable housing, inflation and election tampering. In the last month, however, the rhetoric has become harsher and more violent. At one rally, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trumps-already-harsh-rhetoric-migrants-is-turning-darker-election-day-nears-2024-10-04/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told supporters}}}\uc2  that migrants were \u8220\'20\'1Cstone cold killers\u8221\'20\'1D that would \u8220\'20\'1Cgrab young girls and slice them up right in front of their parents\u8221\'20\'1D without a second thought.\par \par \uc2 The apocalyptic messaging relies on racist tropes, characterising migrants who have crossed the US-Mexico border as sexually violent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/28/trump-wisconsin-immigration-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Cmonsters\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cvile animals\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 , who are the cause of a \u8220\'20\'1Ccrime wave\u8221\'20\'1D. There is no evidence that immigration is a driving factor of crime.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policy solution is simple: mass deportation. \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , a former Trump White House adviser, has said that the goal is to eject 1 million people per year. There are few details about how this would work in practice but Trump himself admitted last month that it would be a \u8220\'20\'1Cbloody story\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 A recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1660/immigration.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup}}}\uc2  poll found that 77% of Americans believe the southern border is experiencing either an ongoing crisis or is a major problem. Some 53% support an expansion of the border wall and 63% would support the president temporarily closing the border to asylum seekers when the border is \u8220\'20\'1Coverwhelmed\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As Trump and Vance run towards immigration as an issue, throughout the campaign it has been an anchor for Harris. Although she has condemned Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rhetoric as divisive, the vice-president has seemingly conceded ground on the underlying Republican narrative on immigration: that the system is broken and that the fix is imposing some of the most restrictive immigration and asylum policies in decades. The shift on immigration is an attempt to dispel Republican criticism that she and Biden have been too permissive. Her plans include ramping up prosecutions for those who cross the border illegally, and curtailing asylum applications.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Trump bets on the economy\par \par \uc2 Across the board, polls show that the economy is the top concern for voters.\par \par \uc2 Trump has had a persistent advantage on the topic \u8211\'20\'13 earlier this year, one poll found that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/4447348-biden-trails-trump-by-20-points-on-handling-of-economy-poll/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he was 20 points ahead of Biden}}}\uc2  on the economy. Harris has narrowed that gap considerably, but Trump still has the edge. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/651719/economy-important-issue-2024-presidential-vote.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gallup}}}\uc2  poll found that 54% of voters view Trump as better equipped than Harris to handle the economy, in comparison to 45% who believed that Harris would be better.\par \par \uc2 The Democrats have concentrated on making Harris the candidate for the middle class, as opposed to Trump, whom she claims is only interested in helping \u8220\'20\'1Chimself, and people like himself\u8221\'20\'1D if he regains the presidency.\par \par \uc2 Instead of focusing on the positive macroeconomic changes, as Biden did, Harris is centring the cost of living in her messaging, targeting families, small businesses, young people and manufacturers.\par \par \uc2 She has offered first-time homebuyers a $25,000 tax credit; a $6,000 tax credit for parents of newborns; a universal preschool programme for 4-year-olds; a reintroduction of the pandemic-era expanded child tax credit; and the expansion of a small business creation tax break.\par \par \uc2 Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/14/kamala-harris-economic-policy-aides"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has also pledged}}}\uc2  to enact a federal ban on corporate price gouging and to hike taxes on the wealthiest Americans to pay for the social safety net that she wants to implement.\par \par \uc2 Coasting on the perception of a strong economic record, Trump has maintained the line that the way to prosperity is through enormous tariffs on imported goods, cutting taxes \u8211\'20\'13 including capital gains tax to 15% \u8211\'20\'13 and widespread, aggressive deregulation. He also wants to boost US energy production and to invest more in fossil fuels. His policies, he says, will reduce inflation and improve the quality of life for the average American. The Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget, a nonpartisan group, found that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s proposals {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.crfb.org/papers/fiscal-impact-harris-and-trump-campaign-plans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could add up to $15tn to national debt}}}\uc2  over the next decade.\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights on the ballot?\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s shifting stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised concerns among his most ardent, religious supporters. Though he has taken credit on multiple occasions for overturning Roe v Wade, Trump recognises how fraught and potentially politically damaging the issue is for him, as 63% of Americans say \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/14/abortion-rights-support-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should be legal in all or most cases}}}\uc2 . Trump has confirmed that he would not sign a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, to avoid alienating more moderate voters but has simultaneously angered his evangelical base. The former president has also publicly criticised Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban as too harsh and said that his policies would be great for the \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  of women \u8211\'20\'13 though he has not given any examples of such policies.\par \par \uc2 Democrats have long viewed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a winning platform for them, and Harris has been much clearer and stronger on the issue than Biden. She has urged Congress to codify the rights enshrined in Roe v Wade, called for an end to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/24/election-harris-filibuster-abortion-roe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Senate filibuster}}}\uc2  and has rejected all efforts to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 The clock is ticking, as both candidates continue to try and eke out the final votes that could take them to the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 For the latest\par \par \uc2 on the race, sign up to the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s weekly US election newsletter, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/series/the-stakes-us-election-edition"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  The Stakes}}}\par \par \uc2 What else we\u8217\'20\'19ve been reading\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/music/2024/oct/13/ezra-collective-dance-no-ones-watching-mercury-prize-youth-clubs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Miranda Sawyer\u8217\'20\'19s interview}}}\uc2  with Ezra Collective is a tribute to the jazz agitators who are rising the ranks of UK music while also fostering the next generation of talent. Hannah J Davies, deputy editor, newsletters\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Are you in a vampiric friendship? Not in the gothic-mythical way, in the energy-sucking way. In this piece {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2024/oct/13/our-conversations-were-always-about-her-how-to-recognise-and-escape-an-emotional-vampire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Elle Hunt }}}\uc2  helps us spot the signs of such a friend and lays out ways to navigate the emotional minefield of this kind of relationship. Nimo\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was told once I was not cut out to be an oceanographer\u8221\'20\'1D: dive into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2024/oct/12/oceanographer-dawn-wright-when-we-reached-the-bottom-we-saw-a-beer-bottle"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 this Q&A}}}\uc2  with Dawn Wright, AKA \u8220\'20\'1CDeepsea Dawn\u8221\'20\'1D, the first Black person to venture to the deepest spot on the planet. Hannah\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 42 years ago, Nick Yarris was arrested for a murder he did not commit and spent more than two decades in prison. His story is now being retold on the stage with Oscar-winning actor Adrian Brody taking the lead role. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2024/oct/13/nick-yarris-adrien-brody-the-fear-of-13-donmar-death-row"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Lewis spoke }}}\uc2  with both men. Nimo\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 ICYMI, I really liked Lucy Webster\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2024/oct/11/lyric-belfast-richard-iii-michael-patrick-oisin-kearney"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fascinating piece}}}\uc2  on a new adaptation of Shakespeare\u8217\'20\'19s Richard III, in which the title character and lead actor (Michael Patrick) have motor neurone disease. Hannah\par \par \uc2 Sport\par \par \uc2 Football\par \par \uc2 | England bounced back from disappointment against Greece {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2024/oct/13/finland-england-nations-league-match-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 with a 3-1 victory over Finland}}}\uc2  in Helsinki, thanks to goals from Jack Grealish (pictured above), Trent Alexander-Arnold and Declan Rice.\par \par \uc2 Cricket\par \par \uc2 | England {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2024/oct/13/womens-t20-cricket-world-cup-england-thrash-scotland-top-group-b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 romped home as winners by 10 wickets}}}\uc2  in their T20 World Cup match against Scotland. The wide margin of victory means England now top Group B and have overtaken the net run rates of South Africa and West Indies, putting them in prime position to reach the semi-finals.\par \par \uc2 Tennis\par \par \uc2 | Jannik Sinner secured his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2024/oct/13/jannik-sinner-tennis-novak-djokovic-seventh-title-year-shanghai-masters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seventh title of a remarkable year}}}\uc2  with victory over Novak Djokovic in the final of the Shanghai Masters. Sinner, who is already guaranteed to finish the season as world No 1, was too strong for Djokovic, making it four wins from his last five matches against the Serbian with a 7-6(4), 6-3 triumph. That denied Djokovic a 100th career title, although this week has been another reminder that the 37-year-old remains a factor at the top of the game.\par \par \uc2 The front pages\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  leads with \u8220\'20\'1CSafety fears as Starmer pledges to slash red tape for investors\u8221\'20\'1D. The Telegraph says \u8220\'20\'1CPM\u8217\'20\'19s tax on jobs \u8216\'20\'18will scare away business\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D. The Times reports \u8220\'20\'1CBig money says time is right to buy into Britain\u8221\'20\'1D. i has \u8220\'20\'1CUniversity bosses claim \u163\'00\'A31m expenses amid cash crisis warning\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The Financial Times leads on \u8220\'20\'1CChina\u8217\'20\'19s deflationary pressures mount as investors hope for more stimulus\u8221\'20\'1D. The Mail splashes with \u8220\'20\'1CWho asked the Attorney General to help Taylor Swift get a VIP escort?\u8221\'20\'1D. The Mirror has \u8220\'20\'1CNot a G\u8217\'20\'19Day for Charles\u8221\'20\'1D, on the upcoming royal visit to Australia.\par \par \uc2 Today in Focus\par \par \uc2 How \uc2 Giorgia Meloni\uc2  became Europe\u8217\'20\'19s favourite far-right leader\par \par \uc2 She\u8217\'20\'19s the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2024/oct/14/how-giorgia-meloni-became-europes-favourite-far-right-leader-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 far-right prime minister with whom leaders across Europe seem to love being photographed}}}\uc2 . What\u8217\'20\'19s her appeal and what does she really want?\par \par \uc2 Cartoon of the day | Edith Pritchett\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ablink.email.theguardian.com/ss/c/TBl-lE0k4WbTlFRn6v-lQXxTpTslqnvUsR2ofAkC00vqkHXqakTSxrykj9mrdACFM7X02zB_4eaUcPGwGF8aSdwRgVGO90P9jWCTAme32U5T-vnI6XmWDMj3FJwYRpoHkFNbLC7gF6lJtLXkZEafGPr91zCNJfd75y4srJK7hF9rC7DtMprXX9waLOo6IasUuyiX2WyLj6_QAr2Er-sZ3pUo1lqR8H7xRgc_wdPt5vw6OZTdkayzug3kU3s7Kcsk-XG5uIH5ajjQ81Ur4lb9OdVIWg1quQfk4HV_8czlpcY/3om/atajwSjOR9WSWjozGj9ciw/h43/pcnM5h3gNALOSgMA7uWqlQhxgBX88j6XLDvP4QIlMes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up for Inside Saturday}}}\uc2  to see more of Edith Pritchett\u8217\'20\'19s cartoons, the best Saturday magazine content and an exclusive look behind the scenes\par \par \uc2 The Upside\par \par \uc2 A bit of good news to remind you that the world\u8217\'20\'19s not all bad\par \par \uc2 Hew Locke describes his new \uc2 British Museum\uc2  exhibition as \u8220\'20\'1Ca messing around with colonial history\u8221\'20\'1D, which sees the artist mix objects from the museum\u8217\'20\'19s collection \u8211\'20\'13 many of which are not usually on view \u8211\'20\'13 with his own original works to create something that confronts problematic narratives from the past. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2024/oct/13/hew-locke-what-have-we-here-british-museum-procession-tate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Writes Tim Adams}}}\uc2  of the exhibition, which opens on Thursday, \u8220\'20\'1Cone ambition of Locke\u8217\'20\'19s is to bring some of that colour back into the museum \u8211\'20\'13 not least the range of skin tones that classical statuary once embodied\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Says Locke: \u8220\'20\'1CWe live in a different world to the pre-pandemic world. Pre-pandemic, everybody tried to talk a good game about decolonising the museum and stuff like that. Since the pandemic and \uc2 Black Lives Matter\uc2 , people think: \u8216\'20\'18Well, hang on, we have to put our money where our mouth is.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2018/feb/12/the-upside-sign-up-for-our-weekly-email"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sign up here}}}\uc2  for a weekly roundup of The Upside, sent to you every Sunday\par \par \uc2 Bored at work?\par \par \uc2 And finally, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s puzzles are here to keep you entertained throughout the day. Until tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/quick/16986"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Quick crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/crosswords/cryptic/29513"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptic crossword}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wordiply.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Wordiply}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241014ekae000rt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
