\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Trump wants the \uc2 FCC\uc2  to take \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s license away. This is a dark omen\b0\par\par\uc2 Dennis Aftergut and Austin Sarat \par \uc2 935 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 October 2024\par 21:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 His comments foreshadow a full-on assault on free speech and freedom of the press if he becomes president\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 10 October {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/2024/10/10/trump-harris-cbs-license-60-minutes/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack on CBS}}}\uc2  for editing its 60 Minutes interview with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a normal television process \u8211\'20\'13 is pure distraction. It is designed to draw our attention away from the fact that he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.rollingstone.com/politics/politics-news/trump-harris-cbs-lose-broadcast-license-1235132132/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 afraid}}}\uc2  to give the news magazine its traditional interview with both political candidates. Trump\u8217\'20\'19s statement that the \uc2 Federal Communications Commission\uc2  should \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/elections/2024/10/10/trump-harris-cbs-license-60-minutes/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 take away}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s broadcast license {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2024/10/trump-cbs-60-minutes-fcc-1236112339/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 betrays his ignorance }}}\uc2  of the fact that the \uc2 FCC\uc2  does not license networks and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aclu.org/news/civil-liberties/how-trumps-proposed-radical-expansion-of-executive-power-will-impact-our-freedoms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 foreshadows a full-on assault}}}\uc2  on free speech and freedom of the press if he becomes president.\par \par \uc2 History is clear that dictators move early to take {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nuitalian.org/2023/04/27/fascism-rise-to-power-and-media-manipulation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  control}}}\uc2  of the media in order to censor information unfavorable to their people. Our safety requires preventing that control, as \uc2 Thomas Jefferson\uc2  wrote two centuries ago: \u8220\'20\'1CThe {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://jeffersonhour.com/blog/1323"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 only security of all is in a free press}}}\uc2 . The force of public opinion cannot be resisted when permitted freely to be expressed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Only Rumpelstiltskin would fail to grasp how much Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2017/01/24/politics/trump-legitimacy-voter-fraud-inauguration-crowd/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cannot tolerate }}}\uc2  criticism from the press or anyone. Attacking mainstream media is his way of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thebulwark.com/p/biology-explains-why-people-normalize"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 desensitizing us}}}\uc2  to the important role of the press in a free society.\par \par \uc2 If you want a preview of how first amendment rights will disappear if Trump is elected president, look to his home state of Florida where Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , his Maga copycat, runs that government in a way Trump would like to bring to the whole nation. On 9 October, we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2024/10/09/florida-abortion-tv-ad-caroline/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saw one of the governor\u8217\'20\'19s lackeys }}}\uc2  try to carve away freedom of speech and the press, along with \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 John Wilson, the general counsel to the state\u8217\'20\'19s department of health, threatened the state\u8217\'20\'19s broadcast stations with prosecution unless they removed a campaign ad promoting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Florida_Amendment_4,_Right_to_Abortion_Initiative_(2024)"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 amendment 4.}}}\uc2  It\u8217\'20\'19s the ballot measure to add \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights to the state\u8217\'20\'19s constitution.\par \par \uc2 The amendment 4 ad featured Floridian Caroline Williams {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2024/10/09/florida-abortion-tv-ad-caroline/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 saying }}}\uc2  that she would be dead had the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  been in effect when her health required one in 2022. The irony of the Florida government trying to quash the ad is rich. Here we have a bare-knuckles attempt at censorship from the party that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usnews.com/opinion/articles/2024-07-24/even-while-railing-against-it-the-republican-party-has-become-a-champion-of-cancel-culture"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  purports to oppose}}}\uc2  the \u8220\'20\'1Ccancel culture\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s not the end of the irony. The health department\u8217\'20\'19s letter alleged that the pro-amendment 4 ad violated the state\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.flsenate.gov/Laws/Statutes/2012/Chapter386/All#:~:text=%E2%80%94A%20sanitary%20nuisance%20is%20the,individual%2C%20or%20the%20health%20or"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sanitation nuisance}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D statute. This ground for government censorship, based as it is on a statute designed to prohibit {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://brevard.floridahealth.gov/programs-and-services/environmental-health/sanitary-nuisances/index.html#:~:text=Environmental%20Health%20Services&text=Sanitary%20nuisances%20are%20defined%20in,at%20321%2D631%2D2500."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overflowing septic tanks}}}\uc2  or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://orange.floridahealth.gov/programs-and-services/environmental-health/sanitary-nuisances/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unclean slaughterhouses}}}\uc2 , fails the laugh test, much less the constitution.\par \par \uc2 Still, don\u8217\'20\'19t miss what\u8217\'20\'19s going on here: people\u8217\'20\'19s rights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://protectdemocracy.org/work/the-authoritarian-playbook/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 are not removed in one fell swoop but rather in steps}}}\uc2 . The first stage is eroding people\u8217\'20\'19s expectations that freedoms are sacred and will be respected. By getting us thinking we can live with this or that little invasion of someone else\u8217\'20\'19s rights, autocrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/the-big-idea/2017/1/9/14207302/authoritarian-states-boring-tolerable-fascism-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 normalize those intrusions }}}\uc2  and then expand them to cover all of us. Diminishing the media\u8217\'20\'19s and the public\u8217\'20\'19s rights to criticize a leader is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/article/world/suppressing-free-press-is-how-dictators-get-started-us-senator-mccain-idUSKBN15Y07X/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  how dictatorships get started}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s why American law \u8211\'20\'13 at least in its current state \u8211\'20\'13 forbids what Wilson was threatening. Campaign ads are core political speech, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sgp.fas.org/crs/misc/IF11072.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 entitled to the highest level of first amendment protection}}}\uc2 . That means that content-based restrictions on such speech {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/567/709/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 must promote}}}\uc2  a compelling government interest and be the least intrusive way to promote that interest. Specifically, even false statements in the context of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law campaigning \u8211\'20\'13 and Williams\u8217\'20\'19 statements in the ad were not false \u8211\'20\'13 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fjc.gov/sites/default/files/materials/28/EE-OHS-1-10-cv-720-Susan-B-Anthony-List.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 must survive}}}\uc2  such strict scrutiny.\par \par \uc2 A Florida crocodile\u8217\'20\'19s tears would be more compelling than Wilson\u8217\'20\'19s description of Florida\u8217\'20\'19s interest in protecting women from the ad\u8217\'20\'19s purported \u8220\'20\'1Cdanger\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 that it suggests that they need to go to other states or find unlicensed abortionists if they do not have access to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Florida. That danger arises from the statute, not the ad.\par \par \uc2 If the department of public health is so concerned about women\u8217\'20\'19s safety, why not issue a regulation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/06/06/nx-s1-4995739/abortion-exceptions-life-mother-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 clarifying}}}\uc2  that doctors will not be prosecuted if, in their professional judgment, they believe that a woman has \u8220\'20\'1Cpregnancy complications posing a serious risk of death or substantial and irreversible physical impairment\u8221\'20\'1D?\par \par \uc2 Without that assurance, a doctor\u8217\'20\'19s decision to perform an emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/06/06/nx-s1-4995739/abortion-exceptions-life-mother-florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 so chilled}}}\uc2  that, in effect, there is no exception to Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban. Interviews with Florida doctors establish their understandable unwillingness to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://phr.org/our-work/resources/delayed-and-denied-floridas-six-week-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  risk their liberty}}}\uc2  given the prospect of a district attorney second-guessing their judgment.\par \par \uc2 But whatever the ban\u8217\'20\'19s impact on the practice of medicine, Wilson and DeSantis\u8217\'20\'19s effort to stop groups from promoting their point of view puts all of us in jeopardy.\par \par \uc2 George Washington captured that danger at the beginning of the republic. As he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://founders.archives.gov/documents/Washington/99-01-02-10840"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 put it}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CThe freedom of Speech may be taken away \u8211\'20\'13 and, dumb & silent we may be led, like sheep, to the Slaughter.\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , 250 years later, are sending us a clear message that our lives and our freedoms are on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Dennis Aftergut is a former federal prosecutor, currently of counsel to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://url.emailprotection.link/?bgEVJlnYyhL7SzOl_oqrbjPy6zTm0QFEo7--IYnhh5Vw9NmnSep9Ngtva8TYmIP3YnC5PvxaEO2FRFa_4f7XMFg~~"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lawyers Defending American Democracy}}}\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Austin Sarat, associate dean of the faculty and William Nelson Cromwell professor of jurisprudence and political science at \uc2 Amherst College\uc2 , is the author of Gruesome Spectacles: Botched Executions and America\u8217\'20\'19s Death Penalty\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241012ekac0025t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
