\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Gen Z and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 : is the meet-cute enough to bring her to the White House?\b0\par\par\uc2 Lauren Gambino \par \uc2 4,119 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 October 2024\par 12:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 They call themselves \u8216\'20\'18the coconut army\u8217\'20\'19 and are out in droves to reach young people aged 18-29. Can they turn activism into votes?\par \par \uc2 It was the height of \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/07/22/kamala-harris-campaign-coconut-memes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brat summer}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vanityfair.com/style/story/kamala-harris-chappell-roan-femininomenon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 femininomenon}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D, electrifying a high-stakes presidential race that many of the country\u8217\'20\'19s youngest voters had been dreading: a rematch between the two oldest candidates in American history.\par \par \uc2 Chartreuse-blocked memes and coconut emojis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/25/kamala-harris-tiktok-memes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filled}}}\uc2  social media feeds. The tidal wave of young \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/27/kamala-harris-young-voters-israel-gaza-jayapal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamalove}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D sparked a rush of small-dollar donations and volunteer sign-ups for her days-old campaign. For an extremely online generation of young Democrats, the vibes were so good.\par \par \uc2 On the ground in St Louis, a cadre of young progressives were gathering for an entirely different election \u8211\'20\'13 one with virtually no bearing on the balance of power in Washington, but one they believed mattered deeply. There in Missouri\u8217\'20\'19s first congressional district, representative \uc2 Cori Bush\uc2  was fighting for her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/03/cori-bush-wesley-bell-missouri-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 political survival}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Many of the twentysomethings had traveled from out of state, sacrificing summer jobs and sleeping on yoga mats to campaign for Bush in the sticky August heat. \u8220\'20\'1CWe just stopped our lives and went to St Louis,\u8221\'20\'1D said John Paul Mejia, a 22-year-old student and climate activist.\par \par \uc2 Mejia was there as part of Protect Our Power (Pop), a youth coalition that came together earlier this year for what he described as a \u8220\'20\'1CDavid-and-Goliath\u8221\'20\'1D mission to defend leftwing members of Congress against a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/20/pro-israel-groups-gaza-us-elections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 well-funded effort}}}\uc2  to unseat them.\par \par \uc2 To them, Bush, the nurse turned racial justice activist, was one of the few elected leaders who shared their sense of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/oct/29/cori-bush-interview-midterms-abortion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urgency}}}\uc2  about everything from the country\u8217\'20\'19s affordability crisis to safeguarding \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 As a newly elected member of Congress, Bush had slept on the steps of the US Capitol to protest against the expiration of a federal eviction moratorium. The action paid off: the Biden administration extended the pause. In warning about the threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bush {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/cspan/status/1443592081218277381?lang=en"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 testified}}}\uc2  before a House panel that she had had an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 18 after becoming pregnant by rape. In 2023, she emerged as one of the strongest critics of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza, a stance that reflected a groundswell of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/10/05/gen-z-israel-pro-palestinian-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 youth dissent}}}\uc2  but ultimately imperiled her congressional career.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s pretty much nobody else, even members of Congress who are closer to our age, in some instances, who actually represent what our generation cares about,\u8221\'20\'1D Vincent Vertuccio, a 21-year-old college student and an activist with Pop, said of the progressive Squad members. \u8220\'20\'1CIf we lose these people, even one or two, it\u8217\'20\'19s a direct diminishment of our power.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 On the morning of the election, as the group made a final push to get out the vote, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/kamala-harris-running-mate-tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 news broke}}}\uc2  that Harris, to their delight, had chosen the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/11/tim-walz-evolution"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 progressive midwestern governor}}}\uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  as her running mate. From the trenches of a hard-fought campaign, they spared a moment to celebrate what felt like a win.\par \par \uc2 That night, Bush {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/07/cori-bush-pro-israel-lobby-warning"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost}}}\uc2  her re-election bid in a primary contest decided by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/08/06/us/elections/results-missouri-us-house-1-primary.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fewer}}}\uc2  than 7,000 votes.\par \par \uc2 The defeat stung. Pop had run a scrappy campaign: its volunteers collectively placed 120,000 phone calls and knocked on more than 20,000 doors. But they were up against a torrent of outside spending, primarily by pro-Israel groups, that transformed the race into one of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/AdImpact_Pol/status/1816200736054624582"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most}}}\uc2  expensive House primaries in US history.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are feeling the issues really hard, but I don\u8217\'20\'19t think that they\u8217\'20\'19re feeling people fighting for them equally as hard,\u8221\'20\'1D Mejia reflected afterward. \u8220\'20\'1CThat worries me, especially at a time when we\u8217\'20\'19re also facing a crisis of democracy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Gen Z poised to play decisive role?\par \par \uc2 In interviews with dozens of activists, organizers and candidates working to build youth political power on the left, a portrait emerged of a generation fed up with the status quo in Washington but eager to flex its electoral might this cycle. Many are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/24/kamala-harris-gen-z-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 genuinely enthusiastic}}}\uc2  about the prospect of a Harris presidency. Others hope she will be a bulwark against Republican extremism, if not the transformational figure they crave.\par \par \uc2 With the presidential candidates offering sharply contrasting visions for the economy, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , climate change, foreign policy and democracy itself, there is an understanding among young liberals that the outcome could have profound, generational implications for the country \u8211\'20\'13 and the planet.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going to be the margin of victory,\u8221\'20\'1D said Marianna Pecora, the 20-year-old communications director of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://votersoftomorrow.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  Voters of Tomorrow}}}\uc2 , a gen Z-led group working to mobilize first-time voters and students. As the race moves into its final stretch, her closing pitch is direct: \u8220\'20\'1CDon\u8217\'20\'19t let this election happen to you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Approximately 41 million members of gen Z will be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://circle.tufts.edu/latest-research/41-million-members-gen-z-will-be-eligible-vote-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eligible to vote}}}\uc2  in November, including millions who were too young to vote in the 2020 election. Their participation could be decisive: the presidential contest is deadlocked, probably hinging on tens of thousands of votes in a handful of swing states, and the battle for control of Congress is as close as ever.\par \par \uc2 Yet no generation is a political monolith, and gen Z \u8211\'20\'13 the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/social-trends/2019/01/17/generation-z-looks-a-lot-like-millennials-on-key-social-and-political-issues/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 left-leaning}}}\uc2 , racially diverse cohort born between the late 1990s and early 2010s \u8211\'20\'13 is no exception. Millions of young adults identify as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/09/28/gen-z-men-conservative-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conservative}}}\uc2 , and a widening youth gender gap has emerged as a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americansurveycenter.org/research/the-politics-of-progress-and-privilege-how-americas-gender-gap-is-reshaping-the-2024-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 central}}}\uc2  political fault line.\par \par \uc2 Still, experts say this generation face an unprecedented set of challenges \u8211\'20\'13 from the economic to the existential \u8211\'20\'13 that have eroded their faith in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iop.harvard.edu/youth-poll/47th-edition-spring-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American institutions}}}\uc2  and fueled a deepening {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.berkeley.edu/2024/06/26/young-voters-have-growing-power-but-broken-politics-leave-them-fatalistic-studies-find/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sense of \u8220\'20\'1Cfatalism\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  about their own futures and the fate of the country. \u8220\'20\'1CWe weren\u8217\'20\'19t part of the structures and the systems that created this massive situation but now it\u8217\'20\'19s really on us to fix it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Vertuccio, who has a tattoo that reads, \u8220\'20\'1Corganizing works\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Gen Z has lived through tumultuous times, from the worst recession since the Great Depression, which saw millions of American families lose their homes, jobs and savings with almost no consequence for those who caused it, to a pandemic that closed their schools and their polarized communities.\par \par \uc2 They\u8217\'20\'19ve experienced political whiplash when the country that twice elected \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  chose Trump as his successor. In 2020, they turned out in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://circle.tufts.edu/latest-research/half-youth-voted-2020-11-point-increase-2016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 force}}}\uc2  to defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , only to witness the 45th president refuse to concede and his far-right allies attempt to overturn \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory by force.\par \par \uc2 A growing body of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.thelancet.com/commissions/youth-mental-health"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 research suggests}}}\uc2  that rising economic inequality, climate change and technological advancements are taking a toll on young people\u8217\'20\'19s mental health, leading to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.waltonfamilyfoundation.org/stories/foundation/generation-z-is-waging-a-battle-against-depression-addiction-and-hopelessness"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 high levels of anxiety}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hhs.gov/sites/default/files/surgeon-general-social-connection-advisory.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 loneliness}}}\uc2 . A recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/25085416-nbc-news-stay-tuned-gen-z-poll-topline-results-9424"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  NBC News poll }}}\uc2  of gen Z adults found that nearly half expect life for their generation to be \u8220\'20\'1Cworse than previous generations\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s a feeling of vulnerability and isolation \u8211\'20\'13 that there\u8217\'20\'19s no one really representing their interests, particularly politically,\u8221\'20\'1D said Daniel Cox, director of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americansurveycenter.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Survey Center on American Life at the American Enterprise Institute}}}\uc2  (AEI). \u8220\'20\'1CWhere you have a lot of young women becoming more active in politics because of that, particularly progressive women, a lot of men are just withdrawing completely, whether it\u8217\'20\'19s dating, politics or work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Surveys indicate that both young men and young women favor Harris over Trump. But the youth gender gap is striking. In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iop.harvard.edu/youth-poll/48th-edition-fall-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 youth poll}}}\uc2  released by Harvard Kennedy School\u8217\'20\'19s Institute of Politics, Harris led Trump by 47 percentage points among young women, compared with 17 percentage points among young men.\par \par \uc2 The gulf-wide \u8211\'20\'13 and growing \u8211\'20\'13 divide reflects a dynamic that is shaping the 2024 election and could have lasting implications for both political parties: young women have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/649826/exploring-young-women-leftward-expansion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 become more liberal}}}\uc2 , as young men {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/05/young-men-voters-us-election-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drift away}}}\uc2  from the Democratic party.\par \par \uc2 There is virtually no doubt that Harris will win more young voters than Trump in November, but the margin will matter greatly.\par \par \uc2 For decades, Democrats have dominated the youth vote, with voters aged 18 to 29 favoring Biden by 24 percentage points in 2020, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://circle.tufts.edu/2020-election-center"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tufts University\u8217\'20\'19s Center for Information and Research on Civic Learning and Engagement (Circle)}}}\uc2 . While young people have historically voted at lower rates than older adults, that trend may be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://circle.tufts.edu/research-areas/broadening-youth-voting"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 starting to change.}}}\par \par \uc2 Youth voter turnout rose to 50% in 2020, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://circle.tufts.edu/latest-research/half-youth-voted-2020-11-point-increase-2016"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 probably a modern record}}}\uc2  and a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://circle.tufts.edu/2020-election-center"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 remarkable 11-point increase}}}\uc2  from the 2016 presidential election, according to a Circle analysis. Young voters of color, it found, played a particularly \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://circle.tufts.edu/2020-election-center"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 instrumental}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D role in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s victories in closely contested battlegrounds such as Georgia, Pennsylvania and Arizona.\par \par \uc2 Two years later, young people again voted {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://circle.tufts.edu/2022-election-center"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at high levels}}}\uc2  during the congressional midterms. Their fury over the supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s decision to overturn Roe v Wade {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2022/11/12/us/young-voter-turnout-election-democrats.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was credited}}}\uc2  with helping Democrats defy historical expectations.\par \par \uc2 Young voters are once again poised to play a potentially decisive role this election, said Melissa Deckman, CEO of Public Religion Research Institute (PRRI) and author of the forthcoming book {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cup.columbia.edu/book/the-politics-of-gen-z/9780231560085"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Politics of Gen Z: How the Youngest Voters Will Shape Our Democracy}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen there\u8217\'20\'19s an issue that gen Z is passionate about,\u8221\'20\'1D she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthey\u8217\'20\'19re willing to engage, despite \u8211\'20\'13 or maybe because of \u8211\'20\'13 the fact that institutions aren\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily addressing their concerns.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 From youth activism to youth votes\par \par \uc2 For a segment of gen Z, youth activism has practically become a rite of passage.\par \par \uc2 Rather than despair, many young people mobilized in response to the election of Trump, to school shootings that killed classmates, to the climate crisis, which they believe too many of their leaders still ignore, episodes of police brutality captured on video, the rising tide of post-pandemic book bans and anti-LGBTQ+ laws, a bloody Middle East war playing out in real time on their phones, and the loss of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections that has left young women with fewer rights than their grandmothers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPerhaps the most important, consistent finding over 25 years of analyzing young voters \u8211\'20\'13 the most significant predictor of youth participation \u8211\'20\'13 is that young people participate when they can see a tangible difference in the process,\u8221\'20\'1D said John Della Volpe, director of polling at Harvard\u8217\'20\'19s Institute of Politics and the author of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.harvard.com/book/9781250875518"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fight: How Gen Z Is Channeling Their Fear and Passion to Save America}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This generation of activists, the first born after the release of the smartphone, blends traditional methods of activism \u8211\'20\'13 like old-school marches and campus protests \u8211\'20\'13 with modern digital strategies such as TikTok {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2020/06/21/style/tiktok-trump-rally-tulsa.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trolls}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bbc.com/future/article/20220928-the-surprising-power-of-internet-memes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 internet memes}}}\uc2 . But even more, what makes their activism unique, researchers say, is the way they have translated youth protest into youth voter participation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen the oldest members of gen Z turned voting age, they carried those values forward and voted at rates that previous generations have not even touched,\u8221\'20\'1D Della Volpe said.\par \par \uc2 Despite their low confidence in American institutions, Della Volpe said gen Z, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iop.harvard.edu/youth-poll/47th-edition-spring-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 young men}}}\uc2 , tend to be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/social-trends/2020/05/14/on-the-cusp-of-adulthood-and-facing-an-uncertain-future-what-we-know-about-gen-z-so-far/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pro-government}}}\uc2 . As a cohort, they are more likely than older Americans to say that the federal government should \u8211\'20\'13 and must \u8211\'20\'13 do more to address the country\u8217\'20\'19s problems.\par \par \uc2 Some young people, like Ben Braver, a 22-year-old public school teacher near Tampa, Florida, aren\u8217\'20\'19t waiting for their elected elders to act.\par \par \uc2 Braver, who shares earnest {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tiktok.com/@benbraverfl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 explainer videos}}}\uc2  on TikTok making the case for progressive policies, is running for a seat in the Florida state senate. He decided to challenge his Republican opponent, the incumbent state senator, after he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2022/03/03/florida-abortion-ban-desantis-00014102"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted}}}\uc2  for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/02/florida-abortion-ban-six-weeks#:~:text=On%20Monday%2C%20the%20Florida%20state,takes%20effect%20on%201%20May."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  ban}}}\uc2  that took effect earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to wait until 2040, when we\u8217\'20\'19re already the majority. We have to start now,\u8221\'20\'1D Braver said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need people writing policy that they\u8217\'20\'19ll have to live under.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Building power in a right-leaning structure\par \par \uc2 Santiago Mayer emigrated from Mexico to the US as a teenager in 2017, arriving in the heady months after Trump took office.\par \par \uc2 At his new high school in southern California, he was shocked to learn that many of his classmates were mostly tuned out. Trump, who ran for president on a fiercely anti-immigrant platform, had just implemented a travel ban targeting predominantly Muslim countries and was pushing Republicans to repeal the Affordable Care Act.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf young people had voted in 2016, we might have been able to avoid the Trump administration,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayer, now 22, observed.\par \par \uc2 At the time, the teen turned to \u8220\'20\'1Cpre-Elon\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Twitter\uc2 . His unfiltered anti-Trump musings gathered a following and in 2019, his handle, Voters of Tomorrow, graduated from a \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account to an official political engagement organization \u8220\'20\'1Cfor gen Z, by gen Z\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 just in time to help drive Trump from office. \u8220\'20\'1CThey pissed off the wrong generation,\u8221\'20\'1D emerged as a rallying cry.\par \par \uc2 Mayer\u8217\'20\'19s team became enthusiastic boosters of the Biden administration. They worked to translate the president\u8217\'20\'19s sprawling, sometimes wonky, achievements on climate, gun control and student loan debt for a generation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/journalism/fact-sheet/news-platform-fact-sheet/?tabItem=8b137657-9961-4130-a811-20f854ea2321"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increasingly turns to social media}}}\uc2  for its news.\par \par \uc2 But over the course of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s term, many young people grew disenchanted with the 81-year-old president, harboring reservations about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/17/us-uncommitted-voters-biden-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his foreign policy}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/03/05/us/elections/times-siena-poll-registered-voter-crosstabs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 age}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYoung people want to vote for someone who\u8217\'20\'19s going to shake the system,\u8221\'20\'1D Link Lauren, a young, right-leaning TikTok influencer who worked on Robert F Kennedy\u8217\'20\'19s independent presidential campaign, said in an interview this summer. \u8220\'20\'1CThey want disruption.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Early polls showed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/2024-elections/24125496/young-voters-trump-biden-polling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump performing far better}}}\uc2  with this voting bloc than he had in 2020 and, in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://maristpoll.marist.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/NPR_PBS-NewsHour_Marist-Poll_USA-NOS-and-Tables_202403291554.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some}}}\uc2  cases, drawing even with \u8211\'20\'13 or doing better than \u8211\'20\'13 Biden. The numbers sent shockwaves through the Democratic party. Was gen Z turning Maga?\par \par \uc2 Analysts and organizers, Mayer included, were skeptical. Gen Z, after all, was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gssdataexplorer.norc.org/trends?category=Politics&measure=polviews_r&Measure%20Category=Liberal&Breakdown%20Label=Age%C2%B0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more socially liberal}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aei.org/research-products/report/generation-z-and-the-transformation-of-american-adolescence-how-gen-zs-formative-experiences-shape-its-politics-priorities-and-future/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less religious}}}\uc2 , more educated and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.prri.org/research/generation-zs-views-on-generational-change-and-the-challenges-and-opportunities-ahead-a-political-and-cultural-glimpse-into-americas-future/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more likely to identify as LGBTQ+}}}\uc2  than previous generations. Rather, they saw the numbers as a pulse check: young people were frustrated by the state of the post-pandemic economy, by the slow pace of change in Washington and, yes, by the prospect of a contest between the same (very) old candidates who had dominated much of gen Z\u8217\'20\'19s political memory.\par \par \uc2 Mayer identified a deeper tension: a left-leaning generation was trying to build power within a political system that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2023/09/19/how-americans-view-proposals-to-change-the-political-system/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seemed to structurally}}}\uc2  bend rightward.\par \par \uc2 With Biden as president, there had been an expectation that he would guard against Republican threats to the environment, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, voting rights and gun control. But then the most conservative supreme court in history stepped in and eroded those protections while raising the possibility that other rights could be next.\par \par \uc2 Gerrymandering has made the US House {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2022/feb/12/us-redistricting-house-seats-safe-competitive-districts?utm_source=pocket_mylist"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less competitive}}}\uc2 , harder to govern and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/collection-post/4527291/2016-election-gerrymandering/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more polarized}}}\uc2  while an arcane Senate rule known as the filibuster stands in the way of most major legislation. Beyond Washington, the country is increasingly cracked into red states and blue states with dramatically different laws governing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, LGBTQ+ protections and union membership.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen you see kids gunned down in schools, then the supreme court says domestic abusers can have guns and your \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights are gone, it creates a sense of hopelessness,\u8221\'20\'1D Mayer said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt feels like the government is working against you.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 The coconut army\par \par \uc2 The mood among young Democrats changed entirely on 21 July, when the octogenarian president exited the race and threw his support behind Harris, who, at 59, seemed positively youthful by comparison.\par \par \uc2 Marion Smart, a 21-year-old student organizer with Voters of Tomorrow\u8217\'20\'19s Georgia chapter, was preparing to welcome hundreds of liberal students and activists to the group\u8217\'20\'19s Year of Youth summit in Atlanta when it happened.\par \par \uc2 Summit-goers descended on Atlanta\u8217\'20\'19s Loudermilk center days later, chugging boxes of coconut water as they dashed between a panel on running for office as a member of gen Z and a training led by a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/OrganizerMemes?ref_src=twsrc%5Egoogle%7Ctwcamp%5Eserp%7Ctwgr%5Eauthor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 panda head-wearing digital organizer}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s nascent campaign sent an envoy, Eve Levenson, the national youth engagement director, and the vice-president herself took time in the whirlwind of her elevation to record a pre-taped message, in which she vowed to work for their vote.\par \par \uc2 In response, they pledged to turn out the youth vote. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re all part of the coconut army and we\u8217\'20\'19re gonna take this election by storm,\u8221\'20\'1D Smart said.\par \par \uc2 Ashleigh Ewald, the group\u8217\'20\'19s Georgia state director, felt the political ground shift immediately. She had toiled for months on college campuses around the state, trying to convince her discontented peers to get involved in the November election. Now they were seeking her out, asking how they could help.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBecause of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , that pessimism turned into enthusiasm,\u8221\'20\'1D the 22-year-old said.\par \par \uc2 Gen z voters have flocked to the vice-president, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/MeetThePress/status/1837839352509898849?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1837839352509898849%7Ctwgr%5Ede471272944ae3812e73a6341659b6603af01098%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thedailybeast.com%2Fkamala-harris-has-biggest-favorability-jump-since-george-w-bush-after-911"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 helping to drive up her popularity}}}\uc2 .But Harris\u8217\'20\'19s ground-breaking candidacy \u8211\'20\'13 she would be the first woman to serve as president of the United States \u8211\'20\'13 has particularly energized young women. After she entered the race, youth voter registration among young women rose sharply \u8211\'20\'13 a trend one Democratic data analyst dubbed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/tbonier/status/1828457890228629534"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the \u8220\'20\'1CHarris effect.\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\par \par \uc2 Nearly six in 10 women under age 30 view her potential presidency as a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americansurveycenter.org/research/the-politics-of-progress-and-privilege-how-americas-gender-gap-is-reshaping-the-2024-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 very important}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D milestone in American political history, according to a national survey by AEI\u8217\'20\'19s Survey Center on American Life. The sentiment is notably more pronounced for younger women than it is for older women and significantly more than for younger men.\par \par \uc2 Leaving a \u8220\'20\'1Ccontingency planning\u8221\'20\'1D workshop for a potential Trump victory, Amini Bonane said the session had been a sobering reminder of the stakes this election. It was part of the reason Bonane, a 29-year-old community organizer who came to the US as a refugee from the Democratic Republic of Congo, decided to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aminiforfairfax.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 run for a seat on the city council}}}\uc2  in her home town of Fairfax, Virginia. With Harris as the nominee, she has felt a surge of energy in her own race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m just so excited and \u8211\'20\'13 hello! \u8211\'20\'13 I\u8217\'20\'19ll be on the same ballot as,\u8221\'20\'1D she paused, shaking her hands in excitement, \u8220\'20\'1Cpossibly the first Black woman Potus. That is just so motivating for me.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 Courting gen Z\par \par \uc2 The online hype that followed Harris\u8217\'20\'19s sudden emergence was not only good for the vibes. It helped reset the entire political narrative around her, propelling the once-unpopular vice president into what her campaign playfully coined its \u8220\'20\'1CKamala era\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Conservative media outlets had long amplified Harris\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/25/kamala-harris-speaking-style-memes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quirky}}}\uc2  turns of phrase \u8211\'20\'13derided as \u8220\'20\'1Cword salads\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/news/asian-america/kamala-harris-laugh-criticism-trump-women-color-emotions-rcna164069"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laugh}}}\uc2  to portray her as unserious. Young supporters reinterpreted those same clips as charming and authentic \u8211\'20\'13 a powerful currency in contemporary politics.\par \par \uc2 Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign has nodded back, embracing the viral trends on her gen Z-run TikTok, @kamalahq. It eclipses Trump\u8217\'20\'19s personal account, @realdonaldtrump, in engagement, though he has substantially more followers. During a youth voter drive last month, Harris said young voters were part of the reason she was so optimistic about the future.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYour generation is killing it,\u8221\'20\'1D she said on a call with gen Z organizers. \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re brilliant. You care. You\u8217\'20\'19re impatient in every incredible, good way.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 To offset Harris\u8217\'20\'19s steep advantage with young women, Trump has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2024/aug/05/young-men-voters-us-election-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  heavily courting}}}\uc2  gen Z\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/opinion/columnist/2024/09/09/trump-gen-z-vote-right-wing-influencers-podcasts/75081942007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bro}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D vote with amped up displays of masculinity. He has turned up at Ultimate Fighting Championship bouts and a college {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/donald-trump-ron-desantis-iowa-iowa-state-football-game-f398a634ce11048c5e49b207263994c2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fraternity house}}}\uc2 . Wrestler Hulk Hogan tore off his shirt during a speech at the Republican convention in which he praised Trump as a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.c-span.org/video/?c5124673/hulk-hogan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gladiator}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former president has appeared on shows with the controversial YouTuber {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/09/19/trump-harris-young-men-voters/?itid=lk_inline_manual_42"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Logan Paul}}}\uc2  and video game streamer {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/06/trump-adin-ross-tesla-rolex"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Adin Ross}}}\uc2 , both of whom attract sizable followings of gen Z men. The Nelk Boys, a group of online content creators and pranksters, are helping too, by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://sendthevote.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spearheading}}}\uc2  a voter registration initiative on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s behalf. His team is also relying on Turning Point Action, the political advocacy wing of the far-right youth organization Turning Point USA, to drive out young conservatives.\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign and allied youth groups, meanwhile, are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/08/27/nx-s1-5090804/harris-gen-z-voters"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aggressively targeting}}}\uc2  college students \u8211\'20\'13 nearly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tufts.app.box.com/v/democracy-counts-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two-thirds of whom voted in 2020}}}\uc2 . As part of the push, Harris and Walz {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.essence.com/news/harris-walz-campaign-hbcu-homecoming-tour/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched}}}\uc2  a homecoming tour of historically Black colleges and universities, aiming to reach young Black students across the battleground states.\par \par \uc2 Democratic organizers say Harris has made concerted policy appeals to young people, particularly on housing and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which she highlighted in a recent appearance on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/07/kamala-harris-call-her-daddy-podcast-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Call Her Daddy}}}\uc2  podcast that is popular with gen Z women.Harris has also staked out support for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/2024/09/24/harris-filibuster-abortion-trump-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliminating the filibuster }}}\uc2  to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rightsas well as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/policy/healthcare/4907402-harris-says-she-backs-legalizing-marijuana-going-further-than-biden/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legalizing recreational marijuana}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Still, her pivot to the ideological center since becoming the Democratic nominee has left some young progressives {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sunrisemovement.org/movement-updates/sunrise-has-contacted-344437-young-voters-heres-what-were-hearing/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 disappointed}}}\uc2 . On the campaign trail, Harris frequently promotes her {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/sunrisemvmt/status/1833719577433268254"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 support for fracking}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a reversal from her 2019 presidential run when she embraced a ban. She has also adopted an increasingly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Y8GSbgtbCneEhbbxV1J55tkCUKSOO2TN/view"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hardline approach to illegal immigration}}}\uc2  and resisted calls to endorse an arms embargo on Israel, whose devastating campaign in Gaza has killed more than 41,000 Palestinians.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYoung people right now, our generation in general, are very, very clear-eyed on the fact that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  cannot return to the White House in November,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mejia, the progressive activist with Pop. \u8220\'20\'1CThe question presented to the Democratic party is: how much does it want to invite young people into its coalition in order to defeat \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Something our generation hasn\u8217\'20\'19t seen yet\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 In the weeks since Harris entered the presidential race, she has steadily recaptured lost ground, multiplying Biden\u8217\'20\'19s lead among young voters.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iop.harvard.edu/youth-poll/48th-edition-fall-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harvard Youth Poll}}}\uc2  showed Harris with a commanding 32-point lead over Trump among likely voters aged 18 to 29. Young Democrats expressed a heightened commitment to voting this November, with significantly more \u8220\'20\'1Cdefinitely\u8221\'20\'1D planning to cast a ballot compared with their Republican counterparts. Yet the overall share of young Americans who said they definitely planned to cast a ballot this year was 56%, down slightly from 63% {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iop.harvard.edu/news/harvard-youth-poll-election-2020"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at this point in 2020}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYoung people are right to be cynical and I don\u8217\'20\'19t expect one candidate to change that,\u8221\'20\'1D said Cristina Tzintz\u250\'00\'FAn Ramirez, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nextgenamerica.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the president of NextGen America}}}\uc2 , one of the largest youth-voting groups in the country. \u8220\'20\'1CThat happens over time by government responding.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But the first step is electing leaders who listen to young people, Tzintz\u250\'00\'FAn Ramirez said, arguing that Harris was the only presidential candidate offering solutions to their concerns on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nextgenamerica.org/youthvotepoll072024/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 economy and \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights}}}\uc2 . There are signs young people increasingly agree. A recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2024/10/08/us/elections/times-siena-poll-likely-electorate-crosstabs.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times and Siena College}}}\uc2  poll found that voters under age 30 were significantly more likely than older voters to believe that Harris \u8220\'20\'1Ccares about people like you\u8221\'20\'1D and to see her as a representative of \u8220\'20\'1Cchange\u8221\'20\'1D. They were also more inclined to view Harris as a \u8220\'20\'1Cstrong leader\u8221\'20\'1D and to describe her as \u8220\'20\'1Cfun\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Though the glow of \u8220\'20\'1Cbrat summer\u8221\'20\'1D has faded with the season, organizers say they have been able to convert that energy into lasting on-the-ground efforts to help turn out the vote. Over the next few weeks, youth voter engagement groups will be out in force, knocking on doors, registering students, and making pledges \u8211\'20\'13 and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nextgenamerica.org/vote/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to vote. In true gen Z fashion, youth organizers are also using memes and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.popsugar.com/identity/gen-z-2024-election-voting-events-49398412"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 friendship bracelets}}}\uc2  to drive young people to the polls.\par \par \uc2 In the days ahead, Pecora of Voters of Tomorrow will cast her first vote for president, a mail-in ballot for Harris. It will be counted in California, hardly a presidential battleground but, poignantly, the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s home state.\par \par \uc2 Pecora was just 13 in 2016, when Hillary Clinton conceded the election to Trump. She was in high school, taking classes by Zoom, during the depths of the coronavirus pandemic when Biden won four years later. Then came the nightmarish Capitol riot on January 6, when Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters tried to stop the peaceful transfer of power. \u8220\'20\'1CThere has yet to be a presidential cycle in my lifetime when democracy wasn\u8217\'20\'19t on the line,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Yet the 20-year-old is allowing herself to be hopeful, even as her team pours over numbers that tell the same story \u8211\'20\'13 that the race will be nail-bitingly close. Voters of Tomorrow says its on track to reach its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/jackplobel/status/1844369059942658277"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ambitious goal}}}\uc2  of 15 million direct contacts in hopes, Pecora said, of electing a leader who recognizes the \u8220\'20\'1Cpower and agency\u8221\'20\'1D of young people.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe see an option that tells us that politics can be something different,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt can be more hopeful, more productive, more caring and empathetic and loving. And that\u8217\'20\'19s something that our generation hasn\u8217\'20\'19t really seen yet.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241012ekac001ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
