\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Can ex-governor\u8217\'20\'19s anti-Trump stance swing key Senate seat for Republicans?\b0\par\par\uc2 Martin Pengelly in Washington and Baltimore \par \uc2 2,042 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 October 2024\par 13:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Maryland\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  faces a tough task against Angela Alsobrooks in a race that could decide control of chamber\par \par \uc2 At a conservative thinktank on 14th Street in Washington DC, awaiting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/15/larry-hogan-republican-senate-candidate-poll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Larry Hogan}}}\uc2 , the Republican candidate for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-senate"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US Senate}}}\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/maryland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Maryland}}}\uc2 , one staffer turned to another. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s nice having something to vote for, for a change,\u8221\'20\'1D the staffer wryly said. Shortly after, the former governor arrived for his speech at the Jewish Institute for National Security of America (Jinsa), part of his campaign to win in a state that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t elected a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican}}}\uc2  senator since 1980.\par \par \uc2 When he left the executive mansion in Annapolis last year, Hogan told his friendly audience, he had governed for eight years as a popular moderate but had not been looking for another job \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1CAnd frankly, I didn\u8217\'20\'19t yearn to be a part of the divisiveness and dysfunction in Washington,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut when I saw a bipartisan package to secure our border and to support Israel, Ukraine and Taiwan and other American allies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2024/02/07/politics/senate-border-ukraine-israel-aid-vote/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fail}}}\uc2  because people were told [by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ] to vote against a critical [immigration] bill that they claimed to be for, it made me frustrated enough that I knew I had to step up and try to do something about the mess in Washington.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Washington is not Maryland but the Old Line State is just a few miles up 14th from Jinsa. There, Hogan faces the Prince George\u8217\'20\'19s county executive, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/14/maryland-primary-republicans-democrats"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Angela Alsobrooks}}}\uc2 , for an open seat in November \u8211\'20\'13 a race in which the Democrat, who if she wins will be only the third Black woman ever elected to the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , enjoys significant polling leads.\par \par \uc2 The race has become potentially decisive in determining Senate control, and a test of anti-Trump sentiment on the right. Significant spending and endorsements are pouring in. Highly regarded as a local leader and \u8220\'20\'1Ctough on crime\u8221\'20\'1D Democrat, Alsobrooks defeated a DC establishment candidate, the congressman {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/22/maryland-senate-candidate-slur-apology"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 David Trone}}}\uc2 , in her primary and is now piling on praise from party grandees. She recently released an ad {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/dc-md-va/2024/10/04/obama-alsobrooks-endorsement-ad/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 featuring Barack Obama}}}\uc2  and secured support from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/opinions/2024/10/02/maryland-senate-angela-alsobrooks-endorsement/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington Post}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Thursday night, the two candidates will meet for a high-stakes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.baltimoresun.com/2024/10/07/how-to-watch-thursdays-senate-debate-between-alsobrooks-hogan/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debate}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ***\par \par \uc2 In practical terms, it takes 51 votes \u8211\'20\'13 or 50 if your party holds the presidency \u8211\'20\'13 to control the Senate. Democrats currently hold it 51-49 but face tough contests to hold seats in Republican-leaning states such as Montana and Ohio. It means Maryland counts this year, and Hogan\u8217\'20\'19s toughest challenge may lie in persuading enough Democratic voters they can trust him should Republicans retake the chamber with him as the 51st vote. In turn, Democrats know that if they cannot hold so deep blue a state as Maryland, they will in all likelihood lose control of the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Hogan is therefore seeking to depict himself as an antidote to Trump \u8211\'20\'13 and his rival as too far left. At Jinsa, talking foreign policy, he criticized Trump but he also knocked Alsobrooks, including for \u8220\'20\'1Crepeatedly demand[ing] that Israel enact an immediate and unilateral ceasefire, and [for calling] for cutting off critical military aid\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 I think it\u8217\'20\'19s a very close race. I\u8217\'20\'19ve always been an underdog in every one of my races\par \par \uc2 Republican \uc2 Larry Hogan\par \par \uc2 As popular as Hogan is \u8211\'20\'13 he stepped down as governor with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://marylandmatters.org/2023/01/17/political-notes-hogan-rides-off-into-the-sunset-with-approval-ratings-intact-talmadge-branch-joins-lobbying-firm/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 77% approval rating}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 polling suggests that message is not landing. According to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/senate/2024/maryland/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 538}}}\uc2 , since one tied poll in August, Alsobrooks\u8217\'20\'19s lead has ranged from five to 17 points.\par \par \uc2 Hogan begged to differ. \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s a very close race,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve always been an underdog in every one of my races.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are people out there that we\u8217\'20\'19ve still got to convince,\u8221\'20\'1D he added, \u8220\'20\'1Cand we\u8217\'20\'19ve got [then] 34 more days to do it, and I feel confident we\u8217\'20\'19re going to win the race. It\u8217\'20\'19s tough, though. I mean, we\u8217\'20\'19re a very blue state, and we\u8217\'20\'19re overcoming a huge deficit at the top of the ticket.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has been called many things, but \u8220\'20\'1Chuge deficit\u8221\'20\'1D may be a new one. Hogan has said he won\u8217\'20\'19t vote for Trump (or \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ), but must nonetheless fend off persistent questions about the man who rules his party. One recent ad from Hogan\u8217\'20\'19s campaign {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/09/02/larry-hogan-senate-ad-capitol-riot/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deplored}}}\uc2  the \u8220\'20\'1Chorror\u8221\'20\'1D of January 6. And yet, as Republicans from Trump and the Senate minority leader, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , on down know, sometimes a candidate must be allowed away from the party line.\par \par \uc2 In Maryland, Hogan is free to be Hogan. That\u8217\'20\'19s to his advantage. To his disadvantage, Democrats from the Senate majority leader, \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , to Alsobrooks on down know Hogan has a bigger problem.\par \par \uc2 In June 2022, in the case Dobbs v Jackson, the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  to which Trump appointed three hardliners {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 removed}}}\uc2  the federal right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Two years on, Hogan insists he will not let his party go further.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[Alsobrooks\u8217\'20\'19s campaign] want[s] to focus on making it a cookie-cutter Democratic talking points race but it\u8217\'20\'19s not, because I have a different position than most Republicans,\u8221\'20\'1D he said at the Jinsa event. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd so, you know, I\u8217\'20\'19ve promised to be a sponsor to codify Roe v Wade, the 1973 ruling that previously safeguarded \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, so that nobody comes between a woman and her doctor in any state in America, and to sponsor a bill to protect IVF.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He also insisted that \u8220\'20\'1Cmost people are concerned about the economy. They\u8217\'20\'19re concerned about affordability, inflation, they\u8217\'20\'19re concerned about crime in their communities, and they\u8217\'20\'19re concerned about securing the border and fixing [the] broken immigration system.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among Democratic rejoinders: while a member of the executive committee of the \uc2 Republican Governors Association\uc2 , Hogan worked to elect allies in states that now have stringent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans. In his own state, in 2022, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/maryland-larry-hogan-veto-abortion-access-bill/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vetoed}}}\uc2  a bill to expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access. The same year, he said Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cnominated incredible justices to the supreme court\u8221\'20\'1D, a comment Democrats have brought back to haunt him. Hogan {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.semafor.com/article/08/16/2024/larry-hogan-praised-donald-trumps-incredible-justices-to-the-supreme-court-in-2022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says}}}\uc2  he was not referring to Dobbs but Alsobrooks is happy to keep the spotlight on the issue. As she recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/senate-maryland-angela-alsobrooks-larry-hogan-9237eeff099768e04888bb53fb98baeb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CI think my opponent\u8217\'20\'19s record is very clear where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care is concerned.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many Americans fear a national \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, should Trump be president again. Hogan said he had been against that for decades \u8220\'20\'1Cand I\u8217\'20\'19ll be the one of the ones standing up, regardless of who the president is or who\u8217\'20\'19s in control of Senate\u8221\'20\'1D. But he also said he would not support reform to the filibuster, the Senate rule that requires 60 votes for most legislation, in order to codify Roe.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think it\u8217\'20\'19s a terrible idea, because it\u8217\'20\'19s actually something that \u8230\'20\'26 my opponent and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  both agree on. They want to be able to jam things through on a 51-vote [majority].\par \par \uc2 \u8221\'20\'1DRight now, [the Senate is] a deliberative body where we actually have to find bipartisan cooperation and common sense and kind of common ground for the common good. That\u8217\'20\'19s what I did in Maryland with a 70% Democratic legislature. We got things done.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\par \par \uc2 A few days after Hogan\u8217\'20\'19s event at Jinsa, about 40 miles (65km) north-east in Baltimore, Democrats gathered at a canvassing hub. Once a wedding venue, the Majestic Hall of Events was surrounded by less-than-majestic auto shops and down-at-heel churches. Inside, Alsobrooks addressed a crowd organized by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://delta4womeninaction.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 D4 Women in Action}}}\uc2 , linked to Delta Sigma Theta, one of the Divine Nine Black women\u8217\'20\'19s sororities, to which Alsobrooks belongs.\par \par \uc2 In her speech, Alsobrooks spoke about her links to Baltimore and \u8220\'20\'1Cthe number one issue across our state, and the thing that people most desire to have: economic opportunity\u8221\'20\'1D. She also took shots at her opponent. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat did he do [as governor] when he had the opportunity to stand up for all of our families in Baltimore? He sent back $900m to the federal government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 That was a reference to a 2015 decision to scrap a light rail project, a call that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2015/dec/23/maryland-lawsuit-baltimore-rail-project-racism-larry-hogan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attracted lawsuits}}}\uc2 . But Alsobrooks also looked to the national stage, and the issue she wants foremost in voters\u8217\'20\'19 minds.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis race is bigger than both of us,\u8221\'20\'1D Alsobrooks told the Guardian. \u8220\'20\'1CBigger than \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  the person. It\u8217\'20\'19s bigger than Angela the person. It\u8217\'20\'19s about issues and about the future. It is about reproductive freedom.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Alsobrooks listed other policy priorities \u8211\'20\'13 \u8220\'20\'1Csensible gun legislation \u8230\'20\'26 economic opportunity\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 as part of a platform \u8220\'20\'1Cthat really does favor hard-working people, middle-class families, and that is about preserving freedoms and democracy\u8221\'20\'1D. But protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights was a theme to which she returned.\par \par \uc2 At Jinsa, Hogan said Democrats were trying to turn a state race into a national contest. Alsobrooks embraced the charge: \u8220\'20\'1CThe former governor thinks he\u8217\'20\'19s running to go back to Annapolis. We\u8217\'20\'19re actually running to go to Washington DC, and we would represent Marylanders there.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Marylanders are very savvy and they have seen how [Hogan] has changed \u8230\'20\'26 and will again vote to keep Maryland Democratic\par \par \uc2 Democrat Angela Alsobrooks\par \par \uc2 She added: \u8220\'20\'1CThis [Republican Senate] caucus is led by people like Ted Cruz, \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2 , Rick Scott, \uc2 Mitch McConnell\uc2 , and they \u8230\'20\'26 have really proclaimed war on the reproductive freedoms of women. They have very clear records, and [Hogan has] aligned himself with the party whose policies do not align with the average Marylander.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Much has been made of the warm relationship Hogan and Alsobrooks enjoyed when Hogan was governor. Asked about an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.motherjones.com/politics/2024/10/larry-hogan-angela-alsobrooks-maryland-senate/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unearthed}}}\uc2  Hogan comment \u8211\'20\'13 that Alsobrooks was a better Prince George\u8217\'20\'19s county executive than his own father, the late congressman \uc2 Lawrence Hogan\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 Alsobrooks said: \u8220\'20\'1CHe has become, in a lot of ways, the kind of politician he says he despises, one who\u8217\'20\'19s very disingenuous.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBut I think that people see through it. Marylanders are very savvy and they have seen how he has changed \u8230\'20\'26 and I think they will see through the disingenuous nature of his campaign, and will again vote to keep Maryland Democratic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\u8226\'20\'22\par \par \uc2 Keeping Maryland Democratic will require turning out the vote. At the canvassing hub, one phone-banker wearily said: \u8220\'20\'1CPut in two shifts this morning.\u8221\'20\'1D A friend smiled back: \u8220\'20\'1COnly a hundred more to go.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The same Jinsa staffer who earlier had said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cnice to have something to vote for\u8221\'20\'1D with Hogan also said that he hadn\u8217\'20\'19t felt so good about a Senate race since 2006 \u8211\'20\'13 which was still a defeat \u8211\'20\'13 in which \u8220\'20\'1Cgetting more than 40% felt like a moral victory\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Back then, Ben Cardin, the Democrat retiring this year, beat Michael Steele, a Hogan-esque GOP moderate. Steele went on to chair the \uc2 Republican National Committee\uc2 , then became an MSNBC host and Never Trumper. Asked for his view of the current Maryland race, Steele was not as convinced of an Alsobrooks win as many other observers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis race was not a competitive race until Larry got into it,\u8221\'20\'1D Steele said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe is a popular two-term governor who left, I think, an important mark on how politics play out in Maryland for Republicans and made this very competitive out of the gate, largely because people had come to trust his style of governance.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s open, it\u8217\'20\'19s compassionate, it\u8217\'20\'19s concerned \u8230\'20\'26 I think a lot of people remember that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Steele said Hogan had a good chance of attracting split-ticket voters \u8211\'20\'13 rare beasts, precious to any campaign, in this case prepared to back Harris for president but Hogan for Senate.\par \par \uc2 It all added up to a warning for anyone expecting a comfortable Democratic win.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think the latest polling has Alsobrooks up by 11,\u8221\'20\'1D Steele said. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe that, largely because when I\u8217\'20\'19m out in neighborhoods talking to people, and from everything I can piece together, this race is a lot tighter than the traditionalists who look at Maryland think it to be.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This article was amended on 11 October 2024. It originally stated that \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  chaired the \uc2 Republican Governors Association\uc2 . He was actually a member of its executive committee.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241010ekaa002bf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
