\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Florida threatens news stations over ad in favor of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights measure\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 587 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 October 2024\par 19:53 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 FCC\uc2  chair condemns state health department for sending cease-and-desists over spot supporting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  health department has fired off cease-and-desist letters to local news stations over an advertisement urging people to vote in favor of a ballot measure that would expand \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in the state.\par \par \uc2 In the ad, a woman identified as Caroline from Tampa, Florida, talks about being diagnosed with brain cancer while pregnant. The state currently bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  past roughly six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe doctors knew if I did not end my pregnancy, I would lose my baby, I would lose my life, and my daughter would lose her mom,\u8221\'20\'1D she says. \u8220\'20\'1CFlorida has now banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  even in cases like mine.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She then urges viewers to vote \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D on a Florida ballot measure that would enshrine \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights into the state constitution and restore access to the procedure, which was dramatically curtailed when the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/03/florida-abortion-ban-clinic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 six-week ban went into effect in May}}}\uc2  of this year.\par \par \uc2 John Wilson, general counsel for the Florida department of health, called the claim that women can\u8217\'20\'19t get life-saving abortions in Florida \u8220\'20\'1Ccategorically false\u8221\'20\'1D in letters to local news stations, which were first reported by the journalist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Jason_Garcia/status/1842646033890746744/photo/2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jason Garcia}}}\uc2  and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://floridapolitics.com/archives/700182-department-of-health-sends-cease-and-desist-letter-to-tv-station-over-abortion-ad/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 news outlet Florida Politics}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe advertisement is not only false; it is dangerous,\u8221\'20\'1D Wilson wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CWomen faced with pregnancy complications posing a serious risk of death or substantial and irreversible physical impairment may and should seek medical treatment in Florida.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Although Florida, like every other state with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, permits abortions in cases of medical emergencies, doctors across the country have said that these bans are worded so vaguely and with such little regard for medical realities that they are unworkable in practice. Instead, doctors facing the threat of criminal prosecution for violating the bans say they have been forced to delay women\u8217\'20\'19s care until they are sick enough.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, \uc2 Jessica Rosenworcel\uc2 , the \uc2 Federal Communications Commission\uc2  chair, condemned the cease-and-desist letters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe right of broadcasters to speak freely is rooted in the first amendment,\u8221\'20\'1D Rosenworcel said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThreats against broadcast stations for airing content that conflicts with the government\u8217\'20\'19s views are dangerous and undermine the fundamental principle of free speech.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/feb/01/abortion-ban-tennessee-texas-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dozens of women have come forward}}}\uc2  with stories of being denied medically necessary abortions. In August, a New York state doctor told the Guardian that she had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/30/whole-womans-health-abortion-clinic-virginia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 treated a woman with an ectopic pregnancy}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 which is nonviable and potentially life-threatening if left untreated \u8211\'20\'13 who had been turned away from a Florida emergency department.\par \par \uc2 Over the last several weeks, civil rights and fair election groups have become increasingly alarmed by efforts by Florida\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing government \u8211\'20\'13 led by its Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 to undermine the state\u8217\'20\'19s ballot measure. Law enforcement {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/13/florida-abortion-petition-investigation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 officials have investigated}}}\uc2  voters who signed a petition to get the measure onto the ballot, while a state agency has posted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.miamiherald.com/news/politics-government/state-politics/article293344699.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 website attacking the measure}}}\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures have passed in a number of states since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade in 2022, but Florida\u8217\'20\'19s measure needs to garner 60% of the vote to pass \u8211\'20\'13 and the support for the measure currently appears to be well short of that threshold, a recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/08/us/politics/florida-abortion-ballot-measure-poll.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York Times/Siena College poll found}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/26/election-abortion-ballot-measures-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nine other states are also set}}}\uc2  to vote on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related ballot measures on election day in November.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241009eka90030d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
