\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Both Trump and Harris are swinging to the \u8216\'20\'18center\u8217\'20\'19. What does that even mean?\b0\par\par\uc2 Moira Donegan \par \uc2 1,073 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 October 2024\par 10:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Any voter who is still undecided a month from the election seems like the sort who is unlikely to even remember to vote\par \par \uc2 Who, exactly, could be an undecided voter in 2024? It\u8217\'20\'19s not as if the candidates do not draw a sufficient contrast. There can be few people alive these days, let alone few registered voters in America, who do not know much more than they ever thought they would about the habits, history, and inner psyche of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who has now been a singularly domineering force in national politics for nearly a decade. The Harris campaign has been trying to play their candidates\u8217\'20\'19 comparative newness on the national stage as an asset, rigorously keeping her from saying much of substance, but \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , too, is by now a well-known figure: once a popular and high profile senator from the country\u8217\'20\'19s biggest state, she moved on to a busy, energetic, and extremely visible vice presidency.\par \par \uc2 The candidates are about as familiar to Americans as they\u8217\'20\'19re going to get; anyone still saying they are \u8220\'20\'1Cundecided\u8221\'20\'1D now, just four weeks out from the election, seems like the sort who has been paying so little attention that they\u8217\'20\'19re not likely to remember to vote at all.\par \par \uc2 And yet it is this undecided voter, that irresistible phantom in American politics, who both candidates seem to be chasing as the race enters its final weeks. Both candidates seem, for lack of a better term, to be trying to cast themselves as making a pivot to the center, seemingly in a bid to convince this imaginary voter \u8211\'20\'13 the one who is apparently torn between a center-left bureaucrat of obvious competence and a raving, racist narcissist who wants to be a dictator and has already tried \u8211\'20\'13 to pick them. If such a person exists, I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure that I, for one, would place much value in their esteem. But the campaigns are making a different calculation.\par \par \uc2 On the Republican side, Trump, never one to miss an opportunity for cynicism and dishonesty, has tried to cast himself, in somewhat feeble and unconvincing terms, as a moderate on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He has tried to say that his position is that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be left to the states (which conveniently elides several of his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/donald-trump/trumps-many-abortion-positions-timeline-rcna146601"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 past statements}}}\uc2 , as well as leaving unacknowledged the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 homicidal}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/US/13-year-rape-victim-baby-amid-confusion-states/story?id=108351812"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sadistic}}}\uc2  policies that many states have enacted). Now, his wife is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/03/melania-trump-abortion-pro-choice"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shilling a book}}}\uc2  in which she claims, with conspicuously convenient timing, that she is personally pro-choice. At the vice-presidential debate, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s surrogate, Ohio senator and pronatalist activist JD Vance, spoke in patronizing terms about women who need to be given \u8220\'20\'1Cmore options\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 not the option to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or dictate the fate of their own bodies or the course of their own lives, of course, but the option to drop out of the workforce to stay home and raise babies.\par \par \uc2 The lies, obfuscation, and euphemism from the Trump camp are an effort to conceal the substance of their anti-woman policies behind a slick style of obscurantism. Distressingly, it might be working: polls show that many voters wrongly believe that a second Trump presidency would not further erode \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Harris, for her part, has been seeking to court the imagined undecided voter by bear-hugging Republicans \u8211\'20\'13 sometimes literally. On Thursday, she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/10/03/kamala-harris-liz-cheney-republicans-wisconsin-00182470"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held a rally}}}\uc2  in Ripon, Wisconsin \u8211\'20\'13 the birthplace of the Republican party \u8211\'20\'13 to campaign alongside former Wyoming Congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , who has endorsed Harris. The women stood together in front of large signs that said \u8220\'20\'1CCountry Over Party.\u8221\'20\'1D The official pitch was that Trump is a great enough threat to democracy that figures who agree on little else can unite to oppose him out of a sense of patriotic duty. But the appearance also seemed to signal Harris\u8217\'20\'19s bid to attract Trump-skeptical conservatives, and to lessen her liberal California image in favor of a moderate, conciliatory one.\par \par \uc2 But if the two candidates seem to be looking to gain the same kind of voters, they face very different risks in trying to court them. Trump is the charismatic leader of a personality cult whose voters respond to his efforts to ignite their grievances and largely seem to ignore his own repeated and well-documented lies and contempt for them. This has always been Trump\u8217\'20\'19s paradox: that he is loved by a base of support that he himself seems to profoundly disrespect, and that, in the eyes of his followers, his transparent self-interest only serves to make him more trustworthy, more authentic, with each of his lies seeming to evoke a larger truth.\par \par \uc2 As Trump has ostentatiously tried to pivot to the center on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , there has been some grumbling from the anti-choice movement, which has been not a little bit disturbed by the way their cause has become a political liability for the Republican party. But for all the anti-choice set\u8217\'20\'19s dissatisfaction with Trump\u8217\'20\'19s recent statements, there has never been any real risk that they would withhold their votes from him. Their loyalty is permanent.\par \par \uc2 Not so for Harris. In the Trump age, the Democrats have cobbled together a coalition too large and internally contradictory to be sustainable \u8211\'20\'13 consisting, as it does, of people with fundamentally different worldviews, opposed interests, and a great deal of mutual mistrust. Harris\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to win over Republican voters will run a much greater risk of alienating her party\u8217\'20\'19s progressive base, many of whom see Republican policy preferences as a threat to their civil liberties and way of life. The day after she appeared on stage with Cheney in Wisconsin, Harris met with leaders of the Arab and Muslim communities in Flint, Michigan, many of whom have been distraught at the horrific suffering in Gaza and outraged by the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s complicity in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s increasingly reckless and aggressive actions.\par \par \uc2 Their votes will be crucial to her victory in Michigan, an essential swing state. But it\u8217\'20\'19s not clear how much the meeting will do to reassure them. Back in Wisconsin, Harris had taken time out of her rally with \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  to specifically thank the former Vice President \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the architect of the disastrous 2003 invasion of Iraq. He, too, has endorsed Harris.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Moira Donegan is a Guardian US columnist\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241008eka80015q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
