\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Trump speaks at 7 October event in Florida \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Helen Sullivan (now); Cecilia Nowell , Chris Stein and Martin Belam (earlier) \par \uc2 13,003 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 October 2024\par 07:39 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is closed, thanks for following along. Can\u8217\'20\'19t get enough of the US election? Get our free app and sign up for election alerts\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22am BST\par \par \uc2 This blog is closing now, thanks for following along. You can find the latest US elections coverage {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are the key developments from the last few hours:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pre-recorded 60 Minutes interview aired. She was asked whether Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  is a \u8220\'20\'1Creal close ally\u8221\'20\'1D of the US, and did not say that he was \u8211\'20\'13 she sidestepped the question, saying, \u8220\'20\'1CI think, with all due respect, the better question is do we have an important alliance between the American people and the Israeli people, and the answer to that question is yes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Harris was also asked about how her economic plans, which \uc2 CBS\uc2  reported would add $3tn to the federal deficit over ten years. She was pressed repeatedly on the question, at one point saying, \u8220\'20\'1CWell, one of the things is I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna make sure that the richest among us, who can afford it, pay their fair share in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/kamala-harris-donald-trump-tax-plan-impact-on-your-paycheck/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taxes}}}\uc2 . It is not right that teachers and nurses and firefighters are paying a har-- a higher tax rate than billionaires and the biggest corporations\u8221\'20\'1D, to which Whitaker responded, \u8220\'20\'1CBut we\u8217\'20\'19re dealing with the real world here\u8221\'20\'1D and asked how Harris would get that through Congress, which, he said \u8220\'20\'1Chas shown no inclination to move in your direction.\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said she disagreed, and that, \u8220\'20\'1CThere are plenty of leaders in Congress who understand and know that the Trump tax cuts blew up our federal deficit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An analysis from the Committee for a Responsible Federal budget released on Monday found that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies would send the federal debt climbing by as much as $15.2t through 2035, and as little $1.4t. Over the same period, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s policies could send it up by as much as $8.1t, or nothing at all.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Asked if she would sit down with Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , Harris replied: \u8220\'20\'1CNot bilaterally. Without Ukraine? No.\u8221\'20\'1D But she punted on a question about Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s request for Nato membership. Despite receiving assistance from the US and the western military alliance, Ukraine is not a Nato member. \u8220\'20\'1CThose are all issues that we will deal with if and when it arrives at that point,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, we are supporting Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s ability to defend itself against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s unprovoked aggression.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Earlier on Monday, in response to reports that \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor, will not respond to her calls regarding hurricanes Helene and Milton, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  told reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are in desperate need of support right now, and playing political games at this moment \u8230\'20\'26 is just utterly irresponsible, and it is selfish, and it is about political gamesmanship.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump spoke at a memorial event for 7 October, where he described the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attack as \u8220\'20\'1Ca moment in horrible history\u8221\'20\'1D, and said, \u8220\'20\'1CIt seemed as if the gates of hell had sprung open and unleashed their horrors unto the world. What a moment in time.\u8221\'20\'1D He asked for a moment of silence for those killed and the hostages still held by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . He claims to be friends with a lot of families who lost loved ones that day.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Trump did not make any public remarks as he paid his respects at the final resting place of a famous rabbi in New York earlier on Monday. But he blasted Biden and Harris over their handling of the Middle East in an interview earlier, accusing the incumbent of having the \u8220\'20\'1Cworst foreign policy of anybody in history probably. Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot listening at all\u8221\'20\'1D to Biden, said Trump \u8211\'20\'13 with the property tycoon lamenting that war-torn Gaza could one day be \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter than Monaco\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.17am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump has finished speaking in Florida. \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Richard Luscombe is a the event and reports,\par \par \uc2 Trump spoke for exactly 20 minutes. He ended with a familiar refrain, namely the claim that the 7 October attacks would never have happened if he had still been in the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe last two years have proved that,\u8221\'20\'1D he says. \u8220\'20\'1CViolence, and more. You see that weakness. But there\u8217\'20\'19s also a lot of hatred going around, not just weakness. There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of hatred on a certain side.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat is needed is more than ever unwavering American leadership\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 If elected, Trump says, there will be \u8220\'20\'1Cthe dawn of new, more harmonious Middle East,\u8221\'20\'1D which he insists is \u8220\'20\'1Cfinally within our reach\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will not allow the Jewish state to be threatened with destruction. I will not allow another Holocaust of the Jewish people. I will not allow a jihad to be waged on America or our allies and I will support Israel\u8217\'20\'19s right to win its war.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.19am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02am BST\par \par \uc2 More now from my colleague based in Florida, Richard Luscombe. He is at the Trump event, and reports:\par \par \uc2 Trump says the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attack was \u8220\'20\'1Ca moment in horrible history\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt seemed as if the gates of hell had sprung open and unleashed their horrors unto the world. What a moment in time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He asked for a moment of silence for those killed and the hostages still held by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He claims to be friends with a lot of families who lost loved ones that day.\par \par \uc2 He spoke about the attacks for about 13 minutes before introducing politics, the Republican presidential nominee saying that, \u8220\'20\'1CIf, and when, they say, when I\u8217\'20\'19m president, the US will once again be stronger and closer [to Israel] than it ever was. But we have to win the election.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He mentions \u8220\'20\'1Cleadership of this country\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 meaning the administration of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 and the crowd begins to boo.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe anti-Jewish hatred has returned \u8230\'20\'26 and within the ranks of the Democratic party in particular. The Republican party has not been infected by this horrible disease, and won\u8217\'20\'19t be as long as I\u8217\'20\'19m in charge.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.56am BST\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Richard Luscombe is at the 7 October anniversary event at which Trump is speaking. He writes:\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has finally taken the stage at his golf club in Miami, where the former president is telling a crowd of about 300, mostly from the Jewish community, that he had a bumpy flight down from New York to attend a commemoration of the first anniversary of the 7 October terrorist attacks in Israel.\par \par \uc2 Rising to chants of \u8220\'20\'1Cfight, fight, fight\u8221\'20\'1D, the former president and Republican began his remarks by mentioning Hurricane Milton, about to slam into Florida\u8217\'20\'19s west coast.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt looks like it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a whopper. I hope everyone stays safe,\u8221\'20\'1D he says.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.04am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Here was Harris on how her economic plans will be funded \u8211\'20\'13 an answer she sidestepped, on a subject she has been criticised for being weak on, and one that is generally viewed as key to how people vote:\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala Harris on 60 Minutes: "The other economists that have reviewed my plan versus my opponent, and determined that my plan would strengthen America's economy -- his would weaken it." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JraMOkgvDn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JraMOkgvDn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1843450018214158707?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53am BST\par \par \uc2 That interview has ended. Trump meanwhile has finally taken to the stage at a memorial event in Florida. He started by speaking about Hurricanes Helene and Milton, but eventually moved on to more relevant comments.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.51am BST\par \par \uc2 And Harris on her gun ownership. She has mentioned repeatedly that she owns a gun \u8211\'20\'13 her running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is a gun owner, too \u8211\'20\'13 and Harris now says that the type of gun she owns is a glock.\par \par \uc2 She is asked if she has fired it, and says she has fired it at a shooting range.\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala Harris to 60 Minutes: "I have a glock" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/KBF6dHpRRj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/KBF6dHpRRj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1843452930034208912?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is that exchange with Walz:\par \par \uc2 enltrQ: Why do you think the \u8216\'20\'18weird\u8217\'20\'19 label stuck to Republicans?\par \par \uc2 Gov. Walz: I was talking about the behaviors of being obsessed with people's personal lives in their bedrooms and their \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Making up stories about folks legally here eating cats and dogs. They're\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JB0w8C1AC2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JB0w8C1AC2}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1843451943244435776?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.42am BST\par \par \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Bill Whitaker is now giving Harris\u8217\'20\'19s running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , the \u8220\'20\'1C60 minutes\u8221\'20\'1D treatment. He begins by asking Walz where he and Harris disagree.\par \par \uc2 With a chuckle, Walz said Harris probably wished he was a \u8220\'20\'1Clittle more careful\u8221\'20\'1D about how he speaks publicly. Whitaker quickly follows up, noting that Walz has been caught embellishing stories on several occasions, including that he was in China when the Tiananmen Square massacre occurred.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI will own up to being a knucklehead at times, but the folks closest to me know that I keep my word,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. He insisted voters could trust him, and that mispeaking was hardly on the same plane as Trump, whom he called a \u8220\'20\'1Cpathological liar.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He was also asked about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s criticism of his record as governor of Minnesota. Walz stood by it, saying it was focused on expanding the safety net for families and children. He slipped a joke that in Minnesota, where it gets cold enough that lakes freeze in the winter: \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re so optimistic, we walk on water half the year.\par \par \uc2 Walz was also asked why he believes his description of Republicans as \u8220\'20\'1Cweird\u8221\'20\'1D stuck.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI was really talking about behaviors, being obsessed with people\u8217\'20\'19s personal lives in their bedrooms and their \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , making up stories about legal folks legally here eating cats and dogs,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re dehumanizing. They go beyond weird, because I said this, it becomes almost dangerous. Let\u8217\'20\'19s debate policy in a real way, and let\u8217\'20\'19s try and find an objective truth again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris sidesteps question on how she will pay for economic plans\par \par \uc2 Harris also sidestepped questions on the economy. Here is that tense exchange. It starts with \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Whitaker saying Harris wants to expand the child tax redit and give tax breaks to first-time homebuyers, which Harris agrees are her plans.\par \par \uc2 Then Whitaker says: But it is estimated by the Nonpartisan Committee for Responsible Federal budget that your economic plan would add $3tn to the federal deficit over the next decade. How are you gonna pay for that?\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 : OK, so the other econ- economists that have reviewed my plan versus my opponent and determined that my economic plan would strengthen America\u8217\'20\'19s economy. His would weaken it.\par \par \uc2 Bill Whitaker: But--\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 : My plan, Bill, if you don\u8217\'20\'19t mind, my plan is about saying that when you invest in small businesses, you invest in the middle class, and you strengthen America\u8217\'20\'19s economy. Small businesses are part of the backbone of America\u8217\'20\'19s economy.\par \par \uc2 Bill Whitaker: But-but pardon me, Madame vice-president, the question was, how are you going to pay for it?\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala Harris on 60 Minutes: "The other economists that have reviewed my plan versus my opponent, and determined that my plan would strengthen America's economy -- his would weaken it." {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/JraMOkgvDn"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/JraMOkgvDn}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1843450018214158707?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 : Well, one of the things is I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna make sure that the richest among us, who can afford it, pay their fair share in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/kamala-harris-donald-trump-tax-plan-impact-on-your-paycheck/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taxes}}}\uc2 . It is not right that teachers and nurses and firefighters are paying a har-- a higher tax rate than billionaires and the biggest corporations.\par \par \uc2 Bill Whitaker: But-but\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 : And I plan on making that fair.\par \par \uc2 Bill Whitaker: But we\u8217\'20\'19re dealing with the real world here.\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 : But the real world includes\u8212\'20\'14\par \par \uc2 Bill Whitaker: How are you gonna get this through Congress?\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.37am BST\par \par \uc2 Here is that exchange on Ukraine:\par \par \uc2 enltrQ: Would you meet with Putin?\par \par \uc2 Vice President Harris: Not bilaterally without Ukraine. Ukraine must have a say in the future of Ukraine. If Trump were president, Putin would be sitting in Kyiv right now. He says he can \u8216\'20\'18end the war on day one.\u8217\'20\'19 You know what that is? It's about\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/Zfe6HXqvtv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/Zfe6HXqvtv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1843450231184089484?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 8, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris says she would not sit down with only Putin to discuss Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Asked if she would sit down with Russian president \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , Harris replies: \u8220\'20\'1CNot bilaterally. Without Ukraine? No.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 But she punted on a question about Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s request for Nato membership. Despite receiving assistance from the US and the western military alliance, Ukraine is not a Nato member.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThose are all issues that we will deal with if and when it arrives at that point,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, we are supporting Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s ability to defend itself against Russia\u8217\'20\'19s unprovoked aggression.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She then turned on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s records: \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , if he were president, Putin would be sitting in Kyiv right now. He talks about, \u8216\'20\'18oh, he can end it on day one.\u8217\'20\'19 You know what that is? It\u8217\'20\'19s about surrender.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.31am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.24am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris declines to say Netanyahu is a "real close ally" in 60 minutes interview\par \par \uc2 The interview is under way. As reported in previews, it begins with a question on the spiraling situation in the Middle East, a clip that was released in advance of the sit-down. She declined to say whether Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ca real close ally\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think, with all due respect, the better question is do we have an important alliance between the American people and the Israeli people, and the answer to that question is yes,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president replied in an excerpt from her forthcoming interview on the popular news program.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The interview then turns to the economy. Harris is pressed to say how she would pay for her economic agenda, which she has mostly unveiled in broad strokes. She talked about the importance of making billionaires and big corporations \u8220\'20\'1Cpay their fair share.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not right that teachers and nurses and firefighters are paying a higher tax rate than billionaires and the biggest corporations,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am a devout public servant, you know that, I\u8217\'20\'19m also a capitalist,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I know the limitations of government.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1C60 Minutes\u8221\'20\'1D election special has begun with a lengthy explanation of the effort by \uc2 CBS\uc2  to secure an interview with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Scott Pelley, one of the show\u8217\'20\'19s correspondents who was supposed to interview Trump, detailed the back-and-forth with the Trump campaign to secure the interview that he said was due to take place on Thursday last week. But he said Trump canceled the sit down.\par \par \uc2 Pelley said the campaign provided \u8220\'20\'1Cshifting explanations\u8221\'20\'1D for pulling out of the interview, including that he did not want to be \u8220\'20\'1Cfactchecked\u8221\'20\'1D and that he \u8220\'20\'1Cneeded an apology\u8221\'20\'1D for a 2020 interview related to \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s laptop.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CTrump has said his opponent doesn\u8217\'20\'19t do interviews because she can\u8217\'20\'19t handle them. He had previously declined another debate with Harris,\u8221\'20\'1D Pelley said. \u8220\'20\'1CSo tonight may have been the largest audience for the candidates between now and Election Day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Whitaker asks if the US has a real close ally in prime minister Netanyahu, to which Harris says, \u8220\'20\'1CI think, with all due respect, the better question is do we have an important alliance between the American people and the Israeli people. And the answer to that question is yes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.13am BST\par \par \uc2 During the interview, \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Bill Whitaker will ask \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  about the crisis in the Middle East. Harris sidesteps a question about US support for Israel, and in particular, Netanyahu.\par \par \uc2 Here is that exchange:\par \par \uc2 Bill Whitaker: The events of the past few weeks have pushed us to the brink, if-if not into an all-out regional war in the Middle East. What can the U.S. do at this point to stop this from spinning out of control?\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 : Well, let\u8217\'20\'19s start with 7 October. 1,200 people were massacred, 250 hostages were taken, including Americans, women were brutally raped, and as I said then, I maintain Israel has a right to defend itself. We would. And how it does so matters. Far too many innocent Palestinians have been killed. This war has to end.\par \par \uc2 Bill Whitaker: We supply Israel with billions of dollars in military aid, and yet prime minister Netanyahu seems to be charting his own course. The Biden-Harris administration has pressed him to agree to a ceasefire. He\u8217\'20\'19s resisted. You urged him not to go into Lebanon. He went in anyway. Does the U.S. have no sway over prime minister Netanyahu?\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 : The work that we do diplomatically with the leadership of Israel is an ongoing pursuit around making clear our principles.\par \par \uc2 Bill Whitaker: But it seems that prime minister Netanyahu is not listening.\par \par \uc2 Vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 : We are not gonna stop pursuing what is necessary for the United States to be clear about where we stand on the need for this war to end.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.15am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.57am BST\par \par \uc2 Trump has not yet spoken, but the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s Richard Luscombe is at the event in Florida and will report on anything noteworthy that he says when he does.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s pre-taped interview with 60 Minutes is due to air in two minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time. We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring that to you live as it airs.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.42am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s interview with 60 Minutes will air in 20 minutes\u8217\'20\'19 time. We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you news and analysis from that live.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41am BST\par \par \uc2 People around the world marked the anniversary of the 7 October \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks on Monday, and devastating conflict that has followed.\par \par \uc2 Vigils paid tribute to the 1200 victims of the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks, and the hostages in Gaza, and protests called for an end to the Israeli offensive, which has killed nearly 42,000 people, more than half of them women and children, and injured tens of thousands.\par \par \uc2 US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  participated in a Jewish ceremony to remember the victims of the attack, and UK prime minister \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2  called for an end to the escalating regional violence. The events came as Israel launched a wave of strikes on southern Lebanon, where it claims it has been targeting \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  in recent weeks, leading to fears of a broader war:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.24am BST\par \par \uc2 As we wait for Trump to speak at an event on the anniversary of the 7 October attacks, here are the biggest days to watch out for the next few months. There are no major events scheduled until election day, just a month of campaigning from the candidates.\par \par \uc2 5 November: Election Day. It could take days for the election result to be known, especially if it is close and mail-in ballots are a factor.\par \par \uc2 26 November: Trump, the first sitting or former U.S. president to be convicted of a crime, is due to be sentenced in a Manhattan hush money case where he was found guilty of falsifying documents to cover up a payment to silence a porn star. Trump has denied wrongdoing. Sentencing was originally due to take place on Sept. 18.\par \par \uc2 17 December: Electors, who together form the Electoral College, meet in their respective states and the District of Columbia to select the president and vice-president.\par \par \uc2 25 December: The electoral votes must be received by this date by the president of the Senate \u8211\'20\'13 a role held by the vice-president, now Harris \u8211\'20\'13 and the archivist.\par \par \uc2 6 January 2025: The vice-president presides over the Electoral College vote count at a joint session of Congress, announces the results and declares who has been elected.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of the count on 6 January 2021, then-President Trump lambasted his vice-president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , for refusing to try to prevent Congress from certifying President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s victory over Trump.\par \par \uc2 On that day, the US Capitol was attacked by Trump supporters trying to stop the count. Biden\u8217\'20\'19s win was certified early the next day.\par \par \uc2 Congress has since passed the Electoral Count Reform and Presidential Transition Improvement Act of 2022, which requires approval of one-fifth of the House and Senate to consider a challenge to a state\u8217\'20\'19s results \u8211\'20\'13 a much higher bar than existed before, when at least one member each in the Senate and House of Representatives could together trigger a challenge.\par \par \uc2 20 January: The inauguration of the election winner and their vice-president takes place. At this ceremony, the victor and the vice-president are officially sworn into office.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.30am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is more on the Fema chief\u8217\'20\'19s response to falsehoods spread by Treump about Hurricane Helene:\par \par \uc2 Trump has accused \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s administration of \u8220\'20\'1Cabandoning\u8221\'20\'1D people to the crisis and, baselessly, of being short of disaster relief funds due to money spent on undocumented migrants. Such claims are \u8220\'20\'1Cfrankly ridiculous\u8221\'20\'1D and creating a \u8220\'20\'1Ctruly dangerous narrative that is creating this fear\u8221\'20\'1D among affected people, Criswell said.\par \par \uc2 In multiple rallies in the past week, Trump has accused Biden and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  of favoring migrants over disaster-hit areas. \u8220\'20\'1CThey stole the Fema money, just like they stole it from a bank, so they could give it to their illegal immigrants that they want to have vote for them this season,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump has said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKamala spent all her Fema money, billions of dollars, on housing for illegal immigrants.\u8221\'20\'1D Trump added the places worst hit are \u8220\'20\'1Clargely a Republican area so some people say they did it for that reason\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 JD Vance, Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Republican running mate, echoed this theme on Monday, telling Fox News that Fema\u8217\'20\'19s focus on migrants is \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to distract focus from their core job of helping American citizens in their time of need\u8221\'20\'1D. Last week, \uc2 Stephen Miller\uc2 , a far-right Trump adviser, said that \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  turned Fema into an illegal alien resettlement agency.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Fema does, in fact, have a housing program that offers shelter to migrants leaving detention but this is separate from its disaster relief program. \u8220\'20\'1CNo money is being diverted from disaster response needs. None,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House has stated.\par \par \uc2 Congress recently provided an extra $20bn for disaster relief but Biden has warned that more funding will be needed to help the long-term recovery of places increasingly assailed by powerful storms fueled by global heating.\par \par \uc2 Other conspiracy theories and erroneous claims have swirled online and in areas affected by Helene, such as the assertion that Fema will give only $750 to individuals as a loan (it is in fact a grant and can be followed by further claims for more than $40,000) or that the agency is seizing people\u8217\'20\'19s land.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/07/hurricane-helene-trump-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fema chief warns \u8216\'20\'18dangerous\u8217\'20\'19 Trump falsehoods hampering Helene response}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump did not make any public remarks as he paid his respects at the final resting place of a famous rabbi in New York earlier on Monday.\par \par \uc2 But he blasted Biden and Harris over their handling of the Middle East in an interview earlier, accusing the incumbent of having the \u8220\'20\'1Cworst foreign policy of anybody in history probably.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1Cnot listening at all\u8221\'20\'1D to Biden, said Trump \u8211\'20\'13 with the property tycoon lamenting that war-torn Gaza could one day be \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter than Monaco\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The event in Florida is starting now, though Trump is not yet speaking.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s event in Florida is so far running 30 minutes late. We will bring you any important lines from those remarks on the anniversary of the 7 October attacks by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  when they begin.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 A slew of falsehoods about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hurricane-helene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Helene}}}\uc2 , including claims of funds diverted from storm survivors to migrants and even that Democrats somehow directed the hurricane itself, have hampered the response to one of the deadliest hurricanes to ever hit the US, the nation\u8217\'20\'19s top emergency official has warned.\par \par \uc2 Misinformation spread by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , his supporters and others about the hurricane has shrouded the recovery effort for communities shattered by Helene, which tore through five states causing at least 227 deaths and tens of billions of dollars of damage. Many places, such as in western {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/northcarolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 North Carolina}}}\uc2 , are still without a water supply, navigable roads or vital supplies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s frankly disappointing we are having to deal with this narrative, the fact there are a few leaders having a hard time telling the difference between fact and fiction is creating an impedance to our ability to actually get people the help they need,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 Deanne Criswell\uc2 , administrator of the \uc2 Federal Emergency Management Agency\uc2  (Fema), told MSNBC on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/07/hurricane-helene-trump-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fema chief warns \u8216\'20\'18dangerous\u8217\'20\'19 Trump falsehoods hampering Helene response}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is the press pool report \u8211\'20\'13 by the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s own \uc2 David Smith\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 on \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments earlier on Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  not taking her calls about Hurricane Milton.\par \par \uc2 Harris said:\par \par \uc2 Moments of crisis, if nothing else, should really be the moment that anyone who calls themselves a leader says they\u8217\'20\'19re going to put politics aside and put the people first.\par \par \uc2 People are in desperate need of support right now and playing political games at this moment, in these crisis situations \u8211\'20\'13 these are the height of emergency situations \u8211\'20\'13 it is utterly irresponsible and it is selfish and it is about political gamesmanship instead of doing the job that you took an oath to do, which is to put the people first.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier VPOTUS said she had just come off the phone with Fema Administrator \uc2 Deanne Criswell\uc2 . She commented on remarks made by Trump.\par \par \uc2 And I cannot stress enough to all the folks in Florida in the Tampa area, please listen to evacuation orders. Please listen to your local officials because I know a lot of folks out there have survived these hurricanes before; this one is going to be very, very serious and I urge you to grab whatever you need.\par \par \uc2 The other point I\u8217\'20\'19d make is there\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of misinformation being pushed out there by the former president about what is available, particularly for the survivors of Helene. First of all, it\u8217\'20\'19s extraordinarily irresponsible. It\u8217\'20\'19s about him, it\u8217\'20\'19s not about you. The reality is Fema has so many resources that are available to those who desperately need them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  of Florida is reportedly refusing calls about storm recovery from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2 , more than a week after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hurricane-helene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Helene}}}\uc2  hit the state and two days before intensifying {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/07/hurricane-milton-florida-evacuation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Milton}}}\uc2  is expected to hit the south-west of the state.\par \par \uc2 Citing a DeSantis aide, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/kamala-harris/ron-desantis-harris-call-hurricane-helene-political-rcna174276"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NBC News reported}}}\uc2  on Monday that the Republican governor was dodging the Democratic presidential nominee\u8217\'20\'19s calls because they \u8220\'20\'1Cseemed political\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKamala was trying to reach out, and we didn\u8217\'20\'19t answer,\u8221\'20\'1D the DeSantis aide told the outlet. DeSantis does not appear to have spoken to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2 , either, to the aide\u8217\'20\'19s knowledge.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/florida"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Florida}}}\uc2  governor has, however, been in touch with the Fema director, \uc2 Deanne Criswell\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Last week, DeSantis said Biden had called him, but he was flying at the time so could not take the call. A source familiar with the planning for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s trip to north Florida to survey Helene\u8217\'20\'19s damage said that the Biden team had invited DeSantis to the event but their schedules conflicted.\par \par \uc2 The response to Hurricane Helene has become an intense political issue one month before the presidential election. The White House and local Democratic leaders have appealed for an end to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/04/hurricane-helene-conspiracy-theories-election-misinformation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 misinformation about the storm}}}\uc2  and the response to it.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/07/desantis-harris-florida-hurricane-helene-milton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeSantis reportedly refuses Harris\u8217\'20\'19s calls as Florida braces for new hurricane}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 As we wait for Trump to begin delivering his remarks on the October 7 \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attack in Florida, here is where things stand:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  both attended events today in recognition of the first anniversary of the October 7 \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attack against Israel.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Supreme court upheld a ruling that will prevent abortions from being performed in some emergency circumstances in Texas. The court also rejected an attempt by an Alabama fertility clinic to avoid a wrongful death lawsuit that was at the center of a state high court ruling earlier this year that led to IVF access being briefly curtailed in the state\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Harris campaign launched a week-long media blitz, beginning yesterday with an appearance on the podcast Call Her Daddy, that will include appearances with Howard Stern, Stephen Colbert and The View this week.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida is bracing for Hurricane Milton to make landfall. The state\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , has declined to speak with Harris or \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , but says the federal government has fulfilled his requests for aid.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A report by the Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget suggests that both the Harris and Trump campaigns are making promises that will increase US debt, but that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s proposals are more expensive.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will speak shortly in Miami at a commemoration for the victims and hostages of the 7 October \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attacks.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a relatively small affair, some 350 or so seats are laid out in rows in the ballroom at the Trump National golf resort in Doral. Supporters, some wearing red yamakas in the style of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s traditional Maga (Make America great again) caps, passed memorials to those killed or taken hostage a year ago. Rows of candles accompanied pictures of the victims on a table. And outside the resort, in pouring rain, a man help up a sign that said \u8220\'20\'1CThank you Trump for supporting Israel\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former president is expected to turn the event into an attack on \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , whom he has called \u8220\'20\'1Cweak\u8221\'20\'1D over Israel. In recent days he has called for Israel to bomb nuclear facilities in Iran in retaliation for that country\u8217\'20\'19s missile attack on Israel last week.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Monday, Trump visited Ohel Chabad Lubavitch in Queens, New York, before flying to Florida.\par \par \uc2 enltrJewish supporters of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  are gathering at his golf resort in Doral, Miami, where the former president will shortly give remarks on the anniversary of the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  Oct 7 attacks. Will be interesting to hear what he has to say\u8230\'20\'26 a year ago he called \uc2 Hamas\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cvery smart\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xe4E96Q1nT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xe4E96Q1nT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Richard Luscombe (@richlusc) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/richlusc/status/1843404854443565562?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 In response to reports that \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor, w ill not respond to her calls regarding hurricanes Helene and M ilton, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  tells reporters: \u8220\'20\'1CPeople are in desperate need of support right now, and playing political games at this moment \u8230\'20\'26 is just utterly irresponsible, and it is selfish, and it is about political gamesmanship.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrReporter: There are reports that DeSantis is ignoring your calls..\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 : Playing political games at this moment\u8230\'20\'26It's utterly irresponsible and it is selfish and it is about political gamesmanship instead of doing the job that you took an oath to do {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/lySDD98xO9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/lySDD98xO9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Acyn (@Acyn) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Acyn/status/1843403803707744581?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , the Florida governor, delivered remarks on Hurricane Milton\u8217\'20\'19s impending landfall this afternoon. Although DeSantis has declined calls with Biden and Harris, he told reporters that Fema and the Biden administration have fulfilled his requests for aid.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have gotten what we need from the feds. We have been working constructively with all of the local communities,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, before criticizing a reporter\u8217\'20\'19s question about declining calls with the Biden administration. \u8220\'20\'1CSome of these questions are just trying to create some sort of political angle.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrDeSantis: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have made a pre-landfall declaration request from FEMA for support & the federal government has approved a portion of our request for pre-landfall items. And we expect the remaining parts of our request subsequent to landfall for debris and individual assistance,\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaitlan Collins (@kaitlancollins) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/kaitlancollins/status/1843389276924588241?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 enltr'YOUR PUBLICATION WILL TWIST ANYTHING THAT'S DONE [...] THAT'S HOW YOU GET YOUR CLICKS!': Gov. \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  spats with reporter after being questioned about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  phone call and "politics"\par \par \uc2 "Some of these questions are just trying to create some sort of political angle."\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/rRKBGMX4Eg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/rRKBGMX4Eg}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Florida\u8217\'20\'19s Voice (@FLVoiceNews) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/FLVoiceNews/status/1843389663622647831?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/07/desantis-harris-florida-hurricane-helene-milton"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DeSantis refuses Harris\u8217\'20\'19s storm recovery calls as Florida braces for Hurricane Milton}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking on the Call Her Daddy podcast yesterday, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  hit back at Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 remarks about her lack of biological children.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Edward Helmore writes:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  hit back at the Republican Arkansas governor \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s comments that the vice-president and Democratic White House nominee \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t have anything keeping her humble\u8221\'20\'1D because she does not have children of her own.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think she understands that there are a whole lot of women out here who, one, are not aspiring to be humble,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris told the Call Her Daddy podcast host Alex Cooper in a taped interview released on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Sanders, a deputy White House press secretary during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s presidency, told a rally crowd in September that her \u8220\'20\'1Ckids keep me humble.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have anything keeping her humble,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said.\par \par \uc2 In a taped interview with Cooper, Harris said there are \u8220\'20\'1Ca whole lot of women out here who have a lot of love in their life, family in their life and children in their life, and I think it\u8217\'20\'19s really important for women to lift each other up\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/07/kamala-harris-call-her-daddy-podcast-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris hits back at Republican\u8217\'20\'19s remarks about her lack of biological children}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign has announced that the former president will be traveling to Coachella, California \u8211\'20\'13 a city best known for its music festival \u8211\'20\'13 this weekend.\par \par \uc2 The announcement says that, under Democratic leadership, the \u8220\'20\'1Cnotorious \u8216\'20\'18California Dream\u8217\'20\'19 has turned into a nightmare\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrLess than a month left, and Trump is headed to \u8230\'20\'26 Coachella {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/4686k9YGsX"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/4686k9YGsX}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Matt Dixon (@Mdixon55) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Mdixon55/status/1843390200430600620?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Harris campaign officials appear unconcerned about the rally.\par \par \uc2 enltrOh no. This is extremely concerning for our campaign. Please do not go to Coachella, CALIFORNIA 24 days before the election. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/QJoe3Ysyh4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/QJoe3Ysyh4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Ammar Moussa (@ammarmufasa) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ammarmufasa/status/1843389705846755628?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  commemorated the anniversary of 7 October by visiting the grave of Rabbi Menachem Mendel Schneerson, one of the most influential Jewish leaders of the 20th century and a leader of the Chabad-Lubavitch movement, in Queens, New York, today. Trump was joined by family members of Edan Alexander, an Israeli hostage taken by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  one year ago today.\par \par \uc2 He was also joined by conservative political commentator \uc2 Ben Shapiro\uc2 , who shared photos of the event on X:\par \par \uc2 enltrOctober 7 was the greatest massacre of Jews since the Holocaust. It was an honor to join President Trump in NY today to pay our respects and remember the lives lost in the horrific terrorist attack one year ago today. I had the additional honor of being accompanied by Yael, Adi,\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/DdcFwnrWYl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/DdcFwnrWYl}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Ben Shapiro\uc2  (@benshapiro) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/benshapiro/status/1843369062572622229?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 As more news emerges on preparations for Hurricane Milton, including updates on Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 snub of a phone call from Harris, Fema is trying to dispel disinformation about its response to Hurricane Helene.\par \par \uc2 Deanne Criswell\uc2 , who leads Fema, says false claims and conspiracy theories \u8211\'20\'13 spread most prominently by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 are \u8220\'20\'1Cdemoralizing\u8221\'20\'1D aid workers and spreading fear.\par \par \uc2 Republicans, led by Trump, have spread misinformation since Helene made landfall, including rumors that the federal government was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/kamala-harris-donald-trump-hurricane-helene-3097f1706455929adf5a4eb67f9cdf0f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 intentionally withholding aid}}}\uc2  to people in Republican areas, spending {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/trump-brian-kemp-hurricane-helene-biden-75ed7f49ffd1a9b07ba82e18abecaa47"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 all its money to help immigrants}}}\uc2 , and that it used {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/dubai-united-arab-emirates-oman-flooding-cloud-seeding-2f8c12854017e11ac7438579646b3758"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 weather control technology}}}\uc2  to steer Helene toward Republican voters.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/07/hurricane-milton-florida-evacuation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Milton intensifies to category 5 as Florida braces for \u8216\'20\'18major impacts\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/07/marjorie-taylor-greene-hurricane-helene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene condemned over Helene weather conspiracy theory}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and the second gentleman, Doug Emhoff, planted a pomegranate tree outside her residence at the \uc2 United States Naval Observatory\uc2  before taking questions from members of the press.\par \par \uc2 Before doing so, Harris delivered brief remarks:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe dedicate this tree to the 1,200 innocent souls, in an act of pure evil on October 7, 2023, who were massacred by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  terrorists,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, noting the American civilians who were among the dead and evoking the Jewish mourner\u8217\'20\'19s prayer.\par \par \uc2 She also noted: \u8220\'20\'1CI will always make sure Israel has to defend itself\u8221\'20\'1D before adding: \u8220\'20\'1CWe must work to relieve the immense suffering of innocent Palestinians in Gaza, who have experienced so much pain and loss over the year.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrJoin me and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SecondGentleman?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SecondGentleman}}}\uc2  as we speak about the horror of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 October 7, 2023 terrorist attack in Israel and as we dedicate a tree at the Vice President\u8217\'20\'19s Residence to honor the 1,200 innocent people killed in that heinous attack. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/22fl0rvsXB"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/22fl0rvsXB}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  (@VP) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/VP/status/1843381479994253430?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The Trump campaign is already criticizing the event.\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala uses her remarks on the one-year anniversary of the worst attack against the Jewish people since the Holocaust to play both sides and implicitly criticize Israel's right to self-defense {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/V3QmRJ5vL5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/V3QmRJ5vL5}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Trump War Room (@TrumpWarRoom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TrumpWarRoom/status/1843383954239565890?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris to mark 7 October with memorial tree planting\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , together with the second gentleman, Doug Emhoff, will in a few minutes hold a tree-planting ceremony to mark the one-year anniversary of the 7 October attack in Israel.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president will then deliver remarks at the event held at her residence at the \uc2 United States Naval Observatory\uc2 , which is about three miles from the White House in Washington DC.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s Harris\u8217\'20\'19s only scheduled public speech today, and we will let you know what she has to say.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 DeSantis declines to take Harris's call on Hurricane Milton\par \par \uc2 As Hurricane Milton churns towards Florida\u8217\'20\'19s west coast, ABC News reports that the state\u8217\'20\'19s Republican governor, \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2 , declined to speak to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A nationally prominent conservative, DeSantis mounted a failed campaign for the Republican presidential nomination, and since endorsed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Asked about the episode at the White House press briefing earlier today, press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said it was the governor\u8217\'20\'19s choice to speak to Harris or not:\par \par \uc2 enltrRon DeSantis has refused to take a call from VP Harris on Hurricane Milton, source tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ABC?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @ABC}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 White House Press Sec says "If you have POTUS & VP reaching out to offer up assistance...the governor, it's up to him if he wants to respond to us or not."\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Selina Wang (@selinawangtv) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/selinawangtv/status/1843359734168179085?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reproductive freedom is a \u8220\'20\'1Cdeal-breaker\u8221\'20\'1D issue for voters, especially women, which is fueling Democratic candidates in races that will decide major offices from the state house to the White House.\par \par \uc2 That was the top line from a briefing to reporters by representatives from Emily\u8217\'20\'19s List, the fundraising juggernaut that backs Democratic women candidates who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe question is not, will \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  drive votes in this election? It is, how far, how wide, how deep does that impact go?\u8221\'20\'1D said one senior member of the organization. The briefing was conducted without attribution to allow representatives to speak more freely.\par \par \uc2 She said the issue has allowed Democrats to compete in areas where they otherwise would not typically be competitive, like a seat in Wisconsin and one in Pennsylvania. She also said this election, women candidates who were not previously politically active have \u8220\'20\'1Centered the political ring arena because of the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\u8221\'20\'1D. She pointed to Kristin Lyerly, an ob-gyn, who is running for a seat in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 Polls have consistently found that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a top issue, often second to the economy. But what makes the issue so potent, she said, is how many voters, perhaps a decisive share of voters, view it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a deal-breaker issue,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen they learn information about a Republican who is on the wrong side of this issue that becomes a deal breaker for them, and they just won\u8217\'20\'19t entertain it any further.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another official emphasized that Republicans\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to re-cast their long-held positions on the issue underlined how important the issue would be this cycle.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are going through the collapse of 40 years of Republican branding around the phrase \u8216\'20\'18pro-life,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1Dthat official said. \u8220\'20\'1CVoters hear that now, and they assume that a \u8216\'20\'18pro-life\u8217\'20\'19 politician is for an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban with no exceptions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Flirting with eugenics, Trump says: \u8216\'20\'18We got a lot of bad genes in our country right now\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 In an interview earlier today with conservative broadcaster \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2 , \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  used terminology associated with eugenics to attack migrants.\par \par \uc2 The remark came as the former president discussed the alleged harm done by new arrivals to the United States, saying many were \u8220\'20\'1Cmurderers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNow, a murderer, it\u8217\'20\'19s in their genes,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump continued. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd we got a lot of bad genes in our country right now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It was language similar to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/science/2022/jun/19/where-science-meets-fiction-the-dark-history-of-eugenics"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the beliefs of eugenics}}}\uc2 , which emerged in the late 19th century and held that human ills could be combatted through selective breeding. The theory is today regarded as both inaccurate and racist.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s audio of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s remark:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump rants about \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and migrants to \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2  and says, "we got a lot of bad genes in our country right now" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ybKFF9TDf3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ybKFF9TDf3}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Aaron Rupar (@atrupar) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/atrupar/status/1843308705493966858?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House warns supreme court has allowed Texas to deny women abortions in emergencies\par \par \uc2 At the ongoing White House press briefing, press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said that the supreme court has effectively allowed Texas to deny women abortions even in emergencies, by refusing to take up a Biden administration lawsuit against the state today.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday we saw the supreme court decision and what it means that women in Texas could still be denied critical emergency medical care, because of the state\u8217\'20\'19s dangerous and extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans,\u8221\'20\'1D Jean-Pierre said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have seen and have heard the horrific stories of women being denied the care they need because of these laws.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jean-Pierre also noted that a Georgia court had allowed the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban to go back into effect, and said:\par \par \uc2 All of these laws were made possible when the former president handicapped three Supreme Court justices to overturn Roe v Wade. They are creating chaos and confusion for women and doctors.\par \par \uc2 The administration has been clear that all patients, including women experiencing pregnancy loss and other pregnancy related emergency, must be able to access the emergency medical care they need, and that is required by federal law. The stories we hear of women being denied care they need in emergency situation [are] completely unacceptable.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Georgia supreme court\u8217\'20\'19s reinstatement a little earlier of a six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in the state is provoking reaction.\par \par \uc2 The ban was struck down a week ago and now revived while the court considers more fully the state\u8217\'20\'19s appeal against the ban\u8217\'20\'19s striking.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted on X that: \u8220\'20\'1CDespite this devastating setback, we are prepared to fight like hell when the case goes before the Georgia Supreme Court. This is NOT over, and we are NOT backing down.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrDespite this devastating setback, we are prepared to fight like hell when the case goes before the Georgia Supreme Court. This is NOT over, and we are NOT backing down. Are you with us? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/jOwSIx5zt4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/jOwSIx5zt4}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  (@ReproRights) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ReproRights/status/1843336508084003136?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union of Georgia decried today\u8217\'20\'19s decision.\par \par \uc2 Andrea Young, executive director, said: \u8220\'20\'1CElected officials in our state continue their disrespect of women, treating our bodies as state-owned property. We will persist, using all lawful means to restore dignity, full citizenship and a right to privacy for Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s women.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8226\'20\'22 This post was amended on 8 October 2024. An earlier version misspelt Andrea Young\u8217\'20\'19s first name as \u8220\'20\'1CAndrew\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrToday, the Supreme Court of Georgia ruled to reinstate Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s 6-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban just one week after a lower court ruling allowed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics to resume \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care beyond the earliest weeks of pregnancy. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/GRInIhThld"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/GRInIhThld}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ACLU of Georgia (@ACLUofGA) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ACLUofGA/status/1843349827318612043?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.39am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here is some more detail on the new ruling by Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court reviving the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban on abortions, a week after the ban {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/georgia-abortion-ban-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was struck down}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit challenging the ban was brought by Atlanta-based SisterSong Women of Color Reproductive Justice Collective.\par \par \uc2 Today, the Georgia Supreme Court sided with anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists. Every minute this harmful six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is in place, Georgians suffer,\u8221\'20\'1D SisterSong\u8217\'20\'19s executive director, Monica Simpson, said in a statement, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The office of Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s governor, \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , a Republican, did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 The law bans almost all abortions after what it labels a \u8220\'20\'1Chuman heartbeat\u8221\'20\'1D is detected, typically around six weeks. In fact, at six weeks a fetus has not yet developed a heart, but there may be rudimentary, pulse-like signals. This is before many women know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 The ban was passed in 2019 during \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s presidency but did not take effect until the end of Roe v Wade in 2022.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s Simpson speaking at an event last month.\par \par \uc2 enltrOur keynote speaker and performer, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/monicarsimpson?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @monicarsimpson}}}\uc2 , joins us as we close an incredible two days! {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/powerplus2024?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #powerplus2024}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/nuzlWd4Em9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/nuzlWd4Em9}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 IWPR (@IWPResearch) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/IWPResearch/status/1838631402406822394?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September 24, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.17pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia supreme court reinstates \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban\par \par \uc2 Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s highest court on has today reinstated a ban on nearly all abortions in the state after about six weeks of pregnancy while it considers the US state\u8217\'20\'19s appeal of last week\u8217\'20\'19s ruling by a lower court judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/georgia-abortion-ban-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blocking the law}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The order from the Supreme Court of Georgia allows the ban to take effect at 5pm ET today, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 A week ago, Fulton county superior judge Robert McBurney struck down the state\u8217\'20\'19s six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, ruling that the ban is unconstitutional and blocking it from being enforced.\par \par \uc2 McBurney ruled that the state\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws must revert to what they were before the six-week ban \u8211\'20\'13 known as the Life Act \u8211\'20\'13 was passed in 2019. The ban was blocked as long as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v Wade}}}\uc2  was the law of the land, but went into effect after the \uc2 US supreme court{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jun/24/roe-v-wade-overturned-abortion-summary-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned Roe}}}\uc2  in 2022.\par \par \uc2 So for one week, abortions became legal in Georgia again up until about 22 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 The day so far\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/07/us-election-donald-trump-kamala-harris-joe-biden-supreme-court-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with:block-6703df228f08b6b1865d4cdd#block-6703df228f08b6b1865d4cdd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a media blitz}}}\uc2 , with appearances planned on everything from The View to Howard Stern in the days to come. We will see her later tonight on 60 Minutes, one of the most watched news programs in the country, but based on what we have seen so far, the vice-president doesn\u8217\'20\'19t seem interested in breaking new ground. In excerpts released by \uc2 CBS\uc2 , she {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/07/us-election-donald-trump-kamala-harris-joe-biden-supreme-court-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with:block-6703d9e68f0820cc609e8513#block-6703d9e68f0820cc609e8513"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sidestepped}}}\uc2  a question about how she would cajole Congress into approving higher taxes on the rich, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/07/us-election-donald-trump-kamala-harris-joe-biden-supreme-court-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with:block-6703fb6f8f08ecd425735075#block-6703fb6f8f08ecd425735075"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demurred}}}\uc2  when asked if she regarded Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  as a \u8220\'20\'1Cclose ally\u8221\'20\'1D. Meanwhile, the supreme court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/07/us-election-donald-trump-kamala-harris-joe-biden-supreme-court-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with:block-6704100a8f0867fd8f33969a#block-6704100a8f0867fd8f33969a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 began a new term}}}\uc2  with cases dealing with transgender rights and the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s effort to curb ghost guns on its docket. It also declined to weigh in on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/07/us-election-donald-trump-kamala-harris-joe-biden-supreme-court-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with:block-6703ecca8f089afff9e843a4#block-6703ecca8f089afff9e843a4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a wrongful death lawsuit}}}\uc2  involving an Alabama clinic at the center of the controversy over IVF care, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/07/us-election-donald-trump-kamala-harris-joe-biden-supreme-court-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with:block-6703e7e98f08b6b1865d4d58#block-6703e7e98f08b6b1865d4d58"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Biden administration challenge}}}\uc2  to Texas\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban and how it affects carrying out the procedure in an emergency.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else has happened today:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s policies would add more to the national debt than \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s, an analysis by a nonpartisan budget watchdog {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/07/us-election-donald-trump-kamala-harris-joe-biden-supreme-court-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with:block-6703f4b48f089afff9e84429#block-6703f4b48f089afff9e84429"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 found}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden, Harris and Trump are all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/07/us-election-donald-trump-kamala-harris-joe-biden-supreme-court-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with:block-6703d0668f089afff9e841d2#block-6703d0668f089afff9e841d2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 marking}}}\uc2  today\u8217\'20\'19s one-year anniversary of the 7 October attack in Israel.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/oct/07/us-election-donald-trump-kamala-harris-joe-biden-supreme-court-us-politics-live-latest-news?page=with:block-670405b38f08ecd425735102#block-670405b38f08ecd425735102"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 is bracing}}}\uc2  as Hurricane Milton, which has just been upgraded to a category 5 storm, churns towards it west coast, even as it continues to recover from Hurricane Helene.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court to weigh transgender rights, ghost gun rule in new term\par \par \uc2 The supreme court began a new term today, where the conservative-dominated body could issue major rulings on transgender rights, rules to curb the spread of ghost guns, and a high-profile death penalty case.\par \par \uc2 The court will hear cases in the months to come, and likely issue rulings next year. There is also the chance the justices could be drawn into disputes over the November elections.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/supreme-court-death-sentence-ghost-guns-transgender-rights-926e78c1100f3201fbd99b3d1ef2b747"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 From the Associated Press}}}\uc2 , here are some of the cases they will be considering, starting with ghost guns:\par \par \uc2 The justices will hear a case Tuesday on regulations for ghost guns, privately made weapons that are hard for police to track because they don\u8217\'20\'19t have serial numbers.\par \par \uc2 The number of the firearms found at crime scenes has soared in recent years, from fewer than 4,000 in 2018 to nearly 20,000 recovered by law enforcement in 2021, according to Justice Department data.\par \par \uc2 The numbers have been declining in multiple cities since the Biden administration began requiring background checks and age verification for ghost gun kits that can be bought online.\par \par \uc2 But manufacturers and gun rights groups argue that the administration overstepped and the rule should be overturned.\par \par \uc2 The rights of transgender minors:\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the court\u8217\'20\'19s most closely watched case so far this year is a fight over transgender rights.\par \par \uc2 The case over state bans on gender-affirming care comes as Republican-led states enact a variety of restrictions, including school sports participation, bathroom usage and drag shows.\par \par \uc2 The administration and Democratic-led states have extended protections for transgender people, though the Supreme Court has separately prohibited the administration from enforcing a new federal regulation that seeks to protect transgender students.\par \par \uc2 The justices will weigh a Tennessee law that restricts puberty blockers and hormone therapy for transgender minors. The case does not yet have a hearing date but will likely be argued in December.\par \par \uc2 And the case of death row inmate Richard Glossip :\par \par \uc2 In the decades since Richard Glossip was sentenced to die over a 1997 murder-for-hire scheme, the case has become a rare one where prosecutors are conceding mistakes.\par \par \uc2 Oklahoma\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general has joined with Glossip in seeking to overturn his murder conviction and death sentence.\par \par \uc2 Despite those doubts, an Oklahoma appeals court has upheld Glossip\u8217\'20\'19s conviction, and the state\u8217\'20\'19s pardon and parole board deadlocked in a vote to grant him clemency.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate JD Vance will host a town hall in Greensboro, North Carolina on Thursday, his campaign announced.\par \par \uc2 The Ohio senator and vice-presidential aspirant appears set to continue his criticisms of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s response to Hurricane Helene, which has caused widespread damage to the western part of the swing state.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has completely failed the people of North Carolina. Not only has she released historic inflation and a flood of convicted illegal immigrants onto them, but she completely left North Carolinians behind in the wake of devastation post-Hurricane Helene. Harris\u8217\'20\'19 failures have placed a huge burden on taxpayers, and it shows how little she cares about the well-being of Tar Heel State families,\u8221\'20\'1D the campaign said as it announced the event.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Florida braces as category 5 Hurricane Milton nears\par \par \uc2 Days after weathering Hurricane Helene, Florida is now in the path of Hurricane Milton, which has just been upgraded to a category 5 storm. The hurricane has the potential to become the latest crisis on \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s plate just weeks before the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s the latest on the approaching storm, from the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/anna-betts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Anna Betts}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/07/hurricane-milton-florida-evacuation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Milton predicted to become category 5 storm as Florida braces for \u8216\'20\'18major impacts\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 North Carolina\u8217\'20\'19s Republican senator \uc2 Thom Tillis\uc2  is not happy about the Harris campaign using his words to criticize \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump and his running mate JD Vance have tried to turn Hurricane Helene\u8217\'20\'19s devastation of North Carolina and other parts of the southeast into a campaign issue, by accusing the Biden administration, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  by extension, of ignoring the plight of those affected.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the Harris campaign used Tillis\u8217\'20\'19s comments about the storm in a tweet:\par \par \uc2 undltrcc: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/realDonaldTrump?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @realdonaldtrump}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/xd9DjuLG3V"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/xd9DjuLG3V}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kamala HQ (@KamalaHQ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KamalaHQ/status/1843064213096354103?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 To which Tillis responded today:\par \par \uc2 enltrVP Harris: I was talking about politicians like YOU using this disaster for political posturing. Claiming to be \u8220\'20\'1Cworking around the clock\u8221\'20\'1D while you don\u8217\'20\'19t even plug in your headphones for a staged photo-op. Where were YOU as Ft. Liberty troops were standing by for days? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ncpol?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ncpol}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/azzKEA6yLx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/azzKEA6yLx}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Thom Tillis\uc2  (@ThomTillis) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ThomTillis/status/1843302920084976027?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 Tillis has broken with the GOP on issues like gun control and LGBTQ+ rights, leading his state party to censure him last year:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/12/tom-tillis-censure-gun-control-support-lgbtq-north-carolina"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republicans censure senator for backing LGBTQ+ rights and gun control}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris sidesteps when asked if Israel's Netanyahu is a 'close ally'\par \par \uc2 In her forthcoming interview with \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 60 Minutes program, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  did not quite say yes when ask asked if she would consider Israeli prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Ca real close ally\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think, with all due respect, the better question is do we have an important alliance between the American people and the Israeli people, and the answer to that question is yes,\u8221\'20\'1D the vice-president replied in an excerpt from her forthcoming interview on the popular news program.\par \par \uc2 The US relationship with Israel has grown fraught over the past year, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s efforts to encourage a ceasefire in Gaza have failed and the conflict has expended into Lebanon. The issue is particularly perilous for Democrats, who are facing a backlash from some voters, including Arab and Muslim communities in battleground state Michigan, over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Gaza following the 7 October attack.\par \par \uc2 Harris avoided talking about Gaza in the 60 Minutes interview, instead noting that US military aid has helped protect the country from volleys of missiles shot by Iran. Here\u8217\'20\'19s the full clip:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 National debt would grow more under Trump than Harris - budget watchdog\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s policies would send the national debt higher than those proposed by \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , a nonpartisan budgetary watchdog has found.\par \par \uc2 Both candidates have pitched themselves to voters are responsible stewards of the nation\u8217\'20\'19s economy and the government\u8217\'20\'19s spending, while simultaneously proposing expensive new policies. Harris has focused on efforts to fight poverty, making housing more affordable and improve health care, while Trump has floated lowering taxes and spending more on border security and the military.\par \par \uc2 An analysis from the Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget finds that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s policies would send the federal debt climbing by as much as $15.2t through 2035, and as little $1.4t. Over the same period, Harris\u8217\'20\'19s policies could send it up by as much as $8.1t, or nothing at all:\par \par \uc2 enltr?? NEW DEBT PROJECTIONS ??\par \par \uc2 In the first and comprehensive analysis of the candidates\u8217\'20\'19 plans, we find Vice President Harris would add $3.5 trillion to the debt ($0 to $8.1t) and President Trump would add $7.5 trillion to the debt ($1.4t to $15.2t).\par \par \uc2 See {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/LGMIUjlxIs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/LGMIUjlxIs}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EmdtHzCW7I"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EmdtHzCW7I}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Marc Goldwein\uc2  (@MarcGoldwein) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/MarcGoldwein/status/1843276263794074024?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The project comes as the US deals with a yawning budget deficit and a high debt-to-GDP ratio, which have been fueled by long-term expenditures such as paying for Social Security and Medicare, and short-term emergency responses, such as the stimulus measures approved to offset the impact of Covid-19.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s media blitz has not gone unnoticed by the Trump campaign.\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his allies have lately tried to make Hurricane Helene\u8217\'20\'19s devastation of a swath of the southeastern United States \u8211\'20\'13 including battleground states North Carolina and Georgia \u8211\'20\'13 into a political issue. This morning, his campaign juxtaposed Harris\u8217\'20\'19s comments in her interview with podcast Call Her Daddy with images of the damage:\par \par \uc2 enltrKamala was \u8220\'20\'1Cfeeling great\u8221\'20\'1D as Americans clung to their rooftops in desperation amid the botched federal hurricane response.\par \par \uc2 Kamala is in this race for one reason only: herself. She\u8217\'20\'19s a disgusting, selfish person. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EnhOC3sAi8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EnhOC3sAi8}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Trump War Room (@TrumpWarRoom) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TrumpWarRoom/status/1843112318374482303?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 7, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 The supreme court today also rejected an attempt by an Alabama fertility clinic to avoid a wrongful death lawsuit that was at the center of a state high court ruling earlier this year that led to IVF access being briefly curtailed in the state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/legal/us-supreme-court-rejects-ivf-clinics-appeal-alabama-embryo-ruling-2024-10-07/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Reuters reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  turned away on Monday a bid by an Alabama fertility clinic to avoid a wrongful death claim in a civil lawsuit over the destruction of a couple\u8217\'20\'19s frozen embryo in a case that has caused concern over the legal landscape for in vitro fertilization.\par \par \uc2 The justices denied an appeal by the Mobile-based Center for Reproductive Medicine of a ruling by Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s top court allowing the suit by Felicia Burdick-Aysenne and Scott Aysenne to proceed after deciding that frozen embryos are considered children under state law. The clinic has called the ruling a violation of its constitutional right to due process.\par \par \uc2 The couple sued the Center for Reproductive Medicine and the hospital housing the clinic in 2021 for wrongful death and negligence after a patient at the hospital gained unauthorized access to the cryogenic embryo storage area and removed several embryos, dropping them on the floor, including the couple\u8217\'20\'19s one remaining embryo.\par \par \uc2 The Republican-controlled \uc2 Alabama Supreme Court\uc2  in February ruled in the case that under an Alabama law called the Wrongful Death of a Minor Act, \u8220\'20\'1Cunborn children are \u8216\'20\'18children,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D even outside the womb, allowing the lawsuit seeking monetary damages from the clinic to move forward.\par \par \uc2 The decision prompted IVF providers in Alabama to suspend treatments, while many health advocates and Democratic officials across the United States held up the decision as offered further evidence that \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  are under assault in the aftermath of the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 2022 decision rolling back \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 IVF, which helps couples experiencing infertility issues, is a procedure in which eggs are removed from a woman\u8217\'20\'19s ovary and combined with sperm in a laboratory dish to form embryos. The embryos can be frozen for future implantation.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Supreme court maintains ban on emergency abortions that violate Texas law\par \par \uc2 The supreme court has upheld a ruling that will prevent abortions from being performed in some emergency circumstances in the state, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/supreme-court-emergency-abortion-texas-bf79fafceba4ab9df9df2489e5d43e72?taid=6703e77b7aa3400001ed4e75&utm_campaign=TrueAnthem&utm_medium=AP&utm_source=Twitter"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Associated Press reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Texas is the most populous state in the country with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, and the Biden administration had sued to ensure abortions are available for women suffering medical emergencies, citing a separate supreme court ruling from earlier this year in a case involving Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s how the court weighed in on Texas\u8217\'20\'19s law, from the AP:\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court on Monday let stand a decision barring emergency abortions that violate the law in Texas, which has one of the country\u8217\'20\'19s strictest \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans.\par \par \uc2 Without detailing their reasoning, the justices kept in place a lower court order that said hospitals cannot be required to provide pregnancy terminations that would violate Texas law.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration had asked the justices to throw out the lower court order, arguing that hospitals have to perform abortions in emergency situations under federal law. The administration pointed to the Supreme Court\u8217\'20\'19s action in a similar case from Idaho earlier this year in which the justices narrowly allowed emergency abortions to resume while a lawsuit continues.\par \par \uc2 The administration also cited a Texas Supreme Court ruling that said doctors do not have to wait until a woman\u8217\'20\'19s life is in immediate danger to provide an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legally. The administration said it brings Texas in line with federal law and means the lower court ruling is not necessary.\par \par \uc2 Texas asked the justices to leave the order in place, saying the state Supreme Court ruling meant Texas law, unlike Idaho\u8217\'20\'19s, does have an exception for the health of a pregnant patient and there\u8217\'20\'19s no conflict between federal and state law.\par \par \uc2 Doctors have said the law remains dangerously vague after a medical board refused to specify exactly which conditions qualify for the exception.\par \par \uc2 There has been a spike in complaints that pregnant women in medical distress have been turned away from emergency rooms in Texas and elsewhere as hospitals grapple with whether standard care could violate strict laws against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s running mate, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , is also doing his own media blitz.\par \par \uc2 Her campaign says Walz will be on Jimmy Kimmel Live tonight, and also do an interview with a major US podcast, though they did not say which one. An interview the Minnesota governor gave to 60 Minutes will also air this evening.\par \par \uc2 He will campaign in Reno, Nevada and Arizona, on Tuesday and Wednesday, respectively, where will do interviews with local media and Hispanic outlets.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris plans interviews with Howard Stern, Stephen Colbert and The View\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s media blitz will take her to New York City tomorrow, where the vice-president will appear on three high-profile programs with an eye towards boosting her candidacy ahead of the 5 November election.\par \par \uc2 Harris plans to talk with Howard Stern, a one-time shock jock who has remade himself as an in-depth interviewer, her campaign said. Also on her itinerary is an appearance on The Late Show with Stephen Colbert, whose host has long delighted in pointing out the absurdities of US politics, particularly on the right.\par \par \uc2 Harris will finally appear on The View, much as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  did two weeks ago, and put her policies before the talkshow\u8217\'20\'19s daytime viewership.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris questioned on how she'll get tax rise for the rich through Congress\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  may be doing more media interviews in the final weeks before the 5 November election, but that doesn\u8217\'20\'19t necessarily mean she is saying all that much.\par \par \uc2 CBS\uc2  this morning released a portion of her interview on their high-profile broadcast news staple, 60 Minutes. It shows Harris telling correspondent Bill Whitaker that she supports higher taxes on the wealthy (as does \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and most Democrats in Congress), but sidestepping a question on how she\u8217\'20\'19ll get such a plan through Congress. From \uc2 CBS\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 VICE-PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS: Well, one of the things is I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna make sure that the richest among us who can afford it pay their fair share in taxes. It is not right that teachers and nurses and firefighters are paying a higher tax rate than billionaires and the biggest corporations.\par \par \uc2 VICE-PRESIDENT \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 : And I plan on making that fair.\par \par \uc2 BILL WHITAKER: But we\u8217\'20\'19re dealing with the real world here.\par \par \uc2 VICE-PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS: But the real world includes\u8211\'20\'13\par \par \uc2 BILL WHITAKER: How are you gonna get this through Congress?\par \par \uc2 VICE-PRESIDENT \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 : You know, when you talk quietly with a lot of folks in Congress, they know exactly what I\u8217\'20\'19m talking about \u8216\'20\'18cause their constituents know exactly what I\u8217\'20\'19m talking about. Their constituents are those firefighters and teachers and nurses.\par \par \uc2 Whitaker is getting at a real issue of concern for Democrats. While they may be able to claw back the majority in the House of Representatives from the GOP in November, their ability to maintain control of the Senate hinges on the re-election of two senators from red states, a tough task that they may not be able to pull off. Should they fail but Harris take the White House, she would be the first president since 1989 to be inaugurated without her party in control of Congress, and in this era of heightened partisanship, that may prove fatal for her prospects of passing any significant legislation in the first two years of her term.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps Harris will elaborate on what she would do in this situation when the full 60 Minutes interview airs tonight at 8pm.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 House speaker Mike Johnson raised eyebrows yesterday when in an interview on ABC News he described being asked what the result of the last presidential election was as a \u8220\'20\'1Cgotcha game\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 ABC\u8217\'20\'19s George Stephanopoulos asked Johnson if he could say \u8220\'20\'1Cunequivocally that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  won the 2020 election and Trump lost\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Johnson would only reply \u8220\'20\'1Cthis is the game that is always played by mainstream media with mainstream Republicans. It\u8217\'20\'19s a gotcha game. We\u8217\'20\'19re not going to talk about what happened in 2020. I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to engage in it. We\u8217\'20\'19re not talking about that. I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to play the game.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden, Harris and Trump to mark 7 October anniversary\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  are among the global leaders commemorating the anniversary of the 7 October attack in Israel today, as is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 11.45am ET, the president will hold a ceremony at the White House, where he\u8217\'20\'19ll conduct a yahrzeit candle lighting alongside an unnamed rabbi. Harris and her husband, Doug Emhoff, will at 4pm plant a tree on the grounds of the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s residence in honor of the lives lost in the attack. Harris will also give a speech.\par \par \uc2 Trump will mark the occasion with two events: a visit to the grave of Menachem Mendel Schneerson in New York City, then a speech at his golf club in Doral, Florida later on, Politico {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2024/10/07/how-us-leaders-are-remembering-oct-7-00182671?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 We have a live blog covering the latest on the global commemorations of the attack, as well as the spiraling crisis in the Middle East. You can find it here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/oct/07/middle-east-crisis-live-updates-israel-hezbollah-strikes-october-7-beirut-lebanon-war-news"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Middle East crisis live: 10 firefighters killed by Israeli strike in southern Lebanon, officials say, as vigils mark 7 October anniversary}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Nate Cohn at the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  has also had a look at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/10/07/upshot/polling-trump-harris-election.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest polling figures}}}\uc2 , and has come to the conclusion that polling averages show \u8220\'20\'1C \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  essentially tied across the seven battleground states considered likeliest to decide the presidency, with neither ahead by enough to count as even a modest favorite\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has a light schedule for today. At 11.45am, along with the first lady, he is expected to participate in a candle lighting event at the White House to mark the one-year anniversary of the 7 October attack in Israel. After his regular briefing he is then expected to be briefed on his administration\u8217\'20\'19s response to Hurricane Helene and preparations for Hurricane Milton.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 Sidney Blumenthal, former senior adviser to Bill and \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , has written a lengthy piece for the Guardian today arguing that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/07/donald-trumps-hitlerian-logic-is-no-mistake"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Hitlerian logic is no mistake}}}\uc2  but a deliberate ploy.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2024/oct/07/donald-trumps-hitlerian-logic-is-no-mistake"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump\u8217\'20\'19s Hitlerian logic is no mistake | Sidney Blumenthal}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 A report by the Committee for a Responsible Federal Budget\u8217\'20\'19s report, released on Monday, suggests that both candidates in the election are making promises that will increase US debt, but that it is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s proposals that are more expensive.\par \par \uc2 Tami Luhby {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/10/07/politics/debt-harris-trump-proposals/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports for CNN}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 The national debt would soar by trillions of dollars more regardless of who wins the election, further compounding the country\u8217\'20\'19s fiscal problems. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 plan would boost the debt by $3.5tn over the next decade, while Trump\u8217\'20\'19s platform would cause it to spike by $7.5tn. The watchdog group\u8217\'20\'19s analysis is the latest in a series of reviews of the candidates\u8217\'20\'19 plans, which generally find that Trump\u8217\'20\'19s proposals would have a bigger impact on the national debt than those of Harris.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.36am BST\par \par \uc2 Harris told failure to connect with blue-collar workers could hurt Michigan and Pennsylvania chances\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has been warned that her bid to win the key battleground states of Michigan and Pennsylvania risks being undermined by her failure to connect with unionized blue-collar workers in the same way that \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  historically has done.\par \par \uc2 Jonathan Kott, a Democratic strategist and former Senate aide told the Hill website that the current president is a tough act for Harris to follow in that regard.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is the most pro-union president ever,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CHe was the only president to be on a union picket line, he\u8217\'20\'19s so over-the-top pro-union.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another Democratic strategist, Ray Zaccaro, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4916950-harris-lacks-traction-union-voters/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told the website}}}\uc2  : \u8220\'20\'1CBiden has had a special relationship with labor throughout his entire career. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think there\u8217\'20\'19s anything particularly lacking in Harris\u8217\'20\'19s position on labor, but there probably are some stylistic and relationship differences for her to overcome.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Zaccaro warned: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is a movement within the labor world that is more aligned with Maga, protectionism, nationalist identity,\u8221\'20\'1D adding that some union voters increasingly support \u8220\'20\'1Csome of the messaging that the Trump campaign is putting out\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 3.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.15am BST\par \par \uc2 Florida governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has told residents of the state they have a couple of days to prepare before Hurricane Milton hits. He said: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think there\u8217\'20\'19s any scenario where we don\u8217\'20\'19t have major impacts at this point.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou have time to prepare \u8211\'20\'13 all day Monday, probably all day Tuesday to be sure your hurricane preparedness plan is in place,\u8221\'20\'1D DeSantis said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf you\u8217\'20\'19re on that west coast of Florida, barrier islands, just assume you\u8217\'20\'19ll be asked to leave.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 AP reports DeSantis expanded his state of emergency declaration Sunday to 51 counties and said Floridians should prepare for more power outages and disruption, making sure they have a week\u8217\'20\'19s worth of food and water and are ready to hit the road.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.53am BST\par \par \uc2 Speaking at his rally in Juneau, Wisconsin, last night, former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said he was looking for a \u8220\'20\'1Cmandate\u8221\'20\'1D victory in Nove mber\u8217\'20\'19s election. The current polling is tight, suggesting that the outcome is unlikely to deliver that for either candidate.\par \par \uc2 CNN\u8217\'20\'19s senior data reporter Harry Enten {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://edition.cnn.com/2024/10/06/politics/video/harry-enten-polling-harris-trump-digvid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most recent round-up}}}\uc2  on the state of polling in the key swing states that will decide the election suggests that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has the edge in the Great Lake battleground states of Pennsylvania, Michigan, Wisconsin, while Trump is looking stronger in the southern sunbelt states.\par \par \uc2 However, Enten notes that all of the leads of one or two points in these states are \u8220\'20\'1Cwell within the margin of error and too close to call\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 As it stands he suggests Harris would end up with \u8220\'20\'1C276 electoral votes, slightly more than the 270 she needs to win\u8221\'20\'1D, but he said if the polls have underestimated Trump\u8217\'20\'19s support \u8211\'20\'13 as they did in 2020 \u8211\'20\'13 then he could romp home. Likewise, if the polls are underestimating Democratic party support \u8211\'20\'13 as they did in 2022 \u8211\'20\'13 then she could even reach as many as 319 electoral votes. In a nutshell, all bets are off.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  seeks to gain election edge over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with media blitz\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has begun what has been described as a week-long media blitz with an appearance on Sunday night on the podcast Call Her Daddy.\par \par \uc2 During the interview with Alex Cooper, Harris addressed topics including \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reproductive healthcare, housing and student debt relief.\par \par \uc2 Harris said Trump\u8217\'20\'19s repeated claim that Democrats support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cafter birth\u8221\'20\'1D is a \u8220\'20\'1Clie\u8221\'20\'1D, and that it was insulting to claim that women in their ninth month of pregnancy are electing to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 She also rebuked Arkansas governor \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2 , who had suggested Harris \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t have anything keeping her humble\u8221\'20\'1D because she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have children.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think she understands that there are a whole lot of women out here who are not aspiring to be humble,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have our family by blood and then we have our family by love. And I have both.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harris said economic conditions hinder people having a family, and suggested her aim to build 3m new homes by the end of her first term would assist with that.\par \par \uc2 Harris said: \u8220\'20\'1CI think that most Americans want leaders who understand that the measure of their strength is not based on who you beat down. The real measure of the strength of a leader is based on who you lift up.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cooper has made a point of also asking Trump on to the show if he wants to appear.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 1.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.49am BST\par \par \uc2 Welcome and opening summary \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our rolling coverage of the 2024 US presidential election campaign. Today both vice-president \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  will attend ceremonies to mark the one year anniversary of the 7 October attack on Israel by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Harris is expected to speak at an event at the White House, while Trump will be appearing at a Florida golf course. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will also mark the occasion with an event at the White House.\par \par \uc2 Here are the headlines \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Polling continues to show that November\u8217\'20\'19s election is too close to call.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  appeared on the Call Her Daddy podcast on Sunday, discussing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reproductive healthcare, housing and student debt relief.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  said during an appearance on Fox News that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s agenda would destroy the US economy.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  held a rally in Juneau, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 JD Vance has suggested a second Trump administration would defund \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The supreme court begins sitting again this week with the regulation of ghost guns and transgender rights on their agenda.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Florida is gearing up for what could be the biggest evacuations since 2017 as Hurricane Milton strengthens.\par \par \uc2 It is Martin Belam with you here to start with. You can get in touch with me at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:martin.belam@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 martin.belam@theguardian.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241007eka7000xe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
