\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Georgia supreme court reinstates six-week  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Carter Sherman \par \uc2 468 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2024\par 19:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ruling comes just a week after a judge restored broad access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the swing state\par \par \uc2 Just one week after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/state-of-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Georgia}}}\uc2  judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/georgia-abortion-ban-overturned"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 restored broad access}}}\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state by blocking its six-week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/roe-v-wade"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ban, the Georgia supreme court ruled on Monday to reinstate the ban.\par \par \uc2 The ban will take effect at 5pm local time on Monday and remain in effect while litigation over it plays out.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights supporters quickly condemned the decision, which also came down weeks after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.propublica.org/article/georgia-abortion-ban-amber-thurman-death"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 news broke}}}\uc2  that two Georgia mothers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/20/trump-harris-election-abortion-georgia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Amber Nicole Thurman and Candi Miller}}}\uc2 , died after being unable to access legal abortions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery minute this harmful six-week \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban is in place, Georgians suffer,\u8221\'20\'1D Monica Simpson, executive director of the SisterSong Women of Color Reproductive Justice Collective, said in a statement. SisterSong Women of Color Reproductive Justice Collective is a plaintiff in the legal battle over the ban.\par \par \uc2 Simpson continued: \u8220\'20\'1CDenying our community members the lifesaving care they deserve jeopardizes their lives, safety, and health \u8211\'20\'13 all for the sake of power and control over our bodies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Last week, the Fulton county superior judge Robert McBurney ruled that Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s six-week ban, which outlaws \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before many people even know they are pregnant, is unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWomen are not some piece of collectively owned community property the disposition of which is decided by majority vote,\u8221\'20\'1D McBurney wrote in his fiery 26-page opinion. \u8220\'20\'1CForcing a woman to carry an unwanted, not-yet-viable fetus to term violates her constitutional rights to liberty and privacy, even taking into consideration whatever bundle of rights the not-yet-viable fetus may have.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 McBurney\u8217\'20\'19s ruling permitted Georgia \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to perform abortions up until about 22 weeks of pregnancy. In the week that the six-week ban was not in effect, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://stateaffairs.com/georgia/courts/georgia-abortion-ban/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  clinics and their supporters}}}\uc2  said interest in \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  appointments increased.\par \par \uc2 However, Georgia\u8217\'20\'19s Republican attorney general, \uc2 Chris Carr\uc2 , quickly appealed McBurney\u8217\'20\'19s ruling. On Monday, only one judge dissented in part from the ruling to reinstate the ban. One judge did not participate, while another had been disqualified from taking part in the case.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFundamentally, the state should not be in the business of enforcing laws that have been determined to violate fundamental rights guaranteed to millions of individuals under the Georgia Constitution,\u8221\'20\'1D Justice John Ellington wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CThe \u8216\'20\'18status quo\u8217\'20\'19 that should be maintained is the state of the law before the challenged laws took effect.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the two years since the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  overturned Roe v Wade, more than a dozen states have banned most or virtually all abortions. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also become a major issue in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-elections-2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 presidential elections}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 including in Georgia, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  are jockeying to win.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241007eka7002s3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
