\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harris talks  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights on Call Her Daddy podcast while bashing Trump\u8217\'20\'19s \u8216\'20\'18protector\u8217\'20\'19 of women claim \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Coral Murphy Marcos \par \uc2 5,333 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2024\par 00:10 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This blog is now closed. Read more from our politics coverage here\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 This blog is closed \u8211\'20\'13 thanks for following along. Here is a summary of today\u8217\'20\'19s key developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s interview on Call Her Daddy with Alex Cooper aired on Sunday. The host, whose podcast targets a diverse set of audiences, and the vice-president discussed issues revolving around \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reproductive healthcare, housing and student debt relief.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  delivered his roughly two-hour speech at a rally in Juneau, Wisconsin. The former president was standing behind barriers of bulletproof glass, which is now a standard \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  practice at outdoor rallies.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Arizona senator \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2  criticized \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  during an interview on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union for supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  at a rally in Pennsylvania this weekend.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  ordered 500 more troops to assist with Hurricane Helene relief efforts. The troops will move into western North Carolina and assist with the response and recovery efforts after the deadly and devastating {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/hurricanes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane}}}\uc2  Helene.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  said during his appearance on Fox News this morning that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s agenda would destroy the US economy, while he supported \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plan to lower costs and stimulate job growth.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  finished her interview with Call Her Daddy\u8217\'20\'19s Alex Cooper by pledging to fight for student debt relief and listing key issues she hopes to address if she\u8217\'20\'19s elected president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI care about making sure that people are entitled to and receive the freedoms that they are due,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CI care about lifting people up and making sure that you are protected from harm. I care about tapping into the ambitions and the aspirations of people knowing that we are capable of so much.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alex Cooper and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  discussed JD Vance\u8217\'20\'19s age-old sexist \u8220\'20\'1Cchildless cat ladies\u8221\'20\'1D trope, but Harris was asked what she would do as president to help generations who feel that the economy hinders them from having children.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHousing is too expensive and we need to increase the housing supply,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CPart of my plan is to work with home builders in the private sector to create tax incentives to build by the end of my first term, 3,000,000 more housing units.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPart of my plan is to give 100 million more people who basically are middle class working people, tax cuts, including for young parents, a $6,000 tax cut for the first year of their child\u8217\'20\'19s life, which helps them buy a crib or a car seat or clothing and just get through that first year,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 During an episode of the podcast Call Her Daddy, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  condemned Arkansas governor \uc2 Sarah Huckabee Sanders\uc2  after Sanders said that the presidential candidate \u8220\'20\'1Cdoesn\u8217\'20\'19t have anything keeping her humble\u8221\'20\'1D because she doesn\u8217\'20\'19t have children.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think she understands that there are a whole lot of women out here who, one, are not aspiring to be humble,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said during the podcast.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president discussed her relationship with her stepchildren, Cole and Ella Emhoff, who are the biological children from her husband\u8217\'20\'19s, Doug Emhoff, first marriage.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have our family by blood and then we have our family by love. And I have both,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was asked by Alex Cooper if she could think about any law that \u8220\'20\'1Cgives the government the power to make a decision about a man\u8217\'20\'19s body\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harris laughed and said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are a work in progress.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CPart of the strength of our country and our evolution as a country has been through the fight for the expansion of rights. Not the restriction of rights,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.44pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Alex Cooper asked \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  to clarify a claim former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  made during last month\u8217\'20\'19s presidential debate, where he falsely claimed that Democrats support abortions \u8220\'20\'1Cafter birth\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cexecuting\u8221\'20\'1D babies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat is not happening anywhere in the United States,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt is not happening and it\u8217\'20\'19s a lie.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 She also labeled as \u8220\'20\'1Cinsulting\u8221\'20\'1D his claim that women in their ninth month of pregnancy are electing to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.27pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and Alex Cooper continued to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and reproductive healthcare during a Call Her Daddy episode aired on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou don\u8217\'20\'19t have to abandon your faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be telling her what to do,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said in the podcast.\par \par \uc2 Harris added: \u8220\'20\'1CWhat\u8217\'20\'19s so outrageous about it is a bunch of these guys up in these state capitals are writing these decisions because they somehow have decided that they\u8217\'20\'19re in a better position to tell you what\u8217\'20\'19s in your best interest than you are to know what\u8217\'20\'19s in your own best interest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris condemns Trump for claiming to be 'protector' of women\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  condemned former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for calling himself the \u8220\'20\'1Cprotector\u8221\'20\'1D of women at a rally in Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the same guy who said that women should be punished for having abortions,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said on Alex Cooper\u8217\'20\'19s podcast Call Her Daddy.\par \par \uc2 Harris went on to talk about the state of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access currently in the country.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe majority of women who receive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care are mothers,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery state in the South except for Virginia has an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  responded to questions from Call Her Daddy\u8217\'20\'19s Alex Cooper, elaborating on why she decided to become a prosecutor, the guidelines for reporting sexual assault, and the need to talk about the issue more.\par \par \uc2 enltrThere are a number of young women for whom Call Her Daddy is their go-to source for entertainment. The fact that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is talking directly to them, through an interview with their trusted messenger, Alex Cooper, matters. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/PU3HPtxD1w"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/PU3HPtxD1w}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Rachel Janfaza (@racheljanfaza) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/racheljanfaza/status/1843020804348383731?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 In her interview with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , Alex Cooper asked the vice-president about the lessons she learned from her mother regarding mental health, the ways she has taken accountability during her vice-presidency, and what she thinks her mother would say if she became the next president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 Later on, Cooper referenced some of the harsh descriptions former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has used against Harris during the race, including questioning her mental health. She asked Harris how this affected her.\par \par \uc2 Harris said:\par \par \uc2 I think it\u8217\'20\'19s really important not to let other people define you, and usually those people who will attempt to do it don\u8217\'20\'19t know you.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.01pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  finished his remarks in Juneau, Wisconsin, which ran for about two hours.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 During her interview with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , Call Her Daddy host Alex Cooper quickly touched on a soft spot for the Harris campaign, which is the vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s lack of interviews with the media. She asked Harris why she decided to come on the podcast.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think you and your listeners have really got this thing, right, which is one of the best ways to communicate with people is to be real, you know, and to talk about the things that people really care about,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhat I love about what you do is that your voice in your show is really about your listeners,\u8221\'20\'1D she added. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd I think especially now, this is a moment in the country and in life where people really want to know they\u8217\'20\'19re seen and heard and that they\u8217\'20\'19re part of a community, that they\u8217\'20\'19re not out there alone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 The host of the comedy and advice podcast Call Her Daddy, Alex Cooper, said at the start of her episode with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  that she invited former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to come on the show.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf he also wants to have a meaningful, in-depth conversation about women\u8217\'20\'19s rights in this country, then he is welcome on Call Her Daddy anytime,\u8221\'20\'1D Cooper said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Harris's Call Her Daddy interview drops\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s interview on Call Her Daddy with Alex Cooper just dropped.\par \par \uc2 The host, who targets a diverse set of audiences, begins the episode by explaining to her listeners why she decided to interview the vice-president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs you guys know, I do not usually discuss politics or have politicians on the show,\u8221\'20\'1D Cooper said. \u8220\'20\'1CAt the end of the day, I couldn\u8217\'20\'19t see a world in which one of the main conversations in this election is women, and I\u8217\'20\'19m not a part of it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump brought Dodge county sheriff Dale Schmidt to the stage, along with a group of other Wisconsin sheriffs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI am proud to announce that all of these sheriffs are among a very small amount of sheriffs and law enforcement across our country that support you,\u8221\'20\'1D Schmidt said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Dodge county, in this 2024 election, there are zero drop boxes for the election,\u8221\'20\'1D the sheriff said proudly.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 Eric Hovde\uc2 , Republican Senate candidate in Wisconsin took the stage during Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally.\par \par \uc2 Hovde attacked his rival \uc2 Tammy Baldwin\uc2  and said: \u8220\'20\'1CAll of you go work hard, go grab every friend, colleague, neighbor, and let\u8217\'20\'19s restore this great country and get President Trump and me to Washington.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump also invited Republican senator Ron Johnson to the stage. He congratulated Trump for his alliance with the ex-independent presidential candidate {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/robert-f-kennedy-jr"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robert F Kennedy Jr}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are actually going through a huge problem with chronic health and children\u8217\'20\'19s health, but you are right about the enemy within. They are dividing us. They are destroying this nation. And by aligning with \uc2 Bobby Kennedy\uc2 , you are setting the example,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 Kennedy has been campaigning for Trump since he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/23/robert-f-kennedy-jr-drops-out-endorses-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ended his own independent presidential bid}}}\uc2  to support the Republican nominee.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  baselessly linked inflation and the country\u8217\'20\'19s economic woes to the influx of migrants in the US.\par \par \uc2 He falsely claimed leaders in other countries are emptying their jails and sending inmates to the US.\par \par \uc2 He later presented a chart that shows the rate of migrant entries in the US, suggesting a decline during his presidency.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI kiss it every night,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said about his chart. \u8220\'20\'1CI take it to bed with me every single night.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  called Wisconsin governor \uc2 Tony Evers\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Clousy governor\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hate to say it with your Democrat governor, you have some of the highest electricity prices, and highest energy costs is just about at the top in Wisconsin,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 He then said he plans to double the electricity production for the development of artificial intelligence.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need tremendous electric here so that other people that are into this whole world of this, it\u8217\'20\'19s a new world, but it\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a very big world, a very fascinating world,\u8221\'20\'1D he said about the field of AI.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump attacks Harris's tax policy and calls her a 'tax queen'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attacked \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s tax policy, calling her a \u8220\'20\'1Ctax queen\u8221\'20\'1D and misleading attendees with a claim that Harris plans to raise taxes on US families.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve never seen somebody that openly campaigns on the fact that they\u8217\'20\'19re going to raise taxes,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 He then showed a campaign ad, composed of a compilation of clips of Harris saying wants to raise taxes.\par \par \uc2 In reality, Harris has said she plans to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/25/harris-opportunity-economic-plan-middle-class"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut corporate tax rates}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said rifle owners and the Christian community don\u8217\'20\'19t vote \u8220\'20\'1Cas much as they should\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvangelicals don\u8217\'20\'19t vote that much, and if they did vote, we could never lose an election,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.50pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump claims media favors Harris and they 'hate our country'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  claimed that the media favors \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in their coverage and they \u8220\'20\'1Chate our country\u8221\'20\'1D. He continued to make anti-immigrant and transphobic comments.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI can\u8217\'20\'19t understand. Why do they want open borders? Why do they want sex change operations for people that are too young to even think about it? Why do they want men playing in women\u8217\'20\'19s sports?\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe actually are now the party of common sense,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think that\u8217\'20\'19s what I like calling us now, party of common sense.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.26pm BST\par \par \uc2 The former president called \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cgood guy\u8221\'20\'1D a day after the \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  founder made an appearance at Trump\u8217\'20\'19s rally on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 He also attacked his rival \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , calling her \u8220\'20\'1Cgrossly incompetent\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CKamala is not wonderful,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said. \u8220\'20\'1CWith four more years of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , your long nightmare is just beginning.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.36pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said the response to Hurricane Helene in the south-eastern US was \u8220\'20\'1Cprobably worse than Katrina\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to the devastating storm in 2005.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s hard to beat, right? Worse than Katrina. They didn\u8217\'20\'19t do too good a job, either,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump calls Biden administration 'the most corrupt people'\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  called the Biden administration \u8220\'20\'1Cthe most corrupt people\u8221\'20\'1D during his rally in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the very beginning of this journey, I\u8217\'20\'19ve been on a mission to rescue our nation from a failed and corrupt political establishment and corrupt people,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis country is in big trouble. We\u8217\'20\'19re a failing nation. We are a failing nation. We\u8217\'20\'19re a nation in decline. We\u8217\'20\'19re a nation in distress, and we\u8217\'20\'19re going to get it fixed very quickly,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CJust 30 days from now, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to win the state of Wisconsin, we\u8217\'20\'19re going to defeat \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Trump said.\par \par \uc2 He called his rally on Saturday an \u8220\'20\'1Cunbelievable evening\u8221\'20\'1D, when he returned to Butler, Pennsylvania, the site of his assassination attempt.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe had 100,000 people, and there was love, and I had a fantastic\u8230\'20\'26 opera singer, and he went up and he sang \u8216\'20\'18Ave Maria\u8217\'20\'19,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump starts speech on-time in Juneau, Wisconsin\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  started his speech on time in Juneau, Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 The former president is standing behind barriers of bulletproof glass, which is now a standard \uc2 US Secret Service\uc2  practice at outdoor rallies.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll be following his remarks.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arkansas senator Tom Cotton dodged questions regarding the results of the 2020 elections during an interview with NBC News\u8217\'20\'19s Meet the Press, where he struggled to admit that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost the race.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was elected president in 2020. It was an unfair election in many ways,\u8221\'20\'1D Cotton said on Sunday. \u8220\'20\'1CYou had states that were changing their election practices or election laws, sometimes in violation of their constitution.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was elected president. Everything has gone to hell in a handbasket as a result,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has embarked on a week-long media blitz, hurtling from TV studios and late-night shows to podcast interviews as she seeks to gain an edge over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in the US election\u8217\'20\'19s key battleground states that remain nail-bitingly close.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president\u8217\'20\'19s decision to face a raft of largely friendly media outlets came as the campaigns entered the final 30 days. More than 1.4 million Americans have already cast their ballots in early voting across 30 states.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic nominee\u8217\'20\'19s whirlwind media tour has been carefully crafted for maximum reach and minimum risk. Harris has talked to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/cbs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS}}}\uc2  News show 60 Minutes, along with the popular podcast Call Her Daddy.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday she hits the media capital, New York, for appearances on ABC News\u8217\'20\'19s daytime behemoth The View and the Howard Stern Show, followed by a recording with late-night host {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/stephen-colbert"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Stephen Colbert}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The first of a flurry of comments from Harris was put out by 60 Minutes on Sunday before a full broadcast on Monday. Harris will appear alone, after Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbsnews.com/news/60-minutes-election-special-harris-trump-oct-7/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to be interviewed}}}\uc2  by the election special which has been a staple of US election coverage for more than half a century.\par \par \uc2 In a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/60Minutes/status/1842935494398591073"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 short clip}}}\uc2  released by 60 Minutes, Harris was asked whether the Biden-Harris administration had any sway over the actions of \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , the hardline prime minister of Israel who appears not to listen to Washington. Asked whether the US had a \u8220\'20\'1Creal close ally\u8221\'20\'1D in Netanyahu, she replied: \u8220\'20\'1CWith all due respect, the better question is: do we have an important alliance between the American people and the Israeli people? And the answer to that question is yes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since Harris\u8217\'20\'19s meteoric propulsion as Democratic presidential nominee after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  stepped aside, her relative avoidance of press or TV interviews has become a point of contention on the campaign trail. Republican leaders and pundits on Fox News routinely accuse her of being media-shy.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Harris\u8217\'20\'19s media blitz:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/06/harris-media-whirlwind-trump-battleground-states"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Harris embarks on media blitz and tries to edge out Trump in key swing states}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.25pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden orders 500 more troops to assist with Hurricane Helene relief efforts\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said on Sunday he ordered another 500 active-duty troops to move into western North Carolina and assist with the response and recovery efforts after the deadly and devastating {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/hurricanes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane}}}\uc2  Helene.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith a total of 1,500 troops now supplementing a robust on-the-ground effort - including more than 6,100 National Guardsmen and more than 7,000 Federal personnel - my administration is sparing no resource to support families as they begin their road to rebuilding,\u8221\'20\'1D Biden said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 He also said he was being briefed on tropical storm Milton as it strengthened across the Gulf of Mexico. Milton, which strengthened into a category one hurricane on Sunday, is expected to make landfall on Florida on Tuesday or Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Adam Schiff says Trump 'will contest' election results if he loses\par \par \uc2 California representative Adam Schiff said during an interview with NBC News\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1CMeet the Press\u8221\'20\'1D on Sunday that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cwill contest\u8221\'20\'1D the election results if he loses.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf it is close, if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  loses again, as I expect that he will, he will contest it,\u8221\'20\'1D Schiff said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe has more reason to contest it than he did before, not because of any flaw in the election, but because \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  believes, and perhaps with reason, that if he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t succeed at the ballot box, he may be going to jail. So he\u8217\'20\'19s going to challenge the results.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Republican Senate candidate and former Maryland mayor \uc2 Larry Hogan\uc2  said during an interview on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union that if he\u8217\'20\'19s elected, he will not support cabinet or supreme court nominees who do not garner bipartisan support in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI would make that pledge. If we can\u8217\'20\'19t get any bipartisan buy-in, then I\u8217\'20\'19m not going to vote for that person,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn Washington, we can\u8217\'20\'19t even seem to get one vote,\u8221\'20\'1D Hogan added. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s like Democrats will only vote for Democrats and Republicans will only vote for Republicans. If there\u8217\'20\'19s one place that we should not be playing politics, it\u8217\'20\'19s on appointments to the supreme court.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.22pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Charlotte Observer\u8217\'20\'19s editorial board published an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.charlotteobserver.com/opinion/article293483114.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 op-ed}}}\uc2  titled: Shame on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for worsening NC\u8217\'20\'19s Helene tragedy with political lies.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, Trump accused the federal government and Democratic governor Roy Cooper of \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing out of their way to not help people in Republican areas. MAGA!\u8221\'20\'1D Trump also said that the Biden administration has \u8220\'20\'1Cleft Americans to drown\u8221\'20\'1D in North Carolina and other states.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is not a situation to capitalize on for political gain,\u8221\'20\'1D reads the op-ed. \u8220\'20\'1CBut former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has politicized the situation at every turn, spreading falsehoods and conspiracies that fracture the community instead of bringing it together.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more context on some of the false claims made by Trump:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/sep/30/trump-visits-georgia-after-hurricane-helene-false-biden-claims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump visits hurricane-ravaged Georgia and makes false claims about Biden}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of a rally by the Republic presidential nominee, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in Juneau, Wisconsin, a line began forming near the event venue at the Dodge county airport.\par \par \uc2 enltrQuite the line has formed ahead of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s rally in Dodge County. It\u8217\'20\'19ll be hours yet before he speaks. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/aAQGiI8Bpb"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/aAQGiI8Bpb}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Alison Dirr (@AlisonDirr) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AlisonDirr/status/1842927516505501993?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The Milwaukee Journal Sentinel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.jsonline.com/story/news/politics/elections/2024/10/06/live-updates-donald-trump-rallies-in-juneau-wisconsin-today/75543492007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that attendees were greeted by a \u8220\'20\'1Clarger-than-life Trump inflatable with which some were taking photos\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The former president\u8217\'20\'19s speech is scheduled for 2pm CT, buthe usually starts his speeches at least half an hour after the slated time.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.03pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.42pm BST\par \par \uc2 Arizona senator \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2  criticizes Musk for supporting Trump\par \par \uc2 During an interview on CNN\u8217\'20\'19s State of the Union, Arizona senator \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2  criticized \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  for supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Saturday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/06/donald-trump-makes-a-theatrical-return-to-butler-scene-of-assassination-attempt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Musk joined Trump at a rally}}}\uc2  in Butler, Pennsylvania, and made the baseless claim that if Trump\u8217\'20\'19s supporters fail to turn out, \u8220\'20\'1Cthis will be the last election\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Kelly said that Musk was \u8220\'20\'1Chypocritically standing next to the guy that tried to overturn the last \u8211\'20\'13 the 2020 election on January 6, saying that this is somehow going to be the last election and they\u8217\'20\'19re going to take away your vote.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt just doesn\u8217\'20\'19t pass the logic test,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not lost on me, and it shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t be lost on the American people that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , when he was president, gave a giant tax cut to billionaires,\u8221\'20\'1D Kelly said during the interview. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is the richest person in the world. He\u8217\'20\'19s got a tremendous amount of interest in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  being elected president.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltr. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SenMarkKelly?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @SenMarkKelly}}}\uc2  calls \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  "hypocritical" for supporting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and tells {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DanaBashCNN?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @DanaBashCNN}}}\uc2 , \u8220\'20\'1CHe's got a tremendous amount of interest in \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  being elected president because\u8230\'20\'26 billionaires like \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  will get their giant tax cut again.\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pBuxaKMyDs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/pBuxaKMyDs}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 State of the Union (@CNNSOTU) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CNNSOTU/status/1842951915480461529?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.20pm BST\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , the Republican nominee, has spent years saying the unsayable to entertain, goad and grab attention. But his pronouncements over the past few weeks have plumbed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/24/donald-trump-mental-fitness-campaign"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new depths of absurdity and incoherence}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trump, 78, increasingly slurs or stumbles over his words, raising fears over cognitive decline. He is slipping in polls against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and knows that defeat could lead to criminal trials and even prison. After a decade of dominating American politics, critics say, Trump could be in the throes of a final meltdown.\par \par \uc2 His verbal output now is \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolute batshittery\u8221\'20\'1D, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tarasetmayer.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tara Setmayer}}}\uc2 , a former Republican communications director on Capitol Hill. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are not the musings of a well-adjusted adult. He demonstrates daily how unfit he is to have the most powerful position in the world. \u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump was mostly given a pass by the mainstream media, Setmayer added, because of the intense focus on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2024/07/05/biden-aging-recent-months/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden\u8217\'20\'19s age and mental acuity}}}\uc2  when he was still running. \u8220\'20\'1CNow the focus is solely on him because he is the oldest candidate in this race. His kookery is even more highlighted now than before because he is alone on an island with his deterioration.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump has always thrown dead cats on tables, as the metaphor goes, offering his fans the thrill of transgression and watching with glee as liberals howl with outrage. His run for president in 2016 was characterised by racially divisive rhetoric and a constant stream of controversies that dominated news cycles and forced rival \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  into reactive mode.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more on Trump\u8217\'20\'19s recent pronouncements:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/oct/06/trump-behavior-final-meltdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Undisciplined, unhinged and deranged\u8217\'20\'19: will Trump\u8217\'20\'19s strange behavior hurt him at the polls?}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Speaker Mike Johnson sidestepped questions on the results of the 2020 race during an interview on ABC\u8217\'20\'19s This Week with George Stephanopoulos.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a gotcha game. You want us to litigate things that happened four years ago when we\u8217\'20\'19re talking about the future,\u8221\'20\'1D Johnson said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been the president for almost four years. Everybody needs to get over this and move forward,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.40pm BST\par \par \uc2 Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is expected to arrive at Santa Barbara, California, on Sunday to kick off a West Coast fundraising blitz on behalf of the Harris Victory Fund.\par \par \uc2 The Democratic vice-presidential pick will make his way through California and Washington, delivering campaign remarks in cities along the coast.\par \par \uc2 Walz is scheduled to deliver remarks at receptions in San Diego, Montecito, Los Angeles, and Sacramento before heading up to Washington.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 CBS\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s 60 Minutes will air an interview with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Monday. The network released a sneak peek into the interview, where Bill Whitaker asked Harris if the US lacks influence over Israel\u8217\'20\'19s Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe aid that we have given Israel allowed Israel to defend itself against 200 ballistic missiles that were just meant to attack the Israelis and the people of Israel,\u8221\'20\'1D Harris said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen we think about the threat that Hamas Hezbollah presents [and] Iran, I think that it is, without any question, our imperative to do what we can to allow Israel to defend itself against those kinds of attacks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 enltrMonday, on a 60 Minutes election special, Bill Whitaker asks Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  if the U.S. lacks influence over American ally Israel\u8217\'20\'19s Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/TG3WOCA23A"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/TG3WOCA23A}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IH6MXMjuCP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IH6MXMjuCP}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 60 Minutes (@60Minutes) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/60Minutes/status/1842935494398591073?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 October 6, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 During his appearance on Fox News this morning, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  said \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s agenda would destroy the American economy, while he supported \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s plan to lower costs and stimulate job growth.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWell, we saw a blockbuster jobs report this week,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe saw interest rates come down, and we\u8217\'20\'19ve also seen that Vice-President Harris is laying out a middle-class agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CI was in Ohio yesterday, in Cleveland, in Cincinnati, and talking about this. Folks in Ohio know that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policies led to 180,000 manufacturing jobs leaving.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump: Donald 'knew my beliefs' on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the day they met\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump was asked whether \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  knew she would express strong support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in her upcoming memoir, where she emphasized that women should have the autonomy to decide whether to have children based on their own convictions, without government interference or pressure.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYes, he knew my position and my beliefs since the day we met, and I believe in individual freedom,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI want to decide what I wanted to do with my body. I think I don\u8217\'20\'19t want government in my personal business,\u8221\'20\'1D she added.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.54pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.51pm BST\par \par \uc2 Former first lady Melania Trump sat down with Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Maria Bartiromo\uc2  this morning, where she showed her unwavering support for her husband, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t believe in polls. I never did,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CI think in the end, people really see it, what\u8217\'20\'19s going on in the country and how this leadership is performing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 4.32pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Democratic vice-presidential pick, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , sat down with Fox News Sunday\u8217\'20\'19s Shannon Bream, where he discussed how the overturning of Roe v. Wade has affected women.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe real issue here is women being forced into miscarriages, women being forced to go back home, get sepsis and potentially die,\u8221\'20\'1D Walz said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.39pm BST\par \par \uc2 Good morning, US politics blog readers. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  is scheduled to speak at an event in Juneau, Wisconsin, on Sunday, his fourth scheduled stop in eight days in the state. Republicans are trying to rack up support in Wisconsin, which has only flipped red once in the past 40 years, when Trump won the state in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and her running mate \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  are slated to sit down with major TV personalities this week. Walz is slated to sit down with Fox News\u8217\'20\'19s Shannon Bream on Sunday for his first solo interview. On Monday, he\u8217\'20\'19ll join Jimmy Kimmel Live. On Tuesday, Harris will be in New York for appearances on The View, The Howard Stern Show, and The Late Show with Stephen Colbert.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else is happening:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 After the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US supreme court}}}\uc2  granted \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  significant immunity from prosecution for actions during his presidency, the court is set to embark on its next nine-month term on Monday with public confidence in the court still reeling following the ruling compounded by the ethically dubious conduct of some justices.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The White House moved Saturday to quash claims that government officials control the weather, including a far-fetched rumor circulating on social media that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/hurricane-helene"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hurricane Helene}}}\uc2  was an engineered storm to allow corporations to mine regional lithium deposits.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Republican fearmongering about crime in major cities like Atlanta is serving to stoke racial tensions and suppress the growing political power of Black Democrats, despite a decline in crime rates, writes \uc2 The Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s George Chidi.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241006eka6001gw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
