\par\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 In the US, rats could soon have better birth-control access than women\b0\par\par\uc2 Arwa Mahdawi \par \uc2 1,243 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2024\par 13:03 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 New York is pushing birth control to curb its rodent problem \u8211\'20\'13 at a time when women\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  in other US states are under attack. Oh, the irony\par \par \uc2 The fight for rat-productive rights\par \par \uc2 Eric Adams, we recently learned, seems to have spent the bulk of his time as mayor of New York trying to wangle criminally cheap business class tickets from \uc2 Turkish Airlines\uc2 . But while Adams may have made history by becoming the first sitting mayor of New York to be indicted on federal corruption charges, the fact that he has a slightly wonky moral compass is old news. Even before being appointed mayor, there were questions about Adam\u8217\'20\'19s truthfulness, including a long-running debate about whether the swagger-obsessed candidate lived in Brooklyn, as he insisted he did, or New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 Still, let\u8217\'20\'19s give the mayor his due, shall we? It would be unfair to say he\u8217\'20\'19s spent the entirety of his time in high office trying to live the high life. Adams, who appointed New York City\u8217\'20\'19s first \u8220\'20\'1Crat tsar\u8221\'20\'1D last year, has also spent a lot of time thinking about the city\u8217\'20\'19s rodent problem. \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think there\u8217\'20\'19s been a mayor in history that says how much he hates rats,\u8221\'20\'1D he grandly proclaimed during New York City\u8217\'20\'19s inaugural Rat Summit in September. \u8220\'20\'1CI dislike rats.\u8221\'20\'1D Adams added that he was confident New York could \u8220\'20\'1Clook forward to a new paradigm in urban rat management\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Wheelie bins are part of that exciting new paradigm in urban rat management. There was much mirth on social media over the summer when it transpired that New York City had paid McKinsey over a million dollars to figure out whether it might be a good idea to put loose rubbish in a bin. (Or, in management consultant speech, \u8220\'20\'1Ccontainerize\u8221\'20\'1D it.) Now the brainiacs in Adams\u8217\'20\'19s orbit have come up with an exciting new paradigm shift: the city council recently greenlit pilot schemes to deploy ContraPest, a type of rodent birth control.\par \par \uc2 The irony that New York is investing in rodent contraceptives at a time when women\u8217\'20\'19s access to reproductive services across the US is under fire hasn\u8217\'20\'19t gone unnoticed. Social media has been filled with wry observations along the lines of \u8220\'20\'1Cit\u8217\'20\'19s easier to get \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a rodent in New York than it is for a woman to get \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  in most of the country\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Because pedants never take a day off I will note that \uc2 quip\uc2  isn\u8217\'20\'19t strictly true. At least for the moment it isn\u8217\'20\'19t. But if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins the election and the extremists backing him have their way then it might very well be true that rats will soon have better access to birth control in the US than women. Over the past few years, rightwingers have started to speak more openly about the possibility of banning birth control. In 2022, for example, an Idaho Republican leader suggested he\u8217\'20\'19d consider banning certain forms of birth control, including the morning-after pill. Around the same time the governor of Mississippi refused to rule out future contraception bans during an interview on NBC.\par \par \uc2 This isn\u8217\'20\'19t just all talk. Over the years the right has managed to undermine access to birth control in a number of alarming ways. In 2022, for example, an appeals court ruled that federally funded family planning centers in Texas must receive parental consent before prescribing birth control to teenagers. (Previously federal courts had found that the national title X program guaranteed minors the right to access birth control without parental involvement.) Then, this summer Senate Republicans blocked a bill that would have recognized a legal right to contraception.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps most importantly, anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  activists have also been doggedly trying to argue that certain birth control methods, such as Plan B and certain intrauterine devices (IUDs), are abortifacients because they may prevent the implantation of fertilized eggs. While it\u8217\'20\'19s unlikely that we\u8217\'20\'19ll see any sort of direct push to outlaw access to contraceptives, expect to see anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws sneakily widen to restrict access to birth control. As advocates have noted, Roe was not toppled in a day\u8211\'20\'13and access to contraceptives won\u8217\'20\'19t be overturned imminently. But anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  extremists have made clear what their endgame is. And when these people tell you who they are, you\u8217\'20\'19d better believe them.\par \par \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18I\u8217\'20\'19ve never worn trousers up a mountain, and I never will\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 I find cycling in a dress awkward. Meanwhile, Cecilia Llusco, one of Bolivia\u8217\'20\'19s first female Indigenous mountain climbers, scales icy peaks in a pollera: a traditional voluminous floral skirt. Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this wonderful \uc2 Guardian\uc2  feature on the Cholita climbers of Bolivia\u8211\'20\'13it has some incredible photographs.\par \par \uc2 Melania Trump wants you to know she is passionately pro-choice\par \par \uc2 In her new memoir the former first lady writes, \u8220\'20\'1CWhy should anyone other than the woman herself have the power to determine what she does with her own body.\u8221\'20\'1D Good question Melania! Ever tried asking your husband that? Speaking of which, Melania\u8217\'20\'19s decision to speak out about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights a month before the election feels part of a calculated strategy by the Trump campaign to soften its rhetoric on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Prominent Palestinian journalist Wafa Aludaini killed in an Israeli airstrike\par \par \uc2 Wafa was killed alongside her husband, her five-year-old daughter and her seven-month-old son. As \uc2 Reporters Without Borders\uc2  recently noted: \u8220\'20\'1CAt the rate journalists are being killed in Gaza, there will soon be no-one left to keep you informed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 India\u8217\'20\'19s government thinks criminalizing marital rape would be \u8220\'20\'1Cexcessively harsh\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One in 25 women in India have faced sexual violence from their husbands, the BBC reports. And, of course, nothing happens to most of these men because marital rape is not a criminal offence in India. For years now, campaigners have been petitioning India\u8217\'20\'19s supreme court to try and change this but have faced enormous resistance from the government, religious groups, and men\u8217\'20\'19s rights activists. An affidavait submitted by India\u8217\'20\'19s Interior Ministry on Thursday argued criminalizing marital rape \u8220\'20\'1Cmay seriously impact the conjugal relationship and may lead to serious disturbances in the institution of marriage.\u8221\'20\'1D It also said that while a man \u8220\'20\'1Cdoes not have any fundamental right to violate the consent of his wife\u8221\'20\'1D including marital rape under anti-rape laws would be \u8220\'20\'1Cexcessively harsh\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cdisproportionate\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Mexico\u8217\'20\'19s first woman president announces reforms to battle gender discrimination\par \par \uc2 On her second full day in office, \uc2 Claudia Sheinbaum\uc2  said her government had proposed reforms to broaden women\u8217\'20\'19s rights, including a constitutional guarantee of equal pay for equal work.\par \par \uc2 EU\uc2  court rules gender and nationality enough to grant Afghan women asylum\par \par \uc2 An important ruling by the European court of justice recognizes Afghan women as a persecuted group.\par \par \uc2 The week in podtriarchy\par \par \uc2 In 2012 Melania Trump famously posted a photo of a smiling beluga whale with the caption \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat is she thinking?\u8221\'20\'1D Despite the fact that entire podcast episodes have been devoted to this question, we still don\u8217\'20\'19t know. Scientists have recently discovered, however, that bottlenose dolphins \u8216\'20\'18smile\u8217\'20\'19 at each other to communicate during social play. The open-mouth expression is meant to signal fun and avoid conflict. So, in other words, dolphins have better social skills than many politicians.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020241005eka50015p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
